  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102715270-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "accordingly the protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the description of the claims and the scope of equivalents thereof.1 spawning area 2 water supply area 3 egg transfer unit 10 storage tank 20 drinking water pipe 30 drinking water pump 40 washing nozzle 50 washing pipe 60 washing pump 70 chlorine dioxide gas generating unit 80 gas pipe 90 water pipe a0 water supply valve b0 concentration measurement unit c0 water level measurement unit d0 contamination measurement unit d1 projector d2 camera e0 intensive cleaning section e1 guide rail e2 concentrated cleaning nozzle e3 concentrated cleaning pipe e4 concentrated washing pump e5 drive unit 110 1st tank 120 2nd tank 130 3rd tank 210 1st reaction tank 220 second reaction tank 230 third reaction tank 310 1st gas discharge pipe 320 2nd gas discharge pipe 330 3rd gas discharge pipe 400 integrated pipe 710 1st metering pump 720 2nd metering pump 730 3rd quantitative pump 1110 1st auxiliary tank 1120 second auxiliary tank 1130 third auxiliary tank 1200 level sensor 1300 alarm 1400 reservoir tank 1500 aeration device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_622", "text": "therefore if the water is confined in a certain place for a long time the pollution is further increased by the material decomposition action and the material bonding action so the water stored in the water storage space is always maintained at the full water level and the water flowing from the upstream through the lower part of the water gate frequent discharge is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and if water is used to discharge water from the reservoir through the lower part of the water gate the substances contained in the water are combined to combine the substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which the power generation water movement line 331 is installed in a form that goes over mountains and hills 221 and then an upward discharge line 332 is formed in a shape at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the lower height and horizontal state of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by going over mountains and hills due to the action of gravity a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which the lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inflow amount and an upper and lower raising and lowering device 5810 is connected to adjust the pipe in the upper and lower direction according to the inflow level of river water that changes frequently and a rising discharge pipe 101 a falling discharge pipe 103 a right angled falling pipe 202 a water storage tank 201 a discharge amount control unit 203 a right angled falling pipe 202 and in a method of producing electricity by using the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 equipped with a power generation unit 33 a structure in which a water storage tank 8000 and a water purification promotion storage tank 11111 are constructed by dredging to a depth 20 to 600 times deeper than the surface 9000 of the soil layer constituting a river or stream and then the foundation concrete 800 is poured on the surface 9000 constituting a river or stream and the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 are constructed on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 and the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 is constructed to store river water on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 a structure in which an intermediate storage water inflow line 501 is formed to pump the stored water stored inside the upstream side of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 toward the rear side starting from the internal ground surface 9000 in the upstream direction of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 penetrating the middle part of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 to the rear part a structure in which a lower movement line 1919 is connected to the end of the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 to move the power generation water introduced through the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 downward a structure in which an entrance 1332 used for inspecting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 after constructing the above power generation water transfer line 331 by crossing mountains and hills 221 a structure in which a v shaped rising discharge line 332 is formed at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the horizontal state and the bottom height of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by gravity over mountains and hills a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which a lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706118-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "due to this replenishment when the water level in the brine reservoir 5 reaches the upper limit the electric valve 11 is automatically closed to block the supply of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "moreover the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "it is preferable that the upper portion of the soil 113 is filled with sand and gravel 114 to prevent the soil 113 filled in the soil receiving groove 111a from being lost due to the water level fluctuation as well as an optimum natural condition for scattering aquatic insects and fish in the aquatic space 112a can be formed as described later"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100744631-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "hydrologic control unit for adjusting the connected via the plurality of chlorine ion meter and wired and wireless communication means and stores the concentration data received from the chlorine ion meter and to identify the variation in the water quality compared to the comparative chlorine ion concentration data stored in the database and stores the result a main server for outputting and transmitting to a remote place and a management server connected to the main server through a wired wireless communication means and controlling the operation of the water level or the sewage treatment plant of the reservoir into which the initial rainwater flows in accordance with the change in the water quality of the initial rainwater transmitted from the main server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100437342-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a two way transmission and reception wireless data signal using a dedicated frequency between a motor pump of a water supply and a remote intake tank for storing water so that the water level can be controlled while checking the operation state in the intake tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102092239-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "generating a deep learning model using a first water level value and determining a pump operation value in a pressure field for a second water level value received in a subsequent cycle based on the abnormal time point based on the deep learning model it may include steps.according to the present invention when the communication state with the water level meter installed in the reservoir does not satisfy a predetermined level based on the deep learning model generated using the water level value previously received from the water level meter the pump operation value in the pressurization field is determined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at this time the middle layer water and the lower layer water is lower than the temperature of the surface water due to the difference in density to cool the water stored in the intake tower to form a low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "on the other hand in the lower fixing structure 70 of the water intake tower 12 when the water level is located on the bottom the fixing rod 76 in accordance with the corresponding position so that the impact preventing member 32 provided on the buoyancy member 26 is placed the vertically fixed structure 78 is installed to prevent breakage of the buoyancy member 26 and to prevent the screen 38 from colliding with the bottom of the reservoir to prevent damage and damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784777-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "the rod 22 is rotated to the discharge side the connecting link 23 is connected to the operating rod 22 acts in the direction to push the auxiliary sluice 40 to the discharge side the auxiliary sluice 40 is applied to this force by blocking the outlet 30 while moving along the guide rail 12 to block the water flowing into the outlet 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714328-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after deeply dredging the upstream and downstream portions by blocking the above mentioned river the above mentioned river embankment 100 on one side and the other side of the above mentioned river is obliquely prepared the above mentioned concrete 111 is installed on the riverbed and on the sides of the bottom of one side of the bank and the other side of the bank a fish habitat facility 112 is constructed using rocks or bank structures so that amphibians benthic animals or fish can easily inhabit it and then various bank structures 113 are stored inside the above mentioned fish habitat facility 112 so that fish can easily inhabit it a structure comprising an eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is configured as a dam reservoir lake or estuary structure configured to hold water in the upper part of the above concrete 111 a structure in which a bottom water rising passage 7777 is formed by combining a bottom inlet 311 that acts to discharge heavy bottom water between one side and the other side of the front part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae occurrence and a bottom water rising passage 7777 is formed by a structure in which the bottom part is narrow and the upper part is formed by a gradually wider inclined plate 322 a structure in which an air inlet 321 for preventing gravity generation is formed in the upper part of the above mentioned low level water rising passage 7777 to prevent low level water which automatically rises by the action of gravity and siphon action from being discharged in the downstream direction of the river when it reaches a certain water level a structure in which a material friction and material explosion generating unit 889 is combined to generate electricity by separating the light gravity river water and the heavy gravity river water into upper and lower parts through the gravity material friction and material explosion generated between the light gravity river water and the light gravity river water thereby causing the polluted river water with a light specific gravity to float to the upper part while simultaneously automatically separating the clean river water with a heavy specific gravity to the lower part and simultaneously discharging it in the downstream direction of the river through the lower inlet 311 and the bottom water rising passage 7777 a structure in which the lower layer water rising passage 7777 and the upper part power generation water movement passage 211 formed on the rear part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae occurrence are each formed with a plurality of upper discharge ports 151 a structure in which an exhaust emission control valve 163 is combined at one end of the upper exhaust port 151 a structure in which an induction pipe 152 for generating gravitational acceleration caused by the action of gravity is formed at the lower part of the rear portion of the upper discharge port 151 a structure in which a gravity acceleration generating unit 911 is formed in the upper part of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 with a height that is 10 to 1 000 times wider and a volume that is larger than the thickness area and volume ratio of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 a structure in which an air inlet 158 is formed at the upper part of the above mentioned gravity acceleration generating unit 911 a structure in which dual control valves 161 162 are respectively formed in the upper and lower parts of the induction pipe 152 for generating the above mentioned gravitational acceleration effect to control the discharge amount of river water the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae which is connected to an electric power generation unit 331 that generates electricity at the lower end of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 is installed in a river a reservoir a dam a lake or an estuary to hold water and then the double control valve 162 is closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "more specifically when the water level of the reservoir rises to a high level due to a failure of the existing water level control valve it is discharged through the overflow water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "referring to the operation and effect of the present invention configured as described above the safety shut off device 10 of the present invention detects that the water level of the reservoir 1 is high by the float float 6 to block the inlet pipe 2 can be installed and used together in the reservoir 1 provided with a water level control valve 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "that is the safety shut off device 10 is obtained so as to prevent the occurrence of various accidents due to the water overflow of the reservoir 1 when the water level control valve 5 which frequently malfunctions is damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100367232-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a water supply flow control system for water purifiers installed in the water supply source and the reservoir is used to control the pressure and flow rate of the water flowing through the raw water supply line a plurality of series connected filter and the water purification discharge line a pressure control valve installed in the raw water supply line to adjust the pressure of the raw water supplied from the water supply source to the filter according to a preset reference supply pressure a water shutoff valve installed in the water purification line so as to close as the water level of the reservoir rises to a predetermined reference level and remain open at a level lower than the reference level a water purifier comprising a raw water shutoff valve installed in the raw water supply line to block the raw water supply line when the pressure in the purified water discharge line is higher than a preset reference discharge pressure and receive a control pressure from the purified water discharge line through a pilot line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100367232-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "it can be stably controlled in accordance with the water purification capability of the product and it can be expected to have an industrially useful effect of minimizing the generation of noise caused by various valve operations and greatly extending the life of the valve parts"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101233804-B1", "para_id": "para_127", "text": "therefore if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the contamination is further increased by the material decomposition action and the material binding action so that the water stored in the reservoir always maintains the full water level and the water coming from the upstream through the lower part of the water gate often discharged is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and also by using the method to discharge water in the reservoir through the lower part of the sluice by the material binding action that combines the substances contained in the water it releases pollutants such as aggregated sewage sludge and at the same time generates material acceleration phenomenon material scavenging phenomenon material decomposition action material flotation action and naturally cleans the contaminated water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101427989-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "at this time it is possible to increase or decrease the hydrogen generation and the circulation time according to the quantity so that the hydrogen dissolved amount can be prevented from rising excessively by checking the ph value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101427989-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "in the extraction mode when the water supply button of the operation button 13 is pressed the electrolysis unit 100 is kept in the off state while the first pump p1 is in the locked state and the first solenoid s1 is also closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502305-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to operate a warning alarm when the unwanted water due to the closing of the main water supply valve and to enter the inspection state to prevent damage due to leakage of the product and the space in which the product is installed in the case of the ion water purifier with the reservoir the alarm sounds together with the alarm and at the same time the water level of the reservoir is automatically forced by the automatic drain valve and in the case of the reservoir type the alarm and the warning sound operate quickly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502305-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition the present invention operates a warning alarm at the time of undesired intake due to poor closing of the main water supply valve and enters the inspection state to prevent damage due to water leakage in the product and the space where the product is installed due to water overflow in case of the attached ion water purifier the alarm sounds with alarm and the water level of the reservoir is automatically forced by the automatic drain valve at the same time as the alarm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330869-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore since the electrode 2 and the main body 1 are separated separately installation is inconvenient which may cause malfunctions due to immersion such as moisture.the present invention is to solve the conventional drawbacks as described above the main body and the electrode for the sensor composed of the same body and waterproof construction to solve the conventional drawbacks and to prevent malfunction due to leakage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the sterilizing water purifier of the present invention comprises a water tank a u type sterilizing lamp mounted inside the water storage tank a level sensor provided in the sterilizing lamp and a controller electrically connected to the water level sensor wherein the water level sensor senses that water is introduced into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp inside the water reservoir and the controller controls the power of the sterilizing lamp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046601-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "first the water storage tank 20 connects the water supply pipe 11 to the water supply port 12 formed in the lower water storage portion 21b with the water supply valve 12 interposed therebetween thereby opening and closing the water supply valve 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the pressure pump in operation is controlled to stop due to a drop in the primary pressure in the water pipe connecting the pressure pump and the primary side reservoir and the water level in the secondary side is below the specified water level"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1st embodiment concerns on invention of claim 1 comprising it is an early detection system which monitors abnormal water discharge or water leak by distribution reservoir water level abnormal fall monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0022 reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100466336-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water level control system of a freshwater facility that measures the level of a reservoir containing fluid that is distilled water condensate in a freshwater facility and controls the discharge or supply of distilled water condensed water according to the degree of contamination of the distilled water condensed water while maintaining the proper level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth c