reducing the size of the reservoir it is preferable to install the initial excellent water separation facility 101 so that only the initial excellent water can be introduced into the reservoir before the rainwater is introduced into the reservoir and it is desirable not to install it in the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889975-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the storeroom 100 may include a grating seating surface 121 formed in a boundary area between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 wherein the grating 200 comprises a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insert tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 formed in a grid shape inside the grating frame 210 to block rainwater into the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter the grating frame 210 is formed to protrude at a predetermined interval in an area contacting the grating seating surface 121 so that the soil introduced into the grating frame 210 from the grating insertion tube 120 and the grating frame 210 is separated from the grinding frame 210 and a plurality of the soil inflow teeth 240 for inflowing into the interior of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101314575-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition the present invention by lifting and replacing or repairing the entire rainwater treatment unit including the membrane module at the top of the reservoir after installing it in place very easy to maintain and can be easily applied to new and existing facilities application of this technology to existing simple rainwater storage tanks can contribute to securing water resources as well as existing good storage effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101314575-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "in addition the present invention by lifting and replacing or repairing the entire rainwater treatment unit including the membrane module at the top of the reservoir after installing it in place very easy to maintain and can be easily applied to new and existing facilities application of this technology to existing simple rainwater storage tanks can contribute to securing water resources as well as existing good storage effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414264-Y1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in the rainwater collection modification the rainwater collection pipe 1 is connected to induce rainwater and the rainwater collection pipe 1 is installed at the end of the rainwater contaminant treatment device and a rainwater reservoir is connected to the end of the rainwater reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100665619-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in particular in the lining method using the metal material of the prior art of figure 1 the bending of the metal material due to the swelling phenomenon due to the water pressure applied to the lining treatment site by the infiltration water such as water and rainwater flowing out of the concrete of the reservoir and the water pressure during fresh water as the repetition was repeated the metal material was stretched or cracked which was the biggest drawback"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "US-12338143-B2", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the collection of rainwater is of particular interest because it is naturally distilled and because ocean air has fewer atmospheric contaminants as compared to air over populated areas"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101208694-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the blockage of the filter media is frequent the filtration efficiency is lowered there is a need for frequent backwashing there was a problem such that the function of storm water storage facilities to prevent the contamination of the river water is not properly performed.the present invention has been made to solve the conventional problems as described above can improve the excellent filtration efficiency and recycling degree can improve the backwashing efficiency during the backwashing of the first filtration unit and the washing of the reservoir it is possible to reduce the sludge sedimentation on the bottom surface while facilitating the drainage of washing water at the same time to perform additional filtration of rainwater without additional power and to prevent the re injury of sediment deposited on the floor surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100550824-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "the water gate 530 is to discharge the purified water in the rainwater storage tank 520 to the ground as shown in figure 13 opening and closing by vertical operation the rubber ring 531 is installed on the outer peripheral surface rainwater it is adapted to prevent leakage of the water stored in the reservoir 520"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "it has a cold feeling that is not in harmony with the appearance of a house or a building it is covered with the rainwater reservoir of the color pattern and built in the inside space to prevent direct exposure to direct sunlight rain and wind so that even if it is used for a long time it does not cause deformation or breakage of rainwater reservoir and can prevent water from being spoiled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore foreign substances or impurities accumulated in the body 1 2 times a year it is possible to clean the inside of the body to remove it and the structure of the device is waterproof structure so that water can not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593694-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the lifting projection and the fixing projection coupled to each other are installed the lower box is provided with a plurality of connection pipes are connected to the drain box the upper edge of the upper box is formed with a stepped reservoir box cover is the corrugated pipe is normally folded so that the upper box is adjacent to the lower box by being installed on the step and when rainwater flows from the drain box into the storage box through the connecting pipe the upper box is raised while the corrugated pipe is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "block type rainwater storage tank 100 according to an embodiment of the present invention is a corner block 120 the side block 130 and the inner block 140 is installed in combination on top of the base block 110 forming the bottom of the reservoir space as described above the corner block 120 the side block 130 and the inner block 140 may be installed in multiple layers according to the capacity of the storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101791207-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in addition in the drainage device 520 the slaked lime can be mixed with the feed water in the pipe thereby preventing corrosion of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2486988-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the term liquid is therefore understood below to mean any liquid arriving naturally or artificially in the cavities of the mine or in the natural environment of the mine in particular groundwater or surface water for example rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046131-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in addition it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulated in the initial excellent water tank rainwater tank and sedimentation tank thereby ensuring the long term security of the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity.1 is a block diagram showing an example of the initial excellent water quality treatment system according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "as will be described below the permeable sidewalk block unit 100 may be configured alone without the permeable block member 120 and is intended to be expressed in terms of this"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 1030605the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems and it is an object of the present invention to prevent storm flooding by storing rainwater reduce load on a sewage treatment plant prevent urban heat island and replenish water resources the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a method of constructing a reservoir tank having a non point pollutant reduction type prefabricated reservoir block and a nonpoint source pollution reduction function using the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to purify rainwater collected in a storage tank and to provide it as a landscape water and a living water thereby preventing a water shortage phenomenon and a nonpoint pollution reduction high initial stormwater is stored in the reservoir and purified rainwater is discharged at the end of rainfall or gradually penetrated into the underground to prevent flood maintain groundwater level at a certain level to prevent ground stabilization and river pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889974-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent storage tank 100 which is embedded in the inside of the ground and receives stormwater introduced from the ground a grating 200 rotatably coupled to the upper surface of the superior storage tank 100 for introducing the stormwater into the storage tank and blocking the foreign material a dirt collecting box 400 provided in the superior storage tank 100 for filtering dirt contained in the rainwater and a collection box support 300 provided at an upper portion of the superior storage container 100 and supporting the dirt collection box 400 the storm reservoir 100 a reservoir body 110 in which the storm is stored a grating insert tube 120 formed on the upper portion of the reservoir body 110 and coupled to the grating 200 and a grating seating surface 121 formed on the boundary region between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 so as to be stepped inwardly in a predetermined area so that the grating 200 is seated and supported the grating 200 a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insertion tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 disposed in the grating frame 210 at predetermined intervals in the longitudinal direction and having irregularities formed on the upper surface thereof to block rainwater from the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter a plurality of reinforcing frames 230 arranged in the grating frame 210 in a lateral direction at regular intervals a plurality of protrusions protruding from the ground at a predetermined interval in the lower portion of the outer reinforcing frame 230a to allow the gravel to flow into the gap between the grating insert tube 120 and the grating frame 210 and includes a soil inflow tooth 240 the height of the earth inflow tooth 240 and the height of the outer reinforcement frame 230a may be greater than the height of the reinforcement frame 230 located inside the outer reinforcement frame 230a and the reinforcing frame 230 is formed at the same height as the reinforcing frame 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow regulating tank for storing effluent treated and discharged in the sewage treatment plant a reaction tank connected to the flow rate adjusting tank and having an inlet reaction tank and an oxidation tank communicated with each other an ultra fine bubble generating unit for generating ultra bubbles after supplying ozone to the process water introduced from the flow rate adjusting tank or the inflow reaction tank and supplying the bubbles to a lower region of the oxidation reaction tank the treatment water treated in the oxidation reaction tank flows through an advection tube provided in a region below the water surface of the oxidation reaction tank and contacts with the foamed filter material for inducing the contact reaction of the hydrophilicized polymer material by the ozone a reaction tank and a treatment water tank into which the treated water treated in the contact reaction tank flows wherein the inlet reaction tank and the oxidation reaction tank are separated from each other through a partition wall the partition wall is spaced apart from the bottom surface of the reaction tank to form a spacing space and through the passage provided by the spacing space a pressure is generated in the lower direction of the oxidation reaction tank by the flow of the treatment water which is reversely circulated in the oxidation reaction tank and flows into the lower region of the oxidation reaction tank by the pressure in the lower direction the rate of rise of minute bubbles in the water is delayed and the rate of dissolution of the minute bubbles is increased and the treatment water in which the residence time in the oxidation reaction tank is increased due to the delay of the floatation rate is passed through the advection tube is introduced into the contact reaction tank wherein the foamed filter medium is disposed at a middle portion of the contact reaction tank the treated water is introduced into the upper portion of the contact reaction tank and flows in the lower direction and passes through the foamed filter medium further comprising an air supply unit for supplying air to the lower portion of the foamed filter medium to induce the floating of the sludge deposited on the foamed filter medium when the foamed filter medium is occluded by the sludge wherein the treatment tank is provided with an advection pipe having an a shaped structure at one side of the upper part of the contact reaction tank and treatment water staying in the contact reaction tank lower region passing through the foamed filter medium in the contact reaction tank through the admission pipe and a rainwater reservoir for storing incoming rainwater and further comprising an inflow control unit for allowing the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank to flow into the inflow reaction tank or the treatment water tank depending on the degree of contamination"}]</data>
