"communicate", "freeze", "designate", "discharge", "unseat", "cool", "store", "corrode", "bush", "start", "detect", "fit", "decrease", "design", "capture", "net", "permit", "analyze", "drive", "spot", "change", "pull", "guide", "include", "act", "incline", "operate", "perform", "dispose", "open", "expand", "enter", "block", "blow", "mean", "react", "constitute", "experience", "side", "supply", "mainraine", "absorb", "use", "transfer", "propeller", "stop", "recognize", "charge", "cut", "estimate", "asphyxiate", "straighten", "know", "throttle", "recite", "transport", "finish", "sense", "require", "close", "draw", "rotate", "heat", "classify", "galvanize", "decontaminate", "maintain", "install", "improve", "control", "transmit", "case", "register", "monitor", "characterize", "select", "input", "keep", "adhere", "damage", "be", "age", "rack", "bypass", "utilize", "collect", "generate", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "thus as water in reservoir 142 freezes its expanding volume lifts piston 130 unseating valve head 132 and opening a fluid path between conduit 110 and exhaust ports 120 through which water is continuously discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326272-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "raw water is produced in pure water through the reverse osmosis process ro in a 25 kg day grade flame retardation device and a portion of the produced pure water is supplied to the brine reservoir 10 to produce saturated salt water"}, {"pat_id": "US-6182453-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "this embodiment also provides an optional recirculation loop and optional computer programmed timer to control the compressor s off on time interval to maximize condensate collection when the evaporator is freezing due to environmental conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-6182453-B1", "para_id": "para_296", "text": "by means of the temperature sensors positioned in various zones of the water reservoir one or more known heating devices mounted within the unit housing or adjacent to the water reservoir including the peltier probe itself can be activated in reverse to provide a sufficient amount of heating to prevent freezing of the lines valves and reservoir when the ambient or housing panel temperature falls into the range 5 to 5 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-6182453-B1", "para_id": "para_297", "text": "the communications interface may be of any known type including ordinary phone circuits cellular phone circuits or a receiver for electromagnetic signals of a selected frequency such as radio short wave fm microwave etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "bethridge on ca transferred to the inflowing solvent before entering the thus heat exchanger 925 preheated the water and reduced the energy requirements of the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at this time the middle layer water and the lower layer water is lower than the temperature of the surface water due to the difference in density to cool the water stored in the intake tower to form a low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "thereby the object to be cleaned 1 is firstly cleaned by high pressure air bubbling through the lower spray nozzle 233 by driving the spray pump 235 in a state of being immersed in the cleaning liquid in the cleaning tank 210 the spray nozzle 233 is driven by the spray pump 235 to discharge the cleaning solution through the upper spray nozzle 233 before being lifted from the cleaning tank 210 by the driving of the cleaning lifting driver 225 the washing liquid is circulated through the upper spray nozzle 233 by the clean wash water accommodated in the regenerating wash fluid reservoir 240 by the driving of the regenerating wash fluid circulating pump 245 and the steam supply pipe 117 the drying and residual washing liquid is removed by the high temperature steam supplied from the waste water regeneration apparatus 100 and sprayed through the upper spray nozzle 233 and then discharged to the outside of the cleaning loading unit 220 or the cleaning quality of the object to be cleaned 1 can be further improved without consuming energy"}, {"pat_id": "US-8398733-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "and yet another disadvantage of other water generators is that they are not energy efficient because they use compressors that operate to maintain a cold set point temperature within the water reservoir that requires the operation of the compressors even when the generators do not actively produce water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4159235-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "this increases the electrical conductivity of the water and thus lowers the energy requirement so that a constant temperature develops whose level depends on the current load in the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8486269-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the mineral may be a clay in particular clays of the smectite type such as montmorillonite pyrophillite type kaolinite type illite type and glauconite type"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100779721-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "as described above according to the waterproofing device of the concrete water tank according to the present invention in the concrete water tank so that the polyethylene sheet is lining construction on the inner wall surface to have a waterproof function water leakage due to damage of the polyethylene sheet or the concrete condensed water caused by temperature difference between the inside and outside of the reservoir or outside water through the fill in the state in which the concrete reservoir is buried so that water is generated between the polyethylene sheet and the inner wall surface of the concrete reservoir in one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101908294-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "patent literature 3 discloses a vegetation gypsum in which a vegetation block contained in a vegetation gypsum is contained a vegetation block contains vegetation soil and plant seeds and a vegetation block contains natural decomposition and the vegetation block is a tubular shape with the upper surface opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101756200-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the communication check module 71 pumps a certain percentage of water into the tank in the morning lunch evening so as to block the number of steps during the rf network check time and the communication check module 71 is used to prevent freezing of the winter water pipe the temperature sensor s39 is attached to the groundwater protecting apparatus 2 and the temperature is lower than the temperature set by the temperature detecting module 73 the motor is repeatedly operated at a predetermined time interval to forcibly start the water and the water in the water pipe is moved the power check module 72 allows the surveillance camera s34 to photograph the monitoring camera s34 only at the moment when the guard means 25 is opened and closed in the groundwater monitoring system and the leakage check module 75 detects the leakage of the water from the occlusion portion 222 it is possible to check the leakage by comparing the sound at the normal time and the sound with the sound sensor in the event of leakage and the leakage position of the water pipe through the pressure sensor of the pipe can be grasped when water is reduced to a certain level or less through a level sensor using an angle sensor at a time when water below a fixed value is used in order to estimate the water leakage of the water supply pipe using a specific time in order to check water shortage phenomenon when water is depleted data is collected by dividing the water depletion time and recovery time by using an electrode and if the motor is not operated for a certain period of time the controller 3 controls the reservoir 4 to charge the reservoir 4 with a certain amount of chlorine so that the management server 7 installs an electrode at a specific point on the end of the reservoir tank accumulate along the curve points"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435698-Y1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "as described above according to the waterproofing device of the concrete reservoir according to the present invention in the concrete reservoir tank so that the polyethylene sheet is lining construction on the inner wall surface having a waterproof function water leakage due to damage of the polyethylene sheet the concrete reservoir condensate due to the temperature difference between the inside and outside or the outside water through the fill in the state in which the concrete reservoir is buried so that the water generated between the polyethylene sheet and the inner wall surface of the concrete reservoir to collect to either side as a result the water does not accumulate between the inner wall of the concrete reservoir and the polyethylene sheet thereby preventing corrosion of the concrete structure"}, {"pat_id": "US-8075652-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "and yet another disadvantage of other water generators is that they are not energy efficient because they use compressors that operate to maintain a cold set point temperature within the water reservoir which requires the operation of the compressors even when the generators do not actively produce water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759677-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the portion of untreated water that does not evaporate is transported back into untreated water chamber 104 via recirculation reservoir 108"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101030980-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "figure 2 shows the overall block diagram of the water quality multi item measuring device 20 according to the present invention as shown in figure 2 temperature ph turbidity residual chlorine concentration and electrical conductivity in the water treatment plant and the reservoir of the water purification plant in order to measure the items of water quality such as the measured number of samples to be supplied to each sensor measuring sensor unit 21 for measuring each water quality items and each signal measured by the measuring sensor unit and the respective sensors and the digital sensor converts the digital data into digital data using the calibration factor stored for each sensor and transmits the signal to the main control unit 23 via the sensor interbase unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad b