to one embodiment the collector tube 214 acts as a conduit for transporting the thermal transfer fluid through the solar concentrator 212 and the tube 214 has a substantially rectangular shape with dimensions of approximately one 1 inch wide by three 3 inches high which the applicants believe provides advantageous heat transfer characteristics over conventional collector tubes 214 having a circular cross sectional shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101265963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "aerobic reservoir having apparatus for mainraining reacting temperature the present invention relates to an aerobic tank in a sewage and sewage advanced treatment system comprising an apparatus for maintaining a reaction temperature in an aerobic tank and forming an optimum reaction condition in the aerobic tank even with an external temperature change thereby improving the efficiency of organic matter oxidation and nitrification and thereby stable discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101815298-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "2 the cooling water recycling system 200 for lowering the temperature of the water used as the cooling water for the cooling tower of the lng combined cycle power generation cooling plant and for removing contaminant contaminants during the cooling process is used as the cooling water for the cooling tower of the lng combined an ultrafiltration unit 210 for removing fine contaminants in the raw water and an ultrafiltration storage unit 220 connected to the ultrafiltration unit 210 to store filtered water filtered by the ultrafiltration unit 210 a microfilter 230 connected to the storage tank 220 to remove microfilms generated or contaminated in the filtered water stored in the ultrafiltration storage tank 220 and a microfilter 230 connected to the microfilter 230 the reverse osmosis filter 240 is connected to the reverse osmosis filter 240 so as to remove the filtered water from the reverse osmosis filter 240 a cooling water reverse osmosis treatment reservoir 250 for storing the ozone water for use as an ozone generator and a reverse osmosis filter 240 connected to the ultrafilter 210 and the reverse osmosis filter 240 to remove contaminants adhered to the ultrafilter 210 and a wastewater treatment tank 196 for wastewater treatment of the concentrated water generated during the treatment in the reverse osmosis filter 240"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0385568 2003.05.15 designated by reservoir control system registered and filed by the present applicant the groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200479774-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "since the compartments 115 are provided on the front and rear sides of the storm reservoir 110 to relieve the heat transfer between the outer surface of the compartment 10 and the storeroom reservoir 110 by the space in the compartment 115 it is possible to minimize the temperature rise and decay due to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200479774-Y1", "para_id": "para_82", "text": "however in the present invention the compartment 115 is provided on the front rear left and right sides of the storm reservoir 110 and the heat transfer between the outer surface of the compartment 10 and the storeroom reservoir 110 is alleviated by the space in the compartment 115 it is possible to minimize the temperature rise and decay of the rainwater in the stor age storage tank 110 due to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100468450-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "which is the maximum operating temperature of the membrane system may be used"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318395-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the portion of untreated water that does not evaporate is transported back into untreated water chamber 104 via recirculation reservoir 108"}, {"pat_id": "US-4123340-A", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "this increases the electrical conductivity of the water and thus lowers the energy requirement so that a constant temperature develops whose level depends on the current load in the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "according to one embodiment the collector tube 214 acts as a conduit for transporting the thermal transfer fluid through the solar concentrator 212 and the tube 214 has a substantially rectangular shape with dimensions of approximately one 1 inch wide by three 3 inches high which the applicants believe provides advantageous heat transfer characteristics over conventional collector tubes 214 having a circular cross sectional shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101276139-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition by the water supply cooling means 140 it is possible to suppress the direct heat transfer to the material constituting the wall surface or the like of the combustion chamber 120 so as to reduce deformation or corrosion due to heat"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "the present invention discloses other breakthrough achievement the air return mechanism instead of spring return the air return mechanism with the shutter valve not only does increases output force or torques without decreasing air acting forces unlike the conventional spring return mechanism which share the acting force about 40 and 10 converting loss from total capacity 100 of double acting forces or torque but also eliminates the spring return sets which is heavy big and expensive and porn to corrosion with breath air holes furthermore there is no entry of unfilled air into the actuator or air reservoir other than air supply so no corrosion or particle would damage the actuator cylinder or air reservoir more importantly the air return mechanism is constantly monitored by air pressure gauge and ready to act at any moment with the highest level of reliability while spring set return is not constantly monitored it can be weaken or corroded without any information of its condition for over time under some working conditions like hot temperature high humility or offshore platform the air return reservoir can perform well at the designed condition for long service where the spring return may not work well due to spring corrosion creeping finally the air return reservoir can be installed at any position vertical horizontal and between and with other actuators linear actuator rack and pinion or vane actuators there is no material fatigue issue finally hot weather can help air return reservoir perform better without increasing heating cost or solar power consumption with heat absorbing material or dark color coating on the cylinder to increase pressure of the air on the reservoir or it can be added insulation layers and internal heater for cool weather locations or subsea as well finally it is very suitable for earthquake area or high vibration applications most actuators with spring return mechanisms are unbalanced if with net spring set the matter even gets even worse so the actuators may not even survive to preform is out of question"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629806-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "during installation the winch not shown is used to pull the liner assembly 20 into the pipeline p via a winch cable 84 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131549-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in addition the collection of condensate on the surface of the condensate collecting plate 80 to maintain a lower state than the temperature of the convection to collect the condensate which is formed on both sides of the condensate collecting plate 80 while inclined similarly downward the cross section is provided in a shape so as to flow down but the lower side thereof is provided with a \uc751\ucd95 type condensate guide 75 to match the length of the condensate collecting plate 80 and then the condensate guide 75 the lower side of the is connected to the induction pipe 92 to be connected in accordance with the upper edge of the support wall 55 of the reservoir 66 formed in the block 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101328093-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in addition by the water supply cooling means 140 it is possible to suppress the direct heat transfer to the material constituting the wall surface or the like of the combustion chamber 120 so as to reduce deformation or corrosion due to heat"}, {"pat_id": "US-6368511-B1", "para_id": "para_116", "text": "the associated fecl2 catalyst solution is already added with the raw sludge stream that is to say upstream of the stirred vessel 1 to the acidification stage via the line 7 from the fecl2 reservoir 6"}, {"pat_id": "US-12345140-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the one or more reservoir factors of the present disclosure may include mineralogical content temperature pressure formation wettability minimum fracture pressure formation layers the like or any combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-12345140-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the method of any one of embodiments 1 3 wherein the reservoir factor comprises mineralogical content temperature pressure formation wettability minimum fracture pressure formation layers or any combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-6890429-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the system of claim 4 further comprising a holding reservoir and wherein during cold ambient conditions the elevated temperature waste water is fed from the biological reactor back to the animal barn bypassing the holding reservoir and during warm ambient conditions the elevated temperature waste water is fed from the biological reactor to the holding reservoir where the waste water is cooled prior to being fed back to the animal barn"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "a purpose of the filler material 649 is to increase the surface area of the reservoir 645 to keep the fluid temperature constant during pressure decay"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102340325-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "reservoir installed in various types of buildings for each region to store drinkable drinking water ph sensor to measure hydrogen ion concentration ph tds sensor to measure total dissolved solids tds in water liquid medium including a turbidity sensor for measuring the turbidity of the liquid medium a temperature sensor for measuring the temperature of the liquid medium and a residual chlorine sensor for measuring the residual chlorine of the liquid medium it is installed in each of the storage tanks to measure the water quality of drinking water in the storage tank water quality multi item iot sensor the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank measured by the water quality multi item iot sensor hydrogen ion concentration ph temperature temp total dissolved solids tds residual chlorine residual chlorine turbidity ntu dissolved oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp and conductivity cond a gateway that collects and analyzes data of multi item measurement values of water quality for each water tank transmitted from the gateway and builds a big data database a water quality management platform server that is used for water quality analysis a real time water quality information monitoring device that receives water quality multi item measurement data for each water tank from the water quality management platform server and monitors the water quality status of each water tank in each area in real time the real time water quality information the terminal of the environment safety officer and each water tank that receives an alarm message generated when any one of the water quality multi item measured value data approaches or reaches the standard value from the monitoring device and sends a cleaning request notification for the water tank to the cleaning company terminal transmitting water quality multi item measured value data to the lora gateway through the lora modem and transmitting the water quality multi item measured value data transmitted through the lora modem to the real time water quality information monitoring device through the lte network in the gateway at preset intervals a communication device wherein the water quality management platform server includes an iot sensor data collection unit for collecting water quality multi item measurement value data for each water tank transmitted from the gateway and water quality multi item measurement for each water tank collected by the iot sensor data collection unit value data iot sensor data water quality analysis unit that analyzes the water quality condition including real time measurement values for each water quality measurement item and the change value of the real time measurement values based on water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank collected by a big data analysis unit and the iot sensor data collection unit that analyzes big data in relation to environmental factors and information analyzed by the iot sensor data water quality analysis unit and the big data analysis unit and a monitoring system interworking unit for integrated interfacing by transmitting to the real time water quality information monitoring device wherein the real time water quality information monitoring device receives iot sensor data receiving unit for receiving water quality multi item measurement data for each water tank from the water quality management platform server displays water quality status information according to the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank received from the iot sensor data receiver through a real time water quality information monitoring system and hydrogen ion concentration ph total dissolved in water through the water quality status board measured values for solid matter tds turbidity residual chlorine and temperature and water quality status information determined based on the measured values are displayed in real time and the real time water quality information monitoring system warns and cautions the water quality status for the entire area and normal displays regional selection information displays on site inspection status information schematized as one of water quality check purifier chlorine input and others displays residual chlorine status total dissolved solids tds status and hydrogen iot sensor data display unit that displays ion concentration ph status information by dividing it into warning caution and normal grades hydrogen ion concentration ph for each of multiple water tanks total dissolved solids tds turbidity ntu collected oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp conductivity cond temperature temp and residual chlorine residual chlorine for each item and the average standard of each item deviation and mean when the difference between the measured value for each item and the average among multiple storage tanks by calculating the deviation exceeds the standard deviation and the average deviation the water tank water quality comparison unit that transmits a danger warning of the water quality of the water tank to the environment safety officer when the difference between the measured value for each item and the average is greater than a preset x multiple of the standard deviation and a preset x multiple of the average deviation a water quality risk warning of the corresponding water tank and a sensor error suspicious warning are issued at the same time as the environment any one of the sensor error detection unit that transmits to the safety officer the website app linkage unit that links the web server or smart phone application to share the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank and the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank water quality abnormal signal notification unit that generates a water quality abnormal signal alarm when it approaches or reaches the reference value a water quality multi item iot sensor for water quality measurement is additionally installed in the iot sensor error monitoring unit and the water tank of a specific local institution or place so that the administrator can control the local institution or place where the water quality multi item iot sensor is added through the user interface and a monitoring addition generating unit that recognizes this when selected and additionally creates a target for monitoring the water quality of the water tank wherein the water tank transmits the location of the water tank closest to the user s location to the web server or the smart phone application"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101522630-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a water supply unit for supplying water to the water storage unit so that the water storage unit maintains a predetermined water level is formed at one side of the water storage unit and a plurality of switches for operating the drive is provided on the front side a water tank mounted on a water supply part of the main body and storing water to be supplied to the water supply part of the main body and a water reservoir coupled to an upper part of the main body so that the water storage part is not exposed to the outside and an upper case provided with a blowing fan for blowing water to the water storage part and promoting evaporation of water in the water storage part and regulating the temperature of the water in the water storage part of the evaporation type humidifier a cold water induction surface in which a relatively low temperature water is collected among the water contained in the reservoir portion is formed at a lower portion of the reservoir portion and a slope reservoir portion having a relatively shallow depth in the reservoir portion around the reservoir portion a valve plate formed at an outlet of the water supply unit so that a passage of water flowing into the reservoir unit is formed downward a block membrane disposed behind the valve membrane to inhibit heat transfer through convection of water and further comprising an am capturing membrane disposed behind the block membrane to suppress heat transfer through convection of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101522630-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a water supply unit for supplying water to the water storage unit so that the water storage unit is maintained at a predetermined water level and a plurality of water storage units a cylindrical or polygonal water bottle which is connected to the water supply part and is connected to the other side of the water supply part connected to the main body the air blowing fan is installed to be spaced apart from the upper inner circumferential edge of the main body so as to form an air suction hole and forcedly discharges moisture convectively flowing from the upper portion of the water reservoir to the upper side communicating with the outside the humidifier of the natural evaporation type including the exhaust pipe body a cold water induction surface in which a relatively low temperature water is collected among the water contained in the reservoir portion is formed at a lower portion of the reservoir portion and a slope reservoir portion having a relatively shallow depth in the reservoir portion around the reservoir portion a valve plate formed at an outlet of the water supply unit so that a passage of water flowing into the reservoir unit is formed downward a block membrane disposed behind the valve membrane to inhibit heat transfer through convection of water and further comprising an am capturing membrane disposed behind the block membrane to suppress heat transfer through convection of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101522630-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in the lower portion of the low water portion a cold water in which water of a relatively low water temperature is collected among the water contained in the low drawings and a slope bottom portion in which a shallow water depth is relatively formed in the bottom portion of the bottom portion wherein a valve is formed at an outlet of the water supply portion so that a passage of water flowing downward into the bottom portion is formed downward a block membrane disposed behind the valve membrane to inhibit heat transfer through convection of water and an am capturing membrane disposed behind the block membrane for suppressing heat transfer through convection of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101522630-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the natural evaporative humidifier according to the present invention includes a water supply unit for supplying water to the water storage unit a cylindrical or polygonal water bottle connected to the other side of the water supply part connected to the main body and storing water supplied to the water supply part the air blowing fan is installed at a predetermined distance from the upper inner circumference of the main body so as to form an intake hole along an open top inner periphery of the main body and an exhaust pipe body serving as a water temperature control the reservoir has a lower surface that the water in the cold water guided to the relatively low temperature of the water contained in the reservoir set and a slope bottom portion in which a shallow water depth is relatively formed in the bottom portion of the bottom portion wherein a valve is formed at an outlet of the water supply portion so that a passage of water flowing downward into the bottom portion is formed downward a block membrane disposed behind the valve membrane to inhibit heat transfer through convection of water and an am capturing membrane disposed behind the block membrane for suppressing heat transfer through convection of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to solve the above mentioned problem the automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a water tank of a public building according to the present invention comprises a main storage tank storing a predetermined amount of chlorine solution inside one or more auxiliary storage tanks installed on one side of the main storage tank and replenishing the chlorine solution to the main storage tank a cooling device installed in the main storage tank and cooling the chlorine solution stored in the main storage tank and the auxiliary storage tank to maintain the same at a predetermined temperature a quantitative pump installed inside or outside the main storage tank and quantitatively discharging the chlorine solution stored inside the main storage tank and it includes a control device installed on one side of the main storage tank and controlling the operation of the cooling device and the quantitative pump wherein the control device detects the water level of tap water stored inside the reservoir to calculate the real time storage capacity of the tap water measures the chlorine concentration of the tap water and determines the chlorine injection time and injection amount based on the change in tap water usage according to the day of the week and time thereby operating the quantitative pump"}, {"pat_id": "US-5348623-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "another object of the present invention is to heat water within the hot water reservoir utilizing a heat transfer device having a working fluid which has a boiling point above the temperature of the water to be heated but not higher than the water within the hot water reservoir to thereby minimize sediment accumulation and scaling within the hot water reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "US-6289689-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "a water collection and dispensing machine as recited in claim 12 wherein said temperature detection assembly includes a detection head structured to be immersed in said water contained in said fluid reservoir and a shielding assembly structured to communicably shield said detection head from said water so as to prevent rusting and deterioration thereof while also permitting the temperature of said water to be readily detected by said detection head so as to correspondingly direct said cooling operation of said cooling assembly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171689-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "case 100 a plurality of led lamps 110 pump 230 water supply sensor 240 the heating wire 250 the heater 270 and the heater body temperature sensor 272 is configured to include the case 100 has a rectangular parallelepiped shape a pedestal 101 is formed at a lower portion thereof a cover 102 is formed at an upper portion thereof and a plurality of led lamps 110 and steam on on are provided at the front of the case 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-4448032-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "US-4370865-A", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564334-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the drug feeder may include a stock solution reservoir in which the liquid polymer is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100689108-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0 385 568 2003.05.15 titled reservoir control system which is filed and filed by the present applicant has a groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_215", "text": "if it does not pass the necessary decontamination level partially decontaminated water 353 is sent back via return pipe for insufficient decontaminated water 354 to specialized freezing separation ellipsoidal tank for tritiated water heavy water 350 for further freezing decontamination process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100906654-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a display unit for displaying an external storage device for storing the dangerous situation data output from the controller a controller including a response device unit for checking movement and internal temperature and transmitting a check result to the controller and an external transmission unit for transmitting the water quality analysis result data and the location information output by the controller to the water quality management server it is configured to float in small reservoirs and reclaimed freshwater lake water including and measure the water quality and current location of the small reservoirs and reclaimed freshwater lakes in real time and the measured current position information and movement information and water quality measurement signal automatic water quality measuring device for transmitting wirelessly and receive and analyze the water quality measurement signal transmitted from the water quality automatic telemetry device and store it in the built db and the unspecified number of users who have made an online connection through the data communication network are provided with the analysis results stored in the db for small reservoirs and a water quality management server for checking the water quality state management information of reclaimed freshwater lake agricultural water and the position and movement of the automatic water quality measuring device in real time small water reservoir and reclaimed freshwater lake remote water quality automatic observation system characterized in that made including"}, {"pat_id": "US-9670080-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "thus the proppant particles having the curable coating are used for high pressure and temperature conditions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200366454-Y1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore as the cooling cooling water flowing into the electrolytic cell 7 is discharged to the acidic ionized water during the electrolysis process which is inevitably passed in the process of extracting the alkaline ionized water for drinking through the electrolytic cell 7 the cooling reservoir as much as the discharged amount the temperature of the water in the cooling reservoir 6 rises rapidly due to the constant temperature introduced into 6 and as a result the extraction amount of the cold alkaline ionized water also has a problem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200366454-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "in addition it is possible to increase the extraction amount of the cold alkaline ionized water by inhibiting the temperature rise of the water in the cooling reservoir by mixing with the room temperature purified water introduced as much as the ionized water discharged during the electrolysis process"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "it is a further aspect of the present invention to implement the aforementioned monitoring step by utilizing sensors which have been used in the oil industry such as the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring and or the sensors used for leak detection soil heating and temperature mapping"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "various types of sensors can be used the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring that are disclosed in the first reference cited above and or the sensors used for leak detection soil heating and temperature mapping that are disclosed in the second set of references cited above"}]</data>
