ervoir i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200422043-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "it is possible to carry out work while preserving and to selectively dredge only the parts that require dredging and to perform dredging to separate the gravel or sand contained in dredging soil for recycling purposes and to clean the stream the present invention relates to a sludge removal and sewage water treatment device of dredged soil which can be re introduced into a reservoir or reservoir to prevent secondary contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-10156321-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "conversely in order to improve power plant efficiencies it may be necessary to accept contaminant components in excess of 1 by mole in the co2 flow stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434028-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition it is possible to suppress the load and delay that may occur according to the operation change of the management means for such verification and to optimize the installation and operation state through an active response to the external environment.the present invention provides a water pipe connection system of a prefabricated water intake tower for water intake and a method for installing the same comprising the steps of manufacturing a water pipe connection system the manufactured water pipe connection system is inspected at the inspection site and the water pipe connection system is installed at the installation site wherein the water pipe connection system is managed by monitoring facilities disposed at the inspection site and the installation site respectively the handling situation of the water pipe connection system and the surrounding environment the water pipe connection system includes an excavation hole 10 penetrating in an up stream direction at a predetermined position of the dam body 100 installed to block and confine water a water intake pipe connection system of a prefabricated water intake tower for water intake including a discharge pipe 20 having one end connected to the lower part of the water intake tower body 200 built in a prefabricated manner in the water in the reservoir and the other end extending toward the excavation hole 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-4345996-A", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the satellite or associated units of the assembly comprise conduit and in line mixer connected reagent containers respectively containing gaseous sulfur dioxide sulfuric acid sodium hydroxide lime e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_307", "text": "actions increase water contamination but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method according to claim 1 or 2 the permeable sidewalk block unit each box shaped reservoir formed in the box shape is connected to each other to be installed on the ground and to form an excellent storage space therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "as will be described below the permeable sidewalk block unit 100 may be configured alone without the permeable block member 120 and is intended to be expressed in terms of this"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "pumped and transported to the sludge dehydrator 50 using a pump and when the transportation is completed open the closed blocking gate 23 and close the blocking gate 23 on the top of the other sedimentation tank to prevent the inflow of river water pumping and transporting the sludge dewatering device 50 and then dewatering and purifying the moisture contained in the journey is discharged back to the reservoir 11 characterized in that the stream water purification by sedimentation and dredging"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object to form a coriander site on both sides of the sewer and formed in the central longitudinal direction to form embankment on both sides of the coriander site to let the river water flowing through the river flows through the stream in the river the sewer and coriander site has a block size to the river flow inflow to the side of the river inflow to the side of the river flows into a predetermined size so as not to affect the water flow capacity of the river so that the dredging of the journey to facilitate a housing having a bottom surface on which river water is discharged and having a plurality of sedimentation tanks divided by a sedimentation basin divider in a direction parallel to the reservoir in the center of the sedimentation basin so as to control the river water during the dredging operation a front end of the enclosure that is a sedimentation inlet flow path with a head protruding from the center connected to the sedimentation basin divider having a jaw and a groove at the bottom and an upper rod hook groove at the top the prefabricated movable blocking gate installed in the blocking gate installation unit is achieved by installing a sedimentation basin consisting of several prefabricated clasp plates that are miniaturized for easy transportation and an upper hook rod to support the prefabricated clasp plates"}, {"pat_id": "US-7704385-B2", "para_id": "para_158", "text": "is similarly separated by the shearing force of the reverse flow of the water and is returned to the reservoir 53 of sewage 6 via the water pipe 52 which is equipped with the valve 51"}]</data>
</edge>
