  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a structure in which a rainwater discharge blocking wall 990 is configured to fail to flow into the interior of the rainwater collection channel 999 combined with the stairs through the rainwater inlet 998 the upper position of the combined rainwater collecting channel 999 is a structure configured to be equal to the upper surface portion 980 of the land a structure in which a floor covering material 880 composed of rocks is installed at a lower end of the waterway wall 100 so that water swimmers or swimmers can play or swim in water with confidence at the lower end of the combined rainwater collection channel 999 a rainwater or contaminants contaminated with rivers or rivers or reservoirs or dams while constructing a stepped artificial reef 890 where organisms amphibians or fish can be easily inhabited"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_703", "text": "the stream river reservoir lake lagoon or contaminated river water flowing in the vicinity of a dam characterized in that the purified water is naturally purified by floating the river water to the upper part of the eco friendly water purification device 200 used as the water purifier a nature friendly friendliness that naturally purifies polluted water while producing electricity by using an eco friendly water purification device that combines pollutants and soil water and purifies and cleans the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172182-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention provides a water supply step of continuously supplying the flowing water through the water inlet a power supply step of supplying power by sensing the water supply according to the continuous supply of the flowing water through the water inlet and the water inlet an ionized water generation step of automatically generating gold and silver nano ionized water by an electro ionization reaction by applying a variable alternating dc voltage supplied to gold or silver plates installed on both sides of the channel while continuously supplying flowing water flowing through the channel a water discharge step of discharging the gold and silver nano ionized water continuously generated in the water channel through a water outlet and a power cut off to detect power supply interruption by a flow switch according to a blockage of flow of water through the water inlet"}, {"pat_id": "US-6315886-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "any undissolved gases generated by electrolysis in contrast are vented upwardly from the cell to the atmosphere or may be drawn into a fume collector or hood if necessary for collection or further processing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "as a method of separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water by using green energy such as sunlight or hydropower a producing power through the solar power generation unit 1510 and supplying power to the power supply unit 140 to supply electricity through the electrode 130 s210 b temporarily storing the purified seawater in the storage tank 110 and first electrolyzing the electrode 130 through the electrode 130 s220 c performing second electrolysis through the electrode 130 in the waterway 120 while flowing the first electrolyzed seawater from the reservoir 110 s230 d injecting the caustic soda contai