  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 after constructing the above power generation water transfer line 331 by crossing mountains and hills 221 a structure in which a v shaped rising discharge line 332 is formed at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the horizontal state and the bottom height of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by gravity over mountains and hills a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which a lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "bethridge on ca transferred to the inflowing solvent before entering the thus heat exchanger 925 preheated the water and reduced the energy requirements of the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h thermocouple and compensation wire 103i temperature measurement contact 103j thermocouple 103k compensation contact 103l compensation wire 103m reference contact 103n type of thermocouple 103o no protection tube 103p protection tube 103q high temperature object 103r protection tube there is 103s sis type 103t temperature measuring terminal 103u temperature measuring contact 103v stainless steel metal sheath 103w platinum temperature 