  <data key="d6">["suck", "expose", "make", "combine", "backwashe", "solve", "connect", "carry", "accord", "remain", "achieve", "cause", "minimize", "have", "flow", "can", "interrupt", "pump", "provide", "contain", "prevent", "meet", "describe", "form", "shut", "measure", "seal", "build", "pool", "decay", "couple", "fill", "do", "lower", "manufacture", "facilitate", "lock", "accumulate", "purify", "slide", "mount", "submerge", "seat", "latch", "remove", "show", "reduce", "reservoir", "inject", "may", "discharge", "store", "interlock", "drive", "separate", "guide", "dispose", "perform", "incline", "include", "open", "block", "enter", "deposit", "supply", "use", "cut", "gate", "prefabricate", "close", "rotate", "extend", "control", "improve", "register", "be", "utilize", "collect", "instal", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "4 517 207 registered on may 28 2010 entitled structure for reservoir penetration of storm water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "8a 19 is provided to prevent leakage of rainwater stored in the storm water reservoir into the gap between the blocks 1 2 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-8808497-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "water and other fluids often accumulate various contaminants and it is often desirable or necessary to separate the fluid from the contaminant to meet various purity targets or reduce the volume of liquid within an open reservoir which may be necessary for practical legal or other reasons"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101770268-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "4 517 207 registered on may 28 2010 entitled structure for reservoir penetration of storm water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248173-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "patent registration 10 0582121 excellent storage tank patent registration 10 0938223 assembly type excellent storage tank patent 10 1118263 excellent storage tank and pre construction method using precast concrete block patent 10 1013235 method of manufacturing excellent storage tank the present invention is a prefabricated rainwater storage tank column and the bottom and top of the columnar block and the prefabricated block for easy to carry out the vertical assembly process was a high difficulty in the process of building an excellent storage tank by pc block assembly the purpose is to provide a bottom column beam coupling structure of the prefabricated rainwater storage tank combined with a simple and stable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101398010-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a reservoir installed on the lower side of the gutter a connection pipe connecting the storm water pipe and the storage tank a storage tank installed in the connection pipe for controlling the stormwater flowing into the storage tank through the connection pipe a first sensor installed on the upstream side of the connection pipe among the gross conduits and measuring a contamination degree and a quantity of the ozone flowing into the gutter tube a second sensor installed inside the storage tank for measuring a contamination level and a water level of the storm water filled in the storage tank a discharge pump installed in the storage tank for sucking the rainwater in the storage tank and discharging the rainwater to the outside and a control unit for opening and closing the storage tank gates in accordance with an initial stormwater inflow signal and an initial wastewater termination signal of the first sensor and driving the discharge pump according to the high water level signal or the contamination signal of the second sensor the storage tank gates a connection pipe interlocking part installed to be rotatable at an inlet of the connection pipe and interrupting the connection pipe while rotating and an excellent pipe shut off part slidably installed in the connection pipe cut off part and slid in a state where the connection pipe cut off part is opened to cut off the excellent pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101208694-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the blockage of the filter media is frequent the filtration efficiency is lowered there is a need for frequent backwashing there was a problem such that the function of storm water storage facilities to prevent the contamination of the river water is not properly performed.the present invention has been made to solve the conventional problems as described above can improve the excellent filtration efficiency and recycling degree can improve the backwashing efficiency during the backwashing of the first filtration unit and the washing of the reservoir it is possible to reduce the sludge sedimentation on the bottom surface while facilitating the drainage of washing water at the same time to perform additional filtration of rainwater without additional power and to prevent the re injury of sediment deposited on the floor surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
