  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "according to the present invention only a crush stone is installed at the lower end of the reservoir structure so as to penetrate not only the reservoir of the storm but also the stormwater and by implementing the water circulation system penetrating into the ground through the reservoir with the upper reservoir and the lower reservoir it is possible to keep reservoirs and infiltration for water circulation and thus to prevent flooding even in temporary storms in areas where the impervious area is wide and the effect on the water circulation system is large.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101286960-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "at the end of the discharge guide 18 a discharge port 19 for changing the discharging direction of the deposit or the like may be formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101286960-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "when the storm reservoir 12 has a cylindrical shape since the inflow storm is struck against the inner surface of the storm reservoir 12 it is possible to obtain the same effect as a centrifugation of a kind 12 it has the advantage of being able to deposit on the floor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101788120-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "according to the present invention the storm reservoir is capable of originally suppressing the inflow of the initial stormwater or the sewage selectively picking up only the peak flow rate in the stormwater storage and drainage system does not generate odor reduce administrative costs and effort by reducing.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the rainwater introduced into the storm reservoir is formed at the half point of the height of the slab 3 as described above so that the rainwater flowed into the storm reservoir is about 50 of the water into the basement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "thus when th