nto the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "1 a is a top plan view of several storm reservoir block slabs and is stacked 1 where the multiple storm reservoir block slabs meet to become one"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "finally when the storm reservoir block assembly is completed the storm reservoir block consists of fixing the end wall plate to the storm reservoir block column using a piece anchor bolt along the storm reservoir block requiring the wall and installing the laminated structure by frp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101433517-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent discharge pipe which is vertically fixed to the side wall of the building or pier and discharges the storm downward a cylindrical foreign matter removing cylinder which is detachably fitted to a lower end of the storm drain pipe and discharges the foreign matter contained in the stormwater in a state where the foreign matter is filtered out a drain hole formed in a lower surface of the lower surface of the foreign matter filtering tube to control a discharge rate while filtering out foreign matter in the rainwater a waste pipe formed to communicate with the outside of the foreign matter filtering