luding filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101724155-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a rainwater purification plant the present invention relates to rainwater purification and water supply facilities for trees and more particularly to a rainwater purification and water supply facility for trees which comprises a sidewalk covered with concrete and asphalt a rainwater flowing along a sidewalk and a road surface it is introduced into the reservoir soil and supplied to the foundation soil again through many wicks to prevent contamination of the river or ground water prevent flooding due to heavy rainfall improve the urban aesthetics and prevent the trees from dry the present invention relates to a rainwater purification and water supply facility for trees"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 0894022 april 10 2009 in the treatment of non point pollutants contained in the initial rainfall effluent waterproofing the effluent purified in the non point pollutant treatment apparatus the variable wear is formed to protrude upwards to the inside so that the initial rainfall outflow water flows in the rain pipe is formed on one side a gripping portion is formed at an upper end and a screen is formed on an outer surface thereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "and part of the circulating water through the circulating water supply pipe 61 through the circulating water supply pipe 61 is sent to the buried contact medium storage facility 70 and the circulating water introduced into the void contact medium storage facility is purified while passing through the pore medium is distributed and collected the facility 80 is moved to the distribution collection basin 81 and is supplied from the collection basin 81 to the pond 30 formed at the bottom of the reservoir so that the water in the pond is always kept purified while the pond 30 water overflowed to the free fall into the overflow wear room 31 this operation is to be re introduced to the filtration purification 40 of the repeatedly formed through the air outlet pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "1 to 6 to separate the initial rainfall effluent and to form a rainwater toil chamber 11 having a settling function the rainwater toil chamber 11 is an inlet pipe 12 rainwater discharge pipe 13 and tea collection rainwater collection facility 10 having a storage facility inlet pipe 14 and the settling space 15 connected to the reservoir so that rainwater flows into the reservoir while having a function and the screen facility 16 to block the inflow of contaminants into the reservoir the rainwater collection facility in the rainwater collection facility 11 the storage facility 20 through which the rainwater flows into the reservoir through the reservoir inlet pipe 14 and installed on the bottom of the reservoir to produce a water change pipe and the overflow wear room on one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "it moves to the distribution collection basin 81 which is a collecting facility 80 and supplies it to the pond 30 formed at the bottom of the reservoir from the sump 81 so that the water in the pond is always kept purified water while the pond 30 water overflowed to the free fall into the overflow wear room 31 this operation is to be re introduced to the filtration purification 40 of the repeatedly formed through the air outlet pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "US-6120210-A", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "the sand deposit can be that deposited in the stream or may be constructed as an artificial debris filled water storage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the first method is to install water gates valves and movable wear to control the discharge amount at the outlet and open these facilities at normal times to drain the reservoir water and then close the water gate to settle down after a certain period of time"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2895662-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "when there is heavy rainfall a reservoir or tank may become overwhelmed by a sudden rush of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to purify rainwater collected in a storage tank and to provide it as a landscape water and a living water thereby preventing a water shortage phenomenon and a nonpoint pollution reduction high initial stormwater is stored in the reservoir and purified rainwater is discharged at the end of rainfall or gradually penetrated into the underground to prevent flood maintain groundwater level at a certain level to prevent ground stabilization and river pollution"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
