gitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck the permeable concrete bottom layer comprises a deck walkway rainwater storage device for the filtering space characterized in that it comprises at least one overflow plate having a relatively lower height than the outer wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the second vertical plate extending a certain length directly below the lower surface of the deck and relative to the permeable concrete bottom layer of the reservoir portion than the outer wall and a second filtration plate installed to be replaceable in an opening formed in an opening formed at a lower end in contact with an upper end of the overflow partition which is provided at a low height to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow partition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101468324-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "10 a the third open close board 40 of the present invention can be shut off passively so that even when the rain is over in the event of an emergency the river floods or exceeds the sewage treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant it is possible to block a multiple of the initial storm stored in the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101016329-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "nothing has been done.the present invention has been proposed in order to solve the conventional problems as described above the object of the construction is to replace the roof of the existing storage tank while being constructed in a simplified structure to block the inflow of dust and lower the construction cost as well as drainage of rain water the present invention provides a reservoir cover device and a reservoir including the same which can smoothly and easily handle odors or harmful gases and in particular the height of the lid can be adjusted according to the reservoir level thereby enabling the adjustment of the storage capacity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200499514-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "a typical vinyl house 100 is structured so that rain or snow accumulates on the roof and therefore if a large amount of rain or snow accumulates on the roof due to heavy rain or heavy snow the vinyl house may collapse"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "at this time the rain inlet 45 may be formed in the upper plate 40 as described above but the upper end of the outer wall block 10 10a that is the outer wall according to the rain storage tank 1 of the present invention buried underground in the case of rainwater drain port 46 