hereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "US-6932540-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "although not wishing to be bound by theory applicants hypothesize that foam based floatation panels having a particular range of buoyancies may be used to form reservoir covers exhibiting a heretofore unknown balance of properties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101351825-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "in one embodiment a sufficient amount of rainwater is stored in the side reservoir panel 130 to block the inflow of rainwater or once stored so that foreign matter does not block the inlet 121 or the filter portion 122 while it is not raining"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321399-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "here the filtration unit 10 is filtered while the rain water is passed through the pitcher block 11 in the rain the heavy water is converted into the heavy water the heavy water through the reservoir block 12 the drain hole 14 and the fitting pipe 15 21"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "rain gutters formed with an opening toward the upper portion grating which is installed in the upper opening of the rain gutters consisting of a plate shaped between the ceiling of the rainwater reservoir main body while being set at a predetermined distance from the first outlet hole inside the rainwater reservoir body an excellent storage tank including a baffle forming a overflow portion at the top a sewage box connected to the first outlet hole of the rainwater storage tank through a connecting pipe to store rainwater discharged from the rainwater storage tank wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a bottom of the rainwater storage tank body corresponding to a lower portion of the rainwater reservoir a container seating portion formed in a groove shape in the portion the upper structure is provided with a lifting hook and is characterized in that it comprises a container which is collected in the container seating portion to collect the contaminants introduced to the rainwater reservoir body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a reservoir which is buried in a drainage passage in a basement of a road the upper surface of which is open to the surface of the road and which is empty inside and which has bottom drains and side drains on the bottom and sides thereof a grating provided with an opening closing portion covering the open upper surface of the storage container to control rainwater and foreign substances into the storage container and it is connected to the opening and closing portion of the grating in a state arranged in the reservoir and buoyancy body for opening and closing the opening and closing while being elevated in accordance with the flow rate of the rain in the reservoir the grating the outer frame seated on the upper edge of the reservoir and the center portion penetrated a plurality of fixed gratings fixedly disposed at the central through hole of the outer frame and spaced apart at regular intervals along the length direction respectively and having an excellent inlet hole the opening and closing portion is disposed between each of the fixed grate and made up of a plurality of lifting grate for opening and closing the gap between the fixed grate while lifting up and down according to the lifting of the buoyancy body and a connecting frame one end of which is connected to each bottom surface of the plurality of lifting bars and the other end of which is connected to the buoyancy body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater drainage for roads apparatus for draining of rain water for road the present invention relates to a rainwater drainage system for roads and more particularly between a plurality of stationary grates provided with rainwater inlet holes in the grating and each of the fixed grates while being lifted up and down according to the lifting of the buoyant body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "by opening a large amount of rainwater into the reservoir quickly and allowing it to be discharged into the drain it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather conditions of the road and also to prevent leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside and the introduction of foreign substances into the drain can be controlled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "opening and closing part made up of a plurality of lifting grate to open and close when small rain occurs the opening and closing part is closed state rainwater inlet through the rain inlet hole to prevent the inflow of foreign matters and in case of many rain the opening and closing part is opened so that a large amount of rainwater can be quickly flowed into the reservoir and discharged to the drainage so that it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather situation of the road and also to prevent leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside and of foreign substances in the drainage can be cracked down get the effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "when a certain load when a certain amount of rain is filled into the reservoir is applied to the lifting plate 41a the weight 41b opposite to the opening and closing plate 41a is lifted upward while the opening and closing plate 41a is axially rotated downward while the the bottom drain 11 is opened to drain the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore according to the present invention it is possible to efficiently use the storages stored in the road boundary block since the water is stored without discharging the water in the wet state immediately after the rain and the storm is drained to the ground when the ground is dry.1 is a perspective view showing a state in which a road boundary block according to an embodiment of the present invention is installed fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102266083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sewage odor blocking device for manholethe present invention relates to a sewage odor blocking device for a manhole and more particularly a plate having an inlet hole formed in the center so that external fluid flows in while supporting the manhole cover a storage tube formed at the lower end of the plate and the storage container it is composed of a blocking film that closes the lower end of the bin and the barrier film automatically closes the lower end of the reservoir by gravity in normal times to smoothly block odors flowing back from the water supply and sewerage system and an open film is formed on the barrier film and the open film is a barrier film and by rotating in the opposite direction the upper and lower sewer pipes overflow in the rainy season or rain and are opened to the backflowing fluid to discharge the fluid to the outside thereby preventing the manhole from being opened by water pressure thereby preventing personal injury and the upper part of the plate by installing a blocking net on the side it is possible to filter out foreign substances in the fluid flowing through the inlet hole and prevent the water supply sewerage or odor blocking device from being blocked by foreign substances and safety information for maintaining manhole management and preventing safety accidents it relates to a sewage odor blocking device for manholes marked with"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "it has a cold feeling that is not in harmony with the appearance of a house or a building it is covered with the rainwater reservoir of the color pattern and built in the inside space to prevent direct exposure to direct sunlight rain and wind so that even if it is used for a long time it does not cause deformation or breakage of rainwater reservoir and can prevent water from being spoiled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore foreign substances or impurities accumulated in the body 1 2 times a year it is possible to clean the inside of the body to remove it and the structure of the device is waterproof structure so that water can not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2895662-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the capacity of such a drainage system as at risk of being overwhelmed with water during storms and it is consequently desirable to prevent an excessive amount of water arriving at a reservoir or tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in the first aspect of the present invention the permeable sidewalk block unit is installed on the grou