  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100983829-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a wastewater treatment method for treating wastewater containing organic substances via an input tank a methane fermentation tank a fermentation filtrate collection tank a measuring tank an aeration tank a precipitation tank a distribution tank a culture tank a sludge storage tank and a treatment tank a stirrer is installed in the input tank to agitate the corrosive reaction and the activated silicate having completed the corrosive reaction returned from the raw water and the culture tank to activate the corrosive reaction introducing the raw water which has undergone the corrosion reaction from the charging tank into a methane fermentation tank to proceed with fermentation by methane from the methane fermentation tank the fermentation complete digestion liquid is introduced into the fermentation filtrate collection tank and in a state in which the fermentation filtrate collection tank is introduced into the metering tank a predetermined amount of digestion liquid is introduced into the aeration tank and the remaining amount is returned to the fermentation filtrate collection tank to the aeration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101833173-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a supply pipe for supplying a branch pipe which is split at one side of the supply pipe a solenoid valve for shielding the branch pipe a drug reservoir containing a chlorine liquid a chemical liquid conduit connected to the chemical reservoir for introducing the chlorine liquid into the branch pipe a metering pump for injecting the chlorine liquid into the chemical liquid transfer conduit a merging pipe formed in a y shape and mixing raw water introduced through a supply pipe with treated water in which a chlorine liquid flowing through the chemical liquid transfer pipe and a part of the raw water flowing through the branch pipe are mixed a controller for controlling the solenoid valve and the metering pump the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water flowing from the measurement branch pipe is set to a value obtained by subtracting the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water from the measurement branch pipe and a residual chlorine measuring unit including a residual chlorine measuring sensor for measuring the residual chlorine and a zinc ionizing electrode for removing anions contained in the introduced dilution water wherein a plurality of partition walls are provided between the zinc ionizing electrode and the residual chlorine measuring sensor and a display window is provided on one side of the controller and the measurement is made from the current chlorine measuring unit to measure the concentration of the foreign matter in the precipitation chamber the information of the residual chlorine is displayed on the display window of the controller and the opening closing sensor provided in the water supply and the controller drives the solenoid valve and the metering pump at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100612249-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "however this precipitation method is difficult to neutralize the acid rain and the quality of the stored rainwater is worse because the decay begins when the particles are small or floating contaminants or microorganisms mixed in the rainwater into the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "US-7031927-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "elevated nutrient levels are also required for this growth in the reservoir and such nutrient levels are most often produced by watershed runoff thus by precipitation as another predictable weather condition"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4444366-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "a work hole communicating in a vertical direction is provided by the skeleton block partly cut out and the reinforcing plate partly cut out a partition wall is provided so as to surround the precipitation tank and the precipitation tank and the size of the skeleton block provided in the water reser