de of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388941-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in order to prevent such contamination of mine drainage in advance conventionally it can be selectively installed before and after a shophouse successive alkaltnity producting system tank that can purify heavy metals in the middle of a mine a marsh planted with aquatic plants and a shophouse tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021035-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "physical washing using a brush or a loofah may be used for washing the reservoir but chemical washing using a cleaning solution containing a specific component is generally used"}, {"pat_id": "US-9797613-B2", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "this can both prolong the working life of the transducers 160 and inhibit any degradation in the illumination of the stored water by the uv lamp 170"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "to limit contamination of the receiving flows and streams by untreated combined sewage the diverted flow may enter the receiving stream by direct overflow only when the soil percentage of the water to be discharged has been reduced to a level such that there is no further risk of appreciable contamination of the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545740-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a house comprising an inner house formed from the ground to form an inner space and an outer house surrounding the inner house and spaced apart from the outer side of the inner house so as to have a water film space a water film forming pipe installed in the longitudinal direction of the inner house at an upper portion of the water film space to allow groundwater to flow to the outer surface of the inner house to form a water film a positive water gauge located at a position adjacent to the house groundwater supply means for pumping groundwater from the hydropower reservoir and supplying it to the water film forming pipe and a sedimentation inducing means disposed proximate the screen region formed in the amphibious well to induce precipitation of iron or manganese wherein the precipitation inducing means includes a metal having a higher reactivity than iron in order to react with the iron before the iron is oxidized to prevent formation of precipitates by iron oxidation and is replaceable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "therefore the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the second embodiment of the present invention is configured such that only the reservoir 200 is maintained until the level of the reservoir 200 reaches the highest level in the u shape reversed to the siphon channel 295 a sufficient amount of time for the primary precipitation treatment is ensured and then an initial excellent standoff contamination is supplied to the sedimentation paper 400 through the flow rate reducing manhole 300 at a limited flow rate and is discharged through the discharge water gate 500 and the excellent non point pollution is discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937004-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention of the above described configuration is disposed on the reservoir water and subjected to the electrolysis and electrocoagulation treatment the precipitation treatment and the microbial treatment and the vegetation filtration decomposition of the green algae propagated water thereby completely eliminating the green algae remaining in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937004-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition because no chemicals are used to remove the algae in the water secondary pollution is not generated by the treated water returned to the reservoir and the water treatment is purely electrolysis and electrocoagulation precipitation biochemical treatment by microorganisms and aquatic life"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "US-9850152-B2", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "treated water is then passed to a degassifier 25 to remove any residual gases and then fed to a downstream filter 26 to remove precipitated salts collecting the de scaled water in the reservoir 27"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of inflow distribution tank aeration part contact oxidation tank sediment part contact oxidation tank outflow storage tank sludge storage tank and acid pipe and by applying contact oxidation method using contact media in the aeration part and precipitation contact oxidation tank polluted river water and sewage in the apparatus for treating sewage installed on one side of the inflow distribution tank to adjust the level of the treated water flowing from the inlet each movable bank for adjusting the level of the treated water installed and installed on one side of the outlet storage tank perforated perforated walls 7 15 of area formed in the interface between the inlet distribution tank and the aeration contacting tank the interface between the aeration contacting tank and the sludge hopper and the interface between the precipitation contacting oxidation tank and the outflow reservoir a supernatant water storage tank which is formed by trapping the sludge hopper formed in the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration contacting oxidation tank and the precipitation contacting oxidation tank to the sludge storage tank through an air lift and partitioned by an operation full width bank on one side of the sludge storage tank an diffuser installed in the inflow distribution tank and the outflow storage tank to supply dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to the inside of the contact oxidation tank and the treated water discharged while being prevented from being closed by sludge and contact oxidation method further comprises at least one contact medium selected from the group consisting of crushed stone of 30 to 40 of porosity or plastic of 80 or more of porosity in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and precipitation part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "precipitate contact oxidation tank 4 sludge hopper 5 to collect precipitated sludge outflow reservoir 10 to collect treated effluents outlet 11 to dispose of treated water and precipitation contact oxidation 4 it consists of a sludge storage tank 13 for sedimentation by storing the sludge precipitated in the"}, {"pat_id": "US-10350653-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "bacterial contamination is usually observed in crude oil whilst fungi usually cause contamination of aviation fuel"}]</data>
