  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "US-8221029-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "conduit 24 may be constructed of pvc but other materials can be used"}, {"pat_id": "US-8808497-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "water and other fluids often accumulate various contaminants and it is often desirable or necessary to separate the fluid from the contaminant to meet various purity targets or reduce the volume of liquid within an open reservoir which may be necessary for practical legal or other reasons"}, {"pat_id": "US-7031927-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "elevated nutrient levels are also required for this growth in the reservoir and such nutrient levels are most often produced by watershed runoff thus by precipitation as another predictable weather condition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in vegetation reservoirs for preventing pollution and creating a healthy urban environment a reservoir for storing rainfall runoff on the surface of the ground a vegetation filtration reservoir located at a lower portion of the reservoir and having a height of 25 to 60 cm including humus soil and sand at least one es filtration layer located below the vegetation filtration reservoir a collecting part located below the es filtration layer and having a storage part including a first gravel layer and a second gravel layer and a permeate part disposed in a lower part of the storage part and including a third gravel layer and a sand layer a pouring pipe disposed in the infiltration portion and being buried in the pouring portion to collect rainwater flowing out from the pouring portion an outlet pipe connected to the pipe a drain pipe provided in the vegetation filtration reservoir and a water pipe for collecting the water collected in the pipe pipe upward a bypass pipe connected to the drain port for bypassing the rainwater flowing out of the storage compartment of the storage compartment a second accommodating portion having a first accommodating portion having an inflow port into which the rainwater effluent flows an outlet provided with a screen for removing foreign matter in the rainwater inflow water flowing from the first accommodating portion and a vertical partition wall arranged so as to be communicated with each other an es expanded shale filter medium is disposed at a boundary between the vegetation filtration reservoir and the original soil and a bottom surface of the bottom of the water outlet is at least 30 cm away from the bottom of the bottom of the water outlet the vegetation filtration reservoir includes fly ash within 5 of the volume of the vegetation filtration reservoir wherein an aerobic condition layer is formed on the upper part of the basin of the drain hole and an anaerobic anaerobic condition layer is formed on the lower part of the basin of the drain hole to prevent pollution and to provide a healthy urban environment"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}]</data>
