  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "this tendency is only amplified due to the fact that porosity reservoirs are typically constructed within the alluvial soils of a river bed so that there is an upstream and downstream portion to the reservoir corresponding to the overall valley gradient"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "due to a natural gradient of the land where porosity reservoir is formed e.g"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_130", "text": "20 water leakage detection system 50 distribution reservoir 100a 100b 510 800 piping network 101a 101b sensor 110a 110b estimated water leakage area 120 piping 200 monitoring device 210 sensor device 220 communication unit 230 303 pressure sensor 240 access point 250 internet 301 control unit 302 317 communication if 305 318 internal bus 311 processor 312 memory 313 storage 314 external device if 315 input if 316 output if 401 data acquisition unit 402 dynamic water level calculator 403 difference calculator 404 visualization unit 405 abnormality determination unit 406 estimation unit 407 output unit 408 estimation data storage unit 409 judgment data storage unit 500 ground 501 502 503 504 650 810a 810b 810c 810d 810e location 520 water surface 525 hydrodynamic gradient 530 hydrostatic pressure 540 hydrodynamic pressure 550 booster pump 560 hydrostatic level 561 hydrostatic head 562 572 altitude 570 dynamic water level 571 dynamic water head 600a 600b dynamic water level distribution 620a 620b 750 760 normal vector 710 difference 900 910 simulation result 1000 1100 1210 visualization information 1200 1410 1420 1430 screen 1220 map 1310 1320 1330 contour map"}]</data>
