  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102207360-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a first motor and a suction hopper mounted in front of the body to suck the sediment a discharge pipe connected in communication with the suction hopper to send the sucked sediment to the outside and installed inside the suction hopper to crush the sediment an underwater cleaning robot comprising a crushing screw and a second motor for driving the crushing screw and a hydraulic pressure generating device mounted on the body and configured to drive the first and second motors using hydraulic pressure and control remotely the technology is also presented"}, {"pat_id": "US-10384960-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "to increase its effectiveness fracturing fluid often comprises a propping agent used to hold open cracks in rock formations after hydraulic pressure dissipates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101874096-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in addition the analysis of the water supply pipe network can also determine the control time of the water control valve v2 by calculating the time during which the water pressure falls at the critical point c from the water control valve control point a at the reservoir control point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal 120b is operated by receiving power from the emergency storage battery 20 and information such as whether the valve is opened or closed flow rate hydraulic pressure water level in each reservoir leakage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition the analysis of the water supply pipe network can also determine the control time of the water control valve v2 by calculating the time during which the water pressure falls at the critical point c from the water control valve control point a at the reservoir control point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition there is a fear of secondary contamination such as microbial growth due to the stagnation of the treated water in the storage tank it was necessary to increase the processing capacity of the process to be treated at the rear end of the storage tank.the present invention was devised to solve the above mentioned problems and does not install a reservoir and does not apply a brake to the flow of treated water and does not require an additional pump and does not additionally install a reservoir and a pump in the middle of a water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101630268-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for estimating whether or not a water supply pipe is disconnected between blocks using an information processing apparatus including a database unit for providing information on a block and a water pipe and a control unit for processing the information the first hydraulic pressure measuring part provided on the target block and the second hydraulic pressure measuring part provided on the adjacent block are set to a unit time ttot and the control unit sets the water pressure measured by the first water pressure measurement unit at the first head and the water pressure measured by the second water pressure measuring unit is converted into a second head lt rti and wherein the control unit is configured to set a water level at a drainage peak of the target block and the peak level of the reservoir of the adjacent block and if they do not coincide with each other proceeding to the first processing step and if they are coincident with each other proceeding to the second processing step the first process may include a first data collecting step of collecting a plurality of first data r1 t generated at different time points t according to whether or not the formula 1 is satisfied and when the ratio p1 of the number of first data generated by satisfying the following formula 1 to the total number of the first data is equal to or larger than a predetermined first specific ratio pa and a first result output step of estimating and outputting an inter block disconnection when the second specific ratio is less than a first specific ratio pa and less than a second predetermined ratio pb the second process may include the first head unit time per change which is the absolute value of the first head variation value at each time point t and calculates the second head unit time per change which is the absolute value of the second head variation value at each time point t after the head variation value calculation step the first head variation value rti id 0.0 of the first average head variation value and calculates the second head variation value ttot during the entire measurement time ttot of the second average head variation value calculating an average head variation value the method of claim 1 further comprising determining whether at least one first specific time point t1 satisfying the following equations 2 and 3 exists during the total measurement time ttot t2 satisfying all of the following equations 4 and 5 if at least one of the first specific time t1 and the second specific time t2 does not exist after the specific time calculating step the total time ttot is reset by adding the additional time tp t1 and the second specific time point t2 are all present in the first and second time points t1 t2 the average head variation value calculating step determining an observation interval to by summing all the intervals during a predetermined time ta and at a specific time t1 and after the second specific time t2 after the observation interval determination step a plurality of second data r2 t generated by varying a result value according to whether or not the following equation 6 is satisfied for each time point t within the observation interval to is collected a second data collecting step of collecting data and and when the ratio p2 of the number of second data generated by satisfying the following formula 6 with respect to the total number of the second data is equal to or greater than a predetermined third specific ratio pc and a second result outputting step of estimating and outputting an inter block disconnection when the third specific ratio pc is less than a predetermined fourth specific ratio pd"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050751-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "foul smell isolation installation of manhole the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of the manhole and more particularly a plate in which an inlet hole is formed in the center portion to support the manhole cover to inflow the external fluid a reservoir formed in the lower end of the plate and the reservoir it is composed of a blocking film to seal the lower end is normally closed by gravity and magnetic material the blocking film automatically seals the lower end of the reservoir to smoothly block odors flowing back and forth from the water and sewage an open film is formed on the blocking film the open film is a blocking film by rotating to the contrary in rainy or rainy days the water and sewage pipes are flooded and opened to the backflowing fluid to discharge the fluid to the outside to prevent the opening of the manhole by hydraulic pressure thereby preventing personal injury blocking network is installed on the upper surface so that filtering out substances relate to the odor barrier device of a manhole which can prevent clogging of a phase by a foreign matter sewage or bad smell blocking device"}]</data>
