  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102715270-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "accordingly the protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the description of the claims and the scope of equivalents thereof.1 spawning area 2 water supply area 3 egg transfer unit 10 storage tank 20 drinking water pipe 30 drinking water pump 40 washing nozzle 50 washing pipe 60 washing pump 70 chlorine dioxide gas generating unit 80 gas pipe 90 water pipe a0 water supply valve b0 concentration measurement unit c0 water level measurement unit d0 contamination measurement unit d1 projector d2 camera e0 intensive cleaning section e1 guide rail e2 concentrated cleaning nozzle e3 concentrated cleaning pipe e4 concentrated washing pump e5 drive unit 110 1st tank 120 2nd tank 130 3rd tank 210 1st reaction tank 220 second reaction tank 230 third reaction tank 310 1st gas discharge pipe 320 2nd gas discharge pipe 330 3rd gas discharge pipe 400 integrated pipe 710 1st metering pump 720 2nd metering pump 730 3rd quantitative pump 1110 1st auxiliary tank 1120 second auxiliary tank 1130 third auxiliary tank 1200 level sensor 1300 alarm 1400 reservoir tank 1500 aeration device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200395622-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "such a sluice generally adopts a movable structure through hydraulic pressure to open and close the drainage and adjust the amount of storage of the levee but it is true that the function to prevent the contamination of water stored for a long time is insufficient.therefore an object of the present invention is to solve such a problem and to provide a hydraulic hydrologic structure to prevent water pollution by sprinkling and discharging the deep water of the stored water to the outside according to the low water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200395622-Y1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "even if the waterway 70 is completely closed the water is prevented from being contaminated because the stored water is continuously discharged over a part of the water pipe 50.as described above according to the present invention the deep water of the stored water is sprinkled and discharged to the outside according to the low water level thereby inducing the movement of the stored water thereby preventing water pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_622", "text": "therefore if the water is confined in a certain place for a long time the pollution is further increased by the material decomposition action and the material bonding action so the water stored in the water storage space is always maintained at the full water level and the water flowing from the upstream through the lower part of the water gate frequent discharge is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and if water is used to discharge water from the reservoir through the lower part of the water gate the substances contained in the water are combined to combine the substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133174-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in addition to the investigation of the water quality items for the treated water body 10 as described above the volume of the treated water body 10 and the capacity of the untreated water to be treated are determined and the degree of contamination of the water to be treated is determined to determine what is the substance to be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the end part is immersed in the water level of undischarged sewage that always remains in the storage state in the sewage tank so that the negative effects such as contamination of indoor air due to odors during the sewage discharge operation can be eliminated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100744631-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "hydrologic control unit for adjusting the connected via the plurality of chlorine ion meter and wired and wireless communication means and stores the concentration data received from the chlorine ion meter and to identify the variation in the water quality compared to the comparative chlorine ion concentration data stored in the database and stores the result a main server for outputting and transmitting to a remote place and a management server connected to the main server through a wired wireless communication means and controlling the operation of the water level or the sewage treatment plant of the reservoir into which the initial rainwater flows in accordance with the change in the water quality of the initial rainwater transmitted from the main server"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "as a result contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "a certain water level difference in this case indicates a reduced flow of water between the pelvic chamber 5 and the storage space 10 via the retaining elements 11 wherein contamination of the retaining elements 11 can be concluded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484030-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "when a large amount of sewage having a high degree of contamination due to rainstorms flows into the interior of the retention space 400 the interior of the retention space 400 is gradually filled with water from the bottom of the retention space 400 when the water level is higher than the inlet the sewage flows into the interior of the pretreatment needle sink 110 through the inflow hole 111 while passing through the inflow pipe 112"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0418572-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "by increasing the water level 34a and the pressure generated thereby a vertical flow of the purified water in the space between the walls of the inner pot 42 and the pot like extension 41 is then promoted from top to bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674355-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "however such a water intake tower has a problem in that the sediment sludge is introduced into the bottom of the foundation concrete and the sediment sludge 1 is introduced into the intake port 13 to contaminate the water supply.the present invention is to solve the problems as described above to prevent the sewage sludge is introduced into the water intake and to discharge the incoming soil sludge to prevent the contamination of the water supply by the sewage sludge installed water tap inlet water level the purpose is to provide a structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674355-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "according to the present invention the water intake tower low water level installation structure configured as described above by preventing the sediment sludge is introduced into the water intake and discharges the incoming sediment sludge to prevent contamination of the water supply by the sediment sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102258856-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a fish farm that can supply vegetable and animal food is provided and each water level control device is applied to maintain the water level of the fish farm but contamination of excrement containing ammonia nitrogen generated during the process of growing fish inside the fish farm it is applied to transfer water to the activated sludge tank and the contaminated water stored in the activated sludge tank is converted into harmless nitrate nitrogen from harmful ammonia nitrogen by the activated sludge method including photocatalyst microbial carrier and bubbling and vegetable crops after changing to propagate a large amount of beneficial microorganisms the activated sludge treatment water is configured to be transferred to the vegetable cultivation area and the crops in the vegetable cultivation area absorb the nutrient water provided by the activated sludge treatment water resulting in excellent freshness and high quality of the crop"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101233804-B1", "para_id": "para_127", "text": "therefore if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the contamination is further increased by the material decomposition action and the material binding action so that the water stored in the reservoir always maintains the full water level and the water coming from the upstream through the lower part of the water gate often discharged is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and also by using the method to discharge water in the reservoir through the lower part of the sluice by the material binding action that combines the substances contained in the water it releases pollutants such as aggregated sewage sludge and at the same time generates material acceleration phenomenon material scavenging phenomenon material decomposition action material flotation action and naturally cleans the contaminated water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974535-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "also as described above the time point at which the initial rainwater drain valve v1 is closed closed can be closed only for a time period in which the water level precipitation amount is maintained on the high water level of the flowmeter chamber 112c when the rainwater is not continuously detected the initial rainwater exclusion valve v1 is closed closed to prevent contamination of the body portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101004130-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water level control system water level controll system the present invention relates to a water level control system and more particularly it is possible to prevent the contamination of groundwater by sealing the upper part of the groundwater well as well as to control the operation of the pump by sensing the water pressure formed in the upper part of the groundwater well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101004130-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the water level control system 100 according to an embodiment of the present invention may not only prevent the contamination of groundwater by sealing the upper portion of the groundwater well 1 but also by detecting the water pressure formed in the groundwater well 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102436761-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the end part is immersed in the water level of undischarged sewage that always remains in the storage state in the sewage tank so that the negative effects such as contamination of indoor air due to odors during the sewage discharge operation can be eliminated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100466336-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water level control system of a freshwater facility that measures the level of a reservoir containing fluid that is distilled water condensate in a freshwater facility and controls the discharge or supply of distilled water condensed water according to the degree of contamination of the distilled water condensed water while maintaining the proper level"}, {"pat_id": "US-6582563-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "it is to be realized that the inlet valve 52 the float switche