r may be calculated through a water meter and water supply time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306263-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the height of the coagulant layer obtained through experiments and calculations and the amount of coagulant input correspond to the degree of contamination of the wash water and are stored in the operation unit of the washing machine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102544552-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "generated in aquaculture is leaked to the outside together with the effluent thereby causing contamination of the water system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042852-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "therefore if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the pollution is further increased by the material decomposition and material binding action so that the water stored in the reservoir always maintains the full water level while the water that flows upstream from the upstream frequent discharge through the phone is the best way to prevent the contamination of the river water and also by using the method of discharging the water in the reservoir through the cyphon constituted in the sluice the substances contained in the water are combined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087796-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "according to one embodiment the sewage water level adjusting device 100 is installed at the bottom of the sand filtration tank to pass through the powder activated carbon filtration tank formed by the powdered activated carbon is a certain thickness of the sand filtration the contamination contained in the concentrated water it may include an activated carbon filter for adsorbing the material by the powdered activated carbon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0178112-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "therefore by supplying activated carbon using the present invention not only there is no fear of contamination of the surrounding environment but also the working environment of workers can be greatly improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100191863-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore the present invention has been made to solve the above problems the raw water is filtered through a multi stage pre treatment filter membrane filter post treatment filter to store the water in the storage tank and to circulate the drained concentrated water refiltered a reverse osmosis water purification device comprising a water quality sensor installed at a front end of a pretreatment filter to detect a pollution concentration of raw water and to block inflow of raw water according to a contamination state of concentrated water a first drain valve branched between the water quality sensor and the pretreatment filter and configured to drain according to the pollution concentration of the raw water a solenoid valve disposed between the primary drain valve and the pretreatment filter and configured to open close the water channel by an electric operation according to the pollution concentration and the water level of the auxiliary reservoir tank and the reservoir tank an auxiliary reservoir installed between the all carbon filter and the membrane filter to pump water from the all carbon filter to the membrane filter and to receive the drained water of the membrane filter a secondary drain valve connected to a lower portion of the auxiliary reservoir and configured to drain according to a contamination state of the concentrated water a timer for setting a time of the maximum pollution value of the concentrated water circulated in the auxiliary reservoir and opening the secondary drain valve when the time expires detect the contamination concentration from the water quality sensor close the solenoid valve open the primary drain valve pump the membrane water when the auxiliary reservoir is full and secondary when the timer expires"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_273", "text": "therefore if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the contamination is further increased by the material decomposition and material binding action so that the water stored in the reservoir is always kept at the full water level and water flowing from the upstream through the lower part of the sluice gate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309643-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the bad smell source sucked by operating the blower 2 in the operation panel 15 is inside the first carrier storage chamber 5 1 via the vacancy 4 1 in order to facilitate the flow of air through the inlet 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101184099-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "drinking water dispenser adopting soft drink container is less likely to contaminate the drink in the drink container but the water inside the feeder tank is supplied with external air due to the fluctuation of the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "in addition in the present embodiment since the sensing unit 58 that detects the water level of the sewage is installed outside the tank 30 the sensing unit 58 may be prevented from malfunctioning due to severe contamination of the sensing unit 58"}, {"pat_id": "US-10377649-B2", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "the fermentation tank is preferably washed between different batches of microbial growth to remove attached growth at the waterline which may cause build up of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101702294-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case the groundwater well having a multi stage inflow hole on the circumference surface so as to correspond to the water level of the groundwater the basket is placed on the floor for the management so that the deposit of the pollutant and the soil sludge is made in the basket a portion of the groundwater discharged from the pump is supplied through the purifier to prevent contamination due to the groundwater contamination in the underground water congestion zone between the bottoms"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7709393-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in the present invention the water level gauge 300 is preferably a non contact type and more preferably an ultrasonic type from the viewpoint of the risk of false detection due to contamination of the sensor unit"}]</data>
</edge>
