  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drainage tank that has a function to prevent the inflow of pests etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706118-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "due to this replenishment when the water level in the brine reservoir 5 reaches the upper limit the electric valve 11 is automatically closed to block the supply of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "thus it is composed of one set including a control panel that moves the sewage in the sewage tank along the sewage discharge path and discharges it through the sewage discharge pipe one set of sewage treatment equipment is installed one or more depending on the installation area the air supply path includes an air supply pipe installed between the air storage tank and the first end of the three way valve and an air inlet pipe installed between the second end of the three way valve and the sewage tank the control panel operates the compressor to supply the air in the air storage tank to the sewage tank through the air supply pipe the first and second ends of the three way valve and the air inlet pipe a regulator set is installed in the air supply pipe the regulator set includes a regulator for discharging air from the air storage tank to a preset pressure it further comprises at least one of a filter for removing moisture and impurities contained in the air from the air storage tank and an oil removal unit for removing oil contained in the air from the air storage tank the sewage auxiliary tank is installed in the sewage inflow path to remove the bubbles inside the sewage auxiliary tank to prevent the operation of the sewage treatment device due to the inflow of bubbles into the sewage tank when the control panel receives a notification of reaching the lowest water level from the water level sensor it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete it is counted after the operation of discharging the sewage from the sewage tank is performed and when a preset time elapses it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete when the discharge of sewage in the sewage tank is completed the knife valve installed on the sewage inflow path is controlled to be in an open state to open the sewage inflow path so that the sewage is moved to the sewage tank through the sewage inflow path and the three way valve of the air inlet and outlet installed on the air supply path is controlled so that the second end of the three way valve on the sewage tank side and the third end of the air discharge pipe are in an open state and the first end of the air storage tank side control to be closed to move the air in the sewage tank along the air discharge path and discharge it through the air discharge pipe after receiving the notification of reaching the highest water level and performing the operation of discharging wastewater when the notification of reaching the lowest water level is not notified from the water level sensor even after a predetermined time has elapsed after receiving the notification of the notification of reaching the highest water level a warning message to a preset terminal sewage treatment device characterized in that for transmitting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water level indicating device 40 capable of confirming the water level a connector connected to an end of the ultraviolet lamp 32 so that the ultraviolet lamp 32 the quartz tube 32 that transmits the ultraviolet light of the ultraviolet lamp 32 and at the same time may be replaced with water and the ultraviolet lamp can be easily exchanged an ultraviolet sterilizer 30 composed of 52 a hemispherical housing in which a display portion 11 in which a low water quantity appears by operation of the water level indicating device 30 is located and display windows 12a and l2b are installed to easily identify the operation of the ultraviolet lamp 32 on the side of the display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "moreover the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a water level indicating device 40 which is composed of a water level indicating member 44 having a built in level a connector connected to an end of the ultraviolet lamp 32 so that the ultraviolet lamp 32 the quartz tube 32 that transmits the ultraviolet light of the ultraviolet lamp 32 and at the same time may be replaced with water and the ultraviolet lamp can be easily exchanged an ultraviolet sterilizer 30 composed of 52 a hemispherical housing in which a display portion 11 showing a low amount of water is operated by the operation of the water level indicating device 30 and the display windows 12a and l2b are installed to easily identify the operation of the ultraviolet lamp 32 on the side of the display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 2 when the water level of the water tank is a high water level when the ball tower rises to block the pipe while the pressure in the water pipe increases to detect the increase in the amount of current according to the load rise of the well pump when the first well pump this is a device that measures the rated current amount except the starting current and sets the high water level of the water tank based on this and turns off the well pump according to the weight of the current"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "it is preferable that the upper portion of the soil 113 is filled with sand and gravel 114 to prevent the soil 113 filled in the soil receiving groove 111a from being lost due to the water level fluctuation as well as an optimum natural condition for scattering aquatic insects and fish in the aquatic space 112a can be formed as described later"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584084-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a barn bottom forming a through hole for discharging the manure of the livestock while providing a livestock breeding space a storage tank provided at a lower side of the barn bottom to maintain livestock wastewater by washing water and the manure at a predetermined level and to form a bottom with an inclined surface for smooth discharge of the wastewater a washing water control valve provided on an upstream side of the storage tank to control the washing water supplied to the storage tank from the outside and when the water level in the storage tank by the wash water supplied by the opening of the wash water check valve is a first class water level discharge of the wastewater in storage is started and discharged until it reaches the lowest water level and the supply of the wash water through the wash water check valve at the lowest water level is performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359449-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "that is when the water level is above a certain level the ball tower 30 floats due to the buoyancy of the water to block the water intake pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "to this end a separate water level sensor not shown in the drawing may be provided inside the storage block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261839-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention does not return the high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin so as to reduce the impact of the return of high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin and bioreactor it is economical and eco friendly because it can reduce the amount of injected chemicals and the power is reduced by adopting the slant plate settling tank and the sludge concentration can be automatically adjusted by continuously discharging the sludge and changing the hydraulic pressure difference using the hydraulic pressure difference.figure 1a is a block diagram of a conventional wake water treatment apparatus figure 1b is a flow chart of the prior art flocculation flotation 2 is a block diagram of a semi water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 3 is a cutaway showing the flow of sewage treatment in the inclined plate shaped sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 4 is a block diagram of the sludge automatic discharge line of the inclined plate type sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention 5 6 is a perspective view of the water level control of the sludge automatic discharge device of the inclined plate type sedimentation apparatus of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879208-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a flow and ph regulating tank which regulates the water level of the incoming raw water and adjusts the ph to 5.0 to 7.0 for the optimum condition of the chemical input the characteristics of the inflow water whose ph is adjusted and the water level is stabilized in the flow rate and ph adjusting tank a flocculating tank for adding the mixed mineral to the flocculant and mixing the flocculant with the flocculant to perform chemical treatment while mixing the flocculant a coagulation tank for increasing the floc size of the flocculant produced in the rapid a sedimentation tank and a mixed mineral weighted flocculant recovery and circulation apparatus for continuously reusably separating recovering and circulating the weighted flocculant from the sludge sediment separated from the sedimentation tank and a circulation apparatus for filtering the chemical water treated or precipitated in the sedimentation tank a filtration tank for finally removing the flocs that have not been removed and a filter in the high speed water treatment apparatus using a coagulant adding to mineral mix containing the treated water tank the mixed mineral weighted flocculant recovery and recycling apparatus includes a centrifugal hydrocyclone hereinafter referred to as quot hydrocyclone quot that receives the sludge precipitated in the lower part of the sedimentation tank 1400 and supplies the sludge to the high pressure pump 1410 a centrifugal separator 1500 using a hydrocyclone and a stirring separator 1600 constituting an agitating collecting tank in series after passing through the centrifugal separator the agitator 1600 includes an inlet pipe 1610 through which some mixed minerals and sludge not separated from the centrifugal separator 1500 are introduced and an inlet pipe 1610 formed to receive the inlet pipe therein an inner hole 1620 an agitator 1630 rotatably installed at the center of the inner hole block an outer hopper 1640 surrounding the inner hole block and having a square shape a sludge discharge pipe 1650 installed to discharge the sludge and a mixed mineral discharge pipe 1660 connected to a lower portion of the outer hopper to discharge mixed minerals wherein the mixed mineral is used as a weighted flocculant high speed water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784777-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "the rod 22 is rotated to the discharge side the connecting link 23 is connected to the operating rod 22 acts in the direction to push the auxiliary sluice 40 to the discharge side the auxiliary sluice 40 is applied to this force by blocking the outlet 30 while moving along the guide rail 12 to block the water flowing into the outlet 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101060253-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the intake pipe 3 inserted into the water tank 1 is provided in an inverted u shape to automatically transfer the valley water in the state in which foreign matter is filtered from the filtration tank 10 by the siphon phenomenon to the water tank 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714328-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after deeply dredging the upstream and downstream portions by blocking the above mentioned river the above mentioned river embankment 100 on one side and the other side of the above mentioned river is obliquely prepared the above mentioned concrete 111 is installed on the riverbed and on the sides of the bottom of one side of the bank and the other side of the bank a fish habitat facility 112 is constructed using rocks or bank structures so that amphibians benthic animals or fish can easily inhabit it and then various bank structures 113 are stored inside the above mentioned fish habitat facility 112 so that fish can easily inhabit it a structure comprising an eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is configured as a dam reservoir lake or estuary structure configured to hold water in the upper part of the above concrete 111 a structure in which a bottom water rising passage 7777 is formed by combining a bottom inlet 311 that acts to discharge heavy bottom water between one side and the other side of the front part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae occurrence and a bottom water rising passage 7777 is formed by a structure in which the bottom part is narrow and the upper part is formed by a gradually wider inclined plate 322 a structure in which an air inlet 321 for preventing gravity generation is formed in the upper part of the above mentioned low level water rising passage 7777 to prevent low level water which automatically rises by the action of gravity and siphon action from being discharged in the downstream direction of the river when it reaches a certain water level a structure in which a material friction and material explosion generating unit 889 is combined to generate electricity by separating the light gravity river water and the heavy gravity river water into upper and lower parts through the gravity material friction and material explosion generated between the light gravity river water and the light gravity river water thereby causing the polluted river water with a light specific gravity to float to the upper part while simultaneously automatically separating the clean river water with a heavy specific gravity to the lower part and simultaneously discharging it in the downstream direction of the river through the lower inlet 311 and the bottom water rising passage 7777 a structure in which the lower layer water rising passage 7777 and the upper part power generation water movement passage 211 formed on the rear part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae occurrence are each formed with a plurality of upper discharge ports 151 a structure in which an exhaust emission control valve 163 is combined at one end of the upper exhaust port 151 a structure in which an induction pipe 152 for generating gravitational acceleration caused by the action of gravity is formed at the lower part of the rear portion of the upper discharge port 151 a structure in which a gravity acceleration generating unit 911 is formed in the upper part of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 with a height that is 10 to 1 000 times wider and a volume that is larger than the thickness area and volume ratio of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 a structure in which an air inlet 158 is formed at the upper part of the above mentioned gravity acceleration generating unit 911 a structure in which dual control valves 161 162 are respectively formed in the upper and lower parts of the induction pipe 152 for generating the above mentioned gravitational acceleration effect to control the discharge amount of river water the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae which is connected to an electric power generation unit 331 that generates electricity at the lower end of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 is installed in a river a reservoir a dam a lake or an estuary to hold water and then the double control valve 162 is closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall that is the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in particular the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve it is protected by the outer wall and between the inner wall and the outer wall that is a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "more specifically when the water level of the reservoir rises to a high level due to a failure of the existing water level control valve it is discharged through the overflow water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "referring to the operation and effect of the present invention configured as described above the safety shut off device 10 of the present invention detects that the water level of the reservoir 1 is high by the float float 6 to block the inlet pipe 2 can be installed and used together in the reservoir 1 provided with a water level control valve 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "that is the safety shut off device 10 is obtained so as to prevent the occurrence of various accidents due to the water overflow of the reservoir 1 when the water level control valve 5 which frequently malfunctions is damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also when the water level rises the retractable watershed wall prevents the backwash of the river water to prevent flooding damage and the impoundment collection box having a filter net for filtering the contaminants contained in the sewage and storm seats is installed so that the contaminants do not flow into the wells and an odor chamber connected to the ceiling of the sewage pipe at an upper portion of the open the curtain can be installed to block the malodor generated in the sewer line and to move the sewer line along the moving rail to the left and right sides of the sewer line to conveniently remove and remove the contaminant lifting device connected with the wire have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101704960-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole inserted in the ground to block the odor coming out to the outside 10 having an inlet space 12 through which a manhole cover 1 or a rainwater inlet frame 2 10 the rainwater and the wastewater discharged from the main body 10 10 are discharged while the rainwater and the wastewater flowing into the inflow space 12 of the main body 10 a of the water tank 21 in a state of being integrally fused with the inside of the main body 10 10 and the water level a which is provided with a cleaning means 26 for selectively removing the foreign matter in the lower direction by selectively using either the a blocking portion 23 or the rotation blocking portion 24 20 the main body 10 is inserted into the main body 10 so that the upper portion of the main body 10 is inserted and stacked so that the height of the main body 10 30 having a support base 31 with a mounting groove 32 so that the upper part of another body 10 is inserted and stacked while supporting a pressure externally integrally in the interior of the body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "47 a body 31 having a space 46 is provided an opening closing ball 48 for closing and opening the water supply port 43 by buoyancy is introduced into the space 46 when water flows in or out a shock absorber 49 is provided below the open close ball 48 to provide a shock absorbing action when the open close ball 48 falls an upper lid 42 having a water supply inlet 41 is installed on the upper side of the body 47 wherein a lower cover 50 for closing the space 46 is provided below the body 47 to prevent the opening closing ball 48 and the shock absorber 49 from being separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention relates to an unmanned water supply system for supplying groundwater to a water tank by controlling the motor pump by sensing the pressure in the water tank by sensing the pressure applied to the water supply pipe the water level of the water supply pipe is instantaneously released by supplying air to the water supply pipe when the water level of the water storage tank reaches the low water level detection hole formed in the second branch pipe requiring the water supply replenishment so as to detect the low water level when the water level of the water storage tank reaches a high water level that requires stop of the water supply the water level sensing unit is operated to close the water supply port by the operation of the opening closing ball of the water level sensing unit to block the groundwater flowing into the water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to another embodiment of the present invention an air opening closing unit is provided on the side of the low level sensing hole formed in the second branch of the level sensing device and the same structure as the high level sensing unit is provided.the present invention relates to an unmanned water supply system for watering underground water to a water storage tank by controlling a motor pump for unloading groundwater by sensing the pressure applied to a water supply pipe and reading the water level the water level of the water supply pipe is sensed by instantaneously releasing the pressure of the water supply pipe by supplying air to the water supply pipe and when the water level of the water storage tank reaches the high water level requiring the water supply stop the water supply port is closed the water level sensor in the water tank can be accurately sensed by detecting the pressure change applied to the water supply pipe by providing a simple structure of the water level sensing device for blocking the pressure of the water supply pipe not only can a malfunction be significantly reduced but also a semi permanent number by keeping the present invention relates to unmanned water supply apparatus to contribute to improving reliability.1a and 1b are block diagrams of a conventional unattended water supply device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673081-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it includes a shield plate forming a plate shape and connected to the end of the support rope wound or unwound on the winding shaft a lower end of the shielding plate includes a stopper protruding to have a space toward the deposit receiving container 120 and an insertion hole into which the stopper is inserted is formed on an upper surface of the base to which the lower end of the shielding plate abuts the insertion hole is closed by being covered with a locking block plate which is rotatably fixed around the shaft and the shaft is positioned at the deposit container of the insertion hole and one end of the locking block plate closes the insertion hole and the other end is positioned around the shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100367232-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a water supply flow control system for water purifiers installed in the water supply source and the reservoir is used to control the pressure and flow rate of the water flowing through the raw water supply line a plurality of series connected filter and the water purification discharge line a pressure control valve installed in the raw water supply line to adjust the pressure of the raw water supplied from the water supply source to the filter according to a preset reference supply pressure a water shutoff valve installed in the water purification line so as to close as the water level of the reservoir rises to a predetermined reference level and remain open at a level lower than the reference level a water purifier comprising a raw water shutoff valve installed in the raw water supply line to block the raw water supply line when the pressure in the purified water discharge line is higher than a preset reference discharge pressure and receive a control pressure from the purified water discharge line through a pilot line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100367232-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "it can be stably controlled in accordance with the water purification capability of the product and it can be expected to have an industrially useful effect of minimizing the generation of noise caused by various valve operations and greatly extending the life of the valve parts"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102526149-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "mixed air supply unit having a an exhaust pipe having one end connected to the wastewater storage tank a gas remover connected to the other end of the exhaust pipe to intake and remove gas in the wastewater storage tank and a gas removal unit equipped with a water trap a