nected to the control panel 260 and is controlled to stop operation when the water level is below a predetermined water level the open upper part of the rainwater garden 200 is further provided with a plurality of sealing plates 300 sealing the rainwater to prevent the rainwater from being directly introduced into the rainwater garden 200 when it rains 312 and a grid grid 314 and a pitcher control plate 320 which is seated on the grid 312 and forms a fine pore by blocking the grid grid hole 314 the permeable control plate 320 is a plate like structure in which a first rectangular plate 322 and a second rectangular plate 324 are laminated in a multilayer structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101577663-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the step of manufacturing the inner tube is manufactured by fusing two half inner tubes having a half shape to each other.as described above according to the present invention in order to prevent the water level inserted into the water level measuring pipe in the groundwater level measurement from being adhered to the inner circumferential surface of the water level measuring pipe an adhesion preventing portion is formed on the inner circumferential surface of the water level measuring pipe when the water level is lowered by inserting the water level into the measuring pipe or when the water level is recovered by raising the water level after the water level measurement the water level can not be stuck to the wa