having an overflow pipe 111 protruding upward and communicating with a constant height from the top of the drainage connection part 120 at the center of the bottom of the main body 110 in a hollow cylindrical shape a sealing cap 200 that wraps around the upper part of the overflow pipe 111 of the drain trap sleeve 100 and is assembled so that the lower part is a certain distance upward from the bottom of the drain trap sleeve 100 and maintains the sealing cap at a certain water level from the bottom of the drain trap sleeve 100 to block foul odors rising from the drain connection 120 a base panel 300 installed on the upper part of a drain trap sleeve 100 but embedded in an interlayer slab s forming an indoor floor and having an inwardly facing step 310 protruding upward at a certain distance from the bottom so that water gathers in the center and is guided downward an upper filter net 400 installed to cover the upper part of the base panel 300 and filtering out foreign substances including hair and the upper outer periphery is installed on the assembly step 310 on the lower inner side of the base panel 300 and includes an inner filter 500 that filters out foreign substances including hair passing through the upper filter 400 while guiding water to drain downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102859794-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "1 a drain trap according to the prior art includes a drain trap sleeve 1 that is buried in an indoor floor and has an overflow pipe 1a that protrudes upward in the center of the floor a base panel 10 that is buried in an indoor floor and is positioned in the upper center of the drain trap sleeve 1 and has a joint formed in the center of a space that is recessed to collect water a sealing cap 20 that is installed to cover the upper part of the overflow pipe 1a of the drain trap sleeve 1 to block an unpleasant odor that rises through the overflow pipe 1a of the drain trap sleeve 1 while maintaining a water level at a certain level from the inner bottom of the drain trap sleeve 1 an upper strainer 30 that is formed to cover the upper part of the base panel 10 and filter out foreign substances and the upper part is installed in the joint of the base panel 10 and is composed of an inner filter 40 that filters out foreign substances such as hair from water passing through the upper filter 30 while guiding downward water to drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102859794-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "that is a drain trap having a sealing cap structure according to the present invention is a drain trap having a sealing cap structure that is embedded in an inter floor slab to form a drain trap the drain trap sleeve being embedded in an inter floor slab forming an indoor floor of a building and having a drain connection portion protruding downwardly and communicatingly with a constant diameter at the center of the bottom of the main body and an overflow pipe protruding upwardly and communicatingly from the top of the drain connection portion in a hollow cylindrical shape at a constant height at the center of the bottom of the main body a sealing cap that wraps around the upper part of the overflow pipe of the drain trap sleeve and is assembled so that the lower part is spaced upwardly at a constant distance from the bottom of the drain trap sleeve and maintains a sealing cap at a constant water level from the bottom of the drain trap sleeve in order to block an unpleasant odor rising from the drain connection portion a base panel is installed on the upper part of a drain trap sleeve and is embedded in an inter floor slab forming an indoor floor and has an inwardly facing step formed by protruding upward at a certain distance from the bottom so that water gathers in the center and is guided downward an upper filter net is installed to cover the upper part of the base panel and filters out foreign substances including hair and an inner filter net has an upper outer periphery that is installed on the inner side of the lower part of the base panel and filters out foreign substances including hair passing through the upper filter net while guiding water to drain downward"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of hardware configurations of a sensor device 210 and a monitoring device 200 fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of a functional block configuration of a water leakage detection system 20 according to an embodiment fig.it is a figure which shows the concept of a static water pressure a dynamic water pressure a static water level and a dynamic water level.it is a figure which shows an example of the dynamic water level before and after water leakage occurrence and its normal vector.it is a figure which shows an example of the variation change_quantity of the normal vector before and behind water leakage occurrence.it is a figure which shows an example of the block of the piping network used for simulation.8 is a diagram showing an example of the amount of change in the normal vector on the dynamic water level distribution when water leakage occurs in the pipe network 800"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "for example the monitoring device 200 uses the measurement data of the sensor devices 210 distributed in the a block to calculate the dynamic water level at each location in the a block"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "in one aspect the water leakage detection system 20 uses the measurement data obtained from the sensor device 210 installed at each branch point on the pipe network or part of the pipe to calculate the dynamic water level at each monitoring location a dynamic water level distribution can be created from the calculated dynamic water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the above mentioned patent of the prior art the opening and closing plate is provided as a buoyancy body to increase the internal water level by the inf