ation system of the pump according to the present invention the main control unit receives the real time water level value from the sensor unit calculates the speed at which the water level increases or the water level decreases through the water level value received in real time the power consumption due to the driving of the discharge pump can be minimized.1 is a schematic diagram showing an emergency operation system of a pump according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101630268-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for estimating whether or not a water supply pipe is disconnected between blocks using an information processing apparatus including a database unit for providing information on a block and a water pipe and a control unit for processing the information the first hydraulic pressure measuring part provided on the target block and the second hydraulic pressure measuring part provided on the adjacent block are set to a unit time ttot and the control unit sets the water pressure measured by the first water pressure measurement unit at the first head and the water pressure measured by the second water pressure measuring unit is converted into a second head lt rti and wherein the control unit is configured to set a water level at a drainage peak of the target block and the peak level of the reservoir of the adjacent block and if they do not coincide with each other proceeding to the first processing step and if they are coincident with each other proceeding to the second processing step the first process may include a first data collecting step of collecting a plurality of first data r1 t generated at different time points t according to whether or not the formula 1 is satisfied and when the ratio p1 of the number of first data generated by satisfying the following formula 1 to the total number of the first data is equal to or larger than a predetermined first specific ratio pa and a first result output step of estimating and outputting an inter block disconnection when the second specific ratio is less than a first specific ratio pa and less than a second predetermined ratio pb the second process may include the first head unit time per change which is the absolute value of the first head variation value at each time point t and calculates the second head unit time per change which is the absolute value of the second head variation value at each time point t after the head variation value calculation step the first head variation value rti id 0.0 of the first average head variation value and calculates the second head variation value ttot during the entire measurement time ttot of the second average head variation value calculating an average head variation value the method of claim 1 further comprising determining whether at least one first specific time point t1 satisfying the following equations 2 and 3 exists during the total measurement time ttot t2 satisfying all of the following equations 4 and 5 if at least one of the first specific time t1 and the second specific time t2 does not exist after the specific time calculating step the total time ttot is reset by adding the additional time tp t1 and the second specific time point t2 are all present in the first and second time points t1 t2 the average head variation value calculating step determining an observation interval to by summing all the intervals during a predetermined time ta and at a specific time t1 and after the second specific time t2 after the observation interval determination step a plurality of second data r2 t generated by varying a result value according to whether or not the following equation 6 is satisfied for each time point t within the observation interval to is collected a second data collecting step of collecting data and and when the ratio p2 of the number of second data generated by satisfying the following formula 6 with respect to the total number of the second data is equal to or greater than a predetermined third specific ratio pc and a second result outputting step of estimating and outputting an inter block disconnection when the third specific ratio pc is less than a predetermined fourth specific ratio pd"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101630268-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the peak level of the reservoir block of the target block and the peak level of the reservoir of the adjacent block may be different from each other or may be the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "is protruded is provided so as to be spaced apart from the bottom of the road side catch port 10 the horizontal catch plate 94 is adjusted to the height according to the water level flowing through the road side catch port 10 by the buoyancy body 92 and the coarse coarse collusion through lower rainwater downflow horizontal collecting plate 94 it is characterized in that it is provided to be filtered through the water filtration network 96 .according to the above configuration and operation the present invention is to embed the storage tank in the bottom of the flower bed formed between the road and the sidewalk to quickly absorb and collect rainwater flowing along the road during rainy weather and to supply the rainwater stored in the storage tank to the lower flower bed it helps to drown landscaping water and in particular contaminants contained in rainwater can be easily filtered and recycled into water resources including road cooling water road washing water and digestive water to contribute to water shortage.1 is a block diagram showing the stormwater storage system as a whole for vegetation infiltration according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425676-Y1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "when the water level in the water tank 40 reaches a predetermined height the float 56 serves to block the water inlet pipe 50 while rising upward according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200364573-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "more sp