d for replacing a water gate using a shutoff device for water gate maintenance of a water intake tower for replacing a water gate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468890-Y1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "and the present invention is the water w in the steam tank 10 is changed to the steam s as the water w level is gradually lowered as the water is discharged lower than the installation position of the overheat sensor 34 w when the water level is lowered and the water w is almost exhausted heat energy is continuously generated from the electric heater 20 and thus the steam s in the steam tank 10 becomes overheated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804115-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of side panels connected in series to form side surfaces of the water tank a top panel connected to a side surface of the water tank and connected in series so as to form an upper surface of the water tank a bottom panel connected to a bottom of the water tank so as to close the bottom of the side panel and and a reinforcing portion that maintains a gap between the side panels facing each other so as to prevent deformation of the water tank and a gap between the top panel and the bottom panel which are arranged to face each other the joint portion formed between the plurality of bottom panels is formed to protrude to the outside of the water tank further comprising a freezing prevention unit for preventing freezing of water to be dewatered in the water tank and providing thermal energy to the water surface of the fresh water to enable freezing of water frozen from the water surface to be more effectively prevented the above a control box installed on the upper panel a guide rod inserted into the water tank from the control box a moving block slidably installed in the vertical direction along the guide bar and having a support extending laterally a heater installed in the support for suppressing freezing by providing thermal energy to water and a buoyant body mounted on the support for lifting the support block and the moving block along the water level and flowing along the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100191863-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore the present invention has been made to solve the above problems the raw water is filtered through a multi stage pre treatment filter membrane filter post treatment filter to store the water in the storage tank and to circulate the drained concentrated water refiltered a reverse osmosis water purification device comprising a water quality sensor installed at a front end of a pretreatment filter to detect a pollution concentration of raw water and to block inflow of raw water according to a contamination state of concentrated water a first drain valve branched between the water quality sensor and the pretreatment filter and configured to drain according to the pollution concentration of the raw water a solenoid valve disposed between the primary drain valve and the pretreatment filter and configured to open close the water channel by an electric operation according to the pollution concentration and the water level of the auxiliary reservoir tank and the reservoir tank an auxiliary reservoir installed between the all carbon filter and the membrane filter to pump water from the all carbon filter to the membrane filter and to receive the drained water of the membrane filter a secondary drain valve connected to a lower portion of the auxiliary reservoir and configured to drain according to a contamination state of the concentrated water a timer for setting a time of the maximum pollution value of the concentrated water circulated in the auxiliary reservoir and opening the secondary drain valve when the time expires detect the contamination concentration from the water quality sensor close the solenoid valve open the primary drain valve pump the membrane water when the auxiliary reservoir is full and secondary when the timer expires"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100191863-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "therefore when the water level of the auxiliary reservoir 60 is detected by the water level sensor 61 the controller 80 turns on the boosting pump 64 and the water supply valve 66 and turns off the solenoid valve 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100397886-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the installation screen is automatically lifted according to the water level 30 to block the impurities such as garbage flowing along the water and the rake 10 of the upper side while elevating by the driving force of the chain inside the rail 20 arc type by angular movement to handle the waste caught in the floating screen 30 in particular the rake 10 is vertically lowered from the upper side of the inside of the rail 20 in the state fixed to the shaft 11 floating screen 30 after going down the water along the rails 20 and angularly moving in an arc shape without receiving the interference of garbage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100923508-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "on the other hand in order to solve this problem as shown in figure 2 in the interior of the water intake tower 6 is formed of reinforced concrete the screen 8 to block the inflow of dirt and the main pipe 7 although a fixed water intake device having a plurality of water intake ports 9 and opening and closing sides 10 in the middle part and the lower layer is disclosed there is a problem in that the intake of surface water due to the change of the water level is difficult.the present invention has been made to solve the above problems it is an object of the present invention to provide a multi functional water intake device that allows the separate or simultaneous withdrawal of the surface water middle water and deep water with one facility.in order to achieve the above object the present invention has a multifunctional water intake device a cylinder formed in multiple stages a winch for lifting the cylinder a packing for sealing between the cylinders a stopper for controlling the working distance of each cylinder and water storage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218082-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand the continuous flow type escal water treatment device 10 according to the present embodiment is to consume the relatively low energy while stably introducing the inflow water into the reaction tank 2 within a predetermined flow rate when the flow rate adjustment tank is exceeded in order to flow into the 1 to install the water level restriction block 26 so that the buoyancy unit 40 has a buoyancy body 42 and the gate 24"}, {"pat_id": "US-8034236-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in this storm water filter box a pair of baffles 36 are mounted along the bottom for capturing sand gravel or non floatable trash but it should be clear that these baffles may or may not be included within the filter box 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the sewage discharge odor blocking device of the present invention for achieving the above object is normally blocked at the distal end of the sewage pipe to block the discharge of odor and discharge of odors and when rain rains in large quantities when the rain flows to open the sewage to guide the river a discharge opening odor blocking device comprising a box frame installed at an upper end discharge port of a sewer pipe at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber and seated at an outer circumference of an open sewage discharge port a primary blocking door connected to the upper end of the box frame to block odors by closing the sewage discharge outlets in usual times a second blocking door connected to the first blocking door to block the odor by blocking the sewage discharge outlet it is characterized by consisting of a hinge connecting portion to be connected to the upper side of the secondary barrier door to be separated from each other in order to open and close the plurality of blocking doors in order to correspond to the water level in accordance with the water level and water pressure of the rain flowing in large quantities in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in addition the sewage treatment apparatus for the winder according to the present invention has the advantage that can be prevented from malfunctioning the water level detecting unit by the sewage because the water level detecting unit is installed outside the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "referring to figures 1 to 5 the network structure 200 as a function to block the floating material g floating on the river while moving up and down along the water level of the dimension control structure 100 in the present embodiment is composed of a support frame 210 the strainer 220 and the buoyancy body 230 is installed so as to be elevated in the blown beam 110 through the buoyancy body 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200397612-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water flow plate that guides the water supplied from the upper side to the bottom to form a water curtain film a lower water tank whose water level is maintained at a predetermined interval on the bottom of the water flow plate and the lower water tank the coating booth which sprays a liquid and performs a painting work the exhaust apparatus which is provided along one side of the said painting booth and the lower end is formed so that it may communicate with the inside of a painting booth and the airflow formed and exhausted in the said communication site may collide a curved vortex plate that forms a vortex by guiding it to change direction a plurality of impingement plates provided to guide the exhaust flow in a zigzag manner to the exhaust device and an exhaust fan that sucks air in the painting booth and discharges it to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the above mentioned prior art patents the open close plate is provided as a buoyant body and when the internal water level is raised by the inflow of sewage the open close plate is rotated to block the manhole entrance to prevent the backwashing of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "and a tubular body 50 formed on the upper end of the inner circumferential surface to form a stopper 51 by being inclined downward inwardly from the inner circumferential surface side end so that a certain width protrudes inward on the same horizontal line a shaft guide 60 to which the upper ends of the elevating shafts 61 having a predetermined length are connected is formed at the middle of the length of the stopper 51 a backflow preventing plate 70 for blocking an upper and lower space instantaneously as the end portion is brought into close contact with the stopper 51 of the tubular body 50 while rotating at a predetermined angle according to the water level flowing into the manhole body 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5235641-B2", "para_id": "para_118", "text": "it is a schematic diagram which shows the mode of the operation work using a wireless tag with respect to the water detection in a manhole by embodiment of this invention.it is a block diagram which shows the structure of the radio wireless tag improved for water detection by this embodiment.it is a block diagram for demonstrating the determination circuit in the radio wireless tag of this embodiment.it is a conceptual diagram for demonstrating the installation form of the wireless tag 21 mentioned above by 1st embodiment of this invention.it is a conceptual diagram for demonstrating the installation form of the wireless tag 21 mentioned above by 2nd embodiment of this invention.in 2nd embodiment of this invention it is a flowchart for demonstrating operation movement at the time of using two types of radio wireless tags 21v and 21w.it is explanatory drawing for demonstrating the relationship between the wireless tag which responds to the water immersion in the manhole in 2nd embodiment of this invention.it is explanatory drawing which shows the structure of the wireless tag 21 and the installation form to a manhole by 3rd embodiment of this invention.it is explanatory drawing for demonstrating the relationship between the wireless tag which responds to the water immersion in the manhole in 3rd embodiment of this invention.it is explanatory drawing for demonstrating the structure of the water level monitoring system using the wireless tag 21 by 4th embodiment of this invention.it is explanatory drawing which shows the relationship between the wireless tag which responds with the water immersion in a manhole by 4th embodiment of this invention.it is a flowchart for demonstrating operation movement at the time of using three radio wireless tags 21d 21m and 21u by 4th embodiment of this invention.it is explanatory drawing for demonstrating the structure of the water level monitoring system using the radio wireless tag 21 which multihops by 5th embodiment of this invention.it is a block diagram which shows the structure of the radio wireless tag with a multihop by 5th embodiment of this invention.it is a flowchart for demonstrating the operation movement at the time of using the radio wireless tags 21d 21m and 21u with three multihops by 5th embodiment of this invention.it is a flowchart for demonstrating the operation movement at the time of using the radio wireless tags 21d 21m and 21u with three multihops by 5th embodiment of this invention.it is a flowchart for demonstrating the operation movement of the multihop transmission by the radio wireless tags 21m and 21u by 5th embodiment of this invention.it is explanatory drawing which shows the labeled pipe opening formation member currently disclosed by patent document 1 as a prior art.it is explanatory drawing which shows the intelligent manhole system currently disclosed by the nonpatent literature 1 as a prior art"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101127289-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "when the water level control valve 140 is open the water in the reservoir 150 is moved to the sterilization tank 160 to increase the level of the sterilization tank 160 and the water level is increased to detect the water level sensor 170"}]</data>
</edge>
