  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which the power generation water movement line 331 is installed in a form that goes over mountains and hills 221 and then an upward discharge line 332 is formed in a shape at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the lower height and horizontal state of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by going over mountains and hills due to the action of gravity a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which the lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 after constructing the above power generation water transfer line 331 by crossing mountains and hills 221 a structure in which a v shaped rising discharge line 332 is formed at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the horizontal state and the bottom height of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by gravity over mountains and hills a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which a lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as a result the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank and also if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at this time the middle layer water and the lower layer water is lower than the temperature of the surface water due to the difference in density to cool the water stored in the intake tower to form a low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100656932-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "this multi branch piping has no problem in general water supply but if there are sub pipes 30 and 40 requiring fresh water to control the water level the sub pipes 30 and 30 may be opened due to the continuous opening and closing of the main pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100656932-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "third by connecting the sub pipe to the device for controlling the water level by desalination of water it is possible to prevent the micro leakage of the device to control the water level by desalting water by the check valve to maintain a constant water level at all times there is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102308038-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it passes through the side wall member 61 and extends to the outside and is connected to a sludge pump and is sealed to prevent leakage between the through part 62 and the sludge discharge pipe 23 passing therethrough a fresh water discharge pipe 45 is connected to the fresh water discharge hole 43 the fresh water discharge pipe 45 extends from the inside of the water tank 20 in the radial direction through the inclined wall 21 of the water tank 20 to the fresh water tank 60"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore a septic tank abnormality alarm device is indispensable"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "abnormalities in the septic tank include for example aeration stop due to blower failure aeration failure due to clogging of the diffuser blower overload aeration failure due to air pipe breakage sewage underground penetration due to water leakage discharge piping and discharge destination abnormalities such as water level rise and water level rise due to abnormal discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100323046-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "while installing the chemical input pipe 4a 4b 4c has a plurality of inlet 6a in the upper end and the venturi tube venturi tube 6 formed with a through hole 6b on both sides of the lower end the venturi tube 6 sealing between the input pipes 5a 95b 5c and the venturi pipe 6 through the rubber ring 23 on the upper and lower outer surfaces to prevent leakage of chemicals the venturi pipe 6 the valve 13 is located on the lower inner inclined surface and the lock nut 15 and the vertical float 24 are coupled to the lower end of the valve shaft 14 to finely adjust to correspond to the water level of the chemical 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502305-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to operate a warning alarm when the unwanted water due to the closing of the main water supply valve and to enter the inspection state to prevent damage due to leakage of the product and the space in which the product is installed in the case of the ion water purifier with the reservoir the alarm sounds together with the alarm and at the same time the water level of the reservoir is automatically forced by the automatic drain valve and in the case of the reservoir type the alarm and the warning sound operate quickly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502305-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition the present invention operates a warning alarm at the time of undesired intake due to poor closing of the main water supply valve and enters the inspection state to prevent damage due to water leakage in the product and the space where the product is installed due to water overflow in case of the attached ion water purifier the alarm sounds with alarm and the water level of the reservoir is automatically forced by the automatic drain valve at the same time as the alarm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330869-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore since the electrode 2 and the main body 1 are separated separately installation is inconvenient which may cause malfunctions due to immersion such as moisture.the present invention is to solve the conventional drawbacks as described above the main body and the electrode for the sensor composed of the same body and waterproof construction to solve the conventional drawbacks and to prevent malfunction due to leakage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101729735-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "due to the coupling structure of the watertight packer 325 the water level is raised through the tubular packer 320 and the leakage of the sewage can be completely blocked"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the pressure pump in operation is controlled to stop due to a drop in the primary pressure in the water pipe connecting the pressure pump and the primary side reservoir and the water level in the secondary side is below the specified water level"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0022 reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 0850307 registration date july 29 2008 sewer pipe maintenance monitoring system remotely monitors the inside of the sewer pipe by image and monitors the sewage flow rate data measured by the flow meter sensor in conjunction with the image it relates to a sewage pipe maintenance monitoring system capable of remotely monitoring and managing sewage pipes based on accurate information by supplementing errors in flow data and a flowmeter sensor installed in a sewer pipe to measure the flow rate and water level of sewage an underwater camera installed inside the manhole to take an image of the inside of the sewer pipe an on site control panel that receives the flow rate and water level of the flow meter sensor and the captured image of the underwater camera calculates the flow rate and processes the captured image according to the transmission format sewage related data and image data are collected from the field control panel through a communication network and flow velocity water level and flow data fluctuations are analyzed to determine whether ingress water inflow water leakage occurs and image data is output to the screen to analyze data and video data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition the present invention is provided with a pressure automatic replenishment device to replenish the pressure but it is only possible to replenish a small amount of pressure for a limited time only when the water supply is provided through the pumping pipe to completely fill the leaked pressure completely it is not possible to do this but even if it is assumed that the normal positive pumping is very effective.the present invention is to actively solve all the problems in the groundwater supply apparatus of the above described prior invention and when the disk interlocking up and down with the mouth according to the change in water level reaches the minimum water level automatically the flow path of the water cylinder by closing the air pressure to prevent leakage to the outside and when the water supply to the water cylinder is started by the water supply pressure acting on the upper side of the disk forcibly moved upwards to open the flow path to smoothly supply water to the pressurized water tank it is to be an object of the invention.the present invention is to provide an air pressure leakage blocking device on the lower side of the pressurized water tank as a means for solving the above problems the air pressure leakage blocking device is connected to the water supply pipe to one side of the water chamber the other side of the water chamber a shaft guide holder is installed at the center of the flow path of the water supply cylinder formed on the upper part and a disk shaft is installed at the upper and lower sides of the shaft guide holder respectively and a disk is provided at the cover bracket radially installed on the outer circumferential surface of the water cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "as it is buried underground it prevents freezing in winter by improving heat retention and effectively suppresses bacterial propagation while completely blocking contact between the inside of the pressurized water tank and the outside air thereby increasing the utility of drinking water.1 is a longitudinal sectional view of an embodiment of a water supply device to which the present invention is applied figure 2 is a longitudinal sectional view showing the internal structure of the air pressure leakage preventing device of the present invention 3 is a cross sectional view taken along the line aa of the present invention figure 2 figure 4 is a partially cut away perspective view of the present invention air pressure leakage preventing device figure 5 is an enlarged cross sectional view of the disk of the present invention to block the flow path at the minimum water level 6 is an enlarged cross sectional view of a disk of the present invention in a state in which a flow path is opened figure 7 is another embodiment longitudinal section of the present invention water supply device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "and the air pressure present in the air layer of 