el pattern it is determined that water leakage has occurred due to a break in the water pipeline and the actual water level exceeds the water level upper limit allowable pattern or the water level lower limit allowable pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0005 means for solving the problems in order to solve the above mentioned problems plant information is time series informationized filed as a plant information actual value in a plant information actual value file and a water level plan prediction on the day of water leakage monitoring based on the filed information actual value a predicted water level pattern plan processing unit that creates a pattern and creates a water leakage occurrence water level pattern a water level upper limit value allowable pattern and a water level lower limit value allowable pattern based on the water level plan predicted pattern and these patterns compares the predicted water level pattern memory that stores the actual water level on the day of leakage monitoring and the water level pattern on which leakage occurred and compares the actual water level on the leakage monitoring day with the water level upper limit allowable pattern or water level lower limit allowable pattern and a water leakage monitoring calculation processing unit for processing when the actual water level exceeds the leak generation water level pattern water pipes determined by the fracture and leakage occurs when the actual water level exceeds level upper limit allowable pattern or level lower limit allowable pattern it is determined that the abnormal operation of the apparatus to which equipment to a water conduit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here with regard to information on the equipment installed in the water pipeline that causes disturbance in water leakage monitoring information related to the water level plan prediction pattern of the equipment installed in the water pipeline is stored in the prediction water level pattern memory and the prediction the information in the water level pattern memory and the information in the plant information actual value file are compared and if there is a difference in the state of the equipment installed in the water pipeline the water level plan prediction pattern is corrected"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition when activated at a cycle of 1 minute information in the predicted water level pattern memory 11 and the plant information actual value file 14 regarding information such as the operating state of the pump and the open closed state of the inflow valve that become disturbances in water leakage monitoring the inside information is compared and if a difference occurs in the state the water level plan prediction pattern in the predicted water level pattern memory 11 is corrected"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "test whether or not there is a difference between the actual water level of the reservoir b28 at the current time and if there is a difference and the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence level pattern it is determined that there is water leakage and the water leakage print water leak occurrence information is issued to the output processing unit 8 and the alarm output processing unit 9"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 when the actual water level d on the leakage monitoring day of the distribution reservoir b28 has changed to the current time the leakage monitoring calculation processing unit 12 compares the actual water level d with the leakage occurrence water level pattern e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to the smart type water tank having the earthquake proof function according to the present invention the water tank is managed through the pollution level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 and the water leakage sensor 33 thereby enabling clean and safe water quality management control and monitoring of the opening closing state of the valve 40 and the water drainage amount by monitoring the sudden change of the water level and the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the control unit 50 determines the state of the raw water by comparing the measured values of the sensors sensed above with predetermined reference values controls the valve 40 according to the determination result and transmits the state of the raw water to the manager it is a means to provide a process for that is the controller 50 is electrically connected to the pollution level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 the vibration sensor 32 and the water leakage sensor 33 to receive measured values from the sensors the water level of the raw water in the water tank the leakage of the raw water from the water tank and the vibration transmitted to the tank main body 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the cleaning means 140 may be formed on the bottom of the floating filter media 130 and a plurality of injection nozzles 144 formed on the washing inflow line 141 and the washing inflow line 141 into which the air or the washing water is introduced and the floating filter material is occluded through the water level sensor 160 rising water level due to leakage is not smooth and the automatic backwashing is carried out by automatically activating the washing means"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of hardware configurations of a sensor device 210 and a monitoring device 200 fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of a functional block configuration of a water leakage detection system 20 according to an embodiment fig.it is a figure which shows the concept of a static water pressure a dynamic water pressure a static water level and a dynamic water level.it is a figure which shows an example of the dynamic water level before and after water leakage occurrence and its normal vector.it is a figure which shows an example of the variation change_quantity of the normal vector before and behind water leakage occurrence.it is a figure which shows an example of the block of the piping network used for simulation.8 is a diagram showing an example of the amount of change in the normal vector on the dynamic water level distribution when water leakage occurs in the pipe network 800"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "6 is a diagram showing an example of the dynamic water level and its normal vector before and after the occurrence of water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "in one aspect the water leakage detection system 20 uses the measurement data obtained from the sensor device 210 installed at each branch point on the pipe network or part of the pipe to calculate the dynamic water level at each monitoring location a dynamic water level distribution can be created from the calculated dynamic water level"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "in step s1520 the water leakage detection system 20 calculates the time series dynamic water level at each monitoring location installation location of each sensor device 210"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_130", "text": "20 water leakage detection system 50 distribution reservoir 100a 100b 510 800 piping network 101a 101b sensor 110a 110b estimated water leakage area 120 piping 200 monitoring device 210 sensor device 220 communication unit 230 303 pressure sensor 240 access point 250 internet 301 control unit 302 317 communication if 305 318 internal bus 311 processor 312 memory 313 storage 314 external device if 315 input if 316 output if 401 data acquisition unit 402 dynamic water level calculator 403 difference calculator 404 visualization unit 405 abnormality determination unit 406 estimation unit 407 output unit 408 estimation data storage unit 409 judgment data storage unit 500 ground 501 502 503 504 650 810a 810b 810c 810d 810e location 520 water surface 525 hydrodynamic gradient 530 hydrostatic pressure 540 hydrodynamic pressure 550 booster pump 560 hydrostatic level 561 hydrostatic head 562 572 altitude 570 dynamic water level 571 dynamic water head 600a 600b dynamic water level distribution 620a 620b 750 760 normal vector 710 difference 900 910 simulation result 1000 1100 1210 visualization information 1200 1410 1420 1430 screen 1220 map 1310 1320 1330 contour map"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087622-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "in the discharging process a floating decanter moving according to the water level of the batch reactor to prevent sludge leakage while the floating decanter moves upward and downward by buoyancy a roller type decanter moving device capable of preventing inclination or pinching is configured between the buoyant fluid for buoyancy control and the support the decanter moving device is configured to configure the support in a cylindrical shape and the two rollers are disposed to the left and right with the cylinder in between the two rollers and the floating decanter are bound through the support of the roller and the support binding unit is configured in the buoyancy control floating fluid comprising two or more supports to move the floating decanter a lower stopper configured to prevent the floating decanter from moving further under the support the water level meter for measuring the water level of the batch reactor the floating material measuring device moving according to the movement of the floating decanter in order to prevent sludge from flowing out of the sludge interface layer in the lower portion of the batch reactor the suspended solids meter is positioned 200 to 400 mm below the end of the inlet configured in the lower portion of the buoyancy control buoyant fluid but is lowered together with the buoyancy control buoyant fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087622-B1", "para_id": "claim_15", "text": "in the discharging process the plc method control panel receives the signals of the timer the water level meter and the suspended solids meter that can prevent the leakage of sludge as a safety device when the discharge command signal is given to the treatment water extraction pump the treatment water extraction pump is driven water is sucked into the surging tank preventing the loss of suction pressure and accordingly the check valve configured at the suction port is opened and the lower treatment water is drawn in order to prevent the sludge from flowing into the interfacial layer of the lower sludge of the batch reactor the suspended solids meter is positioned to be 200 to 400 mm lower than the end of the inlet configured in the lower part of the buoyancy control buoyant fluid but configured to descend together with the buoyancy control buoyant fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087622-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "in particular in the discharge process a floating decanter decanter comprising a quadruple safety device interlocked with a timer a bottom stopper a water level meter and a suspended solids meter to prevent sludge leakage and a suction water tank to prevent loss of suction pressure"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops for example due to leakage losses the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200329887-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "piping using 12 can be satisfactorily satisfied with the operating conditions.therefore the present invention can prevent sludge loss with rapid treatment water discharge and if necessary the structure of the height of the surface and the discharge port can be adjusted to prevent the leakage of suspended substances such as scum"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676999-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "therefore according to the present invention it is possible to monitor the state of water leakage or foreign matter introduced into the water tank 1 by monitoring the rapid change of the water level and the water quality thereby enabling cleaner and safer water quality management"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4441460-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "2 the method for identifying the location of the water leak in the water channel 20 is that the at least the downstream end 21 of the target area 20 a of the water channel 20 is partitioned by a corner drop 31 as an example of a partition plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "in addition the processor 110 determines that a leak has occurred in the sewage treatment plant tank when the measured water level change is high compared to the measured power consumption and the measured water pressure based on the third correlation and the manager terminal 200 may transmit a warning message for checking and responding to water leakage in the sewage treatment plant water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "receiving tank automatic control system capable of real time monitoring characterized in that consisting of a communication unit 36 for receiving and transmitting to the display unit 32"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "that is the circuit for detecting the conduction between the electrodes due to the water leakage is designed using the circuit for detecting the water level of the water receiving tank conventionally used"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "for this reason there is no fear of corrosion of the electrode due 