y while supplying water regardless of location"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937578-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the lower part of the unit part has a funnel shaped bottom connection part and a coupling part for coupling with a water pipe to prevent deformation or leakage even at high water pressure so that the flow meter and valve facilities from foreign substances such as sand or slime that are contained in the groundwater together it is to prevent the failure of the lamp in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "5 does not form a conduit in the main body because the motor is installed outside and in addition to the water level measurement tube 220 a separate tube is not formed in order to prevent leakage of pressure from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore in the middle of the night when the constant use is low the water level of the water stored in the reservoir rises and the flow rate of the constant water in the water supply pipe decreases there is a problem that the water pressure of the water tank is excessively increased to increase the water leakage rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100874616-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "when commanding water supply leakage occurs by automatically shutting off the external solenoid valve when the input signal is not supplied from the high water level sensor due to breakdown or internal leakage even though the water supply time set according to the water supply time normally obtained is exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101917676-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drug reservoir 100 a pumping unit 200 for supplying the medicine from the medicine reservoir 100 a drug dispensing tank 320 having a chemical inlet pipe 320 at an upper portion of a front side of the housing 310 and a medicine discharge pipe 330 at a rear lower side of the housing 310 to uniformly distribute medicines supplied from the pumping unit 200 300 comprising a leakage detection switch 370 is provided to detect chemicals leaked to the barrier wall 400 while forming a barrier wall 400 to collect chemicals leaking into a proper space on the floor where the medicine dispensing tank 300 is located and a medicine insertion visual identification unit 340 provided at a lower portion of the housing 310 in which the distal end of the medicine inlet pipe 320 is located so as to identify the inflow situation of the medicine with the naked eye the chemical injection detecting means 350 disposed directly below the water ejector 312 formed at the upper end of the front surface of each distribution chamber 311 formed at the rear portion of the housing 310 when the float switch 353 is vertically provided in the auxiliary water tank 352 provided in the support body 351 and the float 353a descends below the appropriate water level wherein the control unit is configured to notify that the inflow is stopped and to monitor the infusion of the medicine in the water supply chemical supply system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101296571-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3 the stopper is a water level sensor comprising a leak prevention packing to prevent leakage by contacting the water purification tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101296571-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "as such when it is seated and fixed to the protrusion 520 of the binding device 500 the water purification tank 31 the leakage preventing packing 460 and the binding device 500 are brought into contact with each other thereby allowing the water level sensor 40 to be in contact with each other"}, {"pat_id": "US-9290923-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment the drive 46 is responsive to changes in water level in the storage chamber 16 to move the valving member 44 between opened and closed positions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100689108-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "receiving tank automatic control system capable of real time monitoring characterized in that consisting of a communication unit 36 for receiving and transmitting to the display unit 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102744945-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "9 shows a case where activated carbon parts 166 are installed at two intervals which means that a space 167 is formed between the upper and lower activated carbon parts 166 so that the odorous substances move slowly in the upper and lower activated carbon parts 166 and are adsorbed on the activated carbon and move quickly in the space 167 without resistance thereby shortening the time for removing the odor.100 manhole pump station 110 manhole pump station body 111 upper space 112 lower space 113 manhole 114 exhaust pipe 115 foothold 116 doorway 117 opening door 118 railing 119 ladder 120 inlet pipe unit 121 inlet pipe 122 inlet pipe 123 curved pipe 124 diffusion guide plate 130 pump 131 discharge pipe 140 opening closing opening 141 hinge pin 142 rotating cover 143 handle 144 cover holder 150 odor exhaust device 151 lower exhaust pipe 152 exhaust fan 153 exhaust hood 154 upper exhaust pipe 155 flexible corrugated pipe 156 corrugated pipe holder 157 detachable member 160 secondary odor remover 161 door 162 casing 163 support guide 164 wire mesh box 165 activated carbon 166 activated carbon part 170 fermentation liquid part 171 inlet 172 fermentation tank 172a fermentation tank body 173 hollow section 174 ring shaped space 175 fermentation liquid storage section 176 upward protrusion 177 leakage 178 absorbing tube 179 downward protrusion pipe 180 em fermentation solution 181 water level sensor 182 body support 183 bottom 184 protruding edge wall 190 primary odor remover 191 fermentation tank 192 drain pipe 193 opening closing valve 194 dispersing drop plate 195 bubble generator 196 air hose 197 air pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0641138-Y2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "next when running water is generated in the pipe 2 due to a leakage accident or the like it rises above the overflow water level 10 in the water reservoir 8"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5450286-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "then immediately after the drive of the water pump 30 is stopped the control unit 15 calculates the flow path loss \u03b4f and the water leakage coefficient k s309"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "when the water level becomes abnormal drops the water level drops from the normal level due to factors such as water leakage caused by damage to the contact aeration tank 12 damage to the disinfection tank 16 or a short circuit caused by gaps in the discharge pipe joints and the float 1 no longer tilts"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the remote terminal device can determine and monitor the leakage of hazardous chemicals or the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3017891-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "next the circulating pump 4 is driven to apply pump pressure to the return pipe 9 via the hot water feed pipe 8 and the branch pipe 14 and at the same time time measurement is started by the water level change time measurement circuit 16 and this time is measured"}, {"pat_id": "US-9950935-B2", "para_id": "para_151", "text": "the power off operation if quickly performed upon a significant rise of the water level may effectively prevent electrical leakage to peripheral devices even if water flows out of the water tank 31"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100836904-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it consists of a drive 22 for driving the unit 23 the display unit 23 is a filter loss amount display unit 24 for displaying the loss of each filter 5 stored by the wired terminal 70 connected from the outside in percentage and when the filter 5 is replaced filter replacement display section 25 in which the lamp is selectively flashed when the lamp is reached the water level level display section 26 in which the lamp is selectively lit according to the water level level of the water tank 6 and the driving of the pump 3 and it consists of a drive display unit 27 the lamp is turned on when the water leakage and a water temperature display unit 28 for displaying cold and hot water the output terminal of the mpu 21 is installed on one side of the facet 8a is connected to the facet lamp 9 for providing a refreshing feeling when the water is discharged the water level sensor 30 is installed in the water tank 6 at the input end of the mpu 21 and senses the water level in four stages and the water leakage sensor is installed on the bottom surface of the case 1 to detect water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200194172-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "with the increase the flange is placed upright and upside down with the conventional upper and lower body upside down flange joining is easier to join"}]</data>
