discharge pipe path 183 but one end is the body part 131 a guide that is rotatably connected to the and the other end is rotatably connected with respect to the discharge pipe line 183 to guide the elevating path of the main body 131 while rotating according to the lifting and lowering movement of the main body 131 according to the water level change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300891-B1", "para_id": "para_107", "text": "and a guide pipe 133 for guiding the elevating path of the main body 131 while rotating according to the lifting and lowering movement of the main body 131 according to the water level change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a batch wastewater treatment system equipped with a floating rectifier a reactor having an inlet for wastewater a treated water outlet and a sludge outlet a stirrer for stirring the wastewater in the above reactor a rectifier plate arranged so as to be able to rise and fall within the above reactor a rectifier plate lifting unit that raises or lowers the rectifier plate a sensor that detects the inflow of wastewater through the inlet and a batch type wastewater treatment system characterized by including a control unit that controls the rectifier lifting unit according to the signal of the sensor thereby raising the rectifier in conjunction with the rise in the water level of the reaction tank when wastewater flows in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "1 to 3 a batch type wastewater treatment system 1 according to one embodiment of the present invention comprises a reaction tank 10 having an inlet for introducing wastewater on one side a treated water discharge outlet on the other side and a sludge discharge outlet on the bottom side an agitator 20 installed to agitate the wastewater in the reaction tank 10 a rectifier 30 formed by a plurality of inclined plates opening in an inclined manner up and down to form a flow path and arranged to be able to rise and fall within the reaction tank 10 a rectifier plate lifting unit 40 including a float 42 connected to the rectifier plate 30 and raising or lowering the rectifier plate 30 by an increase or decrease in buoyancy of the float 42 a sensor 50 for detecting the inflow of wastewater into the reaction tank 10 through the inlet and or the amount of wastewater inflow a timer 60 and a timer 50 for detecting the sensor 50 and the according to the signal of the timer 60 the control unit 90 controls the rectifier lifting unit 40 to raise the rectifier 30 according to the rise in the water level of the reaction tank 10 when wastewater flows into the reaction tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the batch type wastewater treatment system 1 according to the present embodiment is configured such that a sensor 1 capable of measuring the inflow and inflow rate of wastewater is installed in a wastewater inflow line l1 connected to a wastewater inlet of a reaction tank 10 and a rectifier plate lifting unit 40 including an air pump 44 and a float 42 is configured to raise the rectifier plate 30 in conjunction with the inflow of wastewater and the rise in the water level in the reaction tank 10 due to the inflow of wastewater under the control of a control unit 90 so that after the inflow of wastewater and the raising of the rectifier plate stable and even mixing of wastewater is induced during the aeration time and rapid settling of sludge is induced during settling thereby shortening the settling time and ensuring the stability of the treated water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541589-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the anoxic water softening system according to the present invention comprises a river filtration water an underground water filtration water an indirect water intake which is installed at a certain depth of a river bed and is filtered and introduced through an aquifer of the river bed an ion donating part connected to the collecting part for filtering the divalent ionized water through the indirect water withdrawing water which is directly pumped in an oxygen free state which does not contact with oxygen in the collecting part a water supply unit for collecting and supplying the soft water that has passed through the ion water filtration unit and an enriched water treatment unit for collecting and processing the hard water including the divalent ion water that has not permeated through the ion water filtration unit wherein the indirect water intake accommodated in the water collection is disposed inside the air intake and the air intake prevent catalyst while floating on the surface of the water intake indirect include shielding for lifting in accordance with the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the waste water collecting device for drainage to remove a resistance shaft 39 provided on the bottom surface of the water channel 10 a voltage variable element 37 provided at the end of the resistance shaft 39 to output a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 it is provided on the outside of the resistance shaft 39 is raised and lowered according to the water level level is provided with a water level sensor 36 made of a float 38 for changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 the control unit 31 is a waste collection device for drainage characterized in that to adjust the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in proportion to the water level level of the channel 10 detected by the water level sensor 36"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention is a drainage sewage collection device for continuously removing the contaminants introduced into the waterway by a rake installed in a chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller the bottom surface of the waterway a resistance variable provided in the resistor shaft a voltage variable element disposed at an end of the resistance shaft and outputting a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft and installed outside the resistance shaft to increase and decrease according to the level of water thereby changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the present invention is a control method of a waste water collecting device for the drainage to repeatedly remove the contaminants introduced into the waterway by the rake installed in the chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller a current level determination process of reading the water level of the water flowing in the waterway a water level determination process of determining whether the current water level read through the current water level determination process is a set low water level a medium water level a high water level and the water level determination process if the current level of the water channel is judged to be low drive the lifting motor at low speed.if the current level is judged to be medium drive the lifting motor to medium speed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "therefore the output voltage of the voltage variable element 37 that changes according to the water level level introduced into the channel 10 is applied to the control unit 31 which is the control unit 30 of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "by automatically controlling the operating speed of the lifting motor if the inflow of water increases such as during rainy weather the speed of collecting the contaminants can be smoothed thereby smoothing the flow of water into the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "as a preferred embodiment of the present invention the water level adjusting part is seated at the end of the lifting and drained by the pressure of the effluent flowing into the inlet pipe and is supported by the guide to prevent the reverse flow of the effluent by falling the hydrological member the compression spring that is installed in an upright position on the upper part of the hydrological member provides a compression force and the upper end of the compression spring is coupled and a moving ruler that determines the moving distance when the compression spring is pressurized passes through the cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as a preferred embodiment of the present invention the water level adjusting portion is seated at the end of the lifting and turning by drainage by the pressure of the effluent flowing into the inlet pipe and by turning the vice versa to support the slide hinge to prevent the inflow of the effluent it is installed in the up and down state of the shanghai swivel hydrological member the link is installed to be rotated to the upper portion of the hydrological member the guide pipe is connected to the link and pivoted to the link and the support plate of the guide pipe in an upright state compression springs providing compression force and the upper end of the compression spring are combined and a moving ruler that determines the moving distance when pressurizing the compression spring is inserted into the inside of the guide pipe and the pressure member exposed to the outside through the cover and pressurized in order to provide the pressing force to the member a screw shaft which is screwed in is screwed through the cover of the body and freed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200395350-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "of course when the pumping pipe 36 uses a weak material such as a plastic pipe instead of a steel pipe the pump may support a weight of the cardiac pump and additionally configure a hole for installing a lifting rope used for lifting installation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804115-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of side panels connected in series to form side surfaces of the water tank a top panel connected to a side surface of the water tank and connected in series so as to form an upper surface of the water tank a bottom panel connected to a bottom of the water tank so as to close the bottom of the side panel and and a reinforcing portion that maintains a gap between the side panels facing each other so as to prevent deformation of the water tank and a gap between the top panel and the bottom panel which are arranged to face each other the joint portion formed between the plurality of bottom panels is formed to protrude to the outside of the water tank further comprising a freezing prevention unit for preventing freezing of water to be dewatered in the water tank and providing thermal energy to the water surface of the fresh water to enable freezing of water frozen from the water surface to be more effectively prevented the above a control box installed on the upper panel a guide rod inserted into the water tank from the control box a moving block slidably installed in the vertical direction along the guide bar and having a support extending laterally a heater installed in the support for suppressing freezing by providing thermal energy to water and a buoyant body mounted on the support for lifting the support block and the moving block along the water level and flowing along the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100923508-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "on the other hand in order to solve this problem as shown in figure 2 in the interior of the water intake tower 6 is formed of reinforced concrete the screen 8 to block the inflow of dirt and the main pipe 7 although a fixed water intake device having a plurality of water intake ports 9 and opening and closing sides 10 in the middle part and the lower layer is disclosed there is a problem in that the intake of surface water due to the change of the water level is difficult.the present invention has been made to solve the above problems it is an object of the present invention to provide a multi functional water intake device that allows the separate or simultaneous withdrawal of the surface water middle water and deep water with one facility.in order to achieve the above object the present invention has a multifunctional water intake device a cylinder formed in multiple stages a winch for lifting the cylinder a packing for sealing between the cylinders a stopper for controlling the working distance of each cylinder and water storage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442471-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 installed on the waterway so as to be movable in the transverse direction a beam stand 11 mounted to the main body 10 to be elevated a rake 12 installed at the tip of the beam stand 11 to scrape up dirt in a waterway as the beam stand 11 moves up and down an elevating driver 15 for elevating the beam stage 11 a water level sensor 14 for detecting the water level in the water channel a controller 40 for controlling the lift position of the beam stage 11 by controlling the lift driver 15 according to the level detected by the water level sensor 14 a parallel moving drive unit 130 for moving the main body in the lateral direction and it includes a timer for measuring the lifting time of the beam stage 11 and the moving time of the main body 10 the controller 40 controls the beam stage 11 to be elevated to a predetermined depth below the water surface in the water channel according to the result measured by the timer and controls the horizontal movement amount of the main body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "accordingly when the water level flowing along the water channel 10 is lowered the contaminant transporting section having a circular shape on the flat section is extended downward to descend the up and down gate 250 to transport the contaminants filtered by the filtration screen 100 it is possible to smoothly carry out the contaminant transport without loss"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4637561-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "doing so may cause damage to the cable and the water quality measuring device or may make it impossible to lift the manhole cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171325-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "it is characterized in that it is further provided with a level sensor for detecting the level difference and a control unit for controlling the rpm of the drive motor by the output signal according to the level sensor of the level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171325-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "on the other hand the present invention detects the water level difference between the water inlet ip and the water outlet op into which the sewage and waste water flows and when the water level is higher than the set water level the rapid lifting and removing process according to the rpm control of the drive motor 1 is automatically controlled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101915884-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the driving unit 231 is driven at the upper portion and a lifting type water gate 230 vertically lifted and lowered according to the measured water level of the water level meter 300 the watertight housing 210 allows the water to be dewatered to the height of the watertight housing 210 at the ultraviolet sterilizer 100 at a normal time in the control unit 400 when the discharge water level corresponding to the height below the height of the water gate housing 210 is detected in the measurement of the ultrasonic level meter 300 the water gate 230 is completely accommodated in the water receiving groove 211 and when the discharged water level above the height of the water gate housing 210 is sensed the water gate 230 is elevated to a height corresponding to the discharged water level to reduce the flow rate of discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101915884-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object there is provided an ultraviolet disinfector which is installed on the inflow portion side of a drainage path and a water level control means which adjusts the water level formed on the outlet portion side of the ultraviolet disinfecting device in the drainage passage a control unit for controlling the operation of the water level control unit on the basis of the water level of the water discharged from the ultrasonic level meter the ultrasonic level meter measuring the water level of water discharged from the water level adjusting unit the ultraviolet disinfection system of the present invention comprises the water a hydrologic housing which is installed from the bottom of the drainage passage and has an upper openable hydrological receiving groove formed therein a pair of hydrologic guides vertically installed at both ends in the width direction of the hydrologic housing and and the upper portion is provided with a driving portion which is driven according to the signal of the control portion so that the lifting type water gate which is lifted up and down according to the measured water level of the ultrasonic level gauge lt rti gt the watertight housing normally allows the water to be dewatered to the height of the watertight housing on the ultraviolet sterilizer side in the control section when the discharge water level below the height of the water gate housing is detected in the measurement of the ultrasonic water level meter the water gate is completely housed in the water receiving groove when the discharged water level above the height of the hydrologic housing is sensed the water gate is raised to a height corresponding to the discharged water level to reduce the flow rate of the discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439293-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "on the other hand the controller 10 continuously detects the pressure drop while the raw water is discharged through the water supply pipe 51 but when the raw water is near the high water level h and the middle water level m or the low water level l the pressure drop detected when close is different"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100717368-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "while fitting the flow flange 200 to the outside of the encasing 20 to fit the rubber ring 300 and put the well cap 100 on the top of the casing 20 to combine the pumping pipe 50 the water level measuring tube 11 is coupled and the operating rod 130 is coupled to the operation lever 120 and then the lifting flange 200 is lifted upward so that the rubber ring 300 is fitted into the support space 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100984372-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "rain gutters 20 including a rain box 40 communicating with the first outlet hole 21b of the rain gutter through a connecting pipe 30 to store rainwater flowing into the rain gutter it includes a rooftop excellent induction pipe 2 for leading the rainwater collected on the roof of the building around the road to the rain gutter the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar in the driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility comprising an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge a sleeve 51 having the same size as the thickness of the bottom of the rain gutter main body and inserted into an insertion hole formed in the bottom of the rain gutter main body a perforated pipe 50 inserted into the sleeve so as to communicate with the inside of the rain gutter and installed by a filling material filled in the bottom of the rain gutter and penetrating the rainwater stored in the rain gutter into the ground a valve installed at an inlet side of the hole tube to adjust an opening degree of the hole tube driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility characterized in that it comprises a filter 52 is attached to the filter mounting portion 21c formed concave at the bottom of the rain gutter to remove the foreign matter from the rainwater flowing into the hole"}]</data>
