  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-0161641-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "another object of the present invention is a water level sensor failure detection method of the cold and hot water purifier that can prevent the occurrence of freezing of the cold water tank caused by the failure of the water level sensor of the cold and hot water purifier a failure due to the overheat of the heater or excessive waste of purified water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0167322-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "therefore the cold air supplied to the upper side moves along the surface of the cold water storage tank 12 and since more cold air is supplied to the interface of the water level b than the normal state the surface of the purified water freezes and the freezing grows gradually over time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the automatic dripping device for preventing freezing may include a falling water providing pipe installed to communicate with the falling water storage tank and to supply the falling water stored in the falling water storage tank to a user a water level detection and alarm unit installed in the fall water storage tank detecting the level of the fluid stored in the fall water storage tank and alerting an operator through an alarm member when the detected level exceeds a preset range and a falling water drain pipe installed to communicate with the falling water providing pipe and discharging the falling water from the falling water providing pipe to the outside when an alarm is generated by the alarm member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the automatic dripping device for preventing freezing of the present invention the falling water stored in the falling water storage tank can be re supplyed to the user by providing a falling water providing pipe a water level detection and alarm unit and a falling water drain pipe that perform specific roles it is possible to prevent the waste of water and the capacity of the water stored in the water storage tank can be adjusted within a safe range thereby providing an automatic water fall device for preventing freezing that can prevent an accident in which water overflows in the water storage tank during operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "is possible and such variations fall within the protection scope of the present invention.10 piping entering the object to be frozen or bursting or piping exiting from the object 20 external power 100 automatic dripping device for freezing prevention 110 body part 111 opening and closing lid 112 power indicator lamp 113 operation indicator lamp 114 storage space 120 temperature detection unit 130 control unit 131 external power input terminal 132 transformer 133 relay 140 on off valve 150 on off valve driving unit 150e emergency operation button 151 opening and closing valve coupling part 152 rotary drive unit 153 heat supply unit 154 opening and closing valve warming part 161 additional mounting piping 161a extension pipe 162 additionally installed on off valve 163 falling water storage tank 164 falling water flow rate detection unit 165 falling water supply pipe 166 water level detection and alarm unit 167 water drain pipe 171 power supply unit 172 power supply part warming part 173 wireless communication module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102537944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of fresh water tanks that naturally fall from a natural water supply source and receive and store water including a jurisdiction server for remote control of the freshwater tank in the forest fire fighting water management system the plurality of fresh water tanks are installed on one side of the mountain and one of the two connected to the water supply pipe is located above the other one the fresh water tank includes a water tank for receiving water therein including evacuation space where people can be located the two fresh water tanks connected by the water supply pipe are connected by two water supply pipes among the two water supply pipes a one of them includes a valve on one side so that the water contained in the upper water tank is dropped by the opening of the valve and the water is transferred to the lower water tank b the other one by using a pump the water contained in the lower freshwater tank is transferred to the upper freshwater tank when the valve is opened for the transfer of water a collision between water transferred from the upper water tank to the lower water tank and water transferred from the lower water tank to the upper water tank is prevented from occurring the water supply pipe is buried in the ground to prevent the water supply pipe from freezing and interfering with water supply between each water tank the jurisdiction server by selectively controlling the water supply pipe of the water supply source the valve of the water supply pipe of the fresh water tank or the pump of the water supply pipe of the fresh water tank according to the water level information of each fresh water tank it is possible to adjust the water to each fresh water tank by building a database based on the identification information of the freshwater tank and the identification information of the mountain in advance and providing it as information it is easy to use the water in the freshwater tank necessary for firefighting in case of disaster the fresh water tank a hose connector connected to the water tank is configured on the outside the hose connector is wound by a large reel and the fire hose connected to the hose connector is coupled to the flight means the hose connector of the fresh water tank is coupled to the fresh water tank by extending the pipe downward from the lower flange part and securing a separation space between the lower flange part and the upper surface of the fresh water tank to provide a plurality of ball valve plates arranged in the circumferential direction the hose connector is configured to be rotated by the rotation of the ball valve so that the movement of the fire hose connected to the hose connector is flexible"}, {"pat_id": "US-9765508-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the hewitt invention is a device to collect and dispense roof rain water comprising a container to collect water having an opening a pump to drive the water out of the container a debris disposal mechanism a sensor to measure the water level wherein the pump is activated at a specific water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the water supply control device of claim 1 wherein further comprising a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value wireless automatic water level control system further comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "as it is buried underground it prevents freezing in winter by improving heat retention and effectively suppresses bacterial propagation while completely blocking contact between the inside of the pressurized water tank and the outside air thereby increasing the utility of drinking water.1 is a longitudinal sectional view of an embodiment of a water supply device to which the present invention is applied figure 2 is a longitudinal sectional view showing the internal structure of the air pressure leakage preventing device of the present invention 3 is a cross sectional view taken along the line aa of the present invention figure 2 figure 4 is a partially cut away perspective view of the present invention air pressure leakage preventing device figure 5 is an enlarged cross sectional view of the disk of the present invention to block the flow path at the minimum water level 6 is an enlarged cross sectional view of a disk of the present invention in a state in which a flow path is opened figure 7 is another embodiment longitudinal section of the present invention water supply device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102789712-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a brine tank 10 10 in which brine is stored at a certain level and sprayed through brine nozzles individually installed at a number of habitual freezing points a b c d a detection sensor 20 that detects the water level of brine stored in the brine tank 10 of each of the above points a central control unit 30 that manages information on the brine storage level through the above detection sensor 20 in order to transport brine stored in a brine tank 10 at a point where the amount of brine is relatively large to a point where the amount of brine is insufficient by the control of the central control unit 30 a brine guide pipe 40 through which brine stored in the brine tank 10 is withdrawn by the operation of a pump p a coupler 50 that is connected to the end of the brine guide pipe 40 and is connected to the transfer tank 110 of the brine transfer vehicle 100 a salt water supply system for road deicing spraying characterized in that the salt water transport tank 110 configured in the salt water transport vehicle 100 is provided with a plurality of bubble generators 111 on the bottom surface to prevent freezing or precipitation of salt water during the transport process an ultraviolet lamp 112 is provided on the top surface and a deterioration prevention layer 113 is formed on the inner wall surface to prevent deterioration of salt water during transport"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition when it is determined that the communication state is good the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe measured by the temperature sensor and if the pump abnormality can be determined preferably a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385568-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention was devised to solve the above mentioned problems and an object of the present invention is to simply detect the water level of a water well or a storage means by the conduction of a power source having a predetermined voltage and to prevent damage to the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a closed cylinder portion 100 coupled to the lower side of the groundwater protection part a piezoelectric tube 210 installed at one side to prevent the groundwater from expanding due to internal pressure generated when the groundwater rises is coupled to one side of the piezoelectric pipe the other side is coupled to the plate check valve sand filter 220 for filtering the sand contained in the groundwater plate check valve 230 is coupled to one side of the sand filter the other side is coupled to the meter to prevent the groundwater filtered by the sand filter backflow a meter 240 coupled to one side of the plate check valve and the other side coupled to a pressure gauge a pressure gauge 250 coupled to one side of the meter and coupled to a three way valve on the other side a three way valve 260 coupled to the pressure gauge to form a flow path in the direction of the emergency water supply pipe 600 or the water supply pipe 700 an underground water level protection hole 200 including an underground water level protection column 270 formed along an inner circumference to prevent freezing waves it is configured to include and the controller 500 for supplying power to the underground water protection unit if the temperature is below the set temperature the controller 500 a temperature sensor 510 for detecting the ambient temperature a temperature setting unit 520 for setting a reference temperature for supplying power to the ground water protection protection vessel a memory unit 530 for storing the reference temperature set by the temperature setting unit a power supply unit 540 for supplying power to the ground water protection protection line a temperature comparison unit 550 for comparing the temperature sensed by the temperature sensor with the reference temperature stored in the memory unit a power supply signal transmitter 560 for transmitting a power supply signal to a power supply unit when the temperature compared by the temperature comparison unit is less than a reference temperature freezing prevention comprising a central control unit 570 for controlling the signal flow between the temperature sensor the temperature setting unit the memory unit the power supply unit the temperature comparison unit the power supply signal transmission unit and groundwater upper protection device capable of underwater discharge sterilization treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080527-A", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "a further feature of having a screen located over the inlet to the drain valve that is spaced sufficiently far into the water supply pipe so that the water flowing past the screen produces a cleaning action on the screen to remove particles deposited on the screen"}, {"pat_id": "US-12017929-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the control and monitoring tool comprises the control panel with microprocessor and control boards connected with it control valves and water level sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0385568 2003.05.15 designated by reservoir control system registered and filed by the present applicant the groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "prevents freezing the control unit is further provided with a sticking prevention function when the operation time of the discharge pump is stopped for a specific time or more the discharge pump is operated for a specific time at a specific period to prevent sewage from sticking to the storage tank or the discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "when the water level measured by the water level sensor is less than a certain level in the case of performing the first shut off valve and open the second on off valve to prevent the freezing as the sewage of the storage tank is circulated inside can be"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to the present invention a wastewater drainage device and a management system therefor can efficiently manage a pump used in the wastewater drainage device to prolong the service life and prevent the wastewater storage tank from freezing or failing due to the sewage of the wastewater pump or the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the configuration of the present invention for achieving the above object the motor pump for supplying the raw water is supplied to the storage tank remotely through the pipe and installed in the intake well and the inner upper side of the storage tank to sense the water level of the storage tank an ultrasonic sensor installed in the outer circumferential surface to prevent freezing a temperature sensing sensor installed inside the storage tank to measure a temperature in the storage tank and installed outside the storage tank and measured from the ultrasonic sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "US-7396459-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "one of the advantages of placing the uv lamps in a water tank rather than a poe uvdu is the ability of the larger quantity of water to resist warming too quickly and thereby decreasing the uv output of the lamp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100996949-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "therefore there is a vulnerability to freeze or conserve heat in the freezing and condensation in winter.accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a water ejecting portion at the distal end of an inlet pipe capable of injecting water into the water tank so as to diffusely spray the water flowing into the water tank and to reduce the pressure at the end of the inlet pipe residual pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-4448032-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "US-5163779-A", "para_id": "para_82", "text": "a further feature of having a screen located over the inlet to the drain valve that is spaced sufficiently far into the water supply pipe so that the water flowing past the screen produces a cleaning action on the screen to remove particles deposited on the screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "US-4370865-A", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100689108-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0 385 568 2003.05.15 titled reservoir control system which is filed and filed by the present applicant has a groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804115-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of side panels connected in series to form side surfaces of the water tank a top panel connected to a side surface of the water tank and connected in series so as to form an upper surface of the water tank a bottom panel connected to a bottom of the water tank so as to close the bottom of the side panel and and a reinforcing portion that maintains a gap between the side panels facing each other so as to prevent deformation of the water tank and a gap between the top panel and the bottom panel which are arranged to face each other the joint portion formed between the plurality of bottom panels is formed to protrude to the outside of the water tank further comprising a freezing prevention unit for preventing freezing of water to be dewatered in the water tank and providing thermal energy to the water surface of the fresh water to enable freezing of water frozen from the water surface to be more effectively prevented the above a control box installed on the upper panel a guide rod inserted into the water tank from the control box a moving block slidably installed in the vertical direction along the guide bar and having a support extending laterally a heater installed in the support for suppressing freezing by providing thermal energy to water and a buoyant body mounted on the support for lifting the support block and the moving block along the water level and flowing along the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101627965-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the upper insulating member 6a the intermediate insulating member 6b the upper surface of the laminated upper heat insulating material 6a is adhered to the lower surface of the lid 1 with a strong adhesive agent so as to be bonded.the water leveling lid according to the present invention can enlarge the inside of the meter box without opening the cover while pressing the galvanized steel sheet in a multi stage so as to bear a high load and transmit the sunlight to the inside of the meter box by condensing drying and disinfection of the inside of the meter box can be achieved and a triple insulating material is provided at the lower part of the lid to generate a remarkable action effect for preventing freezing of the meter in the winter season.fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673091-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "2000 0013937 july 15 2000 the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the conventional system for preventing the freezing of the water supply system for railway cars as described above and it is an object of the present invention to provide a system for preventing the freezing of the water the water at the rear end of the water supply pipe 33 is drained to the water level in the water tank so that it is possible to prevent the freezing of the pipe in the vehicle interior during the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102713396-B1", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "fourth by forming the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit evaporator 2 1 2 and the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit concentrated water circulating water ejector 7 1 2 and controlling the residence time of the concentrated water flowing out of the concentrated water tank 15 1 supercooling and the formation of fine ice seed water in the salt separation tank 5 1 were promoted thereby reinforcing the formation and growth of the brine water containing organic and inorganic substances contained in the influent into an ice slurry"}]</data>
