  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200160111-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "if the inflow of the wastewater increases accidentally or the wastewater level such as the channel increases by more than a certain level because the gap of the screen material 16 is blocked by a contaminant due to the failure of the wastewater treatment screen 10 the water level sensor the controller immediately detects this and transmits the control means and the over water signal and the control means receiving the over water signal operates the floodgate driving means 21 to drive the emergency water gate 18 upward to open the frame 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484030-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent soil purification apparatus for purifying sewage discharged to a superior soil through a secondary collector a pretreatment needle settling vessel 110 having an inflow hole 111 formed at a lower side thereof so as to allow contaminated sewage to flow therein so as to gradually increase the water level from the bottom surface and to precipitate and remove contaminant particles and contaminants having a large specific gravity and a communication hole 121 for receiving the sewage introduced into the pre processing settling tank 110 and disposed above the settling tank 110 so that the water level of the sewage gradually increases and the purified water a space forming part 100 including a purifying space part 120 formed with an outflow hole 122 through which the exhaust gas flows a buoy 210 floating on the sewage flowing into the purifying space 120 and a filter material 220 compressed as the buoy 210 rises by the sewage flowing continuously a purifier 200 comprising compression means 230 for causing the filter media 220 to compress each other as the buoy 210 rises lt rti the compression means 230 includes a circulation induction plate 231 fixed at a predetermined height of the purification space 120 on the lower side of the buoy and having a plurality of flow holes 231a penetrated therethrough a moving plate 232 having a plurality of flow holes 231a formed therein so as to be able to move upward and downward in the lower space 220 of the purifying space 120 and having one end fixed to the buoy 210 and the circulation induction plate 231 and the other end is connected to the moving plate 232"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also when the water level rises the retractable watershed wall prevents the backwash of the river water to prevent flooding damage and the impoundment collection box having a filter net for filtering the contaminants contained in the sewage and storm seats is installed so that the contaminants do not flow into the wells and an odor chamber connected to the ceiling of the sewage pipe at an upper portion of the open the curtain can be installed to block the malodor generated in the sewer line and to move the sewer line along the moving rail to the left and right sides of the sewer line to conveniently remove and remove the contaminant lifting device connected with the wire have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "when the height of the water level due to an increase in the amount of contaminant collecting is detected to be higher than a predetermined value when the artificial filter media is cleaned a separate outlet pipe is formed to allow the blower to spray the high pressure air and the washing water is supplied by the pump to perform backwashing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "when the height of the water level due to an increase in the amount of contaminant collecting is detected to be higher than a predetermined value when the artificial filter media is cleaned a separate outlet pipe is formed to allow the blower to spray the high pressure air and the washing water is supplied by the pump to perform backwashing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100510269-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102761954-B1", "para_id": "para_156", "text": "that is if the water level of the water tank 200 and the wind speed of the fan continue to change the contaminant concentration band continues to be pushed up in the opposite direction of the distribution rod 500 so that contaminants may continue to be concentrated and fixed on the drying filter 700"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101223419-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "if the water is not inhaled because it is located above the water level and the water is introduced into the well where the water soluble contaminant and the water are mixed the lower end of the nozzle 140 is submerged into the water soluble contaminant in the well thereby recovering the light water pollutant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the initial rainwater collecting weir is the same as the initial upper water level of the upper weir the initial rainwater is filled in the initial rainwater storage tank while the initial rainwater is transferred to the initial rainwater storage tank through the contaminant blocking pipe rainwater filtration and collection device excluding the initial excellent after the rain reaches the upper end of the water level to perform the function of overflowing the rainwater to the top"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101279418-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "meanwhile the high concentration overflow water storage tank 220 is provided at the front end of the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 and the reason for placing the location of the high concentration overflow water inlet 211 below the low concentration overflow water inlet 212 may be due to a high contaminant concentration of the initial overflow water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank 1 having a contaminant collecting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the pretreatment tank 1 may further include a dirt collecting tank 13 and a ditch water tank 14 therein"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "specifically when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122 and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "for example in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level the amount of effluent water can be derived from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "thus the data manager on the central monitoring device 170 side or the owner user maintenance manager and cleaner of the water treatment device 200 that has received information from the central monitoring device 170 side as the water treatment status in the treatment tank 101 the water quality information detected by the water quality detec