ontaminant remover installed in the reaction tank so as to circulate the contaminants to remove contaminants generated in the reaction tank a distillation unit installed at a lower portion of the reaction tank and supplying air to the treated water from a lower portion of the reaction tank and and a control unit for receiving the water level information of the treated water from a water level sensor for sensing the water level of the treated water and controlling the operation of the debris remover in accordance with the level of the treated water the contaminant a transporting conveyor for circulating and moving the inside and outside of the reaction tank a collecting removing unit being coupled to the transporting conveying unit and a conveying roller unit disposed adjacent to the conveying conveyor and connected to the driving unit to move the conveying conveyor by rotation and a driving unit connected to the conveying unit to move the conveying unit and controlled to be driven by the control unit wherein a concave shaped collecting part is formed to collect contaminants deposited on the bottom of the reaction tank and connected to the conveying conveyor so as to move along the bottom surface of the reaction tank and to circulate the inside and the outside of the reaction tank according to the movement of the conveying conveyor and a collecting removing unit for discharging and removing the contaminants collected by the collecting unit while moving the conveying conveyor a part of which is annularly immersed in the reaction tank and disposed adjacent to the bottom and side surfaces of the reaction tank so as not to interfere with the flow of the treated water to reduce the screening effect the collecting wherein the collecting unit is located on the bottom surface of the reaction vessel so as to observe the moving direction while being immersed in the reaction tank a collecting body for collecting contaminants and a separation preventing part formed at both ends of the collecting part body to prevent separation of the contaminants collected in the collecting part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101851689-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "this is because when the contaminant 2 in the reaction tank 100 is generated the screen unit 200 is closed and when the screen unit 200 is closed the entire water level in the reaction tank 100 or the water level in the vicinity of the screen unit 200 rises the control unit 400 can detect the degree of generation of the contaminants 2 from the water level sensor 110 and operate the contaminant remover 300 to effectively remove the contaminants 2 it is possible to reduce the waste of energy and reduce the power cost thereby providing economical effects"}, {"pat_id": "US-7678235-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "such controls can attenuate flow of inlet water and or other functions of the system such that production of product water is responsive to demand therefore"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044357-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is a fence installed to have a certain area on the water surface a micro bubble generator mbp for generating bubble water containing microbubbles and a flocculant at a predetermined depth to flocculate contaminants in the fence collecting means installed inside the fence to move the contaminant sludge flocculated by the bubble water to one side a sludge storage tank installed at one end of the fence to store the sludge collected by the collecting means a first water level sensor detecting a level of sludge collected in the sludge storage tank a control unit configured to control the operation of the sludge feed pump by receiving the detection signal of the first water level sensor and a sludge transfer pump installed adjacent to the sludge storage tank to transfer the sludge to the land storage tank and the bubble water is mixed with the lake water while maintaining a constant flow reacting and agglomerating and forming a floc and at the same time the microbubble is sucked into the floc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101058919-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "if the treatment unit is high water may include the step of discharging the filtered rainwater to the outside of the first initial excellent treatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100397886-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the installation screen is automatically lifted according to the water level 30 to block the impurities such as garbage flowing along the water and the rake 10 of the upper side while elevating by the driving force of the chain inside the rail 20 arc type by angular movement to handle the waste caught in the floating screen 30 in particular the rake 10 is vertically lowered from the upper side of the inside of the rail 20 in the state fixed to the shaft 11 floating screen 30 after going down the water along the rails 20 and angularly moving in an arc shape without receiving the interference of garbage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101432516-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as a result the operation differential pressure is reduced to less than half of the operation differential pressure generated in the membrane of the conventional membrane bioreactor so that the filtration process can be performed without using the pressurization or decompression pump and the operation cost can be remarkably reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "summary of the invention an object of the present invention is to provide a water borne contaminant removal apparatus capable of continuously removing contaminants while maintaining the water level in a water channel and dehydrating water so that the water content contained in the contaminants is removed to lower the water content"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "this allows the scrapers to be filtered by the screw scraper 300 which is erected vertically to the water channel 10 and is rotated inside the filtration screen 100 when the sewage is passed through the water channel 10 the screw scraper 300 does not interfere with the collection and transport of the contaminants by causing the water level of the water channel 10 to change when the contaminant is pushed up by the rotation which is capable of maintaining the water level of the water channel 10 as it is so as to smoothly remove contaminants continuously and at the same time to remove moisture contained in the contaminants by the dehydrating unit 500 so as to lower the water content can be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "accordingly when the water level flowing along the water channel 10 is lowered the contaminant transporting section having a circular shape on the flat section is extended downward to descend the up and down gate 250 to transport the contaminants filtered by the filtration screen 100 it is possible to smoothly carry out the contaminant transport without loss"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080805-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "meanwhile the high concentration overflow water storage tank 220 is provided at the front end of the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 and the reason for placing the location of the high concentration overflow water inlet 211 below the low concentration overflow water inlet 212 may be due to a high contaminant concentration of the initial overflow water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the method of claim 1 wherein the continuous continuous micro contaminant recovery processing device further comprises a water level detecting means the water level detecting means both ends are vertical pipe shape connected to the upper and lower ends of the outer processing tank 100 respectively the sensing unit 310 at the upper end of the water level sensing means is fixed a reed switch 320 is provided in the lower bottom surface of the sensing unit 310 two terminals 330 of the reed switch 320 a buoy 340 in the vertical pipe of the water level detecting means and the magnet 350 is attached to the upper end of the buoy 340 sensing means consisting of is provided so as to be able to move freely inside the vertical pipe of the water level sensing means the bottom surface of the lower end of the sensing unit 310 is provided with the reed switch 320 fine contaminants characterized in that configured to be fixed to the position of the water level of the contaminated soil mixed with water in the external treatment tank 100 continuous recovery processing device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "the method of claim 9 wherein the fine contaminant continuous recovery apparatus further comprises a water level detecting means the water level detecting means both ends are vertical pipe shape connected to the upper and lower ends of the outer processing tank 100 respectively the sensing unit 310 at the upper end of the water level sensing means is fixed a reed switch 320 is provided in the lower bottom surface of the sensing unit 310 two terminals 330 of the reed switch 320 a buoy 340 in the vertical pipe of the water level detecting means and the magnet 350 is attached to the upper end of the buoy 340 sensing means consisting of is provided so as to be able to move freely inside the vertical pipe of the water level sensing means with a control unit 600 for receiving a signal of the water level detected from the two terminals 330 of the reed switch 320 the control unit 600 according to the on off of the reed switch 320 the above described flow regulating valve and the treatment chemical pump control signal sc of the treatment chemical providing unit 500 microcontaminant continuous recovery apparatus characterized in that configured to provide the pump control signals vic and voc provided in the contaminated treated water supply pipe 130 and the purified treated water recovery pipe 140"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "to this end the water level detecting means of the present invention is a vertical pipe shape whose both ends are connected to the upper and lower ends of the outer processing tank 100 respectively the sensing unit 310 is fixed to the upper end of the water level detecting means the sensing unit a reed switch 320 is provided inside the bottom bottom of the 310 and two terminals 330 of the reed switch 320 are drawn out to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the inflow chamber may further include a water level sensor installed penetrating inward from an upper surface of the inflow chamber so as to sense the water level inside the inflow chamber to control the operation of the contaminant treatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in other words the water level detector 12 is to operate the contaminant processing unit 40 only when the waste water reaches a constant level in the inflow chamber 10 to prevent unnecessary waste of power"}, {"pat_id": "US-4582610-A", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thus the present invention generally contemplates providing spray holes in the well pipe at a location below the top of the well and above the average static water level in the well spraying and aerating a fractional portion of the well water pumped through the well pipe and permitting the fractional portion of well water to fall back down the well and checking the backflow of water in the well pipe from the building above the spray holes when pumping of water in the well pipe stops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100794198-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a sewage separation tank 20 capable of separating non organic non degradable foreign matter by receiving sewage and temporarily storage and decomposition of organic solids a conversion flow rate adjustment tank 30 for sharing the mutual conversion characteristics of the physical function flow rate control and the biological treatment function so that the characteristics of the water quality can be developed as an exhalation function primary contact aeration tank 40 which is the main treatment process to maintain the aerobic phase characteristics of the microorganism by maintaining the active range of the microorganism to the heavy load primary settling tank 50 for firstly separating the desorbed sludge secondary contact aeration tank 60 which is an auxiliary treatment process having an increase in the food chain and natural purification characteristics between the microorganisms by obtaining a function having a preliminary preliminary function by affording a specific surface area for attachment of organic matter and purified microorganisms secondary settling tank 70 for separating the sewage sludge secondary sludge storage tank 80 and the sludge collected in the first and second primary settling tank 50 70 and a discharge tank 90 for discharging the supernatant after disinfection under the boundary wall 22 of the contaminant separation tank 20 and the switching flow adjustment tank 30 an opening 23 for preventing the accumulation of organic matter based on the change in water level and the agitation of the switching flow adjustment tank 30 contact switching frames 31 41 61 disposed in the switching flow rate adjustment tank 30 the primary contact aeration tank 40 and the secondary contact aeration tank 60 upper and lower contact contact frames 31 41 61 and mesh fixing nets 33 43 63 in the purification processing apparatus having the contact support frame 31 41 61 having at least one diffuser 36 44 64 at the bottom the switching flow rate adjustment tank 30 side has a first stage air lift 35 for solving the factor of reducing the amount of transport due to the water level and increasing the efficiency of the flow rate adjustment the water tank 34 connected to the upper end of the first stage air lift 35 has two stages to transfer the quantity of raw water to the air float so that the transfer effort for the first contact aeration tank 40 which is a later process is low"}]</data>
