vanced treatment management unit 1340 that performs accident and failure prediction through the status information of the ozone generating device and the maintenance of the water level of the purified water and optimum chlorine it is preferable to provide a purified water disinfection ability management unit 1350 for deriving the contact time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101890574-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the decanter 1000 may be further provided with a water level checker 1800 for checking the level of raw water in the reaction tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "in another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method of operating a hybrid pipeline transportation system for a marine waste treatment plant the method comprising the steps of a a marine purification treatment facility installed in a marine waste treatment plant b measuring the water level inside the shielding facility of the shore waste treatment plant and the external water level of the sea level c checking whether the internal water level is greater than a preset reference value d collecting the contaminated water in the shielded facility so that the internal water level of the shielded facility is lowered and storing the polluted water in the polluted water storage tank when the internal water level is higher than a preset reference value e determining the amount of polluted water transported by the control unit to be transported to the land storage tank f driving the pressure feed pump for transporting the contaminated water through the first pipeline and g storing the contaminated water transported by the onshore storage tank wherein the control unit is operable to transport the contaminated water to the land storage tank when the internal water level of the shielded facility is higher than a preset reference value and the first pipeline in step f transports the polluted water stored in the polluted water storage tank to the land storage tank thereby lowering the internal water level of the shielded facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102246564-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "providing a number of hydroxyl radicals 3 including hydroxyl radicals ozone and microbubbles to the pressurized flotation tank 200 a floc discharge pipe 110 is provided in the lower portion of the chemical reaction tank 100 to discharge flocs which are solid pollutants that cannot be aggregated into suspended solids but naturally precipitate and accumulate to the bottom and discharged to the outside a drain part 210 for discharging the contaminated water 1 stored for a certain period of time to the outside is provided at the lower part of the pressurization floating tank 200 the treated water discharge pipe 600 is provided with a water level maintenance air suction unit 610 for inhaling external air so as to adjust the internal appropriate water level of the pressure floating tank 200 to be branched an integrated water treatment system for a pressurized flotation tank and a chemical reaction tank using hydroxyl radicals and ozone characterized in that a confirmation filter unit 800 for checking the state of the purified water 4 is installed at the end of the treated water discharge pipe 600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100813181-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "and a relief valve 16 which is a stabilizer for maintaining the set pressure and deformation and breakage of the pneumatic water tank 37 due to the abnormal pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_22", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a plurality of upstream biological water treatment filters each filter having a variable water level an inflow into the base of the filter and an outflow from the top of the filter the filter comprising a automatically checking the level of each filter to check whether the level is as high as degassing is necessary b if the water level indicates that degassing is required in the selected filter locking the inlet valve from the first filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the filter c opening the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve of the selected first filter d starting the backwash pump e flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter f next closing the inlet valve from the selected filter and then opening the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the selected filter g closing the backwash fresh water valve to the selected first filter h opening the inlet valve from the selected first filter i repeating steps d through h for each additional filter j flushing the finally selected filter k turning off the backwash water pump l opening the inlet valve from the finally selected filter m closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the finally selected filter and n maintaining the outlet valve open for steps a to m"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102577141-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "there is no leakage outside the frame so it can be used safely while supplying water regardless of location"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102884754-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "of course a user may also open the corresponding overflow pipe after visually checking the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101358438-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "the level sensor 64 and the actuator 65 may be installed on the slab 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102391446-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "specifically the control device 30 may determine whether filter cleaning is necessary by checking whether the water level in the water tank is equal to or greater than a preset threshold value based on the water level detection information"}, {"pat_id": "US-6893571-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "an apparatus for storing water separated from fuels using a fuel filter having a water accumulator said apparatus comprising an absorber connected to the water accumulator of the fuel filter via a connection line wherein said connection line is provided with a closing element and wherein said closing element comprises a sensor for checking the water level in the accumulator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "at this time a process of checking the initial water level in the reactor 10 may be accompanied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102694533-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step for taking action in the event of an abnormality in the above 4 demineralizer outlet and system water level is as follows when the na concentration of the steam generator exceeds 0.8 ppb the cpp standby demineralizer is additionally introduced and operated in parallel to purify the system when the na concentration of the steam generator continues to increase after exceeding 0.8 ppb the cpp eta type operation is stopped and then the cpp hydrogen type operation is resumed to purify the system a method for operating and managing an ethanolamine type desalination facility characterized in that the ion exchange resin of the above step 1 limits the sodium na content to a maximum of 0.5 ppm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102555542-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "third by providing a water tank equipped with a water level sensor to automatically supply water to the moss medium while storing water in the frame it is possible to automatically supply water by checking the water according to the water level therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200447886-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the water purifying apparatus may include a raw water tank in which raw water supplied through the bucket is stored for the first time and a water level sensor installed to detect a level of stored raw water a pump for sucking the raw water stored in the raw water tank to circulate in the water purifying apparatus a filter unit for purifying the raw water introduced by the suction force of the pump a storage tank in which the purified water purified by the filter unit is stored and a water level sensor capable of detecting a level of the stored purified water is installed and checking whether the raw water is stored in the raw water tank through the water level sensor of the raw water tank and controlling the raw water to be purified and stored in the storage tank by purifying the raw water through the filter unit when the raw water is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "70 is opened and the effluent is collected into the sump 100 while the current groundwater level is lower than the set ground level the effluent water due to the closing pressure of the water level control device 40 70 in the water level control device of the sump well configured to block the collection of water so that the current ground level is lower than the set ground level it is possible to reduce the number of continuous water block and pumping the water level control device 40 70 one end is connected to the collecting pipe 10 and the inlet pipes 22 52 84 provided with hydraulic pressure gauges 21 51 81 for checking the water pressure of the effluent and the inlet pipe 22 52 84 the drain pipe 23 53 85 and the main pipe 24 54 87 connected to the drain pipe 23 53 85 the inlet pipe 22 52 84 is provided with locking ends 25 52a 82 on the upper inner circumferential surface and a cover for preventing foreign matter from penetrating the upper ends of the main tubes 24 54 and 87 body parts 20 50 and 80 fastened to open and close 27 55 and 86 installed inside the body parts 20 50 80 the eluent water flowing into the inlet pipes 22 52 84 is opened and is drained to the drain pipes 23 53 85"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681132-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention provides a method of installing a water level plate that can block a connection pipe of a water intake tunnel while being easily installed and capable of withstanding water pressure and is capable of installing an already manufactured device in a water intake tunnel without producing water the present invention provides a method for replacing a water gate using a shutoff device for water gate maintenance of a water intake tower for replacing a water gate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681132-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition the connection pipe connecting the water gate of the water intake and the water intake tunnel is blocked by the water level plate so that the water is prevented from falling into the water intake tunnel during the water gate replacement and the water drain valve installed on the support pipe connected to the water level plate it is possible to drain the water between the plates and to check whether the water gate is installed properly by checking the pressure in the drain valve thereby preventing a safety accident that may occur when the water gate is not properly installed after the water gate is replaced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102048239-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "one side of the part 220 further includes a water pipe 230 provided to flow the water tank 110 and water the water introduced from the water pipe 230 is purified through the water filter 220 after the flow to the water spraying unit 140 may be injected into the water injection pipe 120"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5450286-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "in that case the operator starts or stops driving the water pump 30 while checking the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is higher than the minimum value opening the three way valve so that the water of the second tank is supplied through the downpipe and connected to the supply pipe and preventing the water of the first tank from being supplied to the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is higher than the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe purified in the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joined from the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joined including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so that the charge level of the battery is lower than the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is below the minimum value turning on the three way valve to connect the other discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is above the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joins including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 if the charge level of the battery is below the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "another eco friendly greenhouse control method according to the present invention may include the steps of determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and opening the three way valve if it is equal to or greater than the minimum value so that water from the second tank is supplied through the downdraft pipe and communicates with the supply pipe and preventing water from the first tank from being supplied to the supply pipe checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is equal to or greater than the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and if the charge level of the battery is less than the minimum value turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so as to stop the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joins including a sterilizing component"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "another eco friendly greenhouse control method according to the present invention may include the steps of determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is below the minimum value turning on the three way valve to connect another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the supply pipe 26 checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is above the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve 20 is branched off from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and if the charge level of the battery is below the minimum value turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so as to stop the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched off and joins including a sterilizing component"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "refrigerant tank type ionizer water level check method of the present invention another embodiment the water level check step of detecting the water level of the refrigerant tank to determine the water level and the step of determining the number of water level confirmed for a certain time and when the predetermined number or more it is characterized in that it comprises a step of opening and draining the drain valve of the refrigerant tank the step of determining whether full water is confirmed within a predetermined time and the level check step of checking the full water level when the full water is confirmed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "another embodiment of the refrigerant tank type ionizer automatic drainage method of the present invention the water level check step of detecting the water level of the refrigerant tank to determine the water level and the step of determining the number of water level is confirmed for a predetermined time and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed opening and draining the drain valve of the coolant tank determining whether full water is confirmed within a predetermined time checking a water level when full water is confirmed and draining step of opening and draining the drain valve of the coolant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_95", "text": "water purifier automatic drainage method of another embodiment of the present invention the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed drainage of the water tank and opening the valve and draining the water determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time checking the water level when the water level is confirmed and draining the water by opening the water drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "water purifier control method of the present invention the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time the water level checking step to check the water level if more than a predetermined number of times it characterized in that it comprises a drainage step of draining open the drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "another embodiment of the water purifier control method of the present invention the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water and the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time and when the predetermined number or more the drain valve of the water tank it is characterized in that it comprises a step of opening and draining the step of determining whether full water is confirmed within a predetermined time the level checking step of checking the water level when the full water is confirmed and the draining step of opening and draining the drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "second after checking the water level including the drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the water tank it is possible to automatically adjust the water level to prevent the overflow of the refrigerant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_102", "text": "third when the water level is confirmed for a predetermined number of times or more a drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the refrigerant tank determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time and a water level checking step of checking the water level when the water level is confirmed as a result errors due to internal factors can be recognized"}, {"pat_id": "US-4582610-A", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thus the present invention generally contemplates providing spray holes in the well pipe at a location below the top of the well and above the average static water level in the well spraying and aerating a fractional portion of the well water pumped through the well pipe and permitting the fractional portion of well water to fall back down the well and checking the backflow of water in the well pipe from the building above the spray holes when pumping of water in the well pipe stops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100977056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this case even if there is an error the manager does not immediately check this and because it is confirmed in the process of checking the control panel there is a problem in pumping operation.the present invention solves the problem of installing the case by welding on the upper casing of the well while alleviating the water shock phenomenon in which the pressure rises or falls due to the rapid flow rate changes inside the pump pipe and also pumping pressure it solves the problem of inadequate disinfection of groundwater by supplying chlorine from outside when the set value is reached and the control panel checks the change of internal pressure of the pump along with the water level of the well in the meantime if an abnormality occurs in the groundwater pumping the manager is immediately notified to take action.the present invention inserts the packing cap on the upper side of the out casing the outer side of the case is fitted to the outside of the packing cap while the inner side of the case is supported by the upper portion of the packing cap the case the wire inlet and pump pipe connector while fixing the cover to the upper side the inside of the case to install a flexible pipe connected to the pump and the water shock protector and a pressure valve the flexible pipe is a meter installed in the meter case through the meter connector and ground water passing through the meter is discharged after being mixed with the chlorine of the quantity supplied from the chlorine injector and the ground water pump and the chlorine pump by detecting the water level of the well and the water pressure and the amount of chlorine control the operation and notify the administrator wirelessly when an error occurs it will be written by providing the urban"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}]</data>
