  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method according to claim 1 or 2 the purified water tank unit 1000 is a water purification tank unit 1100 for storing purified water flowing in from the outside an outflow filter unit 1200 for filtering foreign substances included while discharging the purified water stored in the water purification tank unit 1100 a temporary storage unit 1300 for storing the purified water discharged from the outflow filter unit 1200 a water level sensor unit 1400 installed on one side of the temporary storage unit 1300 to detect the water level of the stored purified water a purified water metering pump 1500 for discharging the purified water stored in the temporary storage unit 1300 in a fixed amount from one side according to a corresponding control signal total hydrocarbon reduction system in the advanced oxidation process of environmental pollution around livestock facilities including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100762919-B1", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "therefore the controller 900 controls the reactor in an appropriate operation mode in response to the measured value of the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the biological filter system of present invention includes a filter unit receiving a filter medium providing an enhanced growth environment for microbial flora an underdrain unit collecting water during filtration and distributing air and water uniformly during backwashing an air and or oxygen supply unit to increase dissolved oxygen in the water to be used by the microbial flora in the filter medium and to be used in the oxidation process of metal species in raw water an air and water backwashing system supplying air and water under strictly controlled sequence to clean the media most efficiently and troughs maintaining the constant water level during the backwashing and draining the water rising over that level"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "however in case the water in the filter chamber rises over a water level of the overflow weir 37 placed at the filtrate outflow chamber 36 the injected oxidation air cannot rise over the water surface of the filter chamber but can be moved to the outflow side due to the air pressure by the water head difference with the outflow side"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "further as a result of spraying the air laden water into tank 33 the entrained air and any residual non oxidized gases in the water such as h2 s methane natural gas or the like are separated from the water resulting in a water column 55 in the bottom of tank 33 and an air and gas column 56 in the top of tank 33"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time the modular wetland infrastructure is preferably provided with a maintenance manhole for managing the contact oxidation tank installed at the bottom of the wetland infrastructure and the inflow water collected in the facility due to the increase of inflow flow rate it is desirable to have a water level control pipe that directly delivers water to the contact oxidation tank at the bottom of the modular wetland infrastructure and a bypass channel that bypasses the influent when the water level control is impossible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand in the water purification process if the inflow water flows into a direct contact oxidation tank through the water level control pipe of the wetland infrastructure without the physical purification step because the inflow flow exceeds a certain amount the modular wetland infrastructure it is preferred to have a physical filtration device between the contact oxidation tank and to add a physical purification process for the influent water introduced into the contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the modular wetland infrastructure 300 maintenance to be connected to the lower contact oxidation tank 500 to maintain the contact oxidation tank 500 located in the lower portion of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 manhole 330 and if the water level of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to precipitation exceeds a certain level in order to protect the wetland by transferring the influent directly to the sedimentation tank 400 modular wetland infrastructure 300 it is preferable to have a water level control pipe 340 is installed at the bottom of the through water connection with the drainage layer connected to the settling tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "on the other hand if the inflow water is directly transmitted to the sedimentation tank 400 through the water level control pipe 340 installed in the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to the inflow of excess flow screen 430 of the sedimentation tank 400 physical filtration occurs thereby preventing the inflow of untreated water directly into the contact oxidation tank 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "it has the advantage of being convenient and because it is multi functional it is effective to expand the scope of application to the non point source removal facility or storage facility such as urban complex"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "primary microbial baths 120 220 320 the primary to tertiary oxidizing aeration tanks 130 230 and 330 that separate ozone into treated water and suspended solids containing oxidizing organic matter by injecting ozone into the seawater wastewater supplied from each of the primary to tertiary microorganism tanks 120 220 and 320 and the primary to tertiary oxidation aeration tanks 130 230 and 330 are adjusted to control the water level thereby allowing floating substances including oxidized organic substances to be discharged upward and the treated water is primary to tertiary microorganism tanks 120 through the circulation pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "primary oxidation aeration process processing unit 100 secondary oxidation aeration process processing unit equipped with a secondary filter tank 210 for secondary removal of foreign substances in seawater wastewater supplied from the primary oxidation aeration process processing unit 100 200 a tertiary oxidation aeration process processing unit 300 and a tertiary oxidation aeration equipped with a tertiary filter tank 310 for tertiary removal of foreign substances in seawater wastewater supplied from the secondary oxidation aeration processing unit 200 the discharge treatment unit 400 provided with a fourth filter tank 410 for filtering the sludge remaining in the seawater wastewater supplied from the process processing unit 300 the primary to tertiary oxidation aeration process processing units 100 200 and 300 remove contaminants by passing seawater wastewater supplied from each of the primary to tertiary filter tanks 110 210 and 310 through a filter medium containing coral sand"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the primary water level adjusting tank 140 may be provided with a water level adjusting unit c which will be described later which will be described later in detail"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a water level adjusting unit c which will be described later may be installed in the tertiary water level adjusting tank 340 which will be described later in detail"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7487812-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "2 water treatment units other than the reverse osmosis membrane device 33 are omitted but other water treatment units may be present between the reverse osmosis membrane device 33 and the pressure gauge 61"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "10 water treatment device 100 agitator 110 rapid stirring 120 slow stirring 121 coagulation tank 122 first coagulation tank 123 second