ce 300 ballast tank 400 oxidation device 500 concentration measuring sensor 1000 process water treatment system n neutralizing agent t1 ballast water inlet pipe t2 ballast water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102302030-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the main treatment reaction tank may include a water level control water tank for controlling the level of the discharged water supplied from the catalytic oxidation reaction tank and a partition wall formed inside the water level control water tank and ascending and descending by a handle operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102361906-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "however the use may be changed to a pump and tank for supplying chlorine dioxide or hydrogen peroxide for color removal of wastewater and oxidation of difficult to decomposable substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100418419-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "this is a plan view of an oxidizing sphere with a floating sedimentation basin specifically two underwater rotors which act as aeration and agitation are installed in each of the oxidation holes 1 and 2 and a connecting pipe connecting both oxidation holes is installed at the upper part so that the free flow can be carried out due to the water level difference"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "the method according to claim 7 or 8 if the influent flows directly to the sedimentation tank through the water level control pipe of the modular wetland based facility due to the increase in inflow flow rate the screen material installed in the sump is not provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time the modular wetland infrastructure is preferably provided with a maintenance manhole for managing the contact oxidation tank installed at the bottom of the wetland infrastructure and the inflow water collected in the facility due to the increase of inflow flow rate if it is exceeded it is necessary to have a water level control pipe that directly transfers water to the contact oxidizing tank through a drainage layer installed therein and a bypass channel for bypassing the influent if the water level control is impossible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "on the other hand in the combined purification method when the inflow water flows into the direct contact oxidation tank through the water level control pipe of the wetland infrastructure without the physical purification step because the inflow flow exceeds a certain amount the modular wetland based it is desirable to have a physical filtration device between the facility and the catalytic oxidation tank to add a physical purification process for the influent water introduced into the catalytic oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the modular wetland infrastructure 300 maintenance to be connected to the lower contact oxidation tank 500 to maintain the contact oxidation tank 500 located in the lower portion of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 manhole 330 and if the water level of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to precipitation exceeds a certain level in order to protect the wetland by transferring the influent directly to the sedimentation tank 400 modular wetland infrastructure 300 it is preferable to have a water level control pipe 340 is installed at the bottom of the through water connection with the drainage layer connected to the settling tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "on the other hand if the inflow water is directly transmitted to the sedimentation tank 400 through the water level control pipe 340 installed in the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to the inflow of excess flow screen 430 of the sedimentation tank 400 physical filtration occurs thereby preventing the inflow of untreated water directly into the contact oxidation tank 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991257-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "50 the groundwater to be measured is the water temperature temperature electrical conductivity conductivity salinity salinity dissolved oxygen dissolved oxygen hydrogen ion concentration ph oxidation reduction potential orp depth to view and analyze each water temperature monitoring sensor 51 electrical conductivity monitoring sensor 52 salinity monitoring sensor 53 dissolved oxygen monitoring sensor 54 hydrogen ion concentration monitoring sensor 55 redox power monitoring sensor 56 water level monitoring it is configured to include a sensor 57 and is connected to the processor control 22 through the data port 24 of the data logger 20 while being installed at the ground water depth of the groundwater well 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "therefore the inflow path into which the river water flows into the primary storage tank is always lower than the river water level"}, {"pat_id": "US-7204930-B2", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "during the course of filtration an emergency such as a high level water sensor may be engaged the sensor then immediately sends from the plc a signal to set off the alarm 111 and alert the owners of the system that there is a high water level within the aeration tower 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200208477-Y1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "this is a plan view of an oxidizing sphere with a floating sedimentation basin specifically two underwater rotors which act as aeration and agitation are installed in each of the oxidation spheres 1 and 2 and a connection pipe connecting both oxidation spheres is installed at the upper portion to allow free transfer due to the water level difference"}, {"pat_id": "US-10273165-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "the one or more sensors probes or instruments may include for example flow meters water level sensors conductivity meters resistivity meters chemical concentration meters turbidity monitors chemical species specific concentration sensors temperature sensors ph sensors oxidation reduction potential orp sensors pressure sensors or any other sensor probe or scientific instrument useful for providing an indication of a desired characteristic or parameter of water entering or exiting any one or more of the one or more unit operations"}, {"pat_id": "US-4992181-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for treating water removed from the ground to reduce the content of noxious sulfur containing impurities therein before the water is supplied to an associated water system said method comprising the steps of spraying the water to be treated in the upper portion of a closed standpipe which has an inlet for the water to be treated and an outlet through which water can flow from the standpipe into a closed tank containing a bed of a catalyst for the oxidation of sulfur and sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions the inlet and the outlet of the standpipe being so positioned that air which becomes disassociated from water can collect in the upper portion of the standpipe and the closed tank being operably connected for the flow of water which has flowed through the catalyst bed therein into the associated water system controlling the spraying of water in the upper portion of the closed standpipe to maintain a superatmospheric pressure therein to pressurize the associated water system entraining air with the water before it is sprayed in the standpipe maintaining the water level in the standpipe that is required to enable the flow of water therefrom through the catalyst bed to the associated water system and controlling the amount of air entrained with the water sprayed in the standpipe and the residence time of the water in the catalyst bed so that entrained air separates from the water and forms an air pocket inside the standpipe and there is a substantially complete oxidation of sulfur and sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions"}, {"pat_id": "US-4992181-A", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "a method for treating water removed from the ground to reduce the content of noxious sulfur containing impurities therein before the water is supplied to an associated water system said method comprising the steps of spraying the water to be treated in the upper portion of a closed standpipe which has an inlet for the water to be treated and an outlet through which water can flow to the associated water system the inlet and the outlet of the standpipe being so positioned that air which becomes disassociated from water can collect in the upper portion of the standpipe controlling the spraying of water in the upper portion of the closed standpipe to maintain a superatmospheric therein to pressurize the associated water system entraining air with the water before it is sprayed in the standpipe said last named step being carried out in a vessel in which the ground water is sprayed upwardly maintaining the water level in the standpipe that is required to enable the flow of water therefrom to the associated water system containing the ground water before it is delivered to the associated water system with a catalyst for the oxidation of sulfur and sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions and controlling the time of contact between the ground water and the catalyst the amount of air entrained with the water sprayed in the vessel and the amount of air entrained with the water sprayed in the standpipe so that entrained air separates from the water and forms an air pocket inside the standpipe and there is a substantially complete oxidation of sulfur and sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions"}, {"pat_id": "US-4992181-A", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the method comprises the steps of spraying the water to be treated in the upper portion of a standpipe upon demand from an associated water system to cause a flow of water from within the standpipe through a bed of a catalyst for the oxidation of sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions and from the catalyst bed to the associated water system entraining air with the water sprayed in the standpipe and maintaining the water level in the standpipe that is required to enable the flow of water and entrained air therefrom to pass through the catalyst bed and to the associated water system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100607719-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "however in the present invention by using the underwater aerator 6 the aeration is made from the depth of the oxidation sphere 300 so even if the fluctuations in the water level is not affected by the sewage circulating the oxidation sphere 300 oxygen transfer is possible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100607719-B1", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "by using the underwater aerator 6 it is possible to effectively transmit oxygen to the water level fluctuation and by operating the stirrer 7 it is possible to prevent the maintenance of the flow rate in the oxidation sphere 300 and the precipitation of sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-6171480-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the distributed control system dcs is composed of multiple sensors transducers that convert environmental conditions into electrical signals communication multiplexers that convert the sensor s electrical signals into digital code computer hardware that can receive the transmitted signals from and to the multiplexers computer hardware that interfaces to the human user and computer software configured to provide a graphical interface for representing floor plans trending incoming data and trending historical data"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7745028-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "for example a water treatment device such as an ultraviolet oxidation device that irradiates the water to be treated with ultraviolet rays and decomposes organic matter contained in the water may be installed upstream of the electrodeionized water production devices 213 1 to 213 4"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7745028-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "for example a water treatment device such as an ultraviolet oxidation device that irradiates ultraviolet light on the water to be treated and decomposes organic matter contained in the water may be installed upstream of the electrodeionized water production devices 213 1 to 213 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971536-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "while injecting ozone into the raw water of 20 the inlet pipe 23 is opened and the ozone is introduced by closing the outlet pipe 26 to which the raw water is supplied to the filter unit 50 through the distributor 41"}, {"pat_id": "US-10501343-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the one or more sensors probes or instruments may include for example flow meters water level sensors conductivity meters resistivity meters chemical concentration meters turbidity monitors chemical species specific concentration sensors temperature sensors ph sensors oxidation reduction potential orp sensors pressure sensors or any other sensor probe or scientific instrument useful for providing an indication of a desired characteristic or parameter of water entering or exiting any one or more of the one or more unit operations"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102340325-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "reservoir installed in various types of buildings for each region to store drinkable drinking water ph sensor to measure hydrogen ion concentration ph tds sensor to measure total dissolved solids tds in water liquid medium including a turbidity sensor for measuring the turbidity of the liquid medium a temperature sensor for measuring the temperature of the liquid medium and a residual chlorine sensor for measuring the residual chlorine of the liquid medium it is installed in each of the storage tanks to measure the water quality of drinking water in the storage tank water quality multi item iot sensor the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank measured by the water quality multi item iot sensor hydrogen ion concentration ph temperature temp total dissolved solids tds residual chlorine residual chlorine turbidity ntu dissolved oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp and conductivity cond a gateway that collects and analyzes data of multi item measurement values of water quality for each water tank transmitted from the gateway and builds a big data database a water quality management platform server that is used for water quality analysis a real time water quality information monitoring device that receives water quality multi item measurement data for each water tank from the water quality management platform server and monitors the water quality status of each water tank in each area in real time the real time water quality information the terminal of the environment safety officer and each water tank that receives an alarm message generated when any one of the water quality multi item measured value data approaches or reaches the standard value from the monitoring device and sends a cleaning request notification for the water tank to the cleaning company terminal transmitting water quality multi item measured value data to the lora gateway through the lora modem and transmitting the water quality multi item measured value data transmitted through the lora modem to the real time water quality information monitoring device through the lte network in the gateway at preset intervals a communication device wherein the water quality management platform server includes an iot sensor data collection unit for collecting water quality multi item measurement value data for each water tank transmitted from the gateway and water quality multi item measurement for each water tank collected by the iot sensor data collection unit value data iot sensor data water quality analysis unit that analyzes the water quality condition including real time measurement values for each water quality measurement item and the change value of the real time measurement values based on water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank collected by a big data analysis unit and the iot sensor data collection unit that analyzes big data in relation to environmental factors and information analyzed by the iot sensor data water quality analysis unit and the big data analysis unit and a monitoring system interworking unit for integrated interfacing by transmitting to the real time water quality information monitoring device wherein the real time water quality information monitoring device receives iot sensor data receiving unit for receiving water quality multi item measurement data for each water tank from the water quality management platform server displays water quality status information according to the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank received from the iot sensor data receiver through a real time water quality information monitoring system and hydrogen ion concentration ph total dissolved in water through the water quality status board measured values for solid matter tds turbidity residual chlorine and temperature and water quality status information determined based on the measured values are displayed in real time and the real time water quality information monitoring system warns and cautions the water quality status for the entire area and normal displays regional selection information displays on site inspection status information schematized as one of water quality check purifier chlorine input and others displays residual chlorine status total dissolved solids tds status and hydrogen iot sensor data display unit that displays ion concentration ph status information by dividing it into warning caution and normal grades hydrogen ion concentration ph for each of multiple water tanks total dissolved solids tds turbidity ntu collected oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp conductivity cond temperature temp and residual chlorine residual chlorine for each item and the average standard of each item deviation and mean when the difference between the measured value for each item and the average among multiple storage tanks by calculating the deviation exceeds the standard deviation and the average deviation the water tank water quality comparison unit that transmits a danger warning of the water quality of the water tank to the environment safety officer when the difference between the measured value for each item and the average is greater than a preset x multiple of the standard deviation and a preset x multiple of the average deviation a water quality risk warning of the corresponding water tank and a sensor error suspicious warning are issued at the same time as the environment any one of the sensor error detection unit that transmits to the safety officer the website app linkage unit that links the web server or smart phone application to share the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank and the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank water quality abnormal signal notification unit that generates a water quality abnormal signal alarm when it approaches or reaches the reference value a water quality multi item iot sensor for water quality measurement is additionally installed in the iot sensor error monitoring unit and the water tank of a specific local institution or place so that the administrator can control the local institution or place where the water quality multi item iot sensor is added through the user interface and a monitoring addition generating unit that recognizes this when selected and additionally creates a target for monitoring the water quality of the water tank wherein the water tank transmits the location of the water tank closest to the user s location to the web server or the smart phone application"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200182581-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sewage or treated water is transferred to the transfer pump 14 and the rest uses a natural flow method due to water level difference.the sewage treatment apparatus of the present invention including a two stage contact aeration tank is capable of treating bod and ss to 5ppm or less using only a contact oxidation apparatus using microorganisms and it is excellent in treatment efficiency and does not require an additional physical and chemical treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100316688-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sewage or treated water is transferred to the transfer pump 14 and the rest uses a natural flow method due to water level difference.the sewage treatment apparatus of the present invention including a two stage contact aeration tank is capable of treating bod and ss to 5 ppm or less using only a contact oxidation apparatus using microorganisms and is excellent in treatment efficiency and does not require an additional physical and chemical treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "US-7678235-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "such controls can attenuate flow of inlet water and or other functions of the system such that production of product water is responsive to demand therefore"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889229-B1", "para_id": "para_102", "text": "while the present invention has been described in connection with the preferred embodiments thereof with reference to the accompanying drawings it is to be noted that various changes and modifications will be apparent to those skilled in the art.a sludge 1 body case 10 water tank 2 20 collection receptacle 201 201a first filter 202 drainage part 202a second filter 203 21 sludge filter net 22 first ultrasonic oscillator 3 water circulation part 30 water level sensor 31 water supply valve 311 water supply line 32 circulation pump 33 filtrate water supply valve 4 sludge transfer part 40 sludge detection sensor 41 suction pump 5 sludge drying unit 50 drying 501 opening door 502 filter installation part 51 sludge tank 511 heating means 52 third filter 53 cooling fan 54 supply damper 55 second ultrasonic oscillator 56 separation net 6 oxidation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959915-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore since the inlet 113a is installed spaced apart from the bottom of the wetland 10 the wetland 10 can always maintain a constant water level to function as the wetland 10 and also the water of the wetland 10 when this is drained the sediment deposited on the bottom of the wetland 10 can be prevented from being sucked toward the inlet 113a side as well as the habitat of the fish by amber and gravel and reverse contact oxidation by amber and gravel it is possible to purify 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102336536-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "however the use may be changed to a pump and tank for supplying chlorine dioxide or hydrogen peroxide for color removal of wastewater and oxidation of difficult to decomposable substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "air sludge deposited on the wall and the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration portion contact oxidation tank and the precipitation contact oxidation tank transfer to the sludge storage tank through the shaft but one side of the sludge storage tank and the supernatant water storage tank partitioned by the operation of the full width bank installed in the inlet distribution tank and the outflow storage tank and prevented from being closed by the sludge while being discharged from the inside of the contact oxidation tank at least one selected from the group consisting of an acid pipe for supplying dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to water and crushed stone having a porosity of 30 to 40 or plastic having a porosity of 80 or more in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and the settling part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the inlet 1 has a circular or rectangular shape as a part for collecting the polluted river water and sewage the effluent from the sewage treatment facility to flow into the contact oxidation tank and has a movable bank in the inlet distribution tank 2 18 weir is installed and the flow rate in the inlet distribution tank 2 is kept constant by adjusting the water level using the movable bank 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100794198-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a sewage separation tank 20 capable of separating non organic non degradable foreign matter by receiving sewage and temporarily storage and decomposition of organic solids a conversion flow rate adjustment tank 30 for sharing the mutual conversion characteristics of the physical function flow rate control and the biological treatment function so that the characteristics of the water quality can be developed as an exhalation function primary contact aeration tank 40 which is the main treatment process to maintain the aerobic phase characteristics of the microorganism by maintaining the active range of the microorganism to the heavy load primary settling tank 50 for firstly separating the desorbed sludge secondary contact aeration tank 60 which is an auxiliary treatment process having an increase in the food chain and natural purification characteristics between the microorganisms by obtaining a function having a preliminary preliminary function by affording a specific surface area for attachment of organic matter and purified microorganisms secondary settling tank 70 for separating the sewage sludge secondary sludge storage tank 80 and the sludge collected in the first and second primary settling tank 50 70 and a discharge tank 90 for discharging the supernatant after disinfection under the boundary wall 22 of the contaminant separation tank 20 and the switching flow adjustment tank 30 an opening 23 for preventing the accumulation of organic matter based on the change in water level and the agitation of the switching flow adjustment tank 30 contact switching frames 31 41 61 disposed in the switching flow rate adjustment tank 30 the primary contact aeration tank 40 and the secondary contact aeration tank 60 upper and lower contact contact frames 31 41 61 and mesh fixing nets 33 43 63 in the purification processing apparatus having the contact support frame 31 41 61 having at least one diffuser 36 44 64 at the bottom the switching flow rate adjustment tank 30 side has a first stage air lift 35 for solving the factor of reducing the amount of transport due to the water level and increasing the efficiency of the flow rate adjustment the water tank 34 connected to the upper end of the first stage air lift 35 has two stages to transfer the quantity of raw water to the air float so that the transfer effort for the first contact aeration tank 40 which is a later process is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100221225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the raw water from the raw water storage tank 1 is mixed with sand and anthracite as a filter medium through the transfer pump 2 the filter material 3 and the filter material are mixed with the anthracite and sand and the activated carbon or sequentially passed through the second filter 4 which is an activated carbon filter used singly to remove the floating substances and odors and the filtered water is passed through the stainless steel housing polypropylene material 1 5 a pretreatment step of finely filtering through a precision filter 5 used as a disposable or semipermanently backwashed cartridge having pores therein the filtered water filtered through the pretreatment step is passed through the raw water transfer pump 6 to the high pressure vessel made of stainless steel or reinforced plastic and it is made of cellulose acetate or polyamide material and has a diameter of 37 203 and a length of 298 1 524 sized reverse osmosis membrane which is formed of a hollow fiber type a plate type a spiral type or a rotational vibration type is sequentially introduced into a reverse osmosis separator 7 13 arranged in two stages in series the raw water flowing into the reverse osmosis separator 7 from the reverse osmosis separator 7 is prevented from being contaminated by the microbial propagation through the ultraviolet sterilizer 14 while passing through the reverse osmosis separator 7 the permeated water is stored in the washing tub 8 and is used to clean the surface of the reverse osmosis membrane of the reverse osmosis separators 7 and 13 by the washing pump 17 and is transferred to the treated water storage tank 9 in order to prevent the oxidation and scale of the filtration membrane with hydrochloric acid or sulfuric acid which adjusts the ph of the raw water through the feed tank 16 it is possible to automatically inject the disinfectant such as sodium hydrogencarbonate and sodium bisulfite or sodium sulfite station an osmotic phase the treated water stored in the treated water storage tank 9 which is a high pressure vessel made of reinforced plastic or polyethylene or stainless steel is introduced into the crush stone filter 10 by the supply fence 11 to replenish mineral components and a post treatment step of circulating the treated water to the treated water storage tank 9 and supplying it as potable water or water to the potable water via the water supply pump 12"}]</data>
