  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "the salt monitoring system of claim 13 wherein said sensor is configured for generating a signal at a regular interval and said controller is configured so that upon said received signal depicting one of a slower than average decline of salt level indicating low brine dosage an increased salt or water level and an increased rate of salt usage reflecting high brine dosage a leak to the brine tank or overfilling of the brine tank an alarm signal is generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "yet another feature of the present system is that the programmer is configured so that a measured signal return time distance from the salt level that is inconsistently shorter closer is an indication that the water level in the brine tank is higher than the salt level indicating further that the brine has not fully drawn due to a softener system leak or malfunction and an appropriate alarm is generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "11 the sensor 40 is configured for generating a signal in the form of the sensor beam 42 at a regular interval and the controller 62 is also preferably configured so that upon multiple signals being received by the receiver 44 over a plurality of regenerations that indicate a first phase 84 of regular salt consumption followed by a second phase 86 of increase signal level or water level indicating a leak to the brine tank 12 an alarm signal is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "for example when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120 even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "connect with the test tube of the tester and check the water level of the test tube for a certain time to determine whether the leak"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2099716-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the medium is supplied above the maximum water level of the container and the medium has not yet reacted with the mp and therefore no precipitation occur in the pipe and also resulting in a minimum impact from precipitations on the bearings 19"}, {"pat_id": "US-12270186-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "if the water level within housing 32 reaches the upper sensor 54 an alert signal may issue indicating that a leak or other serious error event is occurring"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "it can be very difficult to determine whether a reduced water level is due to evaporation only or also due to a leak"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1st embodiment concerns on invention of claim 1 comprising it is an early detection system which monitors abnormal water discharge or water leak by distribution reservoir water level abnormal fall monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0022 reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water supplying apparatus which uses a pressure air tank with function preventing air leak the present invention does not use a separate power supply it uses only the air pressure compressed and stored in the pressurized air tank to supply the water in the pressurized water tank quickly and to each household as well as when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level the present invention relates to a technology that automatically closes the flow path of the water cylinder to prevent air pressure from leaking to the outside thereby improving water supply"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is a water pipe leakage monitoring device that converts plant information into time series files it as a plant information actual value file in a plant information actual value file and detects whether a plant abnormality has occurred a water level plan prediction pattern on the day of water leakage monitoring is created based on the filed information actual value and a water leak occurrence water level pattern a water level upper limit value allowable pattern and a water level lower limit based on the water level plan prediction pattern a predicted water level pattern planning processing unit for creating a value acceptable pattern a predicted water level pattern memory for storing these patterns leakage monitoring calculation processing for comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water leakage occurrence water level pattern and comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water level upper limit allowable pattern or the water level lower limit allowable pattern and when the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence water level pattern it is determined that water leakage has occurred due to a break in the water pipeline and the actual water level exceeds the water level upper limit allowable pattern or the water level lower limit allowable pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0005 means for solving the problems in order to solve the above mentioned problems plant information is time series informationized filed as a plant information actual value in a plant information actual value file and a water level plan prediction on the day of water leakage monitoring based on the filed information actual value a predicted water level pattern plan processing unit that creates a pattern and creates a water leakage occurrence water level pattern a water level upper limit value allowable pattern and a water level lower limit value allowable pattern based on the water level plan predicted pattern and these patterns compares the predicted water level pattern memory that stores the actual water level on the day of leakage monitoring and the water level pattern on which leakage occurred and compares the actual water level on the leakage monitoring day with the water level upper limit allowable pattern or water level lower limit allowable pattern and a water leakage monitoring calculation processing unit for processing when the actual water level exceeds the leak generation water level pattern water pipes determined by the fracture and leakage occurs when the actual water level exceeds level upper limit allowable pattern or level lower limit allowable pattern it is determined that the abnormal operation of the apparatus to which equipment to a water conduit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here with regard to information on the equipment installed in the water pipeline that causes disturbance in water leakage monitoring information related to the water level plan prediction pattern of the equipment installed in the water pipeline is stored in the prediction water level pattern memory and the prediction the information in the water level pattern memory and the information in the plant information actual value file are compared and if there is a difference in the state of the equipment installed in the water pipeline the water level plan prediction pattern is corrected"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition when activated at a cycle of 1 minute information in the predicted water level pattern memory 11 and the plant information actual value file 14 regarding information such as the operating state of the pump and the open closed state of the inflow valve that become disturbances in water leakage monitoring the inside information is compared and if a difference occurs in the state the water level plan prediction pattern in the predicted water level pattern memory 11 is corrected"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "test whether or not there is a difference between the actual water level of the reservoir b28 at the current time and if there is a difference and the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence level pattern it is determined that there is water leakage and the water leakage print water leak occurrence information is issued to the output processing unit 8 and the alarm output processing unit 9"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 when the actual water level d on the leakage monitoring day of the distribution reservoir b28 has changed to the current time the leakage monitoring calculation processing unit 12 compares the actual water level d with the leakage occurrence water level pattern e"}, {"pat_id": "US-10184221-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in the event of a leak of the impoundment area if the water level observed is falling relatively quickly and unrelated to the operation of the water control device for gate weir movement this could alert a user that the area needs to be checked for an impoundment leak such as the breach of a impoundment wall"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of hardware configurations of a sensor device 210 and a monitoring device 200 fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of a functional block configuration of a water leakage detection system 20 according to an embodiment fig.it is a figure which shows the concept of a static water pressure a dynamic water pressure a static water level and a dynamic water level.it is a figure which shows an example of the dynamic water level before and after water leakage occurrence and its normal vector.it is a figure which shows an example of the variation change_quantity of the normal vector before and behind water leakage occurrence.it is a figure which shows an example of the block of the piping network used for simulation.8 is a diagram showing an example of the amount of change in the normal vector on the dynamic water level distribution when water leakage occurs in the pipe network 800"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "in one aspect the water leakage detection system 20 uses the measurement data obtained from the sensor device 210 installed at each branch point on the pipe network or part of the pipe to calculate the dynamic water level at each monitoring location a dynamic water level distribution can be created from the calculated dynamic water level"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480163-B2", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "unsuccessful delivery may be indicative of a pump failure a valve failure a misconnection of the fluid conduit a leak in the fluid conduit a leak in one or both of the reservoirs or a trailer reservoir water level sensor failure"}, {"pat_id": "US-10894724-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "the sensor configuration in a wastewater treatment system such as system 12 may be as follows each pipe has a leak sensor conductivity sensor each tank has a water level sensor mechanical level sensor every electronic component in the system including pumps has a voltmeter and an ammeter all water tanks have level sensors and treated water has the requisite water quality sensors to determine if treatment is happening"}, {"pat_id": "US-10894724-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the sensors may use any suitable communication protocol to allow the system to be flexible for example the following communication protocols would work for the previously listed sensors clarity sensors usb cdc turbidity ammeter and voltmeter sensors modbus water level sensors rs485 and leak sensors sdi 12"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6432810-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "thus according to the present embodiment since the unitized power generation apparatus 100 and the pump 200 are mounted on the vehicle m the installation work and the removal work are simplified compared with the conventional construction method and the construction period the cost of the construction period can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4441460-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "2 the method for identifying the location of the water leak in the water channel 20 is that the at least the downstream end 21 of the target area 20 a of the water channel 20 is partitioned by a corner drop 31 as an example of a partition plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "in addition the processor 110 determines that a leak has occurred in the sewage treatment plant tank when the measured water level change is high compared to the measured power consumption and the measured water pressure based on the third correlation and the manager terminal 200 may transmit a warning message for checking and responding to water leakage in the sewage treatment plant water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321244-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the present invention has been invented to solve the above problems the leakage preventing device is installed in the connection portion of the raw water supply pipe and the reservoir connected from the outside of the connection pipe for connecting a plurality of water filters the fresh water stored in the reservoir by having a structure that operates according to the water level when a certain amount of fresh water is loaded into the reservoir tank the buoyancy member of the leak prevention device is lifted and at the same time the inflow of raw water supplied from the outside can be prevented in advance to prevent leakage of the water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7244310-B2", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the output of the supply pump 3 is finely adjusted so that the values of the flowmeters fi 1 and fi 2 become the values before the leak test step s37"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "monitor screen which is attached to said cable s second end said cable s semi rigidness further provides limited means for inserting said camera lights and housing into said pipeline via access hole one and aiming generally in the direction of the flow route to access hole two and controlling the attitude or aim of the remote camera lens said remote camera also has on its anterior surface a means such as an eyelet or recessed peg eccentrically located whereon the attached lanyard thereto and with the combination of said semi rigid camera cable and said lanyard attached to said camera housing manipulating said cable and lanyard to position said camera lens anterior of or beneath said rubber test ball with said lens aiming at said test ball e attaching another said lanyard reel end to said test ball which has anterior or posterior ends by means such as a spring clip or pneumatic hose coupling or camera access cable dummy coupling or a loop formed on said lanyard end f connecting said test ball s posterior end to a pneumatic hose which allows the test ball to be inflated thereby and which hose has first and second ends and is connected on said first end to a supply of pneumatic air pulling on said lanyard s service end thereby inserting at least one inflatable test ball into said pipeline via access hole two said test ball which has anterior and posterior ends and said lanyard s reel end is connected to said test ball s anterior end and the test ball is inserted via access hole two in said pipeline wherein when said test ball is manipulated by virtue of the retrieval lanyard and pneumatic hose to a point in a pipeline which said test ball is inflated to produce a temporary passageway seal or blockage in said pipeline by virtue of said test ball s exterior surface coming in contact with said pipelines interior wall and by virtue of its ball shape g attaching a mechanism for measuring the amount of cable or lanyard that has passed into or out of a pipeline wherein said mechanism has a numerical display which can be directly read h inflating said test ball to produce a seal or blockage in the pipeline being tested h filling the vertical pipe being tested with test fluid or water and by viewing the monitor checking to see whether the test ball has effectively sealed off the pipe from the test fluid or water column above the test ball i repositioning the test ball or manipulating it to produce a satisfactory seal if required j viewing the column of water via the access hole two into which the water or test fluid was pumped into the pipe being tested for stability k determine that the pipeline segment thus tested is leak free if stability of the water level is positive or leaking if the water level recedes into the pipeline l repositioning the camera and the test ball to check further down the pipeline if the prior step indicated no leakage or further up the pipeline if the prior step indicated leakage m continuing to narrow the search for the leak by eliminating sections of non leaking pipe segments by the technique described above"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "still by having at least one high point where water levels can be viewed to either remain constant or recede or by using two test balls wherein the camera can be located between the test balls and the water level stability viewed from within the pipe segment defined between the two test balls by the monitor most domestic systems may be inexpensively and thoroughly checked for leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "still by having at least one high point where water levels can be viewed to either remain constant or recede or by using two test balls wherein the camera can be located between the test balls and the water level stability viewed from within the pipe segment defined between the two test balls by the monitor most domestic and industrial sewer drainage systems may be inexpensively and thoroughly checked for leaks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100768328-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "therefore even if rainwater present in the soil around the underground reservoir 10 further penetrates underground or evaporates due to a subsequent drought the water inside the underground reservoir 10 does not penetrate or evaporate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101252155-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "thus it is a way to detect the leakage through the change in the water level of the test tube"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480824-B2", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "further water either from a leak condition or a non leak condition condensation may accumulate in the bottom pan 200 and trigger the leak sensor 1200 when the water level in the bottom pan 200 rises approximately by the distance d e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480824-B2", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "accordingly water that accumulates in the bottom pan may contact the leak sensor 1200 via the opening at the bottom portion 1195 of the sensor housing 1000 when the water level rises to the elevation at which the leak sensor 1200 is disposed in the sensor channel 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480824-B2", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "accordingly the water level in the bottom pan 200 must rise above the thickness of the bottom annular flange 1606 to trigger the leak sensor 1700"}, {"pat_id": "US-10480824-B2", "para_id": "para_107", "text": "accordingly the water level in the bottom pan 200 must rise above the thickness of the bottom annular flange 2114 to access or contact the leak sensor 1200 and trigger a leak condition"}, {"pat_id": "US-6627073-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "consequently it is possible to more reliably prevent the possibility that the water level on the upstream side of the gas separating filter in the electrolytic tank is too high because the gas separating filter is clogged causing the water to leak or the possibility that the water level on the downstream side of the gas separating filter of the electrolytic tank is too low so that air is sucked into the water returned to the pool from the electrolytic tank through the water treating path making the water in the pool muddy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_64", "tex