  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102780153-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the remote monitoring system of the filter assembly for installation in a water pipe according to the present invention comprises a water storage tank in which water is stored inside a water pipe is provided on one side to discharge the water stored inside to the outside and a filter assembly is provided inside the water pipe to filter out harmful pests and foreign substances from water flowing along the water pipe and a plurality of filter assemblies are provided in a group form a water level sensor provided on one side inside the water storage tank to detect the water level of the water a pressure sensor provided in the water pipe to detect the flow pressure through the water pipe when the water is discharged and a control unit which calculates the degree of blockage of the filter assembly as the pressure difference between the water head pressure detected by the water level sensor and the flow pressure detected by the pressure sensor based on the result detected by the water level sensor and the result detected by the pressure sensor and transmits the calculated data to an integrated control unit which performs remote monitoring from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102780153-B1", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "more specifically the control unit 400 is configured as a computing platform that processes digital signals using a microcontroller and uses data p \u03b3h transmitted from a water level sensor 200 as a governing function and compares it with data transmitted from a pressure sensor 300 to analyze the obstruction of the fluid flow passing through the filter assembly 120 determine the degree of blockage of the filter assembly 120 and transmit the analyzed data in real time to the integrated control unit 500 so that the manager can check the replacement cycle and operating plan of the filter assembly 120 in the integrated control unit 500"}, {"pat_