ormation control unit 40 through the internet hub 50 and displays them on a monitor located in a building where the pipe p is installed a local management control unit 60 the water level value h and the pipe blockage state s transmitted from the sensor information control unit 40 through the internet hub 50 are the total number of pipes the number for each state the pipe status list the date and contents of the pipe inspection and the sensor error internet data center 70 which is a main server that receives and stores the communication error notification when it occurs and checks the error itself as a computer device that receives the water level value h and the pipe blockage state s stored in the internet data center 70 and displays them on a monitor the remote management control unit 80 located at a remote location outside the building where the pipe p is installed the sensor information control unit 40 measures the water level value h as the number of times of the water level duration frequency value lasting at a certain percentage for a certain time and includes it in the water level information the local management controller 60 displays a water level duration frequency value for each period in which the water level value h is maintained at a certain percentage for a certain time period the local management control unit 60 is a computer and monitoring device installed inside or near a building so that a building manager can grasp water level information including water level values and collection schedule information and high middle low positions for each pipe section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a pipe blockage prediction system a central control system that can predict the possibility of blockage in each section of the pipe by measuring the water level in each section of the pipe by utilizing the fact that the water level in the vicinity of the pipeline where sediment is accumulated and the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the water level information measures the number of times that the time when the pipe line is measured as the medium or high level is detected for a certain period of time or more and the local management control unit or the remote management control unit displays the pipeline blockage state in color according to a predetermined criterion so that the manager can there is an excellent effect of intuitively grasping the state of pipe clogging due to the accumulation of sediment for each section of the pipe.1 is a conceptual diagram of a pipe clogging prediction system according to an embodiment of the present invention 2 is a conceptual diagram of water level measurement when there is no pipe clogging of the pipe clogging prediction system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the local management control unit 60 is a computer and monitoring device installed inside or near a building so that a building manager can grasp water level information including water level values and collection schedule information and high middle low positions for each pipe section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the technical spirit of the appended claims.p pipe r conduit m sediment h water level value s pipeline blockage 10 water level sensor 20 sensor board 30 data collection device 40 sensor information control unit 50 internet hub 60 local management control unit 70 internet data center 80 remote management control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "that is when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320 the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622378-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "depending on the size the size of the carriers collected in the collection unit 600 are different the cover 400 is an upper cover 401 covering the upper part of the belt 310 and it includes a lower cover 402 that covers a portion of the lower belt 320 other than the belt receiving portion 325 and the belt receiving portion 325 is exposed to the outside air the upper cover 401 is a drip hood 410 located at the rear end of the drip unit 200 and it is located on the upper side of the belt upper part 310 at the rear end of the drip hood 410 and includes a plurality of upper hoods 420 whose starting portion is inclined in the moving direction of the conveyor belt 300 the lower cover 402 is a rinsing hood 430 located at the beginning of the lower cover 402 in the moving direction of the conveyor belt 300 and it includes a return hood 440 located at the end of the lower cover 402 the raw materials include freeze dried microorganisms pva polyvinyl alcohol and peg polyethylene glycol and the carrier is a microbial carrier for wastewater treatment the heat storage unit 800 receives heat from the heating unit 130 and the heat exchanger 650 and provides it to the heating blower 500 so that the heating blower 500 generates heated air and the inside of the cover 400 is maintained at 115 to 120 c if the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 is higher than the preset water level or the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is lower than the preset drop height the plurality of drop holes 211 warns of blockage in any one or more of the