the contact carrier 333b for increasing the activated sludge suspended solids mlss and increase the nitrification rate and do reduction a nitrification water conveying pump 333c for conveying nitric oxide to the anoxic tank 320 as a previous step a flow rate rectifier 341 for allowing the treated water to flow into the primary sedimentation tank 340 and a overflow device 342 for allowing the treated water to flow into the storage tank 410 which is the next step a sludge collecting device 343 for collecting sludge the sludge collected is guided to the sludge drawing pipe 344 and the sludge drawing pump 345 to the end of the sludge drawing pipe 344 to convey the sludge to the anaerobic tank 310 of the previous process or to process the excess surplus the storage tank 410 has a stirring device for agitating 411 which can stir the treated water introduced into the interior slowly a second operation control system 412 for controlling only the control water to be supplied to the rapid reaction tank 420 which is the next step the inlet of the rapid reaction tank 420 has a horizontal water flow control panel 422 having a reddish elbow type inlet 421 for rapid mixing of the treated water and the flocculant and the upper and lower portions in the body center an stirrer 423 to simultaneously perform upstream and downstream stirring a chemical input unit 424 for injecting a coagulant having an increased cohesive force on the rapid reaction tank 420 an outflow separation wall 425 for guiding the outflow water to a flocculation tank 430 which is the next step the flocculation tank 430 is a slow stirring device for coagulation 431 the final agglomerate is an outflow separation wall 433 for outflow to the secondary settling tank 440 which is the next process the secondary settling tank 440 rectifies the flow rate as a final flocculation floc and flows the treated water separated from the flow rate rectifier 441 for dividing the treated water and sludge into the disinfecting discharge tank 510 which is the next process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101383594-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in addition the variable water level screen filter according to the present invention is configured to filter the contaminants contained in the sewage first by the filter member only to be discharged through the drain hole thereby improving the filtration efficiency for the contaminants and the size of the drain hole as it secures the maximum it improves the discharge efficiency of the treated water thereby increasing the filtration process speed of the sewage and effectively preventing the blockage of the drain hole caused by the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-7294257-B2", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "in this case blockage of the mesh 13 will lead to reduction in the water level in the downstream container thus activating the float switch and pump 17"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102634268-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "this is to control device failure due to pipe blockage by blocking the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "is dried and f the conveyor belt 300 continues to move so that the portion of the conveyor belt where the drop was located is located at the bottom of the drop unit 200 again g1 if the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 is higher than a preset water level or the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is lower than the preset drop height the plurality of warning of blockage in one or more of the drip holes 211 and g2 the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 exceeds the preset drop height or the shape of the bottom surface of the drop detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is different from the preset shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622379-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition a supply level sensor s1 that detects the water level of the raw material is located in the supply unit 100 and a drop shape sensor s1 that detects the height of the dropped drop and detects the shape of the bottom surface of the drop on the conveyor belt 300 s2 is located and a carrier sensor s3 that detects the height of the collected carrier is located in the collection unit 600 and after step f g1 the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 if the water level is higher than the preset water level or if the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is lower than the preset drop height it warns of blockage in one or more of the plurality of drop holes 211"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622379-B1", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "if the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 is higher than the preset water level or the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is lower than the preset drop height the drop used is less than the normal amount"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "monitor screen which is attached to said cable s second end said cable s semi rigidness further provides limited means for inserting said camera lights and housing into said pipeline via access hole one and aiming generally in the direction of the flow route to access hole two and controlling the attitude or aim of the remote camera lens said remote camera also has on its anterior surface a means such as an eyelet or recessed peg eccentrically located whereon the attached lanyard thereto and with the combination of said semi rigid camera cable and said lanyard attached to said camera housing manipulating said cable and lanyard to position said camera lens anterior of or beneath said rubber test ball with said lens aiming at said test ball e attaching another said lanyard reel end to said test ball which has anterior or posterior ends by means such as a spring clip or pneumatic hose coupling or camera access cable dummy coupling or a loop formed on said lanyard end f connecting said test ball s posterior end to a pneumatic hose which allows the test ball to be inflated thereby and which hose has first and second ends and is connected on said first end to a supply of pneumatic air pulling on said lanyard s service end thereby inserting at least one inflatable test ball into said pipeline via access hole two said test ball which has anterior and posterior ends and said lanyard s reel end is connected to said test ball s anterior end and the test ball is inserted via access hole two in said pipeline wherein when said test ball is manipulated by virtue of the retrieval lanyard and pneumatic hose to a point in a pipeline which said test ball is inflated to produce a temporary passageway seal or blockage in said pipeline by virtue of said test ball s exterior surface coming in contact with said pipelines interior wall and by virtue of its ball shape g attaching a mechanism for measuring the amount of cable or lanyard that has passed into or out of a pipeline wherein said mechanism has a numerical display which can be directly read h inflating said test ball to produce a seal or blockage in the pipeline being tested h filling the vertical pipe being tested with test fluid or water and by viewing the monitor checking to see whether the test ball has effectively sealed off the pipe from the test fluid or water column above the test ball i repositioning the test ball or manipulating it to produce a satisfactory seal if required j viewing the column of water via the access hole two into which the water or test fluid was pumped into the pipe being tested for stability k determine that the pipeline segment thus tested is leak free if stability of the water level is positive or leaking if the water level recedes into the pipeline l repositioning the camera and the test ball to check further down the pipeline if the prior step indicated no leakage or further up the pipeline if the prior step indicated leakage m continuing to narrow the search for the leak by eliminating sections of non leaking pipe segments by the technique described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_136", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in the filtration process the contaminants penetrate deeply into the media and increase the fouling collection layer in the media thereby reducing the frequency of maintenance due to the blockage of the media"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6952930-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "an excessive increase in tmp causes a malfunction of the device such as damage to the filtration membrane 1 so it is desirable to constantly monitor the tmp to grasp the degree of fouling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171869-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "that is when the pumping of the stream water 2 collected in the sump 120 continues while the collection efficiency of the screen 110 is lowered due to the blockage of the lower bed 4 the water level in the sump 120 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "method of monitoring drainage systems of rainwater reservoirs wherein a drainage pipe with which a throttling member is associated is associated with the rainwater reservoir and wherein the flow of sewage through the drainage pipe serving to divert sewage from the rainwater reservoir can be restricted to a predetermined nominal value characterised in that the flow through the drainage pipe is monitored to determine whether a predetermined excessively high value has been exceeded and or in that if the flow through the drainage pipe is restricted in a controlled manner to a predetermined nominal value monitoring is carried out to determine whether excessively rapidly succeeding changes in the direction of travel by the throttling member are effected by the controller and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether the water level in the rainwater reservoir or in a feed channel preceding the rainwater reservoir exceeds a predetermined depth while at the same time a predetermined low value for the flow through the drainage pipe is fallen below resulting in a blockage of the drainage pipe at this water level and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether permanent tightening of the throttling member is occurring and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether the actuator of the throttling member is overloaded and if so the throttling member is transferred into a safety position preventing the nominal value of the flow through the drainage pipe from being exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "monitoring arrangement for drainage systems of rainwater reservoirs for carrying out the method according to one of claims 1 to 3 characterised in that the monitoring arrangement 25 comprises first monitoring means which respond in a predetermined manner if a predetermined excessively high value of the flow through the drainage pipe is exceeded and or second monitoring means which respond in a predetermined manner to excessively rapidly succeeding changes of direction of travel by the throttling member caused by the controller if the flow through the drainage pipe 13 is restricted in controlled manner to a predetermined nominal value and or third monitoring means which detect if the water level in the rainwater reservoir or in a feed channel 11 preceding the rainwater reservoir exceeds a predetermined depth while at the same time a predetermined low value of the flow through the drainage pipe 13 is fallen below implying a blockage of the drainage point with this water level and or fourth monitoring means which respond to permanent tightening of the throttling member and or fifth monitoring means which respond to overloading of the actuator of the throttling member 14 and as a result of this response trigger a transfer of the throttling member into a safety position preventing the nominal value of the flow through the drainage pipe from being exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "if both yes signals are present at the and gate 41 at the same time then there is a blockage in the drain pipe 13 because otherwise the flow through the drain pipe 13 would be significantly greater at such high water levels and there will therefore be a fault message indicating this blockage reports and or triggered a security process"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "controlling the restricting device by the tail water in this way has the advantage of improved throttle element regulation since in the event of a disturbance in the sewage discharge the water level in the shaft or gallery drops immediately and the throttle element opens fully"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "calculating means for judging the water level and the relationship between the increasing and decreasing tendency of the water level which can be expressed as various patterns based on the relative positional relationship between the water level sensor installation point and the blockage occurrence position when the snowfall channel is closed and the relationship before and after the start of the change"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a water level sensor having a plurality of closed circuit resistances disposed at predetermined intervals in a flowing direction of a snowfall ditch monitor each measurement data obtained from two water level sensors adjacent in the direction sequentially calculate the water level difference between the two water level sensor installation points calculating means for determining the tendency of the water level difference to increase or decrease and the relationship between the water level fluctuation start time of the water level sensor installation point and the water level sensor installation point a storage means for storing a combination of a water level increase decrease tendency and a relationship before and after the start of fluctuation which can be represented as various patterns by a relative positional relationship with the combination pattern a blockage position specifying unit that specifies the position of the snowfall groove where the blockage has occurred by referring to the storage unit and a plurality of blockage occurrence signals according to the level of the water level difference together with the specified blockage position data"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "if the water level does not return after the elapse of the predetermined time and it is determined that the blockage is not resolved no in step 811 an instruction is issued to output an alarm of a higher rank to each of the water level monitoring panels i to iii 8 13 are closed or the pump 4 is stopped to stop the discharge to the snow drift 15 and a process for avoiding overflow from the snow drift 15 is performed step 813"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "failure of the discharge pump or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5213295-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a decrease in pump discharge due to an air lock or suction blockage is determined based on the actual water level at the expected arrival time"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5213295-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in the prior art the upper limit water level arrival time when water supply is completed is predicted and a decrease in the actual pump discharge amount air lock or suction blockage is determined according to the water level state at the predicted time so it cannot be determined until the expected time is reached there is a drawback that it takes time to determine the decrease in the actual discharge amount of the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1 the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to a wastewater purification system and in particular a compressed air supply means for producing and supplying compressed air to a filtration filter formed in a floating separation tank and at the same time a water level detector water level detector it is equipped with a discharge device to achieve a smooth filtration operation of the filtration filter during the purification of wastewater and wastewater and to prevent the blockage of the purification system and to improve the filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above problems an object of the present invention is to monitor the water level change of the storage tank by the water level detector installed in the storage tank to quickly and accurately check whether the filtration filter is blocked and at the same time filtering by supplying compressed air to the lower part of the filter it is possible to provide a waste water purification system such as to improve the treatment efficiency of the wastewater and reduce the maintenance cost by preventing the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the additional installation of the conveying pipe and the pump complicates the overall device structure makes it difficult to quantify the sewage transfer can cause the blockage of the pipe during long term operation and can not maintain the high water level due to the upper conveying pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the conventional internal conveying pipe and an anoxic tank conveying pump are removed to eliminate the blockage of the device and the pipe due to the sludge s deposition"}]</data>
