  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at this time the middle layer water and the lower layer water is lower than the temperature of the surface water due to the difference in density to cool the water stored in the intake tower to form a low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "accordingly the feed water is supplied to the filtration membrane portion 3 and the feed water is first filtered through the reverse osmosis membrane not shown to remove the corrosion promoting component"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "in this case the water level in the production water tank 5 reaches the water level l even after the operation time set to sufficiently remove the corrosion promoting component in the feed water as described above to prevent the deterioration of the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100688965-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "an additional portion is formed and the effluent purified through the purifying unit is moved to a water level control tank through a pore tube formed at the lower end of the limestone layer and discharged to the outside through a discharge port formed at an upper end of the water level control tank and thus the acidic rock drainage is conventionally the present invention relates to a slope acid rock drainage treatment facility that prevents serious environmental pollution engineering damage namely concrete corrosion cracks in the bottom of the structure due to sulfate expansion and slope instability at the incision"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100688965-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "by moving to the water level control tank through the discharge port formed in the upper end of the water level control tank to the outside conventional environmental damage by acid rock drainage engineering damage namely concrete corrosion sulphate expansion by the bottom of the structure the purpose of this is to prevent cracking and slope instability at the incision site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100688965-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the enclosed suspended solids settle and are the final purification.as described above the slope acid rock drainage natural purification treatment facility of the present invention the acid rock drainage flows into the treatment tank formed on the cut slope or the fill section slope the purification part composed of an organic material layer and a limestone layer to clean the acid rock drainage it is formed and the effluent water purified through the purifying unit is moved to the water level control tank through the hole pipe formed in the lower end of the limestone layer and discharged to the outside through the discharge port formed on the upper end surface of the water level control tank by conventional acid rock drainage it is effective in preventing severe environmental pollution engineering damage namely concrete corrosion cracks in the bottom of the structure due to sulfate expansion slope instability at the incision"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2556401-Y2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pump for pumping a water receiving tank 1 and a makeup water tank 2connected with a pumping line 4 into which a pump 3 is inserted and connected to a hot water boiler 5hot water storage tank 6 is connected with hot water storage line 9 and water supply line 8.and an upstream position of the water supply pump 7 in the water supply line 8and the makeup water tank 2 are connected by a makeup water line 10 the hot water storage tank 6 and the load 11 are connected to a hot water supply line 13 andconnected by return line 14 the hot water storage tank 6 and the replenishmenthot water supply piping system connected to the water tank 2 via a relief line 15in the formation the membrane type deaerator 20 is inserted into the pumping line 4.and the water in the makeup water tank 2 isa water level detection sensor 16 for detecting the water level the output signal from the sensor 16 is determined and the pump 3 andand a control device 1 for controlling the operation of the membrane type deaerator 207"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200167943-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "according to one feature of the automatic water supply device of the present invention both the discharge valve and the water level valve installed in the water tank are made of plastic and rubber packing to prevent rust or corrosion and to have durability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "therefore since water is supplied to the water tank 10 without opening and closing the lid secondary pollution of the water tank 10 contaminated by contaminated air occurs when water is supplied in the conventional water tank which opens the lid to supply water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8650892-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a system for providing drinkable water created from purified potable water derived from an atmosphere said system comprising a housing having an air inlet port and an air exhaust port a refrigerant compressor at least one multi way solenoid operated refrigerant control valve a controller for monitoring and for controlling said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve and other electrical subsystems within the system an evaporator wherein said evaporator has fins for maximizing surface area contact and heat transfer with ambient air wherein said fins are coated with non toxic anti corrosion materials that comply with applicable regulatory food standards for paint or a ptfe protective layer said coating promoting rapid collection of condensate water and wherein said evaporator can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive chilled refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to chill air passing across said evaporator fins and wherein said evaporator can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive hot refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to defrost said evaporator fins an anti static anti mold air filter wherein said anti static anti mold air filter is installed upstream of said evaporator a condenser for the system s refrigeration cycle a fan or blower wherein said fan or blower circulates ambient air from said air inlet port through said anti static anti mold air filter across said evaporator said condenser then out said air exhaust port a collector with highly polished surfaces a preliminary filter to remove any smell of condensate water and ammonia wherein said preliminary filter is comprised of activated carbon or zeolite a condensate collection tank wherein said highly polished surfaces of said collector facilitate gravity flow of condensate water into said condensate collection tank and wherein said condensate collection tank is equipped with a water level detector said water level detector and controller causing said evaporator to stop receiving chilled refrigerant at a predetermined high level setpoint at least one water pump a particle filter for filtering particles to protect an intake of said at least one water pump a water purification filtration assembly to filter out bacteria viruses and heavy metals as well as to remove unwanted smells comprising at least one activated carbon filter at least one reverse osmosis filter wherein said reverse osmosis filter has an aperture of less than or equal to 0.0001 \u03bcm and wherein said reverse osmosis filter can be back flushed such that a waste water can be directed to said collector via a three way valve that is controlled by a waste water proportion controller at least one zeolite filter wherein said at least one water pump pumps condensate water from said condensate collection tank through said water purification assembly a purified water collection tank for collecting purified water wherein said purified water collection tank is equipped with a water level detector said water level detector and controller causing said at least one water pump to stop