"KR-102286436-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "including the step of operating s50 the sensing unit includes a plurality of sensors for detecting the state of sewage including flow rate water level dissolved oxygen amount metal component acidity and chemical component and is connected to the control unit through wiring and grounding the management server receives the detected values detected from a plurality of sewage treatment systems and converts them into data searches for optimal outliers according to the detected values from the data and derives the operating conditions of the pump and the aeration unit which are the optimal operating state values the control unit controls the operation of the pump and the aeration unit by preferentially applying the operating status value transmitted from the management server over the preset operating status value the detection unit 10 includes a plurality of sensors 11 for detecting the state of sewage a communication module 12 for transmitting the detection values of the sensors 11 to the controller 20 through wireless communication and a plurality of sensors 11 through the detection module 13 which detects whether an abnormal operation occurs normally and transmits whether an abnormal comprising a correction unit 14 for correcting the abnormal state of the sensor 11 with a control signal transmitted from the control unit 20 or for detecting the state of sewage by operating the sensor 11 provided in advance the detection module detects a malfunction of the sensor due to deterioration and corrosion of the ground wiring that causes insulation resistance breakdown electrical noise or output instability the detection value of the sensing unit the state value of the sensing unit and the operation status of the pumps and aeration unit are converted into data in the management server and the pump and the aeration unit are automatically operated under the optimal operating conditions corresponding to the detection value of the sensing unit and in the sewage treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102500623-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the contaminated air and contaminants inside the wastewater treatment tank 100 are removed and then exhausted to minimize environmental pollution and secondary infection and the sterilizing liquid according to the amount of infected wastewater introduced through the water level sensor 140 it relates to an infected wastewater treatment system that is supplied according to the measured water level increase or decrease inside the wastewater treatment tank 100 so that the infected wastewater can be smoothly treated so that the sterilized wastewater can be smoothly discharged to a wastewater treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "for this reason there is no fear of corrosion of the electrode due to electrolysis even if a direct current voltage is applied between the electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373478-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drain device of manholethe present invention relates to a non power drainage device of the manhole and more specifically to detect the inundation through the water level sensing buoy in the presence of the manhole inside and operate the ejector installed in the connection pipe line and the manhole pipe with a non powered water in the manhole the present invention relates to a non powered drainage device of a manhole that is quickly discharged to the outside to prevent corrosion and breakdown of facilities due to flooding inside the manhole and to maintain a clean state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373478-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention when a flooding occurs in a manhole the opening and closing valve is automatically opened by a buoy rising and falling by the water level to quickly discharge the flooded water in the manhole to the outside by the suction force generated through the ejector thereby preventing corrosion or failure of the facility due to the flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "therefore in the non power source immersion prevention system of the present invention the opening and closing valve 300 is automatically opened by the access port 200 that ascends and descends by the water level when the flooding occurs in the manhole and the water is flooded in the manhole by the suction force generated through the ejector 500 water can be rapidly discharged to the outside through the suction pipe 400 to prevent corrosion or breakdown of the facility by flooding and it is possible to immediately cope with the flooding by the person without any operation the installation cost is reduced as compared with the drainage method using the conventional pump and the pause time is set during the operation by the amount of water flowing into and discharged from the water collection container 630 provided at the upper portion of the water inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101699031-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method according to claim 1 a case fixing groove is formed so as to be interchangeably fitted and fixed in a sliding manner along the wall surface of the groove portion of the overflow wall constituting the overflow groove wherein the filter case is made of a corrosion resistant metal a handle ring is formed on the filter case wherein the filter medium is formed of any one selected from a palm mat a palm mat or filtration geotextiles wherein a height of a central portion of the filtration member sandwiched in the flow channel is formed so as to correspond to an average water level of the sediment separation water flowing over the flow channel and flowing into the flow rate adjustment tank wherein the size of the filter material pores of the filter material is within a range of 70 \u03bcm to 100 \u03bcm"}, {"pat_id": "US-6214204-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "the salt solution was circulated through the electrodes through the honeycomb cells via a peristaltic pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "thus corrosion and rust thereby preventing the deterioration of the life of the wiping valve.1 is a longitudinal sectional view of an installation state of a water level shield according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-7383157-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the system of claim 1 wherein said aged pipe evaluation factor data includes at least one among a sewer based buried area a road a buried year a damage state a soil condition an inner corrosion degree a basic construction method a soil condition a pipe diameter a joint method the number of divides a underground water level an i i ratio and a pipe flow speed state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a method of monitoring and controlling a low carbon permeable ecological structure consisting of a plurality of corrosion resistant piles a plurality of horizontal framing frames in the form of spacers an ecological block for water purification and an ecological block for fishes and fishes first the low carbon permeable ecological installed at a predetermined position of the structure 100 receives the detected data from a plurality of sensors 210 to detect the conductivity water quality water temperature or quantity of river water by wire or wireless"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315306-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 wherein a flow meter which is mounted at a predetermined position on a line connecting the dissolution tank and the water supply means to maintain the level of the dissolution tank an alarm means located at one side of the flow meter to notify the outside of the water level change corrosion water quality control system for water purification treatment to reduce the corrosion of the water supply pipe including a screen for removing the turbidity induced material is provided at the water inlet of the dissolution tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485292-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "it is arranged to be close to one side and this one bactericidal electrode can be used as a water level detection electrode so that a humidifier capable of miniaturizing the electrode installation space can be provided while reducing the cost"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634146-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in preferred embodiments a high water level sensor 20 may comprise two corrosion resistant electrodes that may be placed in a sump 99 above the regular water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185905-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "however when the gate 51 is not normally opened due to corrosion of the rotating shaft 53 or interference with foreign matter the level sensor 54 maintains a state in which it is in contact with the compression spring 80"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101040678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the operation of the open circulating cooling water system having a cooling water storage tank of the cooling tower in which the replenishment water is supplied to maintain a constant water level and supplying a phosphate based anticorrosive to reduce the corrosion degree if the cooling water concentration in the cooling water storage tank is below a predetermined control value the cooling water is continuously circulated until the predetermined control value and the concentrated operation is performed so that the ca ion component included in the cooling water reacts with the po 4 component of the anticorrosive agent to prevent corrosion of the coating on the metal surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101040678-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "corrosion reduction method of the open circulating cooling water system through the concentrated operation of the present invention for achieving the above object is provided with a cooling water storage tank of the cooling tower is supplied with supplemental water to maintain a constant water level to reduce the corrosion degree in the operation of the open circulation cooling water system to supply the system anticorrosive"}, {"pat_id": "US-7678235-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "such controls can attenuate flow of inlet water and or other functions of the system such that production of product water is responsive to demand therefore"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2556399-Y2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "0003 therefore in recent years a pipe corrosion prevention apparatus using a membrane type deaerator which is high in safety and low in cost has been adopted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101118626-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "conventional water supply control of simple tap water has been adjusted automatically by using a manual method operated by a person or by automatically filling a line between a water tank and a well but when a failure occurs due to corrosion of the buried line because of the fact that it is not known before digging up all the land where the problem occurred several different automatic water level control methods have been developed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175882-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above problems the object of the present invention is to supply the square wave of the ac type to the water level sensor and to eliminate the voltage difference between the both ends of the water level sensor to prevent sensor corrosion by electrolysis in addition it is to provide a water level detection device of the water purifier that can accurately detect the water level of the water purification tank to prevent the overflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175882-B1", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "according to the water level detection device of the water purifier according to the present invention as described above it is possible to supply a square wave of the ac type to the water level sensor and to eliminate the voltage difference between both ends of the water level sensor to prevent sensor corrosion by electrolysis it has the excellent effect of accurately detecting the water level to prevent overflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321349-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as in the conventional case it is possible to detect the amount of water introduced through the inlet by using a flow meter but the flow meter has a high price and the zero point is inaccurate due to corrosion and breakage causing problems in performance"}]</data>
</edge>
