  <data key="d6">["enable", "place", "receive", "collide", "include", "dispose", "make", "operate", "purify", "deleteaccorde", "apply", "solve", "position", "prevent", "turn", "rise", "supply", "correspond", "connect", "mount", "use", "stop", "introduce", "accord", "cut", "actuate", "calculate", "sense", "locate", "devise", "close", "cause", "maintain", "have", "control", "improve", "send", "minimize", "contact", "transmit", "follow", "complete", "check", "fix", "configure", "instal", "activate", "flow", "sterilize", "can", "do", "discharge", "be", "protect", "determine", "detect", "describe", "provide", "come", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "on the other hand in the lower fixing structure 70 of the water intake tower 12 when the water level is located on the bottom the fixing rod 76 in accordance with the corresponding position so that the impact preventing member 32 provided on the buoyancy member 26 is placed the vertically fixed structure 78 is installed to prevent breakage of the buoyancy member 26 and to prevent the screen 38 from colliding with the bottom of the reservoir to prevent damage and damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "abnormalities in the septic tank include for example aeration stop due to blower failure aeration failure due to clogging of the diffuser blower overload aeration failure due to air pipe breakage sewage underground penetration due to water leakage discharge piping and discharge destination abnormalities such as water level rise and water level rise due to abnormal discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "water tank a sterilizing lamp having an arc tube a discharge electrode provided at both ends of the arc tube and a quartz tube for protecting the arc tube the sterilizing lamp being installed inside the water tank a level sensor provided in the sterilizing lamp a controller electrically connected to the level sensor and an inflow valve for opening and closing an inflow pipe for introducing purified water into the water storage tank the water level sensor senses that the water is introduced into the sterilizing lamp by the breakage of the sterilizing lamp inside the water storage tank the water level sensor comprises at least a part of which is disposed between the arc tube and the quartz tube so as to be disposed at a position lower than the lower end of the discharge electrode wherein the at least one of the first electrode and the second electrode contacts the at least one of the discharge electrode and the water flowing into the sterilizing lamp by the breakage of the sterilizing lamp when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp the controller activates the inlet valve to close the inlet tube sterilization water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method according to claim 1 wherein when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp the controller turns off the power of the sterilizing lamp sterilization water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the sterilizing water purifier of the present invention comprises a water tank a u type sterilizing lamp mounted inside the water storage tank a level sensor provided in the sterilizing lamp and a controller electrically connected to the water level sensor wherein the water level sensor senses that water is introduced into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp inside the water reservoir and the controller controls the power of the sterilizing lamp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to the above described aspect of the present invention all of the discharge electrodes can be positioned on the water surface of the water tank by using the u type sterilizing lamp so that even if water is introduced due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp and the water level detection sensor senses the water before the water is contacted with the discharge electrode so as to cut off the power of the sterilizing lamp so that the discharge electrode which receives the high voltage can not come into contact with the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilization lamp due to breakage of the sterilization lamp is configured to actuate the inlet valve to close the inlet tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "as described below when the water level sensor senses the water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp the controller 140 is configured to operate the inlet valve 150 to close the inlet pipe 151"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "therefore the water level sensor 130 is configured to detect at least the water level sensor 130 in contact with the water flowing into the sterilizing lamp by the breakage of the sterilizing lamp at least before the discharge electrode"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "according to the above described aspect of the present invention all of the discharge electrodes can be positioned on the water surface of the water tank by using the u type sterilizing lamp so that even if water is introduced due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp so that it can not be contacted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "accordingly when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp the controller 140 operates the inlet valve 150 to close the inlet tube so as not to be supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201275-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the conventional problems as described above to improve the structure of the water level control valve so that the predetermined raw water is discharged from the water level control valve and or check valve until the operation of the pump is completed in addition the purpose of preventing the overload of the pump cracking of the pipe and or breakage of the seam by stopping the operation of the pump by detecting the occurrence of the back flow pressure in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and an object of the present invention is to accurately check the water level by sensing the water level and temperature in the storage tank through the water level sensor and the temperature sensor to send to the storage tank remote water level management can effectively control the quantity and use the water level sensor as an ultrasonic sensor to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and to prevent the water level from being incorrectly detected due to breakage or malfunction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101630395-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the control unit 100 receives data on the operation state of the air compressor 30 and the air discharger 40 transmitted from the detection circuit unit 50 and the real time pressure value and the water level transmitted from the pressure sensor 10 a real time water level value transmitted from the sensor 20 is calculated by an operation state analysis algorithm and a water shock is prevented by determining whether the water shock equipment is operating normally according to the operation result in the control unit 100 when the water level rises during a periodic change that does not follow the pressure change by applying the analysis algorithm the compressed air leaks due to the breakage of the air supply line portion wherein the water hammer is a water hammer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100813181-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "and a relief valve 16 which is a stabilizer for maintaining the set pressure and deformation and breakage of the pneumatic water tank 37 due to the abnormal pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321349-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as in the conventional case it is possible to detect the amount of water introduced through the inlet by using a flow meter but the flow meter has a high price and the zero point is inaccurate due to corrosion and breakage causing problems in performance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100907502-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "however such a conventional manhole water level and flow rate detection device has a problem such as inflow of abnormal water due to breakage due to aging of the pipe or clogging of the pipe at the rear end of the flow rate detection unit so that the sewage in the manhole is not normally discharged"}]</data>
</edge>
