 sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4019893-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "a pipe shaped water level detection unit a pressure guiding pipe having one end connected to the water level detection unit a pressure air supply means for supplying a substantially constant air pressure to the water level detection unit via the pressure guiding tube and rotation of the pipe schema pressure switch that detects when the tip of the overflow section and the water level detection section which are one side of the opening is submerged under the water surface and detects the predetermined depth from the water surface of the settling basin when the air pressure in the pressure guiding tube reaches the predetermined pressure with the door to form the water level detection unit by a material having a low wear coefficient characterized in that bent downward such that the water surface substantially perpendicular to the tip portion of the water level detection part when entering the water surface water level detection device in the scum removing apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118704-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "as an example the floating overflow plate 322 may be formed in the form of a flat front overflow type belt and may be formed to surround the groove upper portion according to the fixed lower wall wear groove and the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118704-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "however the pontoon wall wear wear 320 of the present invention always moves the upstream wear load of the sedimentation basin 300 constantly while the floating wall plate 322 surrounding the wall wear wear channel 321 automatically moves in the vertical direction according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101799993-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "therefore it should be understood that the above described embodiments are to be considered in all respects as illustrative and not restrictive the scope of the invention being indicated by the appended claims rather than the foregoing description all changes or modifications that come within the scope of the present invention should be construed as being included within the scope of the present invention.100 multifunction holding tank 110 sewage inlet 120 screen 130 outlet 140 sludge diaphragm structure 200 bioreactor 210 anoxic 211 anoxic tank inlet 212 first perforated plate diaphragm structure 220 221 exhaust system outlet 230 the living organ 300 settling tank 310 settling tank inlet 320 flocculant tank 330 coagulant pump 340 settling tank outlet 350 vortex diaphragm structure 360 swash plate 370 overwater wear 380 sludge outlet 410 first air lift line 420 second air lift line 430 gravity sedimentation line 500 blower 600 controller 700 disinfection tank 710 disinfection tank inlet 720 chemical tank 730 drug pump 740 second perforated plate diaphragm structure 750 water level sensor 760 disinfection tank outlet 800 discharge pump 810 first discharge line 820 second discharge line 900 air vent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100888713-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the horizontal wear 22 is formed to correspond to the outlet of the settling basin 10 to flow in one direction of the settling basin 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101765868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the replenishing water space 711 a branch plate 710 formed with a hollow 713 for communicating the fire water space 712 with each other opening and closing means 720 connected to the branch plate 710 so as to be located in the water repellent space 712 and opening closing the hollow 713 and and a wear prevention member 732 provided around the hollow 713 to prevent wear of the periphery of the hollow 713 due to contact with water supplied from the makeup water space 711 to the water 730 the fire extinguishing water space 712 so that the level of the water contained in the water repellent water space 712 can be increased quickly with a relatively small space as compared with the make up water space 711 so that the water can be smoothly discharged through the water pipe 210 the branch plate 710 the upper and lower ends of the front and rear ends abut the inner front and rear surfaces of the fire water tank 140 and the upper surface thereof is spaced apart from the inner upper surface of the fire water tank 140 water overlapping in the replenishing water space 711 or the water repellent water space 712 can be introduced into another space the opening closing means 720 an opening closing door 721 rotatably connected to the branch plate 710 such that an upper portion thereof is located above the hollow 713 and and a weight 722 disposed under the opening closing door 721 the weight 722 may include and the water pressure of the makeup water space 711 is maintained at a predetermined value by the water pressure of the water conserving space 712 and the weight 722 so that the opening closing door 721 can be closed as the water pressure in the makeup water space 711 becomes equal to the water pressure in the fire water space 712 in addition the opening closing door 721 when the water pressure of the water stored in the replenishing water space 711 is stronger than the water pressure of the fire water stored in the water reservoir space 712 the lower portion is rotated upward to be opened so that the water stored in the replenishing water space 711 when the water pressure of the fire water stored in the water repellent water space 712 is higher than the water pressure of the water stored in the replenishing water space 711 so that the fire water stored in the fire water space 712 is prevented from flowing out into the makeup water space 711 to maintain a certain water level in the fire water space 712 the water level holding unit 700 and a sensing sensor 740 for sensing the opening of the opening closing door 721 the control unit 600 the shutoff valve 142 is opened in a state in which the opening closing door 721 is opened according to a detection signal of the detection sensor 740 so that water can be replenished into the replenishing water space 711 the supply of water to the replenishing water space 711 is stopped by interrupting the shutoff valve 142 in a state where the water shutoff valve 721 is closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101765868-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "therefore the water level holding unit 700 can keep the water level of the water repellent water space 712 constant so that the water can be smoothly supplied when an emergency such as a fire occurs.1 apartment 2 equipment for protection and safety of fire fighting water 5 floor 60 firefighter 61 primary constant 62 secondary constant 65 heavy water 66 leachate 110 wall 120 slab 130 rooftop 140 fire tank 150 heavy water tank 160 leaching correction 170 an elevated tank 210 a water supply pipe 220 second loan 310 collecting pipe 320 vacuum pump 400 410 heavy water suction pipe 420 purified water discharge pipe 430 settling 440 transfer pipe 450 hydrocyclone 500 fire detector 600 control unit 700 water level maintenance unit 710 branch plate 720 opening closing means 721 opening closing door 722 730 anti wear member 740 detection sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11536276-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "running multiple pumps at once is quite inefficient as for example running two pumps at once requires 100 more energy than one pump while only pumping 50 more water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357600-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "water level control to adjust the water level so that all parts of the electrode and the plurality of electrode set 20 to the electrolytic module 10 which is a kind of frame of cylindrical or cylindrical shape and two electrode plates installed inside the module as a set it is composed of a wear 30"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1866487-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "advantageously the computing part according to a further development comprise a floating element so that it is moved upwards by a rising water level and thereby releases the previously retained in the lower vorsperrenposition solids for effective discharge of solids over the outflow surge again"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wear type rainwater chute device characterized in that to prevent the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "as shown in the accompanying drawings in this embodiment the lower end of the sewage pipe 1 in contact with the river or the coast is hingedly coupled to the wear 100 erected or laid down and the sewage pipe in front of the wear 100 the vehicle collection pipe connection pipe 200 branched to the side of 1 the drive means 300 for rotating the wear 100 and the wear 100 are interlocked to open and close the entrance of the vehicle collection pipe connection pipe 200 sluice gate 400 sensors s1 s2 installed at the rear of the weir 100 to detect reverse flow of river water or seawater and the water level of ou water flowing down the sewage pipe by being installed in front of the weir 100 a control unit 500 that opens and closes the wear 100 and the sluice 400 in an interlocking manner by operating the driving means 300 by sensing a sensor s3 s4 for detecting a signal from the sensors s1 to s4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "therefore the sensor s3 s4 for detecting the water level when there is no detection signal the wear 100 is kept in an erect state and an alarm for separate inspection is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344711-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "by controlling the water level of the flow control valve device 20 at the inlet part and the overflow wear 50 at the outlet part it is possible to prevent the outflow of fine flocs by preventing the uneven distribution of solid liquid separated sedimentation sludge by uniform inflow distribution of the inflow activated sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand the quantitative waste water is discharged quantitatively and discharged into the aeration tank 50 equipped with the oxygen supply nozzle 57 by the water level difference through the first wear 31 via the flow rate control anoxic tank 40 the coarse sewage flows through the weir 35 into the sedimentation filtration tank 20 in which the sludge s is precipitated in a downward upward flow by the induction pipe 93 in the sedimentation filtration tank 20 and the treated supernatant is the discharge vessel"}]</data>
