  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102715270-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "accordingly the protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the description of the claims and the scope of equivalents thereof.1 spawning area 2 water supply area 3 egg transfer unit 10 storage tank 20 drinking water pipe 30 drinking water pump 40 washing nozzle 50 washing pipe 60 washing pump 70 chlorine dioxide gas generating unit 80 gas pipe 90 water pipe a0 water supply valve b0 concentration measurement unit c0 water level measurement unit d0 contamination measurement unit d1 projector d2 camera e0 intensive cleaning section e1 guide rail e2 concentrated cleaning nozzle e3 concentrated cleaning pipe e4 concentrated washing pump e5 drive unit 110 1st tank 120 2nd tank 130 3rd tank 210 1st reaction tank 220 second reaction tank 230 third reaction tank 310 1st gas discharge pipe 320 2nd gas discharge pipe 330 3rd gas discharge pipe 400 integrated pipe 710 1st metering pump 720 2nd metering pump 730 3rd quantitative pump 1110 1st auxiliary tank 1120 second auxiliary tank 1130 third auxiliary tank 1200 level sensor 1300 alarm 1400 reservoir tank 1500 aeration device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101089024-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "this is because the cavitation phenomenon is prevented when the non suction single stage volute pump is used and pumping suction may occur even at low tide so durability and pumping efficiency are excellent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inf