specting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133174-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in the untreated water inlet line 20 may be provided with a transfer pump 60 for pumping and supplying untreated water"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "simultaneously therewith the battery operated audible alarm which is electrically connected to a water sensor on the conduit senses the rising water and makes a circuit thus causing the alarm to sound to notify the building occupant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 2 when the water level of the water tank is a high water level when the ball tower rises to block the pipe while the pressure in the water pipe increases to detect the increase in the amount of current according to the load rise of the well pump when the first well pump this is a device that measures the rated current amount except the starting current and sets the high water level of the water tank based on this and turns off the well pump according to the weight of the current"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100437342-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a two way transmission and reception wireless data signal using a dedicated frequency between a motor pump of a water supply and a remote intake tank for storing water so that the water level can be controlled while checking the operation state in the intake tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102092239-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "generating a deep learning model using a first water level value and determining a pump operation value in a pressure field for a second water level value received in a subsequent cycle based on the abnormal time point based on the deep learning model it may include steps.according to the present invention when the communication state with the water level meter installed in the reservoir does not satisfy a predetermined level based on the deep learning model generated using the water level value previously received from the water level meter the pump operation value in the pressurization field is determined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101102443-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present application as a means for solving the above problems as a water treatment method for obtaining purified water suitable for drinking water or industrial water for the target water selected from the treated water selected from river river water ground water wastewater treatment plant after pretreatment of the water to be treated in a sulphate denitrification tank or an ultrasonic electrolysis tank an ozone containing water is made and supplied to a high precision filtration tank to remove residual contaminants while passing through the filter bed of the biofilm separation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879208-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a flow and ph regulating tank which regulates the water level of the incoming raw water and adjusts the ph to 5.0 to 7.0 for the optimum condition of the chemical input the characteristics of the inflow water whose ph is adjusted and the water level is stabilized in the flow rate and ph adjusting tank a flocculating tank for adding the mixed mineral to the flocculant and mixing the flocculant with the flocculant to perform chemical treatment while mixing the flocculant a coagulation tank for increasing the floc size of the flocculant produced in the rapid a sedimentation tank and a mixed mineral weighted flocculant recovery and circulation apparatus for continuously reusably separating recovering and circulating the weighted flocculant from the sludge sediment separated from the sedimentation tank and a circulation apparatus for filtering the chemical water treated or precipitated in the sedimentation tank a filtration tank for finally removing the flocs that have not been removed and a filter in the high speed water treatment apparatus using a coagulant adding to mineral mix containing the treated water tank the mixed mineral weighted flocculant recovery and recycling apparatus includes a centrifugal hydrocyclone hereinafter referred to as quot hydrocyclone quot that receives the sludge precipitated in the lower part of the sedimentation tank 1400 and supplies the sludge to the high pressure pump 1410 a centrifugal separator 1500 using a hydrocyclone and a stirring separator 1600 constituting an agitating collecting tank in series after passing through the centrifugal separator the agitator 1600 includes an inlet pipe 1610 through which some mixed minerals and sludge not separated from the centrifugal separator 1500 are introduced and an inlet pipe 1610 formed to receive the inlet pipe therein an inner hole 1620 an agitator 1630 rotatably installed at the center of the inner hole block an outer hopper 1640 surrounding the inner hole block and having a square shape a sludge discharge pipe 1650 installed to discharge the sludge and a mixed mineral discharge pipe 1660 connected to a lower portion of the outer hopper to discharge mixed minerals wherein the mixed mineral is used as a weighted flocculant high speed water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0418572-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "by increasing the water level 34a and the pressure generated thereby a vertical flow of the purified water in the space between the walls of the inner pot 42 and the pot like extension 41 is then promoted from top to bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a temporary storage tank for chemicals having a cover installed on the unit one side is connected to the drug storage space of the drug temporary storage tank and the other side is connected to the connection pipe connected to the flocculation settler or the immersion well via the injector the drug discharge pipe is installed on the pipeline chemical discharge pump a discharge side bypass pipe bypassing the chemical discharge pipe and having a discharge side bypass valve in the middle a supply side bypass pipe bypassing the supply pipe and having a supply side bypass valve in the middle a control device electrically connected to the leak detection sensor a ph sensor a chemical discharge pump and a supply side shutoff valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "47 a body 31 having a space 46 is provided an opening closing ball 48 for closing and opening the water supply port 43 by buoyancy is introduced into the space 46 when water flows in or out a shock absorber 49 is provided below the open close ball 48 to provide a shock absorbing action when the open close ball 48 falls an upper lid 42 having a water supply inlet 41 is installed on the upper side of the body 47 wherein a lower cover 50 for closing the space 46 is provided below the body 47 to prevent the opening closing ball 48 and the shock absorber 49 from being separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention relates to an unmanned water supply system for supplying groundwater to a water tank by controlling the motor pump by sensing the pressure in the water tank by sensing the pressure applied to the water supply pipe the water level of the water supply pipe is instantaneously released by supplying air to the water supply pipe when the water level of the water storage tank reaches the low water level detection hole formed in the second branch pipe requiring the water supply replenishment so as to detect the low water level when the water level of the water storage tank reaches a high water level that requires stop of the water supply the water level sensing unit is operated to close the water supply port by the operation of the opening closing ball of the water level sensing unit to block the groundwater flowing into the water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to another embodiment of the present invention an air opening closing unit is provided on the side of the low level sensing hole formed in the second branch of the level sensing device and the same structure as the high level sensing unit is provided.the present invention relates to an unmanned water supply system for watering underground water to a water storage tank by controlling a motor pump for unloading groundwater by sensing the pressure applied to a water supply pipe and reading the water level the water level of the water supply pipe is sensed by instantaneously releasing the pressure of the water supply pipe by supplying air to the water supply pipe and when the water level of the water storage tank reaches the high water level requiring the water supply stop the water supply port is closed the water level sensor in the water tank can be accurately sensed by detecting the pressure change applied to the water supply pipe by providing a simple structure of the water level sensing device for blocking the pressure of the water supply pipe not only can a malfunction be significantly reduced but also a semi permanent number by keeping the present invention relates to unmanned water supply apparatus to contribute to improving reliability.1a and 1b are block diagrams of a conventional unattended water supply device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490133-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "disinfection treatment system according to the present invention by checking the amount of breeding water supplied through the main transfer pump 3 in real time with the scale bar 17 it is possible to carry out the simultaneous transfer operation of breeding water and infectious organisms more efficiently such as a quantitative supply type treatment cycle of breeding water tailored to the treatment capacity of 1"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5479252-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "and by arranging the discharge port 41 at the lower end of the drainage pipe 4 connected from the pumping pipe 3 via the separation tank 2 so as to be always submerged under the water surface in the sand basin the piping of the system during operation the equipment was watertight lifting pipe 3 separation tank 2 since the water inside the pipe conduit consisting of drainage tube 4 can be kept filled with the state can the principle of the siphon in pumping operation of the entire system it is sufficient if there is a head higher than the water level loss and the pressurized water pump 5 has an advantage that a pump with a low head and a small output is sufficient"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "when the height of the water level due to an increase in the amount of contaminant collecting is detected to be higher than a predetermined value when the artificial filter media is cleaned a separate outlet pipe is formed to allow the blower to spray the high pressure air and the washing water is supplied by the pump to perform backwashing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "when the height of the water level due to an increase in the amount of contaminant collecting is detected to be higher than a predetermined value when the artificial filter media is cleaned a separate outlet pipe is formed to allow the blower to spray the high pre