he turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "abnormalities in the septic tank include for example aeration stop due to blower failure aeration failure due to clogging of the diffuser blower overload aeration failure due to air pipe breakage sewage underground penetration due to water leakage discharge piping and discharge destination abnormalities such as water level rise and water level rise due to abnormal discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101427989-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "at this time it is possible to increase or decrease the hydrogen generation and the circulation time according to the quantity so that the hydrogen dissolved amount can be prevented from rising excessively by checking the ph value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101427989-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "in the extraction mode when the water supply button of the operation button 13 is pressed the electrolysis unit 100 is kept in the off state while the first pump p1 is in the locked state and the first solenoid s1 is also closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101427989-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "on the other hand at the detection level of the first water level sensor w l 1 the first pump p1 operates until the idle rotation is detected for 5 seconds or more to clean the flow path and the electrolysis unit you can go out completely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "accordingly the feed water is supplied to the filtration membrane portion 3 and the feed water is first filtered through the reverse osmosis membrane not shown to remove the corrosion promoting component"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102537944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of fresh water tanks that naturally fall from a natural water supply source and receive and store water including a jurisdiction server for remote control of the freshwater tank in the forest fire fighting water management system the plurality of fresh water tanks are installed on one side of the mountain and one of the two connected to the water supply pipe is located above the other one the fresh water tank includes a water tank for receiving water therein including evacuation space where people can be located the two fresh water tanks connected by the water supply pipe are connected by two water supply pipes among the two water supply pipes a one of them includes a valve on one side so that the water contained in the upper water tank is dropped by the opening of the valve and the water is transferred to the lower water tank b the other one by using a pump the water contained in the lower freshwater tank is transferred to the upper freshwater tank when the valve is opened for the transfer of water a collision between water transferred from the upper water tank to the lower water tank and water transferred from the lower water tank to the upper water tank is prevented from occurring the water supply pipe is buried in the ground to prevent the water supply pipe from freezing and interfering with water supply between each water tank the jurisdiction server by selectively controlling the water supply pipe of the water supply source the valve of the water supply pipe of the fresh water tank or the pump of the water supply pipe of the fresh water tank according to the water level information of each fresh water tank it is possible to adjust the water to each fresh water tank by building a database based on the identification information of the freshwater tank and the identification information of the mountain in advance and providing it as information it is easy to use the water in the freshwater tank necessary for firefighting in case of disaster the fresh water tank a hose connector connected to the water tank is configured on the outside the hose connector is wound by a large reel and the fire hose connected to the hose connector is coupled to the flight means the hose connector of the fresh water tank is coupled to the fresh water tank by extending the pipe downward from the lower flange part and securing a separation space between the lower flange part and the upper surface of the fresh water tank to provide a plurality of ball valve plates arranged in the circumferential direction the hose connector is configured to be rotated by the rotation of the ball valve so that the movement of the fire hose connected to the hose connector is flexible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200385155-Y1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore the raw water is smoothly filtered by the suction pump 40 by the suction pump 40 and then a small amount of the treated water is discharged and each separator of the membrane unit 11 is suspended by the air supplied from the broa 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102772397-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore when necessary the processor 80 can operate the circulation pump 40 to supply water to the humidifying member 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102772397-B1", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "therefore the plurality of nozzles 72 are always in an open state and the amount of water supplied to the distributor 71 by the circulation pump 40 can be set to be greater than the amount of water discharged from the distributor 71 to the humidifying element 75 through the plurality of nozzles 72"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2099716-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the medium is supplied above the maximum water level of the container and the medium has not yet reacted with the mp and therefore no precipitation occur in the pipe and also resulting in a minimum impact from precipitations on the bearings 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100431512-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "in the optimized communication state the local server reads registers in block units to increase the overall data transfer efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101004130-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water level control system water level controll system the present invention relates to a water level control system and more particularly it is possible to prevent the contamination of groundwater by sealing the upper part of the groundwater well as well as to control the operation of the pump by sensing the water pressure formed in the upper part of the groundwater well"}, {"pat_id": "US-5351337-A", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "a second novel feature of the water system of the present invention is the inclusion of at least two low pressure detection switches 54 and 56 respectively to protect the system from potential damage due to low water level or pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-9765508-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the hewitt invention is a device to collect and dispense roof rain water comprising a container to collect water having an opening a pump to drive the water out of the container a debris disposal mechanism a sensor to measure the water level wherein the pump is activated at a specific water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a second water level sensing unit 140 for intermittently operating the circulating pump 150a in accordance with the set water level value of the second water level detection unit 140 to operate the circulation pump 150a while continuously operating the primary electrolysis cell 130a so that the circulating sterilizing material is repeatedly electrolyzed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "at this time the primary electrolysis panel unit 100 is provided with a level sensor 111 for measuring the water level of the brine tank 110a while opening and closing the solenoid valve 112 in accordance with the set water level to replenish the time a first water level detecting unit 110 a salt water supply unit 120 configured to pump the brine in the brine tank 110a through a brine injection pump 120a to supply the primary electrolysis cell 130a a first power supply unit 130 for applying electricity to the positive and negative plates of the primary electrolysis cell 130a to electrolyze the brine supplied from the brine supply unit 120 as the brine electrolyzed by the first power supply unit 130 is converted into sterilized material and stored a level sensor 141 is installed to measure the level of the stored sterilized material and the salt water supply unit 120 is set according to the set level value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "a second water level sensing unit 140 for intermittently operating the circulating pump 150a in accordance with the set water level value of the second water level detection unit 140 to operate the circulation pump 150a while continuously operating the primary electrolysis cell 130a so that the circulating sterilizing material is repeatedly electrolyzed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "on the other hand the drug generating unit 150 is interlocked according to the set water level value of the second water level detection unit 140 to operate the circulation pump 150a while the circulating sterilizing material is repeatedly electrolytically electrolysis it is formed to continuously operate the cell 130a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472622-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the present invention is to solve the above problems an object of the present invention is to operate the pump only at a predetermined predetermined time to reduce the number of start of the pump can prevent the durability degradation and failure of the pump due to frequent starting of the pump it is to provide a method and apparatus for adjusting the water level of a water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472622-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "in addition the method and the apparatus for adjusting the water level of the water storage tank according to the present invention accumulate the data on the operating time of the pump in the state connected with the water level sensing means and operates the pump during the operating time of the pump calculated from the information including the data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the water supply control device of claim 1 wherein further comprising a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value wireless automatic water level control system further comprises"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the pressure pump in operation is controlled to stop due to a drop in the primary pressure in the water pipe connecting the pressure pump and the primary side reservoir and the water level in the secondary side is below the specified water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100466336-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thereby increasing the amount of distilled water condensed water filled in the evaporator brine heater 1 thereby raising the water level"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604858-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "primary microbial baths 120 220 320 the primary to tertiary oxidizing aeration tanks 130 230 and 330 that separate ozone into treated water and suspended solids containing oxidizing organic matter by injecting ozone into the seawater wastewater supplied from each of the primary to tertiary microorganism tanks 120 220 and 320 and the primary to tertiary oxidation aeration tanks 130 230 and 330 are adjusted to control the water level thereby allowing floating substances including oxidized organic substances to be discharged upward and the treated water is primary to tertiary microorganism tanks 120 through the circulation pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "primary oxidation aeration process processing unit 100 secondary oxidation aeration process processing unit equipped with a secondary filter tank 210 for secondary removal of foreign substances in seawater wastewater supplied from the primary oxidation aeration process processing unit 100 200 a tertiary oxidation aeration process processing unit 300 and a tertiary oxidation aeration equipped with a tertiary filter tank 310 for tertiary removal of foreign substances in seawater wastewater supplied from the secondary oxidation aeration processing unit 200 the discharge treatment unit 400 provided with a fourth filter tank 410 for filtering the sludge remaining in the seawater wastewater supplied from the process processing unit 300 the primary to tertiary oxidation aeration process processing units 100 200 and 300 remove contaminants b