ter supply pressurizing unit for receiving and storing the ground water taken in and stored in the ground water storage tank for temporarily storing and then applying pressure by the pressure pump and discharging the ground water through the water supply pipe to the water pipe and an intermediate pressurizing part installed at a predetermined distance on the water line to temporarily store the water flowing through the water line from the water supply and pressurizing part and then applying pressure by a pressurizing pump and discharging the water through the water outlet pipe the water supply a body for receiving and storing groundwater through a water inlet pipe installed in the ground from the ground water storage tank a water intake pipe installed in the body to receive groundwater stored therein a pressurizing pump installed inside the water intake pipe to pressurize the ground water a water outlet pipe connected to the water intake pipe and discharging the ground water pressurized by the pressure pump to the water pipe a slug filter installed in the form of a plate having a plurality of perforations to block the bottom of the body and installed to penetrate the water inlet pipe and the water intake pipe to filter the slug accumulated on the bottom of the body a slug cleaning pipe inserted into the body from the outside and having a lower end penetrating the slug filter a water level sensor mounted inside the slag cleaning pipe and a power panel for controlling the operation of the pressure pump by the level detected by the level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175882-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "drive control of the water supply valve 57 receives the control signal output from the control means 125 to supply or block the supply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore it is characterized by controlling and managing the operation of the pump by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal drainage reservoir water level of the