ater circulated in the auxiliary reservoir and opening the secondary drain valve when the time expires detect the contamination concentration from the water quality sensor close the solenoid valve open the primary drain valve pump the membrane water when the auxiliary reservoir is full and secondary when the timer expires"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100191863-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "therefore when the water level of the auxiliary reservoir 60 is detected by the water level sensor 61 the controller 80 turns on the boosting pump 64 and the water supply valve 66 and turns off the solenoid valve 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101432516-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as a result the operation differential pressure is reduced to less than half of the operation differential pressure generated in the membrane of the conventional membrane bioreactor so that the filtration process can be performed without using the pressurization or decompression pump and the operation cost can be remarkably reduced"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5450286-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "then immediately after the drive of the water pump 30 is stopped the control unit 15 calculates the flow path loss \u03b4f and the water leakage coefficient k s309"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5450286-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "in that case the operator starts or stops driving the water pump 30 while checking the water level"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "failure of the discharge pump or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052946-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopp