having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is below the minimum value turning on the three way valve to connect the other discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is above the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joins including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 if the charge level of the battery is below the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "the method of claim 9 wherein the fine contaminant continuous recovery apparatus further comprises a water level detecting means the water level detecting means both ends are vertical pipe shape connected to the upper and lower ends of the outer processing tank 100 respectively the sensing unit 310 at the upper end of the water level sensing means is fixed a reed switch 320 is provided in the lower bottom surface of the sensing unit 310 two terminals 330 of the reed switch 320 a buoy 340 in the vertical pipe of the water level detecting means and the magnet 350 is attached to the upper end of the buoy 340 sensing means consisting of is provided so as to be able to move freely inside the vertical pipe of the water level sensing means with a control unit 600 for receiving a signal of the water level detected from the two terminals 330 of the reed switch 320 the control unit 600 according to the on off of the reed switch 320 the above described flow regulating valve and the treatment chemical pump control signal sc of the treatment chemical providing unit 500 microcontaminant continuous recovery apparatus characterized in that configured to provide the pump control signals vic and voc provided in the contaminated treated water supply pipe 130 and the purified treated water recovery pipe 140"}, {"pat_id": "US-10377649-B2", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "the fermentation tank is preferably washed between different batches of microbial growth to remove attached growth at the waterline which may cause build up of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102336536-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "however the use may be changed to a pump and tank for supplying chlorine dioxide or hydrogen peroxide for color removal of wastewater and oxidation of difficult to decomposable substances"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5213295-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a decrease in pump discharge due to an air lock or suction blockage is determined based on the actual water level at the expected arrival time"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5213295-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in the prior art the upper limit water level arrival time when water supply is completed is predicted and a decrease in the actual pump discharge amount air lock or suction blockage is determined according to the water level state at the predicted time so it cannot be determined until the expected time is reached there is a drawback that it takes time to determine the decrease in the actual discharge amount of the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101702294-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case the groundwater well having a multi stage inflow hole on the circumference surface so as to correspond to the water level of the groundwater the basket is placed on the floor for the management so that the deposit of the pollutant and the soil sludge is made in the basket a portion of the groundwater discharged from the pump is supplied through the purifier to prevent contamination due to the groundwater contamination in the underground water congestion zone between the bottoms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100836904-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it consists of a drive 22 for driving the unit 23 the display unit 23 is a filter loss amount display unit 24 for displaying the loss of each filter 5 stored by the wired terminal 70 connected from the outside in percentage and when the filter 5 is replaced filter replacement display section 25 in which the lamp is selectively flashed when the lamp is reached the water level level display section 26 in which the lamp is selectively lit according to the water level level of the water tank 6 and the driving of the pump 3 and it consists of a drive display unit 27 the lamp is turned on when the water leakage and a water temperature display unit 28 for displaying cold and hot water the output terminal of the mpu 21 is installed on one side of the facet 8a is connected to the facet lamp 9 for providing a refreshing feeling when the water is discharged the water level sensor 30 is installed in the water tank 6 at the input end of the mpu 21 and senses the water level in four stages and the water leakage sensor is installed on the bottom surface of the case 1 to detect water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a water pressure control encoder switch for adjusting the intensity of the water output the temperature of the water ph concentration the operation button to receive the output time the water level sensor for measuring the water level an input unit configured of a temperature sensor measuring a temperature of water a pump for raising the water to the shampoo ware a heater for heating the water to a temperature set by the operation button an electrolysis tank for ionizing the water and performing electrolysis to match the ph concentration input to the operation button ac power is supplied to the shampoo ware the auxiliary tank equipped with a heater an electrolysis tank a drain box for collecting sewage a solenoid opened and closed to control the flow of water between a water supply tank into which water is input and the solenoid a pump a compressor and a heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100977056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this case even if there is an error the manager does not immediately check this and because it is confirmed in the process of checking the control panel there is a problem in pumping operation.the present invention solves the problem of installing the case by welding on the upper casing of the well while alleviating the water shock phenomenon in which the pressure rises or falls due to the rapid flow rate changes inside the pump pipe and also pumping pressure it solves the problem of inadequate disinfection of groundwater by supplying chlorine from outside when the set value is reached and the control panel checks the change of internal pressure of the pump along with the water level of the well in the meantime if an abnormality occurs in the groundwater pumping the manager is immediately notified to take action.the present invention inserts the packing cap on the upper side of the out casing the outer side of the case is fitted to the outside of the packing cap while the inner side of the case is supported by the upper portion of the packing cap the case the wire inlet and pump pipe connector while fixing the cover to the upper side the inside of the case to install a flexible pipe connected to the pump and the water shock protector and a pressure valve the flexible pipe is a meter installed in the meter case through the meter connector and ground water passing through the meter is discharged after being mixed with the chlorine of the quantity supplied from the chlorine injector and the ground water pump and the chlorine pump by detecting the water level of the well and the water pressure and the amount of chlorine control the operation and notify the administrator wirelessly when an error occurs it will be written by providing the urban"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100221225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the raw water from the raw water storage tank 1 is mixed with sand and anthracite as a filter medium through the transfer pump 2 the filter material 3 and the filter material are mixed with the anthracite and sand and the activated carbon or sequentially passed through the second filter 4 which is an activated carbon filter used singly to remove the floating substances and odors and the filtered water is passed through the stainless steel housing polypropylene material 1 5 a pretreatment step of finely filtering through a precision filter 5 used as a disposable or semipermanently backwashed cartridge having pores therein the filtered water filtered through the pretreatment step is passed through the raw water transfer pump 6 to the high pressure vessel made of stainless steel or reinforced plastic and it is made of cellulose acetate or polyamide material and has a diameter of 37 203 and a length of 298 1 524 sized reverse osmosis membrane which is formed of a hollow fiber type a plate type a spiral type or a rotational vibration type is sequentially introduced into a reverse osmosis separator 7 13 arranged in two stages in series the raw water flowing into the reverse osmosis separator 7 from the reverse osmosis separator 7 is prevented from being contaminated by the microbial propagation through the ultraviolet sterilizer 14 while passing through the reverse osmosis separator 7 the permeated water is stored in the washing tub 8 and is used to clean the surface of the reverse osmosis membrane of the reverse osmosis separators 7 and 13 by the washing pump 17 and is transferred to the treated water storage tank 9 in order to prevent the oxidation and scale of the filtration membrane with hydrochloric acid or sulfuric acid which adjusts the ph of the raw water through the feed tank 16 it is possible to automatically inject the disinfectant such as sodium hydrogencarbonate and sodium bisulfite or sodium sulfite station an osmotic phase the treated water stored in the treated water storage tank 9 which is a high pressure vessel made of reinforced plastic or polyethylene or stainless steel is introduced into the crush stone filter 10 by the supply fence 11 to replenish mineral components and a post treatment step of circulating the treated water to the treated water storage tank 9 and supplying it as potable water or water to the potable water via the water supply pump 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the additional installation of the conveying pipe and the pump complicates the overall device structure makes it difficult to quantify the sewage transfer can cause the blockage of the pipe during long term operation and can not maintain the high water level due to the upper conveying pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand the quantitative waste water is discharged quantitatively and discharged into the aeration tank 50 equipped with the oxygen supply nozzle 57 by the water level difference through the first wear 31 via the flow rate control anoxic tank 40 the coarse sewage flows through the weir 35 into the sedimentation filtration tank 20 in which the sludge s is precipitated in a downward upward flow by the induction pipe 93 in the sedimentation filtration tank 20 and the treated supernatant is the discharge vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the conventional internal conveying pipe and an anoxic tank conveying pump are removed to eliminate the blockage of the device and the pipe due to the sludge s deposition"}]</data>
</edge>
