  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage section provided in an excavation section dug down the ground and comprising a space skeleton section configured by assembling a skeleton block and a water permeable layer covering at least the top surface of the space skeleton section a first filter unit that is provided above the water storage unit and filters water flowing into the water storage unit a pipe line that is attached to the water storage unit and extends from the water storage unit to the ground surface a pump unit attached to the conduit and pumping out water from the reservoir a second filter unit for purifying water pumped out by the pump unit a clay layer provided on the side of the water reservoir or an impermeable layer as a layer of soil treated with a soil conditioner an impermeable layer provided below the water reservoir a water permeable layer that covers the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton inside the water impermeable layer comprising at least by using a water permeable sheet of polyester nonwoven fabric with a water permeability coefficient of 10 2 to 10 1 cm sec a tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more in the longitudinal direction and a tensile elongation of 60 or more in the longitudinal direction even if a part of the impermeable layer breaks and breaks groundwater penetrates and flows into the reservoir through a permeable sheet with a predetermined permeability so that sudden rapid inflow of groundwater into the reservoir during an earthquake at the same time to suppress the water storage facility characterized in that the water storage unit in buoyancy due to ground water that is lifted is suppressed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "c attaching to the flow path from which before the step b or the step c a step of forming an impermeable layer as a clay layer or a soil layer treated with a soil improver on the side o