  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an apparatus for treating undigested wastewater sludges the apparatus comprising a a pump adapted to receive a feed mixture and pressurize the feed mixture to a pressure above the critical pressure for water the feed mixture comprising a wastewater sludge b a heat exchanger arrangement connected to receive the pressurized feed mixture from the pump in a heat exchange relationship with at least one heat exchange fluid c a heater connected to receive the feed mixture from the heat exchanger arrangement through a first reaction conduit d oxidant injection means for introducing an oxidant into the feed mixture at least at a point after the feed mixture has exchanged heat with the heat exchange fluid in the heat exchanger arrangement and before the heater and e a supercritical water oxidation reactor connected to receive a partially reacted mixture from the heater through a second reaction conduit the partially reacted mixture comprising partially oxidized feed mixture the supercritical water oxidation reactor for maintaining the partially reacted mixture at a supercritical temperature and supercritical pressure for a time sufficient to oxidize substantially all organic material within the partially reacted mixture and produce a supercritical effluent"}, {"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the reaction initiating temperature may range from 200 f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102239966-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a pump that supplies external water to the inlet of the steam generating pipe a water supply hose that connects the external water to the pump a steam discharge hose that discharges the steam supplied from the outlet of the steam generating pipe to the outside of the housing and the operation of the heater and the pump it comprises a control unit for controlling the the pedestal consists of a front plate and a rear plate bent in a vertical state and the front plate has a display unit indicating temperature and error code while screwing one side of the cover to the rim a steam amount control lever a steam switch a residual water removal switch and a socket for connecting the steam discharge hose is mounted the rear plate is made by perforating the entrance while screwing the other side of the cover to the edge portion the lower end is screwed inside the doorway formed on the rear plate of the pedestal and both sides are screwed to the cover and a socket connecting the earth leakage circuit breaker and water supply hose is mounted and the power supply line is connected so that it can flow into the inside and the accessories can be stored an inner plate providing a storage space is provided a spray gun having a nozzle connected to the front end of the steam discharge hose to inject steam is provided a plurality of drainage holes are drilled in lower corners of the front plate and the rear plate of the pedestal so that moisture can be discharged to the outside a plurality of first vents are formed on the upper side of the inner plate to discharge heat inside the housing while preventing the inflow of moisture scattered from the outside and a plurality of second vents are formed on one side of the cover to be mounted on the pedestal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187534-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "if it is controlled as much as possible it is preferable because it can be adjusted to a temperature that can properly maintain the shading concentration of the shading in the shading tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101247110-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "bubbles generated by cavitation collapse and cause serious damage to ship propellers and pump impellers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101776914-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the handle 26 and the screw engagement portion 27 are provided on the inside of the steam hose 29 and an auxiliary convex portion 28 is inserted into the lower portion of the screw coupling portion 27 so that the screw coupling portion 27 is inserted into the auxiliary block portion 28 and the lower part of the airtight packing 24 is brought into close contact with the convex part 23 so that the inner circumferential surface of the airtight packing 24 is directed toward the steam hose 29 airtight means 20 which expands and seals the circumferential surface of the steam hose 29 to prevent the steam inside the steam generator 12 and the tube t from leaking to the outside a discharge pipe 41 is inserted into a front surface of the tube t inverted into the inside of the pipe and the automatic pressure member 42 is coupled to the upper portion of the discharge pipe 41 a temperature and pressure control unit 43 is installed in the temperature and pressure control unit 43 and an automatic valve 44 is provided under the temperature and pressure control unit 43 to automatically discharge the internal pressure of the tube t to the outside an automatic pressure regulating device 40 having a first outlet 45 formed at a lower end of the automatic valve 44 and a second outlet 46 formed at a side of the automatic valve 44 and a condensate storage chamber 51 is formed at the end of the recovery line 47"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101282136-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in particular the high speed thaw 100 of the present invention is the injection pump 140 the inflow pump 130 according to the hot water outflow amount flowing out through the injector 150 while the hot water supply 400 is heating the cold water to hot water of a predetermined temperature by supporting the control of the burner 120 and the like at the same time it is possible for the operator to provide a fast hot water supply to the freezing conduit 220 without discomfort to adjust the respective components individually to support faster thawing work"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326272-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the apparatus may further include a concentration sensor for measuring the concentration of sodium hypochlorite generated in the electrolysis tank wherein the controller is installed in the dilution water supply pipe so that the concentration measured by the concentration sensor is maintained at 5 000 to 6 500 ppm"}, {"pat_id": "US-8801923-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "according to the present invention when magnetic flocs are electrolyzed by an electrolysis device disposed at a stage prior to the high pressure pump in a case in which water to be treated includes salt content such as nacl the ph is shifted to the alkali side by the electrolysis and energy generated by the electrolysis is ultimately imparted to the flocs in the form of heat so that the temperature also increases"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0448924-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "1400 l of wastewater with an initial concentration of 0.01 nmmo and 0.02 softening were fed with the pre pressure pump 4 via the heat exchanger 5 which ensured that a temperature of 30 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "a substantially contaminant free water stream is introduced into the system via conduit 213"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a substantially contaminant free water stream is preferably introduced into the system via conduit 309"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101286956-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to prevent the freezing of the pipe conventionally the insulation is wrapped in the pipe the heating wire is wrapped in the outside of the pump or the heater is installed in the pump room to install the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "bethridge on ca transferred to the inflowing solvent before entering the thus heat exchanger 925 preheated the water and reduced the energy requirements of the system"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "due to the high temperature some of the apiin was degraded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102741539-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a cooling device 10 comprising a circulation pump installed on one side of an engine 1 and supplying water from an external coolant supply source to a coolant tank of the engine 1 and a cooling means for cooling high temperature water stored in the coolant tank a generator 20 connected to the engine 1 and configured to produce power by the output of the engine 1 and supply the produced power to each receiving location or store it in an ess battery 21 a first clutch 30 provided inside the engine 1 and allowing or releasing transmission of output by the driving force of the engine 1 to the generator 20 a drive control unit 40 configured to selectively supply power of the generator 20 to each receiving location and ess battery 21 according to a signal from the control unit below a drinking water supply line 50 having one end connected to an external drinking water source and configured to supply water from the external drinking water source by operating a pump 51 by the output of the engine 1 a hydrogen peroxide h 2 o 2 supply line 60 connected to a pipe formed by a branch from the above drinking water supply line 50 a cavitation unit 70 connected to the other end of the drinking water supply line 50 and receiving water moving through the drinking water supply line 50 to cause a cavitation sterilization reaction a second clutch 80 provided inside the engine 1 and allowing or releasing the operation of the pump 51 by the driving force of the engine 1 with respect to the cavitation unit 70 a drinking water storage tank 90 for storing water discharged through the above cavitation unit 70 and it comprises a control unit 100 equipped with a control timer 101 that controls whether the first clutch 30 or the second clutch 80 operates at a preset time between the above drinking water supply line 50 and the cavitation unit 70 a contaminant remover 52 is provided to remove or filter various contaminants including floating substances from water supplied from an external drinking water supply source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102741539-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to the first embodiment of the present invention for achieving the above described solution the engine power generation combined cavitation sterilization and disinfection system comprises a cooling device 10 which is installed on one side of an engine 1 and comprises a circulation pump which supplies water from an external coolant supply source to a coolant tank of the engine 1 and a cooling means which cools high temperature water stored in the coolant tank a generator 20 which is connected to the engine 1 and generates electric power by the output of the engine 1 and supplies the generated electric power to each recipient or stores it in an ess battery 21 a first clutch 30 which is provided inside the engine 1 and allows or releases transmission of output by the driving force of the engine 1 to the generator 20 a drive control unit 40 which is configured to selectively supply electric power of the generator 20 to each recipient and the ess battery 21 according to a signal of the following control unit a drinking water supply line 50 having one end connected to an external drinking water source and configured to operate a pump 51 by the output of the engine 1 to supply water from the external drinking water source a hydrogen peroxide h 2 o 2 supply line 60 connected to a pipe branched from the drinking water supply line 50 a cavitation unit 70 connected to the other end of the drinking water supply line 50 and receiving water moving through the drinking water supply line 50 to cause a cavitation sterilization reaction a second clutch 80 provided inside the engine 1 and allowing or releasing the operation of the pump 51 by the driving force of the engine 1 with respect to the cavitation unit 70 a drinking water storage tank 90 storing water discharged through the cavitation unit 70 it comprises a control unit 100 equipped with a control timer 101 that controls whether the first clutch 30 or the second clutch 80 operates at a preset time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102741539-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the cooling device 10 is provided to prevent deformation or damage to the engine 1 due to high temperature heat when the engine 1 is driven and is specifically composed of a circulation pump and a cooling means"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100735544-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "a chemical treatment method using an antifoaming agent has a problem of lowering oxygen transfer efficiency due to residual silicone and other chemicals in the antifoaming agent.the present invention has been made in view of this point and install a straight or radial air supply means on the bottom of the high temperature aerobic digestion reaction tank and supply air to the blower while supplying wastewater to the internal circulation pump to supply air from the discharge nozzle of the air supply means and wastewater are mixed and discharged to form conditions for activating high temperature aerobic microorganisms through the complete mixing of the wastewater in the high temperature aerobic digestion reactor and oxygen transfer through air supply thereby increasing the decomposition efficiency of organic matter and the purpose is to remove the pathogenic microorganisms and e"}, {"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the present invention describes an automated with a hybrid power capacity connected to an electrical current or a photovoltaic power facility for wastewater treatment by oxidative and biological degradation of the liquids originated from a sewage installation utilizing aerobic digestion which is comprised of one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a source of wastewater to one or more rough solid crushing pump pits 2 comprised by an electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a float type level sensor 4 where the activation of the electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid shredder pusher 5 allows it to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 which has the purpose of removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system with air presence consisting of an electrical submersible pump 8 that through an eductor aerator 9 oxygenates the water contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the operation of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a series of sensors a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 for monitoring and controlling the oxygen in the aeration process and a suspended solids sensor 12 for the biological sludge and microorganisms generation which are used for the organic matter degradation the mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 which has a screen 14 to guarantee the passage of only water to a sedimentation and mud separation tank 15 in which the separation of the liquid phase and the solid phase occurs through a process of sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is the water with dejected and clarified organic material while the solid phase is the sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has an electrical submersible pump 16 at its bottom that allows the recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the result of the liquid phase of the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 which has a screen 18 to guarantee the passage of only water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium hypochlorite 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 has sensors in order to automate the operation of this and guarantee the quality of the resulting water a ph sensor 23 a suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 likewise the disinfection tank 19 considers a screen system 21 that is utilized to prevent the passage of solids to the final filtration process alongside with an electro valve 37 that eliminates solid materials that may have passed to this tank the disinfected water in the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by an electrical submersible pump 22 and a connection hose 26 that is connected to a filtration tank 27 which contains gravel 28 with different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is obtained furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for its continuous use during the night where the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that operates the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to providing it during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains its continuous operation the charge controller allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for its dynamic graphs display in the control panel 32 and sends it to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 composed by at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and its nearby surroundings this lamps are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamps have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain periods of time and or real time video of everything that is happening around the facility and with this a visual monitoring of it finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 that allow it to be transported from one place to another easily and it is mounted in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6159912-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "the moisture condensate 20 is moved to the carry in out chamber 11a with a slight inclination fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "the anti freezing unit 70 is installed on the treated water suction pump 24 close to the central processing unit 60 and the pipe exposed to the outdoors around the pump and can prevent freezing due to cold weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-4857185-A", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "this will provide higher temperature of the water to keep it from freezing in winter and also assist the treatment process for better performances the process thus becoming highly energy efficient"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "thereby the object to be cleaned 1 is firstly cleaned by high pressure air bubbling through the lower spray nozzle 233 by driving the spray pump 235 in a state of being immersed in the cleaning liquid in the cleaning tank 210 the spray nozzle 233 is driven by the spray pump 235 to discharge the cleaning solution through the upper spray nozzle 233 before being lifted from the cleaning tank 210 by the driving of the cleaning lifting driver 225 the washing liquid is circulated through the upper spray nozzle 233 by the clean wash water accommodated in the regenerating wash fluid reservoir 240 by the driving of the regenerating wash fluid circulating pump 245 and the steam supply pipe 117 the drying and residual washing liquid is removed by the high temperature steam supplied from the waste water regeneration apparatus 100 and sprayed through the upper spray nozzle 233 and then discharged to the outside of the cleaning loading unit 220 or the cleaning quality of the object to be cleaned 1 can be further improved without consuming energy"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the controller 88 could be equally effective in a case of a fixed nozzle cavitation system wherein a number of inputs to the controller 88 from inlet pressure 90 outlet pressure 92 vacuum 99 temperature 101 and flow 102 produce signals to pump 18 and valve 96 to control cavitation to provide an optimum process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "however since the pressure of the high pressure pump may fluctuate due to the water quality of the raw water the inflow flow rate the water temperature and the hydraulic effects of the pretreatment of the high pressure pump it is difficult to judge only the pressure increase rate due to the membrane contaminant thus increasing the frequency of unnecessary chemical cleaning"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "next the control unit 200 calculates the influence value a4 due to membrane contamination in a predetermined manner by using the calculated pretreatment filter the water temperature and the influence values a1 a2 a3 due to the osmotic pressure and the initial expected pump operation rate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4802665-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a measurement mechanism that includes measurement means that outputs measurement data collected by automatic management and a transmission mechanism that transmits the measurement data a measurement database in which the measurement data is recorded and an observation by an administrator of the water treatment plant an observation database in which the obtained observation data is recorded a storage means including an operation database in which diagnosis data for diagnosing the operation status of the water treatment plant is stored and the measurement data and the observation data are diagnostic means for diagnosing the operation status of the water treatment plant and outputting the diagnosis result in comparison with the diagnostic data a portable computer comprising observation data input means for inputting the observation data observation data transmission means for transmitting the observation data to the storage means and display means for displaying the diagnosis result output from the diagnosis means a terminal and a position display tag attached to at least one of the water treatment device and the pipe and having position information and the portable terminal further includes a reading means for reading the position information of the position display tag the observation data is the liquid color and coloring degree the presence and degree of water leakage in the pipe the presence and degree of abnormal noise the presence and absence of abnormal odor the degree and type the temperature of the pipe water treatment equipment and pump the position information read by the reading means is recorded in the observation database and the diagnosis means includes the position information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "vacuum apparatus for evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means an air compressor for injecting high pressure compressed air into a sealed conduit detecting unit for detecting the pressure and temperature changes in the test tank connected to the vacuum device and the air compression device and connected to the interior of the conduit a controller which controls the driving of the vacuum apparatus and the air compressor and determines whether there is a leakage based on a result detected by the sensing unit it includes a supply device for supplying power and power to each device from the power take off device of the vehicle when the vehicle is mounted or to supply each device the power produced by the generator when mounted on the vehicle to be movable with the vehicle the supply device includes a noise blocking circuit for blocking the noise of the power supplied to each device the power cable connected to the front and rear ends of the noise blocking circuit is provided with a twisted cable to block the noise by increasing the capacitance by twisting the wire the controller is installed inside the main body that forms the appearance and executes the program stored in the storage to control the operation of each device a central processing unit and a printed circuit board for determining a leakage test result according to the detection signal of the detection unit a plurality of operation switches provided on one side of the main body and receiving an operation for controlling driving of each device it is provided on the other side of the main body and includes a plurality of connection ports electrically connected to each device the operation switch is provided with a power switch a vacuum pump provided in the vacuum device a vacuum valve first to fifth switches electrically connected to the compressor and the compressor valve provided in the air compressor the connection port is provided with the vacuum pump and the vacuum valve the compressor and the compressor valve the vent valve for releasing the pressure in the test tank and the first to seventh ports respectively connected to the sensing unit the supply device the first to fifth switches can be set to manual and automatic modes and operation off the cable connecting the sensing unit and the controller is a leakage inspection apparatus of the conduit facility characterized in that provided with a shielded cable shielded to reduce noise"}, {"pat_id": "US-10092851-B2", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "this is done to prevent formation of deposits scales fouling etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the microprocessor monitors the water temperature in storage tank and the temperature of the heat sink and activates the solar circulation pump to cause the heat sink to deliver heat to the storage tank when the possibility of freezing exists in order to delay the need to dump water from the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "if at step 116 the program determines that the water utilization system is calling for water then the program follows the yes branch to step 124 where the pump is activated and the water in the current storage tank is directed by means of the diverter valve to the primary outlet and therefore to the water utilization system"}, {"pat_id": "US-6350376-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a further purpose of the present invention is to perform control for optimal temperature through adjustment of the flow rate of the heat exchange water to accomplish lower flow rate and lower pressure of the heat exchange water so as to reduce installation space and vibration due to the pump and to achieve a heat exchange system that minimizes cost increase"}, {"pat_id": "US-6350376-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the heat insulating material 73 prevents increase of the circulating water cooling water temperature due to the influence of the ambient temperature allowing more efficient operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101739419-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a constant temperature system for leachate and wastewater treatment plants installed in a nitrification tank in a leachate treatment plant including a tiller a flow control tank a mixing tank a nitrification tank a settling tank a thickening tank a fenton oxidation treatment tank or a reverse osmosis treatment tank a plurality of nitrification vessels buried in the ground and purifying and discharging the supplied leachate from the outside and having a plurality of chambers partitioned by a plurality of partition walls for setting the movement path of the leachate therein at least one agitator disposed on the bottom surface of the nitrification tank to mix the leachate while rotating a first heat pump disposed in an upper part of the nitrification tank on the ground to heat the nitrification tank and heat exchanging the first chamber leachate and the heat exchanged refrigerant disposed in front of the nitrification tank in the direction in which the leachate flows 3 heat pump a fourth heat pump to a sixth heat pump arranged in parallel with the first heat pump to the third heat pump and arranged in the rear along the direction in which the leachate of the nitrification tank flows and the heat exchanged refrigerant is heat a first heat exchanger connected to the first heat pump to a third heat pump and disposed in the first chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a second heat exchanger connected to the fourth heat pump to the sixth heat pump and disposed in the second chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a first circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the first heat exchange unit a second circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the second heat exchange unit a preliminary circulation pump interposed between the first circulation pump and the second circulation pump and capable of temporarily operating corresponding to the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump a three way valve connected between any one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump and selectively supplying the heat exchanged refrigerant to the first chamber or the second chamber a sensor unit provided on the three way valve for sensing the temperature or pressure of the refrigerant flowing into the three way valve a first heat pump to a sixth heat pump a first circulation pump and a second circulation pump and a control unit controlling the temperature of the leachate in the nitrification tank to a set range by controlling the agitator an expansion tank provided to compensate for a pressure of the heat exchanged refrigerant supplied through the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump and an air blower unit for supplying air supplied from the outside to the periphery of the agitator in the nitrification tank the air blower unit includes an air flow path for introducing outside air into the vicinity of the agitator a compressor for forcibly supplying external air through the air flow path and a nozzle provided at an end portion of the air flow path for discharging air toward the agitator and wherein the agitator includes a housing fixed to the bottom of the nitrification tank and passing through the inside in a vertical direction a propeller for rotating the inside of the housing to mix the leachate a driving motor for driving the propeller and a guide arm provided on the outer circumferential surface of the housing so as to be guided through the air passage when installed wherein the control unit controls the at least one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump to selectively operate the heat pumps when the temperature of the nitrification tank reaches the set temperature by receiving the data of the sensor unit the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump operates first and controls the heat pumps to operate after the set time has elapsed wherein the nitrification tank includes a plurality of ventilation doors formed with openings communicating with the outside at upper portions of the chambers and selectively opening and closing the openings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681502-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the water supply pipe 31 for guiding the seawater supplied from the pump 22 and the fish farm 21 and the water supply pipe 31 may include an auxiliary pipe 32 for guiding the seawater to each fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "US-4159235-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the thus treated waste water is preneutralized to a ph of 5.2 in a vessel 4 by the addition of sodium hydroxide solution"}, {"pat_id": "US-4159235-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "the thus treated waste water is conducted into vessel 4"}, {"pat_id": "US-4446881-A", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "furthermore if the fluid is a liquid the pumps used at the site of shipment each relay pump station and the destination are generally multi stage centrifugal pumps because they are suitable for elevating the pressure of large quantities of the fluid to a high pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-4446881-A", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "in conjunction with the method of handling the liquid composition at each relay pump station using the above mentioned installation the operation at the station can be safely carried out while preventing not only the liquid composition that is to be transported to the next station but also the liquid composition that is to be used as the fuel for the gas turbine from coming into contact with air before the latter is fed to the combustion chamber 47 and thereby avoids the increase in the formic acid content that would otherwise be caused by contact of the liquid composition with air in accordance with the aforementioned reactions 3 and 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102480228-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "was proposed and the proposed automatic spraying system automatically sprays water according to the ground temperature and the amount of fine dust so that the heat island effect and fine dust can be efficiently removed in spring summer and autumn the injection pressure of salt water is compensated so that it can be sprayed sufficiently but a pump and water supply pipe are required to store water in the water tank as a result there is a problem in that the life of the water pipe is shortened due to damage of the water pipe in the winter or corrosion in the summer because the water or salt water remains inside the water pipe after the water or salt water is sprayed while the cost is additionally spent"}, {"pat_id": "US-8857473-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the flexible hose is pushed through the compression fitting towards the frozen blockage and emits a stream of water under pressure from the pump that erodes and eliminates the frozen blockage and return water is pushed from the blockage back to the return fitting and through the return hose to the container thereby providing a closed loop system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 that stores and stores rainwater flowing through the filter a pump that is installed at the bottom of the storage tank and rotates the rainwater stored in the storage tank from time to time or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 90 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the event of a malfunction the filter 10 of the rainwater recycling device s configured including a control unit 60 equipped with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 on one side an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "for this reason there is a possibility that the flow rate of the concentrated water decreases with respect to the flow rate of the produced water the flow velocity on the surface of the filtration membrane decreases and clogging of the filtration membrane due to fouling may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "this may occur.the problem to be solved by the present invention is to suppress unnecessary power consumption in the feed pump for supplying water to the filtration membrane portion and to prevent clogging of the filtration membrane in the filtration membrane portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "as a result it is possible to prevent unnecessary power consumption in the feed pump for supplying water to the filtration membrane portion and to maintain the flow rate on the surface of the filtration membrane to prevent the filtration membrane from clogging due to fouling"}, {"pat_id": "US-5306397-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "this is compensated by an automatically controlled pumping off of the brine with the lifting pump for the brine 13 and by subsequent refilling of the evaporation chamber 5 with new de aerated seawater via the tube 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200342540-Y1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "1 is a view of a dental automatic water supply temperature control water purification apparatus according to the present invention raw water is supplied to the inlet 14 and the raw water is passed through the sediment filter 16 for pretreatment purified water sand in the water rust and the like are removed and the chemical pump is removed while passing through the carbon filter 20 22 by receiving the appropriate pressure to the purified water while passing through the pressure pump 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080818-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "in the practical embodiment of the submerged pump 60 of the present invention the liquid intake amount volume unit to the air intake amount stp volume unit in terms of standard temperature standard pressure condition is up to 4.0 vol and the intake amount of the liquid is somewhat it was found to be reduced but not significantly affected by cavitation"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7343863-B2", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "this warms the road surface of the road 30 from the inside and as a result it is possible to prevent snow from accumulating on the road surface and from freezing the road surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101628749-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a method for controlling a pump drive of a steam cracking device when the temperature of the steam heating element is lower than the set temperature in a state in which the heater is turned off by interrupting the heater power supply by turning off the steam generating switch while the controller generates steam by the steam heating element detecting the water supply amount of the water supply pipe through the water detection sensor and confirming whether or not the supply water is present during driving of the pump until the pump is driven if the control unit confirms that the supply water is not supplied the water supply abnormal led lamp of the display unit is blinked to warn the water supply abnormal state and it is confirmed whether or not the state that the water supply can not be continued is continued for the set time when the control unit determines that the state in which the water supply can not be maintained is continued for a set time stops driving the pump by shutting off the pump power and continuously illuminates the water supply abnormality state by turning on the water supply abnormality led lamp of the display unit when the control unit confirms that the power switch is reset while continuing to alarm the water supply abnormality state supplying the pump power and driving the pump again"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101628749-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a steam freezing apparatus for generating steam at a high temperature for melting piping such as a frozen water pipe or a sewer and the pump is driven to reflect the presence of residual water to remove the residual water thereby preventing the pump from being burned due to continuous pump driving at the time of stopping the water supply and reliably preventing the freezing caused by the residual water in winter and a method of controlling the pump drive thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101628749-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "when the user turns off the steam generating switch 170 to terminate the steam generation while the steam generating body 140 generates steam the controller 150 controls the heater power supply to the steam heating element 140 the temperature of the steam heating element 140 is measured by the steam heating element temperature sensor 130 and the driving of the pump 110 is stopped when the temperature measurement value of the measured steam heating element 140 is lower than the set temperature if the temperature measurement value of the measured steam heating element 140 is not lower than the set temperature the pump 110 is driven to circulate water through the water supply pipe 113 the pump 110 is driven to supply water to the steam heating element 140 while detecting the supply water of the supply pipe 113 and checking whether the supply water is circulated"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100896597-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the circulation pump 23 is installed to be discharged to the cooler inner cylinder 22 to be circulated again and the bottom of the cooler inner cylinder 22 senses the cooling temperature of the coolant to be cooled and unnecessarily compresses the compressor on the freezing cycle 30 it is preferable that the temperature sensor 21 is installed to prevent the lamp from operating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the water supply control device of claim 1 wherein further comprising a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value wireless automatic water level control system further comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "water supply control device according to an additional aspect of the present invention further comprises a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit is the freezing wave to prevent the freezing of the water supply pipe by intermittently driving the pump when the outside temperature detected by the temperature sensor is less than the reference value it further comprises a prevention drive"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "that is when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270 the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 in the water supply line by installing a temperature sensor electrically connected to the control unit in the winter when the temperature of the water passing through the water supply line falls below a certain temperature by sending a signal to the control unit causes the control unit is installed at one end of the water supply line and the control unit and by operating the electrically connected circulation pump the water supply circulating in the water supply line characterized in that to prevent the freezing of the water supply line due to the freezing of the water flowing in the water supply line in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "another object of the present invention is to install a temperature sensor in the water supply line to detect when the temperature of the water flowing in the water supply line falls below an appropriate temperature to operate the circulation pump installed at one end of the water supply line thereby operating the water in the water supply line the purpose is to provide a drinking fountain that circulates to prevent freezing of the water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition in the water supply line by installing a temperature sensor electrically connected to the control unit in the winter when the temperature of the water passing through the water supply line falls below a certain temperature by sending a signal to the control unit to be installed at one end of the water supply line by operating the circulation pump electrically connected to the control unit the water inside the water supply line is circulated to prevent freezing of the water supply line due to freezing of water flowing in the water supply line during the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "by sending a signal to the circulation pump 90 is operated to prevent the freezing of the water supply line 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "when the water flowing in the water supply line 20 falls below a predetermined temperature the control unit 40 by receiving a signal from the water in the water supply line 20 is to circulate by preventing the freezing of the water supply line 20 due to the freezing of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101190250-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first heat exchanger 3b a second heat exchanger which heats the waste heat of the condensed water generated and discharged from the first heat exchanger 3b by the condensation of the water vapor and the external air supplied to the evaporator 1 to increase the temperature of the external air 3c wastewater containing low boiling pollutants characterized in that the waste heat remaining after the heat exchange in the second heat exchanger 3c and the raw waste water supplied to the evaporative condenser 1 to increase the temperature of the raw waste water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101190250-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "thus there is a need for a simple low cost and complete treatment method.the above problem the evaporation concentrator 1 receiving the raw wastewater from the wastewater supply pump 400 and the external air from the air supply blower 300 the heat storage combustor 2 which is supplied with water vapor and gaseous contaminants from the evaporative concentrator 1 through the duct 2b by the blower 100 and burns them to maintain the oxidation temperature of the organic matter contained in the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-4199406-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "however if the liquid temperature of the block 1 