the circulation pump and a second temperature sensor for measuring the ambient temperature of the pipe for transferring the liquid further comprising the control unit supplies the water supplied from the water tank to the circulation pump through the selection unit when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a set temperature and when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is lower than the set temperature the water supplied from the antifreeze tank is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the present invention according to one aspect for achieving the above object is an antifreeze tank in which a mixture of antifreeze and water is stored in a predetermined ratio antifreeze hose installed along the pipe for transferring the liquid to transfer the liquid a circulation pump for supplying and circulating the mixed solution into the antifreeze hose a first temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the mixed solution flowing through the antifreeze hose a heater for heating the mixed solution stored in the antifreeze tank to a predetermined temperature a temperature controller for adjusting the temperature of the mixed solution and while the temperature information of the mixed solution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to drive the mixed solution it provides a system for preventing freezing and freezing of piping for liquid transport characterized in that it comprises a control unit for heating the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the supplied water may be supplied to the circulation pump and when the temperature is lower than a set temperature the mixed liquid supplied from the