alled inside or outside the main storage tank and quantitatively discharging the chlorine solution stored inside the main storage tank and it includes a control device installed on one side of the main storage tank and controlling the operation of the cooling device and the quantitative pump wherein the control device detects the water level of tap water stored inside the reservoir to calculate the real time storage capacity of the tap water measures the chlorine concentration of the tap water and determines the chlorine injection time and injection amount based on the change in tap water usage according to the day of the week and time thereby operating the quantitative pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention provides an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a public building water tank which stores a large amount of chlorine in an automatic chlorine injection device and enables timely injection and replenishment and also prevents deterioration of chlorine solution due to changes in ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-12522516-B2", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the primary pump 130a is thus used to enable the sample collection to occur within a desired temperature range provided within the interior space preventing the intake liquid from freezing or being overheated by the exterior conditions i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634146-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in preferred embodiments the processing unit 50 may receive temperature data from a temperature sensor 24 which may indicate that the temperature sensor 24 is measuring temperatures close to freezing 32 degrees fahrenheit plus or minus 5 degrees or temperatures below freezing below 33 degrees fahrenheit and the processing unit 50 may cause the primary pump 13 and or the secondary pump 14 to pulse to prevent freezing of water in the sump 99 pumps 13 14 or piping and conduits 98"}, {"pat_id": "US-12127513-B2", "para_id