on.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a graph showing the effect of dissolved zinc on the crack growth rate of sensitized alloy 600.it is a graph showing the relationship between stress corrosion crack length and time showing the effect of zinc in reducing the crack growth rate of 316ss in high temperature water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the present invention proposes a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention provides a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a temperature lower than the preset temperature water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 and at the same time water is supplied into the rainwater storage tank 200 by the bypass pipe 620 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 .the present invention proposes a rainwater storage structure for a road and a rainwater storage method using the same which can prevent urban flood damage caused by localized heavy rain due to climate change and distortion of the water circulation system due to overdevelopment of urban areas.figure 1 below illustrates an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-4203806-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "discontinuance of dental services in case of malfunction or exhaustion of water in the single pressure storage tank 2 9 in order to prevent the occurrence of a separate simple auxiliary metal or plastic material inside the device the tank 2 14 is installed and in case of emergency the tank cap 2 14 1 is opened and the user can be used to pour the graft in addition a small load is provided at the inlet 