 water level level display section 26 in which the lamp is selectively lit according to the water level level of the water tank 6 and the driving of the pump 3 and it consists of a drive display unit 27 the lamp is turned on when the water leakage and a water temperature display unit 28 for displaying cold and hot water the output terminal of the mpu 21 is installed on one side of the facet 8a is connected to the facet lamp 9 for providing a refreshing feeling when the water is discharged the water level sensor 30 is installed in the water tank 6 at the input end of the mpu 21 and senses the water level in four stages and the water leakage sensor is installed on the bottom surface of the case 1 to detect water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "10 is extended to the outside through the through hole 21a and the waterproof clamp 20 to prevent the water flowing through the fire water supply pipe 3 a backflow pipe 30 having both ends connected to the front and rear ends of the fire water supply pipe 30 so as to communicate with the front and rear ends of the installation position of the heater 10 a pump 40 connected to the backflow pipe 30 so that water flowing through the firefighting water supply pipe 3 flows back through the backflow pipe 30 the waterproof clamp 20 is formed in a semi circular shape the through hole 21a is formed the inner peripheral surface is provided with a waterproof portion 21 having a packing 21b for blocking the periphery of the through hole 4 and the bolt 22 combination with the waterproof portion 21 is composed of a semi circular fixing portion 23 for fixing the waterproof portion 21 to the circumferential surface of the fire water supply pipe 3 the power supply system rechargeable battery 50 is applied to the charge is connected to the heater 10 and the auxiliary heater 10 to supply power a control unit 60 for controlling charging and discharging of the rechargeable battery 50 and operations of the heater 10 and the pump 40 a water temperature sensor 70 around the heater 10 and fixedly installed on an inner circumferential surface of the fire water supply pipe 3 so as to be positioned at a circumference of the heater 10 it includes a detection sensor 80 for detecting the operation of the fire fighting equipment connected to the fire water supply pipe 3 the control unit 60 receives the signals of the water temperature sensor 70 and the sensor 80 to prevent the water heater 10 from freezing only water around the heater 10 when the water temperature is lower than the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "and the heater 10 is extended to the outside through the through hole 4 formed in the fire water supply pipe 3 in the state installed inside the fire water supply pipe 3 the waterproof clamp 20 installed in the fire water supply pipe 3 since water is used to prevent leakage there is an advantage that the installation and maintenance of the heater 10 is very easy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452662-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "flow control tank 1 anaerobic tank 2 for removing phosphorus in the water to be treated flowing in from the flow rate control tank 1 an anaerobic tank 3 for removing nitrate nitrogen in the treated water flowing in from the anaerobic tank 2 an aerobic tank 4 for nitrifying nitrogen by aeration of air into the water to be treated introduced from the anoxic tank 3 a fenton oxidation unit 10 for fenton oxidation treatment of the water to be treated flowing in from the aerobic tank 4 a sedimentation tank 5 for separating the water to be treated from the fenton oxidation unit 10 into a supernatant and sludge a high temperature sterilization unit 20 for high temperature sterilization of the water to be treated by heat exchange a flotation filtration tank 1000 having an inlet 1010 into which the wtbt is introduced a flotation filtration device 1020 mounted on the wtbt inlet space 1040 and a discharge part 1030 from which the wtbt is discharged and circulation guide part 40 for guiding the water to be treated in the inlet space 1040 of the flotation filtration tank 1000 to the flotation filtration device 1020 the fenton oxidation unit 10 a reaction tank 100 having a reaction space therein a wastewater supply unit 200 provided to supply wastewater fenton oxide supply unit 300 provided to supply the fenton oxide a main supply unit 400 provided to supply the wastewater and fenton oxide supplied from the wastewater supply unit 200 and the fenton oxide supply unit 300 to the reactor 100 the crystals 500 are located in a large amount in the reaction space 110 of the reaction tank 100 and are provided to attach the sludge generated in the reaction process while flowing in the wastewater supplied from the main supply unit 400 a treated water discharge unit 600 provided to discharge the treated water treated in the reaction tank 100 a sediment discharge unit 700 provided for discharging precipitated sludge among sludge generated in the reaction process in the reaction tank 100 a circulation unit 800 provided to circulate a portion of the treated water treated in the reaction space unit 110 to the main supply unit 400 and and a fenton filter membrane 900 provided to prevent the crystals 500 of the reaction space 110 from being discharged to the treated water discharge unit 600 the circulation unit 800 a circulation pipe 810 having an inlet end connected to the reactor 100 and an outlet end connected to the main supply unit 400 the circulation pump 820 is for supplying a portion of the treated water to the lower end of the reaction space 110 through the circulation pipe 810 and is supplied to the lower end of the reaction space 110 by the main supply unit 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a water pressure control encoder switch for adjusting the intensity of the water output the temperature of the water ph concentration the operation button to receive the output time the water level sensor for measuring the water level an input unit configured of a temperature sensor measuring a temperature of water a pump for raising the water to the shampoo ware a heater for heating the water to a temperature set by the operation button an electrolysis tank for ionizing the water and performing electrolysis to match the ph concentration input to the operation button ac power is supplied to the shampoo ware the auxiliary tank equipped with a heater an electrolysis tank a drain box for collecting sewage a solenoid opened and closed to control the flow of water between a water supply tank into which water is input and the solenoid a pump a compressor and a heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102029117-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the mixing preheater the inclined stirrer is installed to be inclined inside to increase the mixing efficiency of the waste heat and the substrate and drawn up from the bottom to the upper and lower stirring to completely mix the preheated substrate in such a way that it is introduced into the upper supply pump consisting of a mono pump consisting of piping is installed the inclined stirrer a drive motor installed inclined at an upper portion of the mixing preheater and shifting or decelerating a rotational force through a reduction gear or a reduction gear to provide a rotational driving force an inclined rotating shaft installed on the upper portion of the mixing preheater to be inclined upward by 30 to 60 inclination angle \u03b8 and connected to the driving motor to receive the driving force a downward stirring blade installed at a lower portion of the inclined rotating shaft to form a downward flow at a lower portion of the inclined rotating shaft to circulate up and down a first upward stirring blade installed at an upper one side of the inclined rotary shaft to form an upstream in the upper one of the inclined rotary shaft and circulate up and down and thermal hydrolysis anaerobic treatment for organic wastes comprising a second up stirring blade installed on the other side of the inclined rotary shaft to form an upstream on the other side of the inclined rotary shaft to circulate up and down fire extinguisher"}]</data>
</edge>
