  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while allowing it to flow to one side of the upper portion eco friendly rainwater management system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "it is configured to be made as a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while being possible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "it is configured to be made as a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while allowing it to flow to one side of the upper portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101782356-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 1617616 registered on april 27 2016 a problem to be solved by the present invention is that there is no need for a separate equipment installation space in a swimming pool a water purification plant a wastewater treatment plant a sewage treatment plant discharge tank a rainwater reuse facility and the like requiring chlorination and oxidation decomposition of pollutants in water the present invention provides an electrode module for water treatment which has a large electrode installation area per unit volume and does not require any auxiliary equipment such as a pump and a water treatment system employing the electrode module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a soil cement layer formed to a predetermined thickness on the bottom surface and an inner surface of the underground space formed by digging the ground of the outer side of the building to a predetermined depth and the soil cement layer formed on the bottom surface of the underground space portion a sand layer formed at a height an activated carbon layer formed at a predetermined height above the sand layer a gravel layer formed at a predetermined height above the activated carbon layer and an opening in the underground space seated horizontally on an upper surface of the gravel layer a fire fighting water supply tank having a shielding plate to shield the a first hollow rainwater inlet pipe inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank by vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and having one end inserted into the through hole formed in the boundary stone perpendicular to the outer wall of the building a hollow second rainwater inlet pipe that is installed as an inlet and has one end connected to the eaves gutter that collects rainwater falling to the roof of the building and the other end vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank vertically penetrating the shielding plate of the fire water supply tank and vertically buried in the fire water supply tank with the upper end exposed to the outside an inner space is provided an opening is formed in the center of the upper surface and a plurality of water collecting holes are formed on the lower outer surface the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the a hollow water intake unit introduced into the inner space through a water collecting hole one end is connected to an opening formed in the water intake unit so that fire water collected in the inner space of the water intake unit is supplied and the other end is connected to an opening formed in the steel pipe pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101246202-B1", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "the water collecting groove 402 provides a volume for collecting water introduced into the concrete structure 400 due to leakage of water supply pipes or inflow of rainwater and a worker is provided with a water pump hereinafter not shown separately provided through the inspection opening 401"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101987814-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "as another modification of the present invention an auxiliary pipe is further connected between the storage tank and the backwash water tank and a hand pump is mounted on the auxiliary pipe.as described above according to the present invention the backwashing function is normally maintained even when the raw water is not continuously supplied in the course of processing the initial rainwater with high contamination degree thereby improving the economical efficiency and the efficiency of labor saving.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052943-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 92 roof 93 washing wastewater spray device 94 washing wastewater recirculation mechanism 100 ground 101 drainage groove 102 collecting drainage groove 103 convex 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 107 left vertical frame 108 right vertical frame 10 horizontal frame 111 water supply pipe 112 drainage nozzle 113 intermediate pipe 114 cleaning waste water supply pipe 115 cleaning waste supply pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition in order to prevent the decay and odor caused by long term storage of high concentration early rainfall brower is installed to supply minimum air to maintain dissolved oxygen concentration of more than 0.1mg l in the acid pipe installed at the bottom of the storage tank and to detect rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the road structure includes a housing 32 on which an opening 34 is formed on an upper side and is inserted into the road surface 12 and a housing 32 on which an upper end is mounted so as to be elevated and retracted upward a lift block 30 having a rack gear 31 extending downward a spring 40 connected to a lower side of the elevating block 30 to press the elevating block 30 upward a drive shaft 60 connected to the pinion gear 50 via the ratchet 61 and rotated forward only when the rack gear 31 is lowered a rotation limiting device 70 coupled to the drive shaft 60 to restrict the drive shaft 60 to rotate only in the normal rotation direction a rotary shaft 83 coupled to the housing 81 and rotatable together with the housing 81 and a rotary shaft 83 coupled to the housing 81"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 that stores and stores rainwater flowing through the filter a pump that is installed at the bottom of the storage tank and rotates the rainwater stored in the storage tank from time to time or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 90 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the event of a malfunction the filter 10 of the rainwater recycling device s configured including a control unit 60 equipped with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 on one side an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater frequently accumulates in the block when it is raining due to outdoor work"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "more specifically the vacuum pump 140 is operated while only the vacuum valve 123a is opened and the remaining suction valve 121a the siphon valve 122a and the residual water valve 111a are shut off see fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "in addition the suction pipe of the drain pump introduced into the water reservoir 1 through the rainwater inlet pipe 15 may be located at the lower side of the front body block 10 and the rear body block 10a to drain the rainwater stored in the fire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "and it is installed below the lower plate 70 so as to correspond to the suction pipe inserting hole 71 to seat the suction pipe of the drain pump supplied through the suction pipe inserting hole 71 and the drainage action by the suction pipe is smooth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "the suction pipe seating member 75 is installed at the lower end of the lower plate 70 so as to correspond to the suction pipe insertion hole 71 so that the drainage action by the suction pipe of the drainage pump can be performed smoothly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101239389-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "if it is over the designed quantity in the treatment tank the rainwater collected in the treatment tank is pulled up by the pump and reintroduced into the second pollution reduction portion formed of the gravel layer the crushed stone layer and the zeolite layer to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100760969-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "supplying step of the untreated water flows into the through hole of the inlet packing material inside the filtering means and then the untreated water is filtered while leaving the contaminant on the outer diameter side of the filter membrane while passing through the filter membrane from the outer diameter side to the inner diameter side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a fire storage tank configured to temporarily store rainwater and use it as fire protection water a connecting block of hollow rectangular cylinders or cylindrical bodies which are stacked one or more to form a tank of a predetermined capacity an upper plate formed at an upper end of the upper connection block and having an inlet pipe coupling hole formed therein so that the rainwater inlet pipe is coupled a lower plate installed inside the upper end of the lowermost connection block to form a bottom surface of the reservoir and a suction pipe insertion hole penetrated so that the suction pipe of the drain pump can be inserted a suction pipe seating member installed at a lower side of the lower plate to correspond to the suction pipe inserting hole to seat the suction pipe of the drain pump supplied through the suction pipe inserting hole and to facilitate drainage by the suction pipe fired water tank characterized in that the upper plate and the connecting block the lower plate through the self weight of each member is laminated in the vertical direction to form a closed vertical water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a seating groove having an arc shaped bottom surface is formed and an upper end edge of the suction pipe seating member is further provided with an index member to prevent leakage of rainwater between the bottom plate which is the bottom surface of the reservoir and the suction pipe seating member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "in addition the suction pipe of the drain pump introduced into the water reservoir 1 through the rainwater inlet pipe 15 may be located at the lower side of the front body block 10 and the rear body block 10a to drain the rainwater stored in the fire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "and it is installed below the lower plate 70 so as to correspond to the suction pipe inserting hole 71 to seat the suction pipe of the drain pump supplied through the suction pipe inserting hole 71 and the drainage action by the suction pipe is smooth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "the suction pipe seating member 75 is installed at the lower end of the lower plate 70 so as to correspond to the suction pipe insertion hole 71 so that the drainage action by the suction pipe of the drainage pump can be performed smoothly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that the upper portion is exposed from the filter medium over the entire length the upper portion of the filter material is exposed from the filter material to the inside of the filtration tank and the exposed portion is formed with an inlet hole for allowing the filter material washing water to flow into the discharge passage while the opposite end is installed in the partition wall 111b a filter media wash and contaminant discharge line configured to communicate with the filter material discharge outlet a filter material cleaning device installed under the filter material washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe to be buried in the filter material and spraying high pressure air or backwash water for washing the filter material and a filter medium washing water and contaminants which are installed outside the pretreatment tank and are washed by the filter material cleaning device and flowed into the pretreatment tank through the washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe and stagnant water accumulated in the water treatment tank and a stagnant water exclusion pump for removing the stagnant water when it is confirmed that stagnant water is present in the water treatment tank contaminants separated from the filter media and the filter media wash water used for the filter media are supplied to the discharge passage and the filtering water discharge port 135 having the reverse opening closing door 136 of the partition wall 111b to be forcedly sucked into the pretreatment tank and forcedly excluded to the outside by the congestion water exclusion pump the operation of the filter medium washing device is stopped and only the stagnant water exclusion pump is operated with the stagnant water of the water treatment tank to be operated until the complete removal of sediment deposited at the bottom of the tank has been confirmed initial treatment is a solid system of jing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100751233-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "rainwater which is free of organic matter and the pollutant load fluctuation is mitigated by the installation of rainwater rainwater without organic matter and the second flocculation tank is used to control the flow rate of sewage and to induce oxidation and decomposition of microorganisms the treated water was removed by sand filtration using a pump and ultrafiltered water treated first in a microfilter it is possible to carry out advanced treatment by using a membrane and it is possible to carry out antibacterial and deodorization by using a carbon filter while maintaining the filter clean by high pressure backwashing and chlorination thereby increasing the life and efficiency the present invention relates to an ultrafiltration type heavy water treatment apparatus capable of preventing the above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100528077-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "of course various modifications and variations can be made by those skilled in the art.drainage treatment apparatus according to the present invention configured as described above is to be discharged to the sewer pipe after the foreign matter contained in the water such as surface water or rainwater to be discharged to the sewage pipe to prevent the foreign matter deposited on the sewage pipe the drain pump by the foreign matter can be prevented from malfunctioning"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rear inclined portion 34 is formed at an end portion of both side walls 39 protruding from both side edges of the front inclined portion 31 in the section of the inclined surface 80 a moving section 59 fixed to the bottom surface 33 on which the guide wall 53 is in contact so that the moving section 59 is formed on the inner side of the moving section 59 and a vegetation block 30 through which the passage hole 57 passes the safety rib 61 at the upper end of the projecting wall 521 for the drainage passage formed in the drainage passage 52 and the safety ribs 61 at the upper end of the drainage passage projecting wall 521 formed in the drainage passage 52 the rib 61 is connected to an induction rod 66 curved in the direction of the bottom of the drainage path and a drain pipe 70 sloped along the surface of the inclined surface 80 while being connected to the through in this case a separate water storage tank 62 for storing water in an upper section of a drainage path 52 buried in an inclined land adjacent to the vegetation block 30 and a drainage pipe 70 at a side wall 72 of the water storage tank 62 and a branch pipe 76 connected at one side between the sections of the supply pipe 75 is connected to the inlet port 79 of the drain pipe 70 while being pushed downward wherein the discharge port 77 is provided with a high pressure water jetted from the supply pipe 75 by a pressurizing pump 68 so that drainage of rainwater is promoted by the drainage pipe 70 drainage accelerator in drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "a separate water storage tank 62 for storing water in an upper section of a drainage path 52 buried in an inclined land adjacent to the vegetation block 30 and a drainage pipe 70 at a side wall 72 of the water storage tank 62 and a branch pipe 76 connected at one side between the sections of the supply pipe 75 is connected to the inlet port 79 of the drain pipe 70 while being pushed downward and the discharge port 77 is provided with a high pressure water jetted from the supply pipe 75 by the pressurizing pump 68 so that drainage of the rainwater is promoted by the drainage pipe 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "the supply pipe 75 described above is provided with a pressurizing pump 68 so as to be connected to a control device of a power supply unit not shown at the time of rainstorming so as to reinforce the discharge output of rainwater due to heavy rains.30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101099777-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the four manholes are formed to be spaced apart from each other and the connection portion forms a rectangular border shape by connecting the four manholes to each other one of the manholes is connected to an inflow pipe to which rainwater is introduced and a filtration screen for filtering foreign substances contained in the rainwater to be introduced is installed in the uppermost storage block of the manholes to which the inflow pipes are connected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101099777-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the four manholes are formed to be spaced apart from each other and the connecting portion interconnects the four manholes to form a square rim shape one of the manholes is connected to the inlet pipe to which rainwater is introduced the inlet pipe is the uppermost storage block of the manhole portion to be connected is provided with a filtration screen for filtering foreign matter contained in the rainwater flowing in the lower portion of the filtration screen is provided with a filtration layer filled with elvan rock and is not connected to the inlet pipe the remaining manhole portion is preferably provided with an oxygen supply portion for supplying oxygen to the inside and a discharge pump for pumping the stored rainwater to the outside.prefabricated rainwater storage facility according to the present invention can be made easily and quickly construction can minimize the time and cost of construction there is an advantage that easy maintenance.1 is a perspective view showing a prefabricated rainwater storage system according to the present invention 2 is a cross sectional view of the prefabricated rainwater storage device of fig"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "system for transferring foul discharges from a rainwater sewer 2 into a dirty water sewer 4 a connecting conduit 5 being provided between the rainwater sewer 2 and the dirty water sewer 4 characterized in that the rainwater sewer 2 has a manhole 1 the floor 9 of the rainwater sewer 2 is arranged above the floor 10 of the manhole 1 and the rainwater sewer 2 has a lateral orifice within the manhole 1 and furthermore a sill 18 being arranged in the region of the orifice in the rainwater sewer 2 obliquely relative to the extension of the latter and there being arranged at the floor level of the manhole 1 a pump 34 which is connected to the dirty water sewer 4 via a conduit 5"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "due to the use of the pump the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the assembled rainwater storage tank 10 according to the present invention having the above described structure can be installed rapidly and firmly to meet the capacity suitable for the building at low cost and can use rainwater as drinking water for drinking water and emergency drinking water it is possible to prevent flood control in the rainy season and typhoon as well as to surely prevent pollution by contaminated initial rainwater by eliminating a large but early power without extra power.10 assembly type stormwater tank 20 water storage tank tower 2