nk 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention provides a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a temperature lower than the preset temperature water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 and at the same time water is supplied into the rainwater storage tank 200 by the bypass pipe 620 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 .the present invention proposes a rainwater storage structure for a road and a rainwater storage method using the same which can prevent urban flood damage caused by localized heavy rain due to climate change and distortion of the water circulation system due to overdevelopment of urban areas.figure 1 below illustrates an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition in order to form a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 a bypass pipe 620 may be installed on the opposite edge of the suction pipe 710 to supply water into the interior of the rainwater storage tank 200 by a pump 700"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "the structure of the suction pipe 710 or bypass pipe 620 of the pump 700 forms a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 separately from the agitating unit 500"}, {"pat_id":