  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100498266-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "it has the effect of preventing the blockage of flood gates the blocking of running water and the failure of drainage facilities such as pump stations"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101776163-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "on the other hand in the case where flooding occurs due to pipe rupture or flood of the pump room in which the water treatment pump motor 100 is installed the remote controller 200 is installed in a proper position of the pump room in which the water treatment pump motor 100 is installed the immersion detection signal detected by the installed immersion sensor 230 is transmitted to the instrument control apparatus 100 so that the operation of the water treatment pump motor 110 being driven by the instrument control apparatus 100 is stopped the controller 100 causes the immersion sensing signal to be wirelessly transmitted to the wireless terminal 300 so that the immersion status is displayed on the wireless terminal 300"}, {"pat_id": "US-4815492-A", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "the flood control valve of claim 12 further characterized by said means for activating the pump being operable to turn the pump on and discharge any leaked fluid from a flood back into a sewer line to prevent sewage from leaking into the building should the flapper valve become corroded or clogged with protein accumulations allowing waste to leak there through"}, {"pat_id": "US-4815492-A", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "according to still further features of my invention the flapper valve if it should be corroded or clogged with protein accumulations allowing waste fluid to leak there through whereupon the means for activating the pump can be caused to operate and to turn the pump on and discharge the leaked fluid from a flood back into the city sewer line to prevent sewage from leaking into the building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for underground passage flood prevention is configured to supply power to each pump using the marine hydroelectric power generator 213 facilities to prevent underground passage flooding in the above underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment the hydraulic power generator 213 is installed a device 218 for pushing a rotary shaft under an upper rotary shaft 217 is positioned and a stator coil 219 a stator frame 220 and a central stator 221 are positioned at the bottom of the device 218 for pushing the rotary shaft and an electric wire 71 is inserted into the gap of the central stator 221 and a fan 195 is positioned at the bottom of the central stator 221 and a braking device ring 223 a brake jack 224 and a low speed rotary shaft 225 are positioned at the bottom of the fan 195 and a low speed cooler 222 is positioned at the bottom of the low speed rotary shaft 225 and a rotating electromagnet rotor coil formed along the circumference of the rotary shaft 198 and an armature coil for a non rotating coil generator installed along the circumference of the rotor coil and a lower end of the rotary shaft 198 the conventional marine hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment which is provided with several waterwheels and turbines 267 for setting up positions turbine rotating shafts 227 casings 141 vane pumps guide vanes 142 and impellers 228 supplies power to each pump of the hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment to prevent underground passage flooding and is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flooding prevention and flood control equipment the vertical multi stage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the above underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is as follows according to the control block diagram and the vertical multi stage pump operation method of the bf model the pump power 272 and the control power 273 are separated and distinguished and the emergency operation sequence circuit 274 of the control power 273 is connected to the dc power spray supply circuit 275 and the m c drive signal contact output circuit 279 and the output circuit terminal and then the m c switch contact of the pump power 272 and the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the contacts that enable each pump to be operated in emergency mode and at the same time the dc power supply circuit 275 of the control power 273 provides the input setting of the diac switch setting circuit 277 and the switch input circuit 58 to the micro control unit 276 and at the same time the led display circuit 278 and the drive signal contact output circuit 279 outputs a signal and the motor overload signal input circuit 280 is installed so that the circuit contacts of the unit 276 and the pump power supply 272 tip are connected to the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the inverter operation data input output circuit 281 is formed as a circuit for mutual input and output between the inverter 47 circuit and the micro control unit 276 and the discharge pressure transmitter 284 is connected to the pressure detection circuit 282 and then the circuit 282 is input set to the unit 276 and then the suction discharge pressure switch 285 is connected to the external status input circuit 283 and then the input circuit 283 is input set to the micro control unit 276"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire hose 9 and a fire nozzle frame 11 and a hook 13 in a detection sensor 12 and a jig 22 in a pipe 14 are configured to control the flow rate to the disaster prevention waterway 17 while forming a vertical multistage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for flood prevention of underground passages the flood control equipment which consists of fire pumps and high performance submersible pumps a hook and a wire rope a machined hole and a shackle a bolt and nut a washer and a hinge a flange or a flange stopper a wire mesh a coupling a coupling female threaded body 30 a coupling male threaded body 31 a gasket or rubber packing a nozzle hose equipment holder a reducer and a pump wheel spray the discharged water through the fire hose and in the fire station 40 a water film or a curtain water film is formed and a double vinyl tent or bag controls the flow rate and an elbow or tie elbow changes the flow rate to prevent underground flooding and a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and flood control equipment the power supply which is a power supply device supplied from a hydroelectric power generator 213 is inverter 47 and inverter vio access point and internet network vertical multistage pump control server and monitor to pump control board or tagger winch control box and short range wireless communication antenna to short range wireless communication device wireless communication control module and display to electronic control device adc and switch input circuit to electronic control device mcu and electronic control device diac overcurrent breaker brake is connected to power supply to display screen and analog input and digital input are operated by hand to control on off of each pump main switch button and auxiliary switch button to configure vertical multistage pump operation method inside main body 1 of underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment in addition to the above mentioned vertical multi stage pump turbine pump 140 diaphragm pump vane pump or guide vane and propeller pump screw pump plunger pump axial plunger pump radial plunger pump and jet pump 157 are provided and are connected to an introduction pipe and a water supply port or a fire prevention and disaster prevention pipe line 168 and a water discharge port 169 and are connected to a limit switch or a limit switch and a power motor body 192 is provided with a hood and a snap ring a fan and a body frame a body front reinforcing plate a rotor assembly on a rotating shaft a stator assembly on a front rotating shaft support a motor protection casting frame a terminal box and a lifting bolt a terminal box cover a rear rotating shaft support a rear reinforcing plate a gap a fan cover or a protective cover a rotor core and a stator core with stator windings and are connected and connected and underground passage flood prevention a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_279", "text": "the piston pump is suitable for cases where the pumping amount is small and the head is large because the water pressure fluctuation is large and it is difficult to control the water quantity and the plunger pump 148 has little leakage from around the plunger 253 and is used for high pressure pumps for water and other liquids and the washington pump is suitable for the feedwater pump of a high pressure boiler because the pump is directly connected to a steam engine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_382", "text": "in addition a reciprocating pump can adjust the discharge amount without a large change in the discharge pressure according to the change in the rotation speed but if it is increased too quickly the valve operation may not follow or the liquid may not rise in time causing cavitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_390", "text": "13 the main problems during the operation of the pump of the conventional flood control equipment are as follows first the standard gland packing is a universal packing method using cotton or a packing material impregnated with grease in cotton second the liquid injected lantern ring attached packing 155 is the most commonly used type which installs a lantern ring in the center of the stuffing box inserts approximately the same number of packings on both sides and injects liquid into the lantern ring and third the double gland packing is a method to reduce the leakage of high pressure or harmful liquid by double layering the ordinary gland packing 155 but the pump extinguisher main part is divided into the standard gland packing 344 and the liquid injected lantern ring attached packing 346 and the double gland type packing 348 and is formed by the shaft sealing device of each pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_397", "text": "while the gland packing prevents leakage by sealing at the inner surface of the cylinder the mechanical seal has absolutely no leakage or only a small amount of leakage by sealing at the cross section of the cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_403", "text": "13 the main problem during the operation of the pump of the conventional underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is that if the temperature rises due to the heat of the liquid being handled or the frictional heat of the wetted surface the material may wear out or corrode or the packing may stick so in order to suppress this the following basic methods are used to have cooling and lubrication functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_419", "text": "finally when disassembling the cylinder head slowly loosen the bolts in the order of the opposing sides up to the last two relatively located bolts of course confirm that there is no abnormality during the operation of the pump of the water damage control device system and then loosen these last two bolts"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_487", "text": "16 the gear pump 326 of the conventional underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment has the advantages of being compact lightweight and inexpensive and can withstand harsh operating conditions contamination by dust rise in oil temperature overload so it is particularly suitable for hydraulic drive in construction machinery industrial vehicles agricultural machinery etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_545", "text": "the flood control equipment configured inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment is configured to prevent the dispatch of conventional forest fire fighting equipment such as transport equipment and to achieve zero disaster by using a plurality of nozzle holes of the pipe nozzles inside the pipe nozzle body for fire prevention and disaster prevention measures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1127", "text": "the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for underground passage flood prevention is configured to supply power to each pump using the marine hydroelectric power generator 213 facilities to prevent underground passage flooding in the above underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment the hydraulic power generator 213 is installed a device 218 for pushing a rotary shaft under an upper rotary shaft 217 is positioned and a stator coil 219 a stator frame 220 and a central stator 221 are positioned at the bottom of the device 218 for pushing the rotary shaft and an electric wire 71 is inserted into the gap of the central stator 221 and a fan 195 is positioned at the bottom of the central stator 221 and a braking device ring 223 a brake jack 224 and a low speed rotary shaft 225 are positioned at the bottom of the fan 195 and a low speed cooler 222 is positioned at the bottom of the low speed rotary shaft 225 and a rotating electromagnet rotor coil formed along the circumference of the rotary shaft 198 and an armature coil for a non rotating coil generator installed along the circumference of the rotor coil and a lower end of the rotary shaft 198 the conventional marine hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment which is provided with several waterwheels and turbines 267 for setting up positions turbine rotating shafts 227 casings 141 vane pumps guide vanes 142 and impellers 228 supplies power to each pump of the hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment to prevent underground passage flooding and is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flooding prevention and flood control equipment the vertical multi stage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the above underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is as follows according to the control block diagram and the vertical multi stage pump operation method of the bf model the pump power 272 and the control power 273 are separated and distinguished and the emergency operation sequence circuit 274 of the control power 273 is connected to the dc power spray supply circuit 275 and the m c drive signal contact output circuit 279 and the output circuit terminal and then the m c switch contact of the pump power 272 and the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the contacts that enable each pump to be operated in emergency mode and at the same time the dc power supply circuit 275 of the control power 273 provides the input setting of the diac switch setting circuit 277 and the switch input circuit 58 to the micro control unit 276 and at the same time the led display circuit 278 and the drive signal contact output circuit 279 outputs a signal and the motor overload signal input circuit 280 is installed so that the circuit contacts of the unit 276 and the pump power supply 272 tip are connected to the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the inverter operation data input output circuit 281 is formed as a circuit for mutual input and output between the inverter 47 circuit and the micro control unit 276 and the discharge pressure transmitter 284 is connected to the pressure detection circuit 282 and then the circuit 282 is input set to the unit 276 and then the suction discharge pressure switch 285 is connected to the external status input circuit 283 and then the input circuit 283 is input set to the micro control unit 276"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1127", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire hose 9 and a fire nozzle frame 11 and a hook 13 in a detection sensor 12 and a jig 22 in a pipe 14 are configured to control the flow rate to the disaster prevention waterway 17 while forming a vertical multistage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for flood prevention of underground passages the flood control equipment which consists of fire pumps and high performance submersible pumps a hook and a wire rope a machined hole and a shackle a bolt and nut a washer and a hinge a flange or a flange stopper a wire mesh a coupling a coupling female threaded body 30 a coupling male threaded body 31 a gasket or rubber packing a nozzle hose equipment holder a reducer and a pump wheel 