r balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the assembled rainwater storage tank 10 according to the present invention having the above described structure can be installed rapidly and firmly to meet the capacity suitable for the building at low cost and can use rainwater as drinking water for drinking water and emergency drinking water it is possible to prevent flood control in the rainy season and typhoon as well as to surely prevent pollution by contaminated initial rainwater by eliminating a large but early power without extra power.10 assembly type stormwater tank 20 water storage tank tower 21 lower block 22 water quality observation block 23 upper block 24 capacity adjustment block 30 drain pipe assembly 31 first drain pipe 32 opening and closing means 33 second drain pipe 34 filter pipe 40 water supply pipe 50 water pump 60 advanced water purification device 70 fountain hose 80 sterilization device 90 water storage tank 100 building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "there is a place where a drainage facility should be installed place where the equipment is expected to be damaged by flooding a valve room where electricity is not supplied it is installed in a place where there is a risk of leakage of drainage pump due to submersion"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892658-A", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "to provide about one inch ponding in the stone distribution beds overlying the 11 200 square foot of sand filter surface 2000 gallons of clarified wastewater should be derived at each dose"}, {"pat_id": "US-5536411-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "demineralized water is removed from the demineralization unit 60 and transported via pipeline 48 to flood water storage tank 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_19", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a plurality of downflow biological water treatment filters each filter having a variable level an inflow into the top of the filter and an outflow from the base of the filter the filter comprising a locking the outlet valve from the first filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the filter b opening the backwash fresh water valve of the selected first filter c starting the backwash pump d automatically checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level f flushing the selected first filter to release the trapped gas from the filter g next closing the outlet valve from the selected filter and then opening the backwash fresh water valve to the selected filter h closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the selected first filter i opening the outlet valve from the selected first filter j repeat steps d to i successively for each additional filter where the next successive filter in steps d to g of the previous order is a subsequent step d a first filter selected from f k flushing the last selected filter l turning off the backwash water pump m opening the outlet valve from the finally selected filter n closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the finally selected filter and o maintaining the inlet valve open in steps a to n"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "flood pumping stations are usually integrated in the relief structure and have the task of lifting the accumulation target in the channel crossing inflow water from mixed or rainwater channels in the flood on the flood above the critical flood mark of the receiving water to prevent flooding in the drainage area of the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "to prevent the possible torque perpendicular to the flow direction 10 the forced plates 32 engage laterally in the guide slot 12 of the abutment 30 and reduce the possible torque of the lifting platform 17 when lowering perpendicular to the flow direction 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention provides a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a temperature lower than the preset temperature water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 and at the same time water is supplied into the rainwater storage tank 200 by the bypass pipe 620 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 .the present invention proposes a rainwater storage structure for a road and a rainwater storage method using the same which can prevent urban flood damage caused by localized heavy rain due to climate change and distortion of the water circulation system due to overdevelopment of urban areas.figure 1 below illustrates an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "para_472", "text": "after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring suggests a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a structure that is coupled to a conveyance belt for conveying contaminants to the outside on the rear side of the lifting bar the underwater pump connected to the conveyor belt constitutes a submerged pump at the lower end of the purifier box to remove the particulate contaminants remaining in the inside of the lifting jacket when lifting the particulate contaminants floating on the upper end of the booster box a pipeline coupled with the submersible pump an underwater pump for completely removing fine contaminants introduced into the purifier box by using a water injection nozzle formed at an end of a pipe connected to the pipeline and a discharge control valve coupled to a discharge control valve for controlling discharge of light organic matter molecules floating at the upper end of the purifier box at a downstream portion of the purifier box the process of cleansing polluted river water or contaminated rainwater using a river water or rain water purification system configured to purify polluted river water and contaminated rainwater by separate discharge is characterized in that the multifunctional water gate configured to store the river water to store river water or rainwater and to open the inflow adjusting gate constructed in the purifying box to inflow river water or rainwater into the inside of the purifying box and the air discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
