  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_703", "text": "the stream river reservoir lake lagoon or contaminated river water flowing in the vicinity of a dam characterized in that the purified water is naturally purified by floating the river water to the upper part of the eco friendly water purification device 200 used as the water purifier a nature friendly friendliness that naturally purifies polluted water while producing electricity by using an eco friendly water purification device that combines pollutants and soil water and purifies and cleans the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inflow amount and an upper and lower raising and lowering device 5810 is connected to adjust the pipe in the upper and lower direction according to the inflow level of river water that changes frequently and a rising discharge pipe 101 a falling discharge pipe 103 a right angled falling pipe 202 a water storage tank 201 a discharge amount control unit 203 a right angled falling pipe 202 and in a method of producing electricity by using the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 equipped with a power generation unit 33 a structure in which a water storage tank 8000 and a water purification promotion storage tank 11111 are constructed by dredging to a depth 20 to 600 times deeper than the surface 9000 of the soil layer constituting a river or stream and then the foundation concrete 800 is poured on the surface 9000 constituting a river or stream and the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 are constructed on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 and the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 is constructed to store river water on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 a structure in which an intermediate storage water inflow line 501 is formed to pump the stored water stored inside the upstream side of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 toward the rear side starting from the internal ground surface 9000 in the upstream direction of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 penetrating the middle part of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 to the rear part a structure in which a lower movement line 1919 is connected to the end of the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 to move the power generation water introduced through the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 downward a structure in which an entrance 1332 used for inspecting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "bethridge on ca transferred to the inflowing solvent before entering the thus heat exchanger 925 preheated the water and reduced the energy requirements of the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101102443-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present application as a means for solving the above problems as a water treatment method for obtaining purified water suitable for drinking water or industrial water for the target water selected from the treated water selected from river river water ground water wastewater treatment plant after pretreatment of the water to be treated in a sulphate denitrification tank or an ultrasonic electrolysis tank an ozone containing water is made and supplied to a high precision filtration tank to remove residual contaminants while passing through the filter bed of the biofilm separation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101161857-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the driver sitting in the driver s seat 2 to drive directly the conventional sludge removing device has a brush to sweep the sludge stack therein and connected to the suction hose 3 in the upper center of the sludge removing device and it is provided in a structure having an outlet to float the sludge deposit deposited on the river bottom by sweeping the sludge deposit on the bottom surface through a brush that is rotated by a motor and the suspended sludge laminate is connected to the suction hose 3 and the outlet port"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4538604-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "since the difference in electrical conductivity is a value proportional to the amount of organic matter present in the water sample it is possible to detect contamination of harmful organic matter by monitoring this difference"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas c