otection casting frame a terminal box and a lifting bolt a terminal box cover a rear rotating shaft support a rear reinforcing plate a gap a fan cover or a protective cover a rotor core and a stator core with stator windings and are connected and connected and underground passage flood prevention a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7363875-B2", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "further the place where the chemical is added is not particularly limited and may be any place in the cooling water system for example a blowing means a watering means a pit a make up water supply means a chemical injection means a circulation waterway a transfer pump a heat exchanger etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7363875-B2", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "in the open circulation cooling water system 1 water containing the component a copolymer and the component b maleic acid polymer is transferred from the pit 15 to the heat exchanger 30 via the circulation waterway 20 by the transfer pump 21"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the soil removed by the soil damper 100 is picked up through the obstacle receiver 8 and the impurity conveying conveyor not shown and then transported to the outside.1 tributary cloth 2 waterway entrance 3 waterway 4 drainage pumping station 5 drain pump 5a winch motor 6 hydrograph 7 main stream 8 container receiver 9 waterway exit 10a upper fixed frame part 10b lower movable frame part 11 connecting shaft 13 roller guide rail 13a upper guide rail 13b lower guide rail 14 roller chain 15 blocking plate 16a drive sprocket 16b lower guide roller 17 roller chain drive motor 21 pulling wire take up roller 22 pull wire 23 drive sprocket 24 take up roller 25 chain 26 winding roller drive motor 27 28 support block 29 limit switch 30 control unit 31 internal level sensor 40 auxiliary screen member"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7456522-B1", "para_id": "para_111", "text": "further the place where the chemical is added is not particularly limited and may be any place in the cooling water system such as a water sprinkling means a pit a make up water supply means a chemical injection means a circulation waterway a transfer pump a heat exchanger etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7456522-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "then it returns to the open cooling tower 10 via the circulation waterway 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101355194-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "hydraulic and rotary vibration dampers are commercially installed to prevent the above problems but when a large amount of debris suddenly floats upstream from the upstream of the waterway the vibration damper fails to handle or breaks down due to overload"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102560238-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it solves the problem of the drainage pump malfunctioning as it falls off while descending to the stage effectively separating impurities attached to the rake and configuring the main screen and the potential screen of the damper to be lifted at the same time so that the inflow water flows smoothly when the waterway is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "para_472", "text": "after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring suggests a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
