  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100402289-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "there was no deterioration of the treated water or efficiency of the wind pressure and air volume of the blower 15b and only the contamination of the membrane increased resulting in a shortening of the membrane life due to membrane contamination such as a decrease in the amount of treated water.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art the flow control and the aeration and membrane separation function can be performed at the same time in the aeration and membrane separation tank facility is minimized hollow fiber membrane of the aeration and membrane separation tank it is protected by this separate facility to remove the metering tank and sedimentation tank at the same time to prevent contamination of the hollow fiber membrane and the waste water to be transported to each tank is made by the natural discharge the transfer pump is removed to reduce the manufacturing cost of the device it is an object of the present invention to provide a wastewater treatment method and apparatus for reducing power usage costs"}, {"pat_id": "US-5160435-A", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "suitable thrust bearings 34 and stabilizing bearings 36 are included to provide for ease of rotation and to minimize wear during any rocking motion that may occur during high wind conditions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413569-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "because it is installed on the ground due to the weakness of the material that is weak in insulation and sound insulation of general concrete a separate insulation construction is required to wind the heating wire or install the insulation to prevent freezing of the motor pump"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1350028-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an electrically operated lift pump 52 conveys the brackish water via the raw water lift pipe 54 the rotary union 26 and the storage tank 27 to the pressure pump 20 in the nacelle 22"}, {"pat_id": "US-9024461-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "according to this conception the present invention provides a tidal energy seawater desalination system characterized in that it comprises a tidal energy power device a seawater evaporation tower and a steam condensation tower in which the seawater evaporation tower is configured with a vacuum pump which connects with a power output shaft of the tidal energy power device such that the tidal energy power device is capable of driving the vacuum pump to work the vacuum pump connecting the seawater evaporation tower via pipelines the output end of the vacuum pump connecting the steam condensation tower via pipelines and the steam condensation tower connecting a fresh water receiver via pipelines"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "while the present invention has been particularly shown and described with reference to exemplary embodiments thereof it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed exemplary embodiments but on the contrary is intended to cover various modifications and equivalent arrangements included within the spirit and scope of the appended claims.10 water circulation system 20 water circulation device 21 floating frame 22 wind blade 23 buoyant body 24 solar panel 25 housing 25a inner space 26 gear device 27 cold water jetting portion 27a cold water induction pipe 27b cold water nozzle 28 motor 29 hot water jetting part 29a hot water induction pipe 29b hydrothermal nozzle 30 impeller 31 expansion contraction tube 33 first sensor part 35 second sensor part 37 fixed wire 37a anchor 41 pump 43 freezing part 45 heating section 47 purge control section 49 battery 51 circulation line 52 block holder 52a 52b horizontal rod 53 cutting block 53a upper inclined surface 53b lower inclined surface 53c fitting end portion 55 55a inward gear 55b traveling groove 57 underwater motor 57b drive shaft 57c drive gear 59 59a height holding holder 59b receiving arm 59c roller bearing 59d 