75", "text": "therefore the purpose of this invention is to provide power and equipment for collection in an economical and environmentally friendly manner by providing a renewable energy power generation device which is the main component of the present invention and a suction pump suction pipe and storage facility connected thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102435204-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "when it reaches the top an overflow pipe that discharges the treated water located at the top to the outside of the measuring tank 2 is installed the oxygen supply means 5 is a main pipe 51 and blowing means 52 installed on the inlet side of the main pipe 51 to blow wind into the main pipe 51 branch pipe 53 branching at least two from the main pipe 51 each outlet communicating with each bioreactor 1 and an opening rate adjusting means 54 installed on the branch pipe 53 to adjust the opening rate inside the branch pipe 53 the blowing means 52 includes a blower 521 blower for blowing wind into the main pipe 51 and an rpm adjusting means 522 for adjusting the amount of oxygen flowing into the main pipe 51 by adjusting the number of revolutions per unit time of the blower 521 in the measuring tank 2 the dissolved oxygen concentration sensing means 4 ph sensing means 21 mlss sensing means 22 orp sensing means 23 temperature according to the control signal of the control unit 6 a cleaning means 27 for cleaning the contaminants attached to the surface of the sensing means 24 is additionally mounted the washing means 27 uses antifoam water as washing water to remove contaminants in the upper and lower portions of the vortex prevention wall fitting groove 28 a female side sine wave groove 29a processed in the form of a sine wave is processed the upper and lower portions of both ends of the vortex prevention wall 26 are processed in the form of a sine wave and a sine wave groove 29b on the male side engaged with the sine wave groove 29a on the female side is processed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102435204-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the dissolved oxygen concentration sensing means 4 in the measuring tank 2 the ph sensing means 21 the mlss sensing means 22 the orp sensing means 23 and the temperature sensing means 24 are included in the measurement tank 2 it is installed at an angle of 35 to 75 degrees from the horizontal plane to accurately measure the water quality of the treated water sample and to remove the suspended substances on the surface naturally"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "therefore any water lines exposed to outside temperatures including any water line runs inside the heated interior 206 that may be subject to freezing temperatures are protected and warmed by the circulating warming loops"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "reasonable shielding of the fresh water tank 12 from wind chill effects and or providing some insulation will increase efficiency of the warming system 50 and reduce pump 16 and water heater 14 cycling"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_173", "text": "103 may be located at other points in the water line run including the area near water pump 16 if warmed by the warming system 50 is required"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4931039-B2", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "measurement procedure the procedure for measuring the degree of contamination of raw water by the water quality monitoring apparatus shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101780266-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "as described above the method of reducing the amount of sludge of a wastewater dehydrating sludge using the jar drum type sludge reducing apparatus and the jar drum type sludge reducing apparatus in which the blades of the present invention are installed is characterized in that the high temperature fermenting microorganism ty em and a ceramic ball serving as a swelling fire can be supplied to facilitate the reduction of dehydrated sludge by smooth supply of temperature and oxygen and the high temperature heat and moisture inside the drum type drum body can be supplied to the blowing air pressure and the high temperature heat and moisture gathered on the upper part of the drum type drum body by the convection phenomenon can be recovered by a hot air blower and reused thereby saving energy.1"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2486988-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "from the de 100 28 41 it is known to provide a hydroelectric power plant as a block like structural unit with a cylindrical basic shape which stands on the ground surface or in the terrain is wholly or partially admitted in order to make irrespective of natural terrain topographies and natural water potentials artificially exploitable hydropower"}]</data>
