sing the basic concept of the present invention defined in the following claims also fall within the scope of the present invention.g1 landfill layer g2 cover layer 1 leachate recovery section 11 leachate plate 111 leachate channel 12 blocking member 13 leachate drain 2 leachate purification unit 21 leachate inlet line 22 purification unit 211 purification body 211a 1st body 211b 1st purification space 211c 2nd body 211d 2nd purification space 222 ceramic filter 223 1st activated carbon layer 224 2nd activated carbon layer 225 zeolite layer 226 silica sand layer 227 compartment filter 23 purification storage 231 storage space 24 natural stone 25 heating section 3 landfill gas recovery section 31 gas pipe 311 through hole 32 flow pipe 33 landfill gas purification unit 34 storage tank 35 landfill gas pump 36 control valve 4 high temperature sterilization unit 41 steam generator 42 storage unit connection line 43 steam line 44 steam pump 5 uv sterilization section 51 substrate section 52 uv ray generation unit 6 dust suppression unit 61 spray line 62 drum 63 spraying unit 64 supply pipe 65 spray pump 7 wheel washing unit 71 tunnel section 711 car wash area 711a entrance 711b exit 72 lower wash section 73 side wash section 74 rear wash section 741 hinge block 742 shaft 743 drive motor 744 spray pipe 744a vertical pipe 744b horizontal pipe 75 front wash section 76 wash water supply storage unit 77 sterilization wash unit 78 dry car wash unit 79 car wash water recovery unit 8 pedestrian safety section 8a pedestrian safety passage 81 outer structure 811 entrance 82 frame section 821 pedestrian passage 83 roof 84 blocking 85 1st rail section 86 2nd rail section 87 frame drive unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the non circulating non discharge manure treatment method for purifying the manure and sewage discharged from the toilet the manure treatment method comprises the steps of installing a flush toilet in the toilet the sewage and manure from the flush toilet anaerobic storage tank 10 anaerobic digestion filtering the treated water while treating nitrogen phosphorus and the like which are physically and biologically organic suspended solids and eutrophication agents in the aerobic bioreactor 20 and treating the treated water in the flow regulating tank 30 storing in the anaerobic state of the treated water and stabilizing the stored treatment water while the waste water is sprayed onto the wood chip layer by the water spray nozzle in the organic decay reaction tank 40 while the manure and sewage flows through the adsorption adsorption to the wood chip layer decomposing and removing the organic substances and various suspended substances contained in the step of discharging the leachate the pump well 46 operating a transfer pump that operates when a predetermined water level is reached while storing water removing organic components and nitrogen phosphorus color odor and the like physically and biologically from the advanced treatment tank 50 by contact aeration with the media physically filtration of the discharged water storing the treated water in the second flow rate adjusting tank 60 and stabilizing the stored treated water organic suspended solids remaining in the treated water passing through the wood chip layer and nitrogen phosphorus decomposing the chromaticity odor in the bioreactor 70 and then removing the leachate storing the treated water in the pump well 77 operating the transfer pump when the water level reaches a certain value decolorizing the treated water discharging while discoloring in the disinfection filtration tank 80 storing the treated water in the treated water storage tank 90 and supplying the stored treated water to the toilet and excessively introduced the excess water to the outside jidoe comprises a step of output the rainwater storage tank is installed on the roof of the manure treatment device and rainwater flows into the treatment water storage tank through a pipe and an electric shutoff valve is installed between the rainwater storage tank and the treatment water storage tank so that the water level of the treatment water storage tank is set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102724384-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of apartments 33 are installed in the space between a plant factory 41 and another plant factory 41 and the road surface of the access road 15 and the rooftop of the apartment 33 are installed at the same height the upper part of the rooftop of the apartment 33 and the rooftop of the plant factory 41 are connected to each other to install a hollow plate shaped building an emergency shelter 09 and a cultivation space for plants 11 are installed on the upper surface of the hollow plate building and a building formation part in which led lighting 07 is installed on the upper part of the cultivation space a number of water tanks 29 are installed in the outer underground area outside the outer perimeter of the pit a wastewater tank 96 and a sewage tank 97 are installed in a location larger than the installation diameter of the water tank 29 and deeper than the depth of the bottom surface of the pit a water generator 23 is installed on the ground surface with a larger installation diameter than the water tank 29 and a dome outer installation section in which graphene ropes 21 are installed in a net shape on the water generator 23 installed on the opposite side of the water generator 23"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1960608-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "via a feed line 4 a waste water is introduced into the container 2 and conveyed via a drain line 5 in the form of a pressure line via a backflow level 6 to drain from there into a sewer system 7"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 sand rinse device 62 coarse aggregate rinse device 63 washing waste water evaporation device 64 belt conveyor 65 sand supply device 66 rinse water spray device 67 cleaning waste water receiving tank 68 drive roller 68a shaft 69 driven roller 69a shaft 70 conveyor belt 71 support roller 72 guide plate 74 belt conveyor 75 coarse aggregate supply device 76 rinsing water spray device 77 cleaning waste water receiving tank 78 driving roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveyor belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 cleaning waste water discharge passage 84 cl