ormed in the valve body 111 an opening closing plate 117 installed in the valve body 111 to open and close the valve seat 116 a lifting and lowering rod 118 coupled to an upper end of the nut 117 and a nut box 119 screwed to the lifting and lowering rod 118 and an opening and closing drive means 120 for rotating the nut box 119 including the valve cap 112 includes an elevation guide portion 113 for vertically supporting the elevating and lowering rod 118 a rotation support portion 114 for rotatably supporting the nut box 119 and a reinforcing connecting portion 115 connecting the portion 113 and the rotation supporting portion 114 the opening and closing drive means 120 includes a drive motor 123 mounted on a motor mount 122 fixed to a support plate 121 integrally formed with the rotary support 114 and a driven gear 126 coupled to an upper end of the nut box 119 and engaged with the driving gear 125 the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 and the first and second sprinkler pipe flowmeters 410 and 420 are controlled by controlling the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 according to the detection signals of the water discharge pipes 510 and 520 and the discharge pipe flow meter 620 and a control means 700 the control means 700 includes a fire detector 710 installed on the building an input unit 720 for inputting the normal mode and the test mode a main opening closing valve sensor 730 for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve 110 the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and the 3 way valve 610 according to the fire detection signal of the fire detector 710 and the input signal of the input unit 720 the flow rate of the refrigerant is detected on the upstream side in accordance with the sensing signals of the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 the first and second sprinkler pipe flow meters 510 and 520 the drain pipe flow meter 620 it is possible to judge the abnormality of the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main water supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 to determine an abnormality position display command and an alarm command a control unit 740 for outputting a command to display the degree of opening of the main on off valve 110 a valve driver 750 for sending a driving signal to the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 and the three way valve 610 according to a control command of the controller 740 a display unit 760 for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the controller 740 and an alarm unit 770 for outputting an alarm according to an alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "US-10738603-B2", "para_id": "para_158", "text": "when wells are shut down for repairs or are put out of service due to contaminant discharges that exceed the maximum allowable concentrations mcls the wells can be off or non pumping for many days weeks months or even years"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014010-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the crushing mixer 10 is connected to a drive motor 13 and an inverter 14 for driving it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101227166-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "connected via a hose h to the connecting pipe 21 of the pipe pipe flange 20 installed at one end and the water flowing through the water inlet 31 through the water outlet 32 pipe line 1 1 a manifold 30 to be delivered to it a pump 40 which is operated by being supplied with power and is connected to the inlet 31 of the manifold 30 to continuously supply water block piping line hydraulic test integrated system including a pressure measuring device 50 installed between the outlet 32 and the hose h of the manifold 30 to measure the water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101227166-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "that need a hydraulic pressure test the test was carried out while moving to the block and after the test was completed the pipe pipe flange the hose the pressure gauge and the pump were stored in a separate place"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4087351-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "and according to this hydraulic pressure drive unit 13 as shown in fig.1 and fig.2 by operating the 2nd switching valve 37 the pressure water sent out from the pump 31 is made into the water softening apparatus 16 and the hydraulic cylinder apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102785581-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide a sterilizing water generator for livestock quarantine which comprises manufacturing the cover of the capillary cluster with an elastic material to absorb a certain amount of pressure energy of the pump and return it to the capillaries thereby spraying water at the same pressure regardless of the position of each capillary so that there is no change in the amount of oh radicals absorbed due to electrostatic spraying and the produced sterilizing water can be sprayed on livestock or fed directly to livestock to block the inflow of viruses through the respiratory tract.to this end one embodiment of the present invention comprises a plasma reactor having a grounding electrode plate connected to the electrode of a high voltage generator a capillary cluster separated from the plasma reactor comprises a plurality of capillaries extending to the plasma reactor and connected to the electrode of the high voltage generator when drinking water is supplied through a pump the capillary cluster diffuses water in the form of mist from each capillary into the interior of the plasma reactor and through electrostatic spraying mist containing oh radicals adheres to the grounding electrode plate in the form of droplets and is then collected in a sterilizing water tank and the pump has a feature in that the rotational speed is maintained constant through a hydraulic pressure gauge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the groundwater meter and the hydraulic pressure freeze protection device installed inside the upper ground water protection hole characterized in that to prevent freezing by draining into the well 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "64 a disk valve 66 for opening and closing the water passage 61a of the valve housing 61 is selectively installed while moving up and down and is elastic between the disk valve 66 and the elastic member support frame 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the time consuming problem is caused.the present invention is to actively solve the problems caused by the freezing of the ground water meter and the hydraulic pressure meter installed in the above described conventional ground water upper protection hole when the operation of the submersible motor pump stops the water supply line automatically shuts off the water supply line the problem of the present invention is to prevent backflow to the pumping device in the upper groundwater protection hole and to prevent freezing by draining the water remaining in the groundwater meter and the hydraulic meter which are components of the pumping device to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the present invention is a technique for branching and installing the drainage branch pipe on one side of the water supply pipe connecting the drainage control valve to the bottom of the drainage branch pipe connecting the residual water drainage pipe to the bottom of the drainage control valve take a look.according to the present invention when the operation of the submersible motor pump is stopped automatically by the water pipe to prevent the water flow back to the water pipe and at the same time draining the water remaining in the pumping device in the upper ground water protective device to the outside cold water pumping device it provides the effect of preventing the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which is a component of the components in advance and greatly reduces the time and manpower associated with checking or replacing the groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge as well as providing convenience of post management after construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in the case of the submersible motor pump 3 provided with a water supply pipe 20 groundwater meter 21 a branching pipe 22 for collecting water which is a component of the pumping device 5 installed inside the upper ground water protection hole 10 and underground water is left in the hydraulic pressure gauge 23 to cause freezing in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "on the other hand the present invention in the case of a general low cost submersible motor pump 3 is not provided with a check valve for preventing the backflow of water in the water supply pipe 12 is automatically prevented backflow and at the same time the stop of the pumping device 5 water remaining in the water supply pipe 20 the groundwater meter 21 the branching pipe 22 and the hydraulic pressure meter 23 which are components passes through the inside of the submersible motor pump 3 while passing through the water supply pipe 4 the total amount of water drained to 1 prevents freezing of the freezing wave thus eliminating the need for the electronic residual water automatic drainage device 50"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "according to one or more embodiments the variable speed high pressure pump that operates to push the pretreated water through the treatment block 260 may be controlled by monitor 226 and may comprise any pump suitable to generate the hydraulic pressure necessary to push the water through the one or more membrane pressure vessels"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "therefore the first passage 851a is opened and closed by the ball valve 855a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "the drive motor 44a operates the hydraulic pump 42a and the hydraulic pump 42a includes the first and second piston pumps 30a and 31a the drive motor 29a of the introduction device 20a and the first and second hydraulic pumps 42a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041191-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "underwater motor pump and pumping device installed inside the upper surface of the ground water protection pump during the freezing of the groundwater water pipe characterized in that it further comprises a hydraulic pressure release device 50 for releasing the water pressure while forcibly opening the ball 41 2 component protector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041191-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the submersible motor pump in the state that the normal water can not be delivered to the water tank due to the freezing of the water pipe the overload pressure is generated as the water pump continues to be sustained the load on the submersible motor pump is heavily loaded and the life may be significantly reduced or damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101759711-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "0563988summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above circumstances and an object of the present invention is to provide a shredding unit in which a plurality of blades are radially provided and new towing elements for replacement are connected successively the sewage pipe is crushed and the new sewer pipe is automatically replaced in succession while being moved using a wire driven as a pulling unit that intermittently pulls together with union and release the present invention provides a sewer pipe replacement device which can reduce the unit cost and replace the sewer pipe can shorten the construction period and reduce the cost.summary of the invention it is an object of the present invention to provide a replacement apparatus for a non drilling sewage pipe in which an old or damaged synthetic resin drain pipe buried in the ground for drainage of sewage or wastewater is replaced with a new one a crushing unit provided with a number of blades radially in a conical body and provided with new traction elements for replacement and a pair of upper and lower actuators arranged in parallel on the base and reciprocating forward and backward using hydraulic pressure a pulling unit having first and second gripping elements which are mounted on each of the fixed and movable stages and which are tied and released in a reciprocating manner depending on whether a frictional force acts or not wherein the first gripping element is adapted to move forward and backward in the reciprocating motion of the traction unit and the second gripping element is repeatedly held to maintain the position of the wire pulled back while the wire is retracted the wire is intermittently moved and the old sewing pipe is crushed by using the crushing unit so that replacement work can be performed easily"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100861685-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in this case the liquid chlorine injector may include a liquid chlorine tank in which liquid chlorine is stored a venturi pipe connecting the liquid chlorine tank and the final treatment pipe a chlorine injection pump installed to inject liquid chlorine into the liquid chlorine tank and a chlorine input control means for receiving a rotational speed of the water wheel rotary blade of the non powered contaminant remover and providing the same as a feedback signal to the chlorine input pump to control the amount of chlorine input through the chlorine input pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition there is a fear of secondary contamination such as microbial growth due to the stagnation of the treated water in the storage tank it was necessary to increase the processing capacity of the process to be treated at the rear end of the storage tank.the present invention was devised to solve the above mentioned problems and does not install a reservoir and does not apply a brake to the flow of treated water and does not require an additional pump and does not additionally install a reservoir and a pump in the middle of a water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore by controlling the pump 10 and the valve 33 installed on the raw water inlet side of the membrane filtration unit 100 the advanced oxidation tank 210 activated carbon adsorption constituting the residual contamination removal unit 200 installed at the rear end by adjusting the hydraulic pressure in the tank 220 and the disinfection tank 230 it is possible to smoothly perform each water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the heat exchange which takes place in the exchanger 20 at the upper portion of the tank melts the upper portion of the ice block in the zones a and b so that pure water may be withdrawn from the zone a at the outlet 24"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_95", "text": "according to one or more embodiments the variable speed high pressure pump that operates to push the pretreated water through the treatment block 260 may be controlled by monitor 226 and may comprise any pump suitable to generate the hydraulic pressure necessary to push the water through the one or more membrane pressure vessels"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102186791-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore in this embodiment the compression portion 200 formed in a cylinder structure descends along the outer circumferential surface of the grouting casing 10 by the hydraulic pressure formed by the hydraulic pump to compress the shielding portion 100 thereby causing the expansion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306445-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the pipeline expansion device 1 includes an expander 11 for reshaping the deformation of the pipeline a a hydraulic electric pump 12 for generating hydraulic pressure to supply the expander 11 it is composed of a hydraulic line 13 for supplying the hydraulic pressure to the expander 11 and the hydraulic pressure is recovered to the hydraulic electric pump 12 the pipeline image photographing apparatus 2 includes a cctv camera 21 for inspecting the state inside the pipeline a and monitoring the rehabilitation work with the expander 11 it is composed of a rotating device unit 22 having a circumferential rotation device 221 to enable the cctv camera 21 to rotate in the circumferential direction and a vertical rotation device 222 to enable angle adjustment up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100899657-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "on the other hand a check valve 170 may be provided at one side of the pressure cylinder 152 to block the back flow of the produced water that has passed through the discharge port 145 of the valve housing 142.the reverse osmosis wastewater treatment backpressure pump according to the present invention configured as described above is configured such that the piston is easily moved in the storage space of the valve housing by the operation of a pressurizing cylinder that receives pneumatic pressure or hydraulic pressure to overcome the water pressure applied to the filter portion thereby providing a pressure capable of easily reversing the production water"}, {"pat_id": "US-3871792-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pump system comprising a pump an electric motor in drive connection with said pump a service line a service valve in said service line a pressure switch in electric circuit with said motor and a control valve assembly comprising a valve housing having an input opening for flow connection thereto of said pump a discharge opening for flow connection to said service line and a main flow passageway interconnecting said input opening and said discharge opening a main valve spanning said main passageway means biasing said main valve toward closing position a first auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end with said main passageway on the downstream side of said main valve and terminating in an opening in said housing for hydraulic pressure connection to said pressure switch means coupling said pressure switch to said valve housing at said last opening a pilot valve assembly spanning said first auxiliary passageway and including a valve seat and a valve means normally biasing said pilot valve toward open condition and a second auxiliary passageway said second auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end to said main passageway on the upstream side of said main valve and terminating at said pilot valve in pressure opposing relationship to said biasing means whereby development of hydraulic pressure against said valve in excess of any opposing pressure against said valve will close said valve and block said first auxiliary passageway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "even in the cold weather in winter it provides a useful effect to prevent the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which are components of the well facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "on the other hand when the operation of the submersible motor pump 4 is stopped there is no further groundwater flow in the water supply pipe 10 the water pressure applied to the piston valve 40 is released and the piston valve 40 is the elastic member 60 the groundwater remaining in various well facilities such as the groundwater meter 6 the hydraulic pressure gauge 8 the branching pipe 7 for the ground water by automatically opening the drainage passage 52 while moving upwards as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101932393-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in order to obtain a stable amount of treated water w1 it is necessary to increase the pressure of the supply pump for supplying the for treatment water w so that not only the power consumption is increased there is a problem that the risk of leakage from the ion device becomes high"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6686893-B2", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "the measured value deviates from the predicted value control target due to the unintended start or end of water use an increase in the amount of water leakage water theft a pump or pipe failure or a hydraulic pressure measurement device failure or physical failure"}, {"pat_id": "US-10352505-B2", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "a smaller scale rupture that does not result in an uncommanded pump trip but does satisfy similar criteria as set against steady state empirically determined normal hydraulic pressure flowrate or combinational analysis profile behavior"}]</data>
