  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101776163-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "on the other hand in the case where flooding occurs due to pipe rupture or flood of the pump room in which the water treatment pump motor 100 is installed the remote controller 200 is installed in a proper position of the pump room in which the water treatment pump motor 100 is installed the immersion detection signal detected by the installed immersion sensor 230 is transmitted to the instrument control apparatus 100 so that the operation of the water treatment pump motor 110 being driven by the instrument control apparatus 100 is stopped the controller 100 causes the immersion sensing signal to be wirelessly transmitted to the wireless terminal 300 so that the immersion status is displayed on the wireless terminal 300"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to the automatic detection system for small scale septic tank abnormality detection disclosed in patent document 1 even if a failure of the septic tank blower is detected by an abnormal current and an abnormality in treated water quality can be detected by the water quality sensor the contents of the septic tank abnormality aeration failure mainly due to blower failure stop aeration failure due to piping damage leakage due to damage cracking of tank body flooding in tank due to malfunction of discharge pump flooding in tank due to abnormal discharge destination etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9771712-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "a sump pump connects directly to the sewer drain pipe using a drain pipe coupler or is located adjacent thereto within the tank where overflow from the drain triggers the sump pump to discharge fluid and sewage into an outlet pipe and out of the basement to prevent flooding and contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for underground passage flood prevention is configured to supply power to each pump using the marine hydroelectric power generator 213 facilities to prevent underground passage flooding in the above underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment the hydraulic power generator 213 is installed a device 218 for pushing a rotary shaft under an upper rotary shaft 217 is positioned and a stator coil 219 a stator frame 220 and a central stator 221 are positioned at the bottom of the device 218 for pushing the rotary shaft and an electric wire 71 is inserted into the gap of the central stator 221 and a fan 195 is positioned at the bottom of the central stator 221 and a braking device ring 223 a brake jack 224 and a low speed rotary shaft 225 are positioned at the bottom of the fan 195 and a low speed cooler 222 is positioned at the bottom of the low speed rotary shaft 225 and a rotating electromagnet rotor coil formed along the circumference of the rotary shaft 198 and an armature coil for a non rotating coil generator installed along the circumference of the rotor coil and a lower end of the rotary shaft 198 the conventional marine hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment which is provided with several waterwheels and turbines 267 for setting up positions turbine rotating shafts 227 casings 141 vane pumps guide vanes 142 and impellers 228 supplies power to each pump of the hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment to prevent underground passage flooding and is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flooding prevention and flood control equipment the vertical multi stage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the above underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is as follows according to the control block diagram and the vertical multi stage pump operation method of the bf model the pump power 272 and the control power 273 are separated and distinguished and the emergency operation sequence circuit 274 of the control power 273 is connected to the dc power spray supply circuit 275 and the m c drive signal contact output circuit 279 and the output circuit terminal and then the m c switch contact of the pump power 272 and the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the contacts that enable each pump to be operated in emergency mode and at the same time the dc power supply circuit 275 of the control power 273 provides the input setting of the diac switch setting circuit 277 and the switch input circuit 58 to the micro control unit 276 and at the same time the led display circuit 278 and the drive signal contact output circuit 279 outputs a signal and the motor overload signal input circuit 280 is installed so that the circuit contacts of the unit 276 and the pump power supply 272 tip are connected to the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the inverter operation data input output circuit 281 is formed as a circuit for mutual input and output between the inverter 47 circuit and the micro control unit 276 and the discharge pressure transmitter 284 is connected to the pressure detection circuit 282 and then the circuit 282 is input set to the unit 276 and then the suction discharge pressure switch 285 is connected to the external status input circuit 283 and then the input circuit 283 is input set to the micro control unit 276"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the 