rator 213 is inverter 47 and inverter vio access point and internet network vertical multistage pump control server and monitor to pump control board or tagger winch control box and short range wireless communication antenna to short range wireless communication device wireless communication control module and display to electronic control device adc and switch input circuit to electronic control device mcu and electronic control device diac overcurrent breaker brake is connected to power supply to display screen and analog input and digital input are operated by hand to control on off of each pump main switch button and auxiliary switch button to configure vertical multistage pump operation method inside main body 1 of underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment in addition to the above mentioned vertical multi stage pump turbine pump 140 diaphragm pump vane pump or guide vane and propeller pump screw pump plunger pump axial plunger pump radial plunger pump and jet pump 157 are provided and are connected to an introduction pipe and a water supply port or a fire prevention and disaster prevention pipe line 168 and a water discharge port 169 and are connected to a limit switch or a limit switch and a power motor body 192 is provided with a hood and a snap ring a fan and a body frame a body front reinforcing plate a rotor assembly on a rotating shaft a stator assembly on a front rotating shaft support a motor protection casting frame a terminal box and a lifting bolt a terminal box cover a rear rotating shaft support a rear reinforcing plate a gap a fan cover or a protective cover a rotor core and a stator core with stator windings and are connected and connected and underground passage flood prevention a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "according to claim 1 wherein the high concentration reservoir is formed in the upper side of the plurality of odor discharge pipes for sucking the internal odor the plurality of odor discharge pipes are integrated into one odor main pipe extending to the outside one side of the washing water the sewage pit for collecting the sewage generated by the concave is formed the sewage pit is located in the sewage pit is disposed to pump the sewage collected in the sewage pit to the outside to discharge to the sewage treatment plant characterized in that the initial excellent pollution reduction and multifunctional storage systems for urban flooding prevention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "multifunctional storage system to reduce initial rain pollution and prevent urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "there is a place where a drainage facility should be installed place where the equipment is expected to be damaged by flooding a valve room where electricity is not supplied it is installed in a place where there is a risk of leakage of drainage pump due to submersion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "therefore in the non power source immersion prevention system of the present invention the opening and closing valve 300 is automatically opened by the access port 200 that ascends and descends by the water level when the flooding occurs in the manhole and the water is flooded in the manhole by the suction force generated through the ejector 500 water can be rapidly discharged to the outside through the suction pipe 400 to prevent corrosion or breakdown of the facility by flooding and it is possible to immediately cope with the flooding by the person without any operation the installation cost is reduced as compared with the drainage method using the conventional pump and the pause time is set during the operation by the amount of water flowing into and discharged from the water collection container 630 provided at the upper portion of the water inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "US-8725301-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "upon the internal clock timing a complete fill period five seconds for the preferred embodiment without the top switch 240 dropping but no more than 15 minutes to prevent running the pump dry and to prevent flooding in the event of a leak the efc 100 shuts off the fill pump 400 and waits until the next signal from the timer 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063307-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "not only burnout occurred but there was a problem of property damage due to flooding due to drainage.the present invention is to solve the above problems the air is compressed in the inside of the air pressure tank by the suction force of the drain pump during the drainage process was compressed in the air pressure tank when the water in the drain pipe back flow after the completion of drainage as the air expands it supports the check valve for preventing the backflow to prevent water hammer and at the same time to discharge the end of the drain pipe to constitute a water collecting tank drainage device equipped with a water hammer prevention air pressure tank to remove the foreign matter caught in the filter net of the drain pump biodegradation that is sucked together with water by suction power of the drainage pump when the drainage pump is installed by installing a vacuum netting connecting socket to which the vacuum gauge is connected to the suction end of the drainage pump and a plurality of foreign matter crushing blades are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100949384-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "dirt and trash are mixed and if it is left unattended the pump will be damaged or the pumping function will be significantly weakened and these wastes will block the waterways causing problems such as flooding due to poor drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102464092-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "due to the interruption there is a high risk of facility flooding and sewage leakage and water quality deterioration problems frequently occurred due to the occurrence of capitalization due to over aeration due to continuous aeration time maintenance during leakage.republic of korea patent registration 10 1579488no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101355194-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "hydraulic and rotary vibration dampers are commercially installed to prevent the above problems but when a large amount of debris suddenly floats upstream from the upstream of the waterway the vibration damper fails to handle or breaks down due to overload"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1960608-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "this condition may occur even if the pump fails"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101132083-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "since wastes are mixed if they are left unattended the pump may be damaged or the pumping function may be significantly weakened and these wastes may block the waterways causing drainage due to heavy rains causing flooding"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "flood pumping stations are usually integrated in the relief structure and have the task of lifting the accumulation target in the channel crossing inflow water from mixed or rainwater channels in the flood on the flood above the critical flood mark of the receiving water to prevent flooding in the drainage area of the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101980335-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided an all surface circulation injection device for flooding a water surface through a buoyant body an air intake pipe for sucking outside air and a suction pipe composed of a flexible hose a circulating pump for sucking and discharging the deep water and the outside air by extending the suction port to the deep layer an oil leakage preventing rope used to be hung on hooks formed on the buoyant body a filtration device which is composed of a filtration net that is laid on the outer circumferential surface of the suction pipe to filter suspended substances or foreign matter to prevent clogging of the suction port"}]</data>
</edge>
