  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the present invention describes an automated with a hybrid power capacity connected to an electrical current or a photovoltaic power facility for wastewater treatment by oxidative and biological degradation of the liquids originated from a sewage installation utilizing aerobic digestion which is comprised of one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a source of wastewater to one or more rough solid crushing pump pits 2 comprised by an electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a float type level sensor 4 where the activation of the electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid shredder pusher 5 allows it to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 which has the purpose of removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system with air presence consisting of an electrical submersible pump 8 that through an eductor aerator 9 oxygenates the water contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the operation of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a series of sensors a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 for monitoring and controlling the oxygen in the aeration process and a suspended solids sensor 12 for the biological sludge and microorganisms generation which are used for the organic matter degradation the mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 which has a screen 14 to guarantee the passage of only water to a sedimentation and mud separation tank 15 in which the separation of the liquid phase and the solid phase occurs through a process of sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is the water with dejected and clarified organic material while the solid phase is the sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has an electrical submersible pump 16 at its bottom that allows the recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the result of the liquid phase of the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 which has a screen 18 to guarantee the passage of only water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium hypochlorite 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 has sensors in order to automate the operation of this and guarantee the quality of the resulting water a ph sensor 23 a suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 likewise the disinfection tank 19 considers a screen system 21 that is utilized to prevent the passage of solids to the final filtration process alongside with an electro valve 37 that eliminates solid materials that may have passed to this tank the disinfected water in the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by an electrical submersible pump 22 and a connection hose 26 that is connected to a filtration tank 27 which contains gravel 28 with different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is obtained furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for its continuous use during the night where the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that operates the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to providing it during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains its continuous operation the charge controller allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for its dynamic graphs display in the control panel 32 and sends it to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 composed by at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and its nearby surroundings this lamps are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamps have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain periods of time and or real time video of everything that is happening around the facility and with this a visual monitoring of it finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 that allow it to be transported from one place to another easily and it is mounted in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100755486-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "this may eventually have the effect of preventing the occurrence of chemical precipitation to prevent the blockage of the membrane aperture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101385841-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "therefore the treated water discharge device 300 of the present invention can completely block the mixed liquid and solids from flowing into the apparatus in the stirring aeration and settling steps"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0752222-Y2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "that is the sewage generated from the household is collected in the sewer pipe and the sewage pipe is inclined so that the sewage of other sewer pipes that have branched gradually are collected and gradually become a large sewer pipe and at the final end sewage was pumped up by a pressure pump sent into the sewage treatment tank and treated by decay and precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7364451-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "in this case the specified flow rate of the constant flow valve 13 can be reduced and as a result energy saving can be realized by using the pressurizing pump 21 with a smaller capacity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200317348-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the economic loss was inevitably large compared to the cost.therefore the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and by increasing the flow rate of the constant and water reducing the exposure time of the inner wall of the water pipe from the corrosives that activate the corrosion sediment contained in the constant and water its purpose is to provide a structure of water supply pipes with increased drainage which can minimize the likelihood of precipitation and economically realize the above effects"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2099716-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the medium is supplied above the maximum water level of the container and the medium has not yet reacted with the mp and therefore no precipitation occur in the pipe and also resulting in a minimum impact from precipitations on the bearings 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927629-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first step of depositing and removing heavy foreign matter from the introduced waste water through an immersion tank a second step of filtering and removing large foreign substances from the wastewater flowing into the screen tank through the sedimentation tank through the mesh a third step of constantly discharging wastewater introduced into the flow rate adjustment tank through the pump through the pump a fourth step of removing nitrate nitrogen from the wastewater discharged through the flow rate adjustment tank and introduced into the anaerobic tank through a denitrification reaction a fifth step of supplying oxygen to the treated water introduced into the aerobic tank from the anoxic tank to induce nitrification and phosphorus intake of organic substances in the treated water a sixth step of removing phosphorus by precipitation of iron ions precipitated through the electrolysis of the iron electrolysis unit in the treated water introduced into the fnr reactor from the aerobic tank by precipitation with phosphorus in the treated water a seventh step of depositing the foreign matter in the treated water introduced into the filtered water tank from the fnr reaction tank and discharging the filtered treated water through a pump an eighth step of removing organic matter from the filtered water tank through the aerobic microorganisms of the biofilm carrier filter a ninth step of storing the treated water introduced from the biofilm carrier filter in a backwash bath in the tenth step of disinfecting and discharged the treated water used in the backwash tank through the discharge tank in the wastewater treatment method to be treated through the biofilm carrier filter the treated water flowing through the inlet is directed upward through the microbubble generator to allow the treated water to pass through the biofilm carrier and the treated water passing through the biofilm carrier is moved upward through the micropores of the strainer and continuously filtered through the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102292971-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as the main body 10 and the groundwater 12 installed on one side of the main body 10 are filled with an amount of groundwater 12 set by the driving of the first pump 11 it is contaminated while passing through a plurality of segment filters 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a reaction tank for mixing the electrolytic decontamination electrolytic waste solution with a precipitation accelerator to produce a precipitate a filter unit connected to the reaction tank through a regeneration circulation line a regeneration return line and a regeneration circulation pump so as to be circulatable for separating the precipitate from the electrolysis waste liquid component detecting means for detecting components of the electrolytic waste liquid flowing into the reaction tank the regeneration circulation line and the regeneration return line a regeneration liquid storage tank connected to the regeneration return line and the regeneration discharge line and storing the regeneration electrolyte in which the precipitate is removed and and a first three way valve installed at a position where the regeneration return line and the regeneration discharge line are connected to flow the electrolytic waste liquid toward the reaction tank or the regeneration liquid storage tank the electrolytic waste liquid is repeatedly circulated between the reaction tank and the filter unit to remove the precipitate generated in the reaction tank from the filter unit and the regenerated electrolytic waste liquid is removed from the regeneration liquid storage tank and the component detection means has a sample discharge line in the reaction tank allows the sample discharged from the sample discharge line to be stored in the sample storage container the filter unit includes first and second filtering lines disposed in parallel between the regeneration circulation line and the regeneration return line and connected at both ends to an upstream side second three way valve and a downstream side third three way valve respectively first and second metal filters provided respectively in the first and second filtering lines for filtering precipitates from electrolytic waste liquid a first cleaning line connected between the first metal filter of the first filtering line and the third side three way valve on the downstream side to supply the washing water to the first metal filter in a direction opposite to the flow direction of the electrolytic waste liquid a second cleaning line connected between the second metal filter of the second filtering line and the third side three way valve on the downstream side for supplying the washing water to the second metal filter in a direction opposite to the flow direction of the electrolytic waste liquid a first washing discharging line connected between a first metal filter of the first filtering line and a second tri directional valve at an upstream side through a fourth three way valve to discharge washing wastewater that has passed through the first metal filter a second cleaning discharge line connected between a second three way valve on the upstream side of the second metal filter of the second filtering line by a fifth three way valve to discharge washing wastewater that has passed through the second metal filter a washing wastewater storage tank for storing washing wastewater discharged to the first and second cleaning discharge lines and and a waste water evaporation processing unit for evaporating the washing waste water from the washing waste water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a method for producing electrolytic decontamination comprising a reaction tank for mixing a electrolytic decontamination electrolytic waste solution with a precipitation accelerator to produce a precipitate a filter unit connected to the reaction tank through a regeneration circulation line a regeneration return line and a regeneration circulation pump so as to be circulatable for separating the precipitate from the electrolysis waste liquid a regeneration liquid storage tank connected to the regeneration return line and the regeneration discharge line and storing the regeneration electrolyte in which the precipitate is removed and a first three way valve installed at a position where the regeneration return line and the regeneration discharge line are connected to flow the electrolytic waste liquid toward the reaction tank or the regeneration liquid storage tank wherein the electrolytic waste liquid is repeated between the reaction tank and the filter unit the regeneration liquid is supplied to the regeneration liquid storage tank through the regeneration discharge line and the regeneration liquid is discharged from the regeneration return line first and second filtering lines disposed in parallel between the lines and having opposite ends connected to the upstream side second three way valve and the downstream side third three way valve respectively first and second metal filters provided respectively in the first and second filtering lines for filtering precipitates from electrolytic waste liquid a first cleaning line connected between the first metal filter of the first filtering line and the third side three way valve on the downstream side to supply the washing water to the first metal filter in a direction opposite to the flow direction of the electrolytic waste liquid a second cleaning line connected between the second metal filter of the second filtering line and the third side three way valve on the downstream side for supplying the washing water to the second metal filter in a direction opposite to the flow direction of the electrolytic waste liquid a first washing discharging line connected between a first metal filter of the first filtering line and a second tri directional valve at an upstream side through a fourth three way valve to discharge washing wastewater that has passed through the first metal filter a second cleaning discharge line connected between a second three way valve on the upstream side of the second metal filter of the second filtering line by a fifth three way valve to discharge washing wastewater that has passed through the second metal filter a washing wastewater storage tank for storing washing wastewater discharged to the first and second cleaning discharge lines and a waste water evaporation processing unit for evaporating the washing waste water in the washing waste water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102789712-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a brine tank 10 10 in which brine is stored at a certain level and sprayed through brine nozzles individually installed at a number of habitual freezing points a b c d a detection sensor 20 that detects the water level of brine stored in the brine tank 10 of each of the above points a central control unit 30 that manages information on the brine storage level through the above detection sensor 20 in order to transport brine stored in a brine tank 10 at a point where the amount of brine is relatively large to a point where the amount of brine is insufficient by the control of the central control unit 30 a brine guide pipe 40 through which brine stored in the brine tank 10 is withdrawn by the operation of a pump p a coupler 50 that is connected to the end of the brine guide pipe 40 and is connected to the transfer tank 110 of the brine transfer vehicle 100 a salt water supply system for road deicing spraying characterized in that the salt water transport tank 110 configured in the salt water transport vehicle 100 is provided with a plurality of bubble generators 111 on the bottom surface to prevent freezing or precipitation of salt water during the transport process an ultraviolet lamp 112 is provided on the top surface and a deterioration prevention layer 113 is formed on the inner wall surface to prevent deterioration of salt water during transport"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in order to prevent corrosion generated during the preheating of the organic matter containing waste liquid an appropriate neutralizing agent is added to the waste liquid and preheated under anoxic conditions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100370345-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "however the slurry waste liquid rotates because the concentration in the liquid tends to change due to natural sedimentation and because the impeller of the water level decreases the number of revolutions rises and the impeller of the stirrer 2 d is markedly worn by cavitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in the non point pollution backwash automation system that treats non point pollutants generated by precipitation including a pre treatment tank and a screen tank formed with a partition wall therebetween the pre treatment tank is connected to a pipe at the bottom of the partition wall at a predetermined height inside and overflows an advection pipe for supplying the raw water accommodated therein to the screen tank a drain door provided at the bottom of the bulkhead to open and close only in the direction of the pretreatment tank from the screen tank to discharge all remaining water in the screen tank to the pretreatment tank it is provided on the floor and consists of a drain pump for pumping the residual water accommodated in the pre treatment tank and the screen tank has a perforated panel to filter out foreign substances while the raw water flowing into the lower part through the advection pipe moves upstream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes con