t a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100518722-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the culture medium is supplied to the secondary aeration tank 16 while the culture medium circulates through the magnetic field of the magnet by the pump 32 and the blue water which is fed to the upper portion of the secondary precipitation tank 17 is sent to the oxidation tank 20 to peroxide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "oxides and phosphates generated to react to remove insoluble precipitate the blower 52 for supplying oxygen to the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 and the oxygen contained in the air introduced from the blower 52 an diffuser 51 for generating air bubbles to increase the speed of water transfer an electrolysis device 60 for electrolyzing iron or aluminum electrodes and an aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 by suction force"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "organic substances in the mixed solution introduced into the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 are removed by the metabolic activity of aerobic microorganisms present in the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 ammonia nitrogen and nitrite nitrogen is blower 52 it is oxidized to nitrate nitrogen by oxygen supplied by the phosphate and the phosphate reacts with an oxide produced by the electrolysis of the electrolysis module 61 in the electrolysis device 60 to precipitate and remove as an insoluble precipitate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101094321-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "s100 screen precipitation process s200 stationary precipitation process s300 continuous filtration process s400 soil improvement process 10 10 pressure pump 20 pressure filtration tank 21 inlet 23 outlet 24 discharge pipe 25 float discharge outlet 26 screw 27 closed tube 30 filter 31 filter hole 40 floating material removal means 41 wing anchor 42 wing to remove the float 43 rotation device 44 rotating shaft 45 guide rail 46 guide block 51 injection nozzle 52 fastening portion 53 injection nozzle guide 54 inline transfer pipe 55 inline coupler 56 inline coupler inlet 57 pivot shaft inlet 60 reflux blocking plate 61 vibration generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315306-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "corrosion of the pipelines leads to a reduction in the service life of the pipeline and a decrease in water supply capacity resulting in economic losses by increasing the load of the pump and also causing consumer complaints and complaints due to deterioration of water quality due to corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "US-7128081-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the trapping column 407 resides away from the cold surfaces of the two sub regions 401 402 so that its contents are not subject to freezing that could give rise to sample precipitation or other undesired effects"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0372293-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "all of these process water heating systems as well as the thermal disinfection carried out with them require a considerable increase in energy in the form of circulation and leakage losses"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "naturally it belongs to the scope of the invention.100 multi purpose thermostat 120 liquid corrosion tank 121 aerobic generation 125 diffuser 127 air inlet 128 air outlet 130 cooling tank 131 intake port 132 exhaust port 141 air supply fan 142 exhaust fan 150 wastewater injection unit 153 conical dispersion induction member 154 wastewater outlet 156 wastewater supply pipe 157 liquid circulation pump 170 shatterproof device 171 inlet 172 outlet 174 scattering prevention device body 176 178 plate 179 slope 182 flushing pump 184 flushing piping 185 chemical pump 187 chemical piping 300 chemical flocculation precipitation filter 320 flocculation reactor 340 sedimentation unit 342 sludge collector 343 treated water outlet 345 pressure sensor 347 rectifying plate 349 sludge discharge pump 350 filter unit 352 filter unit frame 352a round border 352b spokes 354 filtration cell 357 rotary drive shaft 361 wash water nozzle 362 wash water pump 363 wash water receiver 365 wash water discharge pipe 367 electric valve 371 control panel 373 sump tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the pump aeration and precipitation tank pressure tank and filter tank may be included in a pump house or in a basement substantially to reduce outdoor installation and servicing problems encountered particularly in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "the pressure differential between the water drive line 10 and water return line 26 assures that air will be entrained into the water during the entire pumping cycle to enhance oxidation of the contaminants contained therein for removal in the aeration and precipitation tank 27 and or filter tank 88"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102207832-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "is linked to compost treatment and the desorption liquid is linked to liquid manure or purification treatment the active decomposition circulation device 400 is connected to the dewatered sludge treatment device 300 and a free radical reaction in contact with the organic wastewater of the desorption liquid using the ozone o3 generator 411 and the activated radical oxidation device 412 is configured to induce oxidative decomposition the decomposition flotation treatment device 500 is connected to an active decomposition circulation device 400 and uses a flotation treatment device 512 for the complex oxide material dissolved in the biological treatment device 511 and the pressure decomposition flotation treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-5340468-A", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a system adapted for regulating the addition of lime to reduce water alkalinity comprising a treatment vessel having 1 a mixing zone wherein a stream of untreated water is mixed with lime and 2 a flocculation zone that receives said mixture of water and lime from said mixing zone and allows precipitation of the resulting insoluble salts a first sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said stream of untreated water entering said mixing zone a second sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said water in said flocculation zone pump means for adding said lime to said untreated water in said mixing zone and a controller operable for regulating said pump means by periodically sampling said conductivities measured by said first sensor and said second sensor computing the ratio of said conductivities for each sample computing the slope of said conductivity ratio and determining the minimum value of said conductivity ratio said controller being operable for regulating said pump means so that sufficient lime is added to said water to pass through said minimum conductivity ratio and further turning said pump means off when said ratio exceeds a predetermined maximum set point and said slope is positive and turning said pump means on when said ratio falls below a predetermined minimum set point and said slope is negative"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200234791-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in this case the amount is small so when you do not have to worry about the inflow of earth and sand the present invention can effectively pre