age hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200427833-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition in order to prevent the decay and odor caused by long term storage of high concentration early rainfall brower is installed to supply minimum air to maintain dissolved oxygen concentration of more than 0.1mg l in the acid pipe installed at the bottom of the storage tank and to detect rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "US-5069693-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the cooling of the air increases its density thus adding gravity boost to the air flow induced by the downstream air pump at the exhaust and filtering zone"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200234791-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in this case the amount is small so when you do not have to worry about the inflow of earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing cross sectional area reduction of the drainage pipe and burning of the pump in the sewage treatment plant and reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080805-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "like the high concentration overflow water storage tank 220 a slope a solid pit and a pump may be provided at the lower portion of the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 and the storage stored in the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 after the rainfall is terminated through the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-910009261-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "the method of claim 12 wherein the rainfall prediction step includes receiving time series rainfall distribution data to calculate a center point where each set of rainfall overlaps checking whether the center point moves according to a predetermined rule and calculating the position of the center point before the predetermined time from the present by calculating the average value and the variance of the position of the center point in the past when moving according to the predetermined rule or when the center point moves without the predetermined rule the rainfall increase decrease rate acquisition step of acquiring the increase decrease rate of rainfall from the local mean of the region and the position where the latest rainfall distribution at the current calculation time does not fluctuate within a predetermined period and the latest rainfall distribution is limited by the calculated center point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
