  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-9765508-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the hewitt invention is a device to collect and dispense roof rain water comprising a container to collect water having an opening a pump to drive the water out of the container a debris disposal mechanism a sensor to measure the water level wherein the pump is activated at a specific water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100760969-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of backwashing the filtration means in the case of filtering the rain water or the like while the filtration means is lowered the filtration efficiency due to contaminants the pressure of the untreated water transferred to the filtration means 120 by the transfer pump 114 is measured by the pressure measuring sensor ps to inform the control means of the information when the pressure exceeds the preset pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100760969-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "in addition the present invention relates to a method of using the water treatment apparatus such as rain water the method of automatically backwashing the filtration means when the filtration means drops the filtration efficiency due to contaminants while filtering the rain water or the like normally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100549466-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "after being stored in the bubble generator 60 to prevent rain and eutrophication and decay of the rain for a certain period of time after the rainy weather \u6c23 \ud558\uba74 simply operate the pump 50 when water is needed for plants in the park rain water of the water tank 10 is sucked into the pump 50 through the suction pipe 51 and then transferred through the transfer pipe 52 and the trees or grasses of the park through the spray nozzle 52a such as a sprinkler 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value o