  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101840603-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "the smart watering method using the number of floors according to the preferred embodiment of the present invention having the above described structure is characterized in that a water pipe is connected or deep water is developed to extract water and a large amount of underwater pump is installed unlike the existing method which was charged for the installation fee and the production cost it extracts the number of storm floors from the first impervious layer penetrating into the basement and substitutes all the power required for extraction and watering from the natural resource power module it is possible to implement irrigation with a low cost and low budget and to contribute to environmental preservation by utilizing the number of floors with the possibility of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that the upper portion is exposed from the filter medium over the entire length the upper portion of the filter material is exposed from the filter material to the inside of the filtration tank and the exposed portion is formed with an inlet hole for allowing the filter material washing water to flow into the discharge passage while the opposite end is installed in the partition wall 111b a filter media wash and contaminant discharge line configured to communicate with the filter material discharge outlet a filter material cleaning device installed under the filter material washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe to be buried in the filter material and spraying high pressure air or backwash water for washing the filter material and a filter medium washing water and contaminants which are installed outside the pretreatment tank and are washed by the filter material cleaning device and flowed into the pretreatment tank through the washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe and stagnant water accumulated in the water treatment tank and a stagnant water exclusion pump for removing the stagnant water when it is confirmed that stagnant water is present in the water treatment tank contaminants separated from the filter media and the filter media wash water used for the filter media are supplied to the discharge passage and the filtering water discharge port 135 having the reverse opening closing door 136 of the partition wall 111b to be forcedly sucked into the pretreatment tank and forcedly excluded to the outside by the congestion water exclusion pump the operation of the filter medium washing device is stopped and only the stagnant water exclusion pump is operated with the stagnant water of the water treatment tank to be operated until the complete removal of sediment deposited at the bottom of the tank has been confirmed initial treatment is a solid system of jing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "since the manhole connection pipe is formed by dividing into the upper pipe 140b and the lower pipe 140a and the storm line manhole 150 may include a cleaning pump facility and a pit space for collecting sediment is formed deeper than the surrounding excellent line space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank 1 having a contaminant collecting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the pretreatment tank 1 may further include a dirt collecting tank 13 and a ditch water tank 14 therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes for collecting only contaminants generated during the filtration process and sludge from the second storage tank which are formed in the filtration tank and a backwash water drain pump configured to discharge contaminants and sludges introduced into the inside of the backwash drainage storage tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637562-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "the supply means and the water pumping means are automatically controlled by a monitoring system driven by signals of a detection sensor not shown for detecting the water level of the settling tank 3 the filtration tank 4 and the rectifying tank 5 at an appropriate position and manual control may be performed depending on the contamination level of the storm and the degree of contamination of the filter 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stormwater inflow tank 100 through which stormwater flows one end of the storm that is stored in the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 is connected to one side of the lower end of the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 and the other end is connected to the storm inflow reservoir 100 a sedimentation tank 200 connected through an initial storm inflow pipe 200a communicated with a central portion opposed to the first storm inflow pipe 200a to deposit foreign matter in the stormwater flowing through the initial storm inflow pipe 200a the filtration tank 200 is connected to the other side of the settling tank 200 through a filtration tank transfer pipe 300a and is connected to the lower portion of the one side of the settling tank 200 opposite to the other lower side of the settling tank 200 via the filtration tank transfer pipe 300a 310 for filtering the foreign substances in the rainwater conveyed from the water tank 200 and increasing the water level to a predetermined upward level a filtration tank 300 and is connected to the other central portion of the filtration tank 300 at the other side of the filtration tank 300 through a backwash water tank transfer pipe 400a and is connected to the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash water tank 400 through which the filtered water from the filtration tank 300 flows into the water tank 400a at a certain level is connected to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 through a discharge jaw delivery pipe 500a the filtrate discharged from the backwash water tank 400 is discharged to the outside via the piping 500a and the bypass pipe 100a is connected to the bypass pipe 100a in the case where the water level of the stormwater an excellent stormwater tank 500 through which stormwater flows the sedimentation tank 200 is disposed at a certain distance from the sedimentation tank 200 and is connected to the congestion water conveyance pipe 600a from the inside of the sedimentation tank 200 to selectively enter the sedimentation tank 200 a stagnant water storage tank 600 for discharging the stagnant water to the outside by extending the pipe 610 upwardly to be transferred to the vehicle through the vehicle transfer pipe 610 and the backwash water is selectively supplied from the backwash water tank 400 to the lower side of the filtration tank 300 so that the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 are backwashed by the backwash water and backwashing means for supplying air back into the filtration tank 300 to perform backwashing of the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 by backwash air the backwashing means may be configured to perform backwashing by the backwash water and then backwash with backwash air a sedimentation water drainage pump 710 disposed at the center of the bottom of the sedimentation tank 200 for selectively pumping sedimentation water in the sedimentation tank 200 to be transported to the congestion water storage tank 600 via the congestion water delivery pipe 600a wow a filtration trap water delivery pipe 210 provided on a drainage groove 210 that is downwardly recessed on one side of the bottom of the settling tank 200 and communicates with one side of the lower end of the filtration tank 300 which is conveyed from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side during the opening operation of the check valve 722 formed at the end of the filtration stagnant water transfer pipe 721 via the inlet 721 a filtration water drainage pump 720 for pumping water to be sent to the congestion water storage tank 600 the water level in the drainage groove 210 of the sedimentation tank 200 is detected so as to be sent to the stagnant water storage tank 600 and the sediment stagnant water and the filtered stagnant water are delivered to the stagnant water storage tank 600 a sedimentation tank water level sensor 730 for selectively activating the sedimentation water discharge pump 710 and the filtration water discharge pump 720 until detection the sedimentation tank water drain pump 710 is operated when the level of the sedimentation tank 200 is above the central portion of the sedimentation tank 200 during backwashing by the backwash water washing water level sensor 740 for transferring an excess amount of the backwash water into the stagnant water storage tank 600 a backwash water transfer pipe not shown connected to the backwash water supply pipe 753 provided in the lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 a backwash pump 750 for selectively supplying backwash water for backwash to the filtration tank 300 via the backwash water tank 400 through the backwash water tank 751 the filtration tank 300 is provided at a lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 and is disposed above the backwash water supply pipe 753 and selectively supplied with backwash air from the outside to supply air to the filtration tank 300 a backwashing air supply pipe 810 for upwardly floating the filtered suspended solids in the filter quartz layer 310 while moving upward from a lower portion of the filter quartz layer 310 the suspended solids suspended in the upper portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 are transferred from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 by the backwash air supplied through the backwash air supply pipe 810 one end of which is connected to one side of the upper part of the filter element layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 the other side is connected to the central part of one side of the settling tank 200 and the other end is selectively a backwash floating transfer pipe 820 having a check valve 821 for guiding a suspended material from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through an air transfer pipe 831 and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through the air transfer pipe 831"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101764398-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "a contamination abatement facility is provided in the lower wall 16 of the housing 10 a filtering partition wall 31 which is formed so as to have an upper end which is equal to or lower than the lowest point height of the inflow pipe 17 and which is separated from the space of the filtration tank 30 formed on the rear side the filtration unit 30a which is located between the rear wall 31 and the rear wall 12 and has both ends vertically fixed to the left and right side walls 13 and 14 so that only the space on the upper side of the filtration tank 30 is filtered and an upper support partition wall 37 for separating the upper support partition wall 30a and the upper support partition wall 30b into a management section 30b for a worker to enter and work for management of the filtration section 30a a mesh chain filter mesh net 32 having a front end portion fixed to the left and right side walls 13 and 14 and a lower end of the filtration partition 31 and the upper support partition 37 30a of the filtration mesh net 32 and is held in the sedimentation tank 20 a filtration material layer 33 having at least one filter medium 33a that is filtered while flowing an initial storm that flows into the filtration section 30a of the filtration tank 30 through the filtration tank 30 the grill 38 is fixedly supported on the upper support partition wall 37 and the rear wall 12 at the lower side of the discharge pipe 18 and a filter medium 33a of the filter medium layer 33 by spraying water at a predetermined pressure toward the filter medium layer 33 through the filter mesh network 32 located below the filter mesh network 32 of the filter medium 30 a water distribution pipe 34 having at least one water injection nozzle 34a for separating foreign matter adhering to the filter medium 30 and a filtering mesh network 32 located below the filtering mesh network 32 of the filtration tank 30 33a of the filter material layer 33 by discharging air bubbles at a predetermined pressure toward the filter material layer 33 and an air bubble spraying tube 35 having one or more air bubble spray nozzles 35a for facilitating the initialization of the sedimentation tank 20 and a filtration tank discharge pump 36 disposed at the lower end of the filtration tank 30 and discharging the filtered stormwater through the filtration tank discharge pipe 36a to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
