  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the non point pollutant reduction facility a back washing water supply unit for washing the filter media by using the filtered water introduced into the back washing tank as back washing water and a backwashing means including a backwashing means for discharging the backwashing water after washing the filter media to the outside of the treatment structure further comprising the reverse wash water supply unit a first pump installed on the bottom of the backwashing tank and including a backwash water supply pipe connected to the discharge portion side of the first pump the backwash supply pipe extends to an upper side of the filtration tank while branching in a plurality so as not to interfere with the lifting operation unit of the filtering means and the first filter plate and the first filter plate on the backwash supply pipe extending to the upper side of the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "specifically the non point pollutant reduction facility includes a back washing water supply unit for washing the filter media using the filtered water introduced into the back washing tank as back washing water and a backwashing means for discharging the backwashing water after washing the filter materials to the outside of the treatment structure further comprising the backwashing supply unit a first pump installed at the bottom of the backwashing tank and a backwash water supply pipe connected to the discharge portion side of the first pump but the backwash water supply pipe extends to the upper side of the filtration tank while branching into a plurality so as not to interfere with the lifting operation unit of the filtering means and to the upper side of the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101398010-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a reservoir installed on the lower side of the gutter a connection pipe connecting the storm water pipe and the storage tank a storage tank installed in the connection pipe for controlling the stormwater flowing into the storage tank through the connection pipe a first sensor installed on the upstream side of the connection pipe among the gross conduits and measuring a contamination degree and a quantity of the ozone flowing into the gutter tube a second sensor installed inside the storage tank for measuring a contamination level and a water level of the storm water filled in the storage tank a discharge pump installed in the storage tank for sucking the rainwater in the storage tank and discharging the rainwater to the outside and a control unit for opening and closing the storage tank gates in accordance with an initial stormwater inflow signal and an initial wastewater termination signal of the first sensor and driving the discharge pump according to the high water level signal or the contamination signal of the second sensor the storage tank gates a connection pipe interlocking part installed to be rotatable at an inlet of the connection pipe and interrupting the connection pipe while rotating and an excellent pipe shut off part slidably installed in the connection pipe cut off part and slid in a state where the connection pipe cut off part is opened to cut off the excellent pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-5462655-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a fluid recapture system collects residual waste fluids generated during airplane washing or de icing procedures and separates and recycles these fluids to prevent contamination of storm water drainage and sewer systems and ground water supplies"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
