  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2643691-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "because it is pulled the same given filtering surface is only in contact with the liquid for a short period of time and does not have time for significant fouling to occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106330-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 1 tilt detection sensor 40 is provided on the circumference of the main body 10 to detect the gradient change of the main body 10 leakage detection means 50 provided on the outer circumference of the body 10 to detect water leakage from the body 10 a sewage detection sensor 60 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to detect when sewage is supplied through the water supply pipe 14 a flow rate measurement means 70 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to measure the flow rate of sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 further comprising a washing means 80 for washing the flow rate measuring means 70 using the discharged water discharged to the drain pipe 15 the leak detection means 50 it is formed in a cylindrical shape extending in the front rear direction and having an opening 51a formed on one surface and the collecting case 51 provided so that the opening 51a is in close contact with the circumferential surface of the main body 10 it is provided inside the catchment case 51 and includes a leak detection sensor 52 for detecting the collected waste water inside the catchment case 51 the flow rate measurement means 70 a support bracket 71 provided inside the water supply pipe 14 an impeller 72 rotatably coupled to the support bracket 71 and rotated by sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 it is connected to the impeller 72 and includes a rotation sensor 73 for measuring the rotational speed of the impeller 72 the cleaning means 80 a water storage tank 81 connected to the drain pipe 15 through a connection pipe 81a to store a portion of the discharged water discharged through the drain pipe 15 an injection nozzle 82 provided to face the impeller 72 inside the water supply pipe 14 and connected to the water storage tank 81 through a supply pipe 82a it includes a water supply pump 83 provided in the middle of the supply pipe 82a the management server a receives the signals of the tilt detection sensor 40 the leak detection means 50 the sewage detection sensor 60 and the flow rate measurement means 70 the slope of the main body 10 is set it is changed to a reference value or more or the sewage detection means 50 detects the sewage or the sewage detection sensor 60 the sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 is sensed to the flow rate measuring means 70 when it is detected that the signal of the sewage measured by the dropping below a preset speed a warning signal or a message is transmitted to the portable terminal b if the rotation of the impeller 72 is not detected by the rotation detection sensor 73 in the state in which water passing through the drain pipe 15 is sensed by the sewage detection sensor 60 the water feed pump 83 is operated"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "when an on off event happens to the heating supply pump unit at the starting end of the pipeline a great gradient variation of the pressure in the pipeline may be caused which can cause a false leakage early warning easily therefore the plc collects data from the pressure sensors and the temperature sensors to form a pressure dataset p1 p2 p3 p4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "when the process water is introduced from the flow rate regulator 120 and the ozone gas is injected into the ultrahigh strength oxygen generating unit 132 the mixing is performed by the mixing pump and the line mixer and thereby the ozone gas is decomposed into the ultra accordingly the contact efficiency between the ozone gas decomposed in a mist state and the treated water can be maximized and the oxidation reaction of the treated water occurs"}]</data>
