from the centrifugal separator 1500 are introduced and an inlet pipe 1610 formed to receive the inlet pipe therein an inner hole 1620 an agitator 1630 rotatably installed at the center of the inner hole block an outer hopper 1640 surrounding the inner hole block and having a square shape a sludge discharge pipe 1650 installed to discharge the sludge and a mixed mineral discharge pipe 1660 connected to a lower portion of the outer hopper to discharge mixed minerals wherein the mixed mineral is used as a weighted flocculant high speed water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a temporary storage tank for chemicals having a cover installed on the unit one side is connected to the drug storage space of the drug temporary storage tank and the other side is connected to the connection pipe connected to the flocculation settler or the immersion well via the injector the drug discharge pipe is installed on the pipeline chemical discharge pump a discharge side bypass pipe bypassing the chemical discharge pipe and having a discharge side bypass valve in the middle a supply side bypass pipe bypassing the supply pipe and having a supply side bypass valve in the middle a control device electrically connected to the leak detection sensor a ph sensor a chemical discharge pump and a supply side shutoff valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "more specifically when the water level of the reservoir rises to a high level due to a failure of the existing water level control valve it is discharged through the overflow water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101359001-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the present invention is further provided with a winch 210 a wire 220 and a water level sensor 230 in the flow control settler 200 as shown in figure 6 while allowing the shape deformation of the discharge pipe 600 according to the variable level it will be possible to prevent problems such as twisting and twisting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102308038-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it passes through the side wall member 61 and extends to the outside and is connected to a sludge pump and is sealed to prevent leakage between the through part 62 and the sludge discharge pipe 23 passing therethrough a fresh water discharge pipe 45 is connected to the fresh water discharge hole 43 the fresh water discharge pipe 45 extends from the inside of the water tank 20 in the radial direction through the inclined wall 21 of the water tank 20 to the fresh water tank 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the scum removal device is installed in the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to discharge only scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing device it has a hopper shaped body which is located inside the waterway and introduces a scum to the outside of the waterway through the discharge pipe formed at the bottom thereof and a support bar for supporting the scum detection sensor and the water level detection sensor on the upper part of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in the scum removing apparatus according to the present invention for achieving this object in the scum removing apparatus is installed in the water channel of the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to flow only the scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing apparatus includes a scum hopper positioned inside the channel and flowing in the scum to flow out of the channel through a discharge pipe formed at a lower portion thereof an elevating unit configured to elevate the scum hopper a support part supported on the upper side of the waterway to support the lifting part a scum detecting sensor installed at a front portion of the scum hopper to sense an amount of floating scum a water level sensor installed at a rear portion of the scum hopper to detect a water level and a controller for adjusting the height of the scum hopper by controlling the lifting unit according to the detection state of the scum detecting sensor and the water level detecting sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101469248-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the support block may further include a water level sensor for sensing the level of groundwater being dewatered to the main body and transmitting a water level signal to the control unit and a controller for sensing the concentration of the pce contained in the groundwater passing through the water level sensor a concentration sensor for transmitting to the control unit and a discharge valve for opening and closing the discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 the water level controller 32 includes a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor 29 the second sensor 30 and the third sensor 31 of the water level sensor portion the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 16 may be discharged through the discharge pipe 22 for a predetermined discharge time when the time counted by the timer 33 becomes longer than a predetermined time wherein the control unit controls the discharge valve 21 so that the discharge water 21 is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level controller may further include a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor the second sensor and the third sensor of the water level sensor portion and controls the discharge valve so that the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank can be discharged through the discharge pipe for a preset discharge time when the discharge time exceeds the predetermined set time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102458731-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the technical spirit of the appended claims.10 neutralizer storage tank 20 hydrometer 30 water level gauge 40 neutralizer supply pipe 50 pump 60 injection valve 70 neutralizer storage unit 80 fresh water storage unit 100 200 neutralizing device 300 ballast tank 400 oxidation device 500 concentration measuring sensor 1000 process water treatment system n neutralizing agent t1 ballast water inlet pipe t2 ballast water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the control unit if the emergency valve is normally closed determine whether the flow rate in the drain pipe is present based on the flow rate measured by the second flow meter if the flow rate in the drain pipe is measured to be present it is determined that there is a problem with the emergency valve and information on the condition of the emergency valve is transmitted to the control terminal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100964741-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the second discharge pipe 112b is provided with a second pump 114b to be able to handle the sewage stored in the sewage collection well 110b to the ground to prevent contamination of groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "prevents freezing the control unit is