  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inflow amount and an upper and lower raising and lowering device 5810 is connected to adjust the pipe in the upper and lower direction according to the inflow level of river water that changes frequently and a rising discharge pipe 101 a falling discharge pipe 103 a right angled falling pipe 202 a water storage tank 201 a discharge amount control unit 203 a right angled falling pipe 202 and in a method of producing electricity by using the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 equipped with a power generation unit 33 a structure in which a water storage tank 8000 and a water purification promotion storage tank 11111 are constructed by dredging to a depth 20 to 600 times deeper than the surface 9000 of the soil layer constituting a river or stream and then the foundation concrete 800 is poured on the surface 9000 constituting a river or stream and the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 are constructed on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 and the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 is constructed to store river water on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 a structure in which an intermediate storage water inflow line 501 is formed to pump the stored water stored inside the upstream side of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 toward