mes larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101788811-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an activated carbon filtration unit in which raw water sucked from an emergency water feeder or a river or a river side is subjected to filtration treatment with a large particle while foreign substances are filtered through the sand and filtered water filtered by the sand filtration unit is re a filter cloth for holding a filter medium between the filter plates stacked in multiple means so that small foreign substances contained in the filtered water are filtered by the filter medium coated with the filter cloth while being supplied with the filtered water filtered by the activated carbon filter unit is provided a pressurized filter portion connected to a third raw milk feed inlet for feeding raw water to one side of the filter plate and connected to the other side of the third filtered water discharge pipe through which the filtered water is discharged from the filter plate and the filter cloth a membrane filter in which filtered water filtered by the filter is sucked and highly filtered to fine foreign matters a modular water production system comprising a part a filtration data storage unit for presetting and storing a state value of a water quality to be filtered by the modular water production system and a limit pressure value inside the operation unit a state of the water quality filtered by the modular water production system a water quality measurement data comparing unit for storing the data and a pressure measurement data verifying unit for checking and storing the filtration state by measuring the pressure inside each of the actuating units a water quality measurement monitoring unit a failure confirmation monitoring unit for checking the operation state of each operation unit of the modular water production system to check for a failure a system general status data storage unit in which the installation location and related information of the modular water production system are stored a water quality status data storage unit for storing information on the status of the water quality and the water quality status and quantity on the site a central control unit including an operating unit data storage unit for storing a value of a proper pressure value and a proper filtering throughput in each operating unit a system data transmitting and receiving unit for wirelessly transmitting measured data and data confirmed by the fault checking and monitoring unit to the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit and receiving a signal of a central control unit a central data transmitting and receiving unit provided in the central control unit for receiving data transmitted through the system data transmitting and receiving unit and transmitting an instruction command to the modular water producing system and when the water quality measurement value measured by the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit is out of the range of a predetermined set value or when a malfunction of each of the operating units occurs and the malfunction confirmation monitoring unit confirms it and an emergency monitoring control unit for generating an emergency signal in the central control unit when the water quality and pressure data measured and transmitted from the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit is out of the predetermined water quality and pressure data range wherein the control unit controls the operation of each of the actuating units of the modular water production system to automatically perform backwashing by operating each valve of the modular water production system to stop the supply of raw water and a washing automatic control unit is additionally provided to the water supply unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a structure in which the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir frame 830 and white paper 88 are combined to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity on top of the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir 8888 is formed a structure in which a shaped siphon action generating assembly partition 836 is sequentially fixed to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a structure in which the power generation water discharge pipe 3151 is constructed at an angle along the slope of the downstream part of the river starting from the lower part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth a structure in which an upward discharge pipe 3150 is formed in an l shape at a height that is 5 to 20 lower than the height of the lower part of the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is formed in the upstream part of the river at the end of the above mentioned power generation water discharge pipe 3151 a structure in which a terminal discharge pipe 3152 is formed in a t shape at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 3150 a structure in which an air exhaust unit 381 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a plurality of power generation water final pipes 262 each having a different thickness are connected around the end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a control unit 266 configured to control the discharge amount is connected to the upper part of the final power generation water pipe 262 a structure in which an upper storage tank 259 is connected to a lower discharge unit 256 configured in a different form with each storage capacity to store power generation water and discharge it to the lower part at the lower part of the above mentioned power generation water final pipeline 262 a structure in which a hydroelectric power generation unit 335 configured to generate electricity by hydraulic power is combined at the lower end of the above mentioned lower discharge unit 256 a nature friendly eco friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water using an eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae growth that is characterized by generating hydroelectric power by using an eco friendly movable dam that acts to prevent green algae growth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4538604-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "since the difference in electrical conductivity is a value proportional to the amount of organic matter present in the water sample it is possible to detect contamination of harmful organic matter by monitoring this difference"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "distribution step a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms and wetland plants of the wetland and comprehensively purified a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module of the modular wetland infrastructure a third purification step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure is biologically purified while passing through the contact oxidation tank in which the microbial contact material is installed a fourth purification step of finally removing fine sludge and suspended solids not filtered in the contact oxidation tank through the filtering tank and a flow rate adjusting step of adjusting a flow rate discharged into the water channel through the discharge pipe through the discharge control tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floating bucket for collecting suspended solids a fourth floating material collection conveyor for transporting the collected particulate matter and the ultra fine particles in the rear portion of the floating material collection rotating bucket fine particles rising from the rear portion of the fourth floating material collection conveyor to the upper portion of the river water a fourth contaminant screw feeder configured to collect and collect sex contaminants and ultra fine magnetic contaminants to push and transport the contaminants to the outside of the river water processing box and combine the rotor and the rotor support a fifth floating material collection conveyor for transporting and collecting the collected particulate matter and the ultrafine particles on the rear part of the fourth contaminant screw feeder the suspended solids removing plate and the particulate collecting guide plate sequentially coupled with the rotating belt coupled to the rotating body a fifth suspended solids material collector in which the suspended particulate floating material plate which serves to prevent the collected suspended solids molecules from being separated from the outside of the rotating belt is combined and a water reservoir and a rainwater reservoir for connecting the lower end of the river water processing box and the river water discharge pipe by using a discharge control valve and storing the processed river water and at the end of the river water processing box from an upstream of the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1 further comprising a processing device for pulverizing and processing the contaminated river water into ultra fine particles the processing device a contaminated stream water final discharge pipe configured at an end of the river water processing box coupled with the water gate a driven shaft and a drive shaft by connecting one side and the other side of the processing apparatus a driven gear and a driving gear disposed on one side of the driven shaft and one side of the driving shaft respectively a separation prevention coupling configured at one side and the other side of the driven shaft in the processing apparatus a rotating rod support ring disposed between the release preventing couplings a plurality of rotating rods disposed on the rotating rod support ring to strike fluid pollutant molecules and solid pollutant molecules a circular rotating striking body configured to be coupled to the anti separation ring in the processing apparatus so that the drive shaft cross couples with the rotating rod a plurality of grooves having a u shape arranged to strike fluid contaminant molecules and solid contaminant molecules on the outer circumferential surface of the circular rotating striking body a plurality of grooves striking fluid contaminant molecules and solid contaminant molecules in the disk of the circular rotating striking body an upper discharge pipe discharging fluid contaminant molecules on the upper side of the processing apparatus included in the lower side of the processing apparatus the lower end discharge pipe for discharging the fluid material molecules with a relatively heavy weight relative to the fluid contaminant molecules discharged through the top discharge pipe eco friendly power generation system that combines nature friendly water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1 further comprising a processing device for pulverizing and processing the contaminated river water into ultra fine particles the processing device a contaminated stream water final discharge pipe configured at an end of the river water processing box coupled with the water gate a driven shaft and a drive shaft by connecting one side and the other side of the processing apparatus a driven gear and a driving gear disposed on one side of the driven shaft and one side of the driving shaft respectively a driven circular rotary striker having a disk shape in which a groove is formed in an irregular shape between the separation rings for maintaining a constant distance to a driven shaft configured in the processing apparatus a disk shaped driving circular rotary striking body in which a groove is formed in a straight shape between spaced rings to maintain a constant distance to a drive shaft configured in the processing apparatus an upper discharge pipe discharging fluid contaminant molecules on the upper side of the processing apparatus included in the lower side of the processing apparatus the lower end discharge pipe for discharging the fluid material molecules with a relatively heavy weight relative to the fluid contaminant molecules discharged through the top discharge pipe eco friendly power generation system that combines nature friendly water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "in the case of installing the product constituted according to the present invention in the whole river it is possible to quickly supply a large amount of industrial water and agricultural water by using the river water secured in a large capacity while saving the river ecosystem and farming a large amount of fish"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102207360-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a first motor and a suction hopper mounted in front of the body to suck the sediment a discharge pipe connected in communication with the suction hopper to send the sucked sediment to the outside and installed inside the suction hopper to crush the sediment an underwater cleaning robot comprising a crushing screw and a second motor for driving the crushing screw and a hydraulic pressure generating device mounted on the body and configured to drive the first and second motors using hydraulic pressure and control remotely the technology is also presented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920007-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "by sprinkling the treated water to the side opening 10 the contaminant is filtered while passing through the water passage layer 20 and the multi filtration layer 40 of the soil filter layer 30 which are the main structural parts of the purification facility buried in the slope and the catchment layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869158-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "rainwater flowing into the rainwater discharge pipe 140 by the above process is to discharge to the river or lake to prevent contamination of the river or lake and groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102524681-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the ice cleaning duct washing discharge control method required to clean the water supply duct using the ice washing medium in the water supply duct the ice cleaning duct washing discharge control method in the water supply duct blocking the water valve on the supplier side and the water valve on the consumer side of the pipeline to be cleaned s11 opening the washing water inlet valve configured at the rear end of the water valve on the supplier side and injecting the washing medium into the conduit while applying pressure using the inlet pump s12 washing the inside of the pipe while passing the cleaning medium by increasing the pressure with the inlet pump inside the pipe s13 washing the inside of the water supply pipe with a washing medium and discharging washing discharged water discharged after washing through a discharge pipe formed in front of the water supply valve on the receiving side s14 a step of firstly and periodically transmitting the sensed water quality data to a controller by a water quality sensor installed at a rear end of the discharge pipe and sensing water quality data of discharged water flowing through the discharge pipe s15 determining whether or not the received first water quality data is equal to or less than a predetermined effluent water quality standard s16 in the case of the following the controller opens the solenoid valve installed in the discharge pipe to discharge the washing discharge water to the river s17 sensing the amount of discharged water discharged into the river by the flow sensor unit of the drained water discharge pipe installed at the rear end of the water quality sensor unit and transmitting the sensed discharged water quantity information to the controller s18 transmitting by the controller primary water quality data and discharged water flow rate information to a center server of a water quality management center s19 determining whether the received water quality data meets drinking water quality standards by a controller that periodically receives water quality data from the water quality sensor unit s20 if appropriate turning off the washing water inlet valve configured in the washing water inlet to stop the injection of the washing water and opening the water supply valve to supply tap water to the corresponding pipe s21 monitoring the secondary water quality data transmitted from the water quality sensor unit by the controller while discharging tap water supplied to the water supply pipe through the discharge pipe s22 and if the received water quality data meets the drinking water quality standards transmitting the water quality data to the manager smart terminal to block the discharge valve of the discharge pipe and open the water valve on the consumer side to supply tap water to the consumer s23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "the manhole 200 is configured to discharge contaminants through the discharge pipe 2 and the induction apparatus 100 is configured to discharge contaminants to the river in the contaminant discharge chamber 12 and may include a recovery pipe 260 so that contaminants discarded in the induction apparatus 100 can be collected and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "first the high initial initial rainfall that occurs at the time of sewage or rainfall inflowing into the city can be collected in the sewage subway pipeline through the sewage discharge section and the large amount of rainfall introduced into the large amount during rainfall is increased by the water pressure the opening of the sewage water discharge pipe is reduced by rotating the rotating plate by the linkage part and the link part linked with the open front water gate and the linkage part linked thereto to prevent the inflow of rainwater and soil to the sewage water supply pipe channel and discharging it to the discharge river it is possible to reduce the dredging cost by cutting off the earth and sand and it is possible to reduce the sewage treatment cost because it is possible to collect only the planned amount of sewage in the sewage subway pipeline as well as the breakage of the sewer pipeline and manhole due to the water pressure caused by the over can be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101445209-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drinking water supply device for supplying raw water after obtaining raw water from a river or a well by means of a water intake pump and purifying the water in a usable state a container box having a raw water storage tank and a purified water storage tank respectively a contaminant remover installed in the container box and primarily purifying raw water flowing from the water intake pump toward the raw water storage tank to remove contaminants contained in raw water a cartridge filter for purifying the raw water transferred from the raw water storage tank to remove foreign matter having a particle size of 5 to 10 mu m in the solid matter a pressure type filter installed on one side of the cartridge filter for purifying the raw water by the third order and removing minute turbidity included in the raw water with a predetermined pressure and a uv sterilizer for sterilizing the microorganisms contained in the water before the water having passed through the pressure filter is introduced into the water storage tank wherein the raw water storage tank and the purified water storage tank are each provided with a level switch which is provided to control the supply amount of raw water supplied from the water intake pump to the raw water storage tank and the water supply amount of water supplied from the purified water storage tank a raw water pump which is located at one side of the raw water storage tank and is installed so as to be dischargeable at a stable flow rate and pressure toward the cartridge filter and the pressure type filter and a raw water pump which is located at one side of the purified water storage tank and a water pump for discharging the water the water pump includes a plurality of discharge pipes connected to one discharge port"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in an initial high boiling point contamination treatment system 100 connected to the end of the conduit or the river water from which the polluted water is discharged to provide pollution excellence and selectively supply only the initial nonpoint pollution excellence a reservoir 200 for storing initial boiling impurity contamination provided to the water collection channel 130 of the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants a siphon pipe 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the water level of the reservoir 200 becomes equal to or higher than the height of the highest part in the reversed u shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200285740-Y1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "therefore in order to prevent obstruction by fine suspended matter and environmental microorganisms the lower sludge discharge facility 24 is installed at the lower part of the gravel contact oxidation facility 11 and the charcoal biofilm filtration tank 13 and is excessive by the diffuser 21 device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894568-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 0477945 march 10 2005 water treatment device using electrolysis summary of the invention accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems occurring in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an electrolytic apparatus and a method for supplying electrolytic water to an enclosed cylindrical electrolytic cell by receiving ground