  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inflow amount and an upper and lower raising and lowering device 5810 is connected to adjust the pipe in the upper and lower direction according to the inflow level of river water that changes frequently and a rising discharge pipe 101 a falling discharge pipe 103 a right angled falling pipe 202 a water storage tank 201 a discharge amount control unit 203 a right angled falling pipe 202 and in a method of producing electricity by using the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 equipped with a power generation unit 33 a structure in which a water storage tank 8000 and a water purification promotion storage tank 11111 are constructed by dredging to a depth 20 to 600 times deeper than the surface 9000 of the soil layer constituting a river or stream and then the foundation concrete 800 is poured on the surface 9000 constituting a river or stream and the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 are constructed on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 and the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 is constructed to store river water on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 a structure in which an intermediate storage water inflow line 501 is formed to pump the stored water stored inside the upstream side of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 toward the rear side starting from the internal ground surface 9000 in the upstream direction of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 penetrating the middle part of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 to the rear part a structure in which a lower movement line 1919 is connected to the end of the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 to move the power generation water introduced through the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 downward a structure in which an entrance 1332 used for inspecting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "US-6811705-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the impact with which these bubbles hit the plate may result in a phenomena called cavitation which will enhance the oxidation process by creating very aggressive oxidation species"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floating bucket for collecting suspended solids a fourth floating material collection conveyor for transporting the collected particulate matter and the ultra fine particles in the rear portion of the floating material collection rotating bucket fine particles rising from the rear portion of the fourth floating material collection conveyor to the upper portion of the river water a fourth contaminant screw feeder configured to collect and collect sex contaminants and ultra fine magnetic contaminants to push and transport the contaminants to the outside of the river water processing box and combine the rotor and the rotor support a fifth floating material collection conveyor for transporting and collecting the collected particulate matter and the ultrafine particles on the rear part of the fourth contaminant screw feeder the suspended solids removing plate and the particulate collecting guide plate sequentially coupled with the rotating belt coupled to the rotating body a fifth suspended solids material collector in which the suspended particulate floating material plate which serves to prevent the collected suspended solids molecules from being separated from the outside of the rotating belt is combined and a water reservoir and a rainwater reservoir for connecting the lower end of the river water processing box and the river water discharge pipe by using a discharge control valve and storing the processed river water and at the end of the river water processing box from an upstream of the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1 further comprising a processing device for pulverizing and processing the contaminated river water into ultra fine particles the processing device a contaminated stream water final discharge pipe configured at an end of the river water processing box coupled with the water gate a driven shaft and a drive shaft by connecting one side and the other side of the processing apparatus a driven gear and a driving gear disposed on one side of the driven shaft and one side of the driving shaft respectively a separation prevention coupling configured at one side and the other side of the driven shaft in the processing apparatus a rotating rod support ring disposed between the release preventing couplings a plurality of rotating rods disposed on the rotating rod support ring to strike fluid pollutant molecules and solid pollutant molecules a circular rotating striking body configured to be coupled to the anti separation ring in the processing apparatus so that the drive shaft cross couples with the rotating rod a plurality of grooves having a u shape arranged to strike fluid contaminant molecules and solid contaminant molecules on the outer circumferential surface of the circular rotating striking body a plurality of grooves striking fluid contaminant molecules and solid contaminant molecules in the disk of the circular rotating striking body an upper discharge pipe discharging fluid contaminant molecules on the upper side of the processing apparatus included in the lower side of the processing apparatus the lower end discharge pipe for discharging the fluid material molecules with a relatively heavy weight relative to the fluid contaminant molecules discharged through the top discharge pipe eco friendly power generation system that combines nature friendly water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1 further comprising a processing device for pulverizing and processing the contaminated river water into ultra fine particles the processing device a contaminated stream water final discharge pipe configured at an end of the river water processing box coupled with the water gate a driven shaft and a drive shaft by connecting one side and the other side of the processing apparatus a driven gear and a driving gear disposed on one side of the driven shaft and one side of the driving shaft respectively a driven circular rotary striker having a disk shape in which a groove is formed in an irregular shape between the separation rings for maintaining a constant distance to a driven shaft configured in the processing apparatus a disk shaped driving circular rotary striking body in which a groove is formed in a straight shape between spaced rings to maintain a constant distance to a drive shaft configured in the processing apparatus an upper discharge pipe discharging fluid contaminant molecules on the upper side of the processing apparatus included in the lower side of the processing apparatus the lower end discharge pipe for discharging the fluid material molecules with a relatively heavy weight relative to the fluid contaminant molecules discharged through the top discharge pipe eco friendly power generation system that combines nature friendly water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "in the case of installing the product constituted according to the present invention in the whole river it is possible to quickly supply a large amount of industrial water and agricultural water by using the river water secured in a large capacity while saving the river ecosystem and farming a large amount of fish"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173850-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "according to the present invention in treating livestock waste water the solid matter and the urine waste water are separated and the solid matter is effective to be recycled as an organic fertilizer and the urine waste water as water is disinfected to prevent contamination of the stream and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920007-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "by sprinkling the treated water to the side opening 10 the contaminant is filtered while passing through the water passage layer 20 and the multi filtration layer 40 of the soil filter layer 30 which are the main structural parts of the purification facility buried in the slope and the catchment layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in this process when the clogging phenomenon is confirmed in the filter medium 140 the contamination adhered to the filter medium 140 is removed by supplying the compressed air through the air blowing pipe 144 thereby improving the filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "an inflow water distribution step of evenly distributing the energy of the stream water the lake water or the outflow water flowing into the integrated water purification device through the flow distribution tank to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step in which the inflow water which has passed the precipitation step is biologically purified while being introduced and passed through the contact oxidation tank in which the microbial contact material is installed a fourth purification step of finally removing fine sludge and suspended solids not filtered in the contact oxidation tank through the filtering tank a flow rate adjusting step of adjusting a flow rate discharged into the water channel through the discharge pipe through the discharge control tank it is configured to include"}, {"pat_id": "US-8465653-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a stream of macerated slurry may be diverted back to the wastewater collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434028-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition it is possible to suppress the load and delay that may occur according to the operation change of the management means for such verification and to optimize the installation and operation state through an active response to the external environment.the present invention provides a water pipe connection system of a prefabricated water intake tower for water intake and a method for installing the same comprising the steps of manufacturing a water pipe connection system the manufactured water pipe connection system is inspected at the inspection site and the water pipe connection system is installed at the installation site wherein the water pipe connection system is managed by monitoring facilities disposed at the inspection site and the installation site respectively the handling situation of the water pipe connection system and the surrounding environment the water pipe connection system includes an excavation hole 10 penetrating in an up stream direction at a predetermined position of the dam body 100 installed to block and confine water a water intake pipe connection system of a prefabricated water intake tower for water intake including a discharge pipe 20 having one end connected to the lower part of the water intake tower body 200 built in a prefabricated manner in the water in the reservoir and the other end extending toward the excavation hole 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "for example when 100 of the river water flows down from the upstream of the river 98 of the river water is discharged through the double discharge water gate 713 and the remaining 2 of the river water is discharged through the double discharge pipe 715 and at the same time the organic substance material molecules having a specific gravity are moved smoothly while the clean stream water having a specific gravity floats naturally to the upper layer portion of the purifying box 7000 by a material pushing action of pushing light substance molecules of a specific gravity and is pushed out of the purge box 7000 while being naturally contained in the lifting gang 711 coupled to the purge box 712"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102660526-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pool built to a predetermined depth on the banks of a stream or river a balancing tank connected to the pool by an overflow pipe and a drainage pipe to store water discharged from the pool a filtration device connected to the balancing tank and the supply pipe to filter the water in the balancing tank and connected to the pool and the water supply pipe to supply the filtered water to the pool and it includes a piping control manhole built between the pool and the balancing tank to control the overflow pipe drain pipe and water supply pipe to prevent contaminants from the pool from flowing into the balancing tank the piping control manhole is a first contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the overflow pipe a second contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the drainage pipe a third pollutant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the water supply pipe a first pollutant discharge pipe and a first pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle portion of the front overflow pipe of the first pollutant penetration blocking valve a second pollutant discharge pipe and a second pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the drainage pipe in front of the second pollutant penetration blocking valve a water damage recovery system for a swimming pool comprising a third pollutant discharge pipe and a third pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the water supply pipe in front of the third pollutant penetration blocking valve"}]</data>
