the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms to the inlet water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "on the other hand the air discharge pipe 60 is to return the carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms to the inlet water storage tank not shown to prevent the outflow of bubbles or odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "on the other hand carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms are returned to the inlet water storage tank not shown through the air discharge pipe 60 to prevent the outflow of bubbles or odors"}, {"pat_id": "US-8398733-B2", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "as a result of heat exchange the air mixture is heated and evacuated outside and the vapor of the refrigerant transforms into liquid and then passes through the temperature regulating valve trv 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356118-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition by immediately detecting the illegal opening of the upper groundwater protector to generate a warning sound to thoroughly maintain the security of the groundwater upper protector as well as to prevent theft or damage of the pumping device components and contaminated groundwater and poison it provides the effect of supplying safe groundwater by preventing inflow.1 is a longitudinal cross sectional view of the installation state of the upper ground water protection ball applied the present invention 2 is an installation state diagram of the groundwater temperature sensor the discharge pipe and the automatic discharge valve of the present invention figure 3 is an enlarged cross sectional view of the installation state of the present invention groundwater temperature sensor 4 is a state in which the discharge pipe and the automatic discharge valve of the present invention