peripheral surface of the partition has a top plate of a predetermined thickness to seal the top of the body is coupled to the top of the body a water pipe coupling portion a fire prevention valve accommodated between the inner circumferential surface of the body and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall at a lower side of the upper plate a fireproof shape memory alloy spring coupled to the lower side of the upper plate and accommodated between an inner circumferential surface of the body and an outer circumferential surface of the partition wall and coupled with a fire valve a freeze proof shape memory alloy spring having an upper end coupled to the inside of the partition wall a stopper coupled to a lower end of the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring it is coupled to the lower end of the body to receive the stopper the top is open and comprises a freeze proof coupling having a water discharge pipe at the bottom the freezing hole is formed at the lower end of the body and at room temperature the fireproof valve and the stopper form a sealed structure and the fireproof shape memory alloy spring is compressed at a predetermined fire temperature to open the fire valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064947-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "water is injected through the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring is tensioned at a predetermined freezing temperature to provide a sprinkler with a freeze protection structure characterized in that the water flows through the freeze protection hole and the water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064947-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a sprinkler comprising a body having a cylindrical shape the top of which is open and having at least one water jet it is connected to the sprinkler water supply pipe and has a partition having an outer diameter of a predetermined size smaller than the inner diameter of the body the outer peripheral surface of the partition has a top plate of a predetermined thickness to seal the top of the body coupled to the top a water pipe coupling portion a fire prevention valve accommodated between the inner circumferential surface of the body and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall at a lower side of the upper plate a fireproof shape memory alloy spring coupled to the lower side of the upper plate and accommodated between an inner circumferential surface of the body and an outer circumferential surface of the partition wall and coupled with a fire valve it is coupled to the lower end of the body and the freeze proof coupling body having an upper portion and a water discharge pipe in the lower portion a freeze protection shape memory alloy spring coupled to one side of the freeze protection assembly a stopper accommodated inside the freeze protection assembly and coupled to a freeze protection shape memory alloy spring the freezing hole is formed at the lower end of the body and at room temperature the fireproof valve and the stopper form a sealed structure and the fireproof shape memory alloy spring is compressed at a predetermined fire temperature to open the fire valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064947-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "water is injected through the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring is compressed at a predetermined freezing temperature to allow the water to flow through the freeze protection hole and the water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064947-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to the present invention in the sprinkler the body 1 having a cylindrical shape the top is open and at least one water injection port 101 on the side it is connected to the sprinkler water supply pipe and has a partition 201 having an outer diameter smaller than the inner diameter of the body 1 the outer peripheral surface of the partition 201 to seal the upper end of the body 1 a water pipe coupling part 2 having an upper plate 202 having a predetermined thickness and coupled to an upper end of the body 1 a fire valve 3 received below the upper plate 202 between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 a fire prevention shape memory alloy spring 21 coupled to the lower side of the upper plate 202 and accommodated between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 and coupled to the fire valve 3 a freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 having an upper end coupled to the partition 201 a stopper 221 coupled to a lower end of the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring 22 it is coupled to the lower end of the body 1 to receive the stopper 221 the top is open and comprises a freeze proof coupling body 4 having a water discharge pipe 401 at the bottom the lower end of the body 1 is formed with a freeze protection hole 102 at room temperature through the fire valve 3 and the stopper 221 to form a sealed structure the fire proof shape memory alloy spring 21 is predetermined the water is injected through the water injection port 101 by compressing at the fire temperature of the fire valve 3 and the freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 is tensioned at a predetermined freezing temperature to freeze proof hole 102 and it provides a sprinkler with a freeze protection structure characterized in that the water flows through the water discharge pipe 401"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064947-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a sprinkler comprising a body 1 having a cylindrical shape and having an open top and having at least one water jet 101 on a side surface thereof it is connected to the sprinkler water supply pipe and has a partition 201 having an outer diameter smaller than the inner diameter of the body 1 the outer peripheral surface of the partition 201 to seal the upper end of the body 1 a water pipe coupling part 2 having an upper plate 202 having a predetermined thickness and coupled to an upper end of the body 1 a fire valve 3 received below the upper plate 202 between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 a fire prevention shape memory alloy spring 21 coupled to the lower side of the upper plate 202 and accommodated between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 and coupled to the fire valve 3 it is coupled to the lower end of the body 1 the freeze proof coupling body 4 having an upper portion and a water discharge pipe 401 in the lower portion a freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 coupled to one side of the freeze proof coupling body 4 a stopper 221 accommodated inside the freeze protection assembly 4 and coupled to the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring 22 the lower end of the body 1 is formed with a freeze protection hole 102 at room temperature through the fire valve 3 and the stopper 221 to form a sealed structure the fire proof shape memory alloy spring 21 is predetermined the water is injected through the water injection port 101 by being compressed at the fire temperature of the fire valve 3 and the freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 is compressed at a predetermined freezing temperature to freeze proof hole 102 and water can flow through the water discharge pipe 401"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7151025-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after reacting for 0 hours the reacted reaction solution enters the filter cylinder 122 through the discharge pipe 115 and is filtered and washed with deionized water in order to obtain modified chitosan among them the ratio of the amount of glutamic acid dimethyl sulfoxide and concentrated sulfuric acid used is 1 g 10 0 ml 0.25 0.3 ml and the mass ratio of chitosan and glutamic acid is 2 1 step and step 2 using the drive mechanism 3 the modified chitosan prepared in step 1 is put into the electroplating wastewater in the stirring reaction chamber 2 through the material outlet 1222 and p h is adjusted to 2 to 8 the temperature in the stirring reaction chamber 2 is adjusted to 10 to 50 c by the heating tube 27 and at the same time the stirring rod 21 is rotated to 120 to 150 rpm by the driving mechanism 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "prevents freezing the control unit is further provided with a sticking prevention function when the operation time of the discharge pump is stopped for a specific time or more the discharge pump is operated for a specific time at a specific period to prevent sewage from sticking to the storage tank or the discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101528712-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore they can be stored and maintained for a long time in the water to be treated under the condition of being pressurized at normal temperature and the gas having ultrafine bubbles in addition to the dissolution effect it is possible to enhance the immunity of living organisms living in the for treatment water due to the purifying action of oxygen and ozone the sterilization action and the increased dissolved oxygen generated when the bubbles burst due to the self pressurizing effect and improve the living environment of the food.the microbubble generator for sterilization including oxygen and ozone according to the present invention can produce the same product repeatedly in the manufacturing industry of the water quality improvement device for sterilizing and purifying the water to be treated can do.10 raw milk input 20 ozone feed pipe 30 mixer 40 micro bubble generator 41 rotating disk 42 motor 50 micro bubble water flow tube 60 pressurized dissolving tank 61 vibration part 62 partial partition wall 70 discharge pipe 80 bypass pipe 90 bubble number size adjuster 100 pressure gauge 110 ozone regulator 120 ozone generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "groundwater contamination prevention structure 1 1 is built in the space inside the combined structure to combine and directly connected to each other and sealed to each other structural structure 1 1 1 is installed inside the underground rock well inside the casing 4 4 to prevent the groundwater contamination by itself and to automatically drain and drain the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100569649-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "therefore in the heat exchanger the discharge pipe 214 and the waste water conveying pipe 201 are heat exchanged so that the fluorine containing waste water rises a certain temperature and the treated water is preferably transferred to the next process while maintaining a temperature of 40 c or less"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654101-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in more detail a bypass pipe for freeze and burst prevention is connected between the suction pipe and the discharge pipe so that the temperature detected by the temperature sensor in winter is lowered below the set temperature if there is no water flow because the user does not use water the pump is driven so that the pressure of the discharge pipe is higher than the opening pressure of the relief valve and water circulates through the bypass pipe to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654101-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore the purpose of the present invention is to connect a bypass pipe for freeze prevention between the suction pipe and the discharge pipe so that in the winter if the temperature detected by the temperature sensor falls below the set temperature and there is no water flow because the user does not use water the pump is driven so that the pressure of the discharge pipe is higher than the opening pressure of the relief valve allowing water to circulate through the bypass pipe thereby providing a freeze prevention water supply pressurization device and a control method thereof that can prevent freezing in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101517040-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "however according to the conventional techniques as described above the ground water is discharged from the inside of the tunnel and the emergency water supply pipe 300 and the discharge pipe 400 constituted in the prior art of the former and the discharge pipe 139 when the ambient temperature falls below freezing in the cold winter season due to the closed state of the inside of the pipe when the valve is closed by the opening and closing valve 139a which is caused by the flow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171689-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "case 100 a plurality of led lamps 110 pump 230 water supply sensor 240 the heating wire 250 the heater 270 and the heater body temperature sensor 272 is configured to include the case 100 has a rectangular parallelepiped shape a pedestal 101 is formed at a lower portion thereof a cover 102 is formed at an upper portion thereof and a plurality of led lamps 110 and steam on on are provided at the front of the case 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569729-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in order to accelerate the generation and condensation of water vapor which is the main part of the present invention the jet ports 33 are arranged at predetermined intervals so as to generate high temperature steam while being immersed in the water surface 11 at both side edges in the longitudinal direction of the work line 10 not shown at both side ends of a plurality of discharge pipes 12 which are continuously drilled are connected to the discharge surface of the discharge pipe 12 which is submerged in the water surface 11 by a shielding film 37 12 to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101840639-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "2 the inlet pipe 401 the discharge pipe 402 and the inlet port 410 are cut to form a hole in the connection pipe 403 and then the inlet pipe 400 the processing part of the discharge pipe 402 and the inlet 410 and the processing part of the connection pipe 403 and the rear end part of the connection pipe 403 are assembled to each other through welding so that the manufacturing process is complicated there is a problem in that the assembling can not be performed due to heat deformation due to high temperature welding and deviation between the assembled parts and it is difficult to weld the partition 404 in the connecting pipe 403"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention can be operated to prevent the freezing in winter by wrapping a heating wire not shown in all the connection pipes to make the water supply including the water supply pipe and the water discharge pipe in particular the temperature sensor when the heating wire is preferentially operated by the control of the controller c according to the temperature value measured in 13 so that the heating wire is organically interlocked with the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention and the heating wire is not operated due to a short circuit of the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100701887-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the present invention having the above configuration is configured to operate using the waste heat hot steam generated in the incinerator the connection pipes 211a 211b provided on the rotary shaft 22 of the crushing impeller 21 the steam supply pipe and the steam discharge pipe not shown are hermetically connected and installed to allow hot steam to be discharged via the rotating shaft 22 and the paddle 210 and the connection port of the heating tank 35 37 and the drainage port 38 is also connected to the steam supply pipe and the steam discharge pipe not shown in an airtight manner so that the hot steam can be discharged via the heating zone 36 the drying chamber 30 air blowing pipe not shown for supplying high temperature air via a heat exchanger not shown to the drying barrel 31 of it is configured and used to be injected into the crushing chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100718246-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a liner of a folded and flexible material which is inserted into the existing buried pipe using a retraction means for repair or reinforcement and is used as a deformation pipe one or more elastic members attached to both ends of the buried pipe inner wall and the liner a packer member mounted at both ends of the buried pipe in order to seal the buried pipe into which the liner of the folded shape is inserted one side of which is provided with an injection pipe and an opposite side of the packer member a fluid supply unit for supplying a fluid to be injected into the buried pipe and discharged through the discharge pipe so that the folded liner is expanded and tightly adhered to the inner wall of the buried pipe and deformation preventing means is installed on the inner wall of the liner to prevent deformation of the liner in close contact with the inner wall of the buried pipe deformation tube inserting device for preventing deformation due to temperature changes including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100718246-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in addition the present invention is a liner of a folded and flexible material which is inserted into the existing buried pipe using the introduction means for repair or reinforcement and used as a deformation pipe one or more elastic members attached to both ends between the inner wall of the buried pipe and the liner to improve adhesion between the inner wall of the buried pipe and the liner a packer member mounted at both ends of the buried pipe in order to seal the buried pipe into which the liner of the folded shape is inserted one side of which is provided with an injection pipe and an opposite side of the packer member a fluid supply unit for supplying a fluid to be injected into the buried pipe and discharged through the discharge pipe so that the folded liner is expanded and tightly adhered to the inner wall of the buried pipe and it provides a strain pipe inserting device for preventing deformation due to temperature change including a deformation preventing means installed on the inner wall of the liner to prevent deformation of the liner in close contact with the inner wall of the buried pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100718246-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "and polyvinyl chloride composite materials are expanded and adhered to the inner wall of the sewer pipe 100 the packer member 500 is removed after the expansion contacted liner 300 is cooled in order to prevent deformation of the liner 300 in close contact with the inner wall of the sewage pipe 100 a deformation preventing means 700 is installed on the inner wall of the liner 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100966852-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it has a configuration in which a pressure relief valve is installed to be discharged to the outside to close the exhaust port.as described above according to the freeze protection device of the water pipe of the present invention by operating the hydraulic cylinder with a small amount of water flowing out according to the external temperature change and the force of the water the freeze with the water discharged through the operation of the cylinder effectively also by replacing the capacity of the hydraulic cylinder only it is possible to secure as much water as possible to prevent freezing at any water pipe size or water pressure and more precisely by controlling the amount of discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100846473-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the first and second valve assemblies 122 and 126 allow the regeneration mode to proceed while the mode is in progress"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100926077-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "subsequently looking at the plurality of pipe lines w1 to w14 provided in the water softener according to the present invention by connecting the external cold hot water pipes to the first valve assembly 350 to remove the cold hot raw water of the cold hot water pipes the first valve assembly 1 by connecting the first and second raw water supply lines w1 w2 to the first valve assembly 350 and the first valve assembly 350 to the first and second soft water tanks 710 720"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101166906-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "through the present invention by maintaining the temperature of the digester and the concentration tank in the distributed urban organic waste recycling facility installed in the central heating complex by using hot water or heating circulating water in the central heating complex the variation of urban organic inflow and outflow it is possible to increase the efficiency of digesters in distributed urban organic waste recycling facilities which are difficult to maintain constant temperature because they are installed large and small digesters"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100850033-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the organic matter thus pulverized is transferred to the at least one sterilization transfer screw 9 of the sterilization tank 10 by the first transfer screw 7"}]</data>
</edge>
