  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102027469-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in being installed in bridge and draining storm of bridge the top plate collecting part may be embedded in the top plate of the bridge and the rainwater of the top plate may be introduced into a protection catcher located at one side of the upper catchment part and connected vertically to the upper catchment part and buried in a protection wall of the bridge and a protective catchment space into which sewage of the upper plate is introduced a line drain connected to the upper plate collecting part and communicating with the upper plate collecting part and embedded in the upper plate a discharge pipe connected to the protection catchment unit and in communication with the protection catchment space and penetrating the protection wall the display unit is disposed in the upper collecting portion and may be erected if rainwater is accumulated in the upper collecting space of the upper collecting portion and the rainwater is not drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the metering water guide 30 excludes a certain amount of initial storm the initial storm is inadequate to use due to a high degree of contamination due to various pollutants in the air and in the present invention a certain amount of initial storm is stored in the user storage 300 that is discharging to the discharge pipe 12 and some rainwater flowing into the catchment tank 10 is collected in the buoyancy chamber 15 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that the upper portion is exposed from the filter medium over the entire length the upper portion of the filter material is exposed from the filter material to the inside of the filtration tank and the exposed portion is formed with an inlet hole for allowing the filter material washing water to flow into the discharge passage while the opposite end is installed in the partition wall 111b a filter media wash and contaminant discharge line configured to communicate with the filter material discharge outlet a filter material cleaning device installed under the filter material washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe to be buried in the filter material and spraying high pressure air or backwash water for washing the filter material and a filter medium washing water and contaminants which are installed outside the pretreatment tank and are washed by the filter material cleaning device and flowed into the pretreatment tank through the washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe and stagnant water accumulated in the water treatment tank and a stagnant water exclusion pump for removing the stagnant water when it is confirmed that stagnant water is present in the water treatment tank contaminants separated from the filter media and the filter media wash water used for the filter media are supplied to the discharge passage and the filtering water discharge port 135 having the reverse opening closing door 136 of the partition wall 111b to be forcedly sucked into the pretreatment tank and forcedly excluded to the outside by the congestion water exclusion pump the operation of the filter medium washing device is stopped and only the stagnant water exclusion pump is operated with the stagnant water of the water treatment tank to be operated until the complete removal of sediment deposited at the bottom of the tank has been confirmed initial treatment is a solid system of jing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 1002809 has a main body having an inlet pipe and a discharge pipe a contaminant collecting part provided inside the body and collecting floating contaminants and water soluble contaminants in the initial rainwater flowing through the inflow pipe a sedimentation tank in which the initial stormwater that has passed through the clogging trapping unit is stored a swirling screen for filtering precipitable contaminants in the initial storm that are stored in the settling tank and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside the swirl screen includes an inlet through which the initial storm flows an external vessel through which the sediment is discharged and an inner vessel which is installed in the outer vessel to be separated from the outer vessel and has a lower portion communicating with the outer vessel and a side of which is provided with a flow pipe for supplying an initial storm with the filtration tank an initial stormwater is discharged from the sedimentation tank to the filtration tank due to a difference in water level between the sedimentation tank and the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101433517-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent discharge pipe which is vertically fixed to the side wall of the building or pier and discharges the storm downward a cylindrical foreign matter removing cylinder which is detachably fitted to a lower end of the storm drain pipe and discharges the foreign matter contained in the stormwater in a state where the foreign matter is filtered out a drain hole formed in a lower surface of the lower surface of the foreign matter filtering tube to control a discharge rate while filtering out foreign matter in the rainwater a waste pipe formed to communicate with the outside of the foreign matter filtering barrel so as to discharge the foreign matter to the outside of the foreign matter filtering barrel when the water flows into the foreign substance filtering barrel due to the resistance generated in the process of discharging the outdoor water through the drain and an excellent reservoir for storing water discharged through the right side hall wherein the foreign substance filtering cylinder is formed by a stepped shape having a gradually increasing diameter in the downward direction and is divided by an upper foreign body trash passing through lower foreign body trash can while the side trunk of the upper foreign body trash can is connected to the inside of the lower foreign body trash receptacle wherein when the water level in the lower foreign matter squeeze box rises the floating member is raised to block the discharge site of the upper foreign matter squeeze sump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 1604465 filed and patented by the applicant of the present application includes a collecting tank having an initial storm drainage chamber and a buoyancy chamber collecting stormwater a screen installed in the water collecting tank and filtering the foreign substances contained in the water flowing through the inlet of the water collecting tank an initial storm drain pipe for discharging stormwater and foreign matter collected in the initial storm drain chamber to the initial storm drain chamber after being supplied through the screen a clean water discharge pipe connected to the buoyancy chamber of the water collecting tank and guiding the stormwater collected in the buoyancy chamber to the storage unit for recycling a metering water guide installed in the water collecting tank and guiding part of the water flowing into the water collecting tank to the buoyancy chamber when the initial storm is discharged through the initial storm drain pipe by storing a predetermined amount of metering water by the metering water guide while guiding the storm introduced into the catchment tank to the initial storm drainage chamber of the catchment tank but also an initial high level of high contamination is introduced into the buoyancy chamber and water is supplied through a clean and excellent discharge pipe collected in the buoyancy chamber although it is excellent in purification there is a disadvantage that the pollution degree is high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a filtration tank provided with a filtration quartz for allowing the fine water to be filtered through a predetermined distance upward from a position spaced upward from the inner bottom the filtration tank is connected to the other side of the filtration tank via a backwash water tank transfer pipe at a central portion of one side facing the other central portion of the filtration tank and is filtered from the filtration tank through the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash tank where stormwater level is reached and is connected to a central portion of one side of the backwash water tank opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank through a discharge pipe to be introduced into the backwash water tank through the outlet pipe an effluent tank for discharging the filtered desulfur to the outside and bypassing the desulfurized effluent when the level of the desulfurized effluent storage tank is higher than a certain level through the bypass pipeline the sedimentation tank is disposed at a predetermined distance from the sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "a filtration tank provided with a filtration quaternion for allowing a rise in the height of the water to be filtered from a position spaced upward from the inner bottom by a predetermined distance upward the filtration tank is connected to the other side of the filtration tank via a backwash water tank transfer pipe at a central portion of one side facing the other central portion of the filtration tank and is filtered from the filtration tank through the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash tank where stormwater level is reached and is connected to a central portion of one side of the backwash water tank opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank through a discharge pipe to be introduced into the backwash water tank through the outlet pipe an effluent tank for discharging the filtered desulfur to the outside and bypassing the desulfurized effluent when the level of the desulfurized effluent storage tank is higher than a certain level through the bypass pipeline a bottom wastewater pipe disposed at a predetermined distance from the settling tank and connected to the transfer pipe from the inside of the settling tank selectively introducing the stagnant water of the settling tank and the backwash water is selectively supplied from the backwash water tank to the lower side of the filtration tank to backwash the filtration tank and the settling tank by the backwash water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715445-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "in addition the reason for the installation of the second screen 19b is to block the dumping of the solids or food waste through the storm discharge pipe 13 due to the lack of awareness of the residents to the integrated storm drain and sewage collector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715445-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in addition since the first screening network is assembled while the second screening network is completely fixed it is easy to block the dumping of solids or food waste through the storm discharge pipe due to the lack of consciousness of the residents for the integrated rainwater catchment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101764398-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "a contamination abatement facility is provided in the lower wall 16 of the housing 10 a filtering partition wall 31 which is formed so as to have an upper end which is equal to or lower than the lowest point height of the inflow pipe 17 and which is separated from the space of the filtration tank 30 formed on the rear side the filtration unit 30a which is located between the rear wall 31 and the rear wall 12 and has both ends vertically fixed to the left and right side walls 13 and 14 so that only the space on the upper side of the filtration tank 30 is filtered and an upper support partition wall 37 for separating the upper support partition wall 30a and the upper support partition wall 30b into a management section 30b for a worker to enter and work for management of the filtration section 30a a mesh chain filter mesh net 32 having a front end portion fixed to the left and right side walls 13 and 14 and a lower end of the filtration partition 31 and the upper support partition 37 30a of the filtration mesh net 32 and is held in the sedimentation tank 20 a filtration material layer 33 having at least one filter medium 33a that is filtered while flowing an initial storm that flows into the filtration section 30a of the filtration tank 30 through the filtration tank 30 the grill 38 is fixedly supported on the upper support partition wall 37 and the rear wall 12 at the lower side of the discharge pipe 18 and a filter medium 33a of the filter medium layer 33 by spraying water at a predetermined pressure toward the filter medium layer 33 through the filter mesh network 32 located below the filter mesh network 32 of the filter medium 30 a water distribution pipe 34 having at least one water injection nozzle 34a for separating foreign matter adhering to the filter medium 30 and a filtering mesh network 32 located below the filtering mesh network 32 of the filtration tank 30 33a of the filter material layer 33 by discharging air bubbles at a predetermined pressure toward the filter material layer 33 and an air bubble spraying tube 35 having one or more air bubble spray nozzles 35a for facilitating the initialization of the sedimentation tank 20 and a filtration tank discharge pump 36 disposed at the lower end of the filtration tank 30 and discharging the filtered stormwater through the filtration tank discharge pipe 36a to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in an initial high boiling point contamination treatment system 100 connected to the end of the conduit or the river water from which the polluted water is discharged to provide pollution excellence and selectively supply only the initial nonpoint pollution excellence a reservoir 200 for storing initial boiling impurity contamination provided to the water collection channel 130 of the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants a siphon pipe 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the water level of the reservoir 200 becomes equal to or higher than the height of the highest part in the reversed u shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101778786-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the initial storm having a high contamination degree from being supplied to the sedimentation tank guide pipe"}]</data>
