  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102027469-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in being installed in bridge and draining storm of bridge the top plate collecting part may be embedded in the top plate of the bridge and the rainwater of the top plate may be introduced into a protection catcher located at one side of the upper catchment part and connected vertically to the upper catchment part and buried in a protection wall of the bridge and a protective catchment space into which sewage of the upper plate is introduced a line drain connected to the upper plate collecting part and communicating with the upper plate collecting part and embedded in the upper plate a discharge pipe connected to the protection catchment unit and in communication with the protection catchment space and penetrating the protection wall the display unit is disposed in the upper collecting portion and may be erected if rainwater is accumulated in the upper collecting space of the upper collecting portion and the rainwater is not drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101138988-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "as shown the outlet pipe 31 may control the opening and closing of the outlet pipe via a separate valve 35"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a road surface 12 formed by packing asphalt or concrete and a collecting unit 10 installed on both sides of the road surface 12 to collect rainwater and a rainwater collecting unit 20 connected to the collecting unit 10 in a road structure provided with an excellent discharge pipe 20 for discharging to a sewer a housing 32 formed with an opening 34 on the upper side and inserted into the road surface 12 a lifting block 30 mounted on the housing 32 such that the upper end of the lifting block 30 can be lifted up and down and the rack gear 31 is extended downward a spring 40 connected to a lower side of the elevating block 30 to press the elevating block 30 upward a pinion gear 50 meshing with the rack gear 31 a drive shaft 60 rotatably shaft connected to the pinion gear 50 and connected to the pinion gear 50 through a ratchet 61 and positively rotated only when the rack gear 31 is lowered a rotation limiting device 70 coupled to the drive shaft 60 to restrict the drive shaft 60 to rotate only in the normal rotation direction a housing 81 formed in a cylindrical shape and having a through hole 81a through which the drive shaft 60 is rotatably inserted is formed on one side of the center axis and a housing 81 having a central end 82a and an outer end 82b the center end 82a is connected to the driving shaft 60 extending to the inside of the housing 81 and the outside end 82b is fixed to the inner circumferential surface of the housing 81 and a rotation shaft 83 coupled to the outer side of the housing 81 so as to be coaxial with the drive shaft 60 so as to rotate together with the housing 81"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533930-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "18 2012 it is not easy to clean it when the foreign matter accumulates in the part and in particular when the part of the water discharge pipe is blocked because the rainwater is discharged to the end of the water discharge pipe along the water discharge pipe a problem that becomes ineffective because it can not be exercised occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130757-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "wow an elbow shaped rainwater discharge pipe communicating with the partition plate and discharging rainwater to the outside of the body a sewage inlet pipe configured at one side of the sewage collecting container and configured to protrude a trap into the sewage collecting container and having a heating wire installed therein the sewage inlet pipe is formed in a lower position than the sewage inlet pipe characterized in that the sewage inlet pipe particularly in the trap portion of the sewage freezes during the winter the sewage flow back to the problem the sewage inlet pipe it is to prevent freezing of winter sewage by heat generation by installing heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130757-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "it will be able to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130757-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in addition in the present invention between the rainwater discharge pipe 120 and the sewage inflow pipe 130 the heat insulating layer 150a 150b 150c in which the heat insulating material 152a 154b 152c is embedded is further configured to communicate with the atmosphere it is possible to prevent the cold air of the winter season from being delivered to the lower portion from the sump a can be delivered to the sewage inflow pipe 130 to prevent the sewage freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 the water level controller 32 includes a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor 29 the second sensor 30 and the third sensor 31 of the water level sensor portion the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 16 may be discharged through the discharge pipe 22 for a predetermined discharge time when the time counted by the timer 33 becomes longer than a predetermined time wherein the control unit controls the discharge valve 21 so that the discharge water 21 is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level controller may further include a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor the second sensor and the third sensor of the water level sensor portion and controls the discharge valve so that the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank can be discharged through the discharge pipe for a preset discharge time when the discharge time exceeds the predetermined set time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200318223-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "through the sewage fume pipe 10 is to be firmly bound with the anchor 30 .according to the present invention as described above the sewage collected in the discharge device is discharged from a long distance by the discharge pipe while the sewage collected in the discharge device is blocked by the discharge pipe to prevent the sewage due to leakage and rainwater to the ground directly supporting the sewage pipe for sewage since it is treated it is possible to suppress ground erosion and collapse by sewage as much as possible and also to suppress as much as possible the distortion and warpage of the sewage fume pipe due to partial ground collapse while being firmly connected through the anchor and the wire having excellent fixing force"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the metering water guide 30 excludes a certain amount of initial storm the initial storm is inadequate to use due to a high degree of contamination due to various pollutants in the air and in the present invention a certain amount of initial storm is stored in the user storage 300 that is discharging to the discharge pipe 12 and some rainwater flowing into the catchment tank 10 is collected in the buoyancy chamber 15 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that the upper portion is exposed from the filter medium over the entire length the upper portion of the filter material is exposed from the filter material to the inside of the filtration tank and the exposed portion is formed with an inlet hole for allowing the filter material washing water to flow into the discharge passage while the opposite end is installed in the partition wall 111b a filter media wash and contaminant discharge line configured to communicate with the filter material discharge outlet a filter material cleaning device installed under the filter material washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe to be buried in the filter material and spraying high pressure air or backwash water for washing the filter material and a filter medium washing water and contaminants which are installed outside the pretreatment tank and are washed by the filter material cleaning device and flowed into the pretreatment tank through the washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe and stagnant water accumulated in the water treatment tank and a stagnant water exclusion pump for removing the stagnant water when it is confirmed that stagnant water is present in the water treatment tank contaminants separated from the filter media and the filter media wash water used for the filter media are supplied to the discharge passage and the filtering water discharge port 135 having the reverse opening closing door 136 of the partition wall 111b to be forcedly sucked into the pretreatment tank and forcedly excluded to the outside by the congestion water exclusion pump the operation of the filter medium washing device is stopped and only the stagnant water exclusion pump is operated with the stagnant water of the water treatment tank to be operated until the complete removal of sediment deposited at the bottom of the tank has been confirmed initial treatment is a solid system of jing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102441986-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "in addition since the contaminant screen 210 of the present invention discharges large foreign substances contained in the rainwater into the lower part of the sedimentation tank 100 in advance the vortex inducing part discharge pipe 221 or the vortex inducing part discharge pipe 221 is closed due to large foreign substances due to large foreign substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101174757-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "as described above it is possible to easily manufacture high quality drinking water by the effect of oxidation and coagulation in the line mixer so that ground water surface water rainwater etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floating bucket for collecting suspended solids a fourth floating material collection conveyor for transporting the collected particulate matter and the ultra fine particles in the rear portion of the floating material collection rotating bucket fine particles rising from the rear portion of the fourth floating material collection conveyor to the upper portion of the river water a fourth contaminant screw feeder configured to collect and collect sex contaminants and ultra fine magnetic contaminants to push and transport the contaminants to the outside of the river water processing box and combine the rotor and the rotor support a fifth floating material collection conveyor for transporting and collecting the collected particulate matter and the ultrafine particles on the rear part of the fourth contaminant screw feeder the suspended solids removing plate and the particulate collecting guide plate sequentially coupled with the rotating belt coupled to the rotating body a fifth suspended solids material collector in which the suspended particulate floating material plate which serves to prevent the collected suspended solids molecules from being separated from the outside of the rotating belt is combined and a water reservoir and a rainwater reservoir for connecting the lower end of the river water processing box and the river water discharge pipe by using a discharge control valve and storing the processed river water and at the end of the river water processing box from an upstream of the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100375130-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the past there was a poverty that caused social controversy such as untreated and discharged to the terminal treatment discharge pipe in the untreated state contaminating the water quality of the water supply source or adversely affect the biological growth in the water.the present invention has been invented to prevent the above closed end of the present invention is to be installed in the initial sedimentation tank cold dust chamber to the front end inlet of the body having a fastening flange portion is attached to the hinge portion formed on the upper surface of the body disc it is installed to be opened and closed by means of the connecting pipe through the fastener is installed on the left and right sides of the upper connecting portion between the supports connected to the shaft of the hinge portion the fitting section of the connecting pipe through the support between the buckle is installed in the early stage of rain when a large amount of rainwater flows in at this time as the floats fastened to the left and right connectors and the floats fastened to the disks the disks in the open open state move downwards to the support point to block the inlet formed at the tip of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101030108-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "as described above when the rain rain gutter of the present invention does not rain the elastic member 30 extends due to its own weight and its lower end contacts the inner bottom surface 12 of the outer cylinder 10 to block backflow of odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "20 0433333 installed on the top of the casing casing developed for waterworks to block the inflow of external pollutants to make waterproof to prevent the inflow of rainwater into the inside of the city when submerged can be cleaned with a simple method when cleaning with compressed air of the number of wells for an antifouling structure is disclosed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102072963-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the non point contaminant collecting device included in the initial excellent water to collect the contaminant is provided at the end of the sewage pipe 10 discharged to the initial excellent rainwater and sewage basic framework 14 is formed in the end of the sewage pipe 10 is formed in the form of a connection and the inner side drain 14 which is discharged through the sewage pipe 10 the initial excellent rainwater and living sewage discharged to the inside the other side of the base frame 14 is formed in a plate shaped connection is provided with the discharge hole 16 corresponding to the discharge hole 12 is formed on the inside and the protruding end is protruded forward on the outer surface except the upper portion a sliding guide plate 20 having a sliding guide part 18 formed to be bent inwardly the sliding guide part 18 of the sliding guide plate 20 is formed in a plate shape so as to be inserted into the slide from the top to the bottom the receiving hole 22 penetrating corresponding to the discharge hole 16 is formed inside sliding plate 24 the other side of the sliding plate 24 is formed in a cylindrical shape and one side is connected to the sliding plate 24 the outer periphery spaced from the other side is formed in a disk like extension and a plurality of through holes in the inside a binding plate 28 having a 26 is formed and the discharge pipe retainer strip 30 protruding from the outside is formed and the discharge pipe ring 32 which is formed to be hooked to the discharge pipe retainer s