facility f described later through the discharge pipe 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "to this end a discharge pipe 160 may be connected to the storage block unit 140 and when the groundwater stored in the storage block unit 140 is above a certain level the groundwater may be discharged to an adjacent rainwater treatment facility f through the discharge pipe 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "here when one storage block unit 140 is composed of multiple storage blocks the discharge pipe 160 may be connected to the storage block located at the outermost end based on the building wall w that is the storage block closest to the adjacent rainwater treatment facility f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "for example the discharge pipe 160 connected to a rainwater manhole f1 in a rainwater treatment facility f may be provided in a form of a non porous pipe and the discharge pipe 160 connected to a rainwater receiver f2 or a rainwater infiltration retention block f3 may be provided in a form of a hollow pipe having a spiral gap whose outer side is wrapped with geotextile"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "accordingly groundwater stored in the storage block unit 140 may be discharged to the rainwater receiver f2 through the discharge pipe 160 and may flow into a rainwater recharge well along the pipe of the rainwater receiver f2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "additionally the discharge pipe 160 may be connected to a rainwater infiltration retention block f3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "according to the groundwater reduction system 100 by the permanent drainage method of a building linked to a rainwater treatment facility f with improved operational stability according to an embodiment of the present invention which includes a permanent drainage material d a foundation layer b a permane