 is continuously introduced along with rainwater and the like and the heights of the sewage w deposited in the sewage storage units 14 and 43 and the waste checking and discharging unit 64 increase gradually"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226173-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention blocks the inflow of pollutants in the initial rainwater and removes particulate matter from the filtration device by centrifugation and filtering and in a large rainwater storage tank has a waterway structure using a flow wall to induce one way flow and thus discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101778786-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the initial storm having a high contamination degree from being supplied to the sedimentation tank guide pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101778786-B1", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "the scope of the present invention is defined by the appended claims and all changes or modifications derived from the meaning and scope of the claims and their equivalents should be construed as being included within the scope of the present invention.1 inlet pipe 2 settling tank guide pipe 3 discharge pipe 10 rotating pipe 12 foreign matter removing protrusion 20 shielding film member 22 abrasive film pattern 30 foreign matter filtering unit 40 first path guide part 50 second path guide part 60 receiving tube 70 connecting tube member 100 initial excellent excretion part 200 sedimentation tank 230 wave preventing part 240 partition wall 300 treatment tank 400 cyclone type separation unit 500 purified water supply part 600 filtration part 1000 rainwater purification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101768117-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "as a result pollution sources included in the initial rainwater and the cleaning water can be guided to the sewage pipe rather than the gutter pipe thereby preventing contamination of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "failure of the discharge pump or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894568-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 0477945 march 10 2005 water treatment device using electrolysis summary of the invention accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems occurring in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an electrolytic apparatus and a method for supplying electrolytic water to an enclosed cylindrical electrolytic cell by receiving ground water river water rainwater inflow water the main object of the present invention is to provide a water treatment apparatus using an electric device which can easily cope with increase decrease of treatment capacity through a simple structure in which the number of modules is increased or decreased according to the treatment capacity by means of a module in which an electrode is installed.the present invention provides a cylindrical electrolytic cell 12 having a to be treated water inflow pipe 16a and a treated water discharge pipe 16b 14 provided inside the electrolytic cell 12 and having a cylindrical shape with different diameters and composed of two anodes 14a 14c and one cathode 14b 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "block the discharge to the outside of the flow induction manhole 20 through 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is higher than the minimum value opening the three way valve so that the water of the second tank is supplied through the downpipe and connected to the supply pipe and preventing the water of the first tank from being supplied to the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is higher than the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe purified in the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joined from the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joined including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so that the charge level of the battery is lower than the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is below the minimum value turning on the three way valve to connect the other discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is above the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joins including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 if the charge level of the battery is below the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "together with and an inflow control gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at an upstream portion of the purifier box constructed upstream of the multifunctional watercourse constituting a double discharge regulating gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at a downstream portion of the purge box a structure in which a double air duct coupled to the regulating water gate is formed at the lower end of the double discharge adjusting water gate a dust collector is configured to lift up a large contaminant at an upstream portion of the purifier box the structure of the vibration damper includes a first screen installed at an inclined position with respect to inflow water and a damper main body for filtering contaminants such as inflow water through a first screen and a second screen the rolling chains being configured to be continuously rotated by a driving force of a first driving poly that is belt coupled with a driving motor along a plurality of sprocket wheels formed opposite to both sides of the main body of the vibration damper a first driven poly configured on the other side of a rotational axis associated with said first driven poly a large lifting rake pin coupled with the rolling chain so as to lift large contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain not shown so as to prevent the pins from being separated from one side and the other of the outer surface of the pin a transverse coupling plate formed between the rolling chain and one side of the large lifting rake coupled with the pin a plurality of large lifting rakes formed between the transverse coupling plates a third screen having a plurality of water discharging holes for filtering small sized contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain wherein the upper end of the third screen is coupled to the plate member to form a curved surface up to the upper end of the upper sprocket wheel a first upper and lower guide rails which are combined with the large lifting rake and act to assist the rectilinear motion of the rolling chain while preventing the pin which is simultaneously engaged with the rolling chain from being sagged by the weight of the obstacle lower guide rails third and lower guide rails and fourth and lower guide rails are disposed between one side of the pin and the other side by the four upper and lower guide rails structure a hitting rake for hitting and removing the impurities contained in the large lifting rake wherein the driving rake is joined to one side and the other side of the driving rake case by a white bond a structure coupled to a second driven poly on one side of the white paper the second driven pulley which rotates the pulley in the reverse direction a first driven pulley axially coupled to the driving motor and a rotary belt coupled to the driving pulley wherein the pulley is rotated counterclockwise to remove contaminants trapped between the large lifting rakes a discharge conveyor installed at a rear side of the main body of the damper to receive the dirt falling and discharge it to the outside an air pump operative to float light contaminants having a specific gravity introduced into the inside of the purifier box the air discharge pipe coupled to the air pump is installed in the inside of the purifier box to float the organic matter material molecules of light specific gravity contained in the rainwater or river water flowing into the purifier box to the upper end of the purifier box a conveyor belt to which a binding plate and a lifting barrel for pouring and removing lightweight contaminants introduced into the inside of the purifier box are coupled a structure in which the coupling plate and the lifting bristle are combined with a white paper a structure in which a plurality of holes are formed in the lower end of the lifting bar a structure in which a nonwoven fabric is installed on the bottom of the lifting jacket and then the nonwoven fabric is fixed to the lifting jacket using an engaging member having a plurality of water discharging holes formed at an upper end of the non woven fabric the conveyor belt is coupled with a plurality of roller motors not shown to rotate the conveyor belt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a structure that is coupled to a conveyance belt for conveying contaminants to the outside on the rear side of the lifting bar the underwater pump connected to the conveyor belt constitutes a submerged pump at the lower end of the purifier box to remove the particulate contaminants remaining in the inside of the lifting jacket when lifting the particulate contaminants floating on the upper end of the booster box a pipeline coupled with the submersible pump an underwater pump for completely removing fine contaminants introduced into the purifier box by using a water injection nozzle formed at an end of a pipe connected to the pipeline and a discharge control valve coupled to a discharge control valve for controlling discharge of light organic matter molecules floating at the upper end of the purifier box at a downstream portion of the purifier box the process of cleansing polluted river water or contaminated rainwater using a river water or rain water purification system configured to purify polluted river water and contaminated rainwater by separate discharge is characterized in that the multifunctional water gate configured to store the river water to store river water or rainwater and to open the inflow adjusting gate constructed in the purifying box to inflow river water or rainwater into the inside of the purifying box and the air discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "air is continuously blown into the purge box 7000 through the air discharge pipe 737 coupled with the air pump 719 so that the specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifier box 7000 the light pollutant molecules float up to the upper part of the purifier box 7000 and at the same time the purifier 8000 is rotated to continuously rotate the large lifting rake 701 constructed in the purifier 8000 to remove the pollutants contained in the river water or rainwater the large scum and small scum are removed while the lifting scion 711 coupled with the conveyor belt 712 is continuously rotated to remove the organic material scum that is light in specific gravity and accumulated in the upper part of the contaminated river water or rainwater the underwater pump 990 and the jetting nozzle 992 are continuously operated while removing the water from the purge box 7000 the process of eliminating the remaining particulate organic matter completely removes the various wastes and contaminants contained in river water and rainwater and completely eliminates them reuse or clean them"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "223 is provided the sediment discharge valve 223 is preferably operated while controlling the opening and closing interval according to the generation amount of the pollutant in the case of a typical rainwater treatment is preferably operated once every 1 to 3 hours"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "there was a problem of not being able to.the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above the object of the present invention is to ensure the maximum amount of water through the rain unit to the discharge pipe side through the drainage unit seated in the cover to ensure the maximum amount of water it is to provide a facility for preventing the smell and backflow of road rainwater receivers that can reliably block the outflow of odor due to wastewater and also effectively cope with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "in addition the rainwater discharge pipe 5 has a configuration in which it is integrated and extended in a downwardly sloping structure as shown in figure 3 or 5 on the lower surface of the installation finishing piece 4 and the extended inner surface space is it is a means for bypassing and discharging rainwater flowing into the drainage space 1 into a sewer pipe buried in the road surface while connected to the drainage space 1 in an open structure"}]</data>
