  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "first the high initial initial rainfall that occurs at the beginning of sewage or rainfall that is normally introduced into the sewage discharge pipeline can be collected through the sewage discharge section and the stormwater flowing in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall is increased by the water pressure the opening and closing of the sewer water discharge pipe is controlled by rotating the rotating plate by the opening and closing type of the flow wall and the link linkage portion and the link portion interlocked with the opening and closing section of the sewage water discharge pipe to prevent the inflow of sewage water it is possible to reduce the dredging cost by preventing the inflow of the accumulated sediments and to reduce the sewage treatment cost by allowing only the planned amount of sewage to be collected in the sewage pipeline and the breakage of the manhole can be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904287-B1", "para_id": "para_99", "text": "it only plays a role in preventing decay due to water retention by leaving only the impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 0894022 april 10 2009 in the treatment of non point pollutants contained in the initial rainfall effluent waterproofing the effluent purified in the non point pollutant treatment apparatus the variable wear is formed to protrude upwards to the inside so that the initial rainfall outflow water flows in the rain pipe is formed on one side a gripping portion is formed at an upper end and a screen is formed on an outer surface thereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "1 to 6 to separate the initial rainfall effluent and to form a rainwater toil chamber 11 having a settling function the rainwater toil chamber 11 is an inlet pipe 12 rainwater discharge pipe 13 and tea collection rainwater collection facility 10 having a storage facility inlet pipe 14 and the settling space 15 connected to the reservoir so that rainwater flows into the reservoir while having a function and the screen facility 16 to block the inflow of contaminants into the reservoir the rainwater collection facility in the rainwater collection facility 11 the storage facility 20 through which the rainwater flows into the reservoir through the reservoir inlet pipe 14 and installed on the bottom of the reservoir to produce a water change pipe and the overflow wear room on one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "first the high initial initial rainfall that occurs at the time of sewage or rainfall inflowing into the city can be collected in the sewage subway pipeline through the sewage discharge section and the large amount of rainfall introduced into the large amount during rainfall is increased by the water pressure the opening of the sewage water discharge pipe is reduced by rotating the rotating plate by the linkage part and the link part linked with the open front water gate and the linkage part linked thereto to prevent the inflow of rainwater and soil to the sewage water supply pipe channel and discharging it to the discharge river it is possible to reduce the dredging cost by cutting off the earth and sand and it is possible to reduce the sewage treatment cost because it is possible to collect only the planned amount of sewage in the sewage subway pipeline as well as the breakage of the sewer pipeline and manhole due to the water pressure caused by the over can be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101349613-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the lower end of the filter member which is filled with the upper end and is sealed is provided with a coupling tool detachably assembled to a coupling hole provided in the discharge pipe and downwardly discharged downward along the inner cylinder after the contaminant is removed while passing through the filter medium"}]</data>
