  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the scum removal device is installed in the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to discharge only scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing device it has a hopper shaped body which is located inside the waterway and introduces a scum to the outside of the waterway through the discharge pipe formed at the bottom thereof and a support bar for supporting the scum detection sensor and the water level detection sensor on the upper part of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in the scum removing apparatus according to the present invention for achieving this object in the scum removing apparatus is installed in the water channel of the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to flow only the scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing apparatus includes a scum hopper positioned inside the channel and flowing in the scum to flow out of the channel through a discharge pipe formed at a lower portion thereof an elevating unit configured to elevate the scum hopper a support part supported on the upper side of the waterway to support the lifting part a scum detecting sensor installed at a front portion of the scum hopper to sense an amount of floating scum a water level sensor installed at a rear portion of the scum hopper to detect a water level and a controller for adjusting the height of the scum hopper by controlling the lifting unit according to the detection state of the scum detecting sensor and the water level detecting sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200203441-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "as shown here the present invention induces the circulation of water in the canal waterway and supplies dissolved oxygen in the circulation process for the purpose of improving the water quality of the canal waterway to maintain the ecosystem and to prevent the water impact of the discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100629151-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "initially excellent multi filtration facility characterized in that the installation of the vertical two stage filter 50 coupled to the 80 while the discharge pipe 91 is connected to the lower portion of the vertical two stage filter 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226173-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention blocks the inflow of pollutants in the initial rainwater and removes particulate matter from the filtration device by centrifugation and filtering and in a large rainwater storage tank has a waterway structure using a flow wall to induce one way flow and thus discharge pipe"}]</data>
