space 750 formed at a lower portion of the drainage guide plate 710 through a drainage connection pipe 770.according to the present invention it is possible to increase the ventilation efficiency so as to prevent a safety accident that may lead to a short circuit or an electric shock accident due to the nature of a distribution line installed in the ground it can prevent secondary electrical safety accidents caused by external damage to the shelf inside the underground pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100375130-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the past there was a poverty that caused social controversy such as untreated and discharged to the terminal treatment discharge pipe in the untreated state contaminating the water quality of the water supply source or adversely affect the biological growth in the water.the present invention has been invented to prevent the above closed end of the present invention is to be installed in the initial sedimentation tank cold dust chamber to the front end inlet of the body having a fastening flange portion is attached to the hinge portion formed on the upper surface of the body disc it is installed to be opened and closed by means of the connecting pipe through the fastener is installed on the left and right sides of the upper connecting portion between the supports connected to the shaft of the hinge portion the fitting section of the connecting pipe through the support between the buckle is installed in the early stage of rain when a large amount of rainwater flows in at this time as the floats fastened to the left and right connectors and the floats fastened to the disks the disks in the open open state move downwards to the support point to block the inlet formed at the tip of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101030108-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "as described above when the rain rain gutter of the present invention does not rain the elastic member 30 extends due to its own weight and its lower end contacts the inner bottom surface 12 of the outer cylinder 10 to block backflow of odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "multifunctional storage system to reduce initial rain pollution and prevent urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100629151-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "initially excellent multi filtration facility characterized in that the installation of the vertical two stage filter 50 coupled to the 80 while the discharge pipe 91 is connected to the lower portion of the vertical two stage filter 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 0894022 april 10 2009 in the treatment of non point pollutants contained in the initial rainfall effluent waterproofing the effluent purified in the non point pollutant treatment apparatus the variable wear is formed to protrude upwards to the inside so that the initial rainfall outflow water flows in the rain pipe is formed on one side a gripping portion is formed at an upper end and a screen is formed on an outer surface thereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275666-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "contained in the rain water is first filtered by the grating cover 3 but those passing through the sedimentation chamber 9 formed at the bottom of the sump 1 after the accumulation the discharge pipe 2 has a structure that is discharged through the drain pipe 2 thereby becoming a main factor to block the drain pipe 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101865757-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a manhole body having a lid formed by spacing a plurality of penetrating holes communicating with the ground for natural discharge of rainwater and at least the upper end thereof from the bottom of the manhole body is arranged at a height corresponding to the inflow pipe and divides the inside thereof into two chambers and in order to induce deceleration of the flow velocity of the rainwater flowing from the inflow pipe to the outflow pipe there is disclosed a rainwater storage and manhole facility apparatus including a partition wall provided with a distribution hole for communicating compartments.1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101316530-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the sedimentation tank 20 is a rainwater inlet pipe 21 is installed to be introduced into the bottom portion from the upper side is to be able to precipitate the sludge in rainwater the sludge permeation network 22 on the bottom side of the sedimentation tank 20 and the sludge collection unit 23 is provided directly below the sludge permeation network 22 to block foreign substances from the rainwater introduced into the sedimentation tank 20 by the sludge permeation network 22 and the sludge collection unit 23 the sludge collected in this way is installed in the sludge collection unit 23 and to be discharged to the rain pipe 12 by the first transfer pump 25 connected to the first discharge pipe 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826482-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to accomplish the above objects there is provided a vertical channel rain water filtration apparatus comprising a vertical water channel type rainwater filtration apparatus having a collecting pipe through which rainwater flows upwardly and a drain pipe for discharging contaminants downward a vertical pipe case having an expansion part having a diameter relatively larger than that of the water collecting pipe and the drain pipe a funnel shaped funnel pipe communicating with the water collecting pipe and disposed on the upper side of the expanding unit so that the rainwater flowing downward is in surface contact with the swirl like shape due to the acceleration due to the gravity and the turning force and a mesh screen provided on the upper side of the expansion unit for separating the rainwater falling from the funnel pipe and the rainwater and the rainwater through the collision caused by the dropping of the rainwater and a rainwater collecting part having a rainwater collecting compartment for collecting separated rainwater and having a rainwater outlet formed at one side of the rainwater collecting compartment and a contaminant discharge path through which the contaminants separated to the outside of the inclined surface of the mesh screen are discharged thereby discharging the contaminants to the contaminant discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100647994-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "rainwater storage device of the present invention for achieving the object of the present invention as described above is the cylindrical body is provided with an inlet is formed in the inlet through which the rainwater flows inlet is formed with a discharge valve for discharging the rainwater flowing into the lower portion a filter member provided at the inlet side of the body to prevent a large amount of foreign substances from entering the body a shutoff valve provided inside the body to block the rainwater introduced through the inlet at a predetermined amount an initial excellent separation means in which a discharge port is formed in the cutoff valve upper side body to discharge rainwater blocked by the cutoff valve to the outside of the body the supply pipe for supplying rainwater stored in the space portion to the outside having a sludge discharge pipe is provided in the lower portion having a space portion of a predetermined size to accommodate and store the rain water discharged from the discharge port of the body of the initial excellent separation means and a water level sensor formed on one side of the storage tank and sensing the level of rain water stored in the space to control an inlet valve so that tap water can be introduced through the tap water inlet pipe and above the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894568-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 0477945 march 10 2005 water treatment device using electrolysis summary of the invention accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems occurring in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an electrolytic apparatus and a method for supplying electrolytic water to an enclosed cylindrical electrolytic cell by receiving ground water river water rainwater inflow water the main object of the present invention is to provide a water treatment apparatus using an electric device which can easily cope with increase decrease of treatment capacity through a simple structure in which the number of modules is increased or decreased according to the treatment capacity by means of a module in which an electrode is installed.the present invention provides a cylindrical electrolytic cell 12 having a to be treated water inflow pipe 16a and a treated water discharge pipe 16b 14 provided inside the electrolytic cell 12 and having a cylindrical shape with different diameters and composed of two anodes 14a 14c and one cathode 14b 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "together with and an inflow control gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at an upstream portion of the purifier box constructed upstream of the multifunctional watercourse constituting a double discharge regulating gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at a downstream portion of the purge box a structure in which a double air duct coupled to the regulating water gate is formed at the lower end of the double discharge adjusting water gate a dust collector is configured to lift up a large contaminant at an upstream portion of the purifier box the structure of the vibration damper includes a first screen installed at an inclined position with respect to inflow water and a damper main body for filtering contaminants such as inflow water through a first screen and a second screen the rolling chains being configured to be continuously rotated by a driving force of a first driving poly that is belt coupled with a driving motor along a plurality of sprocket wheels formed opposite to both sides of the main body of the vibration damper a first driven poly configured on the other side of a rotational axis associated with said first driven poly a large lifting rake pin coupled with the rolling chain so as to lift large contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain not shown so as to prevent the pins from being separated from one side and the other of the outer surface of the pin a transverse coupling plate formed between the rolling chain and one side of the large lifting rake coupled with the pin a plurality of large lifting rakes formed between the transverse coupling plates a third screen having a plurality of water discharging holes for filtering small sized contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain wherein the upper end of the third screen is coupled to the plate member to form a curved surface up to the upper end of the upper sprocket wheel a first upper and lower guide rails which are combined with the large lifting rake and act to assist the rectilinear motion of the rolling chain while preventing the pin which is simultaneously engaged with the rolling chain from being sagged by the weight of the obstacle lower guide rails third and lower guide rails and fourth and lower guide rails are disposed between one side of the pin and the other side by the four upper and lower guide rails structure a hitting rake for hitting and removing the impurities contained in the large lifting rake wherein the driving rake is joined to one side and the other side of the driving rake case by a white bond a structure coupled to a second driven poly on one side of the white paper the second driven pulley which rotates the pulley in the reverse direction a first driven pulley axially coupled to the driving motor and a rotary belt coupled to the driving pulley wherein the pulley is rotated counterclockwise to remove contaminants trapped between the large lifting rakes a discharge conveyor installed at a rear side of the main body of the damper to receive the dirt falling and discharge it to the outside an air pump operative to float light contaminants having a specific gravity introduced into the inside of the purifier box the air discharge pipe coupled to the air pump is installed in the inside of the purifier box to float the organic matter material molecules of light specific gravity contained in the rainwater or river water flowing into the purifier box to the upper end of the purifier box a conveyor belt to which a binding plate and a lifting barrel for pouring and removing lightweight contaminants introduced into the inside of the purifier box are coupled a structure in which the coupling plate and the lifting bristle are combined with a white paper a structure in which a plurality of holes are formed in the lower end of the lifting bar a structure in which a nonwoven fabric is installed on the bottom of the lifting jacket and then the nonwoven fabric is fixed to the lifting jacket using an engaging member having a plurality of water discharging holes formed at an upper end of the non woven fabric the conveyor belt is coupled with a plurality of roller motors not shown to rotate the conveyor belt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a structure that is coupled to a conveyance belt for conveying contaminants to the outside on the rear side of the lifting bar the underwater pump connected to the conveyor belt constitutes a submerged pump at the lower end of the purifier box to remove the particulate contaminants remaining in the inside of the lifting jacket when lifting the particulate contaminants floating on the upper end of the booster box a pipeline coupled with the submersible pump an underwater pump for completely removing fine contaminants introduced into the purifier box by using a water injection nozzle formed at an end of a pipe connected to the pipeline and a discharge control valve coupled to a discharge control valve for controlling discharge of light organic matter molecules floating at the upper end of the purifier box at a downstream portion of the purifier box the process of cleansing polluted river water or contaminated rainwater using a river water or rain water purification system configured to purify polluted river water and contaminated rainwater by separate discharge is characterized in that the multifunctional water gate configured to store the river water to store river water or rainwater and to open the inflow adjusting gate constructed in the purifying box to inflow river water or rainwater into the inside of the purifying box and the air discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102694540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 having an upper inlet 11 and a sewage inlet 12 for introducing rain or sewage into the above ground and an outlet 13 for discharging the introduced rain or sewage a grating 20 formed through a penetration to remove foreign substances such as fallen leaves contained in rain or sewage by being placed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 an odor blocking means 30 comprising a first inclined plate 31 and a second inclined plate 32 formed at the upper and lower portions corresponding to each other while being inclined so that rain or sewage flowing into the interior of the main body 10 can be discharged downward while rain or sewage flowing in from the upper inlet 11 can be discharged downward and a rotating plate 34 formed at each end of the first inclined plate 31 and the second inclined plate 32 can be rotated through a hinge 33 at the upper portion to block odors rising along with opening due to the load of rain or sewage the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 are provided with a catch net a to prevent pests such as cockroaches and rats from entering the inside while being installed on the sewage inlet 12 and the discharge pipe 13 of the above body 10 and respectively inserted to induce or discharge rain or sewage a fixing member 43 inserted on the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 to prevent detachment a packing 44 to prevent the outflow of rain or sewage and fixing means 45a 45b 45c to fix the inlet pipe 41 the discharge pipe 42 and the catch net 43 to each other and the fixing means 45a 45b 45c are provided with a plurality of catch protrusions 46 protruding in the opposite direction from the outer surface of the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 and a plurality of catch protrusions 46 protruding in the opposite direction from the direction of inflow into the inside of the sewage inlet 12 and the discharge pipe 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "there was a problem of not being able to.the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above the object of the present invention is to ensure the maximum amount of water through the rain unit to the discharge pipe side through the drainage unit seated in the cover to ensure the maximum amount of water it is to provide a facility for preventing the smell and backflow of road rainwater receivers that can reliably block the outflow of odor due to wastewater and also effectively cope with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}]</data>
