fter washing the filter materials to the outside of the treatment structure further comprising the backwashing supply unit a first pump installed at the bottom of the backwashing tank and a backwash water supply pipe connected to the discharge portion side of the first pump but the backwash water supply pipe extends to the upper side of the filtration tank while branching into a plurality so as not to interfere with the lifting operation unit of the filtering means and to the upper side of the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-6334953-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the flaps enable excess water from the runoff water flow to drain from the filter bag as the filter bag becomes filled with silt and other debris to prevent a back up or blockage of runoff water within the discharge pipe of the storm water discharge system"}]</data>
