  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869158-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a preprocessing unit a screen unit which rotates the rainwater supplied from the pretreatment unit in a streamline to precipitate the precipitated nonpoint pollutants an oil water separator for supplying rainwater having precipitated nonpoint pollutants precipitated to the precipitation unit while floating and separating the floating nonpoint pollutants of oil in the screen unit precipitating unit for reducing the precipitated non point pollutant by sedimenting to the own weight of the precipitated non point pollutant contained in the rainwater supplied from the oil and water separation unit a solid liquid separation unit configured to separate sedimentary non point pollutants contained in the rainwater by sedimentation with their own weight while the rainwater passing through the precipitation unit moves left and right along a plurality of separator guide holes a rainwater supply unit for supplying rainwater in which the precipitated non point pollutant is precipitated in the solid liquid separator to the lower part of the filtration unit a filtering unit for filtering the floating nonpoint pollutant contained in the rainwater in the filtering member while the rainwater supplied from the rainwater supply unit moves from the lower portion to the upper portion initial rainwater non point contaminant purification apparatus comprising an outflow guide for outflowing the rainwater finally filtered by the filtering unit to the rainwater discharge pipe of the pretreatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "an inflow water distribution step of evenly distributing the energy of the stream water the lake water or the outflow water flowing into the integrated water purification device through the flow distribution tank to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step in which the inflow water which has passed the precipitation step is biologically purified while being introduced and passed through the contact oxidation tank in which the microbial contact material is installed a fourth purification step of finally removing fine sludge and suspended solids not filtered in the contact oxidation tank through the filtering tank a flow rate adjusting step of adjusting a flow rate discharged into the water channel through the discharge pipe through the discharge control tank it is configured to include"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426852-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "this causes suction of the blocking plate 5 of the inlet 6 thereby opening the blocking plate 5 by suction force that cancels the load of the blocking plate 5 and sucking the symbolic water through the discharge pipe 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100496348-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "in the flocculation tank 4 and the precipitation tank 5 the sludge may be aggregated and precipitated using a flocculant but in the present invention it is possible to treat the wastewater without using chemicals and electrolysis in the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101094321-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "s100 screen precipitation process 