 "link", "suppress", "view", "elapse", "warm", "expose", "combine", "apply", "drill", "live", "confirm", "weld", "contaminate", "interfere", "rise", "grout", "reach", "trigger", "aerate", "engage", "extract", "schematize", "display", "extinguish", "level", "sld", "achieve", "dump", "increase", "refer", "agglomerate", "soften", "maximize", "rail", "peg", "leach", "retain", "disclose", "circulate", "notify", "will", "restore", "refiltere", "provide", "wrap", "contain", "space", "mention", "uncoil", "ship", "amplify", "compare", "withdraw", "scale", "load", "water", "arrange", "leak", "size", "calculate", "process", "fight", "limit", "regard", "repair", "figure", "release", "oil", "do", "bring", "settle", "create", "facilitate", "lock", "understand", "deleteaccorde", "align", "motorize", "exceed", "consider", "baffle", "slide", "judge", "sound", "run", "focus", "weave", "insert", "direct", "spawn", "seat", "overload", "box", "cover", "show", "rake", "bifurcate", "configure", "match", "overheat", "cool", "derive", "start", "fit", "grate", "enable", "supplement", "guide", "perform", "act", "consist", "thereto", "occlude", "open", "house", "mean", "supply", "use", "predetermine", "propeller", "scour", "cut", "estimate", "swirl", "ascend", "recess", "draw", "conserve", "stagnate", "extend", "control", "transmit", "case", "bite", "monitor", "elevate", "exist", "scrape", "groove", "collect", "instal", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102715270-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "accordingly the protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the description of the claims and the scope of equivalents thereof.1 spawning area 2 water supply area 3 egg transfer unit 10 storage tank 20 drinking water pipe 30 drinking water pump 40 washing nozzle 50 washing pipe 60 washing pump 70 chlorine dioxide gas generating unit 80 gas pipe 90 water pipe a0 water supply valve b0 concentration measurement unit c0 water level measurement unit d0 contamination measurement unit d1 projector d2 camera e0 intensive cleaning section e1 guide rail e2 concentrated cleaning nozzle e3 concentrated cleaning pipe e4 concentrated washing pump e5 drive unit 110 1st tank 120 2nd tank 130 3rd tank 210 1st reaction tank 220 second reaction tank 230 third reaction tank 310 1st gas discharge pipe 320 2nd gas discharge pipe 330 3rd gas discharge pipe 400 integrated pipe 710 1st metering pump 720 2nd metering pump 730 3rd quantitative pump 1110 1st auxiliary tank 1120 second auxiliary tank 1130 third auxiliary tank 1200 level sensor 1300 alarm 1400 reservoir tank 1500 aeration device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161641-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "another object of the present invention is a water level sensor failure detection method of the cold and hot water purifier that can prevent the occurrence of freezing of the cold water tank caused by the failure of the water level sensor of the cold and hot water purifier a failure due to the overheat of the heater or excessive waste of purified water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200160111-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "if the inflow of the wastewater increases accidentally or the wastewater level such as the channel increases by more than a certain level because the gap of the screen material 16 is blocked by a contaminant due to the failure of the wastewater treatment screen 10 the water level sensor the controller immediately detects this and transmits the control means and the over water signal and the control means receiving the over water signal operates the floodgate driving means 21 to drive the emergency water gate 18 upward to open the frame 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "thus it is composed of one set including a control panel that moves the sewage in the sewage tank along the sewage discharge path and discharges it through the sewage discharge pipe one set of sewage treatment equipment is installed one or more depending on the installation area the air supply path includes an air supply pipe installed between the air storage tank and the first end of the three way valve and an air inlet pipe installed between the second end of the three way valve and the sewage tank the control panel operates the compressor to supply the air in the air storage tank to the sewage tank through the air supply pipe the first and second ends of the three way valve and the air inlet pipe a regulator set is installed in the air supply pipe the regulator set includes a regulator for discharging air from the air storage tank to a preset pressure it further comprises at least one of a filter for removing moisture and impurities contained in the air from the air storage tank and an oil removal unit for removing oil contained in the air from the air storage tank the sewage auxiliary tank is installed in the sewage inflow path to remove the bubbles inside the sewage auxiliary tank to prevent the operation of the sewage treatment device due to the inflow of bubbles into the sewage tank when the control panel receives a notification of reaching the lowest water level from the water level sensor it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete it is counted after the operation of discharging the sewage from the sewage tank is performed and when a preset time elapses it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete when the discharge of sewage in the sewage tank is completed the knife valve installed on the sewage inflow path is controlled to be in an open state to open the sewage inflow path so that the sewage is moved to the sewage tank through the sewage inflow path and the three way valve of the air inlet and outlet installed on the air supply path is controlled so that the second end of the three way valve on the sewage tank side and the third end of the air discharge pipe are in an open state and the first end of the air storage tank side control to be closed to move the air in the sewage tank along the air discharge path and discharge it through the air discharge pipe after receiving the notification of reaching the highest water level and performing the operation of discharging wastewater when the notification of reaching the lowest water level is not notified from the water level sensor even after a predetermined time has elapsed after receiving the notification of the notification of reaching the highest water level a warning message to a preset terminal sewage treatment device characterized in that for transmitting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837300-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel portion for guiding water to move in a predetermined direction an infiltration inducing pipe portion penetrating through the bottom surface of the water channel portion and communicating with an underground aquifer below the impermeable layer in the ground layer a filtering unit installed at a connection portion between the infiltration induction pipe and the water channel unit and composed of several layers for removing foreign matter from water flowing into the underground aquifer and having a lower porosity toward the lower layer and and an opening closing part for selectively shielding the infiltration induction tube part the water a sediment guiding part having a guide protruding from the bottom surface of the water channel part and a settling groove formed between the guide and the guide an induction intrusion section having an inclined surface inclined upward in the moving direction of the water on the bottom surface of the water channel part and an inlet port formed on the opposite vertical surface and and a water film portion for controlling the amount and movement of water moving along the water channel portion the infiltration induction pipe portion may include an induction pipe connected to the induction pier at the upper end and connected to the underground aquifer below a flow rate measuring unit installed at an upper side of the guide pipe to measure an amount of water moving along the guide pipe and a water level control valve provided below the flow rate measuring unit and passing through the induction pipe the water level control valve includes a cylindrical body through which upper and lower parts pass a first inlet connected to an upper portion of the induction pipe a second inlet connected to a lower portion of the induction pipe and a buoyant body selectively shielding the first inlet and the second inlet while moving up and down along the body the opening a high level sensor installed at a relatively high position in the infiltration induction pipe a low water level sensor installed at a relatively low position in the permeation guide pipe a door unit provided at a relatively higher position than the high level sensing sensor to selectively shield the induction pipe and a control unit for receiving the signal of the high level sensing sensor and the low level sensing sensor and the signal of the flow rate measurement unit and controlling the door unit when the signal of the high level sensing sensor is received the control part shields the door part so as to prevent the water in the waterway part from flowing into the underground aquifer"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "simultaneously therewith the battery operated audible alarm which is electrically connected to a water sensor on the conduit senses the rising water and makes a circuit thus causing the alarm to sound to notify the building occupant"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "float 11 lifts due to a rising water level in sump pit 50 thus causing float arm 14 to disengage rollers 16 16 as it rotates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water level indicating device 40 capable of confirming the water level a connector connected to an end of the ultraviolet lamp 32 so that the ultraviolet lamp 32 the quartz tube 32 that transmits the ultraviolet light of the ultraviolet lamp 32 and at the same time may be replaced with water and the ultraviolet lamp can be easily exchanged an ultraviolet sterilizer 30 composed of 52 a hemispherical housing in which a display portion 11 in which a low water quantity appears by operation of the water level indicating device 30 is located and display windows 12a and l2b are installed to easily identify the operation of the ultraviolet lamp 32 on the side of the display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a water level indicating device 40 which is composed of a water level indicating member 44 having a built in level a connector connected to an end of the ultraviolet lamp 32 so that the ultraviolet lamp 32 the quartz tube 32 that transmits the ultraviolet light of the ultraviolet lamp 32 and at the same time may be replaced with water and the ultraviolet lamp can be easily exchanged an ultraviolet sterilizer 30 composed of 52 a hemispherical housing in which a display portion 11 showing a low amount of water is operated by the operation of the water level indicating device 30 and the display windows 12a and l2b are installed to easily identify the operation of the ultraviolet lamp 32 on the side of the display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0167322-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "therefore the cold air supplied to the upper side moves along the surface of the cold water storage tank 12 and since more cold air is supplied to the interface of the water level b than the normal state the surface of the purified water freezes and the freezing grows gradually over time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method according to claim 1 or 2 the purified water tank unit 1000 is a water purification tank unit 1100 for storing purified water flowing in from the outside an outflow filter unit 1200 for filtering foreign substances included while discharging the purified water stored in the water purification tank unit 1100 a temporary storage unit 1300 for storing the purified water discharged from the outflow filter unit 1200 a water level sensor unit 1400 installed on one side of the temporary storage unit 1300 to detect the water level of the stored purified water a purified water metering pump 1500 for discharging the purified water stored in the temporary storage unit 1300 in a fixed amount from one side according to a corresponding control signal total hydrocarbon reduction system in the advanced oxidation process of environmental pollution around livestock facilities including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "at this time it is preferable to further attach a water level sensor to the upper inner surface of the guide water pipe body 20 so that when rainwater flows in and moves to the height of the water level sensor a detection signal is transmitted to the lifting lowering guide cylinder 62 to operate it thereby lowering the water level and preventing rainwater from stagnating"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "the salt monitoring system of claim 13 wherein said sensor is configured for generating a signal at a regular interval and said controller is configured so that upon said received signal depicting one of a slower than average decline of salt level indicating low brine dosage an increased salt or water level and an increased rate of salt usage reflecting high brine dosage a leak to the brine tank or overfilling of the brine tank an alarm signal is generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "11 the sensor 40 is configured for generating a signal in the form of the sensor beam 42 at a regular interval and the controller 62 is also preferably configured so that upon multiple signals being received by the receiver 44 over a plurality of regenerations that indicate a first phase 84 of regular salt consumption followed by a second phase 86 of increase signal level or water level indicating a leak to the brine tank 12 an alarm signal is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "to this end a separate water level sensor not shown in the drawing may be provided inside the storage block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as a result the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "for example when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120 even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank and also if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102780153-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the remote monitoring system of the filter assembly for installation in a water pipe according to the present invention comprises a water storage tank in which water is stored inside a water pipe is provided