lizing material is repeatedly electrolyzed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "at this time the primary electrolysis panel unit 100 is provided with a level sensor 111 for measuring the water level of the brine tank 110a while opening and closing the solenoid valve 112 in accordance with the set water level to replenish the time a first water level detecting unit 110 a salt water supply unit 120 configured to pump the brine in the brine tank 110a through a brine injection pump 120a to supply the primary electrolysis cell 130a a first power supply unit 130 for applying electricity to the positive and negative plates of the primary electrolysis cell 130a to electrolyze the brine supplied from the brine supply unit 120 as the brine electrolyzed by the first power supply unit 130 is converted into sterilized material and stored a level sensor 141 is installed to measure the level of the stored sterilized material and the salt water supply unit 120 is set according to the set level value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the water supply control device of claim 1 wherein further comprising a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value wireless automatic water level control system further comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100466336-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thereby increasing the amount of distilled water condensed water filled in the evaporator brine heater 1 thereby raising the water level"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604858-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": 