l duration frequency value for each period in which the water level value h is maintained at a certain percentage for a certain time period the local management control unit 60 is a computer and monitoring device installed inside or near a building so that a building manager can grasp water level information including water level values and collection schedule information and high middle low positions for each pipe section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 0850307 registration date july 29 2008 sewer pipe maintenance monitoring system remotely monitors the inside of the sewer pipe by image and monitors the sewage flow rate data measured by the flow meter sensor in conjunction with the image it relates to a sewage pipe maintenance monitoring system capable of remotely monitoring and managing sewage pipes based on accurate information by supplementing errors in flow data and a flowmeter sensor installed in a sewer pipe to measure the flow rate and water level of sewage an underwater camera installed inside the manhole to take an image of the inside of the sewer pipe an on site control panel that receives the flow rate and water level of the flow meter sensor and the captured image of the underwater camera calculates the flow rate and processes the captured image according to the transmission format sewage related data and image data are collected from the field control panel through a communication network and flow velocity water level and flow data fluctuations are analyzed to determine whether ingress water inflow water leakage occurs and image data is output to the screen to analyze data and video data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the local management control unit 60 is a computer and monitoring device installed inside or near a building so that a building manager can grasp water level information including water level values and collection schedule information and high middle low positions for each