uest alarm according to the set time and an alarm generation module configured to generate a hydrogen water generation request alarm when hydrogen water is not generated for a predetermined period in the iot tumbler for generating hydrogen water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stirring device unit 800 having a blade 820 forcibly dispersing and stirring together with the sewage a water level sensor 900 for detecting that the water level of the sewage introduced into the manhole 100 rises above a predetermined height a pump 1000 for forcibly inhaling and discharging the mixture of the sewage and sludge s stirred by the stirring device 800 the first valve 500 and the second valve 600 are opened or closed at the same time respectively and received the displacement measured from the sludge detection unit 700 to determine whether there is deposition and flows into the interior by the water level sensor 900"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the first and second valves are opened or closed at the same time respectively and receiving the displacement measured from the sludge detection unit to determine whether there is a deposit and detecting that the water level of the sewage introduced into the inside by the water level sensor rises above a certain height"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention the manhole 100 embedded in the ground e the inlet pipe 200 communicated to one side of the outer peripheral surface of the manhole 100 and the outflow pipe 300 communicated to the other side of the outer peripheral surface of the manhole 200 and a manhole cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the manhole 100 to block odors and backflows from being discharged to the outside a first valve 500 mounted on the distal outer circumferential surface of the inflow pipe 200 to adjust an inflow amount of sewage flowing into the manhole 100 a second valve 600 mounted on an outer c