 stored at a certain level and sprayed through brine nozzles individually installed at a number of habitual freezing points a b c d a detection sensor 20 that detects the water level of brine stored in the brine tank 10 of each of the above points a central control unit 30 that manages information on the brine storage level through the above detection sensor 20 in order to transport brine stored in a brine tank 10 at a point where the amount of brine is relatively large to a point where the amount of brine is insufficient by the control of the central control unit 30 a brine guide pipe 40 through which brine stored in the brine tank 10 is withdrawn by the operation of a pump p a coupler 50 that is connected to the end of the brine guide pipe 40 and is connected to the transfer tank 110 of the brine transfer vehicle 100 a salt water supply system for road deicing spraying characterized in that the salt water transport tank 110 configured in the salt water transport vehicle 100 is provided with a plurality of bubble generators 111 on the bottom surface to prevent freezing or precipitation of salt water during the transport process an ultraviolet lamp 112 is provided on the top surface and a deterioration prevention layer 113 is formed on the inner wall surface to prevent deterioration of salt water during transport"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "that is when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320 the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "10 water treatment device 100 agitator 110 rapid stirring 120 slow stirring 121 coagulation tank 122 first coagulation tank 123 second flocculation tank 124 partition wall 124a euro 125 stirrer 126 drive motor 127 stirring shaft 128 horizontal paddle 129 vertical paddle 200 flotation tank 210 discharge part 220 scum discharge unit 300 bubble generation unit 310 pressurized water supply unit 312 pump 314 pressure tank 316 compressor 320 fine bubble injection unit 322 branch piping 323 pressurized water inlet valve 324 injection pipe 326 decompression tube 330 backwash 332 backwash valve 334 water level sensor 336 control unit 400 guide unit 410 injured guide slope 420 dead zone prevention slope 500 floating scum removing unit 510 blade 600 sediment sludge removal unit 610 chain 620 scraper 700 outflow collecting part 710 porous pipe 720 block type sump 800 advanced oxidation processing unit 810 oxidizing gas supply unit 812 am generator 814 ozone storage tank 816 ozone pressurizer 820 uv contact unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition when it is determined that the communication state is good the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe measured by the temperature sensor and if the pump abnormality can be determined preferably a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the sensing unit may be a water level sensor for detecting the amount of sewage an electrical conductivity or a suspended solids ss measuring sensor for detecting the degree of contamination but is not limited thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101357244-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the door panel 330 for selectively opening closing the waterway 101 the drive unit 340 for rotating the door panel 330 and the drive unit 340 respectively are provided at the 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_253", "text": "to this end the sensor block 402 as shown in figure 5 for example dissolved oxygen sensor 501 water temperature sensor 502 chlorophyll a sensor 503 water temperature weak layer sensor 504 orp oxidation reduction potential ec sensor 505 electric conductivity ec sensor 506 toc sensor 507 ss sensor 508 na sensor 509 cod sensor 510 tp sensor 511 tn sensor 512 flow sensor 513 ph sensor 514 turbidity sensor 515 light intensity sensor 516 alkalinity sensor 517 nh 4 n sensor 518 po 4 the p sensor 519 the cl sensor 520 the fe 2 sensor 521 the air temperature sensor 522 the residence time sensor 523 the water level sensor 524 and the like may be included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_287", "text": "that is the measurement position of the dissolved oxygen sensor 501 may vary in position according to the water level measurement information provided from the water level sensor 524"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102617623-B1", "para_id": "para_116", "text": "the above mentioned terms included or consisted of should be interpreted to mean that the corresponding component may be included and that other components may be additionally included.10 housing member 20 ejector member 30 air outflow part 40 flow path forming member 50 water dispersion member 60 discharge member 70 crushing member 80 water guiding member 90 filter member 100 radon purification device 110 post processing member 120 radon detection member 150 deep pump 160 chlorine input device 200 water tank 220 water quality detection sensor 230 water level sensor 250 circulation pump 300 surveillance camera unit 500 control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-11014837-B2", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "furthermore the monitoring unit 360 may monitor a temperature degree of electrolysis and or water level of the sea or river which is measured using an sbe37im sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to the smart type water tank having the earthquake proof function according to the present invention the water tank is managed through the pollution level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 and the water leakage sensor 33 thereby enabling clean and safe water quality management control and monitoring of the opening closing state of the valve 40 and the water drainage amount by monitoring the sudden change of the water level and the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the level sensor 31 may be of an electroconductive type that utilizes the flow of current when it comes into contact with water or a capacitive type that utilizes a change in electrostatic capacity according to a water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the control unit 50 determines the state of the raw water by comparing the measured values of the sensors sensed above with predetermined reference values controls the valve 40 according to the determination result and transmits the state of the raw water to the manager it is a means to provide a process for that is the controller 50 is electrically connected to the pollution level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 the vibration sensor 32 and the water leakage sensor 33 to receive measured values from the sensors the water level of the raw water in the water tank the leakage of the raw water from the water tank and the vibration transmitted to the tank main body 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "on the other hand the smart type water tank having the earthquake proofing function of the present invention is provided with a control unit 50 hereinafter referred to as quot water level sensor quot based on the measured values received from the contamination level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 the vibration sensor 32 the control unit 50 compares the measured value received from each of the sensors with a predetermined reference value and determines whether the measured value is equal to or greater than a predetermined value when it is determined that an abnormal situation has occurred in the tank the alarm output unit 60 may be controlled to generate an alarm sound or to turn on off the warning lamp so that the administrator can recognize the situation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank 1 having a contaminant collecting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the cleaning means 140 may be formed on the bottom of the floating filter media 130 and a plurality of injection nozzles 144 formed on the washing inflow line 141 and the washing inflow line 141 into which the air or the washing water is introduced and the floating filter material is occluded through the water level sensor 160 rising water level due to leakage is not smooth and the automatic backwashing is carried out by automatically activating the washing means"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the pretreatment tank 1 may further include a dirt collecting tank 13 and a ditch water tank 14 therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622378-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "depending on the size the size of the carriers collected in the collection unit 600 are different the cover 400 is an upper cover 401 covering the upper part of the belt 310 and it includes a lower cover 402 that covers a portion of the lower belt 320 other than the belt receiving portion 325 and the belt receiving portion 325 is exposed to the outside air the upper cover 401 is a drip hood 410 located at the rear end of the drip unit 200 and it is located on the upper side of the belt upper part 310 at the rear end of the drip hood 410 and includes a plurality of upper hoods 420 whose starting portion is inclined in the moving direction of the conveyor belt 300 the lower cover 402 is a rinsing hood 430 located at the beginning of the lower cover 402 in the moving direction of the conveyor belt 300 and it includes a return hood 440 located at the end of the lower cover 402 the raw materials include freeze dried microorganisms pva polyvinyl alcohol and peg polyethylene glycol and the carrier is a microbial carrier for wastewater treatment the heat storage unit 800 receives heat from the heating unit 130 and the heat exchanger 650 and provides it to the heating blower 500 so that the heating blower 500 generates heated air and the inside of the cover 400 is maintained at 115 to 120 c if the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 is higher than the preset water level or the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is lower than the preset drop height the plurality of drop holes 211 warns of blockage in any one or more of the following the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 exceeds the preset drop height or the shape of the bottom surface of the drop detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is different from the preset shape or if the height of the collected carrier detected by the carrier sensor s3 is outside the preset collection height range warning of a defect in the carrier carrier manufacturing device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622378-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition a supply water level sensor s1 located in the supply unit 100 to detect the water level of the raw material a drop shape sensor s2 that detects the height of the drop dropped on the conveyor belt 300 and detects the shape of the bottom surface of the drop and a carrier sensor s3 located in the collection unit 600 to detect the height of the collected carrier and the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 is higher than a preset water level or if the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is below the preset drop height a blockage phenomenon is warned in any one or more of the plurality of drop holes 211 and the drop shape sensor s2 detects the drop height"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102622378-B1", "para_id": "para_111", "text": "if the water level detected by the supply water level sensor s1 is higher than the preset water level or the drop height detected by the drop shape sensor s2 is lower than the preset drop height the drop used is less than the normal amount"}, {"pat_id": "US-8069676-B2", "para_id": "para_518", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of hardware configurations of a sensor device 210 and a monitoring device 200 fig.2 is a diagram showing an example of a functional block configuration of a water leakage detection system 20 according to an embodiment fig.it is a figure which shows the concept of a static water pressure a dynamic water pressure a static water level and a dynamic water level.it is a figure which shows an example of the dynamic water level before and after water leakage occurrence and its normal vector.it is a figure which shows an example of the variation change_quantity of the normal vector before and behind water leakage occurrence.it is a figure which shows an example of the block of the piping network used for simulation.8 is a diagram showing an example of the amount of change in the normal vector on the dynamic water level distribution when water leakage occurs in the pipe network 800"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "for example the monitoring device 200 uses the measurement data of the sensor devices 210 distributed in the a block to calculate the dynamic water level at each location in the a block"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "in one aspect the water leakage detection system 20 uses the measurement data obtained from the sensor device 210 installed at each branch point on the pipe network or part of the pipe to calculate the dynamic water level at each monitoring location a dynamic water level distribution can be created from the calculated dynamic water level"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "in step s1520 the water leakage detection system 20 calculates the time series dynamic water level at each monitoring location installation location of each sensor device 210"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_130", "text": "20 water leakage detection system 50 distribution reservoir 100a 100b 510 800 piping network 101a 101b sensor 110a 110b estimated water leakage area 120 piping 200 monitoring device 210 sensor device 220 communication unit 230 303 pressure sensor 240 access point 250 internet 301 control unit 302 317 communication if 305 318 internal bus 311 processor 312 memory 313 storage 314 external device if 315 input if 316 output if 401 data acquisition unit 402 dynamic water level calculator 403 difference calculator 404 visualization unit 405 abnormality determinati