ized by controlling the opening and closing of the water supply valve and the emergency valve.according to the present invention it is possible to automatically detect whether an event has occurred in the water tank and when an event occurs it has the effect of blocking the supply of water from the water tank to the customer.1 to 2 are diagrams showing the configuration of a water supply management system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599590-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the control unit 400 may control the opening and closing of the pump 120 the water supply valve 211 and the emergency valve 221 by receiving the signal output from the detection unit 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected s