r lowers the rectifier plate a sensor that detects the inflow of wastewater through the inlet and a batch type wastewater treatment system characterized by including a control unit that controls the rectifier lifting unit according to the signal of the sensor thereby raising the rectifier in conjunction with the rise in the water level of the reaction tank when wastewater flows in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "1 to 3 a batch type wastewater treatment system 1 according to one embodiment of the present invention comprises a reaction tank 10 having an inlet for introducing wastewater on one side a treated water discharge outlet on the other side and a sludge discharge outlet on the bottom side an agitator 20 installed to agitate the wastewater in the reaction tank 10 a rectifier 30 formed by a plurality of inclined plates opening in an inclined manner up and down to form a flow path and arranged to be able to rise and fall within the reaction tank 10 a rectifier plate lifting unit 40 including a float 42 connected to the rectifier plate 30 and raising or lowering the rectifier plate 30 by an increase or decrease in buoyancy of the float 42 a sensor 50 for detecting the inflow of wastewater into the reaction tank 10 through the inlet and or the amount of wastewater inflow a timer 60 and a timer 50 for detecting the sensor 50 and the according to the signal of the timer 60 the control unit 90 controls the rectifier lifting unit 40 to raise the rectifier 30 according to the rise in the water level of the reaction tank 10 when wastewater flows into the reaction tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the batch type wastewater treatment system 1 according to the present embodiment is configured such that a sensor 1 capable of measuring the inflow and inflow rate of wastewater is installed in a wastewater inflow line l1 connected to a wastewater inlet of a reaction tank 10 and a rectifier plate lifting unit 4