the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171325-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "it is characterized in that it is further provided with a level sensor for detecting the level difference and a control unit for controlling the rpm of the drive motor by the output signal according to the level sensor of the level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171325-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "on the other hand the present invention detects the water level difference between the water inlet ip and the water outlet op into which the sewage and waste water flows and when the water level is higher than the set water level the rapid lifting and removing process according to the rpm control of the drive motor 1 is automatically controlled"}, {"pat_id": "US-7640792-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "when the water level reaches the nominal level the float 185 on the float sensor 184 moves up sufficiently to trigger the float sensor 184 causing the pit supply valve 162 to close and generally also stopping the agitator motor 48 auger motor 70 and vibrator 58 optionally after a preset time delay"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the inflow chamber may further include a water level sensor installed penetrating inward from an upper surface of the inflow chamber so as to sense the water level inside the inflow chamber to control the operation of the contaminant treatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in other words the water level detector 12 is to operate the contaminant processing unit 40 only when the waste water reaches a constant level in the inflow chamber 10 to prevent unnecessary waste of power"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102713396-B1", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "fourth by forming the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit evaporator 2 1 2 and the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit concentrated water circulating water ejector 7 1 2 and controlling the residence time of the concentrated water flowing out of the concentrated water tank 15 1 supercooling and the formation of fine ice seed water in the salt separation tank 5 1 were promoted thereby reinforcing the formation and growth of the brine water containing organic and inorganic substances contained in the influent into an ice slurry"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3276575-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "since the flow rate and pressure of the sample water sent when the valve 5 is opened become constant and the sample water stored in the sample water tank 6 is sent by gravity the pressure of the sample water at the hardness sensor 4 is maintained at a low value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7709393-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in the present invention the water level gauge 300 is preferably a non contact type and more preferably an ultrasonic type from the viewpoint of the risk of false detection due to contamination of the sensor unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100836904-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it consists of a drive 22 for driving the unit 23 the display unit 23 is a filter loss amount display unit 24 for displaying the loss of each filter 5 stored by the wired terminal 70 connected from the outside in percentage and when the filter 5 is replaced filter replacement display section 25 in which the lamp is selectively flashed when the lamp is reached the water level level display section 26 in which the lamp is selectively lit according to the water level level of the water tank 6 and the driving of the pump 3 and it consists of a drive display unit 27 the lamp is turned on when the water leakage and a water temperature display unit 28 for displaying cold and hot water the output terminal of the mpu 21 is installed on one side of the facet 8a is connected to the facet lamp 9 for providing a refreshing feeling when the water is discharged the water level sensor 30 is installed in the water tank 6 at the input end of the mpu 21 and senses the water level in four stages and the water leakage sensor is installed on the bottom surface of the case 1 to detect water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "another object of the present invention is to adjust the ph concentration by using a water level sensor rather than a ph sensor it is possible to minimize the failure rate due to the failure and replacement of the ph sensor even in a building without drainage drainage by air pressure using the compressor to provide a shampoo device using the electrolysis method possible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a water pressure control encoder switch for adjusting the intensity of the water output the temperature of the water ph concentration the operation button to receive the output time the water level sensor for measuring the water level an input unit configured of a temperature sensor measuring a temperature of water a pump for raising the water to the shampoo ware a heater for heating the water to a temperature set by the operation button an electrolysis tank for ionizing the water and performing electrolysis to match the ph concentration input to the operation button ac power is supplied to the shampoo ware the auxiliary tank equipped with a heater an electrolysis tank a drain box for collecting sewage a solenoid opened and closed to control the flow of water between a water supply tank into which water is input and the solenoid a pump a compressor and a heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101127289-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "when the water level control valve 140 is open the water in the reservoir 150 is moved to the sterilization tank 160 to increase the level of the sterilization tank 160 and the water level is increased to detect the water level sensor 170"}]</data>
</edge>
