  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_189", "text": "accordingly whether the impedance response of interest is due to the liquid property of the circulating liquid and the electrode surface coating or due to the change in temperature is required to be known which would otherwise provide a concern of malfunction of the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-8658095-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a device for measuring oxidation reduction potential orp and a temperature in a hot water system the device comprising a a flow through cell having a plurality of ports comprising a first port and a second port b a controller c an integrated sensor component associated with the first port comprising an orp probe and a temperature detector said integrated sensor component residing at least partially inside of the flow through cell the orp probe further comprising at least one electrical connection operable to relay information to said controller wherein the orp probe is operable to measure orp in the hot water system at operating temperature and pressure and the temperature detector further comprises a plurality of negative leads and a plurality of positive leads operable to relay information to said controller wherein the controller is operable to determine whether a real time orp is within an ideal orp range and further operable to cause addition of an effective amount of oxygen or an effective amount of one or more reductants to a feedwater of the hot water system if the real time orp is not within the ideal orp range and d an external pressure balanced reference electrode assembly associated with the second port comprising a tube containing an electrolyte solution having a first end residing at least partially inside of the flow through cell and a second end a porous frit disposed on said first end and a multi fitting housing comprising a seal attached to said second end the multi fitting housing having a silver silver chloride half cell reference electrode partially immersed in said electrolyte solution and having an electrical connection operable to relay information to said controller"}, {"pat_id": "US-8658095-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the tube functions to provide support for noble metal band 26c band and may include any corrosion resistant material such as stainless steel of any suitable composition aluminum other metals and plastics and combinations thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102518322-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the front sensor unit 300 and the rear sensor unit 500 may measure water quality information in real time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102518322-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the shear sensor unit 300 may measure water quality information in real time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102518322-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the rear sensor unit 500 may measure water quality information in real time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "6 in the same manner as the temperature sensor 110a it is possible to detect that leakage occurs when the humidity value becomes higher than the second detection signal of the neighboring sensing unit 100 because the humidity becomes higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "if only the temperature sensor 110a is applied if the temperature of the soil is lowered due to reasons other than leakage in order to compensate for this it is possible to compare the temperature and humidity sensing values together"}, {"pat_id": "US-12337259-B2", "para_id": "para_1210", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump bottom of the container 139 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365041-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "control the heating element 40 based on the information provided by 64 but the plug 61 receiving ac 220v power from the outside and after converting the supplied ac 220v power into dc 12v the valve 30 a converter 62 supplied to and an earth leakage breaker 63 integrally coupled with a plug to cut off power in the event of an earth leakage accident in the heating element 40 the temperature sensor 64 installed in the water supply pipe detects the temperature of the water supply pipe transmits the detected information to the controller box 60 and the controller box analyzes the detected information to determine the prediction of freezing and bursting including those operated by current supply when judged to be at risk of freezing as the water supply pipe 10 further surrounds the insulator 41 around the heating element 40 wound in a spiral shape a filter 70 made of a micron mesh network is installed in the setting area while preventing loss of warmth caused by the heating element"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100357289-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in the center of the crystal growth tank 2 is a central axis in which two blade propeller stirrers 2 1 are connected to the upper power source 7 and rotated to increase the mixing and heat transfer efficiency while the ice crystals grow to a sufficient size 7 1 fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102678075-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide plate 24 formed with 24a it includes a water circulation means a provided in the lower cultivation unit 19b to push the water inside the lower cultivation unit 19b forward the water circulation means a is a guide rod 51 provided inside the lower cultivation portion 19b to extend laterally a slide block 52 laterally slideably coupled to the guide rod 51 a plurality of blades 53 extending in the front and rear directions and rotatably coupled to the front of the slide block 52 laterally within a certain angle a floating aquatic weed production system comprising a reciprocating drive means 54 connected to the slide block 52 to cause the slide block 52 to reciprocate laterally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102678075-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a floating aquatic weed production system is provided comprising a plurality of blades 53 and a reciprocating drive means 54 connected to the slide block 52 to cause the slide block 52 to reciprocate laterally"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3878645-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "alternatively the temperature inside the wts unit 20 may be controlled using a separate temperature sensing circuit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101893417-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in one example the control device receives the incoming water quality value and the flow rate value from the first sensor derives the influent load receives the outflow water quality value from the second sensor receives the temperature value from the third sensor a data portion for data wise the water quality by temperature a driving unit for driving the valve to introduce the water into the pre treatment tank and the bioreactor the real time influent load value is derived from the real time influent water quality value and the real time flow value from the first sensor and the real time runoff water quality value is derived from the derived real time influent load and the real the real time recirculated water load value is obtained from the fourth sensor by receiving the real time recirculated water quality value and the real time flow rate value from the fourth sensor and the real real time flow rate value is received and a real time connection load is derived and when the real time reflux water load and real time connection water load exceeds the above mentioned additional connection water load and additional reflux water load the valve is driven to the pre so that the real time counter current load and the real time connection water load are set to the above characterized in that it comprises a load by driving the valve and can be linked or less wake analysis unit such that flowing into the bioreactor through the raw water inlet line.as described above according to the system of the present invention in the continuous treatment of the wastewater it is possible to automatically determine whether or not the pre treatment of the reflux water and the connection water is performed by the sensing basis thereby reducing the cost required for the pretreatment and improving the treatment efficiency of the pretreatment it is possible to improve the treatment efficiency of the whole system by preventing the load of the bioreactor.1 is a block diagram illustrating a system of the present invention 2 is a schematic view showing an example of a bioreactor which is a constitution of the present invention 3 is a block diagram showing a detailed configuration of a control apparatus which is a constitution of the present invention figures 4a and 4b are operational state diagrams of the system of the present invention 5 is a schematic view showing an example of a pretreatment tank which is a constituent of the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326272-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the apparatus may further include a concentration sensor for measuring the concentration of sodium hypochlorite generated in the electrolysis tank wherein the controller is installed in the dilution water supply pipe so that the concentration measured by the concentration sensor is maintained at 5 000 to 6 500 ppm"}, {"pat_id": "US-9857803-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "generally a user 300 may use a control device 400 to interact with the processing unit 50 of the system 100 thereby allowing the user 300 to control or receive information from one or more elements of the system 100 such as an ambient temperature sensor 17 a flow control valve 13 any other automated valves a flow meter 16 and or a pressure sensor 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101435107-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "therefore the function of controlling the supply of electricity to the thermoelectric device is performed by measuring the temperature of the present cold water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102818339-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a temperature detection sensor installed in a water pipe that detects the external temperature and sends a notification to the manager terminal when it falls below a preset temperature in a freeze prevention water pipe automatic opening closing device including an automatic opening closing module installed in the water pipe and equipped to open close the water pipe s opening closing valve by controlling it using the manager terminal based on a notification transmitted from the temperature detection sensor a power supply module provided to supply power to the above automatic opening closing module a foreign matter removal module arranged adjacent to the water pipe and equipped to vibrate while moving along the water pipe to separate foreign matters a control module provided to control the operations of the temperature detection sensor the automatic opening closing module the power supply module and the foreign substance removal module using the above administrator terminal including a step in which the above temperature detection sensor monitors the external temperature in real time a step for the temperature detection sensor to send a notification to the administrator terminal when the external temperature falls below a preset temperature a step in which the above administrator terminal transmits a control signal toward the above control module a step of controlling power to the power supply module by the control signal transmitted by the control module a step in which the power supply module supplies power to the automatic opening closing module and the foreign matter removal module a step for controlling the opening closing valve of the water pipe by using the automatic opening closing module according to the control signal transmitted by the control module a step in which the automatic opening closing module controls the opening closing valve to open close the water pipe a step of removing ice and foreign substances from the water pipe by using the foreign substance removal module according to a control signal transmitted by the control module an automatic water pipe opening closing device for preventing freezing comprising a feature for performing the above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102818339-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention for solving the above problem an automatic water pipe opening closing device for preventing freezing includes a temperature detection sensor 10 installed in a water pipe to detect an external temperature and transmit a notification to an administrator terminal when the temperature drops below a preset temperature an automatic opening closing module 30 installed in the water pipe to control an opening closing valve of the water pipe by using the administrator terminal in response to a notification transmitted from the temperature detection sensor 10 a power supply module 40 equipped to supply power to the automatic opening closing module 30 a foreign substance removal module 100 arranged adjacent to the water pipe to vibrate while moving along the water pipe to separate foreign substances a control module 20 equipped to control the operations of the temperature detection sensor 10 the automatic opening closing module 30 the power supply module 40 and the foreign substance removal module 100 by using the administrator terminal and a step for the temperature detection sensor 10 to monitor an external temperature in real time the method may include the steps of a step for the temperature detection sensor 10 to transmit a notification to the administrator terminal when the external temperature drops below a preset temperature a step for the administrator terminal to transmit a control signal toward the control module 20 a step for the control module 20 to control power to the power supply module 40 by the transmitted control signal a step for the power supply module 40 to supply power to the automatic opening closing module 30 and the foreign substance removal module 100 a step for the control module 20 to control the opening closing valve of the water pipe using the automatic opening closing module 30 by the transmitted control signal a step for the automatic opening closing module 30 to control the opening closing valve to open close the water pipe a step for the control module 20 to remove ice and foreign substances from the water pipe using the foreign substance removal module 100 by the transmitted control signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102818339-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the temperature detection sensor monitors the external temperature in real time and sends a notification to the manager terminal when it drops below a preset temperature allowing for a quick response"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102818339-B1", "para_id": "para_150", "text": "furthermore such modifications should not be individually understood from the technical idea or prospect of the present invention.temperature detection sensor 10 control module 20 automatic opening closing module 30 power supply module 40 foreign matter removal module 100 ball vibration body 110 vibration removal ball 120 body rotation gear 130 ball support home 131 module rotation axis 140 module moving gear 150 ball support home 151 module moving rail 160 ball vibrator 200 vibration body 210 vibration pressure tank 220 vibration pressure pipe 230 vibration spring 240 vibration ball 250 vibrat