filter unit 2500 it is fixed at the top in a sealed state and electrolyzes purified water according to the corresponding control signal so that oh groups and hydrogen peroxide are generated to generate radical water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 includes a purified water inlet 2100 for receiving purified water flowing in a fixed amount from the purified water tank unit 1000 a housing part 2200 connecting the purified water inlet 2100 to one side of the lower end and storing purified water flowing in from the purified water inlet 2100 in an external cavity 2210 a purified water heating unit 2300 that is fixedly installed in a coil shape in a portion of the external cavity 2210 in which the purified water is stored in the housing 2200 and heats the purified water according to a corresponding control signal a temperature sensor unit 2400 that is fixedly installed on the other side of the outer cavity of the housing unit 2200 and detects the temperature of purified water according to a corresponding control signal a water filter unit 2500 that is fixedly installed in a part of the inner space of the housing 2200 divides the outer cavity 2210 and the inner cavity 2520 removes foreign substances contained in purified water passes it and introduces it into the inner cavity 2520 while being installed in the central position of the internal cavity 2520 of the water purification filter unit 2500 it is fixed at the top in a sealed state and electrolyzes purified water according to the corresponding control signal so that oh groups and hydrogen peroxide are generated to generate radical water"}, {"pat_id": "US-6182453-B1", "para_id": "para_296", "text": "by means of the temperature sensors positioned in various zones of the water reservoir one or more known heating devices mounted within the unit housing or adjacent to the water reservoir including the peltier probe itself can be activated in reverse to provide a sufficient amount of heating to prevent freezing of the lines valves and reservoir when the ambient or housing panel temperature falls into the range 5 to 5 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359449-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "accordingly the sterilizing water provided to the patient is not cold so that the patient can solve problems such as toothache during dental treatment and also has the effect of preventing freezing in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175854-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "in addition on the outer circumferential surface of the flow path tube 74 in contact with the ion exchange resin 64 a temperature sensor for detecting the temperature t of the softening means 60 that changes according to the season for example winter 110 is attached to the inner circumferential surface of the flow path tube 74 to prevent freezing of the softening means 60 according to the temperature t of the softening means 60 detected by the temperature sensor 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175854-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "according to the softening apparatus and the control method of the washing machine according to the present invention as described above by mounting a heater and a temperature sensor in the softening means to detect whether the softening means is frozen and when the softening means is frozen in order to prevent freezing of the softening means even in winter by driving the heater to thaw the softening means it is possible to prevent freezing of the softening means and deterioration of softening performance and to take prompt measures according to the freezing of the softening means"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101286956-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "the water heater installed in any one of the first to fifth channel regions is selectively operated by an electronic control unit connected to the relay unit via a relay unit and relaying whether or not the temperature is lower than a set temperature of the unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "the controller 129 is a temperature measured by the water temperature sensor 128 is a temperature close to the freezing point and the internal space temperature measured by the temperature sensor 147 is the temperature measured by the water temperature sensor 128 if a lower freeze of water is expected the heater 140 and the screw 125 may be activated immediately to prevent freezing of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "110 170 wall 120 water tank 121 drain pipe 125 screw 126 drive motor 127 freezing prevention spring 128 water temperature sensor 129 controller 130 180 spacer 140 heater 147 temperature sensor 150 opening and closing door 160 support leg"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5154707-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "thus in accordance with the temperature change in the case of a direct electrolysis type ozone water generator the applied voltage is controlled and in the case of a gas dissolution type ozone water generator by discharge the supply amount of oxygen gas the frequency and it is necessary to control the applied voltage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5154707-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "further the ozone water thermometer 30 b a and the concentration detection sensor 50 may be provided in the direct electrolysis type ozone water generator 100 as in the first embodiment shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an automated mobile low power consumption with a hybrid power capacity wastewater treatment facility comprising one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a wastewater generation source to one or more rough solid crushing pumping pit 2 comprising a first electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a level sensor 4 wherein the first electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid crushing impeller 5 allows to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 for removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system comprising a second electrical submersible pump 8 that oxygenates the wastewater and the wastewater treatment contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen by means of an eductor or aerator 9 which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the function of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 and a suspended solids sensor 12 to control the generation of biological sludge and microorganisms which are used for the organic matter degradation a mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 including a screen 14 to allow the passage of water to a sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 in which the separation of a liquid phase and a solid phase occurs by sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is water while in the solid phase is sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has a third electrical submersible pump 16 that allows a recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the liquid phase resulting from the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 including a screen 18 to allow the passage of water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium chloride 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 comprises a ph sensor 23 the suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 the disinfection tank 19 further comprises a screen system 21 to prevent the passage of solids to a filtration tank 27 and an electric valve 37 to eliminate solid materials passed to the disinfection tank disinfected water from the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by a fourth electrical submersible pump 22 to a connection hose 26 that is connected with the filtration tank which contains gravel 28 of different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is achieved furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for continuous use during the night in which the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that performs the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to provide during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains continuous operation the local charge controller also allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for displaying dynamic graphs in the control panel 32 and sends the information to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 comprising at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and nearby surroundings the lamp towers are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamp towers have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain time periods or live video of everything that is happening around the facility and with a visual monitoring finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 to transport and mount in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the present invention describes an automated with a hybrid power capacity connected to an electrical current or a photovoltaic power facility for wastewater treatment by oxidative and biological degradation of the liquids originated from a sewage installation utilizing aerobic digestion which is comprised of one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a source of wastewater to one or more rough solid crushing pump pits 2 comprised by an electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a float type level sensor 4 where the activation of the electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid shredder pusher 5 allows it to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 which has the purpose of removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system with air presence consisting of an electrical submersible pump 8 that through an eductor aerator 9 oxygenates the water contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the operation of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a series of sensors a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 for monitoring and controlling the oxygen in the aeration process and a suspended solids sensor 12 for the biological sludge and microorganisms generation which are used for the organic matter degradation the mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 which has a screen 14 to guarantee the passage of only water to a sedimentation and mud separation tank 15 in which the separation of the liquid phase and the solid phase occurs through a process of sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is the water with dejected and clarified organic material while the solid phase is the sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has an electrical submersible pump 16 at its bottom that allows the recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the result of the liquid phase of the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 which has a screen 18 to guarantee the passage of only water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium hypochlorite 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 has sensors in order to automate the operation of this and guarantee the quality of the resulting water a ph sensor 23 a suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 likewise the disinfection tank 19 considers a screen system 21 that is utilized to prevent the passage of solids to the final filtration process alongside with an electro valve 37 that eliminates solid materials that may have passed to this tank the disinfected water in the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by an electrical submersible pump 22 and a connection hose 26 that is connected to a filtration tank 27 which contains gravel 28 with different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is obtained furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for its continuous use during the night where the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that operates the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to providing it during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains its continuous operation the charge controller allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for its dynamic graphs display in the control panel 32 and sends it to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 composed by at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and its nearby surroundings this lamps are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamps have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain periods of time and or real time video of everything that is happening around the facility and with this a visual monitoring of it finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 that allow it to be transported from one place to another easily and it is mounted in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102836249-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention provides a device for producing slightly acidic hypochlorous acid water comprising an electrolysis chamber having an electrolyte and an electrolytic cell having an anode electrode and a cathode electrode and electrolyzing the electrolyte a raw water input portion for inputting raw water into the electrolysis result of the electrolysis chamber a heater for heating the input raw water to increase the temperature of the raw water and a slightly acidic hypochlorous acid water tank for storing slightly acidic hypochlorous acid water generated by the reaction of the electrolysis result of the electrolysis chamber and the input raw water wherein before inputting the raw water the device further comprises a hardness sensor that is spaced apart from the raw water input portion and measures the hardness of the raw water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102836249-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "a second embodiment of the present invention provides a device for producing slightly acidic hypochlorous acid water comprising an electrolysis chamber 110 comprising an electrolyte 111 and an electrolytic cell 115 having an anode electrode and a cathode electrode and electrolyzing the electrolyte a raw water input unit 120 for inputting raw water into the electrolysis result of the electrolysis chamber 110 a heater 130 for heating the input raw water to increase the temperature of the raw water and a slightly acidic hypochlorous acid water tank 150 for storing slightly acidic hypochlorous acid water generated by the reaction of the electrolysis result of the electrolysis chamber 110 and the input raw water wherein the device further comprises a hardness sensor 140 that is spaced apart from the raw water input unit 120 and measures the hardness of the raw water before inputting the raw water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aeration tank for aerating the treated water so that aerobic microorganisms propagate in the treated water by the supplied oxygen to form floes a measurement unit for measuring and monitoring a treatment state by sampling a predetermined amount of the treated water being treated in the aeration tank a suction unit connected to one or more of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water from each of the aeration tanks and supplying the collected water to the measuring unit a discharge unit connecting the measurement unit and the aeration tank so that the treated water measured by the measurement unit is discharged back to the aeration tank and a central processing unit that receives the measurement data measured by the measurement unit analyzes the measurement data and controls the measurement unit the suction unit and the discharge unit the suction part one or more aeration tank connection pipes connected to each of the aeration tanks one end of which is disposed so as to be submerged in each of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water in each aeration tank and a scoring point control unit installed at the bottom of the aeration tank connection pipe installed to be drawn into the lower part of the aeration tank connection pipe or drawn out to the outside and to adjust the depth inserted into the aeration tank the measuring unit a measuring tank accommodating the treated water supplied through the inlet and having a washing water inlet through which washing water flows a spray nozzle installed at the washing water inlet inside the measuring tank to inject washing water into the measuring tank an angle adjusting unit rotatably installed at an end of the spray nozzle and adjusting a spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle a rotating inner tube installed on an inner circumferential surface of the measuring tank and having a plurality of through holes a rotary driving unit installed to be connected to the rotating inner tube to transmit power to the rotating inner tube and to rotate the rotating inner tube inside the measuring tank to form a vortex inside the measuring tank a washing state confirmation unit installed inside the measuring tank to photograph the inside of the measuring tank the control unit of the central processing unit analyzes the degree of contamination of the measurement tank through the image of the inside of the measurement tank captured by the washing state confirmation unit and analyzes whether or not cleaning of the inside of the measurement tank is necessary or a part requiring cleaning when the control unit confirms a position requiring washing the spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle is adjusted as the angle adjuster rotates a washing unit for cleaning the inside of the measurement tank by spraying washing water into the measurement tank after the treated water measured in the measurement tank is discharged to the aeration tank through the discharge unit and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting the freeze protection unit a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe a heating unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction part the treated water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part and when the temperature sensed by the temperature sensing unit is equal to or less than a predetermined temperature a temperature control unit for adjusting the heating temperature of the heating unit so that the treated water or washing water inside the pipe does not freeze"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021938-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "night minimum flow rate detection method to reduce gas flow gas injection type to find out leaked gas after filling the gas inside the pipe and the radar detection to find the leak by using the temperature of the leak point is lower than the leak point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102688285-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the environmental factor is a sensing value sensed by the sensor constituting the sensor unit 4 and includes ph temperature dissolved oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp sludge concentration sludge generation amount water quality and flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "the washing tub 210 may further include a washing tub contamination measuring sensor for measuring the degree of contamination of the washing liquid and transmitting the measurement result to the controller 59"}, {"pat_id": "US-11559765-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "if so the method 700 proceeds to block 740 where the controller 180 activates the auxiliary condenser 14 to expel heat from the water recovery system 10 and reduce the temperature of the one or more internal condenser coils 48 and then the method 700 proceeds to block 745"}, {"pat_id": "US-7661662-B2", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "there may be difficulties in using the concentration as the control signal and provided the airflowrate remains constant and provided the concentration of contaminant in the incoming wastewater remains constant the designer may arrange that the system is operated by controlling the gas so as to keep the signal from the temperature sensor 49 constant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356118-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "groundwater upper protection ball safety device characterized in that to prevent the freezing of the water pipe 20 by opening the automatic discharge valve 50 when the temperature is reached by setting the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356118-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition by immediately detecting the illegal opening of the upper groundwater protector to generate a warning sound to thoroughly maintain the security of the groundwater upper protector as well as to prevent theft or damage of the pumping device components and contaminated groundwater and poison it provides the effect of supplying safe groundwater by preventing inflow.1 is a longitudinal cross sectional view of the installation state of the upper ground water protection ball applied the present invention 2 is an installation state diagram of the groundwater temperature sensor the discharge pipe and the automatic discharge valve of the present invention figure 3 is an enlarged cross sectional view of the installation state of the present invention groundwater temperature sensor 4 is a state in which the discharge pipe and the automatic discharge valve of the present invention installed inside the groundwater upper protection hole figure 5 is a longitudinal cross sectional view of the installation state of the lid sensor according to the first embodiment of the present invention 6 is a state in which the upper protection cover is installed with a cover detection sensor according to the first embodiment of the present invention is opened figure 7 is a longitudinal cross sectional view of the installation state of the lid sensor according to a second embodiment of the present invention 8 is a state in which the upper protection cover is installed with a cover detection sensor according to a second embodiment of the present invention is opened 9 is a block diagram showing the overall configuration of the master control box and the slave control box of the present invention 10 is a block diagram showing the overall configuration of a slave control box of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "it is possible to determine whether or not leakage of conduit facilities"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3520440-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "abnormality information signals inside or outside the pipeline or inside the strata and inside the structure due to fluctuations from the normal state of the signal are measured and among the specified distance sections set many by analyzing the measurement signal ground depression ground subsidence radioactivity leakage or abnormality in a specific distance section we found the sign of a disaster accident due to a rise in temperature and found the site of the accident"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3520440-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "abnormality information signals inside or outside the pipeline or inside the strata and inside the structure due to fluctuations from the normal state of the signal are measured and among the specified distance sections set many by analyzing the measurement signal we have adopted a method that allows us to identify the location of the occurrence site and predict it in advance by discovering the sign of a disaster accident due to ground depression ground subsidence radiation leakage or abnormal temperature rise in a specific distance section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101739419-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a constant temperature system for leachate and wastewater treatment plants installed in a nitrification tank in a leachate treatment plant including a tiller a flow control tank a mixing tank a nitrification tank a settling tank a thickening tank a fenton oxidation treatment tank or a reverse osmosis treatment tank a plurality of nitrification vessels buried in the ground and purifying and discharging the supplied leachate from the outside and having a plurality of chambers partitioned by a plurality of partition walls for setting the movement path of the leachate therein at least one agitator disposed on the bottom surface of the nitrification tank to mix the leachate while rotating a first heat pump disposed in an upper part of the nitrification tank on the ground to heat the nitrification tank and heat exchanging the first chamber leachate and the heat exchanged refrigerant disposed in front of the nitrification tank in the direction in which the leachate flows 3 heat pump a fourth heat pump to a sixth heat pump arranged in parallel with the first heat pump to the third heat pump and arranged in the rear along the direction in which the leachate of the nitrification tank flows and the heat exchanged refrigerant is heat a first heat exchanger connected to the first heat pump to a third heat pump and disposed in the first chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a second heat exchanger connected to the fourth heat pump to the sixth heat pump and disposed in the second chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a first circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the first heat exchange unit a second circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the second heat exchange unit a preliminary circulation pump interposed between the first circulation pump and the second circulation pump and capable of temporarily operating corresponding to the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump a three way valve connected between any one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump and selectively supplying the heat exchanged refrigerant to the first chamber or the second chamber a sensor unit provided on the three way valve for sensing the temperature or pressure of the refrigerant flowing into the three way valve a first heat pump to a sixth heat pump a first circulation pump and a second circulation pump and a control unit controlling the temperature of the leachate in the nitrification tank to a set range by controlling the agitator an expansion tank provided to compensate for a pressure of the heat exchanged refrigerant supplied through the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump and an air blower unit for supplying air supplied from the outside to the periphery of the agitator in the nitrification tank the air blower unit includes an air flow path for introducing outside air into the vicinity of the agitator a compressor for forcibly supplying external air through the air flow path and a nozzle provided at an end portion of the air flow path for discharging air toward the agitator and wherein the agitator includes a housing fixed to the bottom of the nitrification tank and passing through the inside in a vertical direction a propeller for rotating the inside of the housing to mix the leachate a driving motor for driving the propeller and a guide arm provided on the outer circumferential surface of the housing so as to be guided through the air passage when installed wherein the control unit controls the at least one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump to selectively operate the heat pumps when the temperature of the nitrification tank reaches the set temperature by receiving the data of the sensor unit the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump operates first and controls the heat pumps to operate after the set time has elapsed wherein the nitrification tank includes a plurality of ventilation doors formed with openings communicating with the outside at upper portions of the chambers and selectively opening and closing the openings"}, {"pat_id": "US-6575662-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the chain may be copper plated to prevent bio fouling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200375794-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "by stopping the heating operation of the heater 5 to heat the heat meter so that the water meter 1 does not freeze to prevent freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "dual heating system to prevent freezing of receiving piping"}, {"pat_id": "US-10898826-B2", "para_id": "para_773", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump bottom of the container 139 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 that stores and stores rainwater flowing through the filter a pump that is installed at the bottom of the storage tank and rotates the rainwater stored in the storage tank from time to time or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation d