in the feed pump for supplying water to the filtration membrane portion and to maintain the flow rate on the surface of the filtration membrane to prevent the filtration membrane from clogging due to fouling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature water saving type washing water supply device containing ozone and free radicals characterized in that consisting of a heater unit 151 for heating the washing water under the control of the washing water temperature sensor 152"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature it is characterized in that it comprises a heater unit 151 for heating the washing water under the control of the washing water temperature sensor 152"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102428233-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "an object of the present invention as described above is installed in a tunnel to prevent freezing of the fire extinguishing water in the tunnel comprising a water supply unit including a water supply pipe installed in the tunnel heating means mounted along the outer peripheral surface of the water supply pipe an outdoor temperature sensor mounted on one side of the water supply pipe located at the entrance or exit of the tunnel among the water supply pipes to sense the outside temperature a power saving control unit that receives outdoor temperature information corresponding to the outdoor temperature and transmits an output signal for each section co