ock diagram of a conventional water quality multi item measuring device of water purification equipment the signal detected from a plurality of sensors s1 s5 for measuring temperature ph turbidity residual chlorine concentration and electrical conductivity respectively is transferred to the main control unit 7 through the sensor transducers 1 to 5 and the analog signal lines 6 and the ad conversion unit inside the main control unit 7 transmits the analog signal inputted through the analog signal lines 6 8 converts the signal into a digital signal and processes the signal in the main control unit 7 to make digital data and the main control unit 7 displays these data via the lcd display unit 9 and simultaneously communicates with rs 232c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101030980-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "figure 2 shows the overall block diagram of the water quality multi item measuring device 20 according to the present invention as shown in figure 2 temperature ph turbidity residual chlorine concentration and electrical conductivity in the water treatment plant and the reservoir of the water purification plant in order to measure the items of water quality such as the measured number of samples to be supplied to each sensor measuring sensor unit 21 for measuring each water quality items and each signal measured by the measuring sensor unit and the respective sensors and the digital sensor converts the digital data into digital data using the calibration factor stored for each sensor and transmits the signal to the main control unit 23 via the sensor interbase unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-10036143-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in an alternative embodiment the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-10036143-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the alternative embodiment works by taking the temperature at the temperature sensor package of the leak detection system the external environment temperature sensor and the additional temperature sensor package and feeding the data to a microprocessor where they are analyzed to determine whether the fluid is expanding by comparing the temperature data to the user inputted data stored in a control rom and flash memory"}, {"pat_id": "US-11774044-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "a vertical comparison time sequence allows the hydrogen concentration curve at each evacuation pipe to be derived over time and a horizontal comparison sensor position allows the specific leak position of the pipeline to be determined"}, {"pat_id": "US-11774044-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "while realizing the real time whole pipeline detecting of the pipeline for transporting hydrogen the composite pipeline for transporting hydrogen provided by the present disclosure has the advantages of light weight good flexibility hydrogen corrosion resistance high safety good insulation performance and long service life etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-11774044-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "due to the thermal expansion effect of the plastic welding pipe the evacuation pipe and the cutting area are fused together and cooled to the required time to complete the welding"}, {"pat_id": "US-11774044-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "when manufacturing the system of real time whole pipeline monitoring hydrogen leakage a plurality of evacuation pipes with a diameter of 15 mm and a plurality of fiber optic hydrogen sensors with temperature and hydrogen concentration measurement functions are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102732710-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "as described above the electrode of the ph sensor 1330 must be free of contamination and may require periodic renewal and correction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a device capable of generating sodium hypochlorite saturated salt water tank receiving soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine the water level is controlled by a water gauge and a water supply valve a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank sodium hypochlorite generator having an automatic valve and a flow sensor characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-2