d to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "US-11095960-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "since the market introduction of audio central hubs with intelligent listening microphone transducer that coverts sound into an corresponding electrical signal and speaker that is a device that converts an electrical digital or analog audio signal into a corresponding sound capability in a single apparatus the applicant is disclosing and claiming using this technology to control or receive information from a water meter and leak detection system in this patent application"}, {"pat_id": "US-11095960-B2", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "in the alternate shower monitoring embodiment for measuring or monitoring the temperature of the water flowing from the shower or bath head the use of various thermocouples or thermistor sensors 70 as depicted in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240028-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "another important aspect of the bi metallic disk is that after the predetermined temperature of for example 36 has been reached and the disk has warped to break the electrical contact of the switch the disk will maintain the warped shape until manually re set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "oxygen management block an oxygen control block for generating an oxygen supply control signal corresponding to the measured dissolved oxygen concentration when the measured dissolved oxygen concentration is less than the preset discharge allowable dissolved oxygen concentration oxygen supply means for supplying pressurized air to a predetermined depth position based on the oxygen supply control signal a green algae management block that monitors whether the measured surface layer water temperature the middle layer water temperature and the lower layer water temperature are outside the preset allowable temperature difference range and instructs a corresponding green algae alarm when the preset allowable temperature difference is out of range an alarm generation block for generating a green algae generation alarm for alarming that green algae is generated by an increase in nutrients caused by a conductive phenomenon in which the surface layer and the lower layer are mixed based on the commanded green algae alarm and sending the green algae generation alarm to the management means the management means for operating each winch installed in each of the plurality of winch machine rooms when the floodgate opening request signal is received to open the corresponding movable walkway gates and visually generating a green algae alarm when the green algae generation alarm is received"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_252", "text": "the water temperature algae concentration and organic pollutant concentration may be selectively delivered to the oxygen control block 404 and the algae management block 410"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_253", "text": "to this end the sensor block 402 as shown in figure 5 for example dissolved oxygen sensor 501 water temperature sensor 502 chlorophyll a sensor 503 water temperature weak layer sensor 504 orp oxidation reduction potential ec sensor 505 electric conductivity ec sensor 506 toc sensor 507 ss sensor 508 na sensor 509 cod sensor 510 tp sensor 511 tn sensor 512 flow sensor 513 ph sensor 514 turbidity sensor 515 light intensity sensor 516 alkalinity sensor 517 nh 4 n sensor 518 po 4 the p sensor 519 the cl sensor 520 the fe 2 sensor 521 the air temperature sensor 522 the residence time sensor 523 the water level sensor 524 and the like may be included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_257", "text": "the measurement may be continuously performed according to a set cycle and then transferred to the oxygen management block 404"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_276", "text": "next the green algae management block 410 compares the water temperature difference between the surface layer water temperature the middle layer water temperature and the lower layer water temperature measured by the water temperature sensor and the preset allowable water temperature difference range and the water temperature surface layer water temperature when the middle layer water temperature and the lower layer water temperature difference is determined to be out of the preset allowable temperature difference range the alarm generation block 412 may provide a function of instructing a corresponding green algae alarm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_295", "text": "here algae related sensors may include for example chlorophyll a sensor 503 ss sensor 508 turbidity sensor 506 and the like and organic contaminant related sensors may include for example water temperature medicine layer sensor 504 orp and the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-8926834-B2", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "or polyone corporation of avon lake ohio which contacts the fluid flow 98 though in other embodiments the temperature and flow measurement sensors may be encased in other corrosion resistant materials"}, {"pat_id": "US-11014837-B2", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "furthermore the monitoring unit 360 may monitor a temperature degree of electrolysis and or water level of the sea or river which is measured using an sbe37im sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102561600-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition a sensor for detecting the internal temperature of the hydrant and a heating wire for supplying heat are provided inside the hydrant housing to keep the inside of the hydrant warm thereby exhibiting an advantageous effect of protecting the hydrant from freezing in winter.1 is a view of a replacement process of an antifreeze hydrant according to the prior art 2 and 3 are views of an automatic heating antifreeze hydrant according to an embodiment of the present invention 4 and 5 show only some configurations to show the operating principle of the automatic heating antifreeze hydrant according to the present invention figure 6 is an internal heating component using a hot wire of the antifreeze hydrant according to the present invention 7 is a coupling structure of the lower end of the middle pipe which is a part of the antifreeze hydrant according to the present invention 8 and 9 are the coupling structure of the upper end of the intermediate pipe which is a part of the non freezing hydrant according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102561600-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in the present invention a heating wire is disposed inside the housing to supply heat in order to prevent freezing before water supply during a cold wave in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102415233-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "intake tank a water intake pipe inserted into the groundwater layer and connected to the water intake tank an intake pump disposed in the intake pipe to supply groundwater to the intake tank a groundwater sensor module inserted into the groundwater layer to measure the level of the groundwater the radon concentration of the groundwater the temperature of the groundwater the electrical conductivity and the ph concentration of the groundwater a water tank connected to the water intake tank through a water tank supply pipe an intake tank sensor module disposed inside the intake tank to measure the temperature of the stored water in the intake tank the electrical conductivity of the stored water the radon concentration of the stored water and the ph concentration of the stored water a supply pump disposed in the water tank supply pipe to supply water from the water intake tank to the water tank and a control center for controlling the groundwater sensor module the water intake tank and the supply pump when the radon concentration measured in at least one of the groundwater sensor module and the intake tank sensor module exceeds a reference value the control center prevents the supply pump and the intake pump from operating the groundwater sensor module is case a body portion disposed inside the case and it is inserted into the body portion and a first sensor unit for detecting radon in water and the first sensor unit a first insertion part inserted into the body part a fixing part connected to the first insertion part a first sensor disposed inside the fixing part and measuring the radon partly exposed to the outside of the fixing part a shielding part disposed on the fixing part to shield the first sensor part exposed to the outside of the fixing part and a humidity sensor disposed around the first sensor to measure humidity provided an integrated control system for artificial cultivation in response to drought using a wireless sensor network"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385568-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in this case in the case of groundwater after the operation of the temperature sensor 80 that detects the freezing temperature due to the characteristics of the groundwater the water temperature 0 or more it is preferable to have a timer to stop the continuous operation"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3814772-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the sensor devices may also include an electronic circuit board analog and digital circuitry to control the operation of the sensors based upon a real time schedule"}, {"pat_id": "US-9534300-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the plurality of sensors can comprise for example sensors for measuring conductivity corrosion inhibitor concentration ph oxidation reduction potential orp fluorescence biocide concentration turbidity temperature flow and dissolved oxygen do in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102554668-B1", "para_id": "para_175", "text": "water softening in the pretreatment module 160 may alternatively or additionally be achieved using an anti scalant such as lime softening ion exchange resin or polyphosphate as is known in the art"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430457-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the conventional technique is to install a heating wire in the shape of caps on the outside of the water meter and to arrange a sensor to heat it when the temperature is below a certain temperature to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a closed cylinder portion 100 coupled to the lower side of the groundwater protection part a piezoelectric tube 210 installed at one side to prevent the groundwater from expanding due to internal pressure generated when the groundwater rises is coupled to one side of the piezoelectric pipe the other side is coupled to the plate check valve sand filter 220 for filtering the sand contained in the groundwater plate check valve 230 is coupled to one side of the sand filter the other side is coupled to the meter to prevent the groundwater filtered by the sand filter backflow a meter 240 coupled to one side of the plate check valve and the other side coupled to a pressure gauge a pressure gauge 250 coupled to one side of the meter and coupled to a three way valve on the other side a three way valve 260 coupled to the pressure gauge to form a flow path in the direction of the emergency water supply pipe 600 or the water supply pipe 700 an underground water level protection hole 200 including an underground water level protection column 270 formed along an inner circumference to prevent freezing waves it is configured to include and the controller 500 for supplying power to the underground water protection unit if the temperature is below the set temperature the controller 500 a temperature sensor 510 for detecting the ambient temperature a temperature setting unit 520 for setting a reference temperature for supplying power to the ground water protection protection vessel a memory unit 530 for storing the reference temperature set by the temperature setting unit a power supply unit 540 for supplying power to the ground water protection protection line a temperature comparison unit 550 for comparing the temperature sensed by the temperature sensor with the reference temperature stored in the memory unit a power supply signal transmitter 560 for transmitting a power supply signal to a power supply unit when the temperature compared by the temperature comparison unit is less than a reference temperature freezing prevention comprising a central control unit 570 for controlling the signal flow between the temperature sensor the temperature setting unit the memory unit the power supply unit the temperature comparison unit the power supply signal transmission unit and groundwater upper protection device capable of underwater discharge sterilization treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-5646863-A", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "consequently the ems can be applied to a vast number of contaminant problems and is not limited to the application cited above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200452318-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the heating element is a planar or linear heating element.the present invention for achieving the above object the heat insulating material is installed inside the cover of the tap water meter box having a check hole the heating element is installed inside the heat insulating material the temperature sensor is installed on the heating element to sense the current temperature and characterized in that it comprises a height adjustment port for adjusting the installation height of the heating element.the present invention as described above has the effect of preventing the freezing in winter by removing the cover of the existing water metering box and installing a cover having a heating element and heat insulator or installing a water metering device box in which the heating element is installed on one side of the inner side in the new building in addition even when installed in the ground by applying power to the heating element to generate heat there is an effect that can prevent the freezing of the water supply meter box from the freezing in winter.1 is a view showing a first embodiment of the present invention 2 is an enlarged view of the heating element of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200452318-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "since it is applied heat is generated from the heating element 6 to prevent freezing of the meter and the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102061131-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the metal heater 110 is installed to be in contact with the pipe 10 under the heat insulating material 11 surrounding the pipe 10 and supplies power to the metal heater 110 to generate heat to prevent freezing of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102061131-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when an operation command of the heater 110 is issued the metal heater controller 130 supplies power to the metal heater 110 based on this and the metal heater 110 generates heat to prevent freezing of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in one aspect of the invention the contaminant detection system includes an electrochemical ph reduction module for lowering the ph of the waste water stream prior to the waste water stream reaching the contaminant sensor or water quality sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the contaminant sensor 175 may include instrumentation that monitors multiple channels for various water quality parameters including ph conductivity temperature among others that can impact the detection of lead and other heavy metals by electrochemical methods"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "for example as noted above the rate of deposit of lead oxide on the contaminant sensor 175 is dependent on ph temperature conductivity and ionic strength"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "in one aspect of the invention the algorithm uses information from the particle sensor to determine the size and quantity of lead oxide particles and consequently use this data along with electrochemical data to determine the total dissolved and particulate lead and other heavy metals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100635856-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the temperature is detected to determine the concentration of the silver solution sterilized water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "according to claim 1 the raw water inlet pipe is attached to one side before the raw water is injected into the virus sterilization device is attached to the contaminant sensor to determine the degree of contamination to prevent the inflow and inflow of raw water to the raw water inlet valve the virus sterilization device is the location where the raw water inflow distributing large particles by distributing large screens distributing raw water to virus sterilizers plural uv lamps or uvleds are installed inside virus sterilizers and ozone injection hoses installed outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the raw water inlet pipe 10 is attached to one side before the raw water is injected into the virus sterilization device 16 is attached to the contaminant sensor 12 to determine the degree of contamination to prevent the inflow and inflow of raw water to the raw water inlet valve 14 in addition the virus sterilization device 20 installs a distribution screen 22 at a position where raw water is introduced to filter foreign matter having large particles distributes and supplies the raw water into the virus sterilization device 20 and a virus sterilization device 20 a plurality of uv lamps or uvleds 24 are installed therein and ozone is introduced through an ozone injection hose 28 from an ozone generator 26 installed outside to sterilize viruses and a virus sterilizer 20 it provides a water supply system for supplying fish farm facilities capable of controlling water temperature and virus sterilization of raw water passing through the virus sensor 16 and then measuring the virus through the filtration device 30"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5027325-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "measure the abnormal information signals inside or below the underground pipes in the underground structure or structure by fluctuation of the detection signal from the normal state and within the specific distance section set by the analysis of the measurement signal a method was adopted to detect the signs of disaster accidents caused by ground depression ground subsidence radioactivity leakage or abnormal temperature rise in a specific distance section and to identify the site of occurrence and predict it in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "by the temperature sensor and the power is supplied to the power storage unit 20 thereby preventing freezing of the main body 1 and the tube 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161642-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "pump 4 a sterilizing filter 9 for sterilizing bacteria contained in the filtered purified water while passing through the filter a display setting unit 11 for displaying temperature and operating conditions and a cold water storage tank 14 the cold water temperature sensor 14 for measuring the purified water temperature of the hot water the hot water temperature sensor 15 for measuring the purified water temperature of the hot water storage tank 12 and the purified water temperature stored in the hot water storage tank 12 are raised"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_460", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_465", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may in block 7392 receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_525", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from for example a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_584", "text": "in block 7528 the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_591", "text": "in block 7832 the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor s 6082a d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_594", "text": "in some embodiments the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_595", "text": "in some embodiments if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a d are less than the threshold the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_598", "text": "if in block 7604 flow of source water into the system 6000 exists the temperature of the source water may be obtained from a source water temperature sensor 6036 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_600", "text": "obtaining the temperature of the water source in block 7652 may include reading an output from one or more sensor such as a source water temperature sensor 6036 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_603", "text": "in block 6718 a delta between the target temperature and the temperature indicated by the electronics temperature sensor may be input to a pid loop run by the controller 6034"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_604", "text": "if in block 6724 the sensor data indicates that the current temperature of the electronics housing is greater than a high temperature limit the target temperature value may be set to a low temperature limit in block 6726"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_604", "text": "if instead in block 6728 the sensor data indicates that the current temperature of the electronics housing is less than the low temperature limit the target temperature value may be set to the high temperature limit in block 6730"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0385568 2003.05.15 designated by reservoir control system registered and filed by the present applicant the groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-7749360-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "water is circulated through this feedback loop and valve 41 is manually set to minimize and or reduce the buildup of sediment or scaling material in the evaporator 12"}, {"pat_id": "US-5895565-A", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "an integrated water treatment control system as set forth in claim 2 in which the water treatment elements include a total dissolved solids element and in which the second means senses the conductivity of the circulating water to determine the total dissolved solids in the water and in which the third means treats circulating water to return the total dissolved solids to with a given range the water treatment elements include a heater and in which the second means senses the temperature of the circulating water and in which the third means treats the circulating water in a manner to return the temperature of the recirculating water to within a given range the water treatment elements include a ph adjusting components and in which the second means senses the ph of the circulating water and in which the third means treats the circulating water in a manner to adjust acidity or alkalinity to a ph within a given range the water treatment elements includes a sanitizer and in which the second means includes a sensor to measure the oxidation reduction potential of the circulating water and in which the third means treats the circulating water to return the orp level to within a given range and in which the second means includes a ppm sensor to sense the concentration of sanitizer in the circulating water and in which the third means treats the circulating water to maintain the concentration of sanitizer within a given range"}, {"pat_id": "US-4773991-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the pressure switch 28 thereby protects the pump against cavitation"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as used herein the term second compartment may be used interchangeably with the terms sensor compartment or sensor tank and unless otherwise specified is the compartment in which various parameters such as temperature ph and corrosion are measured in the spray water generally now particle free according to the disclosed system and methods"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "for example temperature sensors may be situated in first settling compartment 21 in second sensor compartment 23 to determine the temperature at the ph and corrosion sensors and permit correction of their readings at the outlet section of the system to measure temperature in the outlet flow and or at automated pinch valve 22 to detect if the drain is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "in the second compartment a corrosion monitor ph meter and temperature sensor were installed for continuous monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_106", "text": "temperature is also a key parameter to monitor because of its impact on corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101716466-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation sensor 18 installed in a drainage passage 213 of the solar cell module 21 to measure the amount of precipitation water collected in the solar cell module 21 an opening and closing unit 225 connected at both ends to the drainage passage 213 and connected to an elastic string 281 for detecting the amount of precipitation by the precipitation sensor 18 to determine the opening and closing level of the collecting tube 221 a collecting connection unit 12 connected to the drainage passage 213 for collecting the precipitation a control server 11 for controlling the operation of the opening closing means installed in the collection connection unit 12 based on the information transmitted from the precipitation sensor 18 a storage unit 15 in which the precipitation is stored a detection unit 16 for detecting the state of water stored in the storage unit 15 and and a branch unit 14 operated by the control server 11 based on the information transmitted from the detection unit 16 the storage unit 15 is installed under the solar cell module and is shielded by the solar cell module"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3699440-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "for example temperature sensors may consist of thermocouples and position deformation sensors may consist of laser sensors configured to detect the distance between the sensor and the controlled element"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101327389-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "that is by checking the condensate and curing temperature throughout the construction by the moisture sensor and the temperature sensor it is possible to contribute to the quality improvement by checking the uniform curing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101363635-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "7 the control box 50 controls the heating wire 30 for dissipating heat to prevent the water pipe 1 from freezing due to low temperature thereby freezing the water pipe 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-12404043-B2", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "thus reflectivity is the primary variable that is subject to effect of pressure and or temperature associated with the sensor being located at a respective subsea depth"}, {"pat_id": "US-6315886-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the purification system may also include sensor means and computerized means for receiving input from the sensor means and providing output for controlling at least one operating condition of the system selected from the group consisting of current density flow rate of contaminated aqueous solution to the electrolysis cell temperature and ph of the contaminated aqueous electrolyte solution"}, {"pat_id": "US-8038881-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the on line sensors 140 are used to measure and feed the control unit information on multiple parameters such as tph nitrogen dissolved oxygen toc and temperature listed in table 1 below anticipate inlet fluctuations in conjunction with the controller that has been specifically designed for predefined flow rates and identify contamination type as well as level of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101928816-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "s10 transmitting a measured value from the first temperature sensor and the conductivity sensor to the control unit by draining a large amount of cooling water and supplying new raw water to replace the cooling water s20 of calculating the electric conductivity calculated value from the measured value received in step s20 and when the electric conductivity calculated value is equal to or more than the first reference electric conductivity s30 and the step of calculating the electric conductivity calculated in the step s20 s40 of opening the drain valve when the quasi electroconductivity is exceeded measuring the value of the total dissolved solids of the cooling water accommodated in the cooling tower at the first and second points of view through the tds meter calculating a tds increase rate from a value obtained by the first and second pressure sensors s50 determining whether the tds increase rate exceeds a preset reference tds increase rate s51 s60 and when the difference between the two pressure values received in the step s60 exceeds the reference pressure difference range through the control unit the discharge valve is opened to discharge foreign matter s07"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "prevents freezing the control unit is further provided with a sticking prevention function when the operation time of the discharge pump is stopped for a specific time or more the discharge pump is operated for a specific time at a specific period to prevent sewage from sticking to the storage tank or the discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in a preferred embodiment of the present invention the control unit is further provided with a temperature sensor for sensing the temperature of the storage tank so that when the temperature of the storage tank is less than a specific temperature the freezing wave for operating the discharge pump for a specific time period predetermined prevention may be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "at this time the temperature sensor 270 is to monitor whether the sewage stored in the storage tank 100 freezes it will be common that the sensing unit is installed in the storage tank 100 and connected to the control unit 250 if necessary the sensing unit may be installed around the outside of the storage tank 100 or provided in a control box provided with a pcb so that the freezing prevention function may operate according to the ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045455-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however this method has a problem that can not effectively prevent the decay of the water due to the green algae occurring during the summer and also in the winter to empty the water of the pond to freeze and prevent freezing of the water to become a pond of ugly landscape facilities there is this.the present invention has been made to actively solve the above problems and after pumping ground water 100m underground through a jet pump to maintain an average temperature of 22 in the summer and 12 in the winter the purpose is to provide artificial ecological mooring pond using groundwater geothermal heat that is configured to circulate with the supply to the pond.as a means for achieving the above described technical problem the present invention after forming a core ball groove having a depth of 100m underground through boring work and accommodates a jet pump for supplying water to the inside of the core ball groove and then through the jet pump the discharged water is discharged into the pond through the water supply pipe and the water accumulated in the pond is purified through the uv sterilizer and the filter connected to the purified water pump and the purified water discharge line and then discharged to the external pipe housed inside the protective pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-5062442-A", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "apparatus for monitoring a fluid conduit system for leakage points comprising a main valve having a housing that includes an inlet an outlet and a valve seat interposed between the inlet and outlet and a valve member in the housing operable between an open and a closed position for controlling fluid flow through the valve seat and volumetric flow meter shunt means for defining a shunt flow path that opens to the inlet and outlet bridging the valve seat and controlling the opening of the valve member as a function of the flow volume in the shunt path and maintaining the main valve member closed until the volume in the shunt path exceeds a predetermined value the shunt means including a measuring section having laminar flow therethrough a first heat source for heating fluid flowing through the measuring section detecting means for detecting the temperature of the fluid prior to heating by the heat source and evaluating means for determining the flow volume from the temperature detected by the detecting means and the amount of heat given off by the heat source the detecting means including first and second temperature sensors the sensors respectively comprising first and second thin layer metal foil resistors adapted for having a constant voltage applied thereto with the first resistor being downstream of the second resistor and defining the first heat source and the second resistor serving to determine the temperature of the fluid the upstream temperature sensor being an electric resistance that is about 10 times as great as that of the downstream resistor"}, {"pat_id": "US-5013344-A", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a system for providing purified ice and purified water from a source of unpurified water comprising a continuous refrigerant flow path including a compressor an evaporator condenser means and a metering device an ice forming surface means responsive to energization of said compressor for cooling selected areas of said ice forming surface to a temperature below the freezing temperature of water by conducting thermal energy to said evaporator from said selected areas means for issuing a stream of the unpurified water over said selected areas to form ice at said selected areas while washing impurities away from the formed ice with said stream means for increasing the temperature at said selected areas at various times to remove said ice from said ice forming surface a bin for collecting ice removed from said ice forming surface heating means for warming a portion of said bin at selected times to melt some of the ice collected therein into purified liquid water container means for collecting the purified liquid water formed by melting the ice in said bin bin sensor means for sensing the amount of ice collected in said bin container sensor means for sensing the amount of purified liquid water collected in said container control means responsive to both said bin sensor means and said container means for de energizing said compressor when the amount of said collected ice in said bin exceeds a first predetermined amount and when the amount of said collected purified liquid water in said container exceeds a second predetermined amount said control means further including means for reenergizing said compressor in response to either or both of the following conditions 1 the amount of collected ice in said bin falling below the first predetermined amount and 2 the amount of collected purified liquid water in said container falling below the second predetermined amount wherein said condenser means in said refrigerant flow path includes first and second condensers disposed in said respective parallel and alternatively conductive first and second path sections said second condenser being disposed at the underside of said bin to heat collected ice at the bottom of said bin means for utilizing rejected heat from said second condenser to melt ice in said bin at a temperature of approximately 32 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-11939244-B2", "para_id": "para_155", "text": "the efc according to any embodiment may further include an oxidation reduction potential sensor a ph sensor a chlorine sensor a conductivity sensor a flow rate sensor a temperature sensor or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101935863-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "in addition the protective film layer is coated on the discolored portion thereby preventing the discolored portion from being damaged due to external impact easily recognizing discoloration of the discolored portion and considering the weakness of the temperature discolored material is preferably used.10 12 pressure pump 14 raw water supply line 16 cooling line 20 oxygen generator 30 discharge tube 32 ozone supply line 40 ozone melting tank 42 ozonated water discharge line 44 gas liquid separator 46 return line 48 connection piping 50 ozone concentration sensor 60 ozone controller 70 inverter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454420-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the outdoor toilet according to the present invention having the configuration as described above has a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature in the dirt tank and a heater operated based on a signal sensed by the temperature sensor thereby solidifying the toilet in the dirt tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_460", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_465", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may in block 7392 receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_524", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from for example a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_583", "text": "in block 7528 the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_590", "text": "in block 7832 the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor s 6082a d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_593", "text"