ly covering the upper portion of the interrupted portion it is configured to include in the center of the ceiling inside the cover a support roller via a wire rope connecting the winch device and the protective cover is installed around the side of the floating means the concrete block and weight installed in the water pulleys passing through the connecting rope to connect is characterized in that it is installed in a plurality of equal intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972396-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a lid formed of a rim shaped lower end portion an inclined rim shaped stop portion of upper and lower light beams extending from an upper portion of the lower portion and a roof completely covering the upper portion of the interrupted portion it is configured to include in the center of the ceiling inside the cover a support roller via a wire rope connecting the winch device and the protective cover is installed around the side of the floating means the concrete block and weight installed in the water pulleys passing through the connecting rope to connect is characterized in that it is installed in a plurality of equal intervals"}, {"pat_id": "US-9534978-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in an alternative embodiment the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-9534978-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the alternative embodiment works by taking the temperature at the temperature sensor package of the leak detection system the external environment temperature sensor and the additional temperature sensor package and feeding the data to a microprocessor where they are analyzed to determine whether the fluid is expanding by comparing the temperature data to the user inputted data stored in a control rom and flash memory"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318395-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the portion of untreated water that does not evaporate is transported back into untreated water chamber 104 via recirculation reservoir 108"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177518-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the long term use of the water tank 10 the weld bead 31 has a problem of contaminating the filtered water by contacting the drinking water in the water tank 16 due to corrosion and also in order to connect the temperature sensor 15 located on the upper surface or the cold water discharge port 13 through which the water is discharged with the upper cylinder 17 welding was performed at the contacting part and the lower cylinder 18 was inserted into the lower surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177518-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "34 and the water supply connection pipe 29 is configured to be screwed to connect without welding can not only block the penetration of harmful substances to the human body due to welding but also to form a simple structure for assembly work.as described above according to the water tank for cold and warm water purifier according to the embodiment of the present invention after forming a flange to the outside at the portion where the upper cylinder and the lower cylinder is in contact the inner space is formed by welding the upper cylinder the temperature sensor fitting hole and the cold water discharge port formed on the upper surface of the upper surface of the sensor are combined with the temperature sensor and the outflow pipe by the screw projections"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102911115-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "specifically the second water quality analysis step s5 may include a second blockage phenomenon detection step s51 for detecting a blockage phenomenon of the member 40 through the second sensor unit 70 and a pretreatment completion inspection step s52 for measuring do nitrate ammonia ph temperature water depth and pressure of the pretreated wastewater through the first sensor unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101862825-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a brine tank in which salt is stored a water softener for supplying water supplied from an external water supply system and softening the water supply water into soft water a brine diluting device for supplying the brine from the brine tank and diluting salinity of the brine introduced into the brine tank from the water softener a soft water supply unit for supplying soft water from the water softener to the brine tank so that salt water can be supplied to the brine tank from the brine tank and supplied to the salt water dilution unit an electrolytic cell for electrolyzing the salt water diluted through the saline dilution device and the soft water introduced from the water softener into sodium hypochlorite a pressure reducing valve for reducing the supply water supplied from the outside and supplying the water to the water softener at a constant pressure to regulate the pressure of the soft water discharged from the water softener a decontamination controller for controlling the supply of low voltage and high current dc used in the electrolytic cell and for managing and monitoring the generation of sodium hypochlorite a brine supply unit supplying brine from the brine tank to the saline dilution device and a temperature control system and a temperature controller wherein the liquid phase decontamination containing sodium hypochlorite stored in the decontamination storage tank and formed from the electrolytic cell is preliminarily a liquid decontamination room temperature regulating device provided with constant temperature information from the temperature transmission system to maintain the optimum temperature set at 15 c 1 c a sodium hypochlorite generation system comprising wherein the temperature transmission system includes a permeation amount sensor in addition to a temperature sensor formed inside the decontamination storage tank and an rfid transmission and reception end formed outside the decontamination storage tank wherein the controller is configured to receive the temperature information from the temperature transmission system and provide a heating operation signal to the heating module of the temperature adjusting device when the current temperature information is lower than a predetermined threshold temperature providing a heating shutdown signal to a heating module of the temperature controller the temperature sensor generates temperature measurement information in a state of being in contact with the decontamination storage tank and provides the temperature measurement information to the decontamination occurrence controller the permeate sensor may be configured such that when the conical salt storage tank is formed of a transparent material and the temperature control device is enclosed in the transparent conical salt storage tank a light emitting end a measuring means formed to have a structure in which a light receiving end is additionally provided at the other end of the inside of the position where the light source is received through the transparent dye storage tank from the light emitting end and the concentration of the salt is analyzed through the amount of transmitted light based on the intensity of the light source by the secondary salt generation controller the concealment generation controller may include a step of controlling the intensity of the light source intensity information the first light source intensity step to the n th light source intensity step n is a natural number of 2 or more the temperature information range received from the temperature transmission system a step of extracting the intensity of the extracted light source intensity information a temperature range of the extracted temperature information and a range of temperature information which are inputted in advance the control unit controls the temperature control unit to determine whether or not heating is required according to the extracted sodium chloride concentration information and determines whether or not the liquid phase stored in the secondary salt storage tank in order to suppress the change in concentration and the generation of carcinogenic substances with respect to the carrageenan a preset optimum temperature of 15 1 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948131-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "moreover in some embodiments the control sub system 50 may determine fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 based on sensor data determined by a fluid temperature annulus sensor 54 process block 118"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in an alternative embodiment the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the alternative embodiment works by taking the temperature at the temperature sensor package of the leak detection system the external environment temperature sensor and the additional temperature sensor package and feeding the data to a microprocessor where they are analyzed to determine whether the fluid is expanding by comparing the temperature data to the user inputted data stored in a control rom and flash memory"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a steam melting apparatus a steam heating element for heating water supplied through the water supply pipe to generate steam a pump for introducing water into the water supply pipe a water supply pipe temperature sensor for detecting the temperature of the water supply pipe a steam heating element temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the steam heating element a water detection sensor for detecting water in the water supply pipe a steam generating switch for instructing steam generation according to manual operation a display unit for displaying various conditions related to preheating thawing and steam generation in the state of receiving the power supply the freezing of the water supply pipe is checked through the water supply pipe temperature sensor the heater power is applied to the steam heating element to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe and while the steam is generated according to the instruction of the steam generation switch a controller for notifying the user of a water supply abnormality state by checking a water supply abnormality state of the water supply pipe through the sensor and controlling the steam heating element in response to the water supply abnormality state to prevent overheating of the steam heating element a power switch for switching the input of the ac power source by manual operation and a transforming unit for converting a voltage of a power source applied through the power switch and supplying the converted voltage to the control unit as a control power source to use the control unit as its own circuit driving power source and a power supply for operating the heater and a power supply for operating the pump are supplied to the control unit through the power switch"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the control unit a heater power switching unit for controlling the heating of the steam heating element by switching the power source for heater operation applied through the power switch according to the control of the microprocessor a pump power switching unit for switching the pump power supply applied through the power switch according to the control of the microprocessor to control the driving of the pump in the case of heating the steam heating element to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe while receiving the power through the power switch the steam heating element is heated while grasping the temperature of the water supply pipe through the water supply pipe temperature sensor the steam heating element is heated in a stepwise manner so as to reach a set heating temperature corresponding to the detected temperature of the water supply pipe by applying the heater power to the steam heating element a microprocessor for controlling the duty cycle of the heater power applied to the steam heating element by controlling the duty of the steam heating element when the temperature reaches a predetermined temperature thereby reducing the power supplied to the steam heating element and a control power source for rectifying the control power applied through the transformer and supplying the rectified control power to the microprocessor the heater power switching unit the pump power switching unit and the display unit as the driving power"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a heating control method for a steam cracking device when the control unit confirms that the temperature of the water supply pipe measured through the water supply pipe temperature sensor corresponds to the freezing temperature while the power switch is on the control by the operation of the steam generating switch is locked and the freeze led turning on the lamp to inform the user that it is in a frozen state the control unit notifying the user that the defrosting led lamp of the display unit is being turned on while the heater power is being applied to the steam heating element controlling the heater power supply to the steam heating body so that the control unit heats the steam heating body to reach the set heating temperature corresponding to the temperature of the water supply pipe measured through the water supply pipe temperature sensor thereby heating the steam heating body stepwise if the control unit determines that the temperature of the steam heating element measured through the steam heating element temperature sensor is not lower than the predetermined temperature cutting off the heater power supply to the steam heating element by the heater power switching part and terminating the thawing process if the control unit confirms that the temperature of the water supply pipe measured through the water pipe temperature sensor is equal to or higher than the set thawing temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a heating control method for a steam cracking device a step of applying a heater power to the steam heating element when the steam generating switch is turned on while the power switch is turned on and measuring the temperature of the steam heating element through the steam heating element temperature sensor if the controller determines that the measured temperature of the steam heating element is lower than or equal to a set specific temperature the controller may continue applying the heater power to the steam heating element when the control unit confirms that the water supply pipe is not supplied with water through the water detection sensor the water supply led of the display unit is blinked and the buzzer is driven to inform the user that the water supply is abnormal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this way when the remaining freezing water in the heating tube is continuously heated by the heater the ice of the heating tube instantaneously vaporizes over the boiling point to the vapor state so that the vaporization pressure may be increased and the vaporized vapor may be discharged somewhere however if there is no outlet the heating pipe may be exploded by the high pressure by the vaporized steam which may cause the steam freezing state to be unusable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "10 1157388 registered on june 11 2012 the present invention has been made in order to solve the problems of the conventional art as described above and it is an object of the present invention to provide a steam generating device which is capable of preheating a steam heating element the speed of the steam thawing operation is improved by preparing steam for stable and rapid freezing of the water supply pipe of the steam generator to control the steam heating element in response to an abnormal state of the feed water during the steam generation it is possible to prevent overheating of the steam heating element due to overheating by preventing the overheating of the steam heating element by preventing the overheating of the steam heating element due to the shortage of the water temporarily or the water supply failure and a heating control method thereof the purpose is to provide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to achieve the above mentioned object the present invention provides a steam generator comprising a steam heating element for generating water by heating water supplied through a water supply pipe a pump for introducing water into the water supply pipe a water supply pipe temperature sensor for detecting the temperature of the water supply pipe a steam heating element temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the steam heating element a water detection sensor for detecting water in the water supply pipe a steam generating switch for instructing steam generation according to manual operation a display unit for displaying various conditions related to preheating thawing and steam generation in the state of receiving the power supply the freezing of the water supply pipe is checked through the water supply pipe temperature sensor the heater power is applied to the steam heating element to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe and while the steam is generated according to the instruction of the steam generation switch a controller for notifying the user of a water supply abnormality state by checking a water supply abnormality state of the water supply pipe through the sensor and controlling the steam heating element in response to the water supply abnormality state to prevent overheating of the steam heating element a power switch for switching the input of the ac power source by manual operation and a transforming unit for converting a voltage of a power source applied through the power switch and supplying the converted voltage to the control unit as a control power source to use the control unit as its own circuit driving power source and a power source for operating the heater and a power source for driving the pump are supplied to the control unit through the power switch"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a steam defrosting apparatus comprising a heater power switching unit that controls heating of a steam heating element by switching a power source for heater operation applied through a power switch under the control of a microprocessor a pump power switching unit for switching the pump power supply applied through the power switch according to the control of the microprocessor to control the driving of the pump in the case of heating the steam heating element to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe while receiving the power through the power switch the steam heating element is heated while grasping the temperature of the water supply pipe through the water supply pipe temperature sensor the steam heating element is heated in a stepwise manner so as to reach a set heating temperature corresponding to the detected temperature of the water supply pipe by applying the heater power to the steam heating element a microprocessor for controlling the duty cycle of the heater power applied to the steam heating element by controlling the duty of the steam heating element when the temperature reaches a predetermined temperature thereby reducing the power supplied to the steam heating element and a control power source for rectifying the control power applied through the transformer and supplying the power to the microprocessor the heater power switch the pump power switch and the display as drive power"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to a first aspect of the present invention there is provided a method for controlling heating of a steam cracking device comprising the steps of when a power switch is turned on if it is confirmed that the temperature of the supply pipe corresponds to the sub zero temperature the step of locking the control by the operation of the steam generating switch and notifying the user that the frozen led lamp of the display unit is in the frozen state the control unit notifying the user that the defrosting led lamp of the display unit is being turned on while the heater power is being applied to the steam heating element controlling the heater power supply to the steam heating body so that the control unit heats the steam heating body to reach the set heating temperature corresponding to the temperature of the water supply pipe measured through the water supply pipe temperature sensor thereby heating the steam heating body stepwise if the control unit determines that the temperature of the steam heating element measured through the steam heating element temperature sensor is not lower than the predetermined temperature cutting off the heater power supply to the steam heating element by the heater power switching part and terminating the defrosting process if the control unit confirms that the temperature of the water supply pipe measured through the water supply pipe temperature sensor is equal to or higher than the set freeze off temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "according to a third aspect of the present invention there is provided a method for controlling heating of a steam cracking device wherein a steam generating switch is turned on in a state where a power switch is turned on measuring a temperature of the steam heating element through a steam heating element temperature sensor by applying a heater power to the steam heating element if the controller determines that the measured temperature of the steam heating element is lower than or equal to a set specific temperature the controller may continue applying the heater power to the steam heating element when the control unit confirms that the water supply pipe is not supplied with water through the water detection sensor the water supply led of the display unit is blinked and the buzzer is driven to inform the user that the water supply is abnormal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the control unit 150 measures the temperature of the water supply pipe 113 through the water supply pipe temperature sensor 125 when the power switch 160 is turned on so that the temperature measurement value of the water supply pipe 113 is set to a subzero temperature the steam heating element 140 is heated so that the freezing of the water supply pipe 113 is heated and the steam heating element 140 is preheated to maintain the set temperature when the temperature measurement value of the water supply pipe 113 corresponds to the image temperature thereby preparing to generate steam"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "when the steam heating element 140 is heated to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe 113 the microprocessor 151 detects the temperature of the water supply pipe 113 through the water supply pipe temperature sensor 125 the steam heating element 140 is heated by the heater power switch 152 so as to reach the set heating temperature corresponding to the detected temperature of the water supply pipe 113 the steam heating element 140 is heated step by step so that the water supply pipe 113 is gradually heated to prevent a sudden increase in the vaporization pressure due to the rapid overheating of the water supply pipe 113"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "according to the present invention regardless of whether or not the steam generating operation is instructed in a state in which power is input to the steam defrosting apparatus the steam heating element is preheated to prepare for steam generation and the freezing of its own water supply pipe is steadily and quickly thawed in winter thereby preventing the steam heating element from overheating due to insufficient water supply or water supply failure by controlling the steam heating element in response to occurrence of abnormality in the supply water during steam generation the steam heating element is prevented from being overheated by controlling the heating of the steam heating element so as not to reach the overheated state in case of shortage or water supply failure thereby preventing the interruption of the steam freezing operation due to overheating.100 a steam cracker 110 pump 113 a water supply pipe 120 water sensor 125 a water supply pipe temperature sensor 130 steam heating element temperature sensor 140 steam heating element 150 the control unit 151 a microprocessor 152 heater power switching part 153 a pump power switching unit 154 control power supply 160 power switch 165 the transformer 170 a steam generating switch 180 display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102602389-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should include not only the above embodiments but also other variously modified embodiments according to the technical spirit of the invention described in the claims below.10 body 11 protruding end 11a 1st pass 11b second pass 11c third pass 12 1st peduncle 13 printed circuit board 20 water tank 21 exterior wall 22 inner wall 23 insulation 24 receptor 25 second peduncle 30 connection information board 31 1st wit home 32 2nd wit home 33 self adhering member 40 temperature sensor 50 sterilization lamp 60 water level sensor 70 cooling means 71 thermoelectric element 72 cooling rod 73 water cooler 73a water block 73b first connection hose 73c second connection hose 73d radiator 73e circulation pump 73f cooling fan 80 water fountain 81 water nozzle 82 water level control ball 83 auxiliary water nozzle 90 water supply means 91 proximity sensor 92 water pump 93 water hose 100 height adjustable 110 recovery stand 111 recovery plate 111a drain hole 111b 1st hose passage hole 112 noise reduction hopper 112a second hose passage hole 113 filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "valve 44 at an outlet of deuterium separation container 30 is connected via a conduit 48 to an inlet of a tank 50 which forms a part of an irradiation unit 52"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100643176-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "it is configured to prevent the phenomenon from occurring and to prevent freezing and condensation due to the temperature difference between the temperature inside the sensor unit 52 and the sample when measuring the sample in a low temperature state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100897438-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level detecting means is installed on the inner bottom surface of the water tank and has a body in which deformation occurs according to the hydraulic pressure of the fluid filled in the water tank and the first optical fiber grating sensor is installed in the body of the fluid it is formed to measure the deformation amount of the main body generated by the hydraulic pressure in accordance with the filling amount the motor temperature measuring means is attached to one side of the motor so that the heat generated by the drive of the motor can be transferred the third optical fiber grating sensor is preferably installed inside the main body so as to measure the amount of deformation of the main body due to heat generated from the motor.the control device of the water treatment plant according to the present invention accurately measures the flow rate of water supplied or returned to each tank for the purification of sewage the water level of the sewage filled in each tank and the temperature of the motors thereby effectively purifying the chemical"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991257-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "50 the groundwater to be measured is the water temperature temperature electrical conductivity conductivity salinity salinity dissolved oxygen dissolved oxygen hydrogen ion concentration ph oxidation reduction potential orp depth to view and analyze each water temperature monitoring sensor 51 electrical conductivity monitoring sensor 52 salinity monitoring sensor 53 dissolved oxygen monitoring sensor 54 hydrogen ion concentration monitoring sensor 55 redox power monitoring sensor 56 water level monitoring it is configured to include a sensor 57 and is connected to the processor control 22 through the data port 24 of the data logger 20 while being installed at the ground water depth of the groundwater well 40"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3807221-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the one or more additional sensors can include a temperature sensor a ph sensor an oxidation reduction potential orp sensor a conductivity sensor an inductive conductivity sensor a corrosion monitoring sensor for a specific metal such as copper and different types of steel biofilm monitoring devices chemical fouling devices turbidity monitoring devices and online instruments for measuring residual biocides such as free and total chlorine"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3652115-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "lastly it helps act as a thermal insulator and therefore decreases the thermal leakage in undesired directions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "for example the error state data includes an error state open or short for the hot water temperature sensor 634 or the cold water temperature sensor 624 a leak state such as cold hot water there may be a state in which the lamp 633 is heated for more than the threshold time during heating of the heater 633 a state in which the evaporator 623 is operated for more than the threshold time at the time of heating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold hot water supply device 100 and may include for example a water level sensor 612 cold water hot water temperature sensors 624 and 634 wire or the like sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640 660 a water leakage sensor 670 one or more overflow sensors 690 can do"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "this hybrid pressure protection system combines relief and block functions in one unit and not only release overpressure fluid into lower pressure zone but also isolate overpressure fluid from normal pressures zone with novel thermal actuators and simple normal open and normal closed valves this system greatly reduce total executing time and increase reliability with at least two redundancies the block subsystem has a normal open standard pressure class valve integrated with the thermal actuation system and has the isolating time less than 2 second without damaging seat and shaft seal packing the releasing subsystem has a normal closed standard pressure class valve integrated with the thermal actuation system and has the releasing time less than 2 second without damaging seat and shaft seal packing the system with redundancy feature for the valves and the actuators include at least two pressure sensing devices combination of blocking and relief at the same time greatly reduce the system cost and has the highest level of system reliability over all prior arts or existing products"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the control chamber assembly is the brain of the system in this invention it combines all control elements pre set condition sensing and judgment seamlessly as one unit at the highest level of adaptability and controllability for most control applications like the level control as the sense piston move up and down as a liquid level increase or decrease in the sensing cavity or temperature control as a temperate change in the sensing cavity the piston can move up and down or motion control and so on the control chamber assembly is based on two human brain function with two systems high level of control of the cerebrum system and a low level control of the cerebellum system at the cerebrum system the control chamber can make decision either to release restore or block the line pressure and acts with or without electric signal or power and with a self feedback function from the line pressure while at the cerebellum system it check the set pressure in the activity cavity against the line pressure in the sensing cavity with the center shutter valve safety valve the pressure sensor as redundant devices at the low level of control the valve functions become simpler and is no longer to define a block valve or relief valve just simple normal closed and normal open valves it integrates this pressure protection system at the lightest level of reliability simplicity and lowest level of barrier over all exiting pressure systems in the market or in research and over all prior arts while electronic sensor digital control wireless communication devices still can be added on this system to communicate with other devices or human through buses like profit bus foundation bus or wireless communication the control chamber system can be used for both linear or rotary actuation system and subsea bop or valve or tree well flow or pressure controls so there is no block or release but release block actuator only single control chamber system it not only increase integrity of protection system but also simplify the valve design and selection and eliminate the partial stroke testing by switching functions between normally open positions to normally closed in the two valves with full stroke test and increase the reliability"}, {"pat_id": "US-5993669-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the information regarding flow rate temperature and conductivity which is monitored by sensor 32 is sent to controller 38 via line 40"}, {"pat_id": "US-7403839-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "such sensors 12 can be hard wired into the electrical supply of the structure or battery operated but are preferably hard wired and include a battery backup in the event of a power failure a condition where flooding is more likely"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "in another embodiment not covered by the claimed invention moreover the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after pressure such for example a cylindrical body so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "preferably in addition the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after liquid flow so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468179-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is difficult to find a sensor on the market that can detect leakage while enduring high temperature particularly in a very high temperature pipe.accordingly the present invention has an object to provide a leak detection device that can withstand high temperatures and can stably detect leakage.leakage detection device according to an embodiment of the present invention a plurality of heat shields made of an insulating material and a pair of through holes formed in parallel the plurality of heat shields in series through a pair of through holes of the heat shield and a sensing unit connected to the wire and connected to the wire to measure a resistance change due to the energization caused by the fluid leaked from the pipe.as described above according to the present invention the wire is formed to penetrate into the heat shield made of insulating material thereby preventing heat conduction to the leak detection device so that the leak can be stably detected for a long time in a pipe where a high temperature fluid flows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "is installed outside the water tank 1 to control the operation of the heater member 20 when the temperature of the water in the water tank 1 is 30 or more or 4 or less by operating the heater member 20 when the temperature of the water in the water tank 1 by the above described water temperature sensor 23 in the summer season is 30 or more by operating the heater member 20 to pasteurize the temperature of the water in the water tank 1 in winter when 4 or less to operate the heater member 20 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "or lower the water tank 1 the heater member 20 is operated to maintain the temperature of the water inside 4 6 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "in addition although the external temperature of the winter season is measured by the external temperature sensor but may be lower than the temperature actually measured by obstacles or other factors such as wind the controller 30 of the present invention has an external temperature of 4 when the temperature of the water inside the water tank 1 becomes 4 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "thus a single set of localized sensors flow rate sensor 105 optional pressure sensor 65 optional acoustic sensor and or optional temperature sensor 93 can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "washing machine dishwasher shower for a time period and the water meter and leak detection system s monitors the water flow rate water duration and total water volume and if applicable utilizes optional temperature sensors optional pressure sensors and optional acoustic sensors to observe patterns water valves movement and noise to identify water valves for specific water use devices"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "to increase wireless range and provide compatibility with wireless routers or corporate networks the water meter and leak detection system 10 126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_145", "text": "for measuring or monitoring the temperature of the water flowing through the water meter and leak detection system 10 126 the use of various thermocouples or thermistor sensors 70 as depicted in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and an object of the present invention is to accurately check the water level by sensing the water level and temperature in the storage tank through the water level sensor and the temperature sensor to send to the storage tank remote water level management can effectively control the quantity and use the water level sensor as an ultrasonic sensor to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and to prevent the water level from being incorrectly detected due to breakage or malfunction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the configuration of the present invention for achieving the above object the motor pump for supplying the raw water is supplied to the storage tank remotely through the pipe and installed in the intake well and the inner upper side of the storage tank to sense the water level of the storage tank an ultrasonic sensor installed in the outer circumferential surface to prevent freezing a temperature sensing sensor installed inside the storage tank to measure a temperature in the storage tank and installed outside the storage tank and measured from the ultrasonic sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "on the other hand the ultrasonic sensor 30 is not frozen even in winter as it is installed in the storage tank 20 but there is room for freezing when the temperature is drastically lowered so as to prevent this ultrasonic sensor as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "on the other hand when the winter temperature is lowered below the set temperature the heater 32 is operated to prevent the ultrasonic sensor from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11505478-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the automated chemical dosing system may but need not further comprise a chlorine dosing device positioned downstream of the coagulant dosing device and the acid base dosing device and any one or more of a turbidity sensor positioned upstream of the coagulant dosing device and the acid base dosing device and configured to collect data relating to the turbidity of the water stream and communicate these data to the computer an iron and or manganese content sensor positioned upstream of the coagulant dosing device and the acid base dosing device and configured to collect data relating to the iron and or manganese content of the water stream and communicate these data to the computer an additional organics sensor selected from the group consisting of a toc sensor and a uv254 sensor positioned upstream of the coagulant dosing device and the acid base dosing device or downstream of the chlorine dosing device and configured to collect data relating to the organic contaminant content of the water stream and communicate these data to the computer at least one additional ph and temperature sensor positioned upstream of the coagulant dosing device and the acid base dosing device or downstream of the chlorine dosing device and configured to collect data relating to the ph and temperature of the water stream and communicate these data to the computer and at least one sensor positioned downstream of the chlorine dosing device and configured to collect data relating to the concentration of at least one of chloride sulfate and chlorine in the water stream and communicate these data to the computer and the instructions when executed by the processor may but need not cause the processor to further perform the steps of determining in a fourth pid control loop and based on the data communicated to the computer a target disinfection parameter setpoint or range and commanding in the fourth pid control loop the chlorine dosing device to increase decrease or maintain a chlorine dosing rate to achieve the target disinfection parameter setpoint or range"}, {"pat_id": "US-11505478-B2", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "1 is a block diagram illustrating elements of an exemplary computing device in which embodiments of the present disclosure may be implemented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102355027-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an outer housing 10 having a frame structure having a predetermined size the inner housing 20 is installed inside the outer housing 10 the upper surface is opened to accommodate the object to be treated therein a stirring unit 30 installed horizontally inside the inner housing 20 to stir the object to be treated a driving unit 40 installed on an outer side of the inner housing 20 to rotate the stirring unit 30 a heating unit 50 installed along the inner bottom surface of the inner housing 20 to heat the inner housing 20 an air exhaust unit 60 installed on one upper side of the inner housing 20 to discharge the air of the inner housing 20 to the outside an air supply unit 70 installed inside the outer housing 10 to supply compressed air into the inner housing 20 and a controller 80 installed on one side of the outer housing 10 to control the operation of the driving unit 40 the heating unit 50 the air exhaust unit 60 and the air supply unit 70 including the stirring unit 30 a rotating shaft 31 installed to horizontally cross the inner housing 20 a plurality of fixing clamps 32 installed at predetermined intervals on the rotating shaft 31 a mounting table 33 of a predetermined length installed on the plurality of fixing clamps 32 a main stirring blade 34 installed on the mounting table 33 including the mounting base 33 is it is arranged so as to be spaced apart from another adjacent installation table 33 by 90 the main stirring blade 34 is two or more are installed so as to connect the ends of the three adjacent installation tables 33 in an arc shape to space them 180 apart in the fixing clamp 32 auxiliary stirring blades 35 of a predetermined length are installed at intervals of 90 from the mounting table 33 so that the object to be treated is stirred between the rotation shaft 31 and the main stirring blades 34 the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is the tip of the three auxiliary stirring blades 35 is connected and formed in an arc shape in the opposite direction to the main stirring blade 34 the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is the tip is installed to be inclined at a predetermined angle a to one side with respect to the fixing clamp 32 and the tip of the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is positioned in the space between the pair of installation tables 33 the heating unit 50 a rectangular shaped body 51 with an open upper surface a heater 52 installed on one side of the main body 51 and installed to have a predetermined length in a horizontal direction including in the body 51 a temperature sensor 53 for detecting the temperature of the thermal medium stored therein and an inlet and outlet pipe 54 for supplying heat medium oil to the inside of the body 51 or discharging the inside heat medium oil to the outside is provided the heating unit 50 it is installed horizontally along the middle part of the bottom surface of the inner housing 20 and is integrally fixed by welding the air exhaust unit 60 it is configured so that the air and moisture inside the inner housing 20 are discharged together the air supply unit 70 compressor 71 for generating compressed air a flow path 72 connected to the compressor 71 and a plurality of injection nozzles connected to the flow path 72 and supplying compressed air to the inside of the inner housing 20 including between the injection nozzle and the flow path 72 food characterized in that a check valve 73 is installed to allow compressed air to be discharged toward the inner housing 20 and to block moisture inside the inner housing 20 from being discharged through the flow path 72"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681403-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition in order to solve the problem that the water of the body is frozen and the ceramic insulator is broken if the outside air temperature in winter falls below freezing for a long time without using active water acco