ted on the inlet side of the condenser 5 see fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021123-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body having an inlet through which water is introduced and an outlet through which silver ionized water is discharged a purified water filter installed in the main body to purify water and a silver ionizer installed in the main body to produce silver ionized water through electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021123-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a main body having an inlet through which water is introduced and an outlet through which silver ionized water is discharged a silver ionizer installed in the main body to produce silver ionized water through electrolysis a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of water introduced into the main body and in the control method of the silver ionized water production apparatus comprising a control unit for controlling the power applied to the ionizer after sensing the temperature of the water flowing into the main body the production of silver ion water is characterized in that the voltage applied to the silver ionization device is lowered as the temperature of the water flowing into the main body increases and the voltage applied to the silver ionization device increases as the temperature of the water flowing into the main body decreases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021123-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a main body having an inlet through which water is introduced and an outlet through which silver ionized water is discharged a silver ionization device installed in the main body to produce silver ionized water through electrolysis a flow rate sensor for detecting the amount of water introduced into the main body and in the control method of the silver ionized water production apparatus comprising a temperature sensor for sensing the temperature of the water flowing into the main body and a control unit for controlling the power applied to the ionizer after sensing the amount and temperature of water flowing into the main body as the amount of water flowing into the main body increases the voltage applied to the silver ionizer is controlled to increase"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0752203-Y2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "this means that the non freezing temperature of 0 to 2 c or higher is set as the energization time of 0 while the lowest expected temperature is set as the energization time of 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0752203-Y2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the unit body 1 includes a power supply circuit 4 a differential amplification circuit 5 a gain adjustment circuit 6 a schmitt circuit 7 a trigger circuit 8 and a switching circuit 9 on a substrate 14 housed in a casing 11 and the temperature sensor 2 described above is used"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0752203-Y2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "then the energization display led 16 lights up the heater 3 connected via the outlet 10 provided in the casing 11 is heated and the water temperature in the water pipe 20 is warmed so as not to be below freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102641234-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a lid portion that rotates to connect or separate the pumping portion from the container portion a necklace portion connected to the case portion or the lid portion an ozonated water generator installed inside the container unit to generate ozonated water within the container unit through electrolysis a lighting unit disposed on one side of the ozonated water generating unit and illuminating light of different colors according to a driving time mode of the ozonated water generating unit a heating unit disposed on the other side of the ozone water generating unit to maintain the water inside the container unit at a constant temperature a body temperature sensor unit provided on one side of the case unit a display unit provided on the other side of the case unit to display the body temperature detected by the body temperature sensor unit a power supply unit that receives power from the outside a control unit provided at the bottom of the case unit to receive a user s control command and a control module unit disposed in the lower space of the case unit and controlling the operation of the ozone water generator the lighting unit the heating unit the body temperature sensor unit and the display unit according to an input signal from the operation unit including a user"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101338951-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "to prevent damage to the sensor the exhaust air was cooled through a condenser to condense the vapor before reaching the gas analyzer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a fluid accommodating member in which fluid freezing at a low temperature and increasing in volume thereof is accommodated therein one side has an open cylindrical shape the outer circumferential surface is formed with a male screw to be screwable the middle portion of the inner receiving space is formed with a locking projection protruding to a predetermined height the other end of the outer member formed with a female screw and the inner diameter is inserted into the inner receiving space of the outer member has a cylindrical shape that is moved in the longitudinal direction and the o ring is mounted on one end thereof and the inner diameter reduced to be slidable through the locking jaw from the middle region to the other end the stepped surface is formed and the inner end of the stepped surface is formed with a male screw the male screw of the inner member is fastened to the locking jaw to prevent the inner member is separated from the outside of the outer member the inner receiving space of the outer member is fastened to the stopper and the female screw formed on the other end of the outer member a ground member having a rod shape protruding from the inner surface of the inner member and a ground terminal to which the other end surface of the inner member is temporarily in contact with the inner member to generate a detection signal and one side surface of the inner member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in this case when the pressure sensed by the pressure sensor is greater than a predetermined pressure the solenoid valve is operated to flow the fluid contained in the fluid receiving member to prevent freezing to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as the solenoid valve 22 is operated as described above to flow out the fluid in the stopped state until the frozen fluid melts preventing the fluid from freezing due to the fluid flow inside the pipeline of the water pipe 11 and at the same time it will thaw the frozen fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at least one temperature sensor installed at two or more different locations in the room a heater a fan blowing the air heated by the heater and a freeze protection device of a hot air heater including a power supply as a freeze protection method performed to prevent freezing measuring the indoor temperature through a temperature sensor every sensing cycle in a state in which power is not supplied to the heater and the fan from the power supply wow and controlling the operation of the heater and the fan by controlling the supply of power from the power supply unit to the heater and the fan based on the moving average temperatures obtained by moving average of the measured indoor temperatures the step of controlling the operation of the heater and the fan when the indoor temperature is measured by the temperature sensors installed at two or more different locations the lowest indoor temperature among the indoor temperatures measured by the temperature sensors installed at each of the two different locations is calculated as the moving average temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method according to claim 1 or 3 measuring the indoor temperature through a temperature sensor while generating and blowing warm air by operating the heater and the fan wow the freeze protection method further comprising the step of stopping the operation of the heater and the fan when the indoor temperature measured while blowing the warm air is equal to or greater than the freezing prevention safe temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "accordingly the operation of the hot air fan to prevent freezing of the water pipe or the like can be performed in a timely manner"}, {"pat_id": "US-5555747-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a directional freeze crystallization system comprising a a crystallizer means consisting of a heat exchanger b a vessel for containing liquid to be purified c a cooling means for conveying a heat transfer fluid to said heat exchanger said heat transfer fluid being at a temperature less than the freezing point of said liquid to be purified d a filling means for conveying said liquid to be purified into said vessel e a draining means for conveying unfrozen liquid from said vessel f a heating means for melting ice frozen on said heat exchanger g a transfer means for conveying melted ice from said vessel h an accumulator connected by a fluid conduit to said vessel i a quantity sensor to determine the volume of unfrozen liquid in said accumulator j a state sensor to determine the absence of frozen liquid in said vessel j control means for repeatedly sequentially actuating said filling means cooling means draining means heating means and transfer means responsive to said quantity sensor and said state sensor to fill said vessel with liquid to be purified freeze a fraction of said liquid to be purified adjacent to said heat exchanger drain the unfrozen fraction of said liquid to be purified melt the frozen fraction of said liquid to be purified and convey the melted fraction from said vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-12043992-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the meter data may include readings from temperature sensors at the windings of the transformer"}, {"pat_id": "US-12043992-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "5 where short circuit alerts in conjunction with over temperature alerts may indicate a fire short circuit alerts with the absence of over temperature alerts tamper alerts or other alerts would indicate a flood rather than another type of event e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a method of monitoring and controlling a low carbon permeable ecological structure consisting of a plurality of corrosion resistant piles a plurality of horizontal framing frames in the form of spacers an ecological block for water purification and an ecological block for fishes and fishes first the low carbon permeable ecological installed at a predetermined position of the structure 100 receives the detected data from a plurality of sensors 210 to detect the conductivity water quality water temperature or quantity of river water by wire or wireless"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the pipe 310 and the vertical pipe 310 are installed in the upper and lower positions respectively to guide water to be purified while passing water in the upper and lower zigzag directions and a net 331 form a temperature sensor 340 for providing information to the controller 700 by frequently checking the temperature inside the water purification natural mineral particles 330 and the water purification tube 300 which are contained in a bag of and filled in the vertical tube 310 and the in accordance with the operation control of the controller 700 that received the information from the temperature sensor 340 the heating wire 350 that operates to prevent freezing and the water purification tube 300 prevents foreign substances from flowing into the interior and at the same time natural mineral particles for water purification the vertical pipe 310 according to the operation control of the airtight cover 360 for cleaning 330 and the controller 700 installed under the vertical pipe 310 to receive information from the ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 a water purification tube 300 including an electromagnetic valve 370 for individually washing the natural mineral particles 330 for water purification by water pressure by opening and closing the lower portion of the water purification body wow a branch pipe 400 connected so that the drinking water treated while passing through the purified water pipe 300 may be supplied to a storage tank or a user and an ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 fixed to the side of the branch pipe 400 to check the turbidity of water and provide information to the controller 700 wow a flow rate sensor 600 fixed to the side of the branch pipe 400 to check the flow rate of water and provide information to the controller 700 wow the supply pump 100 and the temperature sensor 340 the heating wire 350 the solenoid valve 370 the ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 and the flow rate sensor 600 are signal connected to control the supply pump 100 according to the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the supply pump 100 is connected the other side is a water supply pipe 200 connected to the water purification pipe 300 and the water supply pipe 200 and the water supply pipe 200 are connected and fixed to facilitate passage and the inside is for water purification at the same time as the natural mineral particles 330 are filled a plurality of vertical pipes 310 arranged in a vertical direction so that water can be passed through zigzag 3 to 5 times or more and at the upper and lower positions of the sides of the vertical pipe 310 respectively a water purification guide pipe 320 that is installed and guides water to be purified while passing through the upper and lower zigzag directions and a natural mineral particle 330 for water purification that is contained in a bag in the form of a net 331 and filled in the vertical pipe 310 wow according to the operation control of the temperature sensor 340 which provides information to the controller 700 by checking the temperature inside the water purification tube 300 from time to time and the controller 700 receiving the information from the temperature sensor 340"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at one side of the vertical pipe 310 a temperature sensor 340 that checks the temperature inside the water purification pipe 300 at any time and provides information to the controller 700 is installed and a controller receiving information from the temperature sensor 340 in accordance with the operation control of 700 a heating wire 350 that operates to prevent freezing is installed but the vertical pipe 310 and the water purification guide pipe 320 in which the heating wire 350 is installed become a pipe through which water passes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in addition in winter the controller 700 controls the operation to operate the heating wire 350 according to the value measured by the temperature sensor 340 to prevent freezing and the flow rate sensor 600 checks the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3774668-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "next at block 806 a functionality check of the tank temperature sensor 744 and a board temperature sensor not shown is run to determine if the sensors are operating properly within an acceptable temperature difference e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-4877519-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a waste water treatment system for high temperature hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream said system having a reactor constructed to operate at a sufficiently high temperature and pressure to effect hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream introduced to said reactor and a heat exchanger system with a means for flowing an influent waste water stream through said heat exchanger system prior to introduction to said reactor and a means for an effluent stream from said reactor through said heat exchanger system the improvement comprising said heat exchanger system having a first double pipe heat exchanger for said influent stream and a second double pipe heat exchanger for said effluent stream each of said double pipe heat exchangers having an inner tube which defines a tube side tube of the heat exchanger and an annular space between an outer tubular shell and said inner tube to define an annular space tube of the heat exchanger said first and second heat exchanger each having an inlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an inlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger a first conduit for delivering said influent stream to said tube side inlet of first heat exchanger a second conduit for delivering said effluent stream from said reactor to said tube side inlet of said second heat exchanger said first and second heat exchanger each having an outlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an outlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger means for circulating a heat exchange medium through said annular space inlets and outlets of said first and second heat exchangers to preheat said influent stream prior to introduction into said reactor where energy for preheating is extracted by said second heat exchanger from said effluent stream passing through said second heat exchanger to add heat energy to said heat exchange medium said first heat exchanger removing heat energy from said heat exchange medium to preheat said influent stream whereby influent and effluent streams pass through said tube side of each inner tube of said first and second heat exchangers to minimize clogging of said first and second heat exchanger said reactor comprising a closed vessel with an inlet and an outlet a third conduit extending from said tube side outlet of said first heat exchanger to said reactor inlet said second conduit being connected to said reactor outlet said reactor having a level control device located below said inlet to provide a liquid level in said reactor below said inlet to ensure that said inlet is above reacting liquid in said reactor said outlet located at a lower level in said reactor to define a downflow reactor zone said level control device comprising a control valve for controlling liquid flow in said reactor located below said inlet said liquid level sensor generating a signal to open fully said control valve when said liquid level sensor senses liquid means for fully closing said valve after sufficient liquid is drained from said reactor to drop reacting liquid level below said liquid level sensor to provide an intermittent flow of effluent to said second conduit"}, {"pat_id": "US-4877519-A", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "in a waste water treatment system for high temperature hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream said system having a reactor constructed to operate at a sufficiently high temperature and pressure to effect hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream introduced to said reactor and a heat exchanger system with means for flowing an an influent waste water stream flowing through said heat exchanger system prior to introduction to said reactor and a means for flowing an effluent stream from said reactor through said heat exchanger system the improvement comprising said heat exchanger system having a first double pipe heat exchanger for said influent stream and a second double pipe heat exchanger for said effluent stream each of said double pipe heat exchangers having an inner tube which defines a tube side tube of the heat exchanger and an annular space between an outer tubular shell and said inner tube to define an annular space tube of the heat exchanger said first and second heat exchangers each having an inlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and inlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger a first conduit for delivering said influent stream to said tube side inlet of said first heat exchanger a second conduit for delivering said effluent stream from said reactor to said tube side inlet of said second heat exchanger said first and second heat exchangers each having an outlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an outlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger means for circulating a heat exchange medium through said annular space inlets and outlets of said first and second heat exchangers to preheat said influent stream prior to introduction into said reactor where energy for preheating is extracted by said second heat exchanger from said effluent stream passing through said second heat exchanger to add heat energy to said heat exchange medium said first heat exchanger removing heat energy from said heat exchange medium to preheat said influent stream whereby influent and effluent streams pass through said tube side of each inner tube of said first and second heat exchangers to minimize clogging of said first and second heat exchangers said reactor comprising a closed vessel with an inlet and an outlet a third conduit extending from said outlet of said first heat exchanger to said reactor inlet said second conduit being connected to said reactor outlet said reactor having a level control device located below said inlet to provide a liquid level in said reactor below said inlet to ensure that said inlet is above reacting liquid in said reactor said outlet is at a lower level in said reactor to define a downflow reactor zone said level control device comprising a control valve for controlling liquid flow in said second conduit and a liquid level sensor in said reactor located below said inlet said liquid level sensor generating a signal to open fully said control valve when said liquid level sensor senses liquid means for fully closing said valve after sufficient liquid is drained from said reactor to drop reacting liquid level below said liquid level sensor to provide an intermittent flow of effluent to said second conduit wherein said control valve is a ball valve with a fully open position and a fully closed position said fully open position of said ball valve avoiding clogging and abrasion of said ball valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-4877519-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a waste water treatment system for high temperature hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream said system comprising a reactor constructed to operate at a sufficiently high temperature and pressure to effect hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream introduced to said reactor a heat exchanger system through which an influent waste water stream flows prior to introduction to said reactor and an effluent stream flows after treatment in said reactor the heat exchanger system comprising a first double pipe heat exchanger for said influent stream and a second double pipe heat exchanger for said effluent stream each of said double pipe heat exchangers having an inner tube which defines a tube side tube of the heat exchanger and an annular space between an outer tubular shell and said inner tube to define an annular space of the heat exchanger said first and second heat exchangers each having an inlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an inlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger a first conduit for delivering said influent stream to said tube side inlet of said first heat exchanger a second conduit for delivering said effluent stream from said reactor to said tube side inlet of said second heat exchanger said first and second heat exchangers each having an outlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an outlet means for circulating a heat exchange medium through said annular space inlets and outlets of said first and second heat exchangers to preheat said influent stream prior to introduction into said reactor where energy for preheating is extracted by said second heat exchanger from said effluent stream passing through said second heat exchanger to add heat energy to said heat exchange medium said first heat exchanger removing heat energy form said heat exchange medium to preheat said influent stream whereby influent and effluent streams pass through said tube side of each inner tube of said first and second heat exchangers to minimize clogging of said first and second heat exchangers a surge tank in fluid communications with and located downstream of said first heat exchanger and upstream of said second heat exchanger a variable speed pump associated with said surge tank said pump being located in said second conduit and having means for adjusting the flow rate in said first conduit and means for controlling the speed of said pump including a temperature sensor located in said first conduit"}, {"pat_id": "US-6171480-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the distributed control system dcs is composed of multiple sensors transducers that convert environmental conditions into electrical signals communication multiplexers that convert the sensor s electrical signals into digital code computer hardware that can receive the transmitted signals from and to the multiplexers computer hardware that interfaces to the human user and computer software configured to provide a graphical interface for representing floor plans trending incoming data and trending historical data"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "in other words in such embodiments fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40 for example via one or more external fluid conduits 62 such as a hose process block 98"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "additionally or alternatively determining the one or more fluid parameters associated with the fluid in the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 may include determining fluid temperature present within the tubing annulus 25 for example via an upstream fluid temperature sensor 58a process block 120"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "nevertheless in some such embodiments the predetermined duration threshold may be adaptively adjustable for example based at least in part on fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "for example a particular faucet when used may cause the flow pressure acceleration and or temperature sensor 244 240 238 248 readings to fluctuate in a predictable manner such that the pattern profile can be matched to current readings to conclude usage is occurring at a particular egress point"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "readings from the pressure sensor 524 are used to test the prv 408 well pump water supply freeze conditions and pipe for leaks as well as identify normal egress from the water fixtures and appliances"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the water heater system of claim 7 wherein the condensate collector 390 includes a drain 398 and wherein the controller 142 is further configured to determine a drain blockage of the drain 398 based on a comparison between a temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 and a temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418 when the water heater is in the heating mode optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller 142 when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "the method of claim 12 wherein the condensate collector 390 further includes a drain 398 configured to receive the condensate the method further comprising determining a drain blockage of the drain 398 by the controller 142 based on a comparison between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 and the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418 when the water heater 10 is in the heating mode optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller 142 when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a controller ensures that a siphon filling programme is activated after a certain time period and uses a temperature sensor to determine the temperature in the area of the siphon"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the method further includes monitoring by a controller a rate of temperature change detected by a first temperature sensor positioned to sense a temperature of the condensate within a condensate collector of the exhaust assembly"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the o ring 170 is configured to inhibit leakage of a condensate stream e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the controller 142 concludes that the cause of the stagnation is a blockage somewhere in the drain assembly 90 e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "for example should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c one f to three f between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "if during the standby mode the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 114 are different than different leakage rates may be indicated to the controller"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "in particular the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "the leakage temperature limit 690a may be proximate the maximum temperature limit 685a of the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "although the leaked water may lose some heat during the wait period 695 while accumulating in the drain pipe 394 this is not significant enough to prevent the change in state of the temperature reading from the negative rate of change to the positive rate or change or to prevent the increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "9 11 only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "further since any slight increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 at the end of the wait period 695 might indicate that there is a leak the controller may be able to detect even smaller leaks"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "alternatively the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "in particular when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the controller thus concludes at 550 that there is leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654101-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in more detail a bypass pipe for freeze and burst prevention is connected between the suction pipe and the discharge pipe so that the temperature detected by the temperature sensor in winter is lowered below the set temperature if there is no water flow because the user does not use water the pump is driven so that the pressure of the discharge pipe is higher than the opening pressure of the relief valve and water circulates through the bypass pipe to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654101-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore the purpose of the present invention is to connect a bypass pipe for freeze prevention between the suction pipe and the discharge pipe so that in the winter if the temperature detected by the temperature sensor falls below the set temperature and there is no water flow because the user does not use water the pump is driven so that the pressure of the discharge pipe is higher than the opening pressure of the relief valve allowing water to circulate through the bypass pipe thereby providing a freeze prevention water supply pressurization device and a control method thereof that can prevent freezing in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "on the other hand in the case of using a heating wire there is a concern of excessive use of energy a fire occurrence problem due to overheating and a loss of thermal insulation function due to breakage of the heating wire.the present invention was devised to improve such a conventional problem and it is configured to determine whether the intake pump is operated not only by the internal level of the water tank but also by the outside temperature detected by the temperature sensor so that water of water temperature higher than the outside temperature in winter is it is an object of the present invention to provide a freeze proof intermittent tap water to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe by heat exchange occurring in the process along the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101761216-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "preferably the oxidation reaction tank further comprises a chamber capable of receiving the transferred sample and a heating module surrounding the chamber wherein the chamber may be formed of a dual structure including an outer tube and an inner tube the heating module including a heater for heating the chamber and a temperature sensor for measuring the temperature inside the chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101761216-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "it is to be understood that the present invention is not limited to the above embodiments and various changes and modifications may be made by those skilled in the art without departing from the spirit and scope of the invention.10 total phosphorus or total nitrogen measuring device 100 sample and reagent supply unit 110 multi channel valve 200 sample and reagent feed pump 300 oxidation reaction tank 310 chamber 311 inner pipe 312 appearance 320 heating module 321 heater 322 temperature sensor 323 overheat prevention sensor 324 upper cover 325 lower cover 326 o ring 330 pressure valve 400 mixing feed pump 500 mixing tank 600 detector feed pump 700 detector 800 3 way valve 801 first port 802 second port 803 third port 900 sensing sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970306-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to form a negative electrode or a positive electrode separately so that the negative electrode or the positive electrode can be replaced individually during replacement due to corrosion breakage respectively.in order to achieve the above object the present invention is a sensor for measuring the temperature or hydrogen ion concentration such as constant sewage is coupled to the holder the amount of residual chlorine in which a negative electrode and a positive electrode is formed on one side of the holder a device for measuring the amount of residual chlorine in the indicator by measuring the amount of residual chlorine contained in the measured water by galvanic cell electrolysis by combining the measuring sensor separately"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "typical sensors for monitoring water quality in a spa include in line sensors which monitor physical parameters temperature and flow and chemical sensors which monitor conductivity oxidation reduction potential orp and acidity ph"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "temperature sensors traditionally used within the industry are of resistive temperature detector rtd type and are typically configured with a stainless steel dome to prevent malfunction due to corrosion and water ingress issues"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the sensor assemblies discussed herein provide an inexpensive water quality measure with a fast response time requiring little or no maintenance and a durability on the order of months of continuous use with minimal or no issues"}, {"pat_id": "US-10501343-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the one or more sensors probes or instruments may include for example flow meters water level sensors conductivity meters resistivity meters chemical concentration meters turbidity monitors chemical species specific concentration sensors temperature sensors ph sensors oxidation reduction potential orp sensors pressure sensors or any other sensor probe or scientific instrument useful for providing an indication of a desired characteristic or parameter of water entering or exiting any one or more of the one or more unit operations"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102340325-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "reservoir installed in various types of buildings for each region to store drinkable drinking water ph sensor to measure hydrogen ion concentration ph tds sensor to measure total dissolved solids tds in water liquid medium including a turbidity sensor for measuring the turbidity of the liquid medium a temperature sensor for measuring the temperature of the liquid medium and a residual chlorine sensor for measuring the residual chlorine of the liquid medium it is installed in each of the storage tanks to measure the water quality of drinking water in the storage tank water quality multi item iot sensor the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank measured by the water quality multi item iot sensor hydrogen ion concentration ph temperature temp total dissolved solids tds residual chlorine residual chlorine turbidity ntu dissolved oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp and conductivity cond a gateway that collects and analyzes data of multi item measurement values of water quality for each water tank transmitted from the gateway and builds a big data database a water quality management platform server that is used for water quality analysis a real time water quality information monitoring device that receives water quality multi item measurement data for each water tank from the water quality management platform server and monitors the water quality status of each water tank in each area in real time the real time water quality information the terminal of the environment safety officer and each water tank that receives an alarm message generated when any one of the water quality multi item measured value data approaches or reaches the standard value from the monitoring device and sends a cleaning request notification for the water tank to the cleaning company terminal transmitting water quality multi item measured value data to the lora gateway through the lora modem and transmitting the water quality multi item measured value data transmitted through the lora modem to the real time water quality information monitoring device through the lte network in the gateway at preset intervals a communication device wherein the water quality management platform server includes an iot sensor data collection unit for collecting water quality multi item measurement value data for each water tank transmitted from the gateway and water quality multi item measurement for each water tank collected by the iot sensor data collection unit value data iot sensor data water quality analysis unit that analyzes the water quality condition including real time measurement values for each water quality measurement item and the change value of the real time measurement values based on water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank collected by a big data analysis unit and the iot sensor data collection unit that analyzes big data in relation to environmental factors and information analyzed by the iot sensor data water quality analysis unit and the big data analysis unit and a monitoring system interworking unit for integrated interfacing by transmitting to the real time water quality information monitoring device wherein the real time water quality information monitoring device receives iot sensor data receiving unit for receiving water quality multi item measurement data for each water tank from the water quality management platform server displays water quality status information according to the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank received from the iot sensor data receiver through a real time water quality information monitoring system and hydrogen ion concentration ph total dissolved in water through the water quality status board measured values for solid matter tds turbidity residual chlorine and temperature and water quality status information determined based on the measured values are displayed in real time and the real time water quality information monitoring system warns and cautions the water quality status for the entire area and normal displays regional selection information displays on site inspection status information schematized as one of water quality check purifier chlorine input and others displays residual chlorine status total dissolved solids tds status and hydrogen iot sensor data display unit that displays ion concentration ph status information by dividing it into warning caution and normal grades hydrogen ion concentration ph for each of multiple water tanks total dissolved solids tds turbidity ntu collected oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp conductivity cond temperature temp and residual chlorine residual chlorine for each item and the average standard of each item deviation and mean when the difference between the measured value for each item and the average among multiple storage tanks by calculating the deviation exceeds the standard deviation and the average deviation the water tank water quality comparison unit that transmits a danger warning of the water quality of the water tank to the environment safety officer when the difference between the measured value for each item and the average is greater than a preset x multiple of the standard deviation and a preset x multiple of the average deviation a water quality risk warning of the corresponding water tank and a sensor error suspicious warning are issued at the same time as the environment any one of the sensor error detection unit that transmits to the safety officer the website app linkage unit that links the web server or smart phone application to share the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank and the water quality multi item measured value data for each water tank water quality abnormal signal notification unit that generates a water quality abnormal signal alarm when it approaches or reaches the reference value a water quality multi item iot sensor for water quality measurement is additionally installed in the iot sensor error monitoring unit and the water tank of a specific local institution or place so that the administrator can control the local institution or