nt of the present invention includes a body 110 in which air is introduced into the enclosure shape a thermoelectric element 120 that is installed so that heat absorption heating phenomena occur oppositely at both ends according to the flow of current and one end is exposed to the inside of the main body 110 and the other end is exposed to the outside of the main body 110 a dense structure 130 coupled to one end of the thermoelectric element 120 and disposed inside the main body 110 and a first mode of applying a forward current to the thermoelectric element 120 so that the dense structure 130 is cooled to a freezing point or less and the forward current to the thermoelectric element 120 so that the dense structure 130 is heated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "antifreeze tank in which a mixture of antifreeze and water is stored in a certain ratio antifreeze hose installed along the pipe for transferring the liquid to transfer the liquid a circulation pump for supplying and circulating the mixed solution into the antifreeze hose a first temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the mixed solution flowing through the antifreeze hose a heater for heating the mixed solution stored in the antifreeze tank to a predetermined temperature a temperature controller for adjusting the temperature of the mixed solution and the temperature information of the mixed solution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit while the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to heat the mixed solution heating control unit including water tank for storing water a selection unit which selects any one of the mixed solution or water stored in the antifreeze tank or the water tank in response to a control signal of the control unit and transmits it to the circulation pump and a second temperature sensor for measuring the ambient temperature of the pipe for transferring the liquid further comprising the control unit supplies the water supplied from the water tank to the circulation pump through the selection unit when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a set temperature and when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is lower than the set temperature the water supplied from the antifreeze tank is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the present invention according to one aspect for achieving the above object is an antifreeze tank in which a mixture of antifreeze and water is stored in a predetermined ratio antifreeze hose installed along the pipe for transferring the liquid to transfer the liquid a circulation pump for supplying and circulating the mixed solution into the antifreeze hose a first temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the mixed solution flowing through the antifreeze hose a heater for heating the mixed solution stored in the antifreeze tank to a predetermined temperature a temperature controller for adjusting the temperature of the mixed solution and while the temperature information of the mixed solution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to drive the mixed solution it provides a system for preventing freezing and freezing of piping for liquid transport characterized in that it comprises a control unit for heating the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the supplied water may be supplied to the circulation pump and when the temperature is lower than a set temperature the mixed liquid supplied from the antifreeze tank may be supplied to the circulation pump.as described above according to the system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipe for liquid transport according to the present invention an antifreeze hose through which antifreeze mixture heated to a predetermined temperature flows along the pipe for liquid transport is installed and the antifreeze flowing through the antifreeze hose it is possible to prevent freezing and freezing of the liquid transport pipe in winter by transferring the heat source of the liquid to the liquid transport pipe.1 is a view showing a system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipes for liquid transport according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the heat sensor 47 is to turn off the entire system according to the temperature of the waste water and to restart after revealing the cause of the temperature rise which is supplied to the electrolytic cell 30 when the electrolysis continues and stabilizes"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2516325-Y2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of a gain adjusting circuit the output of this temperature measuring means is connected to a switching means which is connected to an ac power source via a zero cross switch and the pulse that gates the triac of the ching trigger circuit synchronized to the frequency of the power supply gas is rutotomoni connected heater is on off controlled by a change in outside air temperature to the switching means the switch this switching device uses a bidirectional thyristor as the switching means"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2516325-Y2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "consists integer circuit connects the output of the temperature measuring means to the switching means the switching means is connected to an ac power source through a zero cross switch and switching hands the pulse that gates the stage triac is the triggered by a trigger circuit synchronized to the wave number connected heater switching means is on off controlled by a change in ambient temperature rutotomoni switching means a bidirectional thyristor is used for this switching means are pulsed either positively or negatively in the weak freezing temperature range"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2516325-Y2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by repeating such on off operation the water pipe is kept warm to prevent damage due to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634146-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in preferred embodiments the processing unit 50 may receive temperature data from a temperature sensor 24 which may indicate that the temperature sensor 24 is measuring temperatures close to freezing 32 degrees fahrenheit plus or minus 5 degrees or temperatures below freezing below 33 degrees fahrenheit and the processing unit 50 may cause the primary pump 13 and or the secondary pump 14 to pulse to prevent freezing of water in the sump 99 pumps 13 14 or piping and conduits 98"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102362392-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "a turbidity measuring sensor for measuring the residual chlorine measuring sensor for measuring residual combustion chlorine for the water quality of the sewage c1 hydrogen ions for measuring the hydrogen ion concentration ph for the water quality of the sewage c1 a concentration measuring sensor 130 an oxidation reduction potential sensor for measuring the oxidation reduction potential orp for the water quality of the sewage c1 a dissolved oxygen sensor for measuring the dissolved oxygen do for the water quality of the sewage c1 an electrical conductivity sensor for measuring the electrical conductivity of the water quality of the sewage c1 a salinity sensor for measuring the salinity of the water quality of the sewage c1 for the water quality of the sewage c1 a total dissolved solids sensor for measuring total dissolved solids tds ss may include at least one of a suspended substance concentration sensor for measuring and ozone sensors for measuring ozone for the water quality of the sewage c1 and the plurality of water quality measuring sensors 130 are it may include all of the sensors disclosed above"}, {"pat_id": "US-11998860-B2", "para_id": "para_1116", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the produced water or wastewater temperature in the sump bottom of the container 139 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101882879-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as an embodiment of the present invention a device for preventing freezing temperature sensor contact relay may be further included in the upper casing 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-10589230-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "furthermore sensor 340 head 342 may further comprise a temperature sensitive element 346 for example a thermocouple or rtd that provides an additional signal on output 344 representative of supply water 1 temperature which can then be utilized in controller 210 to correct orp and ph readings since both the oxidation reduction potential and ph of water are temperature dependent"}, {"pat_id": "US-8967186-B2", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "the controller also communicates with a locally visible station status indication via a separate connection 86 on the sensor station"}, {"pat_id": "US-8967186-B2", "para_id": "para_127", "text": "depending on the nature of the rupture the sensor network may be damaged albeit in rare circumstances and stop reporting from that location which in itself shall serve as a locator for the rupture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102111311-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "storing the stirring time of each food reducer the number of openings and closings of the input port and the input amount monitoring the condition of the food reducer calculating and controlling the rpm of the motor by referring to the temperature information of the temperature sensor according to the stirring time the number of openings and closings of the input port and the amount of input on the control board controlling the heating tank heating wire and shoot valve checking whether it is in an optimal control state transmitting the current status information and a solution to the manager when the control status is not optimal remotely monitoring the food reducer by the control board confirming that a specific event has occurred in the control board and transmitting each device data to a data management relay management server to manage users and points the control board controlling a motor a heating tank a heating wire and a shoot valve through a food reducer control board and a waste water management control board checking whether the control board has a problem including the step of transmitting a message to the control board for dispatch to the site for the problem occurrence the control board includes a food reducer control board for controlling a food reducer and a waste water management control board for managing waste water through a waste water quality sensor and a waste water flow measurement sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102111311-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention comprises the steps of storing the stirring time of each food reducer the number of opening and closing of the input port and the input amount monitoring the condition of the food reducer calculating and controlling the rpm of the motor by referring to the temperature information of the temperature sensor according to the stirring time the number of openings and closings of the input port and the amount of input on the control board controlling the heating tank heating wire and shoot valve checking whether it is in an optimal control state if it is not the optimal control state the step of transmitting the current state information and a solution to the manager"}, {"pat_id": "EP-4190981-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "this is because when the temperature on the supply line drops below a limit value there is an increasing risk of icing which in turn increases the risk of leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-10180414-B2", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "for example the sensor assembly may include one or more piezoelectric sensors acoustic sensors acoustic transducers hydrophones pressure sensors pressure transducers temperature sensors accelerometers flow sensors chlorine sensors leak detectors vibration sensors or other types of sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102578604-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the control unit is a first coolant pump control unit that operates the first coolant pump the second coolant pump and the third coolant pump when the electrolysis reactor temperature measured from the electrolysis reactor temperature sensor is higher than the set temperature the second coolant it may further include a pump control unit and a third coolant pump control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102578604-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "the first second and third coolant pump control units 240 250 and 260 receive electrolysis reactor temperature data measured from the electrolysis reactor temperature sensor 140 and when the electrolysis reactor temperature is higher than the set temperature the first coolant pump p1 serves to operate the second coolant pump p2 and the third coolant pump p3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102578604-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the technical spirit of the attached patent claims.10 rectification unit 20 raw water tank 30 electrolysis reactor 40 indirect oxidation reaction tank 50 discharge tank 60 circulation pump 80 water supply department v indirect oxidation reaction tank discharge valve p1 1st coolant pump p2 second coolant pump p3 third coolant pump c electrolysis reactor cooling device 100 ph sensor 110 tn sensor 120 electrical conductivity sensor 130 image acquisition unit 140 electrolysis reactor temperature sensor 200 control unit 210 circulation pump operation time control unit 220 rectifier output current control unit 230 indirect oxidation reaction tank discharge valve control unit 240 first coolant pump control unit 250 second coolant pump control unit 260 third coolant pump control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the flow sensor circuit is used by the control unit to determine when water is flowing so that the ultraviolet lamp assembly can be energized and to keep track of the volume of water that is being processed by the water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171689-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "case 100 a plurality of led lamps 110 pump 230 water supply sensor 240 the heating wire 250 the heater 270 and the heater body temperature sensor 272 is configured to include the case 100 has a rectangular parallelepiped shape a pedestal 101 is formed at a lower portion thereof a cover 102 is formed at an upper portion thereof and a plurality of led lamps 110 and steam on on are provided at the front of the case 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in an alternative embodiment the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the alternative embodiment works by taking the temperature at the temperature sensor package of the leak detection system the external environment temperature sensor and the additional temperature sensor package and feeding the data to a microprocessor where they are analyzed to determine whether the fluid is expanding by comparing the temperature data to the user inputted data stored in a control rom and flash memory"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_127", "text": "in addition the primary temperature sensor package 702 and the secondary temperature sensor package 706 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 720 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_131", "text": "in addition the primary temperature sensor package 806 and the secondary temperature sensor package 840 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 810 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_141", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_157", "text": "the second threshold temperature tps2 and max time at second threshold temperature tpsmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_159", "text": "the second threshold temperature tss2 and max time at second threshold temperature tssmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_161", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle12 and max time at second threshold temperature tle1max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle22 and max time at second threshold temperature tle2max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_165", "text": "the second threshold temperature tet2 and max time at second threshold temperature tetmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-10526548-B2", "para_id": "para_116", "text": "for example the temperature sensor 176 may be the engine block sensor which may already be used to provide the engine block temperature for example to an ecu"}, {"pat_id": "US-10526548-B2", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "in one example a low temperature fault may be determined and set in response to a low temperature signal from the temperature sensor 176 which may impact the ability to evacuate water due to freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "US-9719234-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the computer executable code when executed at a processor of an iot device is configured to request and receive a temperature signal from at least one iot temperature sensor wherein the at least one iot temperature sensor is disposed on a water pipe of a water supply system configured to detect an environmental temperature of the water pipe and generate the temperature signal based on the environmental temperature and the iot device is disposed on a tap of the water supply system wherein the tap is connected to the water pipe and is switchable between an open state and a closed state wherein water supplied by the water pipe flows out from the tap in the open state and does not flow out from the tap in the closed state determine the environmental temperature based on the temperature signal and when the environmental temperature is at or below a threshold temperature control the tap to switch to the open state such that water flows out from the tap wherein the threshold temperature is a temperature of a freezing point of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102797750-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first tank 1100 softening tank equipped with a level sensor 1110 capable of detecting the lowest and highest water levels as well as the supply of raw water a first channel q1 installed to be able to send the fluid discharged to the lower part of the first tank softening tank a circulation pump 1200 installed at a predetermined position of the first channel a cooling device 1300 installed at a predetermined position of the circulation pump to be able to cool the temperature of the fluid passing through the circulation pump a second channel q2 installed to be able to send the fluid passing through the cooling device at high pressure a reverse osmosis membrane high pressure pump 1400 installed at a predetermined position of the second channel and a reverse osmosis membrane 1500 ro membrane or a second tank 1700 ro produced water storage tank having a reverse osmosis membrane ro membrane or ro membrane and a third channel q3 for discharging the product water produced in the reverse osmosis membrane a reverse osmosis membrane produced water supply valve 1600 installed at a predetermined position of the third channel a level sensor 1710 installed at an end of the third channel for storing the product water and detecting the lowest and highest water levels and capable of discharging the product water downward a fourth channel q4 through which concentrated water is discharged from the reverse osmosis membrane ro membrane or ro membrane and a concentrated water drain valve 1810 and a concentrated water recovery valve 1820 installed in the fourth channel for discharging the concentrated water as waste water or supplying it to the first tank softening water tank and a connection between the concentrated water valve and the first tank softening water tank in a concentrated wastewater reduction device of an ro system which comprises a concentrated water recovery path q5 connected internally a produced water recovery path q6 branched from a third path located between the reverse osmosis membrane and the reverse osmosis membrane produced water supply valve and connected to the inside of the first tank softening water tank and equipped with a produced water circulation valve 1900 and a control unit s connected to control the level sensors of the first and second tanks and the pumps valves and electrical components installed in each path a first electrical conductivity sensor 1001 installed at a predetermined position of the third flow path q3 installed between the reverse osmosis membrane product water supply valve 1600 and the product water circulation valve 1900 and the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 so as to detect the electrical conductivity of the fluid passing through the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 and send it to the control unit s a second electrical conductivity sensor 1002 installed between the cooling device 1300 and the reverse osmosis membrane high pressure pump 1400 to detect the electrical conductivity of the fluid being transported through the second channel q2 and send it to the control unit s and when a fluid having an electrical conductivity higher than a certain value flows through the second channel q2 the control unit s blocks the concentrated water recovery valve 1820 installed in the concentrated water recovery channel q5 and opens the concentrated water drain valve 1810 to prevent the fluid having an electrical conductivity higher than the set value from being continuously supplied to the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 thereby preventing the failure of the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 and extending its lifespan"}, {"pat_id": "US-11623178-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "if so the method 700 proceeds to block 740 where the controller 180 activates the auxiliary condenser 14 to expel heat from the water recovery system 10 and reduce the temperature of the one or more internal condenser coils 48 and then the method 700 proceeds to block 745"}, {"pat_id": "US-7277822-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "5 862 030 teaches an electrical safety device comprised of a sensor strip disposed in the insulation of a wire or in the insulation of a sheath enclosing a bundle of electrical conductors where the sensor strip comprises a distributed conductive over temperature sensing portion comprising an electrically conductive polymer having a positive temperature coefficient of resistivity which increases with temperature sufficient to result in a switching temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 the controller is a boiler driving unit for driving a combustion device constituting the boiler a driving state detection unit for detecting the driving state of the boiler driving unit and as a result of the detection of the driving state detection unit when the boiler driving unit is in a non operational state and the external temperature sensed through the temperature sensor is less than a set temperature the valve control unit controls the water pipe by repeatedly opening and closing the electromagnetic valve at regular time intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in order to prevent the water stagnant in the water pipe 3 from freezing when the temperature detected by the temperature sensor 5 falls below the set temperature detected by the temperature sensor 5 during the idle period of the boiler 1 by the valve control unit 13 of the controller 10 the electromagnetic valve 3 is opened and at the same time the electromagnetic valve 7a is automatically closed through the valve control unit 13 and the pump 6 provided in the boiler 1 is operated to the inside through the water pipe 3 the supplied water is discharged by bypassing the drain pipe 4c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "during the idle period of the boiler 1 the electromagnetic valve 3 is automatically opened and closed according to the external temperature sensed through the temperature sensor 5 to discharge the water stagnated in the water pipe 2 to the outside through the drain pipe 4c to the outside of the water pipe by allowing water to flow at regular intervals through 2 it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from being frozen by increasing the freezing point freezing point of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "on the other hand it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from freezing in advance by adjusting the freezing point freezing point of water according to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101744461-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in order to achieve the above mentioned object the present invention provides a method for detecting a temperature of a cooling water comprising the steps of detecting a ph an electric conductivity a calcium concentration a scale or a fouling of the cooling water and a plurality of chemical liquid tanks electrically connected to the first sensor unit and provided with a space in which a plurality of chemical liquids separately containing a ph adjusting agent a sterilizing agent a scale remover and a fouling removing agent are separately contained at least one of the cooling water and the cooling water a second sensor unit electrically connected to the first sensor unit and the management unit and detecting a liquid level of each of the plurality of chemical liquid tanks in real time and a controller for controlling operations of the first sensor unit the management unit and the second sensor unit wherein the controller controls the first sensor unit and the second sensor unit so that when the remaining amount of one of the plurality of chemical liquid tanks is within a set value the control unit may stop supply of the plurality of chemical liquids and transmit a movement signal for supplementing the chemical liquid that is equal to or less than the set value to the management unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100292426-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "a coagulant injection control device capable of controlling the amount of coagulant required by measuring water quality such as water temperature and the like may be added"}, {"pat_id": "US-4448032-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "US-11693434-B2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "wherein the environmental parameters may include temperature ph value salinity oxidation reduction potential and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101780266-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "as described above the method of reducing the amount of sludge of a wastewater dehydrating sludge using the jar drum type sludge reducing apparatus and the jar drum type sludge reducing apparatus in which the blades of the present invention are installed is characterized in that the high temperature fermenting microorganism ty em and a ceramic ball serving as a swelling fire can be supplied to facilitate the reduction of dehydrated sludge by smooth supply of temperature and oxygen and the high temperature heat and moisture inside the drum type drum body can be supplied to the blowing air pressure and the high temperature heat and moisture gathered on the upper part of the drum type drum body by the convection phenomenon can be recovered by a hot air blower and reused thereby saving energy.1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of fire fighting equipment and freezing water in the winter season a technology including a heating wire and a temperature sensor that generates heat by using electrical energy on the outside of the fire fighting equipment has been developed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to the freeze protection firefighting apparatus according to the present invention in order to prevent the freezing and freezing of the pipeline in which fire water is discharged from a fire hydrant a hose reel a fire truck etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_102", "text": "as described in detail above in order to prevent the pipeline from which fire water is discharged from a fire hydrant a hose reel a fire truck etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7009733-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "2 the microwave pretreatment apparatus of the present invention physically modifies the protein conformation and denatures the protein and in particular promotes the secondary conformational change of the protein thereby promoting the hydrolysis of the protein"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the pet water dispenser may also include an illumination assembly having a lighting device a water level sensor a water temperature sensor a proximity sensor a contamination level sensor a thermoelectric element or device and a sterilizing filter e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the wireless power transmitter 72 and the wireless power receiver 73 may exchange information such as state condition or coupling information of the docking station 71 water tank 10 and or the inner assembly 100 power usage information battery charging information of the battery b battery output voltage current information control information or information from various sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "the sensor 72c may also sense a temperature of the plurality of transmitting coils 721 724 and or shielding layer 725 and provide a measurement to the power circuit device 715 so that a controller of the printed circuit device 715 may determine whether or not the wireless power transmitter 72 is overheated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101508672-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a sensor 60 the medicine inlet pipe 30 is provided with a branch connecting member 31 at one end for facilitating installation in the water supply pipe 2 a heat sink 70 is installed in the main body 10 and a temperature sensor 71 interlocked with the heat sink 70 is installed to radiate heat to the inside of the main body 10 to prevent freezing due to cold"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101508672-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a medicine dispensing apparatus for dispensing medicine formed by injecting medicine into water supplied to a water supply pipe the apparatus comprising a main body a medicine supply pipe 30 which is installed inside the main body and is for supplying medicines in a medicine storage tank provided in the medicine storage tank to the water supply pipe one side connected to the medicine storage tank and the other side connected to the water supply pipe a chemical supply pump provided with the chemical supply pump a motor interlocked with the medicine dispensing pump and adjusting a dose of the medicine by adjusting a rotation speed a control unit electrically connected to the motor to control the driving and rotating speed of the motor and a pressure sensor for sensing a pressure inside the medicine inlet pipe and electrically connected to the motor so that the medicine is supplied to the medicine inlet pipe only when water flows inside the water supply pipe the pipe is provided with a branch connecting member at one end for facilitating installation in the water supply pipe a heat radiating plate is installed inside the main body a temperature sensor interlocked with the heat radiating plate is further installed and a heating wire is installed on the medicine inlet pipe to prevent freezing of the medicine a side wall of the main body is connected to a first medicine inlet pipe connected to a medicine storage tank and supplying medicines to the inside of the main body and a second medicine inlet pipe connected to a water supply pipe for supplying medicines to the water supply pipe and a hose connecting the two connection ports"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101508672-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the medicine dispensing apparatus according to the present invention is provided with a heat dissipating plate 70 inside the main body 10 to prevent the freezing due to heavy snow or cold in the winter and a temperature for sensing the temperature inside a sensor 71 is further installed"}, {"pat_id": "US-12188689-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the local controller 40 may also transmit the tb measurement of the temperature sensor 32 to the load manager 48 and the index si may be computed by the load manager 48 to decide if it may interrupt or not the water heater during a power demand management request"}, {"pat_id": "US-7105095-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "the lithium ion electrode is therefore preferably placed directly in a cooling water pit cooling water tank or cooling water piping of the cooling water system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hot wire control apparatus for controlling power supply to a hot wire installed in close contact with a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe a temperature sensor for sensing an external temperature a relay for switching the supply of external power to the hot wire heater a power supply to the hot wire is provided when the external temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is lower than a first temperature and a power supply is not supplied to the hot wire when the external temperature is equal to or higher than a second temperature higher than the first temperature a control unit a first display unit for turning on the lamp when power is normally supplied from the external power source to the control unit a second display unit for turning on the lamp when the control unit is operating normally when power is supplied to the hot line a third display unit indicating that power is supplied to the hot wire without any abnormality and and a case enclosing the relay the first display unit the second display unit the third display unit and the control unit the control unit wherein the timer counts a pulse signal using the timer when the power is supplied to the hot wire and controls the relay to stop power supply to the hot wire if the power is supplied to the hot wire for a first time or longer counts a pulse signal by using the timer when the power is cut off and controls the relay when the pulse signal is counted for a second time different from the first time to supply power to the hot wire again when the external temperature becomes lower than a preset third temperature at which the freeze wave can occur the power supply to the hot wire is continuously supplied independently of the timer wherein the case is waterproof and has a hole in which the first display unit the second display unit and the third display unit are installed the waterproof is maintained by providing a rubber hook to the hole wherein the first display unit is turned on and the second display unit and the third display unit are turned off when the external temperature is higher than the second temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore when using the bimetallic controlled frost protector a power of about 38 w to 76 w per household is leaked for 24 hours every day for about 5 months november march during winter there is a problem in that the electric charge is lost.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in an effort to solve the problems of the conventional freezing prevention apparatus having a bimetallic sensor control system the present invention provides a water pipe heating line control device for preventing the freezing of the water pipe by increasing the efficiency of energy consumption by increasing the efficiency of energy consumption"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a hot water line controller for controlling the supply of power to a hot wire installed in close contact with a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe a temperature sensor for sensing and a power supply unit for supplying power to the hot wire when the external temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is lower than a first temperature and supplying power to the hot wire when the external temperature is equal to or higher than a second temperature higher than the first temperature wherein the control unit interrupts the power supply to the hot wire when the power supply to the hot wire is continued for a first time or more and the power supply is cut off at a temperature lower than the second temperature and the power source is supplied again to the hot wire if it continues for 2 hours or more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "one embodiment of the configuration of the water pipe heat line control device according to the present invention is a heat line control device for controlling the supply of power to a hot line installed in close contact with a water pipe to prevent the water pipe from being frozen and includes a temperature sensor 210 and a controller 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "for example when the first temperature is set to 2 deg c and the first temperature is set to 4 deg c when the external temperature sensed by the temperature sensor 210 becomes 2 deg c power is supplied to the heat line installed in the water pipe to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100874616-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "by filling the sensing unit it is possible to prevent the malfunction of the leak detection sensor due to the small amount of condensate formed in the water supply pipe due to the difference between the water supply temperature and the room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200186594-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of upper and lower cases 1 2 having an o ring 3 in the coupling portion to achieve a predetermined size and shape and waterproof and the lower case 2 is suction of water to perform a buoyancy control function the ballast 16 is provided with discharge ports 9a and 9b and the piston 7a is moved up and down by forward and reverse rotation of the dc motor 5a above the ballast 16 to obtain diving and buoyancy"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035713-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the electronics 120 may include elements configured to receive information from the actuator m 107 temperature sensor t pressure sensor p and the like process and or store the information therein and communicate the information to a remote location via the radio module 130"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035713-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "1 in some embodiments a pressure sensor p a temperature sensor t and the like may fit into the standard water meter pit i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "at this time the determination unit 346 may determine that the chemical cleaning is performed when the temperature of the raw water is equal to or higher than the reference temperature the current time is included in the reference time zone or the date is included"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the pipe adjacent the location of the thermal sensor drops below freezing the sensor is actuated and completes an electrical circuit from a power source to a solenoid actuated valve to thereby cause it to open and allow water to trickle from the water supply pipe through an existing water outlet fixture and down its adjacent and pre existing drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing the sensor is de actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid actuated valve and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "for example the processor 206 may communicate in a bidirectional manner with each of the transceiver 202 physical input module 204 electronically actuated ball valve 208 flow sensor 210 temperature sensor 212 and leak sensor 214"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "in some implementations the flow sensor 210 the temperature sensor 212 and leak sensor 214 may be contained within the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "for example the processor 206 can receive sensor data from the flow sensor 210 the temperature sensor 212 and the leak sensor 214"}, {"pat_id": "US-9494480-B2", "para_id": "para_112", "text": "because the present invention water use and water energy monitoring apparatus can be used in situations where the source of water comes for a well or non commercial operation and furthermore where the commercial operations water treatments plants are under pressure to provide more water supplies or where problems breakdowns or accidental situations can cause contamination of the water source the present invention can be fitted with display parameters of and provide warning for numerous mineral elements and biological contaminates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100217951-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "when the heater 25 is operated by the temperature sensor 15 mounted on the fermentation vessel 70 to keep the temperature constant and to promote the fermentation the fermentation is more easily performed when the enzyme is added.according to the present invention as described above the food waste residue fermentation and wastewater treatment device of the present invention is a device for disinfecting food waste removing water from a centrifuge fermenting the remaining semi dry food waste it is an extremely useful invention in the environmental industry because it has an effect of preventing contamination of soil and water quality by enabling fermentation and sewage treatment"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3274541-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as described above the substance judging device 14 and the computer device 20 are composed of the plankton measuring device 10 the water quality measuring device 11 and the toxic substance monitoring device 12 from the water intake source 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-11359989-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "memory which when all combined enable the detection of a leak increase the accuracy of locating the leak and reduce the occurrence of an erroneous leak identification that is common when traditional rarefaction leak detection techniques are used"}, {"pat_id": "US-11359989-B2", "para_id": "para_231", "text": "further the fluid properties of the pipeline may be continuously measured using the pressure sensing means e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention detects the temperature sensor 13 to prevent freezing of the connection pipe passing through the inside of the flush toilet 10 and when the temperature falls below the set temperature the controller c controls a predetermined time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the temperature sensor 13 may be set to operate at a temperature for example 5 to 10 at which the freezing wave is expected in winter and the controller c may measure the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the controller c is a circulation pump p and the first opening and closing valve to prevent freezing of the water supply line 11 connected to the flush toilet 10 in accordance with the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 13 pneumatic or electric signals are controlled to actuate v\u2081 and second open close valves v\u2082"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "thus the controller c opens the first opening closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention can be operated to prevent the freezing in winter by wrapping a heating wire not shown in all the connection pipes to make the water supply including the water supply pipe and the water discharge pipe in particular the temperature sensor when the heating wire is preferentially operated by the control of the controller c according to the temperature value measured in 13 so that the heating wire is organically interlocked with the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention and the heating wire is not operated due to a short circuit of the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262046-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "1 and 2 the present inventors electric power control system 120 includes a power supply unit 10 for supplying electricity to the electric power control system a filter unit 20 for filtering water and contaminants that are flowing into the inlet formed at one side of the electrolytic cell in the state in which electricity is supplied to the power supply and moving to the supply pipe a flow rate or flow rate part 30 for measuring the amount and flow rate of water when the water passing through the filter part flows through the supply pipe through a flow meter or a flow rate meter a temperature sensor unit 40 for measuring a temperature of water passing through the flow rate or flow rate through a temperature sensor in order to generate the concentration of germicidal ions through the electrolysis of the water passing through the flow rate or flow rate a mesh type electrode having a plurality of perforated shapes is laminated or used within a range that does not affect the flow rate of water or a lattice electrode portion 50 to increase the sterilization concentration by reducing the flow rate of water passing through the electrode by causing a phenomenon in the electrode and the electrode stacked in the form an electric leakage blocking unit 50 1 which blocks or prevents an electric leakage phenomenon due to residual electricity remaining in the electrode unit or water even when the electric power is supplied from the power source or when the electric power is cut off a current sensor unit 60 for sensing an amount of current supplied to the electrode of the electrode unit with a current sensor and monitoring water quality of the supply water a voltage sensor unit 70 for inferring electric conductivity or total dissolved solids tds by measuring the supply voltage supplied to the power supply unit a direct current power generator 80 for generating direct current power according to the electrical conductivity or total dissolved solids tds value inferred by the voltage sensor the amount of power required by controlling the flow rate or flow rate the current sensor unit the voltage sensor unit and the dc power generating unit to read the electrical conductivity of the water and the tds value and the electrical resistance value according to the water flow rate flow rate and temperature change an electrical control unit 90 for generating control a wired or wireless communication unit 100 supporting communication by transmitting information of the electric resistance value obtained from the electric control unit to an external terminal or a computer by wire or wirelessly a display unit 110 which displays a state of operation by the electric control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101207999-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102587945-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "additionally it is possible to prevent freezing of the air valve 90 in a convenient and effective manner by configuring the heating element 44 solar cell 55 temperature sensor signal transmitter and control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-4370865-A", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in certain embodiments data from this flow meter is transmitted via a low power wireless transmitter to a gateway and hub assembly"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the leak sensor may or may not have temperature and motion tamper detecting capabilities inside the sensor s housing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "data collected from ultrasonic flow sensor 37 provides users reactive preventative and predictive recommendations"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "daily averages of temperature and pressure measurements are shared on a twelve hour basis by leak sensor 20 and water control unit 30 via the gateway 40"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3979250-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5 232080 problems to be solved by the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above when measuring the hydrogen concentration in the liquid phase it is not necessary to apply a high temperature sensitive part and to prevent these degradation diaphragm or the electrolytic solution as required it is another object of the present invention to provide a hydrogen gas sensor that can be reduced in size and weight and an electrolyzed water generator including the hydrogen gas sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102172981-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "to measure the water quality of multi sampling samples collected from multiple series by using a sensor it is easy to maintain while reducing the installation cost of the sensor and it is possible to reduce the deviation of the measured value due to sensor contamination and measurement consistency by measuring the multi sampling sample with the same measuring instrument sensor at one measurement location"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102172981-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "3 the system of the present invention which includes a monitoring control unit based on the iot technology attaches an additional sensor to the main equipment and equipment failure or water quality status using equipment operation information and equipment temperature information such as operation stop maintenance etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101583008-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "1 the bimetal 23 or 23 the heater power is directly applied to the steam generating part 20 and the power is not applied to the bimetal 23 or 23 so that the bimetal 23 or 23 can not function as a temperature sensor accordingly the bimetal 23 or 23 can not block the input of the heater power when the steam generating part 20 overheats and thus the steam thawing device can not be operated safely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a synthetic resin structure having a network structure including a plurality of pores and a water permeable base layer block comprising a porous concrete composition accommodated in the plurality of pores of the synthetic resin structure a water pocket block positioned on the permeable base layer block a water collecting tank configured to store water collected through the water permeable base layer block a sprinkler pipe positioned under the permeable base block and configured to sprinkle water stored in the water collecting tank under the permeable base block at least one sensor unit configured to measure at least one of a surface temperature and humidity of the water pocket block a water supply pump operating to supply water stored in the water collecting tank to the sprinkling pipe a communication unit configured to receive public data on one or more of weather population and vehicles of an installation area of the permeable base block from an external server and an automatic watering system using a water permeable base layer block comprising a control unit configured to control an operation of the water supply pump by further using the public data together with at least one of the surface temperature and the humidity measured by the sensor unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "weather data api application programming interface based data to predict the road temperature and to reduce the road temperature by utilizing the latent heat of vaporization by permeating rainwater and tap water back to the lower part of the road in proportion to the predicted temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "for example the controller 130 may operate the water supply pump 140 when the current state determined through sensor data is dry compared to a set state and or the temperature is high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "in an embodiment the control unit 130 of the watering system may calculate a temperature predicted value of the installation area eg road of the permeable base block based on the acquired sensor data and or public data s3"}, {"pat_id": "US-4635668-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "apparatus for automatically controlling flow in a water line to avoid freeze damage comprising a temperature sensor adapted for connection to the water line the water line a normally closed valve adapted for connection to a housing control circuit means within said housing and responsive to said temperature sensor for continuously monitoring the temperature of water in the line and selectively opening and closing said valve to allow increased periodic flow in the water line with decreasing water temperature and indicator means associated with said housing and connected to said control circuit means for indicating the temperature proximity of water in the line to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 1 the control unit drives the temperature sensor at regular intervals the heat pipe leakage monitoring device characterized in that to cut off the power at the remaining time except the driving time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the mounting table is provided with a plurality of temperature sensors 120 for monitoring whether leakage occurs in the heat pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore the present invention by simply installing the device around the water pipe and connecting only the power supply the sensor detects that the temperature drops to sub zero temperatures and heats the heating sheet to prevent freezing phenomenon that the water pipe freezes or freezes in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the sensor operates to supply electric current to the electric line surrounding the water pipe to heat the water pipe to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "after that when the temperature rises to the image the temperature sensor 5 detects this and the circuit board 4 operates to stop the supply of electricity to the heating sheet thereby eliminating the consumption of electricity"}, {"pat_id": "US-9109349-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "because first electronic valve 12 is shut no additional water is permitted to enter from connection line 22 into structure 70 until system 10 is reset thus significantly reducing the volume of damaging water capable of escaping connection line 22 or other tributary within structure 70 during a leak"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5313597-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "one aspect of the present invention includes a heater wire inserted into a heater guide tube provided along a pipe for water supply and or hot water supply a power supply line for supplying power to the heater wire and a heater guide tube together with the heater wire and a control unit for controlling the switching element for turning on and off the power supplied to the heater line via the power supply line and the switching element based on the detected temperature of the pipe temperature sensor"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5313597-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "therefore the control unit inside the control box 60 can detect the resistance value of the thermistor 71 or a change in the resistance value via the lead wire sensor wire 36 and can detect the temperature of the environment where the thermistor 71 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5313597-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore each antifreeze heater 20 is independently a heater based on the conditions of each of the tubes 12a to 12e and 13a to 13c with the heat insulating material and the outside temperature and the inside temperature detected by the sensor of each antifreeze heater 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the warm air device that is installed on the ceiling or wall of the interior of the toilet through a built in case to supply hot air to prevent freezing of water pipes a heater installed in the case to generate heat for freezing of water pipes a fan installed in the case adjacent to the heater to supply heat from the heater to the room a temperature sensor installed in the case and detecting an indoor temperature used as data for determining whether the heater and the fan are operated it is built in the case so as to be connected to the heater the fan and the temperature sensor the operation of the heater and fan based on the room temperature from the temperature sensor when the power is supplied or when the operation is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is installed in the ceiling or wall of the interior of the toilet through a built in case in the warm air device for supplying hot air to prevent the freezing of water pipes etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is a process to prevent the freezing of water pipes by controlling the operation of 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "that is when the second set temperature is set to the control unit 50 at 8 c and the third set temperature to 12 c the room 50 is detected from the temperature sensor 40 in the state in which the operation is stopped the operation of the heater 20 and the fan 30 is controlled such that the temperature is between 8 c and 12 c to prevent freezing of water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4964402-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "5 the communication unit 27 that transmits receives data to from the center facility 2 side and the operating device side such as the drive current value of the pump 4 are provided on the board provided inside"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4964402-B2", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "it is a whole block diagram of the management system of a water treatment facility.it is a schematic diagram of a manhole pump facility.it is a front view in a control box.it is a front view of a controller.it is a block diagram of a controller.it is a flowchart figure of an automatic drainage process.it is a timing chart figure which shows the drive timing of the pump by a reverse drive means.it is a block diagram of a monitoring control server.it is a facility condition screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an operating current history management screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is a pump daily report screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an alarm management screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an alarm detail screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an apparatus operation condition display screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.4 pump 6 controller 7 monitoring control server management device 13 internet communication line 14 manhole water tank 17 control box 18 water level sensor 19 temperature sensor temperature detection means 22 pump breaker 27 communication unit communication means 30 breaker sensor 33 automatic calling means 38 packet charging communication network communication network 39 information display means 51 operating current management screen 63 alarm details screen 64 device status display screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101595915-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "according to the present invention since the steam is generated at high speed at the time of starting the speed of the thawing operation is improved and the start is terminated to prevent the damage of the self components at the time of termination of the operation.100 a steam cracker 110 pump 113 a water supply pipe 130 steam heating element temperature sensor 140 steam heating element 150 the control unit 151 a microprocessor 152 heater power switching part 153 a pump power switching unit 154 control power supply 160 power switch 165 the transformer 170 a steam generating switch 180 display portion"}, {"pat_id": "US-11754545-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in some embodiments the sensor probe 106 may be provided as a single probe that is designed to measure one or more of the ph value of the water the oxidation reduction potential of the water water temperature and combinations thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101873877-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "when the measured temperature of the temperature sensor is lower than a predetermined reference value heat is generated through the heating element to prevent the water meter from being frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101873877-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "if the control device can communicate via the iot chip and the water meter is an electronic meter remote meter reading meter reading at a remote location can be implemented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564334-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the drug feeder may include a stock solution reservoir in which the liquid polymer is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102913250-B1", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "the detection unit 1100 can measure real time temperature values via a temperature sensor and calculate an average value fluctuation range and or frequency of occurrence of outliers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100689108-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0 385 568 2003.05.15 titled reservoir control system which is filed and filed by the present applicant has a groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-9690303-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "because first electronic valve 12 is shut no additional water is permitted to enter from connection line 22 into structure 70 until system 10 is reset thus significantly reducing the volume of damaging water capable of escaping connection line 22 or other tributary within structure 70 during a leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "however since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside the temperature sensor often malfunctions and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as a result the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100898189-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "51 is connected to the output terminal of the signal transmission unit 51 through the drive 53 in accordance with the output information of the water level sensor 11 the oxygen sensor 12 and the temperature sensor 13 the first to sixth solenoid valves 21 22 23 24 25 26 and the hot and cold water coolers 5 6 and the first pump a micro process unit hereinafter referred to as mpu 54 that controls 31 is connected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100898189-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "figure 2b is a block diagram of the control system of the live fish tank according to the present invention the water level sensor 11 oxygen sensor 12 temperature sensor 13 salinity sensor 14 and turbidity sensor 15 is connected to a signal transmission unit 51 for focusing and transmitting the output signal of each sensor and the output level of the signal transmission unit 51 through the drive 53 through the level sensor 11 and oxygen detection first to eighth solenoid valves for adjusting oxygen hot cold water supplementary water supply and salinity according to the output information of the sensor 12 the temperature sensor 13 the salinity sensor 14 and the turbidity sensor 15 21 22 23 24 25 26 27 28 and hot cold water 5 6 and the first and second pumps 31 32 the controlling mpu 54 is connected"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_197", "text": "by using a salinity sensor for salt water industrial brine 202 and a temperature sensor not specifically shown in figures throughout this patent inside freezing desalination cell unit enclosure 271 the freezing process can be automatically controlled via a computer microprocessor control system"}, {"pat_id": "US-8532829-B2", "para_id": "para_82", "text": "or polyone corporation of avon lake ohio which contacts the fluid flow 98 though in other embodiments the temperature and flow measurement sensors may be encased in other corrosion resistant materials"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101997339-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "when the flow rate in the pipe is stopped the power supplied to the heater is cut off and the operation power of the heater is limited in proportion to the temperature signal inputted through the temperature sensor if the system is for the purpose that to maximize electrical efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2749860-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in a further embodiment an additional sensor system can be provided on the base part namely for sound measurement for the purpose of leak detection and or for recording the quantitative water supply via the hydrant and or for the detection of water parameters such as pressure ph hardness turbidity and temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100846473-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the first and second valve assemblies 122 and 126 allow the regeneration mode to proceed while the mode is in progress"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102722253-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in paragraph 5 a pipe trench collapse prediction monitoring system characterized in that the first sensor module can be fitted and fixed into a slot formed inside the receiving tube as a substrate and is connected to a vibration sensor a temperature sensor and a gas sensor and transmits measurement values from each sensor to a second sensor module via a cable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102722253-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "in order for the gas sensor 270 to operate a membrane hole through which gas can pass may be formed in the lower part of the housing portion 100 although not shown in the drawing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102722253-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the present invention described above is not limited to the above described drawings and detailed description and it goes without saying that various modifications and changes made by those skilled in the art within the scope and spirit of the present invention as described in the claims below are also included within the scope of the present invention.1 collapse prediction monitoring system 10 detection work 11 conduit 12 conduit trench 13 gas pipe 14 heat pipe 20 remote observation tower 21 camera 22 communications department 30 control server 40 worker terminal 41 sensor trigger 42 data reader 100 housing section 110 hollow 120 cover 121 wrench home 130 extension tube 140 hollow thread 150 screw 160 insertion groove 200 detector 210 reception hall 211 reception space 213 coupling screw thread 220 vibration sensor water pipe 230 power supply unit 250 1st sensor module 260 vibration sensor 261 probe pin 270 temperature sensor 280 gas sensor 300 surface protrusion 310 top cap 311 relief stud 312 cap screw thread 320 upper tube 321 external screw thread 322 slot 330 alarm 331 flasher 340 tilt sensor 350 2nd sensor module 351 mcu 352 communication chip 353 antenna 354 memory 355 gps 360 sensor for trigger"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "another important aspect of the bi metallic disk is that after the predetermined temperature of for example 36 has been reached and the disk has warped to break the electrical contact of the switch the disk will maintain the warped shape until manually re set"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "moreover the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak for incipient freeze condition and thus the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100342599-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "during the ultrasonic sterilization a heat jacket 25 for circulating a cooling water was attached to the outside of the sterilization reactor in order to remove the generated heat because heat is generated due to the cavitation phenomenon of ultrasonic waves"}, {"pat_id": "US-9605904-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the processor may calculate the dew point for the primary air flow based on the at least one environmental condition sensed by the at least one sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102735412-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the sensors may include for example a ph sensor an oxidation reduction potential orp sensor a chlorine sensor a temperature sensor etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100926077-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "subsequently looking at the plurality of pipe lines w1 to w14 provided in the water softener according to the present invention by connecting the external cold hot water pipes to the first valve assembly 350 to remove the cold hot raw water of the cold hot water pipes the first valve assembly 1 by connecting the first and second raw water supply lines w1 w2 to the first valve assembly 350 and the first valve assembly 350 to the first and second soft water tanks 710 720"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "tm ti h ti to cp \u03c1 \u03b4 wherein ti is a temperature of fluid in the pipeline and the unit is k h is a convection heat transfer coefficient of steam and a thermal insulation layer 6 in the pipeline and the unit is w m2 k cp is a specific heat capacity of steam and the unit is j kg k \u03c1 is a steam density and the unit is kg m3 \u03b4 is a wall thickness of the pipeline namely a distance by which steam flows out from the inside of the pipeline via a leakage hole to the outer wall of the pipeline in unit time and the unit is m s \u03b4 mt\u03c1 a wherein m is a mass flow of steam namely a fluid mass of the fluid that passes through an effective cross section of a closed pipeline in unit time and the unit is kg s t is a unit time namely 1 s and a is the area of the leakage hole and the unit is m2 a corresponding relationship between a steam pressure and a temperature in the heating pipeline is obtained by an antoine empirical formula or by looking up a table of steam pressure and temperature enthalpy values as shown in a formula 7 below ln p 9.3876 3826.36t 45.47 7 wherein p is the steam pressure and the unit is mpa t is the steam temperature and the unit is k a value p calculated by substituting tm as the steam temperature into the formula 7 is the pipeline leakage transient pressure pm corresponding to the pipeline leakage transient steam temperature tm in step 3 the process of positioning a leakage location by the plc according to a pressure gradient method is specifically as follows firstly a pressure gradient p x leftbracketingbar u upstream of a leakage point and a pressure gradient p x leftbracketingbar d downstream of the leakage point are calculated p x leftbracketingbar u p 1 pmx 8 p x leftbracketingbar d pm p 2l s x 9 wherein l is a distance from a pressure sensor within a region of the leakage point to a temperature sensor downstream thereof and the unit is m s is a distance from a temperature sensor within the region of the leakage point to a pressure sensor downstream thereof and the unit is m x is a distance from the location of the leakage point to a pressure sensor upstream within the region of the leakage point and the unit is m x represents a gradient direction dot over p 1 is a pressure value detected by the pressure sensor upstream of the leakage point and the unit is mpa dot over p 2 is a pressure value detected by a pressure sensor downstream of the leakage point and the unit is mpa and pm is the pipeline leakage transient pressure and the unit is mpa it is known from a formula for conservation of momentum within a steam pipeline p x leftbracketingbar u f \u03c1 u22 d 10 p x leftbracketingbar d f \u03c1 u22 d wherein f is a friction coefficient u is a flow velocity of steam and the unit is m s \u03c1 is a steam density and the unit is kg m3 d is a pipeline diameter and the unit is m the aperture of a leakage hole is less than the pipeline diameter and a pipeline length and the variation of friction coefficients of two adjacent sides of the leakage hole within a short distance are ignored in the case of pipeline leakage no phenomena of obvious free outflow and flow reduction of steam occur because of the presence of the thermal insulation layer 6 and therefore pressure gradients upstream and downstream of the leakage point are approximately the same and after being stabilized the pressures restore an original pressure distribution along the pipeline it can be obtained from simultaneous equations 8 10 that x l s p 1 pm p 1 p 2 since the arrangement locations of the sensors are known the location of the leakage point can be positioned accurately according to a calculated value x and in step 3 in the process of positioning the location of the leakage point a correction coefficient \u03be is introduced and the value x is corrected by a method of using temperatures to correct pressures wherein the correction coefficient is represented by a formula below \u03be 2 tmt 1 t 2 a corrected new value x is x l s p 1 pm p 1 p 2 \u03be wherein tm is the pipeline leakage transient steam temperature and the unit is k dot over t 1 is a temperature value detected by the temperature sensor upstream of the leakage point and the unit is k and dot over t 2 is a temperature value detected by the temperature sensor downstream of the leakage point and the unit is k"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "since the heating pipeline is long a temperature sensor is arranged within a certain distance downstream of the pressure sensor according to a common construction method and the heating pipeline needs a unit division to facilitate monitoring analysis"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "when an on off event happens to the heating supply pump unit at the starting end of the pipeline a great gradient variation of the pressure in the pipeline may be caused which can cause a false leakage early warning easily therefore the plc collects data from the pressure sensors and the temperature sensors to form a pressure dataset p1 p2 p3 p4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101504545-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "on the other hand by installing a temperature sensor to prevent freezing of the water purification equipment in case of installation in the winter or cold weather areas it is possible to prevent damage to facilities by freezing membranes and system protection devices for mobile water treatment devices bars are untested"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0738408-Y2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore while suppressing the waste of tap water as much as possible as a device that prevents freezing with no maintenance cost a faucet as seen in kaisho 62 156445an electric valve is installed in the bypass pipe that connects the upstream side of therutotomoni a temperature sensor thatdetect the outside air temperatureis provided the outside airwhen the temperature reaches around 0 c the electric power is applied at a constant cycle.the water in the water pipe is intermittently opened by opening the valve for a short time.a device that discharges water from the bypass pipe to the outsideis proposed"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325646-B2", "para_id": "para_358", "text": "the efc according to any embodiment may further include an oxidation reduction potential sensor a ph sensor a chlorine sensor a conductivity sensor a flow rate sensor a temperature sensor or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325646-B2", "para_id": "para_367", "text": "the efc according to any embodiment may further include an oxidation reduction potential sensor a ph sensor a chlorine sensor a conductivity sensor a flow rate sensor a temperature sensor or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130731-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an automatic cleaning unit for cleaning the foreign matter attached wherein the uv treatment unit uv lamp unit for irradiating the ultraviolet light to the filtered water in the filtering unit a washing unit for removing the foreign matter attached to the ultraviolet lamp unit and the ultraviolet ray uv intensity meter for measuring the intensity of ultraviolet light from the lamp and on temperature for measuring the temperature inside the body including a sensor it can prevent secondary pollution due to by products prevent contamination of tanks efficient and easy to maintain sterilization effect and product miniaturization and an integrated water treatment device using an ultraviolet lamp"}, {"pat_id": "US-10633265-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a device for the filtration of water in containers comprising an electrolysis cartridge with electrified plates and an automation device which act synergistically the device including at least three metal rectangular plates on the electrolysis cartridge each of the rectangular plates includes one end having a groove that forms a folded terminal at least one interleaved plate placed between the at least three rectangular metal plates the at least one interleaved plate is placed equidistantly between the plates with terminals the at least three metal rectangular plates and the interleaved plates are placed inside a casing having threaded ends and with an inner walls having a pair of grooved insulating plates with channels disposed towards a center of the casing each channel of each one of the grooved insulation plate coincides in arrangement and size with respect to the channel of the opposing grooved insulation plate in such a way that the plates and the interleaved plates are inserted into each pair of the channels of the insulation plates an innermost end of each insulation plate includes a stop to detain the advance of the plates and at the opposite end of each insulation plate includes a lock having a t shape having at least one groove wherein if one of the grooves is at a crossing point of the lines forming it and that said groove coincides in size and shape to accommodate the fold of the extension being in the at least one of the metal rectangular plates on an opposite section from where the groove is located the lock has a fold having a form of a square u to be supported on the edge of the insulation plate in which the lock is placed and that the insulation plate has an groove to ensure a correct positioning of the lock when the lock is placed in the groove a cross section that forms the t shape presses the plates avoiding that they travel in the channels at the same time the fold has a flange that when closing the cartridge is arranged on the inside of a first lid causing the closure a lid includes a first cylindrical section attached to a surrounding plate which at an end of which is attached to the cylindrical section has a stop which engages in a notch at the edge of the casing toward the center of the lid on the side where the stop is located there is a second cylindrical section which supports a gasket which performs an airtight seal between the casing and the lid the casing and the lid are secured by a threaded ring in its internal section and grooved by its outer face whose thread is engaged in the casing since the latter has the counterpart of the thread of the ring on the outside of the casing immediately after the ring a surrounding casing is placed which contacts the terminals of the plates in such a way that by employing as many conventional cables attached to the terminals as are inserted into a insulating casing submerged in epoxy resin which protects them the opposite end is attached to a conventional automation control box in order to electrify the plates inside the housing at the opposite end of the casing a second cap is screwed with the same characteristics as the first cap however the automation device comprises a t connection in the cross section of a plug that seals are inserted and has a hole centered through which is a stem forming a single piece with a blade positioned inside the connection the opposite end of said rod activates a flow sensor which is conventionally connected to a pcb electronic board and in the same way the card is connected to a temperature sensor which is placed in the t connection on one side of the stem said sensor measures the temperature of the water flow through the t connection at the same time the water passage activates the stem and the previous measurements are sent to a logical processing unit to automate the process"}, {"pat_id": "US-10633265-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the above described device therefore constitutes an electrochemical cell which is manipulated from an automated control box from which the energy arriving at the plates and the charges positive and negative is emitted producing the electrolysis inside the housing of the cartridge at the same time the flow levels are measured by a sensor that takes the pulse of the hydraulic flow converting it into an electrical signal which is transmitted to the automation control box similarly a second sensor measures the temperature and is transmitted to the same control box which can be controlled manually or fully automated either by synchronous asynchronous or real time connection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541137-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "the control unit 500 may apply a driving signal to the fan 100 when the temperature of the ballast water w sensed by the sensor unit 300 becomes lower than a preset freezing point of the ballast water w"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541137-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "3 when the temperature of the ballast water w sensed by the sensor unit 300 becomes higher than the freezing point of the preset ballast water w the control unit 500 outputs a drive stop signal can be applied"}, {"pat_id": "US-12276638-B2", "para_id": "para_111", "text": "to facilitate such an arrangement component 202 may be any suitable sensor for tolerating a given environment such as a high temperature piezo bender and any suitable wires such as high temperature wires with shielding jacketing and or conduit may be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008089-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in addition according to the wireless communication terminal system and a method of driving the built in smart metering based temperature sensor according to the present invention the management server transmits the status information of the water meter to the user terminal according to the temperature information of the water supply pipe transmitted from the wireless communication terminal therefore the effect that the user can prevent the freezing of the water pipe in advance is also obtained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008089-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "1 is a diagram illustrating an example of a system for monitoring a state of underground facilities using a manhole cover based on a low power wide area network lpwan 2 is a block diagram of a wireless communication terminal system incorporating a smart metering based temperature sensor according to the present invention 3 is a block diagram for explaining the configuration of the wireless communication terminal shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "6 the controller unit 130 applied to the present invention controls the raw water pump which may be configured in the raw water supply line to supply the raw water to the raw water supply unit and to control the on and off of the filtered water supply valve 109"}, {"pat_id": "US-10410501-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the water use and water energy use can use non invasive flow and temperature sensors for monitoring and thus no cutting into the water pipe is necessary"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "various types of sensors can be used the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring that are disclosed in the first reference cited above and or the sensors used for leak detection soil heating and temperature mapping that are disclosed in the second set of references cited above"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "in such a configuration a sensor such as a temperature sensor may be included to determine the source of a particular leak among one of a plurality of fluid sources"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100836904-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it consists of a drive 22 for driving the unit 23 the display unit 23 is a filter loss amount display unit 24 for displaying the loss of each filter 5 stored by the wired terminal 70 connected from the outside in percentage and when the filter 5 is replaced filter replacement display section 25 in which the lamp is selectively flashed when the lamp is reached the water level level display section 26 in which the lamp is selectively lit according to the water level level of the water tank 6 and the driving of the pump 3 and it consists of a drive display unit 27 the lamp is turned on when the water leakage and a water temperature display unit 28 for displaying cold and hot water the output terminal of the mpu 21 is installed on one side of the facet 8a is connected to the facet lamp 9 for providing a refreshing feeling when the water is discharged the water level sensor 30 is installed in the water tank 6 at the input end of the mpu 21 and senses the water level in four stages and the water leakage sensor is installed on the bottom surface of the case 1 to detect water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "10 is extended to the outside through the through hole 21a and the waterproof clamp 20 to prevent the water flowing through the fire water supply pipe 3 a backflow pipe 30 having both ends connected to the front and rear ends of the fire water supply pipe 30 so as to communicate with the front and rear ends of the installation position of the heater 10 a pump 40 connected to the backflow pipe 30 so that water flowing through the firefighting water supply pipe 3 flows back through the backflow pipe 30 the waterproof clamp 20 is formed in a semi circular shape the through hole 21a is formed the inner peripheral surface is provided with a waterproof portion 21 having a packing 21b for blocking the periphery of the through hole 4 and the bolt 22 combination with the waterproof portion 21 is composed of a semi circular fixing portion 23 for fixing the waterproof portion 21 to the circumferential surface of the fire water supply pipe 3 the power supply system rechargeable battery 50 is applied to the charge is connected to the heater 10 and the auxiliary heater 10 to supply power a control unit 60 for controlling charging and discharging of the rechargeable battery 50 and operations of the heater 10 and the pump 40 a water temperature sensor 70 around the heater 10 and fixedly installed on an inner circumferential surface of the fire water supply pipe 3 so as to be positioned at a circumference of the heater 10 it includes a detection sensor 80 for detecting the operation of the fire fighting equipment connected to the fire water supply pipe 3 the control unit 60 receives the signals of the water temperature sensor 70 and the sensor 80 to prevent the water heater 10 from freezing only water around the heater 10 when the water temperature is lower than the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "do not freeze only the surrounding water to prevent freezing of the fire water supply pipe 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "and the heater 10 is extended to the outside through the through hole 4 formed in the fire water supply pipe 3 in the state installed inside the fire water supply pipe 3 the waterproof clamp 20 installed in the fire water supply pipe 3 since water is used to prevent leakage there is an advantage that the installation and maintenance of the heater 10 is very easy"}, {"pat_id": "US-4250391-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the predetermined temperature of the appendix is then set by means of the heater 9 which in turn is regulated via the sensor 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-6096202-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the information regarding flow rate temperature and conductivity which is monitored by sensor 32 is sent to controller 38 via line 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a water pressure control encoder switch for adjusting the intensity of the water output the temperature of the water ph concentration the operation button to receive the output time the water level sensor for measuring the water level an input unit configured of a temperature sensor measuring a temperature of water a pump for raising the water to the shampoo ware a heater for heating the water to a temperature set by the operation button an electrolysis tank for ionizing the water and performing electrolysis to match the ph concentration input to the operation button ac power is supplied to the shampoo ware the auxiliary tank equipped with a heater an electrolysis tank a drain box for collecting sewage a solenoid opened and closed to control the flow of water between a water supply tank into which water is input and the solenoid a pump a compressor and a heater"}]</data>
</edge>
