biofouling which is expected in a typical treated wastewater stream and associated wastewater handling equipment it is beneficial for the tss sensor 5a to include a wiper system not shown per se which periodically cleans the face of the sensor component not shown per se of the tss sensor 5a"}, {"pat_id": "US-11407653-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "it will be understood be a person skilled in the relevant art that components of the water quality and monitoring device 2 may be made of any suitable material including but not limited to pvc abs brass or any other suitable material known to a person skilled in the relevant art for the various fittings and components lids valves sensor ports etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-11407653-B2", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "this sensor can indicate possible contamination via bacteria colonies that have greater potential to be present in water with higher levels of turbidity or indicate other potential contaminants ranging from lead to various ions e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100839026-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention also provides a method for converting the agricultural water into agricultural reuse water by removing salt from river water using the desalination system.desalination system according to the present invention by using a salt decomposition system to remove salts in the water such as sewage treatment plant effluent and stream inflow water to provide agricultural reuse water that can be used as agricultural water by filtration and disinfection the ec sensor connected to the control box it is effective to monitor and control the whole process of hydrolysis by using it"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3468925-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "the method may further comprise providing instructions to direct substantially all of the wastewater to the first wastewater stream until the contaminant sensor measures a threshold wastewater flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3468925-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "the method may further comprise directing overflow wastewater to the overflow wastewater stream responsive to the sensor measuring a concentration of contaminants exceeding the threshold concentration"}, {"pat_id": "US-10464021-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "the one or more sensors 160 can be configured to the presence absence or concentration of one or more markers in the feed stream 112 the feed concentrate 116 the draw stream 122 the diluted draw stream 126 or the ro permeate 156 via one or more of uv visible spectroscopy fluorimetry conductivity or a fluoride selective electrode probe"}, {"pat_id": "US-11278880-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "we also provide a method of operating the water softening device including a filter configured to remove hardness from a first stream of raw water to produce a second stream of softened water wherein the filter includes an ion exchange material the iex material is loaded with a first cationic ion species deriving from a tracer salt the iex material has a lower affinity to the first cationic ion species than to the hardness the iex material is loaded with a second cationic ion species deriving from a regenerant salt and the iex material has a lower affinity to the second cationic ion species than to the first cationic ion species wherein a first stream of raw water is passed through a filter including an iex material configured to remove hardness from the first stream of raw water thereby producing a second stream of softened water the iex material is loaded with the first cationic ion species the iex material is loaded with the second cationic ion species and an electrical property of the second stream is monitored by a sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_508", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-5340468-A", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a system adapted for regulating the addition of lime to reduce water alkalinity comprising a treatment vessel having 1 a mixing zone wherein a stream of untreated water is mixed with lime and 2 a flocculation zone that receives said mixture of water and lime from said mixing zone and allows precipitation of the resulting insoluble salts a first sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said stream of untreated water entering said mixing zone a second sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said water in said flocculation zone pump means for adding said lime to said untreated water in said mixing zone and a controller operable for regulating said pump means by periodically sampling said conductivities measured by said first sensor and said second sensor computing the ratio of said conductivities for each sample computing the slope of said conductivity ratio and determining the minimum value of said conductivity ratio said controller being operable for regulating said pump means so that sufficient lime is added to said water to pass through said minimum conductivity ratio and further turning said pump means off when said ratio exceeds a predetermined maximum set point and said slope is positive and turning said pump means on when said ratio falls below a predetermined minimum set point and said slope is negative"}, {"pat_id": "US-8097212-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the simplest way to prevent biofouling of the platinum redox sensor is to locate it in a strongly flowing part of the water stream in the pipe e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102224305-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore the contamination detection sensor 50 is configured to sense all or part of the factor and continuously transmits real time sensing information for each factor or when a value equal to or greater than a threshold set for a specific factor is sensed the corresponding sensing information it can be configured to send out only"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102224305-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "the management unit 150 may set an opening time of the on off valve 40 and an opening closing control period of the on off valve 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101489530-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "this river is equipped with a sensor to measure the electrical conductivity of water to determine the degree of contamination of the flowing water"}, {"pat_id": "US-6657546-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the input from either sensor 34 or 36 or both can be used to determine activation of a chemical feeder 42 for maintaining the proper sanitizer level in the flowing water stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082127-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "consisting of a salinity meter installed on the ballast water inlet pipe to measure salinity of the ballast water introduced a chemical tank supplying a sterilant to the ballast water inlet pipe through a metering pump a physical treatment device installed on the main transport pipe to kill remove and damage the zooplankton and the underwater microorganisms by physical impact using the flow rate and pressure of ballast water it is connected to the outlet of the physical processing device the positive electrode plate and the negative electrode plate is installed alternately therein the variable rectifier capable of controlling the voltage and current according to the flow rate of the incoming fluid the flow rate inside the pipe and the salt concentration of seawater an electrolysis device that receives power and generates residual chlorine to perform sterilization treatment on microorganisms in water a tro sensor connected to the outlet of the electrolysis device and measuring the concentration of the oxidant and on the basis of the salinometer measurement value or the measured value of the tro sensor including a control device for controlling the inflow into the ballast water inlet pipe the inflow into the ballast water transport pipe the chemical input amount or the amount of power supplied from the rectifier when the salinity of ballast water measured by the salinity meter is 0 to 8 psu the sterilant is supplied to the ballast water inlet pipe through the chemical tank and the ballast water supplied with the sterilizer is either front or rear of the physical pretreatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377605-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention has an advantageous effect of enabling a quick response by directly detecting the contamination leakage by a sensor directly installed in the field.1 is a diagram showing a state in which in the water treatment instrumentation control system for a smart city of the present invention a pair of sensors for water quality inspection are installed at regular intervals symmetrically left and right at the edges of a tributary p and a main stream m"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300 connected to the unit and capable of checking and operating managing measurement data of the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360 for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420 for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers for water supply and sewage treatment by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430 for storing measured data of quantity and water quality of each region and state information and manager information of each unit receiving the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote location the transmission unit for transmitting the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the sewage treatment automatic control unit or integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine 410 wow water quality management remote control system comprising a control system unit 400 consisting of a mobile communication terminal text transmission unit 440 for generating a short text message"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}]</data>
</edge>
