  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5574769-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "on the other hand during rainy weather rainwater may flow in along with dirty water and rainy unknown water may be generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102009623-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "eighth the fine dust detection sensor rainfall detection sensor road surface detection sensor cctv to detect the dust state of the road outside the injector is equipped with the effect that can remove the dust completely by spraying when checking the site situation in real time have.1 is a schematic diagram showing a clean rod watering system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "therefore the inflow path into which the river water flows into the primary storage tank is always lower than the river water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101604772-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "according to the present invention the phenomenon occurring when the lid technique is applied to the watershed the phenomenon such as erosion scouring and sedimentation occurring in the river due to the increase and decrease of the effluent the total amount of suspended substances contained in the generated effluent it is possible to easily carry out a phenomenon such as erosion and scouring of the surface soil analysis of the correlation between the degree of compaction and the increase or decrease in the amount of penetration and more reliable data can be secured"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102261819-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the simulation and prediction unit uses turbidity and alkalinity as main factors during rainfall among the factors of the inflow flow rate of raw water hydrogen ion concentration turbidity alkalinity electrical conductivity and water temperature and hydrogen ion concentration and the mixed paper drug injection derivation unit 1310 that derives the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper with the water temperature as the main factor the raw water inflow of the flocculated paper and the settling basin the g value of the flocculated paper water temperature turbidity and the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper through the visualized interface image a flocculation paper settling cell sludge management unit 1320 that establishes a plan detects changes in the sludge interface through a sensor and corrects the sludge by checking the degree of agglomeration through light intensity detection and the number of loss head filtration duration and filtered water the filter paper management unit 1330 that establishes a plan for autonomous backwashing through turbidity information the advanced treatment management unit 1340 that performs accident and failure prediction through the status information of the ozone generating device and the maintenance of the water level of the purified water and optimum chlorine it is preferable to provide a purified water disinfection ability management unit 1350 for deriving the contact time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101959509-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a monitoring system for a rainfall runoff pollutant filtration apparatus comprising a rainfall runoff having an opening at an upper end thereof an outlet formed at one or more sides of the lower runoff the filtration unit is installed inside the main body and filters rainwater effluent flowing into the opening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101959509-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "that is the non contact sensor 146 is installed in the waterproof and dustproof spring cylinder 142 to operate as a switch and the increase in weight of the filtration part 120 of the rainfall effluent contaminant filtering device 100 can be confirmed at the lowest standby power state have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102340325-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "in addition in the present invention it is possible to provide an iot based drinking water storage tank management platform service through real time water quality information monitoring an analysis algorithm exceeding the standard value and big data related to season rainfall and water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the control unit provided in the terminal box can receive the rainfall information measured by the rainfall measurement sensor to control the initial rainfall non point pollution source system characterized in that for controlling the operation of the valve drive motor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "non point source contaminant treatment system and method of first rain the present invention relates to an initial rainfall non point source treatment system to separate the initial rainwater containing a large amount of non point source during the rainfall to discharge to the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the present invention provides a method for separating and discharging a nonpoint source from initial rainfall a rainfall measurement step s1 in which the rainfall measurement sensor 200 measures rainfall a closing switch operation step s2 of operating a switch to close the pollution separation pipe 140 when the rainfall measured in the rainfall measurement step reaches the pollution separation pipe closing rainfall amount the closing signal generated in the closing switch operation step is transmitted to the control unit 310 and the control unit 310 receives the closing signal to drive the valve driving motor 142 through the electric valve 141 pollution separation pipe 140 s3 to separate the contaminant pipe closing step after the contamination separation pipe opening step is closed the control unit after the pollution separation pipe opening setting time set by the manager through the input unit 330 provided in the terminal box 300 has elapsed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 power generation unit 11 solar module 20 support 100 rainboard 110 first settling tank 120 second settling tank 130 valve box 140 contamination separation pipe 141 electric valve 142 valve drive motor 143 backflow prevention trap 144 gas backflow prevention albo 150 suspended solids filter 160 steel grating 200 rainfall sensor 210 rain gauge case 211 rain gauge bottom 212 lever 213 coupling member 220 bucket 221 bucket pillar 222 bucket pillar support 223 lever 224 weight 225 magnet 226 switch 227 lever pin 230 water inlet 240 filter medium 300 terminal box 310 control unit 320 charging unit 330 input unit 340 timer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this configuration although it consumes electrical energy and requires installation of a separate sensor motor and controller the initial rainwater inlet 61 of the initial rainwater storage unit 60 is clogged with contaminants or the initial rainwater storage unit even if the initial rainfall is not stored due to breakage of 60 the storm guide unit 50 may be driven as a driving source based on the information detected from the sensor thereby storing the storm"}]</data>
</edge>
