  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5574769-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "on the other hand during rainy weather rainwater may flow in along with dirty water and rainy unknown water may be generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "at this time it is preferable to further attach a water level sensor to the upper inner surface of the guide water pipe body 20 so that when rainwater flows in and moves to the height of the water level sensor a detection signal is transmitted to the lifting lowering guide cylinder 62 to operate it thereby lowering the water level and preventing rainwater from stagnating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102047325-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a storage tank 20 into which rainwater flows into the road rain gutter 10 buoyancy material 30 is installed in the storage tank 20 a sensor 40 installed inside the storage tank 20 consists of including when the buoyancy material 30 is raised by the excellent buoyancy introduced into the storage tank 20 is in contact with the sensor 40 the waterproof door 100 is automatically operated a guide 50 is further installed at the bottom of the sensor 40 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement along the guide 50 one side 53 of the guide 50 is attached to the inner wall of the storage tank 20 and the other side of the guide 50 is formed with a projection 55 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement by the buoyancy while being bitten by the projection 55 the storage tank movable structure using buoyancy characterized in that the water level control material 70 is installed in the storage tank 20 to adjust the waterproof door movable water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water level detection sensor 290 is installed inside the rainwater garden 200 the water level detection sensor 290 is connected to the control panel 260 and is controlled to stop operation when the water level is below a predetermined water level the open upper part of the rainwater garden 200 is further provided with a plurality of sealing plates 300 sealing the rainwater to prevent the rainwater from being directly introduced into the rainwater garden 200 when it rains 312 and a grid grid 314 and a pitcher control plate 320 which is seated on the grid 312 and forms a fine pore by blocking the grid grid hole 314 the permeable control plate 320 is a plate like structure in which a first rectangular plate 322 and a second rectangular plate 324 are laminated in a multilayer structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "a water level detection sensor 290 is installed inside the rainwater garden 200 the water level detection sensor 290 is connected to the control panel 260 and is controlled to stop operation when the water level is below a predetermined water level the open upper part of the rainwater garden 200 is further provided with a plurality of sealing plates 300 sealing the rainwater to prevent the rainwater from being directly introduced into the rainwater garden 200 when it rains 312 and a grid grid 314 and a pitcher control plate 320 which is seated on the grid 312 and forms a fine pore by blocking the grid grid hole 314 the permeable control plate 320 is a plate like structure in which a first rectangular plate 322 and a second rectangular plate 324 are laminated in a multilayer structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 that stores and stores rainwater flowing through the filter a pump that is installed at the bottom of the storage tank and rotates the rainwater stored in the storage tank from time to time or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 90 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the event of a malfunction the filter 10 of the rainwater recycling device s configured including a control unit 60 equipped with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 on one side an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200480951-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a grating apparatus having a clogging alarm and an odor shielding function according to the present invention for introducing rainwater and sewage on a road or a ship into a sewer line buried underground an outer frame which is seated on the upper surface of the sewer installed on the surface a plurality of bearing bars spaced apart from each other by a predetermined distance on the inner side of the outer frame and having a sewage inlet formed in mutually spaced spaces an opening closing plate for opening closing the sewage inlet with a plate member having a shape corresponding to the sewage inlet one end portion of the plate is pivotally coupled to the opening closing plate and is supported on the bottom surface of the opening closing plate so as to open close the sewage inlet and the other end is coupled to the inner frame of the outer frame or the bearing bar spring at least one hydraulic pressure sensor provided on an upper surface of the opening closing plate a data transmission means for transmitting the water pressure information sensed through the water pressure sensor to the management office by wire or wirelessly wherein when the water pressure sensed by the water pressure sensor is equal to or greater than a predetermined value it is determined that the upper part of the grating is blocked and an alarm sound is generated in the management office"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2885467-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "if the occurrence of water is detected this can be passed on via the control unit just like any other leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2885467-B1", "para_id": "para_173", "text": "the controller 210 is connected to a moisture sensor via a long cable and provides information to the server about moisture from other sources such as rainwater that does not leak from the monitored water installation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101361634-B1", "para_id": "claim_15", "text": "a screen installed in a flow path of a wastewater and wastewater and sewage treatment facility or a rainwater drainage pumping station and inclined to block a contaminant a ground guide part installed parallel to the upper portion of the screen a lake driving unit coupled to the inner side of the ground guide part so as to remove the impurities and it is coupled to the outside of the ground guide portion includes a moving means for moving the ground guide portion the moving means may include a first moving frame coupled to the front surface of the ground guide part a first moving device installed on the first moving frame a first moving guide rail on which the first moving device is guided and the ground guide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the air nozzle 20 is provided integrally with the injection pipe 21 and at the same time one or more are fixed so that the supplied air is sprayed so that water can circulate in the storage tank 80 and at the end of the injection pipe 21 a fitting 22 is provided so that one touch coupling with the air supply hose 23 is possible and the fitting 22 is installed on the side surface 12 of the main body 10 and the inner receiving space of the main body 10 11 is filled with anti pollution means 30 in which elvan quartz loess balls activated carbon and charcoal are mixed to prevent contamination or deterioration of stored water and a perforated groove 41 at the upper end thereof to prevent separation the formed cover plate 40 is coupled and fixed to the main body while on one side of the edge of the main body 10 a heating wire 50 for preventing freezing and a temperature at which the inside temperature is sensed to transmit a signal to the controller 70 one or more water pollution prevention units d having the sensor 60 installed and fixed are disposed on the bottom of the storage tank and fixing the water pollution prevention units installed and fixed in series or parallel when the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe passes through the filter and is stored as water in the storage tank the stored water is contamination prevention means 30 by spraying air from the air nozzle 20 of the water pollution prevention unit d and sprayed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 the water level controller 32 includes a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor 29 the second sensor 30 and the third sensor 31 of the water level sensor portion the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 16 may be discharged through the discharge pipe 22 for a predetermined discharge time when the time counted by the timer 33 becomes longer than a predetermined time wherein the control unit controls the discharge valve 21 so that the discharge water 21 is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level controller may further include a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor the second sensor and the third sensor of the water level sensor portion and controls the discharge valve so that the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank can be discharged through the discharge pipe for a preset discharge time when the discharge time exceeds the predetermined set time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "fourthly the present invention provides a bollard type hot water leak inspection panel protector suitable for guiding rainwater to the ground by the geometry of the inlet cover and the exhaust cover to prevent rainwater penetration more efficiently.bollard type hot water leak detection panel protector according to the present invention for achieving the above object the bollard is provided with a hot water leak detection panel electrically connected to the hot water leak detection sensor for detecting the leakage of the hot water supply pipe buried in the ground type hot water leakage meter panel protector a wiring through hole for passing the cable of the hot water leak detection sensor embedded in the ground is formed at the bottom and a hot water leak meter panel is installed"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0525594-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the seal can also be installed above the waste body surface seal to prevent the ingress of rainwater and thus the washing out of pollutants from the waste"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192404-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a control server for controlling water purification by informing replacement time of media based on measurement data wow water supply protection and non point source reduction control system using a green dam characterized in that it comprises a central control unit for receiving and monitoring the discharge amount and the water purification control data from the control server and controls the control server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sensor unit for sensing water data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility and a controller for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed value of the sensor unit and a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of the field sub control panels and for controlling the equipment section and the field sub control panel through bidirectional communication with the plurality of field sub control panels a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile terminal of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a sensor unit for sensing water data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility and a controller for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed value of the sensor unit and a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of the field sub control panels and for controlling the equipment section and the field sub control panel through bidirectional communication with the plurality of field sub control panels a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile terminal of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided an application for supporting an integrated remote management system for a plurality of water treatment facilities including a sensor unit for sensing water resource data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility a plurality of on site sub control units for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed values of the sensor unit and installed in the water treatment facility a water treatment system comprising a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of field sub control boards in two way communication with the plurality of the field sub control boards and controlling the facility and the sub control boards a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile application of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method of operating an integrated remote management system for a plurality of water treatment facilities including a sensor unit for sensing water resource data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility a plurality of on site sub control units for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed values of the sensor unit and installed in the water treatment facility a water treatment system comprising a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of field sub control boards in two way communication with the plurality of the field sub control boards and controlling the facility and the sub control boards a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile application of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system a method for operating an integrated remote management system for a facility the method comprising the steps of collecting and processing information measured by the sensor unit in the field main control panel and transmitting the current operating state a first step of sending an urgent maintenance message to a mobile terminal of a remote manager using a text message if urgent maintenance is required a second step of the mobile terminal of the remote manager receiving the text message transmitted through the first process when the emergency message is received through the second process the remote manager confirms the text message executes the application ratm and the third step of checking the necessity of urgent inspection by the administrator when the water treatment time requested through the text message is confirmed including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method for operating an integrated remote management system for a plurality of water treatment facilities including a sensor unit for sensing water resource data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility a plurality of on site sub control units for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed values of the sensor unit and installed in the water treatment facility a water treatment system comprising a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of field sub control boards in two way communication with the plurality of the field sub control boards and controlling the facility and the sub control boards a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile application of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system a method for operating an integrated remote management s