and a removal conveyor that is embedded in the removal box so that the inside of the removal box is separated to block the movement of the solid foreign material to the rear end and a foreign material removal unit comprising a removal motor rotating the removal conveyor so that the solid foreign material blocked by the removal conveyor is discharged to the outside an initial filter installed on the exit side of the foreign material removal unit and in which sand and activated carbon are sequentially stacked an induction pipe installed on the exit side of the initial filter to supply the initial rainwater to the raw water storage tank a supply pipe for supplying the raw water passing through the separation box to the raw water storage tank a rotary bulkhead rotatably installed inside the separation box so that the inlet pipe passes through either side of the bypass pipe or the supply pipe and a control unit that receives the detection value of the detection sensor and operates the driving motor to rotate the rotary partition wall.as described above the present invention detects the contamination state of raw water flowing in from the outside and separately treats raw water initial rainwater or wastewater that contains a large amount of solid foreign substances and is heavily polluted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102342900-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "this will allow for the rapid treatment of large volumes of sewage.100 drain pipe 110 separation box 120 detection sensor 130 bypass pipe 140 supply pipe 150 control unit 160 foreign material removal unit 170 initial filter 171 sand 172 activated carbon 180 guide tube 190 initial foreign matter removal unit 191 housing 192 door 193 moving box 194 drain hole 199 inlet pipe 200 drive motor 210 rotating bulkhead"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101058919-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "if the treatment unit is high water may include the step of discharging the filtered rainwater to the outside of the first initial excellent treatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this configuration although it consumes electrical energy and requires installation of a separate sensor motor and controller the initial rainwater inlet 61 of the initial rainwater storage unit 60 is clogged with contaminants or the initial rainwater storage unit even if the initial rainfall is not stored due to breakage of 60 the storm guide unit 50 may be driven as a driving source based on the information detected from the sensor thereby storing the storm"}, {"pat_id": "US-7997295-B2", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "the system may work in a similar manner to the systems described in au 2003262296 and the controller 410 may receive a signal from for example a rainwater sensor 490 to indicate whether or not there is sufficient rainwater to fulfil demand"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102227198-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "to this end although not shown in the drawing the rainwater pipe connected to the storage tank 10 may be provided with a pollution detection sensor that detects the degree of contamination of incoming rainwater and a shut off valve module that blocks the inflow of rainwater from the rainwater pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102227198-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "at this time the shut off valve module may block the inflow of rainwater from the rainwater pipe when it is determined that rainwater flowing through the rainwater pipe is contaminated above a reference value based on the detection information detected by the pollution detection sensor"}]</data>
</edge>
