ion according to the water level measurement information provided from the water level sensor 524"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_295", "text": "here algae related sensors may include for example chlorophyll a sensor 503 ss sensor 508 turbidity sensor 506 and the like and organic contaminant related sensors may include for example water temperature medicine layer sensor 504 orp and the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-11014837-B2", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "specifically the present embodiments relate to a technology for providing an energy self contained oceanic drone on which an ocean survey and monitoring complex sensor is mounted using a polymer electrolyte fuel cell and a solar cell based on new renewable energy complexly"}, {"pat_id": "US-11014837-B2", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "furthermore the monitoring unit 360 may monitor a temperature degree of electrolysis and or water level of the sea or river which is measured using an sbe37im sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the contaminant sensor 12 prevents the inflow of contaminated water by closing the raw water inlet valve 14 when oil leakage or rapid deterioration of water by a vessel occurs in the sea shore or river and the virus sterilization device 20 by removing harmful bacteria such as norovirus vibrio bacteria and cholera bacteria water is evenly introduced into the virus sterilizer 20 through the distribution screen 22 to remove the bacteria by contacting the raw water to the uv lamp or uvled 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101994814-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention the control unit 150 controls the first hydraulic cylinder 112 and the second hydraulic cylinder 122 of the first and second driving units 110 and 120 and detects the operation of the piston through the sensor to determine whether to open or close the water level door 200 and the water gate 700.the system for preventing backflow of seawater and river water in a sewer system of coastal cities and lowlands according to the present invention is characterized in that a river or sea flows backward by controlling a sluice passage and a sluice gate formed between a sewer pipe and a sluice outlet to flow river water or seawater into a sewer pipe there is an effect that can be prevented.1 is an exemplary view of a conventional sewage system 2 is a perspective view of a movable backflow prevention system for seawater and river water in a sewer system of a coastal city and a lowland according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102524681-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the ice cleaning duct washing discharge control method required to clean the water supply duct using the ice washing medium in the water supply duct the ice cleaning duct washing discharge control method in the water supply duct blocking the water valve on the supplier side and the water valve on the consumer side of the pipeline to be cleaned s11 opening the washing water inlet valve configured at the rear end of the water valve on the supplier side and injecting the washing medium into the conduit while applying pressure using the inlet pump s12 washing the inside of the pipe while passing the cleaning medium by increasing the pressure with the inlet pump inside the pipe s13 washing the inside of the water supply pipe with a washing medium and discharging washing discharged water discharged after washing through a discharge pipe formed in front of the water supply valve on the receiving side s14 a step of firstly and periodically transmitting the sensed water quality data to a controller by a water quality sensor installed at a rear end of the discharge pipe and sensing water quality data of discharged water flowing through the discharge pipe s15 determining whether or not the received first water quality data is equal to or less than a predetermined effluent water quality standard s16 in the case of the following the controller opens the solenoid valve installed in the discharge pipe to discharge the washing discharge water to the river s17 sensing the amount of discharged water discharged into the river by the flow sensor unit of the drained water discharge pipe installed at the rear end of the water quality sensor unit and transmitting the sensed discharged water quantity information to the controller s18 transmitting by the controller primary water quality data and discharged water flow rate information to a center server of a water quality management center s19 determining whether the received water quality data meets drinking water quality standards by a controller that periodically receives water quality data from the water quality sensor unit s20 if appropriate turning off the washing water inlet valve configured in the washing water inlet to stop the injection of the washing water and opening the water supply valve to supply tap water to the corresponding pipe s21 monitoring the secondary water quality data transmitted from the water quality sensor unit by the controller while discharging tap water supplied to the water supply pipe through the discharge pipe s22 and if the received water quality data meets the drinking water quality standards transmitting the water quality data to the manager smart terminal to block the discharge valve of the discharge pipe and open the water valve on the consumer side to supply tap water to the consumer s23"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3169203-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water quality sensor installation device in which a water quality sensor immersed in a river or the like is housed in a light shielding container having an outflow inflow port for water wherein the container is formed in a cylindrical shape extending vertically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "therefore the inflow path into which the river water flows into the primary storage tank is always lower than the river water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101604772-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "according to the present invention the phenomenon occurring when the lid technique is applied to the watershed the phenomenon such as erosion scouring and sedimentation occurring in the river due to the increase and decrease of the effluent the total amount of suspended substances contained in the generated effluent it is possible to easily carry out a phenomenon such as erosion and scouring of the surface soil analysis of the correlation between the degree of compaction and the increase or decrease in the amount of penetration and more reliable data can be secured"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101682161-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "first a certain volume of space is provided in a measurement chamber provided with a measurement sensor and water supplied from a water source such as a ground water intake point and a river or a lake can be stored in this space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore it is possible to block the supply of river water or seawater backflowing to the stormwater chamber 110 to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a method of monitoring and controlling a low carbon permeable ecological structure consisting of a plurality of corrosion resistant piles a plurality of horizontal framing frames in the form of spacers an ecological block for water purification and an ecological block for fishes and fishes first the low carbon permeable ecological installed at a predetermined position of the structure 100 receives the detected data from a plurality of sensors 210 to detect the conductivity water quality water temperature or quantity of river water by wire or wireless"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100839026-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention also provides a method for converting the agricultural water into agricultural reuse water by removing salt from river water using the desalination system.desalination system according to the present invention by using a salt decomposition system to remove salts in the water such as sewage treatment plant effluent and stream inflow water to provide agricultural reuse water that can be used as agricultural water by filtration and disinfection the ec sensor connected to the control box it is effective to monitor and control the whole process of hydrolysis by using it"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "motorized valve 11 21 electric valve control panel 12 22 manual valve 13 23 electric valve 14 24 adjustment tank 15 25 snow drift 16 18 26 29 water level monitoring panel 19 optical cable 31 electric pole 32 pipe 33 road 35 inspection pit 36 water level measuring pipe 37 communication pipe 38 sheath heater 46 cable 101 cpu 102 rom 103 ram 104 crt 105 a d converter 106 multiplexer 107 108 amplifier 109 keyboard 110 buffer 111 112 interface 113 photoelectric converter s1 to s13 water level sensor r river w1 to w13 alarm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "as shown in the accompanying drawings in this embodiment the lower end of the sewage pipe 1 in contact with the river or the coast is hingedly coupled to the wear 100 erected or laid down and the sewage pipe in front of the wear 100 the vehicle collection pipe connection pipe 200 branched to the side of 1 the drive means 300 for rotating the wear 100 and the wear 100 are interlocked to open and close the entrance of the vehicle collection pipe connection pipe 200 sluice gate 400 sensors s1 s2 installed at the rear of the weir 100 to detect reverse flow of river water or seawater and the water level of ou water flowing down the sewage pipe by being installed in front of the weir 100 a control unit 500 that opens and closes the wear 100 and the sluice 400 in an interlocking manner by operating the driving means 300 by sensing a sensor s3 s4 for detecting a signal from the sensors s1 to s4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "therefore the sensor s3 s4 for detecting the water level when there is no detection signal the wear 100 is kept in an erect state and an alarm for separate inspection is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in the present embodiment two sensors s1 s2 are installed but the present invention is not limited thereto and only one sensor for detecting the level of river water or seawater may be installed and used at a predetermined height behind the wear 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition when the sensor s3 does not respond and a signal is generated from the sensor s1 or s2 the driving means 300 made of a lifting bag is operated to raise the wear 100 to prevent reverse flow of river water or seawater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand when a signal is generated from the sensor s4 the weir 100 is unconditionally inverted and laid down thereby blocking the sluice gate 400 on the side of the pipe connection pipe 200 to block the inflow of river water or seawater to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101489530-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "this river is equipped with a sensor to measure the electrical conductivity of water to determine the degree of contamination of the flowing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102257822-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "comprehensive management by receiving the information collected by the flow meter sensor 100 installed in the sewage pipe 110 which is a monitoring point the data collector 200 installed in the field control panel and the flow meter sensor 100 and the data collector 200 to include a monitoring server 300 installed in the central control room a water quality purification biofilm unit is further installed at the river discharge end ex of the sewage pipe 110 wherein the water quality purification biofilm unit is a dam dam installed to block drainage by blocking a part of the discharge end ex a purification groove hom formed in a predetermined depth at a predetermined interval in a part of the length of the dam dam a pair of vertical frames ver standing and fixed at both ends of the width center of the dam dam a horizontal frame hoz connecting and fixing the upper end of the vertical frame ver a double shaft winch wic fixed on the horizontal frame hoz to be positioned directly above each purification groove hom a drum dr fixed to both shafts of the winch wic and wound around a wire wr in the sewage inflow data management system including a net shaped biofilm purification tank 1000 in which an end of the wire wr is fixed inserted into the purification groove hom and filled with a purification ball therein the biofilm cleaning container 1000 includes a pair of side frames 1100 an upper frame 1200 assembled and fixed to an upper end of the side frame 1100 and a tip of the side frame 1100 and the upper frame 1200 and a front frame 1300 and a rear frame 1400 respectively assembled at the rear end the side frame 1100 the upper frame 1200 the front frame 1300 and the rear frame 1400 are fixed with a wire mesh net w to the rectangular frame f so that water flowing along the river can escape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101102066-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "in addition by grasping the turbidity of the dredging it is effective to separate the water sediment and sludge at the same time to prevent secondary river pollution caused by the drug by applying the appropriate drug.1 is a view illustrating a conventional dredging device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300 connected to the unit and capable of checking and operating managing measurement data of the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360 for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420 for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers for water supply and sewage treatment by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430 for storing measured data of quantity and water quality of each region and state information and manager information of each unit receiving the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote location the transmission unit for transmitting the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the sewage treatment automatic control unit or integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine 410 wow water quality management remote control system comprising a control system unit 400 consisting of a mobile communication terminal text transmission unit 440 for generating a short text message"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}]</data>
