ipment the power supply which is a power supply device supplied from a hydroelectric power generator 213 is inverter 47 and inverter vio access point and internet network vertical multistage pump control server and monitor to pump control board or tagger winch control box and short range wireless communication antenna to short range wireless communication device wireless communication control module and display to electronic control device adc and switch input circuit to electronic control device mcu and electronic control device diac overcurrent breaker brake is connected to power supply to display screen and analog input and digital input are operated by hand to control on off of each pump main switch button and auxiliary switch button to configure vertical multistage pump operation method inside main body 1 of underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment in addition to the above mentioned vertical multi stage pump turbine pump 140 diaphragm pump vane pump or guide vane and propeller pump screw pump plunger pump axial plunger pump radial plunger pump and jet pump 157 are provided and are connected to an introduction pipe and a water supply port or a fire prevention and disaster prevention pipe line 168 and a water discharge port 169 and are connected to a limit switch or a limit switch and a power motor body 192 is provided with a hood and a snap ring a fan and a body frame a body front reinforcing plate a rotor assembly on a rotating shaft a stator assembly on a front rotating shaft support a motor protection casting frame a terminal box and a lifting bolt a terminal box cover a rear rotating shaft support a rear reinforcing plate a gap a fan cover or a protective cover a rotor core and a stator core with stator windings and are connected and connected and underground passage flood prevention a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172182-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in order to block the water supply 15 while descending according to the water supply cutoff again the water supply is separated from the operation sensor to cut off the power supply to the gold or silver plate and the water tank 40 in the lower portion of the waterway inside the frame is turned off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101357244-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the door panel 330 for selectively opening closing the waterway 101 the drive unit 340 for rotating the door panel 330 and the drive unit 340 respectively are provided at the 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102559283-B1", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "the method of claim 16 wherein the step s350 sensing the sludge level through a sludge level sensor s351 the limit switch box for sludge drain is connected to various contacts of the solenoid valve for sludge drain and drives and controls the solenoid valve for sludge drain according to the control signal of the smart control unit s352 the solenoid valve for sludge drain is driven according to the signal of the limit switch box for sludge drain to supply or block air transmitted to the actuator for sludge drain s353 the actuator unit for sludge drain is driven by the solenoid valve for sludge drain and the main valve for sludge drain is directly driven to turn on and off the flow of the waterway on the waterway s354 the main valve for sludge drain is driven according to the drive of the actuator unit for sludge drain and the flow of the waterway is turned on and off s355"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101015621-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "electrode plate fixing bolts for fixing the other end of the electrode plate to the other end of the electrolytic chamber of the main body housing and on the opposite surface of the main body housing to form an electrolytic chamber but formed in the other direction with the inlet sterilization water generation module consisting of a cover housing is formed with an outlet for the discharge of the disinfected sterilized water installed on the water inlet of the inlet water flowing into the disinfectant disinfection water generating module is a positive pressure valve and the sterilization disinfection water to detect the pressure drop is made based on the set pressure inside the waterway tube to operate the sterilization disinfection water generation module static pressure flow rate detection means comprising a flow rate detection sensor for detecting the flow rate inside the water pipe of the inflow water flowing into the module and stopping the flow of the flow rate to stop the operation of the sterilizing disinfection water generating module a filter installed at one side of the water pipe to filter foreign substances contained in influent water flowing into the sterilizing disinfection water generating module supplying power to the disinfectant disinfectant generating module while supplying a positive power and a negative power to the electrolytic reaction to remove the chloride attached to the electrode plate but the chloride generated during electrolysis is applied to the electrode plate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6889881-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a monitoring method and causes the monitoring step the soil pressure or applied to the pipe detected by the earth pressure sensor for storing the detection data of the strain of the pipe detected by the strain sensor to the data logger the tube and leakage determination step of determining the presence or absence of water leakage the said water pressure in the pipe is detected by the pressure sensors used in waterways after the leakage determination step leak location to identify the leakage position by introducing a leak exploration robots it is characterized by having a specific step"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the anti icing system installed inside the sidewalk canal of an underpass a body part which is installed on the floor according to the width of the side channel water pipe and includes a lower frame to which the electric heating wire can be mounted and a column or plate to which a sensor can be attached to either side or one wall side of the water channel pipe can be erected a temperature sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the water pipe to measure the surrounding temperature to derive a temperature measurement value a humidity sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the waterway pipe to measure the surrounding humidity to derive a humidity measurement value a flow measurement device attached to the inner wall of the drain pipe located at the lower end of the side channel waterway and measuring the amount of water flowing from the side channel channel through the drain pipe to the collection well to derive a flow rate a heating wire mounted inside the lower frame of the main body to prevent freezing of the side channel and a control unit controlling driving of the heating wire using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor anti icing system comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "as a means for solving the above described technical problem according to an embodiment of the present invention the anti icing system installed inside the sidewalk canal of the underpass is installed on the floor according to the width of the sidewalk canal so that the electric heating wire can be mounted it includes the body portion that can be erected a pillar or plate to which the sensor can be attached to both or one wall side of the water pipe a temperature sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the water pipe to measure the surrounding temperature to derive a temperature measurement value a humidity sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the waterway pipe to measure the surrounding humidity to derive a humidity measurement value a heating wire mounted inside the lower frame of the main body to prevent freezing of the side channel and a controller for controlling the driving of the heating wire using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the water level of the waterway 3 is high and the flow velocity is high refers to the maximum inside water level when opening of the water channel 3 is required because the obstacle damping device 100 is damaged due to runoff and impurities due to a large amount of impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "on the other hand when the internal water level l measured by the internal water level sensor 31 exceeds the maximum water level lmax that is when the flow rate of the waterway 3 is large due to heavy rain or the like and the flow velocity is high the amount of inflow of the contaminants into the inflow water is large and the size of the contaminants is large"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the soil removed by the soil damper 100 is picked up through the obstacle receiver 8 and the impurity conveying conveyor not shown and then transported to the outside.1 tributary cloth 2 waterway entrance 3 waterway 4 drainage pumping station 5 drain pump 5a winch motor 6 hydrograph 7 main stream 8 container receiver 9 waterway exit 10a upper fixed frame part 10b lower movable frame part 11 connecting shaft 13 roller guide rail 13a upper guide rail 13b lower guide rail 14 roller chain 15 blocking plate 16a drive sprocket 16b lower guide roller 17 roller chain drive motor 21 pulling wire take up roller 22 pull wire 23 drive sprocket 24 take up roller 25 chain 26 winding roller drive motor 27 28 support block 29 limit switch 30 control unit 31 internal level sensor 40 auxiliary screen member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200191686-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "endless chain 14 that rotates along rake 15 of the rake retainer installed on the chain to rotate together the drive motor 16 for driving the chain to prevent the lifting of the contaminated lifting into the water and protect the drive shaft in the vibration damper having a configuration such as an apron 17 a water level sensor 18 is installed on the waterway wall or the vibration suppressor so that the rotational speed of the rake 15 can be varied according to the inflow quantity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the waste water collecting device for drainage to remove a resistance shaft 39 provided on the bottom surface of the water channel 10 a voltage variable element 37 provided at the end of the resistance shaft 39 to output a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 it is provided on the outside of the resistance shaft 39 is raised and lowered according to the water level level is provided with a water level sensor 36 made of a float 38 for changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 the control unit 31 is a waste collection device for drainage characterized in that to adjust the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in proportion to the water level level of the channel 10 detected by the water level sensor 36"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention is a drainage sewage collection device for continuously removing the contaminants introduced into the waterway by a rake installed in a chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller the bottom surface of the waterway a resistance variable provided in the resistor shaft a voltage variable element disposed at an end of the resistance shaft and outputting a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft and installed outside the resistance shaft to increase and decrease according to the level of water thereby changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "by automatically controlling the operating speed of the lifting motor if the inflow of water increases such as during rainy weather the speed of collecting the contaminants can be smoothed thereby smoothing the flow of water into the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442471-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 installed on the waterway so as to be movable in the transverse direction a beam stand 11 mounted to the main body 10 to be elevated a rake 12 installed at the tip of the beam stand 11 to scrape up dirt in a waterway as the beam stand 11 moves up and down an elevating driver 15 for elevating the beam stage 11 a water level sensor 14 for detecting the water level in the water channel a controller 40 for controlling the lift position of the beam stage 11 by controlling the lift driver 15 according to the level detected by the water level sensor 14 a parallel moving drive unit 130 for moving the main body in the lateral direction and it includes a timer for measuring the lifting time of the beam stage 11 and the moving time of the main body 10 the controller 40 controls the beam stage 11 to be elevated to a predetermined depth below the water surface in the water channel according to the result measured by the timer and controls the horizontal movement amount of the main body 10"}]</data>
</edge>
