  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-4304996-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "devices of this nature are subject to contamination of the sensor surface and solarization of the sensor itself and are limited in resolution"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1846689-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the diameter of the sensor unit should also be large enough so that the sensor unit can roll easily over small obstacles such as a discontinuity in the wall of the pipeline where two pipe sections join and so that the drag of the water will cause it to continue rolling onwards even when the pipe tilts uphill"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226945-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "it is obvious that maintenance is easy due to the configuration and the nature of the installation outside the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102320839-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to the present invention consisting of the above described configuration the temperature sensor or the timer sensor accurately grasps the external temperature situation and fundamentally blocks the freezing of the water supply pipe by operating the heating wire built into the water supply pipe and the heating wire as it operates based on the renewable energy produced by solar panels it not only has an excellent level of energy efficiency but also has the effect of contributing to nature conservation as a nature friendly technology"}, {"pat_id": "US-11299878-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "4 691 731 also discloses a sump vent valve which may be interposed within vacuum hose 98 and is closed by a low vacuum condition to prevent communication of the low vacuum to sensor controller 66 which can cause atmospheric pressure in sensor valve chamber 79 to leak and thereby compromise the sealed nature of chamber 79 that otherwise keeps sewage out of sensor controller 66"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102132376-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "that is it is difficult to prevent the reduction of the amount of dissolved hydrogen over time due to the nature of the hydrogen water so the user can check and process the change in the amount of dissolved hydrogen detected in real time through the dissolved hydrogen measurement sensor 333 in real time ex by performing electrolysis additionally on the remaining hydrogen water discarding the remaining hydrogen water and generating new hydrogen water etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9010356-B2", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "depending on the nature of the rupture the sensor network may be damaged albeit in rare circumstances and stop reporting from that location which in itself shall serve as a locator for the rupture"}, {"pat_id": "US-8967186-B2", "para_id": "para_127", "text": "depending on the nature of the rupture the sensor network may be damaged albeit in rare circumstances and stop reporting from that location which in itself shall serve as a locator for the rupture"}, {"pat_id": "US-11333304-B2", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "the pipe apparatus of claim 1 in which at least one sensor is integrated into the wireless information and communication stations to monitor the conditions within the annular gap in any given segment of the pipe apparatus the at least one sensor helping to identify the nature of any leak from the inner or outer piper layer into the annular gap in that segment"}, {"pat_id": "US-11333304-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "at least one sensor may be integrated into the wireless information and communication stations to monitor the conditions within the annular airgap in any given segment of the pipe apparatus the at least one sensor helping to identify the nature of any leak from the inner or outer piper layer into the annular airgap in that segment"}]</data>
