  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-4602939-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the elbow body e prevents corrosion and dust accumulation and contamination due to the wind and rain of the elbow and serves as an installation base for laying the sensor unit s which is an accessory device and the overflow water that has passed through the elbow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974919-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the control unit controls the water circulation unit to move to the first installation point when the water circulation unit is out of the setting radius based on the location information provided by the gps module the frame is provided with a weather vane and is controlled so as to be able to maintain the position by discharging water to the discharge port in the direction opposite to the wind direction so as to prevent movement according to the wind direction when the frame moves by the wind the angle adjusting means includes a center bar provided at a center of the frame a guide raised and lowered along the center bar and a connection link connected between the guide and the solar panel the lower end of the solar panel is connected to the frame by a hinge structure so as to be rotatable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "while the present invention has been particularly shown and described with reference to exemplary embodiments thereof it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed exemplary embodiments but on the contrary is intended to cover various modifications and equivalent arrangements included within the spirit and scope of the appended claims.10 water circulation system 20 water circulation device 21 floating frame 22 wind blade 23 buoyant body 24 solar panel 25 housing 25a inner space 26 gear device 27 cold water jetting portion 27a cold water induction pipe 27b cold water nozzle 28 motor 29 hot water jetting part 29a hot water induction pipe 29b hydrothermal nozzle 30 impeller 31 expansion contraction tube 33 first sensor part 35 second sensor part 37 fixed wire 37a anchor 41 pump 43 freezing part 45 heating section 47 purge control section 49 battery 51 circulation line 52 block holder 52a 52b horizontal rod 53 cutting block 53a upper inclined surface 53b lower inclined surface 53c fitting end portion 55 55a inward gear 55b traveling groove 57 underwater motor 57b drive shaft 57c drive gear 59 59a height holding holder 59b receiving arm 59c roller bearing 59d support roller 61 sensor gateway 63 middleway 65 monitoring section 67 manual control section"}, {"pat_id": "US-11472717-B2", "para_id": "para_232", "text": "for example sensing or receiving weather conditions sensing relative humidity within an interior opening of the evaporation panel using timers providing automated wastewater loading based on timing or sensor driven analytics or the like can be used to automatically determine when the system should run should be loaded with wastewater and can actually control the actual running profile and or wastewater loading fluidics etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility po