  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-4602939-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the elbow body e prevents corrosion and dust accumulation and contamination due to the wind and rain of the elbow and serves as an installation base for laying the sensor unit s which is an accessory device and the overflow water that has passed through the elbow"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank 1 according to at least one of the preceding claims characterized in that a sensor device is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining element 11 can be derived from the measurement data of the sensor device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102047325-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a storage tank 20 into which rainwater flows into the road rain gutter 10 buoyancy material 30 is installed in the storage tank 20 a sensor 40 installed inside the storage tank 20 consists of including when the buoyancy material 30 is raised by the excellent buoyancy introduced into the storage tank 20 is in contact with the sensor 40 the waterproof door 100 is automatically operated a guide 50 is further installed at the bottom of the sensor 40 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement along the guide 50 one side 53 of the guide 50 is attached to the inner wall of the storage tank 20 and the other side of the guide 50 is formed with a projection 55 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement by the buoyancy while being bitten by the projection 55 the storage tank movable structure using buoyancy characterized in that the water level control material 70 is installed in the storage tank 20 to adjust the waterproof door movable water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water level detection sensor 290 is installed inside the rainwater garden 200 the water level detection sensor 290 is connected to the control panel 260 and is controlled to stop operation when the water level is below a predetermined water level the open upper part of the rainwater garden 200 is further provided with a plurality of sealing plates 300 sealing the rainwater to prevent the rainwater from being directly introduced into the rainwater garden 200 when it rains 312 and a grid grid 314 and a pitcher control plate 320 which is seated on the grid 312 and forms a fine pore by blocking the grid grid hole 314 the permeable control plate 320 is a plate like structure in which a first rectangular plate 322 and a second rectangular plate 324 are laminated in a multilayer structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "a water level detection sensor 290 is installed inside the rainwater garden 200 the water level detection sensor 290 is connected to the control panel 260 and is controlled to stop operation when the water level is below a predetermined water level the open upper part of the rainwater garden 200 is further provided with a plurality of sealing plates 300 sealing the rainwater to prevent the rainwater from being directly introduced into the rainwater garden 200 when it rains 312 and a grid grid 314 and a pitcher control plate 320 which is seated on the grid 312 and forms a fine pore by blocking the grid grid hole 314 the permeable control plate 320 is a plate like structure in which a first rectangular plate 322 and a second rectangular plate 324 are laminated in a multilayer structure"}, {"pat_id": "US-9765508-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the hewitt invention is a device to collect and dispense roof rain water comprising a container to collect water having an opening a pump to drive the water out of the container a debris disposal mechanism a sensor to measure the water level wherein the pump is activated at a specific water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100760969-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of backwashing the filtration means in the case of filtering the rain water or the like while the filtration means is lowered the filtration efficiency due to contaminants the pressure of the untreated water transferred to the filtration means 120 by the transfer pump 114 is measured by the pressure measuring sensor ps to inform the control means of the information when the pressure exceeds the preset pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100760969-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "in addition the present invention relates to a method of using the water treatment apparatus such as rain water the method of automatically backwashing the filtration means when the filtration means drops the filtration efficiency due to contaminants while filtering the rain water or the like normally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75