frame 888e lower frame 888f rack line 888g rope guide 888h boom tendon 888i bridle 888j boom hoist rope 888k front drum 888l rear drum 888m parallel weights 889 macadam roller 890 tandem roller 891 tamping roller 892 tire roller 893 tractor 894 trailer 895 ram 896 lead 897 coolant cooling 898 pile 899 helmet 900 fuel pump 901 cam 902 fuel tank 903 starting device 904 boom front pin 905 cad work 906 adapter 907 fish finder sonar 908 drilling machine for crude oil 909 manganese nodule 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016232-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of heavy rain urban sewage pipe control method the clogged sewage pipe is to be connected to the main pipe with a large diameter directly through the emergency pipe or to control the existing sewage pipe to the shortest distance by dividing a certain area of the city into a block to prevent the sewage flowing into a certain area the sewage pipe exiting from a certain area is controlled to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or connected to the shortest distance the sensor is a speed sensor to measure the flow rate of rainwater to calculate the flow rate of each sewage pipe and if the flow rate reaches the dangerous water level is to send an alarm signal to the smartphone of the manager in advance a meter is installed in each sewage pipe installed in the city and if the controller receiving the signal of the meter is judged that no sewage flows in the sewage pipe it is determined that some pipes of the sewage pipes are blocked and the manager through the communication unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869052-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention to achieve the above object an adhesive tape 110 in close contact with an outer surface of a pipe material buried underground such as a water supply pipe a sewage pipe or an rain pipe sensing lines 120 formed on the outer surface of the adhesive tape at regular intervals so as to receive power from the outside in the electronic tag so as to detect leaks and damages and check the pipe positions a removable tape 130 formed on an outer surface of the sensing line a good adhesion treatment layer 140 formed on an outer surface of the detachable tape and for adhesion upon application of a material for protecting the tape consisting of the protective layer 150 formed on the outer surface of the adhesion layer in the sensing pipe that can easily detect the leakage and damage of the piping material using the detection tape 100 and the position of the pipe the sensing tape 100 is composed of a finishing layer 220 to finish the outer surface with a coating the sensing line of the sensing tape 100 is composed of four strands and a separate set of two strands of the four strands is connected to the electronic tag attached to the pipe connection for the exploration of the pipeline from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016233-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the blocked sewage pipe is to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or to be connected to the shortest distance by dividing a certain area of the city into a block to prevent the sewage flowing into a certain area the sewage pipe exiting from a certain area is controlled to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or connected to the shortest distance the sensor is a speed sensor to measure the flow rate of rainwater to calculate the flow rate of each sewage pipe and when the flow rate reaches the dangerous water level is to send an alarm signal to the smartphone of the manager in advance each sewage pipe installed in the city is provided with a meter reading and the control unit receiving the signal of the meter if it is determined that the sewage does not flow in the sewage pipe it is determined that some of the sewage pipes are blocked the manager through the communication unit since the smartphone sends a signal that a problem has occurred the smartphone receives a signal and shows the location of the pipe on which the problem occurred and the administrator moves to the location shown on the screen of the smartphone to clean the pipe endoscope to penetrate through the smart phone outputs a screen on which a flow rate is above a dangerous water level or a blocked pipe and when the application installed in the smart phone is executed a main screen is output and the main screen flows sewage from the city"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200427833-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage it automatically adjusts the rainwater inflow switch to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank 1 according to at least one of the preceding claims characterized in that at least one sensor device 18a 18b is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining elements 8 22 is derived from the measurement data of the sensor device 18a 18b preferably from the measurement data of two sensor devices 18a 18b"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "at least one sensor device can expediently be provided in order to determine the degree of contamination of the retaining elements"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "non point source contaminant treatment system and method of first rain the present invention relates to an initial rainfall non point source treatment system to separate the initial rainwater containing a large amount of non point source during the rainfall to discharge to the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 power generation unit 11 solar module 20 support 100 rainboard 110 first settling tank 120 second settling tank 130 valve box 140 contamination separation pipe 141 electric valve 142 valve drive motor 143 backflow prevention trap 144 gas backflow prevention albo 150 suspended solids filter 160 steel grating 200 rainfall sensor 210 rain gauge case 211 rain gauge bottom 212 lever 213 coupling member 220 bucket 221 bucket pillar 222 bucket pillar support 223 lever 224 weight 225 magnet 226 switch 227 lever pin 230 water inlet 240 filter medium 300 terminal box 310 control unit 320 charging unit 330 input unit 340 timer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100647994-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "rainwater storage device of the present invention for achieving the object of the present invention as described above is the cylindrical body is provided with an inlet is formed in the inlet through which the rainwater flows inlet is formed with a discharge valve for discharging the rainwater flowing into the lower portion a filter member provided at the inlet side of the body to prevent a large amount of foreign substances from entering the body a shutoff valve provided inside the body to block the rainwater introduced through the inlet at a predetermined amount an initial excellent separation means in which a discharge port is formed in the cutoff valve upper side body to discharge rainwater blocked by the cutoff valve to the outside of the body the supply pipe for supplying rainwater stored in the space portion to the outside having a sludge discharge pipe is provided in the lower portion having a space portion of a predetermined size to accommodate and store the rain water discharged from the discharge port of the body of the initial excellent separation means and a water level sensor formed on one side of the storage tank and sensing the level of rain water stored in the space to control an inlet valve so that tap water can be introduced through the tap water inlet pipe and above the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100801684-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage pipe sewer pipe comprising a sewage pipe 1 having at least one manhole 11 and rainwater pipe 2 installed separately from the sewage pipe 1 and provided with at least one manhole 21 a detection means 3 provided with a plurality in one side of the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 and a turbidimeter which is a sensor for detecting a false contact and leakage of the pipe on the discharge side of the rain pipe 2 is provided with a collecting conduit 4 including at least one inlet hole 41 the inlet hole 41 is a soil inflow prevention device to prevent the soil from entering the conduit 4 5 classification means provided with a sensing means characterized in that it comprises a manhole 6 is provided between the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 used to connect the sewage pipe 1 and rain pipe 2 at the same time sewerage"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "in this example if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation but that there are water levels above a threshold the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4637560-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "according to the present invention since the sensor is washed by the washing unit as described above the sensitivity reduction due to the contamination due to the sewage is prevented so that the reliability of the detection data on the water quality is improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "however since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside the temperature sensor often malfunctions and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as a result the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this configuration although it consumes electrical energy and requires installation of a separate sensor motor and controller the initial rainwater inlet 61 of the initial rainwater storage unit 60 is clogged with contaminants or the initial rainwater storage unit even if the initial rainfall is not stored due to breakage of 60 the storm guide unit 50 may be driven as a driving source based on the information detected from the sensor thereby storing the storm"}]</data>
</edge>
