  <data key="d6">["manage", "receive", "elapse", "suck", "make", "happen", "compose", "backwashe", "treat", "position", "descend", "connect", "reach", "trigger", "carry", "aerate", "backwash", "extract", "display", "introduce", "indicate", "accord", "base", "embed", "achieve", "cause", "have", "send", "complete", "wash", "flow", "add", "can", "sample", "relate", "pump", "provide", "merge", "lift", "contain", "expect", "recover", "set", "prevent", "compare", "withdraw", "oxygenate", "feed", "scan", "inspect", "correspond", "describe", "form", "measure", "divide", "eliminate", "crush", "calculate", "overflow", "spray", "action", "adsorb", "suspend", "filter", "pass", "occur", "couple", "follow", "check", "mix", "compress", "say", "determine", "lower", "settle", "convert", "automate", "interface", "purify", "regulate", "turn", "exceed", "consider", "track", "mount", "split", "disinfect", "fall", "dissolve", "integrate", "clarify", "move", "serve", "ionize", "allow", "compute", "originate", "result", "reflect", "illuminate", "locate", "remove", "guarantee", "surround", "reduce", "branch", "inject", "may", "configure", "learn", "adapt", "activate", "match", "designate", "discharge", "store", "derive", "detect", "fit", "interlock", "analyze", "drive", "obtain", "separate", "guide", "include", "perform", "dispose", "operate", "consist", "open", "enter", "mean", "constitute", "supply", "use", "shield", "predetermine", "transfer", "raise", "stop", "sensor", "swirl", "reprocess", "subtract", "transport", "sense", "identify", "require", "draw", "rotate", "maintain", "control", "transmit", "monitor", "characterize", "elevate", "exist", "be", "utilize", "generate", "re", "collect", "instal", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-7052613-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "after the ozone sensor 120 monitoring ozone usage rates in the cell 10 indicates to the sensor processor control unit 60 that the ozone is no longer being utilized for oxidation of biological or chemical contamination discharge valve 76 opens allowing water from the cell 10 to flow into the storage tank 107 and ozone distribution to the cell 10 is stopped through the closing of the ozone valve 86 completing the disaffection treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an automated mobile low power consumption with a hybrid power capacity wastewater treatment facility comprising one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a wastewater generation source to one or more rough solid crushing pumping pit 2 comprising a first electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a level sensor 4 wherein the first electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid crushing impeller 5 allows to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 for removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system comprising a second electrical submersible pump 8 that oxygenates the wastewater and the wastewater treatment contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen by means of an eductor or aerator 9 which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the function of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 and a suspended solids sensor 12 to control the generation of biological sludge and microorganisms which are used for the organic matter degradation a mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 including a screen 14 to allow the passage of water to a sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 in which the separation of a liquid phase and a solid phase occurs by sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is water while in the solid phase is sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has a third electrical submersible pump 16 that allows a recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the liquid phase resulting from the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 including a screen 18 to allow the passage of water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium chloride 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 comprises a ph sensor 23 the suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 the disinfection tank 19 further comprises a screen system 21 to prevent the passage of solids to a filtration tank 27 and an electric valve 37 to eliminate solid materials passed to the disinfection tank disinfected water from the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by a fourth electrical submersible pump 22 to a connection hose 26 that is connected with the filtration tank which contains gravel 28 of different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is achieved furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for continuous use during the night in which the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that performs the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to provide during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains continuous operation the local charge controller also allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for displaying dynamic graphs in the control panel 32 and sends the information to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 comprising at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and nearby surroundings the lamp towers are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamp towers have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain time periods or live video of everything that is happening around the facility and with a visual monitoring finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 to transport and mount in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the present invention describes an automated with a hybrid power capacity connected to an electrical current or a photovoltaic power facility for wastewater treatment by oxidative and biological degradation of the liquids originated from a sewage installation utilizing aerobic digestion which is comprised of one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a source of wastewater to one or more rough solid crushing pump pits 2 comprised by an electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a float type level sensor 4 where the activation of the electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid shredder pusher 5 allows it to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 which has the purpose of removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system with air presence consisting of an electrical submersible pump 8 that through an eductor aerator 9 oxygenates the water contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the operation of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a series of sensors a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 for monitoring and controlling the oxygen in the aeration process and a suspended solids sensor 12 for the biological sludge and microorganisms generation which are used for the organic matter degradation the mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 which has a screen 14 to guarantee the passage of only water to a sedimentation and mud separation tank 15 in which the separation of the liquid phase and the solid phase occurs through a process of sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is the water with dejected and clarified organic material while the solid phase is the sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has an electrical submersible pump 16 at its bottom that allows the recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the result of the liquid phase of the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 which has a screen 18 to guarantee the passage of only water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium hypochlorite 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 has sensors in order to automate the operation of this and guarantee the quality of the resulting water a ph sensor 23 a suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 likewise the disinfection tank 19 considers a screen system 21 that is utilized to prevent the passage of solids to the final filtration process alongside with an electro valve 37 that eliminates solid materials that may have passed to this tank the disinfected water in the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by an electrical submersible pump 22 and a connection hose 26 that is connected to a filtration tank 27 which contains gravel 28 with different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is obtained furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for its continuous use during the night where the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that operates the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to providing it during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains its continuous operation the charge controller allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for its dynamic graphs display in the control panel 32 and sends it to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 composed by at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and its nearby surroundings this lamps are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamps have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain periods of time and or real time video of everything that is happening around the facility and with this a visual monitoring of it finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 that allow it to be transported from one place to another easily and it is mounted in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923165-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a color conversion unit 44 for converting the filtered ultrasonic signal into a color to visually check the state of the interface using the difference between the intensity and the intensity of the filtered ultrasound signal the interface state is displayed in color by the color conversion unit 44 the concentration value of the sludge at a specific position by the color difference is calculated and the sludge average concentration from the upper part of the sedimentation tank and the concentration tank 8 to the lower sludge the sludge concentration calculating unit 48 calculates the sludge concentration at the present interface by checking the state and concentration of the interface by the sludge concentration calculating unit 48 and a check valve operation part 46 for comparing the value with a concentration value determined to require a predetermined sludge drawing and automatically drawing the sludge the interfacial measurement filtering unit 42 previously sets a frequency signal value serving as a reference for interfacial height measurement among the frequencies reflected on the medium in order to set the measurement range in advance at the interface measurement at the place where the interface system 2 is installed an interfacial scanning unit 42 for scanning the ultrasonic frequency information transmitted and received through the detector 6 in a graphical form and an interfacial scanning unit 42 for interfacing the frequency signal values previously set by the initial setting unit 50 a matching unit 54 for comparing frequency measurement values through the state scanning unit 52 and a scraper 54 for collecting sludge at the bottom of the settling tank and thickener 8 while comparing the frequencies of ultrasonic waves by the matching unit 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102155071-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "sedimentation tank consisting of an external sedimentation tank configured to be made a water level sensing unit for sensing the level of the treated water introduced from the sedimentation tank an elevating means configured therein and configured to perform an elevating operation and coupled to the elevating means collecting the introduced treated water a collection means a water quality inspection unit that inspects the water quality of the treated water collected through the collection means a recovery line for recovering effluent water having an unsuitable water quality test result to the sedimentation tank and re inflow of the treated water reprocessed from the sedimentation tank a first discharge tank including a re inflow line to make it a second discharge tank including a plurality of discharge units connected to the first discharge tank and a discharge opening closing door configured to be configured with the plurality of discharge units and operated so that only discharged water having a suitable water quality test result is introduced the water level information of the treated water is received from the water level detection unit and when the water level is higher than a certain level the lifting and lowering operation of the elevating means is controlled and the water quality test result is received from the water quality inspection unit and the recovery line and the discharge opening and closing door are includes a driving control unit for controlling the driving and controlling whether or not the re inflow line is opened so that the re inflow of the reprocessed treated water is made and the elevating means it is configured on one side of the water quality inspection unit and when a driving signal is transmitted from the driving control unit a transfer driving unit that provides a predetermined power to perform an elevating and descending operation and the collecting means are coupled and connected to the transfer driving unit consisting of a transfer member for transferring the collecting means while lifting or lowering operation is performed when the transfer driving unit is driven in the first discharge tank a seating panel whose one end is fixedly coupled to an outer surface of the elevating means and a rotating panel rotatably coupled to the front end of the seating panel and configured to rotate vertically upward when the elevating means is moved upward and the a drive cylinder for controlling the rotation of the rotation panel and a drive control sensor that is interlocked by contact with the water quality inspection unit and receives a drive signal from the drive control unit to control the drive of the drive cylinder and the drive control unit a signal transmission unit configured to perform a water quality inspection while driving the water quality inspection unit only when the water quality inspection unit and the drive control sensor contact each other under the control of effluent water inspection device for a wastewater treatment facility comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101833173-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a supply pipe for supplying a branch pipe which is split at one side of the supply pipe a solenoid valve for shielding the branch pipe a drug reservoir containing a chlorine liquid a chemical liquid conduit connected to the chemical reservoir for introducing the chlorine liquid into the branch pipe a metering pump for injecting the chlorine liquid into the chemical liquid transfer conduit a merging pipe formed in a y shape and mixing raw water introduced through a supply pipe with treated water in which a chlorine liquid flowing through the chemical liquid transfer pipe and a part of the raw water flowing through the branch pipe are mixed a controller for controlling the solenoid valve and the metering pump the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water flowing from the measurement branch pipe is set to a value obtained by subtracting the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water from the measurement branch pipe and a residual chlorine measuring unit including a residual chlorine measuring sensor for measuring the residual chlorine and a zinc ionizing electrode for removing anions contained in the introduced dilution water wherein a plurality of partition walls are provided between the zinc ionizing electrode and the residual chlorine measuring sensor and a display window is provided on one side of the controller and the measurement is made from the current chlorine measuring unit to measure the concentration of the foreign matter in the precipitation chamber the information of the residual chlorine is displayed on the display window of the controller and the opening closing sensor provided in the water supply and the controller drives the solenoid valve and the metering pump at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102789712-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a brine tank 10 10 in which brine is stored at a certain level and sprayed through brine nozzles individually installed at a number of habitual freezing points a b c d a detection sensor 20 that detects the water level of brine stored in the brine tank 10 of each of the above points a central control unit 30 that manages information on the brine storage level through the above detection sensor 20 in order to transport brine stored in a brine tank 10 at a point where the amount of brine is relatively large to a point where the amount of brine is insufficient by the control of the central control unit 30 a brine guide pipe 40 through which brine stored in the brine tank 10 is withdrawn by the operation of a pump p a coupler 50 that is connected to the end of the brine guide pipe 40 and is connected to the transfer tank 110 of the brine transfer vehicle 100 a salt water supply system for road deicing spraying characterized in that the salt water transport tank 110 configured in the salt water transport vehicle 100 is provided with a plurality of bubble generators 111 on the bottom surface to prevent freezing or precipitation of salt water during the transport process an ultraviolet lamp 112 is provided on the top surface and a deterioration prevention layer 113 is formed on the inner wall surface to prevent deterioration of salt water during transport"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101716466-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation sensor 18 installed in a drainage passage 213 of the solar cell module 21 to measure the amount of precipitation water collected in the solar cell module 21 an opening and closing unit 225 connected at both ends to the drainage passage 213 and connected to an elastic string 281 for detecting the amount of precipitation by the precipitation sensor 18 to determine the opening and closing level of the collecting tube 221 a collecting connection unit 12 connected to the drainage passage 213 for collecting the precipitation a control server 11 for controlling the operation of the opening closing means installed in the collection connection unit 12 based on the information transmitted from the precipitation sensor 18 a storage unit 15 in which the precipitation is stored a detection unit 16 for detecting the state of water stored in the storage unit 15 and and a branch unit 14 operated by the control server 11 based on the information transmitted from the detection unit 16 the storage unit 15 is installed under the solar cell module and is shielded by the solar cell module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101716466-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the level of the stored precipitation measured by the ultrasonic sensor 161 or the contamination level may be transmitted to the control server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102457723-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage treatment facility management system for checking the situation of a sewage treatment facility located in a remote place in real time the sewage treatment facility management system a sewage treatment facility unit configured to aerate the incoming sewage to separate the sludge from the treated water to discharge the treated water and a facility management unit that receives the facility status of the sewage treatment facility unit in real time and provides it to the central management server unit and to receive and store real time status information of the sewage treatment facility unit from the facility management unit compare the stored information with preset information store the failure information provided in real time and learn and analyze the stored information to detect the lifespan of the sewage treatment facility unit and a central management server unit that transmits control information of the sewage treatment facility unit to the facility management unit so that the sewage treatment facility can be managed according to the input information and it consists of a manager terminal for the manager to check real time status information from the central management server unit the sewage treatment facility department a sewage treatment module configured to treat and discharge the incoming sewage and a facility condition detection module formed on one side of the sewage treatment module to detect the flow rate noise vibration load and water level generated by the sewage treatment module it consists of a facility driving module formed on one side of the sewage treatment module to receive control information from the facility management unit and provide information to the sewage treatment module and the facility condition detection module the sewage treatment module a sewage inlet formed on one side of the sewage treatment module so that either sewage or sewage from the outside flows into the flow storage tank a flow storage tank formed on one side of the sewage treatment module to store either sewage or sewage flowing in through the sewage inlet an aeration tank formed on one side of the flow storage tank to aerate by injecting air into either sewage or sewage that overflows from the flow storage tank and moves a sludge precipitation tank formed on one side of the aeration tank so that the aeration overflows the bulkhead and the sludge settles toward the bottom a treated water discharge port formed on the other side of the upper side of the sewage treatment module so that the treated water formed at the upper part of the sludge settling tank can be discharged to the outside it consists of a bulkhead formed between the flow storage tank and the aeration tank and between the aeration tank and the sludge settling tank so that sewage and treated water overflow according to the water level the facility state detection module an air flow sensor formed on a bulkhead on one side of the aeration tank to detect the flow rate of air supplied to the aeration tank a sewage flow sensor formed on one side of the sewage inlet to detect the amount of sewage flowing in through the sewage inlet a noise sensor formed on one side of the upper part of the sewage treatment module to detect noise generated from the sewage treatment module a vibration sensor formed on one side of the upper part of the sewage treatment module to detect vibrations generated from the sewage treatment module a load detection sensor formed on one side of the treated water outlet to detect the load discharged when the treated water is discharged it consists of a water level sensor formed on the bulkhead of one side of the flow storage tank to detect the water level of either sewage or sewage stored in the flow storage tank the facility driving module is sensing information formed on the upper side of the sewage treatment module to provide real time status information provided from the facility condition detection module to the real time transmission reception module side of the facility management unit or to receive change and input information provided from the real time transmission module to the central management server unit it consists of a sending receiving module the facility management department a real time transmission reception module for receiving change information and input information from the sewage treatment facility unit from the remote site management information transmission reception module and providing it to the facility control module it consists of a facility control module for receiving information from the real time transmission reception module and providing it to the sensing information transmission reception module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes for collecting only contaminants generated during the filtration process and sludge from the second storage tank which are formed in the filtration tank and a backwash water drain pump configured to discharge contaminants and sludges introduced into the inside of the backwash drainage storage tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "in this example if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation but that there are water levels above a threshold the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-5340468-A", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a system adapted for regulating the addition of lime to reduce water alkalinity comprising a treatment vessel having 1 a mixing zone wherein a stream of untreated water is mixed with lime and 2 a flocculation zone that receives said mixture of water and lime from said mixing zone and allows precipitation of the resulting insoluble salts a first sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said stream of untreated water entering said mixing zone a second sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said water in said flocculation zone pump means for adding said lime to said untreated water in said mixing zone and a controller operable for regulating said pump means by periodically sampling said conductivities measured by said first sensor and said second sensor computing the ratio of said conductivities for each sample computing the slope of said conductivity ratio and determining the minimum value of said conductivity ratio said controller being operable for regulating said pump means so that sufficient lime is added to said water to pass through said minimum conductivity ratio and further turning said pump means off when said ratio exceeds a predetermined maximum set point and said slope is positive and turning said pump means on when said ratio falls below a predetermined minimum set point and said slope is negative"}]</data>
</edge>
