  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100238498-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the weight of the flute 286 must be made to overcome the vacuum pressure temporarily applied to the upper surface 292 so that the flute 286 can be lowered in response to the fall of the sewage level in the sump pit 154"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200480951-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a grating apparatus having a clogging alarm and an odor shielding function according to the present invention for introducing rainwater and sewage on a road or a ship into a sewer line buried underground an outer frame which is seated on the upper surface of the sewer installed on the surface a plurality of bearing bars spaced apart from each other by a predetermined distance on the inner side of the outer frame and having a sewage inlet formed in mutually spaced spaces an opening closing plate for opening closing the sewage inlet with a plate member having a shape corresponding to the sewage inlet one end portion of the plate is pivotally coupled to the opening closing plate and is supported on the bottom surface of the opening closing plate so as to open close the sewage inlet and the other end is coupled to the inner frame of the outer frame or the bearing bar spring at least one hydraulic pressure sensor provided on an upper surface of the opening closing plate a data transmission means for transmitting the water pressure information sensed through the water pressure sensor to the management office by wire or wirelessly wherein when the water pressure sensed by the water pressure sensor is equal to or greater than a predetermined value it is determined that the upper part of the grating is blocked and an alarm sound is generated in the management office"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a leak detection device for a tap water pipe installed in a water pipe by a flange to detect leakage of tap water a pressure sensor provided at one end of the water pipe facing the water pipe to detect a hydraulic pressure drop occurring during leakage an acoustic sensor connected to the pressure sensor in the longitudinal direction and detecting a sound wave generated during leakage and a second printed circuit board connected to the acoustic sensor and connected to the pressure sensor to generate a pressure sensor signal the second printed circuit board being connected to the acoustic sensor to generate an acoustic sensor signal a printed circuit board portion an inner housing that watertightly surrounds the printed circuit board portion a pipe holder connected to the printed circuit board part in a longitudinally watertight manner an extension pipe having one end connected to the pipe holder and extending in the longitudinal direction and cables for transmitting sensor signals of the first and second printed circuit boards are arranged therein and and an outer housing which surrounds the acoustic sensor and the inner housing so that the pipe holder is coupled at one end and the tap is coupled to the flange at the other end the pressure sensor includes a pressure cell for generating an electric signal relating to a change in water pressure through a strain gauge attached to a diaphragm to which a hydraulic pressure acts and a pressure cell housing surrounding the pressure cell and having a ring the acoustic sensor includes an acoustic sensor holder having one end connected to the pressure cell housing and the other end protruding a ring shaped protrusion corresponding to the ring shaped step and the other end inserted into the inner housing in a watertight manner and an epoxy molding unit for integrating the pressure cell housing and the acoustic sensor holder the acoustic vibration sensor comprising a cylinder shaped vibrator installed in the cavity of the acoustic transducer and an epoxy molding unit surrounding the outer periphery of the cylindrical vibrator and integrating the pressure cell housing and the acoustic sensor holder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a water leakage detection apparatus for a water supply pipe provided with a sound pressure composite sensor comprising a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks one of the first and second printed circuit boards connected to the pressure sensor is arranged on one side of the support plate of the substrate support and the first and second printed circuit boards are connected to the acoustic sensor the other one of the two printed circuit boards is arranged side by side on the other side of the support plate of the substrate support which also has the advantage that the overall size or length is not excessively increased due to the compact arrangement described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "here the pressure sensor 10 senses the water leakage due to a cause such as rupture or the like in the water pipe 5 by detecting the water pressure drop generated when water is immersed in the tap water flowing through the water pipe 5 a pressure cell 11 for generating an electric signal relating to a hydraulic pressure change through a strain gauge attached to a diaphragm to which a hydraulic pressure acts as well as a general gauge type pressure sensor not shown in detail and a pressure cell housing 13 on which an annular step 13a is formed on which an end of the coplanar 23a of the acoustic sensor 20 is seated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "one of the circuit boards 33 and 35 is arranged on one side of the support plate 31c of the substrate support 31 and the other of the first and second printed circuit boards 33 and 35 connected to the acoustic sensor 20 are arranged side by side on the other side of the support plate 31c of the substrate support 31 so that the overall size and length are not excessively increased due to the above described compact arrangement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it is a second object to provide a sediment removal device of a sewage treatment facility that can be adjusted to prevent breakage or breakage of the chain and to improve worker operability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to the present invention the tension sensor of the hydraulic cylinder detects an abnormality such as the tension and break of the chain and sends a signal to the control unit if there is an abnormality in the tension amount by operating the hydraulic unit to supply the hydraulic pressure to the hydraulic cylinder chain tension of the lifting part it can be adjusted during operation which prevents the chain from falling off and damage and improves the workability of the worker"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an upstream side main water supply pipe 101 connected to a water supply source and provided with a water supply pump 130 a downstream side main water supply pipe 102 connected to the upstream side main water supply pipe 101 through a main on off valve 110 a sprinkler bridge 200 branched from the downstream main supply pipe 102 and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and a sprinkler head 300 installed at a lower end of the sprinkler double pipe 200 first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the main opening closing valve 110 respectively further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flow meters 510 520 respectively installed at an inlet end and an outlet end of the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 a drain pipe 600 connected to the sprinkler bridge pipe 200 through the three way valve 610 and provided with a drain pipe meter 620 between the second sprinkler bridge pipe flow meter 520 and the sprinkler head 300 lt rti the main on off valve 110 includes a valve body 111 connected to the upstream main supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 a valve cap 112 covering the upper portion of the valve body 111 a valve seat 116 formed in the valve body 111 an opening closing plate 117 installed in the valve body 111 to open and close the valve seat 116 a lifting and lowering rod 118 coupled to an upper end of the nut 117 and a nut box 119 screwed to the lifting and lowering rod 118 and an opening and closing drive means 120 for rotating the nut box 119 including the valve cap 112 includes an elevation guide portion 113 for vertically supporting the elevating and lowering rod 118 a rotation support portion 114 for rotatably supporting the nut box 119 and a reinforcing connecting portion 115 connecting the portion 113 and the rotation supporting portion 114 the opening and closing drive means 120 includes a drive motor 123 mounted on a motor mount 122 fixed to a support plate 121 integrally formed with the rotary support 114 and a driven gear 126 coupled to an upper end of the nut box 119 and engaged with the driving gear 125 the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 and the first and second sprinkler pipe flowmeters 410 and 420 are controlled by controlling the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 according to the detection signals of the water discharge pipes 510 and 520 and the discharge pipe flow meter 620 and a control means 700 the control means 700 includes a fire detector 710 installed on the building an input unit 720 for inputting the normal mode and the test mode a main opening closing valve sensor 730 for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve 110 the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and the 3 way valve 610 according to the fire detection signal of the fire detector 710 and the input signal of the input unit 720 the flow rate of the refrigerant is detected on the upstream side in accordance with the sensing signals of the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 the first and second sprinkler pipe flow meters 510 and 520 the drain pipe flow meter 620 it is possible to judge the abnormality of the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main water supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 to determine an abnormality position display command and an alarm command a control unit 740 for outputting a command to display the degree of opening of the main on off valve 110 a valve driver 750 for sending a driving signal to the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 and the three way valve 610 according to a control command of the controller 740 a display unit 760 for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the controller 740 and an alarm unit 770 for outputting an alarm according to an alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100897438-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level detecting means is installed on the inner bottom surface of the water tank and has a body in which deformation occurs according to the hydraulic pressure of the fluid filled in the water tank and the first optical fiber grating sensor is installed in the body of the fluid it is formed to measure the deformation amount of the main body generated by the hydraulic pressure in accordance with the filling amount the motor temperature measuring means is attached to one side of the motor so that the heat generated by the drive of the motor can be transferred the third optical fiber grating sensor is preferably installed inside the main body so as to measure the amount of deformation of the main body due to heat generated from the motor.the control device of the water treatment plant according to the present invention accurately measures the flow rate of water supplied or returned to each tank for the purification of sewage the water level of the sewage filled in each tank and the temperature of the motors thereby effectively purifying the chemical"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100897438-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "therefore it is possible to convert the water level of the water tank 301 according to the size of the hydraulic pressure the second optical fiber grating sensor 320 based on this by measuring the amount of hydraulic pressure applied to the main body 310 through the deformation amount of the main body 310 the water level of the tank 301 can be calculated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014010-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the crushing mixer 10 is connected to a drive motor 13 and an inverter 14 for driving it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "analog to digital converter for converting to a digital signal a microcontroller for receiving the output value of the analog to digital converter in a pin to pin pin to pin method and corrected by an algorithm and output the output signal of the microcontroller in a serial method a sensor unit comprising a plurality of measuring devices including a hydraulic pressure measuring device including a communication unit which transmits to a field collecting device of a water supply pipe management system but transmits accurate data through a parity bit check for checking crc errors a plurality of field collecting devices collecting data provided from a plurality of measuring devices forming the sensor unit a data collection device collecting data through the plurality of field collection devices a water supply pipe network gis geographic information system device that organizes and manages geographic and facility data such as pipe codes installation blocks pipe diameters pipe types buried years pipe ages joint methods and coordinates of water pipes pipeline code date of report start of construction completion of construction whether to dismantle closure depth water pressure leakage surface leakage amount leakage area leakage classification cause of damage damage type construction subsidy measures an accident management device that stores and manages data related to the water supply pipe such as contents accident route photos and personnel opinions a weight extraction device that receives the factors necessary for weight calculation from the water supply network gis device and the accident management device and calculates the weight for each factor through the opinion of an expert integrate and organize the data received from the water supply network gis device and the incident management device by block and factor and unify the limit value and the comparison unit so that the strength of data can be compared and then determine the search order of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "water supply pipe network integrity evaluation system using the hydraulic pressure measurement information according to the present invention for achieving these objects comprises a sensor unit comprising a plurality of measuring devices including the hydraulic pressure measurement device according to the present invention a plurality of field collecting devices collecting data provided from a plurality of measuring devices forming the sensor unit a data collection device collecting data through the plurality of field collection devices a water supply pipe network gis geographic information system device that organizes and manages geographic and facility data such as pipe codes installation blocks pipe diameters pipe types buried years pipe ages joint methods and coordinates of water pipes pipeline code date of report start of construction completion of construction whether to dismantle closure depth water pressure leakage surface leakage amount leakage area leakage classification cause of damage damage type construction subsidy measures an accident management device that stores and manages data related to water supply pipes such as contents accident pipeline photos and personnel opinions a weight extraction device that receives the factors necessary for weight calculation in the water supply network gis device and the accident management device and calculates a weight for each factor through opinion of an expert integrate and organize the data received from the water supply network gis device and the incident management device by block and factor and unify the limit value and the comparison unit so that the strength of data can be compared and then determine the search order of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "sensor unit 100 a plurality of field collection apparatuses 200 collecting data provided from a plurality of measurement apparatuses constituting the sensor unit 100 a collection management device 300 for managing data collected through the plurality of field collection devices 200 a weight extraction device 400 which receives the factors necessary for calculating the weight from the collection management device 300 and calculates the weight for each factor through the opinion of an expert the central processing unit for unifying and arranging the data received from the collection management device 300 for each block and factor unifying the limit value and the comparison unit to compare the strength of the data and then determine the search rank of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": ".100 sensor 110 hydraulic pressure measuring device 111 water pressure sensor 112 analog input amplifier 113 adc 114 mcu 115 communication unit 120 flow measurement device 130 water quality measurement device 200 field collection device 300 collection management device 310 data collection device 320 gis device 330 accident management device 400 weight extraction apparatus 410 indirect factor extraction module 420 expert opinion collection module 430 survey data extraction module 440 integrated opinion module 450 weight calculation module 500 central processing unit 510 block collection module for each block 520 data purification module 530 matrix calculation module 540 ranking module 600 input and output display device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102257822-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "at this time since check valves are built in the upper inlet j1 and the lower inlet j2 of the hydraulic jack 2350 it is possible to maintain a stable state because it does not leak easily unless the supplied hydraulic pressure is pressed and removed.100 flow meter sensor 110 sewage pipe 200 data collection device 300 monitoring server"}]</data>
