  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore the present inventors install a sensor that can detect the concentration even if the height of the ware and the connecting pipe diameter are increased in order to prevent an overflow accident so that the amount of the sewage flowing into the collecting pipe according to the inflow of the sewage and the degree of contamination is appropriate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101357244-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the door panel 330 for selectively opening closing the waterway 101 the drive unit 340 for rotating the door panel 330 and the drive unit 340 respectively are provided at the 320"}, {"pat_id": "US-10487480-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "thus if a water leak were to occur coincidentally with an electrical power outage such as may occur with a large storm the valve will fail to accomplish its purpose unless auxiliary power is available"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank 1 having a contaminant collecting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the pretreatment tank 1 may further include a dirt collecting tank 13 and a ditch water tank 14 therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes for collecting only contaminants generated during the filtration process and sludge from the second storage tank which are formed in the filtration tank and a backwash water drain pump configured to discharge contaminants and sludges introduced into the inside of the backwash drainage storage tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637562-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "the supply means and the water pumping means are automatically controlled by a monitoring system driven by signals of a detection sensor not shown for detecting the water level of the settling tank 3 the filtration tank 4 and the rectifying tank 5 at an appropriate position and manual control may be performed depending on the contamination level of the storm and the degree of contamination of the filter 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stormwater inflow tank 100 through which stormwater flows one end of the storm that is stored in the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 is connected to one side of the lower end of the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 and the other end is connected to the storm inflow reservoir 100 a sedimentation tank 200 connected through an initial storm inflow pipe 200a communicated with a central portion opposed to the first storm inflow pipe 200a to deposit foreign matter in the stormwater flowing through the initial storm inflow pipe 200a the filtration tank 200 is connected to the other side of the settling tank 200 through a filtration tank transfer pipe 300a and is connected to the lower portion of the one side of the settling tank 200 opposite to the other lower side of the settling tank 200 via the filtration tank transfer pipe 300a 310 for filtering the foreign substances in the rainwater conveyed from the water tank 200 and increasing the water level to a predetermined upward level a filtration tank 300 and is connected to the other central portion of the filtration tank 300 at the other side of the filtration tank 300 through a backwash water tank transfer pipe 400a and is connected to the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash water tank 400 through which the filtered water from the filtration tank 300 flows into the water tank 400a at a certain level is connected to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 through a discharge jaw delivery pipe 500a the filtrate discharged from the backwash water tank 400 is discharged to the outside via the piping 500a and the bypass pipe 100a is connected to the bypass pipe 100a in the case where the water level of the stormwater an excellent stormwater tank 500 through which stormwater flows the sedimentation tank 200 is disposed at a certain distance from the sedimentation tank 200 and is connected to the congestion water conveyance pipe 600a from the inside of the sedimentation tank 200 to selectively enter the sedimentation tank 200 a stagnant water storage tank 600 for discharging the stagnant water to the outside by extending the pipe 610 upwardly to be transferred to the vehicle through the vehicle transfer pipe 610 and the backwash water is selectively supplied from the backwash water tank 400 to the lower side of the filtration tank 300 so that the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 are backwashed by the backwash water and backwashing means for supplying air back into the filtration tank 300 to perform backwashing of the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 by backwash air the backwashing means may be configured to perform backwashing by the backwash water and then backwash with backwash air a sedimentation water drainage pump 710 disposed at the center of the bottom of the sedimentation tank 200 for selectively pumping sedimentation water in the sedimentation tank 200 to be transported to the congestion water storage tank 600 via the congestion water delivery pipe 600a wow a filtration trap water delivery pipe 210 provided on a drainage groove 210 that is downwardly recessed on one side of the bottom of the settling tank 200 and communicates with one side of the lower end of the filtration tank 300 which is conveyed from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side during the opening operation of the check valve 722 formed at the end of the filtration stagnant water transfer pipe 721 via the inlet 721 a filtration water drainage pump 720 for pumping water to be sent to the congestion water storage tank 600 the water level in the drainage groove 210 of the sedimentation tank 200 is detected so as to be sent to the stagnant water storage tank 600 and the sediment stagnant water and the filtered stagnant water are delivered to the stagnant water storage tank 600 a sedimentation tank water level sensor 730 for selectively activating the sedimentation water discharge pump 710 and the filtration water discharge pump 720 until detection the sedimentation tank water drain pump 710 is operated when the level of the sedimentation tank 200 is above the central portion of the sedimentation tank 200 during backwashing by the backwash water washing water level sensor 740 for transferring an excess amount of the backwash water into the stagnant water storage tank 600 a backwash water transfer pipe not shown connected to the backwash water supply pipe 753 provided in the lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 a backwash pump 750 for selectively supplying backwash water for backwash to the filtration tank 300 via the backwash water tank 400 through the backwash water tank 751 the filtration tank 300 is provided at a lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 and is disposed above the backwash water supply pipe 753 and selectively supplied with backwash air from the outside to supply air to the filtration tank 300 a backwashing air supply pipe 810 for upwardly floating the filtered suspended solids in the filter quartz layer 310 while moving upward from a lower portion of the filter quartz layer 310 the suspended solids suspended in the upper portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 are transferred from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 by the backwash air supplied through the backwash air supply pipe 810 one end of which is connected to one side of the upper part of the filter element layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 the other side is connected to the central part of one side of the settling tank 200 and the other end is selectively a backwash floating transfer pipe 820 having a check valve 821 for guiding a suspended material from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through an air transfer pipe 831 and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through the air transfer pipe 831"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this configuration although it consumes electrical energy and requires installation of a separate sensor motor and controller the initial rainwater inlet 61 of the initial rainwater storage unit 60 is clogged with contaminants or the initial rainwater storage unit even if the initial rainfall is not stored due to breakage of 60 the storm guide unit 50 may be driven as a driving source based on the information detected from the sensor thereby storing the storm"}]</data>
