sphalt mixing plant 871 asphalt finisher 872 asphalt spreader 872a power driven pump 872b valve control 872c spray bar 872d burner 872e discard pipe 873 aggregate spreader 874 crusher 874a gyreto crusher 874b sash frame 874c feeder hopper 874d vibrating grease repeater 874e first jaw crusher of the crushing head 874f second jaw crusher at the rear of the crushing chamber 874g vibrating screen 874h drum elevator 875 air compressor 876 perforator 877 pilot and extractor 878 sand collector 879 dredger 879a pump dredger 879b bucket dredger 879c spotted shear 879d cab or control room 879e red shear 879f spotted 879g blast tank 879h blast pump 879i red 879j engine room 879k dipper dredger 879l grab dredger 879m bucket drive 879n after spotted 879o spotted winch 879p bucket 879q left and right front spotted 879r dipper 879s winch 879t anchor store 879u belt conveyor 879v grab 880 separately designated construction machinery 882 pile driver 882a boom 883 diesel pile hammer 884 steam hammer 885 hydraulic crane 885a piston motor 886 tower crane 886a names of each part of the guy derrick structure 886b guy derrick 886c main 886d boom 886e boom foil 886f turnbuckle 886g sling 886h triangular derrick 886i main 886j boom 886k boom foil 886l rack 887 drag crane 887a structure of drag crane 887b hoist cable 887c dump cable 887d bucket 887e lower boom 887f retroflex cable 887g cable roller 887h boom cable 887i cable roller 887j boom hoist cable 887k cable drum 887l cable drum 887m parallel weight 888 crane with clamshell attachment 888a holding line 888b opening line 888c clamshell bucket 888d upper frame 888e lower frame 888f rack line 888g rope guide 888h boom tendon 888i bridle 888j boom hoist rope 888k front drum 888l rear drum 888m parallel weights 889 macadam roller 890 tandem roller 891 tamping roller 892 tire roller 893 tractor 894 trailer 895 ram 896 lead 897 coolant cooling 898 pile 899 helmet 900 fuel pump 901 cam 902 fuel tank 903 starting device 904 boom front pin 905 cad work 906 adapter 907 fish finder sonar 908 drilling machine for crude oil 909 manganese nodule 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016232-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of heavy rain urban sewage pipe control method the clogged sewage pipe is to be connected to the main pipe with a large diameter directly through the emergency pipe or to control the existing sewage pipe to the shortest distance by dividing a certain area of the city into a block to prevent the sewage flowing into a certain area the sewage pipe exiting from a certain area is controlled to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or connected to the shortest distance the sensor is a speed sensor to measure the flow rate of rainwater to calculate the flow rate of each sewage pipe and if the flow rate reaches the dangerous water level is to send an alarm signal to the smartphone of the manager in advance a meter is installed in each sewage pipe installed in the city and if the controller receiving the signal of the meter is judged that no sewage flows in the sewage pipe it is determined that some pipes of the sewage pipes are blocked and the manager through the communication unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101994814-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention the control unit 150 controls the first hydraulic cylinder 112 and the second hydraulic cylinder 122 of the first and second driving units 110 and 120 and detects the operation of the piston through the sensor to determine whether to open or close the water level door 200 and the water gate 700.the system for preventing backflow of seawater and river water in a sewer system of coastal cities and lowlands according to the present invention is characterized in that a river or sea flows backward by controlling a sluice passage and a sluice gate formed between a sewer pipe and a sluice outlet to flow river water or seawater into a sewer pipe there is an effect that can be prevented.1 is an exemplary view of a conventional sewage system 2 is a perspective view of a movable backflow prevention system for seawater and river water in a sewer system of a coastal city and a lowland according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016233-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the blocked sewage pipe is to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or to be connected to the shortest distance by dividing a certain area of the city into a block to prevent the sewage flowing into a certain area the sewage pipe exiting from a certain area is controlled to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or connected to the shortest distance the sensor is a speed sensor to measure the flow rate of rainwater to calculate the flow rate of each sewage pipe and when the flow rate reaches the dangerous water level is to send an alarm signal to the smartphone of the manager in advance each sewage pipe installed in the city is provided with a meter reading and the control unit receiving the signal of the meter if it is determined that the sewage does not flow in the sewage pipe it is determined that some of the sewage pipes are blocked the manager through the communication unit since the smartphone sends a signal that a problem has occurred the smartphone receives a signal and shows the location of the pipe on which the problem occurred and the administrator moves to the location shown on the screen of the smartphone to clean the pipe endoscope to penetrate through the smart phone outputs a screen on which a flow rate is above a dangerous water level or a blocked pipe and when the application installed in the smart phone is executed a main screen is output and the main screen flows sewage from the city"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "initial flow rate and flow rate information measured by the smart meter 30 water quality information measured by the first sensor device 40 and the second sensor device 50 and the consumer 90 measured by the water pressure sensor 70 is provided immediately before the flow rate and flow rate information or water pressure information leak detection sensor 60 the connection node terminal 400 for collecting the leakage information measured by wired or wireless communication method and an integrated control server 600 in the ict integrated monitoring water management system for building a smart water city that includes the integrated control server 600 ict integrated monitoring for building a smart water city water management and maintenance of the block where the water management system 1 is installed analysis of the flow rate in the block prediction and flow of abnormal signs and operating and monitoring the network through constant monitoring of water pressure in order to build a smart water city corresponding to the scada system the flow rate flow rate water quality and water pressure information on the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 are connected to each sensor by wired wireless communication from the connected node terminal 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if at least one or more of the parameters constituting the water quality measured by the formed second sensor unit 50 does not match a preset criterion control not only to control the turbidity drain valve 300 but also to discharge the turbid water water pressure measured by the water pressure detection sensor 70 among the flow rate control valve 80 and the water pressure detection sensor 70 sequentially formed between the turbid water drain valve 300 and the consumer 90 is outside the preset water pressure range if not by controlling the flow rate control valve 80 to maintain the flow rate and flow rate to be maintained in a preset water pressure range the administrator mobile terminal accessible through the network 500 for the database 630 800 provides a real time monitoring and monitoring module 621 that provides a function to support decision making ict integrated monitoring for smart water city construction send and receive to receive the location and property information of natural and artificial objects existing on the surface and underground and ground spaces of the water management system 1 from the big data server 700 through the network 500 after controlling the unit 610 the received information is matched and generated based on gis information based on the water pipe of the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for smart water city construction and then through the network 500 by controlling the transmitter receiver 610 to transmit to the manager mobile terminal 800 the manager can directly control the water supply network block and facility information db as well as support various planning and decision making and industrial activities in connection with the manager s work"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to the control by the connection node terminal 400 the second sensing device 50 the turbidity control valve 300 the leak detection sensor 60 the water pressure detection sensor 70 the flow rate control valve 80 is formed integrated ict monitoring water management system for building a smart water city characterized by providing tap water to a consumer 90 via a water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "water is supplied directly to the consumer 90 through the water supply pipe between the consumer 90 where the valve 80 is formed but the leak detection sensor 60 for each predetermined distance between the consumer 90 and the turbidity control valve 300 is formed ict integrated monitoring water management system for smart water city construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the ict integrated monitoring water management system for building a smart water city according to an embodiment of the present invention includes initial flow rate and flow rate information measured by the smart meter 30 and a first sensor unit 40 and the water quality information measured by the second sensor unit 50 the flow rate and flow rate information or water pressure information immediately before being provided to the consumer 90 measured by the water pressure sensor 70 the leak detection sensor 60 connection node terminal 400 for collecting the leakage information measured in by wired or wireless communication method and an integrated control server 600 which is a central control monitoring system that performs integrated management and monitoring after receiving all measurement information collected by the access node terminal 400 through the network 500 it characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "referring to figure 1 ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is the intake station 10 ground water 20 smart meter 30 the first sensor unit 40 the second sensor device unit 50 leak detection sensor 60 water pressure sensor 70 flow control valve 80 consumer 90 water purification plant 100 rechlorination injection facility 200 turbidity drain valve 300 a connection node terminal 400 a network 500 an integrated control server 600 and a big data server 700 and a manager mobile terminal 800"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "to this end the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is a system that manages each of the grid type waterworks network formed in the downtown area and the waterworks network formed in the outskirts of the city as an integrated system to manage the network"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "it is apparent to those skilled in the art to which the present invention pertains that other modified examples based on the technical idea of the present invention can be implemented in addition to the embodiments disclosed herein.1 1a ict integrated monitoring water management system for smart water city construction 10 intake point 20 groundwater 30 smart meter 40 first sensor unit 50 second sensor unit 60 leak detection sensor 70 water pressure sensor 80 flow control valve 90 accommodation 100 water purification plant 200 re chlorine injection equipment 300 turbid drainage valve 400 connection node terminal 500 network 600 integrated control server 700 big data server 800 manager mobile terminal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101293190-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the data transmission unit that transmits to the server configures the field equipment to enable intelligent leakage monitoring of water and sewage pipes in large areas such as u city"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377605-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention has an advantageous effect of enabling a quick response by directly detecting the contamination leakage by a sensor directly installed in the field.1 is a diagram showing a state in which in the water treatment instrumentation control system for a smart city of the present invention a pair of sensors for water quality inspection are installed at regular intervals symmetrically left and right at the edges of a tributary p and a main stream m"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102156126-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "in the present invention when the wastewater flows into the wastewater inlet 101 through the discharge pipe p of a wastewater discharge source such as an industry or a livestock industry as described above the wastewater inlet passage before supplying it to the treatment facility 102 part of the wastewater flowing from 101 is continuously acquired and the wastewater purified through a multi stage cyclone device is supplied to the water quality tms 170 and various sensors provided inside the water quality tms 170 not shown city measures this and provides information on contamination of wastewater"}]</data>
</edge>
