  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101398010-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a reservoir installed on the lower side of the gutter a connection pipe connecting the storm water pipe and the storage tank a storage tank installed in the connection pipe for controlling the stormwater flowing into the storage tank through the connection pipe a first sensor installed on the upstream side of the connection pipe among the gross conduits and measuring a contamination degree and a quantity of the ozone flowing into the gutter tube a second sensor installed inside the storage tank for measuring a contamination level and a water level of the storm water filled in the storage tank a discharge pump installed in the storage tank for sucking the rainwater in the storage tank and discharging the rainwater to the outside and a control unit for opening and closing the storage tank gates in accordance with an initial stormwater inflow signal and an initial wastewater termination signal of the first sensor and driving the discharge pump according to the high water level signal or the contamination signal of the second sensor the storage tank gates a connection pipe interlocking part installed to be rotatable at an inlet of the connection pipe and interrupting the connection pipe while rotating and an excellent pipe shut off part slidably installed in the connection pipe cut off part and slid in a state where the connection pipe cut off part is opened to cut off the excellent pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}]</data>
