ody center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-8418754-B2", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "since the lower valve 42 in the static chamber 32 is one way in the upwards direction the water 26 in the static chamber 32 travels through a left t connector 46a and over to the water line via another right t connector 46b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "that is when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320 the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "10 water treatment device 100 agitator 110 rapid stirring 120 slow stirring 121 coagulation tank 122 first coagulation tank 123 second flocculation tank 124 partition wall 124a euro 125 stirrer 126 drive motor 127 stirring shaft 128 horizontal paddle 129 vertical paddle 200 flotation tank 210 discharge part 220 scum discharge unit 300 bubble generation unit 310 pressurized water supply unit 312 pump 314 pressure tank 316 compressor 320 fine bubble injection unit 322 branch piping 323 pressurized water inlet valve 324 injection pipe 326 decompression tube 330 backwash 332 backwash valve 334 water level sensor 336 control unit 400 guide unit 410 injured guide slope 420 dead zone prevention slope 500 floating scum removing unit 510 blade 600 sediment sludge removal unit 610 chain 620 scraper 700 outflow collecting part 710 porous pipe 720 block type sump 800 advanced oxidation processing unit 810 oxidizing gas supply unit 812 am generator 814 ozone storage tank 816 ozone pressurizer 820 uv contact unit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition when activated at a cycle of 1 minute information in the predicted water level pattern memory 11 and the plant information actual value file 14 regarding information such as the operating state of the pump and the open closed state of the inflow valve that become disturbances in water leakage monitoring the inside information is compared and if a difference occurs in the state the water level plan prediction pattern in the predicted water level pattern memory 11 is corrected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the safety facility of the rainwater storage tank 150 is stored in a slightly higher than the high water level hwl in order to prevent the water level rises and overflows when the amount of rainwater entering the rainwater storage tank 150 more than the planned quantity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100314663-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the pressurizing tank 40 and the extinguishing pressurizing tank for use in extinguishing 41 is connected the water supply pressure tank 40 and the fire extinguishing pressure tank 41 is basically a pressure gauge 15 18 pressure switch 16 19 to know the pressure in the tank pressure sensors 17 20 and water level 36 37 is provided the electronic safety valve e automatically discharged to the outside when abnormal pressure to maintain the set pressure and to prevent damage and deformation of the tank 39 and automatic air discharge valves 34 and 35 are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100314663-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "and automatically discharges the excess air supplied to the automatic air discharge valve 34 and when the pressure in the water supply pressure tank 40 rises to a constant pressure the electronic safety valve 39 to prevent deformation or damage of the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201275-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "therefore the lifting rod 8 may be attached to the bottom surface of the opening and closing opening 7b via the through hole 72 through the hole 7e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to the smart type water tank having the earthquake proof function according to the present invention the water tank is managed through the pollution level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 and the water leakage sensor 33 thereby enabling clean and safe water quality management control and monitoring of the opening closing state of the valve 40 and the water drainage amount by monitoring the sudden change of the water level and the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the level sensor 31 may be of an electroconductive type that utilizes the flow of current when it comes into contact with water or a capacitive type that utilizes a change in electrostatic capacity according to a water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the control unit 50 determines the state of the raw water by comparing the measured values of the sensors sensed above with predetermined reference values controls the valve 40 according to the determination result and transmits the state of the raw water to the manager it is a means to provide a process for that is the controller 50 is electrically connected to the pollution level sensor 30 the level sensor 31 the vibration sensor 32 and the water leakage sensor 33 to