he effect of blocking the supply of water from the water tank to the customer.1 to 2 are diagrams showing the configuration of a water supply management system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599590-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the control unit 400 may control the opening and closing of the pump 120 the water supply valve 211 and the emergency valve 221 by receiving the signal output from the detection unit 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding