o block the noise by increasing the capacitance by twisting the wire the controller is installed inside the main body that forms the appearance and executes the program stored in the storage to control the operation of each device a central processing unit and a printed circuit board for determining a leakage test result according to the detection signal of the detection unit a plurality of operation switches provided on one side of the main body and receiving an operation for controlling driving of each device it is provided on the other side of the main body and includes a plurality of connection ports electrically connected to each device the operation switch is provided with a power switch a vacuum pump provided in the vacuum device a vacuum valve first to fifth switches electrically connected to the compressor and the compressor valve provided in the air compressor the connection port is provided with the vacuum pump and the vacuum valve the compressor and the compressor valve the vent valve for releasing the pressure in the test tank and the first to seventh ports respectively connected to the sensing unit the supply device the first to fifth switches can be set to manual and automatic modes and operation off the cable connecting the sensing unit and the controller is a leakage inspection apparatus of the conduit facility characterized in that provided with a shielded cable shielded to reduce noise"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "if at step 116 the program determines that the water utilization system is calling for water then the program follows the yes branch to step 124 where the pump is activated and the water in the current storage tank is directed by means of the diverter valve to the primary outlet and therefore to the water utilization system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101739419-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a constant temperature system for leachate and wastewater treatment plants installed in a nitrification tank in a leachate treatment plant including a tiller a flow control tank a mixing tank a nitrification tank a settling tank a thickening tank a fenton oxidation treatment tank or a reverse osmosis treatment tank a plurality of nitrification vessels buried in the ground and purifying and discharging the supplied leachate from the outside and having a plurality of chambers partitioned by a plurality of partition walls for setting the movement path of the leachate therein at least one agitator disposed on the bottom surface of the nitrification tank to mix the leachate while rotating a first heat pump disposed in an upper part of the nitrification tank on the ground to heat the nitrification tank and heat exchanging the first chamber leachate and the heat exchanged refrigerant disposed in front of the nitrification tank in the direction in which the leachate flows 3 heat pump a fourth heat pump to a sixth heat pump arranged in parallel with the first heat pump to the third heat pump and arranged in the rear along the direction in which the leachate of the nitrification tank flows and the heat exchanged refrigerant is heat a first heat exchanger connected to the first heat pump to a third heat pump and disposed in the first chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a second heat exchanger connected to the fourth heat pump to the sixth heat pump and disposed in the second chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a first circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the first heat exchange unit a second circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the second heat exchange unit a preliminary circulation pump interposed between the first circulation pump and the second circulation pump and capable of temporarily operating corresponding to the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump a three way valve connected between any one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump and selectively supplying the heat exchanged refrigerant to the first chamber or the second chamber a sensor unit provided on the three way valve for sensing the temperature or pressure of the refrigerant flowing into the three way valve a first heat pump to a sixth heat pump a first circulation pump and a second circulation pump and a control unit controlling the temperature of the leachate in the nitrification tank to a set range by controlling the agitator an expansion tank provided to compensate for a pressure of the heat exchanged refrigerant supplied through the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump and an air blower unit for supplying air supplied from the outside to the periphery of the agitator in the nitrification tank the air blower unit includes an air flow path for introducing outside air into the vicinity of the agitator a compressor for forcibly supplying external air through the air flow path and a nozzle provided at an end portion of the air flow path for discharging air toward the agitator and wherein the agitator includes a housing fixed to the bottom of the nitrification tank and passing through the inside in a vertical direction a propeller for rotating the inside of the housing to mix the leachate a driving motor for driving the propeller and a guide arm provided on the outer circumferential surface of the housing so as to be guided through the air passage when installed wherein the control unit controls the at least one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump to selectively operate the heat pumps when the temperature of the nitrification tank reaches the set temperature by receiving the data of the sensor unit the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump operates first and controls the heat pumps to operate after the set time has elapsed wherein the nitrification tank includes a plurality of ventilation doors formed with openings communicating with the outside at upper portions of the chambers and selectively opening and closing the openings"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an automatic liquid flow control unit adapted to be attached to a liquid line to enable liquid to trickle therethrough in order to avoid liquid freeze up said unit comprising a rigid conduit means having an inlet including threaded fastening means for attaching said inlet to said liquid line an electrical conduit a solenoid actuated pilot valve mounted to said conduit means downstream of said inlet and being in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough said valve including an electric solenoid connected to said electric circuit to be actuable to open said valve to a predetermined trickling mode wherein liquid trickles through said conduit means and temperature sensitive switch means mounted against an outer surface of said conduit upstream of said valve and downstream of said fastening means and arranged for sensing the temperature of said outer surface and being electrically connected to said electrical conduit and said solenoid for actuating said solenoid to open said valve to said liquid trickling mode in response to the sensed temperature approaching the freezing temperature of the liquid said valve including a manual bleed valve means for actuating said pilot valve independently of said temperature sensitive switch means to establish a flow rate greater than said trickling mode"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "an automatic liquid flow control unit adapted to be attached to an externally threaded spigot to enable liquid to trickle therethrough in order to avoid liquid freeze up said unit comprising rigid conduit means having a horizontal portion and an upwardly inclined inlet portion which includes internally threaded fastening means for attaching said inlet to said externally threaded spigot an electric circuit a solenoid actuated pilot valve mounted to said horizontal portion of said conduit means downstream of said inlet and being in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough said valve including an electric solenoid connected to said electric circuit to be actuable to open said valve to a predetermined trickling mode wherein liquid trickles through said conduit means and temperature sensitive switch means mounted against an outer surface of said horizontal portion of said conduit upstream of said valve for sensing the temperature of said outer surface and being electrically connected to said electrical circuit and said solenoid for actuating said solenoid to open said valve to said liquid trickling mode in response to the sensed temperature approaching the freezing temperature of the liquid said valve including manual bleed valve means for actuating said pilot valve independently of said temperature sensing switch means to establish a flow rate greater than said trickling mode"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in many dwellings especially those without basements there is no interior shut off valve within the dwelling to prevent such bursting"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a solenoid actuated valve is mounted to the conduit downstream of the inlet and is in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102480228-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in addition when water is sprayed during the summer season and a certain period of time elapses with the water remaining inside when the water freezes due to the temperature difference during the winter season the pipe itself is prevented from cracking and the life span can be further extended"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101069857-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "temperature detection unit 220 for detecting the temperature of the purified water genuine filter detection unit 230 for detecting whether the genuine filter is mounted valve drive unit 240 for driving various solenoid valves 245 provided in the ionizer neutral electrolyzer driving unit 250 for driving an electrolytic cell for electrolysis of water a chiller driving unit 260 for driving a cooling device for cooling purified water an indicator 275 for displaying various operating states of the device and an indicator for driving the electrolytic cell driving unit 250"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 that stores and stores rainwater flowing through the filter a pump that is installed at the bottom of the storage tank and rotates the rainwater stored in the storage tank from time to time or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 90 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the event of a malfunction the filter 10 of the rainwater recycling device s configured including a control unit 60 equipped with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 on one side an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "as a result it is possible to prevent unnecessary power consumption in the feed pump for supplying water to the filtration membrane portion and to maintain the flow rate on the surface of the filtration membrane to prevent the filtration membrane from clogging due to fouling"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "when fluid 40 which is typically not water based in chamber 42 reaches a point it will contract as it loses heat and changes phase from a liquid to a solid at the freezing point of the fluid and will cause piston 38 biased open by the spring 44 to retract from seat 34"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the cap which may be self tapping is then threaded in with tool 31 until the o ring 22 contacts the inner walls of the fluid chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454816-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the apparatus for filtering the overflow water exceeding the facility capacity of the sewage terminal treatment plant a floc forming tank 10 having an inlet 110 for guiding the overflow water and at least one mixed paper 120 and a medicine supply unit 121 for administering a flocculant to the mixed paper 120 an opening 210 positioned on the bottom surface in fluid communication with the floc forming tank 10 and the first guide tube 11 and connected to the first guide tube 11 and disposed on the opening 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water valve for preventing freezing of a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe by discharging water little by little as the stem holder operates and a waterway is partially opened when the temperature is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in the case of a water valve located outdoors it is difficult to use the water pipe or the tap water inside the water valve due to the freezing temperature in winter and the volume expansion of the frozen tap water causes the water pipe or the connection parts of the water pipe to deteriorate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of tap water conventionally a method of warming the water valve and the water pipe by wrapping the surroundings of the water valve and the water pipe with a heat insulating material has been most widely used but the effect is insufficient when the temperature drops significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition a method of preventing freezing and bursting due to a decrease in temperature in winter has been disclosed by winding a heating wire spirally around a water valve or water pipe applying power thereto and maintaining the water valve or water pipe at a constant temperature due to heat generated from the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "therefore when the temperature drops such as in the winter when the inside of the valve body is closed by the opening closing ball the remaining water inside the flow path freezes and the volume of ice expands causing a problem that inevitably causes freezing and rupture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "therefore when the temperature drops such as in the winter freezing due to residual water inside the flow path is inevitable and when freezing occurs the entire water angle valve must be replaced which inevitably results in excessive costs"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3813064-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 is a block diagram showing a processing flow of the monitoring system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 by measuring the temperature of the water by the temperature sensor 5 in the water pipe p2 when the temperature is less than the set temperature the inlet valve 7 and the outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time to prevent freezing by circulation of water secondary water purification equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "and the flow sensor to prevent the freezing of the filter and the device by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature sensor 5 located in the water pipe p2 below a set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "manufacturing cost and management of secondary water purification equipment designed to prevent freezing by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature of the water is measured without the heat insulator and auxiliary materials such as heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4521319-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in this case it is possible to set the iron phosphate so as to be in a dissolved state by adjusting the ph but there is a possibility that precipitation may occur little by little in the piping or the like due to the rise in temperature or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430463-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "conventional water meter is to be installed in the thermal insulation case to prevent freezing in winter but there is a limit to the thermal insulation capacity of the thermal insulation case and if water is left inside the meter it is frozen when the temperature drops so it cannot be completely prevented"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035484-B2", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "practically however it is very difficult to reduce the cross section to zero due to production tolerances on the valve bore and the valve bodies and dimensional changes in operation due to temperature influences and or wear"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the system comprises a water pipe including a water stop valve a pipe connected with the water pipe through a first electromagnetic valve and a second electromagnetic valve the system allowing the first valve to close temporarily while said second valve is held open in order to drain water from the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as the ambient temperature has dropped to about 5 c or below the first valve is heated by a heater in which it is housed thereby preventing its freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "however if the liquid temperature of the block 1 decreases the liquid is supplied to the block through the means for measuring the flow rate in an amount of the liquid corresponding to the reduction in the liquid volume due to the decrease in the liquid temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101467038-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the leakage detection control device 200 a time temperature setting unit 210 for setting the respective temperatures of the boiler drive time on off the hot water and the heating water a pressure sensor setting unit 220 for setting a reference pressure value to be compared with a pressure value sensed from each of the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 160 170 and 180 a valve control unit 230 for controlling opening and closing angles of the water supply control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve 130 and the recovery control valve 140 the water supply control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve 110 and the heating control valve 120 are operated to operate at a set temperature of the boiler drive time and the hot water the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 160 170 and 180 and the first to fourth pressure sensors 130 and 170"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200398138-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "as the drainage hole penetrated to the outside is opened the drinking water remaining inside the barrel is discharged to the outside to prevent freezing of the tap water due to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-5318059-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the water temperature within certain pipes within the dwelling may fall below freezing despite the use of a temperature sensitive valve unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5318059-A", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "as noted earlier even in moderate climates the outside temperature may occasionally be expected to fall below freezing whereby water at the outside faucet might freeze thereby presenting the risk of a pipe burst which can produce damage to the pipe and dwelling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a device capable of generating sodium hypochlorite saturated salt water tank receiving soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine the water level is controlled by a water gauge and a water supply valve a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank sodium hypochlorite generator having an automatic valve and a flow sensor characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "sodium hypochlorite generating device equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor according to the present invention to achieve the above object by supplying soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine but by the water gauge and water supply valve a saturated brine tank in which the water level is controlled a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank it characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100553167-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a soft water tank 40 having an outlet 54 which is divided into at least two soft water areas 42a 42b 42c and 42d and communicated with the soft water areas 42a 42b 42c and 42d and the ion a tank unit 20 including a regeneration container 60 filled with regeneration material 61 of the exchange resin 41 a drive unit 90 including a switching valve v in communication with each of the water softening regions 42a 42b 42c and 42d and an adjusting assembly 160 for controlling the valve v a raw water supply pipe 82 connecting the pretreatment filter barrel 30 and the switching valve v and a regeneration water pipe 86 and a regeneration water pipe connecting the switching valve v and the regeneration tank 60 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100553167-B1", "para_id": "para_117", "text": "at this time the four operation modes of the switching valve v is directly controlled through the control assembly 160 while the control assembly 160 is controlled by the control unit 188 the control unit 188 is an inlet on the basis of the detection results of the temperature sensor 36 and the flow meter 38 installed in 32 the control assembly 160 is controlled in accordance with a predetermined alg