ipe the other side is coupled to the plate check valve sand filter 220 for filtering the sand contained in the groundwater plate check valve 230 is coupled to one side of the sand filter the other side is coupled to the meter to prevent the groundwater filtered by the sand filter backflow a meter 240 coupled to one side of the plate check valve and the other side coupled to a pressure gauge a pressure gauge 250 coupled to one side of the meter and coupled to a three way valve on the other side a three way valve 260 coupled to the pressure gauge to form a flow path in the direction of the emergency water supply pipe 600 or the water supply pipe 700 an underground water level protection hole 200 including an underground water level protection column 270 formed along an inner circumference to prevent freezing waves it is configured to include and the controller 500 for supplying power to the underground water protection unit if the temperature is below the set temperature the controller 500 a temperature sensor 510 for detecting the ambient temperature a temperature setting unit 520 for setting a reference temperature for supplying power to the ground water protection protection vessel a memory unit 530 for storing the reference temperature set by the temperature setting unit a power supply unit 540 for supplying power to the ground water protection protection line a temperature comparison unit 550 for comparing the temperature sensed by the temperature sensor with the reference temperature stored in the memory unit a power supply signal transmitter 560 for transmitting a power supply signal to a power supply unit when the temperature compared by the temperature comparison unit is less than a reference temperature freezing prevention comprising a central control unit 570 for controlling the signal flow between the temperature sensor the temperature setting unit the memory unit the power supply unit the temperature comparison unit the power supply signal transmission unit and groundwater upper protection device capable of underwater discharge sterilization treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "preventing freezing by flowing tap water as described above is a waste of tap water is generated badly because the water must continue to flow while the temperature is falling there is a problem that the inconvenience to use by always operating the valve manually"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in order to solve the above problems a heating freeze protection device has been proposed which installs a separate heater around the valve and the pipe to prevent freezing by heating the pipe when the ambient temperature drops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in the case of a freeze prevention module equipped with such a temperature type automatic valve the temperature is measured to prevent freezing through heat transfer but if the module is exposed to sub zero weather for a long time abnormal operation may be executed"}, {"pat_id": "US-5646863-A", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "to reduce the effect of organic contamination on the electrode surfaces an absorptive stripping voltage combined with a unique voltage is applied to measuring cell working electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "US-9238904-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the temperature sensing device detects the temperature of the fluid within the flushing device 100 measuring for freezing conditions and triggers the freeze control valve 710 to open under predetermined temperatures such as freezing condition temperatures to prevent freezing of the fluid within the flushing device 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-4239601-A", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "decreasing the time between cycles of water overflow will of course produce a cooler temperature for the condenser and for the output of the distiller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100635856-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the temperature is detected to determine the concentration of the silver solution sterilized water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "according to claim 1 the raw water inlet pipe is attached to one side before the raw water is injected into the virus sterilization device is attached to the contaminant sensor to determine the degree of contamination to prevent the inflow and inflow of raw water to the raw water inlet valve the virus sterilization device is the location where the raw water inflow distributing large particles by distributing large screens distributing raw water to virus sterilizers plural uv lamps or uvleds are installed inside virus sterilizers and ozone injection hoses installed outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the raw water inlet pipe 10 is attached to one side before the raw water is injected into the virus sterilization device 16 is attached to the contaminant sensor 12 to determine the degree of contamination to prevent the inflow and inflow of raw water to the raw water inlet valve 14 in addition the virus sterilization device 20 installs a distribution screen 22 at a position where raw water is introduced to filter foreign matter having large particles distributes and supplies the raw water into the virus sterilization device 20 and a virus sterilization device 20 a plurality of uv lamps or uvleds 24 are installed therein and ozone is introduced through an ozone injection hose 28 from an ozone generator 26 installed outside to sterilize viruses and a virus sterilizer 20 it provides a water supply system for supplying fish farm facilities capable of controlling water temperature and virus sterilization of raw water passing through the virus sensor 16 and then measuring the virus through the filtration device 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161642-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "pump 4 a sterilizing filter 9 for sterilizing bacteria contained in the filtered purified water while passing through the filter a display setting unit 11 for displaying temperature and operating conditions and a cold water storage tank 14 the cold water temperature sensor 14 for measuring the purified water temperature of the hot water the hot water temperature sensor 15 for measuring the purified water temperature of the hot water storage tank 12 and the purified water temperature stored in the hot water storage tank 12 are raised"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "an apparatus for oxidative decomposition of an organic matter containing waste solution using the supercritical water oxidation method according to the present invention includes a waste liquid heater 31 for preheating the mixture of the organic matter containing waste solution 11 and the neutralizing agent 13 to a subcritical temperature under anoxic conditions a preheat mixer 33 which allows the waste liquid preheated from the waste liquid heater 31 to be mixed with the pressurized oxidant 12 the neutralizing agent 13 and the auxiliary heat source 14 which is preheated by heat exchange with the treated water of the reactor a reactor 34 which rises to a supercritical temperature by an exothermic reaction of the preheated auxiliary heat source and the organic matter containing waste liquid discharged from the preheater 33 maintains a high flow rate and undergoes an organic oxidation reaction a supercritical heat exchanger 35 which heats the treated water discharged from the reactor 34 to a supercritical temperature and heats the auxiliary heat source 14 while cooling the treated water above the supercritical temperature a quench mixer 36 for quenching the treated water by mixing the treated water passing through the supercritical heat exchanger 35 with quenched water a subcritical heat exchanger 37 which heats the mixed water discharged from the quench mixer 36 and the organic matter containing waste liquid 11 to further cool the mixed water and simultaneously heat the organic containing waste liquid 11 a pressure reducing device 38 and a pressure drop valve 39 for reducing the pressure of the mixed water a gas liquid separator 41 for separating the reduced pressure of the treated water into a gas phase and a liquid phase characterized in that consists of"}, {"pat_id": "US-7043934-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the ice maker can be identical or similar to those used in refrigerator freezers although is should have its own evaporator for freezing purposes and should have an expansion device that controls the temperature levels so that ice making is possible or may be a flake ice maker or other such device as known in the art"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_608", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may use the output from the blowdown temperature control loop as the extra source valve command value in block 8024"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in or leak into the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-7749360-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "water is circulated through this feedback loop and valve 41 is manually set to minimize and or reduce the buildup of sediment or scaling material in the evaporator 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145007-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "water remaining inside the floating tube is automatically drained to the outside through the drain hole which prevents the freezing and freezing of water at low temperature in winter because there is no water remaining in the floating tube"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5333487-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a water softening device for producing soft water by softening raw water in a cation exchange resin bed tower a reverse osmosis membrane separation device for separating soft water produced by the hard water softening device into permeated water and concentrated water by a reverse osmosis membrane module an electrodeionization module an ion exchange resin mixed bed tower or a cation exchange resin single bed tower for deionizing the permeated water obtained by the reverse osmosis membrane separator a softening process for producing soft water by passing raw water in a downward flow through a cation exchange resin bed having a depth of 300 to 1500 mm housed in the cation exchange resin bed tower a first regeneration process for regenerating the entire cation exchange resin bed by generating a downward flow of the regenerated liquid by collecting at the bottom while distributing liquid to the top of the bed and regenerating after the first regeneration process a second regeneration process for regenerating a part of the cation exchange resin bed by generating an ascending flow of the regeneration liquid by collecting the liquid at the middle while distributing the liquid to the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed valve means switchable to in the second regeneration process the amount of regeneration liquid that provides a regeneration level of 1 to 6 eq lr is supplied to a hardness leak prevention bed whose depth is set to 100 mm with the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed as a base point"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5333487-B2", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a water softening device for producing soft water by softening raw water in a cation exchange resin bed tower a first reverse osmosis membrane separation device for separating soft water produced by the hard water softening device into permeated water and concentrated water by a first reverse osm