a predetermined position of the third flow path q3 installed between the reverse osmosis membrane product water supply valve 1600 and the product water circulation valve 1900 and the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 so as to detect the electrical conductivity of the fluid passing through the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 and send it to the control unit s a second electrical conductivity sensor 1002 installed between the cooling device 1300 and the reverse osmosis membrane high pressure pump 1400 to detect the electrical conductivity of the fluid being transported through the second channel q2 and send it to the control unit s and when a fluid having an electrical conductivity higher than a certain value flows through the second channel q2 the control unit s blocks the concentrated water recovery valve 1820 installed in the concentrated water recovery channel q5 and opens the concentrated water drain valve 1810 to prevent the fluid having an electrical conductivity higher than the set value from being continuously supplied to the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 thereby preventing the failure of the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 and extending its lifespan"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 the controller is a boiler driving unit for driving a combustion device constituting the boiler a driving state detection unit for detecting the driving state of the boiler driving unit and as a result of the detection of the driving state detection unit when the boiler driving unit is in a non operational state and the external temperature sensed through the temperature sensor is less than a set temperature the valve control unit controls the water pipe by repeatedly opening and closing the electromagnetic valve at regular time intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in order to prevent the water stagnant in the water pipe 3 from freezing when the temperature detected by the temperature sensor 5 falls below the set temperature detected by the temperature sensor 5 during the idle period of the boiler 1 by the valve control unit 13 of the controller 10 the electromagnetic valve 3 is opened and at the same time the electromagnetic valve 7a is automatically closed through the valve control unit 13 and the pump 6 provided in the boiler 1 is operated to the inside through the water pipe 3 the supplied water is discharged by bypassing the drain pipe 4c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "during the idle period of the boiler 1 the electromagnetic valve 3 is automatically opened and closed according to the external temperature sensed through the temperature sensor 5 to discharge the water stagnated in the water pipe 2 to the outside through the drain pipe 4c to the outside of the water pipe by allowing water to flow at regular intervals through 2 it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from being frozen by increasing the freezing point freezing point of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "on the other hand it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from freezing in advance by adjusting the freezing point freezing point of water according to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "by doing so it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from being frozen in advance by increasing the freezing point of water when the boiler 1 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "1b gases may be fed into the ionization chamber 44 via a gas conduit 33"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_106", "text": "via the ion source block the surfaces of conduit 150 are thus preferably maintained at temperature greater than the set point of pid 3"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "a water warming and circulating apparatus for a recreational vehicle the recreational vehicle having a holding tank for holding an on board water supply of cold water and heated water an exposed portion of the water supply being in thermal communication with outside air and having a water temperature affected by the temperature of the outside air particularly when the outside air temperature falls to near the freezing point of water and below a pump with an associated switch to selectively activate and deactivate the pump the pump drawing the cold water from the holding tank a water heater having a heating tank the pump pumping water from the holding tank to the water heater the water heater heating and storing a supply of the heated water in the heating tank the water heater heating the heated water to a desired temperature a water fixture having at least one manual valve to selectively dispense the heated water and the cold water a heated supply line providing a flow path from the holding tank through the pump and water heater to the water fixture and a cold supply line providing a flow path from the holding tank through the pump and to the water fixture said water warming and circulating apparatus comprising"}, {"pat_id": "US-12050157-B2", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "the information may include for example the current water flow past water flow status of the automatic shut off valve status of whether a leak is detected home or away mode status and water temperature current and past temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11693434-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the water quality monitoring system of claim 4 wherein the control module further controls the heating rod according to the temperature controls the water change valve according to the ph value and or the salinity and or controls the water wheel and or the water change valve according to the oxidation reduction potential"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102274711-B1", "para_id": "para_133", "text": "alternatively the automatic ito valve control module 330 may control to open the automatic ito valve device 410 even if one of the water temperature and the temperature is the reference water temperature or the reference temperature or less"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100806134-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "it is composed of a double wall having a minimum temperature difference between the ground and the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent condensation inside the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent corrosion of the valve facility 110 disposed in the valve chamber structure 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102593825-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "the control unit 300 may include a display unit 310 that generates an alarm signal or shows the water leakage situation to the user visually and visually and provides electrical signals to the three way heat source supply valve the flow control valve for controlling the hot water temperature and the water supply and blocking valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the pipe adjacent the location of the thermal sensor drops below freezing the sensor is actuated and completes an electrical circuit from a power source to a solenoid actuated valve to thereby cause it to open and allow water to trickle from the water supply pipe through an existing water outlet fixture and down its adjacent and pre existing drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing the sensor is de actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid actuated valve and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "with the circuit thus closed solenoid actuated valve 66 will open and allow water to pass through from conduit 65 to faucet 22 via conduit 67"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "that is upon such a rise in temperature contact arm 51 of thermal switch 50 opens to interrupt the electrical circuit conveying electricity between power source 70 and solenoid actuate valve 66 and thereby cause valve 66 to close in a manner well known in the art"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the smart water valve can include a housing unit that uses various sensors for monitoring water flowing into the property from the main pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "for example the processor 206 may communicate in a bidirectional manner with each of the transceiver 202 physical input module 204 electronically actuated ball valve 208 flow sensor 210 temperature sensor 212 and leak sensor 214"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "in some implementations the flow sensor 210 the temperature sensor 212 and leak sensor 214 may be contained within the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "for example the smart water valve 126 can determine that the temperature of the water leak of 60 degrees f matches the temperature of water consumed by the toilet of 177 degrees c 62 degrees f"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "in some examples the smart water valve 126 can determine that temperature of the water leak matches the temperature of the particular water consuming device based on the temperatures matching within a threshold variance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "discontinuance of dental services in case of malfunction or exhaustion of water in the single pressure storage tank 2 9 in order to prevent the occurrence of a separate simple auxiliary metal or plastic material inside the device the tank 2 14 is installed and in case of emergency the tank cap 2 14 1 is opened and the user can be used to pour the graft in addition a small load is provided at the inlet of the pipe 3 9 to which the water of the unit chair to which each is connected is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "freeze protection system of flush toilet freezing burst prevention system for water closet the present invention relates to a freeze protection system of a flush toilet and more particularly by detecting a change in temperature in a water supply pipe line of a flush toilet an electric valve is automatically opened and closed according to an electrical signal thereby allowing a certain amount of water to flow into the flush toilet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe the water supply valve was opened slightly so that the water flow was always maintained in the water supply pipe so that water was always circulated in the water supply pipe or a separate heat radiator was installed to increase the temperature of the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "by doing so while minimizing power consumption water pipes are prevented from freezing and water supply is controlled to save water.1 is a conceptual diagram schematically showing a freeze protection system of the flush toilet according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the controller c is a circulation pump p and the first opening and closing valve to prevent freezing of the water supply line 11 connected to the flush toilet 10 in accordance with the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 13 pneumatic or electric signals are controlled to actuate v\u2081 and second open close valves v\u2082"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "thus the controller c opens the first opening closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0941968-B1", "para_id": "para_135", "text": "thus the amount of time the brine valve remains open during the refill phase of the regeneration cycle will determine the quantity of sodium ions which are used to replenish the media"}, {"pat_id": "US-5921711-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "a variety of factors can affect the timing as to how long a particular field remains active including such factors as surge usage weather ambient soil temperature dewatering rate etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102587945-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "additionally it is possible to prevent freezing of the air valve 90 in a convenient and effective manner by configuring the heating element 44 solar cell 55 temperature sensor signal transmitter and control unit"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "data collected from ultrasonic flow sensor 37 provides users reactive preventative and predictive recommendations"}, {"pat_id": "US-4954151-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "vaporization of the refrigerant within the evaporator 17 absorbs heat through the freeze plate 19 from water and ice 21 in the water vessel 23 and the refrigerant temperature is essentially established by the expander 15 which may include a conventional capillary or expansion valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-4635668-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "apparatus for automatically controlling flow in a water line to avoid freeze damage comprising a temperature sensor adapted for connection to the water line the water line a normally closed valve adapted for connection to a housing control circuit means within said housing and responsive to said temperature sensor for continuously monitoring the temperature of water in the line and selectively opening and closing said valve to allow increased periodic flow in the water line with decreasing water temperature and indicator means associated with said housing and connected to said control circuit means for indicating the temperature proximity of water in the line to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-9109349-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "because first electronic valve 12 is shut no additional water is permitted to enter from connection line 22 into structure 70 until system 10 is reset thus significantly reducing the volume of damaging water capable of escaping connection line 22 or other tributary within structure 70 during a leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101758303-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "when t3 approaches t3set pumps 14 and 72 begin as shown in control action block 432 and return to 410 via control steps 433 434 and 480"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5851260-Y2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "an anti freeze valve 2 low temperature valve connected to piping 1 is used to prevent freezing by lowering the water temperature to a temperature equal to or close to that of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100966852-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it has a configuration in which a pressure relief valve is installed to be discharged to the outside to close the exhaust port.as described above according to the freeze protection device of the water pipe of the present invention by operating the hydraulic cylinder with a small amount of water flowing out according to the external temperature change and the force of the water the freeze with the water discharged through the operation of the cylinder effectively also by replacing the capacity of the hydraulic cylinder only it is possible to secure as much water as possible to prevent freezing at any water pipe size or water pressure and more precisely by controlling the amount of discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102756589-B1", "para_id": "para_23"