tection of water parameters such as pressure ph hardness turbidity and temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100846473-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the first and second valve assemblies 122 and 126 allow the regeneration mode to proceed while the mode is in progress"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714895-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide a non excavation complete water and sewage repair method which can shorten the work time by automatically controlling and performing construction work through a controller of a wireless control member thereby eliminating the inconvenience of having to manually operate a steam supply valve while checking a thermometer and a pressure gauge one by one in the past and which can precisely measure the temperature and pressure of steam for hardening a tube to secure data according to the work conditions thereby enabling more precise work to be performed"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "another important aspect of the bi metallic disk is that after the predetermined temperature of for example 36 has been reached and the disk has warped to break the electrical contact of the switch the disk will maintain the warped shape until manually re set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100342599-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "during the ultrasonic sterilization a heat jacket 25 for circulating a cooling water was attached to the outside of the sterilization reactor in order to remove the generated heat because heat is generated due to the cavitation phenomenon of ultrasonic waves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100926077-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "subsequently looking at the plurality of pipe lines w1 to w14 provided in the water softener according to the present invention by connecting the external cold hot water pipes to the first valve assembly 350 to remove the cold hot raw water of the cold hot water pipes the first valve assembly 1 by connecting the first and second raw water supply lines w