  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in addition when it is determined that the wastewater treatment capacity information is obtained by communicating with the wastewater treatment capacity management terminal configured in the wastewater treatment facility 210 to determine whether the treatment capacity limit is reached at the time of initial discharge by delaying the opening of the water gate or valve 500 for a connection and sewage treatment plant connection by a predetermined time the effect of preventing the processing capacity limit can be prevented in advance.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "as described above the pc structural type manhole 300 is provided with a water gate or valve 500 for a connection pipe of a wastewater treatment plant which is a water gate or valve for discharging an initial storm water to a wastewater treatment plant or a valve 600 for a river connection which is a water gate or a valve for performing opening and closing of the water gate or valve and constitutes an opening and closing device 550 or 650 for opening and closing the water gate by controlling according to the control signal of the configured rtu it is possible to prevent manhole accidents efficiently and to manage the initial storm including contamination source in advance"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "bethridge on ca transferred to the inflowing solvent before entering the thus heat exchanger 925 preheated the water and reduced the energy requirements of the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101102443-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present application as a means for solving the above problems as a water treatment method for obtaining purified water suitable for drinking water or industrial water for the target water selected from the treated water selected from river river water ground water wastewater treatment plant after pretreatment of the water to be treated in a sulphate denitrification tank or an ultrasonic electrolysis tank an ozone containing water is made and supplied to a high precision filtration tank to remove residual contaminants while passing through the filter bed of the biofilm separation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101055889-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "dam is supplied with water without difficulty in accordance with the water supply the supply of water for the first and second elevating the floating in the water tank to gyohyo by controlling the up and down valve by raising and lowering the water the water is filled and discharged into the first and second tanks and the air generated by this is prevented from eutrophication caused by the lack of dissolved oxygen due to the contaminant such as freshwater fish farm and sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101788811-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an activated carbon filtration unit in which raw water sucked from an emergency water feeder or a river or a river side is subjected to filtration treatment with a large particle while foreign substances are filtered through the sand and filtered water filtered by the sand filtration unit is re a filter cloth for holding a filter medium between the filter plates stacked in multiple means so that small foreign substances contained in the filtered water are filtered by the filter medium coated with the filter cloth while being supplied with the filtered water filtered by the activated carbon filter unit is provided a pressurized filter portion connected to a third raw milk feed inlet for feeding raw water to one side of the filter plate and connected to the other side of the third filtered water discharge pipe through which the filtered water is discharged from the filter plate and the filter cloth a membrane filter in which filtered water filtered by the filter is sucked and highly filtered to fine foreign matters a modular water production system comprising a part a filtration data storage unit for presetting and storing a state value of a water quality to be filtered by the modular water production system and a limit pressure value inside the operation unit a state of the water quality filtered by the modular water production system a water quality measurement data comparing unit for storing the data and a pressure measurement data verifying unit for checking and storing the filtration state by measuring the pressure inside each of the actuating units a water quality measurement monitoring unit a failure confirmation monitoring unit for checking the operation state of each operation unit of the modular water production system to check for a failure a system general status data storage unit in which the installation location and related information of the modular water production system are stored a water quality status data storage unit for storing information on the status of the water quality and the water quality status and quantity on the site a central control unit including an operating unit data storage unit for storing a value of a proper pressure value and a proper filtering throughput in each operating unit a system data transmitting and receiving unit for wirelessly transmitting measured data and data confirmed by the fault checking and monitoring unit to the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit and receiving a signal of a central control unit a central data transmitting and receiving unit provided in the central control unit for receiving data transmitted through the system data transmitting and receiving unit and transmitting an instruction command to the modular water producing system and when the water quality measurement value measured by the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit is out of the range of a predetermined set value or when a malfunction of each of the operating units occurs and the malfunction confirmation monitoring unit confirms it and an emergency monitoring control unit for generating an emergency signal in the central control unit when the water quality and pressure data measured and transmitted from the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit is out of the predetermined water quality and pressure data range wherein the control unit controls the operation of each of the actuating units of the modular water production system to automatically perform backwashing by operating each valve of the modular water production system to stop the supply of raw water and a washing automatic control unit is additionally provided to the water supply unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_536", "text": "second the structure of the sump tank 34 is improved so that the height can be adjusted with the hose of the manometer type level fire nozzle which is similar to the water hammer action in that it has no breakdowns and has a semi permanent lifespan and the pumping pipe 89 formed by the valve of the tank 34 is formed by a plastic flow pipe and it can be selected for environmental improvement projects as an opportunity to prevent in advance not only the hydraulic equipment but also the economic loss caused by dredging the nakdong river sediment due to the above mentioned shape difference in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 8