he discharge pipe to discharge the washing discharge water to the river s17 sensing the amount of discharged water discharged into the river by the flow sensor unit of the drained water discharge pipe installed at the rear end of the water quality sensor unit and transmitting the sensed discharged water quantity information to the controller s18 transmitting by the controller primary water quality data and discharged water flow rate information to a center server of a water quality management center s19 determining whether the received water quality data meets drinking water quality standards by a controller that periodically receives water quality data from the water quality sensor unit s20 if appropriate turning off the washing water inlet valve configured in the washing water inlet to stop the injection of the washing water and opening the water supply valve to supply tap water to the corresponding pipe s21 monitoring the secondary water quality data transmitted from the water quality sensor unit by the controller while discharging tap water supplied to the water supply pipe through the discharge pipe s22 and if the received water quality data meets the drinking water quality standards transmitting the water quality data to the manager smart terminal to block the discharge valve of the discharge pipe and open the water valve on the consumer side to supply tap water to the consumer s23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100960367-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "thus the water introduced into the drain pit 18d through the drain pipe 18c is stored in the drain pit 18d by the height at which the outlet 18e is formed and then discharged into the river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in 1988 piper alpha platform fire accident killed 167 people and costed 3.4 billion because of removing the pump a s pressure safety valve in 1999 a pressure relief valve failed on a 16 inch gasoline pipeline operated by the olympic pipe line company in bellingham wash"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882065-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and has a double sealing structure comprising an inner cover coupled to the upper end of a pipe connection socket and an outer cover coupled to the upper end of a sluice valve housing thereby preventing damage such as corrosion inside and outside of the sluice valve due to the inflow of foreign substances such as sewage from the ground and when supplying water to plants along a river the purpose is to provide a sluice valve having a double sealing structure in which a pipe connection pipe formed to be able to rotate 360 degrees is coupled to a pipe connection socket and a screw elbow and a hose is coupled to a hose connection of the screw elbow so that water can be supplied to plants along a river without tangling of the hose in any direction in the surrounding area"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4087351-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water softening device for softening water a hydraulic drive unit that is operated by the softened water and is used for opening and closing the gate gate of a river that is not opened and closed for a long time and a pump for sending water and a water pressure drive unit including a water softening device having a switching valve capable of supplying pressure water sent from the pump to a desired side of the water softening device and the water pressure drive unit the water sent out from the water softening device and the water pressure drive unit can be returned to the tank and the water in the tank can be sent out by the pump a hydraulic drive unit comprising a water softening device wherein the hydraulic drive unit is a hydraulic cylinder device and the switching valve is of a spool type"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the river water to be treated which has passed through the pretreatment unit 10 flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 is purified in the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 and then passes through the discharge tank 40 to be discharged into a river or lake thereby performing the functions of water quality purification and management during normal times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100351111-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the sludge in the raw water introduced into the tertiary tank 12c is discharged by opening the sludge valve 26 and the purified water is circulated to the bath or river the swamp the lake and the sea via the recovery pipe 28"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102230241-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "that is while installing the first pump p1 and the first valve v1 on the outlet 12 side of the water resource pretreatment unit 10 the level of purified water or river water artificially recharged into the lower stratum s3 when is exceeding the set reference water level or when water pollution occurs the remote server 80 remotely controls the first valve v1 by closing while the lower stratum s3 through the horizontal well 31 it is able to block the inflow of purified water or river water into the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100408854-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "in winter the floating hull 210 is submerged below a certain level by controlling the open pressure in the pipe through the valve to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "motorized valve 11 21 electric valve control panel 12 22 manual valve 13 23 electric valve 14 24 adjustment tank 15 25 snow drift 16 18 26 29 water level monitoring panel 19 optical cable 31 electric pole 32 pipe 33 road 35 inspection pit 36 water level measuring pipe 37 communication pipe 38 sheath heater 46 cable 101 cpu 102 rom 103 ram 104 crt 105 a d converter 106 multiplexer 107 108 amplifier 109 keyboard 110 buffer 111 112 interface 113 photoelectric converter s1 to s13 water level sensor r river w1 to w13 alarm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100960370-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "thus the water introduced into the drain pit 18d through the drain pipe 18c is stored in the drain pit 18d by the height at which the outlet 18e is formed and then discharged into the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101347132-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "here only experimental experiments confirming the removal performance of suspended solids ss bod cod total phosphorus p and nitrogen n on a laboratory scale but the functional carriers presented herein during the water treatment process it is merely an example of the application and the technical concept of the present application is applied not only to the wastewater treatment plant but also to the bottom of the river or to the retreat block which can be applied to the field that can remove poisons or pollutants in the water while giving stability to the aquatic ecosystem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102660526-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pool built to a predetermined depth on the banks of a stream or river a balancing tank connected to the pool by an overflow pipe and a drainage pipe to store water discharged from the pool a filtration device connected to the balancing tank and the supply pipe to filter the water in the balancing tank and connected to the pool and the water supply pipe to supply the filtered water to the pool and it includes a piping control manhole built between the pool and the balancing tank to control the overflow pipe drain pipe and water supply pipe to prevent contaminants from the pool from flowing into the balancing tank the piping control manhole is a first contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the overflow pipe a second contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the drainage pipe a third pollutant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the water supply pipe a first pollutant discharge pipe and a first pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle portion of the front overflow pipe of the first pollutant penetration blocking valve a second pollutant discharge pipe and a second pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the drainage pipe in front of the second pollutant penetration blocking valve a water damage recovery system for a swimming pool comprising a third pollutant discharge pipe and a third pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the water supply pipe in front of the third pollutant penetration blocking valve"}]</data>
</edge>
