  <data key="d5">["logic", "protection", "sidewall", "sedimentation", "valve", "position", "flange", "part", "tank", "river", "signal", "ring", "order", "level", "solid", "accident", "default", "assembly", "rail", "chamber", "rain", "pad", "coupling", "flow", "pipe", "communication", "pump", "force", "rtu", "outside", "protrusion", "space", "wastewater", "utilization", "capsule", "debris", "chemical", "time", "feed", "driving", "housing", "water", "brush", "extension", "advance", "sealing", "crush", "member", "portion", "circumscribing", "condensation", "switch", "period", "manhole", "filter", "filtration", "plate", "operation", "rod", "detection", "cleaning", "storage", "scraper", "hole", "rainwater", "substance", "controller", "system", "support", "pipeline", "winery", "surface", "stormwater", "panel", "insertion", "treatment", "split", "pc", "closing", "matter", "storm", "source", "drug", "ground", "waterway", "end", "inflow", "aspect", "frame", "separation", "reservoir", "actuator", "section", "response", "discharge", "contamination", "removal", "drive", "opening", "guide", "passage", "invention", "device", "suppression", "type", "plant", "supply", "piece", "sensor", "sump", "port", "runoff", "gate", "department", "material", "inlet", "control", "connection", "drain", "collection", "isolation", "unit", "manner", "input", "embodiment", "groove", "ball", "body", "flocculation", "expansion"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["drive", "manage", "receive", "lock", "hold", "guide", "include", "perform", "dispose", "incline", "treat", "prevent", "block", "open", "collect", "enter", "mean", "constitute", "connect", "mount", "form", "float", "move", "accord", "clean", "actuate", "encapsulate", "allow", "sense", "seal", "locate", "close", "build", "seat", "latch", "pass", "extend", "control", "have", "bind", "couple", "may", "fix", "configure", "stir", "enclose", "elevate", "keep", "flow", "massage", "can", "discharge", "be", "groove", "store", "utilize", "pump", "describe", "provide", "comprise", "lift"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "as described above the pc structural type manhole 300 is provided with a water gate or valve 500 for a connection pipe of a wastewater treatment plant which is a water gate or valve for discharging an initial storm water to a wastewater treatment plant or a valve 600 for a river connection which is a water gate or a valve for performing opening and closing of the water gate or valve and constitutes an opening and closing device 550 or 650 for opening and closing the water gate by controlling according to the control signal of the configured rtu it is possible to prevent manhole accidents efficiently and to manage the initial storm including contamination source in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}]</data>
</edge>
