  <data key="d5">["sedimentation", "valve", "part", "purpose", "tank", "river", "signal", "ring", "settling", "adjustment", "trench", "accident", "rain", "coupling", "flow", "apparatus", "rate", "pipe", "rtu", "outside", "protrusion", "wastewater", "utilization", "reaction", "time", "housing", "water", "leak", "extension", "advance", "settler", "portion", "manhole", "filter", "plate", "storage", "hole", "rainwater", "substance", "system", "support", "surface", "outage", "treatment", "pc", "closing", "storm", "source", "ground", "end", "inflow", "wall", "contaminant", "box", "cover", "reservoir", "amount", "sewage", "response", "discharge", "contamination", "conduit", "opening", "change", "guide", "power", "invention", "device", "type", "plant", "side", "supply", "piece", "basin", "transfer", "hour", "gate", "quality", "inlet", "control", "connection", "drain", "unit", "manner", "ball", "efficiency", "expansion", "processing"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["manage", "lock", "guide", "include", "perform", "dispose", "incline", "settle", "prevent", "block", "collect", "enter", "open", "constitute", "supply", "connect", "mount", "form", "measure", "divide", "accord", "seal", "increase", "require", "close", "seat", "suspend", "latch", "occur", "control", "have", "improve", "send", "extend", "couple", "may", "configure", "fail", "flow", "accomplish", "can", "discharge", "be", "store", "utilize", "will", "adjust", "describe", "provide", "shorten", "lift"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "as described above the pc structural type manhole 300 is provided with a water gate or valve 500 for a connection pipe of a wastewater treatment plant which is a water gate or valve for discharging an initial storm water to a wastewater treatment plant or a valve 600 for a river connection which is a water gate or a valve for performing opening and closing of the water gate or valve and constitutes an opening and closing device 550 or 650 for opening and closing the water gate by controlling according to the control signal of the configured rtu it is possible to prevent manhole accidents efficiently and to manage the initial storm including contamination source in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-10487480-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "thus if a water leak were to occur coincidentally with an electrical power outage such as may occur with a large storm the valve will fail to accomplish its purpose unless auxiliary power is available"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100416293-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "conventionally since the raw water which has been settled through the initial settler is sent to the flow adjusting tank to supply a predetermined amount to the subsequent reaction tank the processing time is long and the sedimentation tank and the flow adjusting tank are separately required but the present invention requires a separate settling tank and a flow adjusting tank it is not necessary and the processing time can be shortened to about 0.5 to 3 hours thereby increasing the processing efficiency.as described above the present invention divides the water tank of the water quality adjustment tank 10 into the blocking wall 40 but the blocking wall 40 is lifted up and down by the lifting part 30 and the water quality of the incoming raw water and by measuring the flow rate to control the blocking wall 40 the transfer valve 60 the storm discharge valve 70 it is possible to increase the treatment efficiency of the sewage treatment system in response to the water quality change of the incoming water no settling basin or flow adjustment tank is required and the treatment efficiency of the system can be improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101851938-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the apparatus includes a box 10 an inlet pipe 12 formed at an upper side of the inner side of the housing 10 and supplied with initial rainwater from the upper part thereof a trench cover 14 connected to the inflow conduit 12 and extending downwardly and being supplied with an initial storm and a trench cover 14 connected to the inflow conduit 12 to prevent inflow of contaminants suspended substances etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}]</data>
</edge>
