l line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-10005682-B1", "para_id": "para_250", "text": "one or both of the primary and secondary flow paths can optionally comprise a flow meter or a ph meter or both"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in 1988 piper alpha platform fire accident killed 167 people and costed 3.4 billion because of removing the pump a s pressure safety valve in 1999 a pressure relief valve failed on a 16 inch gasoline pipeline operated by the olympic pipe line company in bellingham wash"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the system includes a water meter inline to a main water valve wherein the water meter is configured to provide water usage data to a collector unit and an irrigation system configured to receive weather data city requirements for water use and soil moisture levels and provide a water consumption data from different regions to the collector unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if at least one or more of the parameters constituting the water quality measured by the formed second sensor unit 50 does not match a preset criterion control not only to control the turbidity drain valve 300 but also to discharge the turbid water water pressure measured by the water pressure detection sensor 70 among the flow rate control valve 80 and the water pressure detection sensor 70 sequentially formed between the turbid water drain valve 300 and the consumer 90 is outside the preset water pressure range if not by controlling the flow rate control valve 80 to maintain the flow rate and flow rate to be maintained in a preset water pressure range the administrator mobile terminal accessible through the network 500 for the database 630 800 provides a real time monitoring and monitoring module 621 that provides a function to support decision making ict integrated monitoring for smart water city construction send and receive to receive the location and property information of natural and artificial objects existing on the surface and underground and ground spaces of the water management system 1 from the big data server 700 through the network 500 after controlling the unit 610 the received information is matched and generated based on gis information based on the water pipe of the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for smart water city construction and then through the network 500 by controlling the transmitter receiver 610 to transmit to the manager mobile terminal 800 the manager can directly control the water supply network block and facility information db as well as support various planning and decision making and industrial activities in connection with the manager s work"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "water is supplied directly to the consumer 90 through the water supply pipe between the consumer 90 where the valve 80 is formed but the leak detection sensor 60 for each predetermined distance between the consumer 90 and the turbidity control valve 300 is formed ict integrated monitoring water management system for smart water city construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "referring to figure 1 ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is the intake station 10 ground water 20 smart meter 30 the first sensor unit 40 the second sensor device unit 50 leak detection sensor 60 water pressure sensor 70 flow control valve 80 consumer 90 water purification plant 100 rechlorination injection facility 200 turbidity drain valve 300 a connection node terminal 400 a network 500 an integrated control server 600 and a big data server 700 and a manager mobile terminal 800"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "to this end the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is a system that manages each of the grid type waterworks network formed in the downtown area and the waterworks network formed in the outskirts of the city as an integrated system to manage the network"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "it is apparent to those skilled in the art to which the present invention pertains that other modified examples based on the technical idea of the present invention can be implemented in addition to the embodiments disclosed herein.1 1a ict integrated monitoring water management system for smart water city construction 10 intake point 20 groundwater 30 smart meter 40 first sensor unit 50 second sensor unit 60 leak detection sensor 70 water pressure sensor 80 flow control valve 90 accommodation 100 water purification plant 200 re chlorine injection equipment 300 turbid drainage valve 400 connection node terminal 500 network 600 integrated control server 700 big data server 800 manager mobile terminal"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "while this may not point to the exact location of the leak this data combined with a geo spatial map will allow cities to gather insight into a potential section sub section or branch of the city plumbing that could be leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore it is virtually impossible to install a decompression valve in a jurisdiction block where a manhole structure is mainly installed in a road network where city traffic is frequent"}]</data>
