  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "with valve 10 closed no further water will be permitted to pass from drain pipe 53 into sump pit 50 thereby preventing basement 61 from flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "without proper maintenance backwater valves can become blocked or stuck giving building managers and homeowners a false sense of security that they will be protected during a flooding event"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "however many homeowners and residents are not aware of the presence or operation of a backwater valve and if the valve is closed due to a flooding event or blockage many residents will not be aware of it until sanitary sewage begins flowing back into their building"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "in this case when the backwater valve to the building is closed building occupants should be aware that sewer water generated in the building has nowhere to go and therefore should limit or stop water use to prevent backflow of generate sewage into the building until the water level in the sewer has subsided and water can flow normally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200335039-Y1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore the groundwater leakage or flooding is minimized through the basement outer wall where the waterproofing is not performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire h