nger pump and jet pump 157 are provided and are connected to an introduction pipe and a water supply port or a fire prevention and disaster prevention pipe line 168 and a water discharge port 169 and are connected to a limit switch or a limit switch and a power motor body 192 is provided with a hood and a snap ring a fan and a body frame a body front reinforcing plate a rotor assembly on a rotating shaft a stator assembly on a front rotating shaft support a motor protection casting frame a terminal box and a lifting bolt a terminal box cover a rear rotating shaft support a rear reinforcing plate a gap a fan cover or a protective cover a rotor core and a stator core with stator windings and are connected and connected and underground passage flood prevention a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-6439260-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "4 848 389 issued to pirkle the feature of providing electrical control to shut off the water main supply with a first valve and draining the pipes in a building with a second valve in a tee joint to prevent freezing and bursting of the pipes is disclosed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373478-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention when a flooding occurs in a manhole the opening and closing valve is automatically opened by a buoy rising and falling by the water level to quickly discharge the flooded water in the manhole to the outside by the suction force generated through the ejector thereby preventing corrosion or failure of the facility due to the flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "there is a place where a drainage facility should be installed place where the equipment is expected to be damaged by flooding a valve room where electricity is not supplied it is installed in a place where there is a risk of leakage of drainage pump due to submersion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "therefore in the non power source immersion prevention system of the present invention the opening and closing valve 300 is automatically opened by the access port 200 that ascends and descends by the water level when the flooding occurs in the manhole and the water is flooded in the manhole by the suction force generated through the ejector 500 water can be rapidly discharged to the outside through the suction pipe 400 to prevent corrosion or breakdown of the facility by flooding and it is possible to immediately cope with the flooding by the person without any operation the installation cost is reduced as compared with the drainage method using the conventional pump and the pause time is set during the operation by the amount of water flowing into and discharged from the water collection container 630 provided at the upper portion of the water inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by pre and when the main opening closing valve can not be opened the fire extinguishing water can be bypassed without passing through the main opening closing valve by the water pressure of the fire extinguishing water applied to the main water supply pipe and the main opening closing valve so that fire suppression is always possible to prevent the flooding caused by the digested water from being generated by the fire extinguishing system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "therefore when the opening closing valve can not be opened by the driving motor and the lifting lowering rod and the nut box the water is pressurized by the water pressure of the water to be applied to the main water supply pipe and the main opening it is possible to suppress the fire at all times and to prevent the water from being flooded at the installation position of the main opening closing valve so as to prevent the flooding damage caused by the water.korea registered utility model no"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "the shutoff valve 532 can be used to prevent flooding for leaks downstream of the water device 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345691-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in the above embodiment when the flow rate increases there is a limit value in the pipeline and when the pressure rises reverse flow of sewage occurs to prevent flooding damage at the upstream site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100555925-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the first balltop 283 is the first in accordance with the rise in the water level even if the automatic intake valve 282 is submerged in water due to abnormal weather conditions or flooding in the state in which the automatic intake valve 282 is open by closing the open channel of the automatic intake valve 282 by the operation of the sub ball 283a to block the contaminants of the surface water flowing into the intake pipes 200 210 through the automatic intake valve 282 do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100587771-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "therefore the groundwater leakage or flooding is minimized through the basement outer wall where the waterproofing is not performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187840-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it includes a rainwater management block that allows rainwater to be stored in rainwater storage blocks and a rainwater management block that opens a drain valve to allow rainwater to penetrate into the infiltration facility after a rainfall has passed and discharges stored rainwater depending on the situation to prevent flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the flood diffusion prevention system of a building structure that is installed in a multi story building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to leakage from spreading to the elevating facility space a drainage passage formed on the floor of the common space for each floor in the building structure a drainage trench installed on the upper portion of the drainage passage to shield the drainage passage and a plurality of drainage holes for draining the inflowing water into the drainage passage a drain module connected to and configured to include a pipe for discharging the water to the outside a flood detection sensor installed in the drainage module to detect whether water has flowed in a water supply shutoff valve installed in a water supply line of the building structure to block water supply by a control signal and a flood signal received from the flood detection sensor a control unit for transmitting the control signal to the water supply shut off valve so as to be blocked and it is installed in front of the opening closing door of the elevator installed in the building structure and is raised to a preset height from the floor and includes a blocking module to prevent water from flowing into the elevator when submerged the blocking module is a blocking member installed in front of the opening closing door to open or shield the front lower part of the opening closing door according to the elevation an elevating wire having one end coupled to the upper portion of the blocking member to elevate the blocking member and the flooding prevention system of a building structure characterized in that it is connected to the other end of the elevating wire and configured to include a wire driving unit for elevating and lowering the elevating wire in conjunction with the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention provides a system for preventing the spread of water in a building structure that is installed in a multi storey building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to a leak from spreading to an elevating facility space the it is installed on the upper part of the drain to shield the drain and includes a drain trench having a plurality of drain holes through which the inflowing water is drained into the drain and a piping part connected to the drain to drain the water to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200482925-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a cover is provided on the upper part of the outer case installed on the outside of the water pipe to prevent external exposure of the water pipe and the opening closing valve to prevent freezing and freezing of the water pipe in winter it is related to the excellent floating heat insulation by inserting the winter exclusive valve to increase the efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439852-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "by the way the water flowing through the water pipe is also transported with foreign matters lighter than water and these foreign matters are adsorbed by the air valve and the distillation valve to form a gap and cause an accident such as leakage and flooding"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2749860-B1", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "the signal interruption takes place at an open main valve 5 for the purpose of targeted water removal from the hydrant 1 or in case of leak a defective main valve 5 or with a closed main valve 5 if the drainage aperture 116 penetrates through the drainage sheet 118 and in the hydrant 1 waste water as a result of flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659063-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "there are many systems for automatically controlling a valve to interrupt the water supply in the event that flooding occurs due to a leak somewhere in a water system"}]</data>
</edge>
