  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101893417-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in one example the control device receives the incoming water quality value and the flow rate value from the first sensor derives the influent load receives the outflow water quality value from the second sensor receives the temperature value from the third sensor a data portion for data wise the water quality by temperature a driving unit for driving the valve to introduce the water into the pre treatment tank and the bioreactor the real time influent load value is derived from the real time influent water quality value and the real time flow value from the first sensor and the real time runoff water quality value is derived from the derived real time influent load and the real the real time recirculated water load value is obtained from the fourth sensor by receiving the real time recirculated water quality value and the real time flow rate value from the fourth sensor and the real real time flow rate value is received and a real time connection load is derived and when the real time reflux water load and real time connection water load exceeds the above mentioned additional connection water load and additional reflux water load the valve is driven to the pre so that the real time counter current load and the real time connection water load are set to the above characterized in that it comprises a load by driving the valve and can be linked or less wake analysis unit such that flowing into the bioreactor through the raw water inlet line.as described above according to the system of the present invention in the continuous treatment of the wastewater it is possible to automatically determine whether or not the pre treatment of the reflux water and the connection water is performed by the sensing basis thereby reducing the cost required for the pretreatment and improving the treatment efficiency of the pretreatment it is possible to improve the treatment efficiency of the whole system by preventing the load of the bioreactor.1 is a block diagram illustrating a system of the present invention 2 is a schematic view showing an example of a bioreactor which is a constitution of the present invention 3 is a block diagram showing a detailed configuration of a control apparatus which is a constitution of the present invention figures 4a and 4b are operational state diagrams of the system of the present invention 5 is a schematic view showing an example of a pretreatment tank which is a constituent of the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426715-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank and the initial excellent effluent which has been filtered by the stencil strainer flows into the storage tank and stores the initial excellent effluent while storing the initial excellent effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100791422-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "an object of the present invention is a tank having a hollow inside the inlet formed on the upper surface the storage tank and the narrowing storage tank formed by partitioning the inner space of the lower side of the inlet by the partition wall respectively the narrow surface on the upper surface of the storage tank a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-12127513-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in another aspect one or more of said water collection modules internal horizontal and vertical edges are made leak proof via the addition of mechanical or chemical components forming a fluid holding internal volume wherein said edge leak proof mechanical component include one of silicone gel amp sealing or silicone model seals wherein each said water collection internal volume is hydraulically connected to at least one more other water collection module s internal volume and at least one or more of said water collection module s top panel or said wall panels openings has a plug cap hose flow restrictor drip hose faucet valve spigot or similar component"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}]</data>
