  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102329033-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "when the valve hemisphere 34 is installed to keep the degree of opening inside the valve body 32 in a narrowly open state excessive expansion can be avoided for closure so durability is not reduced but the opening inside the valve body 32 there was a problem that the sewage inside the rainwater chamber could not be discharged quickly due to the narrow degree and the amount of sewage flowing in varies depending on the place where the rainwater chamber is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101138988-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "as shown the outlet pipe 31 may control the opening and closing of the outlet pipe via a separate valve 35"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052943-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 92 roof 93 washing wastewater spray device 94 washing wastewater recirculation mechanism 100 ground 101 drainage groove 102 collecting drainage groove 103 convex 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 107 left vertical frame 108 right vertical frame 10 horizontal frame 111 water supply pipe 112 drainage nozzle 113 intermediate pipe 114 cleaning waste water supply pipe 115 cleaning waste supply pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through a filter a pump installed at the bottom of the storage tank to frequently rotate the rainwater stored in the storage tank or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 30 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the case of a malfunction in the rainwater recycling device s comprising a control unit 60 configured with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 at one side of the filter 10 an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60 and installed at one side of the solenoid valve 80 the turbidity sensor 90 that inspects the turbidity of rainwater flowing into the solenoid valve 80 and transmits the turbidity state of the inspected rainwater to the control unit and a full water level sensor that inspects and transmits the water level of the water inside the storage tank to the control unit 100 and a low water level sensor 110 that inspects the low water level of the water inside the storage tank and transmits it to the control unit the control unit 60 includes a function of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102206293-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "one selected from a storage tank 20 that stores and stores rainwater flowing through the filter a pump that is installed at the bottom of the storage tank and rotates the rainwater stored in the storage tank from time to time or a compressor that injects air the installed water circulation device 30 and the temperature sensor 40 that periodically measures the temperature of the water stored in the storage tank 20 and provides information to the control unit 60 and the temperature sensor 40 the operation of the heating wire 50 driven by the control of the controller 60 the water circulating device 90 the temperature sensor 40 and the heating wire 50 according to the set temperature value is controlled according to the input program at the same time in the event of a malfunction the filter 10 of the rainwater recycling device s configured including a control unit 60 equipped with a transmission and receiver 61 that transmits a warning signal to the manager s smartphone 70 on one side an electromagnetic valve 80 is configured to block or control rainwater flowing into the filter according to a signal sent from the control unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706162-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "a odor blocking tube formed of a synthetic resin material having a cylindrical shape having a narrow bottom and widening toward the top and having a ring shaped weight added to the bottom a circular flange having a plurality of first bolt holes and coupled to an upper surface of the malodor blocking tube and a second bolt hole corresponding to the first bolt hole thereof so as to be coupled to the circular flange and a fastening ring inserted into an inner circumferential surface of the manhole cover wherein the odor blocking tube comprises a plurality of supports having the same curvature is further attached to the inner side and the upper side of the upper side discharges rainwater flowing through the manhole cover and the elastic valve is fixed to the support to block the sewage of the main body backflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100885534-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 includes a valve means 24 for guiding discharge through the outlet the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar rainfall reduction facility characterized in that it comprises an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge according to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "more specifically the vacuum pump 140 is operated while only the vacuum valve 123a is opened and the remaining suction valve 121a the siphon valve 122a and the residual water valve 111a are shut off see fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403906-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in such a state when rainwater flows instantaneously when the rainwater is instantaneously introduced the floats 40 are raised to block the inlet 12 of the buoy automatic shutoff valve body 10 due to the disk 20 and the sewage and rainwater are sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 the water level controller 32 includes a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor 29 the second sensor 30 and the third sensor 31 of the water level sensor portion the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 16 may be discharged through the discharge pipe 22 for a predetermined discharge time when the time counted by the timer 33 becomes longer than a predetermined time wherein the control unit controls the discharge valve 21 so that the discharge water 21 is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level controller may further include a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor the second sensor and the third sensor of the water level sensor portion and controls the discharge valve so that the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank can be discharged through the discharge pipe for a preset discharge time when the discharge time exceeds the predetermined set time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974535-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "also as described above the time point at which the initial rainwater drain valve v1 is closed closed can be closed only for a time period in which the water level precipitation amount is maintained on the high water level of the flowmeter chamber 112c when the rainwater is not continuously detected the initial rainwater exclusion valve v1 is closed closed to prevent contamination of the body portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100666662-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "when the drainage is completed in this way the weight of the weight 123 of the lever valve 120 to the original position the valve surface 122 can block the drain groove 141 to prevent the introduction of various wastes fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "manual valve operation method is unrealistic because the manager must operate the valve in the early stage of rainfall and it has the disadvantage of high cost and difficulty of maintenance such as failure when using devices such as flow meters and sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100672275-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "2 the general operation of the rainwater toss is usually performed by sliding the valve valve plate 17 to the lower guide block 27 of the torsion housing 1 by the operation of the drive motor 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_824", "text": "to the exhaust port of the valve to prevent dust etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the safety facility of the rainwater storage tank 150 is stored in a slightly higher than the high water level hwl in order to prevent the water level rises and overflows when the amount of rainwater entering the rainwater storage tank 150 more than the planned quantity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101303849-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "after being purified while passing through the purification treatment means built in the space is discharged to the inner space of the drain pipe through the drain hole of the drain pipe and then descends along the drain pipe is discharged to the outside through the discharge hole of the housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599839-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "for example the valve may automatically release the gas cartridge pressure upon swelling of the support wall in contact with water such as in a life raft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101614687-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a double type screen device installed in a high 0001 the present invention relates to a cube type valve block device installed in a double type screen device installed in an excellent purification apparatus and more particularly to a cube type valve block apparatus provided with a third screen on the inlet side of the main body a first screen is provided on the upper side of the second screen and the foreign matter in the rainwater flowing through the inlet is purified in various stages through the first screen to the third screen the efficiency of the filtration apparatus is increased by removing a certain amount of foreign matter and thus the purified water can be utilized as the river water thereby providing a practical double screen apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6164161-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "furthermore it is possible to prevent rainwater including condensation dust and the like from accumulating inside the welded portion between the water storage tank 10 and the valve chamber 30 52 and causing corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192404-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a control server for controlling water purification by informing replacement time of media based on measurement data wow water supply protection and non point source reduction control system using a green dam characterized in that it comprises a central control unit for receiving and monitoring the discharge amount and the water purification control data from the control server and controls the control server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192404-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the water source protection and non point source reduction control system using the green dam according to the present invention by controlling the discharge valve by remote control from the central control unit to freely regulate the discharge size of the outlet the green dam is secured after the rainfall rainwater can be continuously discharged and in the dry season the size of the outlet can be further narrowed to obtain the effect of preventing the dryness of the river as the water always flows or is absorbed by the aquifer.1 is a side cross sectional view showing the structure of a conventional treatment facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426715-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the second pre application is a cylindrical shape of the hollow inside the housing having a water collecting port on the upper surface a plurality of water collection tanks having an inlet on an upper surface and a drain hole on a lower surface thereof the plurality of water collection tanks being fixed to the inside of the housing as a pipe one end is connected in communication with the sump of the housing the other end is drawn out through the housing and connected in parallel with the inlet and the drain of each of the respective sump in parallel to the initial rainwater into the respective sump a bypass pipe for supplying the effluent and receiving the purified initial rainwater discharged from each water tank and discharging it to the outside while bypassing the initial rainwater water flowing through the water collecting port when the water tank is in full water it is installed on the upper side of the catchment inclined to discharge the initial rainwater discharged from the bridge drain pipe into the catchment and the strainer to filter the confinement purifying processing means for purifying the initial excellent effluent water introduced into the respective collecting tanks by filling the inner space of the respective collecting tanks so as to be exchanged with a predetermined height from the bottom it is composed of a plurality of one way valve is fixed to each inlet of the respective collection tank to open and close the inlet in one direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200163545-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and prevents foreign matters and rainwater from accumulating around the valve tube and facilitates the installation and dismantling of the drinking water and prevents freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200163545-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "by connecting to the welded spiral pipe it prevents foreign matters and rainwater from accumulating around the valve pipe and also makes it easy to install and dismantle the drinking water while preventing the valve pipe from freezing in winter so that it can be used for a long time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200448229-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the pin shaft 66 which is the pivot center point for the rotational moment to close the manhole opening is installed so as to be eccentrically located from the center position to the lower side and the rainwater flows in through the manhole cover 33 so when gathered the drain valve plate 36 which rotates around the pin shaft 66 in the direction in which the rainwater s own weight acts to open the manhole opening 34 to introduce rainwater into the sewer pipe a back drain hole 43 formed at an inclined upper side of the drain valve plate 36 and formed as a passage formed by drilling in an inlet shape so as to discharge to the outside when water in the sewer pipe overflows it is formed so as to cover the reverse drain hole 43 of the drain valve plate 36 from the upper side and is connected rotatably by a hinge 67 at the inclined upper end of the drain valve plate 36 close to the drain valve plate 36 to block the back drain hole 43 and when water in the sewer pipe overflows it is pushed up by water pressure to rotate the hinge 67 to the pivot point to the back drain hole 43"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399489-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the wastewater treatment apparatus using ozone comprising a collecting tank ozone generator ozone oxidation tank pressurized flotation tank pressure filter sludge collector and treated water tank a screen tank installed at all stages of the collection tank and integrally including a filtering means consisting of a flow blocking valve and an activated carbon fiber double screen to block unnecessary rainwater mixing an ozone oxidation tank for forming a vortex through the swirl flow multi contact device to increase the contact between the ozone supplied from the ozone generator and the waste water supplied from the collecting tank an improved ozonation type wastewater treatment apparatus for strengthening the pretreatment process comprising a pressurized floatation tank integrally containing a microbubble type ceramic spraying unit for microbubbling the dissolved air supplied by the eject"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399489-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at the same time the present invention relates to an improved ozone oxidation wastewater treatment system that has enhanced the pretreatment process to improve the facility margin and contaminant removal rate according to the effect of reducing pollutant load in the downstream equipment by performing the pretreatment process to filter foreign substances such as contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an automatic on off valve having a wave protection plate that prevents malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to waves of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the auxiliary valve is installed on the outer periphery of the main valve and consists of a water shielding plate and a projecting floating body that floats it and the outer periphery of the projecting floating body is used to prevent malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to the wave of rain water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_204", "text": "in addition it is economical as it can reduce the construction cost by the short term construction period that can be completed in 1 2 days based on 100 tons storage and it can cope with 25 tons load and level 2 earthquake 6.5 magnitude of earthquake or more it can be suppressed more than 99 has the advantage of low maintenance cost of the storage tank osmosis storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100416293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a blocking wall 40 having a height at which the overflow may occur in the two tanks 12 a lifting part 30 for raising or lowering the blocking wall 40 by a predetermined control signal solid concentration measurement unit 20 for measuring the concentration of the solids contained in the raw water a stirrer 50 installed at the bottom of the first water tank 11 to stir organic matter precipitated by a predetermined control signal a transfer valve 60 installed in the second water tank 12 to transfer the treated water to the reaction tank rainwater discharge valve 70 is installed in the second water tank 12 to discharge the influent and the lifting wall 30 is raised or lowered by operating the lifting unit 30 according to the solids concentration of the raw water measured by the solids concentration measuring unit 20 or a user s key input and the rainwater discharge valve 70 and a control valve 100 which opens or closes the transfer valve 60 and outputs a control signal for stopping or operating the operation of the stirrer 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100416293-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "when the descending the blocking wall 40 having a height that can cause the overflow from the first tank 11 to the second tank 12 to the upper end a lifting part 30 for raising or lowering the blocking wall 40 by a predetermined control signal solid concentration measurement unit 20 for measuring the concentration of the solids contained in the raw water a stirrer 50 installed at the bottom of the first water tank 11 to stir organic matter precipitated by a predetermined control signal a transfer valve 60 installed in the second water tank 12 to transfer the treated water to the reaction tank rainwater discharge valve 70 is installed in the second water tank 12 to discharge the influent and operating the lifting unit 30 according to the solids concentration of the raw water measured by the solids concentration measuring unit 20 or the user s key input to raise or lower the blocking wall 40 and the rainwater discharge valve"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however this type of catchment can cause an unpleasant odor generated from the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to leak out into the atmosphere due to a malfunction of the valve member provided between the catchment and the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus conventionally as a drainage device that is attached to a water collecting tank in a side groove and prevents the release of odors mosquitoes etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "for example if only a small floating member 36 can be provided due to structural limitations of the device and the buoyancy for floating the valve body 20 is insufficient the contraction force is increased in the direction of lifting the floating member 36 to the umbrella member 56"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200333348-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "will be easier.as described above the present invention is provided with a valve inclined toward the discharge side on the sewage pipe to prevent the reverse flow of sewage and at the same time to block the odor the size of the discharge port can be maximized 