art gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599839-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "for example the valve may automatically release the gas cartridge pressure upon swelling of the support wall in contact with water such as in a life raft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449313-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "there is a limit to solve the problem as described above.the present invention is designed to solve the problems caused by the above mentioned pain the purpose of the present invention is first can not effectively regulate the use of water drawn into their farmland by drilling a hole in the barrel arbitrarily but artificially in order to prevent the necessity of drilling by installing a drain valve that can be opened and closed at the bottom of the barrel and the manufacturing process of the barrel it is possible to prevent the barrel from being punctured by inducing water to the surrounding farmland through the drain valve in the farming season"}, {"pat_id": "US-7157011-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "for instance when rain causes film of water to overlay the soil surface closing of the throttle valve will cause visible air bubbles in the surface which are not present when the vent is unthrottled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the auxiliary valve is installed on the outer periphery of the main valve and consists of a water shielding plate and a projecting floating body that floats it and the outer periphery of the projecting floating body is used to prevent malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to the wave of rain water surface"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus conventionally as a drainage device that is attached to a water collecting tank in a side groove and prevents the release of odors mosquitoes etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "US-4997312-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when backup water pressure builds up the back flow preventing valve is closed or closes to prevent the water in the sanitary sewer line from backing up into the user s home"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the entry of rainwater into the water leveling protector 10 thereby providing a special effect of effectively preventing corrosion and rusting of the water stop valve 7 due to rain"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when backup water pressure builds up the back flow preventing valve is closed or closes to prevent the water in the sanitary sewer line from backing up into the user s home"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the river water to be treated which has passed through the pretreatment unit 10 flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 is purified in the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 and then passes through the discharge tank 40 to be discharged into a river or lake thereby performing the functions of water quality purification and management during normal times"}, {"pat_id": "US-12127513-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in another aspect one or more of said water collection modules internal horizontal and vertical edges are made leak proof via the addition of mechanical or chemical components forming a fluid holding internal volume wherein said edge leak proof mechanical component include one of silicone gel amp sealing or silicone model seals wherein each said water collection internal volume is hydraulically connected to at least one more other water collection module s internal volume and at least one or more of said water collection module s top panel or said wall panels openings has a plug cap hose flow restrictor drip hose faucet valve spigot or similar component"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100918431-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition the contaminants accumulated in the rain gutters are provided between the odor reflux preventing device to provide a reason that the part to be closed to prevent the backflow is always open"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 power generation unit 11 solar module 20 support 100 rainboard 110 first settling tank 120 second settling tank 130 valve box 140 contamination separation pipe 141 electric valve 142 valve drive motor 143 backflow prevention trap 144 gas backflow prevention albo 150 suspended solids filter 160 steel grating 200 rainfall sensor 210 rain gauge case 211 rain gauge bottom 212 lever 213 coupling member 220 bucket 221 bucket pillar 222 bucket pillar support 223 lever 224 weight 225 magnet 226 switch 227 lever pin 230 water inlet 240 filter medium 300 terminal box 310 control unit 320 charging unit 330 input unit 340 timer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100647994-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "rainwater storage device of the present invention for achieving the object of the present invention as described above is the cylindrical body is provided with an inlet is formed in the inlet through which the rainwater flows inlet is formed with a discharge valve for discharging the rainwater flowing into the lower portion a filter member provided at the inlet side of the body to prevent a large amount of foreign substances from entering the body a shutoff valve provided inside the body to block the rainwater introduced through the inlet at a predetermined amount an initial excellent separation means in which a discharge port is formed in the cutoff valve upper side body to discharge rainwater blocked by the cutoff valve to the outside of the body the supply pipe for supplying rainwater stored in the space portion to the outside having a sludge discharge pipe is provided in the lower portion having a space portion of a predetermined size to accommodate and store the rain water discharged from the discharge port of the body of the initial excellent separation means and a water level sensor formed on one side of the storage tank and sensing the level of rain water stored in the space to control an inlet valve so that tap water can be introduced through the tap water inlet pipe and above the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method according to claim 4 wherein the valve means the lifting port 25a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rainwater storage tank body the transfer means for transmitting the lifting of the float the lifting force of the float through the transfer means receiving transmission includes an opening and closing plate 25d for opening and closing the second outlet hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 25b to move up and down with the buckle both sides of the lifting bar and the opening and closing plate is fixed road side opening characterized in that between the two sides is rotatably coupled to the baffle through a hinge to open and close the opening and closing the driving plate while rotating under the guide of the hinge according to the lifting of the elevating rod 25c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "according to the above configuration and action according to the present invention the downstream circulation hole connecting the plurality of storage block valves to communicate with each other is provided to be opened and closed by the valve so that the storage space is flexibly adjusted according to the rainfall during rain and thus the unused storage space is always kept clean"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100984372-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "rain gutters 20 including a rain box 40 communicating with the first outlet hole 21b of the rain gutter through a connecting pipe 30 to store rainwater flowing into the rain gutter it includes a rooftop excellent induction pipe 2 for leading the rainwater collected on the roof of the building around the road to the rain gutter the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar in the driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility comprising an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge a sleeve 51 having the same size as the thickness of the bottom of the rain gutter main body and inserted into an insertion hole formed in the bottom of the rain gutter main body a perforated pipe 50 inserted into the sleeve so as to communicate with the inside of the rain gutter and installed by a filling material filled in the bottom of the rain gutter and penetrating the rainwater stored in the rain gutter into the ground a valve installed at an inlet side of the hole tube to adjust an opening degree of the hole tube driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility characterized in that it comprises a filter 52 is attached to the filter mounting portion 21c formed concave at the bottom of the rain gutter to remove the foreign matter from the rainwater flowing into the hole"}]</data>
</edge>
