  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100885534-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 includes a valve means 24 for guiding discharge through the outlet the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar rainfall reduction facility characterized in that it comprises an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge according to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "manual valve operation method is unrealistic because the manager must operate the valve in the early stage of rainfall and it has the disadvantage of high cost and difficulty of maintenance such as failure when using devices such as flow meters and sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101303849-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "after being purified while passing through the purification treatment means built in the space is discharged to the inner space of the drain pipe through the drain hole of the drain pipe and then descends along the drain pipe is discharged to the outside through the discharge hole of the housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192404-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the water source protection and non point source reduction control system using the green dam according to the present invention by controlling the discharge valve by remote control from the central control unit to freely regulate the discharge size of the outlet the green dam is secured after the rainfall rainwater can be continuously discharged and in the dry season the size of the outlet can be further narrowed to obtain the effect of preventing the dryness of the river as the water always flows or is absorbed by the aquifer.1 is a side cross sectional view showing the structure of a conventional treatment facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "meanwhile when it rains rains the rainwater flows into the pretreatment unit as the water to be treated but the first passage is closed the second passage is open the introduced water to be treated passes through the pretreatment unit and flows into the non point pollutant filtration unit through the second passage to remove non point pollutants and the water to be treated from which the non point pollutants have been removed flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit through the third passage to be purified and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262194-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore it is required to be able to more efficiently handle the overload overflow water generated during rainfall in the combined sewer conduit and to facilitate the maintenance and management by the automation of the facility.an object of the present invention for solving the above problems by allowing the stormwater influent generated in the rainwater in the combined sewage conduit to be discharged by the upflow type automatic overflow of the overflow water is mixed with sewage overload of the combined sewage conduit it is to provide a combined sewage contaminant overflow water treatment device that allows for more efficient treatment of overflow water and makes it easier to maintain and manage by using a non return valve or floating valve to enable automation without additional electrical facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the control unit provided in the terminal box can receive the rainfall information measured by the rainfall measurement sensor to control the initial rainfall non point pollution source system characterized in that for controlling the operation of the valve drive motor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in addition the gas backflow prevention albo 144 is bent to the bottom of the second settling tank 120 which is to prevent the harmful gas flow back by the water stored in the second settling tank 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the present invention provides a method for separating and discharging a nonpoint source from initial rainfall a rainfall measurement step s1 in which the rainfall measurement sensor 200 measures rainfall a closing switch operation step s2 of operating a switch to close the pollution separation pipe 140 when the rainfall measured in the rainfall measurement step reaches the pollution separation pipe closing rainfall amount the closing signal generated in the closing switch operation step is transmitted to the control unit 310 and the control unit 310 receives the closing signal to drive the valve driving motor 142 through the electric valve 141 pollution separation pipe 140 s3 to separate the contaminant pipe closing step after the contamination separation pipe opening step is closed the control unit after the pollution separation pipe opening setting time set by the manager through the input unit 330 provided in the terminal box 300 has elapsed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 power generation unit 11 solar module 20 support 100 rainboard 110 first settling tank 120 second settling tank 130 valve box 140 contamination separation pipe 141 electric valve 142 valve drive motor 143 backflow prevention trap 144 gas backflow prevention albo 150 suspended solids filter 160 steel grating 200 rainfall sensor 210 rain gauge case 211 rain gauge bottom 212 lever 213 coupling member 220 bucket 221 bucket pillar 222 bucket pillar support 223 lever 224 weight 225 magnet 226 switch 227 lever pin 230 water inlet 240 filter medium 300 terminal box 310 control unit 320 charging unit 330 input unit 340 timer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187840-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it includes a rainwater management block that allows rainwater to be stored in rainwater storage blocks and a rainwater management block that opens a drain valve to allow rainwater to penetrate into the infiltration facility after a rainfall has passed and discharges stored rainwater depending on the situation to prevent flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "according to the above configuration and action according to the present invention the downstream circulation hole connecting the plurality of storage block valves to communicate with each other is provided to be opened and closed by the valve so that the storage space is flexibly adjusted according to the rainfall during rain and thus the unused storage space is always kept clean"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102748045-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0494565.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above and more specifically it aims to provide a water treatment facility capable of preventing waste of chemicals and cracking down on illegal discharge of wastewater by controlling the opening and closing of a valve according to sensing information of a rain sensor installed in a storage facility and controlling the opening and closing history of the valve to be transmitted to a supervisory agency.in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a car wash water treatment facility and a water treatment method thereof comprising a water treatment unit including a storage unit in which water discharged from a car wash is temporarily stored a rain sensor installed at an arbitrary point of the car wash to detect rainfall information a rain discharge valve opening or closing a rain discharge pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be discharged immediately without being purified and a wastewater inflow valve opening or closing a wastewater treatment pipe passage so that the water stored in the storage unit can be introduced into a wastewater treatment facility to be purified using chemicals a control unit electrically connected to the water treatment unit and controlling the rain discharge valve or the wastewater inflow valve to be opened or closed respectively based on the rainfall information detected by the rain sensor and controlling the opening and closing information of the rain discharge valve and the wastewater inflow valve to be stored in a database so that it cannot be deleted and it is characterized by including a supervisory unit that receives the opened closed information that is stored in an irrevocable manner and compares it with the rainfall data of the korea meteorological administration in the area of the car wash thereby determining whether the rainwater discharge valve is opened only when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}]</data>
