  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100238498-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the weight of the flute 286 must be made to overcome the vacuum pressure temporarily applied to the upper surface 292 so that the flute 286 can be lowered in response to the fall of the sewage level in the sump pit 154"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "one of the circuit boards 33 and 35 is arranged on one side of the support plate 31c of the substrate support 31 and the other of the first and second printed circuit boards 33 and 35 connected to the acoustic sensor 20 are arranged side by side on the other side of the support plate 31c of the substrate support 31 so that the overall size and length are not excessively increased due to the above described compact arrangement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137769-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition a number of filters shorten the filter life due to the continuous hydraulic pressure of the raw water may cause waste of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306389-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "it is discharged out of the system as it is via the drain valve 18 from the lower part of 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100697628-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "therefore even if the magnitude of the hydraulic pressure is greatly increased the force of the hydraulic pressure is dispersed by the sealing member 150 so that the disk plate 120 can resist the large hydraulic pressure so that there is no fear of leakage due to the hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101228687-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore the inaccuracy of the filtration eventually has a disadvantage in that the structure of the non return valve 200 mounted through the opening does not block the correct flow path when the hydraulic pressure flows back when foreign matter is caught in a simple flat state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101228687-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "by installing a bushing as the outlet of the outlet pipe to prevent leakage while maintaining the specification of the outlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100727599-B1", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "in other words when the first buckle 7 is raised by buoyancy during full water to block the second orifice 19a the blocking diaphragm 24 and the blocking rib by the blocking diaphragm 24 constituting the booster 200 the first diaphragm 22 and the first support plate 21 are lowered by the hydraulic pressure concentrated in the second chamber and the third chamber while the flow path between the first and second chambers is blocked thereby immersing in the water more deeply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101083035-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "therefore power consumption of the pressure sensor and the pressure transmitter installed in the water valve can be minimized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101083035-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "by constructing the conditional reaction pressure gauge in this way even when bubbles are contained in the water it is possible to measure accurate water pressure to the extent that it is possible to determine whether there is a leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100273822-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water pipe 14 of the water intake well 12 the water meter 14 for displaying the feed amount of the raw water control valve 15 for adjusting the discharge of raw water a check valve 16 for discharging raw water in the pipe 19 in only one direction a pressure gauge 26 displaying hydraulic pressure in the pipe 19 an air valve 25 for discharging air remaining in the pipe 19 or when raw water is pumped from the pumping means 18 and a reverse circulation line 27 for backflowing the remaining raw water in the pipe 19 to the pumping means 18 to prevent freezing when raw water is not being pumped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an upstream side main water supply pipe 101 connected to a water supply source and provided with a water supply pump 130 a downstream side main water supply pipe 102 connected to the upstream side main 