ters 410 and 420 and the first and second sprinkler pipe flowmeters 410 and 420 are controlled by controlling the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 according to the detection signals of the water discharge pipes 510 and 520 and the discharge pipe flow meter 620 and a control means 700 the control means 700 includes a fire detector 710 installed on the building an input unit 720 for inputting the normal mode and the test mode a main opening closing valve sensor 730 for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve 110 the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and the 3 way valve 610 according to the fire detection signal of the fire detector 710 and the input signal of the input unit 720 the flow rate of the refrigerant is detected on the upstream side in accordance with the sensing signals of the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 the first and second sprinkler pipe flow meters 510 and 520 the drain pipe flow meter 620 it is possible to judge the abnormality of the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main water supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 to determine an abnormality position display command and an alarm command a control unit 740 for outputting a command to display the degree of opening of the main on off valve 110 a valve driver 750 for sending a driving signal to the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 and the three way valve 610 according to a control command of the controller 740 a display unit 760 for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the controller 740 and an alarm unit 770 for outputting an alarm according to an alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "at this time the drive motor 123 fails or a failure occurs between the lifting lowering rod 118 and the nut box 119 when the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally due to the adhesion the digested water supplied through the upstream main water pipe 101 flows into the upstream side valve body 910 through the upstream side bypass pipe 810 the hydraulic pressure applied to the cone 940 is greater than the elastic force of the valve spring 950 so that the valve cone 940 moves away from the valve seat portion 930 to the downstream side and the hydraulic pressure sensitive on and the extinguishing water passes through the upstream side internal space 911 of the upstream valve body 910 and the downstream side internal space 921 of the downstream valve body 920 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and the t side water supply pipe 102 through the water supply pipe 821 water is supplied to the sprinkler head 300 through the pipe 200 and a normal fire suppression is performed see fig"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4087351-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "and according to this hydraulic pressure drive unit 13 as shown in fig.1 and fig.2 by operating the 2nd switching valve 37 the pressure water sent out from the pump 31 is made into the water softening apparatus 16 and the hydraulic cylinder apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4087351-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as a result the hydraulic cylinder device 15 and the spool type switching valve can be applied to the hydraulic drive unit 13 including the water softening device 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200142277-Y1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "thus the present invention does not provide a shutoff valve operated by hydraulic pressure of a tank for storing purified water between the filter 2 and the membrane 3 having a large hydraulic pressure and the two filters 1 and 2 and the membrane by installing at the wastewater outlet 5 flowing under reduced pressure by 3 even if high pressure water flows into the inlet source a the inlet source is blocked only by the water pressure of the storage tank 6 to prevent leakage of the inlet water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4253351-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a cylindrical chlorine removal filter to be removed an outflow pipe connected to the casing from which tap water flows out a head cap mounted on an end of the casing and one end fixed to the head cap and the other end a cylinder inserted into one end side of the hollow portion of the chlorine removal filter a cylinder water passing portion opened in a side surface of the cylinder and a manual or electric drive disposed inside or outside the cylinder a valve body that rotates or moves up and down and the valve body changes a degree of opening and closing of the bypass passage that communicates the cylindrical water passage portion and the hollow portion and the inflow side is closed when the bypass passage is closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "64 a disk valve 66 for opening and closing the water passage 61a of the valve housing 61 is selectively installed while moving up and down and is elastic between the disk valve 66 and the elastic member support frame 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the present invention is a technique for branching and installing the drainage branch pipe on one side of the water supply pipe connecting the drainage control valve to the bottom of the drainage branch pipe connecting the residual water drainage pipe to the bottom of the drainage control valve take a look.according to the present invention when the operation of the submersible motor pump is stopped automatically by the water pipe to prevent the water flow back to the water pipe and at the same time draining the water remaining in the pumping device in the upper ground water protective device to the outside cold water pumping device it provides the effect of preventing the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which is a component of the components in advance and greatly reduces the time and manpower associated with checking or replacing the groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge as well as providing convenience of post management after construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156125-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "while opening the backwash valve 37b of the backwashing pipe 40c the air blower 38 communicating with the lower part of the filtration section 2 is operated to operate the reactor 21 and the coagulation tank perforated block portion 4 or strainer provided at the bottom of the filtration section 2 simultaneously or sequentially with the raw water provided by the hydraulic pressure difference from any one of the 22 and the air supplied through the air blower 38 it feeds into said filtration compartment 2 via section 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101874096-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "at this time the emergency operation valve 400 may be driven in a non power based manner so as to be able to perfectly cope with interruption of the constant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "therefore the first passage 851a is opened and closed by the ball valve 855a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "the drive motor 44a operates the hydraulic pump 42a and the hydraulic pump 42a includes the first and second piston pumps 30a and 31a the drive motor 29a of the introduction device 20a and the first and second hydraulic pumps 42a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_99", "text": "accordingly as the piston 87a of the piston valve 87a is pushed to the left side the through hole 876a of the blocking rod 875a is positioned on the second passage 852a thereby opening the second passage 852a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal 120b is operated by receiving power from the emergency storage battery 20 and information such as whether the valve is opened or closed flow rate hydraulic pressure water level in each reservoir leakage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041191-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "underwater motor pump and pumping device installed inside the upper surface of the ground water protection pump during the freezing of the groundwater water pipe characterized in that it further comprises a hydraulic pressure release device 50 for releasing the water pressure while forcibly opening the ball 41 2 component protector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the automatic decompression management device for each water supply block a number of water supply jurisdiction blocks with an inflow water pressure of 3 to 5 kg cm 2 the water supply unit is installed for each water supply jurisdiction block and reports the field value including the flow rate measurement value and the water pressure measurement value of the corresponding jurisdiction block to the upper side each having a globe type pressure reducing valve monitor and manage by real time communication with each of the water supply block control panels and each jurisdiction block calculated based on the normal altitude value of the customers in the water supply block and the lowest water pressure value to be applied to the lowest water supply among the water users an integrated monitoring control station for downloading the block outflow water pressure target value to the corresponding water supply block control panel and transmitting the block outflow water pressure control value for the change of the block outflow water pressure target value to the waterworks block control panel each of the waterworks block control panel the water supply line for supplying water to the relevant jurisdiction block users is configured to pass through and the water supply line is equipped with first and second hydraulic pressure gauges at front and rear ends and the water supply line between the first and second hydraulic pressure gauges is automatically controllable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow meter for measuring the flow rate of the water supply line with a pressure reducing valve of the type a block outflow water pressure target value from the integrated monitoring and control station is stored in an internal memory and the stored block outflow water pressure target value the inflow water pressure measurement value detected by the first hydraulic pressure gauge and the outflow water pressure measurement value detected by the second hydraulic pressure gauge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the furnace is provided with a flow control for measuring the flow rate of the water supply line with a globe type pressure reducing valve that can be automatically controlled and stores the target block effluent pressure from the integrated monitoring and control station in the internal memory and the stored block effluent pressure the pressure reducing valve is controlled using a target value an inlet pressure measurement value detected by the first hydraulic pressure gauge and an outlet pressure measurement value detected by the second hydraulic pressure gauge but the inlet pressure measurement value is greater than the block outlet pressure target value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in an embodiment of the present invention by installing a water supply block control panel for each jurisdiction block by zone and installing a pressure reducing valve that can automatically control itself according to the jurisdiction block region the flow inflow pressure and hydraulic pressure gauge are also installed to provide a block inflow water pressure of approximately 3 to 3 even if the pressure is 5kg it performs the decompression function as well as performs the optimum decompression control to take a constant outflow water pressure to the jurisdiction block with the flow monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "when the opening degree control of the globe type pressure reducing valve 20 is performed as described above after reaching the target block water pressure target value the frequent operation of the pressure reducing valve 20 is minimized to prevent water shaking and the amount of water used by the customer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "meanwhile the dry fire extinguishing system according to the present invention can be designed to prevent corrosion due to water remaining inside the pipe after a hydraulic pressure test and water leakage due to valve leakage by installing a dry air facility or an air compressor equipped with a heater that supplies dry air and also to install a drain cock at the lowest part of a branch pipe and a cross pipe to discharge and dry water remaining in the pipe by dry air or compressed air thereby blocking corrosion due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "US-4946574-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "after the electrolysis is completed the electrolyzed water from said electrolytic cell 12 is divided into alkaline water 101 and acidic water 102 wherein said acidic water 102 is directly drained out since it cannot be used for drinking while said alkaline water flows into an ultraviolet sterilizing tank 15 to be sterilized therein before flowing out therefrom to be used for drinking purposes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to prevent interruption of the supply of water during an emergency including the occurrence of a leak in a water pipe and the replacement of a water pipe water is installed in the bypass pipe so that water flows along a bypass pipe connected to the water pipe and water is supplied to the water pipe a non powered emergency operating valve driven by an operating water pressure which is a hydraulic pressure difference between a water pressure of a supply side constant and a user side constant of a water supply pipe a valve body installed in the bypass pipe the valve body having an inlet through which a constant water flows and an outlet through which water is discharged a disk rotatably coupled to an upper end portion of the inlet port so as to be rotatable inside the valve body and to open and close the inlet port a disk rotating unit provided on the valve body and disposed above the disk for rotating the disk in accordance with the working water pressure and and a shock absorbing unit provided on the valve body and connected to a lower portion of the disk to prevent the disk from being damaged by reducing the rotation speed of the disk when the disk is rotated to open the inlet emergency operating valves for systems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "at this time the emergency operation valve 400 may be driven in a non power based manner so as to be able to perfectly cope with interruption of the constant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore by controlling the pump 10 and the valve 33 installed on the raw water inlet side of the membrane filtration unit 100 the advanced oxidation tank 210 activated carbon adsorption constituting the residual contamination removal unit 200 installed at the rear end by adjusting the hydraulic pressure in the tank 220 and the disinfection tank 230 it is possible to smoothly perform each water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "meanwhile the dry fire extinguishing system according to the present invention can be designed to prevent corrosion due to water remaining inside the pipe after a hydraulic pressure test and water leakage due to valve leakage by installing a dry air facility or an air compressor equipped with a heater that supplies dry air and also to install a drain cock at the lowest part of a branch pipe and a cross pipe to discharge and dry water remaining in the pipe by dry air or compressed air thereby blocking corrosion due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100899657-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "on the other hand a check valve 170 may be provided at one side of the pressure cylinder 152 to block the back flow of the produced water that has passed through the discharge port 145 of the valve housing 142.the reverse osmosis wastewater treatment backpressure pump according to the present invention configured as described above is configured such that the piston is easily moved in the storage space of the valve housing by the operation of a pressurizing cylinder that receives pneumatic pressure or hydraulic pressure to overcome the water pressure applied to the filter portion thereby providing a pressure capable of easily reversing the production water"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "9 water flow through the channel 131 is blocked and the water in bore 126 can only move through water drive line 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-3871792-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pump system comprising a pump an electric motor in drive connection with said pump a service line a service valve in said service line a pressure switch in electric circuit with said motor and a control valve assembly comprising a valve housing having an input opening for flow connection thereto of said pump a discharge opening for flow connection to said service line and a main flow passageway interconnecting said input opening and said discharge opening a main valve spanning said main passageway means biasing said main valve toward closing position a first auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end with said main passageway on the downstream side of said main valve and terminating in an opening in said housing for hydraulic pressure connection to said pressure switch means coupling said pressure switch to said valve housing at said last opening a pilot valve assembly spanning said first auxiliary passageway and including a valve seat and a valve means normally biasing said pilot valve toward open condition and a second auxiliary passageway said second auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end to said main passageway on the upstream side of said main valve and terminating at said pilot valve in pressure opposing relationship to said biasing means whereby development of hydraulic pressure against said valve in excess of any opposing pressure against said valve will close said valve and block said first auxiliary passageway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "on the other hand when the operation of the submersible motor pump 4 is stopped there is no further groundwater flow in the water supply pipe 10 the water pressure applied to the piston valve 40 is released and the piston valve 40 is the elastic member 60 the groundwater remaining in various well facilities such as the groundwater meter 6 the hydraulic pressure gauge 8 the branching pipe 7 for the ground water by automatically opening the drainage passage 52 while moving upwards as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the water pipe inspection device equipped with a valve 130 between the manhole 110 and the water connection pipe 120 the manhole 110 is formed in a cylindrical shape so that any one is not subjected to concentrated stress due to hydraulic pressure and a b shaped mounting groove 111 is formed around the upper opening 115 and has a disc shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266017-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "to this end the downstream water supply pipe 4 connected to the elevated water tank installed on the roof of the high rise building the horizontal pipe 5 installed in parallel with the downward water supply pipe 4 and the horizontal pipe 5 connected to the meter 6 is provided and the interior pipe 11 having the bent portion 12 the intermediate valve 21 installed in the cross pipe 5 for reducing the water pressure to a predetermined pressure or less and the cross pipe 5 in the water supply piping device of the high rise building consisting of a first noise canceling unit 23 consisting of a pressure gauge 22 installed in the pressure gauge 22 to measure the pressure of the intermediate valve 21 the diameter of the indoor pipe 11 it is the same as the main hole 25 is formed in the central portion the outer space of the main hole 25 is formed at equal intervals of the fasteners 27 formed with a number of auxiliary through holes 26 the main formed in the fastener 27 it is attached to the through hole 25 to gently form the angle of the bent portion 12 of the indoor pipe 11 by the hydraulic pressure the second silencer made of a soft inner tube 28 having a step 30 formed on one side and a packing 29 installed at the front of the fixture 27 to prevent leakage when connected to the meter 6"}]</data>
