  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-9024461-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "according to this conception the present invention provides a tidal energy seawater desalination system characterized in that it comprises a tidal energy power device a seawater evaporation tower and a steam condensation tower in which the seawater evaporation tower is configured with a vacuum pump which connects with a power output shaft of the tidal energy power device such that the tidal energy power device is capable of driving the vacuum pump to work the vacuum pump connecting the seawater evaporation tower via pipelines the output end of the vacuum pump connecting the steam condensation tower via pipelines and the steam condensation tower connecting a fresh water receiver via pipelines"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5360550-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "due to this series of circulation flow rates the small intake port with adjustment valve 16 becomes negative pressure and air is introduced through the intake hose 17"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing wa