the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "sensing switch.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided an air conditioning system comprising an upstream main water supply pipe connected to a water supply source and having a water supply pump a downstream main water supply pipe connected to the upstream main water supply pipe through a main on a sprinkler multistage pipe branched from the downstream main supply pipe and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve first and second main water supply flowmeters respectively installed at the inflow end and the outflow end of the main opening closing valve and a sprinkler head installed at the lower end of the sprinkler multi branch pipe the sprinkler system according to claim 1 further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flowmeters installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the sprinkler opening closing valve respectively and connected to the sprinkler multi wherein the main on off valve includes a valve body connected to the upstream main supply pipe and the downstream main supply pipe a valve cap covering the upper portion of the valve body a lifting screw rod coupled to an upper end of the opening closing plate a nut box screwed to the lifting lowering rod and an opening closing drive means for rotating the nut box wherein the valve cap supports the lifting lowering rod so as to be movable up and down a rotation support portion for rotatably supporting the nut box and a reinforcing connection portion for connecting the elevation guide portion and the rotation support portion wherein the opening and closing drive means is fixed to the support plate integrally formed with the rotation support portion a drive gear fixed to a motor shaft of the drive motor and a driven gear coupled to an upper end of the nut box and engaged with the drive gear a sprinkler opening closing valve a three way valve and an upstream side main water supply pipe and a downstream side main water supply pipe in accordance with detection signals of the first and second main water supply flowmeters first and second sprinkler multi and a control means for judging the presence or absence of abnormality of the multi branch pipe and the drain pipe and outputting an alarm wherein the control means is installed in the building and smoke detectors an input unit for inputting a normal mode and a test mode a main opening closing valve sensor for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve a sparkler opening closing valve and a 3 way valve according to a fire detection signal of the fire detector and an input signal of an input unit and outputs control commands to the first and second main water supply flow meters the first and second it is possible to determine the abnormality of the upstream main supply pipe downstream main supply pipe sprinkler discharge pipe and drain pipe according to the detection signal of the sprinkler flow meter drain pipe flow meter and main opening closing valve detector a controller for outputting a command for displaying the degree of opening of the main opening closing valve according to a detection signal of the detector a valve driving unit for sending a driving signal to the main opening closing valve the sprinkler opening closing valve and the three way valve according to a control command of the control unit a display unit for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the control unit and an alarm unit for outputting an alarm in response to an alarm command of the control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore the ball top valve 35 of the embodiment shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "therefore in the filtration device of the second embodiment including the ball top valve 35 of the above embodiment when the level of rainwater filled in the upper portion of the horizontal blocking plate 31 is low or there is no rainwater the buoyant elevation part 353 descends the lifting valve plate 352 is lowered to block the lower portion of the vertical pipe 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102697803-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the above object is achieved by the present invention and according to one aspect of the present invention a water pipe freeze prevention device is provided comprising a water pipe a water faucet connected to the upper portion of the water pipe an opening closing handle for raising lowering an opening closing rod installed inside the water pipe and an antifreeze device mounted at the lower end of the water pipe for opening and closing the movement of tap water to the water pipe wherein the antifreeze device comprises a housing having a lower end communicated with the water pipe and an upper end communicated with the water pipe an outlet formed in the housing for discharging tap water contained in the water pipe to the outside and it is composed of an opening closing member mounted inside the housing to control tap water being conveyed to the faucet by the elevation of the opening closing rod so that when the tap water being conveyed to the faucet is blocked by the operation of the opening closing member tap water contained in the water pipe flows out to the outside through the outlet and the opening closing member is mounted at the lower end of the opening closing rod to prevent tap water from flowing out to the outside through the outlet when it is elevated the method comprises forming a step in the housing that is connected to the water pipe when the lower surface of the lifting valve is spaced from the step tap water is transferred to the water pipe when the lifting valve is in close contact with the step the tap water is blocked from being transferred to the water pipe a sunken cylindrical pinhole is formed on an outer surface located at the upper portion of the opening closing rod a connecting portion is formed at the lower portion of the opening closing handle into which an upper portion of the opening closing rod in which the cylindrical pinhole is formed is inserted a spring pin is mounted on the connecting portion so that the cylindrical surface of the spring pin is seated in the cylindrical pinhole so that the opening closing rod is moved up and down by the rotation of the opening closing handle the lifting valve is made of a rubber material and a valve body having a plurality of transfer holes through which tap water is transferred is formed the valve body is made of a metal material and is embedded in the valve body and is connected to the lower end of the opening closing rod by a screw thread and an upper ring and a lower ring in the shape of rings are formed on the outer surface of the valve body and a fin ring is additionally formed to protrude outwardly from the edge of the upper surface of the valve body so that the fin ring is in close contact with the inner surface of the housing and a fastening nut is additionally connected to the opening closing rod that is connected to the valve connecting portion by a screw so that the valve connecting portion and the opening closing rod are compressed and connected and the lower end of the water pipe is bent outwardly to form an expanded extension piece and a sealing ring is installed between the expansion piece and the housing and the sealing ring is in the shape of a ring and has a mounting protrusion formed on which the expansion piece is installed and a sealing projection that protrudes outwardly is formed on a portion that comes into contact with the housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102393706-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "there is a difficulty in performing the original function of the flotation jeon due to freezing and if the operation of the flotation jeon is not smooth in this way there is a problem in that the flotation jeon buried underground by excavating a standing pipe must be replaced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the flood diffusion prevention system of a building structure that is installed in a multi story building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to leakage from spreading to the elevating facility space a drainage passage formed on the floor of the common space for each floor in the building structure a drainage trench installed on the upper portion of the drainage passage to shield the drainage passage and a plurality of drainage holes for draining the inflowing water into the drainage passage a drain module connected to and configured to include a pipe for discharging the water to the outside a flood detection sensor installed in the drainage module to detect whether water has flowed in a water supply shutoff valve installed in a water supply line of the building structure to block water supply by a control signal and a flood signal received from the flood detection sensor a control unit for transmitting the control signal to the water supply shut off valve so as to be blocked and it is installed in front of the opening closing door of the elevator installed in the building structure and is raised to a preset height from the floor and includes a blocking module to prevent water from flowing into the elevator when submerged the blocking module is a blocking member installed in front of the opening closing door to open or shield the front lower part of the opening closing door according to the elevation an elevating wire having one end coupled to the upper portion of the blocking member to elevate the blocking member and the flooding prevention system of a building structure characterized in that it is connected to the other end of the elevating wire and configured to include a wire driving unit for elevating and lowering the elevating wire in conjunction with the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "US-7238286-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "during normal operation of the tank water flows over the filter media 90 and falls to the floor 80 where it is conveyed to an underdrain channel 78 via a sloped floor 80"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423212-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a microbial resistant water purification and collection system said system comprising a reverse osmosis filter assembly having a filter inlet in selective fluid communication with a system inlet and a filter outlet said filter inlet and said filter outlet being separated by a filter membrane a water storage container in fluid communication with said filter outlet and adapted to store filtrate at least a portion of said storage container being located at an elevation above said filter membrane such that filling of said storage container creates a head pressure in said storage container relative to said filter membrane to enable a backflow of filtrate therethrough and a mechanical shut off valve interposed said system inlet and said filter inlet said shut off valve being adapted to block fluid communication from said system inlet to said filter inlet activation of said shut off valve occurring by physical contact thereof with said storage container upon reaching a minimum head pressure in said storage container relative to said filter membrane said minimum head pressure being at least 0.5 pounds per square inch"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "it relates to a seismic valve chamber 100 for preventing water accumulation to collect condensation caused by a temperature difference between a chamber a pipe and the underground and water storage due to water loss in a pipe when a facility is replaced"}]</data>
</edge>
