  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102715270-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "accordingly the protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the description of the claims and the scope of equivalents thereof.1 spawning area 2 water supply area 3 egg transfer unit 10 storage tank 20 drinking water pipe 30 drinking water pump 40 washing nozzle 50 washing pipe 60 washing pump 70 chlorine dioxide gas generating unit 80 gas pipe 90 water pipe a0 water supply valve b0 concentration measurement unit c0 water level measurement unit d0 contamination measurement unit d1 projector d2 camera e0 intensive cleaning section e1 guide rail e2 concentrated cleaning nozzle e3 concentrated cleaning pipe e4 concentrated washing pump e5 drive unit 110 1st tank 120 2nd tank 130 3rd tank 210 1st reaction tank 220 second reaction tank 230 third reaction tank 310 1st gas discharge pipe 320 2nd gas discharge pipe 330 3rd gas discharge pipe 400 integrated pipe 710 1st metering pump 720 2nd metering pump 730 3rd quantitative pump 1110 1st auxiliary tank 1120 second auxiliary tank 1130 third auxiliary tank 1200 level sensor 1300 alarm 1400 reservoir tank 1500 aeration device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drainage tank that has a function to prevent the inflow of pests etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3347959-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "0003 in a vacuum valve unit of this type of vacuum type sewer system when a sewage water level abnormality of a sewage tank occurs due to a vacuum valve failure or the like it is necessary to quickly detect this and notify a manager"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which the power generation water movement line 331 is installed in a form that goes over mountains and hills 221 and then an upward discharge line 332 is formed in a shape at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the lower height and horizontal state of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by going over mountains and hills due to the action of gravity a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which the lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inflow amount and an upper and lower raising and lowering device 5810 is connected to adjust the pipe in the upper and lower direction according to the inflow level of river water that changes frequently and a rising discharge pipe 101 a falling discharge pipe 103 a right angled falling pipe 202 a water storage tank 201 a discharge amount control unit 203 a right angled falling pipe 202 and in a method of producing electricity by using the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 equipped with a power generation unit 33 a structure in which a water storage tank 8000 and a water purification promotion storage tank 11111 are constructed by dredging to a depth 20 to 600 times deeper than the surface 9000 of the soil layer constituting a river or stream and then the foundation concrete 800 is poured on the surface 9000 constituting a river or stream and the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 are constructed on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 and the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 is constructed to store river water on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 a structure in which an intermediate storage water inflow line 501 is formed to pump the stored water stored inside the upstream side of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 toward the rear side starting from the internal ground surface 9000 in the upstream direction of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 penetrating the middle part of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 to the rear part a structure in which a lower movement line 1919 is connected to the end of the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 to move the power generation water introduced through the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 downward a structure in which an entrance 1332 used for inspecting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 after constructing the above power generation water transfer line 331 by crossing mountains and hills 221 a structure in which a v shaped rising discharge line 332 is formed at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the horizontal state and the bottom height of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by gravity over mountains and hills a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which a lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161641-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "another object of the present invention is a water level sensor failure detection method of the cold and hot water purifier that can prevent the occurrence of freezing of the cold water tank caused by the failure of the water level sensor of the cold and hot water purifier a failure due to the overheat of the heater or excessive waste of purified water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133174-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in addition to the investigation of the water quality items for the treated water body 10 as described above the volume of the treated water body 10 and the capacity of the untreated water to be treated are determined and the degree of contamination of the water to be treated is determined to determine what is the substance to be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101560279-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage tank for mixing storages of fresh water and fresh water a main body 100 on which a fine flow path 200 is formed the top side of which is flown out and and is formed as a lower settled space relative to the clearance passage 200 so as to be formed on the clearance passage 200 and to deposit only the initial clearance of the clearance moving in the clearance passage 200 an initial fine precipitation tank 300 the upper part of the bleed passage 200 is opened a baffle wall 400 is formed around the baffle 200 so as to prevent escape of the baffle introduced onto the baffle 200 one side of the escape prevention wall 400 is connected to the end of the roof 500 so that the storm that flows along the slope of the roof 500 of the house can be introduced into the clearance passage 200 the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the main flow path 110 lt rti gt the downflow channel is formed along the flow direction of the stormwater a first space 121 and a second space 122 that divides the inner space of the main body 100 into a first space 121 and a second space 122 123 are formed on the partition wall 120 the overflow passage 123 is formed at a predetermined distance from the lower surface of the main body 100 the storm inlet 110 is formed on the storeroom 200 where the first space 121 is located and a fresh water inlet 140 formed in the second space 122 and into which fresh water flows into the second space 122 and a mixed water outlet 150 formed in the second space 122 and mixed with water mixed with fresh water and fresh water stored in the second space 122 to be discharged to the outside of the main body 100 the mixed water outlet 150 is formed below the fresh water inlet 140 when the water level of the mixed water is lower than the position of the fresh water inlet 140 the fresh water inlet 140 is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "thus it is composed of one set including a control panel that moves the sewage in the sewage tank along the sewage discharge path and discharges it through the sewage discharge pipe one set of sewage treatment equipment is installed one or more depending on the installation area the air supply path includes an air supply pipe installed between the air storage tank and the first end of the three way valve and an air inlet pipe installed between the second end of the three way valve and the sewage tank the control panel operates the compressor to supply the air in the air storage tank to the sewage tank through the air supply pipe the first and second ends of the three way valve and the air inlet pipe a regulator set is installed in the air supply pipe the regulator set includes a regulator for discharging air from the air storage tank to a preset pressure it further comprises at least one of a filter for removing moisture and impurities contained in the air from the air storage tank and an oil removal unit for removing oil contained in the air from the air storage tank the sewage auxiliary tank is installed in the sewage inflow path to remove the bubbles inside the sewage auxiliary tank to prevent the operation of the sewage treatment device due to the inflow of bubbles into the sewage tank when the control panel receives a notification of reaching the lowest water level from the water level sensor it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete it is counted after the operation of discharging the sewage from the sewage tank is performed and when a preset time elapses it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete when the discharge of sewage in the sewage tank is completed the knife valve installed on the sewage inflow path is controlled to be in an open state to open the sewage inflow path so that the sewage is moved to the sewage tank through the sewage inflow path and the three way valve of the air inlet and outlet installed on the air supply path is controlled so that the second end of the three way valve on the sewage tank side and the third end of the air discharge pipe are in an open state and the first end of the air storage tank side control to be closed to move the air in the sewage tank along the air discharge path and discharge it through the air discharge pipe after receiving the notification of reaching the highest water level and performing the operation of discharging wastewater when the notification of reaching the lowest water level is not notified from the water level sensor even after a predetermined time has elapsed after receiving the notification of the notification of reaching the highest water level a warning message to a preset terminal sewage treatment device characterized in that for transmitting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the end part is immersed in the water level of undischarged sewage that always remains in the storage state in the sewage tank so that the negative effects such as contamination of indoor air due to odors during the sewage discharge operation can be eliminated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water level indicating device 40 capable of confirming the water level a connector connected to an end of the ultraviolet lamp 32 so that the ultraviolet lamp 32 the quartz tube 32 that transmits the ultraviolet light of the ultraviolet lamp 32 and at the same time may be replaced with water and the ultraviolet lamp can be easily exchanged an ultraviolet sterilizer 30 composed of 52 a hemispherical housing in which a display portion 11 in which a low water quantity appears by operation of the water level indicating device 30 is located and display windows 12a and l2b are installed to easily identify the operation of the ultraviolet lamp 32 on the side of the display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "moreover the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a water level indicating device 40 which is composed of a water level indicating member 44 having a built in level a connector connected to an end of the ultraviolet lamp 32 so that the ultraviolet lamp 32 the quartz tube 32 that transmits the ultraviolet light of the ultraviolet lamp 32 and at the same time may be replaced with water and the ultraviolet lamp can be easily exchanged an ultraviolet sterilizer 30 composed of 52 a hemispherical housing in which a display portion 11 showing a low amount of water is operated by the operation of the water level indicating device 30 and the display windows 12a and l2b are installed to easily identify the operation of the ultraviolet lamp 32 on the side of the display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 2 when the water level of the water tank is a high water level when the ball tower rises to block the pipe while the pressure in the water pipe increases to detect the increase in the amount of current according to the load rise of the well pump when the first well pump this is a device that measures the rated current amount except the starting current and sets the high water level of the water tank based on this and turns off the well pump according to the weight of the current"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0167322-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "therefore the cold air supplied to the upper side moves along the surface of the cold water storage tank 12 and since more cold air is supplied to the interface of the water level b than the normal state the surface of the purified water freezes and the freezing grows gradually over time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102316706-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "existing electrolysis equipment should be provided with a water tank for generating hydrogen by supplying water for electrolysis and recovering water that will not be used for electrolysis and a device for controlling regulating the water level in these water tanks is separately configured however in the present invention by employing a solenoid valve the structure is simplified by opening and closing the solenoid valve only while the electrolysis device is in operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method according to claim 1 or 2 the purified water tank unit 1000 is a water purification tank unit 1100 for storing purified water flowing in from the outside an outflow filter unit 1200 for filtering foreign substances included while discharging the purified water stored in the water purification tank unit 1100 a temporary storage unit 1300 for storing the purified water discharged from the outflow filter unit 1200 a water level sensor unit 1400 installed on one side of the temporary storage unit 1300 to detect the water level of the stored purified water a purified water metering pump 1500 for discharging the purified water stored in the temporary storage unit 1300 in a fixed amount from one side according to a corresponding control signal total hydrocarbon reduction system in the advanced oxidation process of environmental pollution around livestock facilities including"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5192294-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "when checking and maintaining the water level detection device it is possible to reduce the amount of water to be drained and the working time by draining only the water in the sub water tank after blocking the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584084-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a barn bottom forming a through hole for discharging the manure of the livestock while providing a livestock breeding space a storage tank provided at a lower side of the barn bottom to maintain livestock wastewater by washing water and the manure at a predetermined level and to form a bottom with an inclined surface for smooth discharge of the wastewater a washing water control valve provided on an upstream side of the storage tank to control the washing water supplied to the storage tank from the outside and when the water level in the storage tank by the wash water supplied by the opening of the wash water check valve is a first class water level discharge of the wastewater in storage is started and discharged until it reaches the lowest water level and the supply of the wash water through the wash water check valve at the lowest water level is performed"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "the salt monitoring system of claim 13 wherein said sensor is configured for generating a signal at a regular interval and said controller is configured so that upon said received signal depicting one of a slower than average decline of salt level indicating low brine dosage an increased salt or water level and an increased rate of salt usage reflecting high brine dosage a leak to the brine tank or overfilling of the brine tank an alarm signal is generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "yet another feature of the present system is that the programmer is configured so that a measured signal return time distance from the salt level that is inconsistently shorter closer is an indication that the water level in the brine tank is higher than the salt level indicating further that the brine has not fully drawn due to a softener system leak or malfunction and an appropriate alarm is generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-12061108-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "11 the sensor 40 is configured for generating a signal in the form of the sensor beam 42 at a regular interval and the controller 62 is also preferably configured so that upon multiple signals being received by the receiver 44 over a plurality of regenerations that indicate a first phase 84 of regular salt consumption followed by a second phase 86 of increase signal level or water level indicating a leak to the brine tank 12 an alarm signal is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064409-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "100 flow control unit 110 inlet pipe 120 outlet 130 primary storage container 131 water supply port 140 secondary storage container 150 flow control plate 151 coupling groove 160 anti friction plate 200 rotating body 210 rotating plate 220 bucket 230 first rotating shaft 240 first gear 250 second gear 260 second rotation shaft 300 chemical injection device 310 body 320 rotating shaft 330 pressure port 340 chemical hose 410 vertical frame 420 horizontal frame 500 main tank 510 raw water supply pipe 520 purified water discharge pipe 530 bypass pipe 531 bypass valve 540 water level detection unit 550 controller 600 chlorine injector 700 chlorine storage unit 710 chemical tank 720 chemical supply pipe 800 first identification device 810 rotary drive unit 820 vertical rotating rod 830 rotating plate 840 sealing means 900 second identification device 910 guide tube 911 inlet hole 920 floating body 930 lifting rod 940 flag"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as a result the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "for example when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120 even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank and also if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "US-6655402-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the impoundment floor must have a slope of 5 to 20 to prevent debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102780153-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the remote monitoring system of the filter assembly for installation in a water pipe according to the present invention comprises a water storage tank in which water is stored inside a water pipe is provided on one side to discharge the water stored inside to the outside and a filter assembly is provided inside the water pipe to filter out harmful pests and foreign substances from water flowing along the water pipe and a plurality of filter assemblies are provided in a group form a water level sensor provided on one side inside the water storage tank to detect the water level of the water a pressure sensor provided in the water pipe to detect the flow pressure through the water pipe when the water is discharged and a control unit which calculates the degree of blockage of the filter assembly as the pressure difference between the water head pressure detected by the water level sensor and the flow pressure detected by the pressure sensor based on the result detected by the water level sensor and the result detected by the pressure sensor and transmits the calculated data to an integrated control unit which performs remote monitoring from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101660087-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "therefore it is normal that the water level of the mixture s is sequentially sensed by the first level sensor 21 from the third level sensor 23 via the second level sensor 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261839-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention does not return the high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin so as to reduce the impact of the return of high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin and bioreactor it is economical and eco friendly because it can reduce the amount of injected chemicals and the power is reduced by adopting the slant plate settling tank and the sludge concentration can be automatically adjusted by continuously discharging the sludge and changing the hydraulic pressure difference using the hydraulic pressure difference.figure 1a is a block diagram of a conventional wake water treatment apparatus figure 1b is a flow chart of the prior art flocculation flotation 2 is a block diagram of a semi water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 3 is a cutaway showing the flow of sewage treatment in the inclined plate shaped sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 4 is a block diagram of the sludge automatic discharge line of the inclined plate type sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention 5 6 is a perspective view of the water level control of the sludge automatic discharge device of the inclined plate type sedimentation apparatus of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100437342-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a two way transmission and reception wireless data signal using a dedicated frequency between a motor pump of a water supply and a remote intake tank for storing water so that the water level can be controlled while checking the operation state in the intake tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101102443-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present application as a means for solving the above problems as a water treatment method for obtaining purified water suitable for drinking water or industrial water for the target water selected from the treated water selected from river river water ground water wastewater treatment plant after pretreatment of the water to be treated in a sulphate denitrification tank or an ultrasonic electrolysis tank an ozone containing water is made and supplied to a high precision filtration tank to remove residual contaminants while passing through the filter bed of the biofilm separation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879208-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a flow and ph regulating tank which regulates the water level of the incoming raw water and adjusts the ph to 5.0 to 7.0 for the optimum condition of the chemical input the characteristics of the inflow water whose ph is adjusted and the water level is stabilized in the flow rate and ph adjusting tank a flocculating tank for adding the mixed mineral to the flocculant and mixing the flocculant with the flocculant to perform chemical treatment while mixing the flocculant a coagulation tank for increasing the floc size of the flocculant produced in the rapid a sedimentation tank and a mixed mineral weighted flocculant recovery and circulation apparatus for continuously reusably separating recovering and circulating the weighted flocculant from the sludge sediment separated from the sedimentation tank and a circulation apparatus for filtering the chemical water treated or precipitated in the sedimentation tank a filtration tank for finally removing the flocs that have not been removed and a filter in the high speed water treatment apparatus using a coagulant adding to mineral mix containing the treated water tank the mixed mineral weighted flocculant recovery and recycling apparatus includes a centrifugal hydrocyclone hereinafter referred to as quot hydrocyclone quot that receives the sludge precipitated in the lower part of the sedimentation tank 1400 and supplies the sludge to the high pressure pump 1410 a centrifugal separator 1500 using a hydrocyclone and a stirring separator 1600 constituting an agitating collecting tank in series after passing through the centrifugal separator the agitator 1600 includes an inlet pipe 1610 through which some mixed minerals and sludge not separated from the centrifugal separator 1500 are introduced and an inlet pipe 1610 formed to receive the inlet pipe therein an inner hole 1620 an agitator 1630 rotatably installed at the center of the inner hole block an outer hopper 1640 surrounding the inner hole block and having a square shape a sludge discharge pipe 1650 installed to discharge the sludge and a mixed mineral discharge pipe 1660 connected to a lower portion of the outer hopper to discharge mixed minerals wherein the mixed mineral is used as a weighted flocculant high speed water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484030-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent soil purification apparatus for purifying sewage discharged to a superior soil through a secondary collector a pretreatment needle settling vessel 110 having an inflow hole 111 formed at a lower side thereof so as to allow contaminated sewage to flow therein so as to gradually increase the water level from the bottom surface and to precipitate and remove contaminant particles and contaminants having a large specific gravity and a communication hole 121 for receiving the sewage introduced into the pre processing settling tank 110 and disposed above the settling tank 110 so that the water level of the sewage gradually increases and the purified water a space forming part 100 including a purifying space part 120 formed with an outflow hole 122 through which the exhaust gas flows a buoy 210 floating on the sewage flowing into the purifying space 120 and a filter material 220 compressed as the buoy 210 rises by the sewage flowing continuously a purifier 200 comprising compression means 230 for causing the filter media 220 to compress each other as the buoy 210 rises lt rti the compression means 230 includes a circulation induction plate 231 fixed at a predetermined height of the purification space 120 on the lower side of the buoy and having a plurality of flow holes 231a penetrated therethrough a moving plate 232 having a plurality of flow holes 231a formed therein so as to be able to move upward and downward in the lower space 220 of the purifying space 120 and having one end fixed to the buoy 210 and the circulation induction plate 231 and the other end is connected to the moving plate 232"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101161021-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the water discharged to the outside of the intake tank is mixed with the drug there was a problem that the drug was wasted.an object of the present invention is to solve the above problems