ction of controlling the opening and closing operation of the electromagnetic valve 80 according to the state of rainwater and the storage water level by receiving information or signals from the turbidity sensor 90 and the water level sensor 100 and the low water level sensor 110 it is equipped with a function that transmits a warning signal to the user s smartphone while receiving a signal from and emitting a warning sound and a temperature sensor 40 a turbidity sensor 90 a full water level sensor 100 and a low water level sensor 110 provides periodic electrical stimulation or electronic signal to check whether it is operating normally compares and calculates whether the output signal value is within the normal voltage range and sends a warning signal to the user s smartphone when an abnormality occurs"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore a septic tank abnormality alarm device is indispensable"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3976072-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "abnormalities in the septic tank include for example aeration stop due to blower failure aeration failure due to clogging of the diffuser blower overload aeration failure due to air pipe breakage sewage underground penetration due to water leakage discharge piping and discharge destination abnormalities such as water level rise and water level rise due to abnormal discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715990-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water tank 10 for storing ground water or valley water it is formed in a two shape the end of the engaging projection 21 is formed so as to protrude downwardly mounted on the upper portion of the tank 10 a water level sensing unit 30 installed at an upper side of the cradle 20 to detect a water level it is installed on one side of the water level detection unit 30 installed in the cradle 20 to control the on off of the power according to the water level detected by the water level detection unit 30 and at the same time to control the operation time according to the off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "accordingly the feed water is supplied to the filtration membrane portion 3 and the feed water is first filtered through the reverse osmosis membrane not shown to remove the corrosion promoting component"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "in this case the water level in the production water tank 5 reaches the water level l even after the operation time set to sufficiently remove the corrosion promoting component in the feed water as described above to prevent the deterioration of the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100652934-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a secondary filtration device 4 for reacting acidic nitrogen a flow rate adjustment tank 6 for aeration of the outflow water introduced from the secondary filtration device 4 activated carbon filtration device 8 filled with activated carbon to remove odor adsorb organic matter decompose biological matters and remove suspended matters on the effluent flowing from the flow rate adjustment tank 6 and a storage tank 10 for storing the effluent flowing from the activated carbon filtration device 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100652934-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a secondary filtration device 4 for reacting acidic nitrogen a flow rate adjustment tank 6 for aeration of the outflow water introduced from the secondary filtration device 4 activated carbon filtration device 8 filled with activated carbon to remove odor adsorb organic matter decompose biological matters and remove suspended matters on the effluent flowing from the flow rate adjustment tank 6 it characterized in that it comprises a storage tank 10 for storing the outflow water introduced from the activated carbon filtration device 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330869-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore since the electrode 2 and the main body 1 are separated separately installation is inconvenient which may cause malfunctions due to immersion such as moisture.the present invention is to solve the conventional drawbacks as described above the main body and the electrode for the sensor composed of the same body and waterproof construction to solve the conventional drawbacks and to prevent malfunction due to leakage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "water tank a sterilizing lamp having an arc tube a discharge electrode provided at both ends of the arc tube and a quartz tube for protecting the arc tube the sterilizing lamp being installed inside the water tank a level sensor provided in the sterilizing lamp a controller electrically connected to the level sensor and an inflow valve for opening and closing an inflow pipe for introducing purified water into the water storage tank the water level sensor senses that the water is introduced into the sterilizing lamp by the breakage of the sterilizing lamp inside the water storage tank the water level sensor comprises at least a part of which is disposed between the arc tube and the quartz tube so as to be disposed at a position lower than the lower end of the discharge electrode wherein the at least one of the first electrode and the second electrode contacts the at least one of the discharge electrode and the water flowing into the sterilizing lamp by the breakage of the sterilizing lamp when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp the controller activates the inlet valve to close the inlet tube sterilization water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the sterilizing water purifier of the present invention comprises a water tank a u type sterilizing lamp mounted inside the water storage tank a level sensor provided in the sterilizing lamp and a controller electrically connected to the water level sensor wherein the water level sensor senses that water is introduced into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the ster