sting the water level of a water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472622-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "in addition the method and the apparatus for adjusting the water level of the water storage tank according to the present invention accumulate the data on the operating time of the pump in the state connected with the water level sensing means and operates the pump during the operating time of the pump calculated from the information including the data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100466336-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thereby increasing the amount of distilled water condensed water filled in the evaporator brine heater 1 thereby raising the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the initial rainwater collecting weir is the same as the initial upper water level of the upper weir the initial rainwater is filled in the initial rainwater storage tank while the initial rainwater is transferred to the initial rainwater storage tank through the contaminant blocking pipe rainwater filtration and collection device excluding the initial excellent after the rain reaches the upper end of the water level to perform the function of overflowing the rainwater to the top"}, {"pat_id": "US-6582563-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "it is to be realized that the inlet valve 52 the float switches 76 82 and the overflow line 68 each act to prevent water spillage from the system 10 by preventing overfilling of the control tank 22 the boiling tank 24 and the water tank 14"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "primary microbial baths 120 220 320 the primary to tertiary oxidizing aeration tanks 130 230 and 330 that separate ozone into treated water and suspended solids containing oxidizing organic matter by injecting ozone into the seawater wastewater supplied from each of the primary to tertiary microorganism tanks 120 220 and 320 and the primary to tertiary oxidation aeration tanks 130 230 and 330 are adjusted to control the water level thereby allowing floating substances including oxidized organic substances to be discharged upward and the treated water is primary to tertiary microorganism tanks 120 through the circulation pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "primary oxidation aeration process processing unit 100 secondary oxidation aeration process processing unit equipped with a secondary filter tank 210 for secondary removal of foreign substances in seawater wastewater supplied from the primary oxidation aeration process processing unit 100 200 a tertiary oxidation aeration process processing unit 300 and a tertiary oxidation aeration equipped with a tertiary filter tank 310 for tertiary removal of foreign substances in seawater wastewater supplied from the secondary oxidation aeration processing unit 200 the discharge treatment unit 400 provided with a fourth filter tank 410 for filtering the sludge remaining in the seawater wastewater supplied from the process processing unit 300 the primary to tertiary oxidation aeration process processing units 100 200 and 300 remove contaminants by passing seawater wastewater supplied from each of the primary to tertiary filter tanks 110 210 and 310 through a filter medium containing coral sand"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the primary water level adjusting tank 140 may be provided with a water level adjusting unit c which will be described later which will be described later in detail"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102120910-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a water level adjusting unit c which will be described later may be installed in the tertiary water level adjusting tank 340 which will be described later in detail"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water supplying apparatus which uses a pressure air tank with function preventing air leak the present invention does not use a separate power supply it uses only the air pressure compressed and stored in the pressurized air tank to supply the water in the pressurized water tank quickly and to each household as well as when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level the present invention relates to a technology that automatically closes the flow path of the water cylinder to prevent air pressure from leaking to the outside thereby improving water supply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition the present invention is provided with a pressure automatic replenishment device to replenish the pressure but it is only possible to replenish a small amount of pressure for a limited time only when the water supply is provided through the pumping pipe to completely fill the leaked pressure completely it is not possible to do this but even if it is assumed that the normal positive pumping is very effective.the present invention is to actively solve all the problems in the groundwater supply apparatus of the above described prior invention and when the disk interlocking up and down with the mouth according to the change in water level reaches the minimum water level automatically the flow path of the water cylinder by closing the air pressure to prevent leakage to the outside and when the water supply to the water cylinder is started by the water supply pressure acting on the upper side of the disk forcibly moved upwards to open the flow path to smoothly supply water to the pressurized water tank it is to be an object of the invention.the present invention is to provide an air pressure leakage blocking device on the lower side of the pressurized water tank as a means for solving the above problems the air pressure leakage blocking device is connected to the water supply pipe to one side of the water chamber the other side of the water chamber a shaft guide holder is installed at the center of the flow path of the water supply cylinder formed on the upper part and a disk shaft is installed at the upper and lower sides of the shaft guide holder respectively and a disk is provided at the cover bracket radially installed on the outer circumferential surface of the water cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "as it is buried underground it prevents freezing in winter by improving heat retention and effectively suppresses bacterial propagation while completely blocking contact between the inside of the pressurized water tank and the outside air thereby increasing the utility of drinking water.1 is a longitudinal sectional view of an embodiment of a water supply device to which the present invention is applied figure 2 is a longitudinal sectional view showing the internal structure of the air pressure leakage preventing device of the present invention 3 is a cross sectional view taken along the line aa of the present invention figure 2 figure 4 is a partially cut away perspective view of the present invention air pressure leakage preventing device figure 5 is an enlarged cross sectional view of the disk of the present invention to block the flow path at the minimum water level 6 is an enlarged cross sectional view of a disk of the present invention in a state in which a flow path is opened figure 7 is another embodiment longitudinal section of the present invention water supply device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "and the air pressure present in the air layer of the pressurized water tank 100 in any case by automatically blocking the flow path 321 of the water cylinder 320 when the disk 360 interlocking with the air pressure filled in the air tank 200 provides a special effect of blocking leakage to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7487812-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "2 water treatment units other than the reverse osmosis membrane device 33 are omitted but other water treatment units may be present between the reverse osmosis membrane device 33 and the pressure gauge 61"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6779430-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an internal or water level adjusting mechanism which is installed outside the tank the water level control mechanism the degradation accumulated amount of the treated water in the storage tank is allowed to overflow exceeds a predetermined level constant the water level of the decomposition storage tank while maintaining the level the water level in the food waste disposer is the same as the water level in the decomposition storage tank in conjunction with this water level and exceeds the perforated plate and is one of the stirring mechanisms in the stirring chamber"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6779430-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it is necessary to arbitrarily change how much the stirring tank is submerged and how much the water surface of the storage tank is immersed in the stirring part while checking the type and amount of food waste and the viscosity of the water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6779430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an internal or water level adjusting mechanism which is installed outside the tank the water level control mechanism the degradation accumulated amount of the treated water in the storage tank is allowed to overflow exceeds a predetermined level constant the water level of the decomposition storage tank while maintaining the level the water level in the food waste disposer is the same as the water level in the decomposition storage tank in conjunction with this water level and exceeds the perforated plate and is one of the stirring mechanisms in the stirring chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-970007651-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "filtration tank 20 for primary filtering the wash water drained from the air purifier 1 and the lower portion of the filtration tank 20 the upper part of the filtration filter 21 of the filtration tank 20 and the storage tank 30 communicates with the connecting pipe 15 and is divided into left and right sides by a filter 31 installed at an oblique plate and the external water supply pipe 13 is connected to receive secondary filtration and external water supply and the water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 6 it is installed at the lower side of the check valve and the third non power flow control device which operates in the shielding direction by the water pressure when the water level rises in the filtration tank and operates so as to be open while being homed by the weakening water pressure after the end of the rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "that is the structure of the second third non powered flow control device 14 15 for example the center of gravity of the water level sensing plate 54 and the gate 51 is maintained in parallel with the hinge to be in an open state the water level rises if the water pressure is taken according to the gate the water level is lowered if the water pressure is weakened the center of gravity can be made in a structure that is open while returning to a parallel state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "at this time the third non power flow control device 15 also operates in the shielding direction due to the water pressure applied as the water level rises in the filtration tank 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as shown in the figure the sewage is upflowed as the water level rises while the medial 10 is floated and the wastewater 16 is disposed on the top of the sewage treatment tank 2 after proper treatment is performed through the media 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2556401-Y2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pump for pumping a water receiving tank 1 and a makeup water tank 2connected with a pumping line 4 into which a pump 3 is inserted and connected to a hot water boiler 5hot water storage tank 6 is connected with hot water storage line 9 and water supply line 8.and an upstream position of the water supply pump 7 in the water supply line 8and the makeup water tank 2 are connected by a makeup water line 10 the hot water storage tank 6 and the load 11 are connected to a hot water supply line 13 andconnected by return line 14 the hot water storage tank 6 and the replenishmenthot water supply piping system connected to the water tank 2 via a relief line 15in the formation the membrane type deaerator 20 is inserted into the pumping line 4.and the water in the makeup water tank 2 isa water level detection sensor 16 for detecting the water level the output signal from the sensor 16 is determined and the pump 3 andand a control device 1 for controlling the operation of the membrane type deaerator 207"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a device capable of generating sodium hypochlorite saturated salt water tank receiving soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine the water level is controlled by a water gauge and a water supply valve a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank sodium hypochlorite generator having an automatic valve and a flow sensor characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "another object of the present invention is to maintain a constant water level using a float valve and to supply a constant concentration of brine to the electrolysis tank so that sodium hypochlorite is equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor to produce a constant concentration of sodium hypochlorite it is to provide a generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "sodium hypochlorite generating device equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor according to the present invention to achieve the above object by supplying soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine but by the water gauge and water supply valve a saturated brine tank in which the water level is controlled a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank it characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as such by maintaining the water level at all times using the float valve 131 the suction pressure of saturated brine can be kept constant and a constant concentration of salt water can be supplied to the electrolysis tank to produce sodium hypochlorite of a constant concentration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in an embodiment the groundwater softening system further includes a first water level sensor installed inside the first tank and a second water level sensor installed inside the second tank wherein the control device includes groundwater stored in a tank having a higher water level among the first tank and the second tank may be selectively discharged through the drain pipe based on the measured values of the first water level sensor and the second water level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in one embodiment the groundwater softening system may include a water supply pipe connected from the water pump to the first tank and the second tank a first water supply valve disposed on the inlet side of the first tank among the water supply pipes and a second water supply valve disposed on the inlet side of the second tank in the water supply pipe wherein the control device controls the first water supply valve when the measured value of the first water level sensor is higher than or equal to a preset reference water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in an embodiment the groundwater softening system further includes a first water level sensor installed inside the first tank and a second water level sensor installed inside the second tank wherein the control device includes groundwater stored in a tank having a higher water level among the first tank and the second tank may be selectively discharged through the drain pipe based on the measured values of the first water level sensor and the second water level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in one embodiment the groundwater softening system may include a water supply pipe connected from the water pump to the first tank and the second tank a first water supply valve disposed on the inlet side of the first tank among the water supply pipes and a second water supply valve disposed on the inlet side of the second tank in the water supply pipe wherein the control device controls the first water supply valve when the measured value of the first water level sensor is higher than or equal to a preset reference water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "in this case the time required for the softening of the water stored in the second tank 20 may be set to be similar to the time for which the water of the reference water level stored in the first tank 10 is supplied to the field"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200167943-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "according to one feature of the automatic water supply device of the present invention both the discharge valve and the water level valve installed in the water tank are made of plastic and rubber packing to prevent rust or corrosion and to have durability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_533", "text": "the above mentioned firefighter nozzle 10 is connected to multiple pipe nozzles 10 at a distance of 1 meter or 3 meters using a flexible hose 190 for forest fire prevention or indoors or outdoors of a building and a flexible high pressure hose 190 used in the event of an internal fire is formed by a hydraulic press with wire and rubber and a cloth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or p