fficulty the polluted water is transported to the land storage tank 140 and the contaminated water stored in the land storage tank 140 is transported to the contaminated water storage tank 130"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the control unit 180 drives the pressurization pressurizing pump 170 when the water purifying treatment facility 120 alone can not lower the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 because the difference between heavy rain heavy rain or tide water is large and the contaminated water stored in the storage tank 130 is transported to the land storage tank 140"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in order to prevent the polluted water from leaching to the sea side the water level of the collecting tank is formed lower than the water level of the ocean so as not to leach out to sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "in another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method of operating a hybrid pipeline transportation system for a marine waste treatment plant the method comprising the steps of a a marine purification treatment facility installed in a marine waste treatment plant b measuring the water level inside the shielding facility of the shore waste treatment plant and the external water level of the sea level c checking whether the internal water level is greater than a preset reference value d collecting the contaminated water in the shielded facility so that the internal water level of the shielded facility is lowered and storing the polluted water in the polluted water storage tank when the internal water level is higher than a preset reference value e determining the amount of polluted water transported by the control unit to be transported to the land storage tank f driving the pressure feed pump for transporting the contaminated water through the first pipeline and g storing the contaminated water 