 third side three way valve on the downstream side for supplying the washing water to the second metal filter in a direction opposite to the flow direction of the electrolytic waste liquid a first washing discharging line connected between a first metal filter of the first filtering line and a second tri directional valve at an upstream side through a fourth three way valve to discharge washing wastewater that has passed through the first metal filter a second cleaning discharge line connected between a second three way valve on the upstream side of the second metal filter of the second filtering line by a fifth three way valve to discharge washing wastewater that has passed through the second metal filter a washing wastewater storage tank for storing washing wastewater discharged to the first and second cleaning discharge lines and and a waste water evaporation processing unit for evaporating the washing waste water from the washing waste water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a method for producing electrolytic decontamination comprising a reaction tank for mixing a electrolytic decontamination electrolytic waste solution with a precipitation accelerator to produce a precipitate a filter unit connected to the reaction tank through a regeneration circulation line a regeneration return line and a regeneration circulation pump so as to be circulatable for separating the precipitate from the electrolysis waste liquid a regeneration liquid storage tank connected to the regeneration return line and the regeneration discharge line and storing the regeneration electrolyte in which the precipitate is removed and a first three way valve installed at a position where the regeneration return line and the regeneration discharge line are connected to flow the electrolytic waste liquid toward the reaction tank or the regeneration liquid storage tank wherein the elec