ion tank outlet pipe 310 which is transferred from the sedimentation tank 300 to the separation device is provided with a line mixer for crushing floc of the sediment the second separator 500 may include a second separator main body 510 having a bottom portion having an upper and lower narrow structure two or more inclined plates 521 and an inclined plate 521 disposed to be inclined at a predetermined angle and alternate with each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101994785-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in the wastewater treatment apparatus using the magnetic flocculant of the present invention for solving the above problems the reaction tank 100 to generate agglomerated mixed water by injecting and stirring a flocculant containing a magnetic material to the incoming wastewater a magnetic body storage tank 200 for supplying a magnetic body to the reactor 100 a settling tank 300 which receives the coagulated mixed water discharged from the reaction tank 100 and performs solid liquid separation into a supernatant and a precipitate a first separation device 400 or a second separation device 500 which receives the precipitate from the precipitation tank 300 and separates the magnetic material contained in the precipitate and a concentration tank 700 for reducing the water of the sediment from which the magnetic substance is separated wherein the sedimentation tank outlet pipe 310 transferred from the sedimentation tank 300 to the separation device is provided with a line mixer for crushing flocs of the sediment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101779726-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "this patent document discloses a high efficiency batch wastewater treatment facility and a method thereof in which after precipitation process of a batch reaction tank is combined with an inverse filter module for discharging only the filtrate filtered out in treated water while separating fine contaminant particles"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4444366-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "a work hole communicating in