r level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101278230-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "there is no expectation of floc precipitation produced by binding and adsorption reactions due to flocculation and flocculation sedimentation agents and there is a high speed flocculation tank 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "an influent distribution step of reducing the energy of river water lake water or effluent flowing into the water purification apparatus through a flow distribution tank and evenly distributing it to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step of biologically purifying the inflow water having passed through the precipitation step into the contact oxidation tank having the microbial contact material installed therein river water that combines modular wetland infrastructure and modular catalytic oxidation and filtration facilities including a 4th purification step that finally removes fine sludge and suspended solids that were not filtered through the contact oxidation tank through a filter tank equipped with filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "an inflow water distribution step of evenly distributing the energy of the stream water the lake water or the outflow water flowing into the integrated water purification device through the flow distribution tank to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland