ugh the concentrated sludge inlet pipe 12 to be hydrolyzed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100883979-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the solubilization liquid discharged through the solubilization liquid discharge pipe 16 may be disposed of through a separate process or recycled for other purposes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315874-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "1b is a modification of the a 2 o method to increase the removal efficiency of phosphorus and nitrogen wastewater through the first settling tank 100 anaerobic reactor 200 the first anoxic reactor 300 the first aerobic oxidation tank 400 the second anoxic reactor 500 the second aerobic reactor 600 and the second precipitation tank 700 etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5738390-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "in addition when applying to the activated sludge treatment method of the mbr method membrane separation method it is desirable to take appropriate measures so that the membrane breakage phenomenon due to the addition of powdered activated carbon does not occur in a short time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102778291-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "the above reverse osmosis membrane filtration unit is provided to maintain the temperature during the second reverse osmosis membrane filtration process by the second reverse osmosis membrane filtration module by using the recovered sensible heat at a temperature that reduces or prevents the occurrence of cooling precipitation that may occur depending on the salt type of the high concentration wastewater concentrated through the second reverse osmosis membrane filtration process a high salt wastewater zero discharge treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102230365-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "after chemical treatment in the reaction tank 120 colloidal fine clay which is difficult to remove due to precipitation is removed by passing through the filter tank 140 and reused as process water washing water thereby lowering the process load due to colloidal fine clay"}, {"pat_id": "KR-10116902