nd returning a part of the sludge to the first anoxic tank nitrogen removal method of the anaerobic digestion and desorption liquid comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100512251-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "a contact agent having carrier particles attached to the surface is mainly used to induce automatic dropping of the aging deposited microbial group and to increase the swelling and culture efficiency of aerobic microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and converting the heavy metal into a corrosion precursor which is insoluble in water by a biological corrosion reaction and sends it to the primary precipitation tank 5a to precipitate and remove the solid material and then to the primary treatment tank 13 and then to the primary precipitation tank 5a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "activated humic substances and active minerals in the form of mineral complexes of chelate peroxyfulvic acid which have a catalytic function that promotes the corrosive reactions that convert into macromolecular substances oxidation reduction potential orp value is supplied to the culture tanks 8a b and the sump tank 1 by supplying a large amount of rhyolite or dacite like pumice and oxidation water of the oxidizing tank 15 corrosion of organic contaminants and heavy metals in wastewater by supplying aeration tanks 3a b with microorganisms cultured at 350mv to promote the activation of corrosive microorganisms and microorganisms that have mutual symbiosis with these microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "in the primary aeration tank 3a when organic pollutants and heavy metals in the waste water are converted into corrosion precursors that are insoluble in water by biological corrosion reactions they are sent to the primary precipitation tank 5a to remove the corrosion precursors and microorganisms that exist in the solid state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533649-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a ph adjustment step s100 in which sulfuric acid is added to the wastewater to adjust the acidity of the wastewater to ph 2 to 3 so that a stable micro electrolysis reaction can occur in the subsequent process an electrolytic reaction tank 20 filled with a microelectrolyte m which is a porous sintered product sintered at a high temperature of 1300 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533649-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "therefore according to the present invention while the conventional electrochemical wastewater treatment and the treatment of wastewater by fenton oxidation have all the advantages the disadvantages of the prior art are solved and the supply of external power bivalent iron and hydrogen peroxide is not necessary on the other hand it maximizes the production of oh radicals which is a strong oxidizing agent and greatly improves wastewater treatment efficiency such as removing contaminants through various routes as well as removing nitrogen components by the reaction of reducing metals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101153772-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular the technology for removing inorganic salts or ions for pure water production is a general technique and since the standardization is not a problem in utilizing the technology it is essential to remove components that cause membrane fouling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100969734-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition the filtrate storage tank 800 for temporarily storing the dewatered filtrate separated from the dehydrator 400 the oxidation treatment tank 900 for processing by adding a strong oxidant to the filtrate supplied from the filtrate storage tank 800 and the oxidation treatment tank precipitation separation tank 1000 for segregating and separating the treatment liquid flowing out of the 900 and ph adjustment tank 1100 for automatically adjusting the ph of the treated water flowing out of the precipitation separation tank 1000 may be configured to include will do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0139147-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "therefore the present invention has been devised to improve the problem of the flocculation apparatus of the sedimentation tank according to the prior art so that the agglomerates attached to the wall surface of the sedimentation tank can be easily removed by means of a separate wall aggregate removal means on the central axis of the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100661074-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in addition figure 4 is a conceptual diagram showing the use of the carrier in the sewage treatment facility to control the flow rate of the incoming error in the flow control tank remove the organic matter nitrogen and phosphorus in the contact oxidation aeration tank precipitate the solid material in the precipitation tank in the defoaming tank the foam generated in the previous process is removed and the water is filtered and discharged through the disinfection process in the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0183334-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "eutrophication refers to the phenomenon of overgrowth of plants or algae which causes odor problems due to algae decay and low dissolved oxygen concentration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674018-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition the multi stage complex process was combined into one treatment tank to reduce installation and operation costs and to be installed in a narrow space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "another aspect of the present invention is to remove the ss by the organic coagulant only in the first dehydrator and the inorganic coagulant in the chemical coagulation sedimentation filtration device having a second removal of the desorption solution with the flocculation reaction tank and the precipitation unit and the filter unit after flocculation using organic coagulant the sedimentary solids are removed from the sediment and the suspended solids are removed from the filter reducing the amount of inorganic coagulant and reducing the size of subsequent process equipment and civil structures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "naturally it belongs to the scope of the invention.100 multi purpose thermostat 120 liquid corrosion tank 121 aerobic generation 125 diffuser 127 air inlet 128 air outlet 130 cooling tank 131 intake port 132 exhaust port 141 air supply fan 142 exhaust fan 150 wastewater injection unit 153 conical dispersion induction member 154 wastewater outlet 156 wastewater supply pipe 157 liquid circulation pump 170 shatterproof device 171 inlet 172 outlet 174 scattering prevention device body 176 178 plate 179 slope 182 flushing pump 184 flushing piping 185 chemical pump 187 chemical piping 300 chemical flocculation precipitation filter 320 flocculation reactor 340 sedimentation unit 342 sludge collector 343 treated water outlet 345 pressure sensor 347 rectifying plate 349 sludge discharge pump 350 filter unit 352 filter unit frame 352a round border 352b spokes 354 filtration cell 357 rotary drive shaft 361 wash water nozzle 362 wash water pump 363 wash water receiver 365 wash water discharge pipe 367 electric valve 371 control panel 373 sump tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-7494588-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "accordingly the primary means of the operational management for a purification tank is in the inflow aeration precipitation and effluence steps to control the appropriate aeration intensity and aeration time without upsetting the timing based on the fluctuating raw water conditions and activated sludge amount and thereby control the oxidation of bod and cod the oxidation nitrification of ammonia and the reduction denitrification of the resulting nitric acid and nitrous acid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442932-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention has a high concentration of organic wastewater such as livestock wastewater manure landfill leachate food processing plant discharge wastewater aquatic product plant wastewater slaughterhou