d polysilicate iron porcelain waste powder and abalone shell 5 to 8 by weight of a precipitate increasing agent obtained by mixing one or more shell powders selected from powder pearl shell powder seashell powder clathrate shell powder carrot shell powder and oyster shell powder and sodium silicate dolomite powder and acetic acid mixed flux enhancers 9 to 16 jidoe comprises a percent by weight wherein the precipitation enhancer is one or more shell powder selected from a ceramic waste powder an abalone shell powder a pearl shell powder a shell crust powder a carrot crust powder and an oyster shell powder at a ratio of 1 0.5 0.8 wherein the flux enhancer is mixed with sodium silicate dolomite powder and acetic acid at a ratio of 1 0.2 0.5 0.05 0.1"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5518246-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "the water storage sterilization container l7 is a treatment tank for temporarily storing the purified circulating water while storing and sterilizing the water with ultraviolet rays"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a dispersing hopper 110 to which wastewater is transported and a dispersing hopper 110 a quantitative supply unit 100 including a disk roller 120 spaced apart from the upper portion to supply a fixed amount of wastewater to a predetermined height the screen drum 210 through which a plurality of drain holes 212 are formed to dehydrate the moisture contained in the wastewater supplied through the quantitative supply unit 100 and the coarse contaminants subjected to dehydration treatment by rotational movement within the screen drum 210 a screen dehydrator 200 including a first transfer screw 220 for transferring the a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method a disk drum 410 in which a fixed disk ring 412 and a rotating disk ring 414 are alternately arranged to rec