dy vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101425965-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a filtration step 100 of charging the filtration tank 10 to remove contaminants from sewage treatment water an advanced oxidation step 200 of removing from the treated water discharged from the filtration step 100 incombustible contaminants with respect to the treated water whose electric conductivity is lower than or equal to a reference value and disinfecting the treated water into the advanced oxidation apparatus 20 an ultrafiltration step 300 of putting the treated water discharged from the altitude oxidation step 200 into the ultrafiltration device 30 so as to remove contaminants from the treated water discharged from the altitude oxidation step 200 a step 710 of supplying the treated water discharged from the ultrafiltration step 300 to agricultural water industrial water and city reusing water b a step 720 of supplying the treated water having the electric conductivity exceeding the reference value among the treated water discharged from the filtration step 100 to the industrial water or the reclaimed water wherein the wastewater treatment method comprises the steps of"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101425965-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a system for reusing sewage treated water using the method for reuse of sewage treated water according to any one of claims 1 to 8 a filtration tank 10 configured to remove contaminants from sewage treatment water an advanced oxidation device 20 formed in the treated water discharged from the filtration tank 10 so as to remove and disinfect the refractory contaminants with respect to the treated water whose electric conductivity is lower than or equal to a reference value an ultrafiltration device 30 configured to remove contaminants from the treated water discharged from the advanced oxidation apparatus 20 a supplying section 71 for supplying the treated water discharged from the ultrafiltration apparatus 30 to agricultural water industrial water and city reusing water a b supplying unit 72 for supplying from the treated water discharged from the filtration tank 10 treated water whose electric conductivity exceeds a reference value as industrial water or recycled water wherein the waste water treatment system is a waste water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101425965-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in order to solve the above mentioned problems the present invention provides a filtering method comprising a filtration step 100 of putting filtrate into a filtration tank 10 to remove contaminants from sewage treatment water an advanced oxidation step 200 of removing from the treated water discharged from the filtration step 100 incombustible contaminants with respect to the treated water whose electric conductivity is lower than or equal to a reference value and disinfecting the treated water into the advanced oxidation apparatus 20 an ultrafiltration step 300 of putting the treated water discharged from the altitude oxidation step 200 into the ultrafiltration device 30 so as to remove contaminants from the treated water discharged from the altitude oxidation step 200 a step 710 of supplying the treated water discharged from the ultrafiltration step 300 to agricultural water industrial water and city reusing water b a step 720 of supplying treated water having an electric conductivity exceeding a reference value among the treated water discharged in the filtration step 100 to industrial water or recycled water and b we suggest a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101425965-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the present invention is a system for reusing sewage treated water using the method for reusing sewage treated water comprising a filtration tank 10 configured to remove contaminants from sewage treated water an advanced oxidation device 20 formed in the treated water discharged from the filtration tank 10 so as to remove and disinfect the refractory contaminants with respect to the treated water whose electric conductivity is lower than or equal to a reference value an ultrafiltration device 30 configured to remove contaminants from the treated water discharged from the advanced oxidation apparatus 20 a supplying section 71 for supplying the treated water discharged from the ultrafiltration apparatus 30 to agricultural water industrial water and city reusing water and a b supplying unit 72 for supplying from the treated water discharged from the filtration tank 10 treated water having an electric conductivity exceeding a reference value as industrial water or recycled water system together"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101425965-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "1 and subsequent drawings the method for reuse of sewage water according to the present invention includes a filtration step 100 for inputting sewage water to a filtration tank 10 to remove contaminants an advanced oxidation step 200 of removing from the treated water discharged in the filtration step 100 incombustible contaminants with respect to the treated water whose electric conductivity is lower than or equal to a reference value and disinfecting the treated water an ultrafiltration step 300 for introducing the treated water discharged from the altitude oxidation step 200 into the ultrafiltration device 30 so as to remove contaminants from the treated water discharged from the ultrafiltration step 200 a step 710 of supplying treated water discharged in the ultrafiltration step 300 to agricultural water industrial water and city reusing water b a step 720 of supplying the treated water discharged from the filtration step 100 to the industrial water or the reclaimed water whose electric conductivity exceeds the reference value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "multi function water storage system and method for reducing the contamination by initial rain and preventing a city from flooding the present invention relates to a multi functional next generation storage system and storage method that can be easily applied to urban areas and can be used to control the initial excellent pollution load caused by rainfall to prevent urban flooding and to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "the inclined screen causes the rainwater accelerated by the rainwater guiding plate to fall down by the gravity by the rainwater while the obstruction filtered by the screen is sent to the obstacle processing unit 232a at the lower end of the inclined screen the lower end portion is connected to the city gutter through the connection pipe 232 of the city gutter to discharge the habitat of the insect caused by the continuous maintenance and the water gutter phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "accordingly in order to supply water to hilly areas and to cultivate forests by pumping groundwater flowing underground as a water vein with electricity generated from renewable energy in the ground that is drying up due to climate change adjacent to the city center 84 the invention comprises a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 forming the afforestation block 30 a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to allow for the planting of landscaping trees 46 by protruding a moving gap 42 provided between a separate outer wall 32 in the rear wall 31 and afforestation blocks 30 30 assembled in a stack so that the moving gaps 42 are connected to each other"}, {"pat_id": "US-5525213-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "the exemplary heating element 98 is capable of slowly boiling the decontaminated waste water which is introduced into the evaporating chamber 124 thereby producing steam"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161569-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore the float bowel 63 will follow the water level to move up and down causing the water stop cock 65 to stop at or release from the stub tube 52"}, {"pat_id": "US-6846407-B2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "running the water through this many times can increase the reheat temperature up to 100 to 110 degrees fahrenheit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "induce the rainwater guided to the ground is conveyed through the conveying pipe member filtering rainwater conveyed through the conveying pipe member through a filtration unit storing the filtered rainwater in a storage tank pumping the stored rainwater through at least one of river water maintenance water irrigation canal water vegetation water around the river and waterfront park landscaping fountain supplying the necessary power to the filtration unit and the pumping means by at least one of a photovoltaic device or a wind turbine wherein a portion of the rainwater is permeable in the step of inducing rainwater through the permeable sidewalk block"}]</data>
