t an end of the spray nozzle and adjusting a spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle a rotating inner tube installed on an inner circumferential surface of the measuring tank and having a plurality of through holes a rotary driving unit installed to be connected to the rotating inner tube to transmit power to the rotating inner tube and to rotate the rotating inner tube inside the measuring tank to form a vortex inside the measuring tank a washing state confirmation unit installed inside the measuring tank to photograph the inside of the measuring tank the control unit of the central processing unit analyzes the degree of contamination of the measurement tank through the image of the inside of the measurement tank captured by the washing state confirmation unit and analyzes whether or not cleaning of the inside of the measurement tank is necessary or a part requiring cleaning when the control unit confirms a position requiring washing the spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle is adjusted as the angle adjuster rotates a washing unit for cleaning the inside of the measurement tank by spraying washing water into the measurement tank after the treated water measured in the measurement tank is discharged to the aeration tank through the discharge unit and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting the freeze protection unit a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe a heating unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction part the treated water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part and when the temperature sensed by the temperature sensing unit is equal to or less than a predetermined temperature a temperature control unit for adjusting the heating temperature of the heating unit so that the treated water or washing water inside the pipe does not freeze"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "is possible and such variations fall within the protection scope of the present invention.10 piping entering the object to be frozen or bursting or piping exiting from the object 20 external power 100 automatic dripping device for freezing prevention 110 body part 111 opening and closing lid 112 power indicator lamp 113 operation indicator lamp 114 storage space 120 temperature detection unit 130 control unit 131 external power input terminal 132 transformer 133 relay 140 on off valve 150 on off valve driving unit 150e emergency operation button 151 opening and closing valve coupling part 152 rotary drive unit 153 heat supply unit 154 opening and closing valve warming part 161 additional mounting piping 161a extension pipe 162 additionally installed on off valve 163 falling water storage tank 164 falling water flow rate detection unit 165 falling water supply pipe 166 water level detection and alarm unit 167 water drain pipe 171 power supply unit 172 power supply part warming part 173 wireless communication module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "thereby the object to be cleaned 1 is firstly cleaned by high pressure air bubbling through the lower spray nozzle 233 by driving the spray pump 235 in a state of being immersed in the cleaning liquid in the cleaning tank 210 the spray nozzle 233 is driven by the spray pump 235 to discharge the cleaning solution through the upper spray nozzle 233 before being lifted from the cleaning tank 210 by the driving of the cleaning lifting driver 225 the washing liquid is circulated through the upper spray nozzle 233 by the clean wash water accommodated in the regenerating wash fluid reservoir 240 by the driving of the regenerating wash fluid circulating pump 245 and the steam supply pipe 117 the drying and residual washing liquid is removed by the high temperature steam supplied from the waste water regeneration apparatus 100 and sprayed through the upper spray nozzle 233 and then discharged to the outside of the cleaning loading unit 220 or the cleaning quality of the object to be cleaned 1 can be further improved without consuming energy"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3319944-B2", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "according to the present invention as described above when the photographing means is housed in a camera case having a transparent monitoring window on the lower surface and the light shielding hood is placed on the water surface together with the lighting means since it is arranged at a certain distance from the water surface in the space above the water surface in the light blocking hood determined by the float mounting position the photographing means the lighting means and the monitoring window of the camera case are connected to the water in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-3876536-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a pressure between 150 and 4 000 psig so that a reduction of between 30 and 70 percent in chemical oxygen demand is obtained separating the gaseous liquid and solid phases from said oxidation and biologically oxidizing the liquid phase in an aeration contact tank containing a biomass suitable to effect biological oxidation of the organic solutes present in said liquid phase the improvement which comprises maintaining powdered activated carbon in the aeration contact tank in an amount sufficient to enhance the biooxidation and substantially reduce the odor and color of said liquid phase carrying out the biological oxidation until excess biomass builds up and the activated carbon becomes spent transferring a mixture of the excess biomass and spent carbon to a wet oxidation reactor and oxidizing said mixture under conditions similar to those used for wet air oxidation of the raw sewage sludge or night soil so as to regenerate the powdered activated carbon for further use in the biological oxidation step and at the same time disposing of the excess biomass"}, {"pat_id": "US-8398733-B2", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "thus the water generation purification and its pumping to the tank of water dispensing block continues"}, {"pat_id": "US-5518624-A", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "operations were continued for a period of four weeks to identify any long term membrane leaching or shedding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "vacuum apparatus for evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means an air compressor for injecting high pressure compressed air into a sealed conduit detecting unit for detecting the pressure and temperature changes in the test tank connected to the vacuum device and the air compression device and connected to the interior of the conduit a controller which controls the driving of the vacuum apparatus and the air compressor and determines whether there is a leakage based on a result detected by the sensing unit it includes a supply device for supplying power and power to each device from the power take off device of the vehicle when the vehicle is mounted or to supply each device the power produced by the generator when mounted on the vehicle to be movable with the vehicle the supply device includes a noise blocking circuit for blocking the noise of the power supplied to each device the power cable connected to the front and rear ends of the noise blocking circuit is provided with a twisted cable to block the noise by increasing the capacitance by twisting the wire the controller is installed inside the main body that forms the appearance and executes the program stored in the storage to control the operation of each device a central processing unit and a printed circuit board for determining a leakage test result according to the detection signal of the detection unit a plurality of operation switches provided on one side of the main body and receiving an operation for controlling driving of each device it is provided on the other side of the main body and includes a plurality of connection ports electrically connected to each device the operation switch is provided with a power switch a vacuum pump provided in the vacuum device a vacuum valve first to fifth switches electrically connected to the compressor and the compressor valve provided in the air compressor the connection port is provided with the vacuum pump and the vacuum valve the compressor and the compressor valve the vent valve for releasing the pressure in the test tank and the first to seventh ports respectively connected to the sensing unit the supply device the first to fifth switches can be set to manual and automatic modes and operation off the cable connecting the sensing unit and the controller is a leakage inspection apparatus of the conduit facility characterized in that provided with a shielded cable shielded to reduce noise"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "authenticating permissions for c conducting a vacuum test or a pressurization test by evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means using a vacuum means or injecting high pressure compressed air into the conduit facility based on the test mode setting state step d detecting changes in pressure and temperature inside the test tank connected to the conduit using a detector and e using the control unit to determine whether the conduit is leaked based on the result detected by the detection unit the leakage inspection method of the conduit facility characterized in that in the step a the supply device cuts off the noise of the power supplied to each device by using a noise blocking circuit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", 