y checking tank wherein the diffuser includes an acoustic resonance engine for increasing oxygen transfer rate to the microorganisms in the reactor and reducing power cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102705352-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in an electrolysis device that sterilizes ballast water flowing into a ballast tank through a ballast water main line using a sterilizing substance generated through electrolysis of seawater an electrolysis unit that produces a sterilizing substance by electrolyzing seawater a rectifier connected to the electrolytic unit and detecting the voltage value of the electrolytic unit a controller for controlling the operation of the electrolytic unit and the rectifier and an electrolysis device including a tro measuring device that measures the salinity or temperature of seawater flowing into the electrolysis unit calculates the concentration of a sterilizing substance by using the measured salinity measurement value or temperature measurement value the input current of the electrolysis unit and the flow rate value measured by a flow meter provided in the ballast water main line thereby detecting the concentration of a sterilizing substance in the ballast water of the ship at the point where the flow meter is located"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102705352-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a ballast water main line that transports seawater flowing in from outside the ship to the ballast tank an electrolytic device that produces a sterilizing substance by electrolyzing seawater a flow meter installed in the ballast water main line and measuring the flow rate of ballast water transported through the ballast water main line and a ballast water treatment system including a tro measuring device that measures the salinity or temperature of seawater flowing into the electrolysis device calculates the concentration of the sterilizing substance using the measured salinity measurement value or temperature measurement value the input current of the electrolysis