very to the engine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200190678-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "conventionally in order to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes in an apartment water tanker or a water meter protection container many schiropols are built in the water meter and water pipes to prevent freezing in cold weather or cold regions falling below a certain temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502599-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "therefore the use problem is pointed out that the rust preventive agent is not uniformly dissolved in tap water immediately before use due to seasonal temperature change so that the residual concentration is too high or too low and energy consumption is large and manufacturing time including melting process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101615356-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "this is excellent in durability so it is excellent in filtration because it is spherical with less wear on backwashing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100249452-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "to date such a phase separation method using electrodialysis for example chloroform carbon tetrachloride oxygen oxidation to selectively remove methane producing bacteria in acid forming tanks using reduction potentials to control environmental factors such as ph and temperature affecting the growth rate of microorganisms and to control hydraulic and microbial retention times kinetic control methods have been proposed but it was difficult to fundamentally prevent the inflow of microorganisms and solids in the acid forming tank into the methane forming tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "the heater 16 then raises the temperature in the water tank 10 under the control of the controller 64 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100328970-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the outer circumferential surface of the hopper tank 101 the apparatus for discharging the contaminants characterized in that the constant temperature wire coil 111 is attached to prevent freezing of the contaminants in the hopper tank 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100328970-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the circumferential surface of the hopper tank is characterized in that a constant temperature wire coil is attached to prevent freezing of the contaminants in the hopper tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100693184-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the treatment efficiency of the aeration tank is affected by the design conditions such as the load of organic matter the aeration time and the amount of air and the conditions of the growing environment such as water temperature and ph"}, {"pat_id": "US-8661819-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "according to one embodiment the collector tube 214 acts as a conduit for transporting the thermal transfer fluid through the solar concentrator 212 and the tube 214 has a substantially rectangular shape with dimensions of approximately one 1 inch wide by three 3 inches high which the applicants believe provides advantageous heat transfer characteristics over conventional collector tubes 214 having a circular cross sectional shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102415233-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "intake tank a water intake pipe inserted into the groundwater layer and connected to the water intake tank an intake pump disposed in the intake pipe to supply groundwater to the intake tank a groundwater sensor module inserted into the groundwater layer to measure the level of the groundwater the radon concentration of the groundwater the temperature of the groundwater the electrical conductivity and the ph concentration of the groundwater a water tank connected to the water intake tank through a water tank supply pipe an intake tank sensor module disposed inside the intake tank to measure the temperature of the stored water in the intake tank the electrical conductivity of the stored water the radon concentration of the stored water and the ph concentration of the stored water a supply pump disposed in the water tank supply pipe to supply water from the water intake tank to the water tank and a control center for controlling the groundwater sensor module the water intake tank and the supply pump when the radon concentration measured in at least one of the groundwater sensor module and the intake tank sensor module exceeds a reference value the control center prevents the supply pump and the intake pump from operating the groundwater sensor module is case a body portion disposed inside the case and it is inserted into the body portion and a first sensor unit for detecting radon in water and the first sensor unit a first insertion part inserted into the body part a fixing part connected to the first insertion part a first sensor disposed inside the fixing part and measuring the radon partly exposed to the outside of the fixing part a shielding part disposed on the fixing part to shield the first sensor part exposed to the outside of the fixing part and a humidity sensor disposed around the first sensor to measure humidity provided an integrated control system for artificial cultivation in response to drought using a wireless sensor network"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102458775-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition in the case of a conventional sewage treatment system when the water temperature is lowered as in winter the biological treatment efficiency is reduced as the activity of microorganisms is lowered and accordingly bod and cod increase so that normal water treatment cannot be performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102554668-B1", "para_id": "para_175", "text": "water softening in the pretreatment module 160 may alternatively or additionally be achieved using an anti scalant such as lime softening ion exchange resin or polyphosphate as is known in the art"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101265963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "aerobic reservoir having apparatus for mainraining reacting temperature the present invention relates to an aerobic tank in a sewage and sewage advanced treatment system comprising an apparatus for maintaining a reaction temperature in an aerobic tank and forming an optimum reaction condition in the aerobic tank even with an external temperature change thereby improving the efficiency of organic matter oxidation and nitrification and thereby stable discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "internal temperature sensing means for sensing the internal temperature cold water temperature sensing means for sensing the cold water temperature of the cold water tank the internal temperature detected by the internal temperature sensing means and the cold water temperature detected by the cold water temperature sensing means the four way valve for controlling the four way valve to prevent the freezing of the cold water tank by changing the flow path through which the refrigerant is circulated according to the control of the control means and the control means for controlling the overall operation by determining whether the cold water tank is frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "under the control of the drive means and the control means the temperature of the cold water tank is raised to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "however in this conventional method since the refrigerant circulates only according to the freezing cycle for cooling the purified water when the indoor temperature especially in winter of the product installation place is low and the freezing point or the cold water temperature is a freezing condition there is a problem that the cold water tank is frozen the user can not take the purified water as well as reduce the reliability of the product"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the present invention has been made to solve the above problems an object of the present invention is to determine the freezing of the cold water tank according to the changing product intern