s equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "receiving tank automatic control system capable of real time monitoring characterized in that consisting of a communication unit 36 for receiving and transmitting to the display unit 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0385568 2003.05.15 designated by reservoir control system registered and filed by the present applicant the groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as used herein the term second compartment may be used interchangeably with the terms sensor compartment or sensor tank and unless otherwise specified is the compartment in which various parameters such as temperature ph and corrosion are measured in the spray water generally now particle free according to the disclosed system and methods"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100245825-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the same members are denoted by the same reference numerals as described above and the heat exchange means is a cylinder in which a certain amount of groundwater is introduced and stored while being buried in the ground at a depth not affected by the freezing depth of the ground that is the temperature of the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101163512-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the organic substance drying method of drying a hydrous organic substance a first step of heating the hydrous organic material to hydrolyze it into a liquid liquid organic material a second step of heating the liquid organic material by heating the liquid organic material and using the heat generated in the process of condensing the vaporized water vapor while condensing the vaporized water vapor and a third step of performing the second step to concentrate the liquid organic material into a concentrated organic material the first step is the step of supplying the water containing organic matter to the decomposition tank 130 by supplying steam to the decomposition tank 130 to heat the temperature of the water containing organic matter 180 c 250 c a hydrolysis step of hydrolyzing the liquid organic matter and a step of heat exchanging the hydrolyzed high temperature liquid organic material with a low temperature hydrous organic material to be hydrolyzed the second step is the step of supplying the liquid organic matter into the internal space of the evaporator 80 the step of supplying water vapor discharged from the internal space of the evaporator 80 to the steam compressor 87 the steam compressor 87 compresses the steam to high temperature steam according to the steam pressure curve"}, {"pat_id": "US-4940549-A", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "or at least to some elevated temperature prior to introduction to a stage i treatment tank 18 as shown"}, {"pat_id": "US-4940549-A", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "the slurry of brine solution iron and sulfur is agitated substantially constantly in the stage i tank to prevent scaling up and falling out of iron from the slurry"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102808335-B1", "para_