ution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit while the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to heat the mixed solution heating control unit including water tank for storing water a selection unit which selects any one of the mixed solution or water stored in the antifreeze tank or the water tank in response to a control signal of the control unit and transmits it to the circulation pump and a second temperature sensor for measuring the ambient temperature of the pipe for transferring the liquid further comprising the control unit supplies the water supplied from the water tank to the circulation pump through the selection unit when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a set temperature and when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is lower than the set temperature the water supplied from the antifreeze tank is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the present invention according to one aspect for achieving the above object is an antifreeze tank in which a mixture of antifreeze and water is stored in a predetermined ratio antifreeze hose installed along the pipe for transferring the liquid to transfer the liquid a circulation pump for supplying and circulating the mixed solution into the antifreeze hose a first temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the mixed solution flowing through the antifreeze hose a heater for heating the mixed solution stored in the antifreeze tank to a predetermined temperature a temperature controller for adjusting the temperature of the mixed solution and while the temperature information of the mixed solution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to drive the mixed solution it provides a system for preventing freezing and freezing of piping for liquid transport characterized in that it comprises a control unit for heating the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the supplied water may be supplied to the circulation pump and when the temperature is lower than a set temperature the mixed liquid supplied from the antifreeze tank may be supplied to the circulation pump.as described above according to the system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipe for liquid transport according to the present invention an antifreeze hose through which antifreeze mixture heated to a predetermined temperature flows along the pipe for liquid transport is installed and the antifreeze flowing through the antifreeze hose it is possible to prevent freezing and freezing of the liquid transport pipe in winter by transferring the heat source of the liquid to the liquid transport pipe.1 is a view showing a system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipes for liquid transport according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101522630-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a water supply unit for supplying water to the water storage unit so that the water storage unit maintains a predetermined water level is formed at one side of the water storage unit and a plurality of switches for operating the drive is provided on the front side a water tank mounted on a water supply part of the main body and storing water to be supplied to the water supply part of the main body and a water reservoir coupled to an upper part of the main body so that the water storage part is not exposed to the outside and an upper case provided with a blowing fan for blowing water to the water storage part and promoting evaporation of water in the water storage part and regulating the temperature of the water in the water storage part of the evaporation type humidifier a cold water induction surface in which a relatively low temperature water is collected among the water contained in the reservoir portion is formed at a lower portion of the reservoir portion and a slope reservoir portion having a relatively shallow depth in the reservoir portion around the reservoir portion a valve plate formed at an outlet of the water supply unit so that a passage of water flowing into the reservoir unit is formed downward a block membrane disposed behind the valve membrane to inhibit heat transfer through convection of water and further comprising an am capturing membrane disposed behind the block membrane to suppress heat transfer through convection of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101816805-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "the efficiency of the electrolysis unit 13 is low due to a low temperature or low salinity of the ballast water but can not be sufficiently sterilized only by operation of the ultraviolet unit 12 during ballasting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the conventional automatic chlorine injection system as described above and the problem to be solved by the present invention is to provide an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a water tank of a public building which can store a large amount of chlorine in the automatic chlorine injection device and timely inject and replenish it and also prevent deterioration of the chlorine solution due to changes in the surrounding temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to solve the above mentioned problem the automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a water tank of a public building according to the present invention comprises a main storage tank storing a predetermined amount 