ines in a medicine storage tank provided in the medicine storage tank to the water supply pipe one side connected to the medicine storage tank and the other side connected to the water supply pipe a chemical supply pump provided with the chemical supply pump a motor interlocked with the medicine dispensing pump and adjusting a dose of the medicine by adjusting a rotation speed a control unit electrically connected to the motor to control the driving and rotating speed of the motor and a pressure sensor for sensing a pressure inside the medicine inlet pipe and electrically connected to the motor so that the medicine is supplied to the medicine inlet pipe only when water flows inside the water supply pipe the pipe is provided with a branch connecting member at one end for facilitating installation in the water supply pipe a heat radiating plate is installed inside the main body a temperature sensor interlocked with the heat radiating plate is further installed and a heating wire is installed on the medicine inlet pipe to prevent freezing of the medicine a side wall of the main body is connected to a first medicine inlet pipe connected to a medicine storage tank and supplying medicines to the inside of the main body and a second medicine inlet pipe connected to a water supply pipe for supplying medicines to the water supply pipe and a hose connecting the two connection ports"}, {"pat_id": "US-8117998-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "as described above according to a hot water supplying system of the invention since a water tank storing a predetermined amount of water is provided with the hot water supplying system and water stored in the water tank and remaining in the pipelines is preheated even when the hot water is not used it is possible to supply hot water heated to a set temperature in the shortest time whenever a user wants to use the hot water and to prevent the pipelines from freezing and bursting in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "US-7105095-B2", "para_id": "par