n of said tank"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4332915-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "powdered activated carbon can adsorb and remove organic compounds corresponding to environmental hormones by using a device that is stirred and mixed with environmental hormone containing water in an adsorption tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-11596874-B2", "para_id": "para_136", "text": "system 100 includes air blower 106 that bubbles ambient air 110 through standing water 112 in tank 102 in this non limiting example the bubbling is accomplished via air stone 108"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045975-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "nitrite oxidation step that promotes silver and inhibits the growth of nitrifiers thereby oxidizing more ammonia in the leachate to nitrite than nitrate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200186594-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of upper and lower cases 1 2 having an o ring 3 in the coupling portion to achieve a predetermined size and shape and waterproof and the lower case 2 is suction of water to perform a buoyancy control function the ballast 16 is provided with discharge ports 9a and 9b and the piston 7a is moved up and down by forward and reverse rotation of the dc motor 5a above the ballast 16 to obtain diving and buoyancy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the contamination index calculating unit 343 calculates the contamination index of the membrane filtration tank 320 by using a pressure gauge p for measuring the inter membrane pressure difference kpa a viscometer c for measuring the viscosity of the raw water that has been pretreated q for measuring the flow rate of the filtrate and may include a calculator not shown for calculating the contamination index fi according to equation 1 by applying each measured value additionally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "at this time the determination unit 346 may determine that the chemical cleaning is performed when the temperature of the raw water is equal to or higher than the reference temperature the current time is included in the reference time zone or the date is included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the present invention proposes a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention provides a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a temperature lower than the preset temperature water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 and at the same time water is supplied into the rainwater storage tank 200 by the bypass pipe 620 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 .the present invention proposes a rainwater storage structure for a road and a rainwater storage method using the same which can prevent urban flood damage caused by localized heavy rain due to climate change and distortion of the water circulation system due to overdevelopment of urban areas.figure 1 below illustrates an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200299813-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "therefore the heat discharged from the condenser 2c is blown by the blower 3 to the evaporation chamber 1b through the blower opening 2w and the internal temperature of the evaporation chamber 1b is raised to about 35 40 degreec"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "however the coupling by bearing is possible in a fermentation device operated at room temperature and normal pressure but there is room for problems such as leakage and deformation due to thermal expansion in a drying device supplied with high temperature and high pressure dry air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "10 since there is little influence by high temperature and high pressure inside there is an advantage in that the sealing is reliable and the replacement cycle is long"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100232360-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "the present invention is an anaerobic tank anoxic tank aerobic tank sedimentation tank sludge in order to improve the point that the conventional technique is different in performance and inefficient in order to remove residual nitrogen and phosphorus after treating organic wastewater providing a novel system that properly connects thickeners sludge storage tanks and dehydrators and simultaneously removes nitrogen and phosphorus biologically eliminating the problem of releasing nitrogen into nitrogen gas and eluting phosphorus and promoting the self oxidation of excess sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-4203806-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "discontinuance of dental services in case of malfunction or exhaustion of water in the single pressure storage tank 2 9 in order to prevent the occurrence of a sepa