t water tank 90 for storing sterilized treated water in the sterilization means 80 and supplying purified water to the sterilization means 80 a mineralsetron connected to the treated water tank 90 for supplying the minerals removed from the membranes 50 and 60 tds turbidity and temperature measurement values of the supply means 95 and the water collecting tank 10 to measure the total dissolved solids tds turbidity and temperature of the water collecting tank 10 50 60 to drive the water purification apparatus in accordance with the raw water conditions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101938119-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "by adopting the heater channel the heat insulating layer and the frp layer which are provided so as to cover the inner circumferential surface of the microbial reaction tank it is possible to block the cold heat transmitted from the ground during the cold season and to increase the temperature of the sewage introduced into the microbial reaction tank it is possible to maximize the treatment efficiency by microorganisms.1 is a view for explaining a configuration of a large capacity wastewater treatment apparatus according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330905-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the treatment efficiency of the aeration tank 4 is affected by the design operation conditions such as the load of organic matter the aeration time the air amount and the conditions of the growing environment such as the water temperature and ph"}, {"pat_id": "US-5055180-A", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "thus an uninsulated tank will normally last for a much longer period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-12297129-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "however conductivity readings can be adversely affected by other factors such as water conductivity and temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904534-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition it is possible to precisely control the temperature of the cold hot water and to compensate for the change in the ph concentration due to the temperature change of the drinking water thereby supplying the drinking water having a constant ph concentration.1 is a block diagram showing a cold warm water purifier according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101166906-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "through the present invention by maintaining the temperature of the digester and the concentration tank in the distributed urban organic waste recycling facility installed in the central heating complex by using hot water or heating circulating water in the central heating complex the variation of urban organic inflow and outflow it is possible to increase the efficiency of digesters in distributed urban organic waste recycling facilities which are difficult to maintain constant temperature because they are installed large and small digesters"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100768274-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "as described above the present invention can be mass produced while being molded by injection molding and the air flow is blocked inside the unit hollow plate in which the injected first and second hollow plates are fixed by high frequency heat fusion thereby condensing due to temperature difference between indoor and outdoor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the dewatering cake having the liquid component removed is sent to the mixer 500 or the mixing and high temperature fermenter 519 in the composting step the high concentration wastewater as the dehydration filtrate is sent to the high temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 or the anaerobic digestion process in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater or the dehydration filtrate having high salinity concentration is desalted by the electrolysis method or the electric extraction method or less desalted water is returned to the front side of the primary dehydration process and used as a washing water for washing the salt a pretreatment step of the organic waste sent to the high tempe