f high concentration wastewater a biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage a secondary aeration tank 414 in the low concentration wastewater secondary biological treatment stage and a secondary microorganism culture tank the sludge which has been settled in the primary settling tank 310 is supplied to the primary microorganism culture tank 314 by the primary transfer pump 313 and supplied to the primary microorganism culture tank 314 the air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the primary bioreactor 315 and the lower portion of the primary microorganism culture tank 314 to supply the wastewater while the aeration is performed to convert the polyphenol compounds into metabolites corrosive microorganisms that convert water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors humic substances precursors or corrosive substances humic substances and microorganisms that are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms are excreted by the corrosion reaction and then sent to the aeration tank 310 where the primary biological wastewater treatment the entire system is induced to become wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and microorganisms that are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms the solids are precipitated in the first settling tank 311 and the overflowed the first biologically treated water which is the overflow is treated with the first biological treatment stage of the low concentration wastewater sent to the first biological treatment tank 400 when the primary biological treatment water is supplied to the primary biological treatment water storage tank 400 electrolytic oxidation treatment electron beam treatment eelectron beam treatment or electrolytic oxidation treatment and electronic pretreatment are performed to remove the biodegradable organic matter contained in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the settled solids are supplied to the secondary settling tank 416 by the central cone cone it is possible to deposit active erosion material pellets minerals containing active minerals minerals or ceramics that emit negative ions and ultraviolet rays that emit far infrared rays and negative ions by the secondary transfer pump 417 the excess sludge is returned to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 and the secondary aeration tank 414 in which the secondary bioreactor 419 filled with the mineral or ceramics packing 420 is loaded and the excess sludge discharged is discharged temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater and the biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage together with the excess sludge to be discharged to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 sludge precipitated in the secondary settling tank 415 is supplied to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the secondary bioreactor 419 and the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 a corrosive microorganism which transforms water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors or corrosive substances by providing a polyphenol compound as a metabolite by supplying a wastewater and microbes in symbiotic relationships and sent to the secondary aeration tank 414 to induce the whole of the secondary biological wastewater treatment system to be subjected to the wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and the microorganisms which are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms and the secondary settling tank 415 the second biologically treated water which is the overflowing water is the second biological treatment step of the low concentration wastewater sent to the final biological treatment water tank 421 the secondary biologically treated water is subjected to sterilization treatment by a combination of at least one of oxidizing agent oxidizing agent ultraviolet ray irradiation electrolytic oxidation or electron beam irradiation and then subjected to sand filtration to remove suspended solids a final treatment step of the wastewater discharging the treated water when the dehydrated cake dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process is supplied to the mixer 500 a moisture adjuster and a soil conditioner are injected into the mixer mixer 501 while stirring to adjust the water content to 60 to 65 wt and fed to a fermentation tank 503 which is opened and straightened by the fermentation tank feed conveyor 502 and then flipped to the fermentation tank mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 30 to 50 days"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "para_302", "text": "when the dehydrated cake the additive and the moisture control agent swelling agent are mixed in the mixer 500 and supplied to the fermentation tank 503 of the fermentation process in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process co 2 h 2 o and nh 3 the temperature increases to 60 70 c due to the heat of reaction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "para_315", "text": "the dehydrated cake is dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process and the soil conditioner and the moisture control agent are introduced into the mixer and the high fermentation is carried out for 4 to 6 days while stirring with a mixer and a hot fermentor mixer 520 and then the fermentation device 503 is fed into the medium temperature fermenter feed conveyor 515 the ripe compost is subjected to aerobic fermentation while being flipped to the fermentation unit mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 25 to 50 days and the ripened compost is injected into the ripe compost infusion hopper 506 with a poclain 505 then it is sent to the foreign matter sorting unit 507 the removed mature compost is returned 20 to 50 based on the amount of the mixture of the dehydrated cake of the organic waste and the swelling agent introduced into the front end of the fermentation tank 503 by the mature compost conveying conveyor 508 or the shovel 505 the compost is sent to the ripe compost storage facility or the packaging facility process by the mature compost conveying conveyor 509 and is packaged and commercialized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101816806-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "the efficiency of the electrolysis unit 13 is low due to a low temperature or low salinity of the ballast water but can not be sufficiently sterilized only by operation of the ultraviolet unit 12 during ballasting"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5224799-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in daily life and organic wastewater treatment wastewater treatment is effectively performed by making the most of the action of various useful microorganisms and creating an environment in which the microorganisms are easily active in the treatment water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102188540-B1", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "10 flow adjustment tank 20 pretreatment unit 30 bioreactor 100 electrolysis system 120 electrolysis unit 140 combustion unit 160 control unit 161 monitoring module 163 temperature control module 165 operation mode determination module 167 output module 169 transmission module 180 gas supply unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5227055-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "water treatment apparatus for recirculating water in a closed cycle aquaculture system for rearing fish comprising a fish rearing containment means including water means supplying feed and oxygen to said water in said containment means and water treatment means connected to said containment means to clean and nitrify said water and to maintain it at a selected temperature said treatment means including a water tank for receiving water to be cleaned from said containment means a rotatable biological contactor mounted for rotation through water in said tank said contactor comprising a drum having an axial support shaft and a plurality of media tubes surrounding said shaft and closely spaced thereto to form a packed generally cylindrical bundle a plurality of circumferential band hoops extending around said drum to secure said tubes and a plurality of spokes extending radially from and being secured at their inner ends to said support shaft said spokes being secured at their outer ends to said band hoops to maintain said closely packed bundle of media tubes each said media tube having a length approximately equal to the length of said support shaft each tube having a longitudinal axis parallel to said axial shaft and each tube incorporating a plurality of circumferential rings spaced along the length thereof with a plurality of integral longitudinal fins spaced around said tube and extending radially inwardly from said rings said rings and fins providing a media tube having a surface area of between about 20 and 80 ft2 ft3 with a void space of between about 88 and 94 a bacterial film on said media tubes means for rotating said biological contactor shaft to cause said drum to rotate through water in said tank to thereby cause said media tubes to enter the water and thereafter exit the water and means for directing a flow of air through said media tubes and through said media tube void spaces to cause air to contact water which clings to said media tubes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008089-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "use cloth old clothes or cloth to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100513311-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "water meter protection container is a device to prevent the water meter from freezing or being damaged by external impact in the winter when the temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100850033-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the organic matter thus pulverized is transferred to the at least one sterilization transfer screw 9 of the sterilization tank 10 by the first transfer screw 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100850033-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the pulverized material thus pulverized is introduced into the sound sterilization tank 10 by the first transfer screw 7 and then the temperature of steam injected by the steam injection tube 9 is 120 c and 2.5 kg cm 2 pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102810409-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a high concentration wastewater treatment device which sprays a high temperature flame on the water surface in a concentration tank to evaporate the water surface after filtering the concentrate in an ro membrane filtration device cools the evaporated water vapor in a wet scrubber and discharges it as condensate so that foreign substances can be removed by oxidation combustion and are chemically stabilized so that they can easily coagulate and precipitate with a coagulant and dehydrate the precipitated sludge to form a cake so that it can be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102810409-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to the present invention the concentrate filtered in the ro membrane filtration device is sprayed onto the water surface in a concentration tank by high temperature flames to evaporate the water surface the evaporated water vapor is cooled in a wet scrubber and discharged as condensate so that foreign substances can be removed by oxidation combustion and thus are chemically stabilized so that they easily coagulate and precipitate with a coagulant and the precipitated sludge is dehydrated and turned into a cake for treatment thereby improving the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "after a block of ice is formed the temperature of the insulation chamber may be increased to melt the surfaces of the block of ice that contact the internal wall of the tank in order to facilitate vertical movement of the block of ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "during this freezing process water molecules crystallize to form a lattice structure which allows the ice layer 60 to float on top of the water 10 while rejecting salt organic compounds minerals or other impurities into the water 10 beneath the layer of ice 60"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "4 feed water 10a is then pumped into the tank 20 to raise the block of ice 60a above at least one wall of the tank 20 and a mechanical device such as a push rod 70 or moveable arm is used to remove the block of ice 60a from the tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "after the block of ice 60a is formed the temperature of the internal walls 26 may be increased to facilitate vertical movement of the block of ice 60a by pumping a higher temperature fluid 80a not shown through the insulation intake pipe 34 and purging or removing the lower temperature fluid 80 through an insulation exhaust pipe 36"}, {"pat_id": "US-4343683-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the storage tank 41 for collecting odors 72 a stirrer 51 which is charged for the fermentation and decomposition treatment of the food waste a to be evenly supplied and stirred by the stirring blade 511 together with the microorganism and the wood chip 512 a nozzle 52 for spraying washing water b at a predetermined temperature for washing to prevent anaerobically progressing due to the saccharide enzyme microorganism carcass and the like and to provide aerobic condition a driving motor 54 for rotating the