construction space and fills the rainwater collected in the water collecting tank of the road block into the filling storage space of the compartment water trap a filling section in which a filling pipe is vertically penetrated in each water collecting tank of the road block a sedimentation section is formed on the outside of the filling section to be relatively deeper than the filling section to precipitate foreign substances contained in rainwater flowing into the water collection tank the rainwater flowing into the collecting tank precipitates and removes foreign substances while passing through the settling section and the rainwater from which the foreign substances are precipitated and removed flows into the filling section and is filled in the filling storage space of the compartment pitcher bag through the filling pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in addition a filling section in which a filling pipe is vertically penetrated in each water collecting tank of the road block a sedimentation section is formed on the outside of the filling section to be relatively deeper than the filling section to precipitate foreign substances contained in rainwater flowing into the water collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "therefore rainwater flowing into each water collection tank 41 of the road block 40 while moving along the road surface 100 does not directly flow into the filling pipe 52 disposed in the filling section 41a but settles in the sedimentation section 41b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "thus the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40 so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101817003-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "next the rainwater that has been purified through the water purification apparatus 2 is moved to the storage tank 3 along the connection line 52 thereby enabling a large amount of water to be supplied as moisture necessary for growing the water loss water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674110-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes and modifications may be made without departing from the scope of the present invention.1 rainwater catcher 2 3 by drain pipe 4 infiltration ball 10 penetration ditch 10a infiltration ditch inflow section 11 perforated fan for flow equalization 12 shovel rake 12a contamination 13 flooding bumps 14 drainage filter fiber 15 observation 15a 15b plug 20 pretreatment tank 20a pretreatment tank inflow section 21 sand pack 22 stagnant water outlet 30 runoff water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847553-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore there is a need for a practical and applicable technology that can easily control the size of the storage space as well as facilitate maintenance while preventing float or pollutants contained in rainwater from being easily introduced into the soil through the storage tank it is a fact that is demanded.patent registration publication no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399489-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the wastewater treatment apparatus using ozone comprising a collecting tank ozone generator ozone oxidation tank pressurized flotation tank pressure filter sludge collector and treated water tank a screen tank installed at all stages of the collection tank and integrally including a filtering means consisting of a flow blocking valve and an activated carbon fiber double screen to block unnecessary rainwater mixing an ozone oxidation tank for forming a vortex through the swirl flow multi contact device to increase the contact between the ozone supplied from the ozone generator and the waste water supplied from the collecting tank an improved ozonation type wastewater treatment apparatus for strengthening the pretreatment process comprising a pressurized floatation tank integrally containing a microbubble type ceramic spraying unit for microbubbling the dissolved air supplied by the eject"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399489-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at the same time the present invention relates to an improved ozone oxidation wastewater treatment system that has enhanced the pretreatment process to improve the facility margin and contaminant removal rate according to the effect of reducing pollutant load in the downstream equipment by performing the pretreatment process to filter foreign substances such as contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101158550-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the present invention is to pinch and fix the side wall panel from the top between the support beam installed to maintain a predetermined interval after the excavation to a predetermined depth and area and to secure the side wall panel without using a separate component and at the same time the side panel there is a unique effect that can quickly and easily build a storage tank that can prevent leakage between the rainwater flowing into the storage tank to prevent leakage to the outside.1 is a perspective view showing a side wall panel according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the prefabricated storage tank in which a plurality of blocks of different types are combined to form an excellent storage space the block is a plurality of basic block portions having a rectangular tubular shape and coupled to each other by a concave portion and a convex portion formed around both side ends and having two or more rows arranged in parallel two or more single finishing block parts coupled to one side end of the basic block part by one side closed and a concave or convex part formed around the other end and at least one composite finishing block portion having one side closed and simultaneously joined to one side end of the two basic block portions arranged in two rows by a concave portion or convex portion formed around the other end to form a passage through which rainwater flows lt rti gt prefabricated storage tank characterized in that the basic block portion a single closing block portion and a composite closing block portion is coupled to each other to form a conduit connecting each block portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "therefore the rainwater flows along the pipeline during the supply or discharge of rainwater thereby minimizing contamination due to the propagation of microorganisms in the rainwater by maintaining uniform time of stagnation in the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the assembled rainwater storage tank 10 according to the present invention having the above described structure can be installed rapidly and firmly to meet the capacity suitable for the building at low cost and can use rainwater as drinking water for drinking water and emergency drinking water it is possible to prevent flood control in the rainy season and typhoon as well as to surely prevent pollution by contaminated initial rainwater by eliminating a large but early power without extra power.10 assembly type stormwater tank 20 water storage tank tower 21 lower block 22 water quality observation block 23 upper block 24 capacity adjustment block 30 drain pipe assembly 31 first drain pipe 32 opening and closing means 33 second drain pipe 34 filter pipe 40 water supply pipe 50 water pump 60 advanced water purification device 70 fountain hose 80 sterilization device 90 water storage tank 100 building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "the inclined screen causes the rainwater accelerated by the rainwater guiding plate to fall down by the gravity by the rainwater while the obstruction filtered by the screen is sent to the obstacle processing unit 232a at the lower end of the inclined screen the lower end portion is connected to the city gutter through the connection pipe 232 of the city gutter to discharge the habitat of the insect caused by the continuous maintenance and the water gutter phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2410094-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "thus a partition tank has been formed capable of mounting a rainwater collecting surface thereon which offers good resistance to deformation by the tubular shape of these tubes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102677255-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "accordingly foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected in the storage tank 20 and transported through the horizontal drain 22 are filtered thereby improving the degree of contamination caused by foreign substances when using the rainwater as vegetation water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102607542-B1", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "the number of times of air washing and or water washing of the filter medium 300f may vary depending on the degree of contamination of the filter medium 300f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101313936-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "naturally the lower spigot 208 interlocked with the float opens and after a certain period of time the rainwater stored in the initial excellent tank is completely discharged to prevent decay due to the residue and to prepare for the next rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200322626-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "vortex induction block body for quickly entering the circular tub through the guide groove supported to be located directly above the block body in the manhole to form a submerged motor pump body for discharging rainwater and sewage flowing into the manhole and a flow path in contact with the submerged motor pump body to close the bottom of the circular tank suction nozzle is formed in the distal end of the suction pipe formed in the expansion the suction nozzle is located in the suction nozzle is connected to the motor pump in rotation and the vortex induction consisting of a screw type impeller to induce vortex generation inside the circular bath when rotating characterized in that it comprises a pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "according to claim 2 or 3 wherein each side of the outer wall of the block formed with openings are formed integrally with a column for standing up the outer wall block according to the opening is formed the opening acts from the upper end of the outer wall block according to the top plate installation rainwater storage tank having a storage block having a weight reduction structure characterized in that formed in a u shape so that the occurrence of cracks from the upper side of the column to the upper end of the outer wall block by the load to be"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition in the excellent storage tank of the present invention by forming the outer wall block and the storage block in the hexahedral structure with the upper and lower sides open while the opening is formed as described above compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure with the upper and lower plates closed the raw material cost is reduced along with this there is another purpose of making the outer wall block and the storage block and the cons