h upper end of the outer wall blocks 10 and 10a and the storage block 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "at this time the rain inlet 45 may be formed in the upper plate 40 as described above but the upper end of the outer wall block 10 10a that is the outer wall according to the rain storage tank 1 of the present invention buried underground in the case of rainwater drain port 46 for draining the rainwater temporarily stored in the rainwater storage tank 1 of the present invention preferably the bottom surface of the rainwater storage tank 1 that is the reservoir bottom plate portion 54 note that it is formed in advance with the rain inlet 45 formed on the outer wall block 10 10a so as to be positioned in a diagonal direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "rainwater storage tank with a storage block of the weight reduction structure for the present invention in the rainwater storage tank to be buried underground to temporarily store rainwater to discharge when necessary both sides are closed and both sides are the upper and lower sides while the opening is formed openings are formed in each of the four sides of the outer wall block structure in which the outer wall is formed by using the outer wall block of the open hexahedral structure and the storage block of the hexahedral structure having the upper and lower sides is installed and the opening of the outer wall block and the storage block are at the same time a separate block connection member is coupled to each one edge portion of the outer wall block and the storage block in contact with each other to form a connection between the blocks and each of the outer wall block and the storage block interconnected by the block connection member by fitting the top plate on the top and forming a sealed rainwater reservoir compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure in which the plate and the lower plate are integrally formed by the pillar there is an excellent effect of reducing the overall weight by reducing the cross sectional area of the block itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408175-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a light shielding hemispherical mining film 20 installed on the ground so that sunlight can be incident on a livestock field 21 formed in the ground the greenhouse 10 is provided with a solar cell module 12 installed on the roof 11 so as to be able to produce electric power by incident solar light a livestock field 21 and a barn 30 which is addressed to the livestock field 21 so that the livestock can use the livestock field 21 and solar light can be incident on the livestock field 21 the livestock manure that is formed in the lower part of the barn 30 and is collected in the barn 30 is used for fermentation of methane to be used as a fermentation broth of a compost or to be used for liquefaction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408175-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention for achieving the above object the first aspect of the present invention is directed to a fused composite livestock system in which solar light is incident on a livestock field 21 formed in the ground a light shielding hemispherical light shielding film 20 provided on the ground and a light shielding film 20 disposed around the light shielding film 20 so that plants can be grown therein a greenhouse 10 in which a solar cell module 12 is installed so as to produce a greenhouse 10 and a greenhouse 10 in which a livestock is used in a livestock field 21 30 that is connected to the livestock field 21 so that sunlight can be incident on the cattle 30 manure fermentation by supplying manure and using it as the fermentation solution of the compost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "to precipitate the untreated fine solids in the first settling tank 130 and the fluid introduced from the first settling tank 130"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a solid separator 232 and a solid separator 232 a first processing unit 230 including an oil water separator 234 and a solids separator 232 formed under the enclosing hollow shape to separate outflow water and oil components and a sedimentation tank 238 for storing solids a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation storage tank 410 in which contaminants included in the effluent are precipitated is formed and fine pollutants and effluent are purified a second processing unit 240 provided with a microfiltration wall 440 to a cartridge porous filter 282 in which a third inlet hole 206 into which the effluent treated by the second processing unit 240 is introduced is formed and a plurality of refinery holes 510 are formed on the outer periphery to finally purify the effluent the inlet and outlet member 284 provided in the cartridge porous filter 282 and having a plurality of inlet and outlet holes 520 on the outer periphery the cartridge porous filter 282 and the inlet member 284 are fixed to a fixing part 288 and a third processing unit 250 including a filter support member 286 connected to the fixing unit 288 a storage tank 280 for storing effluent treated with non point pollutants by the third processing unit 250 and a drainage system in which a discharge line 260 is formed to discharge the effluent treated with non point pollutants and an effluent pipe 214 through which the effluent is waterproofed is formed on one side of the storage tank 280"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in the non point pollution backwash automation system that treats non point pollutants generated by precipitation including a pre treatment tank and a screen tank formed with a partition wall therebetween the pre treatment tank is connected to a pipe at the bottom of the partition wall at a predetermined height inside and overflows an advection pipe for supplying the raw water accommodated therein to the screen tank a drain door provided at the bottom of the bulkhead to open and close only in the direction of the pretreatment tank from the screen tank to discharge all remaining water in the screen tank to the pretreatment tank it is provided on the floor and consists of a drain pump for pumping the residual water accommodated in the pre treatment tank and the screen tank has a perforated panel to filter out foreign substances while the raw water flowing into the lower part through the advection pipe moves upstream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition it is a system that physically stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank without electronic devices by utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater thereby reducing maintenance costs and providing a physical rainwater utilization system that does not require frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "the physical rainwater utilization system according to the present invention is a system that stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank by a physical method without electronic devices utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater and has the advantage of reducing maintenance costs and not requiring frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_117", "text": "as a result cavitation can be prevented and the impeller of the fire pump can be protected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100752792-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "subsequently the amount of rainwater transferred to the flow regulating tank 3 is controlled to increase rapidly and a certain amount of air is supplied through an diffuser installed at the bottom of the flow regulating tank 3 to prevent sedimentation and decay of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102097635-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in the rainwater storage device a storage means 10 for allowing 