verflow portion at the top a sewage box connected to the first outlet hole of the rainwater storage tank through a connecting pipe to store rainwater discharged from the rainwater storage tank wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a bottom of the rainwater storage tank body corresponding to a lower portion of the rainwater reservoir a container seating portion formed in a groove shape in the portion the upper structure is provided with a lifting hook and is characterized in that it comprises a container which is collected in the container seating portion to collect the contaminants introduced to the rainwater reservoir body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in the first paragraph in order to prevent the decay of water stored in the above mentioned rainwater storage tank 200 a stirring unit 500 is installed in the center of the bottom surface of the above mentioned rainwater storage tank 200 so that a flow is formed a superior storage structure for a road characterized by further comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a method for storing rainwater on a road characterized in that when the water level of the above rainwater storage tank 200 reaches the minimum water level h2 the agitating unit 500 is driven to form a flow to prevent decay of the water stored in the above rainwater storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the present invention proposes a method for storing rainwater on a road using the above described rainwater storage structure characterized in that when the water level of the rainwater storage tank 200 has not reached the minimum water level h2 the agitating unit 500 is not driven and when the water level of the rainwater storage tank 200 has reached the minimum water level h2 the agitating unit 500 is driven to form a flow to prevent decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the present invention proposes a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention provides a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a temperature lower than the preset temperature water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 and at the same time water is supplied into the rainwater storage tank 200 by the bypass pipe 620 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 .the present invention proposes a rainwater storage structure for a road and a rainwater storage method using the same which can prevent urban flood damage caused by localized heavy rain due to climate change and distortion of the water circulation system due to overdevelopment of urban areas.figure 1 below illustrates an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "when the water level of the rainwater storage tank 200 reaches the minimum 