ame 210 from the grating insertion tube 120 and the grating frame 210 is separated from the grinding frame 210 and a plurality of the soil inflow teeth 240 for inflowing into the interior of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101314575-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "another object of the present invention by lifting the entire rainwater treatment unit including the membrane module at the top of the storage tank to replace or repair and then install it in place very easy to maintain and can be easily applied to new and existing facilities as well therefore when the present technology is applied to a simple rainwater storage tank that is already installed the present invention provides a water treatment apparatus for using rainwater to contribute to securing water resources as well as existing excellent storage effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "therefore to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank 30 the above described rainwater inflow prevention device 100 is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_144", "text": "water generated in nature such as rainwater and fog may be collected through the smart water collection system 10 of the present invention and specifically the first storage tank 140 of the tree type water collection facility 100 the bench type water collection system it may be temporarily collected through the second storage tank 220 of the facility 200 and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605267-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "applying a structural separation system that combines the swirl swirl method and the filtration method together in a single device at the bottom of the device preventing re injuries of sediment which is a disadvantage of the swirl method by applying a flotation prevention means in which sediment deposited is not injured even in the formation of the vortex and filtering the laminar flow forming t