delay of the floatation rate is passed through the advection tube is introduced into the contact reaction tank wherein the foamed filter medium is disposed at a middle portion of the contact reaction tank the treated water is introduced into the upper portion of the contact reaction tank and flows in the lower direction and passes through the foamed filter medium further comprising an air supply unit for supplying air to the lower portion of the foamed filter medium to induce the floating of the sludge deposited on the foamed filter medium when the foamed filter medium is occluded by the sludge wherein the treatment tank is provided with an advection pipe having an a shaped structure at one side of the upper part of the contact reaction tank and treatment water staying in the contact reaction tank lower region passing through the foamed filter medium in the contact reaction tank through the admission pipe and a rainwater reservoir for storing incoming rainwater and further comprising an inflow control unit for allowing the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank to flow into the inflow reaction tank or the treatment water tank depending on the degree of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 153 may flow into the inflow reaction tank 131 or the treatment water tank 160 depending on the degree of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102227198-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "to this end although not shown in the drawing the rainwater pipe connected to the storage tank 10 may be provided with a pollution detection sensor that detects the degree of contamination of incoming rainwater and a shut off valve module that blocks the inflow of rainwater from the rainwater pipe"}]</data>
