, "build", "decay", "mix", "push", "pack", "assemble", "step", "join", "overwhelm", "support", "penetrate", "fall", "hoist", "submerge", "move", "locate", "latch", "reduce", "bind", "plug", "may", "sand", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "decompose", "design", "net", "spot", "must", "propose", "deposit", "absorb", "shield", "transfer", "construct", "desorb", "charge", "know", "transport", "finish", "rinse", "galvanize", "excavate", "drain", "shape", "select", "keep", "continue", "bypass", "be", "conduct", "flood", "suppress", "warm", "combine", "apply", "drill", "contaminate", "weld", "interfere", "rise", "tank", "reach", "jet", "sld", "achieve", "refer", "increase", "dump", "project", "invent", "leach", "retain", "disclose", "melt", "will", "provide", "wrap", "contain", "space", "uncoil", "ship", "compare", "scale", "enhance", "water", "leak", "arrange", "reuse", "size", "process", "precede", "limit", "oil", "do", "refill", "settle", "create", "lock", "bury", "exceed", "consider", "baffle", "weave", "inflow", "seat", "spawn", "box", "cover", "show", "configure", "derive", "cool", "start", "fit", "enable", "guide", "perform", "act", "consist", "open", "mean", "supply", "use", "propeller", "cut", "draw", "prefabricate", "stagnate", "extend", "control", "case", "transmit", "bite", "need", "monitor", "elevate", "exist", "collect", "instal", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drainage tank that has a function to prevent the inflow of pests etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object in a drainage tank configured to introduce and discharge sewage such as rain and sewage of daily life and to prevent the discharge of odors generated therein or the introduction of mice and pests accommodating sewage inside a main body having an inlet space an upper inlet part having an open upper part to introduce wastewater a side inlet part for introducing wastewater on one side and a discharge part for discharging the wastewater accommodated in the inflow space on the other side a blocking means having a blocking net seated on the main body to block foreign substances in the sewage and a vertical pipe for introducing the sewage into the inflow space and a moving pipe that moves up and down according to the level of sewage in the inflow space on the vertical pipe to block odors or prevent rats and pests from entering and is formed integrally or separately on the moving pipe to generate buoyancy according to the level of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank the water tank is not affected by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust and in particular the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank 1 according to at least one of the preceding claims characterized in that a sensor device is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining element 11 can be derived from the measurement data of the sensor device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101230730-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "according to the present invention as described above while planting vegetation on the side of the vegetation soil while water is continuously supplied to the vegetation through the water storage unit and the water supply surface rain water in the water storage unit through the water supply path formed in rain water by allowing heavy water to be filled such as eco friendly and continuous supply of moisture to the vegetation without additional management work it is very easy to maintain and manage the vegetation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102047325-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a storage tank 20 into which rainwater flows into the road rain gutter 10 buoyancy material 30 is installed in the storage tank 20 a sensor 40 installed inside the storage tank 20 consists of including when the buoyancy material 30 is raised by the excellent buoyancy introduced into the storage tank 20 is in contact with the sensor 40 the waterproof door 100 is automatically operated a guide 50 is further installed at the bottom of the sensor 40 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement along the guide 50 one side 53 of the guide 50 is attached to the inner wall of the storage tank 20 and the other side of the guide 50 is formed with a projection 55 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement by the buoyancy while being bitten by the projection 55 the storage tank movable structure using buoyancy characterized in that the water level control material 70 is installed in the storage tank 20 to adjust the waterproof door movable water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346424-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the gravel bottom penetration facility installed at the bottom of the storage tank should be more than 10 13 mm per hour considering the infiltration rate of the lower layer soil and should be installed in the area where the function is not degraded by freezing in winter.the present invention is to solve the problems as described above the object is to provide a storage and permeation interlocking device of rainwater effluent which can easily adjust the size and shape and excellent workability by using a plastic cell as a pillar of the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101704960-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the malodor shielding means 20 includes a water tub 21 having a discharge hole 22 for discharging excess rainwater and wastewater while receiving a predetermined amount of rainwater and wastewater flowing thereinto the user may select any one of the a cut off portion 23 and the rotation cut off portion 24 so as to cut off the odor according to the water level a of the water tank 21 and the water level of the wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100429686-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "as described above according to the present invention the outflow tank of the present invention treats initial pollutants in various ways in order to infiltrate and treat the pollutants into the sewage treatment plant in the event of rain it is possible to minimize contamination of natural rivers due to excellent discharge thereby reducing the amount of river pollution and an excellent effect of preventing an excessive facility investment cost"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6132141-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "3 is an example of a sewer rainwater switching type storage facility according to the present invention and is a diagram in the case of allowing overflow discharge to a river in the middle of rainfall.fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101736743-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage sludge tank for a sewage sludge sewage treatment system comprising a pretreatment tank in which flocs are formed and the pollutants are settled while overflowing a filtration tank in which contaminants are filtered by a filtration unit including a floating filter medium between filtration nets formed at upper and lower portions after inflow of contaminant removed water via the pretreatment tank and a washing filtr