g a baffle forming a overflow portion at the top a sewage box connected to the first outlet hole of the rainwater storage tank through a connecting pipe to store rainwater discharged from the rainwater storage tank wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a bottom of the rainwater storage tank body corresponding to a lower portion of the rainwater reservoir a container seating portion formed in a groove shape in the portion the upper structure is provided with a lifting hook and is characterized in that it comprises a container which is collected in the container seating portion to collect the contaminants introduced to the rainwater reservoir body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater drainage for roads apparatus for draining of rain water for road the present invention relates to a rainwater drainage system for roads and more particularly between a plurality of stationary grates provided with rainwater inlet holes in the grating and each of the fixed grates while being lifted up and down according to the lifting of the buoyant body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_146", "text": "in other words when the torrential rain starts an overflow phenomenon may occur due to insufficient space accommodated in the first storage tank 140 the second storage tank 220 and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore according to the present invention it is possible to efficiently use the storages stored in the road boundary block since the water is stored without discharging the water in the wet state immediately after the rain and the storm is drained to the ground when the ground is dry.1 is a perspective view showing a state in which a road boundary block according to an embodiment of the present invention is installed fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "moreover the rainwater remaining in the purification treatment tank 10 may contain more non point pollutants which may decay faster"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "according to the above configuration and action according to the present invention the downstream circulation hole connecting the plurality of storage block valves to communicate with each other is provided to be opened and closed by the valve so that the storage space is flexibly adjusted according to the rainfall during rain and thus the unused storage space is always kept clean"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052947-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain storm event these storage tanks can be overwhelmed thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system a body of water or a river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the first object of the present invention due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rain the initial rainwater that has not been purified to exceed the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage terminal treatment plant is discharged to the stream it is to provide an initial excellent storage processing system using a storage tank to prevent the contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-8617390-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "embodiments can also include a second pressure gradient system in fluid communication with the treatment tank where the second pressure gradient system acts on head space in the treatment tank to create a pressure gradient serving to transport head space gases towards the leaching field which may also be referred to as a drain field downstream of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101964855-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the fine dust and contaminants in the roadway 114 may be generated by the exhaust gas of the vehicle c the tire wear of the vehicle c and the asphalt wear of the roadway 114 and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "it is possible to prevent the direct exposure to direct sunlight rain and wind by preventing the rainwater storage tank of the uniform color pattern from being covered with the inside of the rainwater storage compartment or breakage of the water can be prevented and the decay of the water can be prevented and the ceiling portion is formed with a sloped slope at a constant angle so that the snow or rain can flow without falling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101058919-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this collection device is designed to automatically collect and remove only the rainwater so that the initial rain which contains various pollutants in the early days of rain does not mix with the relatively clean rainwater afterwards"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2895662-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the capacity of such a drainage system as at risk of being overwhelmed with water during storms and it is consequently desirable to prevent an excessive amount of water arriving at a reservoir or tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a catchment facility 100 for collecting rainwater in a catchment area a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100 a natural vegetation decomposing tank 300 installed at a downstream side of the contaminant separating tank 200 and for treating non point pollutants discharged with rainwater discharged from the contaminant separating tank 200 a first storage tank 400 installed at a downstream side of the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 having a membrane filtration tank 500 for storing the treated water treated in the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 a second storage tank 600 installed at a downstream side of the first storage tank 400 for storing the treated water treated by the membrane filtration unit 500 and it is composed of a transmission and distribution facility 700 for supplying the treated water treated in the second storage tank 600 to reuse water it is installed in the rear of the water collecting facility 100 and further comprises an initial rain water treatment tank 120 for separately treating the initial rain water falling in the initial rain flowing from the water collecting facility 100 the initial rainwater treatment tank 120 cylindrical rotating portion 121 for discharging the particulate matter contained in the initial rain water to the bottom by the centrifugal force while the initial rain water flows in a tangential direction it is installed on the downstream side of the cylindrical rotating part 121 and precipitates the fine particulate matter in the treated water treated by the cylindrical rotating part 121 the inclined coupled to the bottom of the porous flat plate 131 formed with a plurality of perforations and its lower end eco friendly hybrid rainwater recycling system including an initial rainwater treatment tank comprising a solid liquid separator 124 having a solid liquid separation plate 125"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "eco friendly hybrid rainwater recycling system including the initial rainwater treatment tank of the present invention the water collecting facility 100 for collecting rainwater in the catchment target area a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100 a natural vegetation decomposing tank 300 installed at a downstream side of the contaminant separating tank 200 and for treating non point pollutants discharged with rainwater discharged from the contaminant separating tank 200 a first storage tank 400 installed at a downstream side of the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 having a membrane filtration tank 500 for storing the treated water treated in the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 a second storage tank 600 installed at a downstream side of the first storage tank 400 for storing the treated water treated by the membrane filtration unit 500 and a water supply and drainage system 700 for supplying the treated water treated in the second storage tank 600 to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "partitioning means for partitioning the maintenance tank and the treatment tank the upper part being blocked and the lower part being in communication first filtration means detachably located in the treatment tank and configured to filter adsorb and remove contaminants contained in road surface drainage that rises from a lower portion of the treatment tank to an upper side and it is installed on the upper side of the rain catcher the maintenance tank and the treatment tank to have a size covering the entire area thereof an auxiliary shield plate for shielding the upper opening of the treatment tank is provided on one side of the bottom surface the road drain drain lid formed at a predetermined position with an open passage for forcing flow into the inner space road drainage treatment device having an excellent receiving function including a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "partitioning means for partitioning the maintenance tank and the treatment tank the upper part being blocked and the lower part being in communication first filtration means detachably located in the treatment tank and configured to filter adsorb and remove contaminants contained in road surface drainage that rises from a lower portion of the treatment tank to an upper side and an auxiliary shielding plate installed at an upper side of the rain receiver the maintenance tank and the treatment tank to cover an area of the whole thereof and having an auxiliary shield plate for shielding the upper opening of the treatment tank on one side of the bottom surface and receiving the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as a result deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20 the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "since the penetration and storage tank for water circulation according to one embodiment of the present invention are light in weight and can be fastened in an assembly type the construction work is easy and they are treated with nano silver so rain water can be maintained for a long time we have a hybrid hybrid reinforced structural system that significantly reduces rainwater contamination due to microbe generation etc"}]</data>
