  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100522326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "limestone drain for sedimentation and removal of sludge contained in the runoff flowing out of the pit during mountainous highway construction a storage tank for storing the treated water discharged from the limestone drain but discharged when a predetermined amount is introduced in consideration of the case where a large amount of groundwater flows out due to rainy season or hydrogeological site conditions aquifer and a reaction tank for removing heavy metals contained in the acid drainage by mixing red mud powder with the discharge water discharged from the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200340109-Y1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "limestone drain for sedimentation and removal of sludge contained in the runoff flowing out of the pit during mountainous highway construction a storage tank for storing the treated water discharged from the limestone drain but discharged when a predetermined amount is introduced in consideration of the case where a large amount of groundwater flows out due to rainy season or hydrogeological site conditions aquifer and a reaction tank that mixes red mud powder with effluent discharged from the storage tank and treats acidic drainage on the basis of drinking water quality standards"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101893417-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in one example the control device receives the incoming water quality value and the flow rate value from the first sensor derives the influent load receives the outflow water quality value from the second sensor receives the temperature value from the third sensor a data portion for data wise the water quality by temperature a driving unit for driving the valve to introduce the water into the pre treatment tank and the bioreactor the real time influent load value is derived from the real time influent water quality value and the real time flow value from the first sensor and the real time runoff water quality value is derived from the derived real time influent load and the real the real time recirculated water load value is obtained from the fourth sensor by receiving the real time recirculated water quality value and the real time flow rate value from the fourth sensor and the real real time flow rate value is received and a real time connection load is derived and when the real time reflux water load and real time connection water load exceeds the above mentioned additional connection water load and additional reflux water load the valve is driven to the pre so that the real time counter current load and the real time connection water load are set to the above characterized in that it comprises a load by driving the valve and can be linked or less wake analysis unit such that flowing into the bioreactor through the raw water inlet line.as described above according to the system of the present invention in the continuous treatment of the wastewater it is possible to automatically determine whether or not the pre treatment of the reflux water and the connection water is performed by the sensing basis thereby reducing the cost required for the pretreatment and improving the treatment efficiency of the pretreatment it is possible to improve the treatment efficiency of the whole system by preventing the load of the bioreactor.1 is a block diagram illustrating a system of the present invention 2 is a schematic view showing an example of a bioreactor which is a constitution of the present invention 3 is a block diagram showing a detailed configuration of a control apparatus which is a constitution of the present invention figures 4a and 4b are operational state diagrams of the system of the present invention 5 is a schematic view showing an example of a pretreatment tank which is a constituent of the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101138988-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "as described above the present invention enables to filter the contaminants to be swept into the runoff such as rainwater through the porous media while improving the processing capacity compared to the conventional water contaminant removal device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a second modular wetland infrastructure that physically filters influent through vegetation based modules a sedimentation tank installed at one side of the lower end of the modular wetland infrastructure to collect influent water that has passed through the modular wetland infrastructure and to precipitate foreign substances that are not filtered a contact oxidation tank installed at the bottom of the modular wetland infrastructure and having a modular microbial contact material installed to biologically purify water introduced from the settling tank combined with the modular wetland infrastructure and modular catalytic oxidation and filtration equipment including and the filtration tank connected to the contact oxidation tank and finally removes the fine sludge and suspended matter not filtered through the filter medium installed therein one river lake or runoff clarifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101155948-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in order to prevent this the inflow water distribution pipe 240 is provided and as the rainfall outflow water is supplied into the second media layer 221 having a predetermined depth through the inflow water distribution pipe 240 the entire second filter layer 221 is provided"}, {"pat_id": "US-8221029-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "conduit 24 may be constructed of pvc but other materials can be used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426715-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank and the initial excellent effluent which has been filtered by the stencil strainer flows into the storage tank and stores the initial excellent effluent while storing the initial excellent effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674110-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes and modifications may be made without departing from the scope of the present invention.1 rainwater catcher 2 3 by drain pipe 4 infiltration ball 10 penetration ditch 10a infiltration ditch inflow section 11 perforated fan for flow equalization 12 shovel rake 12a contamination 13 flooding bumps 14 drainage filter fiber 15 observation 15a 15b plug 20 pretreatment tank 20a pretreatment tank inflow section 21 sand pack 22 stagnant water outlet 30 runoff water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "an influent distribution step of reducing the energy of river water lake water or effluent flowing into the water purification apparatus through a flow distribution tank and evenly distributing it to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step of biologically purifying the inflow water having passed through the precipitation step into the contact oxidation tank having the microbial contact material installed therein river water that combines modular wetland infrastructure and modular catalytic oxidation and filtration facilities including a 4th purification step that finally removes fine sludge and suspended solids that were not filtered through the contact oxidation tank through a filter tank equipped with filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "to precipitate the untreated fine solids in the first settling tank 130 and the fluid introduced from the first settling tank 130"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a solid separator 232 and a solid separator 232 a first processing unit 230 including an oil water separator 234 and a solids separator 232 formed under the enclosing hollow shape to separate outflow water and oil components and a sedimentation tank 238 for storing solids a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation storage tank 410 in which contaminants included in the effluent are precipitated is formed and fine pollutants and effluent are purified a second processing unit 240 provided with a microfiltration wall 440 to a cartridge porous filter 282 in which a third inlet hole 206 into which the effluent treated by the second processing unit 240 is introduced is formed and a plurality of refinery holes 510 are formed on the outer periphery to finally purify the effluent the inlet and outlet member 284 provided in the cartridge porous filter 282 and having a plurality of inlet and outlet holes 520 on the outer periphery the cartridge porous filter 282 and the inlet member 284 are fixed to a fixing part 288 and a third processing unit 250 including a filter support member 286 connected to the fixing unit 288 a storage tank 280 for storing effluent treated with non point pollutants by the third processing unit 250 and a drainage system in which a discharge line 260 is formed to discharge the effluent treated with non point pollutants and an effluent pipe 214 through which the effluent is waterproofed is formed on one side of the storage tank 280"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in the non point pollution backwash automation system that treats non point pollutants generated by precipitation including a pre treatment tank and a screen tank formed with a partition wall therebetween the pre treatment tank is connected to a pipe at the bottom of the partition wall at a predetermined height inside and overflows an advection pipe for supplying the raw water accommodated therein to the screen tank a drain door provided at the bottom of the bulkhead to open and close only in the direction of the pretreatment tank from the screen tank to discharge all remaining water in the screen tank to the pretreatment tank it is provided on the floor and consists of a drain pump for pumping the residual water accommodated in the pre treatment tank and the screen tank has a perforated panel to filter out foreign substances while the raw water flowing into the lower part through the advection pipe moves upstream"}, {"pat_id": "US-5366322-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "because the compartments are concentrically arranged water which manages to leak from a particular compartment for example by passing beneath the flexible compartment wall may only pass into an adjacent compartment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100791422-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "an object of the present invention is a tank having a hollow inside the inlet formed on the upper surface the storage tank and the narrowing storage tank formed by partitioning the inner space of the lower side of the inlet by the partition wall respectively the narrow surface on the upper surface of the storage tank a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101604772-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "the surface water introduced into the settling tank 34 contains floating matters due to erosion and scouring phenomenon in accordance with the flow of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-7780855-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "these two factors combined would result in greater total contaminants being brought to the separator tank during peak flows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101959509-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a monitoring system for a rainfall runoff pollutant filtration apparatus comprising a rainfall runoff having an opening at an upper end thereof an outlet formed at one or more sides of the lower runoff the filtration unit is installed inside the main body and filters rainwater effluent flowing into the opening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101450430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "1 to 3 rainfall runoff on roads and other road surfaces is introduced into an existing waterway through an induction waterway and a separate flow distribution structure a pretreatment tank and various abatement facilities are installed in the existing waterway it can be seen that the initial effluent is introduced into the abatement facility and the rainwater effluent from which the non point pollutant is removed through the abatement facility is reintroduced into the existing canal thereby removing the nonpoint contamination of the initial effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300414-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition it is equipped with an inlet line for introducing raw water and an external carbon source into the anoxic tank and by automatically adjusting the inflow of raw water and external carbon source the denitrification efficiency of the anaerobic tank can be improved operating costs can be reduced and the amount of external carbon source can be reduced this can be reduced to prevent further contamination by runoff"}, {"pat_id": "US-9427706-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a portion of the input water prior to the inlet at 80 is directed to the bottom inlet of the lifting column 76 as indicated 88"}, {"pat_id": "US-4934404-A", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as a result it can be stored for extended periods without loss of the water into the ground through leakage or into the air through evaporation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102209260-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank in which rainfall runoff is introduced and non point pollutants are pretreated and a porous concrete cobble layer installed on the impermeable ground and bypassing the rainfall runoff flowing from the pretreatment tank including the porous concrete cable layer a plurality of porous concrete cables are uniformly and continuously arranged and formed on the impermeable ground the diameter of the porous concrete cable is 50 mm to 500 mm the porosity of the porous concrete cable is 5 to 40 the permeability coefficient of the porous concrete cable is 0.01 cm sec to 10 cm sec the pretreatment tank a settling portion in which the rainfall runoff water settles an overflow unit including a swash plate for reducing a flow velocity while the settled rainfall runoff overflows and a filtering unit for filtering non point pollutants of the rainfall runoff passing through the overflow unit including the filtration unit is composed of a net an oil adsorbent is installed the oil adsorbent is provided as a material of polyurethane or urethane foam including a photocatalyst layer coated on the outside of the porous concrete cable the photocatalyst layer zno wo 3 zro 2 sno 2 cds zns nb 2 o 53 zro 2 srtio 3 ktao 3 ni k 4 nb 6 o 17 cds znscdse gap cdte mose it comprises at least any one selected from the group consisting of 2 and wse 2 rainwater runoff and non point source reduction system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101349613-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sand filtration apparatus to reduce the non point pollutants contained in the rainfall runoff and to supply the filtered rainwater to the underground 110 being installed on the lower side of the road surface 120 the first filtration layer 151 the second filtration layer 152 the flow distribution pipe 40 tube the third filtration layer 153 and the lower management space 130 filter box 60 for receiving and it is configured to include and the settling tank 80 in communication with the filter box 60 the first filtration layer 151 lid block assembly 10 is installed on the lower side of the road surface 120 and and a sand layer 20 disposed below the lid block assembly 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}]</data>
