  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101560279-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage tank for mixing storages of fresh water and fresh water a main body 100 on which a fine flow path 200 is formed the top side of which is flown out and and is formed as a lower settled space relative to the clearance passage 200 so as to be formed on the clearance passage 200 and to deposit only the initial clearance of the clearance moving in the clearance passage 200 an initial fine precipitation tank 300 the upper part of the bleed passage 200 is opened a baffle wall 400 is formed around the baffle 200 so as to prevent escape of the baffle introduced onto the baffle 200 one side of the escape prevention wall 400 is connected to the end of the roof 500 so that the storm that flows along the slope of the roof 500 of the house can be introduced into the clearance passage 200 the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the main flow path 110 lt rti gt the downflow channel is formed along the flow direction of the stormwater a first space 121 and a second space 122 that divides the inner space of the main body 100 into a first space 121 and a second space 122 123 are formed on the partition wall 120 the overflow passage 123 is formed at a predetermined distance from the lower surface of the main body 100 the storm inlet 110 is formed on the storeroom 200 where the first space 121 is located and a fresh water inlet 140 formed in the second space 122 and into which fresh water flows into the second space 122 and a mixed water outlet 150 formed in the second space 122 and mixed with water mixed with fresh water and fresh water stored in the second space 122 to be discharged to the outside of the main body 100 the mixed water outlet 150 is formed below the fresh water inlet 140 when the water level of the mixed water is lower than the position of the fresh water inlet 140 the fresh water inlet 140 is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a soil cement layer formed to a predetermined thickness on the bottom surface and an inner surface of the underground space formed by digging the ground of the outer side of the building to a predetermined depth and the soil cement layer formed on the bottom surface of the underground space portion a sand layer formed at a height an activated carbon layer formed at a predetermined height above the sand layer a gravel layer formed at a predetermined height above the activated carbon layer and an opening in the underground space seated horizontally on an upper surface of the gravel layer a fire fighting water supply tank having a shielding plate to shield the a first hollow rainwater inlet pipe inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank by vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and having one end inserted into the through hole formed in the boundary stone perpendicular to the outer wall of the building a hollow second rainwater inlet pipe that is installed as an inlet and has one end connected to the eaves gutter that collects rainwater falling to the roof of the building and the other end vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank vertically penetrating the shielding plate of the fire water supply tank and vertically buried in the fire water supply tank with the upper end exposed to the outside an inner space is provided an opening is formed in the center of the upper surface and a plurality of water collecting holes are formed on the lower outer surface the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the a hollow water intake unit introduced into the inner space through a water collecting hole one end is connected to an opening formed in the water intake unit so that fire water collected in the inner space of the water intake unit is supplied and the other end is connected to an opening formed in the steel pipe pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2556400-Y2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "as described above according to the present invention according to the use of hot water water from which dissolved gas dissolved oxygen has been removed by a membrane deaerator according to use of hot water is supplied from a receiving tank to a hot water tank via a makeup water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the non point contaminant removing device 10 may be rainwater collected from a roof of a building in addition to the above mentioned sump well"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052943-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 92 roof 93 washing wastewater spray device 94 washing wastewater recirculation mechanism 100 ground 101 drainage groove 102 collecting drainage groove 103 convex 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 107 left vertical frame 108 right vertical frame 10 horizontal frame 111 water supply pipe 112 drainage nozzle 113 intermediate pipe 114 cleaning waste water supply pipe 115 cleaning waste supply pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101627819-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent freezing clothes cloths clothes etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100766243-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "by forming a light double blocking the light and cool the upper side of the water tank water is easily heated in the summer to prevent the occurrence of a lot of microorganisms or inhabit and in the winter a lot of snow piled up on the upper side of the water tank the present invention relates to a prefabricated roof for a water tank in which snow is frozen and impurities and dirty water are prevented from flowing into the water tank due to seams gaps etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100766243-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "it is an object of the present invention to provide a prefabricated roof for a water tank which prevents the accumulated snow or frozen snow from melting and prevents dirty water from flowing into seams or gaps thereby maintaining the cleanliness of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100766243-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "this prefabricated roof 1 2 is formed so that even if a lot of snow in winter continues to accumulate or the snow melts and frozen again so that it does not accumulate for a long time unlike the conventional water tank with a flat upper side seams or gaps foreign objects or dirty water will not be introduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100766243-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in addition since the load reinforcement bar 8 can be installed and reinforced according to the water tank capacity a problem that occurs when the roof is installed by placing the bar in the center of the upper surface side of the water tank or by installing the bar in the center of the inner side of the water tank that is in the center of the upper surface side it is possible to reduce the inconvenience such as when pressed or during the internal cleaning work.as described above the present invention is easy to assemble and install can be installed on the existing water tank can be installed by adding the number of parts according to the capacity of the water tank excellent support reinforcement water tank even when used for a long time it is effective to prevent the occurrence and habitat of microorganisms to prevent the inflow of dirty water to maintain the cleanliness of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "manual valve operation method is unrealistic because the manager must operate the valve in the early stage of rainfall and it has the disadvantage of high cost and difficulty of maintenance such as failure when using devices such as flow meters and sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a block for storing wind and solar power in rain or rain in a storage tank 38 while providing blocks for wind and solar power generation in a roof such as a road or a building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102812276-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "although the preferred embodiments of the present invention have been described in detail above the scope of the present invention is not limited thereto and various modifications and improvements made by those skilled in the art using the basic concept of the present invention defined in the following claims also fall within the scope of the present invention.g1 landfill layer g2 cover layer 1 leachate recovery section 11 leachate plate 111 leachate channel 12 blocking member 13 leachate drain 2 leachate purification unit 21 leachate inlet line 22 purification unit 211 purification body 211a 1st body 211b 1st purification space 211c 2nd body 211d 2nd purification space 222 ceramic filter 223 1st activated carbon layer 224 2nd activated carbon layer 225 zeolite layer 226 silica sand layer 227 compartment filter 23 purification storage 231 storage space 24 natural stone 25 heating section 3 landfill gas recovery section 31 gas pipe 311 through hole 32 flow pipe 33 landfill gas purification unit 34 storage tank 35 landfill gas pump 36 control valve 4 high temperature sterilization unit 41 steam generator 42 storage unit connection line 43 steam line 44 steam pump 5 uv sterilization section 51 substrate section 52 uv ray generation unit 6 dust suppression unit 61 spray line 62 drum 63 spraying unit 64 supply pipe 65 spray pump 7 wheel washing unit 71 tunnel section 711 car wash area 711a entrance 711b exit 72 lower wash section 73 side wash section 74 rear wash section 741 hinge block 742 shaft 743 drive motor 744 spray pipe 744a vertical pipe 744b horizontal pipe 75 front wash section 76 wash water supply storage unit 77 sterilization wash unit 78 dry car wash unit 79 car wash water recovery unit 8 pedestrian safety section 8a pedestrian safety passage 81 outer structure 811 entrance 82 frame section 821 pedestrian passage 83 roof 84 blocking 85 1st rail section 86 2nd rail section 87 frame drive unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102368680-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101177255-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "contained in the air which causes a problem that can contaminate the water stored in the water tank.accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above described problems the object of which is to forcibly vent the air inside the stainless steel cylindrical unit assembly type circular water tank to facilitate the flow of air the air due to the enclosed environment it is to provide a ventilation system of a stainless steel cylindrical unit assembled round water tank to prevent contamination in advance.according to the present invention for achieving the above object a bottom plate a circular cylindrical body installed on the top of the bottom plate an upper plate installed on the upper portion of the cylindrical body to cover and protect the cylindrical body the cylindrical body and the top plate a stainless steel cylindrical unit assembly type circular water tank having a finish installed to enclose a solar heat collecting plate wherein the solar heat collecting plate is fixed to the top plate and collects solar heat through a plurality of solar heat collecting cells and is collected through the solar heat collecting plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101016329-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "nothing has been done.the present invention has been proposed in order to solve the conventional problems as described above the object of the construction is to replace the roof of the existing storage tank while being constructed in a simplified structure to block the inflow of dust and lower the construction cost as well as drainage of rain water the present invention provides a reservoir cover device and a reservoir including the same which can smoothly and easily handle odors or harmful gases and in particular the height of the lid can be adjusted according to the reservoir level thereby enabling the adjustment of the storage capacity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200499514-Y1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "here if water is continuously stored in the reservoir 200 there is a risk of the roof collapsing due to the weight of the water but in the present invention the water stored in the reservoir 200 is continuously discharged into the water tank 210 so there is no risk of collapse"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408175-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a light shielding hemispherical mining film 20 installed on the ground so that sunlight can be incident on a livestock field 21 formed in the ground the greenhouse 10 is provided with a solar cell module 12 installed on the roof 11 so as to be able to produce electric power by incident solar light a livestock field 21 and a barn 30 which is addressed to the livestock field 21 so that the livestock can use the livestock field 21 and solar light can be incident on the livestock field 21 the livestock manure that is formed in the lower part of the barn 30 and is collected in the barn 30 is used for fermentation of methane to be used as a fermentation broth of a compost or to be used for liquefaction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408175-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "it is therefore to be understood that the appended claims are intended to cover such modifications and changes as fall within the true scope of the invention.10 greenhouse 11 roof 111 slope 12 solar cell module 20 mining membrane 21 cattle field 30 housing 31 duct 311 perforated plate 40 ventilation part 41 frame 42 inlet 43 outlet 50 filter purifier 51 chamber 52 biofilter 53 diffusion plate 531 through hole 54 exhaust fan 60 manure processing unit 61 contaminant removing tank 62 63 methane production tank 64 filtrate tank 70 collecting tube 80 cogeneration generator 81 gas storage tank 90 excellent water collecting tank 91 water pipe h p hot water pipe m mesh mesh 100 combined animal husbandry system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems according to the prior art described above by heating the water stored in the water tank to be circulated by the convection phenomenon in the summer to cool the water inside the water tank in order to suppress the breeding of microorganisms while improving the water quality of the water stored in the water tank by sterilization in winter the water quality improvement of the roof water tank for extinguishing and preventing freezing by the convection phenomenon by heating the water inside the water tank provided through the main purpose is to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention relates to a heating device for preventing the water quality improvement and freezing of the water tank 1 installed outdoors that is on the roof for fire extinguishing more specifically the inside of the water tank 1 in the form of a float when floated in water above or below a certain temperature the water inside the water tank 1 is heated to inhibit microbial sterilization as well as proliferation and to prevent freezing so that the water tank 1 and the pipe are corroded by the microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "water quality improvement and freeze prevention warming device of fire rooftop water tank to prevent the occurrence of mic as well as to prevent the occurrence of water tank 1 and pipe cracking due to freezing of water to supply fire extinguishing water smoothly"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a container shaped sand container that is disposed on the ground and accommodates water evaporating sand the upper side being opened a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container a cleaning wastewater spraying device for spraying the cleaning wastewater stored in the cleaning wastewater storage tank to the water evaporation sand stored in the sand storage unit a washing waste water recirculation mechanism that recirculates excess washing waste water flowing down through the gaps between the particles of water evaporating sand contained in the sand containing portion to the washing waste water storage tank the soil purification method includes while spraying cleaning wastewater from the cleaning wastewater spraying device on the water evaporation sand accommodated in the sand container the water of the cleaning wastewater adhering to the water evaporation sand is evaporated into the air to remove it from the sandbox introducing the water evaporating sand in which the chelating agent is accumulated for a predetermined period of time in the sand containing unit into the classifying unit and recovering the chelating agent accumulated in the water evaporating sand a method for soil purification wherein a part of the sand discharged from the classification unit is used as water evaporation sand stored in the sand storage unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the non circulating non discharge manure treatment method for purifying the manure and sewage discharged from the toilet the manure treatment method comprises the steps of installing a flush toilet in the toilet the sewage and manure from the flush toilet anaerobic storage tank 10 anaerobic digestion filtering the treated water while treating nitrogen phosphorus and the like which are physically and biologically organic suspended solids and eutrophication agents in the aerobic bioreactor 20 and treating the treated water in the flow regulating tank 30 storing in the anaerobic state of the treated water and stabilizing the stored treatment water while the waste water is sprayed onto the wood chip layer by the water spray nozzle in the organic decay reaction tank 40 while the manure and sewage flows through the adsorption adsorption to the wood chip layer decomposing and removing the organic substances and various suspended substances contained in the step of discharging the leachate the pump well 46 operating a transfer pump that operates when a predetermined water level is reached while storing water removing organic components and nitrogen phosphorus color odor and the like physically and biologically from the advanced treatment tank 50 by contact aeration with the media physically filtration of the discharged water storing the treated water in the second flow rate adjusting tank 60 and stabilizing the stored treated water organic suspended solids remaining in the treated water passing through the wood chip layer and nitrogen phosphorus decomposing the chromaticity odor in the bioreactor 70 and then removing the leachate storing the treated water in the pump well 77 operating the transfer pump when the water level reaches a certain value decolorizing the treated water discharging while discoloring in the disinfection filtration tank 80 storing the treated water in the treated water storage tank 90 and supplying the stored treated water to the toilet and excessively introduced the excess water to the outside jidoe comprises a step of output the rainwater storage tank is installed on the roof of the manure treatment device and rainwater flows into the treatment water storage tank through a pipe and an electric shutoff valve is installed between the rainwater storage tank and the treatment water storage tank so that the water level of the treatment water storage tank is set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "synthetic resin water tanks produced as synthetic resins can be expected to have excellent effects in preventing leakage and corrosion but they are not suitable for use as large tanks installed on the roof of large apartment houses due to their poor ability to handle loads such as large internal water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102724384-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of apartments 33 are installed in the space between a plant factory 41 and another plant factory 41 and the road surface of the access road 15 and the rooftop of the apartment 33 are installed at the same height the upper part of the rooftop of the apartment 33 and the rooftop of the plant factory 41 are connected to each other to install a hollow plate shaped building an emergency shelter 09 and a cultivation space for plants 11 are installed on the upper surface of the hollow plate building and a building formation part in which led lighting 07 is installed on the upper part of the cultivation space a number of water tanks 29 are installed in the outer underground area outside the outer perimeter of the pit a wastewater tank 96 and a sewage tank 97 are installed in a location larger than the installation diameter of the water tank 29 and deeper than the depth of the bottom surface of the pit a water generator 23 is installed on the ground surface with a larger installation diameter than the water tank 29 and a dome outer installation section in which graphene ropes 21 are installed in a net shape on the water generator 23 installed on the opposite side of the water generator 23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387133-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "rainwater contains various suspended substances which causes the storage water to decay making it difficult to store for long periods of time resulting in a decrease in rainwater utilization.in order to achieve the above object by adding a rain filtration filter \u2462 in the process of storing the rainwater collected from the roof of the building or the roof of the rainy weather in the rainwater storage tank in order to achieve the above object by separating the dust or suspended matter and storing only the clean rainwater long term storage prevents decay due to organic substances in rainwater making it possible to use it as water for living and by using a corrosion resistant metal grid filter \u2466 it can be used semi permanently without long term maintenance costs caused by corrosion or aging"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rainwater supply unit that supplies the rinse water and a chelating agent recovery unit that recovers the chelating agent from the cleaning wastewater discharged from the chelating agent removal unit the chelating agent removing unit has a sand rinsing device that sprays or jets rinsing water on the sand separated by the classifying unit to remove the chelating agent held in the sand the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank for receiving and storing cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the sand rinsing device a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 sand rinse device 62 coarse aggregate rinse device 63 washing waste water evaporation device 64 belt conveyor 65 sand supply device 66 rinse water spray device 67 cleaning waste water receiving tank 68 drive roller 68a shaft 69 driven roller 69a shaft 70 conveyor belt 71 support roller 72 guide plate 74 belt conveyor 75 coarse aggregate supply device 76 rinsing water spray device 77 cleaning waste water receiving tank 78 driving roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveyor belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 cleaning waste water discharge passage 84 cleaning waste water storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 91 side groove 9 washing wastewater supply device 93 washing wastewater return path 94 water level holding device 100 ground 101 bottom groove 102 communication hole 103 convex part 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 110 water tank 111 weir 112 washing wastewater supply pump 113 washing waste water supply pipe 116 frame structure 117 roof"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052947-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052946-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 91 side groove 92 washing wastewater supply device 93 washing wastewater return path 94 water level holding device 100 ground 101 bottom groove 102 communication hole 103 projection 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 110 water tank 111 weir 112 washing wastewater supply pump 113 washing waste water supply pipe 116 frame structure 117 roof"}, {"pat_id": "US-5055180-A", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "thus an uninsulated tank will normally last for a much longer period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102411899-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in the case of such a square water tank the inside of the water tank is complicated due to the angles 16 and 17 installed in the inside of the water tank complicatedly the drainage during cleaning is poor and many problems occur during maintenance and also the angle 16 since 17 is joined to the joint 13 of the panel 12 by welding the number of angles 16 and 17 increases in proportion to the number of welds and thus there is a problem that a lot of welding corrosion may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore rainwater or groundwater is collected and stored"}, {"pat_id": "US-10377649-B2", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "the fermentation tank is preferably washed between different batches of microbial growth to remove attached growth at the waterline which may cause build up of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266017-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "is installed and the bent part 12 is formed in the interior pipe 11 the intermediate valve 21 is installed in the cross pipe 5 to reduce the water pressure to a predetermined pressure or less and is installed in the cross pipe 5 in the water supply pipe of the high rise building consisting of a first noise canceling unit 23 made of a pressure gauge 22 for measuring the water pressure by the adjustment of the intermediate valve 21 a fixture 27 having the same diameter as that of the indoor pipe 11 and having a main through hole 25 formed at a central portion and formed at equal intervals to the outside of the main through hole 25 it is attached to the main hole 25 formed in the fixture 27 to form a smooth angle of the bent portion 12 of the indoor pipe 11 by water pressure vortex water and softly formed stepped 30 on one side inner tube 28 water supply pipe noise reduction of the high rise building characterized in that provided with a second noise reduction unit 24 is installed in the front of the fixture 27 and the packing 29 to prevent leakage when connected to the meter 6 device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266017-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "to this end the downstream water supply pipe 4 connected to the elevated water tank installed on the roof of the high rise building the horizontal pipe 5 installed in parallel with the downward water supply pipe 4 and the horizontal pipe 5 connected to the meter 6 is provided and the interior pipe 11 having the bent portion 12 the intermediate valve 21 installed in the cross pipe 5 for reducing the water pressure to a predetermined pressure or less and the cross pipe 5 in the water supply piping device of the high rise building consisting of a first noise canceling unit 23 consisting of a pressure gauge 22 installed in the pressure gauge 22 to measure the pressure of the intermediate valve 21 the diameter of the indoor pipe 11 it is the same as the main hole 25 is formed in the central portion the outer space of the main hole 25 is formed at equal intervals of the fasteners 27 formed with a number of auxiliary through holes 26 the main formed in the fastener 27 it is attached to the through hole 25 to gently form the angle of the bent portion 12 of the indoor pipe 11 by the hydraulic pressure the second silencer made of a soft inner tube 28 having a step 30 formed on one side and a packing 29 installed at the front of the fixture 27 to prevent leakage when connected to the meter 6"}]</data>
