lar it is provided with two stages of filtration to increase the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826790-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "at the upper part a sloping induction plate is installed at the tip of the first drainage guide plate a second settling filtration tank for blocking inflow of fine contaminants accompanied by the storm and having a filter net installed on the downflow channel formed by the lower part of the precipitation inducing plate and the first drainage guide plate to remove the dissolved fine contaminants a second rim hole formed in the upper portion of the first drainage guide plate of the secondary settling filtration tank and having a second rim hole and a second rim hole formed in the second rim of the second settling filtration tank the second partition wall is provided with a drain plate for partitioning the space with the second settling filtration tank and discharging the rainwater having an inclined surface at the inlet side and flowing into the second rinse hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101694827-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention relates to an initial good treatment apparatus capable of effectively preventing contaminants mixed with an initial storm due to contamination of a river lake by effectively treating contamination mixed with the initial rainwater by a pretreatment tank and a filtration tank an inlet pipe for guiding the initial storm of the gut pipe to the pretreatment tank and an inlet pipe connected to the filtration tank of the main body the main body is located at the same depth as the gutter tube and the inlet tube is formed higher than the outlet tube at the position of the water head and the initial gutter inside the main body is moved by the water head difference quot an early stormwater treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100782992-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "582121 excellent storage tank is formed in each corner of the top plate and the bottom plate so that the opening is formed on the side of the cube respectively a plurality of nut settlement grooves are formed on the top and bottom of each column a storage block having a stepped portion formed on at least one side of the top plate and a joining portion formed integrally with the base surface on the bottom plate and an upper surface block having a rectangular plate shape and having an end mounted on the upper surface plate step portion of the storage block to form the same plane as the upper surface plate of the storage block wherein the storage blocks are repeatedly arranged in a straight line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101529143-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the float prevention member 30 is formed in a conical shape inclined so that the outer periphery thereof faces downward and a plurality of outflow holes 32 are formed on the surface to block the clogs and pass the storm surges"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the rainwater introduced into the storm reservoir is formed at the half point of the height of the slab 3 as described above so that the rainwater flowed into the storm reservoir is about 50 of the water into the basement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "thus when the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention is installed in the basement penetration type first digging a pit having a certain width and depth and then flatten the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the metering water guide 30 excludes a certain amount of initial storm the initial storm is inadequate to use due to a high degree of contamination due to various pollutants in the air and in the present invention a certain amount of initial storm is stored in the user storage 300 that is discharging to the discharge pipe 12 and some rainwater flowing into the catchment tank 10 is collected in the buoyancy chamber 15 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277086-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition while the construction of the prior art has many problems in construction due to the dimensional deviation the present invention solved the construction problem by the dimensional deviation using a separate jig using the recess formed on the top of each pillar block it is characterized in that the stability is improved by preventing the fall or fall of the upper sphere during construction to solve the stability problems when assembling and installing the conventional rainwater storage tank and more economical by providing a rainwater storage tank that can be various construction depending on the limited space as an excellent storage tank it has not only satisfactory function but also stability and it is effective to improve long term durability by external wire speech method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that the upper portion is exposed from the filter medium over the entire length the upper portion of the filter material is exposed from the filter material to the inside of the filtration tank and the exposed portion is formed with an inlet hole for allowing the filter material washing water to flow into the discharge passage while the opposite end is installed in the partition wall 111b a filter media wash and contaminant discharge line configured to communicate with the filter material discharge outlet a filter material cleaning device installed under the filter material washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe to be buried in the filter material and spraying high pressure air or backwash water for washing the filter material and a filter medium washing water and contaminants which are installed outside the pretreatment tank and are washed by the filter material cleaning device and flowed into the pretreatment tank through the washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe and stagnant water accumulated in the water treatment tank and a stagnant water exclusion pump for removing the stagnant water when it is confirmed that stagnant water is present in the water treatment tank contaminants separated from the filter media and the filter media wash water used for the filter media are supplied to the discharge passage and the filtering water discharge port 135 having the reverse opening closing door 136 of the partition wall 111b to be forcedly sucked into the pretreatment tank and forcedly excluded to the outside by the congestion water exclusion pump the operation of the filter medium washing device is stopped and only the stagnant water exclusion pump is operated with the stagnant water of the water treatment tank to be operated until the complete removal of sediment deposited at the bottom of the tank has been confirmed initial treatment is a solid system of jing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id"