having a trapezoidal shape in which an upper end of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe is disposed higher than an inner center of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe so that the sedimentation tank inflow pipe is inclined so as to block at least an outlet of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe a screen screen unit detachably coupled to a lower end of the flow velocity reduction unit and and a detailed screen unit connected to the bottom screen of the weft screen unit to have the same width as the weft screen unit and having a relatively small perforation compared to the weft screen unit when the flow rate is attenuated through the flow rate attenuating unit and the storm is introduced the contaminants contained in the storm are collected through the detailed screen unit and when the detailed screen unit is blocked the stormwater is supplied to the settling tank through the screen unit characterized by a nonpoint pollutant treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101615356-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the sedimentation tank flow rate damping device has a trapezoidal shape having a trapezoidal shape in which the upper end of the sedimentation tank flow in pipe is disposed higher than the inner center of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe and is inclined so as to block at least half of the outlet of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe attenuator a screen screen unit detachably coupled to a lower end of the flow velocity reduction unit and a concave screen unit connected to the bottom screen of the weft screen unit to have the same width as the weft screen unit and having relatively small pores as compared with the weft screen unit the contaminants contained in the storm can be collected through the detail screen unit and when the detail screen unit is closed the stormwater can be supplied to the settling tank through the screen screen unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank 1 having a contaminant collecting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the pretreatment tank 1 may further include a dirt collecting tank 13 and a ditch water tank 14 therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the contaminant collecting tank 13 is formed of a rectangular tube body 13a which is enclosed by a vertical wall on the side of the storm inflow port 12 of the pretreatment tank 1 and which has a lower portion closed and an upper portion thereof opened a contaminant collecting net 13c for collecting large sized contaminants contained in the stormwater is provided on the end side of the storm inlet 12 and a pretreatment water having the contaminants removed from the vertical wall of the rectangular watertight vessel 13 and the water retention tank 14 is provided at one side of the rectangular tube body 13a so as to prevent the large contaminants from being removed from the contaminant collecting tank 13 through the through hole 13b of the cylinder 13a so as to be discharged in the tangential direction of the outer diameter of the water separator 14"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847553-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the prefabricated infiltration storage tank according to an embodiment of the present invention includes a superior filtration unit 100 formed in a circular tube shape penetrating a lower sidewall of a manhole 1 to filter out contaminants and suspended matters of excellent quality and at least one storm block unit 200 having a box shaped block body 220 and a plate like block top plate 210 having a water permeable hole 201 formed on a wall surface thereof and a reservoir 20 forming a reservoir space for storing the storm that flows through the reservoir 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847553-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition the present invention has an effect of enhancing construction cost and productivity because a storage tank can be easily installed by using an excellent penetration block box that can be assembled by fastening a block top plate and a block body.1 is a schematic view showing a configuration of a prefabricated infiltration storage tank according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however there is a concern that the void clogging phenomenon may be generated in a part of the filter medium due to a tendency of the initial storm to flow into the filtration tank problems such as water quality decay and odor generation which are secondary water quality pollution caused by water flooding due to no stagnant pollutants being discharged after the end of rainfall may result in deteriorating the overall filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a storage block having a plurality of nut settling grooves formed at upper and lower portions of each pillar at least one side of the top plate having a stepped portion and a bottom portion of the bottom plate having a coupling portion integrally with the base surface it consists of a top block having a rectangular plate shape and the end is mounted on the top plate step of the storage block to form the same plane as the top plate of the storage block the storage block is repeatedly arranged in a straight line a plurality of the upper blocks are configured to be coupled between the storage blocks in a straight line to form a storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in the storm storage tank configured as described above the shape of the main block of the storm storage tank of patent registration no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101770268-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "according to the present invention only a crush stone is installed at the lower end of the reservoir structure so as to penetrate not only the reservoir of the storm but also the stormwater and by implementing the water circulation system penetrating into the ground through the reservoir with the upper reservoir and the lower reservoir it is possible to keep reservoirs and infiltration for water circulation and thus to prevent flooding even in temporary storms in areas where the impervious area is wide and the effect on the water circulation system is large.brief description of the drawi