ortion of the maintenance tank 30 and the lower portion of the treatment tank 40 in turn sedimentary particulate matter with a high specific gravity is precipitated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as a result deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20 the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "then after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20 it is re introduced into the maintenance tank 30 the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220901-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition the present invention can be washed by the non powered method of the natural freshwater and storage tank is completed compared to the existing method can reduce the cost of construction there is no fear of damage due to breakdown or power outage the use of stable storage facilities can handle pollution 1 is a plan view showing a natural freshwater storage system of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 1030605the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems and it is an object of the present invention to prevent storm flooding by storing rainwater reduce load on a sewage treatment plant prevent urban heat island and replenish water resources the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a method of constructing a reservoir tank having a non point pollutant reduction type prefabricated reservoir block and a nonpoint source pollution reduction function using the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889974-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent storage tank 100 which is embedded in the inside of the ground and receives stormwater introduced from the ground a grating 200 rotatably coupled to the upper surface of the superior storage tank 100 for introducing the stormwater into the storage tank and blocking the foreign material a dirt collecting box 400 provided in the superior storage tank 100 for filtering dirt contained in the rainwater and a collection box support 300 provided at an upper portion of the superior storage container 100 and supporting the dirt collection box 400 the storm reservoir 100 a reservoir body 110 in which the storm is stored a grating insert tube 120 formed on the upper portion of the reservoir body 110 and coupled to the grating 200 and a grating seating surface 121 formed on the boundary region between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 so as to be stepped inwardly in a predetermined area so that the grating 200 is seated and supported the grating 200 a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insertion tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 disposed in the grating frame 210 at predetermined intervals in the longitudinal direction and having irregularities formed on the upper surface thereof to block rainwater from the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter a plurality of reinforcing frames 230 arranged in the grating frame 210 in a lateral direction at regular intervals a plurality of protrusions protruding from the ground at a predetermined interval in the lower portion of the outer reinforcing frame 230a to allow the gravel to flow into the gap between the grating insert tube 120 and the grating frame 210 and includes a soil inflow tooth 240 the height of the earth inflow tooth 240 and the height of the outer reinforcement frame 230a may be greater than the height of the reinforcement frame 230 located inside the outer reinforcement frame 230a and the reinforcing frame 230 is formed at the same height as the reinforcing frame 230"}]</data>
