ewage treatment plant and discharged and a high concentration storage tank having an internal washing facility a medium concentration tank configured to temporarily receive and discharge the inflow water when it is difficult to direct discharge at a time when the high concentration tank is full a low concentration storage tank receiving and temporarily storing low concentration influent water in which the contaminant concentration of the influent water falls below a predetermined level and discharging it and receiving water discharged from the medium low concentration storage tank after a simple treatment and through the disinfection process the water discharge below the legal water quality concentration is a simple treatment facility that can be used as a wash water and deodorizing water in the discharge or wash water storage tank corresponding to the water quality flow rate of the influent water is discharged to the sewage treatment plant after a temporary storage through a high concentration storage tank and the outflow water below the legal water concentration discharged from the medium low concentration storage tank is discharged or washed water storage tank after disinfection treatment it can be used as washing water and deodorizing water in the inside the inflow water distribution tank is equipped with sensors for measuring the water quality of the toc ss and ec therein to measure the flow rate and water quality data analyze the measurement data in the control computer and then the high concentration it is configured to automatically open and close the sluice of the channel connected to the medium low concentration storage tank to classify and transfer the influent to any one of the high medium low concentration storage tank to classify and store the inflow by the flow rate and the water quality data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "multifunctional storage system to reduce initial rain pollution and prevent urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "multi functional storage method for the initial excellent pollution reduction and urban flooding prevention characterized in that to predict the to determine the corresponding protocol to achieve the distribution of influent through real time control real time control"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_22", "text": "the method of claim 20 wherein the storage step is to receive the medium influent directly from the influent distribution tank in the medium concentration tank to temporarily store and the contaminant concentration of the medium influent water is treated as a low concentration influent water through a chemical flocculation reaction multifunctional storage method to reduce initial water pollution and prevent urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "multi function water storage system and method for reducing the contamination by initial rain and preventing a city from flooding the present invention relates to a multi functional next generation storage system and storage method that can be easily applied to urban areas and can be used to control the initial excellent pollution load caused by rainfall to prevent urban flooding and to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "provides a multifunctional storage system to prevent flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674110-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes and modifications may be made without departing from the scope of the present invention.1 rainwater catcher 2 3 by drain pipe 4 infiltration ball 10 penetration ditch 10a infiltration ditch inflow section 11 perforated fan for flow equalization 12 shovel rake 12a contamination 13 flooding bumps 14 drainage filter fiber 15 observation 15a 15b plug 20 pretreatment tank 20a pretreatment tank inflow section 21 sand pack 22 stagnant water outlet 30 runoff water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however there is a concern that the void clogging phenomenon may be generated in a part of the filter medium due to a tendency of the initial storm to flow into the filtration tank problems such as water quality decay and odor generation which are secondary water quality pollution caused by water flooding due to no stagnant pollutants being discharged after the end of rainfall may result in deteriorating the overall filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 installed at the inlet of the primary sedimentation tank 1 into which the sewage flows and the suspended matter generated on the water surface of the incoming sewage is led to the suspended debris removal device installed at the downstream of the inflow portion to prevent clogging of the flowing sewage an apparatus for crushing and flooding suspended matters of a primary clarifier a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier 1 to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "therefore the development of the float shattering and anti rust prevention device of the primary sedimentation tank using the acidifier to smooth the flow of the suspended solids through the float remover without the solidification of the suspended solids in the process of moving the sewage from the inlet of the primary sedimentation tank to the suspension .summary of the invention the present invention has been made in order to solve the above mentioned problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a flotage removing device which prevents flotation from stagnating and hardening in the process of moving sewage from an inflow part of a primary clarifier to a flotage removing device the present invention provides an apparatus for preventing flocculation and flooding of a primary clarifier using an acidifier to smooth the flow of the flocculant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides an apparatus for preventing floatation and flooding of a primary clarifier using an acidifier the apparatus comprising an inlet to a first settling tank through which sewage is introduced an apparatus for crushing and preventing floatation of a primary clarifier using an acidifier to prevent clogging of sewage flowing into a sludge removal device installed at a rear end of a site comprising a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101770268-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "according to the present invention only a crush stone is installed at the lower end of the reservoir structure so as to penetrate not only the reservoir of the storm but also the stormwater and by implementing the water circulation system penetrating into the ground through the reservoir with the upper reservoir and the lower reservoir it is possible to keep reservoirs and infiltration for water circulation and thus to prevent flooding even in temporary storms in areas where the impervious area is wide and the effect on the water circulation system is large.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-8691091-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the rapid air escape may also cause the filter media to jump vertically inside the filter tank causing it to be lost through the drain line and possibly causing plugging of the drain and flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-8691091-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "by performing an air release cycle prior to a backwash cycle the release of air may be controlled to prevent the air charge from rushing out to the drain during backwash thereby preventing noise rattling flooding and loss of filter media"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7117022-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "it may also be implemented in a mixed format with a partial hardware module that implements a part of hardware elements.brief description of the drawings it is a block diagram which shows the inland water flooding analysis apparatus which concerns on embodiment 1 of this invention.fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200427026-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the precipitate washed with water from the inclined bottom 13a flows into the sewage treatment plant through the drain pipe 17 together with the washing water.as described above according to the present invention by automating the water washing process of the sediment deposited in the storage tank to facilitate the maintenance of the storage tank and to wash the sediment deposited in the storage tank using the water head difference the siphon structure of the large volume of wash water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063307-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "not only burnout occurred but there was a problem of property damage due to flooding due to drainage.the present invention is to solve the above problems the air is compressed in the inside of the air pressure tank by the suction force of the drain pump during the drainage process was compressed in the air pressure tank when the water in the drain pipe back flow after the completion of drainage as the air expands it supports the check valve for preventing the backflow to prevent water hammer and at the same time to discharge the end of the drain pipe to constitute a water collecting tank drainage device equipped with a water hammer prevention air pressure tank to remove the foreign matter caught in the filter net of the drain pump biodegradation that is sucked together with water by suction power of the drainage pump when the drainage pump is installed by installing a vacuum netting connecting socket to which the vacuum gauge is connected to the suction end of the drainage pump and a plurality of foreign matter crushing blades are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "