  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-12209051-B2", "para_id": "para_516", "text": "when there is heavy rainfall a reservoir or tank may become overwhelmed by a sudden rush of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101669813-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the apparatus is formed into a rectangular box shape extending in forward and backward directions the upper part of the front surface is formed with an inflow port through which rainwater collects and an upper part of the rear surface is formed with an outlet for discharging rainwater filtered for recycling"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6132141-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "3 is an example of a sewer rainwater switching type storage facility according to the present invention and is a diagram in the case of allowing overflow discharge to a river in the middle of rainfall.fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 it is installed to open and close on the upper surface of the treatment tank when the amount of rainfall exceeding the processing capacity the inner lid to block the top of the treatment tank to induce the rainfall to flow into the discharge box road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function further comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition in order to prevent the decay and odor caused by long term storage of high concentration early rainfall brower is installed to supply minimum air to maintain dissolved oxygen concentration of more than 0.1mg l in the acid pipe installed at the bottom of the storage tank and to detect rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "on the other hand it is possible to selectively treat only high initial rainfall by the change in flow rate and in particular to increase the treatment efficiency compared to the increase of the efficiency of filtration and to easily check from the outside by placing the differential pressure portion 23 in the center to measure the replacement cycle due to the clogging of the 1.2 filter medium which is a carbide embedded in the filtration unit due to the occurrence of overload it can prevent life shortening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "it is possible to prevent the end of the waste.as described above the present invention is a device for treating a nonpoint source of pollution caused by an initial rainfall and can be immediately installed in an existing storm conduit 12 and particularly a coarse contaminant such as soil stones and leaves is a contaminant treatment tank 13 is treated preferentially the fine contaminants such as sand or mud is moved to the sediment storage unit 14 by the rotational centrifugal force through the rainwater movement port 16 provided to be eccentric with one side and the rainwater flow prevention plate installed at the bottom 18 and the concave portion 17 to prevent the backflow and settled in the lower part after removing the very fine sludge through the fibrous filtrate of carbide with rainwater can further extend the service life of the filter medium on the other hand it is possible to selectively process only the initial rainfall of high concentration by the amount of change in flow rate and in particular it is provided with two stages of filtration to increase the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280771-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the high level oxidation treatment apparatus 420 may treat the treated water from the wastewater treatment facility 220 stored in the advanced oxidation treatment tank by using ultraviolet rays having a wavelength of 180 to 280 nm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101501179-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "especially it is difficult to secure the site because it requires a separate site to install the contact tank and it is difficult to select the site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102257819-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water purification biofilm unit is further installed at the discharge end ex wherein the water purification biofilm unit includes a dam dam installed to block drainage by blocking a portion of the discharge end ex a purification groove hom formed in a predetermined depth at a predetermined interval in a part of the length of the dam dam a pair of vertical frames ver standing and fixed at both ends of the width center of the dam dam a horizontal frame hoz connecting and fixing the upper end of the vertical frame ver a double shaft winch wic fixed on the horizontal frame hoz to be positioned directly above each purification groove hom a drum dr fixed to both shafts of the winch wic and wound around a wire wr in the integrated management system for automatic monitoring of sewage pipes having a net shaped biofilm purification tank 1000 in which an end of the wire wr is fixed inserted into the purification groove hom and filled with a purification ball therein the biofilm cleaning container 1000 includes a pair of side frames 1100 an upper frame 1200 assembled and fixed to an upper end of the side frame 1100 and a tip of the side frame 1100 and the upper frame 1200 and a front frame 1300 and a rear frame 1400 respectively assembled at the rear end the side frame 1100 the upper frame 1200 the front frame 1300 and the rear frame 1400 are fixed with a wire mesh net w to the rectangular frame f so that water flowing along the river can escape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "in addition regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102009623-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "eighth the fine dust detection sensor rainfall detection sensor road surface detection sensor cctv to detect the dust state of the road outside the injector is equipped with the effect that can remove the dust completely by spraying when checking the site situation in real time have.1 is a schematic diagram showing a clean rod watering system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101239389-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "if it is over the designed quantity in the treatment tank the rainwater collected in the treatment tank is pulled up by the pump and reintroduced into the second pollution reduction portion formed of the gravel layer the crushed stone layer and the zeolite layer to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "manual valve operation method is unrealistic because the manager must operate the valve in the early stage of rainfall and it has the disadvantage of high cost and difficulty of maintenance such as failure when using devices such as flow meters and sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure integrally formed by it has an excellent effect such as reducing the cross sectional area of the block itself to thereby reduce the overall weight"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101155948-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in order to prevent this the inflow water distribution pipe 240 is provided and as the rainfall outflow water is supplied into the second media layer 221 having a predetermined depth through the inflow water distribution pipe 240 the entire second filter layer 221 is provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 6 it is installed at the lower side of the check valve and the third non power flow control device which operates in the shielding direction by the water pressure when the water level rises in the filtration tank and operates so as to be open while being homed by the weakening water pressure after the end of the rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "at this time the third non power flow control device 15 also operates in the shielding direction due to the water pressure applied as the water level rises in the filtration tank 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101279418-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "like the high concentration overflow water storage tank 220 a slope a solid pit and a pump may be provided at the lower portion of the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 and the storage stored in the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 after the rainfall is terminated through the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226649-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the control unit may further include changing to the constant priority supply mode when the water level of the rainwater storage tank is lower than the reference value in the rainwater priority supply operation mode.smart system according to an embodiment of the present invention can efficiently supply water by using a constant and rain water it is possible to save a constant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "it was provided to prevent the collapse and to provide stable drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101644965-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the river water inflow section includes a first river water inflow control apparatus and a second river inflow comprising the element introduced into the pretreatment unit is pretreated and then flows out to the storage unit f the water quality purification unit g or treated water pits the water quality purification unit g includes a first stage water purification unit that receives the river water or the rainwater effluent from the storage unit to purify and discharge the river water or the rainwater effluent from the storage unit and a water purification unit that receives the river water or rainwater discharged from the first a second stage water purification unit inflow control unit and a treated water foot inflow control unit wherein at least one of a fixed phase media and a fluid phase media is filled in the first stage water purification unit and the second stage water purification unit in the case of rainfall the second stage water purification unit inflow control unit is closed the treated water inflow control unit is opened and the first and second soil inflow prevention devices are opened to open the rainwater inflow the first river water inflow control device and the second river water inflow control device are closed so that the river water inflow part b does not receive the river water in the non wastewater treatment the second stage water purification unit inflow control unit is opened the treated water inflow control unit is closed the first soil inflow prevention device and the second earth inflow prevention device are closed to block the rainwater inflow water inflow part a and the first river water inflow control device and the second river inflow control device are closed does not enter the inflow section b at the end of the rainfall the first soil inflow prevention device and the second soil inflow prevention device are closed to block the rainwater inflow water inflow part a and the first river water inflow control device and the second river inflow control device so that the river water inflow part b does not receive the river water wherein the first stage water purification unit is filled with a stationary phase material and a fluid phase filter material wherein the second stage water purification unit is filled with a stationary phase filter medium the preprocessing section includes a needlepoint portion c a screen portion d and a dispensing portion e the distribution section e distributes the raw water treated by the settling section and the screen section d to the storage section f the water quality purification section g or the treated water feet the dispensing unit distributes the raw water flowing out of the pre treatment unit to the storage unit f at the time of rainfall distributes the raw water discharged from the pre treatment unit to the water quality purification unit g the dispensing unit e includes a dispensing tank for introducing and storing the raw water treated by the settling unit and the screen unit d a measuring unit for measuring the quality of the raw water and a raw water source for the water quality purification unit g a water purification unit inflow control unit for controlling inflow and a storage unit inflow control unit for controlling the inflow of raw water into the storage unit f wherein the water quality purification unit inflow control unit and the storage unit inflow control unit are respectively closed when the water quality of the raw water measured by the measurement unit is a water quality capable of being discharged to the river is discharged through a bypass pipe not the storage section characterized in that when the quantity of raw water measured by the measuring section exceeds the treatment capacity of the water quality purification section or the storage section the excess quantity is discharged through the bypass pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "multi functional storage method for the initial excellent pollution reduction and urban flooding prevention characterized in that to predict the to determine the corresponding protocol to achieve the distribution of influent through real time control real time control"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "multi function water storage system and method for reducing the contamination by initial rain and preventing a city from flooding the present invention relates to a multi functional next generation storage system and storage method that can be easily applied to urban areas and can be used to control the initial excellent pollution load caused by rainfall to prevent urban flooding and to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however there is a concern that the void clogging phenomenon may be generated in a part of the filter medium due to a tendency of the initial storm to flow into the filtration tank problems such as water quality decay and odor generation which are secondary water quality pollution caused by water flooding due to no stagnant pollutants being discharged after the end of rainfall may result in deteriorating the overall filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage t