characterized in that the outer peripheral surface of the rainwater storage tank block b is provided with a reinforcement finish panel 60 is fixed via the fastening means so as to block the stored rainwater is discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "second step s2 of seating the excellent storage tank block b consisting of the connecting member 30 to the cut bottom surface the third step s3 of inserting the fastener 40 into the seating groove 21a of the rainwater storage tank blocks b arranged in a multi row species and fixed through the fastening means the fourth step s4 of placing the finishing panel 60 on the outer circumferential surface of the rainwater tank block b and fixing it via the fastening means the fifth step s5 of forming a waterproof layer by applying a waterproofing material to the peripheral surface of the rainwater storage block b in which the finishing panel 60 is installed rainfall storage tank characterized in that it comprises a sixth step s6 after the soil is covered with the top surface of the storm water storage block b having a waterproof layer is chopped or pour concrete into the top surface of the soil after soil cover excellent storage tank construction method using blocks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the first object of the present invention is to prevent contamination of the valley channel by overflowing the partition wall during rainy weather and also to sewage initial rainwater and valley water excellent sewage and valleys using a storage tank that can be discharged to the river and prevented from being discharged to the river by the initial rainwater that has not been purified due to the initial rainfall that is supercharged during rainy weather exceeding the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "accord