  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100402289-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "there was no deterioration of the treated water or efficiency of the wind pressure and air volume of the blower 15b and only the contamination of the membrane increased resulting in a shortening of the membrane life due to membrane contamination such as a decrease in the amount of treated water.the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art the flow control and the aeration and membrane separation function can be performed at the same time in the aeration and membrane separation tank facility is minimized hollow fiber membrane of the aeration and membrane separation tank it is protected by this separate facility to remove the metering tank and sedimentation tank at the same time to prevent contamination of the hollow fiber membrane and the waste water to be transported to each tank is made by the natural discharge the transfer pump is removed to reduce the manufacturing cost of the device it is an object of the present invention to provide a wastewater treatment method and apparatus for reducing power usage costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101385841-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the wire 256 is fixed to the 210 and the drive motor 254 is installed in the middle portion of the rotation guide post 233 so as to wind the wire 256"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3319944-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the light shielding hood is mounted on the wall of the water tank via a link mechanism that moves only in the vertical direction so that the light shielding hood is prevented from moving in the horizontal direction due to an external force such as a strong wind"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3319944-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "further the link mechanism 13 prevents the light shielding hood 3 from moving in the horizontal direction due to an external force such as a strong wind when the detecting section 1 is installed outdoors"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3319944-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the light shielding hood is mounted on the wall of the water tank via a link mechanism that moves only in the vertical direction so that the light shielding hood is prevented from moving in the horizontal direction due to an external force such as a strong wind"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1350028-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an electrically operated lift pump 52 conveys the brackish water via the raw water lift pipe 54 the rotary union 26 and the storage tank 27 to the pressure pump 20 in the nacelle 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h thermocouple an