15-B2", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "since a leakage in the leaking transporting pipeline section 1201 has been detected the multiway valve 801 of the left wind turbine 110 closes the second valve inlet b and directs the electrolyzed gas from the electrolyzer unit 111 and or from the storage tank 901 via the first valve inlet a into the transporting pipeline 131"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377520-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a control method of the water quality improvement system according to claim 1 since the blade 107 is rotated by the wind power the air pump 105 is operated to pressurize air to the exhaust pipe 111 thereby generating bubbles in the aerator 125"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "in addition although the external temperature of the winter season is measured by the external temperature sensor but may be lower than the temperature actually measured by obstacles or other factors such as wind the controller 30 of the present invention has an external temperature of 4 when the temperature of the water inside the water tank 1 becomes 4 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a slope 62 formed over a wide area for the purpose of creating grassland and forest a road 63 formed with a slope 67 at the edge so as to penetrate the slope 62 a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 to prevent the slope 67 from sinking and a vegetation block 30 formed with a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to plant landscaping trees 46 in a protruding manner an assembly block 30 30 assembled in a layered structure and a slope 67 formed in an arid or hilly area where a renewable energy generation device 100 formed with solar and wind power generation devices 60 68 is built near a field 74 or a grassland or forest management area on the slope in a slope 62 in which a plurality of afforestation blocks 30 are stacked on a slope 67 equipped to be planted in the above mentioned vegetation zone 33 a water tank 71 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 of the afforestation blocks 30 30 assembled in the above mentioned stacked structure a vegetation zone 33 33 equipped with a vegetation wall 34 for planting landscaping trees 46 by protruding while a water supply hole 44 is perforated in the front wall 31 a moving gap 42 provided between a separate outer wall 32 in the rear wall 31 and afforestation blocks 30 30 are assembled in a stacked manner so that the moving gaps 42 are connected to each other an installation structure in a hilly area where a renewable energy power generation device for grassland and forest creation can be installed which is provided by assembling an assembly block 30 equipped with a vegetation wall 34 that is fixed to the outer section c of the vegetation block 30 connected to a water supply inlet 44 from a water tank 71 to support the lower section of the vegetation zone 33 33 while being assembled into the lower section of the above mentioned afforestation block 30 30 thereby preventing rainwater from collapsing due to subsidence on a slope 67"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the forest thus created is intended to contribute to preventing heat waves and to prevent the collapse of afforestation blocks due to heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in a slope 62 formed over a wide area for the purpose of creating grassland and forest a road 63 formed with a slope 67 at the edge so as to penetrate the slope 62 a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 to prevent the slope 67 from sinking and a vegetation block 30 formed with a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to plant landscaping trees 46 in a protruding manner an assembly block 30 30 assembled in a layered structure and a slope 67 formed in an arid or hilly area where a renewable energy generation device 100 formed with solar and wind power generation devices 60 68 is built near a field 74 or a grassland or forest management area on the slope"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "here the invention is that the installation of the second renewable energy power generation device 100 installed to prevent subsidence due to the harmful gas 49 or rainwater on the slope is preferably installed in a hilly area 64 where sunlight and wind power are well transmitted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "therefore the purpose of this invention is to provide power and equipment for collection in an economical and environmentally friendly manner by providing a renewable energy power generation device which is the main component of the present invention and a suction pump suction pipe and storage facility connected thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102435204-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "when it reaches the top an overflow pipe that discharges the treated water located at the top to the outside of the measuring tank 2 is installed the oxygen supply means 5 is a main pipe 51 and blowing means 52 installed on the inlet side of the main pipe 51 to blow wind into the main pipe 51 branch pipe 53 branching at least two from the main pipe 51 each outlet communicating with each bioreactor 1 and an opening rate adjusting means 54 installed on the branch pipe 53 to adjust the opening rate inside the branch pipe 53 the blowing means 52 includes a blower 521 blower for blowing wind into the main pipe 51 and an rpm adjusting means 522 for adjusting the amount of oxygen flowing into the main pipe 51 by adjusting the number of revolutions per unit time of the blower 521 in the measuring tank 2 the dissolved oxygen concentration sensing means 4 ph sensing means 21 mlss sensing means 22 orp sensing means 23 temperature according to the control signal of the control unit 6 a cleaning means 27 for cleaning the contaminants attached to the surface of the sensing means 24 is additionally mounted the washing means 27 uses antifoam water as washing water to remove contaminants in the upper and lower portions of the vortex prevention wall fitting groove 28 a female side sine wave groove 29a processed in the form of a sine wave is processed the upper and lower portions of both ends of the vortex prevention wall 26 are processed in the form of a sine wave and a sine wave groove 29b on the male side engaged with the sine wave groove 29a on the female side is processed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102435204-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the dissolved oxygen concentration sensing means 4 in the measuring tank 2 the ph sensing means 21 the mlss sensing means 22 the orp sensing means 23 and the temperature sensing means 24 are included in the measurement tank 2 it is installed at an angle of 35 to 75 degrees from the horizontal plane to accurately measure the water quality of the treated water sample and to remove the suspended substances on the surface naturally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200178694-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "rotating so that the livestock sewage on the atomized ultra mirror is blown by the strong wind of the blower installed in the rear of the evaporator and evaporated into the atmosphere to prevent river water and groundwater contamination and odor pollution and bacterial infection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200439741-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "force is at work therefore the contraction induction weight 11 is in the form of having a floating force in the upper portion and thus has a self supporting force to be raised and lowered in the guide pipe 60 and standing in the water and the floating capacity of the government yugu 2 is an auxiliary floating hole 20 since it is a form of dividing in even if the size of the government piece 2 is made small the flow of the bellows member 5 is reduced by reducing the influence of birds wind and other external forces act on the government piece 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569729-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a work line 10 provided with a water storage tank 22 for water treatment at the water surface 11 a frame 21 fixed to be projected to both sides of the work line 10 a steam jet pipe 12 having a jet port 33 provided to be submerged in the water surface 11 while being fixed a solar cell module 20 which is obliquely projected upwardly symmetrically on the side of the solar cell module 20 at both sides of the frame 21 a guide groove 28 projecting from both sides of the guide groove 29 so that the guide groove 29 is formed in the guide groove 29 a gap section spaced from the upper side of the guide groove 29 on both sides an outlet 19 provided as a wall 18 and a shielding film 37 protruded to the lower side of the water vapor distribution plate 12 at both side ends of the solar power generation plate 20 section 40 an induction part 23 protruding from the upper side of the water storage tank 22 to the lower side of the discharge port 19 and a low pressure section 40 separated from the upper end of the induction part 23 by a moving distance a movement section 47 and a condensation section 54 to be formed a water jetted from the moving interval a is discharged to the upper side of the water storage tank 22 through the water discharge port 19 and a condensing water condensing device provided in the water storage tank so as to flow into the guide part protruding from the water storage tank side walls 31 formed by protrusions of a blocking film 37 fixed to both side ends of the solar cell plate 20 a rotating shaft 42 passing between the side walls 31 a rotary drum 44 provided on the rotary shaft 42 a rotary vane 43 projecting at a plurality of intervals on the outer side surface of the rotary drum 44 an outer wall body 33 connected to the side wall 31 provided on the outer side of the rotary vane 43 a fixing wall 49 provided at both ends of the outer wall body 33 to support the upper side of the solar power generation plate 20 downward and an inlet 21 formed at both sides of the fixed wall a rotary drum 44 for reinforcing the rotational force by the wind force guided to the power generation plate 20 and rain water to the water storage tank 22 by the conveyance pipe 35 passing through the lower side of the solar power generation plate 20 wherein the condenser is configured to store the condensed water"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "therefore any water lines exposed to outside temperatures including any water line runs inside the heated interior 206 that may be subject to freezing temperatures are protected and warmed by the circulating warming loops"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "reasonable shielding of the fresh water tank 12 from wind chill effects and or providing some insulation will increase efficiency of the warming system 50 and reduce pump 16 and water heater 14 cycling"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4931039-B2", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "measurement procedure the procedure for measuring the degree of contamination of raw water by the water quality monitoring apparatus shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100454430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "when the lid 5 is covered on the upper surface of the water meter protector 1 the upper edge 2 of the lid 5 is formed in the taper recess 3 formed inside the water meter protector 1 of the border 2 the middle tape 7 tapered in the triple frame and inserted into the rubber o ring 27 is inserted and the outer frame 6 and the inner frame 8 are covered with the center so that the water meter protection tube 1 and the lid 5 is in close contact with outside snow and non cold wind can not flow into the water meter protection tank 1 thereby increasing the thermal insulation power to prevent the freezing of the water meter etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "it is possible to prevent the direct exposure to direct sunlight rain and wind by preventing the rainwater storage tank of the uniform color pattern from being covered with the inside of the rainwater storage compartment or breakage of the water can be prevented and the decay of the water can be prevented and the ceiling portion is formed with a sloped slope at a constant angle so that the snow or rain can flow without falling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "induce the rainwater guided to the ground is conveyed through the conveying pipe member filtering rainwater conveyed through the conveying pipe member through a filtration unit storing the filtered rainwater in a storage tank pumping the stored rainwater through at least one of river water maintenance water irrigation canal water vegetation water around the river and waterfront park landscaping fountain supplying the necessary power to the filtration unit and the pumping means by at least one of a photovoltaic device or a wind turbine wherein a portion of the rainwater is permeable in the step of inducing rainwater through the permeable sidewalk block"}]</data>
