  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100402289-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "first the sedimentation and flotation were caused by the specific gravity difference while the wastewater flowing into the decay tank 20 due to natural sedimentation remained in the decay tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261839-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention does not return the high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin so as to reduce the impact of the return of high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin and bioreactor it is economical and eco friendly because it can reduce the amount of injected chemicals and the power is reduced by adopting the slant plate settling tank and the sludge concentration can be automatically adjusted by continuously discharging the sludge and changing the hydraulic pressure difference using the hydraulic pressure difference.figure 1a is a block diagram of a conventional wake water treatment apparatus figure 1b is a flow chart of the prior art flocculation flotation 2 is a block diagram of a semi water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 3 is a cutaway showing the flow of sewage treatment in the inclined plate shaped sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 4 is a block diagram of the sludge automatic discharge line of the inclined plate type sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention 5 6 is a perspective view of the water level control of the sludge automatic discharge device of the inclined plate type sedimentation apparatus of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100598365-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "this is because large water tanks which are largely divided from large ones are more likely to leak due to hydraulic pressure in the case of minor gaps and ground subsidence"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137769-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition a number of filters shorten the filter life due to the continuous hydraulic pressure of the raw water may cause waste of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306389-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "it is discharged out of the system as it is via the drain valve 18 from the lower part of 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147924-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "reactor 2 a disk having a plurality of through holes having at least two guide portions protruding in the flow direction of the ballast water at opposite edges thereof and being fitted in a sliding manner along the guide grooves of the reaction tank to flow direction of the ballast water at least one hydraulic interruption plate installed vertically standing with respect to the and 3 the slender anode wire and the cathode wire have an annular shape as a whole so as to be wound in parallel with each other at regular intervals and the parallel wound anode wire and the cathode ray are perpendicular to the flow direction of the ballast water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100948425-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain pipe 20 having an upper end portion opened toward the outlet portion 22 and a discharge tube 25 opened at the lower end thereof in the seating space 24a and embedded in the ground a first door 30 rotatably fixed to the inlet portion 21 so as to be opened by the flow of sewage flowing from the upper sewer pipe 11 and closed by the flow of sewage flowing back a second door 40 rotatably fixed to the outlet portion 22 so as to be opened by the force of the sewage discharged from the drain pipe 20 and closed by the force of the sewage flowing back from the lower sewer pipe 12 a tube 50 seated in the seating space 24a and air flows in and out a bottom plate 60 constructed on the tube 50 to move up and down according to the internal pressure and the hydraulic pressure change of the tube 50 a switch 71 for opening and closing the tube 50 a pump 72 for forcibly transferring air from the tank t for storing air to the tube 50 and a set internal pressure while checking the internal pressure of the tube 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200185447-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "by the way the spherical frp water tank is composed of wall panels to be assembled as a whole and the cross sectional shape is formed as a rectangle so that the wall panel subjected to hydraulic pressure acts on a bending moment around the joint"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100443423-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the present invention for this purpose the sedimentation tank 31 for sedimentation and removal of foreign matter the screen tank 32 for screening and removing large contaminants contained in the effluent of the sedimentation tank the amount of sewage to be treated even when excessive raw water generation to alleviate contaminant load variation function as a flow control tank that maintains constant water and as an aeration tank to remove organic matter from sewage by oxidation and decomposition by microorganisms and floating and colloidal contaminants in the treated water from which dissolved bod is removed by aeration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181549-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the method according to claim 4 or 5 each of the first raw water supply module the second raw water supply module and the third raw water supply module an oil pressure measuring unit installed in the supply pipeline to measure oil pressure of raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder a flow rate control valve installed in the supply pipeline to regulate a flow rate of raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder a bypass pipeline branching from the supply pipeline and bypassing the raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder to the storage tank a bypass valve installed in the bypass pipeline to adjust a flow rate of raw water bypassed to the storage tank the pollution index predictor is configured to determine the hydraulic pressure of the raw water supplied to each of the filter membrane holders based on the hydraulic pressure measured by the hydraulic pressure measuring unit of each of the first raw water supply module the second raw water supply module and the third raw water supply module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101625667-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to a system for regulating the internal water pressure of a sewage treatment apparatus the present invention relates to a system for controlling the internal water pressure of a wastewater treatment apparatus in a sewage treatment field and more particularly to a system for controlling the water pressure of the wastewater treatment apparatus in a stepwise manner and when the high water pressure is generated inside the sewage treatment tank the water pressure is reduced by circulating the liquid material stored in the sewage treatment tank to the outside to a system for controlling the internal water pressure of a sewage treatment apparatus that suppresses horizontal maintenance and vibration to prevent the risk of collapse of the sewage treatment tank as the treatment tank becomes higher in hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101625667-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the present invention has an effect of suppressing horizontal maintenance and vibration to prevent the risk of collapse of the sewage treatment tank which may be generated as the water pressure increases inside the sewage treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200434137-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the sluice means 30 is a door frame 31 fixed to the outer wall surface of the washing tank 20 to surround the opening 23 and is installed to rotate so that the lower portion is pivoted on the top of the door frame 31 a door frame 32 for opening and closing the opening 23 through the door frame 31 a shaft member 33 installed to rotate across the left and right of the door frame 31 under the door frame 32 it is provided with a plurality of predetermined distances along the length of the shaft member 33 to walk the lower portion of the door 32 to close the opening 23 while rotating along the shaft member 33 for locking or freezing a hook member 34 having a groove 34a in the middle and a cylinder member 35a installed at one side of the door frame 31 and linked through an end of the shaft member 33 and a long hole 35d"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200410523-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "a body having a fastening hole formed in the member to concentrate the pressing force to the edge of the panel when the fastening hole is engaged with the flange a triangular side plate coupled to both sides of the body to prevent deformation of the body and having a through hole having the same axis therein wherein the reinforcing bar fixing bolt is inserted into the through hole reinforcing bar fixing bolt inserted into the through hole bolts for tightening the side plate the airtightness to the edge of the panel vulnerable to leakage and to improve the resistance of the panel by the hydraulic pressure of the assembly tank reinforcement bracket characterized in that it is also about the installation structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102092542-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it can increase the transfer efficiency of recycled coal the pressure feeding tank 16 is a structure using a venturi injector using the bernoulli principle to effectively transport water and waste coal using high pressure water wherein the pressure feeding tank 16 is a high pressure water provided from a high pressure water supply pump 17 it serves to forcibly send out the waste coals using the pressure of and the other side of the upper side is connected to the waste coal discharge line 18 extending from the water treatment tank 10 side to one side of the upper side of the pressure feeding tank 16 the high pressure water supply line 19 extending from the high pressure water supply pump 17 side is connected to the side of the lower end of the pressure feeding tank 16 by being connected to the petan storage tank 11 side by the waste coal transfer line 21 through the waste coal discharge line 18 the waste coal in the water treatment tank 10 flows into the inside of the pressure feeding tank 16 and at the same time the high pressure water supplied from the high pressure water supply pump 17 the high pressure water supply line 19 through the feeding tank 16 water and waste coals are discharged from the pressure feeding tank 16 by the hydraulic pressure exerted by the high pressure water at this time and are forcibly transported along the waste coal transport line 20 to be sent to the waste coal storage tank 11 by forcibly transporting the waste carbon depending on the strong earth power exerted by the pressure feeding tank 16 it is possible to shorten the time related to transport for regenerating activated carbon increase the overall transport efficiency and lower the activated carbon loss rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100897438-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level detecting means is installed on the inner bottom surface of the water tank and has a body in which deformation occurs according to the hydraulic pressure of the fluid filled in the water tank and the first optical fiber grating sensor is installed in the body of the fluid it is formed to measure the deformation amount of the main body generated by the hydraulic pressure in accordance with the filling amount the motor temperature measuring means is attached to one side of the motor so that the heat generated by the drive of the motor can be transferred the third optical fiber grating sensor is preferably installed inside the main body so as to measure the amount of deformation of the main body due to heat generated from the motor.the control device of the water treatment plant according to the present invention accurately measures the flow rate of water supplied or returned to each tank for the purification of sewage the water level of the sewage filled in each tank and the temperature of the motors thereby effectively purifying the chemical"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100897438-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "therefore it is possible to convert the water level of the water tank 301 according to the size of the hydraulic pressure the second optical fiber grating sensor 320 based on this by measuring the amount of hydraulic pressure applied to the main body 310 through the deformation amount of the main body 310 the water level of the tank 301 can be calculated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102785581-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide a sterilizing water generator for livestock quarantine which comprises manufacturing the cover of the capillary cluster with an elastic material to absorb a certain amount of pressure energy of the pump and return it to the capillaries thereby spraying water at the same pressure regardless of the position of each capillary so that there is no change in the amount of oh radicals absorbed due to electrostatic spraying and the produced sterilizing water can be sprayed on livestock or fed directly to livestock to block the inflow of viruses through the respiratory tract.to this end one embodiment of the present invention comprises a plasma reactor having a grounding electrode plate connected to the electrode of a high voltage generator a capillary cluster separated from the plasma reactor comprises a plurality of capillaries extending to the plasma reactor and connected to the electrode of the high voltage generator when drinking water is supplied through a pump the capillary cluster diffuses water in the form of mist from each capillary into the interior of the plasma reactor and through electrostatic spraying mist containing oh radicals adheres to the grounding electrode plate in the form of droplets and is then collected in a sterilizing water tank and the pump has a feature in that the rotational speed is maintained constant through a hydraulic pressure gauge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200142277-Y1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "thus the present invention does not provide a shutoff valve operated by hydraulic pressure of a tank for storing purified water between the filter 2 and the membrane 3 having a large hydraulic pressure and the two filters 1 and 2 and the membrane by installing at the wastewater outlet 5 flowing under reduced pressure by 3 even if high pressure water flows into the inlet source a the inlet source is blocked only by the water pressure of the storage tank 6 to prevent leakage of the inlet water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156125-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "while opening the backwash valve 37b of the backwashing pipe 40c the air blower 38 communicating with the lower part of the filtration section 2 is operated to operate the reactor 21 and the coagulation tank perforated block portion 4 or strainer provided at the bottom of the filtration section 2 simultaneously or sequentially with the raw water provided by the hydraulic pressure difference from any one of the 22 and the air supplied through the air blower 38 it feeds into said filtration compartment 2 via section 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_99", "text": "accordingly as the piston 87a of the piston valve 87a is pushed to the left side the through hole 876a of the blocking rod 875a is positioned on the second passage 852a thereby opening the second passage 852a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101026854-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as the bottom plate construction method for the prefabricated water tank placing and curing concrete in a formwork constructed to a size that can support the water tank to form a first base chipping the first base surface and forming a joint in the same shape as the water tank arranging and assembling the base frame to the first base surface in accordance with the joint seating an angle bent to be in close contact with the inner surface of the base frame and the first base surface coupling a fixing bolt having a support member embedded in the concrete of the second base to each fastening hole of the angle and the base frame is supported so as not to be pushed by hydraulic pressure and fastening the fixing support by fastening the fixing nut to the fixing bolt making a step fixing the angle fixed by the fastening support with a set bolt to a first base seating a drain portion of the same block as a drain box and a pipe for guiding drainage of water on an upper surface of the first foundation inside the base frame placing and curing concrete so as to be gradient in the direction of the drain portion in the base frame on which the drain portion is seated to form a second foundation separating a block of the drain portion in the second foundation and installing a plurality of polyethylene sheets so that the ends overlap the upper surface of the second foundation fixing the drain box and the polyethylene sheet by heat fusion in a state in which the drain box of the drain portion is seated on the second base from which the block is separated and a plurality of fastener mounting steps mounted on a second base to prevent the flow of the polyethylene sheet by contraction so as to fix the polyethylene sheet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041191-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the submersible motor pump in the state that the normal water can not be delivered to the water tank due to the freezing of the water pipe the overload pressure is generated as the water pump continues to be sustained the load on the submersible motor pump is heavily loaded and the life may be significantly reduced or damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "US-4946574-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "after the electrolysis is completed the electrolyzed water from said electrolytic cell 12 is divided into alkaline water 101 and acidic water 102 wherein said acidic water 102 is directly drained out since it cannot be used for drinking while said alkaline water flows into an ultraviolet sterilizing tank 15 to be sterilized therein before flowing out therefrom to be used for drinking purposes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100861685-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in this case the liquid chlorine injector may include a liquid chlorine tank in which liquid chlorine is stored a venturi pipe connecting the liquid chlorine tank and the final treatment pipe a chlorine injection pump installed to inject liquid chlorine into the liquid chlorine tank and a chlorine input control means for receiving a rotational speed of the water wheel rotary blade of the non powered contaminant remover and providing the same as a feedback signal to the chlorine input pump to control the amount of chlorine input through the chlorine input pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition there is a fear of secondary contamination such as microbial growth due to the stagnation of the treated water in the storage tank it was necessary to increase the processing capacity of the process to be treated at the rear end of the storage tank.the present invention was devised to solve the above mentioned problems and does not install a reservoir and does not apply a brake to the flow of treated water and does not require an additional pump and does not additionally install a reservoir and a pump in the middle of a water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in detail the hydraulic pressure applied to the treated water is determined by the pressure the pressure due to the height difference h1 between the membrane filtration unit 100 and the residual decontamination unit 200 the pressure due to the height difference h2 between the advanced oxidation tank 210 and the activated carbon adsorption tank 220 in the residual contamination removal unit 200 the pressure due to the height difference h3 between the activated carbon adsorption tank 220 and the disinfection tank 230 of course if there is a height difference between the disinfection tank 230 and the purified water 2 as shown in figure 3 the pressure due to free fall is also applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore by controlling the pump 10 and the valve 33 installed on the raw water inlet side of the membrane filtration unit 100 the advanced oxidation tank 210 activated carbon adsorption constituting the residual contamination removal unit 200 installed at the rear end by adjusting the hydraulic pressure in the tank 220 and the disinfection tank 230 it is possible to smoothly perform each water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing process for obtaining pure water from salt water comprising feeding salt water to a vertically arranged elongated closed tank to establish a column of salt water therein the level of which is above the feed point continuously cooling a body of mercury externally of said tank and injecting said mercury in the form of finely atomized particles into the upper portion of said liquid column withdrawing said mercury from the bottom of said tank and recirculating said mercury through said liquid column to maintain the column at a temperature which is subcooled with respect to the salt water infeed so that the infeed has ice crystals formed therein due to contact with the subcooled column permitting the ice crystals to accumulate and form a solid block of ice in the upper portion of said tank above the level of mercury injection moving said block of ice upwardly in said tank by hydraulic pressure of incoming salt water and melting the upper portion of said block of ice by indirect heat exchange with the salt water feed prior to entry of said feed into said column and withdrawing pure water from the upper portion of the tank between the top of said tank and the top of said ice block and withdrawing concentrated salt water and precipitated salts collected above the mercury from the lower portion of said tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the heat exchange which takes place in the exchanger 20 at the upper portion of the tank melts the upper portion of the ice block in the zones a and b so that pure water may be withdrawn from the zone a at the outlet 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200186812-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore the present invention can exhibit a sufficient reinforcing effect to prevent the deformation of the circumferential direction due to the self weight of the sewage purification tank body by the reinforcing band filled in the reinforcing band and the space in the reinforcing band as well as the thickness"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in addition the present invention has the effect of preventing the malfunction in advance by providing a pressure preventing means for enclosing the third opening and closing plate to prevent the third opening and closing plate is not opened by the water pressure in the storage tank even if the buoyancy chamber level is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101047186-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "other factors to consider include water pressure seawater loads when large fish collide the size and material of the tank the waterproofing and finishing materials that take into account the hydraulic pressure and the selection of materials to prevent fatal toxicity and corrosion to the fish"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102702059-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition the above described non powered scum generator is provided with a cone shaped rotating block that is positioned at the center of the first tank and is capable of non powered rotation by rising hydraulic pressure and a spiral projection is provided on the periphery of the rotating block and a blade that removes scum is connected to the upper portion thereof thereby providing a water circulation treatment system using a high speed oxidation and composite separation process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439293-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "on the other hand the controller 10 continuously detects the pressure drop while the raw water is discharged through the water supply pipe 51 but when the raw water is near the high water level h and the middle water level m or the low water level l the pressure drop detected when close is different"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266017-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "to this end the downstream water supply pipe 4 connected to the elevated water tank installed on the roof of the high rise building the horizontal pipe 5 installed in parallel with the downward water supply pipe 4 and the horizontal pipe 5 connected to the meter 6 is provided and the interior pipe 11 having the bent portion 12 the intermediate valve 21 installed in the cross pipe 5 for reducing the water pressure to a predetermined pressure or less and the cross pipe 5 in the water supply piping device of the high rise building consisting of a first noise canceling unit 23 consisting of a pressure gauge 22 installed in the pressure gauge 22 to measure the pressure of the intermediate valve 21 the diameter of the indoor pipe 11 it is the same as the main hole 25 is formed in the central portion the outer space of the main hole 25 is formed at equal intervals of the fasteners 27 formed with a number of auxiliary through holes 26 the main formed in the fastener 27 it is attached to the through hole 25 to gently form the angle of the bent portion 12 of the indoor pipe 11 by the hydraulic pressure the second silencer made of a soft inner tube 28 having a step 30 formed on one side and a packing 29 installed at the front of the fixture 27 to prevent leakage when connected to the meter 6"}]</data>
</edge>
