  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101501179-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "especially it is difficult to secure the site because it requires a separate site to install the contact tank and it is difficult to select the site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200385155-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in other words if the raw water flows in excess of the design flow due to natural disasters such as rainy season or flood natural disasters or unavoidable circumstances the inflow may not be properly processed and the membrane separation tank overflows and the immersion membrane separator may collapse"}, {"pat_id": "US-4815492-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the tank may also be made from fiberglass if desired"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment 811 the above flood control equipment 811 is the hull position movement construction machinery control equipment 811a the marine hydroelectric power generation control equipment 811b the power transmission control equipment 811c the harmful red tide prevention control equipment 811d the disaster prevention control equipment 811e the fishery spawning control equipment 811f and the dam water gate control control equipment 811g are each individually equipped and the floating dock device of the flood control equipment is connected to the inside of the flood control equipment body 1 to prevent flooding of the underground passage the floating dock device of the above flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding connected to the ocean tunnel traffic device 941 and the ocean hydroelectric power plant the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment has a length of 800 mm a diameter of 300 mm a portable lug connecting pin connection shaft for the inner and outer walls of each tank of the main tank and the outer block tank and a thickness of the steel plate of the portable lug is 150 mm and the pin connecting shaft is inserted into the portable lug to be connected and the processing hole of the connecting pin connecting shaft has a diameter of 30 mm and the portable lug pin has a length and a pin body diameter of 500 2 10 mm and is disassembled and combined with a nut at the threaded position processed into the end portion of the pin connecting shaft inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding the double structure block tank transported by the tugboat is a barge hull on the top of the holding tank assembled by a band jig mounted on a semi submersible work vessel with a length and width of 600 m and a height and steel plate thickness of 800 m and 40 m and 18 mm and the barge hull on the bottom of the holding tank has a pipe bridge at each of the four corners in the length and width of 15 m and a diameter and thickness of \u03c015 m and a length of 24 mm and a thickness of 1 km forming a double structure block tank inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment the size of the external block tank which is composed of the perimeter of the main tank and the inner block tank is individually combined to form a small sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 600 m a length of 800 m a height of 800 m a height of 600 m a medium sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 2 m a length of 3.2 m and a height of 2 m and a large sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 10 m a length of 10 m and a height of 10 m and the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment while operating according to the sea depth the portable lug pin is installed by fastening the bolt nut in the machined hole of the lug connecting shaft and at the same time the pin is bent to prevent the lug pin from coming off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helicopter station 619 and a thermal power plant 626 are equipped with satellite launch pads 643 and mooring towers 644 and space rocket launch pads to detect climate abnormalities and equipment for detecting the weather movement status of the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention flood control equipment to detect climate abnormalities in order to prioritize emergency rescue the flood control equipment in the flooded area is always equipped with several air compressors 80 connected to rescue tubes 130 and ropes 131 at the accident site and before the underground passage is flooded the flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment to prevent flooding by installing a water tank for rescue and flood control in the flooded area so that people can board the tubes 130 and be rescued by rescue workers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire hose 9 and a fire nozzle frame 11 and a hook 13 in a detection sensor 12 and a jig 22 in a pipe 14 are configured to control the flow rate to the disaster prevention waterway 17 while forming a vertical multistage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for flood prevention of underground passages the flood control equipment which consists of fire pumps and high performance submersible pumps a hook and a wire rope a machined hole and a shackle a bolt and nut a washer and a hinge a flange or a flange stopper a wire mesh a coupling a coupling female threaded body 30 a coupling male threaded body 31 a gasket or rubber packing a nozzle hose equipment holder 