r quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the assembled rainwater storage tank 10 according to the present invention having the above described structure can be installed rapidly and firmly to meet the capacity suitable for the building at low cost and can use rainwater as drinking water for drinking water and emergency drinking water it is possible to prevent flood control in the rainy season and typhoon as well as to surely prevent pollution by contaminated initial rainwater by eliminating a large but early power without extra power.10 assembly type stormwater tank 20 water storage tank tower 21 lower block 22 water quality observation block 23 upper block 24 capacity adjustment block 30 drain pipe assembly 31 first drain pipe 32 opening and closing means 33 second drain pipe 34 filter pipe 40 water supply pipe 50 water pump 60 advanced water purification device 70 fountain hose 80 sterilization device 90 water storage tank 100 building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892658-A", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "to provide about one inch ponding in the stone distribution beds overlying the 11 200 square foot of sand filter surface 2000 gallons of clarified wastewater should be derived at each dose"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101699031-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to the water treatment apparatus of the present invention the particulate pollutants contained in the silt treatment water flowing into the flow rate adjusting tank through the run off grooves formed in the flood wall defining the sediment tank and the flow rate adjusting tank are filtered by the filter the flow of the silt treated water flowing into the flow rate adjusting tank via the needle bed is more directional than that of the conventional method so that it has some effect of preventing the settling of the contamination source by the turbulence"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7117022-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "it may also be implemented in a mixed format with a partial hardware module that implements a part of hardware elements.brief description of the drawings it is a block diagram which shows the inland water flooding analysis apparatus which concerns on embodiment 1 of this invention.fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-5536411-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "demineralized water is removed from the demineralization unit 60 and transported via pipeline 48 to flood water storage tank 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition according to the storage tank operating system and operating method through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention it is possible to effectively cope with a disaster such as a flood caused by a sudden sudden change in the flow rate due to a heavy rain or a local rainfall.1 is a view illustrating a storage tank operating system to which a storage tank operating system is applied through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "4 this water softener 30 includes a cylindrical water softener body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center it includes a support cylinder 39 fixed to the bottom of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention provides a method for preventing the heat island phenomenon of a road using the heat island phenomenon prevention structure characterized in that the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 is measured and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a preset temperature the pump 700 is driven to supply water to the spray unit 600 through the water supply pipe 610 and when the temperature of the permeable pavement 100 reaches a temperature lower than the preset temperature water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 is sucked in by the suction pipe 710 of the pump 700 and at the same time water is supplied into the rainwater storage tank 200 by the bypass pipe 620 thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 200 .the present invention proposes a rainwater storage structure for a road and a rainwater storage method using the same which can prevent urban flood damage caused by localized heavy rain due to climate change and distortion of the water circulation system due to overdevelopment of urban areas.figure 1 below illustrates an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 deep dredging of the river having a large length maintenance and construction of the embankment of the dredged river so that it does not collapse using the civil engineering material after installing the foundation concrete on the bottom and side of the river the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algal bloom for both ado and hydroelectric power generation is installed in a multi level step in the upper part to store a large amount of river water to produce eco friendly electricity while polluted after installing an eco friendly artificial fish farm combined rainwater storage tank at the inlet of rivers rivers dams and reservoirs which acts to purify river water naturally and at the same time to prevent flood damage the embankment is equipped with the automatic control system and the monitoring using an eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algal blooms for both a fishway and hydroelectric power generation which is configured by combining a camera and the remote control system a large amount of river water is stored to prevent flood damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "para_472", "text": "after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring suggests a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10526776-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the tank wall 202 the tank top 206 the tank bottom 204 and the couplings there between may be watertight such that the flood water 950 in the storage tank 200 does not leak from the storage tank 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to purify rainwater collected in a storage tank and to provide it as a landscape water and a living water thereby preventing a water shortage phenomenon and a nonpoint pollution reduction high initial stormwater is stored in the reservoir and purified rainwater is discharged at the end of rainfall or gradually penetrated into the underground to prevent flood maintain groundwater level at a certain level to prevent ground stabilization and river pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
