y removing residual organics in the circulating fluid from the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank installed in the liquid corrosion tank and the liquid corrosion tank which oxidizes nh 4 n ammonia nitrogen with nox n nitrogen nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the settled solids are supplied to the secondary settling tank 416 by the central cone cone it is possible to deposit active erosion material pellets minerals containing active minerals minerals or ceramics that emit negative ions and ultraviolet rays that emit far infrared rays and negative ions by the secondary transfer pump 417 the excess sludge is returned to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 and the secondary aeration tank 414 in which the secondary bioreactor 419 filled with the mineral or ceramics packing 420 is loaded and the excess sludge discharged is discharged temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater and the biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage together with the excess sludge to be discharged to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 sludge precipitated in the secondary settling tank 415 is supplied to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the secondary bioreactor 419 and the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 a corrosive microorganism which transforms water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors or corrosive substances by providing a polyphenol compound as a metabolite by supplying a wastewater and microbes in symbiotic relationships and sent to the secondary aeration tank 414 to induce the whole of the secondary biological wastewater treatment system to be subjected to the wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and the microorganisms which are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms and the secondary settling tank 415 the second biologically treated water which is the overflowing water is the second biological treatment step of the low concentration wastewater sent to the final biological treatment water tank 421 the secondary biologically treated water is subjected to sterilization treatment by a combination of at least one of oxidizing agent oxidizing agent ultraviolet ray irradiation electrolytic oxidation or electron beam irradiation and then subjected to sand filtration to remove suspended solids a final treatment step of the wastewater discharging the treated water when the dehydrated cake dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process is supplied to the mixer 500 a moisture adjuster and a soil conditioner are injected into the mixer mixer 501 while stirring to adjust the water content to 60 to 65 wt and fed to a fermentation tank 503 which is opened and straightened by the fermentation tank feed conveyor 502 and then flipped to the fermentation tank mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 30 to 50 days"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "denitrifying removing the remaining organic matter from the circulating fluid from the anaerobic liquid corrosion tank and oxidizing ammonia nitrogen to n0x n nitric acid nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen in an aerobic liquid corrosion tank extracting the liquid corrosion solution treated in the anoxic liquid corrosion tank and the aerobic liquid corrosion tank into a mixing tank while the input and circulation of the organic wastewater is stopped for 1 hour per day injecting the liquid corrosion solution drawn out into the mixing tank into an agglomeration reaction tank and coagulating with a coagulant and a ph adjusting agent and separating the flocculated liquid erosion solution into sludge and desorption solution with a dehydrator when the organic sewage is introduced into the first storage tank 2 vol or less of the circulating fluid circulated between the anoxic liquid corrosion tank and the aerobic liquid corrosion tank is added to the first storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in this case if the treated water is reused as the washing water of the dehydrator the cod of the treated water accumulates and there is a problem of exceeding the target water quality standard.the present invention is to reduce the odor gas generation in the pre treatment process of the collected organic sewage maintain the mlss concentration of organic sewage to be injected into the liquid corrosion tank on an appropriate basis and set the volume and ratio of the anaerobic liquid corrosion tank and aerobic liquid corrosion tank in the case of alternating anoxic respirators the amount of circulation is calculated according to the inflow ammonia concentration and the input amount and the excess bod of the new high concentration organic sewage injected into the aerobic liquid corrosion tank is treated and the amount of bod and ammonia nitrogen flowing out of the aerobic liquid corrosion tank is minimized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the amount of circulation is about 1.5 times the total amount of the anaerobic liquid corrosion bath solution and the aerobic liquid corrosion bath solution and the liquid erosion liquid that has completed liquid erosion is stopped while the input and circulation of the anoxic liquid corrosion bath solution and the aerobic liquid corrosion bath solution are stopped for 1 hour a day"}]</data>
