  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100794491-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "an inlet 110 and an outlet 120 through which rainwater flows in and out of the upper portion is formed and a treatment tank 100 provided with a predetermined inclined surface 130 to deposit sludge in the inner space it is provided on the upper side of the processing tank 100 when the rainwater flowing in from the inlet 110 is less than a predetermined amount to flow only into the interior of the processing tank 100 and partitioned to be divided into the upper and lower sides when the rainwater increase 200 a partition wall 300 formed at a predetermined thickness and length on a lower surface of the cover 200 so that the rainwater introduced through the inlet 110 is treated in an upflow manner it is installed to be detached to one side treatment tank 100 of the partition 300 and consists of a filter medium 400 filled with a filter medium 410 therein the back of the treatment tank 100 has a certain size crushed stone 520 is installed between the crushed stone 520 and the treatment tank 100 mortar 530 is characterized in that the storm water drainage reuse system for reducing non point pollution load"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248173-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "patent registration 10 0582121 excellent storage tank patent registration 10 0938223 assembly type excellent storage tank patent 10 1118263 excellent storage tank and pre construction method using precast concrete block patent 10 1013235 method of manufacturing excellent storage tank the present invention is a prefabricated rainwater storage tank column and the bottom and top of the columnar block and the prefabricated block for easy to carry out the vertical assembly process was a high difficulty in the process of building an excellent storage tank by pc block assembly the purpose is to provide a bottom column beam coupling structure of the prefabricated rainwater storage tank combined with a simple and stable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "and a contaminant treatment means 500 provided between the first compartment member 300 and the second compartment member 400 to remove contaminants from the influent water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition between the second compartment member 400 and the storm water receiving tank 100 is further provided with a contaminant filtration adsorption means 700 filled with a filter medium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "here the storm drainage treatment apparatus according to the present invention may not have a passage for guiding the inflow of water to the upper side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the contaminant material desorbed from the filtering unit 220 and the sludge separated from the stormwater so that the filtered effluent can be prevented from flowing into the filtration means 220 while passing through the filtration means 220"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582121-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the bottom plate has a storage block formed with a coupling portion to be integral with the base surface and and a top block having a rectangular plate shape and end of which is mounted on the top plate stepped portion of the storage block to be coplanar with the top plate of the storage block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582121-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the upper block 30 has a rectangular plate shape having a predetermined thickness and is formed on the stepped portion 15 of the upper plate 11 of the storage block 10 to be coplanar with the upper plate of the storage block"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter recharge chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the non point pollutant reduction facility a back washing water supply unit for washing the filter media by using the filtered water introduced into the back washing tank as back washing water and a backwashing means including a backwashing means for discharging the backwashing water after washing the filter media to the outside of the treatment structure further comprising the reverse wash water supply unit a first pump installed on the bottom of the backwashing tank and including a backwash water supply pipe connected to the discharge portion side of the first pump the backwash supply pipe extends to an upper side of the filtration tank while branching in a plurality so as not to interfere with the lifting operation unit of the filtering means and the first filter plate and the first filter plate on the backwash supply pipe extending to the upper side of the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "specifically the non point pollutant reduction facility includes a back washing water supply unit for washing the filter media using the filtered water introduced into the back washing tank as back washing water and a backwashing means for discharging the backwashing water after washing the filter materials to the outside of the treatment structure further comprising the backwashing supply unit a first pump installed at the bottom of the backwashing tank and a backwash water supply pipe connected to the discharge portion side of the first pump but the backwash water supply pipe extends to the upper side of the filtration tank while branching into a plurality so as not to interfere with the lifting operation unit of the filtering means and to the upper side of the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-7780855-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "these two factors combined would result in greater total contaminants being brought to the separator tank during peak flows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "second step s2 of seating the excellent storage tank block b consisting of the connecting member 30 to the cut bottom surface the third step s3 of inserting the fastener 40 into the seating groove 21a of the rainwater storage tank blocks b arranged in a multi row species and fixed through the fastening means the fourth step s4 of placing the finishing panel 60 on the outer circumferential surface of the rainwater tank block b and fixing it via the fastening means the fifth step s5 of forming a waterproof layer by applying a waterproofing material to the peripheral surface of the rainwater storage block b in which the finishing panel 60 is installed rainfall storage tank characterized in that it comprises a sixth step s6 after the soil is covered with the top surface of the storm water storage block b having a waterproof layer is chopped or pour concrete into the top surface of the soil after soil cover excellent storage tank construction method using blocks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "and in the case of the lower block body 10 is connected to each other via a fastening means long bolt and nut as shown in the enlarged view of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition according to the storage tank operating system and operating method through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention it is possible to effectively cope with a disaster such as a flood caused by a sudden sudden change in the flow rate due to a heavy rain or a local rainfall.1 is a view illustrating a storage tank operating system to which a storage tank operating system is applied through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101398010-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a reservoir installed on the lower side of the gutter a connection pipe connecting the storm water pipe and the storage tank a storage tank installed in the connection pipe for controlling the stormwater flowing into the storage tank through the connection pipe a first sensor installed on the upstream side of the connection pipe among the gross conduits and measuring a contamination degree and a quantity of the ozone flowing into the gutter tube a second sensor installed inside the storage tank for measuring a contamination level and a water level of the storm water filled in the storage tank a discharge pump installed in the storage tank for sucking the rainwater in the storage tank and discharging the rainwater to the outside and a control unit for opening and closing the storage tank gates in accordance with an initial stormwater inflow signal and an initial wastewater termination signal of the first sensor and driving the discharge pump according to the high water level signal or the contamination signal of the second sensor the storage tank gates a connection pipe interlocking part installed to be rotatable at an inlet of the connection pipe and interrupting the connection pipe while rotating and an excellent pipe shut off part slidably installed in the connection pipe cut off part and slid in a state where the connection pipe cut off part is opened to cut off the excellent pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-5462655-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a fluid recapture system collects residual waste fluids generated during airplane washing or de icing procedures and separates and recycles these fluids to prevent contamination of storm water drainage and sewer systems and ground water supplies"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain storm event these storage tanks can be overwhelmed thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system a body of water or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-5806702-A", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "because the storage tanks may be empty or nearly empty for extended periods such tanks must be strong enough to withstand the crushing forces of hydrostatic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "is protruded is provided so as to be spaced apart from the bottom of the road side catch port 10 the horizontal catch plate 94 is adjusted to the height according to the water level flowing through the road side catch port 10 by the buoyancy body 92 and the coarse coarse collusion through lower rainwater downflow horizontal collecting plate 94 it is characterized in that it is provided to be filtered through the water filtration network 96 .according to the above configuration and operation the present invention is to embed the storage tank in the bottom of the flower bed formed between the road and the sidewalk to quickly absorb and collect rainwater flowing along the road during rainy weather and to supply the rainwater stored in the storage tank to the lower flower bed it helps to drown landscaping water and in particular contaminants contained in rainwater can be easily filtered and recycled into water resources including road cooling water road washing water and digestive water to contribute to water shortage.1 is a block diagram showing the stormwater storage system as a whole for vegetation infiltration according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "at this time the rainwater that is filtered through the first storage block 10 and a plurality of storage blocks 10 adjacent to each other repeatedly is introduced into the storage space s connected to each other via the above described downstream guide pipe 16"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain storm event these storage tanks can be overwhelmed thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system a body of water or a river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
