  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-9493370-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "due to the unpredictable nature of these variables there may be a considerable time lag between introduction of treatment chemicals into the wastewater stream and acceptable effluent contamination levels at the outlet of the daf"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102602769-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "during operation the anode catalyst enables electro oxidation reactions for treating wastewater in the tank and can be consumed catalytically over time whereas the cathode catalyst due to the nature of the reactions occurring at the cathode catalytically protected and not consumed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a structure in which the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir frame 830 and white paper 88 are combined to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity on top of the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir 8888 is formed a structure in which a shaped siphon action generating assembly partition 836 is sequentially fixed to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a structure in which the power generation water discharge pipe 3151 is constructed at an angle along the slope of the downstream part of the river starting from the lower part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth a structure in which an upward discharge pipe 3150 is formed in an l shape at a height that is 5 to 20 lower than the height of the lower part of the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is formed in the upstream part of the river at the end of the above mentioned power generation water discharge pipe 3151 a structure in which a terminal discharge pipe 3152 is formed in a t shape at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 3150 a structure in which an air exhaust unit 381 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a plurality of power generation water final pipes 262 each having a different thickness are connected around the end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a control unit 266 configured to control the discharge amount is connected to the upper part of the final power generation water pipe 262 a structure in which an upper storage tank 259 is connected to a lower discharge unit 256 configured in a different form with each storage capacity to store power generation water and discharge it to the lower part at the lower part of the above mentioned power generation water final pipeline 262 a structure in which a hydroelectric power generation unit 335 configured to generate electricity by hydraulic power is combined at the lower end of the above mentioned lower discharge unit 256 a nature friendly eco friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water using an eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae growth that is characterized by generating hydroelectric power by using an eco friendly movable dam that acts to prevent green algae growth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100407498-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "water condenses on the bottom surface of the tank due to condensation which causes the synthetic resin sheet attached by the adhesive to be separated from the wall of the tank.there is a risk that the growth of microorganisms and environmental hormones may occur due to the nature of the synthetic resin"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101207373-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the ph is 2.5 to 7.5 preferably 3.0 to 4.5 and a narrower management width may be selected depending on the contamination concentration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345769-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition the conventional wear and wash tank is provided with a movable beam that is opened and closed by a hydraulic cylinder for the fresh water and discharge of the rainwater or the initial excellent water such a movable beam requires a high cost of construction due to the nature of being submerged in water there is a problem that is not easy to maintain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0148780-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "although activated carbon is dissolved in a dissolution tank and then administered to an object it does not guarantee a miscibility with water due to the nature of these chemicals and for this miscellaneous mechanical forced miscation must be installed separately at the flocculant input stage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102083441-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "when the ozone is circulated as described above it is effective to recirculate the discharged ozone to the inflow side by contacting the water in the ozone reaction tank at the outflow side.the method for treating wastewater containing an organic solvent according to the present invention comprises a thermal treatment step and a forced oxidation treatment step for the treatment of a wastewater containing a high concentration of hardly decomposable organic solvent and the wastewater containing the organic solvent is preheated while passing through a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102319947-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "thus the water pretreatment process affects the amount and nature of the hydrophobic particles which as a quality control parameter for adjusting the dosing of coagulants and or flocculants or other chemicals preferably coagulants and or flocculants in the water pretreatment process"}, {"pat_id": "US-6475395-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "considering the long standing nature of the fouling problem and the fact that the technology relating to in place gas cleaning of tubing type diffusers has been readily available to sewage plant designers for years it might seem reasonable to assume that in place gas cleaning would have long ago become the technique of choice for the tank type aeration facilities equipped with multi pore diffusion elements"}, {"pat_id": "US-11649178-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "some anti corrosion agents may be added in the water tank water heater or boiler but due to their non volatile nature remain there as the water or steam is let out of the water tank water heater or boiler"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200437433-Y1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "due to the nature of the construction work the panel tank is not easy to install the seat due to the irregularities on the upper surface of the concrete foundation and if the panel tank tank cannot be maintained smoothly the water pressure is concentrated in some areas causing frequent leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-10843952-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the hardware of the present invention including the pipes circulation pump 235 air pump 250 water tank s 265 and other primary elements of the system of the present invention remain consistent across all installations however if the demands of the installation require or exhibit higher flow rates than traditional residential or commercial installations multiple iterations of elements of the system of the present invention may be deployed and installed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4332915-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "powdered activated carbon can adsorb and remove organic compounds corresponding to environmental hormones by using a device that is stirred and mixed with environmental hormone containing water in an adsorption tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_144", "text": "water generated in nature such as rainwater and fog may be collected through the smart water collection system 10 of the present invention and specifically the first storage tank 140 of the tree type water collection facility 100 the bench type water collection system it may be temporarily collected through the second storage tank 220 of the facility 200 and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101068164-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition the present invention is to form a glass tile by the glass plate member to prevent the corrosion and water pollution of the water tank in the nature of the glass surface is very smooth and almost no chemical reaction it is easy to wash and clean"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "para_472", "text": "after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring suggests a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8262914-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "due to the unpredictable nature of these variables there may be a considerable time lag between introduction of treatment chemicals into the wastewater stream and acceptable effluent contamination levels at the outlet of the daf"}]</data>
