lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413010-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 1 wherein the interval between the steel square pipe 2 and the lower contact portion of the frp material is provided with a gap 11 to absorb the difference in thermal expansion amount between the steel and the frp material during operation is natural frp cover for preventing odor leak of sewage waste water tank characterized in that to prevent the cracks generated in the frp plate by being absorbed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413010-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in this case the absorption interval to absorb the difference in thermal expansion amount should be determined according to the size and shape of the cover and the operating temperature of the radiant heat generated by solar heat and steam heat generated from sewage wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "however the coupling by bearing is possible in a fermentation device operated at room temperature and normal pressure but there is room for problems such as leakage and deformation due to thermal expansion in a drying device supplied with high temperature and high pressure dry air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100665619-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in general when working in wet environment and water the adhesion between the coating film and the structural material or concrete or steel is weak and peeling due to the difference in coefficient of thermal expansion"}]</data>
