ols the flow rate and an elbow or tie elbow changes the flow rate to prevent underground flooding and a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and flood control equipment the power supply which is a power supply device supplied from a hydroelectric power generator 213 is inverter 47 and inverter vio access point and internet network vertical multistage pump control server and monitor to pump control board or tagger winch control box and short range wireless communication antenna to short range wireless communication device wireless communication control module and display to electronic control device adc and switch input circuit to electronic control device mcu and electronic control device diac overcurrent breaker brake is connected to power supply to display screen and analog input and digital input are operated by hand to control on off of each pump main switch button and auxiliary switch button to configure vertical multistage pump operation method inside main body 1 of underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment in addition to the above mentioned vertical multi stage pump turbine pump 140 diaphragm pump vane pump or guide vane and propeller pump screw pump plunger pump axial plunger pump radial plunger pump and jet pump 157 are provided and are connected to an introduction pipe and a water supply port or a fire prevention and disaster prevention pipe line 168 and a water discharge port 169 and are connected to a limit switch or a limit switch and a power motor body 192 is provided with a hood and a snap ring a fan and a body frame a body front reinforcing plate a rotor assembly on a rotating shaft a stator assembly on a front rotating shaft support a motor protection casting frame a terminal box and a lifting bolt a terminal box cover a rear rotating shaft support a rear reinforcing plate a gap a fan cover or a protective cover a rotor core and a stator core with stator windings and are connected and connected and underground passage flood prevention a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172182-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "moreover the present invention detects running water continuously supplied through waterways inside the frame and applies power only when water is supplied thereby preventing unnecessary electricity use and electrode wear caused by this and always keeps water into the lower water tank in the waterway inside the frame"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172182-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in order to block the water supply 15 while descending according to the water supply cutoff again the water supply is separated from the operation sensor to cut off the power supply to the gold or silver plate and the water tank 40 in the lower portion of the waterway inside the frame is turned off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "frame installed in the upper part of the waterway the drive unit is installed in this frame to rotate when the power is supplied and the lifting unit is capable of lifting various foreign matters such as sand or soil in the sedimentation tank of the waterway while being transferred and received the rotational force of the drive unit and in the sediment removal device of the sewage treatment facility comprising a conveyor portion for transporting to receive the sediment lifted by the lifting portion to be discharged to the outside it is installed on the upper part of the waterway to receive the falling sediment to the conveyor unit 140 receives the sediment the amount of sedimentation is measured in the load cell 151 for a predetermined time and then dropped to the conveyor unit 140 weighing unit 150 it is installed on the frame 110 and configured to receive the calculated amount of sedimentation measured in the load cell 151 of the sedimentation measurement unit 150 as a signal so that the sedimentation lifting speed is automatically variable and controlled according to a large number of the amount of sedimentation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the sediment removal device of the sewage treatment facility of the present invention for achieving the above object the frame is installed on the upper portion of the water channel the drive unit is installed on the frame to rotate when the power is supplied and the rotational force of the drive unit is transferred to transfer the lifting part is capable of lifting various foreign matters such as sand or soil from the sedimentation tank of the waterway and the conveyor part for transporting the sediment lifted by the lifting part so as to be discharged to the outside but falling onto the conveyor part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "drive unit 120 and the lifting unit 130 which is to be transported by receiving the rotational force of the drive unit to lift various foreign materials such as sand or soil in the sedimentation tank of the waterway and receiving the sediment lifted from the lifting unit in addition to having a conveyor 140 for transporting the discharge to the discharge it is installed on the upper portion of the waterway to receive the sediment falling to the conveyor unit 140 receives the sediment from the load cell for a predetermined time measure and then receive the signal of the sedimentation unit 150 to be dropped to the conveyor unit and the amount of sedimentation measured in the load cell of the sedimentation unit is installed in the frame the control unit 160 is configured to automatically control the sedimentation lifting speed according to the number of the sedimentation amount by calculating and preventing the substructure of the salvage part from being buried in accordance with the increase in the amount of sedimentation to prevent electric mechanical damage due to overload"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the modular wetland infrastructure 300 maintenance to be connected to the lower contact oxidation tank 500 to maintain the contact oxidation tank 500 located in the lower portion of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 manhole 330 and if the water level of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to precipitation exceeds a certain level in order to protect the wetland by transferring the influent directly to the sedimentation tank 400 modular wetland infrastructure 300 it is preferable to have a water level control pipe 340 is installed at the bottom of the through water connection with the drainage layer connected to the settling tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "because of this the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "as a method of separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water by using green energy such as sunlight or hydropower a producing power through the solar power generation unit 1510 and supplying power to the power supply unit 140 to supply electricity through the electrode 130 s210 b temporarily storing the purified seawater in the storage tank 110 and first electrolyzing the electrode 130 through the electrode 130 s220 c performing second electrolysis through the electrode 130 in the waterway 120 while flowing the first electrolyzed seawater from the reservoir 110 s230 d injecting the caustic soda containing water electrolyzed through the step c into the inlet through the jet port 1601 and simultaneously heating the same through the evaporation chamber 1610 to generate steam s240 e receiving steam heated in the evaporation chamber 1610 through a moving duct 1615 to generate a steam turbine generator 1620 s250 and f collecting the concentrated caustic soda heated through the evaporation chamber 1610 through the drainage port 1603 in step d and generating and remaining the steam turbine generator 1620 in step e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "on the other hand the method of separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water using the green energy according to another aspect of the present invention for achieving the above object a to produce power by itself through the solar power generation unit 1510 supplying power to the power supply unit 140 and supplying electricity through the electrode 130 s210 b temporarily storing the purified seawater in the storage tank 110 and first electrolyzing the electrode 130 through the electrode 130 s220 c performing second electrolysis through the electrode 130 in the waterway 120 while flowing the first electrolyzed seawater from the reservoir 110 s230 d injecting the caustic soda containing water electrolyzed through the step c into the inlet through the jet port 1601 and simultaneously heating the same through the evaporation chamber 1610 to generate steam s240 e receiving steam heated in the evaporation chamber 1610 through a moving duct 1615 to generate a steam turbine generator 1620 s250 and f collecting the concentrated caustic soda heated through the evaporation chamber 1610 through the drain 1160 in step d and generating the steam turbine generator 1620 in step e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "as shown the device 100 for separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water using the green energy according to the present invention the storage tank 110 for temporarily storing the pumped seawater and then electrolyzed and discharged is connected to one side of the reservoir while flowing through the seawater discharged from the water reservoir 120 for the second electrolysis and installed on both sides of the reservoir 110 and the water channel 120 respectively electrolysis of sea water electrode 130 of the positive and negative electrodes to be installed on one side of the waterway 120 to supply electricity to the electrode 130 and the self produced in the power supply 140 passing the power generation means 150 for supplying power and the caustic soda containing water electrolyzed while passing through the water channel 120 and simultaneously evaporating the water contained therein to separate seawater into caustic soda and fresh water evaporation tower 160 it includes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100555055-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the discharged water passing through the fiber filtration filter coated with the photocatalyst is sterilized while passing through the ultraviolet treatment device c provided in the pipeline or waterway type"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the initial rainwater storage system for sewage and valley water separation using the storage tank according to the present invention by overflowing the dividing wall during rainy weather to prevent contamination of the valley waterway and also to sewage initial rainfall and valley water rainwater on the other hand due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rainy weather the initial rainwater that has not been purified by the excess of the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant is discharged to the river to prevent the river from being polluted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101070989-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the treated water of the four waterway regions 170 is transferred to the treated water outflow inducing unit 190 via the wear 180 and the treated water is disposed at one side of the chamber 110 in the treated water outflow inducing unit 190"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100655393-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in the sewage advanced treatment apparatus configured to penetrate and be discharged to the water tank of the rear end by the water conveyed during the stop period of the device is trapped in the permeation sheet 500 and deposited on the bottom of the waterway body 100 the main body 100 side wall portion 110 forming both side walls blocking the bottom surface between the both side wall portion 110 consisting of a central semicircular central tap 120a and an inclined tap 120b extending upward from both sides of the upper end based on the cross sectional shape drainage from the distribution tank a bottom portion 120 inclined at a predetermined angle along the longitudinal direction to the jaw side a lower catching part 150 formed at an inclined upper end face of both end faces in the longitudinal direction and protruding to a lower side of the end face it is formed on the inclined lower end surface of the both ends in the longitudinal direction the upper engaging portion 160 is formed to protrude to the upper side of the cross section and comprises at least two raceway body 100 is connected in the longitudinal direction to the and a side wall portion 110 and a bottom portion 120 of the raceway body 100 that are connected to the dispensing tank side of the raceway body 100 connected in the longitudinal direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water supply pipe 32a exposed at the upper end a solenoid valve sv1 coupled to the water supply pipe 32a to control water and a solenoid valve sv1 interposed therebetween on both sides to supply water to the water supply pipe 32a it is configured to include a bypass pipe 33 for bypassing and a freeze prevention means 34 coupled to the bypass pipe 33 to bypass the water in the water supply pipe 32a in a small amount to prevent freezing in winter a three way solenoid valve sv2 is further coupled to the water supply pipe 32a which selectively controls the bypassed water and supplies it to the inner space 31a of the water spray stand 31 or the stone water tank 2 artificial waterway with water supply for freeze protection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to the characteristics for achieving the object as described above the first invention relates to an artificial waterway having a water supply unit for preventing freezing for this purpose a stone waterway a water supply unit installed in the inner center of the stone water tank to supply water and a plurality of landscaping stones radially arranged to have different sizes and height differences around the stone water tank the bottom surface is inclined toward the stone waterway and the water supply unit includes a water jet having an internal space communicating with a drain pipe buried underground a water supply pipe exposed to the top of the water jet across the internal space from the ground and the water supply pipe a solenoid valve coupled to the to regulate water a bypass pipe with both sides extending to the water supply pipe with the solenoid valve interposed therebetween to bypass the water and a small amount of water in the water supply pipe to bypass the circulation in winter to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101129512-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition by checking the piping connected to the inside of the water tank during the reinforcement of the water reinforcement it checks whether there is an abnormality in waterproofing at the connection part and repairs it when the aging of the pipes and the waterway proceeds thereby enhancing the effect of remodeling the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101450430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "1 to 3 rainfall runoff on roads and other road surfaces is introduced into an existing waterway through an induction waterway and a separate flow distribution structure a pretreatment tank and various abatement facilities are installed in the existing waterway it can be seen that the initial effluent is introduced into the abatement facility and the rainwater effluent from which the non point pollutant is removed through the abatement facility is reintroduced into the existing canal thereby removing the nonpoint contamination of the initial effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102617451-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a settling basin 10 consisting of a planar circular bottom plate installed in a sewage treatment plant or water purification plant and a side wall 11 outside the bottom plate and a side wall of the settling tank in 11 a planar annular channel 20 is formed which has a concave groove and an overflow wear surrounding the inside of the concave groove with a corrosion resistant steel material a cover portion 110 consisting of an outer frame 120 and a cover casing 130 in the shape of a trapezoid with an outer circumference width larger than the inner width so as to cover the waterway 20 and an outer support member 140 that supports the outer frame 120 on the inner surface of the outer wall 21 of the water channel 20 it is coupled to the sediment side end 151 of the overflow weir 150 of the waterway has a certain height is coupled to the outer frame 120 and consists of a connection hinge that can rotate so that the outer frame 120 can be opened toward the top"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102617451-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sewage treatment plant sludge collector waterway cover sewage treatment plant sludge collector waterway cover device the present invention relates to a sewage treatment plant sludge collector waterway cover and more specifically to covering an overflow weir formed at the edge of a sedimentation tank in a sewage treatment plant or water purification plant with a light shielding cover to prevent moss from growing on the wall of the discharge waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102617451-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however the conventional technology includes a plurality of arm cover members having outward flanges formed while covering the sewage treatment plant waterway and a plurality of arm cover members formed between the plurality of arm cover members covering the waterway and at the same time having inward flanges placed on top of the outward flanges"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0127564-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the inflow water is introduced into the inlet 51 through the inlet 51 is formed in a rectangular shape so that it can be discharged through the other outlet 52 inside the inflow water to the screen unit 10 of the screw device 20 inflow tank portion 50 formed with a waterway guide surface 53 so as to be to detect the water level of the inflow water flowing into the inflow tank portion 50 to stop the operation of the detection signal device or to adjust the speed of the inflow to the inlet port 51 of the tank section 50 and a water level detection control unit 60 for controlling the opening and closing of the gate valve 510 to be engaged with each other a solid conveyance unit 70 formed with the screw 21 in a non spindle shape and having a blade having a predetermined pitch it is formed so as to have a blade in the reverse direction on the screw 21 end drive side of the solid conveying portion 70 and the saw blade shaped cutting blade 81 is integrally formed on the tip side of the blade to crush the compressed and dehydrated solids crushing unit 80 and the brush 91 is planted in the outer peripheral edge of the tip blade of the screw 21 is formed integrally with the crushing unit 80 by the rotation of the screw 21 11 automatic screen device for solid waste collection of the waste water treatment facility characterized in that consisting of the washer portion 90 to sweep up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "para_472", "text": "after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring suggests a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226173-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention blocks the inflow of pollutants in the initial rainwater and removes particulate matter from the filtration device by centrifugation and filtering and in a large rainwater storage tank has a waterway structure using a flow wall to induce one way flow and thus discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102058210-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "therefore the water staying in the puddle 150 is configured to be guided to the storage tank 200 to be described later while being pitched downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102393954-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "accordingly it has the effect of preventing enormous disturbance and damage to the post treatment facility due to a large amount of contaminants in the storage facility such as a storage tank"}]</data>
