ded in the piping after the dissolved portion for driving the fluid pump in accordance with detection of water supply of water and supplying power to the electrolysis portion to perform electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101587697-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the present invention comprises a static pressure maintaining unit comprising a closed container having an open close valve operated by a knitting machine and maintaining a predetermined water level by receiving purified raw water wherein a positive electrode plate is provided in the oxygen generating chamber and a hydrogen generating chamber is provided in the hydrogen generating chamber so that the hydrogen generating chamber is filled with the raw water purified by the positive pressure holding unit an electrolytic unit provided with a cathode plate and performing electrolysis according to power supply a fluid pump for supplying raw water and hydrogen from the hydrogen generation chamber of the electrolysis unit and feeding the raw water and hydrogen a filter unit connected to the fluid pump to receive raw water and hydrogen and to filter out foreign matter and ozone a dissolution part for dissolving hydrogen in the raw water by supplying raw water and hydrogen from the filter part with a nozzle and injecting it and a flow rate detecting sensor which is provided in the piping after the dissolved portion to drive the fluid pump in accordance with detection of water supply of water and to supply power to the electrolysis section to perform electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101587697-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "1 to 3 the apparatus for producing hydrogen water according to the present invention comprises a closed container 230 having an open close valve 220 operated by a knitting machine 210 a static pressure maintaining unit 200 for maintaining the water level and a hydrogen generating chamber 320 supplied with raw water purified by the static pressure holding unit 200 is formed of a closed vessel 340 formed by bifurcating the ion exchange membrane 330 between the oxygen generating chamber 310 supplied with the raw water an electrolysis unit 300 having a cathode plate 311 in the oxygen generating chamber and an anode plate 321 in the hydrogen generating chamber 320 to perform electrolysis according to power supply a fluid pump 400 for supplying raw water and hydrogen from the hydrogen generation chamber 320 of the electrolysis unit 300 and feeding the raw water and hydrogen a filter unit 500 including a filter 510 connected to the fluid pump 400 to receive raw water and hydrogen to remove foreign matter and ozone a dissolution part 600 having a nozzle 610 to supply raw water and hydrogen from the filter part 500 and inject the raw water into the raw water the fluid pump 400 is provided in the piping after the dissolved portion 600 so that the fluid pump 400 is driven in accordance with detection of the supply of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102602389-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should include not only the above embodiments but also other variously modified embodiments according to the technical spirit of the invention described in the claims below.10 body 11 protruding end 11a 1st pass 11b second pass 11c third pass 12 1st peduncle 13 printed circuit board 20 water tank 21 exterior wall 22 inner wall 23 insulation 24 receptor 25 second peduncle 30 connection information board 31 1st wit home 32 2nd wit home 33 self adhering member 40 temperature sensor 50 sterilization lamp 60 water level sensor 70 cooling means 71 thermoelectric element 72 cooling rod 73 water cooler 73a water block 73b first connection hose 73c second connection hose 73d radiator 73e circulation pump 73f cooling fan 80 water fountain 81 water nozzle 82 water level control ball 83 auxiliary water nozzle 90 water supply means 91 proximity sensor 92 water pump 93 water hose 100 height adjustable 110 recovery stand 111 recovery plate 111a drain hole 111b 1st hose passage hole 112 noise reduction hopper 112a second hose passage hole 113 filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141180-B1", "para_id": "para_142", "text": "it should not be understood as being and the scope of rights of the present invention should be understood as the following claims and their equivalent concepts.10 control unit 11 touch screen 12 control unit 13 water directing editorial department 14 storage unit 15 usb connection 16 internet connection 17 ozone and purification chemical supply line 20 inverter 30 audio output device 40 monitoring system 50 smartphone application 100 floor fountain 101 flagstone 102 support frame 110 water tank 111 water level sensor 120 drainage pump 121 drainage line 122 overflow pipe 123 overflow inlet 130 water supply line 131 first water supply 132 second water supply 140 supply pump 141 supply line 142 spray nozzle 150 purifying device 151 inlet 152 outlet 160 washing water supply pump 161 washing water supply line 162 primary cleaning nozzle 200 water playground 210 water tank 211 water level sensor 220 drainage pump 221 drainage line 222 overflow pipe 223 overflow inlet 230 water supply line 232 water supply port 240 supply pump 241 supply line 242 spray nozzle 250 purification device 251 inlet 252 outlet 260 washing water supply pump 261 washing water supply line 262 primary cleaning nozzle 270 recovery line 280 discharge pipe 290 amusement facilities 300 running water 310 water tank 311 water level sensor 320 drainage pump 321 drainage line 322 overflow pipe 323 overflow inlet 330 water supply line 332 water supply port 340 supply pump 341 supply line 342 spray nozzle 350 purification device 351 inlet 352 outlet 360 washing water supply pump 361 washing water supply line 362 primary cleaning nozzle 370 recovery line 380 discharge pipe 390 flowing pool 391 pool 400 floating fraction 410 main pump 411 main line 412 main nozzle 420 auxiliary pump 421 auxiliary line 422 auxiliary nozzle 430 fixed block 431 wire 432 fixed part 440 floating means 500 ultra fine particle cool fog system 530 direct line 532 water supply port 540 supply pump 541 spray line 542 spray nozzle 60 panel case"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the non circulating non discharge manure treatment method for purifying the manure and sewage discharged from the toilet the manure treatment method comprises the steps of installing a flush toilet in the toilet the sewage and manure from the flush toilet anaerobic storage tank 10 anaerobic digestion filtering the treated water while treating nitrogen phosphorus and the like which are physically and biologically organic suspended solids and eutrophication agents in the aerobic bioreactor 20 and treating the treated water in the flow regulating tank 30 storing in the anaerobic state of the treated water and stabilizing the stored treatment water while the waste water is sprayed onto the wood chip layer by the water spray nozzle in the organic decay reaction tank 40 while the manure and sewage flows through the adsorption adsorption to the wood chip layer decomposing and removing the organic substances and various suspended substances contained in the step of discharging the leachate the pump well 46 operating a transfer pump that operates when a predetermined water level is reached while storing water removing organic components and nitrogen phosphorus color odor and the like physically and biologically from the advanced treatment tank 50 by contact aeration with the media physically filtration of the discharged water storing the treated water in the second flow rate adjusting tank 60 and stabilizing the stored treated water organic suspended solids remaining in the treated water passing through the wood chip layer and nitrogen phosphorus decomposing the chromaticity odor in the bioreactor 70 and then removing the leachate storing the treated water in the pump well 77 operating the transfer pump when the water level reaches a certain value decolorizing the treated water discharging while discoloring in the disinfection filtration tank 80 storing the treated water in the treated water storage tank 90 and supplying the stored treated water to the toilet and excessively introduced the excess water to the outside jidoe comprises a step of output the rainwater storage tank is installed on the roof of the manure treatment device and rainwater flows into the treatment water storage tank through a pipe and an electric shutoff valve is installed between the rainwater storage tank and the treatment water storage tank so that the water level of the treatment water storage tank is set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637562-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "the supply means and the water pumping means are automatically controlled by a monitoring system driven by signals of a detection sensor not shown for detecting the water level of the settling tank 3 the filtration tank 4 and the rectifying tank 5 at an appropriate position and manual control may be performed depending on the contamination level of the storm and the degree of contamination of the filter 40"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4532258-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "the simplified block diagram of the whole apparatus.the front view of a muddy water processing apparatus.the side view.the top view of a mixing part.the side view of the drive part of the stirring mixer which comprised the mixing part.part of the front view.1 turbid water supply line 2 infiltration part 2a infiltration tank 2b muddy water outlet 3 muddy water delivery line 4 mixing section 5 solid liquid separation section 6 coagulant feeding section 6a feeding hopper 7 1st control part 8 water level gauge 9 2nd control part 10 watering nozzle 11 strip 12 dispersion plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102713396-B1", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "fourth by forming the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit evaporator 2 1 2 and the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit concentrated water circulating water ejector 7 1 2 and controlling the residence time of the concentrated water flowing out of the concentrated water tank 15 1 supercooling and the formation of fine ice seed water in the salt separation tank 5 1 were promoted thereby reinforcing the formation and growth of the brine water containing organic and inorganic substances contained in the influent into an ice slurry"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand the quantitative waste water is discharged quantitatively and discharged into the aeration tank 50 equipped with the oxygen supply nozzle 57 by the water level difference through the first wear 31 via the flow rate control anoxic tank 40 the coarse sewage flows through the weir 35 into the sedimentation filtration tank 20 in which the sludge s is precipitated in a downward upward flow by the induction pipe 93 in the sedimentation filtration tank 20 and the treated supernatant is the discharge vessel"}]</data>
