e", "discharge", "store", "cool", "decrease", "decompose", "bush", "fit", "start", "capture", "detect", "net", "analyze", "drive", "spot", "change", "obtain", "separate", "compensate", "dispose", "guide", "include", "operate", "perform", "consist", "act", "incline", "should", "open", "expand", "block", "blow", "mean", "constitute", "supply", "use", "perforate", "transfer", "propeller", "stop", "antifoame", "exchange", "charge", "cut", "could", "asphyxiate", "straighten", "disable", "peel", "throttle", "sense", "finish", "identify", "require", "draw", "close", "nozzle", "rotate", "heat", "classify", "galvanize", "install", "maintain", "improve", "control", "transmit", "case", "monitor", "characterize", "waste", "shape", "select", "input", "adhere", "be", "age", "rack", "print", "generate", "adjust", "collect", "instal", "comprise", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101308996-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however such a hollow fiber membrane manufacturing method is too complicated to increase the manufacturing cost and also may cause problems such as peeling due to the interfacial adhesion failure in the heterogeneous process and manufacturing process between each layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102239966-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a pump that supplies external water to the inlet of the steam generating pipe a water supply hose that connects the external water to the pump a steam discharge hose that discharges the steam supplied from the outlet of the steam generating pipe to the outside of the housing and the operation of the heater and the pump it comprises a control unit for controlling the the pedestal consists of a front plate and a rear plate bent in a vertical state and the front plate has a display unit indicating temperature and error code while screwing one side of the cover to the rim a steam amount control lever a steam switch a residual water removal switch and a socket for connecting the steam discharge hose is mounted the rear plate is made by perforating the entrance while screwing the other side of the cover to the edge portion the lower end is screwed inside the doorway formed on the rear plate of the pedestal and both sides are screwed to the cover and a socket connecting the earth leakage circuit breaker and water supply hose is mounted and the power supply line is connected so that it can flow into the inside and the accessories can be stored an inner plate providing a storage space is provided a spray gun having a nozzle connected to the front end of the steam discharge hose to inject steam is provided a plurality of drainage holes are drilled in lower corners of the front plate and the rear plate of the pedestal so that moisture can be discharged to the outside a plurality of first vents are formed on the upper side of the inner plate to discharge heat inside the housing while preventing the inflow of moisture scattered from the outside and a plurality of second vents are formed on one side of the cover to be mounted on the pedestal"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6765582-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "further since the water to be treated 6 supplied from the nozzle 35 to the discharge unit 2 flows down while being in contact with the circular pipe 4 the water to be treated 6 functions as substantial cooling water and the temperature of the circular pipe 4 rises due to the discharge 9"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101282136-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "here the injector 150 may be configured as an injection hose capable of supplying hot water directly into the frozen pipe line 220 and may support hot water of a predetermined temperature into the freezing pipe line 220 through a nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100735544-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "a chemical treatment method using an antifoaming agent has a problem of lowering oxygen transfer efficiency due to residual silicone and other chemicals in the antifoaming agent.the present invention has been made in view of this point and install a straight or radial air supply means on the bottom of the high temperature aerobic digestion reaction tank and supply air to the blower while supplying wastewater to the internal circulation pump to supply air from the discharge nozzle of the air supply means and wastewater are mixed and discharged to form conditions for activating high temperature aerobic microorganisms through the complete mixing of the wastewater in the high temperature aerobic digestion reactor and oxygen transfer through air supply thereby increasing the decomposition efficiency of organic matter and the purpose is to remove the pathogenic microorganisms and e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aeration tank for aerating the treated water so that aerobic microorganisms propagate in the treated water by the supplied oxygen to form floes a measurement unit for measuring and monitoring a treatment state by sampling a predetermined amount of the treated water being treated in the aeration tank a suction unit connected to one or more of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water from each of the aeration tanks and supplying the collected water to the measuring unit a discharge unit connecting the measurement unit and the aeration tank so that the treated water measured by the measurement unit is discharged back to the aeration tank and a central processing unit that receives the measurement data measured by the measurement unit analyzes the measurement data and controls the measurement unit the suction unit and the discharge unit the suction part one or more aeration tank connection pipes connected to each of the aeration tanks one end of which is disposed so as to be submerged in each of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water in each aeration tank and a scoring point control unit installed at the bottom of the aeration tank connection pipe installed to be drawn into the lower part of the aeration tank connection pipe or drawn out to the outside and to adjust the depth inserted into the aeration tank the measuring unit a measuring tank accommodating the treated water supplied through the inlet and having a washing water inlet through which washing water flows a spray nozzle installed at the washing water inlet inside the measuring tank to inject washing water into the measuring tank an angle adjusting unit rotatably installed at an end of the spray nozzle and adjusting a spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle a rotating inner tube installed on an inner circumferential surface of the measuring tank and having a plurality of through holes a rotary driving unit installed to be connected to the rotating inner tube to transmit power to the rotating inner tube and to rotate the rotating inner tube inside the measuring tank to form a vortex inside the measuring tank a washing state confirmation unit installed inside the measuring tank to photograph the inside of the measuring tank the control unit of the central processing unit analyzes the degree of contamination of the measurement tank through the image of the inside of the measurement tank captured by the washing state confirmation unit and analyzes whether or not cleaning of the inside of the measurement tank is necessary or a part requiring cleaning when the control unit confirms a position requiring washing the spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle is adjusted as the angle adjuster rotates a washing unit for cleaning the inside of the measurement tank by spraying washing water into the measurement tank after the treated water measured in the measurement tank is discharged to the aeration tank through the discharge unit and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting the freeze protection unit a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe a heating unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction part the treated water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part and when the temperature sensed by the temperature sensing unit is equal to or less than a predetermined temperature a temperature control unit for adjusting the heating temperature of the heating unit so that the treated water or washing water inside the pipe does not freeze"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "thereby the object to be cleaned 1 is firstly cleaned by high pressure air bubbling through the lower spray nozzle 233 by driving the spray pump 235 in a state of being immersed in the cleaning liquid in the cleaning tank 210 the spray nozzle 233 is driven by the spray pump 235 to discharge the cleaning solution through the upper spray nozzle 233 before being lifted from the cleaning tank 210 by the driving of the cleaning lifting driver 225 the washing liquid is circulated through the upper spray nozzle 233 by the clean wash water accommodated in the regenerating wash fluid reservoir 240 by the driving of the regenerating wash fluid circulating pump 245 and the steam supply pipe 117 the drying and residual washing liquid is removed by the high temperature steam supplied from the waste water regeneration apparatus 100 and sprayed through the upper spray nozzle 233 and then discharged to the outside of the cleaning loading unit 220 or the cleaning quality of the object to be cleaned 1 can be further improved without consuming energy"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "decreasing the throat diameter will increase the pressure differential across the throat and increase the length of the stream that is cavitating"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the controller 88 could be equally effective in a case of a fixed nozzle cavitation system wherein a number of inputs to the controller 88 from inlet pressure 90 outlet pressure 92 vacuum 99 temperature 101 and flow 102 produce signals to pump 18 and valve 96 to control cavitation to provide an optimum process"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "this drop in ph gives immediate indication of the effectiveness of the cavitation nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aerobic digestion tank 100 in which organic matter contained in waste water is oxidatively decomposed by activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms and an air nozzle provided at an inner lower portion of the aerobic digestion tank 100 to discharge air providing a lifting force for circulating the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the aerobic digester in which the organic matter contained in the waste water is oxidatively decomposed due to the activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms and the air nozzle which is provided in the inner lower portion of the aerobic digester to provide the lifting force for circulating the waste water is vertically upward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101739419-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a constant temperature system for leachate and wastewater treatment plants installed in a nitrification tank in a leachate treatment plant including a tiller a flow control tank a mixing tank a nitrification tank a settling tank a thickening tank a fenton oxidation treatment tank or a reverse osmosis treatment tank a plurality of nitrification vessels buried in the ground and purifying and discharging the supplied leachate from the outside and having a plurality of chambers partitioned by a plurality of partition walls for setting the movement path of the leachate therein at least one agitator disposed on the bottom surface of the nitrification tank to mix the leachate while rotating a first heat pump disposed in an upper part of the nitrification tank on the ground to heat the nitrification tank and heat exchanging the first chamber leachate and the heat exchanged refrigerant disposed in front of the nitrification tank in the direction in which the leachate flows 3 heat pump a fourth heat pump to a sixth heat pump arranged in parallel with the first heat pump to the third heat pump and arranged in the rear along the direction in which the leachate of the nitrification tank flows and the heat exchanged refrigerant is heat a first heat exchanger connected to the first heat pump to a third heat pump and disposed in the first chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a second heat exchanger connected to the fourth heat pump to the sixth heat pump and disposed in the second chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a first circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the first heat exchange unit a second circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the second heat exchange unit a preliminary circulation pump interposed between the first circulation pump and the second circulation pump and capable of temporarily operating corresponding to the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump a three way valve connected between any one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump and selectively supplying the heat exchanged refrigerant to the first chamber or the second chamber a sensor unit provided on the three way valve for sensing the temperature or pressure of the refrigerant flowing into the three way valve a first heat pump to a sixth heat pump a first circulation pump and a second circulation pump and a control unit controlling the temperature of the leachate in the nitrification tank to a set range by controlling the agitator an expansion tank provided to compensate for a pressure of the heat exchanged refrigerant supplied through the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump and an air blower unit for supplying air supplied from the outside to the periphery of the agitator in the nitrification tank the air blower unit includes an air flow path for introducing outside air into the vicinity of the agitator a compressor for forcibly supplying external air through the air flow path and a nozzle provided at an end portion of the air flow path for discharging air toward the agitator and wherein the agitator includes a housing fixed to the bottom of the nitrification tank and passing through the inside in a vertical direction a propeller for rotating the inside of the housing to mix the leachate a driving motor for driving the propeller and a guide arm provided on the outer circumferential surface of the housing so as to be guided through the air passage when installed wherein the control unit controls the at least one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump to selectively operate the heat pumps when the temperature of the nitrification tank reaches the set temperature by receiving the data of the sensor unit the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump operates first and controls the heat pumps to operate after the set time has elapsed wherein the nitrification tank includes a plurality of ventilation doors formed with openings communicating with the outside at upper portions of the chambers and selectively opening and closing the openings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the air nozzle 20 is provided integrally with the injection pipe 21 and at the same time one or more are fixed so that the supplied air is sprayed so that water can circulate in the storage tank 80 and at the end of the injection pipe 21 a fitting 22 is provided so that one touch coupling with the air supply hose 23 is possible and the fitting 22 is installed on the side surface 12 of the main body 10 and the inner receiving space of the main body 10 11 is filled with anti pollution means 30 in which elvan quartz loess balls activated carbon and charcoal are mixed to prevent contamination or deterioration of stored water and a perforated groove 41 at the upper end thereof to prevent separation the formed cover plate 40 is coupled and fixed to the main body while on one side of the edge of the main body 10 a heating wire 50 for preventing freezing and a temperature at which the inside temperature is sensed to transmit a signal to the controller 70 one or more water pollution prevention units d having the sensor 60 installed and fixed are disposed on the bottom of the storage tank and fixing the water pollution prevention units installed and fixed in series or parallel when the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe passes through the filter and is stored as water in the storage tank the stored water is contamination prevention means 30 by spraying air from the air nozzle 20 of the water pollution prevention unit d and sprayed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "21 and one or more are fixed at the same time and a fitting 22 is provided at the end of the injection pipe 21 so that it can be one touch coupled with the air supply hose 23 the fitting 22 is the body it is installed on the side surface 12 of the 10 and the internal receiving space 11 of the main body 10 contains a mixture of elvan quartz loess balls activated carbon and charcoal so as to prevent contamination or deterioration of the stored water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10995023-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the vapor bubbles collapse a plurality of effects occurs such as increased heat harmonics and vibration all of which contribute to the sanitation process"}, {"pat_id": "US-10995023-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "as they leave the low pressure region the bubbles begin to collapse creating substantial amount of heat energy and shock waves that propagate through the water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11518666-B2", "para_id": "para_438", "text": "by the lifting of the lifting cover 210 and the water ejection nozzle 240 water may be ejected from a position adjacent to the water receiving container"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101285291-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time the filtration filter device is wrapped through the outer space of the filter case so as to be discharged through the nozzle hole of the cap coupled to the rear end of the filter case is filtered through the inner space without freezing in the winter season the first heating coil may be further controlled by a controller to selectively generate heat periodically for a predetermined time depending on the surface temperature of the filter case"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687400-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "meanwhile unlike the spray nozzle of the cooled hexagonal 