s that can adjust the water content of the sludge to the user s intended level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100271329-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the magnetic fine powder recovery apparatus of the magnetic fluid separation system of suspended solids in wastewater using magnetic fine powder mf slurry tank 21 for storage and supply of magnetic flux ms combined with the magnetic fine powder mf and suspended solids s a medium fluidized bed 24 having upper and lower portions formed in a cone shape and having a porous dispersion plate 25 installed in a predetermined lower portion of the inside thereof and having media particles 26 of a predetermined size introduced therein a slurry supply pump 22 for supplying a certain amount of magnetic flux ms stored in the slurry tank 21 to the nozzle 23 in the medium fluidized bed 24 hot air supply device for supplying a high temperature dry hot air to the lower portion of the medium fluidized bed 24 to flow the media particles 26 and magnetic flux ms introduced into the medium fluidized bed 24 to dry wear and scatter 50 and a magnetic separator installed on the medium fluidized bed 24 and having upper and lower portions formed in a cone shape and a magnet 27 installed at an outer circumference to collect magnetic fine powder mf that is scattered and discharged with hot air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102039925-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "is inside the double shell of the ionized water concentrating device is provided a heating medium for increasing the internal temperature of the ionized water concentrating device to evaporate the ionized water the cross section of the ionized water concentrating device can be combined in plurality in accordance with the processing requirements in the form of a hexagon a positive electrode is applied to the outer wall of the ionized water concentrating device to generate electricity in the ionized water particles inside the ionized water concentrating device the diameter of the spray nozzle is 0.6 to 1 mm the inner surface of the ionized water concentrator is coated with tin to prevent corrosion the gap les between the spray nozzle and the inside of the ionized water concentrating device is 20 to 30 cm an ionized water concentrating device is formed in the rear end of the outlet portion of the ionized water condenser condenser for concentrating the evaporated ion residual water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102602389-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should include not only the above embodiments but also other variously modified embodiments according to the technical spirit of the invention described in the claims below.10 body 11 protruding end 11a 1st pass 11b second pass 11c third pass 12 1st peduncle 13 printed circuit board 20 water tank 21 exterior wall 22 inner wall 23 insulation 24 receptor 25 second peduncle 30 connection information board 31 1st wit home 32 2nd wit home 33 self adhering member 40 temperature sensor 50 sterilization lamp 60 water level sensor 70 cooling means 71 thermoelectric element 72 cooling rod 73 water cooler 73a water block 73b first connection hose 73c second connection hose 73d radiator 73e circulation pump 73f cooling fan 80 water fountain 81 water nozzle 82 water level control ball 83 auxiliary water nozzle 90 water supply means 91 proximity sensor 92 water pump 93 water hose 100 height adjustable 110 recovery stand 111 recovery plate 111a drain hole 111b 1st hose passage hole 112 noise reduction hopper 112a second hose passage hole 113 filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674459-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "8 is a view showing an embodiment in which the turbulence generator according to the present invention is formed in the internal space of the injection nozzle body to generate a turbulent flow rate in the internal space based on the hot water pressure or the cold water pressure supplied from the high pressure water pump 9 is a view showing an embodiment in which a high pressure water pump according to the present invention generates pressure for transferring high pressure hot water or cold water for washing sewage water pipe while receiving power from a power transmission part for a pump fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102355027-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an outer housing 10 having a frame structure having a predetermined size the inner housing 20 is installed inside the outer housing 10 the upper surface is opened to accommodate the object to be treated therein a stirring unit 30 installed horizontally inside the inner housing 20 to stir the object to be treated a driving unit 40 installed on an outer side of the inner housing 20 to rotate the stirring unit 30 a heating unit 50 installed along the inner bottom surface of the inner housing 20 to heat the inner housing 20 an air exhaust unit 60 installed on one upper side of the inner housing 20 to discharge the air of the inner housing 20 to the outside an air supply unit 70 installed inside the outer housing 10 to supply compressed air into the inner housing 20 and a controller 80 installed on one side of the outer housing 10 to control the operation of the driving unit 40 the heating unit 50 the air exhaust unit 60 and the air supply unit 70 including the stirring unit 30 a rotating shaft 31 installed to horizontally cross the inner housing 20 a plurality of fixing clamps 32 installed at predetermined intervals on the rotating shaft 31 a mounting table 33 of a predetermined length installed on the plurality of fixing clamps 32 a main stirring blade 34 installed on the mounting table 33 including the mounting base 33 is it is arranged so as to be spaced apart from another adjacent installation table 33 by 90 the main stirring blade 34 is two or more are installed so as to connect the ends of the three adjacent installation tables 33 in an arc shape to space them 180 apart in the fixing clamp 32 auxiliary stirring blades 35 of a predetermined length are installed at intervals of 90 from the mounting table 33 so that the object to be treated is stirred between the rotation shaft 31 and the main stirring blades 34 the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is the tip of the three auxiliary stirring blades 35 is connected and formed in an arc shape in the opposite direction to the main stirring blade 34 the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is the tip is installed to be inclined at a predetermined angle a to one side with respect to the fixing clamp 32 and the tip of the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is positioned in the space between the pair of installation tables 33 the heating unit 50 a rectangular shaped body 51 with an open upper surface a heater 52 installed on one side of the main body 51 and installed to have a predetermined length in a horizontal direction including in the body 51 a temperature sensor 53 for detecting the temperature of the thermal medium stored therein and an inlet and outlet pipe 54 for supplying heat medium oil to the inside of the body 51 or discharging the inside heat medium oil to the outside is provided the heating unit 50 it is installed horizontally along the middle part of the bottom surface of the inner housing 20 and is integrally fixed by welding the air exhaust unit 60 it is configured so that the air and moisture inside the inner housing 20 are discharged together the air supply unit 70 compressor 71 for generating compressed air a flow path 72 connected to the compressor 71 and a plurality of injection nozzles connected to the flow path 72 and supplying compressed air to the inside of the inner housing 20 including between the injection nozzle and the flow path 72 food characterized in that a check valve 73 is installed to allow compressed air to be discharged toward the inner housing 20 and to block moisture inside the inner housing 20 from being discharged through the flow path 72"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308998-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however such a hollow fiber membrane manufacturing method is too complicated to increase the manufacturing cost and also may cause problems such as peeling due to the interfacial adhesion failure in the heterogeneous process and manufacturing process between each layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-10537921-B2", "para_id": "para_218", "text": "accordingly the object 1 to be washed is primarily washed with high pressure air bubbling via the lower spray nozzles 233 by the driving of the spray pump 235 in the state of being immersed into washing liquid inside the washing tank 210 is lifted from the washing tank 210 by the driving of the washing lifting drive unit 225 and secondarily spray washed via the upper spray nozzles 233 by the driving of the spray pump 235 before being taken from the inside of the washing loading unit 220 is thirdly spray washed with clean washing water contained inside the reclamation washing liquid storage tank 240 via the upper spray nozzle 233 by the driving of the reclamation washing liquid circulation pump 245 is dried with high temperature vapor supplied from the wastewater reclamation apparatus 100 via the vapor supply tube 117 and sprayed via the upper spray nozzle 233 and deprived of remaining washing liquid and is transferred to the outside of the washing loading unit 220 thereby further improving the washing quality of the object 1 to be washed without using separate equipment or causing energy consumption"}, {"pat_id": "US-10537921-B2", "para_id": "para_222", "text": "accordingly the object 1 to be washed is primarily washed with high pressure air bubbling via the lower spray nozzles 233 by the driving of the spray pump 235 in the state of being immersed into washing liquid inside the washing tank 210 is lifted from the washing tank 210 by the driving of the washing lifting drive unit 225 and secondarily spray washed via the upper spray nozzles 233 by the driving of the spray pump 235 before being taken from the inside of the washing loading unit 220 is thirdly spray washed with clean washing water contained inside the reclamation washing liquid storage tank 240 via the upper spray nozzle 233 by the driving of the reclamation washing liquid circulation pump 245 is transferred such that the object 1 to be washed is loaded inside the dry chamber 260 dried with high temperature vapor supplied from the wastewater reclamation apparatus 100 via a vapor supply tube 117 and a vapor nozzle pipeline 263 sprayed via a vapor spray nozzle 261 and deprived of remaining washing liquid and is transferred from the dry chamber 260 via the washing loading unit 220 to the outside thereby further improving the washing quality of the object 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "thus the forwardly directed stream from the nozzle 19 is particularly useful in creating an initial opening through a blockage caused by most materials"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452661-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "at least one oxygen supply unit is mounted in the vertical direction inside the guide partition wall and the oxygen supply unit is composed of an oxygen supply pipe and an oxygen supply nozzle to remove the descending floating filter media and contaminants contained in the water to be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171689-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "case 100 a plurality of led lamps 110 pump 230 water supply sensor 240 the heating wire 250 the heater 270 and the heater body temperature sensor 272 is configured to include the case 100 has a rectangular parallelepiped shape a pedestal 101 is formed at a lower portion thereof a cover 102 is formed at an upper portion thereof and a plurality of led lamps 110 and steam on on are provided at the front of the case 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102370139-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "according to one aspect of the present invention in the strainer for spatially separating both the reaction tank for removing contaminants in the incoming wastewater and the treatment water tank for storing the treated water from which the contaminants have been removed through the reaction tank the strainer block and the strainer block are formed the first nozzle socket and the fastening structure are formed to improve the fastening force with the strainer block including the nozzle disposed in the nozzle hole and the step with the fastening structure formed on each surface the first nozzle socket on one side and the first nozzle socket on the other side it provides a strainer comprising the first nozzle socket and the strainer block and a second nozzle socket that is fastened to the nozzle on the other side and has improved fastening force.as described above according to one aspect of the present invention the temperature of the cooling water can be lowered by heat exchanging the cooling water to cool the data center with the outside while minimizing power consumption and the temperature rise due to the heat exchange with the cooling water is actively used for water treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-11596874-B2", "para_id": "para_136", "text": "system 100 includes air blower 106 that bubbles ambient air 110 through standing water 112 in tank 102 in this non limiting example the bubbling is accomplished via air stone 108"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452663-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "at least one oxygen supply unit is mounted in the vertical direction inside the guide partition wall and the oxygen supply unit is composed of an oxygen supply pipe and an oxygen supply nozzle to remove the descending floating filter media and contaminants contained in the water to be treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-10913414-B2", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3 further comprising responsive to the indication of engine cooling system degradation spraying water via the nozzle while concurrently disabling cylinder fuel injection until the cylinder head temperature is below the threshold"}, {"pat_id": "US-10913414-B2", "para_id": "para_108", "text": "in any or all of the preceding examples additionally or optionally the method further comprises responsive to the indication of engine cooling system degradation spraying water via the nozzle while concurrently disabling cylinder fuel injection until the cylinder head temperature is below the threshold"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102221358-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "6 shows the sequence of the steam injector operating according to the present invention in which steam and a heated fluid are introduced into the steam injector s100 heating and moving the heated fluid s200 and a preset pressure control unit the step of checking whether the pressure is reached s300 and the step of sequentially opening the nozzle 121 while the elastic part 110 is retracted when the predetermined pressure is reached s400 and the step of spraying the steam with increased pressure to the nozzle s500 and the step s600 of increasing the efficiency of the steam injector due to a high temperature and high pressure effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the storage tank 41 for collecting odors 72 a stirrer 51 which is charged for the fermentation and decomposition treatment of the food waste a to be evenly supplied and stirred by the stirring blade 511 together with the microorganism and the wood chip 512 a nozzle 52 for spraying washing water b at a predetermined temperature for washing to prevent anaerobically progressing due to the saccharide enzyme microorganism carcass and the like and to provide aerobic condition a driving motor 54 for rotating the agitation blade 511 of the wooden chip and a driving motor 54 for driving the agitation blade 511 the nozzle 52 the oxygen generator 53 a liquid phase fermentation decomposition unit 50 including a control unit 55 that is electrically connected to the motor 54 and controls it a sedimentation tank 61 for precipitating and separating the effluent c obtained by the liquid fermentation decomposition treatment so as to separate and collect the effluent c as waste water d and solid matter e or a centrifugal separator 62 for rotating and separating the effluent c 60 the separated and collected wastewater d is purified by chemical biological and physical treatments to separate the solid e the solid e1 the nitrogen n and the phosphorus p a purification treatment unit 70 having an adjustment tank 72 an anaerobic tank 73 an anoxic tank 74 an aerobic tank 75 a biological sedimentation tank 76 and a filtration tank 77 the collected and collected solid matter e microbial solids e1 and meat fish and cereal shaped material f for the balance of insufficient nutrient balance are added through the automatic weighing hopper 81 0.0 gt c lt rti gt for 20 to 60 minutes a feed fermentation unit 90 which is charged with the sterilized humidified mixed feed and fermented in the fermenter 91 for 2 to 5 days to produce a functional feed g a feed dryer 100 for feeding the functional feed g and drying in the dryer 101 a feedstock storage tank 1104 for storing the dried functional food g a descendant 1101 for loading the feedstock into the delivery vehicle 1103 to supply the feedstock to the feedstock in a nonpackaged state or in a packed state and a feed packing section 110 having a feed packing machine 1102 for feeding the feed in units of a unit of weight wherein the functional feed and the liquid fertilizer lt rti gt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the storage tank 41 for collecting odors 72 a stirrer 51 which is charged for the fermentation and decomposition treatment of the food waste a to be evenly supplied and stirred by the stirring blade 511 together with the microorganism and the wood chip 512 a nozzle 52 for spraying washing water b at a predetermined temperature for washing to prevent anaerobically progressing due to the saccharide enzyme microorganism carcass and the like and to provide aerobic condition a driving motor 54 for rotating the agitation blade 511 of the wooden chip and a driving motor 54 for driving the agitation blade 511 the nozzle 52 the oxygen generator 53 a liquid phase fermentation decomposition unit 50 including a control unit 55 that is electrically connected to the motor 54 and controls it a sedimentation tank 61 for precipitating and separating the effluent c obtained by the liquid fermentation decomposition treatment so as to separate and collect the effluent c as waste water d and solid matter e or a centrifugal separator 62 for rotating and separating the effluent c 60 the separated and collected wastewater d is purified by chemical biological and physical treatments to separate the solid e the solid e1 the nitrogen n and the phosphorus p a purification treatment unit 70 having an adjustment tank 72 an anaerobic tank 73 an anoxic tank 74 an aerobic tank 75 a biological sedimentation tank 76 and a filtration tank 77 the collected and collected solid matter e microbial solids e1 and meat fish and cereal shaped material f for the balance of insufficient nutrient balance are added through the automatic weighing hopper 81 0.0 gt c lt rti gt for 20 to 60 minutes a feed fermentation unit 90 which is charged with the sterilized humidified mixed feed and fermented in the fermenter 91 for 2 to 5 days to produce a functional feed g a feed dryer 100 for feeding the functional feed g and drying in the dryer 101 a feedstock storage tank 1104 for storing the dried functional food g a descendant 1101 for loading the feedstock into the delivery vehicle 1103 to supply the feedstock to the feedstock in a nonpackaged state or in a packed state and a feed packing section 110 having a feed packing machine 1102 for feeding the feed in units of a unit of weight wherein the functional feed and the liquid fertilizer the object of which is achieved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101361104-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition facilities such as the cooling unit heat exchanger pump valve of the water treatment unit and the heat treatment unit are provided separately from the machine room it is arranged to be protected from the outside.as described above the present invention constitutes a purification treatment part of a predetermined water body of a physical treatment method of increasing dissolved oxygen do while maintaining a constant surface temperature of water in a predetermined water area using geothermal heat exchange and nanobubbles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 is a conventional temperature and humidity control system using a spray nozzle is connected to each of the plurality of water distribution supply unit 10 and the plurality of water distribution supply unit 10 provided along the longitudinal direction of the house h house a plurality of spray nozzles 20 spraying mist therein a distributor 30 connected to each of the plurality of water distribution supply units 10 to distribute water to each of the plurality of water distribution supply units 10 drive pump 40 for supplying water to the distributor 30 side the water tank 50 is connected to the drive pump 40 to store the water supplied to the distributor 30 by the drive pump 40 and a first valve 41 interposed between the driving pump 40 and the distributor 30 to supply or block the water supplied to the distributor 30 the distributor 30 and the water tank 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition another effect of the present invention is to feed back the temperature and humidity of the spraying location by controlling the supply amount of the sterilizing spray liquid supplied to the spray line has the effect of minimizing energy consumption.1 is a configuration diagram of a temperature and humidity control system using a conventional spray nozzle figure 2 is a block diagram of a first embodiment of the present invention nano fog spray system 3 is a configuration diagram of a first embodiment of the present invention nano fog spray system figure 4 is a block diagram of a nano fog spray system using the present invention hypochlorous acid figure 5 is a configuration diagram of a second embodiment of the nano fog spraying system using the present hypochlorous acid water 6 is a detailed block diagram of a controller unit applied to the present invention 7 is a detailed configuration diagram of the second controller unit applied to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "US-5538031-A", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "this procedure fills the pipes with antifreeze thereby preventing freezing of fluid within the pipes when the outdoor temperature falls below thirty two degrees fahrenheit or zero degrees celsius"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452662-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "at least one oxygen supply unit is mounted in the vertical direction inside the guide partition wall and the oxygen supply unit is composed of an oxygen supply pipe and an oxygen supply nozzle to remove the descending floating filter media and contaminants contained in the water to be treated"}]</data>
