  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101908319-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow rate adjusting tank 10 for adjusting the discharge amount according to an inflow amount of the incoming wastewater a bioreactor 20 including a semi tank 21 functioning as an anaerobic tank and an anoxic tank according to time and a sludge buffer tank 23 having a microorganism incubator 24 a raw water transfer system 14 for transferring the wastewater introduced into the flow rate adjusting tank 10 to the semi furnace and first and second batch reactors 30a 30b connected in series with the semi bath 21 and continuously treating the organic substance and nitrogen oxide to discharge the treated water and arranged in parallel with each other first and second inflow transportation systems 25a 25b for transferring wastewater between the semi bath 21 and the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a 30b first and second sludge transfer systems 40a 40b for transferring the sludge collected from the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a 30b to the semi tank 21 and the sludge buffer tank 23 a microorganism conveyance system 45 for conveying the positively ignited microorganisms from the sludge buffer tank 23 to the first and the first batch reaction vessels 30a and 30b and and a control panel 50 for performing overall control for advanced treatment of the wastewater first and second batch reactor tank inflow valves 26a and 26b installed in the first and second inflow transfer systems 25a and 25b first and second sludge drawing pumps 41a and 41b installed in the first and second sludge transfer systems 40a and 40b for drawing sludge from the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a and 30b and first and second microbial distribution tanks 42a and 42b for transferring the sludge drawn through the first and second sludge drawing pumps 41a and 41b to the semi tank 21 and the sludge buffer tank 23 the control panel 50 controls the balance of the sludge microorganism amount while the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a and 30b are operated and the amount of microorganisms necessary for interlocking with the influent load the first and second sludge discharge pumps 41a and 41b are controlled so that the first and second sludge discharge pumps 41a the first and second microorganism distribution tanks 42a and 42b are connected to a maintenance air line to prevent solidification of the v shaped grooves with graduations so as to be measurable and solidification of the remaining sludge under extremely low load"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102292971-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as the main body 10 and the groundwater 12 installed on one side of the main body 10 are filled with an amount of groundwater 12 set by the driving of the first pump 11 it is contaminated while passing through a plurality of segment filters 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101094321-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "s100 screen precipitation process s200 stationary precipitation process s300 continuous filtration process s400 soil improvement process 10 10 pressure pump 20 pressure filtration tank 21 inlet 23 outlet 24 discharge pipe 25 float discharge outlet 26 screw 27 closed tube 30 filter 31 filter hole 40 floating material removal means 41 wing anchor 42 wing to remove the float 43 rotation device 44 rotating shaft 45 guide rail 46 guide block 51 injection nozzle 52 fastening portion 53 injection nozzle guide 54 inline transfer pipe 55 inline coupler 56 inline coupler inlet 57 pivot shaft inlet 60 reflux blocking plate 61 vibration generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "naturally it belongs to the scope of the invention.100 multi purpose thermostat 120 liquid corrosion tank 121 aerobic generation 125 diffuser 127 air inlet 128 air outlet 130 cooling tank 131 intake port 132 exhaust port 141 air supply fan 142 exhaust fan 150 wastewater injection unit 153 conical dispersion induction member 154 wastewater outlet 156 wastewater supply pipe 157 liquid circulation pump 170 shatterproof device 171 inlet 172 outlet 174 scattering prevention device body 176 178 plate 179 slope 182 flushing pump 184 flushing piping 185 chemical pump 187 chemical piping 300 chemical flocculation precipitation filter 320 flocculation reactor 340 sedimentation unit 342 sludge collector 343 treated water outlet 345 pressure sensor 347 rectifying plate 349 sludge discharge pump 350 filter unit 352 filter unit frame 352a round border 352b spokes 354 filtration cell 357 rotary drive shaft 361 wash water nozzle 362 wash water pump 363 wash water receiver 365 wash water discharge pipe 367 electric valve 371 control panel 373 sump tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101725047-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes in form and details may be made therein without departing from the spirit and scope of the invention as defined by the appended claims.1000 non point pollution source treatment device according to the present invention 10 first piping 20 second piping 30 third piping 40 fourth piping 110 pretreatment tank 120 rectifying screen 130 140 temporary storage 210 filtration tank 220 221 filter block 222 first filter paper 222 1 1st pier 223 second material pier 223 1 2nd pier 310 backwater tank 410 first drainage pump 420 second drainage pump 430 backwash pump 500 510 blower 520 inlet pipe 530 communicator 540 distributor 550 partition plate 551 split hole 560 spiral shaft 570 transfer pipe 580 inner wall 600 purified water sprayer 610 connector 620 injection nozzle 621 injection hole 630 injection filter s1 precipitation space s2 storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "description of the related art a food waste b wash water c drain d waste water e solid fraction f meat fish grain g functional feed 1 food waste recycling facility 10 metering unit 11 identification means 111 identification card 112 card reader 113 identification chip 114 scanner 12 weighbridge 13 pick up vehicle 14 management means 20 input portion 21 storage hopper 211 screw feeder 30 screening crushing unit 31 screening crusher 40 supply part 41 storage tank 411 automatic meter 50 liquid phase fermentation distribution processing section 51 stirring tank 511 stirring blade 512 wood chip 52 nozzle 53 oxygen generator 54 drive motor 55 control unit 60 solid separator 61 settling tank 62 centrifugal separator 70 purification treatment section 71 chemical precipitation tank 72 flow rate adjusting tank 73 anaerobic tank 74 anoxic tank 75 aerobic tank 76 biological sedimentation tank 77 filtration tank 78 wastewater recycling unit 79 waste water discharge unit 80 feed sterilization part 81 automatic meter 90 feed fermentation part 100 feed drying unit 110 feed packing unit 1101 1102 feed packing machine 1103 delivery vehicle 1104 feed storage tank 120 odor removing unit 121 biofilter 122 first hood 123 second hood 124 soil deodorization unit 131 liquid fertilizer storage unit s100 collection and transportation process s110 weighing process s111 identification process s112 gross weight input process s113 input amount checking process s120 inputting process s130 screening shredding process s140 supplying process s150 liquid fermentation decomposition process s160 solid separation process s170 purification process s171 chemical precipitation purification process s172 flow regulating tank storing process s173 anaerobic tank removing process s174 anoxic tank denitrification process s175 aeration tank microorganism cultivation process s176 separation process of microbial solids s177 filtration process s178 waste water recycling and discharge process s180 feed sterilization process s190 feed fermentation process s200 feed drying process s210 feed packing process s220 liquid fertilizer storage process s230 liquid fertilizer supplying process s240 odor removing process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}]</data>
