  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637562-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "the supply means and the water pumping means are automatically controlled by a monitoring system driven by signals of a detection sensor not shown for detecting the water level of the settling tank 3 the filtration tank 4 and the rectifying tank 5 at an appropriate position and manual control may be performed depending on the contamination level of the storm and the degree of contamination of the filter 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101764398-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "a contamination abatement facility is provided in the lower wall 16 of the housing 10 a filtering partition wall 31 which is formed so as to have an upper end which is equal to or lower than the lowest point height of the inflow pipe 17 and which is separated from the space of the filtration tank 30 formed on the rear side the filtration unit 30a which is located between the rear wall 31 and the rear wall 12 and has both ends vertically fixed to the left and right side walls 13 and 14 so that only the space on the upper side of the filtration tank 30 is filtered and an upper support partition wall 37 for separating the upper support partition wall 30a and the upper support partition wall 30b into a management section 30b for a worker to enter and work for management of the filtration section 30a a mesh chain filter mesh net 32 having a front end portion fixed to the left and right side walls 13 and 14 and a lower end of the filtration partition 31 and the upper support partition 37 30a of the filtration mesh net 32 and is held in the sedimentation tank 20 a filtration material layer 33 having at least one filter medium 33a that is filtered while flowing an initial storm that flows into the filtration section 30a of the filtration tank 30 through the filtration tank 30 the grill 38 is fixedly supported on the upper support partition wall 37 and the rear wall 12 at the lower side of the discharge pipe 18 and a filter medium 33a of the filter medium layer 33 by spraying water at a predetermined pressure toward the filter medium layer 33 through the filter mesh network 32 located below the filter mesh network 32 of the filter medium 30 a water distribution pipe 34 having at least one water injection nozzle 34a for separating foreign matter adhering to the filter medium 30 and a filtering mesh network 32 located below the filtering mesh network 32 of the filtration tank 30 33a of the filter material layer 33 by discharging air bubbles at a predetermined pressure toward the filter material layer 33 and an air bubble spraying tube 35 having one or more air bubble spray nozzles 35a for facilitating the initialization of the sedimentation tank 20 and a filtration tank discharge pump 36 disposed at the lower end of the filtration tank 30 and discharging the filtered stormwater through the filtration tank discharge pipe 36a to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
