  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101097134-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "to maintain a constant suspended solids mlss concentration in the denitrification tank 22 in the range of 3 000 to 20 000 mg l even in an emergency the excess sludge concentrated in the sludge concentration tank 26 is dewatered when the sludge residence time srt elapses the treated water finally treated in the treatment system is temporarily held in the treatment tank 25 and discharged out of the system separation and filtration process of the micro contamination particles in the batch reaction tank 23 using the flotation filter module 50 according to the present invention after the precipitation process of the batch reaction tank 23 in the batch reaction tank 23 in water while separating filtering the micro contaminant particles at the upper side of the filter only the filtrate filtered in the supernatant is discharged to the treatment tank 26"}, {"pat_id": "US-7052613-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "after the ozone sensor 120 monitoring ozone usage rates in the cell 10 indicates to the sensor processor control unit 60 that the ozone is no longer being utilized for oxidation of biological or chemical contamination discharge valve 76 opens allowing water from the cell 10 to flow into the storage tank 107 and ozone distribution to the cell 10 is stopped through the closing of the ozone valve 86 completing the disaffection treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826790-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "at the upper part a sloping induction plate is installed at the tip of the first drainage guide plate a second settling filtration tank for blocking inflow of fine contaminants accompanied by the storm and having a filter net installed on the downflow channel formed by the lower part of the precipitation inducing plate and the first drainage guide plate to remove the dissolved fine contaminants a second rim hole formed in the upper portion of the first drainage guide plate of the secondary settling filtration tank and having a second rim hole and a second rim hole formed in the second rim of the second settling filtration tank the second partition wall is provided with a drain plate for partitioning the space with the second settling filtration tank and discharging the rainwater having an inclined surface at the inlet side and flowing into the second rinse hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974535-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "also as described above the time point at which the initial rainwater drain valve v1 is closed closed can be closed only for a time period in which the water level precipitation amount is maintained on the high water level of the flowmeter chamber 112c when the rainwater is not continuously detected the initial rainwater exclusion valve v1 is closed closed to prevent contamination of the body portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101716466-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation sensor 18 installed in a drainage passage 213 of the solar cell module 21 to measure the amount of precipitation water collected in the solar cell module 21 an opening and closing unit 225 connected at both ends to the drainage passage 213 and connected to an elastic string 281 for detecting the amount of precipitation by the precipitation sensor 18 to determine the opening and closing level of the collecting tube 221 a collecting connection unit 12 connected to the drainage passage 213 for collecting the precipitation a control server 11 for controlling the operation of the opening closing means installed in the collection connection unit 12 based on the information transmitted from the precipitation sensor 18 a storage unit 15 in which the precipitation is stored a detection unit 16 for detecting the state of water stored in the storage unit 15 and and a branch unit 14 operated by the control server 11 based on the information transmitted from the detection unit 16 the storage unit 15 is installed under the solar cell module and is shielded by the solar cell module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101716466-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the level of the stored precipitation measured by the ultrasonic sensor 161 or the contamination level may be transmitted to the control server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388941-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in order to prevent such contamination of mine drainage in advance conventionally it can be selectively installed before and after a shophouse successive alkaltnity producting system tank that can purify heavy metals in the middle of a mine a marsh planted with aquatic plants and a shophouse tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021035-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "physical washing using a brush or a loofah may be used for washing the reservoir but chemical washing using a cleaning solution containing a specific component is generally used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101710108-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "as described above when the main body a is viewed from the side when the contaminated water passes from the left side to the right side of the main body a the contaminated water bumps the lower surface from the upper surface of the precipitation partition wall 21 the sludge mixed with the contaminated water is allowed to fall down and the contaminated water passes through the lower contaminated water passage section 21a formed in the lower part of the settting partition wall 21 and then passes through the filter plate 22 the sludge mixed with the sludge and the soil mixed with the sludge and soil is filtered and passes through the upper contamination canal section 21a formed on the upper part of the sludge and soil and this process is a series of continuous processes and the contaminated water is serially formed from the lower part to the upper part of the filter plate 22 in a zigzag form so that the contaminated water passes through the inside of the main body a to remove sludge and soil contained in the contaminated water and that before and filtered"}, {"pat_id": "US-3967860-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this precipitation or plating out seriously reduces the operational efficiencies of the pipeline system requiring increased maintenance and causing contamination of the pipeline to a degree which presents serious problems if it is desired to use the same pipeline for transporting other materials in a relatively high state of purity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102778291-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "in other words according to the present invention by having a system capable of continuously recovering the sensible heat of the condensate treated water generated in the s3 stage through a heat exchanger system 132 pipe blockage and scale contamination through cooling precipitation that may occur in the secondary reverse osmosis membrane filtration process bcro in the s2 stage can be effectively reduced or prevented even in winter or extremely cold weather without a separate additional heat source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102778291-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "specifically the heat exchanger system 132 can be provided to recover the sensible heat of the condensate generated in the crystallizer 131 as a heat source for the hot side of the pre heater thereby preventing pipe blockage through cooling precipitation and scale contamination of the high concentration concentrated reverse osmosis membrane filtration process even in winter or extremely cold weather without a separate heat source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102230365-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "after chemical treatment in the reaction tank 120 colloidal fine clay which is difficult to remove due to precipitation is removed by passing through the filter tank 140 and reused as process water washing water thereby lowering the process load due to colloidal fine clay"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "to limit contamination of the receiving flows and streams by untreated combined sewage the diverted flow may enter the receiving stream by direct overflow only when the soil percentage of the water to be discharged has been reduced to a level such that there is no further risk of appreciable contamination of the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102373416-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "buffer storage facility control device and its control methodthe present invention relates to a buffer storage facility control device and more particularly it has a function to block direct inflow of accidental runoff water into a buffer storage facility and to reduce non point pollution during precipitation and link them with the sluice gate of the buffer storage facility according to the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "therefore the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the second embodiment of the present invention is configured such that only the reservoir 200 is maintained until the level of the reservoir 200 reaches the highest level in the u shape reversed to the siphon channel 295 a sufficient amount of time for the primary precipitation treatment is ensured and then an initial excellent standoff contamination is supplied to the sedimentation paper 400 through the flow rate reducing manhole 300 at a limited flow rate and is discharged through the discharge water gate 500 and the excellent non point pollution is discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828913-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "since the large amount of organic matter in the fresh water is contained the membrane contamination due to the organic matter may become serious and the salt water may contain a large amount of polyvalent ions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101351354-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "the injection method may be selected according to the algal bloom or the degree of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200306165-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the water in the storage tank is so pure that biological contamination can easily occur due to contact with air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to achieve the above object as well as other objects that can be easily expressed the present invention applies a contact oxidation method to increase the contact surface of the deeper contaminated river water and sewage or sewage and the contact media to reduce the contamination concentration but as crushed stone"}, {"pat_id": "US-10350653-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "bacterial contamination is usually observed in crude oil whilst fungi usually cause contamination of aviation fuel"}]</data>
