  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101097134-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "to maintain a constant suspended solids mlss concentration in the denitrification tank 22 in the range of 3 000 to 20 000 mg l even in an emergency the excess sludge concentrated in the sludge concentration tank 26 is dewatered when the sludge residence time srt elapses the treated water finally treated in the treatment system is temporarily held in the treatment tank 25 and discharged out of the system separation and filtration process of the micro contamination particles in the batch reaction tank 23 using the flotation filter module 50 according to the present invention after the precipitation process of the batch reaction tank 23 in the batch reaction tank 23 in water while separating filtering the micro contaminant particles at the upper side of the filter only the filtrate filtered in the supernatant is discharged to the treatment tank 26"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "adsorbent cloth 17 is installed inside the oil water separation tank 12 and the rainwater level side of the oil water separation tank 12 flows in through the outflow pipe 18 to bend in a spiral direction along the inclined surface while flowing into the inclined plate settling tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179489-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "in addition the pretreatment tank 2 includes a contaminant removal facility flocculant injection facility flocculation precipitation facility flocculation sand filtration facility flocculation sediment sand filtration facility chlorine injection facility aeration facility flotation separation facility biological treatment facility powder activated carbon facility it may be composed of any one or two or more of ozone generating equipment granular activated carbon equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0126558-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in order to smoothly induce sediment residue a recovery hole 41 is formed at the bottom of the sedimentation chamber 40 composed of the inclined surface so as to drop the sedimentation debris into the decay chamber 20 in the recovery hole 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101453163-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "further in the apparatus for treating contaminants in an early stage rainwater contaminant and a combined sewage pipe according to an embodiment of the present invention the pretreatment tank may have a partition wall formed on the floor and inducing precipitation of sand that can not be filtered through the coarse screen can be installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101779726-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "this patent document discloses a high efficiency batch wastewater treatment facility and a method thereof in which after precipitation process of a batch reaction tank is combined with an inverse filter module for discharging only the filtrate filtered out in treated water while separating fine contaminant particles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869158-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a preprocessing unit a screen unit which rotates the rainwater supplied from the pretreatment unit in a streamline to precipitate the precipitated nonpoint pollutants an oil water separator for supplying rainwater having precipitated nonpoint pollutants precipitated to the precipitation unit while floating and separating the floating nonpoint pollutants of oil in the screen unit precipitating unit for reducing the precipitated non point pollutant by sedimenting to the own weight of the precipitated non point pollutant contained in the rainwater supplied from the oil and water separation unit a solid liquid separation unit configured to separate sedimentary non point pollutants contained in the rainwater by sedimentation with their own weight while the rainwater passing through the precipitation unit moves left and right along a plurality of separator guide holes a rainwater supply unit for supplying rainwater in which the precipitated non point pollutant is precipitated in the solid liquid separator to the lower part of the filtration unit a filtering unit for filtering the floating nonpoint pollutant contained in the rainwater in the filtering member while the rainwater supplied from the rainwater supply unit moves from the lower portion to the upper portion initial rainwater non point contaminant purification apparatus comprising an outflow guide for outflowing the rainwater finally filtered by the filtering unit to the rainwater discharge pipe of the pretreatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100986036-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "separating and removing the coarse contaminants containing the animal manure wastewater by the complex treatment tank a collecting tank collecting livestock manure waste water provided from the contaminant treatment tank separating the supernatant by inputting a polymer flocculant into the livestock manure wastewater provided by the centrifugal aggregation treatment tank a flow rate control tank temporarily storing the symbol water provided from the centrifugation aggregation treatment tank providing some symbol water to the bioreactor and providing the remaining symbol water to the soil microorganism adjustment tank through the raw water supply line bioreactor nitrifying the supernatant water provided from the flow control tank to remove organic matter and nitrogen and to proceed with phosphorus intake by the phosphorus removing microorganism separating the mixed water treated in the bioreactor into the precipitated sludge and the supernatant removing the untreated residual organic material and phosphorus from the supernatant water provided from the precipitation tank by the pressure flotation aggregation tank using a polymer flocculant and a filtration separation tank for removing insoluble organic matter suspended matter and colloidal solid components from the treated water in the pressure flotation aggregation treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100986036-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "livestock manure treatment method of the present invention the composite contaminant treatment tank separating removing the coarse contaminants containing the livestock manure waste water a collecting tank collecting livestock manure waste water provided from the contaminant treatment tank separating the supernatant by inputting a polymer flocculant into the livestock manure wastewater provided by the centrifugal aggregation treatment tank a flow rate control tank temporarily storing the symbol water provided from the centrifugation aggregation treatment tank providing some symbol water to the bioreactor and providing the remaining symbol water to the soil microorganism adjustment tank through the raw water supply line bioreactor nitrifying the supernatant water provided from the flow control tank to remove organic matter and nitrogen and to proceed with phosphorus intake by the phosphorus removing microorganism separating the mixed water treated in the bioreactor into the precipitated sludge and the supernatant removing the untreated residual organic material and phosphorus from the supernatant water provided from the precipitation tank by the pressure flotation aggregation tank using a polymer flocculant and a filtration separation tank for removing insoluble organic matter suspended matter and colloidal solid components from the treated water in the pressure flotation aggregation treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314901-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "5 and the secondary sedimentation tank 6 and the aeration method of activated sludge is the organic contaminant contained in the influent water as a nutrient component to proliferate while decomposing by oxidation adsorption self oxidation and at the same time in the anoxic tank 4 of the nitrogen sludge was removed by reducing the nitrated nitrogen in the internal circulating water passed through the activated sludge tank 5 and then in the secondary precipitation tank 6 to precipitate the activated sludge to separate from the supernatant and to the supernatant the treated water is disinfected and discharged in the discharge tank 7 a part of the activated sludge precipitated in the secondary precipitation tank 6 is returned to the activated sludge tank 5 and the excess sludge is sludge storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100951135-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the lower support plate 224 has a mesh size such that the precipitation medium 222 does not penetrate and preferably a contaminant introduced into the lower portion of the treatment tank 205 may be provided in the lower support plate 224"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100951184-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "pretreatment step decomposing a high concentration of nutrients contained in the wastewater passed through the pretreatment step using a high rate microbial reaction stirrer wherein the step of storing the wastewater filtered out the contaminants and fine solids in the pretreatment step in a first flow rate adjustment tank a first biological treatment step comprising the step of purifying the stored waste water by using a microorganism inside with a high rate microbial reaction stirrer purifying and discharging the waste water and storing the discharged waste water in a second flow control tank separating the wastewater stored in the second flow adjusting tank into sludge and wastewater using a centrifuge used in the pretreatment step storing the wastewater that has undergone the solid liquid separation in a third flow control tank a second biological treatment step of decomposing organic matter and nitrogen contained in the waste water stored in the third flow regulating tank by a biological treatment facility a chemical treatment step of decomposing the hardly decomposable substance and the chromaticity contained in the wastewater having passed through the second biological treatment step by a chemical treatment facility and livestock wastewater or high concentration using a high rate microbial reaction stirrer characterized in that the wastewater stored in the second flow rate adjustment tank to the wastewater ratio for the open field or the wastewater stored in the third flow rate adjustment tank to the facility farm liquid ratio as a method of recycling and purifying wastewater the second biological treatment step may include an aeration tank step of supplying air and removing organic substances contained in the wastewater by using aerobic microorganisms and a first sedimentation tank stage for separating the wastewater and sludge treated in the aeration tank through sedimentation the chemical treatment step comprises a chemical coagulation step of agglomerating the hardly decomposable material using an inorganic coagulant or an organic coagulant and and a second precipitation tank step of separating the aggregates and the wastewater aggregated in the chemical coagulation tank step"}, {"pat_id": "US-4445935-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "during this addition the oxidation reduction potential of the combined solution may be continually monitored by employing a conventional high impedance voltmeter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100237606-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "and after adjusting the flow rate and inducing precipitation in the primary sedimentation tank 102 and then through the activated sludge tank 103 denitrification tank 104 secondary sedimentation tank 105 the active sludge tank 103 as described above in the a method the aeration of air causes the microbial mass called active to come into contact with the microorganism contact medium and the microbial mass is decomposed by self extinguishing while proliferating the organic pollutants contained in the influent as nutrients"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the pump aeration and precipitation tank pressure tank and filter tank may be included in a pump house or in a basement substantially to reduce outdoor installation and servicing problems encountered particularly in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a dispersing hopper 110 to which wastewater is transported and a dispersing hopper 110 a quantitative supply unit 100 including a disk roller 120 spaced apart from the upper portion to supply a fixed amount of wastewater to a predetermined height the screen drum 210 through which a plurality of drain holes 212 are formed to dehydrate the moisture contained in the wastewater supplied through the quantitative supply unit 100 and the coarse contaminants subjected to dehydration treatment by rotational movement within the screen drum 210 a screen dehydrator 200 including a first transfer screw 220 for transferring the a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method a disk drum 410 in which a fixed disk ring 412 and a rotating disk ring 414 are alternately arranged to receive the treated water separated from the sedimentation treatment unit 300 and the treatment injected into the disk drum 410 a disk dehydration unit 400 including a second transfer screw 420 for transferring water and containing and a contaminant discharging unit 500 provided with a third transfer screw 520 to collect and discharge contaminants separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 and the sedimentation unit 300 the screen drum 210 of the screen dehydrator 200 has an inlet 214 for accommodating the waste water flowing from the quantitative supply unit 100 into the inside of the screen drum 210 on one side and the contaminants are discharged on the other side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "quantitative supply unit 100 including a disk roller 120 for supplying the screen drum 210 through which a plurality of drain holes 212 are formed to dehydrate the moisture contained in the wastewater supplied through the quantitative supply unit 100 and the coarse contaminants subjected to dehydration treatment by rotational movement within the screen drum 210 a screen dehydrator 200 including a first transfer screw 220 for transferring the a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method a disk drum 410 in which a fixed disk ring 412 and a rotating disk ring 414 are alternately arranged to receive the treated water separated from the sedimentation treatment unit 300 and the treatment injected into the disk drum 410 a disk dehydration unit 400 including a second transfer screw 420 for transferring water and a contaminant discharging unit 500 provided with a third transfer screw 520 to collect and discharge contaminants separated from the screen dehydrating unit 200 and the sedimentation treatment unit 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in order to achieve the object of the present invention as described above an integrated contaminant processing apparatus according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention has an inlet formed on one side the inlet chamber is formed to open the other side a precipitation chamber installed at an open portion of the inflow chamber having a discharge port formed on the other side a overflowware installed on the inner side corresponding to the discharge port and a sedimentation hopper formed to be inclined at a lower portion thereof a coarse contaminant processing unit having a fixed screen mounted inclined inside the inflow chamber corresponding to the inlet and filtering coarse contaminants it is installed inclined to the inner side of the inlet chamber to the rear side of the fixed screen and having a vibration damping main body having a wedge bar screen a chain having a plurality of rakes for lifting the impurities caught in the wedge bar screen and a chain drive unit for driving the chain a miscellaneous matter processing unit comprising a a settling discharge unit for discharging sand settled to the inner lower portion of the settling chamber to the outside it is characterized by including"}]</data>
