  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-1575875-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "disinfection metal removal and oil water emulsion splitting occurs and contaminants are removed by vacuuming floated material from the surface and removing bottom sediments via the sloped bottom of the vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100661079-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition figure 4 is a conceptual diagram showing the use of the carrier in the sewage treatment facility to control the flow rate of the incoming error in the flow control tank remove the organic matter nitrogen and phosphorus in the contact oxidation aeration tank precipitate the solid material in the precipitation tank in this case the foam generated in the previous process is removed from the defoaming tank the water is filtered and discharged through the disinfection process in the filtration tank and the sludge precipitated in the sedimentation tank is transported to a separate dwarf concentration tank and taken out separately"}, {"pat_id": "US-7052613-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "after the ozone sensor 120 monitoring ozone usage rates in the cell 10 indicates to the sensor processor control unit 60 that the ozone is no longer being utilized for oxidation of biological or chemical contamination discharge valve 76 opens allowing water from the cell 10 to flow into the storage tank 107 and ozone distribution to the cell 10 is stopped through the closing of the ozone valve 86 completing the disaffection treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200412170-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition figure 4 is a conceptual diagram showing the use of the carrier in the sewage treatment facility to control the flow rate of the incoming error in the flow control tank remove the organic matter nitrogen and phosphorus in the contact oxidation aeration tank precipitate the solid material in the precipitation tank in this case the foam generated in the previous process is removed from the defoaming tank the water is filtered and discharged through the disinfection process in the filtration tank and the sludge precipitated in the sedimentation tank is transported to a separate dwarf concentration tank and taken out separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100387324-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by desorption of the biofilm attached to the membrane it prevents anaerobic conditions due to clogging of the filtration pores and provides a growth environment for microorganisms attached to the suspension contact media and also provides direct filtration in the oxidation tank without the need for a separate precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100638424-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "eggplant biological reactor a treatment tank for storing the wastewater from the biological reaction tank and discharging the wastewater to be treated at a constant pressure with a subsequent reverse osmosis membrane treatment system polyamide reverse osmosis composite membrane or cellulose acetate reverse osmosis composite membrane removal rate of nacl when permeate 2000 ppm nacl under 15 recovery conditions under 15 recovery operating at 3 30 bar with recovery rate above 30 a reverse osmosis membrane tank having a reverse osmosis membrane of 98 or more and permeating wastewater introduced from the treatment tank to produce final treated water and a ph adjusting tank for adjusting the ph of the reverse osmosis membrane concentrated water to 2 to 3 a fenton reactor for treating the ph adjusted concentrated water discharged from the ph adjusting tank with fenton s reagent and a ph of the oxidized water introduced from the fenton reactor to 6 to 7 the height ranges from 300 to 2500 mg l h 2 o 2 and includes a ph neutralization tank a flocculation tank which aggregates suspended particles contained in the neutralized treated water and a precipitation tank which precipitates aggregates to produce a supernatant and has a fe 2 the concentration ratio of h 2 o 2 includes an oxidation reactor using a fenton reagent of 1.0 2.0 wastewater treatment apparatus for reducing the dioxane concentration of the treated water is treated in the reverse osmosis membrane and the oxidation reaction tank and finally discharged to the ecosystem to 1 60 mg l"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100638424-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "removing dissolved organics and nitrogen storing the wastewater from the biological reaction tank in a treatment tank which discharges wastewater to be treated at a constant pressure with a subsequent reverse osmosis membrane treatment system polyamide reverse osmosis composite membrane or cellulose acetate reverse osmosis composite membrane the recovery of nacl when permeated at 2000 ppm nacl under 15 recovery conditions at 15 recovery operating at 3 30 bar and under 15 bar pressure producing treated water by permeating wastewater discharged from the treated water tank to a constant pressure in a reverse osmosis membrane tank having a reverse osmosis membrane having a removal rate of 98 or more and a ph adjusting tank for adjusting the ph of the reverse osmosis membrane concentrated water to 2 to 3 a fenton reactor for treating the ph adjusted concentrated water discharged from the ph adjusting tank with fenton s reagent and a ph of the oxidized water introduced from the fenton reactor to 6 to 7 in an oxidation reaction tank including a ph neutralization tank a flocculation tank which aggregates suspended particles contained in the neutralized treated water and a precipitation tank which precipitates the aggregates to produce a supernatant the concentrated water discharged from the reverse osmosis membrane is 300 h 2 o 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100638424-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "according to one aspect of the present invention in a wastewater treatment apparatus raw wastewater containing an average codcr concentration of 10 000 mg l and a dioxane concentration of 50 to 1 000 mg l in a range of 8 000 to 12 000 mg l direct treatment consisting of an anoxic tank at the front and an aeration tank at the rear with a micro or ultrafiltration membrane module in the aeration tank a mixed liquid suspended solids mlss concentration of 8 000 15 000 mg l f of 0.1 0.5 biological reactor having an m ratio and a volume load of 0.1 5 kg m 3 .d a treatment tank for storing the wastewater from the biological reaction tank and discharging the wastewater to be treated at a constant pressure with a subsequent reverse osmosis membrane treatment system polyamide reverse osmosis composite membrane or cellulose acetate reverse osmosis composite membrane removal rate of nacl when permeate 2000 ppm nacl under 15 recovery conditions under 15 recovery operating at 3 30 bar with recovery rate above 30 a reverse osmosis membrane tank having a reverse osmosis membrane of 98 or more and permeating wastewater introduced from the treatment tank to produce final treated water and a ph adjusting tank for adjusting the ph of the reverse osmosis membrane concentrated water to 2 to 3 a fenton reaction tank for treating the ph adjusted concentrated water discharged from the ph adjusting tank with a fenton reagent and adjusting the ph of the oxidized water introduced from the fenton reaction tank to 6 to 7 the furnace height ranges from 300 to 2500 mg l h 2 o 2 including a ph neutralization tank a flocculation tank which aggregates suspended particles contained in the neutralized treated water and a precipitation tank which precipitates the aggregates to produce a supernatant and wherein fe 2 h 2 o 2 concentration ratio is 1.0 2.0 including the oxidation reaction tank using a fenton reagent dioxane concentration of treated water treated in the reverse osmosis membrane and oxidation reaction tank and finally discharged to the ecosystem to 1 60 mg l a wastewater treatment apparatus for reducing is provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100638424-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "removing dissolved organics and nitrogen by adding a biological reactor having a volume load of storing the wastewater from the biological reaction tank in a treatment tank which discharges wastewater to be treated at a constant pressure with a subsequent reverse osmosis membrane treatment system polyamide reverse osmosis composite membrane or cellulose acetate reverse osmosis composite membrane removal rate of nacl when permeate 2000 ppm nacl under 15 recovery conditions under 15 recovery operating at 3 30 bar with recovery rate above 30 producing treated water by permeating the wastewater discharged from the treated water tank to a constant pressure in a reverse osmosis membrane tank having a reverse osmosis membrane of 98 or more and a ph adjusting tank for adjusting the ph of the reverse osmosis membrane concentrated water to 2 to 3 a fenton reaction tank for treating the ph adjusted concentrated water discharged from the ph adjusting tank with a fenton reagent and adjusting the ph of the oxidized water introduced from the fenton reaction tank to 6 to 7 in the oxidation reaction tank including a ph neutralization tank to increase the furnace a flocculation tank which aggregates the suspended particles contained in the neutralized treated water and a precipitation tank which precipitates the aggregates to produce a supernatant the concentrated water discharged from the reverse osmosis membrane is converted into h 2 o 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100201604-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a landfill leachate treatment method comprising an excess sludge treatment process for treating excess sludge separated in a precipitation process the waste landfill leachate treatment method comprising a storage step of temporarily storing a large amount of leachate generated in association with the flow rate adjustment process an organic substance concentration measuring step of measuring an organic substance concentration in the leachate to grasp the characteristics of the leachate introduced into the flow rate adjusting process a leachate supply control process of supplying leachate to a fire extinguishing process or a mixed stirring process according to the characteristics of the leachate introduced into the flow rate adjusting process a digestion process of treating the leachate transferred in the flow rate adjusting process by anaerobic microorganisms in an anaerobic atmosphere a mixing stirring step for mixing the leachate of the flow rate adjusting step with the supernatant treated through the extinguishing step aeration process in which the leachate conveyed in the flow rate adjusting process or the mixed stirring process is treated by an aerobic microorganism in an aerobic atmosphere but an anoxic zone for removing nitrogen is formed at the inlet of the leachate a chemical coagulation process for coagulating and removing the hardly decomposable organic matter contained in the treated water after the aeration process a fenton oxidation step of oxidatively decomposing residual hardly decomposable organic matter contained in the treated water after the chemical coagulation step with an oxidizing agent it comprises a third settling process for solid liquid separation of the sludge agglomerated in the fenton oxidation process to increase the treatment efficiency of the high concentration of ammonia nitrogen and hardly decomposable organic matter contained in the leachate the treatment according to the properties of leachate and the amount of leachate landfill leachate treatment method characterized in that the process is operated variably"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100201604-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "a landfill leachate treatment method comprising an excess sludge treatment process for treating excess sludge separated from a precipitation process and an activated sludge sedimentation process the waste landfill leachate treatment method comprising a storage step of temporarily storing a large amount of leachate generated in association with the flow rate adjustment process an organic substance concentration measuring step of measuring an organic substance concentration in the leachate to grasp the characteristics of the leachate introduced into the flow rate adjusting process a leachate supply control process of supplying leachate to a fire extinguishing process or a mixed stirring process according to the characteristics of the leachate introduced into the flow rate adjusting process a digestion process of treating the leachate transferred in the flow rate adjusting process by anaerobic microorganisms in an anaerobic atmosphere aeration process in which the leachate transported in the flow rate adjusting process or the mixed stirring process is treated by the aerobic microorganisms in an aerobic atmosphere but an anoxic zone for removing nitrogen is formed at the inlet of the leachate a chemical coagulation process for coagulating and removing the hardly decomposable organic matter contained in the treated water after the aeration process a fenton oxidation step of oxidatively decomposing residual hardly decomposable organic matter contained in the treated water after the chemical coagulation step with an oxidizing agent it comprises a third settling process for solid liquid separation of the sludge agglomerated in the fenton oxidation process to increase the efficiency of removal of ammonia nitrogen and hardly decomposable organic matter contained in a large amount in the leachate over the years of landfill it is achieved by the landfill leachate treatment method which can operate the treatment facility variably by changing the flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100454362-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "and an anaerobic oxygen free aerobic step for causing an organic oxidation reaction opening the barrier wall and maintaining the entire reaction chamber in aerobic state for the first time in the state of integrating the first and second reaction chambers to dephosphate excess intake organic matter oxidation reaction and denitrification gas generated in the previous anoxic stage excess sludge a total exhalation excess sludge discharge step of opening the outlet to discharge excess sludge ingested with phosphorus the variable barrier wall is characterized by consisting of the entire anoxic precipitation discharge step of discharging the supernatant by opening the treated water outlet after the sludge for a predetermined time by switching the entire reaction chamber to an anoxic state in the open wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200412169-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in addition figure 4 is a conceptual diagram showing the use of the carrier in the sewage treatment facility to control the flow rate of the incoming error in the flow control tank remove the organic matter nitrogen and phosphorus in the contact oxidation aeration tank precipitate the solid material in the precipitation tank in the defoaming tank the foam generated in the previous process is removed and the water is filtered and discharged through the disinfection process in the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100783789-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the microbial reaction tank nitrogen n phosphorus p and organic by introducing the treated water passing through the first settling tank 10 to the microbial reaction tank consisting of anaerobic tank 20 anoxic tank 30 and aerobic tank 40 remove the material"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the rear end of the aeration tank is a water purification apparatus for removing iron and manganese characterized in that the reaction precipitation tank for aging the oxide of the aerated oxidation water oxidized in the aeration tank and settle the precipitate formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "claim_16", "text": "the method according to claim 15 the water purification method for removing iron and manganese characterized in that it further comprises a reaction precipitation step of oxidizing the aerated oxidation water passed through the aeration step through a reaction precipitation tank and precipitates the precipitate formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in addition in the water purifying apparatus for removing iron and manganese according to the present invention the rear end of the aeration tank is further provided with a reaction precipitation tank for aging the oxide of the aerated oxidation water oxidized in the aeration tank and settle the generated precipitate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "2 the aging reaction of the oxide of the aeration oxidation water oxidized in the aeration tank 100 and precipitates the precipitate produced it is preferable that a reaction precipitation tank 200 for performing the precipitation step is provided"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "this system thus allows the sulphur to oxidize and precipitate in the aeration precipitation tank and the iron to continue its oxidation and precipitation in such aeration precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "it will be understood that the term aeration precipitation tank assembly or means as used herein generically defines means operative to aerate and precipitate to aerate and convert by oxidation and or to aerate precipitate and convert"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100403183-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "a highly concentrated precipitation tank for filtration oxidation and decomposition to remove biochemical oxygen demand bod and suspended solids ss the high concentration sedimentation filtration chamber 2 400b in the rear is formed through the high concentration filtration chamber b and the upper portion the outlet is formed in the upper end of the rear side the disinfection tank 510 is built in the outlet side to filter and purified filthy water from the disinfection tank 510 it consists of a discharge tank 500 which is discharged after contact by sterilization is a basic feature of the technical configuration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100403183-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "therefore it is possible to process even under high load and the oxidation reaction and the filtration action occur simultaneously in a single reaction tank so that it is possible not only to obtain clean treated water with less suspended matter but also to settle the facility site because it does not need a precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the modular wetland infrastructure 300 maintenance to be connected to the lower contact oxidation tank 500 to maintain the contact oxidation tank 500 located in the lower portion of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 manhole 330 and if the water level of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to precipitation exceeds a certain level in order to protect the wetland by transferring the influent directly to the sedimentation tank 400 modular wetland infrastructure 300 it is preferable to have a water level control pipe 340 is installed at the bottom of the through water connection with the drainage layer connected to the settling tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100783790-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the microbial reaction tank nitrogen n phosphorus p and organic substances by introducing the treated water passing through the first settling tank 10 into the microbial reaction tank consisting of anaerobic tank 20 anoxic tank 30 and the aerobic tank 40 remove it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200412171-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition figure 5 is a conceptual diagram showing the use of the carrier in the sewage treatment facility by adjusting the flow rate of the incoming error in the flow control tank remove the organic matter and nitrogen and phosphorus in the contact oxidation aeration tank precipitate the solid material in the precipitation tank in the defoaming tank the foam generated in the previous process is removed and the water is filtered and discharged through the disinfection process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050144-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in general biological treatment apparatus for sewage and wastewater which is widely used at present is provided with an aeration tank which is an organic oxidation tank and a precipitation tank for precipitating microorganisms grown in the aeration tank thereby oxidizing and removing organic matter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100661073-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition figure 5 is a conceptual diagram showing the use of the carrier in the sewage treatment facility by adjusting the flow rate of the incoming error in the flow control tank remove the organic matter and nitrogen and phosphorus in the contact oxidation aeration tank precipitate the solid material in the precipitation tank in the defoaming tank the foam generated in the previous process is removed and the water is filtered and discharged through the disinfection process"}, {"pat_id": "US-5250193-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the use of a cyclone injector was believed to minimize high injector wall temperatures and minimize salt precipitation which might have thus occurred at the wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102361939-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the wastewater treatment methods include physicochemical treatment methods such as filtration facilities chemical coagulation precipitation ozone decomposition and ultraviolet disinfection and biological treatment methods to remove various contaminants by maximizing the metabolic process of microorganisms in the bioreactor in which activated sludge is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100705271-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned conventional problems due to the electrolysis reaction by the aluminum electrode plate formed so that one cathode plate is disposed between the two anode plates smoothly the flow of electrons and the flow of current flow to the waste water it promotes absorption adsorption precipitation and flotation reactions and agitation and aeration through compressed air inlet promotes el