e 400 and uses a flotation treatment device 512 for the complex oxide material dissolved in the biological treatment device 511 and the pressure decomposition flotation treatment"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a plurality of annular movable partitions installed evenly up and down a rotation mechanism installed in the center of the annular closed chamber to rotate and drive the annular movable partition plate and an annular movable partition installed on the inner wall of the annular closed chamber"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "2 in the present invention a discharge hole is installed in the annular movable partition plate a discharge unit is installed below the discharge hole and the annular movable partition plate rotates to effectively clog the pipe due to organic salt precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the vessel 311 the three annular movable partition plates 312 evenly installed vertically inside the annular closed chamber 310 and the rotating mechanism 31 installed in the center of the annular closed chamber 310 to rotate and drive the annular movable partition plate 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442933-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "after the precipitation in the settling tank l2a b to the decoloration treatment by the electrolytic oxidation treatment and untreated to remove the organic pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101589671-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the sludge contained in the sludge storage tank 20 passes through the barrel straw screen 22 to the oxidation tank 30 connected to the pipe wherein the flocculant comprises 55 to 65 wt of at least one aluminum based inorganic flocculant selected from the group consisting of aluminum polysulfate pass aluminum polychlorinated silicate pacs aluminum polychloride pac and aluminum sulfate alum magnetite magnetite powder ferric chloride fecl 3 ferric chloride ferrous chloride fecl 2 ferrous chloride ferric sulfate fe 2 so 4 3 ferrous sulfate fe 20 to 25 wt of at least one iron salt inorganic coagulant selected from the group consisting of so 4 pfc pfs and polysilicate iron porcelain waste powder and abalone shell 5 to 8 by weight of a precipitate increasing agent obtained by mixing one or more shell powders selected from powder pearl shell powder seashell powder clathrate shell powder carrot shell powder and oyster shell powder and sodium silicate dolomite powder and acetic acid mixed flux enhancers 9 to 16 jidoe comprises a percent by weight wherein the precipitation enhancer is one or more shell powder selected from a ceramic waste powder an abalone shell powder a pearl shell powder a shell crust powder a carrot crust powder and an oyster shell powder at a ratio of 1 0.5 0.8 wherein the flux enhancer is mixed with sodium silicate dolomite powder and acetic acid at a ratio of 1 0.2 0.5 0.05 0.1"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5518246-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "the water storage sterilization container l7 is a treatment tank for temporarily storing the purified circulating water while storing and sterilizing the water with ultraviolet rays"}, {"pat_id": "US-10450211-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "when oxidation does occur depending upon the location where the air is aspirated precipitation of mineral elements from solution can occur which can result in blockage and constriction of conveying pipes or the venture itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323711-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "2004 0026405 process for storing microbial treatment of livestock wastewater high speed decomposition into fine particles while oxidizing by adding oxidant to the stored wastewater after microbial treatment an oxidation treatment step of causing a biological reaction by adding oxygen to the treated water that has undergone the oxidation and high speed decomposition process through stirring injecting a flocculant into the treated water that has undergone the oxidation treatment to agglomerate with sludge separating the sludge generated in the flocculation step precipitating the treated water from which the sludge is separated storing the treated water after the precipitation for sorting a process in which the stored treated water is used as a liquefied fertilizer or it discloses a livestock wastewater treatment apparatus comprising a process that is used for disinfection sterilization sterilization disinfection after contact with the oxygen storage after the classification and storage process generally bioreactor type and type is slightly different however the design of the bioreactor for the treatment of livestock wastewater is carried out using an anaerobic tank in consideration of the high cod and the efficiency of the post treatment in the early stages"}, {"pat_id": "US-9670080-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "such additives are thought to for example facilitate entry into rock formations kill bacteria and reduce the risk of fouling stabilize clay provide well maintenance facilitate proppant entry improve surface pressure provide proppant placement prevent precipitation and reduce fluid tension of the composition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of inflow distribution tank aeration part contact oxidation tank sediment part contact oxidation tank outflow storage tank sludge storage tank and acid pipe and by applying contact oxidation method using contact media in the aeration part and precipitation contact oxidation tank polluted river water and sewage in the apparatus for treating sewage installed on one side of the inflow distribution tank to adjust the level of the treated water flowing from the inlet each movable bank for adjusting the level of the treated water installed and installed on one side of the outlet storage tank perforated perforated walls 7 15 of area formed in the interface between the inlet distribution tank and the aeration contacting tank the interface between the aeration contacting tank and the sludge hopper and the interface between the precipitation contacting oxidation tank and the outflow reservoir a supernatant water storage tank which is formed by trapping the sludge hopper formed in the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration contacting oxidation tank and the precipitation contacting oxidation tank to the sludge storage tank through an air lift and partitioned by an operation full width bank on one side of the sludge storage tank an diffuser installed in the inflow distribution tank and the outflow storage tank to supply dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to the inside of the contact oxidation tank and the treated water discharged while being prevented from being closed by sludge and contact oxidation method further comprises at least one contact medium selected from the group consisting of crushed stone of 30 to 40 of porosity or plastic of 80 or more of porosity in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and precipitation part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the tank continuous or intermittent aeration is to be made and trapezoidal sludge hopper is installed at the front end of the contact oxidation tank of the precipitation section and oxygen is supplied to the inlet distribution tank and the outflow storage tank to supply oxygen and the porosity of the contact media to reduce the size of the facility and to install the air lift facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to achieve the above object as well as other objects that can be easily expressed the present invention applies a contact oxidation method to increase the contact surface of the deeper contaminated river water and sewage or sewage and the contact media to reduce the contamination concentration but as crushed stone"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "air sludge deposited on the wall and the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration portion contact oxidation tank and the precipitation contact oxidation tank transfer to the sludge storage tank through the shaft but one side of the sludge storage tank and the supernatant water storage tank partitioned by the operation of the full width bank installed in the inlet distribution tank and the outflow storage tank and prevented from being closed by the sludge while being discharged from the inside of the contact oxidation tank at least one selected from the group consisting of an acid pipe for supplying dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to water and crushed stone having a porosity of 30 to 40 or plastic having a porosity of 80 or more in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and the settling part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "precipitate contact oxidation tank 4 sludge hopper 5 to collect precipitated sludge outflow reservoir 10 to collect treated effluents outlet 11 to dispose of treated water and precipitation contact oxidation 4 it consists of a sludge storage tank 13 for sedimentation by storing the sludge precipitated in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the precipitation part contact oxidation tank 4 is a contact medium used as a portion where the organic and inorganic substances oxidized in the aeration part contact oxidation tank 3 is precipitated and removed and the lower sludge is used to reduce the volume by the oxidation of microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "also the diffuser 9 sludge removal port 7 and air were installed at the lower part to remove the sludge deposited between the contact media 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "the contact oxidation tank is separated into an aeration contact oxidation tank and a precipitation contact oxidation tank and the aeration contact oxidation tank is always or intermittently aerated and a trapezoidal shape at the front end of the contact contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "to minimize the scale of ozone oxidation a filtration ozone oxidation filtration or conditioning bath may be installed in the form of a precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7345713-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "14 alternately clockwise and counterclockwise the bending rocking plate 211 is rotated at each angle along the reaction plate 210 and the oxidizing agent is sprayed onto the reaction plate through each firing hole 2110 at this time the oxidizing agent sufficiently contacts and reacts with the filler bag 2101 on the outer wall of the reaction plate 210 to produce a liquid containing strong oxidizing sulfuric acid radicals which accumulates in the mixing chamber 21 s3 if it is necessary to treat the wastewater in the complex destruction chamber 20 the second suction pump 3 the liquid containing strongly oxidizing sulfuric acid radicals in the mixing chamber 21 is sucked up into each spray plate 342 through the mixing chamber 44 and uniformly sprayed onto the waste water from each spray port 3420 dissociating the metal ions from the complex state at the same time"}]</data>
</edge>
