  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100621791-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore when the drive cylinder 14 is moved up or down the rotary disc 12 having the cylinder rod 14a eccentrically connected to the rim is a sewage treatment unit as the combined use of the leakage preventing means 90a and 90b described below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100621791-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "by the way the decanter device 1 of the present invention is not used continuously in the actual sewage treatment tank 2 for example in the case of sbr the inflow reaction precipitation and discharge steps are performed with a time difference so that the rotary discharge since the rotation of the body 30 is made intermittently and the rotation speed thereof is not required to be performed quickly and rapidly it may be possible to use the rotational leakage preventing means 90b of the second embodiment as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039115-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "that is in the above mentioned construction method since the water pipe is connected in a long direction in one direction and the supporting force against the lateral pressure is extremely weak the water pipe easily buckles or twists due to the slight ground settlement of the water pipe buried ground there is a problem in that leakage of foreign matter and foreign matter may be generated through the gap"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715823-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "since the conventional conduits 20 21 and 22 are connected by only a simple shear key there is a problem in that there is a lack of unity of segment joining and leakage occurs.thus the present invention has been devised to solve the problems described above if the depth ratio of the precipitation precipitation on the road is small the initial flow rate is minimized by minimizing the deposition of sediment the flow rate for the high flow rate ratio by slowing down avoiding the maximum flow rate the scour is controlled and the section that maximizes the transport flow rate is improved to the oval conduit section by the spiral with the most optimal hydraulic characteristics and the same as the streamlined l shaped port and conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904050-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "4 mixed and removed the chemical reactant in the flocculation paper 5 and the raw water from which the chemical reactant was removed from the flocculation paper 6 and the filter paper 7 sequentially passed through the precipitation and filtration and purified discharge to the drain through the discharge pipe 8 1 the chemical main supply pipe 16 installed in the chemical tank 12 is an area formula for identifying and measuring the flow rate of the discharge valve and the valve v4 for controlling the discharge of the chemical each of the chemical supply branch pipes 19 1 and 19 2 fitted with a flow meter 18 and branched from the chemical main supply pipe 16 is a valve v5 v6 and a solenoid valve sv1 sv2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0372293-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "all of these process water heating systems as well as the thermal disinfection carried out with them require a considerable increase in energy in the form of circulation and leakage losses"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101917676-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "this is because when the medicine is introduced through the chemical distributing tank 300 the chemical is not discharged when the discharge end of the pipe located in the mixed paper is clogged due to precipitation hardening phenomenon by the coagulating agent the water is discharged through the overflow pipe 361 provided on one side of the upper part of the housing 310 and collected in the chemical collection tank 362 provided at the lower end of the housing 310"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "in this example if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation but that there are water levels above a threshold the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200423906-Y1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "since the conventional conduits 20 21 and 22 are connected by only a simple shear key there is a problem in that there is a lack of unity of the segment joining and leakage occurs.therefore the present invention was devised to solve the problems described above and when the depth ratio of precipitation precipitation on the road is small the initial flow rate is increased to minimize the deposition of sediment and the flow rate is increased for the flow rate with a high depth ratio"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100994248-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "as a result leakage of water is prevented from occurring during the precipitation of the treated water"}]</data>
</edge>
