  <data key="d4">["thereby", "induce", "due to", "inhibit", "to prevent", "reduce", "limited in", "effect of", "may", "can result in"]</data>
  <data key="d5">["layer", "membrane", "venture", "rise", "cooling", "bcro", "part", "tank", "addition", "concentration", "order", "solid", "agent", "winter", "corrosion", "zone", "osmosis", "phosphate", "iron", "aperture", "deposition", "pipe", "effect", "pump", "growth", "object", "element", "preheating", "blockage", "stage", "exchanger", "reaction", "scale", "load", "water", "possibility", "slurry", "sludge", "oxidation", "process", "fig", "filtration", "plate", "solution", "constriction", "substance", "system", "weather", "surface", "reverse", "area", "treatment", "matter", "source", "occurrence", "state", "wall", "separation", "piping", "contamination", "method", "word", "removal", "location", "adhesion", "temperature", "accumulation", "weight", "mineral", "precipitation", "invention", "device", "side", "condensate", "air", "material", "heat", "problem", "case", "waste", "ph", "liquid", "damage", "reactor", "deformation", "heater", "efficiency"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["contain", "aspirate", "administer", "recover", "set", "treat", "provide", "exhibit", "prevent", "neutralize", "use", "inhibit", "become", "dissolve", "eliminate", "ensure", "accord", "remain", "convey", "result", "lead", "require", "induce", "heat", "suspend", "limit", "remove", "have", "occur", "show", "reduce", "depend", "would", "may", "weaken", "melt", "precipitate", "can", "do", "be", "cool", "decompose", "start", "adjust", "will", "generate"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100755486-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "this may eventually have the effect of preventing the occurrence of chemical precipitation to prevent the blockage of the membrane aperture"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4521319-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in this case it is possible to set the iron phosphate so as to be in a dissolved state by adjusting the ph but there is a possibility that precipitation may occur little by little in the piping or the like due to the rise in temperature or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition due to the neutralizing agent generally administered to inhibit corrosion the problem of precipitation of inorganic substances in the preheating of the waste liquid the reaction of the organic matter and the cooling of the treated water becomes more serious.accordingly an object of the present invention is to oxidatively decompose an organic matter containing waste liquid using a supercritical water oxidation method which can prevent the blockage by corrosion and precipitation of inorganic substances in the waste heater the reactor and the heat exchanger during the supercritical water oxidation treatment of the organic matter containing waste liquid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "however if the temperature of the wall surface is lower than the precipitation temperature of the inorganic material even if the growth starts on the wall surface the precipitated inorganic material starts to melt again weakening the adhesion of the inorganic material and thus the growth of the inorganic material is limited in the present invention as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "also the air cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3794589-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in the upper layer part from the slurry zone a large separation area is required in order to reduce the area load for precipitation separation of the remaining suspended substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358379-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "accordingly it is possible to prevent the accumulation of sludge thereby eliminating the blockage and to prevent damage or deformation of the inclined plate 12 due to the weight of the sludge thereby exhibiting a high inherent sludge removal efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102778291-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "in other words according to the present invention by having a system capable of continuously recovering the sensible heat of the condensate treated water generated in the s3 stage through a heat exchanger system 132 pipe blockage and scale contamination through cooling precipitation that may occur in the secondary reverse osmosis membrane filtration process bcro in the s2 stage can be effectively reduced or prevented even in winter or extremely cold weather without a separate additional heat source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102778291-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "specifically the heat exchanger system 132 can be provided to recover the sensible heat of the condensate generated in the crystallizer 131 as a heat source for the hot side of the pre heater thereby preventing pipe blockage through cooling precipitation and scale contamination of the high concentration concentrated reverse osmosis membrane filtration process even in winter or extremely cold weather without a separate heat source"}, {"pat_id": "US-10450211-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "when oxidation does occur depending upon the location where the air is aspirated precipitation of mineral elements from solution can occur which can result in blockage and constriction of conveying pipes or the venture itself"}, {"pat_id": "US-5776333-A", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "also the air cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the conventional internal conveying pipe and an anoxic tank conveying pump are removed to eliminate the blockage of the device and the pipe due to the sludge s deposition"}]</data>
</edge>
