  <data key="d6">["receive", "subject", "make", "treat", "solve", "take", "connect", "extract", "float", "introduce", "accord", "fasten", "increase", "maximize", "have", "return", "accommodate", "reinforce", "fix", "wash", "instal", "flow", "precipitate", "can", "relate", "will", "pump", "provide", "come", "contain", "compare", "prevent", "load", "correspond", "describe", "form", "divide", "nitrify", "process", "suspend", "filter", "pass", "follow", "fill", "mix", "compress", "fluidize", "protect", "settle", "lower", "understand", "rectify", "purify", "collect", "penetrate", "mount", "pip", "oxidize", "allow", "convey", "locate", "devise", "induce", "seat", "remove", "cover", "surround", "reduce", "dehydrate", "may", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "separate", "incline", "include", "perform", "consist", "block", "mean", "supply", "use", "basin", "define", "cut", "depart", "rotate", "maintain", "inlet", "improve", "control", "drain", "sediment", "characterize", "exist", "be", "adjust", "flood", "link", "generate", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101385841-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "therefore the treated water discharge device 300 of the present invention can completely block the mixed liquid and solids from flowing into the apparatus in the stirring aeration and settling steps"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102404514-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "therefore in the following description it will be described from the stage after the secondary settling tank 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200408180-Y1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "therefore the raw water supplied from the raw water treatment tank 2 passes through the mixing tank 4 the coagulation tank 6 and the settling tank 8 and then flows into the separation membrane system 10 in a treated state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101863695-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in addition in the primary clarifier the flotation separation the precipitation separation and the filtration process are performed at the same time thereby reducing the volume of the device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100288083-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "wherein the filter medium k1 k2 k3 in the form of a plate horizontal or vertical or block in the form of a fixed or fluidized bed to increase the activity and denitrification efficiency of the microorganism through the flow through the weir 33 the wastewater which has passed to the aerobic tank 50 is nitrified by ammonia by the acid pipe 54 installed in the lower part while passing through the filter media k4 k5 and k6 and organic matter is removed and excess by the microorganism of phosphorus intake takes place"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200267142-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a second aeration step for oxidizing contaminants such as organic matter ammonia nitrogen and the like while improving the sludge settling property of the sedimentation basin 50 after the second aeration step in the final sedimentation basin 50 separating the supernatant liquid and sludge purification by liquid separation comprising a precipitation step of discharging and the denitrification step after the organic materials similar to remove the nutrients at the same time a 2 o anaerobic aonxic oxic system at the same time part of the sludge precipitated and discharged in the precipitation step is returned to maintain the microbial residence time srt so that the total denitrification step can be performed and the aeration tank effluent from the first aeration step is returned to the bioreactor 1 before the first aeration step is characterized in that it comprises a biological reaction step of denitrifying from the influent source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100513428-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the struvite crystallization tank 2 in which crystal precipitation takes place and the struvite storage tank 8 connected to the lower part of the struvite crystallization tank 2 and extracting and storing the struvite crystals and the struvite crystals an aerobic reactor 3 in which the wastewater passed through the media 10 separated from the anaerobic reactor 1 through the separator 7 and passed through the struvite crystallization tank 2 is mixed is subsequent to the ready made reaction tank 3 subjected to solid liquid separation to induce the precipitation of the desorbed microorganisms and suspended a block consisting of some microorganisms in the anaerobic settling tank 4 comprising a feed pipe for returning to the reaction tank 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368638-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "conventional ion water treatment device uses a zinc block forming a sacrificial anode inside a brass body and a fluorine resin block which generates potential electrostatic charges to induce the precipitation of harmful substances contained in the fluid by installing a fluid flow therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100866373-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "1 the sewage treatment system 10 may include a pretreatment unit 20 a primary precipitation means 30 a biological reaction tank 40 and a secondary precipitation means 50"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4444366-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "a work hole communicating in a vertical direction is provided by the skeleton block partly cut out and the reinforcing plate partly cut out a partition wall is provided so as to surround the precipitation tank and the precipitation tank and the size of the skeleton block provided in the water reservoir may be the same"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4444366-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "the inner plate 34 has a length corresponding to one pitch of the skeleton block 1 from the side plate 33 but may be a half pitch and the length is not limited"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101094321-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "s100 screen precipitation process s200 stationary precipitation process s300 continuous filtration process s400 soil improvement process 10 10 pressure pump 20 pressure filtration tank 21 inlet 23 outlet 24 discharge pipe 25 float discharge outlet 26 screw 27 closed tube 30 filter 31 filter hole 40 floating material removal means 41 wing anchor 42 wing to remove the float 43 rotation device 44 rotating shaft 45 guide rail 46 guide block 51 injection nozzle 52 fastening portion 53 injection nozzle guide 54 inline transfer pipe 55 inline coupler 56 inline coupler inlet 57 pivot shaft inlet 60 reflux blocking plate 61 vibration generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101169026-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore the raw water supplied from the raw water storage tank a1 flows through the mixing tank a2 the coagulation tank a3 and the settling tank a4 and then flows into the separation membrane a5 in a treated state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102373416-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "buffer storage facility control device and its control methodthe present invention relates to a buffer storage facility control device and more particularly it has a function to block direct inflow of accidental runoff water into a buffer storage facility and to reduce non point pollution during precipitation and link them with the sluice gate of the buffer storage facility according to the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102373416-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since only a sluice gate is installed in the conventional storage facility this function cannot be performed properly so there is a problem in that the purification treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant cannot be accurately improved and the pollution of the river cannot be prevented.the purpose of the present invention which was devised in view of the above is to block the direct inflow of accidental runoff water into the buffer storage facility and to reduce non point pollution during precipitation and to link them with the sluice gate of the buffer storage facility so that the sluice gate can be installed according to the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978238-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a base layer 300 of rainwater permeable material one or more purification tanks 100 which are seated on the upper surface of the base layer 300 to primarily purify the impurities in the rainwater and to purify the firstly purified rainwater by primary treatment located on the upper surface of the base layer 300 and connected to each of the purification tank 100 of the one or more purification tank 100 includes one or more double drain pipe 200 to induce inflow and drainage of rain water the purification tank 100 a water collecting tank 10 having a drainage hole 12 and a permeation hole 14 formed on one upper surface or both sides and one lower surface of the base layer 300 to allow inflow and drainage of rainwater the precipitation box is formed to be accommodated in the inner portion of the sump 10 so that the rain water is introduced from the top to drain through the first through hole 32 formed on one surface of the sedimentation box for the primary purification of the impurities 30 and it is adjacent to the sedimentation box 30 by being accommodated in another portion of the sump 10 the secondary purified rainwater in the sedimentation box 30 drained from the first through hole 32 the filter medium 50 is filled therein to be cleanable and the filter box 50 for draining the secondary purified rainwater to the double drain pipe 200 through the second through hole 52a formed at the side thereof consists of a cover 70 provided to cover the upper portion of the sump 10 the double drain pipe 200 rain water purified secondly from the filter box 50 of the purification tank 100 through the water permeable hole 14 connected to the second through hole 52a can penetrate into the base layer 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978238-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "an object of the present invention the base layer 300 of the rain water can penetrate one or more purification tanks 100 which are seated on the upper surface of the base layer 300 to primarily purify the impurities in the rainwater and to purify the firstly purified rainwater by primary treatment located on the upper surface of the base layer 300 and connected to each of the purification tank 100 of the one or more purification tank 100 includes one or more double drain pipe 200 to induce the inflow and drainage of rain water the purification tank 100 is mounted on the upper surface of the base layer 300 the sump and drain holes 12 and the water permeable hole 14 is formed in the upper one side or both sides and the lower one side to allow the inflow and drainage of rain water respectively 10 and is formed to be accommodated in the inner portion of the water collecting tank 10 the rain is introduced from the top to drain through the first through hole 32 formed on one surface to process the impurities first and primary the sedimentation box 30 to be purified and the sedimentation box 30 adjacent to the sedimentation box 30 by being accommodated in another part of the water collecting tank 10 and drained from the first through hole 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052855-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to control the discharge level of the treated wastewater and to selectively block the supply of microbubbles inside the separation tank to use the separation tank as a sedimentation tank but to induce precipitation in the vertical direction or inclined direction downward to maximize the precipitation efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052855-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "another object of the technology according to the present invention is to allow the sedimentation or flotation of the sludge in the sedimentation tank in which the microbubble is supplied to be selectively made while controlling the discharge level of the sewage recovery or flotation wastewater treated slant plate the unit is rotatable to be selectively inclined at a predetermined angle from the vertical direction to selectively block the supply of microbubbles inside the sedimentation tank so that the sedimentation tank is selectively used as the sedimentation tank but the sedimentation is performed in the vertical or inclined direction downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052855-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "fourth while allowing the sludge settling or flotation inside the sedimentation tank in which the microbubbles are supplied it is possible to adjust the discharge level of sewage recovery or flotation recovery wastewater while the inclined plate unit is selectively fixed from the vertical direction it is rotatable to be inclined at an angle to selectively block the supply of microbubbles inside the sedimentation tank so that the sedimentation tank can be selectively used only as the sedimentation tank but the sedimentation can be maximized by inducing precipitation in the vertical or inclined direction downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101725047-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes in form and details may be made therein without departing from the spirit and scope of the invention as defined by the appended claims.1000 non point pollution source treatment device according to the present invention 10 first piping 20 second piping 30 third piping 40 fourth piping 110 pretreatment tank 120 rectifying screen 130 140 temporary storage 210 filtration tank 220 221 filter block 222 first filter paper 222 1 1st pier 223 second material pier 223 1 2nd pier 310 backwater tank 410 first drainage pump 420 second drainage pump 430 backwash pump 500 510 blower 520 inlet pipe 530 communicator 540 distributor 550 partition plate 551 split hole 560 spiral shaft 570 transfer pipe 580 inner wall 600 purified water sprayer 610 connector 620 injection nozzle 621 injection hole 630 injection filter s1 precipitation space s2 storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100791896-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "therefore the raw water supplied from the raw water treatment tank 2 passes through the mixing tank 4 the coagulation tank 6 and the settling tank 8 and then flows into the separation membrane system 10 in a treated state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the present invention by installing a sedimentation basin is divided into a predetermined size in the sewer and coriander site sedimented pollutants and sludge flowing along the stream to block the flow of the stream compartmentally and then easily sediment first to protect the water quality of rivers and lakes second to prevent the destruction of aquatic ecosystems due to the inflow of soils and sands third to prevent aesthetic and sanitary defects due to sedimentation of soil and journey during rainfall and flooding fourthly the dredging operation is very effective and economical compared to the existing method is to provide a stream water purification apparatus by precipitation and dredging and its method"}]</data>
</edge>
