  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200171293-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "at this time since the amount of water is small so that you do not have to worry about inflow of the earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking the sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing the cross sectional area of the drainage pipe and preventing the burnout of the sewage terminal treatment plant while reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101908319-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow rate adjusting tank 10 for adjusting the discharge amount according to an inflow amount of the incoming wastewater a bioreactor 20 including a semi tank 21 functioning as an anaerobic tank and an anoxic tank according to time and a sludge buffer tank 23 having a microorganism incubator 24 a raw water transfer system 14 for transferring the wastewater introduced into the flow rate adjusting tank 10 to the semi furnace and first and second batch reactors 30a 30b connected in series with the semi bath 21 and continuously treating the organic substance and nitrogen oxide to discharge the treated water and arranged in parallel with each other first and second inflow transportation systems 25a 25b for transferring wastewater between the semi bath 21 and the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a 30b first and second sludge transfer systems 40a 40b for transferring the sludge collected from the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a 30b to the semi tank 21 and the sludge buffer tank 23 a microorganism conveyance system 45 for conveying the positively ignited microorganisms from the sludge buffer tank 23 to the first and the first batch reaction vessels 30a and 30b and and a control panel 50 for performing overall control for advanced treatment of the wastewater first and second batch reactor tank inflow valves 26a and 26b installed in the first and second inflow transfer systems 25a and 25b first and second sludge drawing pumps 41a and 41b installed in the first and second sludge transfer systems 40a and 40b for drawing sludge from the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a and 30b and first and second microbial distribution tanks 42a and 42b for transferring the sludge drawn through the first and second sludge drawing pumps 41a and 41b to the semi tank 21 and the sludge buffer tank 23 the control panel 50 controls the balance of the sludge microorganism amount while the first and second batch reaction tanks 30a and 30b are operated and the amount of microorganisms necessary for interlocking with the influent load the first and second sludge discharge pumps 41a and 41b are controlled so that the first and second sludge discharge pumps 41a the first and second microorganism distribution tanks 42a and 42b are connected to a maintenance air line to prevent solidification of the v shaped grooves with graduations so as to be measurable and solidification of the remaining sludge under extremely low load"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654508-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the precipitation inducing grooves 511 are formed so as to be curved downwardly inclined so as to reach one upper end portion the precipitation inducing groove 511 is formed at a predetermined distance from the upper end of one side of the swash plate 510 and the upper end of one side of the lower flat plate portion toward the other side upper end portion of the lower flat plate portion and curved downward and a plurality of depressions are formed in an inclined shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654508-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "second the upper swash plate unit and the lower swash plate unit are provided and the lower swash plate unit is selectively rotatable such that the lower swash plate unit is inclined at a predetermined angle with respect to the upper end in the vertical state thereby selectively blocking the supply of the minute bubbles into the precipitation the sludge can be guided in an oblique direction to induce sedimentation thereby maximizing the sedimentation efficiency of the sludge.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102155071-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "sedimentation tank consisting of an external sedimentation tank configured to be made a water level sensing unit for sensing the level of the treated water introduced from the sedimentation tank an elevating means configured therein and configured to perform an elevating operation and coupled to the elevating means collecting the introduced treated water a collection means a water quality inspection unit that inspects the water quality of the treated water collected through the collection means a recovery line for recovering effluent water having an unsuitable water quality test result to the sedimentation tank and re inflow of the treated water reprocessed from the sedimentation tank a first discharge tank including a re inflow line to make it a second discharge tank including a plurality of discharge units connected to the first discharge tank and a discharge opening closing door configured to be configured with the plurality of discharge units and operated so that only discharged water having a suitable water quality test result is introduced the water level information of the treated water is received from the water level detection unit and when the water level is higher than a certain level the lifting and lowering operation of the elevating means is controlled and the water quality test result is received from the water quality inspection unit and the recovery line and the discharge opening and closing door are includes a driving control unit for controlling the driving and controlling whether or not the re inflow line is opened so that the re inflow of the reprocessed treated water is made and the elevating means it is configured on one side of the water quality inspection unit and when a driving signal is transmitted from the driving control unit a transfer driving unit that provides a predetermined power to perform an elevating and descending operation and the collecting means are coupled and connected to the transfer driving unit consisting of a transfer member for transferring the collecting means while lifting or lowering operation is performed when the transfer driving unit is driven in the first discharge tank a seating panel whose one end is fixedly coupled to an outer surface of the elevating means and a rotating panel rotatably coupled to the front end of the seating panel and configured to rotate vertically upward when the elevating means is moved upward and the a drive cylinder for controlling the rotation of the rotation panel and a drive control sensor that is interlocked by contact with the water quality inspection unit and receives a drive signal from the drive control unit to control the drive of the drive cylinder and the drive control unit a signal transmission unit configured to perform a water quality inspection while driving the water quality inspection unit only when the water quality inspection unit and the drive control sensor contact each other under the control of effluent water inspection device for a wastewater treatment facility comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102155071-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention for achieving such a problem it is configured to precipitate and transport the treated water introduced from the aeration tank and to perform reprocessing by secondary precipitation of the effluent that does not meet the water quality discharge standard"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "at this time since the amount of water is small so that you do not have to worry about inflow of the earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking the sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing the cross sectional area of the drainage pipe and preventing the burnout of the sewage terminal treatment plant while reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101004287-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the filtration chamber is formed in the center and the precipitation chamber and the aggregation chamber is provided with a main body formed sequentially on the outside of the filtration chamber the agglomeration chamber is it is formed to be supplied to the bottom of the settling chamber through the vertical flow path is formed in the outer side of the settling chamber formed through the inlet formed in the upper portion flowing downwards a plurality of baffle plates in the agglomeration chamber the plurality of obstruction plates being spaced apart from each other in the vertical direction to move along the passage formed in a zigzag shape a lifting wire having one end fixed to the baffle plate positioned at the lowest end and fixed to a fixing unit installed at the upper portion of the main body through a through hole formed in the baffle plate positioned at an upper portion thereof and and a weight member connected to a lower portion of the baffle plate positioned at the lowest end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052855-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "fourth while allowing the sludge settling or flotation inside the sedimentation tank in which the microbubbles are supplied it is possible to adjust the discharge level of sewage recovery or flotation recovery wastewater while the inclined plate unit is selectively fixed from the vertical direction it is rotatable to be inclined at an angle to selectively block the supply of microbubbles inside the sedimentation tank so that the sedimentation tank can be selectively used only as the sedimentation tank but the sedimentation can be maximized by inducing precipitation in the vertical or inclined direction downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200234791-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in this case the amount is small so when you do not have to worry about the inflow of earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing cross sectional area reduction of the drainage pipe and burning of the pump in the sewage treatment plant and reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in order to achieve the object of the present invention as described above an integrated contaminant processing apparatus according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention has an inlet formed on one side the inlet chamber is formed to open the other side a precipitation chamber installed at an open portion of the inflow chamber having a discharge port formed on the other side a overflowware installed on the inner side corresponding to the discharge port and a sedimentation hopper formed to be inclined at a lower portion thereof a coarse contaminant processing unit having a fixed screen mounted inclined inside the inflow chamber corresponding to the inlet and filtering coarse contaminants it is installed inclined to the inner side of the inlet chamber to the rear side of the fixed screen and having a vibration damping main body having a wedge bar screen a chain having a plurality of rakes for lifting the impurities caught in the wedge bar screen and a chain drive unit for driving the chain a miscellaneous matter processing unit comprising a a settling discharge unit for discharging sand settled to the inner lower portion of the settling chamber to the outside it is characterized by including"}]</data>
</edge>
