  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102404514-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "it is preferable to have a stirring facility in the ph adjusting liquid input unit 130 and the crystallization chemical input unit 140 to prevent coagulation or precipitation of the drug and materials with excellent alkali resistance corrosion resistance and durability are used for chemicals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100983829-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a wastewater treatment method for treating wastewater containing organic substances via an input tank a methane fermentation tank a fermentation filtrate collection tank a measuring tank an aeration tank a precipitation tank a distribution tank a culture tank a sludge storage tank and a treatment tank a stirrer is installed in the input tank to agitate the corrosive reaction and the activated silicate having completed the corrosive reaction returned from the raw water and the culture tank to activate the corrosive reaction introducing the raw water which has undergone the corrosion reaction from the charging tank into a methane fermentation tank to proceed with fermentation by methane from the methane fermentation tank the fermentation complete digestion liquid is introduced into the fermentation filtrate collection tank and in a state in which the fermentation filtrate collection tank is introduced into the metering tank a predetermined amount of digestion liquid is introduced into the aeration tank and the remaining amount is returned to the fermentation filtrate collection tank to the aeration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200317348-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the economic loss was inevitably large compared to the cost.therefore the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and by increasing the flow rate of the constant and water reducing the exposure time of the inner wall of the water pipe from the corrosives that activate the corrosion sediment contained in the constant and water its purpose is to provide a structure of water supply pipes with increased drainage which can minimize the likelihood of precipitation and economically realize the above effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "supercritical heat exchanger to recover in the supercritical water with little corrosion and to install the quenching mixture to prevent corrosion and precipitation of inorganic substances in the cooling process of the treated water to secure the stability and continuous operation of the supercritical water oxidation process it was"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in particular it is difficult to prevent corrosion in some subcritical sections under aerobic formation formed near the reactor inlet of the waste liquid preheated to subcritical temperature in order to prevent the precipitation of inorganic materials and to prevent the precipitation of inorganic materials during the discharge of treated water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition due to the neutralizing agent generally administered to inhibit corrosion the problem of precipitation of inorganic substances in the preheating of the waste liquid the reaction of the organic matter and the cooling of the treated water becomes more serious.accordingly an object of the present invention is to oxidatively decompose an organic matter containing waste liquid using a supercritical water oxidation method which can prevent the blockage by corrosion and precipitation of inorganic substances in the waste heater the reactor and the heat exchanger during the supercritical water oxidation treatment of the organic matter containing waste liquid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition by improving the supercritical water oxidation process which consumes a large amount of energy to prevent the precipitation of inorganic substances supercritical heat exchanger and quenching mixer are installed to prevent corrosion of the treated water and precipitation of inorganic substances and to save energy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "there is no formation of critical temperature zones which can suppress corrosion and the linear velocity several times faster than subcritical conditions greatly reduces the likelihood of precipitation of inorganic materials and maintains the supercritical temperature from the inlet of the reactor to increase organic decomposition effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in order to prevent corrosion generated during the preheating of the organic matter containing waste liquid an appropriate neutralizing agent is added to the waste liquid and preheated under anoxic conditions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "it is effective in preventing clogging caused by corrosion and supercritical water oxidation process which consumes a large amount of energy is installed to prevent the precipitation of inorganic materials and supercritical heat exchangers and quenching mixers are installed to prevent corrosion of the treated water and precipitation of inorganic materials"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920462-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sediment equipment with inclined plates for water treatment the present invention relates to an inclined plate sedimentation system for water treatment and in more detail to improve the structure of the inclined plate continuously installed in the sedimentation basin and to install the guide plate for guiding the water flow in the sedimentation basin to be treated the inclined plate therefore there is a feature that the precipitation of the solid content as it flows upward and the slope plate is simple and light structure simple to manufacture and installation and relates to the water treatment slope plate precipitation equipment is eliminated the concern of corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920462-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the present invention relates to an inclined plate sedimentation system for water treatment and in more detail to improve the structure of the inclined plate continuously installed in the sedimentation basin and to install the guide plate for guiding the water flow in the sedimentation basin to be treated the inclined plate therefore there is a feature that the precipitation of the solid content as it flows upward and the slope plate is simple and light structure simple to manufacture and installation and relates to the water treatment slope plate precipitation equipment is eliminated the concern of corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "US-5683748-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the slurry coating adheres well to the crown of the concrete pipe and maintains a ph level of about 10 at the surface of the crown for an extended period of time to prevent the corrosive effects of the sulfuric acid generated by the sewage within the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100992912-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "filtering and immersing the corrosion reactor 62 to convert the solids into corrosion precursor material and to send to the distribution tank 70 wherein the step 6 is the corrosion precursor material converted in the culture separation tank 60 is distributed in the appropriate amount in the distribution tank 70 and conveyed to the flow control tank 10 and the biological reaction tank 30 and the biological reaction tank 30 is equipped with mlss monitoring device 31 is suspended solids constant if the concentration is exceeded the aeration is stopped and the sludge is settled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0611437-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "in those systems treating agents may be lost through chemical microbial degradation precipitation corrosion processes system leaks and low level emissions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100888713-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the installation beam 31 may use an frp beam that is resistant to corrosion and has high strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315306-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "corrosion of the pipelines leads to a reduction in the service life of the pipeline and a decrease in water supply capacity resulting in economic losses by increasing the load of the pump and also causing consumer complaints and complaints due to deterioration of water quality due to corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101791441-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in addition the aqueous solution of ascorbic acid is remarkably lower in corrosion occurrence than the sodium thiosulfate and precipitation of aqueous ascorbic acid is in the form of powder so that there is little phenomenon such as a pipe wall"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0372293-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "all of these process water heating systems as well as the thermal disinfection carried out with them require a considerable increase in energy in the form of circulation and leakage losses"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100480807-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "as described above according to the filter applied slaked lime input device the slaked lime input method and the purified water treatment method using the same according to the present invention it is possible to quantitative injection of slaked lime to maintain the proper alkalinity of the raw water so that the efficiency and stability of coagulation and precipitation of raw water it is possible to effectively prevent the water drainage caused by the excessive injection of slaked lime to prevent sludge increase and to settle the sedimentation basin and its downstream and to maintain the proper alkalinity of purified water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in the present invention corrosion in a heat exchanger of a high heat load device can be suppressed while preventing problems such as precipitation of calcium carbonate due to slaked lime input and cost increase due to chemical input"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978238-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "here the box 52 of the filter box 50 is preferably made of a synthetic resin series such as polyethylene so as to prevent corrosion and contaminate rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978238-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the filter box 50 is embedded in the water collecting tank 10 to be in close contact with or adjacent to the side surface of the through hole 52a of the sedimentation box 30 and is made of synthetic resin series such as polyethylene material to prevent corrosion and contaminate rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "US-5413718-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "then as a second step the oxygen contained in the surface water must be removed to prevent iron precipitation and corrosion of iron and steel components in the processing equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and converting the heavy metal into a corrosion precursor which is insoluble in water by a biological corrosion reaction and sends it to the primary precipitation tank 5a to precipitate and remove the solid material and then to the primary treatment tank 13 and then to the primary precipitation tank 5a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "activated humic substances and active minerals in the form of mineral complexes of chelate peroxyfulvic acid which have a catalytic function that promotes the corrosive reactions that convert into macromolecular substances oxidation reduction potential orp value is supplied to the culture tanks 8a b and the sump tank 1 by supplying a large amount of rhyolite or dacite like pumice and oxidation water of the oxidizing tank 15 corrosion of organic contaminants and heavy metals in wastewater by supplying aeration tanks 3a b with microorganisms cultured at 350mv to promote the activation of corrosive microorganisms and microorganisms that have mutual symbiosis with these microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "in the primary aeration tank 3a when organic pollutants and heavy metals in the waste water are converted into corrosion precursors that are insoluble in water by biological corrosion reactions they are sent to the primary precipitation tank 5a to remove the corrosion precursors and microorganisms that exist in the solid state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938463-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition the electrolytic treatment method is to crush manure and the like and to pass them through the electrode plate with a narrow gap between each other so that the decomposition and oxidation occurs by electricity not only is not easy to crush but also generated during electrolysis of seawater due to the strong oxidizing power of hypochlorous acid hclo 3 corrosion of the structure is easy and the treated water may contain excessive hypochlorous acid which may cause secondary pollution.the present invention was created in order to solve the above problems the object of the present invention is the wastewater by purifying various wastewater including manure generated in the vessel through four steps of microbial decomposition precipitation adsorption filtration and biodegradation disinfection it has good treatment capacity and it is easy to utilize the space of vessels where various equipments are concentrated and it is easy to maintain and adapt to load change or temperature change of waste water and also biochemical sewage treatment for ship that can minimize the sludge generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102478346-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in more detail the decontamination method for removing the radioactively contaminated oxide film of the present invention can be applied to system decontamination of a heavy water nuclear power plant nuclear power plant made of carbon steel for example a sulfuric acid h 2 so 4 hydrazine n 2 h 4 and copper sulfate cuso 4 dissolving the corrosion oxide film by using decontamination process water in which a decontamination agent containing copper sulfate cuso 4 is introduced into process water of a pipeline system b performing a precipitation reaction by mixing ba oh 2 with the decontamination process water in which the corrosion oxide film is decontaminated and c removing insoluble substances by separating the decontamination process water that has undergone the precipitation reaction into solid and liquid to remove insoluble substances as one cycle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0139147-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "therefore the present invention has been devised to improve the problem of the flocculation apparatus of the sedimentation tank according to the prior art so that the agglomerates attached to the wall surface of the sedimentation tank can be easily removed by means of a separate wall aggregate removal means on the central axis of the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "another aspect of the present invention is to remove the ss by the organic coagulant only in the first dehydrator and the inorganic coagulant in the chemical coagulation sedimentation filtration device having a second removal of the desorption solution with the flocculation reaction tank and the precipitation unit and the filter unit after flocculation using organic coagulant the sedimentary solids are removed from the sediment and the suspended solids are removed from the filter reducing the amount of inorganic coagulant and reducing the size of subsequent process equipment and civil structures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "naturally it belongs to the scope of the invention.100 multi purpose thermostat 120 liquid corrosion tank 121 aerobic generation 125 diffuser 127 air inlet 128 air outlet 130 cooling tank 131 intake port 132 exhaust port 141 air supply fan 142 exhaust fan 150 wastewater injection unit 153 conical dispersion induction member 154 wastewater outlet 156 wastewater supply pipe 157 liquid circulation pump 170 shatterproof device 171 inlet 172 outlet 174 scattering prevention device body 176 178 plate 179 slope 182 flushing pump 184 flushing piping 185 chemical pump 187 chemical piping 300 chemical flocculation precipitation filter 320 flocculation reactor 340 sedimentation unit 342 sludge collector 343 treated water outlet 345 pressure sensor 347 rectifying plate 349 sludge discharge pump 350 filter unit 352 filter unit frame 352a round border 352b spokes 354 filtration cell 357 rotary drive shaft 361 wash water nozzle 362 wash water pump 363 wash water receiver 365 wash water discharge pipe 367 electric valve 371 control panel 373 sump tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442932-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention has a high concentration of organic wastewater such as livestock wastewater manure landfill leachate food processing plant discharge wastewater aquatic product plant wastewater slaughterhouse wastewater food waste leachate and dehydration filtrate while having its own oxidation function in the corrosive substances catalytic function of deodorization minerals supply to animals and plants including microorganisms and catalyst function to promote the corrosive reaction which converts organic materials into water insoluble and non volatile stable macromolecular substances"}, {"pat_id": "US-9670080-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "such additives are thought to for example facilitate entry into rock formations kill bacteria and reduce the risk of fouling stabilize clay provide well maintenance facilitate proppant entry improve surface pressure provide proppant placement prevent precipitation and reduce fluid tension of the composition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100885204-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "at this time to prevent corrosion in the b s system and piping if a certain water quality 3 000 ppm of chlorine ion concentration is over a certain amount is blown down from the storage tank and supplemented by the quantity discharged to the replenishment water fresh water"}]</data>
