  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101923165-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a color conversion unit 44 for converting the filtered ultrasonic signal into a color to visually check the state of the interface using the difference between the intensity and the intensity of the filtered ultrasound signal the interface state is displayed in color by the color conversion unit 44 the concentration value of the sludge at a specific position by the color difference is calculated and the sludge average concentration from the upper part of the sedimentation tank and the concentration tank 8 to the lower sludge the sludge concentration calculating unit 48 calculates the sludge concentration at the present interface by checking the state and concentration of the interface by the sludge concentration calculating unit 48 and a check valve operation part 46 for comparing the value with a concentration value determined to require a predetermined sludge drawing and automatically drawing the sludge the interfacial measurement filtering unit 42 previously sets a frequency signal value serving as a reference for interfacial height measurement among the frequencies reflected on the medium in order to set the measurement range in advance at the interface measurement at the place where the interface system 2 is installed an interfacial scanning unit 42 for scanning the ultrasonic frequency information transmitted and received through the detector 6 in a graphical form and an interfacial scanning unit 42 for interfacing the frequency signal values previously set by the initial setting unit 50 a matching unit 54 for comparing frequency measurement values through the state scanning unit 52 and a scraper 54 for collecting sludge at the bottom of the settling tank and thickener 8 while comparing the frequencies of ultrasonic waves by the matching unit 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102457723-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage treatment facility management system for checking the situation of a sewage treatment facility located in a remote place in real time the sewage treatment facility management system a sewage treatment facility unit configured to aerate the incoming sewage to separate the sludge from the treated water to discharge the treated water and a facility management unit that receives the facility status of the sewage treatment facility unit in real time and provides it to the central management server unit and to receive and store real time status information of the sewage treatment facility unit from the facility management unit compare the stored information with preset information store the failure information provided in real time and learn and analyze the stored information to detect the lifespan of the sewage treatment facility unit and a central management server unit that transmits control information of the sewage treatment facility unit to the facility management unit so that the sewage treatment facility can be managed according to the input information and it consists of a manager terminal for the manager to check real time status information from the central management server unit the sewage treatment facility department a sewage treatment module configured to treat and discharge the incoming sewage and a facility condition detection module formed on one side of the sewage treatment module to detect the flow rate noise vibration load and water level generated by the sewage treatment module it consists of a facility driving module formed on one side of the sewage treatment module to receive control information from the facility management unit and provide information to the sewage treatment module and the facility condition detection module the sewage treatment module a sewage inlet formed on one side of the sewage treatment module so that either sewage or sewage from the outside flows into the flow storage tank a flow storage tank formed on one side of the sewage treatment module to store either sewage or sewage flowing in through the sewage inlet an aeration tank formed on one side of the flow storage tank to aerate by injecting air into either sewage or sewage that overflows from the flow storage tank and moves a sludge precipitation tank formed on one side of the aeration tank so that the aeration overflows the bulkhead and the sludge settles toward the bottom a treated water discharge port formed on the other side of the upper side of the sewage treatment module so that the treated water formed at the upper part of the sludge settling tank can be discharged to the outside it consists of a bulkhead formed between the flow storage tank and the aeration tank and between the aeration tank and the sludge settling tank so that sewage and treated water overflow according to the water level the facility state detection module an air flow sensor formed on a bulkhead on one side of the aeration tank to detect the flow rate of air supplied to the aeration tank a sewage flow sensor formed on one side of the sewage inlet to detect the amount of sewage flowing in through the sewage inlet a noise sensor formed on one side of the upper part of the sewage treatment module to detect noise generated from the sewage treatment module a vibration sensor formed on one side of the upper part of the sewage treatment module to detect vibrations generated from the sewage treatment module a load detection sensor formed on one side of the treated water outlet to detect the load discharged when the treated water is discharged it consists of a water level sensor formed on the bulkhead of one side of the flow storage tank to detect the water level of either sewage or sewage stored in the flow storage tank the facility driving module is sensing information formed on the upper side of the sewage treatment module to provide real time status information provided from the facility condition detection module to the real time transmission reception module side of the facility management unit or to receive change and input information provided from the real time transmission module to the central management server unit it consists of a sending receiving module the facility management department a real time transmission reception module for receiving change information and input information from the sewage treatment facility unit from the remote site management information transmission reception module and providing it to the facility control module it consists of a facility control module for receiving information from the real time transmission reception module and providing it to the sensing information transmission reception module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes for collecting only contaminants generated during the filtration process and sludge from the second storage tank which are formed in the filtration tank and a backwash water drain pump configured to discharge contaminants and sludges introduced into the inside of the backwash drainage storage tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102422847-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in addition it is possible to prevent iron precipitation through real time ph measurement and to provide a waste liquid decomposition monitoring device according to decontamination of a nuclear power plant that can be used for uv reaction tank maintenance by checking the ph when washing lamps in the uv reaction tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102422847-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to prevent iron precipitation through real time ph measurement and it is possible to provide a waste liquid decomposition monitoring device that can be used for maintenance of the uv reaction tank by checking the ph when washing the lamp in the uv reaction tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4394261-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in combination with a system for controlling clarification of boiler feed water and the like by precipitation said system comprising a settling tank having an inlet and an outlet for said water means for adding a chemical to said inlet water to cause said precipitation a drain line and first valve means for drawing off precipitate from the bottom of said tank a small sampling line connected into said tank at a predetermined level above the bottom of said tank for continuously sampling water from said tank means for continuously measuring turbidity of said sampled water comprising a switch having a closed position if said turbidity exceeds a predetermined minimum and an open position if not and means for backwashing said precipitate draw off comprising a second valve means for controlling flow through a connecting line between said inlet water and said drain line while said first valve means is closed timing and control means for checking said turbidity at first predetermined intervals and for activating said first valve means for second predetermined intervals if said turbidity exceeds a predetermined minimum and for activating said second valve means with disabling of said first valve means at third predetermined regular intervals said timing and control means comprising first timing means for opening said first valve means for said second predetermined intervals first circuit means for connecting said turbidity switch to said first timing means for activating said first timing means only when said turbidity exceeds said predetermined minimum second timing means for checking said turbidity at said first predetermined intervals second circuit means for connecting said second timing means to said first timing means for activating said second timing means whenever said turbidity switch is closed and third timing means for opening said second valve means at said third predetermined regular intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "description of the related art a food waste b wash water c drain d waste water e solid fraction f meat fish grain g functional feed 1 food waste recycling facility 10 metering unit 11 identification means 111 identification card 112 card reader 113 identification chip 114 scanner 12 weighbridge 13 pick up vehicle 14 management means 20 input portion 21 storage hopper 211 screw feeder 30 screening crushing unit 31 screening crusher 40 supply part 41 storage tank 411 automatic meter 50 liquid phase fermentation distribution processing section 51