  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102789712-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a brine tank 10 10 in which brine is stored at a certain level and sprayed through brine nozzles individually installed at a number of habitual freezing points a b c d a detection sensor 20 that detects the water level of brine stored in the brine tank 10 of each of the above points a central control unit 30 that manages information on the brine storage level through the above detection sensor 20 in order to transport brine stored in a brine tank 10 at a point where the amount of brine is relatively large to a point where the amount of brine is insufficient by the control of the central control unit 30 a brine guide pipe 40 through which brine stored in the brine tank 10 is withdrawn by the operation of a pump p a coupler 50 that is connected to the end of the brine guide pipe 40 and is connected to the transfer tank 110 of the brine transfer vehicle 100 a salt water supply system for road deicing spraying characterized in that the salt water transport tank 110 configured in the salt water transport vehicle 100 is provided with a plurality of bubble generators 111 on the bottom surface to prevent freezing or precipitation of salt water during the transport process an ultraviolet lamp 112 is provided on the top surface and a deterioration prevention layer 113 is formed on the inner wall surface to prevent deterioration of salt water during transport"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102789712-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in order to prevent freezing or precipitation of brine during the transport process a plurality of bubble generators 111 are provided on the bottom surface of a transport tank 110 configured in a brine transport vehicle 100 an ultraviolet lamp 112 is provided on the top surface and a deterioration prevention layer 113 is formed on the inner wall surface to prevent deterioration of brine during transport thereby preventing precipitation and deterioration of brine during the transport process"}, {"pat_id": "US-7128081-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the trapping column 407 resides away from the cold surfaces of the two sub regions 401 402 so that its contents are not subject to freezing that could give rise to sample precipitation or other undesired effects"}]</data>
</edge>
