  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in particular in the case of rainwater tossil that the cross section is wider than the trunk line such solid precipitation is more serious and the wear height is relatively lower due to the solid precipitation so there is a problem that frequent accidents overflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in particular in the case of rainwater tossil that the cross section is wider than the trunk line such solid precipitation is more serious and the wear height is relatively lower due to the solid precipitation so there is a problem that frequent accidents overflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100607719-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "as a result it is possible to maintain a certain level of water in the oxidizing sphere 300 so that the microorganisms that remove organic matter and nitrogen and phosphorus in the sewage can survive as well as the inclined plate installed to improve the precipitation efficiency in the sedimentation basin 400 the damage caused by collision with 9 can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100444099-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the wear plate control valve of claim 1 or 2 wherein the overflow wear in the settling tank has a cylindrical shape or a separate type and a wear plate control valve is configured to adjust the height so as to induce a uniform overflow load maintenance and normal precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100444099-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "is configured so that the treated water overflow wear plate 19 of the settling tank 7 is installed on the upper portion of the inlet pipe 17 the overflow wear plate may be flowed through the cylinder or pipe through which the treated water is directly flowing it is composed of a separate type the height controllable form by using the control valve 32 configured in the overflow control panel 19 is to induce a uniform overflow load maintenance and normal precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428076-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an inlet pipe 11 connected to the outside of the infiltration pipe to introduce the sewage water and a first deep plate 21 installed inside the primary sedimentation tank 10 to change the inflow direction of the sewage water and the a secondary precipitation tank 30 installed inside the first dip plate 21 to induce secondary precipitation and a second dip installed inside the secondary precipitation tank 30 to change the inflow direction of the effluent water a plate 23 and a wear channel 41 formed integrally with the outside of the second deep plate 23 to introduce the treated water into the discharge pipe and a primary settling tank at one side of the wear channel 41 10 the discharge pipe 40 protruding outward to discharge the treated water and connected to the lower portion of the primary settling tank 10 to draw out the settling sludge it is characterized by comprising a sludge drawing pipe 50"}]</data>
