  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage section provided in an excavation section dug down the ground and comprising a space skeleton section configured by assembling a skeleton block and a water permeable layer covering at least the top surface of the space skeleton section a first filter unit that is provided above the water storage unit and filters water flowing into the water storage unit a pipe line that is attached to the water storage unit and extends from the water storage unit to the ground surface a pump unit attached to the conduit and pumping out water from the reservoir a second filter unit for purifying water pumped out by the pump unit a clay layer provided on the side of the water reservoir or an impermeable layer as a layer of soil treated with a soil conditioner an impermeable layer provided below the water reservoir a water permeable layer that covers the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton inside the water impermeable layer comprising at least by using a water permeable sheet of polyester nonwoven fabric with a water permeability coefficient of 10 2 to 10 1 cm sec a tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more in the longitudinal direction and a tensile elongation of 60 or more in the longitudinal direction even if a part of the impermeable layer breaks and breaks groundwater penetrates and flows into the reservoir through a permeable sheet with a predetermined permeability so that sudden rapid inflow of groundwater into the reservoir during an earthquake at the same time to suppress the water storage facility characterized in that the water storage unit in buoyancy due to ground water that is lifted is suppressed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "c attaching to the flow path from which before the step b or the step c a step of forming an impermeable layer as a clay layer or a soil layer treated with a soil improver on the side of the water storage unit in the excavation unit d and a step e of forming a water permeable layer covering the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton by using a water permeable sheet of polyester nonwoven fabric with a water permeability coefficient of 10 2 to 10 1 cm sec a tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more in the longitudinal direction and a tensile elongation of 60 or more in the longitudinal direction even if a part of the impermeable layer breaks and breaks groundwater penetrates and flows into the reservoir through a permeable sheet with a predetermined permeability so that sudden rapid inflow of groundwater into the reservoir during an earthquake a method for constructing a water storage facility wherein the water storage part is prevented from floating due to buoyancy caused by groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a water storage section provided in an excavation section dug down the ground and comprising a space skeleton section configured by assembling a skeleton block and a water permeable layer covering at least the top surface of the space skeleton section a clay layer provided on the side of the water reservoir or an impermeable layer as a layer of soil treated with a soil conditioner an impermeable layer provided below the water reservoir a water permeable layer that covers the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton inside the water impermeable layer comprising at least as a water permeable layer the water permeability is 2 10 1by using a water permeable sheet of polyester nonwoven fabric with a tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more in the longitudinal direction and a tensile elongation of 60 or more in the longitudinal direction a crack occurred in a part of the impermeable layer due to an earthquake and broke"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a water storage unit a first filter unit that is provided above the water storage unit and filters water flowing into the water storage unit a pipe line that is attached to the water storage unit and extends from the water storage unit to the ground surface a pump unit attached to the pipe and pumping out water from the water storage unit a second filter unit for purifying water pumped out by the pump unit and a clay layer provided on a side of the water storage unit or an impermeable layer as a layer of soil treated with a soil improver an impermeable layer provided below the reservoir and a permeable layer that covers the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton portion inside the impermeable layer and at least the ingredients and as a water layer water permeability coefficient is 10 2 10 1 cm sec the vertical tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more the use of the permeable sheet in the longitudinal direction of the tensile elongation of 60 or more of a polyester nonwoven fabric even if a crack occurs in a part of the impermeable layer due to an earthquake groundwater penetrates and flows into the reservoir through a permeable sheet having a predetermined permeability coefficient so the groundwater suddenly enters the reservoir during an earthquake"}, {"pat_id": "US-4619819-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-4451277-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-4537615-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid 