line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5240962-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "4 there is no contamination of groundwater because the total amount of radiation contaminated water that flows in is a collection type"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101517156-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hollow cylindrical outer casing is provided in the area to be excavated and a soil excavation hole having a diameter of 3 to 4 m is formed by excavating and removing the soil layer of the soil layer while penetrating the out casing to expose the rock layer to the soil layer step 1 a second step of introducing a rock punching apparatus into the soil excavation hole to form a plurality of perforation holes having a diameter of 300 to 350 mm at intervals of 50 to 100 mm in the rock layer and a rock excavation hole extending from the excavation excavation hole and having a diameter of 3 to 4 m is formed in the rock excavation hole and a cylindrical incise hole is formed in the rock excavation hole a third step of inserting the ishing a fourth step of forming a plurality of horizontal holes on the inner wall of the rock excavation hole having a diameter of 100 to 300 mm in a horizontal direction up to the water vein portions of the rock layer and a fifth step of inserting a strainer pipe having a double pipe structure into each of the plurality of horizontal holes in the second step the rock piercing apparatus is a drilling apparatus using air and when forming any one of the plurality of piercing holes the other piercing holes are filled with clay or concrete to prevent air leakage wherein the incising member has a structure in which one incising member is formed by assembling cylindrical incising members having a predetermined length the incising members include a first incising member provided at a lower end of the rock excavation hole and having an engaging groove at an upper end thereof and a second incising member engaging with an upper end of the first encasing member and having a coupling groove formed at an upper end thereof and a coupling protrusion formed at a lower end thereof wherein the grooved member is inserted into the engaging groove of the incising member to form the ingression"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3655743-B1", "para_id": "para_175", "text": "for instance this may be whether the soil is sandy or clay based"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337121-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "this approach has limited volume because it is a 360 degree perimeter totally enclosed and has no leakage allowable"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337121-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "these sand lenses or areas of high permeability formed between adjacent grout columns result in grout walls that do not form substantially impermeable water barriers and that are susceptible to relatively high levels of water leakage or seepage"}, {"pat_id": "US-11585467-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "if not treated in time the joint misalignment will cause the pipeline leakage that the sewage in the pipeline leaks and the surrounding soil gradually becomes hollow further causing the environmental pollution and the accident such as the urban road collapse which seriously affects the ecological environment and the travel safety of the residents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100994248-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "as a result leakage of water is prevented from occurring during the precipitation of the treated water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100994248-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "however the ground layer other than the clay layer may prevent the leakage of treated water by forming a clay layer on the floor and the wall after the sedimentation tank 1 construction or by pouring nonwoven fabric or concrete"}]</data>
