  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage section provided in an excavation section dug down the ground and comprising a space skeleton section configured by assembling a skeleton block and a water permeable layer covering at least the top surface of the space skeleton section a first filter unit that is provided above the water storage unit and filters water flowing into the water storage unit a pipe line that is attached to the water storage unit and extends from the water storage unit to the ground surface a pump unit attached to the conduit and pumping out water from the reservoir a second filter unit for purifying water pumped out by the pump unit a clay layer provided on the side of the water reservoir or an impermeable layer as a layer of soil treated with a soil conditioner an impermeable layer provided below the water reservoir a water permeable layer that covers the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton inside the water impermeable layer comprising at least by using a water permeable sheet of polyester nonwoven fabric with a water permeability coefficient of 10 2 to 10 1 cm sec a tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more in the longitudinal direction and a tensile elongation of 60 or more in the longitudinal direction even if a part of the impermeable layer breaks and breaks groundwater penetrates and flows into the reservoir through a permeable sheet with a predetermined permeability so that sudden rapid inflow of groundwater into the reservoir during an earthquake at the same time to suppress the water storage facility characterized in that the water storage unit in buoyancy due to ground water that is lifted is suppressed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "c attaching to the flow path from which before the step b or the step c a step of forming an impermeable layer as a clay layer or a soil layer treated with a soil improver on the side of the water storage unit in the excavation unit d and a step e of forming a water permeable layer covering the outer surface of the side surface and the bottom surface of the space skeleton by using a water permeable sheet of polyester nonwoven fabric with a water permeability coefficient of 10 2 to 10 1 cm sec a tensile strength of 1000 n 5 cm or more in the longitudinal direction and a tensile elongation of 60 or more in the longitudinal direction even if a part of the impermeable layer breaks and breaks groundwater penetrates and flows into the reservoir through a permeable sheet with a predetermined permeability so that sudden rapid inflow of groundwater into the reservoir during an earthquake a method for constructing a water storage facility wherein the water storage part is prevented from floating due to buoyancy caused by groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "such particle size may however be mostly too great for such water to be pumped through the high pressure pumps utilized currently in commercially available storm drain conduit cleaning systems without causing unacceptable wear"}, {"pat_id": "US-8545696-B2", "para_id": "para_128", "text": "prior to placing the test basin two trenches were dug in the underlying soil to accommodate a drainage conduit for each of two outlets one for an embodiment of a sss fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-5476142-A", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in brief the present invention is directed to a flexible grout composition and method of disposing the composition in position in contact with an earthen formation such as a coating on a trench wall or within a bore hole for example to cement a conduit within the bore hole to prevent fluid loss for sealing and grouting well casings plugging abandoned wells and waterproofing earthen structures"}, {"pat_id": "US-5476142-A", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "after complete setting the composition maintains a moldable swellable consistency such as dense native clay or other stiff pastes such as spackling compounds or glazing compounds such that if the conduit develops a void or aperture the composition will fill the void upon additional sodium bentonite hydration to self seal thereby preventing water flow between the earthen formation and the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5476142-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "a trench wall or to cement a conduit to a surrounding earthen formation to prevent fluid loss from the well where the earthen formation contains contaminated water in fluid communication with the well bore or trench wall"}, {"pat_id": "US-4650367-A", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the soil load transferred to a rigid conduit may be several times that imposed on a flexible conduit with a compressibility equal to the adjacent soil"}, {"pat_id": "US-4650367-A", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "creep problems are avoided because plastics specifically pvc are known to be less susceptible to creep phenomena when loaded in compression"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1287212-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "various pipe bursting techniques may be used to burst almost any pipe including but not limited to those formed of vitrified clay reinforced concrete cast iron ductile iron asbestos cement and steel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-7374691-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "as illustrated multiple screens 245 provide an inlet for the groundwater to enter the accessway 240 each of these screens can be as large as the screen at the conduit 260 thereby maximizing the intake capacity for fluids and allowing for some blockage of these water inlet screens over time by silt clay or other fine particles without affecting the designed flow rate through the conduit 260"}, {"pat_id": "US-4596491-A", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the soil load transferred to a rigid conduit may be several times that imposed on a flexible conduit with a compressibility equal to the adjacent soil"}, {"pat_id": "US-4596491-A", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "creep problems are avoided because plastics specifically pvc are known to be less susceptible to creep phenomena when loaded in compression"}]</data>
</edge>
