sor package 840 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 810 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "the system 1100 is configured for use on a fluid conduit system 1102 located within a structure 1101 to prevent the fluid conduit system 1102 from damage due to freezing fluid upon detection of freezing conditions such as the temperature of the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 and the temperature of the environment surrounding the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "the temperature outside of the structure 1101 may be a predictor of freezing conditions for the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_138", "text": "the control system 1140 may also turn on the heating elements to heat up the pipes when the external environment temperature or the local environment temperature reaches a predetermined value to prevent the fluid within the conduit from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_139", "text": "thus a temperature or temperature range may be chosen for the fluid temperature and the environment temperature at which the control system 1140 will add heat energy to the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 before the water reaches 32 degrees fahrenheit to prevent it from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_141", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_142", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_147", "text": "the control system 1230 may also turn on the heating element to heat up the fluid and pipes when the external environment temperature or the local environment temperature reaches a predetermined value to prevent the fluid within the conduit from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_149", "text": "the control system 1230 may turn on the heated recirculation circuit 1220 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the environment temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_149", "text": "the control system 1230 may turn on the heated recirculation circuit 1220 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_157", "text": "the second threshold temperature tps2 and max time at second threshold temperature tpsmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_159", "text": "the second threshold temperature tss2 and max time at second threshold temperature tssmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_161", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle12 and max time at second threshold temperature tle1max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle22 and max time at second threshold temperature tle2max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_165", "text": "the second threshold temperature tet2 and max time at second threshold temperature tetmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3385163-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "for example at an environmental temperature of 10 c the water in the branches 25 27 35 may thaw within 30 min without requiring additional heating"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3385163-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the water in the conduit system 21 may be drained through the respective consumer equipment 5 7 9"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200305126-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "on one side of the solar heat collecting plate is composed of a solar heat collecting plate is connected to a conduit to transfer the temperature and a temperature controller to control the temperature and the heat collected from the solar heat collecting plate is connected to the bottom of the ball through the thermostat and the conduit it is configured to transfer the heat to the river water at the same time as it is selectively configured to transfer the heat to the river water while the temperature of the river water maintains a constant water temperature and at the same time between the buoyancy member and buoyancy member of the thread consisting of freezing and zigzag form by the role of the fish upstream relates to a water purification device using the buoyancy formula kkeunsang acting to improve the role and the contaminated water in the even that is configured to support the role of emitter and fish fins"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200305126-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "of the buoyancy member 1 of the buoyancy member 1 and the buoyancy member 1 between the buoyancy member 1 and the buoyancy member between the buoyancy member 1 is fastened by the connector 6 it is a structure in which many threads 2 such as poly ethylene yarns are formed in freezing form and zigzag form and on the upper side of the buoyancy member 1 selected on one side or the other side of the stream the temperature controller 9 and the conduit 10 due to the structure of the solar heat collecting plate 8 the polluted water flowing from the upstream of the stream passes through the thread 2 of the buoyancy member 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "1b gases may be fed into the ionization chamber 44 via a gas conduit 33"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_106", "text": "via the ion source block the surfaces of conduit 150 are thus preferably maintained at temperature greater than the set point of pid 3"}, {"pat_id": "US-4235680-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to but above the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "when the heater 610 of the heater unit 600 is disposed in the conduit 510 as in one embodiment of the present invention the heater 610 is directly in contact with the fire water in the conduit 510 and the heater 610 can directly heat the fire water in the conduit 510 the heating efficiency and energy utilization efficiency of the fire water in the conduit 510 is excellent thereby freezing the fire water in the conduit 510 quickly it can be heated to the above temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800 and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point the control unit 800 provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "US-12286370-B2", "para_id": "para_115", "text": "chemical feed 40 is generally applied into the return piping 33 after being filtered and where applicable heated to prevent corrosion of the heater 22"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "with the circuit thus closed solenoid actuated valve 66 will open and allow water to pass through from conduit 65 to faucet 22 via conduit 67"}, {"pat_id": "US-4203806-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4808290-A", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "if pool water stops flowing through metal conduit 46 while electrical power continues to be supplied to field wiring block 366 then after approximately five minutes the temperature of metal bar 384 and thermostatic switch 386 rises above the aforementioned predetermined temperature and themostatic switch 386 opens"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100756437-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a checking the internal state and determining the maintenance position by a camera entering the conduit b removing deposits and deposited deposits attached to the interior of the conduit c impregnating a liquid two component thermosetting resin mixed with a two component resin cured at room temperature to a fiber sheet made of synthetic fibers d attaching the order sheet to the outer surface of the fibrous sheet and applying the two component thermosetting resin to the thixotropic order sheet e placing the expansion member into a repair position by winding the repair member on which the fiber sheet and the order sheet are stacked on the outer surface of the expansion member and entering the expansion member into the conduit f supplying compressed air into the expansion member to expand the expansion member by volume expansion to make surface contact with the outer surface of the order sheet on the inner wall of the conduit and press for a predetermined time g curing the thermosetting resin of the repairing material by a heat source provided inside the expansion member to integrate the repairing material on the inner wall of the conduit and h drawing out the retracted expansion member from the conduit to the outside so as to be separated from the conduit integrated into the conduit in the thermosetting conduit repair method comprising a step d is uneven to expand the area in contact with the outer surface while inflating with the expansion member when the expansion member is expanded on the outer surface of the order sheet before attaching the order sheet to the fiber sheet thermosetting type conduit repair method characterized in that it further comprises the step of forming a plurality in parallel to the longitudinal direction of the expansion member"}, {"pat_id": "US-4035241-A", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "after a period of time due to the negative pressure created within the apparatus by the weight of the water contained therein water vapor will begin to form in the conduit 24 and near the tops of the two enclosures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102756589-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the valve 44 is opened and the steam s from the first heating reactor 5 begins to flow into the second heating reactor 6 thereby equalizing the pressure between the reactors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102756589-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "the valve 46 is opened and the steam s from the second heating reactor 6 begins to flow into the first heating reactor 5 thereby equalizing the pressure between the reactors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358103-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the flexible conduit tube is wavy so it is very easy to draw wires and is not subject to temperature changes so there is no need for relaxation measures and it is easy to prevent acid and corrosion resistance and has almost no condensation"}, {"pat_id": "US-4118283-A", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368217-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition according to the present invention when embedding the detection conduit 52 between the water supply pipe 50 and the support 10 the surface close to the support 10 is maintained by the thermal insulation means 20 the surface of the ground which is greatly affected by the atmospheric temperature it prevents freezing by heat insulation without losing heat and also transmits geothermal heat to the internal space 11 of the support 10 to compensate for insufficient heat insulation effect of the thermal insulation materials 21 and 22 and internal space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102722253-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the present 