  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a peripheral wall 110 forming a square frame a partition wall 120 formed in the shape of a \u5341 shape to partition the inside of the peripheral wall 110 and a joint wall 130 formed so that each side extends from the corner portion 111 of the peripheral wall 110 and forms a vertical angle with the corner portion 111 it is configured to include and at each end of the joint wall 130 a plurality of block units 100 in which longitudinal recessed parts 131 and convex parts 132 are formed alternately are arranged sequentially in four horizontal directions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a system to recycle rainwater the rainwater recycling system 100 includes a rainwater inlet grating 10 mounted on a surface of a road 8 to block inflow of large solids a solids removal screen 20 installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen 30 for removing fine solids in rainwater that has passed through the solids removing screen 20 an initial storm drain 40 for discharging rainwater containing pollutants on the road surface during initial stormwater an upper trench conduit 50 for storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration screen 30 a lower trench conduit 60 for storing rainwater flowing over from the upper trench conduit 50 a water purification filtration layer 70 formed on the upper and lower trench conduits 50 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainwater recycling system characterized in that consisting of a permeable layer 80 for introducing the rainwater flowing from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of recycling rainwater the rainwater recycling method includes mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block inflow of large solids into the rainwater 