e inflow of foreign substances into the water conduit and securing a water passage cross section while reducing non point contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783964-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "accordingly by forming the above mentioned drainage expansion port 6 in an l shape the rainwater inside the water conduit body 2 can be discharged more smoothly toward the ground filter 5 through the initial rainwater discharge port 222 formed horizontally penetrating the side wall 22 of the water conduit body 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100678389-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "as cracks breaks or joints are relaxed due to various reasons such as rainwater the rainwater flows into sewage pipes reducing the efficiency of sewage treatment infiltration water and water and soil pollution effluent water due to the discharge of wastewater inside the pipes environmental damage such as ground erosion occurs and there is a problem in that damaged or cracked sewer pipes must be replaced or repaired with new ones"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100753822-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition there has been a problem that the conventional sewage pipe is obsolete in an area or place where the water level is low because the amount of rainwater or sewage is low.the present invention is to solve the above problems the floating foreign matters induced by rain or sewage floating in sewage pipes to both ends to automatically collect and store the induced foreign matters stored in a later period of time the purpose of the present invention is to provide a sewage conduit structure with a sewage pipe that can minimize the obstacle of drainage of the sewage that is collected and remains suspended as well as to facilitate the cleaning of the sewage pipe quickly and easily"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102525988-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a device for reducing the flow rate of running water flowing through a water conduit and more specifically it is installed in a manhole into which rainwater or sewage with high flow velocity flows due to a pipe on a ramp to reduce the flow rate of rainwater or sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102290677-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition due to the inflow of rainwater interception and step by step exclusion are made so it is possible to prevent contamination of small tea houses and damage caused by backflow of rainwater from large tea houses"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore between the facing pieces although rainwater etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "thus the first water conduit is provided so as to pass between the opposing pieces"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "further the drainage tool according to the invention described in claim 3is provided at the upper end of the side wall of the gutter block to prevent rainwater etc.a drainage tool for guiding theit has a water body"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "further the drainage tool according to the invention of claim 4is provided at the upper end of the side wall of the gutter block to prevent rainwater