udge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "system for transferring foul discharges from a rainwater sewer 2 into a dirty water sewer 4 a connecting conduit 5 being provided between the rainwater sewer 2 and the dirty water sewer 4 characterized in that the rainwater sewer 2 has a manhole 1 the floor 9 of the rainwater sewer 2 is arranged above the floor 10 of the manhole 1 and the rainwater sewer 2 has a lateral orifice within the manhole 1 and furthermore a sill 18 being arranged in the region of the orifice in the rainwater sewer 2 obliquely relative to the extension of the latter and there being arranged at the floor level of the manhole 1 a pump 34 which is connected to the dirty water sewer 4 via a conduit 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "