ration storage tanks and the infiltration storage tanks and discharge conduits so that rainwater flows from the sedimentation tank to the infiltration storage tank and overflows into the discharge conduit or infiltrates into the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the second embodiment is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed steps a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed it consists of a tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_130", "text": "a diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed at an inlet of the penetration storage tank 4 to prevent the deposition of sand or foreign matter not completely precipitated in the sedimentation tank 1 to be deposited and the diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater penetration system b according to the third embodiment includes a first step which is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of a part where the sedimentation tank 1 and the penetration storage tank 4 are installed a second step of laying a ground crushed stone to select the excavated ground spread the granulated crushed stone and apply voltage a third step of laying a sheet on the base bottom on which the basic crushed stone 41 is placed to protect the penetration storage tank 4 a fourth step of assembling the unit block body 411 to form the penetration storage assembly 41 a fifth step of completing the penetration storage tank 4 by installing a protective sheet 43 to protect the side portion and the upper surface portion of the penetration storage assembly 41 a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the permeation storage tank 4 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the permeation storage assembly 41 a seventh step of installing the sedimentation tank 1 the inspection cleaning manhole 45 and the inspection manhole 46 of the penetration storage tank 4 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rainwater flows from the sedimentation tank 1 into the infiltration reservoir 4 and overflows into the discharge conduit 5 or penetrates into the water and is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_185", "text": "a diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed at an inlet of the penetration storage tank 4 to prevent the deposition of sand or foreign matter not completely precipitated in the sedimentation tank 1 to be deposited and the diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "smart storm overflow chamber system for collecting an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater and reducing odorsthe present invention relates to a smart rainwater drainage system for collecting an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater and reducing odors and more particularly by opening and closing the inlet and outlet of the rainwater chamber installed in the conduit to provide an appropriate amount of sewage sewage and rainwater in rainy weather or it relates to a smart rainwater discharge system that can block the odor by blocking the exit of the conduit in cheongcheon si while collecting rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781790-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the passage 212 is maintained in a lowered state so that the rainwater flows into the drainage conduit 11 and when the water level of the drainage conduit 11 rises it is injured and maintains a rising state to block the water passage 212 joined sewer pipe with a sewage discharge device characterized in that consisting of the lifting floating means 24 consisting of a lower float 23 to prevent the discharge to the collecting pipe 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781790-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "keep the rising state so that the part 212 is blocked by rain storm consists of a floating lifting means 24 consisting of the lower float 23 to prevent the output"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101112083-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "this is to limit the portion of the rainwater moving to the destination to the flow channel 240 and to prevent the rainwater that is not filtered to move in the longitudinal direction along the overflow portion 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100950100-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "it inhibits the activity and stores it and when it is discharged it adds the optimal amount of oxidizing agent to induce the oxidation of organic substances and odorous substances present in the conduit p"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101851938-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the apparatus includes a box 10 an inlet pipe 12 formed at an upper side of the inner side of the housing 10 and supplied with initial rainwater from the upper part thereof a trench cover 14 connected to the inflow conduit 12 and extending downwardly and being supplied with an initial storm and a trench cover 14 connected to the inflow conduit 12 to prevent inflow of contaminants suspended substances etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100520288-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "however the soil inflow prevention device according to the prior art is a type that the frame plate is opened and closed according to the amount of sewage by using the water pressure and the pressure of the spring it is difficult to precisely adjust the operating time point the tension of the spring or foreign matter to the spring if it is attached it was troublesome to check it frequently to maintain its normal function because it did not work properly and when it was necessary to reinforce the performance of the sediment inflow prevention device repair due to failure or to change the sewage volume in the area when the amount of sewage is required to be adjusted to the installation company there was a problem of delayed maintenance period and additional costs.the present invention has been made in order to solve the problems of the prior art as described above an object of the present invention is to improve the structure of the earth and sand inflow prevention device for opening and closing the collector conduit to the sewage so that the sewage is usually introduced into the collector rainy season in order to provide a means to block the inflow of sediment and rainwater into the dwelling by automatically opening and closing by the weight balance according to the quantity change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178358-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "provides a sewer type sewer pipe without cross piping in the conduit characterized in that consisting of a cover 50 to block the inside and outside of the sewage conduit to three channels.the present invention can be smoothly transported without disturbing the flow of sewage or rainwater because there is no pipe exposed or traversed in storm water or sewage it is easy to maintain the maintenance of the sewage pipe and reduce the cost of maintenance.1 is an exemplary view showing a configuration of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262194-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore it is required to be able to more efficiently handle the overload overflow water generated during rainfall in the combined sewer conduit and to facilitate the maintenance and management by the automation of the facility.an object of the present invention for solving the above problems by allowing the stormwater influent generated in the rainwater in the combined sewage conduit to be discharged by the upflow type automatic overflow of the overflow water is mixed with sewage overload of the combined sewage conduit it is to provide a combined sewage contaminant overflow water treatment device that allows for more efficient treatment of overflow water and makes it easier to maintain and manage by using a non return valve or floating valve to enable automation without additional electrical facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133277-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the height of the purification device 1 of the present invention is lower than the height of the inclined drain conduit 2 so that the contaminants are smoothly conveyed to the contaminant collecting part 40 and also due to the heavy rain the flow rate of rainwater may be high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133277-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the initial rainwater that has passed through the rainwater inlet 11 is filled in the rainwater inlet 10 and the sludge accompanying the initial rainwater is deposited and accumulated at the rear of the rainwater inlet 10 by the barrier wall 32 and the boiling point does not settle"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a ground supported habitable structure comprising a foundation formed by one or more essentially water impervious vertical walls defining an essentially closed perimeter an essentially water impervious floor within the perimeter supported on the ground the floor and foundation defining an open top water enclosure sitting on or at least partially in the ground flooring positioned on the foundation at least substantially covering the open top of the enclosure the foundation supporting the flooring and any load supported by the flooring roofing exposed to the elements and supported six feet or more over the flooring to provide a habitable space between the roofing and the flooring the roofing and any load supported by the roofing being transmitted to the ground through the foundation a catchment supported to receive rainwater running from the roofing and at least one water carrying conduit extending from the catchment to the enclosure interior so as to deposit rainwater running from the roofing into the enclosure beneath the flooring"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the structure further comprises a catchment supported to receive rainwater running from the roofing and at least one water carrying conduit extending from the catchment to the enclosure interior so as to deposit rainwater running from the roof into the enclosure beneath the flooring"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "a catchment indicated generally at 60 is supported by one or more of the upper walls 41 44 and or the roofing 50 or in other conventional ways entirely around the roofing so as to receive all rainwater running from the roofing 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "rainfall conduit installed at least one or more monthly wear inherently so that rainwater flows from the predetermined watershed in rainy weather is separated into the initial rainfall and the continuous runoff a connection pipe connected to the rainwater conduit so that the initial rainwater flows in and a screen for filtering the suspended solids contained in the initial rainwater and filtering rainwater when rainwater exceeding an allowable capacity flows through the connection pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the initial excellent treatment system according to the characteristics of the present invention for achieving the above object the rainwater drainage installed at least one or more monthly wear inherently so that the rainwater flowing from the predetermined watershed during rainy weather is separated into the initial rainwater and the continuous water a connection pipe connected to the rainwater conduit so that the initial rainwater flows in and a screen for filtering the suspended solids contained in the initial rainwater and filtering rainwater when rainwater exceeding an allowable capacity flows through the connection pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "at this time the storm conduit 10 may be provided with a plurality of overflow wear 11 12 13 if necessary the front side of each overflow wear 11 12 13 as a settlement 20 a gate is installed to allow initial rainwater to flow in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101129908-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first opening and closing part installed in a first primary conduit buried in the ground of the sewer to inflow only sewage and initial rainwater a second opening and closing portion installed in a second collecting conduit buried in the ground of a sewer the second opening being closed by a relatively larger initial rainfall than the first opening and closing portion and the storage tank is connected to the first and second secondary conduits so as to increase the amount of initial excellent water flowing through the first opening and closing opening and closing portion inside the storage tank is installed foreign matter removal means for filtering foreign matter introduced during the initial rain the first opening and closing part and the second opening and closing part is an opening and closing plate formed with an inlet an inlet prevention plate fixed to the bottom of the opening and closing plate to block the inlet and a spring cylinder connected to the opening and closing plate by an initial excellent water pressure including and the second opening and closing part is connected to the first opening and closing part through an interlocking means so that the first opening and closing part may be opened simultaneously"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101129908-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the initial excellent treatment system according to the first invention of the present invention for achieving the above object the first opening and closing portion which is installed in the first primary conduit buried in the ground of the sewer to flow only the sewage and initial excellent water and underground of the sewer a second opening and closing portion installed in a second secondary conduit buried in and closed by a relatively higher initial amount than the first opening and closing portion and a storage tank to which the first and second collection pipes are connected so as to increase the amount of initial rainwater flowing in through the first opening and closing openings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "resin sided waterway pipe to prevent deformation in width direction and construction method water conduit the present invention relates to a side channel water pipe water collecting well of the resin material e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101008372-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a discharge conduit coupled to the sewer end while having an inclined end a blocking plate rotatably mounted at an inclined end of the discharge conduit so as to open and close the discharge conduit to guide the discharge of filthy water mixed with rainwater or to block the outflow of odor that is moved from the sewage conduit the upper end portion of the first induction conduit having a locking jaw formed therein with a narrow screen at the bottom of the installation hole of the discharge conduit opened and closed by the blocking plate is protruded to prevent the flow of foreign substances and the end of the first induction conduit and an induction conduit combined with a second induction conduit so as to discharge sewage from the sewage conduit to the conduit a screen net installed on the locking jaw of the first induction pipe to filter foreign substances contained in the sewage sewage collection device characterized in that it comprises a dust collector coupled to the induction pipe to supply the sewage is filtered and discharged from the screen net to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101008372-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "induction pipe 130 is configured to discharge the sewage from the sewage pipe 11 to the drain pipe 150 while connecting the collector pipe 150 is installed in the guide pipe 130 and the foreign matter contained in the sewage screen net 140 is configured to filter and comprises a dust collector 150 coupled to the induction pipe 130 to supply the sewage discharged by the foreign matter is filtered from the screen net 140 to the sewage treatment plant this is more specific if the description is as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-12203859-B2", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "the test liquid 2 in the device 1 for detecting contamination with a photosynthesis inhibitor may be any liquid as long as the liquid does not destroy phytoplankton in a state where contamination with a photosynthesis inhibitor does not occur and in an environment of the pretreatment tank 21 the conduit or the like of the device 1 for detecting contamination with a photosynthesis inhibitor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100801684-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage pipe sewer pipe comprising a sewage pipe 1 having at least one manhole 11 and rainwater pipe 2 installed separately from the sewage pipe 1 and provided with at least one manhole 21 a detection means 3 provided with a plurality in one side of the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 and a turbidimeter which is a sensor for detecting a false contact and leakage of the pipe on the discharge side of the rain pipe 2 is provided with a collecting conduit 4 including at least one inlet hole 41 the inlet hole 41 is a soil inflow prevention device to prevent the soil from entering the conduit 4 5 classification means provided with a sensing means characterized in that it comprises a manhole 6 is provided between the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 used to connect the sewage pipe 1 and rain pipe 2 at the same time sewerage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060765-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore when heavy rain pours within a short time the other manhole of the concrete pipeline 110 is opened to drain the rainwater to the river the composite storage tank is temporarily stored in the river through the open manhole after temporarily storing the rainwater by doing so the quantity of rainwater flowing into the river can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060765-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the door may be made of a mesh structure that can pass rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101305591-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however due to the wide diameter it is easy for sediment to settle in conduits and there is a high possibility that sewage from rainwater tosoil may leak into the body of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100548990-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "if the sewage and rainwater flows in it may cause a problem that would block the inside of the conduit and cause adverse effects such as inspection repair cleaning and maintenance that would be virtually impossible.the present invention is to solve the above problems it is possible to remove the sediment and sludge accumulated in the sewage pipe by washing water without installing the mesh network inside the sewage pipe and even inside the sewage pipe using a small amount of injection means it is to provide a sewage pipe cleaning device for cleaning clean"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101287038-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if water leaks occur at the joint connecting the pipe and the manhole sphere in the sewage or rainwater manhole three dimensional deformation of the manhole and the pipe due to settlement or movement of soil and cracks will occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173254-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "by preventing the rainwater from flowing into the sewer conduit 20 by the rotation of the wear 40 it is possible to maintain a constant treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant by adjusting the inflow amount into the sewage treatment plant thereby maintaining excellent sewage treatment quality"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2486988-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the term liquid is therefore understood below to mean any liquid arriving naturally or artificially in the cavities of the mine or in the natural environment of the mine in particular groundwater or surface water for example rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101834261-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "in addition it is possible to secure excellent water tightness to prevent leakage of sewage or rainwater through the drain pipe connecting hole 210 of the public conduit 200 since the curved surface portion 12 of the curved surface portion 12 is formed so as to correspond to the radius of curvature of the inside of the public conduit 200 it does not interfere with the flow of the wastewater or the excellent flow that flows into the public conduit"}]</data>
