  <data key="d6">["manage", "receive", "compose", "apply", "contaminate", "solve", "weld", "sink", "drink", "connect", "assume", "extract", "display", "accord", "fasten", "refer", "increase", "cause", "secure", "have", "minimize", "clog", "send", "fix", "wash", "pour", "flow", "can", "relate", "twist", "provide", "space", "establish", "bend", "expect", "set", "proceed", "calibrate", "prevent", "compare", "meet", "correspond", "leak", "arrange", "describe", "form", "shut", "measure", "divide", "concentrate", "calculate", "save", "build", "pass", "occur", "follow", "repair", "fill", "bring", "do", "determine", "lower", "settle", "conform", "accumulate", "support", "inquire", "turn", "destroy", "accompany", "slide", "become", "integrate", "clean", "serve", "deform", "protrude", "convey", "locate", "remove", "foam", "surround", "show", "reduce", "bind", "inject", "may", "configure", "freeze", "discharge", "store", "detect", "analyze", "include", "perform", "act", "consist", "open", "block", "mean", "supply", "deposit", "use", "transfer", "construct", "raise", "stop", "scour", "withstand", "estimate", "sense", "transport", "require", "close", "bolt", "maintain", "improve", "control", "excavate", "transmit", "drain", "monitor", "characterize", "waste", "shape", "select", "damage", "exist", "be", "generate", "collect", "instal", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200413616-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the present invention relates to a conduit freeze protection mat installation structure used for sewage waterworks roads river dikes and landfill leachate drainage to prevent freezing of sewage pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413616-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition leakage of water and sewage occurs due to freezing and in the case of sewage there is a problem of causing pollution of surrounding soil and causing settlement of surrounding ground.the present invention is to solve the problems as described above sewage waterworks roads river banks and landfill leachate to prevent the sewage pipes from freezing by forming a foamed urethane layer after welding the reinforcement anchor to the outer surface of the sewage pipe the purpose is to provide a conduit freeze protection mat installation structure used for drainage work"}, {"pat_id": "US-4944872-A", "para_id": "para_172", "text": "also the conduit system serves as a transporting system for bringing the material to the processing facility instead of requiring separate transport"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413254-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "however when the conventional water and sewage pipe constructed in this way is installed on the inclined surface of the ground 1 as shown in figure 1 due to the sliding phenomenon of the water and sewage pipe 10 the joint 11 of the water and sewage pipe 10 are spaced apart from each other a large amount of fluid is leaked to the outside through the separation portion there is a problem that causes serious environmental pollution of surface water and groundwater due to leakage in the case of sewage or waste water.the present invention is to solve the problems as described above by fixing the water supply pipe installed on the inclined surface to the fixed pile through the binding beam and the fastening band to prevent the sliding of the water pipe to prevent the joints from being damaged by the sliding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413255-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the unevenness of the shoring has a sawtooth shape and protrudes upwardly and the unevenness of the lower concrete block is protruded downward to have a sawtooth shape and sewage water supply road river and landfill leachate drainage conduit protection structure installed in construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102100306-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step of the server storing the sub zone information determined to be in need of maintenance in the database the step of receiving and saving the operation history information and and storing the simulation data in connection with the gis data collecting and analyzing measurement data by the server displaying by the server a simulation object rdii parameter and a flow graph using a toolbox the server constructing and calibrating a model for each small area the server further includes performing model verification and simulation evaluation the step of the server building a model for each of the small areas constructing a pipe network for model building and collecting attribute data estimating the input value of the pipeline model calculating a dwf dry weather flow model input value comprising the step of calculating the input value of the simulation object rdii model the step of the server to calibrate each sub area dwf dry weather flow model calibration step wwf wet weather flow model correction step for the selected rainfall event before the server collects and analyzes measurement data inquiring by the server information about an existing zone in a database to divide the small zone selecting by the server an object that is inadequate compared to the sub zone criterion as an object to be divided into sub zones when the division target area is selected the server establishes the boundary of the small area using the boundary of the back road the river and the railway or the boundary of the administrative area while conforming to the area standard determining by the server the compatibility with the sub region criteria by extracting the stored sub region information determining that the boundary condition is met when the server is determined to be suitable for a small area standard if the server determines that the boundary condition is met further comprising the step of storing the set and stored sub zone information as the new divided sub zone information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102524681-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the ice cleaning duct washing discharge control method required to clean the water supply duct using the ice washing medium in the water supply duct the ice cleaning duct washing discharge control method in the water supply duct blocking the water valve on the supplier side and the water valve on the consumer side of the pipeline to be cleaned s11 opening the washing water inlet valve configured at the rear end of the water valve on the supplier side and injecting the washing medium into the conduit while applying pressure using the inlet pump s12 washing the inside of the pipe while passing the cleaning medium by increasing the pressure with the inlet pump inside the pipe s13 washing the inside of the water supply pipe with a washing medium and discharging washing discharged water discharged after washing through a discharge pipe formed in front of the water supply valve on the receiving side s14 a step of firstly and periodically transmitting the sensed water quality data to a controller by a water quality sensor installed at a rear end of the discharge pipe and sensing water quality data of discharged water flowing through the discharge pipe s15 determining whether or not the received first water quality data is equal to or less than a predetermined effluent water quality standard s16 in the case of the following the controller opens the solenoid valve installed in the discharge pipe to discharge the washing discharge water to the river s17 sensing the amount of discharged water discharged into the river by the flow sensor unit of the drained water discharge pipe installed at the rear end of the water quality sensor unit and transmitting the sensed discharged water quantity information to the controller s18 transmitting by the controller primary water quality data and discharged water flow rate information to a center server of a water quality management center s19 determining whether the received water quality data meets drinking water quality standards by a controller that periodically receives water quality data from the water quality sensor unit s20 if appropriate turning off the washing water inlet valve configured in the washing water inlet to stop the injection of the washing water and opening the water supply valve to supply tap water to the corresponding pipe s21 monitoring the secondary water quality data transmitted from the water quality sensor unit by the controller while discharging tap water supplied to the water supply pipe through the discharge pipe s22 and if the received water quality data meets the drinking water quality standards transmitting the water quality data to the manager smart terminal to block the discharge valve of the discharge pipe and open the water valve on the consumer side to supply tap water to the consumer s23"}, {"pat_id": "US-7585413-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "as used herein the term pass passing passed and other conjugations means and refers to convey to direct and or to transport via any method or structure common in the art such as a conduit pipe funnel trough line slope gully trench river stream and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133277-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the initial rainwater that has passed through the rainwater inlet 11 is filled in the rainwater inlet 10 and the sludge accompanying the initial rainwater is deposited and accumulated at the rear of the rainwater inlet 10 by the barrier wall 32 and the boiling point does not settle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200305126-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "on one side of the solar heat collecting plate is composed of a solar heat collecting plate is connected to a conduit to transfer the temperature and a temperature controller to control the temperature and the heat collected from the solar heat collecting plate is connected to the bottom of the ball through the thermostat and the conduit it is configured to transfer the heat to the river water at the same time as it is selectively configured to transfer the heat to the river water while the temperature of the river water maintains a constant water temperature and at the same time between the buoyancy member and buoyancy member of the thread consisting of freezing and zigzag form by the role of the fish upstream relates to a water purification device using the buoyancy formula kkeunsang acting to improve the role and the contaminated water in the even that is configured to support the role of emitter and fish fins"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100408854-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the sludge removal device may not be installed in the water in a place where the curved bottom of the river or the severe curved surface is settled and the sludge settled due to the obstacle of rotational overturning of the scrapers 106 and 106 may be collected"}, {"pat_id": "US-12203859-B2", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "the test liquid 2 in the device 1 for detecting contamination with a photosynthesis inhibitor may be any liquid as long as the liquid does not destroy phytoplankton in a state where contamination with a photosynthesis inhibitor does not occur and in an environment of the pretreatment tank 21 the conduit or the like of the device 1 for detecting contamination with a photosynthesis inhibitor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in an initial high boiling point contamination treatment system 100 connected to the end of the conduit or the river water from which the polluted water is discharged to provide pollution excellence and selectively supply only the initial nonpoint pollution excellence a reservoir 200 for storing initial boiling impurity contamination provided to the water collection channel 130 of the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants a siphon pipe 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the water level of the reservoir 200 becomes equal to or higher than the height of the highest part in the reversed u shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the second embodiment of the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention is characterized in that it comprises an overflow collecting unit 100 which selectively supplies only the initial nonpoint contamination excellent due to the end of the conduit or the contaminated water a reservoir 200 for storing the initial non point contamination excellent provided to the water collection channel 130 of the water collection fixture 100 and performing a primary settlement of the contaminants a siphon channel 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the height of the highest part of the inverted u shape is higher than the height of the highest part of the inverted u shape a flow rate reducing manhole 300 for reducing the flow rate of the initial nonpoint contamination supplied from the siphon duct 295 and a second outlet pipe 320 for supplying the initial non a sedimentation paper 400 which is supplied through the first sedimentation unit and proceeds to second sedimentation and decomposition of contaminants and a drainage basin 500 located at the end of the sedimentation tank 400 and discharging the initial nonpoint contaminated soil from which contaminants have been removed to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101139331-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "here the pair of band rings are arranged in a pair to the upper and lower water pipes and the upper and lower band rings installed with the water pipes therebetween are bolted to each other through the anchor bolt to support the water pipes.as described above the water pipe cross water reinforcement device according to the present invention is connected to the joint connecting panel and the water conduit is arranged on the base panel having a height control function of the water pipe and then the sand mortar layer frp cover layer by forming the nonwoven fabric layer and the gabion layer it is possible to prevent the phenomenon such as sinking bending or twisting the water supply pipe as the bottom of the river is deformed by the flow rate or scour generated in the underwater river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101658740-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore in order to solve this problem a method for repairing the excavated ground or repairing the damaged conduit large sewer pipes for sending a large amount of sewage discharged from densely populated areas to the sewage treatment plant for example sewage pipes around the han river constructed in the 1980s have a cross section of 2.8 x 2.8 m in width and a certain section of the sewer pipe it is very dangerous for a person to perform maintenance work simply by using a clogging membrane and maintained in a dry state and even if it is assumed that the clogging membrane can sufficiently withstand water pressure due to the inflow of a large amount of sewage as the stress concentration concentrates on the surface of the film as the pipeline is expected to be damaged it is urgently necessary to shut off the pipeline or the construction of the pipeline which has been secured as a pretreatment stage for the maintenance of such large sewer pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060765-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore when heavy rain pours within a short time the other manhole of the concrete pipeline 110 is opened to drain the rainwater to the river the composite storage tank is temporarily stored in the river through the open manhole after temporarily storing the rainwater by doing so the quantity of rainwater flowing into the river can be reduced"}]</data>
</edge>
