  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of recycling rainwater the rainwater recycling method includes mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block inflow of large solids into the rainwater inlet grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall recycled from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 storm water recycling method comprising the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-6196762-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the open channels are either waterways in essentially their natural condition or waterways which have been improved by enlargement straightening paving or other means to increase their hydraulic capacity and reduce erosion of their banks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "here the storm drainage treatment apparatus according to the present invention may not have a passage for guiding the inflow of water to the upper side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101993772-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "here the catch forming block 140 may be detachably fixed to the side plate 110 by bolting or integrally fixed by welding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178358-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "provides a sewer type sewer pipe without cross piping in the conduit characterized in that consisting of a cover 50 to block the inside and outside of the sewage conduit to three channels.the present invention can be smoothly transported without disturbing the flow of sewage or rainwater because there is no pipe exposed or traversed in storm water or sewage it is easy to maintain the maintenance of the sewage pipe and reduce the cost of maintenance.1 is an exemplary view showing a configuration of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "in order to prevent cross contamination of services from the various utility lines including the large diameter line 502 the interior space 503 of the utility housing can be filled with a setting foam material such as expanding polyurethane sealant to prevent fluids gases and electrical signals from being conducted from one utility line to another within the utility housing as well as to provide thermal insulation for fluids within the smaller diameter lines"}, {"pat_id": "US-6167916-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the rest of the large central sub conduit 34 is typically provided for storm water drainage as may become necessary in the event of a flood or water overflow during a fire fighting event or burst water main"}]</data>
</edge>
