g water pressure acts during heavy rain or rainfall the pe block due to the strength or durability of the water pressure can not withstand the damage of the installed pe block the connection between the pe block may be a problem that the coupling part or the whole by the fastening protrusion is lost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102100306-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step of the server storing the sub zone information determined to be in need of maintenance in the database the step of receiving and saving the operation history information and and storing the simulation data in connection with the gis data collecting and analyzing measurement data by the server displaying by the server a simulation object rdii parameter and a flow graph using a toolbox the server constructing and calibrating a model for each small area the server further includes performing model verification and simulation evaluation the step of the server building a model for each of the small areas constructing a pipe network for model building and collecting attribute data estimating the input value of the pipeline model calculating a dwf dry weather flow model input value comprising the step of calculating the input value of the simulation object rdii model the step of the server to calibrate each sub area dwf dry weather flow model calibration step wwf wet weather flow model correction step for the selected rainfall event before the server collects and analyzes measurement data inquiring by the server information about an existing zone in a database to divide the small zone selecting by the server an object that is inadequate compared to the sub zone criterion as an object to be divided into sub zones when the division target area is selected the server establishes the boundary of the small area using the boundary of the back road the river and the railway or the boundary of the administrative area while conforming to the area standard determining by the server the compatibility with the sub region criteria by extracting the stored sub region information determining that the boundary condition is met when the server is determined to be suitable for a small area standard if the server determines that the boundary condition is met further comprising the step of storing the set and stored sub zone information as the new divided sub zone information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262194-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore it is required to be able to more efficiently handle the overload overflow water generated during rainfall in the combined sewer conduit and to facilitate the maintenance and management by the automation of the facility.an object of the present invention for solving the above problems by allowing the stormwater influent generated in the rainwater in the combined sewage conduit to be discharged by the upflow type automatic overflow of the overflow water is mixed with sewage overload of the combined sewage conduit it is to provide a combined sewage contaminant overflow water treatment device that allows for more efficient treatment of overflow water and makes it easier to maintain and manage by using a non return valve or floating valve to enable automation without additional electrical facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "rainfall conduit installed at least one or more monthly wear inherently so that rainwater flows from the predetermined watershed in rainy weather is separated into the initial rainfall and the continuous runoff a connection pipe connected to the rainwater conduit so that the initial rainwater flows in and a screen for filtering the suspended solids contained in the initial rainwater and filtering rainwater when rainwater exceeding an allowable capacity flows through the connection pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101129908-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first opening and closing part installed in a first primary conduit buried in the ground of the sewer to inflow only sewage and initial rainwater a second opening and closing portion installed in a second collecting conduit buried in the ground of a sewer the second opening being closed by a relatively larger initial rainfall than the first opening and closing portion and the storage tank is connected to the first and second secondary conduits so as to increase the amount of initial excellent water flowing through the first opening and closing opening and closing portion inside the storage tank is installed foreign matter removal means for filtering foreign matter introduced during the initial rain the first opening and closing part and the second opening and closing part is an opening and closing plate formed with an inlet an inlet prevention plate fixed to the bottom of the opening and closing plate to block the inlet and a spring cylinder connected to the opening and closing plate by an initial excellent water pressure including and the second opening and closing part is connected to the first opening and closing part through an interlocking means so that the first opening and closing part may be opened simultaneously"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060765-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore when heavy rain pours within a short time the other manhole of the concrete pipeline 110 is opened to drain the rainwater to the river the composite storage tank is temporarily stored in the river through the open manhole after temporarily storing the rainwater by doing so the quantity of rainwater flowing into the river can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200423906-Y1", "para_i