  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the storm recycling method is mounted on the road surface to block the inflow of large solids by storm inflow grating a solids removing step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating to remove the medium solids flowing into the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits the rainwater flowing from the lower trench conduit flows into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand the storm recycling method the step of mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block the inflow of large solids to the storm inflow grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall flowing from the lower trench conduit 60 consists of the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "such sediments accumulate over time often to the point of greatly impeding flow through such storm drain conduits so that subsequent storm runoff may be blocked to the point of backing up leaving the storm drain conduits ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "on the other hand it is possible to selectively treat only high initial rainfall by the change in flow rate and in particular to increase the treatment efficiency compared to the increase of the efficiency of filtration and to easily check from the outside by placing the differential pressure portion 23 in the center to measure the replacement cycle due to the clogging of the 1.2 filter medium which is a carbide embedded in the filtration unit due to the occurrence of overload it can prevent life shortening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "even if a small amount of initial rainwater including a contaminant is moved to the storm drain 16 or even a large amount of stormwater moves the storm drain may not move directly toward the storm drain 12 without being purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "it is possible to prevent the end of the waste.as described above the present invention is a device for treating a nonpoint source of pollution caused by an initial rainfall and can be immediately installed in an existing storm conduit 12 and particularly a coarse contaminant such as soil stones and leaves is a contaminant treatment tank 13 is treated preferentially the fine contaminants such as sand or mud is moved to the sediment storage unit 14 by the rotational centrifugal force through the rainwater movement port 16 provided to be eccentric with one side and the rainwater flow prevention plate installed at the bottom 18 and the concave portion 17 to prevent the backflow and settled in the lower part after removing the very fine sludge through the fibrous filtrate of carbide with rainwater can further extend the service life of the filter medium on the other hand it is possible to selectively process only the initial rainfall of high concentration by the amount of change in flow rate and in particular it is provided with two stages of filtration to increase the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102100306-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step of the server storing the sub zone information determined to be in need of maintenance in the database the step of receiving and saving the operation history information and and storing the simulation data in connection with the gis data collecting and analyzing measurement data by the server displaying by the server a simulation object rdii parameter and a flow graph using a toolbox the server constructing and calibrating a model for each small area the server further includes performing model verification and simulation evaluation the step of the server building a model for each of the small areas constructing a pipe network for model building and collecting attribute data estimating the input value of the pipeline model calculating a dwf dry weather flow model input value comprising the step of calculating the input value of the simulation object rdii model the step of the server to calibrate each sub area dwf dry weather flow model calibration step wwf wet weather flow model correction step for the selected rainfall event before the server collects and analyzes measurement data inquiring by the server information about an existing zone in a database to divide the small zone selecting by the server an object that is inadequate compared to the sub zone criterion as an object to be divided into sub zones when the division target area is selected the server establishes the boundary of the small area using the boundary of the back road the river and the railway or the boundary of the administrative area while conforming to the area standard determining by the server the compatibility with the sub region criteria by extracting the stored sub region information determining that the boundary condition is met when the server is determined to be suitable for a small area standard if the server determines that the boundary condition is met further comprising the step of storing the set and stored sub zone information as the new divided sub zone information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "to provide.according to the sewage pipe structure having the foreign matter filter net structure of the present invention the foreign matter mixed in the stormwater flowing along the sidewalk or the roadway is blocked by the foreign matter blocking portion and only the excellent storages are introduced into the storm receiving portion it is possible to minimize the flow resistance of the sewage and to minimize the generation of odor due to the corruption of the foreign matter by reducing the burden on 