  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "it is possible to prevent the end of the waste.as described above the present invention is a device for treating a nonpoint source of pollution caused by an initial rainfall and can be immediately installed in an existing storm conduit 12 and particularly a coarse contaminant such as soil stones and leaves is a contaminant treatment tank 13 is treated preferentially the fine contaminants such as sand or mud is moved to the sediment storage unit 14 by the rotational centrifugal force through the rainwater movement port 16 provided to be eccentric with one side and the rainwater flow prevention plate installed at the bottom 18 and the concave portion 17 to prevent the backflow and settled in the lower part after removing the very fine sludge through the fibrous filtrate of carbide with rainwater can further extend the service life of the filter medium on the other hand it is possible to selectively process only the initial rainfall of high concentration by the amount of change in flow rate and in particular it is provided with two stages of filtration to increase the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272217-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "the support path block 230 has one side that is the surface facing the rainwater storage conduit 100 is formed in a shape corresponding to the outer surface of the rainwater storage conduit 100 hereinafter referred to as a corresponding conduit a communication hole 231 is formed on the corresponding surface of the pipe and communicates with the water supply unit 110 formed in the rainwater storage pipe 100 and the bottom surface communicates with a water hole 211 formed on the upper surface of the rain receiving unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102100306-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step of the server storing the sub zone information determined to be in need of maintenance in the database the step of receiving and saving the operation history information and and storing the simulation data in connection with the gis data collecting and analyzing measurement data by the server displaying by the server a simulation object rdii parameter and a flow graph using a toolbox the server constructing and calibrating a model for each small area the server further includes performing model verification and simulation evaluation the step of the server building a model for each of the small areas constructing a pipe network for model building and collecting attribute data estimating the input value of the pipeline model calculating a dwf dry weather flow model input value comprising the step of calculating the input value of the simulation object rdii model the step of the server to calibrate each sub area dwf dry weather flow model calibration step wwf wet weather flow model correction step for the selected rainfall event before the server collects and analyzes measurement data inquiring by the server information about an existing zone in a database to divide the small zone selecting by the server an object that is inadequate compared to the sub zone criterion as an object to be divided into sub zones when the division target area is selected the server establishes the boundary of the small area using the boundary of the back road the river and the railway or the boundary of the administrative area while conforming to the area standard determining by the server the compatibility with the sub region criteria by extracting the stored sub region information determining that the boundary condition is met when the server is determined to be suitable for a small area standard if the server determines that the boundary condition is met further comprising the step of storing the set and stored sub zone information as the new divided sub zone information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100753822-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition there has been a problem that the conventional sewage pipe is obsolete in an area or place where the water level is low because the amount of rainwater or sewage is low.the present invention is to solve the above problems the floating foreign matters induced by rain or sewage floating in sewage pipes to both ends to automatically collect and store the induced foreign matters stored in a later period of time the purpose of the present invention is to provide a sewage conduit structure with a sewage pipe that can minimize the obstacle of drainage of the sewage that is collected and remains suspended as well as to facilitate the cleaning of the sewage pipe quickly and easily"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-7157011-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "for instance when rain causes film of water to overlay the soil surface closing of the throttle valve will cause visible air bubbles in the surface which are not present when the vent is unthrottled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "on the other hand as shown in figure 6 and 7 while the odor blocking member 220 is maintained in a closed state due to the cause of excessive rain such as rainy season the rainwater is filled in the conduit to the rainwater from the conduit when the backflow is reversed the rainwater flowing back from the conduit pushes the malodor blocking member 220 downward thereby releasing the contact between the first contact portion 227 and the second contact portion 228 to block the malodor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a fifth step of doing a sixth step of connecting the pipe 27 to the storage tank 2 in order to prevent damage to the sheet or the connection with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the sedimentation tank 1 the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 2 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharged to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting piping between the storage tank 2 and piping between the storage tank 2 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of filling the excavated portion remaining after the installation of the sedimentation tank 1 and the storage tank 2 and voltage consists of the tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction the unit block 211 includes a top and bottom assembly 2111 installed at a bottom and a top thereof a basic assembly 2112 installed at a middle of the top and bottom assembly 2111 and a top and bottom assembly 2111 and a base assembly 2112"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "check manhole 26 is formed at the upper end of the storage tank 2 the construction method of the rainwater storage system a comprises a first step of ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed consists of the tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction the unit block 211 includes a top and bottom assembly 2111 installed at a bottom and a top thereof a basic assembly 2112 installed at a middle of the top and bottom assembly 2111 and a top and bottom assembly 2111 and a base assembly 2112"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system includes a first step which is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of a part where the sedimentation tank and the storage tank are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank and laying a sheet on a foundation bottom on which basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block to form the storage assembly a fifth step of installing a water repellent sheet and a protective sheet on the side surface of the storage assembly and a protective sheet on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank a sixth step of connecting the pipe to the storage tank to prevent damage to the sheet or the storage assembly a seventh step of installing the sedimentation tank the inspection cleaning manhole and the inspection manhole of the storage tank an eighth step of connecting the pipe between the rainwater inlet conduit and the sedimentation tank the pipe between the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and the pipe between the storage tank and the discharge conduit so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank to the storage tank a ninth step of filling back the excavated part remaining after the installation of the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and voltage the tenth step is to clean up the rainwater storage system and plant it if necessary"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the second embodiment is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed steps a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed it consists of a tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781790-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "keep the rising state so that the part 212 is blocked by rain storm consists of a floating lifting means 24 consisting of the lower float 23 to prevent the output"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101129908-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first opening and closing part installed in a first primary conduit buried in the ground of the sewer to inflow only sewage and initial rainwater a second opening and closing portion installed in a second collecting conduit buried in the ground of a sewer the second opening being closed by a relatively larger initial rainfall than the first opening and closing portion and the storage tank is connected to the first and second secondary conduits so as to increase the amount of initial excellent water flowing through the first opening and closing opening and closing portion inside the storage tank is installed foreign matter removal means for filtering foreign matter introduced during the initial rain the first opening and closing part and the second opening and closing part is an opening and closing plate formed with an inlet an inlet prevention plate fixed to the bottom of the opening and closing plate to block the inlet and a spring cylinder connected to the opening and closing plate by an initial excellent water pressure including and the second opening and closing part is connected to the first opening and closing part through an interlocking means so that the first opening and closing part may be opened simultaneously"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100801684-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage pipe sewer pipe comprising a sewage pipe 1 having at least one manhole 11 and rainwater pipe 2 installed separately from the sewage pipe 1 and provided with at least one manhole 21 a detection means 3 provided with a plurality in one side of the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 and a turbidimeter which is a sensor for detecting a false contact and leakage of the pipe on the discharge side of the rain pipe 2 is provided with a collecting conduit 4 including at least one inlet hole 41 the inlet hole 41 is a soil inflow prevention device to prevent the soil from entering the conduit 4 5 classification means provided with a sensing means characterized in that it comprises a manhole 6 is provided between the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 used to connect the sewage pipe 1 and rain pipe 2 at the same time sewerage"}]</data>
