  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100715823-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "it forms an oval conduit shape with a spiral curve with the most optimal hydraulic characteristic cross section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715823-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the flow rate is fast and there is a problem of scouring and exceeding the maximum flow rate 3m s"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715823-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "since the conventional conduits 20 21 and 22 are connected by only a simple shear key there is a problem in that there is a lack of unity of segment joining and leakage occurs.thus the present invention has been devised to solve the problems described above if the depth ratio of the precipitation precipitation on the road is small the initial flow rate is minimized by minimizing the deposition of sediment the flow rate for the high flow rate ratio by slowing down avoiding the maximum flow rate the scour is controlled and the section that maximizes the transport flow rate is improved to the oval conduit section by the spiral with the most optimal hydraulic characteristics and the same as the streamlined l shaped port and conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101833173-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a supply pipe for supplying a branch pipe which is split at one side of the supply pipe a solenoid valve for shielding the branch pipe a drug reservoir containing a chlorine liquid a chemical liquid conduit connected to the chemical reservoir for introducing the chlorine liquid into the branch pipe a metering pump for injecting the chlorine liquid into the chemical liquid transfer conduit a merging pipe formed in a y shape and mixing raw water introduced through a supply pipe with treated water in which a chlorine liquid flowing through the chemical liquid transfer pipe and a part of the raw water flowing through the branch pipe are mixed a controller for controlling the solenoid valve and the metering pump the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water flowing from the measurement branch pipe is set to a value obtained by subtracting the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water from the measurement branch pipe and a residual chlorine measuring unit including a residual chlorine measuring sensor for measuring the residual chlorine and a zinc ionizing electrode for removing anions contained in the introduced dilution water wherein a plurality of partition walls are provided between the zinc ionizing electrode and the residual chlorine measuring sensor and a display window is provided on one side of the controller and the measurement is made from the current chlorine measuring unit to measure the concentration of the foreign matter in the precipitation chamber the information of the residual chlorine is displayed on the display window of the controller and the opening closing sensor provided in the water supply and the controller drives the solenoid valve and the metering pump at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0068760-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "for a number of years it has been known that fresh water containing various dissolved minerals such as calcium and magnesium calcareous material could be effectively treated to reduce mineral precipitation from the water when it is heated by passing the water through a strong magnetic field"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-4394261-A", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "consequently the clarified water of the body of water 21 flows out through an exit conduit 23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200423906-Y1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "here when the circular conduit 20 is used for the conventional road drainage structure the flow rate of the water depth ratio of 50 or less is slow due to the inflow of the precipitation rainfall on the road surface and the transport of sediments is difficult"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200423906-Y1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "since the conventional conduits 20 21 and 22 are connected by only a simple shear key there is a problem in that there is a lack of unity of the segment joining and leakage occurs.therefore the present invention was devised to solve the problems described above and when the depth ratio of precipitation precipitation on the road is small the initial flow rate is increased to minimize the deposition of sediment and the flow rate is increased for the flow rate with a high depth ratio"}]</data>
</edge>
