  <data key="d6">["enable", "pull", "include", "perform", "expect", "make", "dispose", "recover", "purify", "compose", "apply", "prevent", "mean", "exceed", "supply", "tow", "arrange", "use", "inspect", "mount", "shut", "rehabilitate", "extract", "harden", "integrate", "withstand", "accord", "refine", "deform", "calculate", "reflect", "process", "require", "cause", "impregnate", "reshape", "rotate", "invert", "normalize", "maintain", "remove", "occur", "have", "reduce", "register", "equip", "inject", "monitor", "fix", "freeze", "can", "damage", "do", "be", "determine", "notify", "adhere", "put", "will", "generate", "relate", "pump", "collect", "instal", "create", "comprise", "lift"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101638096-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "since the size of the conduit is large it is not only dangerous for the person to perform the maintenance work after maintaining a certain section of the conduit by using only the damper membrane but also the damper membrane can withstand the hydraulic pressure due to the influx of the large amount of sewage however since severe stress concentration phenomenon occurs at the conduit site where the gauze gauze is installed it is expected that the gauze gauze will be damaged by the gauze itself"}, {"pat_id": "US-10738603-B2", "para_id": "para_158", "text": "when wells are shut down for repairs or are put out of service due to contaminant discharges that exceed the maximum allowable concentrations mcls the wells can be off or non pumping for many days weeks months or even years"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "collecting data including water pressure data for each water supply network using a network analysis program at a predetermined time with a network extracted from the small block water supply network extracting factors having a relatively high impact on soundness among factors for indirect evaluation that do not require direct on site evaluation from water supply pipe data and accident data arranging the extracted factor specific data in a water conduit and a block unit generating a questionnaire for collecting opinions of the expert group on the extracted factors performing matrix transformation to use the created questionnaire and extracting only the questionnaire content that is valuable from the questionnaire content extracting a weight which is a relative weight value by reflecting all the content of the questionnaire worth of the extracted consistency determining whether it is worth the relative weight value refining the data to enable relative comparison by removing relative extreme values from the data arranged in block units processing the normalized data by applying weights to the purified data to generate a consistency and inconsistency matrix calculating rank between each block by calculating relative strengths in the consistency and inconsistency matrix and 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the water supply network health assessment method using the hydraulic pressure measurement information according to the present invention comprises the steps of collecting data including water pressure data for each water supply network using a pipe network analysis program at regular intervals using a pipe network extracted from the small block water supply network extracting factors having a relatively high impact on soundness among factors for indirect evaluation that do not require direct on site evaluation from water supply pipe data and accident data arranging the extracted factor specific data in a water conduit and a block unit generating a questionnaire for collecting opinions of the expert group on the extracted factors performing matrix transformation to use the created questionnaire and extracting only the questionnaire content that is valuable from the questionnaire content extracting a weight which is a relative weight value by reflecting all the content of the questionnaire worth of the extracted consistency determining whether it is worth the relative weight value refining the data to enable relative comparison by removing relative extreme values from the data arranged in block units processing the normalized data by applying weights to the purified data to generate a consistency and inconsistency matrix calculating rank between each block by calculating relative strengths in the consistency and inconsistency matrix and notifying the user of the final result value in accordance with the user s input requirements"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "collecting data including water pressure data for each water supply network using a network analysis program at a predetermined time interval with the network extracted from the small block water supply network s501 extracting from the water supply pipe data and the accident data factors having a relatively high impact on soundness among factors for indirect evaluation that do not require direct site evaluation s502 arranging the extracted factor specific data in a water conduit and a block unit s503 generating a questionnaire for collecting opinions of the expert group on the extracted factors s504 performing matrix transformation to use the generated questionnaire and extracting only the questionnaire content that is valuable from the questionnaire content s505 extracting a weight which is a relative weight value by reflecting all the contents of the questionnaire with respect to the extracted consistency s506 determining whether there is a value as a relative specific gravity value s507 purifying the data to enable relative comparison by removing relative extreme values from the data arranged in block units s508 processing the normalized data by applying weights to the purified data to generate a consistency and inconsistency matrix s509 calculating a rank between each block by calculating a relative strength in the consistency and inconsistency matrix s510 and notifying the user of the final result value according to the user s input requirements s511"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101613272-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "since the size of the conduit is large it is not only dangerous for the person to perform the maintenance work after maintaining a certain section of the conduit by using only the damper membrane but also the damper membrane can withstand the hydraulic pressure due to the influx of the large amount of sewage however since severe stress concentration phenomenon occurs at the conduit site where the gauze gauze is installed it is expected that the gauze gauze will be damaged by the gauze itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306445-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the pipeline expansion device 1 includes an expander 11 for reshaping the deformation of the pipeline a a hydraulic electric pump 12 for generating hydraulic pressure to supply the expander 11 it is composed of a hydraulic line 13 for supplying the hydraulic pressure to the expander 11 and the hydraulic pressure is recovered to the hydraulic electric pump 12 the pipeline image photographing apparatus 2 includes a cctv camera 21 for inspecting the state inside the pipeline a and monitoring the rehabilitation work with the expander 11 it is composed of a rotating device unit 22 having a circumferential rotation device 221 to enable the cctv camera 21 to rotate in the circumferential direction and a vertical rotation device 222 to enable angle adjustment up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101206997-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "making a step installing fixed tube guide means each having a predetermined shape at an inlet of the manhole and an inlet of the conduit installing a movable traction force attenuator for reducing the traction force of the traction winch between the front fixing portion of the first flexible tube and the wire of the traction winch towing the first flexible tube mounted on the flexible tube feeder equipped with the freezing facility in the state where the curable resin is impregnated into the predetermined section of the pipeline to be rehabilitated through the manhole using a towing winch inverting injecting the resin impregnated second flexible tube inside the first flexible tube pulled into the conduit using hydraulic pressure or air pressure to cause the resin impregnated portions of the first and second flexible tubes to adhere to each other by inverting the second flexible tube a heat source is supplied to the first and second flexible tubes having a state in which the second flexible tube is in close contact with the inner wall of the pipeline to harden and integrate the resin impregnated in the first and second flexible tubes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10 0816410 registered on march 18 2008 more specifically the manhole is made of a cylindrical one of the manhole the present invention relates to a water conduit inspection device which can prevent stress concentration from occurring in a portion and that lifting shafts are disposed at both side ends of the opening closing partition to prevent the lifting shafts from being deformed by hydraulic pressure"}]</data>
