  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5356115-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "furthermore a water storage facility having a structure capable of preventing the skeletal block from rising due to the earthquake at the same time as suppressing the rapid inflow of groundwater into the reservoir during an earthquake and a method for constructing a water storage facility for constructing the same the purpose is to provide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while allowing it to flow to one side of the upper portion eco friendly rainwater management system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "it is configured to be made as a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while being possible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "it is configured to be made as a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while allowing it to flow to one side of the upper portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "in other words in the above described embodiment the planter block while dividing the collection pipe 16 connected between the rainwater collection rig 10 and the storage tank 20 into the first collection pipe 17 and the second collection pipe 35 each end is connected to a different vegetation hole 31 buried in the ground at 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "rainwater flowing through the collecting pipe 16 or the first collecting pipe 17 may be directly supplied to the storage tank 20 or may be supplied to the storage tank 20 via the planter block 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "9 rainwater supplied to the storage tank 20 through the water collection pipe 16 or the second water collection pipe 35 directly from the rainwater collection well 10 or via the planter block 30 is stored in the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a peripheral wall 110 forming a square frame a partition wall 120 formed in the shape of a \u5341 shape to partition the inside of the peripheral wall 110 and a joint wall 130 formed so that each side extends from the corner portion 111 of the peripheral wall 110 and forms a vertical angle with the corner portion 111 it is configured to include and at each end of the joint wall 130 a plurality of block units 100 in which longitudinal recessed parts 131 and convex parts 132 are formed alternately are arranged sequentially in four horizontal directions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the prefabricated rainwater infiltration storage tank 200 provided by the present invention is an underground structure built overall in a square shape and a plurality of the block units 100 are arranged in succession in four horizontal directions and adjacent block units it is constructed by arranging the recessed portion 131 and the convex portion 132 of the joint wall 130 to engage and combine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "fourth storage space it is an empty space in the inner area of the prefabricated rainwater infiltration storage tank 200 and is formed in a form surrounded by a plurality of block units 100 and the surrounding wall 110 and the shape of the space can be freely configured"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the prefabricated rainwater infiltration storage tank 200 may be disposed on the peripheral walls of the block units 100a and 100b forming the outer line of the structure without the joint wall 130 being formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "in claim 1 or 2 a grating for a rainwater drainage system capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention characterized in that the upper surfaces of the fixed grating and the elevating grating are formed in a block like gently curved shape so that sediments including cigarette butts and fallen leaves accumulating on the upper surface of the grating are pushed along the gently curved surface of the upper surface of the grating by the current of water and are induced to quickly drain downward through the rainwater drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "2 3 and 5 the upper surfaces of the fixed grating 60 and the elevating grating 50 described above are formed in a block like gently curved shape so that sediments including cigarette butts and fallen leaves accumulating on the upper surface of the grating are pushed along the gently curved surface of the upper surface of the grating by the current of water and are induced to quickly drain downward through a rainwater drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "at this time since the upper surfaces of the fixed grating 60 and the lifting grating 50 described above are formed in a block like gently curved shape and the support rod 60b forming the grating in a grid like shape is formed to be positioned lower than the upper surface of the grid plate 60a it is possible to minimize the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating and it is possible to induce the various sediments to be pushed along the gently curved upper surface of the grating by the current of water and to flow down through the rainwater drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "4 517 207 registered on may 28 2010 entitled structure for reservoir penetration of storm water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the water intake unit has a pointed cone shape at its lower end a spiral is protruded along the outer diameter and a hollow water intake pipe with open top and bottom communicating with the opening is provided in the inner space and horizontally extending radially from the upper edge to the it is characterized in that the seating wing is formed to be seated on the upper surface of the shielding plate of the fire fighting water supply tank and the lower part where the water collecting hole is formed is buried in the sand layer of the fire water supply tank.the present invention purifies and collects rainwater through a fire water supply tank having a multi layered filter material and when a fire occurs in a building the collected rainwater is ejected through a slit hole of a steel pipe installed inside the building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular in addition to the heavy rainfall due to the rainy season and typhoons the recent changes in global weather patterns caused by el nino and la nia have caused local and local concentration rainfall frequently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in rainy weather sewage such as soil fallen leaves and vinyl flows into the sewers indiscriminately but there is no separate facility to prevent them.these dirts block the flow of rainwater by blocking the inflow of the rain gutters or the inlet of the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "as shown in figure 3 the present invention is characterized in that the jaw 11 is formed to hang the strainer 21 to filter the dirt on the upper part of the rain gutter which is floating leaves floating on the road surface cigarette butts and dirt accumulate in rain gutters to prevent rainwater or sewage inflow or flow flooding the road or these dirt accumulate in sewers through rain gutters impeding the flow of sewage overflowing sewage pipes this is to prevent it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain block formed to protrude downward a media plate formed in a mat shape having a predetermined size such that the drain blocks are stacked at a predetermined thickness on the stacked upper portion a gravel layer filled with a predetermined thickness on an upper portion of the media plate and a cover layer in which the soil is filled with a predetermined thickness to an upper portion of the gravel layer direct drainage rainwater treatment reservoir of the flat site characterized in that the configuration is made including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "on the body formed in the form of a square plate to be installed in a plurality of stacked in the basement space drain passages are formed at regular intervals while an assembly protrusion protruding a certain height toward the upper portion is formed on the upper circumference of the drain passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "direct drainage of the flat site to facilitate the drainage of the flat site where rapid drainage is required in the first place while allowing the stored rainwater to be used as water as well as facilitating the maintenance and management of the facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101229485-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "to quickly drain without it being not cause any inconvenience caused to traffic and flooded with traffic accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the collecting basin 20 to block backflow and the collecting basin for dividing and filtering the soil sand and cigarette butts and rubbish mixed with rainwater or sewage so as to maintain a predetermined distance from the bottom and the side of the inside of the sump 20 in the rain gutter drain provided with 30 the sump 20 is of the upper and lower strait shape having a seating jaw 22b formed at the top edge of the entrance 22a to hang inside the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 of the manhole cover 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the simple manhole of the rain gutter drain according to the present invention the manhole cover 40 fixed to the upper end step surface 14 of the opening 12 of the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 and the manhole 10 mounted to a predetermined height inside to block the backflow of the sewage and backflow of odor and is installed to maintain a certain distance from the bottom and sides of the inside of the sump 20 the sand mixed in rainwater or sewage in the rain gutter sewer having a collecting cabinet 30 for dividing and filtering cigarette butts and garbage respectively the collecting well has a seating jaw at the upper edge of the entrance so as to be suspended inside the manhole through the support frame of the manhole cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100574280-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "referring to the effect of the present invention as described above while the rainwater is introduced into the freshwater lake the ground waste b is mixed together in the rainwater to block the inflow into the freshwater lake the worker is horizontal vertical strainer 1 3 will be moved to the site and assembled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "treatment facility for early rainfall using water retention and its methodthe present invention relates to an excellent treatment facility utilizing a disaster reservoir and a method of forming the same and more specifically to remove impurities in the initial rainwater and to settle the foreign matters to prevent the entry of foreign substances and debris into the reservoir and rivers it induces infiltration and natural purification to maintain the supply of groundwater smoothly and at the same time separates rainwater flowing into the initial rainfall and rainfall discharges or fresh water and minimizes the amount of rainwater remaining in the reservoir to corrupt or pest the present invention relates to a rainwater treatment facility and a method of forming the rainwater that can block breeding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "downstream of the water channel 400 is provided with a discharge portion 600 for discharging the initial excellent and rainwater from the reservoir 1 the discharge portion 600 may be configured to control the discharge amount or to block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102802400-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however since the drainage hole formed on the upper surface of the rainwater pipe block of the conventional road curb stone is formed horizontally to the road surface and covered with a metal grid not only is it difficult to drain the water quickly but the width of the road that can be used by vehicles is narrowed and when the road curb stone is damaged due to a vehicle accident the entire block that comprises the road curb stone and drainage pipe must be replaced and at night especially during heavy rain the positions of the road curb stone and the road cannot be clearly identified which poses a risk of accident"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101230730-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "according to the present invention as described above while planting vegetation on the side of the vegetation soil while water is continuously supplied to the vegetation through the water storage unit and the water supply surface rain water in the water storage unit through the water supply path formed in rain water by allowing heavy water to be filled such as eco friendly and continuous supply of moisture to the vegetation without additional management work it is very easy to maintain and manage the vegetation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a system to recycle rainwater the rainwater recycling system 100 includes a rainwater inlet grating 10 mounted on a surface of a road 8 to block inflow of large solids a solids removal screen 20 installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen 30 for removing fine solids in rainwater that has passed through the solids removing screen 20 an initial storm drain 40 for discharging rainwater containing pollutants on the road surface during initial stormwater an upper trench conduit 50 for storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration screen 30 a lower trench conduit 60 for storing rainwater flowing over from the upper trench conduit 50 a water purification filtration layer 70 formed on the upper and lower trench conduits 50 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainwater recycling system characterized in that consisting of a permeable layer 80 for introducing the rainwater flowing from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of recycling rainwater the rainwater recycling method includes mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block inflow of large solids into the rainwater inlet grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall recycled from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 storm water recycling method comprising the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the storm recycling method is mounted on the road surface to block the inflow of large solids by storm inflow grating a solids removing step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating to remove the medium solids flowing into the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits the rainwater flowing from the lower trench conduit flows into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "rainwater recycling system 100 of the present invention rainwater grating 10 is mounted on the surface of the road 8 to block the inflow of large solids a solids removal screen 20 installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen 30 for removing fine solids in rainwater that has passed through the solids removing screen 20 an initial storm drain 40 for discharging rainwater containing pollutants on the road surface during initial stormwater an upper trench conduit 50 for storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration screen 30 a lower trench conduit 60 for storing rainwater flowing over from the upper trench conduit 50 a water purification filtration layer 70 formed on the upper and lower trench conduits 50 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater it consists of a water permeable layer 80 for flowing rainwater flowing from the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand the storm recycling method th