t_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_203", "text": "in addition in the water flow circulation management method of the present invention may be configured to back convey the rainwater stored in the storage tank to the water permeable sidewalk block through the transfer pipe member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_204", "text": "in addition the storage of rainwater in the storage tank secures the amount of storage during the feng shui season and can also be utilized as the maintenance water for river maintenance or irrigation during the dry season thereby increasing the water resource circulation rate and maintaining the river ecological environment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101366083-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "10 to increase the filtration load of the filter mat 38 and the porous particulate filter 39 described above to shorten the replacement time or a relatively large amount of particulate contaminants introduced with the wash water rainwater that accumulates on the grid fixing plate 36 and blocks the openings and flows normally after the initial rainwater passes through the first filter mat 38 and the porous particulate media 39 and is filtered to pass through the water collecting inlet pipe 31"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 1030605 discloses a flat rectangular plate having a rectangular horizontal plate having a coupling groove at the center or both sides of the diagonal portion one lower end being coupled to the coupling groove of the plastic shaped support block to be coupled with the cast iron panel and the rectangular parallelepiped cast iron panel the straight connection joint for connecting the cast iron panels in parallel the right angle joint for connecting at right angles a cast iron panel assembly constituted by a joint joint connecting the upper and lower ends of the cast iron panel and connected to each other while being connected to each other a finishing cast iron panel coupled to an upper portion of the side wall cast iron panel and a finishing connection joint connecting the finishing cast iron panel and the side wall cast iron panel a rainwater storage tank is constructed by laying and laminating a sieve on the bottom of the rainwater storage tank group is a rainwater storage tank configured for worker access passage by assembling the cast iron panel assembly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 1030605the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems and it is an object of the present invention to prevent storm flooding by storing rainwater reduce load on a sewage treatment plant prevent urban heat island and replenish water resources the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a method of constructing a reservoir tank having a non point pollutant reduction type prefabricated reservoir block and a nonpoint source pollution reduction function using the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to purify rainwater collected in a storage tank and to provide it as a landscape water and a living water thereby preventing a water shortage phenomenon and a nonpoint pollution reduction high initial stormwater is stored in the reservoir and purified rainwater is discharged at the end of rainfall or gradually penetrated into the underground to prevent flood maintain groundwater level at a certain level to prevent ground stabilization and river pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "in this process the rainwater flows into the filtration column 130 through the filtration hole 131 of the filtration column 130 and the contaminants are filtered while passing through the filtration media 140"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is a facility to prevent the occurrence of bad smell and backflow from rainwater receiver installed on the roadside to inflow rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "according to claim 1 wherein the upper edge of the support block 10 is formed with a stepped jaw 11a on which the support plate 32 is seated while at the same time both sides of the inclined surface 12a toward the flow path of the central portion is formed to drain the odor and backflow prevention equipment of the rainwater receiving stand characterized in that the unit 20 is configured to be in close contact with the inclined plate 22a of the lower end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "odor and backflow prevention facility of road receiving stand preventing equipment for bad smell and backflow of rain receptacle the present invention relates to a facility for preventing bad smell and backflow of a road rainwater receiver which can induce and discharge rainwater through rainwater inlets installed on roadsides and continuously block bad odors and cope more effectively with backflow due to rainy season flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "2008 0067603 discloses a odor blocking device and rainwater backflow device for sewer manholes that continuously block the occurrence of odor generated in the manhole of the sewer and also cope sensitively with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "there was a problem of not being able to.the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above the object of the present invention is to ensure the maximum amount of water through the rain unit to the discharge pipe side through the drainage unit seated in the cover to ensure the maximum amount of water it is to provide a facility for preventing the smell and backflow of road rainwater receivers that can reliably block the outflow of odor due to wastewater and also effectively cope with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101907012-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "as described above in the detachable manhole multi screen system of the present invention a multi stage screen is installed in a manhole so as to prevent clogging of a drain pipe by filtering contaminants that are floated or swept away by rainwater or wastewater it is possible to separate and collect various sizes of impurities introduced together with the wastewater to block the inflow of the manholes into the drain hole thereby preventing the manholes and the drain holes from being clogged by the obstacles and easily removing and collecting the filtered contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889974-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent storage tank 100 which is embedded in the inside of the ground and receives stormwater introduced from the ground a grating 200 rotatably coupled to the upper surface of the superior storage tank 100 for introducing the stormwater into the storage tank and blocking the foreign material a dirt collecting box 400 provided in the superior storage tank 100 for filtering dirt contained in the rainwater and a collection box support 300 provided at an upper portion of the superior storage container 100 and supporting the dirt collection box 400 the storm reservoir 100 a reservoir body 110 in which the storm is stored a grating insert tube 120 formed on the upper portion of the reservoir body 110 and coupled to the grating 200 and a grating seating surface 121 formed on the boundary region between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 so as to be stepped inwardly in a predetermined area so that the grating 200 is seated and supported the grating 200 a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insertion tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 disposed in the grating frame 210 at predetermined intervals in the longitudinal direction and having irregularities formed on the upper surface thereof to block rainwater from the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter a plurality of reinforcing frames 230 arranged in the grating frame 210 in a lateral direction at regular intervals a plurality of protrusions protruding from the ground at a predetermined interval in the lower portion of the outer reinforcing frame 230a to allow the gravel to flow into the gap between the grating insert tube 120 and the grating frame 210 and includes a soil inflow tooth 240 the height of the earth inflow tooth 240 and the height of the outer reinforcement frame 230a may be greater than the height of the reinforcement frame 230 located inside the outer reinforcement frame 230a and the reinforcing frame 230 is formed at the same height as the reinforcing frame 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416889-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "therefore the rainwater and sewage that did not flow into the upper portion of the trench cover 31 are diverted to the manhole 20 through the boundary block so that the rainwater and sewage that do not flow through the trench cover 31 flow into other adjacent areas"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the device installed in the large sewer or the catchment inlet of the rainwater manhole to block backflow of various odors and insects the base bottom plate 4 and the base bottom plate 4 having a rectangular long plate shape side vertical plates 5a and 5b integrally attached to both ends of the left and right sides and the front and rear and the top is open but the base seating plate in the outward direction on the upper end of the side vertical plates 5a 5b 6a 6b is formed integrally projecting to the base portion 2 to be fastened to the engaging jaw 7 of the sump 3 and to the open front and rear of the base portion 2 the left assembly fastener 10 and the right assembly fastener 11 each of which is to be assembled and symmetrical in shape respectively wherein the left assembly fastener 10 and the right assembly fastener 11 are respectively inclined downward at one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "a device inserted into a large sewer or a rainwater inlet of a rainwater manhole to block backflow of various odors and bugs the base bottom plate 4 being horizontally positioned in a rectangular long plate shape and provided with the base"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "quot the base portion to form a shape the assembly portion is to be assembled to each of the open front and rear surfaces of the base portion and the sewage inlet is formed in the part assembled to abut the base portion it is attached to the sewage inlet of the odor prevention device which is configured to block backflow of odor from the inside of the sump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "is attached to the assembly hook 9 and the sewage inlet 16 of the assembly hook 9 to prevent odors from the inside of the sump 3 from being reversed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102676884-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the packing ring 30 is inserted into the packing coupling groove 14 formed in the protective cover 100 when the auxiliary cover 200 closes the opening 10 thereby forming a tight seal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100710632-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore in order to prevent the backflow of the odor the vinyl bag may be covered on the grating of the drain but in case of sudden rain the plastic bag may block the drain of the rainwater which may prevent the rainwater from draining and cause a safety accident due to the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218344-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to prevent the re injury of the sediment which is a disadvantage of the swirl method by applying the anti floating means the filtration tank equipped with the filtration means is separately installed to separate the vortex and the laminar flow forming tank capable of forming the laminar flow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102227198-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "to this end although not shown in the drawing the rainwater pipe connected to the storage tank 10 may be provided with a pollution detection sensor that detects the degree of contamination of incoming rainwater and a shut off valve module that blocks the inflow of rainwater from the rainwater pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102227198-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "at this time the shut off valve module may block the inflow of rainwater from the rainwater pipe when it is determined that rainwater flowing through the rainwater pipe is contaminated above a reference value based on the detection information detected by the pollution detection sensor"}]</data>
</edge>
