  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore by the rainwater collecting well 10 of the present invention the initial rainwater is discharged through the drain pipe 11 and the rainwater having a low degree of contamination can be discharged through the collecting pipe 16 to store more clean rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101987814-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "as another modification of the present invention an auxiliary pipe is further connected between the storage tank and the backwash water tank and a hand pump is mounted on the auxiliary pipe.as described above according to the present invention the backwashing function is normally maintained even when the raw water is not continuously supplied in the course of processing the initial rainwater with high contamination degree thereby improving the economical efficiency and the efficiency of labor saving.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100744631-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "hydrologic control unit for adjusting the connected via the plurality of chlorine ion meter and wired and wireless communication means and stores the concentration data received from the chlorine ion meter and to identify the variation in the water quality compared to the comparative chlorine ion concentration data stored in the database and stores the result a main server for outputting and transmitting to a remote place and a management server connected to the main server through a wired wireless communication means and controlling the operation of the water level or the sewage treatment plant of the reservoir into which the initial rainwater flows in accordance with the change in the water quality of the initial rainwater transmitted from the main server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102606021-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in addition cleaning work to regularly remove sediment must be performed frequently but since the concrete blocks are small it is impossible for workers to enter the storage tank and thus cannot be cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224234-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "according to the initial rainwater storage system using the storage tank of the present invention the sewage and the initial rainwater on the sewage that is installed in a number of small rivers at a certain distance is collected and collected but the sewage is directly directed to the sewage terminal treatment plant through the sewer drainage rainwater is collected in the storage tanks buried in the main stream of the main stream and discharged for a long time below the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant after rainy weather to prevent contamination of small rivers and main streams and there is no need to add more facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238199-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition the existing rainwater storage tank made of pp material has a problem that it is difficult to maintain such as removing sludge accumulated inside and the conventional rainwater storage tank has high surface contamination and bioactivity and when the stored rainwater is left for a long time rainwater was contaminated due to the occurrence of microorganisms had a problem that the use of stored rainwater is extremely limited"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826790-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "at the upper part a sloping induction plate is installed at the tip of the first drainage guide plate a second settling filtration tank for blocking inflow of fine contaminants accompanied by the storm and having a filter net installed on the downflow channel formed by the lower part of the precipitation inducing plate and the first drainage guide plate to remove the dissolved fine contaminants a second rim hole formed in the upper portion of the first drainage guide plate of the secondary settling filtration tank and having a second rim hole and a second rim hole formed in the second rim of the second settling filtration tank the second partition wall is provided with a drain plate for partitioning the space with the second settling filtration tank and discharging the rainwater having an inclined surface at the inlet side and flowing into the second rinse hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102281312-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "therefore as ultraviolet rays are irradiated to the rainwater stored in the storage tank 10 various water contaminants such as microorganisms or bacteria contained in the rainwater stored in the storage tank 10 are sterilized by ultraviolet rays"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102281312-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "due to the instantaneous pressure and discharge it is finely pulverized and stabilized while exerting a strong cleaning power thereby preventing contamination of the inside of the storage tank 10 and the rainwater stored inside the storage tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text":