id": "US-12338143-B2", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the collection of rainwater is of particular interest because it is naturally distilled and because ocean air has fewer atmospheric contaminants as compared to air over populated areas"}, {"pat_id": "US-12338143-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "in one embodiment a method of collecting water is disclosed comprising modifying a waterborne vessel for the purposes of collecting rainwater wherein the vessel comprises a plurality of storage compartments a retractable cover a plurality of collectors and an onboard microfiltration system collecting rainwater providing a porous filter cover to the storage compartments to protect the collected rainwater from contamination applying a retractable non porous cover over the collected rainwater so as to prevent evaporation and providing a plumbing medium so as to filter the collected rainwater through a microfiltration system prior to being offloaded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101208694-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the blockage of the filter media is frequent the filtration efficiency is lowered there is a need for frequent backwashing there was a problem such that the function of storm water storage facilities to prevent the contamination of the river water is not properly performed.the present invention has been made to solve the conventional problems as described above can improve the excellent filtration efficiency and recycling degree can improve the backwashing efficiency during the backwashing of the first filtration unit and the washing of the reservoir it is possible to reduce the sludge sedimentation on the bottom surface while facilitating the drainage of washing water at the same time to perform additional filtration of rainwater without additional power and to prevent the re injury of sediment deposited on the floor surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101038336-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "by dispersing rainwater it is possible to prevent flooding of roads and low lying houses and to help counter flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102387766-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "according to the odor prevention device for a sewage pipe according to the present invention it is elastically installed in an existing or new grouting manhole and since it blocks the communication path with the sewage pipe with a limited drainage function of rainwater it is easy to install in response to manholes of various structures while the installation work is simple the facility cost is greatly reduced and the manhole s own drainage function is maintained while preventing contamination of the surrounding area due to bad odors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102387766-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "corresponding to the manhole it is easy to install and easy to install and it is possible to significantly reduce the cost of equipment and to prevent contamination of the surroundings due to odor while maintaining the drainage function of the manhole itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100893952-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in this case since the rainwater continuously passes through the filter cartridge when heavy heavy rain or heavy rain occurs a backflow phenomenon occurs due to an overload and the rainwater cannot be purified but it flows directly into the river where the bridge is installed and the river is flowed into the vehicle s oil or metal powder tire powder or ascon oil on the bridge road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102342900-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a housing 191 having an end of the inlet pipe 199 into which raw water is introduced is installed at the upper end and a door 192 is installed on one side to be able to open and close and is movably installed inside the housing 191 one side an initial foreign material removal unit 190 comprising a moving box 193 having a plurality of drain holes 194 formed therein and a drain pipe 100 connected to the bottom of the housing 191 a separation box 110 connected to the end of the drain pipe 100 and provided with a detection sensor 120 for detecting the contamination state of raw water at the inlet side a bypass pipe 130 installed on one side of the separation box 110 the removal box 161 installed at the end of the bypass pipe 130 to remove the solid foreign matter contained in the raw water and the inside of the removal box 161 are buried in the removal box 161 to separate the solid a foreign material consisting of a removal conveyor 162 that blocks the movement of foreign substances to the rear end and a removal motor 163 that rotates the removal conveyor 162 so that the solid foreign material blocked by the removal conveyor 162 is discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102342900-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "an initial foreign material removal unit installed and comprising a mobile box having a plurality of drain holes formed on one side thereof and a drain pipe connected to the lower surface of the housing a separation box connected to the end of the drain pipe and installed with a detection sensor for detecting contamination of raw water at the inlet side a bypass pipe installed on one side of the separation box a removal box installed at the end of the bypass pipe to remove the solid foreign material contained in the raw water and a removal conveyor that is embedded in the removal box so that the inside of the removal box is separated to block the movement of the solid foreign material to the rear end and a foreign material removal unit comprising a removal motor rotating the removal conveyor so that the solid foreign material blocked by the removal conveyor is discharged to the outside an initial filter installed on the exit side of the foreign material removal unit and in which sand and activated carbon are sequentially stacked an induction pipe installed on the exit side of the initial filter to supply the initial rainwater to the raw water storage tank a supply pipe for supplying the raw water passing through the separation box to the raw water storage tank a rotary bulkhead rotatably installed inside the separation box so that the inlet pipe passes through either side of the bypass pipe or the supply pipe and a control unit that receives the detection value of the detection sensor and operates the driving motor to rotate the rotary partition wall.as described above the present invention detects the contamination state of raw water flowing in from the outside and separately treats raw water initial rainwater or wastewater that contains a large amount of solid foreign substances and is heavily polluted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102342900-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "this will allow for the rapid treatment of large volumes of sewage.100 drain pipe 110 separation box 120 detection sensor 130 bypass pipe 140 supply pipe 150 control unit 160 foreign material removal unit 170 initial filter 171 sand 172 activated carbon 180 guide tube 190 initial foreign matter removal unit 191 housing 192 door 193 moving box 194 drain hole 199 inlet pipe 200 drive motor 210 rotating bulkhead"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102553182-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "a water storage tank 220 may be included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101778786-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the initial storm having a high contamination degree from being supplied to the sedimentation tank guide pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the first object of the present invention due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rain the initial rainwater that has not been purified to exceed the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage terminal treatment plant is discharged to the stream it is to provide an initial excellent storage processing system using a storage tank to prevent the contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101101703-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to effectively purify the rainwater having a high degree of contamination and to variably mount the biostone storage means by the rack and the rack support frame thereby simplifying the installation and removal in the filtration tank and the long term rainwater filtration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101768117-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "as a result pollution sources included in the initial rainwater and the cleaning water can be guided to the sewage pipe rather than the gutter pipe thereby preventing contamination of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102479290-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore the storage tank only serves to prevent flooding by temporarily storing rainwater but it is difficult to reuse the stored rainwater because the water quality is not good"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "thus when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102135152-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "one end 51 may be opened toward the lower side so as to flow the rainwater into the secondary collecting means 30 and may include a bent portion 57"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894740-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the present invention various foreign substances and harmful components contained in the rainwater can be filtered by the filtration unit provided in the water hole of the manhole main body thereby contributing to prevention of contamination of the groundwater and removal of foreign matter is facilitated by the replacement structure of the filtration unit and has a useful effect of securing convenience of cleaning and maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684272-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rainwater storage bin with a structure where the bottom and sides are closed and the top is open forming a rainwater storage space inside to collect and store rainwater a cover plate that is installed to cover and seal the upper surface of the rainwater storage box has a plurality of rainwater inlet holes formed through it to guide rainwater to the rainwater storage space and has a plurality of wick exposure holes through which a wick is installed it consists of a wick installed through the wick exposure hole to absorb rainwater stored in the rainwater storage space and guide it to the upper surface of the cover plate after covering the rainwater storage box with a cover plate and installing a wick vegetation is planted on the cover plate and installed on the roof of the building to realize rooftop greening and improve the urban heat island the wick is made of non woven fabric and is manufactured by impregnating it with a treatment solution and drying it to increase antibacterial properties heat insulation adhesion fixation and anti contamination properties the treatment solution contains 5.5 by weight of hydroxyproline 4.5 by weight of triclosan 3.5 by weight of sodium methylsiliconate 3.0 by weight of sodium orthosilicate a green roof module responsive to heat reduction requirements characterized by 2.5 by weight of prostaglandin and the remainder being polyurethane resin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "since the penetration and storage tank for water circulation according to one embodiment of the present invention are light in weight and can be fastened in an assembly type the construction work is easy and they are treated with nano silver so rain water can be maintained for a long time we have a hybrid hybrid reinforced structural system that significantly reduces rainwater contamination due to microbe generation etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow regulating tank for storing effluent treated and discharged in the sewage treatment plant a reaction tank connected to the flow rate adjusting tank and having an inlet reaction tank and an oxidation tank communicated with each other an ultra fine bubble generating unit for generating ultra bubbles after supplying ozone to the process water introduced from the flow rate adjusting tank or the inflow reaction tank and supplying the bubbles to a lower region of the oxidation reaction tank the treatment water treated in the oxidation reaction tank flows through an advection tube provided in a region below the water surface of the oxidation reaction tank and contacts with the foamed filter material for inducing the contact reaction of the hydrophilicized polymer material by the ozone a reaction tank and a treatment water tank into which the treated water treated in the contact reaction tank flows wherein the inlet reaction tank and the oxidation reaction tank are separated from each other through a partition wall the partition wall is spaced apart from the bottom surface of the reaction tank to form a spacing space and through the passage provided by the spacing space a pressure is generated in the lower direction of the oxidation reaction tank by the flow of the treatment water which is reversely circulated in the oxidation reaction tank and flows into the lower region of the oxidation reaction tank by the pressure in the lower direction the rate of rise of minute bubbles in the water is delayed and the rate of dissolution of the minute bubbles is increased and the treatment water in which the residence time in the oxidation reaction tank is increased due to the delay of the floatation rate is passed through the advection tube is introduced into the contact reaction tank wherein the foamed filter medium is disposed at a middle portion of the contact reaction tank the treated water is introduced into the upper portion of the contact reaction tank and flows in the lower direction and passes through the foamed filter medium further comprising an air supply unit for supplying air to the lower portion of the foamed filter medium to induce the floating of the sludge deposited on the foamed filter medium when the foamed filter medium is occluded by the sludge wherein the treatment tank is provided with an advection pipe having an a shaped structure at one side of the upper part of the contact reaction tank and treatment water staying in the contact reaction tank lower region passing through the foamed filter medium in the contact reaction tank through the admission pipe and a rainwater reservoir for storing incoming rainwater and further comprising an inflow control unit for allowing the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank to flow into the inflow reaction tank or the treatment water tank depending on the degree of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 153 may flow into the inflow reaction tank 131 or the treatment water tank 160 depending on the degree of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102227198-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "to this end although not shown in the drawing the rainwater pipe connected to the storage tank 10 may be provided with a pollution detection sensor that detects the degree of contamination of incoming rainwater and a shut off valve module that blocks the inflow of rainwater from the rainwater pipe"}]</data>
</edge>
