  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100877621-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above the problem to be solved by the present invention but before the introduction into the screen tank of the wastewater treatment device to install a collecting basin to remove the contaminants and soils in advance the catchment is to provide an ozone oxidation type wastewater treatment device that is reinforced with a pretreatment process to be treated regardless of the amount of wastewater including rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100877621-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the cover of the sump is characterized in that formed of a transparent body that can identify the inside of the tank.according to the ozone oxidation type wastewater treatment device which strengthens the pretreatment process of the present invention the pretreatment can be treated irrespective of the amount of wastewater including rainwater in which a collecting basin which removes contaminants and soils in the pretreatment stage before entering the screen tank is treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101782356-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 1617616 registered on april 27 2016 a problem to be solved by the present invention is that there is no need for a separate equipment installation space in a swimming pool a water purification plant a wastewater treatment plant a sewage treatment plant discharge tank a rainwater reuse facility and the like requiring chlorination and oxidation decomposition of pollutants in water the present invention provides an electrode module for water treatment which has a large electrode installation area per unit volume and does not require any auxiliary equipment such as a pump and a water treatment system employing the electrode module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101782356-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the present invention relates to a method for directly supplying electrolytic chlorine to a water tank in a swimming pool a water purification plant a wastewater treatment plant a sewage treatment plant discharge tank and a rainwater reuse facility requiring chlorination and oxidation decomposition of water pollutants the present invention provides an electrode module for water treatment capable of electrolytically disinfecting an electrolytic chlorine tank on the upper part without requiring an additional facility and supplying an electrode into the water tank and supplying brine and air and a water treatment system employing the electrode module the maintenance is simple and the operation is economical"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101174757-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "as described above it is possible to easily manufacture high quality drinking water by the effect of oxidation and coagulation in the line mixer so that ground water surface water rainwater etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100751233-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "rainwater which is free of organic matter and the pollutant load fluctuation is mitigated by the installation of rainwater rainwater without organic matter and the second flocculation tank is used to control the flow rate of sewage and to induce oxidation and decomposition of microorganisms the treated water was removed by sand filtration using a pump and ultrafiltered water treated first in a microfilter it is possible to carry out advanced treatment by using a membrane and it is possible to carry out antibacterial and deodorization by using a carbon filter while maintaining the filter clean by high pressure backwashing and chlorination thereby increasing the life and efficiency the present invention relates to an ultrafiltration type heavy water treatment apparatus capable of preventing the above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the initial rainwater introduced into the rainwater toil 210 is introduced into the septic tank 30 and the initial rainwater introduced into the septic tank 30 is a series of decay tanks 31 a filtration tank 32 an oxidation tank 33 and and is stored in the storage tank 40 in a purified state via the disinfection tank 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177676-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "when freezing and raining due to the rainy season or weather changes in summer rainwater has been introduced into the water meter protection tank which has been a cause of oxidation and corrosion of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399489-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the wastewater treatment apparatus using ozone comprising a collecting tank ozone generator ozone oxidation tank pressurized flotation tank pressure filter sludge collector and treated water tank a screen tank installed at all stages of the collection tank and integrally including a filtering means consisting of a flow blocking valve and an activated carbon fiber double screen to block unnecessary rainwater mixing an ozone oxidation tank for forming a vortex through the swirl flow multi contact device to increase the contact between the ozone supplied from the ozone generator and the waste water supplied from the collecting tank an improved ozonation type wastewater treatment apparatus for strengthening the pretreatment process comprising a pressurized floatation tank integrally containing a microbubble type ceramic spraying unit for microbubbling the dissolved air supplied by the eject"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200399489-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at the same time the present invention relates to an improved ozone oxidation wastewater treatment system that has enhanced the pretreatment process to improve the facility margin and contaminant removal rate according to the effect of reducing pollutant load in the downstream equipment by performing the pretreatment process to filter foreign substances such as contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100950100-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "it inhibits the activity and stores it and when it is discharged it adds the optimal amount of oxidizing agent to induce the oxidation of organic substances and odorous substances present in the conduit p"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435202-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an ecological pond created by supplying collected rainwater a circulation pump operated by a control unit to circulate the supernatant water of the ecological pond through a treatment water line a primary filter installed in the treated water line to remove relatively large contaminants soil and suspended solids a second filter installed at the rear of the primary filter to remove fine turbidity components and to adsorb and remove organic matter and suspended particles and ecological pond water treatment apparatus comprising an advanced oxidation treatment device for sterilizing disinfecting the second filtered supernatant water again by using ultraviolet and ozone"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the artificial wetland which can simultaneously process the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow of the present invention consists of an inflow culvert a wetland space and an outflow culvert the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow from the inflow culvert in the artificial wetland discharged and discharged to the effluent effluent after discharge into the effluent effluent the inflow water consisting of the normal base flow and the rainfall rainfall part of the design rainfall output wqv including nitrogen and organic matter from the inlet culvert a first wetland intake channel connected between the inlet culvert and a wetland space to be introduced into the wetland space deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "meanwhile when it rains rains the rainwater flows into the pretreatment unit as the water to be treated but the first passage is closed the second passage is open the introduced water to be treated passes through the pretreatment unit and flows into the non point pollutant filtration unit through the second passage to remove non point pollutants and the water to be treated from which the non point pollutants have been removed flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit through the third passage to be purified and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow regulating tank for storing effluent treated and discharged in the sewage treatment plant a reaction tank connected to the flow rate adjusting tank and having an inlet reaction tank and an oxidation tank communicated with each other an ultra fine bubble generating unit for generating ultra bubbles after supplying ozone to the process water introduced from the flow rate adjusting tank or the inflow reaction tank and supplying the bubbles to a lower region of the oxidation reaction tank the treatment water treated in the oxidation reaction tank flows through an advection tube provided in a region below the water surface of the oxidation reaction tank and contacts with the foamed filter material for inducing the contact reaction of the hydrophilicized polymer material by the ozone a reaction tank and a treatment water tank into which the treated water treated in the contact reaction tank flows wherein the inlet reaction tank and the oxidation reaction tank are separated from each other through a partition wall the partition wall is spaced apart from the bottom surface of the reaction tank to form a spacing space and through the passage provided by the spacing space a pressure is generated in the lower direction of the oxidation reaction tank by the flow of the treatment water which is reversely circulated in the oxidation reaction tank and flows into the lower region of the oxidation reaction tank by the pressure in the lower direction the rate of rise of minute bubbles in the water is delayed and the rate of dissolution of the minute bubbles is increased and the treatment water in which the residence time in the oxidation reaction tank is increased due to the delay of the floatation rate is passed through the advection tube is introduced into the contact reaction tank wherein the foamed filter medium is disposed at a middle portion of the contact reaction tank the treated water is introduced into the upper portion of the contact reaction tank and flows in the lower direction and passes through the foamed filter medium further comprising an air supply unit for supplying air to the lower portion of the foamed filter medium to induce the floating of the sludge deposited on the foamed filter medium when the foamed filter medium is occluded by the sludge wherein the treatment tank is provided with an advection pipe having an a shaped structure at one side of the upper part of the contact reaction tank and treatment water staying in the contact reaction tank lower region passing through the foamed filter medium in the contact reaction tank through the admission pipe and a rainwater reservoir for storing incoming rainwater and further comprising an inflow control unit for allowing the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank to flow into the inflow reaction tank or the treatment water tank depending on the degree of contamination"}]</data>
