  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101080363-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however since there is no separate facility to remove these floats in the general water well problems such as impeller blockage due to the floats occur during the operation of the drainage pump resulting in damage of the motor due to the motor overload of the drainage pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "at this time the collecting net 34 to filter the bulky cigarette butts and trash which is mixed in the rainwater or sewage and the mud trap portion 38 to the rainwater or sewage flowing through the collecting net 34 by sedimenting the mixed bulky soil sand cigarette butts garbage and soil sand do not accumulate on the bottom of the manhole 10 thereby preventing the blockage of sewer pipes in advance so that the sewage flow is smooth and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101136508-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "miscellaneous goods such as vinyl are accumulated excessively and sewage it is a defect that the rainwater overflows or reflows easily even in small rainfall due to the blockage and it loses the function of the drainage channel and debris such as fallen leaves accumulated in the rain gutter structure is destroyed causing severe odor or surrounding sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102789466-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "10 2014 0012031 title blockage prevention road drainage facility 2014.02.03 as announced in the official gazette includes a bypass drain installed at a location where a curbstone has been removed a manhole is installed at the edge of a road adjacent to the curbstone and the manhole has a bypass groove formed by removing a portion of an upper portion of a surface facing the curbstone to a set width and the bypass drain comprises a rectangular parallelepiped body having an empty interior an inlet formed in an upper portion of a surface facing the manhole of the body into which rainwater flows in an inlet formed at a lower portion of the inlet portion and fitted into the bypass groove of the manhole and formed by opening and protruding a portion of a surface located at a lower portion of the inlet portion on the surface facing the manhole so that rainwater flowing in through the inlet portion passes through an internal space of the body and is discharged to the lower portion of the manhole thereby flowing into a drainage pipe installed underground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200181883-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "it is designed to prevent clogging of gravel layer by blocking pipes of solids garbage gravel sand contained in rainwater.the present invention forms a plurality of through holes 2 in the rain pipe 1 and each through hole 2 is provided with a penetrating hole 3 having a filter 6 foreign matter contained in the rainwater rubble 14 by preventing the inflow into the water by preventing the blockage of the permeable ground rubble to improve the excellent water permeation function to prevent the overflow of the river and also to easily combine the coupling case 5 to the fixed case 4 it can be easy to install the filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a pipe blockage prediction system a central control system that can predict the possibility of blockage in each section of the pipe by measuring the water level in each section of the pipe by utilizing the fact that the water level in the vicinity of the pipeline where sediment is accumulated and the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100772481-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition since the rainwater penetrates into the surrounding ground directly from the rainwater infiltration drainage hole the blockage occurs due to sand contained in the rainwater being stored in the rainwater infiltration drainage hole and the penetration capability is lowered due to the blockage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100772481-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "therefore when penetrating through the permeable sheet and into the ground on the outside the penetration ability due to the blockage of the pores does not decrease"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783964-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "accordingly by forming the above mentioned drainage expansion port 6 in an l shape the rainwater inside the water conduit body 2 can be discharged more smoothly toward the ground filter 5 through the initial rainwater discharge port 222 formed horizontally penetrating the side wall 22 of the water conduit body 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563950-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "it is formed and characterized in that it includes a contaminant removal unit provided to selectively inject high pressure fluid toward the top.the device for preventing clogging of sewage gratings according to the present invention has an effect of temporarily solving clogging of drain gratings.1 is a cross sectional view of a conventional drain box and grating structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102778604-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "5 and 6 in the case where the drain hole 21 is blocked due to foreign matter on the upper portion of the water collecting grating 20 rainwater or sewage flows down through the slope guides 25 formed at both ends of the water collecting grating 20 to maintain the side drainage performance due to the blockage of the upper drain hole 21"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100749128-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "filter bag 80 is provided in the frame 71 of the filter to filter the foreign matter contained in the rainwater flowing into the sump 20 by removing the foreign matter contained in the rainwater it is possible to provide a sewage line structure for sludge removal to prevent sewer pipe blockage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101375866-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "when discharged through the inside of the second drain pipe the upstream and downstream flow is repeated downward to prevent the blockage of the filter medium characterized in that the initial rainwater treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200373653-Y1", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "on the other hand in the rainwater soil chamber 20 in which the control device is installed since the gate 51 is normally open at all times there is no fear of blockage due to coarse suspended matter and all the initial water having high water quality is collected and only the flow rate to be collected in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102634268-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "in other words by further improving the separation efficiency of foreign substances in the main manhole 110 itself it is possible to reduce loads such as pipe blockage at the rear end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102634268-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "this is to control device failure due to pipe blockage by blocking the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200208312-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "when the sediment is separated by stages through the fine holes of the primary filtration network and the bottom plate to provide a rainwater catchment for the road equipped with a filtration tank to prevent the drainage blockage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7161243-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "becomes larger than necessary the cost of sewage treatment is high and the sediment around the sewer pipe may flow into the sewer pipe causing road subsidence and pipe blockage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784989-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in treating rainwater containing a large amount of turbidity a blockage due to a large amount of turbidity may occur in the chamber portion 210 of the vortex valve so that an outflow downstream from the rainwater discharge portion 130 of the manhole body may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200151725-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in addition the upper part of the drainage channel was reveted to prevent vehicle accidents and blockage of the channel by foreign substances and soil and instead water collectors were installed at regular intervals so that rainwater flowed into the drainage channel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200303595-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole drainage blockage preventing device to collect the rainwater or sewage and to prevent foreign substances from entering the clogged drainage pipe of the manhole discharged to the sewer pipe connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102770805-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however in the case of the infiltration trench system according to the conventional technology as time passes after being constructed underground fine pollutants may accumulate during the infiltration process of rainwater which may cause the pores of the infiltration layer 2 to become clogged and furthermore the buried perforated infiltration pipe 3 with side holes may also become clogged or have their side holes blocked which may cause the overall performance of the infiltration trench system to deteriorate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102770805-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "20 0393019 announced on august 17 2005 .the present invention has been developed to overcome the limitations of the prior art as described above and when fine pollutants accumulate during the infiltration process of rainwater over time after construction in an infiltration trench system causing pore blockage in the infiltration layer and blockage of the buried perforated infiltration pipe the purpose of the present invention is to provide a realistic and practical method capable of quickly easily and efficiently solving the problem of pore blockage in the infiltration layer and blockage of the buried perforated infiltration pipe in the field"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "rainwater generated on the road surface in rainy weather is filled with the water tank 132 the center of gravity is moved to one side end and made of a blocking plate opening and closing member 130 to open the blocking plate 120 the normal blocking plate 120 blocks the drain 10 so that foreign substances flowing into the road surface of the road are blocked from entering the drain 10 so that the drainage blockage is blocked by foreign substances and the blocking plate 120 has its frame 110 is installed with a height corresponding to the upper edge of the grate 100 not only can be easily cleaned up by cleaning the foreign matter accumulated on the grate 100 but also on the grate 100 when cleaning with a cleaning car the foreign material has an advantage that the cleaning work by the cleaning car is easy to move away from the grating 100 the cleaning plate is stable structure because the blocking plate 120 is not opened by the pressure applied from the cleaning brush when cleaning the cleaning car it is possible to carry out the odor generated from the sewer and prevents the complaints caused by the inflow of odors from the residential area adjacent to the road and improves the market competitiveness by securing the reliability of the product"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "method of monitoring drainage systems of rainwater reservoirs wherein a drainage pipe with which a throttling member is associated is associated with the rainwater reservoir and wherein the flow of sewage through the drainage pipe serving to divert sewage from the rainwater reservoir can be restricted to a predetermined nominal value characterised in that the flow through the drainage pipe is monitored to determine whether a predetermined excessively high value has been exceeded and or in that if the flow through the drainage pipe is restricted in a controlled manner to a predetermined nominal value monitoring is carried out to determine whether excessively rapidly succeeding changes in the direction of travel by the throttling member are effected by the controller and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether the water level in the rainwater reservoir or in a feed channel preceding the rainwater reservoir exceeds a predetermined depth while at the same time a predetermined low value for the flow through the drainage pipe is fallen below resulting in a blockage of the drainage pipe at this water level and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether permanent tightening of the throttling member is occurring and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether the actuator of the throttling member is overloaded and if so the throttling member is transferred into a safety position preventing the nominal value of the flow through the drainage pipe from being exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "monitoring arrangement for drainage systems of rainwater reservoirs for carrying out the method according to one of claims 1 to 3 characterised in that the monitoring arrangement 25 comprises first monitoring means which respond in a predetermined manner if a predetermined excessively high value of the flow through the drainage pipe is exceeded and or second monitoring means which respond in a predetermined manner to excessively rapidly succeeding changes of direction of travel by the throttling member caused by the controller if the flow through the drainage pipe 13 is restricted in controlled manner to a predetermined nominal value and or third monitoring means which detect if the water level in the rainwater reservoir or in a feed channel 11 preceding the rainwater reservoir exceeds a predetermined depth while at the same time a predetermined low value of the flow through the drainage pipe 13 is fallen below implying a blockage of the drainage point with this water level and or fourth monitoring means which respond to permanent tightening of the throttling member and or fifth monitoring means which respond to overloading of the actuator of the throttling member 14 and as a result of this response trigger a transfer of the throttling member into a safety position preventing the nominal value of the flow through the drainage pipe from being exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore coarse filth containing large amounts of stones and automobile residues contained in the initial rainwater or rainwater downstream flows into the coarse filth filter network 96 by the horizontal collecting plate 94 and undergoes a filtration process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101208694-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the blockage of the filter media is frequent the filtration efficiency is lowered there is a need for frequent backwashing there was a problem such that the function of storm water storage facilities to prevent the contamination of the river water is not properly performed.the present invention has been made to solve the conventional problems as described above can improve the excellent filtration efficiency and recycling degree can improve the backwashing efficiency during the backwashing of the first filtration unit and the washing of the reservoir it is possible to reduce the sludge sedimentation on the bottom surface while facilitating the drainage of washing water at the same time to perform additional filtration of rainwater without additional power and to prevent the re injury of sediment deposited on the floor surface"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "failure of the discharge pump or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102371298-B1", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "in addition there is an effect of preventing blockage of the inflow tank 210 by preventing rainwater passing through the rectification box 120 from directly overflowing into the inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}]</data>
</edge>
