  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in claim 1 or 2 a grating for a rainwater drain capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention characterized in that the support rods forming the grating in the form of a grid structure of the above mentioned fixed grating and the lifting grating are formed below the upper surface of the grid plate thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "2 to 5 the support bar 60b forming the grating in the form of a grid structure of the fixed grating 60 and the lifting grating 50 described above is formed below the upper surface of the grid plate 60a thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "at this time since the upper surfaces of the fixed grating 60 and the lifting grating 50 described above are formed in a block like gently curved shape and the support rod 60b forming the grating in a grid like shape is formed to be positioned lower than the upper surface of the grid plate 60a it is possible to minimize the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating and it is possible to induce the various sediments to be pushed along the gently curved upper surface of the grating by the current of water and to flow down through the rainwater drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "according to the grating for a rainwater drainage ditch capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention according to the embodiment of the present specification as described above in normal times when it does not rain or when the amount of rainfall is small the elevating 