  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-2948204-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "highway steel pier high because many are large and the volume of the hollow part is large suitable for storing large amounts of water many in urban areas highway steel piers may be used effectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100782992-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "an object of the present invention is to solve the above problems the object of the present invention is to add a silicate mineral powder as a mixing material when manufacturing the storage tank of the cement due to the strong adsorption power and the large anion effect released by the silicate mineral it is to provide a low toxic concrete rainwater storage tank that can effectively neutralize the toxicity to prevent pollution of rivers public waters or the ocean by the toxic discharge of cement and to prevent the corrosion of rebar due to the phenomena"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100782992-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "can be neutralized as well as the strong anion various components of the cement by a substitution capacity having at the same time eliminating the alkaline toxic irritant odor of the cement are clay minerals and water hydroxyl groups causing the hydration reaction oh to a strong reduction of the ion therefore it is possible to effectively prevent the end of the whitening phenomenon in the cement to further reduce the toxicity of the cement and to significantly delay the corrosion of the steel reinforcement embedded in the concrete structure thereby improving the durability of the overall low toxic concrete rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100782992-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "provided is a low toxic concrete rainwater storage tank that can prevent pollution of rivers public waters or the ocean due to toxic emissions and can prevent corrosion of rebar due to bleaching"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6164161-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "furthermore it is possible to prevent rainwater including condensation dust and the like from accumulating inside the welded portion between the water storage tank 10 and the valve chamber 30 52 and causing corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_117", "text": "in addition the protrusions 3 may discharge air through the air discharge part 33 and use stainless steel among metals to prevent corrosion due to rust by rainwater flowing from the rainwater inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_154", "text": "and the protrusion 3 is in the inner space 31 through the air outlet 33 air is discharged and it is preferable to use stainless steel among metals to prevent corrosion by rust due to inflow of rainwater from the rainwater inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177676-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "when freezing and raining due to the rainy season or weather changes in summer rainwater has been introduced into the water meter protection tank which has been a cause of oxidation and corrosion of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition it is a system that physically stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank without electronic devices by utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater thereby reducing maintenance costs and providing a physical rainwater utilization system that does not require frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "the physical rainwater utilization system according to the present invention is a system that stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank by a physical method without electronic devices utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater and has the advantage of reducing maintenance costs and not requiring frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200434172-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in addition the square frame 11 the pair of opening and closing plate 15 the hinge shaft fixing block 12 the hinge shaft 13 and the shaft support portion 18 may be made of stainless steel or synthetic resin with high corrosion resistance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449090-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in order to solve this problem it is a device to prevent the backflow of sewage odors to the manhole and the rainwater smoothly flows into the sewer pipe and in the absence of rainwater it blocks the inlet through which rainwater flows into the atmosphere from the sewer pipe or manhole bucket"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the entry of rainwater into the water leveling protector 10 thereby providing a special effect of effectively preventing corrosion and rusting of the water stop valve 7 due to rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783926-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a synthetic resin formwork pipe for protecting a concrete water channel which is installed in close contact with the inner surface of a concrete water channel to substantially form a flow path for rainwater to flow through thereby preventing damage such as corrosion of the concrete"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102058301-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "round water pipe circular drain ditch the present invention relates to a circular waterway pipe installed along the roadside and the waterway side to drain the rainwater smoothly more specifically the pipe made of synthetic resin material is installed in close contact with the inner channel of the circular waterway tube made of concrete material it relates to a circular waterway pipe that allows rainwater to flow through a pipe made of synthetic resin material without directly contacting the inner surface of the inner waterway thereby reducing corrosion of the circular waterway pipe and suppressing the occurrence of odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372189-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole for checking the amount of the deposited foreign matter on the ground at a predetermined interval in the sewage pipe or the drainage pipe or for discharging the precipitate to the ground in the manhole cover net mounted on the upper part of the manhole and connected to the rectangular frame and a plurality of supports in the transverse direction of the frame to prevent a large foreign object or person falling into the manhole a support frame made of a rectangular rod having an upper portion thereof open to be coupled to a lower side of the lateral support of the manhole cover net and having an inner coupling portion coupled to a lower side of the lateral support of the manhole cover net a flow plate extending from the bottom surface of the support frame to the side thereof to insert and block rainwater introduced from the top into the manhole by its elasticity sealed sewer cover plate characterized in that the cover sheet is attached to the upper and lower surfaces of the fluid plate to prevent corrosion of the fluid plate by applying an adhesive on one surface of the fluid plate to be attached to the upper and lower surfaces respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372189-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in order to achieve the above object according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention the manhole for confirming the amount of the foreign matter deposited on the ground at a predetermined interval in the sewage pipe or drainage pipe or to remove the precipitate to the ground in the manhole cover net which is mounted on the upper part of the manhole and is connected to a rectangular frame and a plurality of supports in the transverse direction of the frame in order to prevent bulky foreign objects or people from falling into the manhole the transverse direction of the manhole cover net the support frame is formed in the form of a rectangular rod the upper portion of which is open to be coupled to the lower portion of the support and the inner bottom surface thereof extends to the side thereof and includes a flow plate for introducing and blocking rainwater introduced from the upper portion into the manhole by its elasticity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413103-Y1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "in addition even if rainwater flows into the space 8 side the embossed ledge 8b is configured to open downward thereby minimizing the inflow of rainwater into the coupling portion to which the brackets 5a and the pins 4 are coupled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185905-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "however when the gate 51 is not normally opened due to corrosion of the rotating shaft 53 or interference with foreign matter the level sensor 54 maintains a state in which it is in contact with the compression spring 80"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200315485-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however in the conventional protective casing lid rainwater or sewage flows through the hinge fastening portion around the opening and closing window or the handle thereby causing corrosion in the water meter.the present invention has been proposed to improve the above mentioned conventional problems by forming a watertight structure around the opening and closing of the protective cover lid or the handle fastening portion to solve the adverse effects of the sewage or rainwater due to the inflow into the protective container"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200315485-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the insulation cap 2 from being rotted due to the rainwater flowing into the water meter protection container or the occurrence of corrosion and the malfunction caused by the water meter 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101316530-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention thus made a storage tank body a made of grp using synthetic resin and glass fiber and partitioned into partition walls while being provided as a storage tank body a made of a transverse circular tube and having a rainwater treatment part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200166989-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is characterized in that it consists of a packing part to be in close contact with the frame when the water is discharged to prevent the water is discharged to the outside or water is introduced from the outside the frame and the door part are reinforced with corrosion resistance by using a non metallic material and the hinge part is formed to be able to open and close in a rotatable state in a state where the door part is fixed and coupled to the frame at a corresponding position on the upper side thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202375-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the unit corrugated steel sheet 100 is preferably formed with an anti corrosion coating layer 102 on its inner surface to prevent corrosion see fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387133-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "rainwater contains various suspended substances which causes the storage water to decay making it difficult to store for long periods of time resulting in a decrease in rainwater utilization.in order to achieve the above object by adding a rain filtration filter \u2462 in the process of storing the rainwater collected from the roof of the building or the roof of the rainy weather in the rainwater storage tank in order to achieve the above object by separating the dust or suspended matter and storing only the clean rainwater long term storage prevents decay due to organic substances in rainwater making it possible to use it as water for living and by using a corrosion resistant metal grid filter \u2466 it can be used semi permanently without long term maintenance costs caused by corrosion or aging"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101433900-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in the prior art the silicate mineral powder is added as an admixture when the storage tank is manufactured to solve the toxicity caused by the toxicity of the concrete thereby neutralizing the toxicity of the cement by the strong adsorption power of the silicate mineral and the large amount of the negative ion effect the present invention provides a low toxicity concrete rainwater storage tank capable of preventing contamination of rivers public water bodies or oceans due to toxic discharge of rainwater and preventing corrosion of reinforcing bars due to whitening phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978238-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "here the box 52 of the filter box 50 is preferably made of a synthetic resin series such as polyethylene so as to prevent corrosion and contaminate rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978238-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the filter box 50 is embedded in the water collecting tank 10 to be in close contact with or adjacent to the side surface of the through hole 52a of the sedimentation box 30 and is made of synthetic resin series such as polyethylene material to prevent corrosion and contaminate rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101095835-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention it is possible to build a comfortable sewage treatment facility by greatly reducing the noise of falling water caused by the high drop in the process of inflow of sewage and rainwater into the storage tank to remove odors and to prevent corrosion an improved csos and initial good storage treatment system are provided to facilitate maintenance of the first and second reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321349-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as in the conventional case it is possible to detect the amount of water introduced through the inlet by using a flow meter but the flow meter has a high price and the zero point is inaccurate due to corrosion and breakage causing problems in performance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101791207-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in addition in the drainage device 520 the slaked lime can be mixed with the feed water in the pipe thereby preventing corrosion of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400061-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the screen 115 is installed in the water storage tank 110 and serves to filter rainwater or seawater that is supplied to and stored in the water storage tank 110 to remove impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215873-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "installing to the side and while reinforcing the reinforcing bar 8 in the form of a lattice the inner die 2 is provided with a step of maintaining the gap anchor 10 installing an external formwork 9 perpendicular to the spacing maintenance anchor 10 installation position pouring concrete between the inner and outer molds 2 and 9 to form sidewalls applying concrete mortar to the bottom surface 20 of the bottom foundation structure 1 method for producing a rainwater and combined sewer pipe overflow water storage tank perfect for leaking and corrosion prevention comprising the step of installing a sheet material 3 made of a plastic material on the bottom surface 20 is coated with concrete mortar"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215873-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a method of manufacturing a rainwater and combined sewage pipe overflow water storage tank perfect leakage and corrosion prevention and a rainwater and combined sewage pipe overflow water storage tank thereby"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215873-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition the present invention relates to a method for manufacturing a rainwater and combined sewage pipe overflow water storage tank and a storage tank thereby capable of producing a rainwater and combined sewage pipe overflow water storage tank of perfect structure to prevent leakage excellent corrosion resistance and abrasion resistance large storage capacity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215873-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "to prevent this there have recently been installations of large reservoirs to accommodate rainwater or combined sewer overflows csos reservoirs underground"}]</data>
</edge>
