  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101036279-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "while securing the first filter 112 is laminated to the second filter the upstream and downstream of the case respectively protruding toward the upper and the flow rate reducing wall to guide the rainwater flowing along the side opening to the first filter 115 and rainwater storage system for penetration type non point pollution purification device comprising a rainwater storage wall 116"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "thus when the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention is installed in the basement penetration type first digging a pit having a certain width and depth and then flatten the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore when the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank is drained underground through the drain hole 3a formed in the slab 3 the earth and sand can be prevented from entering the rainwater storage tank together with the rainwater by the nonwoven fabric 23 laid in the pit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the filter unit includes a first vertical plate extending a predetermined length from the lower surface of the deck directly below the lower end of the deck equipped with an assembly step is inserted into the assembly groove is inserted into the assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck it includes a first filtration plate which is replaceably mounted in the mounting hole formed in the lower end of the first vertical plate immersed in the rainwater of the storage space to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater a second vertical plate extending at a predetermined length from the lower surface of the deck to a lower portion of the deck by inserting an assembled jaw into the upper end of the lower surface of the deck and being inserted and assembled in an assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction a lower point of contact with the upper end of the overflow bulkhead provided at a lower level than the outer wall of the concrete bottom layer so as to be replaced with an opening formed in an opening formed therein to remove the nonpoint source of pollution contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow bulkhead including 2 filtration editions the first vertical plate and the second vertical plate is made of a plate body having an assembling jaw on the upper end to be inserted and assembled in the assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck the permeable concrete bottom layer comprises a deck walkway rainwater storage device for the filtering space characterized in that it comprises at least one overflow plate having a relatively lower height than the outer wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the second vertical plate extending a certain length directly below the lower surface of the deck and relative to the permeable concrete bottom layer of the reservoir portion than the outer wall and a second filtration plate installed to be replaceable in an opening formed in an opening formed at a lower end in contact with an upper end of the overflow partition which is provided at a low height to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow partition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it receives the rainwater flowing through the paving layer once delivered to the screening means the water leakage pipe characterized in that it comprises a pit chamber 16 formed to be dug downward from the ground so that rainwater on the paving layer flows therein having basin soil low water increase"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore when the rainwater collected in the pit chamber 16 reaches a level corresponding to the height of the connection hole 44 the rainwater moves from the pit chamber 16 toward the screening chamber 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "therefore the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16 the screening chamber 40 and the grit chamber 48 and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in the rainwater treatment facility according to the present invention in the case of a combined sewer system a lower weir having a height corresponding to the water level due to initial rainfall and a higher weir are provided in a part of the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "therefore it is possible to separately treat the highly polluted initial rainwater and the less polluted rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the first rainwater retaining pipe 5 is parallel to the sewer pipe 1 up to the location corresponding to the underground water diversion chamber 2 the portion from the top of the drainage pit 14 at the lower end of the pit 13 for pumping water gradually descends downward from the sewer line 1 while tilting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101597496-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "preparing a plurality of concrete blocks digging a circular hole having a circular sidewall laying a mixture of soil and quicklime on the bottom of the circular pit to form a compaction layer installing a plurality of concrete blocks along the edges of the compaction layer connecting the adjacent blocks to each other to form the concrete block in a circular shape filling and compacting a mixture of rubble and salt on the compaction layer inside the concrete block to form a filling layer forming a cylindrical frame by connecting the columns to the concrete block so that the columns are spaced apart and connecting the plurality of columns erected at intervals with each other using the column connecting members attaching a plurality of panels to the cylindrical frame to form a cylindrical wall installing a waterproof bag inside the cylindrical wall and providing a passage for allowing the water of the waterproof bag to be discharged to the outside at a lower end portion of the cylindrical wall and providing water discharge means provided with a valve for opening and closing the passage the step of forming the compaction layer comprises the step of mixing 30 to 50 kg of quicklime per cubic meter of the local soil and laying the mixture on the bottom of the circular pit to form a granulated compaction layer the step of forming the filling layer further comprises filling the sandwiching layer on the filling layer formed by filling and mixing the mixture of the rubble and the salt on the compaction layer inside the concrete block a step of covering the floor panel on the sand filling layer a step of installing a filtration device for filtering out foreign substances contained in the rainwater flowing into the upper end of the cylindrical wall attaching the liquid supply device to the outer surface of the cylindrical frame further comprising the step of providing a partition plate dividing the inside of the cylindrical wall into two or more spaces"}, {"pat_id": "US-6120210-A", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "rainwater from the roof or parts of the surrounding ground can be collected to feed into the cistern filled with a porous medium"}, {"pat_id": "US-6120210-A", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "rainwater from the roof or parts of the surrounding ground can be collected to feed into the sand filled cistern"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101644963-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "according to one embodiment the high concentration rainfall runoff that has passed through the first stage purification facility first water purification unit of the water quality purification unit g is transferred to the treated water feet 73 through the treated the polluted river water or low concentration rainwater having passed through the two stage facility second water quality purification unit is transferred to the natural water under the treated water pit 73 and discharged to the river or supplied as reused water or if there is a subsequent linkage facility it may be configured to be transported to that facility"}]</data>
