e discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed consists of the tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction the unit block 211 includes a top and bottom assembly 2111 installed at a bottom and a top thereof a basic assembly 2112 installed at a middle of the top and bottom assembly 2111 and a top and bottom assembly 2111 and a base assembly 2112"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system includes a first step which is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of a part where the sedimentation tank and the storage tank are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank and laying a sheet on a foundation bottom on which basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block to form the storage assembly a fifth step of installing a water repellent sheet and a protective sheet on the side surface of the storage assembly and a protective sheet on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank a sixth step of connecting the pipe to the storage tank to prevent damage to the sheet or the storage assembly a seventh step of installing the sedimentation tank the inspection cleaning manhole and the inspection manhole of the storage tank an eighth step of connecting the pipe between the rainwater inlet conduit and the sedimentation tank the pipe between the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and the pipe between the storage tank and the discharge conduit so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank to the storage tank a ninth step of filling back the excavated part remaining after the installation of the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and voltage the tenth step is to clean up the rainwater storage system and plant it if necessary"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the first embodiment includes a first step of ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the part where the sedimentation tank 1 and the storage tank 2 are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and placing a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed in order to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 are laid in the side surface of the storage assembly 21 and the protective sheet 23 is placed in the upper surface to protect the upper portion thereby completing the storage tank 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the second embodiment is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed steps a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed it consists of a tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102702375-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention was created to solve the above mentioned problems and needs and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a method for manufacturing a sewage prevention and odor blocking permeable grating that increases water permeability by using eco friendly cork and easily drains water even during heavy rain or monsoon rain while preventing sewage from flowing in and blocking odors.in order to achieve the above object a method for manufacturing a dirt prevention and odor blocking water permeable grating according to an embodiment of the present invention comprises an outer frame forming a frame to be installed on the upper part of a rainwater drain or a drain an inner frame forming a plurality of square spaces by intersecting a plurality of horizontal and vertical bars in a grid shape inside the outer frame and a water permeable block filling the square spaces formed in the inner frame the method comprising a a preparatory step of preparing the outer frame and the inner frame and cork b a crushing step of crushing the cork into a size of 6 to 9 mm c a coating step of immersing the crushed cork in a waterproof coating solution and taking it out in a state where the coating solution has been applied d a drying step of drying the waterproof coated cork at 70 to 80 c using a vibrating device b a mixing step of mixing the dried cork with a binder and c a pressing step of pressing the mixed cork into the square space at 80 to 90 c using a heat roller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101839297-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a toilet free system in which a toilet equipped with a flush toilet 10 is disposed and a waste water supplied from the toilet 10 is treated and re supplied a storage tank 20 storing sewage supplied from the toilet bowl 10 and crushing sludge in stored sewage water using a cutter pump an aeration filtration tank 30 for receiving sludge pulverized wastewater from the storage tank 20 to remove organic matter by a microbial reaction and filtering the sludge using an aeration pump and a sludge filter 33 a biological reaction tank 40 for receiving the treated water of the aeration filtration tank 30 by using a suction pump and ultimately removing residual organic matter contained in the wastewater a decolorizing tank 50 for receiving treated water from the bioreactor 40 to decolorize the activated carbon a uv sterilizing chamber 60 for sterilizing the treated water supplied from the decoloring bath 50 using a uv lamp 61 a water supply pump 70 for supplying treated water stored in the uv disinfection chamber 60 to the toilet 10 a controller 80 having a wireless communication module 81 while controlling the operation of the cutter pump the aeration pump the suction pump the uv lamp 61 and the feed pump 70 lt rti gt a portable terminal 140 for monitoring and controlling a system operation state by a user at a remote place using the wireless communication module 81 lt rti gt a rainwater storage tank 150 in which rainwater is stored a rainwater supply pump 151 for selectively supplying the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 150 to the uv sterilization chamber 60 or the treatment water tank treatment water storage tank lt rti gt the controller 80 selectively controls the operation of the rainwater supply pump 151 according to the level of water stored in the uv sterilization chamber 60 or the treatment water tank treatment water storage tank to store the water in the rainwater storage tank 150 so that water is supplied to the uv sterilization chamber 60 or the treatment water tank treatment water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a container shaped sand container that is disposed on the ground and accommodates water evaporating sand the upper side being opened a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container a cleaning wastewater spraying device for spraying the cleaning wastewater stored in the cleaning wastewater storage tank to the water evaporation sand stored in the sand storage unit a washing waste water recirculation mechanism that recirculates excess washing waste water flowing down through the gaps between the particles of water evaporating sand contained in the sand containing portion to the washing waste water storage tank the soil purification method includes while spraying cleaning wastewater from the cleaning wastewater spraying device on the water evaporation sand accommodated in the sand container the water of the cleaning wastewater adhering to the water evaporation sand is evaporated into the air to remove it from the sandbox introducing the water evaporating sand in which the chelating agent is accumulated for a predetermined period of time in the sand containing unit into the classifying unit and recovering the chelating agent accumulated in the water evaporating sand a method for soil purification wherein a part of the sand discharged from the classification unit is used as water evaporation sand stored in the sand storage unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704786-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a method for constructing a non point source pollutant filtering device for a paved road according to article 1 the first stage is to remove the surface layer adjacent to the sidewalk and the rear surface of the paved road and construct a drainage pavement a second step of burying a perforated pipe on the surface of a paved road that has a drainage pavement along an edge adjacent to the side ditch and extending the perforated pipe so as to form a connection from the side ditch to the sump at a position adjacent in the width direction a third step of crushing a portion of a side ditch adjacent to the above mentioned water collection well in the width direction and inserting the body part to connect it with the above mentioned perforated pipe and water collection well and fixing it with cement concrete and a fourth step of sequentially inserting and installing the filter part and the cover part into the receiving space of the body part when the cement concrete is hardened a second compartment plate provided at the lower portion of the receiving space of the above body part has a plurality of second discharge holes formed through which rainwater filtered of non point source pollutants is discharged through the cover part and the filter part"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rainwater supply unit that supplies the rinse water and a chelating agent recovery unit that recovers the chelating agent from the cleaning wastewater discharged from the chelating agent removal unit the chelating agent removing unit has a sand rinsing device that sprays or jets rinsing water on the sand separated by the classifying unit to remove the chelating agent held in the sand the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank for receiving and storing cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the sand rinsing device a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 sand rinse device 62 coarse aggregate rinse device 63 washing waste water evaporation device 64 belt conveyor 65 sand supply device 66 rinse water spray device 67 cleaning waste water receiving tank 68 drive roller 68a shaft 69 driven roller 69a shaft 70 conveyor belt 71 support roller 72 guide plate 74 belt conveyor 75 coarse aggregate supply device 76 rinsing water spray device 77 cleaning waste water receiving tank 78 driving roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveyor belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 cleaning waste water discharge passage 84 cleaning waste water storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 91 side groove 9 washing wastewater supply device 93 washing wastewater return path 94 water level holding device 100 ground 101 bottom groove 102 communication hole 103 convex part 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 110 water tank 111 weir 112 washing wastewater supply pump 113 washing waste water supply pipe 116 frame structure 117 roof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052909-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "10 2010 0038949the present invention has been made to solve such a problem the trench body and the trench body which is installed in a recess recessed downward of the corresponding construction surface such as a road both side walls and the bottom surface is provided the upper side is open a drainage trench having a plurality of shielding plates forming an inlet so that water such as rainwater or sewage is introduced into the trench main body by partially shielding the open upper portion and concrete which is poured into a groove while one side is connected to the drainage trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052909-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in addition in the drain trench set according to an embodiment of the present invention the support cover portion the first horizontal line with the line extending in parallel with the upward curved extension portion the first engaging portion in the upper engaging portion of the side wall body after crushing the cured concrete to the crushing line the drainage trench is allowed to slide flow in the connecting socket the horizontal line with the lower horizontal extension as a second crushing line the first crushing line after the crushed cured concrete up to two crushing line may be the drainage trench can be separated by forcibly pulled out from the connection socket.the drainage trench and the drainage trench set according to the embodiment of the present invention described above are provided in a trench recessed downwardly in a corresponding construction surface such as a road and both sidewall bodies and a bottom surface are provided and the trench body is open upward"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052947-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052946-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 91 side groove 92 washing wastewater supply device 93 washing wastewater return path 94 water level holding device 100 ground 101 bottom groove 102 communication hole 103 projection 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 110 water tank 111 weir 112 washing wastewater supply pump 113 washing waste water supply pipe 116 frame structure 117 roof"}]</data>
