  <data key="d6">["combine", "compose", "fulfill", "connect", "float", "introduce", "accord", "fasten", "embed", "achieve", "cause", "leave", "pervente", "have", "clog", "send", "contact", "complete", "fix", "flow", "face", "can", "relate", "object", "provide", "shorten", "mention", "roadside", "suppress", "prevent", "attach", "evaporate", "leak", "form", "press", "repeat", "eliminate", "build", "limit", "pass", "couple", "repair", "push", "do", "replace", "settle", "cure", "bury", "accumulate", "support", "illustrate", "collect", "penetrate", "mount", "submerge", "clean", "allow", "run", "result", "insert", "remove", "cover", "surround", "show", "reduce", "may", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "detect", "fit", "grate", "change", "guide", "include", "perform", "dispose", "incline", "open", "enter", "block", "deposit", "supply", "use", "transfer", "stop", "cut", "could", "know", "require", "close", "rotate", "maintain", "improve", "control", "extend", "drain", "monitor", "characterize", "select", "keep", "be", "generate", "describe", "instal"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101370248-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "as well as preventing it is possible to prevent the odor generated therefrom to leak into the home or building"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2885467-B1", "para_id": "para_173", "text": "the controller 210 is connected to a moisture sensor via a long cable and provides information to the server about moisture from other sources such as rainwater that does not leak from the monitored water installation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "when the inlet opening closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 11 due to the rainwater condition that does not require a closure a free space provided between surrounding parts for smooth operation of the inlet opening closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "fourthly the present invention provides a bollard type hot water leak inspection panel protector suitable for guiding rainwater to the ground by the geometry of the inlet cover and the exhaust cover to prevent rainwater penetration more efficiently.bollard type hot water leak detection panel protector according to the present invention for achieving the above object the bollard is provided with a hot water leak detection panel electrically connected to the hot water leak detection sensor for detecting the leakage of the hot water supply pipe buried in the ground type hot water leakage meter panel protector a wiring through hole for passing the cable of the hot water leak detection sensor embedded in the ground is formed at the bottom and a hot water leak meter panel is installed"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0525594-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the seal can also be installed above the waste body surface seal to prevent the ingress of rainwater and thus the washing out of pollutants from the waste"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101268337-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "after removing the filtration member 160 to the outside through the check hole 180 to repair or replace the filtration sheet 162 the filtration member 160 may be introduced into the rainwater reservoir 100 again"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "at this time when there is a gap between the manhole body and the water inlet or drainage pipe rainwater or sewage may leak so when the inlet or drainage pipe is connected to the manhole body a hole is formed in the manhole body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "first if there is a small gap between the pipe 40 and the hole of the manhole body 10 in fitting the pipe 40 for introducing or discharging rainwater into the hole 11 of the manhole body 10 rainwater or sewage may leak through the tube 40 to the manhole body 10 when the packing 20 is fitted to have watertightness and flexibility the tube 20 is fitted thereon the tube 20 while pressing the packing 20 in the process of inserting the wing portion 23 of the packing 20 is fixed around the hole 11 of the manhole body 10 through the fixing ring 50 the packing 20 is it can keep its position without being pushed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101077132-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the water flow guide portion 60 is installed to guide the rainwater passing through the perforation portion 51 to the drain hole so that the rainwater passing through the perforation portion 51 to maintain the airtightness so as not to leak to the outside it is formed in close contact with the edge of the 51 and any shape may be any shape as long as the rainwater passing through the perforation 51 is collected and guides the collected rainwater to the drain hole but is parallel to the bottom surface 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "non point contaminants deposited in the sedimentation tank are stored and stored in the tank until they are collected separately so that contaminants may not leak out of the sedimentation tank and the overflow wall is formed at the bottom of the sedimentation tank so that the rainwater quickly flows in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100957464-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore the lower end of the odor prevention unit is also mounted to both sides left and right around the center line.odor prevention and dirt collection device for rain gutter collection basin of the present invention performs the function of a dirt collection device to prevent impurities from flowing into the flow pipe and odor to prevent the odor inside the rain gutter collection basin to leak outside not only does it perform the function of prevention but it also fulfills the first purpose of the rainwater collecting basin without clogging by collecting impurities through a large outflow hole formed in the upper part of the collecting network when an excessive amount of impurities and dirt are instantaneously introduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "odor leak prevention deodorization system 100 of the rainwater collection tank of the present invention is installed in the rainwater collection tank 5 of rainwater pipe 3 connected to the sewage pipe 2 as shown in figure 1 to 6 when rainwater does not flow in and is empty the odor flowing back through the sewage pipe is removed to prevent the odor from leaking to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "operation control for a time to remove the odor by the chemical reaction by ozone but there is a risk that some of the odor may leak around the rainwater collection tank in the early stage of operation because the time required to reduce the odor by the chemical reaction of ozone and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "control to repeat the start and stop for a time for example 30 minutes run 60 minutes stop 30 minutes run in order to supply ozone to the rainwater collection tank in advance to remove the backflow odor from the beginning to eliminate the problem of odor leak to completely prevent it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102678969-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "there is a known water sump for bridge installation that is rotatably coupled to and includes a foreign matter inflow prevention grill that opens and closes the upper opening through a rotating motion thereby improving natural water discharge performance and extending the life of the bridge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201943-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the sewage pipe for rainwater according to the present invention has a leak hole 20 formed on the upper circumferential surface thereof so that a part of the rainwater penetrates into the ground 2 to prevent disasters and to supply water to roadside trees installed in the city"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201943-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the rainwater sewer pipe 10 is installed on the ground 2 with the display portion 11 facing upward thereby preventing the contamination of the contaminants from leaking to the ground 2 by changing the vertical direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201943-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "disasters such as flooding can be prevented and water can be supplied to street trees in urban areas where rainwater is not well supplied because it is covered with an impermeable layer such as asphalt or concrete.as described above according to the present invention since a leak hole is installed in a pipeline in which rainwater flows down a part of the rainwater can be penetrated into the ground so that disasters caused by flooding of rivers where rainwater collects can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however this type of catchment can cause an unpleasant odor generated from the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to leak out into the atmosphere due to a malfunction of the valve member provided between the catchment and the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4886659-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "further the shape is not limited to that illustrated in the figure and various shapes such as a block shape a sand shape a granular shape and a lump shape can be appropriately selected and used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101028522-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the bridge installation catchment port according to the present invention includes a water collecting body installed at a drain hole in which the upper and lower portions of the bridge communicate with each other and a water leak disposed on a circumferential surface of the water collecting body to prevent rainwater from penetrating downward between the water collecting body and the drain hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100768328-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "therefore even if rainwater present in the soil around the underground reservoir 10 further penetrates underground or evaporates due to a subsequent drought the water inside the underground reservoir 10 does not penetrate or evaporate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "apparatus for perventing blow back of foul smell in drainage system the present invention relates to a sewage odor leak prevention device and more particularly to prevent odor leaks that can be installed in the inlet of the sewage or rainwater drainage or with a manhole or grating to prevent odors and pests to enter the ground space relates to a device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to the present invention since the sewage accumulated in the sewer can naturally flow back to the ground through the inlet cover while suppressing odors and pests pressure can accumulate in the lowland sewerage to prevent the problem of loss of facility damage or backflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "when the inlet opening closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 111 due to a rainwater condition that does not require a closure a free space provided between surrounding components for smooth operation of the inlet opening closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thereby the rainwater drained from the lower connecting pipe can be guided to the inside of the gutter and leakage from the connecting portion between the lower connecting pipe and the gutter can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102645553-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in claim 1 a leak free sewage flow rate control device characterized in that the bottom 12 of the rainwater tank 10 is inclined downward toward the sewage outlet 20 to prevent accumulation of sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102645553-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in the sewage treatment plant rainwater flows in from various rainwater cisterns during rainfall resulting in an increase in the treatment load"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101208359-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "this is because the blocking plate is not completely covered by the safety net may leak odor from the drain pipe there is a problem that rainwater or sewage is not easily discharged by the interference of the float while the float floats to a certain height"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100840086-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "construction of the rainwater reservoir above is advantageous for shortening the air and does not require any other security work on various external pressures"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0525593-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the seal can also be installed above the waste body surface seal to prevent the ingress of rainwater and thus the washing out of pollutants from the waste"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100978103-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "forming a rail not shown so that the buoyancy portion 34 is supported by the rainwater collected through the inlet 31a of the lower mounting portion 20 so as to contact the contact portion 33 and detection could also be the sensor 35 is to detect a leak in fact a contact signal via the control section 36 sent to the administrator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200352056-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention is to achieve the above object the present invention is coupled to the connection hole of the sewer pipe is composed of a structure that can prevent the leakage of the sewage as much as possible while the connector protection ring is one side cut off the fastening part is formed horizontally the fastening part is coupled to the fastening part the leak proof rubber ring is attached to the inside the joint pipe connection part is formed on the other side and the circular fixed rubber ring is coupled to both sides so that the connector protection ring is firm it is fixed to the sewer pipe the connection pipe is connected to the joint pipe joint of the connector protection ring while the connection pipe is formed with a bolt portion at the bottom and the fixed bolt is coupled to the upper leak proof rubber ring inside is attached the connection pipe is coupled to the upper portion the connection pipe the bolt installation groove is formed in the lower portion the pleat portion is formed in the middle portion the connection pipe is excellent in the upper it is combined to provide a sewer pipe connector characterized in that the rainwater is collected and transferred to the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101305591-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however due to the wide diameter it is easy for sediment to settle in conduits and there is a high possibility that sewage from rainwater tosoil may leak into the body of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200483342-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore foreign substances or impurities accumulated in the body 1 2 times a year it is possible to clean the inside of the body to remove it and the structure of the device is waterproof structure so that water can not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100734227-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "if the above mentioned injection tube 12 and the exhaust pipe 13 is removed in the cured state the joining is completed and the state is more robust and watertight.the resin reinforcement method of the manhole junction of the present invention as described above and the joint structure using the same as well as the joint of the manhole and the sewer pipe more tightly as well as the watertight joint of the manhole and sewage pipe to allow the external soil or foreign matter inflow and internal sewage and rainwater it is effective to prevent this leak"}]</data>
