  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102588102-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this relates to a sewer cleaning device for rainwater drains and rainwater drain pipes in urban areas using a combined method for dredging trucks that cleans while checking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 the water level controller 32 includes a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor 29 the second sensor 30 and the third sensor 31 of the water level sensor portion the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank 16 may be discharged through the discharge pipe 22 for a predetermined discharge time when the time counted by the timer 33 becomes longer than a predetermined time wherein the control unit controls the discharge valve 21 so that the discharge water 21 is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101412529-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the water level controller may further include a timer for checking the time after the water level is sensed by at least one of the first sensor the second sensor and the third sensor of the water level sensor portion and controls the discharge valve so that the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank can be discharged through the discharge pipe for a preset discharge time when the discharge time exceeds the predetermined set time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the safety facility of the rainwater storage tank 150 is stored in a slightly higher than the high water level hwl in order to prevent the water level rises and overflows when the amount of rainwater entering the rainwater storage tank 150 more than the planned quantity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sensor unit for sensing water data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility and a controller for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed value of the sensor unit and a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of the field sub control panels and for controlling the equipment section and the field sub control panel through bidirectional communication with the plurality of field sub control panels a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile terminal of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a sensor unit for sensing water data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility and a controller for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed value of the sensor unit and a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of the field sub control panels and for controlling the equipment section and the field sub control panel through bidirectional communication with the plurality of field sub control panels a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile terminal of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided an application for supporting an integrated remote management system for a plurality of water treatment facilities including a sensor unit for sensing water resource data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility a plurality of on site sub control units for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed values of the sensor unit and installed in the water treatment facility a water treatment system comprising a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of field sub control boards in two way communication with the plurality of the field sub control boards and controlling the facility and the sub control boards a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile application of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method of operating an integrated remote management system for a plurality of water treatment facilities including a sensor unit for sensing water resource data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility a plurality of on site sub control units for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed values of the sensor unit and installed in the water treatment facility a water treatment system comprising a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of field sub control boards in two way communication with the plurality of the field sub control boards and controlling the facility and the sub control boards a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile application of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system a method for operating an integrated remote management system for a facility the method comprising the steps of collecting and processing information measured by the sensor unit in the field main control panel and transmitting the current operating state a first step of sending an urgent maintenance message to a mobile terminal of a remote manager using a text message if urgent maintenance is required a second step of the mobile terminal of the remote manager receiving the text message transmitted through the first process when the emergency message is received through the second process the remote manager confirms the text message executes the application ratm and the third step of checking the necessity of urgent inspection by the administrator when the water treatment time requested through the text message is confirmed including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101858569-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method for operating an integrated remote management system for a plurality of water treatment facilities including a sensor unit for sensing water resource data of a water treatment facility including a rainwater treatment facility and a septic tank a facility unit for operating the water treatment facility a plurality of on site sub control units for controlling the operation of the facility unit based on the sensed values of the sensor unit and installed in the water treatment facility a water treatment system comprising a field main control panel for monitoring the control status of the water treatment data and the water treatment facility through the plurality of field sub control boards in two way communication with the plurality of the field sub control boards and controlling the facility and the sub control boards a plurality of water treatment systems are provided and a mobile application of a remote manager for receiving detection data of the sensor unit provided in each water treatment system in a wireless internet environment and remotely checking and maintaining the current state in each water treatment system a method for operating an integrated remote management system for a facility the method comprising the steps of collecting and processing information measured by the sensor unit in the field main control panel and transmitting the current operating state if urgent maintenance is required the emergency check message is transmitted in a text message and the unique code and the control signal assigned to the data transmission device itself are generated and extended according to a specific pattern in the transmitted text message integrated data with remote administrator s mobile a first step of sending to the end a second step of the mobile terminal of the remote manager receiving the integrated urgent text message transmitted through the first process a third step of determining whether the integrated urgent text message is received through the second process or not and confirming whether the remote administrator confirms the integrated urgent text message and if the remote manager confirms that the integrated emergency text message is confirmed through the third process the application ratm is automatically activated to display the water treatment facility to be managed by the main control panel included in the integrated emergency text message through the display means and a fourth step of performing the second step"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102088177-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the locking and unlocking of the lid of water meter protector automatic the present invention relates to the opening and closing structure of the lid for the water meter and more specifically the opening and closing of the lid is easy to use and the thermal insulation material case material and heat insulation due to rainwater to facilitate the checking of the meter and pedestrian walking to the upper side of the water meter protection cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_130", "text": "a diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed at an inlet of the penetration storage tank 4 to prevent the deposition of sand or foreign matter not completely precipitated in the sedimentation tank 1 to be deposited and the diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_185", "text": "a diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed at an inlet of the penetration storage tank 4 to prevent the deposition of sand or foreign matter not completely precipitated in the sedimentation tank 1 to be deposited and the diffusion suppression partition 44 is formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372189-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole for checking the amount of the deposited foreign matter on the ground at a predetermined interval in the sewage pipe or the drainage pipe or for discharging the precipitate to the ground in the manhole cover net mounted on the upper part of the manhole and connected to the rectangular frame and a plurality of supports in the transverse direction of the frame to prevent a large foreign object or person falling into the manhole a support frame made of a rectangular rod having an upper portion thereof open to be coupled to a lower side of the lateral support of the manhole cover net and having an inner coupling portion coupled to a lower side of the lateral support of the manhole cover net a flow plate extending from the bottom surface of the support frame to the side thereof to insert and block rainwater introduced from the top into the manhole by its elasticity sealed sewer cover plate characterized in that the cover sheet is attached to the upper and lower surfaces of the fluid plate to prevent corrosion of the fluid plate by applying an adhesive on one surface of the fluid plate to be attached to the upper and lower surfaces respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "and a cap 198 connected to the hinge 190 of the fixed frame 125 provided at the end of the branch pipe 121.the present invention provides a stable drainage of rainwater by providing a stable removal of rainwater or flood caused by heavy rainfall as described above while checking the clogging caused by sedimentation that accumulates while moving in a drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200409378-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the present invention is a bridge drainage system composed of a drain pipe for drainage of rainwater installed on the bridge pier or sidewall of the bridge at high altitude installed between the corner curved pipe portion or the straight pipe drainage pipe of the bridge drainage equipment easily check the sediment status of sand and other materials and easily drain and remove it to the outside so that the drainage system can be eliminated by dirt effectively maintaining and managing bridges and elevated roads"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200409378-Y1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "3 progresses for a long time the waste storage unit 14 of the first shaped curved waste outlet 10 and the waste storage unit 43 of the t and the second curved elbow discharge pipe 60 while the dirt w accompanying the rainwater is separated from the rainwater again by its own weight and the waste storage unit 14 43 and the dirt check discharge unit in the 64 it is continuously introduced along with rainwater and the like and the heights of the sewage w deposited in the sewage storage units 14 and 43 and the waste checking and discharging unit 64 increase gradually"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is higher than the minimum value opening the three way valve so that the water of the second tank is supplied through the downpipe and connected to the supply pipe and preventing the water of the first tank from being supplied to the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is higher than the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe purified in the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joined from the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joined including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so that the charge level of the battery is lower than the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is below the minimum value turning on the three way valve to connect the other discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is above the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joins including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 if the charge level of the battery is below the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101619868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the outdoor fire fighting box a control unit 8 for managing the operation of the firefighting box 100 as a whole an on off valve 2 for automatically injecting the fire fighting water upon opening a pressure gauge unit 6 connected to the transfer pipe 20 for spraying water for spraying water and for checking internal pressure changes is provided and the internal pressure state of the opening a pressure chamber 4 for transmitting the pressure to the pressure chamber 4 the control unit 8 controls the pressure change state of the pressure chamber 4 in real time so that the open close valve 2 operates by the control signal of the control unit 8 at the time of the pressure change in the pressure chamber 4 due to the operation a rotary motor 10 a pump 18 for allowing the fire water flowing through the connection pipe 12 to flow through the transfer pipe 20 at a high pressure by the rotation of the rotary motor 10 a fire hose 32 provided on the transfer pipe 20 for injecting a high pressure fire water for opening the opening closing valve 2 a rainwater receiver 28 for storing rainwater is installed on the ground and a check valve 30 for preventing foreign matter from entering the rainwater receiver 28 is provided at a lower portion of the rainwater receiver 28 a water storage tank 22 for storing the water for fire fighting and supplying the stored water for fire into the fire box 100 through the connection pipe 12 and a power generation unit 14 that supplies power to the fire fighting cabinet 100 by installing a self power generation facility among at least one of power generation using fossil fuel and solar power generation installed outside the control unit 8 checks the pressure in the pressure chamber 4 changed by the opening of the opening and closing valve 2 and operates the rotary motor 10 so that the fire fighting water is automatically injected into the fire hose 32 removable outdoor fire fighting cabinet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226126-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "therefore unlike the conventional state that could not be artificially checked the internal condition the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention has the effect that it is possible to properly clean and remove the floating matter by checking the state of the interior even after construction"}]</data>
