  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102157125-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "with the main pipe a drilling device including a first double acting cylinder and a perforated part for drilling an inner well material of the groundwater well as a device for injecting a first grouting material into a first perforated portion of an inner well material a silicon injection device containing silicon and including a silicon injection cylinder and a second double acting cylinder as a device for injecting a second grouting material into a second perforated part of the inner well material a grouting material injection device including an ultra fast diameter cement injection pipe and a third double acting cylinder a motor part installed outside the groundwater well and applying power to the perforated part of the drilling device by rotating the main pipe a hydraulic pump installed outside the groundwater well and supplying hydraulic pressure to the silicon injection cylinder the first double acting cylinder the second double acting cylinder and the third double acting cylinder it is disposed at the top of the groundwater well and includes a holding part provided with an angle guide for checking the rotation angle of the main pipe while supporting the main pipe each of the perforation device silicon injection device and grouting material injection device is modularized and is connected in the order of a drilling device a silicon injection device and a grouting material injection device in a vertical direction at the bottom of the main pipe injected into the groundwater well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100948425-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain pipe 20 having an upper end portion opened toward the outlet portion 22 and a discharge tube 25 opened at the lower end thereof in the seating space 24a and embedded in the ground a first door 30 rotatably fixed to the inlet portion 21 so as to be opened by the flow of sewage flowing from the upper sewer pipe 11 and closed by the flow of sewage flowing back a second door 40 rotatably fixed to the outlet portion 22 so as to be opened by the force of the sewage discharged from the drain pipe 20 and closed by the force of the sewage flowing back from the lower sewer pipe 12 a tube 50 seated in the seating space 24a and air flows in and out a bottom plate 60 constructed on the tube 50 to move up and down according to the internal pressure and the hydraulic pressure change of the tube 50 a switch 71 for opening and closing the tube 50 a pump 72 for forcibly transferring air from the tank t for storing air to the tube 50 and a set internal pressure while checking the internal pressure of the tube 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100825996-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "35 an auxiliary fixing means 4 is further provided on the outer side of the fixing nut 11 installed at the outer end of the pressure transmitting tube 1 the auxiliary fixing means 4 is a fixing washer 41 installed to face the nut 11 a stopper 42 formed in a tubular shape at one end thereof with a locking jaw 421 which is caught by the fixing washer 41 a pressing jaw 422 being formed inside the suspension and a thread 423 formed at the end thereof an outer jaw 43 which is pushed by the pressing jaw 422 formed on the stopper 42 and whose outer circumferential surface on which the wedge 431 is formed has a conical shape it has a conical inner circumferential surface opposite to the conical inclined surface formed on the outer jaw 43 the outer circumferential surface is composed of a fixing nut 44 formed with a screw thread tightened to the screw thread 423 formed on the stopper 42 hydraulic pressure checking device for checking the water density of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100825996-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the present invention relates to a pressure checking device for checking the water density of the pipe and more specifically to be firmly installed at the end of the pipe to prevent the pressure gauge from being separated by hydraulic pressure or air pressure supplied to the inside of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the present invention is a technique for branching and installing the drainage branch pipe on one side of the water supply pipe connecting the drainage control valve to the bottom of the drainage branch pipe connecting the residual water drainage pipe to the bottom of the drainage control valve take a look.according to the present invention when the operation of the submersible motor pump is stopped automatically by the water pipe to prevent the water flow back to the water pipe and at the same time draining the water remaining in the pumping device in the upper ground water protective device to the outside cold water pumping device it provides the effect of preventing the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which is a component of the components in advance and greatly reduces the time and manpower associated with checking or replacing the groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge as well as providing convenience of post management after construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175904-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "another object of the present invention is to attach a concentrated water discharge amount adjustment table indicating the amount of concentrated water discharged for 1 minute according to the raw water pressure inside the product and during the 1 minute discharged while checking the adjustment table even when measuring the raw water pressure using a separate hydraulic pressure gauge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "analog to digital converter for converting to a digital signal a microcontroller for receiving the output value of the analog to digital converter in a pin to pin pin to pin method and corrected by an algorithm and output the output signal of the microcontroller in a serial method a sensor unit comprising a plurality of measuring devices including a hydraulic pressure measuring device including a communication unit which transmits to a field collecting device of a water supply pipe management system but transmits accurate data through a parity bit check for checking crc errors a plurality of field collecting devices collecting data provided from a plurality of measuring devices forming the sensor unit a data collection device collecting data through the plurality of field collection devices a water supply pipe network gis geographic information system device that organizes and manages geographic and facility data such as pipe codes installation blocks pipe diameters pipe types buried years pipe ages joint methods and coordinates of water pipes pipeline code date of report start of construction completion of construction whether to dismantle closure depth water pressure leakage surface leakage amount leakage area leakage classification cause of damage damage type construction subsidy measures an accident management device that stores and manages data related to the water supply pipe such as contents accident route photos and personnel opinions a weight extraction device that receives the factors necessary for weight calculation from the water supply network gis device and the accident management device and calculates the weight for each factor through the opinion of an expert integrate and organize the data received from the water supply network gis device and the incident management device by block and factor and unify the limit value and the comparison unit so that the strength of data can be compared and then determine the search order of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100521630-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an elastic member disposed between the elastic members to elastically support the display member upstream the display device is changed in position by the hydraulic pressure of the water applied by the filter to the display member while passing through the housing and the elasticity of the elastic member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "70 is opened and the effluent is collected into the sump 100 while the current groundwater level is lower than the set ground level the effluent water due to the closing pressure of the water level control device 40 70 in the water level control device of the sump well configured to block the collection of water so that the current ground level is lower than the set ground level it is possible to reduce the number of continuous water block and pumping the water level control device 40 70 one end is connected to the collecting pipe 10 and the inlet pipes 22 52 84 provided with hydraulic pressure gauges 21 51 81 for checking the water pressure of the effluent and the inlet pipe 22 52 84 the drain pipe 23 53 85 and the main pipe 24 54 87 connected to the drain pipe 23 53 85 the inlet pipe 22 52 84 is provided with locking ends 25 52a 82 on the upper inner circumferential surface and a cover for preventing foreign matter from penetrating the upper ends of the main tubes 24 54 and 87 body parts 20 50 and 80 fastened to open and close 27 55 and 86 installed inside the body parts 20 50 80 the eluent water flowing into the inlet pipes 22 52 84 is opened and is drained to the drain pipes 23 53 85"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the body portion 50 is connected to the water collecting pipe 10 the hydraulic pressure gauge 51 for checking the water pressure of the effluent is installed the inlet pipe 52 is formed with a locking end 52a at the end of the discharge water is discharged a drain pipe 53 having a slide hinge 53a formed inside the upper end and draining the effluent in the opposite direction of the inflow pipe 52 and a main pipe 54 connected to the drain pipe 53 the upper end of the main pipe 54 located between the drain pipe 53 and the inlet pipe 52 is configured to be fastened to open and close the cover 55 to prevent foreign substances from penetrating"}]</data>
