  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101261839-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention does not return the high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin so as to reduce the impact of the return of high concentration of suspended solids organic matter and gross phosphorus to the sedimentation basin and bioreactor it is economical and eco friendly because it can reduce the amount of injected chemicals and the power is reduced by adopting the slant plate settling tank and the sludge concentration can be automatically adjusted by continuously discharging the sludge and changing the hydraulic pressure difference using the hydraulic pressure difference.figure 1a is a block diagram of a conventional wake water treatment apparatus figure 1b is a flow chart of the prior art flocculation flotation 2 is a block diagram of a semi water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 3 is a cutaway showing the flow of sewage treatment in the inclined plate shaped sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention figure 4 is a block diagram of the sludge automatic discharge line of the inclined plate type sedimentation tank in the reflux water treatment apparatus of the present invention 5 6 is a perspective view of the water level control of the sludge automatic discharge device of the inclined plate type sedimentation apparatus of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301965-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper part of the discharge pipe is provided with a water hole is drilled inside the elastic spring is installed therein the upper part of the elastic spring is a piston with a fixed piston rod is located the piston stand is in contact with the lower plate of the pressing plate of the opening and closing the upper plate and a lifting member which is configured to be elastically supported so that the opening and closing member is closed while the piston is lowered by the hydraulic pressure acting on the inlet side by the expansion pressure caused by the freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101955319-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "in particular the hydraulic block 620 includes a main chamber 622 which is filled with hydraulic pressure and is rotatably assembled in a state where the drive spur gear 640 and the idle gear 650 are gear engaged with each other a buffer chamber 626 having a spherical internal space at an interval from the main chamber 622 and a passing chamber 624 for connecting the main chamber 622 and the buffer chamber 626 in the vertical direction are formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100973662-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "sensing unit 110 a measurement signal processor 120 for converting the analog signal measured by the detector 110 into a digital signal a data transmission device 130 for transmitting a digital signal for the hydraulic pressure data the supply flow data the meter reading data and the leak data converted through the measurement signal processing unit 120 to the communication server 141 of the central control room 140 a database server 142 for storing hydraulic pressure data supply flow data meter reading data and leakage data transmitted through the data transmission device 130 and the communication server 141 by dividing them into date position and measured value a first analysis server 143 for setting a leak generation block through data analysis of the database server 142 a second analysis server 144 for inferring a leakage occurrence point by analyzing water pipes in the block set through the first analysis server 143 in the leak position detecting system for detecting the leak position of the water supply pipe consisting of a display unit 150 for indicating the leak predicted point inferred through the second analysis server 144 the second analysis server 144 analyzes the leak detector the water pipe aging degree and mathematical modeling and then infers the predicted leakage point using the statistical method by fuzzy inference"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100973662-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a detector for measuring water pressure data supply flow rate data meter reading data and leak data through a pressure gauge a flow meter a meter and a leak detector installed in a water pipe within a water supply pipe network partitioned by block units a measurement signal processing unit for converting the analog signal measured by the detection unit into a digital signal a data transmission device for transmitting the digital signal for the hydraulic pressure data the supply flow rate data the meter reading amount data and the leakage data converted through the measurement signal processing unit to a communication server of the central control room a database server for storing the hydraulic pressure data the supply flow data the meter reading data and the leak data transmitted through the data transmission apparatus and the communication server by dividing the data into a date a position and a measured value a first analysis server for setting a leak generation block through data analysis of the database server a second analysis server for inferring a leakage occurrence point by analyzing water pipes in the block set through the first analysis server in the leak position detection system for detecting the leak position of the water supply pipe consisting of a display unit for indicating the predicted leakage point inferred through the second analysis server the second analysis server analyzes the leak detector water pipe aging and mathematical modeling and then infers the predicted location of the leak by using a statistical method based on fuzzy inference"}, {"pat_id": "US-12318731-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the loading force may be attributable to normal mechanical springs or hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 an actuator housing for operating a water gate to on