e type pressure reducing valve that can be automatically controlled and stores the target block effluent pressure from the integrated monitoring and control station in the internal memory and the stored block effluent pressure the pressure reducing valve is controlled using a target value an inlet pressure measurement value detected by the first hydraulic pressure gauge and an outlet pressure measurement value detected by the second hydraulic pressure gauge but the inlet pressure measurement value is greater than the block outlet pressure target value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in an embodiment of the present invention by installing a water supply block control panel for each jurisdiction block by zone and installing a pressure reducing valve that can automatically control itself according to the jurisdiction block region the flow inflow pressure and hydraulic pressure gauge are also installed to provide a block inflow water pressure of approximately 3 to 3 even if the pressure is 5kg it performs the decompression function as well as performs the optimum decompression control to take a constant outflow water pressure to the jurisdiction block with the flow monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "therefore when the inflow water pressure measurement value p1 becomes larger than the stored block outflow water pressure target value the supply water pressure control unit 30 proceeds to step 104 of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "when the opening degree control of the globe type pressure reducing valve 20 is performed as described above after reaching the target block water pressure target value the frequent operation of the pressure reducing valve 20 is minimized to prevent water shaking and the amount of water used by the customer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition the analysis of the water supply pipe network can also determine the control time of the water control valve v2 by calculating the time during which the water pressure falls at the critical point c from the water control valve control point a at the reservoir control point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "at this time the emergency operation valve 400 may be driven in a non power based manner so as to be able to perfectly cope with interruption of the constant"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing process for obtaining pure water from salt water comprising feeding salt water to a vertically arranged elongated closed tank to establish a column of salt water therein the level of which is above the feed point continuously cooling a body of mercury externally of said tank and injecting said mercury in the form of finely atomized particles into the upper portion of said liquid column withdrawing said mercury from the bottom of said tank and recirculating said mercury through said liquid column to maintain the column at a temperature which is subcooled with respect to the salt water infeed so that the infeed has ice crystals formed therein due to contact with the subcooled column permitting the ice crystals to accumulate and form a solid block of ice in the upper portion of said tank above the level of mercury injection moving said block of ice upwardly in said tank by hydraulic pressure of incoming salt water and melting the upper portion of said block of ice by indirect heat exchange with the salt water feed prior to entry of said feed into said column and withdrawing pure water from the upper portion of the tank between the top of said tank and the top of said ice block and withdrawing concentrated salt water and precipitated salts collected above the mercury from the lower portion of said tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the heat exchange which takes place in the exchanger 20 at the upper portion of the tank melts the upper portion of the ice block in the zones a and b so that pure water may be withdrawn from the zone a at the outlet 24"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_95", "text": "according to one or more embodiments the variable speed high pressure pump that operates to push the pretreated water through the treatment block 260 may be controlled by monitor 226 and may comprise any pump suitable to generate the hydraulic pressure necessary to push the water through the one or more membrane pressure vessels"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101630268-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for estimating whether or not a water supply pipe is disconnected between blocks using an information processing apparatus including a database unit for providing information on a block and a water pipe and a control unit for processing the information the first hydraulic pressure measuring part provided on the target block and the second hydraulic pressure measuring part provided on the adjacent block are set to a unit time ttot and the control unit sets the water pressure measured by the first water pressure measurement unit at the first head and the water pressure measured by the second water pressure measuring unit is converted into a second head lt rti and wherein the control unit is configured to set a water level at a drainage peak of the target block and the peak level of the reservoir of the adjacent block and if they do not coincide with each other proceeding to the first processing step and if they are coincident with each other proceeding to the second processing step the first process may include a first data collecting step of collecting a plurality of first data r1 t generated at different time points t according to whether or not the formula 1 is satisfied and when the ratio p1 of the number of first data generated by satisfying the following formula 1 to the total number of the first data is equal to or larger than a predetermined first specific ratio pa and a first result output step of estimating and outputting an inter block disconnection when the second specific ratio is less than a first specific ratio pa and less than a second predetermined ratio pb the second process may include the first head unit time per change which is the absolute value of the first head variation value at each time point t and calculates the second head unit time per change which is the absolute value of the second head variation value at each time point t after the head variation value calculation step the first head variation value rti id 0.0 of the first average head variation value and calculates the second head variation value ttot during the entire measurement time ttot of the second average head variation value calculating an average head variation value the method of claim 1 further comprising determining whether at least one first specific time point t1 satisfying the following equations 2 and 3 exists during the total measurement time ttot t2 satisfying all of the following equations 4 and 5 if at least one of the first specific time t1 and the second specific time t2 does not exist after the specific time calculating step the total time ttot is reset by adding the additional time tp t1 and the second specific time point t2 are all present in the first and second time points t1 t2 the average head variation value calculating step determining an observation interval to by summing all the intervals during a predetermined time ta and at a specific time t1 and after the second specific time t2 after the observation interval determination step a plurality of second data r2 t generated by varying a result value according to whether or not the following equation 6 is satisfied for each time point t within the observation interval to is collected a second data collecting step of collecting data and and when the ratio p2 of the number of second data generated by satisfying the following formula 6 with respect to the total number of the second data is equal to or greater than a predetermined third specific ratio pc and a second result outputting step of estimating and outputting an inter block disconnection when the third specific ratio pc is less than a predetermined fourth specific ratio pd"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100603030-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "4 is a block diagram illustrating in more detail the pressure regulator 124 according to one embodiment of the present invention the pressure regulator 124 being adapted to receive water with varying water pressure through the line 123"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100899657-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "on the other hand a check valve 170 may be provided at one side of the pressure cylinder 152 to block the back flow of the produced water that has passed through the discharge port 145 of the valve housing 142.the reverse osmosis wastewater treatment backpressure pump according to the present invention configured as described above is configured such that the piston is easily moved in the storage space of the valve housing by the operation of a pressurizing cylinder that receives pneumatic pressure or hydraulic pressure to overcome the water pressure applied to the filter portion thereby providing a pressure capable of easily reversing the production water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in configuring the odor prevention device 110 to prevent the odor coming up from the ground the odor prevention device 110 includes a prevention body 112 having a seating flange 111 upward to be seated on the bottom surface of the manhole cover 105 the prevention body 112 and the first vertical portion 113 protrudes downward from the mounting flange 111 an inclined portion 114 formed to have a width narrowed inward from an end of the first vertical portion 113 a second vertical portion 115 projecting downward from the end of the inclined portion 114 a plurality of water passages 116 formed to drain a small amount of rainwater to the inclined portion 114 a discharge hole 117 formed to be opened between the second vertical portions 115 to discharge a large amount of rain and garbage deformed by the hydraulic pressure of the sewage to the water hole 116 while being drained down and after completion of drainage to return to the original state to prevent the odor coming up through the water hole 116 fixing the blocking plate 118 of a material having elasticity and excellent return force the discharge hole 117 is a sewer manhole odor prevention device characterized in that it comprises a rotating plate 120 installed so as to block the odor coming up while draining the rain and waste of the opposite"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "9 water flow through the channel 131 is blocked and the water in bore 126 can only move through water drive line 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "70 is opened and the effluent is collected into the sump 100 while the current groundwater level is lower than the set ground level the effluent water due to the closing pressure of the water level control device 40 70 in the water level control device of the sump well configured to block the collection of water so that the current ground level is lower than the set ground level it is possible to reduce the number of continuous water block and pumping the water level control device 40 70 one end is connected to the collecting pipe 10 and the inlet pipes 22 52 84 provided with hydraulic pressure gauges 21 51 81 for checking the water pressure of the effluent and the inlet pipe 22 52 84 the drain pipe 23 53 85 and the main pipe 24 54 87 connected to the drain pipe 23 53 85 the inlet pipe 22 52 84 is provided with locking ends 25 52a 82 on the upper inner circumferential surface and a cover for preventing foreign matter from penetrating the upper ends of the main tubes 24 54 and 87 body parts 20 50 and 80 fastened to open and close 27 55 and 86 installed inside the body parts 20 50 80 the eluent water flowing into the inlet pipes 22 52 84 is opened and is drained to the drain pipes 23 53 85"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in addition the present invention has the effect of preventing the malfunction in advance by providing a pressure preventing means for enclosing the third opening and closing plate to prevent the third opening and closing plate is not opened by the water pressure in the storage tank even if the buoyancy chamber level is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "US-3871792-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pump system comprising a pump an electric motor in drive connection with said pump a service line a service valve in said service line a pressure switch in electric circuit with said motor and a control valve assembly comprising a valve housing having an input opening for flow connection thereto of said pump a discharge opening for flow connection to said service line and a main flow passageway interconnecting said input opening and said discharge opening a main valve spanning said main passageway means biasing said main valve toward closing position a first auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end with said main passageway on the downstream side of said main valve and terminating in an opening in said housing for hydraulic pressure connection to said pressure switch means coupling said pressure switch to said valve housing at said last opening a pilot valve assembly spanning said first auxiliary passageway and including a valve seat and a valve means normally biasing said pilot valve toward open condition and a second auxiliary passageway said second auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end to said main passageway on the upstream side of said main valve and terminating at said pilot valve in pressure opposing relationship to said biasing means whereby development of hydraulic pressure against said valve in excess of any opposing pressure against said valve will close said valve and block said first auxiliary passageway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102702059-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition the above described non powered scum generator is provided with a cone shaped rotating block that is positioned at the center of the first tank and is capable of non powered rotation by rising hydraulic pressure and a spiral projection is provided on the periphery of the rotating block and a blade that removes scum is connected to the upper portion thereof thereby providing a water circulation treatment system using a high speed oxidation and composite separation process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050751-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "foul smell isolation installation of manhole the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of the manhole and more particularly a plate in which an inlet hole is formed in the center portion to support the manhole cover to inflow the external fluid a reservoir formed in the lower end of the plate and the reservoir it is composed of a blocking film to seal the lower end is normally closed by gravity and magnetic material the blocking film automatically seals the lower end of the reservoir to smoothly block odors flowing back and forth from the water and sewage an open film is formed on the blocking film the open film is a blocking film by rotating to the contrary in rainy or rainy days the water and sewage pipes are flooded and opened to the backflowing fluid to discharge the fluid to the outside to prevent the opening of the manhole by hydraulic pressure thereby preventing personal injury blocking network is installed on the upper surface so that filtering out substances relate to the odor barrier device of a manhole which can prevent clogging of a phase by a foreign matter sewage or bad smell blocking device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however the water supply pipe inspection device is disposed in the center of the opening and closing partition lifting shaft the lifting shaft may be deformed or damaged by the water pressure of the water passing through the water pipe the opening and closing partition is inoperable when the lifting shaft is deformed"}]</data>
