"para_id": "para_39", "text": "the sluice means 30 is a door frame 31 fixed to the outer wall surface of the washing tank 20 to surround the opening 23 and is installed to rotate so that the lower portion is pivoted on the top of the door frame 31 a door frame 32 for opening and closing the opening 23 through the door frame 31 a shaft member 33 installed to rotate across the left and right of the door frame 31 under the door frame 32 it is provided with a plurality of predetermined distances along the length of the shaft member 33 to walk the lower portion of the door 32 to close the opening 23 while rotating along the shaft member 33 for locking or freezing a hook member 34 having a groove 34a in the middle and a cylinder member 35a installed at one side of the door frame 31 and linked through an end of the shaft member 33 and a long hole 35d"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100273822-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water pipe 14 of the water intake well 12 the water meter 14 for displaying the feed amount of the raw water control valve 15 for adjusting the discharge of raw water a check valve 16 for discharging raw water in the pipe 19 in only one direction a pressure gauge 26 displaying hydraulic pressure in the pipe 19 an air valve 25 for discharging air remaining in the pipe 19 or when raw water is pumped from the pumping means 18 and a reverse circulation line 27 for backflowing the remaining raw water in the pipe 19 to the pumping means 18 to prevent freezing when raw water is not being pumped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the groundwater meter and the hydraulic pressure freeze protection device installed inside the upper ground water protection hole characterized in that to prevent freezing by draining into the well 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the time consuming problem is caused.the present invention is to actively solve the problems caused by the freezing of the ground water meter and the hydraulic pressure meter installed in the above described conventional ground water upper protection hole when the operation of the submersible motor pump stops the water supply line automatically shuts off the water supply line the problem of the present invention is to prevent backflow to the pumping device in the upper groundwater protection hole and to prevent freezing by draining the water remaining in the groundwater meter and the hydraulic meter which are components of the pumping device to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the present invention is a technique for branching and installing the drainage branch pipe on one side of the water supply pipe connecting the drainage control valve to the bottom of the drainage branch pipe connecting the residual water drainage pipe to the bottom of the drainage control valve take a look.according to the present invention when the operation of the submersible motor pump is stopped automatically by the water pipe to prevent the water flow back to the water pipe and at the same time draining the water remaining in the pumping device in the upper ground water protective device to the outside cold water pumping device it provides the effect of preventing the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which is a component of the components in advance and greatly reduces the time and manpower associated with checking or replacing the groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge as well as providing convenience of post management after construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in the case of the submersible motor pump 3 provided with a water supply pipe 20 groundwater meter 21 a branching pipe 22 for collecting water which is a component of the pumping device 5 installed inside the upper ground water protection hole 10 and underground water is left in the hydraulic pressure gauge 23 to cause freezing in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "on the other hand the present invention in the case of a general low cost submersible motor pump 3 is not provided with a check valve for preventing the backflow of water in the water supply pipe 12 is automatically prevented backflow and at the same time the stop of the pumping device 5 water remaining in the water supply pipe 20 the groundwater meter 21 the branching pipe 22 and the hydraulic pressure meter 23 which are components passes through the inside of the submersible motor pump 3 while passing through the water supply pipe 4 the total amount of water drained to 1 prevents freezing of the freezing wave thus eliminating the need for the electronic residual water automatic drainage device 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041191-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "underwater motor pump and pumping device installed inside the upper surface of the ground water protection pump during the freezing of the groundwater water pipe characterized in that it further comprises a hydraulic pressure release device 50 for releasing the water pressure while forcibly opening the ball 41 2 component protector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041191-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore the submersible motor pump in the state that the normal water can not be delivered to the water tank due to the freezing of the water pipe the overload pressure is generated as the water pump continues to be sustained the load on the submersible motor pump is heavily loaded and the life may be significantly reduced or damaged"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing process for obtaining pure water from salt water comprising feeding salt water to a vertically arranged elongated closed tank to establish a column of salt water therein the level of which is above the feed point continuously cooling a body of mercury externally of said tank and injecting said mercury in the form of finely atomized particles into the upper portion of said liquid column withdrawing said mercury from the bottom of said tank and recirculating said mercury through said liquid column to maintain the column at a temperature which is subcooled with respect to the salt water infeed so that the infeed has ice crystals formed therein due to contact with the subcooled column permitting the ice crystals to accumulate and form a solid block of ice in the upper portion of said tank above the level of mercury injection moving said block of ice upwardly in said tank by hydraulic pressure of incoming salt water and melting the upper portion of said block of ice by indirect heat exchange with the salt water feed prior to entry of said feed into said column and withdrawing pure water from the upper portion of the tank between the top of said tank and the top of said ice block and withdrawing concentrated salt water and precipitated salts collected above the mercury from the lower portion of said tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101206997-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "making a step installing fixed tube guide means each having a predetermined shape at an inlet of the manhole and an inlet of the conduit installing a movable traction force attenuator for reducing the traction force of the traction winch between the front fixing portion of the first flexible tube and the wire of the traction winch towing the first flexible tube mounted on the flexible tube feeder equipped with the freezing facility in the state where the curable resin is impregnated into the predetermined section of the pipeline to be rehabilitated through the manhole using a towing winch inverting injecting the resin impregnated second flexible tube inside the first flexible tube pulled into the conduit using hydraulic pressure or air pressure to cause the resin impregnated portions of the first and second flexible tubes to adhere to each other by inverting the second flexible tube a heat source is supplied to the first and second flexible tubes having a state in which the second flexible tube is in close contact with the inner wall of the pipeline to harden and integrate the resin impregnated in the first and second flexible tubes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "even in the cold weather in winter it provides a useful effect to prevent the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which are components of the well facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "on the other hand when the operation of the submersible motor pump 4 is stopped there is no further groundwater flow in the water supply pipe 10 the water pressure applied to the piston valve 40 is released and the piston valve 40 is the elastic member 60 the groundwater remaining in various well facilities such as the groundwater meter 6 the hydraulic pressure gauge 8 the branching pipe 7 for the ground water by automatically opening the drainage passage 52 while moving upwards as shown in fig"}]</data>
