  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101301965-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the freezing device for water metering device characterized in that consisting of a lifting member 25 for closing the opening and closing member 14 while the piston 29 is lowered by the hydraulic pressure to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301965-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper part of the discharge pipe is provided with a water hole is drilled inside the elastic spring is installed therein the upper part of the elastic spring is a piston with a fixed piston rod is located the piston stand is in contact with the lower plate of the pressing plate of the opening and closing the upper plate and a lifting member which is configured to be elastically supported so that the opening and closing member is closed while the piston is lowered by the hydraulic pressure acting on the inlet side by the expansion pressure caused by the freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301965-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "it is a feature of the present invention that the lifting member is configured to close the opening and closing member while the piston is lowered by the hydraulic pressure acting on the inlet side at the expansion pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301965-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "piece by the hydraulic pressure acting on the inlet side at the expansion pressure due to the freezing of the water meter 3 as 29 is lowered operating consists in the lifting member 25 to be closed while the opening and closing member 14"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100807744-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "supports the water pressure of the sewage filled between the 1 2 stopper 170 180 and the lifting stopper 130 to prevent all the water pressure of the sewage flowing into the drain hole 10 to be concentrated to the lifting stopper 130 do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100739858-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "that is the repair method according to the present invention basically relates to a non excavation pipeline repair method and is configured by the step of removing foreign substances by spraying pressurized water and the step of placing concrete by spraying thereby towing insertion and pneumatic pressure as described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it is a second object to provide a sediment removal device of a sewage treatment facility that can be adjusted to prevent breakage or breakage of the chain and to improve worker operability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to the present invention the tension sensor of the hydraulic cylinder detects an abnormality such as the tension and break of the chain and sends a signal to the control unit if there is an abnormality in the tension amount by operating the hydraulic unit to supply the hydraulic pressure to the hydraulic cylinder chain tension of the lifting part it can be adjusted during operation which prevents the chain from falling off and damage and improves the workability of the worker"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100964324-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the die press fitting device presses the die at a proper position while moving along the rail 510"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an upstream side main water supply pipe 101 connected to a water supply source and provided with a water supply pump 130 a downstream side main water supply pipe 102 connected to the upstream side main water supply pipe 101 through a main on off valve 110 a sprinkler bridge 200 branched from the downstream main supply pipe 102 and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and a sprinkler head 300 installed at a lower end of the sprinkler double pipe 200 first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the main opening closing valve 110 respectively further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flow meters 510 520 respectively installed at an inlet end and an outlet end of the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 a drain pipe 600 connected to the sprinkler bridge pipe 200 through the three way valve 610 and provided with a drain pipe meter 620 between the second sprinkler bridge pipe flow meter 520 and the sprinkler head 300 lt rti the main on off valve 110 includes a valve body 111 connected to the upstream main supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 a valve cap 112 covering the upper portion of the valve body 111 a valve seat 116 formed in the valve body 111 an opening closing plate 117 installed in the valve body 111 to open and close the valve seat 116 a lifting and lowering rod 118 coupled to an upper end of the nut 117 and a nut box 119 screwed to the lifting and lowering rod 118 and an opening and closing drive means 120 for rotating the nut box 119 including the valve cap 112 includes an elevation guide portion 113 for vertically supporting the elevating and lowering rod 118 a rotation support portion 114 for rotatably supporting the nut box 119 and a reinforcing connecting portion 115 connecting the portion 113 and the rotation supporting portion 114 the opening and closing drive means 120 includes a drive motor 123 mounted on a motor mount 122 fixed to a support plate 121 integrally formed with the rotary support 114 and a driven gear 126 coupled to an upper end of the nut box 119 and engaged with the driving gear 125 the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 and the first and second sprinkler pipe flowmeters 410 and 420 are controlled by controlling the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 according to the detection signals of the water discharge pipes 510 and 520 and the discharge pipe flow meter 620 and a control means 700 the control means 700 includes a fire detector 710 installed on the building an input unit 720 for inputting the normal mode and the test mode a main opening closing valve sensor 730 for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve 110 the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and the 3 way valve 610 according to the fire detection signal of the fire detector 710 and the input signal of the input unit 720 the flow rate of the refrigerant is detected on the upstream side in accordance with the sensing signals of the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 the first and second sprinkler pipe flow meters 510 and 520 the drain pipe flow meter 620 it is possible to judge the abnormality of the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main water supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 to determine an abnormality position display command and an alarm command a control unit 740 for outputting a command to display the degree of opening of the main on off valve 110 a valve driver 750 for sending a driving signal to the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 and the three way valve 610 according to a control command of the controller 740 a display unit 760 for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the controller 740 and an alarm unit 770 for outputting an alarm according to an alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "at this time the drive motor 123 fails or a failure occurs between the lifting lowering rod 118 and the nut box 119 when the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally due to the adhesion the digested water supplied through the upstream main water pipe 101 flows into the upstream side valve body 910 through the upstream side bypass pipe 810 the hydraulic pressure applied to the cone 940 is greater than the elastic force of the valve spring 950 so that the valve cone 940 moves away from the valve seat portion 930 to the downstream side and the hydraulic pressure sensitive on and the extinguishing water passes through the upstream side internal space 911 of the upstream valve body 910 and the downstream side internal space 921 of the downstream valve body 920 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and the t side water supply pipe 102 through the water supply pipe 821 water is supplied to the sprinkler head 300 through the pipe 200 and a normal fire suppression is performed see fig"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5725558-B2", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "1a inlet tube section water pipe 1b receiving pipe part water pipe 1a pipe inner peripheral surface 1c expanded base end surface 1d large diameter inner peripheral surface 2a receiving pipe part other water pipes 2b inlet tube part other water pipes 2a pipe inner peripheral surface 2d outer peripheral surface 2e front end surface 10 cylindrical main body 20 annular water stop bag 51 wheel 70 arc shaped mounting portion 70a inner peripheral surface 70b outer peripheral surface 70c insertion front end surface 71 annular portion 71a inner peripheral surface 71b insertion front end surface 72 circular fitting part 72a inner peripheral surface 72b outer peripheral surface 72c insertion tip surface 73 lifting hook 80 support base 81 height adjustment part a hydraulic pressure tester b joint part g in pipe carry in guide device p1 water pipe fluid pipe p2 other water pipes fluid pipes x tube axis fluid tube y axis cylindrical body z axis arc shaped mounting part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156757-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "double manhole cover with lifting structure linked type double manhole cover the present invention relates to a manhole cover installed in the manhole and more particularly by forming a double manhole cover formed in a double so as to be selectively opened and closed while interlocking with the hydraulic pressure inside the manhole the sewage in the manhole the double manhole cover which is selectively opened by water pressure controls the pressure inside the manhole to maintain a certain pressure below a certain pressure even if it flows backward so that the manhole cover is separated by the high water pressure inside the manhole or each connection part of the manhole and the pipe connected thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156757-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole cover installed in the manhole and more particularly by forming a double manhole cover formed in a double so as to be selectively opened and closed while interlocking with the hydraulic pressure inside the manhole the sewage in the manhole the double manhole cover which is selectively opened by water pressure controls the pressure inside the manhole to maintain a certain pressure below a certain pressure even if it flows backward so that the manhole cover is separated by the high water pressure inside the manhole and it relates to a double manhole cover having a hinge type lifting structure characterized in that to prevent the fragile portion from being broken and to facilitate the locking of the double manhole cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10 0816410 registered on march 18 2008 more specifically the manhole is made of a cylindrical one of the manhole the present invention relates to a water conduit inspection device which can prevent stress concentration from occurring in a portion and that lifting shafts are disposed at both side ends of the opening closing partition to prevent the lifting shafts from being deformed by hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however the water supply pipe inspection device is disposed in the center of the opening and closing partition lifting shaft the lifting shaft may be deformed or damaged by the water pressure of the water passing through the water pipe the opening and closing partition is inoperable when the lifting shaft is deformed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439293-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "on the other hand the controller 10 continuously detects the pressure drop while the raw water is discharged through the water supply pipe 51 but when the raw water is near the high water level h and the middle water level m or the low water level l the pressure drop detected when close is different"}]</data>
