  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200253849-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "on the other hand in the flange portion 65 of the main body 60 of the hydraulic pressure buffer means 50 and the flange portion 102 of the sealing cap 100 to form an annular groove 66 105 the groove inserting a fixing sealer 70 for sealing in the 66 and 105 to prevent the leakage of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a leak detection device for a tap water pipe installed in a water pipe by a flange to detect leakage of tap water a pressure sensor provided at one end of the water pipe facing the water pipe to detect a hydraulic pressure drop occurring during leakage an acoustic sensor connected to the pressure sensor in the longitudinal direction and detecting a sound wave generated during leakage and a second printed circuit board connected to the acoustic sensor and connected to the pressure sensor to generate a pressure sensor signal the second printed circuit board being connected to the acoustic sensor to generate an acoustic sensor signal a printed circuit board portion an inner housing that watertightly surrounds the printed circuit board portion a pipe holder connected to the printed circuit board part in a longitudinally watertight manner an extension pipe having one end connected to the pipe holder and extending in the longitudinal direction and cables for transmitting sensor signals of the first and second printed circuit boards are arranged therein and and an outer housing which surrounds the acoustic sensor and the inner housing so that the pipe holder is coupled at one end and the tap is coupled to the flange at the other end the pressure sensor includes a pressure cell for generating an electric signal relating to a change in water pressure through a strain gauge attached to a diaphragm to which a hydraulic pressure acts and a pressure cell housing surrounding the pressure cell and having a ring the acoustic sensor includes an acoustic sensor holder having one end connected to the pressure cell housing and the other end protruding a ring shaped protrusion corresponding to the ring shaped step and the other end inserted into the inner housing in a watertight manner and an epoxy molding unit for integrating the pressure cell housing and the acoustic sensor holder the acoustic vibration sensor comprising a cylinder shaped vibrator installed in the cavity of the acoustic transducer and an epoxy molding unit surrounding the outer periphery of the cylindrical vibrator and integrating the pressure cell housing and the acoustic sensor holder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a water leakage detection apparatus for a water supply pipe provided with a sound pressure composite sensor comprising a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks one of the first and second printed circuit boards connected to the pressure sensor is arranged on one side of the support plate of the substrate support and the first and second printed circuit boards are connected to the acoustic sensor the other one of the two printed circuit boards is arranged side by side on the other side of the support plate of the substrate support which also has the advantage that the overall size or length is not excessively increased due to the compact arrangement described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "here the pressure sensor 10 senses the water leakage due to a cause such as rupture or the like in the water pipe 5 by detecting the water pressure drop generated when water is immersed in the tap water flowing through the water pipe 5 a pressure cell 11 for generating an electric signal relating to a hydraulic pressure change through a strain gauge attached to a diaphragm to which a hydraulic pressure acts as well as a general gauge type pressure sensor not shown in detail and a pressure cell housing 13 on which an annular step 13a is formed on which an end of the coplanar 23a of the acoustic sensor 20 is seated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "one of the circuit boards 33 and 35 is arranged on one side of the support plate 31c of the substrate support 31 and the other of the first and second printed circuit boards 33 and 35 connected to the acoustic sensor 20 are arranged side by side on the other side of the support plate 31c of the substrate support 31 so that the overall size and length are not excessively increased due to the above described compact arrangement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100973662-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "sensing unit 110 a measurement signal processor 120 for converting the analog signal measured by the detector 110 into a digital signal a data transmission device 130 for transmitting a digital signal for the hydraulic pressure data the supply flow data the meter reading data and the leak data converted through the measurement signal processing unit 120 to the communication server 141 of the central control room 140 a database server 142 for storing hydraulic pressure data supply flow data meter reading data and leakage data transmitted through the data transmission device 130 and the communication server 141 by dividing them into date position and measured value a first analysis server 143 for setting a leak generation block through data analysis of the database server 142 a second analysis server 144 for inferring a leakage occurrence point by analyzing water pipes in the block set through the first analysis server 143 in the leak position detecting system for detecting the leak position of the water supply pipe consisting of a display unit 150 for indicating the leak predicted point inferred through the second analysis server 144 the second analysis server 144 analyzes the leak detector the water pipe aging degree and mathematical modeling and then infers the predicted leakage point using the statistical method by fuzzy inference"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100973662-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a detector for measuring water pressure data supply flow rate data meter reading data and leak data through a pressure gauge a flow meter a meter and a leak detector installed in a water pipe within a water supply pipe network partitioned by block units a measurement signal processing unit for converting the analog signal measured by the detection unit into a digital signal a data transmission device for transmitting the digital signal for the hydraulic pressure data the supply flow rate data the meter reading amount data and the leakage data converted through the measurement signal processing unit to a communication server of the central control room a database server for storing the hydraulic pressure data the supply flow data the meter reading data and the leak data transmitted through the data transmission apparatus and the communication server by dividing the data into a date a position and a measured value a first analysis server for setting a leak generation block through data analysis of the database server a second analysis server for inferring a leakage occurrence point by analyzing water pipes in the block set through the first analysis server in the leak position detection system for detecting the leak position of the water supply pipe consisting of a display unit for indicating the predicted leakage point inferred through the second analysis server the second analysis server analyzes the leak detector water pipe aging and mathematical modeling and then infers the predicted location of the leak by using a statistical method based on fuzzy inference"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137769-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition a number of filters shorten the filter life due to the continuous hydraulic pressure of the raw water may cause waste of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100697628-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "therefore even if the magnitude of the hydraulic pressure is greatly increased the force of the hydraulic pressure is dispersed by the sealing member 150 so that the disk plate 120 can resist the large hydraulic pressure so that there is no fear of leakage due to the hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101228687-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "by installing a bushing as the outlet of the outlet pipe to prevent leakage while maintaining the specification of the outlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920502-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it is possible to more easily and accurately calculate the flow rate leakage amount for each small block by installing a flowmeter at the inlet for each small block and measuring the real time supply flow rate while constructing the water pipe network as a block system as described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200185447-Y1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "therefore the conventional wall panel and the wall panel is directly bonded in a planar shape the wall panels arranged adjacent to each other around the joint at the four corners are deformed by the force of the hydraulic pressure the bending moment around the junction there is an advantage to solve the problem that the leakage caused by the gap between the gap between the wall panel is opened by the action"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101083035-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "therefore power consumption of the pressure sensor and the pressure transmitter installed in the water valve can be minimized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200410523-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "a body having a fastening hole formed in the member to concentrate the pressing force to the edge of the panel when the fastening hole is engaged with the flange a triangular side plate coupled to both sides of the body to prevent deformation of the body and having a through hole having the same axis therein wherein the reinforcing bar fixing bolt is inserted into the through hole reinforcing bar fixing bolt inserted into the through hole bolts for tightening 