  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100632978-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "when the driving shaft 411 is rotated the turning ring rear rotating gear 412 1 rotates by being engaged with the driving shaft 411 with the teeth and the turning ring attached to the front surface of the turning ring rear rotating gear 412 1 412 is rotated the hydraulic pressure installed in the excavation bit holder 421 connected to one side of the turning ring 412 while grinding the excavation bit 420 up and down by pulverizing the damaged parts protruded and rotated through the crushing material suction device 402 with a vacuum pump is built in suction the finely ground crushed material after letting 6th process glass fiber spraying process when the drive motor 503 is operated so that the glass fiber spraying unit e located at the rear of the broken portion crushing and crushing material removal unit d is continuously introduced into the sewer pipe and operated it is connected to the drive transmission device 502"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102207360-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a first motor and a suction hopper mounted in front of the body to suck the sediment a discharge pipe connected in communication with the suction hopper to send the sucked sediment to the outside and installed inside the suction hopper to crush the sediment an underwater cleaning robot comprising a crushing screw and a second motor for driving the crushing screw and a hydraulic pressure generating device mounted on the body and configured to drive the first and second motors using hydraulic pressure and control remotely the technology is also presented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014010-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the crushing mixer 10 is connected to a drive motor 13 and an inverter 14 for driving it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101759711-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "0563988summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above circumstances and an object of the present invention is to provide a shredding unit in which a plurality of blades are radially provided and new towing elements for replacement are connected successively the sewage pipe is crushed and the new sewer pipe is automatically replaced in succession while being moved using a wire driven as a pulling unit that intermittently pulls together with union and release the present invention provides a sewer pipe replacement device which can reduce the unit cost and replace the sewer pipe can shorten the construction period and reduce the cost.summary of the invention it is an object of the present invention to provide a replacement apparatus for a non drilling sewage pipe in which an old or damaged synthetic resin drain pipe buried in the ground for drainage of sewage or wastewater is replaced with a new one a crushing unit provided with a number of blades radially in a conical body and provided with new traction elements for replacement and a pair of upper and lower actuators arranged in parallel on the base and reciprocating forward and backward using hydraulic pressure a pulling unit having first and second gripping elements which are mounted on each of the fixed and movable stages and which are tied and released in a reciprocating manner depending on whether a frictional force acts or not wherein the first gripping element is adapted to move forward and backward in the reciprocating motion of the traction unit and the second gripping element is repeatedly held to maintain the position of the wire pulled back while the wire is retracted the wire is intermittently moved and the old sewing pipe is crushed by using the crushing unit so that replacement work can be performed easily"}]</data>
</edge>
