  <data key="d5">["generator", "disinfection", "generation", "projection", "speed", "system", "sedimentation", "center", "decomposition", "membrane", "valve", "decontamination", "invention", "blade", "adsorption", "effluent", "block", "rotation", "load", "variation", "side", "water", "purpose", "tank", "treatment", "fall", "addition", "circulation", "carbon", "bod", "matter", "oxidation", "detail", "portion", "end", "process", "course", "contaminant", "difference", "inlet", "scum", "filtration", "control", "screen", "separation", "microorganism", "figure", "amount", "sewage", "periphery", "unit", "flow", "contamination", "function", "aeration", "removal", "height", "pump", "pressure", "cone"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["contain", "alleviate", "perform", "apply", "treat", "position", "provide", "constitute", "rise", "connect", "use", "dissolve", "float", "rotate", "maintain", "remove", "show", "screen", "control", "activate", "shape", "be", "determine", "adjust", "describe", "instal"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100443423-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the present invention for this purpose the sedimentation tank 31 for sedimentation and removal of foreign matter the screen tank 32 for screening and removing large contaminants contained in the effluent of the sedimentation tank the amount of sewage to be treated even when excessive raw water generation to alleviate contaminant load variation function as a flow control tank that maintains constant water and as an aeration tank to remove organic matter from sewage by oxidation and decomposition by microorganisms and floating and colloidal contaminants in the treated water from which dissolved bod is removed by aeration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in detail the hydraulic pressure applied to the treated water is determined by the pressure the pressure due to the height difference h1 between the membrane filtration unit 100 and the residual decontamination unit 200 the pressure due to the height difference h2 between the advanced oxidation tank 210 and the activated carbon adsorption tank 220 in the residual contamination removal unit 200 the pressure due to the height difference h3 between the activated carbon adsorption tank 220 and the disinfection tank 230 of course if there is a height difference between the disinfection tank 230 and the purified water 2 as shown in figure 3 the pressure due to free fall is also applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101334651-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore by controlling the pump 10 and the valve 33 installed on the raw water inlet side of the membrane filtration unit 100 the advanced oxidation tank 210 activated carbon adsorption constituting the residual contamination removal unit 200 installed at the rear end by adjusting the hydraulic pressure in the tank 220 and the disinfection tank 230 it is possible to smoothly perform each water treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102702059-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition the above described non powered scum generator is provided with a cone shaped rotating block that is positioned at the center of the first tank and is capable of non powered rotation by rising hydraulic pressure and a spiral projection is provided on the periphery of the rotating block and a blade that removes scum is connected to the upper portion thereof thereby providing a water circulation treatment system using a high speed oxidation and composite separation process"}]</data>
</edge>
