  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200166989-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is characterized in that it consists of a packing part to be in close contact with the frame when the water is discharged to prevent the water is discharged to the outside or water is introduced from the outside the frame and the door part are reinforced with corrosion resistance by using a non metallic material and the hinge part is formed to be able to open and close in a rotatable state in a state where the door part is fixed and coupled to the frame at a corresponding position on the upper side thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "meanwhile the dry fire extinguishing system according to the present invention can be designed to prevent corrosion due to water remaining inside the pipe after a hydraulic pressure test and water leakage due to valve leakage by installing a dry air facility or an air compressor equipped with a heater that supplies dry air and also to install a drain cock at the lowest part of a branch pipe and a cross pipe to discharge and dry water remaining in the pipe by dry air or compressed air thereby blocking corrosion due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "according to one embodiment in order to prevent corrosion caused by the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe after discharging the mixed extinguishing water according to a hydraulic pressure test or fire detection the dry extinguishing system may install at least one drain cock not shown in each of the cross pipe 5 and the branch pipe 6 to discharge the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "meanwhile the dry fire extinguishing system according to the present invention can be designed to prevent corrosion due to water remaining inside the pipe after a hydraulic pressure test and water leakage due to valve leakage by installing a dry air facility or an air compressor equipped with a heater that supplies dry air and also to install a drain cock at the lowest part of a branch pipe and a cross pipe to discharge and dry water remaining in the pipe by dry air or compressed air thereby blocking corrosion due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "according to one embodiment in order to prevent corrosion caused by the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe after discharging the mixed extinguishing water according to a hydraulic pressure test or fire detection the dry extinguishing system may install at least one drain cock not shown in each of the cross pipe 5 and the branch pipe 6 to discharge the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101047186-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "other factors to consider include water pressure seawater loads when large fish collide the size and material of the tank the waterproofing and finishing materials that take into account the hydraulic pressure and the selection of materials to prevent fatal toxicity and corrosion to the fish"}]</data>
</edge>
