  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200395622-Y1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "even if the waterway 70 is completely closed the water is prevented from being contaminated because the stored water is continuously discharged over a part of the water pipe 50.as described above according to the present invention the deep water of the stored water is sprinkled and discharged to the outside according to the low water level thereby inducing the movement of the stored water thereby preventing water pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837300-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel portion for guiding water to move in a predetermined direction an infiltration inducing pipe portion penetrating through the bottom surface of the water channel portion and communicating with an underground aquifer below the impermeable layer in the ground layer a filtering unit installed at a connection portion between the infiltration induction pipe and the water channel unit and composed of several layers for removing foreign matter from water flowing into the underground aquifer and having a lower porosity toward the lower layer and and an opening closing part for selectively shielding the infiltration induction tube part the water a sediment guiding part having a guide protruding from the bottom surface of the water channel part and a settling groove formed between the guide and the guide an induction intrusion section having an inclined surface inclined upward in the moving direction of the water on the bottom surface of the water channel part and an inlet port formed on the opposite vertical surface and and a water film portion for controlling the amount and movement of water moving along the water channel portion the infiltration induction pipe portion may include an induction pipe connected to the induction pier at the upper end and connected to the underground aquifer below a flow rate measuring unit installed at an upper side of the guide pipe to measure an amount of water moving along the guide pipe and a water level control valve provided below the flow rate measuring unit and passing through the induction pipe the water level control valve includes a cylindrical body through which upper and lower parts pass a first inlet connected to an upper portion of the induction pipe a second inlet connected to a lower portion of the induction pipe and a buoyant body selectively shielding the first inlet and the second inlet while moving up and down along the body the opening a high level sensor installed at a relatively high position in the infiltration induction pipe a low water level sensor installed at a relatively low position in the permeation guide pipe a door unit provided at a relatively higher position than the high level sensing sensor to selectively shield the induction pipe and a control unit for receiving the signal of the high level sensing sensor and the low level sensing sensor and the signal of the flow rate measurement unit and controlling the door unit when the signal of the high level sensing sensor is received the control part shields the door part so as to prevent the water in the waterway part from flowing into the underground aquifer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654788-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "electrolysis in the electrolytic chamber is performed efficiently to increase the concentration of dissolved hydrogen while suppressing damage to the diaphragm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the scum removal device is installed in the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to discharge only scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing device it has a hopper shaped body which is located inside the waterway and introduces a scum to the outside of the waterway through the discharge pipe formed at the bottom thereof and a support bar for supporting the scum detection sensor and the water level detection sensor on the upper part of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in the scum removing apparatus according to the present invention for achieving this object in the scum removing apparatus is installed in the water channel of the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to flow only the scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing apparatus includes a scum hopper positioned inside the channel and flowing in the scum to flow out of the channel through a discharge pipe formed at a lower portion thereof an elevating unit configured to elevate the scum hopper a support part supported on the upper side of the waterway to support the lifting part a scum detecting sensor installed at a front portion of the scum hopper to sense an amount of floating scum a water level sensor installed at a rear portion of the scum hopper to detect a water level and a controller for adjusting the height of the scum hopper by controlling the lifting unit according to the detection state of the scum detecting sensor and the water level detecting sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve 