 of the drainage side of the watershed and between the support rods and the bottom of the waterway and a lifting cylinder capable of lifting and lowering the water gate is provided in the support base and a guide hole is formed in the longitudinal direction of the support base on a surface of the support base opposed to the water gate and between the rod and the drain side of the water inlet a fixing rod and the lifting cylinder is lifted upwardly in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder in the closed state of the watercourse so that the weight of the watercount which is stored in the watercounting space is clean the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 further comprising the steps of discharging the lower layer water first to purify contaminated river water thereby inducing a substance separation action caused by the action of gravity while purifying the contaminated river water with clean river water the shape of the hydrograph plate 80 is continuously bent in the shape of w in the transverse direction and bonded to the fixed bar 32 the vertical supports 90 and 91 which are continuously arranged in the form of a triangle vertically laid out on the lower surface and the upper surface of the water gate plate 80 to prevent warpage of the water gate plate 80 from 30 cm to 1 m together with zooming at intervals of and an index member not shown is coupled to the horizontal and vertical directions of the water gate plate 80 the water leveling plate 80 and the vertical supports 90 and 91 are combined to form a hybrid type opening closing member of a double layer structure having a flat plate shape the cylinder head according to any one of claims 1 to 5 wherein the cylinder head 51 of the lifting cylinder 50 is driven in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder 50 the water level plate 80 is lowered in accordance with the operation to shut off the discharge of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a