lat plate shape the cylinder head according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the cylinder head 51 of the lifting cylinder 40 is driven in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder 40 the water level plate 800 is lowered in accordance with the operation to shut off the discharge of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "2003 063287 since the structure that drives the gate is complicated it is easy to catch foreign matter and it is possible to prevent the foreign matter from floating in the guide groove formed on the side of the gate of the foreign material floating in the upstream of the flood there is a structural problem that the flood damage will be caused by the action that the foreign substances that are caught in the water supply channel block the water channel and increase the water level"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4441460-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "2 the method for identifying the location of the water leak in the water channel 20 is that the at least the downstream end 21 of the target area 20 a of the water channel 20 is partitioned by a corner drop 31 as an example of a partition plate"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "this means that after the drainage or waste water has been drained off the clean rainwater flowing through the rainwater channel in the event of a rain event is completely conducted to the receiving water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the auxiliary valve is installed on the outer periphery of the main valve and consists of a water shielding plate and a projecting floating body that floats it and the outer periphery of the projecting floating body is used to prevent malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to the wave of rain water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200371586-Y1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "in addition even if the water level in the water channel is low or under water surface it is possible to remove foreign substances and contaminants caught in the lower portion of the potential screen thereby improving the recovery rate of foreign substances and contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102601272-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "it forms a side screening wall 101 and a drain 102a that discharges the filtered water filtered through the screen structure 200 and on the inner surface a gasket covers both ends of the screen structure 200 to prevent the inflow of impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101468197-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "however even in the case of such a rotary water gate it is necessary to further regulate the discharge amount depending on the water level in the water storage space the flow rate of the water and the like even when the water is discharged from the water storage space to the lower end of the water gate plate by further rotating the water gate in the closed state therefore in order to control the discharge amount of the water storage space a plurality of stoppers or limit switches having different positions are provided and the opening degree of the water gate is adjusted by stopping the position of the water gate by the stopper or the limit switch it takes a lot of cost to install the apparatus and further energy is required to open the rotating sluice gate in a multistage manner so that the maintenance cost is high.the present invention allows water to be raised and lowered in a closed state so that the lower water of the water storage space is discharged through the lower space of the water receptacle so that contaminants such as sedimentation sludge are discharged together with the discharged water to purify the water quality so as to purify contaminated water by clean water.in order to solve these problems the present invention is characterized in that the water gate is rotatably fixed to the drive shaft and is configured to be able to open and close the water channel while being self standing or conducting by the operation cylinder and the drive shaft is guided along the guide groove formed in the housing and the drive shaft can be guided in the up and down direction by the lifting cylinder and the lifting link"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the water level of the waterway 3 is high and the flow velocity is high refers to the maximum inside water level when opening of the water channel 3 is required because the obstacle damping device 100 is damaged due to runoff and impurities due to a large amount of impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200191686-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "endless chain 14 that rotates along rake 15 of the rake retainer installed on the chain to rotate together the drive motor 16 for driving the chain to prevent the lifting of the contaminated lifting into the water and protect the drive shaft in the vibration damper having a configuration such as an apron 17 a water level sensor 18 is installed on the waterway wall or the vibration suppressor so that the rotational speed of the rake 15 can be varied according to the inflow quantity"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5699445-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "when the water level in the pit 1d is lowered due to the evaporation and scattering of the cooling water the ball tap 5 is opened the makeup water is supplied from the makeup water channel 6 and the water level of the pit 1d is kept constant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357600-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "water level control to adjust the water level so that all parts of the electrode and the plurality of electrode set 20 to the electrolytic module 10 which is a kind of frame of cylindrical or cylindrical shape and two electrode plates installed inside the module as a set it is composed of a wear 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the waste water collecting device for drainage to remove a resistance shaft 39 provided on the bottom surface of the water channel 10 a voltage variable element 37 provided at the end of the resistance shaft 39 to output a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 it is provided on the outside of the resistance shaft 39 is raised and lowered according to the water level level is provided with a water level sensor 36 made of a float 38 for changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 the control unit 31 is a waste collection device for drainage characterized in that to adjust the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in proportion to the water level level of the channel 10 detected by the water level sensor 36"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the present invention is a control method of a waste water collecting device for the drainage to repeatedly remove the contaminants introduced into the waterway by the rake installed in the chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller a current level determination process of reading the water level of the water flowing in the waterway a water level determination process of determining whether the current water level read through the current water level determination process is a set low water level a medium water level a high water level and the water level determination process if the current level of the water channel is judged to be low drive the lifting motor at low speed.if the current level is judged to be medium drive the lifting motor to medium speed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "by automatically controlling the operating speed of the lifting motor if the inflow of water increases such as during rainy weather the speed of collecting the contaminants can be smoothed thereby smoothing the flow of water into the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100191863-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore the present invention has been made to solve the above problems the raw water is filtered through a multi stage pre treatment filter membrane filter post treatment filter to store the water in the storage tank and to circulate the drained concentrated water refiltered a reverse osmosis water purification device comprising a water quality sensor installed at a front end of a pretreatment filter to detect a pollution concentration of raw water and to block inflow of raw water according to a contamination state of concentrated water a first drain valve branched between the water quality sensor and the pretreatment filter and configured to drain according to the pollution concentration of the raw water a solenoid valve disposed between the primary drain valve and the pretreatment filter and configured to open close the water channel by an electric operation according to the pollution concentration and the water level of the auxiliary reservoir tank and the reservoir tank an auxiliary reservoir installed between the all carbon filter and the membrane filter to pump water from the all carbon filter to the membrane filter and to receive the drained water of the membrane filter a secondary drain valve connected to a lower portion of the auxiliary reservoir and configured to drain according to a contamination state of the concentrated water a timer for setting a time of the maximum pollution value of the concentrated water circulated in the auxiliary reservoir and opening the secondary drain valve when the time expires detect the contamination concentration from the water quality sensor close the solenoid valve open the primary drain valve pump the membrane water when the auxiliary reservoir is full and secondary when the timer expires"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100397886-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the installation screen is automatically lifted according to the water level 30 to block the impurities such as garbage flowing along the water and the rake 10 of the upper side while elevating by the driving force of the chain inside the rail 20 arc type by angular movement to handle the waste caught in the floating screen 30 in particular the rake 10 is vertically lowered from the upper side of the inside of the rail 20 in the state fixed to the shaft 11 floating screen 30 after going down the water along the rails 20 and angularly moving in an arc shape without receiving the interference of garbage etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442471-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 installed on the waterway so as to be movable in the transverse direction a beam stand 11 mounted to the main body 10 to be elevated a rake 12 installed at the tip of the beam stand 11 to scrape up dirt in a waterway as the beam stand 11 moves up and down an elevating driver 15 for elevating the beam stage 11 a water level sensor 14 for detecting the water level in the water channel a controller 40 for controlling the lift position of the beam stage 11 by controlling the lift driver 15 according to the level detected by the water level sensor 14 a parallel moving drive unit 130 for moving the main body in the lateral direction and it includes a timer for measuring the lifting time of the beam stage 11 and the moving time of the main body 10 the controller 40 controls the beam stage 11 to be elevated to a predetermined depth below the water surface in the water channel according to the result measured by the timer and controls the horizontal movement amount of the main body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "summary of the invention an object of the present invention is to provide a water borne contaminant removal apparatus capable of continuously removing contaminants while maintaining the water level in a water channel and dehydrating water so that the water content contained in the contaminants is removed to lower the water content"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "this allows the scrapers to be filtered by the screw scraper 300 which is erected vertically to the water channel 10 and is rotated inside the filtration screen 100 when the sewage is passed through the water channel 10 the screw scraper 300 does not interfere with the collection and transport of the contaminants by causing the water level of the water channel 10 to change when the contaminant is pushed up by the rotation which is capable of maintaining the water level of the water channel 10 as it is so as to smoothly remove contaminants continuously and at the same time to remove moisture contained in the contaminants by the dehydrating unit 500 so as to lower the water content can be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "accordingly when the water level flowing along the water channel 10 is lowered the contaminant transporting section having a circular shape on the flat section is extended downward to descend the up and down gate 250 to transport the contaminants filtered by the filtration screen 100 it is possible to smoothly carry out the contaminant transport without loss"}]</data>
</edge>
