  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200395622-Y1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "even if the waterway 70 is completely closed the water is prevented from being contaminated because the stored water is continuously discharged over a part of the water pipe 50.as described above according to the present invention the deep water of the stored water is sprinkled and discharged to the outside according to the low water level thereby inducing the movement of the stored water thereby preventing water pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_703", "text": "the stream river reservoir lake lagoon or contaminated river water flowing in the vicinity of a dam characterized in that the purified water is naturally purified by floating the river water to the upper part of the eco friendly water purification device 200 used as the water purifier a nature friendly friendliness that naturally purifies polluted water while producing electricity by using an eco friendly water purification device that combines pollutants and soil water and purifies and cleans the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837300-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel portion for guiding water to move in a predetermined direction an infiltration inducing pipe portion penetrating through the bottom surface of the water channel portion and communicating with an underground aquifer below the impermeable layer in the ground layer a filtering unit installed at a connection portion between the infiltration induction pipe and the water channel unit and composed of several layers for removing foreign matter from water flowing into the underground aquifer and having a lower porosity toward the lower layer and and an opening closing part for selectively shielding the infiltration induction tube part the water a sediment guiding part having a guide protruding from the bottom surface of the water channel part and a settling groove formed between the guide and the guide an induction intrusion section having an inclined surface inclined upward in the moving direction of the water on the bottom surface of the water channel part and an inlet port formed on the opposite vertical surface and and a water film portion for controlling the amount and movement of water moving along the water channel portion the infiltration induction pipe portion may include an induction pipe connected to the induction pier at the upper end and connected to the underground aquifer below a flow rate measuring unit installed at an upper side of the guide pipe to measure an amount of water moving along the guide pipe and a water level control valve provided below the flow rate measuring unit and passing through the induction pipe the water level control valve includes a cylindrical body through which upper and lower parts pass a first inlet connected to an upper portion of the induction pipe a second inlet connected to a lower portion of the induction pipe and a buoyant body selectively shielding the first inlet and the second inlet while moving up and down along the body the opening a high level sensor installed at a relatively high position in the infiltration induction pipe a low water level sensor installed at a relatively low position in the permeation guide pipe a door unit provided at a relatively higher position than the high level sensing sensor to selectively shield the induction pipe and a control unit for receiving the signal of the high level sensing sensor and the low level sensing sensor and the signal of the flow rate measurement unit and controlling the door unit when the signal of the high level sensing sensor is received the control part shields the door part so as to prevent the water in the waterway part from flowing into the underground aquifer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide water pipe body fitted into the above drain and having an open upper portion to receive the above rainwater a grating member that is fitted and fixed to the upper part of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain permeation guide holes formed on the side wall of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain a shielding control panel positioned inside the guide water channel body to open or close the above pitching guide holes a lifting and transporting guide means provided in the above guide waterway body and for lifting and transporting the shielding control panel and in a road drainage device for preventing water retention on a road surface the device is composed of a filter net member that is fitted and fixed into the water permeation guide hole formed in the guide water channel body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101415953-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "according to the vibration damping device of the present invention since the driven drum is opened so as to allow the water to be removed from the various sides of the driven drum the flow of the water flowing along the waterway increases without affecting the flow of the water it is possible to prevent an accident that the water overflows in the water channel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the scum removal device is installed in the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to discharge only scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing device it has a hopper shaped body which is located inside the waterway and introduces a scum to the outside of the waterway through the discharge pipe formed at the bottom thereof and a support bar for supporting the scum detection sensor and the water level detection sensor on the upper part of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in the scum removing apparatus according to the present invention for achieving this object in the scum removing apparatus is installed in the water channel of the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to flow only the scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing apparatus includes a scum hopper positioned inside the channel and flowing in the scum to flow out of the channel through a discharge pipe formed at a lower portion thereof an elevating unit configured to elevate the scum hopper a support part supported on the upper side of the waterway to support the lifting part a scum detecting sensor installed at a front portion of the scum hopper to sense an amount of floating scum a water level sensor installed at a rear portion of the scum hopper to detect a water level and a controller for adjusting the height of the scum hopper by controlling the lifting unit according to the detection state of the scum detecting sensor and the water level detecting sensor"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6885661-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "transport and by configuring the rear wheels to cut off the driving force received from the engine the user removes the deposits while manually moving the channel deposit remover and or the rear wheels are the engine"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6885661-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "there is a risk that the posture stability of the deposit removing device 10 may not be maintained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101378786-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "therefore the transfer part 15 is provided inside the pair of support frames 13 to move up down from the outside of the waterway to the inside or to allow the worker to stay in the desired position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403858-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "water channel cover 1 according to an embodiment of the present invention as shown in figure 1 or 2 the water permeable filling block 40 is composed of a hwabar resin and natural gravel in the inner space of the water channel cover 1 it is possible to prevent garbage or foreign substances from entering the sewage by filling them and to make the beauty of beauty by using the permeable filling block 40 of various colors and to display the jurisdiction so that it can be used as a function of the display panel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403858-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "frame 10 which forms the overall shape of the waterway cover 1 and forms a space portion by a partition plate therein and is inserted into the internal space of the frame 10 described above and includes a fiber resin and natural gravel the waterway cover 1 formed of the castle filling block 40 is generally installed at a boundary between a road and a sidewalk or in a terrain where water is likely to collect or in a certain area of a building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101956785-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sludge collecting unit for collecting the sludge settled on the bottom surface into a collecting hopper formed at one end of the bottom while being rotated by an endless track system and a secondary settler for discharging the collected water separated from the activated sludge through an outflow wear trough the induction water channel provided at the upper portion of the secondary clarifier so that the inflow water and the mlss flowing into the secondary clarifier are introduced in the same direction as the flow direction of the sludge of the sludge collector rectification means for supplying the lower portion of the induction water channel with the inflow water supplied from the induction waterway while lowering the drop energy of the mlss to the lower portion thereof a plurality of diffusion means formed in the lower portion of the rectifying means so as to evenly diffuse the mlss in which the dropping energy from the rectifying means is reduced into the secondary settler and the mlss diffused from the diffusion means passes through the diffusion means in front of the diffusion means the kinetic energy of the flow velocity of the mlss is reduced again by collision and the collision between the mlss and the mlss is induced again in the entire cross overlapping means overlapping at least two or more folds so as to have coherency the induction water channel is formed so as to be merged from both sides of the upper part where the collecting hoppers of the secondary settling basin are formed the rectifying means includes an inflow plate having a plurality of inflow holes through which the mlss flows together with inflow water on the upper surface thereof a solid plate and a superposed plate arranged in a lattice form to reduce the drop energy of the mlss in the lower portion of the inflow hole and a slope formed on the lower end of the flow path so that the mlss is not precipitated and guided to the diffusion means wherein the inflow holes are formed with different diameters the intermediate portion is formed with a larger diameter along the transport direction in which the mlss is introduced and the inflow hole is formed with a gradually smaller diameter toward both sides the superimposing means may include at least one superposed plate formed by vertically and horizontally piercing the mlss at a predetermined interval to form a plurality of through holes through which the mlss passes wherein the passage holes of the second settling basin are disposed at different positions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101950860-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a base movable in a width direction of the water channel in which the screen is installed a boom unit having a rack boom pivotally supported on the base so as to be rotatable in the water flow direction of the water channel and having a rake at a lower end thereof for catching the contaminants caught on the screen a boom drive means provided on the boom means for engaging with the rack boom frame so as to rotate forward and backward and having a first rake face for raising and lowering the rack boom frame a rotation angle adjusting means having an arc shaped turning guide rack bar provided on the boom means and a second raker provided on the base so as to rotate forward and backward in engagement with the rotation guide rack bar and and running means for reciprocating the base in the width direction of the waterway the boom means a first stage boom comprising a linear portion having a through hole penetrating through the first racetrack and pivotally supported on the base and an arc portion extending rearward from an upper end of the linear portion a two stage boom bar movably inserted into the linear portion of the first stage boom stand and having a guide slot longitudinally extending through the first pinion a rack bar which is movably inserted into the second stage boom band and engages with the first rack size bar and a rack chain which is connected to an upper end of the rack bar and is movably inserted into the arc shaped portion of the first a stopper provided at an inner lower end of the first stage boom frame and a first and a second slider that are respectively provided at outer and upper ends of the second stage boom frame and are engaged with the stopper when extending or retracting to limit the stroke of the second and further comprising a sag preventing guide slidably contacting the rack bar on an inner surface of a lower end of the second stage boom frame wherein the rack chain is formed with an inclined surface in which both ends of the link plate are parallel to each other and is provided with a restricting projection for restricting the rotation angle of the link plate in contact with the inclined surface of the link plate adjacent to the projection of each of the inclined surfaces further comprising a plurality of rollers in rolling contact with the inner surface of the first stage boom bar at predetermined intervals in the rack chain the base being configured in the form of a plate like bogie and being spaced apart on both sides of the moving direction so as to face two supports the traveling means includes a guide rail mounted on a supporting structure a plurality of traveling rollers mounted on a lower portion of the base and in rolling contact with the guide rail a chain installed in a traveling direction of the base and a sprocket wheel and a traveling motor fixed to the base with a sprocket wheel on a rotary shaft the rack bar assumes a ladder shape in which a plurality of round bars are continuously arranged at equal intervals between two steel bars wherein the sag preventing guide is fitted between two steel bars of the rack bar and slidably contacts the round bars and both ends of the sag preventing guide are inclined so that the round bar can be passed without being caught while being moved wherein the rack chain is formed as an inclined surface in which both ends of a link plate which are connected to each other with a gap therebetween are arranged to be in contact with an inclined surface of a link plate of another adjacent chain module connected to a corner of a protruding portion of the inclined surface via a connecting link is limited to 90 degrees or less the rack chain further includes rolling rollers at regular intervals to allow the rolling rollers to make rolling contact with the inner surface of the first stage boom band the boom drive means includes a reduction gear box rotatably pivoted between the two supports of the base a first rake mounted gear provided at a gear transmission end of the reduction gearbox and meshing with the rack boom of the boom unit and an elevating motor mounted on one side of the reduction gear box for forward and reverse rotation of the first ladle gear the pivoting guide rack bar has a plurality of round rods arranged at intervals of a predetermined angle between two arcs of an arc shape and an idle roller for supporting the pivoting guide rack bar is provided on the opposite side to which the second rack wherein the vibration damper is a vibration damper"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172182-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention provides a water supply step of continuously supplying the flowing water through the water inlet a power supply step of supplying power by sensing the water supply according to the continuous supply of the flowing water through the water inlet and the water inlet an ionized water generation step of automatically generating gold and silver nano ionized water by an electro ionization reaction by applying a variable alternating dc voltage supplied to gold or silver plates installed on both sides of the channel while continuously supplying flowing water flowing through the channel a water discharge step of discharging the gold and silver nano ionized water continuously generated in the water channel through a water outlet and a power cut off to detect power supply interruption by a flow switch according to a blockage of flow of water through the water inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the sediment removal device of the sewage treatment facility of the present invention for achieving the above object the frame is installed on the upper portion of the water channel the drive unit is installed on the frame to rotate when the power is supplied and the rotational force of the drive unit is transferred to transfer the lifting part is capable of lifting various foreign matters such as sand or soil from the sedimentation tank of the waterway and the conveyor part for transporting the sediment lifted by the lifting part so as to be discharged to the outside but falling onto the conveyor part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for purifying contaminated river water by providing a support structure on both sides of a river to form a water channel therebetween and installing a water gate between