e lower side on the front side of each of the ecological blocks installed in the two rows and constructing backfill and planting in that order between the rear walls of the pair of ecological blocks installed in the two rows constructing in that order and the ecological block comprises a front wall an intermediate wall provided on the rear side of the front wall and a front bottom connecting the lower side of the front wall and the intermediate wall the waterway section having an open upper surface and both side surfaces and having a water flow space on the inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the storage section having an open upper surface and a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls a grating installed on the open upper surface of the water channel section and an overflow portion formed on the intermediate wall wherein the overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the intermediate wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of the rainwater within the flow space and when rainwater continues to flow into the storage portion it can overflow the upper side of the pair of side walls and infiltrate into the infiltration space and the lower part of the infiltration space and infiltrate and be stored within the pores of the gravel layer below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "another embodiment of a method for 