ot occur and the binding groove is formed at the end of the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the waste water collecting device for drainage to remove a resistance shaft 39 provided on the bottom surface of the water channel 10 a voltage variable element 37 provided at the end of the resistance shaft 39 to output a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 it is provided on the outside of the resistance shaft 39 is raised and lowered according to the water level level is provided with a water level sensor 36 made of a float 38 for changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 the control unit 31 is a waste collection device for drainage characterized in that to adjust the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in proportion to the water level level of the channel 10 detected by the water level sensor 36"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the present invention is a control method of a waste water collecting device for the drainage to repeatedly remove the contaminants introduced into the waterway by the rake installed in the chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller a current level determination process of reading the water level of the water flowing in the waterway a water level determination process of determining whether the current water level read through the current water level determination process is a set low water level a medium water level a high water level and the water level determination process if the current level of the water channel is judged to be low drive the lifting motor at low speed.if the current level is judged to be medium drive the lifting motor to medium speed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "by automatically controlling the operating speed of the lifting motor if the inflow of water increases such as during rainy weather the speed of collecting the contaminants can be smoothed thereby smoothing the flow of water into the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442471-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 installed on the waterway so as to be movable in the transverse direction a beam stand 11 mounted to the main body 10 to be elevated a rake 12 installed at the tip of the beam stand 11 to scrape up dirt in a waterway as the beam stand 11 moves up and down an elevating driver 15 for elevating the beam stage 11 a water level sensor 14 for detecting the water level in the water channel a controller 40 for controlling the lift position of the beam stage 11 by controlling the lift driver 15 according to the level detected by the water level sensor 14 a parallel moving drive unit 130 for moving the main body in the lateral direction and it includes a timer for measuring the lifting time of the beam stage 11 and the moving time of the main body 10 the controller 40 controls the beam stage 11 to be elevated to a predetermined depth below the water surface in the water channel according to the result measured by the timer and controls the horizontal movement amount of the main body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101976008-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "3 and 9 and water dehydrated and separated in the dirt is discharged again into the water flowing along the waterway 10 a casing 510 having a water discharge port 513 extending downward toward the water channel 10 and a contaminant discharge port 515 for discharging dehydrated contaminants to the outside a dewatering drive unit 530 provided in the casing 510 and providing a rotational driving force to the screw impeller 520 and a dewatering drive unit 530 provided in the casing 510 to supply the rotational force to the screw impeller 520"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330013-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "conventionally when water leakage occurs due to poor construction of the water stop plate 6 of the expansion joint device 1 the rubber like elastic body has been repaired by using an adhesive 5 on the concrete surface of the water leakage producing site with a waterproof cloth 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102058210-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "therefore the water staying in the puddle 150 is configured to be guided to the storage tank 200 to be described later while being pitched downward"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6120732-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the example of this invention which stuck the seal sticker on the seam of the u shaped ditch channel.specific cross sectional structure of a seal.sectional drawing which stuck the sealing material on the joint part of the u shaped ditch water channel via the primer and the sealing material.sectional drawing which affixed the sealing material on the seam part of a u shaped ditch waterway.work process to attach a sealing material to the seam.work process to attach a sealing material to the seam.work process to attach a sealing material to the seam.work process to attach a sealing material to the seam.the external view of the general u shaped concrete block which comprises a u shaped ditch waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102321943-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the present invention relates to a process of excavating to a predetermined depth to form a water channel along the slope of the cut off site a process of constructing a wire mesh block by combining a wire mesh structure to be disposed at the bottom of the excavated water channel and a sustenance structure and a wire mesh block as a waterway the process of arranging the sub wire mesh to the side wall of the wire mesh block and the process of combining the lower part of the sub wire mesh with the bottom wire mesh protruding from the side wall of the wire mesh block the process of arranging the sub wire mesh joined to the lower part of the wire mesh block to be inclined in contact with the side wall of the waterway the process of fixing the side wire mesh and the auxiliary wire mesh using a latch and adjusting the gap between the auxiliary wire mesh and the side wire mesh the process of continuously connecting the wire mesh block and the auxiliary wire mesh configured as above and connecting the wire mesh block and the auxiliary wire mesh the process of inserting anchors into the bottom wire mesh of the wire mesh block the process of fixing the wire mesh block to the ground the process of embedding reinforcing soil between the side wire mesh of the wire mesh block and the auxiliary wire mesh the process of fixing the side wire mesh and auxiliary wire mesh of the block at regular intervals the process of spraying a mixture of grass seeds and adhesive on the treatment pad structure the process of spraying water on the treatment pad structure and the spraying of massato on the bottom of the wire mesh block thus it relates to a construction method of a waterway that reinforces and greens the slope of the incision site which is composed of a process to prevent the grass seeds from drying out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102321943-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the waterway 101 is reinforced while continuously disposing the waterway block 100 configured as described above and the waterway block 100 configured as described above is continuously connected to form an installation structure for waterway reinforcement and the waterway 101 the connection of the wire mesh block 11 and the auxiliary wire mesh 14 of the water channel block 100 disposed in the waterway block 100 is configured so that it can be connected by using the interlocking pack 17"}]</data>
</edge>
