  <data key="d5">["pollutant", "nature", "winch", "sedimentation", "dam", "layer", "turning", "position", "module", "part", "tank", "walkway", "river", "signal", "soil", "vegetation", "solid", "level", "order", "sprocket", "groundwater", "mechanism", "screen", "contact", "sieve", "flow", "rate", "pipe", "outlet", "communication", "pump", "tent", "space", "distribution", "lagoon", "outflow", "electricity", "time", "driving", "water", "lowering", "press", "sludge", "oxidation", "purification", "member", "portion", "eco", "purifier", "channel", "filter", "conveyance", "filtration", "microorganism", "operation", "intake", "storage", "rainwater", "substance", "controller", "system", "chain", "step", "phase", "treatment", "vicinity", "closing", "matter", "storm", "friendliness", "waterway", "end", "inflow", "shaft", "contaminant", "frame", "reservoir", "rake", "pedestrian", "discharge", "contamination", "wetland", "conduit", "drainage", "net", "drive", "opening", "lake", "stream", "temperature", "change", "infrastructure", "guide", "medium", "passage", "precipitation", "device", "block", "mean", "type", "plant", "accordance", "motor", "sensor", "roller", "circulation", "influent", "irrigation", "gate", "air", "quality", "material", "inlet", "control", "upstream", "drain", "station", "parallel", "unit", "energy", "backwashing"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["drive", "receive", "obstruct", "include", "dispose", "combine", "purify", "backwashe", "support", "disturb", "provide", "prevent", "block", "open", "turn", "withdraw", "rise", "plant", "undergo", "descend", "supply", "arrange", "use", "connect", "form", "measure", "float", "integrate", "introduce", "base", "catch", "clean", "distribute", "ascend", "convey", "close", "produce", "adsorb", "suspend", "filter", "pass", "have", "show", "remove", "maintain", "control", "transmit", "wind", "characterize", "fix", "configure", "lower", "communicate", "flow", "fluidize", "precipitate", "discharge", "be", "store", "infiltrate", "decompose", "adjust", "pump", "settle", "output", "instal", "comprise", "lift"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100834924-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "via conduit to a drain not shown to receive filtered water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_703", "text": "the stream river reservoir lake lagoon or contaminated river water flowing in the vicinity of a dam characterized in that the purified water is naturally purified by floating the river water to the upper part of the eco friendly water purification device 200 used as the water purifier a nature friendly friendliness that naturally purifies polluted water while producing electricity by using an eco friendly water purification device that combines pollutants and soil water and purifies and cleans the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "an inflow water distribution step of evenly distributing the energy of the stream water the lake water or the outflow water flowing into the integrated water purification device through the flow distribution tank to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step in which the inflow water which has passed the precipitation step is biologically purified while being introduced and passed through the contact oxidation tank in which the microbial contact material is installed a fourth purification step of finally removing fine sludge and suspended solids not filtered in the contact oxidation tank through the filtering tank a flow rate adjusting step of adjusting a flow rate discharged into the water channel through the discharge pipe through the discharge control tank it is configured to include"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}]</data>
</edge>
