  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide water pipe body fitted into the above drain and having an open upper portion to receive the above rainwater a grating member that is fitted and fixed to the upper part of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain permeation guide holes formed on the side wall of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain a shielding control panel positioned inside the guide water channel body to open or close the above pitching guide holes a lifting and transporting guide means provided in the above guide waterway body and for lifting and transporting the shielding control panel and in a road drainage device for preventing water retention on a road surface the device is composed of a filter net member that is fitted and fixed into the water permeation guide hole formed in the guide water channel body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned conventional problems and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a road drainage device that prevents water from pooling on the road surface by providing a lifting and transporting guide means to open or close the permeable guide holes and the permeable guide holes of a guide water channel pipe main body connected to a road drainage ditch by an opening and closing control panel thereby allowing rainwater flowing into the guide water channel pipe main body during heavy rain to be discharged into the ground through the permeable guide holes thereby preventing rainwater from stagnating and preventing rainwater from flowing back and accumulating on the road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention relates to a road drainage device which is installed in a drainage channel formed by excavating the ground and receives and guides road rainwater and is characterized by comprising a guide water channel pipe body fitted into the drainage channel and having an open upper portion to receive the rainwater a grating member fitted and fixed to the upper portion of the guide water channel pipe body connected to the drainage channel water permeation guide holes formed on a side wall portion of the guide water channel pipe body connected to the drainage channel a shielding control panel arranged inside the guide water channel pipe body to open or close the water permeation guide holes an elevating and lowering guide means provided in the guide water channel pipe body to elevate and lower the shielding control panel and a strainer member fitted and fixed to the water permeation guide holes formed in the guide water channel pipe body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention relates to a road drainage device for preventing water retention on a road surface wherein a guide water channel pipe main body connected to a road drainage ditch is provided with a lifting and transporting guide means for opening or closing the guide water channels with an opening and closing control panel so that rainwater flowing into the guide water channel pipe main body during heavy rain is discharged into the ground through the guide water channels thereby preventing rainwater from stagnating and preventing rainwater from flowing backward and accumulating on the road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "downstream of the water channel 400 is provided with a discharge portion 600 for discharging the initial excellent and rainwater from the reservoir 1 the discharge portion 600 may be configured to control the discharge amount or to block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904287-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "that is when the initial excellent water is collected by the installation of the wear member 115 the existing water channel that is the water drainage section back water due to the reduction of the cross section of the sewage pipe 1 causes an obstacle to the rainwater outflow due to the back water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403858-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to fill the permeable filling block including the fiber resin and natural gravel into the frame so that external soil or foreign matter does not enter the interior while the rainwater or sewage is permeable permeable filling it is to provide a water channel cover so that it can be drained quickly through the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403858-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "water channel cover 1 according to an embodiment of the present invention as shown in figure 1 or 2 the water permeable filling block 40 is composed of a hwabar resin and natural gravel in the inner space of the water channel cover 1 it is possible to prevent garbage or foreign substances from entering the sewage by filling them and to make the beauty of beauty by using the permeable filling block 40 of various colors and to display the jurisdiction so that it can be used as a function of the display panel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "according to one form of the invention it is provided that the incorrect discharges are transferred into the latter due to a flow gradient between the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "this means that after the drainage or waste water has been drained off the clean rainwater flowing through the rainwater channel in the event of a rain event is completely conducted to the receiving water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the auxiliary valve is installed on the outer periphery of the main valve and consists of a water shielding plate and a projecting floating body that floats it and the outer periphery of the projecting floating body is used to prevent malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to the wave of rain water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783926-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a synthetic resin formwork pipe for protecting a concrete water channel which is installed in close contact with the inner surface of a concrete water channel to substantially form a flow path for rainwater to flow through thereby preventing damage such as corrosion of the concrete"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783926-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the circular water channel pipe disclosed in registered patent 10 2058301 is made of concrete is in the shape of a square block with a predetermined length has a circular water channel formed along the longitudinal direction inside and has a rainwater inlet formed along the longitudinal direction in the middle of the upper surface width direction a sealing pipe made of a circular pipe made of a soft synthetic resin material is fixedly installed in close contact with the inner surface of the water channel and has a through hole formed along the longitudinal direction in the upper portion corresponding to the rainwater inlet and a plurality of support rods which penetrate the upper portion of the sealing pipe so as to be positioned below the through hole are installed so that both ends are embedded in the water channel pipe body and are installed in plurality at predetermined intervals along the longitudinal direction of the through hole to support and bear the lower end of the grating inserted into the rainwater inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101978908-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the water channel body 100 is formed in a block shape in which a water channel 120 penetrates along a longitudinal direction and has a water catching hole 110 communicating with the water channel so that rainwater flowing from a road or a road surface is guided by a water channel are formed along the longitudinal direction"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2613145-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "as a result the inside is formed as a water channel 1"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2613145-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "a rainwater outlet 90 is formed on the inner wall of the rectangular block 9 so as to form a stepped shape from the back of the rectangular block 9 to the lower side of the rectangular block 9 and to face the upper part of the filtering particle layer 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826482-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to accomplish the above objects there is provided a vertical channel rain water filtration apparatus comprising a vertical water channel type rainwater filtration apparatus having a collecting pipe through which rainwater flows upwardly and a drain pipe for discharging contaminants downward a vertical pipe case having an expansion part having a diameter relatively larger than that of the water collecting pipe and the drain pipe a funnel shaped funnel pipe communicating with the water collecting pipe and disposed on the upper side of the expanding unit so that the rainwater flowing downward is in surface contact with the swirl like shape due to the acceleration due to the gravity and the turning force and a mesh screen provided on the upper side of the expansion unit for separating the rainwater falling from the funnel pipe and the rainwater and the rainwater through the collision caused by the dropping of the rainwater and a rainwater collecting part having a rainwater collecting compartment for collecting separated rainwater and having a rainwater outlet formed at one side of the rainwater collecting compartment and a contaminant discharge path through which the contaminants separated to the outside of the inclined surface of the mesh screen are discharged thereby discharging the contaminants to the contaminant discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2549584-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in addition to the above a three sided gutter or the like may be used or rainwater may be introduced from a sump block block arranged in the middle of the gutter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel section including a front wall an intermediate wall provided at the rear of the front wall and a front floor connecting the lower portions of the front wall and the intermediate wall the upper surface and both side surfaces being open and having a water flow space inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the upper surface of which is open and has a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls grating installed on the open upper surface of the above water channel and including a flow through portion formed on the above intermediate wall the above overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the middle wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of rainwater within the flow space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the above ecological block is a water channel section including a front wall an intermediate wall provided at the rear of the front wall and a front floor connecting the lower portions of the front wall and the intermediate wall the upper surface and both side surfaces being open and having a water flow space inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the upper surface of which is open and has a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls grating installed on the open upper surface of the above water channel and including a flow through portion formed on the above intermediate wall the above overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the middle wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of rainwater within the flow space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the above ecological block is a water channel section including a front wall an intermediate wall provided at the rear of the front wall and a front floor connecting the lower portions of the front wall and the intermediate wall the upper surface and both side surfaces being open and having a water flow space inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the upper surface of which is open and has a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls grating installed on the open upper surface of the above water channel and including a flow through portion formed on the above intermediate wall the above overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the middle wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of rainwater within the flow space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "the above ecological block is a water channel section including a front wall an intermediate wall provided at the rear of the front wall and a front floor connecting the lower portions of the front wall and the intermediate wall the upper surface and both side surfaces being open and having a water flow space inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the upper surface of which is open and has a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls grating installed on the open upper surface of the above water channel and including a flow through portion formed on the above intermediate wall the above overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the middle wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is filled rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of rainwater within the flow space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the purpose of the present invention is to provide a multifunctional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function and a construction method thereof which includes a water channel a retention section provided at the rear of the water channel section and an inspection port provided on the side of the water channel section thereby reducing the discharge of pollutants flowing out with rainwater to prevent water pollution delaying rainwater from concentrating on rainwater pipes to prevent flood damage and improving groundwater depletion by securing a space through which rainwater can continuously infiltrate the lower soil layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "is collected in the water channel and the inspection hole on the side of the water channel and rainwater with relatively less pollution after the water channel and the inspection hole are filled flows into the storage area through the overflow area formed higher than the grating on the upper side of the water channel thereby minimizing disturbance of the early rainwater thereby providing a multifunctional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function and a construction method thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition by providing an inspection hole on the side of the water channel and making the outlet of the inspection hole higher than the bottom of the inspection hole rainwater flowing into the inspection hole gradually infiltrates underground through the outlet or evaporates into the air through a cover with a hole formed therein and pollutants flowing in together with the rainwater are deposited on the bottom of the inspection hole and the deposited pollutants can be easily recovered and processed by opening the cover thereby providing a multifunctional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function and a construction method thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a multifunctional ecological block having a water collection and infiltration function according to an example of the present invention comprises a water channel section including a front wall an intermediate wall provided on the rear side of the front wall and a front bottom connecting the lower portions of the front wall and the intermediate wall the upper surface and both side surfaces of which are open and the water flow space is provided inside a storage section including the intermediate wall a rear wall provided on the rear side of the intermediate wall a pair of side walls connecting the intermediate wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from the ends of both sides of the intermediate wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the intermediate wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the upper surface of which is open and the water flow space is provided inside and the water flow space is provided outside the pair of side walls a grating installed on the open upper surface of the water channel section and it includes an overflow portion formed on the intermediate wall and the overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the intermediate wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of the rainwater within the flow space and when rainwater continuously flows into the storage portion it may be characterized in that it overflows the upper side of the pair of side walls and infiltrates into the infiltration space and the lower part of the infiltration space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a method for constructing a multifunctional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function according to an example of the present invention comprises the steps of setting a cutting line and excavating the inside of the cutting line forming a gravel layer on the lower side of the excavated inside installing an ecological block on the upper side of the gravel layer and constructing a subbase layer an asphalt concrete layer and an asphalt concrete surface layer in that order from the lower side on the front side of the ecological block and constructing backfill and planting on the rear side of the ecological block in that order and constructing in that order wherein the ecological block comprises a front wall an intermediate wall provided on the rear side of the front wall and a front floor connecting the lower side of the front wall and the intermediate wall and a water channel section having an open upper surface and both side surfaces and a water flow space provided inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the storage section having an open upper surface and a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls a grating installed on the open upper surface of the water channel section and an overflow portion formed on the intermediate wall wherein the overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the intermediate wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of the rainwater within the flow space and when rainwater continues to flow into the storage portion it can overflow the upper side of the pair of side walls and infiltrate into the infiltration space and the lower part of the infiltration space and infiltrate and be stored within the pores of the gravel layer below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "another embodiment of a method for constructing a multi functional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function according to an example of the present invention comprises the steps of setting a cutting line and excavating the inside of the cutting line forming a gravel layer on the lower side of the excavated inside installing a pair of ecological blocks in two rows on the upper side of the gravel layer so that their rear walls face each other and constructing a subbase layer an asphalt base layer and an asphalt surface layer in that order from the lower side on the front side of each of the ecological blocks installed in the two rows and constructing backfill and planting in that order between the rear walls of the pair of ecological blocks installed in the two rows constructing in that order and the ecological block comprises a front wall an intermediate wall provided on the rear side of the front wall and a front bottom connecting the lower side of the front wall and the intermediate wall the waterway section having an open upper surface and both side surfaces and having a water flow space on the inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the storage section having an open upper surface and a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls a grating installed on the open upper surface of the water channel section and an overflow portion formed on the intermediate wall wherein the overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the intermediate wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of the rainwater within the flow space and when rainwater continues to flow into the storage portion it can overflow the upper side of the pair of side walls and infiltrate into the infiltration space and the lower part of the infiltration space and infiltrate and be stored within the pores of the gravel layer below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "another embodiment of a method for constructing a multi functional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function according to an example of the present invention comprises the steps of setting a cutting line and excavating the inside of the cutting line forming a gravel layer on the lower side of the excavated inside installing a pair of ecological blocks in two rows on the upper side of the gravel layer so that their rear walls face each other and constructing a subbase layer an asphalt base layer an asphalt surface layer or a sidewalk block layer in that order from the lower side on the front side of each of the ecological blocks installed in the two rows and constructing backfill and flower bed formation in that order between the rear walls of the pair of ecological blocks installed in the two rows constructing in that order and the ecological block comprises a front wall an intermediate wall provided on the rear side of the front wall and a front floor connecting the lower side of the front wall and the intermediate wall the waterway section having an open upper surface and both side surfaces and having a water flow space on the inside a storage section including the middle wall a rear wall provided at the rear of the middle wall a pair of side walls connecting the middle wall and the rear wall at positions spaced inwardly from both ends of the middle wall and the rear wall and a rear bottom connecting the lower portions of the middle wall the rear wall and the pair of side walls the storage section having an open upper surface and a storage space provided inside and a penetration space provided on the outer side of the pair of side walls a grating installed on the open upper surface of the water channel section and an overflow portion formed on the intermediate wall wherein the overflow portion is formed lower than the upper surface of the intermediate wall and higher than the grating so that rainwater first flows into the flow space of the water channel portion and after the flow space is full rainwater flows into the storage portion through the upper side of the grating and the overflow portion thereby minimizing disturbance of the rainwater within the flow space and when rainwater continues to flow into the storage portion it can overflow the upper side of the pair of side walls and infiltrate into the infiltration space and the lower part of the infiltration space and infiltrate and be stored within the pores of the gravel layer below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101748654-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore a screen is installed in the water channel so as to block the inflow of such impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101975862-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the water channel body 100 is formed in the shape of a block having a water channel passing through the inside thereof along the longitudinal direction and a catching hole 110 communicating with the water channel is formed in the upper part so that rainwater flowing from a road or a road surface is guided by a water channel as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101509202-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "however since the present invention is installed solely with the water channel type collecting cores 2 there is no need to waste a lot of manpower and cost in maintenance because there is no connection part there is no problem of damage or breakage of the connecting portion and it is possible to fundamentally eliminate the soil pollution problem caused by leaking of rainwater and sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "this embodiment is for observing the contaminant removal effect of a water circulation system including a water channel using a titanium dioxide photocatalyst"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102075013-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the channel flow rate reduction apparatus for preventing river overflow according to an embodiment of the present invention has a shape corresponding to the channel and is fixed in position to be in close contact with the inner wall and the bottom surface of the channel a channel installation main body providing a first flow path flowing through the upper rainwater and sliding assembly in the direction intercepting the first flow path from the upper portion of the water channel installation body having a narrow flow cross sectional area than the first flow path at least one block assembly providing a second flow path to reduce storm flow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102075013-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "as a result the blocking plate 150 may block the flow of rainwater through the first flow path 120 see fig"}]</data>
</edge>
