 perforator 877 pilot and extractor 878 sand collector 879 dredger 879a pump dredger 879b bucket dredger 879c spotted shear 879d cab or control room 879e red shear 879f spotted 879g blast tank 879h blast pump 879i red 879j engine room 879k dipper dredger 879l grab dredger 879m bucket drive 879n after spotted 879o spotted winch 879p bucket 879q left and right front spotted 879r dipper 879s winch 879t anchor store 879u belt conveyor 879v grab 880 separately designated construction machinery 882 pile driver 882a boom 883 diesel pile hammer 884 steam hammer 885 hydraulic crane 885a piston motor 886 tower crane 886a names of each part of the guy derrick structure 886b guy derrick 886c main 886d boom 886e boom foil 886f turnbuckle 886g sling 886h triangular derrick 886i main 886j boom 886k boom foil 886l rack 887 drag crane 887a structure of drag crane 887b hoist cable 887c dump cable 887d bucket 887e lower boom 887f retroflex cable 887g cable roller 887h boom cable 887i cable roller 887j boom hoist cable 887k cable drum 887l cable drum 887m parallel weight 888 crane with clamshell attachment 888a holding line 888b opening line 888c clamshell bucket 888d upper frame 888e lower frame 888f rack line 888g rope guide 888h boom tendon 888i bridle 888j boom hoist rope 888k front drum 888l rear drum 888m parallel weights 889 macadam roller 890 tandem roller 891 tamping roller 892 tire roller 893 tractor 894 trailer 895 ram 896 lead 897 coolant cooling 898 pile 899 helmet 900 fuel pump 901 cam 902 fuel tank 903 starting device 904 boom front pin 905 cad work 906 adapter 907 fish finder sonar 908 drilling machine for crude oil 909 manganese nodule 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "according to one form of the invention it is provided that the incorrect discharges are transferred into the latter due to a flow gradient between the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "this takes advantage of the fact that in a separation system the dirty water channel is always lower than the rain water channel and thus the dirty or waste water in the rain water channel can get into the dirty water channel due to the natural flow gradient"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "this corresponds to that previously discussed with the difference that instead of the controller and the connecting line arranged downstream of it a pump conveys the tap water via a line into the dirty water channel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "because of the rain water still flowing in small quantities through the rain water channel 2 the dirty water channel 4 experiences a second flush with rain water through the connecting line 5"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the auxiliary valve is installed on the outer periphery of the main valve and consists of a water shielding plate and a projecting floating body that floats it and the outer periphery of the projecting floating body is used to prevent malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to the wave of rain water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826482-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to accomplish the above objects there is provided a vertical channel rain water filtration apparatus comprising a vertical water channel type rainwater filtration apparatus having a collecting pipe through which rainwater flows upwardly and a drain pipe for discharging contaminants downward a vertical pipe case having an expansion part having a diameter relatively larger than that of the water collecting pipe and the drain pipe a funnel shaped funnel pipe communicating with the water collecting pipe and disposed on the upper side of the expanding unit so that the rainwater flowing downward is in surface contact with the swirl like shape due to the acceleration due to the gravity and the turning force and a mesh screen provided on the upper side of the expansion unit for separating the rainwater falling from the funnel pipe and the rainwater and the rainwater through the collision caused by the dropping of the rainwater and a rainwater collecting part having a rainwater collecting compartment for collecting separated rainwater and having a rainwater outlet formed at one side of the rainwater collecting compartment and a contaminant discharge path through which the contaminants separated to the outside of the inclined surface of the mesh screen are discharged thereby discharging the contaminants to the contaminant discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the upper one side of the circular or rectangular tube has a shape that is open in the longitudinal direction to provide a space for preventing the crossing over the boundary block the drain is formed on the lower side and both ends are connected to other water pipes a concave convex portion is formed in the open end surface wherein a binding groove is formed in a longitudinal direction and the open upper side is installed so that the other side is directed toward the roadway side and an upper portion of the waterway tube installed at the same height as the ground surface of the sidewalk it is a plate having a shape of a memory device with a round cross section so as to cover the open portion in the longitudinal direction of the water pipe a binding piece is inserted into the binding groove at both ends in the longitudinal direction but the binding piece is bent in two stages in the longitudinal direction so that a step with the outer surface of the water channel does not occur and the binding groove is formed at the end of the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}]</data>
</edge>
