  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102207360-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a first motor and a suction hopper mounted in front of the body to suck the sediment a discharge pipe connected in communication with the suction hopper to send the sucked sediment to the outside and installed inside the suction hopper to crush the sediment an underwater cleaning robot comprising a crushing screw and a second motor for driving the crushing screw and a hydraulic pressure generating device mounted on the body and configured to drive the first and second motors using hydraulic pressure and control remotely the technology is also presented"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4253351-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a cylindrical chlorine removal filter to be removed an outflow pipe connected to the casing from which tap water flows out a head cap mounted on an end of the casing and one end fixed to the head cap and the other end a cylinder inserted into one end side of the hollow portion of the chlorine removal filter a cylinder water passing portion opened in a side surface of the cylinder and a manual or electric drive disposed inside or outside the cylinder a valve body that rotates or moves up and down and the valve body changes a degree of opening and closing of the bypass passage that communicates the cylindrical water passage portion and the hollow portion and the inflow side is closed when the bypass passage is closed"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "9 water flow through the channel 131 is blocked and the water in bore 126 can only move through water drive line 10"}]</data>
</edge>
