  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a structure in which a rainwater discharge blocking wall 990 is configured to fail to flow into the interior of the rainwater collection channel 999 combined with the stairs through the rainwater inlet 998 the upper position of the combined rainwater collecting channel 999 is a structure configured to be equal to the upper surface portion 980 of the land a structure in which a floor covering material 880 composed of rocks is installed at a lower end of the waterway wall 100 so that water swimmers or swimmers can play or swim in water with confidence at the lower end of the combined rainwater collection channel 999 a rainwater or contaminants contaminated with rivers or rivers or reservoirs or dams while constructing a stepped artificial reef 890 where organisms amphibians or fish can be easily inhabited"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101473166-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "when the contaminant flows into the conveyance pipe 51 through the discharge hole 12 and the inflow portion 514 the conveyance drive unit is operated to perform the operation of the impurity removing unit 5 having the above the conveyance shaft 53 rotates in one direction and the conveyance plate 52 surrounding the conveyance shaft 53 moves in the right direction of the waterway 1 as the conveyance shaft 53 rotates the contaminants introduced into the pipe 51 are pushed toward the lower discharge portion 512 and the compressed and separated water is discharged to the drain 513a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102601272-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "it forms a side screening wall 101 and a drain 102a that discharges the filtered water filtered through the screen structure 200 and on the inner surface a gasket covers both ends of the screen structure 200 to prevent the inflow of impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "on the other hand when the internal water level l measured by the internal water leve