  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide water pipe body fitted into the above drain and having an open upper portion to receive the above rainwater a grating member that is fitted and fixed to the upper part of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain permeation guide holes formed on the side wall of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain a shielding control panel positioned inside the guide water channel body to open or close the above pitching guide holes a lifting and transporting guide means provided in the above guide waterway body and for lifting and transporting the shielding control panel and in a road drainage device for preventing water retention on a road surface the device is composed of a filter net member that is fitted and fixed into the water permeation guide hole formed in the guide water channel body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the scum removal device is installed in the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to discharge only scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing device it has a hopper shaped body which is located inside the waterway and introduces a scum to the outside of the waterway through the discharge pipe formed at the bottom thereof and a support bar for supporting the scum detection sensor and the water level detection sensor on the upper part of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763876-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in the scum removing apparatus according to the present invention for achieving this object in the scum removing apparatus is installed in the water channel of the sewage treatment plant or water purification plant to flow only the scum floating in the upper portion of the sewage flowing into the water channel to discharge to the outside of the water channel the scum removing apparatus includes a scum hopper positioned inside the channel and flowing in the scum to flow out of the channel through a discharge pipe formed at a lower portion thereof an elevating unit configured to elevate the scum hopper a support part supported on the upper side of the waterway to support the lifting part a scum detecting sensor installed at a front portion of the scum hopper to sense an amount of floating scum a water level sensor installed at a rear portion of the scum hopper to detect a water level and a controller for adjusting the height of the scum hopper by controlling the lifting unit according to the detection state of the scum detecting sensor and the water level detecting sensor"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6885661-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "transport and by configuring the rear wheels to cut off the driving force received from the engine the user removes the deposits while manually moving the channel deposit remover and or the rear wheels are the engine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101378786-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "therefore the transfer part 15 is provided inside the pair of support frames 13 to move up down from the outside of the waterway to the inside or to allow the worker to stay in the desired position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102328070-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "however due to its constitutional characteristics the above dust suppressor for sewage and wastewater pumping station can only filter the contaminants flowing between the main screen and the bottom of the waterway and smoothly and stably lift the contaminants caught in the rear auxiliary screen through the rake"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102328070-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "a vibration damper for a sewage and wastewater pumping station according to the present invention for solving the above problems includes a pair of support frames spaced apart from each other a chain conveyor installed inside the pair of support frames and having a lower end bent in a horizontal direction a screen having a shape corresponding to the chain conveyor and installed between the pair of support frames a guide plate having a shape corresponding to the screen and installed at the lower rear side of the screen to upwardly guide contaminants introduced into the space between the screen and the waterway bottom it is connected to the chain conveyor and installed and it is linked according to the operation of the chain conveyor to include a plurality of rakes for removing and lifting contaminants of the screen and the guide plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102442307-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 1796648 there is a device for supplying water to farmland by automatically lifting and lowering the water supply control plate that opens and closes the inlet of the fixed plate fixed to the inner surface of the wall of the waterway through the lifting drive"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire hose 9 and a fire nozzle frame 11 and a hook 13 in a detection sensor 12 and a jig 22 in a pipe 14 are configured to control the flow rate to the disaster prevention waterway 17 while forming a vertical multistage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for flood prevention of underground passages the flood control equipment which consists of fire pumps and high performance submersible pumps a hook and a wire rope a machined hole and a shackle a bolt and nut a washer and a hinge a flange or a flange stopper a wire m