 on the frame to rotate when the power is supplied and the rotational force of the drive unit is transferred to transfer the lifting part is capable of lifting various foreign matters such as sand or soil from the sedimentation tank of the waterway and the conveyor part for transporting the sediment lifted by the lifting part so as to be discharged to the outside but falling onto the conveyor part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100826575-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "drive unit 120 and the lifting unit 130 which is to be transported by receiving the rotational force of the drive unit to lift various foreign materials such as sand or soil in the sedimentation tank of the waterway and receiving the sediment lifted from the lifting unit in addition to having a conveyor 140 for transporting the discharge to the discharge it is installed on the upper portion of the waterway to receive the sediment falling to the conveyor unit 140 receives the sediment from the load cell for a predetermined time measure and then receive the signal of the sedimentation unit 150 to be dropped to the conveyor unit and the amount of sedimentation measured in the load cell of the sedimentation unit is installed in the frame the control unit 160 is configured to automatically control the sedimentation lifting speed according to the number of the sedimentation amount by calculating and preventing the substructure of the salvage part from being buried in accordance with the increase in the amount of sedimentation to prevent electric mechanical damage due to overload"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for purifying contaminated river water by providing a support structure on both sides of a river to form a water channel therebetween and installing a water gate between the both side support structures to open and close the water channel and a plurality of support rods supporting the watershed are slidably slidable with respect to the watershed respectively in the middle of the drainage side of the watershed and between the support rods and the bottom of the waterway and a lifting cylinder capable of lifting and lowering the water gate is provided in the support base and a guide hole is formed in the longitudinal direction of the support base on a surface of the support base opposed to the water gate and between the rod and the drain side of the water inlet a fixing rod and the lifting cylinder is lifted upwardly in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder in the closed state of the watercourse so that the weight of the watercount which is stored in the watercounting space is clean the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 further comprising the steps of discharging the lower layer water first to purify contaminated river water thereby inducing a substance separation action caused by the action of gravity while purifying the contaminated river water with clean river water the shape of the hydrograph plate 80 is continuously bent in the shape of w in the transverse direction and bonded to the fixed bar 32 the vertical supports 90 and 91 which are continuously arranged in the form of a triangle vertically laid out on the lower surface and the upper surface of the water gate plate 80 to prevent warpage of the water gate plate 80 from 30 cm to 1 m together with zooming at intervals of and an index member not shown is coupled to the horizontal and vertical directions of the water gate plate 80 the water leveling plate 80 and the vertical supports 90 and 91 are combined to form a hybrid type opening closing member of a double layer structure having a flat plate shape the cylinder head according to any one of claims 1 to 5 wherein the cylinder head 51 of the lifting cylinder 50 is driven in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder 50 the water level plate 80 is lowered in accordance with the operation to shut off the discharge of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a method for purifying contaminated river water by providing a support structure on both sides of a river to form a water channel therebetween and installing a water gate between the both side support structures to open and close the water channel and a plurality of support rods supporting the watershed are slidably slidable with respect to the watershed respectively in the middle of the drainage side of the watershed and between the support rods and the bottom of the waterway and a lifting cylinder capable of lifting and lowering the water gate is provided in the support base and a guide hole is formed in the longitudinal direction of the support base on a surface of the support base opposed to the water gate and between the rod and the drain side of the water inlet a fixing rod and the lifting cylinder is lifted upwardly in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder in the closed state of the watercourse so that the weight of the watercount which is stored in the watercounting space is clean the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 further comprising the steps of discharging the lower layer water first to purify contaminated river water thereby inducing a substance separation action caused by the action of gravity while purifying the contaminated river water with clean river water the shape of the hydrograph plate 800 is continuously bent in the shape of a semicircle in the transverse direction and is coupled to the fixed bar 32 the vertical supports 900 and 901 which are continuously arranged in a semicircular plate are vertically arranged on the lower surface and the upper surface of the hydrograph plate 800 to prevent the hydrograph plate 800 from being bent combined with zooming and an index member not shown is coupled to the horizontal and vertical directions of the hydrograph plate 800 the hydrograph plate 800 and the vertical supports 900 and 901 are combined to form a hybrid type opening closing member of a double layer structure having a flat plate shape the cylinder head according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the cylinder head 51 of the lifting cylinder 40 is driven in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder 40 the water level plate 800 is lowered in accordance with the operation to shut off the discharge of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100265245-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to an elliptical drive steeply inclined stepped strainer that can be lifted and transported as it is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the plate like door 27 is installed to open and close the waterway while being coupled by the door lifting member 27 penetrating through the upper center of the upper portion of the door 27 and spaced apart from the front and rear of the door 27 to face each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "door plate 26 which is a shape is coupled to the plate through the door lifting member 27 passing through the center of the upper end of the door frame 26 the plate like door 27 is installed to open and close the waterway and the front and rear of the door 27 is formed so as to face each other the aeration generating plate 22 is fixed to both sides of the intake door wall 21 the aeration generating plate 22 is a constant a plurality of drains 23 are penetrated at intervals to discharge the river water and generate aeration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100413210-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "induction waterway 10 formed by installing water barrier walls 3 3 that can vertically block from the bottom to the surface of the water intake tower 1 to the water inlet tower 2 in front of the water inlet 1 for the inflow of water supply wow a microbubble diffuser 20 installed in the guide channel 10 so as to move up and down from the bottom to the surface thereof microbubble generating means 30 for supplying high pressure water containing air to the microbubble diffuser 20 lifting means 40 for elevating the micro bubble diffuser 20 comprising the microbubble generating means 30 while lifting the micro bubble diffuser 20 to the lifting means 40 in accordance with the distribution of algae supplying high pressure water containing air to the micro bubble diffuser 20 in the algae removal apparatus of the water inlet characterized in that the micro bubbles adhere to the algae in the water to rise above the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100413210-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention is an induction channel formed by installing a water barrier wall that can be vertically blocked from the bottom to the water surface without disturbing the water level fluctuations on both sides in front of the water gate of the water intake tower for introducing the source water a microbubble diffuser which is installed to move up and down from the bottom to the surface of the induction waterway microbubble generating means for supplying water of high pressure containing air to the microbubble diffuser lifting means for elevating the micro bubble diffuser comprising a high pressure water containing air from the microbubble generating means to the microbubble diffuser while lifting the microbubble diffuser in accordance with the distribution of algae it provides the algae removal device of the intake port so that the microbubbles adhere to the algae in the water to rise above the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200191686-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "endless chain 14 that rotates along rake 15 of the rake retainer installed on the chain to rotate together the drive motor 16 for driving the chain to prevent the lifting of the contaminated lifting into the water and protect the drive shaft in the vibration damper having a configuration such as an apron 17 a water level sensor 18 is installed on the waterway wall or the vibration suppressor so that the rotational speed of the rake 15 can be varied according to the inflow quantity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102617451-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however the conventional technology includes a plurality of arm cover members having outward flanges formed while covering the sewage treatment plant waterway and a plurality of arm cover members formed between the plurality of arm cover members covering the waterway and at the same time having inward flanges placed on top of the outward flanges"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101748654-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "technical field 0001 the present invention relates to a dust removing apparatus for removing impurities from a water channel the present invention relates to a vibration damper for removing contaminants from a waterway and more particularly to a vibration damper device configured to remove contaminants caught on a screen while lifting up and down a raising and lowering arm having a multi stage boom bar"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the waste water collecting device for drainage to remove a resistance shaft 39 provided on the bottom surface of the water channel 10 a voltage variable element 37 provided at the end of the resistance shaft 39 to output a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 it is provided on the outside of the resistance shaft 39 is raised and lowered according to the water level level is provided with a water level sensor 36 made of a float 38 for changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft 39 the control unit 31 is a waste collection device for drainage characterized in that to adjust the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in proportion to the water level level of the channel 10 detected by the water level sensor 36"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention is a drainage sewage collection device for continuously removing the contaminants introduced into the waterway by a rake installed in a chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller the bottom surface of the waterway a resistance variable provided in the resistor shaft a voltage variable element disposed at an end of the resistance shaft and outputting a voltage proportional to the resistance value of the resistance shaft and installed outside the resistance shaft to increase and decrease according to the level of water thereby changing the resistance value of the resistance shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the present invention is a control method of a waste water collecting device for the drainage to repeatedly remove the contaminants introduced into the waterway by the rake installed in the chain that rotates along a certain track when the lifting motor is driven by the control signal of the controller a current level determination process of reading the water level of the water flowing in the waterway a water level determination process of determining whether the current water level read through the current water level determination process is a set low water level a medium water level a high water level and the water level determination process if the current level of the water channel is judged to be low drive the lifting motor at low speed.if the current level is judged to be medium drive the lifting motor to medium speed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "by automatically controlling the operating speed of the lifting motor if the inflow of water increases such as during rainy weather the speed of collecting the contaminants can be smoothed thereby smoothing the flow of water into the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_284", "text": "the second operation cylinder is rotatably fixed to the operation plate to open and close the waterway while rotating the water gate by 270 according to the operation of each operation cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442471-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 installed on the waterway so as to be movable in the transverse direction a beam stand 11 mounted to the main body 10 to be elevated a rake 12 installed at the tip of the beam stand 11 to scrape up dirt in a waterway as the beam stand 11 moves up and down an elevating driver 15 for elevating the beam stage 11 a water level sensor 14 for detecting the water level in the water channel a controller 40 for controlling the lift position of the beam stage 11 by controlling the lift driver 15 according to the level detected by the water level sensor 14 a parallel moving drive unit 130 for moving the main body in the lateral direction and it includes a timer for measuring the lifting time of the beam stage 11 and the moving time of the main body 10 the controller 40 controls the beam stage 11 to be elevated to a predetermined depth below the water surface in the water channel according to the result measured by the timer and controls the horizontal movement amount of the main body 10"}]</data>
