  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268810-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain 10 and a height adjustment ring 20 coupled to the drain 10 and including an eccentric hole 21 whose central side is eccentric to one side compared to the central side of the height adjustment ring 20 a water pipe 30 seated on the drain 10 by being coupled to the height adjustment ring 20 protective frames 40 50 for protecting the waterway tube 30 from external force applied from the upper direction of the waterway tube 30 seated on the drainage passage 10 the drain 10 is it includes a u shaped inner space 10a as a predetermined block shape in the inner space 10a the coupling portion 11 to which the height adjustment ring 20 is coupled is configured to protrude along the inner wall of the curved region and the coupling groove 12 is formed in the coupling portion 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "thus the waterway communication hole 23 is opened and tap water is guided through a waterway composed of the first waterway 21 the waterway communication hole 23 and the second waterway 22 and discharged to the tap water outlet 25"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "although the discharge of the water is blocked when the tap water supplied to the first waterway 21 is introduced at a high pressure due to a specific situation the tap water is discharged through the outlet 274 while pushing up the high pressure stem holder 330 and the water valve body 30 is guided to the low pressure opening closing means installation hole 100 guided to the second waterway 22 through the outlet 120 and discharged to the outside through the tap water outlet 25 to prevent the water valve from being damaged by high pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101127810-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1 the upper part of the inlet well 110 protrudes a certain height from the bottom surface of the waterway 10 and the upper end face of the inlet well 110 forms an inclined surface having a higher sidewall in the direction in which water is introduced to prevent inflow of soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403858-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "water channel cover 1 according to an embodiment of the present invention as shown in figure 1 or 2 the water permeable filling block 40 is composed of a hwabar resin and natural gravel in the inner space of the water channel cover 1 it is possible to prevent garbage or foreign substances from entering the sewage by filling them and to make the beauty of beauty by using the permeable filling block 40 of various colors and to display the jurisdiction so that it can be used as a function of the display panel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403858-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "frame 10 which forms the overall shape of the waterway cover 1 and forms a space portion by a partition plate therein and is inserted into the internal space of the frame 10 described above and includes a fiber resin and natural gravel the waterway cover 1 formed of the castle filling block 40 is generally installed at a boundary between a road and a sidewalk or in a terrain where water is likely to collect or in a certain area of a building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101221659-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the height adjustable channel using the connector and the adjustment bolt of the present invention the opening is formed in the upper a plurality of concrete channel blocks formed in the channel along the longitudinal direction while communicating with the opening a waterway assembled and assembled along the longitudinal direction the bracket mounting groove being formed at one side and the other side of both sidewalls of the waterway block a nut accommodating part which is formed in a shape that conforms to the outer shape of the nut so that the nut is accommodated a nut which is coupled to the nut accommodating part as being coupled to the fastening bolt and the nut accommodating part is completely inserted therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101221659-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "height adjustable channel using the connector and the adjustment bolt of the present invention the opening 11 is formed in the upper portion a plurality of concrete material channel forming the flow path 12 along the length direction while communicating with the opening 11 in the channel consisting of the block 10 is assembled along the longitudinal direction the bracket mounting groove 15 formed on one side and the other lower side of both side walls of the waterway block 10 the nut 33 is coupled to the inside of the nut housing 31 which is coupled to the fastening bolt and the nut housing 31 formed to have a shape corresponding to the outer shape of the nut 33 to accommodate the nut 33"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101221659-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand when the connector 30 is buried in the waterway block 10 is installed to expose the inlet hole 36 in the upper portion of the upper end of the connector 30 exposed by blocking the inlet of the through hole 36 with a stopper foreign matter is inserted through the through hole 36 to prevent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172182-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in order to block the water supply 15 while descending according to the water supply cutoff again the water supply is separated from the operation sensor to cut off the power supply to the gold or silver plate and the water tank 40 in the lower portion of the waterway inside the frame is turned off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "therefore the solid matter such as the earth and sand can flow smoothly to the connecting pipe 21 along the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102559283-B1", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "the method of claim 16 wherein the step s350 sensing the sludge level through a sludge level sensor s351 the limit switch box for sludge drain is connected to various contacts of the solenoid valve for sludge drain and drives and controls the solenoid valve for sludge drain according to the control signal of the smart control unit s352 the solenoid valve for sludge drain is driven according to the signal of the limit switch box for sludge drain to supply or block air transmitted to the actuator for sludge drain s353 the actuator unit for sludge drain is driven by the solenoid valve for sludge drain and the main valve for sludge drain is directly driven to turn on and off the flow of the waterway on the waterway s354 the main valve for sludge drain is driven according to the drive of the actuator unit for sludge drain and the flow of the waterway is turned on and off s355"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200203441-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "as shown here the present invention induces the circulation of water in the canal waterway and supplies dissolved oxygen in the circulation process for the purpose of improving the water quality of the canal waterway to maintain the ecosystem and to prevent the water impact of the discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101162228-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "there was.the present invention was created in view of the above mentioned problems in the prior art and the vegetation protrusions and vegetation holes are formed at both sides including the bottom surface of the waterway block so that the movement and vegetation of the animals are easy and the flow rate it reduces the erosion of the channel by reducing the erosion and the width of the channel can be freely changed because the lower part is a prefabricated type and the key is formed at the bottom of the installation to prevent conduction buckling and crushing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "because of this the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100555055-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the discharged water passing through the fiber filtration filter coated with the photocatalyst is sterilized while passing through the ultraviolet treatment device c provided in the pipeline or waterway type"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200346152-Y1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in order to build a waterway put several block supporters 1 for the channel of the present invention while laying the ground and crushing the soil and connecting the support sections with bolts 4 or other connecting means using a coupling plate 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the plate like door 27 is installed to open and close the waterway while being coupled by the door lifting member 27 penetrating through