  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "this operates to open the stem holder installation hole and the tap water in the first waterway is guided to the second waterway through the stem holder installation hole and the outlet of the water valve body and is gradually discharged to the outside through the tap water outlet to prevent the water valve from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water valve for preventing freezing of a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe by discharging water little by little as the stem holder operates and a waterway is partially opened when the temperature is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "by installing a high pressure gauge that opens the waterway together it has a structure that can respond to both low and high pressure so that damage to buildings and pipes due to leaks in connection parts of water pipes when water is supplied at high pressure as well as in case of freezing it is to provide a water valve for preventing freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it is achieved by a water valve for preventing freezing characterized in that configured to prevent the water valve from being frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "since the water valve for preventing freezing according to the present invention has a structure in which the stem holder that selectively opens and closes the waterway in the supplied water valve is automatically operated according to the water pressure in winter when the water pressure is lowered before the water in the water valve freezes the stem as the holder operates and the waterway is partially opened water is discharged little by little which has the effect of preventing the water pipe from freezing and bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "when the water pressure is lowered before the water freezes the low pressure opening and closing means operates to open the waterway to prevent freezing and bursting as well as to prevent water from being supplied at high pressure at this time the high pressure gauge functions as a pressure reducing device which has the effect of preventing the water valve from being damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "it is configured to prevent the water valve from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101159544-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the present invention has been made in order to solve the above problems the present invention flows along the waterway in the water pipes by heating the remaining water to circulate thereby completely freezing the water pipes indoors and outdoors by the cold weather in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449313-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically it prevents freezing and perforation due to freezing in winter when there is little agricultural water flow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200349427-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition the groundwater remaining on the bottom and side of the channel can be swelled or thawed due to the positive pressure buoyancy generated by the expansion or contraction of the earth s crust or increase in rainy season during freezing or thawing due to seasonal changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-940000292-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in addition after the water supply is made when the faucet 25 is locked water still remains in the faucet tube 24 and at this time by locking the adjustment knob 17 forward the valve support pipe 14 is also moved to the front at the same time the on off valve disc 16 coupled to the front end to block the inlet hole 3a between the inner plate 3 no water supply in the faucet tube 24 water remaining in the faucet pipe 24 in the space portion 9a through the space generated between the front end wall of the packing support ring 9 and the on off valve disc 16 while the on off valve disc 16 is moved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the anti icing system installed inside the sidewalk canal of an underpass a body part which is installed on the floor according to the width of the side channel water pipe and includes a lower frame to which the electric heating wire can be mounted and a column or plate to which a sensor can be attached to either side or one wall side of the water channel pipe can be erected a temperature sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the water pipe to measure the surrounding temperature to derive a temperature measurement value a humidity sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the waterway pipe to measure the surrounding humidity to derive a humidity measurement value a flow measurement device attached to the inner wall of the drain pipe located at the lower end of the side channel waterway and measuring the amount of water flowing from the side channel channel through the drain pipe to the collection well to derive a flow rate a heating wire mounted inside the lower frame of the main body to prevent freezing of the side channel and a control unit controlling driving of the heating wire using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor anti icing system comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "underground driveway waterway icing prevention system method and system installation method the present invention relates to a system a method and a method of installing a system for preventing freezing of an underground passageway side channel and more specifically to prevent freezing of a drainage channel such as an underground lane a passageway or a bridge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as such road culverts installed on underground passageways or local roads with side gut water pipes solve these problems because minimal vehicle passage in the underpass may be impossible and traffic safety problems may occur due to the accumulation of ice in the side hole waterway due to freezing of the drain pipe during the cold winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "as a means for solving the above described technical problem according to an embodiment of the present invention the anti icing system installed inside the sidewalk canal of the underpass is installed on the floor according to the width of the sidewalk canal so that the electric heating wire can be mounted it includes the body portion that can be erected a pillar or plate to which the sensor can be attached to both or one wall side of the water pipe a temperature sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the water pipe to measure the surrounding temperature to derive a temperature measurement value a humidity sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the waterway pipe to measure the surrounding humidity to derive a humidity measurement value a heating wire mounted inside the lower frame of the main body to prevent freezing of the side channel and a controller for controlling the driving of the heating wire using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water supply pipe 32a exposed at the upper end a solenoid valve sv1 coupled to the water supply pipe 32a to control water and a solenoid valve sv1 interposed therebetween on both sides to supply water to the water supply pipe 32a it is configured to include a bypass pipe 33 for bypassing and a freeze prevention means 34 coupled to the bypass pipe 33 to bypass the water in the water supply pipe 32a in a small amount to prevent freezing in winter a three way solenoid valve sv2 is further coupled to the water supply pipe 32a which selectively controls the bypassed water and supplies it to the inner space 31a of the water spray stand 31 or the stone water tank 2 artificial waterway with water supply for freeze protection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "according to claim 1 the water supply unit 3 is molded in the shape of a flower stamen each of the landscape stones 4 is molded in the shape of petals of different sizes and the stone water channel 1 is molded in the shape of a stem to serve as a sculpture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "according to claim 1 the freeze prevention means 34 includes a chamber 341 fixed to be exposed to the water jet 31 and stored therein a freeze prevention valve 342 coupled to the bypass pipe 33 and the chamber 341 and a connecting pipe 343 connecting the anti freeze valve 342 to each other and an operating bar built in the connecting pipe 343 to partially open the anti freeze valve 342 according to the increase in the volume of the operating water 344 an artificial waterway having a water supply for freezing prevention characterized in that it consists of"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to the characteristics for achieving the object as described above the first invention relates to an artificial waterway having a water supply unit for preventing freezing for this purpose a stone waterway a water supply unit installed in the inner center of the stone water tank to supply water and a plurality of landscaping stones radially arranged to have different sizes and height differences around the stone water tank the bottom surface is inclined toward the stone waterway and the water supply unit includes a water jet having an internal space communicating with a drain pipe buried underground a water supply pipe exposed to the top of the water jet across the internal space from the ground and the water supply pipe a solenoid valve coupled to the to regulate water a bypass pipe with both sides extending to the water supply pipe with the solenoid valve interposed therebetween to bypass the water and a small amount of water in the water supply pipe to bypass the circulation in winter to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "1 the present invention has the function of a sculpture in the form of a flower in the overall shape and also supplies water to the stone water channel through the water supply part but the water supply pipe provided in the winter water supply part freezes before freezing it relates to an artificial waterway 5 having a water supply unit for freezing prevention in which the operation bar operated by the increase in the volume of the operating water according to the operation bar automatically drains a small amount of water in the water supply pipe thereby preventing the freezing of the water supply unit in advance"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S592439-Y2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a bypass waterway is provided with the other end connected to a waterway downstream of the check valve and the equipment water stop valve is closed to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S592439-Y2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "a small amount of water continues to flow out and the water flow acts to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S592439-Y2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as described above the present invention has an adjustment screw in the bypass waterway and a flow rate regulator that allows only a small amount of water to flow through the hot water tap making it possible to prevent the water stagnant in the piping from freezing due to water flow"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S592439-Y2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in addition this flow rate regulator was installed in the bypass channel that branches from the water supply channel so during hot water dispensing only the small amount of water necessary to prevent freezing is passed through the bypass channel and most of the water is the amount of water that passes through the heat exchanger to the hot water tap can be reduced compared to those without a flow rate regulator in the bypass waterway and by restricting the hot water tap hot water can be delivered even in winter"}]</data>
</edge>
