  <data key="d6">["line", "place", "change", "pull", "separate", "dispose", "bury", "apply", "solve", "prevent", "open", "block", "attach", "descend", "connect", "arrange", "leak", "use", "form", "become", "fall", "introduce", "ensure", "accord", "intertwine", "peel", "remain", "protrude", "increase", "identify", "cause", "produce", "maintain", "extend", "have", "occur", "repair", "characterize", "may", "configure", "fill", "flow", "say", "can", "damage", "malfunction", "be", "age", "determine", "store", "do", "start", "detect", "describe", "instal", "lift"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200381471-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by extending the wire rope and pulling the adjacently arranged waterway pipe units to be connected to each other integrally the packing ring is installed in the socket and the end of the adjacent waterway pipe unit is placed on the inside of the packing ring and the joints of the waterway pipe units by filling the remaining gap in the part with mortar the end of the adjacent water pipe unit is disposed on the packing ring even when the angle changes due to some ground change thereby maintaining watertightness and ensuring leakage prevention"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S6042129-Y2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it increases adhesive strength has a remarkable effect on water leakage prevention and durability and prevents water from leaking from joints causing damage to plants in waterways or causing damage to humans and livestock due to toxic wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102069616-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "leakage monitoring system of leaky water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101131-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "due to this stress the inner circumferential surface of the water pipe becomes seriously damaged such as peeling peeling or cracking and the expansion joint which is a stretch joint is damaged due to elastic deformation due to a temperature difference and leaks are caused by this"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100564058-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "buried in the basement intertwined in the topography and sewer pipes drainage pipes waterway pipes protruded during the ground work for civil engineering and construction work due to lack of aftercare leakage due to aging long term use and some damaged repair work and the construction of roads in areas where external pressure lubrication is not applied due to changes in usage or land use during construction etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200335682-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "thus the outer surface of the other end formed with the second connecting member 130 of the immersion lining 100 for the front side waterway connected to the front and rear by the packing groove 150 is formed on both inner side and bottom surface of the first connecting member 120 as described above it is possible to prevent leakage that may occur on the connection portion with the inner surface of the first connecting member 120 of the submerged lining 100 for the rear side channel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6889881-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a monitoring method and causes the monitoring step the soil pressure or applied to the pipe detected by the earth pressure sensor for storing the detection data of the strain of the pipe detected by the strain sensor to the data logger the tube and leakage determination step of determining the presence or absence of water leakage the said water pressure in the pipe is detected by the pressure sensors used in waterways after the leakage determination step leak location to identify the leakage position by introducing a leak exploration robots it is characterized by having a specific step"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102560238-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it solves the problem of the drainage pump malfunctioning as it falls off while descending to the stage effectively separating impurities attached to the rake and configuring the main screen and the potential screen of the damper to be lifted at the same time so that the inflow water flows smoothly when the waterway is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330013-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "conventionally when water leakage occurs due to poor construction of the water stop plate 6 of the expansion joint device 1 the rubber like elastic body has been repaired by using an adhesive 5 on the concrete surface of the water leakage producing site with a waterproof cloth 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330013-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "according to the present invention since the reinforcement does not protrude from the concrete surface the secondary risk of leakage due to flowing seawater is blocked and water can be blocked in advance from the waterway side of the expansion joint device where the leakage starts to occur"}]</data>
</edge>
