  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an apparatus for treating undigested wastewater sludges the apparatus comprising a a pump adapted to receive a feed mixture and pressurize the feed mixture to a pressure above the critical pressure for water the feed mixture comprising a wastewater sludge b a heat exchanger arrangement connected to receive the pressurized feed mixture from the pump in a heat exchange relationship with at least one heat exchange fluid c a heater connected to receive the feed mixture from the heat exchanger arrangement through a first reaction conduit d oxidant injection means for introducing an oxidant into the feed mixture at least at a point after the feed mixture has exchanged heat with the heat exchange fluid in the heat exchanger arrangement and before the heater and e a supercritical water oxidation reactor connected to receive a partially reacted mixture from the heater through a second reaction conduit the partially reacted mixture comprising partially oxidized feed mixture the supercritical water oxidation reactor for maintaining the partially reacted mixture at a supercritical temperature and supercritical pressure for a time sufficient to oxidize substantially all organic material within the partially reacted mixture and produce a supercritical effluent"}, {"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "may weaken reactor vessel materials to a point at which the material is unable to withstand the force from the pressure of the reaction mixture"}, {"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "for example the pressure may be reduced to produce a 600 psig steam at a temperature of between approximately 650 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the reaction initiating temperature may range from 200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-8658095-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a device for measuring oxidation reduction potential orp and a temperature in a hot water system the device comprising a a flow through cell having a plurality of ports comprising a first port and a second port b a controller c an integrated sensor component associated with the first port comprising an orp probe and a temperature detector said integrated sensor component residing at least partially inside of the flow through cell the orp probe further comprising at least one electrical connection operable to relay information to said controller wherein the orp probe is operable to measure orp in the hot water system at operating temperature and pressure and the temperature detector further comprises a plurality of negative leads and a plurality of positive leads operable to relay information to said controller wherein the controller is operable to determine whether a real time orp is within an ideal orp range and further operable to cause addition of an effective amount of oxygen or an effective amount of one or more reductants to a feedwater of the hot water system if the real time orp is not within the ideal orp range and d an external pressure balanced reference electrode assembly associated with the second port comprising a tube containing an electrolyte solution having a first end residing at least partially inside of the flow through cell and a second end a porous frit disposed on said first end and a multi fitting housing comprising a seal attached to said second end the multi fitting housing having a silver silver chloride half cell reference electrode partially immersed in said electrolyte solution and having an electrical connection operable to relay information to said controller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102518322-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the front sensor unit 300 and the rear sensor unit 500 may measure water quality information in real time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102518322-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the shear sensor unit 300 may measure water quality information in real time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102518322-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the rear sensor unit 500 may measure water quality information in real time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102554421-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore in the present invention the reaction temperature for optimizing the reaction by mixing with the cleaning agent is controlled through the condensation heat control unit 320 including the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-6811705-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "they require hazardous chemical storage on the vessel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3707457-B1", "para_id": "para_136", "text": "in the second period the cooling water flow rate was increased resulting in an increase in the heat transfer coefficient for the heat exchanger proportional to the change in flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102112732-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "the amount of dissolved oxygen do showed a higher value of treated water than raw water and this is considered to be due to the continuous supply of 7.0 l m 2 min of air to the soil treatment tank 60 for 24 hours"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100951955-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "so that the temperature of the discharged water may be lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the air discharge pipe 60 is a high temperature and high pressure aerobic digestion tank characterized in that to return the carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms to the inlet water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "on the other hand the air discharge pipe 60 is to return the carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms to the inlet water storage tank not shown to prevent the outflow of bubbles or odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "on the other hand carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms are returned to the inlet water storage tank not shown through the air discharge pipe 60 to prevent the outflow of bubbles or odors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a purified water tank unit 1000 for introducing purified water to remove foreign substances and supplying a fixed quantity by driving a metering pump an advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 that electrolyzes the purified water supplied from the purified water tank unit 1000 by the operation of a bdd electrode and generates oh groups hydrogen peroxide and ozone to generate radical water in the advanced oxidation process livestock air inlet chamber unit 3000 for forcibly introducing livestock polluted air generated from livestock facilities and containing total hydrocarbons and concentrating it while maintaining a constant temperature radical water is introduced from the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 and livestock polluted air is introduced from the livestock air inlet chamber 3000 to cause an advanced oxidation process reaction sterilize the virus with ultraviolet rays and photocatalytic reaction with a filter ball advanced oxidation filter ball reaction unit 4000 to cause total hydrocarbon reduction system in the advanced oxidation process of environmental pollution around livestock facilities including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3 the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 is a purified water inlet 2100 for receiving purified water flowing in a fixed amount from the purified water tank unit 1000 a housing part 2200 connecting the purified water inlet 2100 to one side of the lower end and storing purified water flowing in from the purified water inlet 2100 in an external cavity 2210 a purified water heating unit 2300 that is fixedly installed in a coil shape in a portion of the external cavity 2210 in which the purified water is stored in the housing 2200 and heats the purified water according to a corresponding control signal a temperature sensor unit 2400 that is fixedly installed on the other side of the outer cavity of the housing unit 2200 and detects the temperature of purified water according to a corresponding control signal a water filter unit 2500 that is fixedly installed in a part of the inner space of the housing 2200 divides the outer cavity 2210 and the inner cavity 2520 removes foreign substances contained in purified water passes it and introduces it into the inner cavity 2520 while being installed in the central position of the internal cavity 2520 of the water purification filter unit 2500 it is fixed at the top in a sealed state and electrolyzes purified water according to the corresponding control signal so that oh groups and hydrogen peroxide are generated to generate radical water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the total hydrocarbon reduction system for the advanced oxidation process of the environmental pollution around the livestock facility of the present invention devised to achieve the above object includes a purified water tank unit 1000 for introducing purified water removing foreign substances and supplying a fixed quantity by driving a metering pump an advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 that electrolyzes the purified water supplied from the purified water tank unit 1000 by the operation of a bdd electrode and generates oh groups hydrogen peroxide and ozone to generate radical water in the advanced oxidation process livestock air inlet chamber unit 3000 for forcibly introducing livestock polluted air generated from livestock facilities and containing total hydrocarbons and concentrating it while maintaining a constant temperature radical water is introduced from the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 and livestock polluted air is introduced from the livestock air inlet chamber 3000 to cause an advanced oxidation process reaction sterilize the virus with ultraviolet rays and photocatalytic reaction with a filter ball advanced oxidation filter ball reaction unit 4000 that causes may include"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 includes a purified water inlet 2100 for receiving purified water flowing in a fixed amount from the purified water tank unit 1000 a housing part 2200 connecting the purified water inlet 2100 to one side of the lower end and storing purified water flowing in from the purified water inlet 2100 in an external cavity 2210 a purified water heating unit 2300 that is fixedly installed in a coil shape in a portion of the external cavity 2210 in which the purified water is stored in the housing 2200 and heats the purified water according to a corresponding control signal a temperature sensor unit 2400 that is fixedly installed on the other side of the outer cavity of the housing unit 2200 and detects the temperature of purified water according to a corresponding control signal a water filter unit 2500 that is fixedly installed in a part of the inner space of the housing 2200 divides the outer cavity 2210 and the inner cavity 2520 removes foreign substances contained in purified water passes it and introduces it into the inner cavity 2520 while being installed in the central position of the internal cavity 2520 of the water purification filter unit 2500 it is fixed at the top in a sealed state and electrolyzes purified water according to the corresponding control signal so that oh groups and hydrogen peroxide are generated to generate radical water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the livestock air inlet chamber unit 3000 is an air inlet duct 3100 that introduces livestock contaminated air from the bottom surface of the livestock facility and has a funnel shaped cross section a foreign material filtering unit 3200 included in the livestock polluted air introduced from the air inlet duct 3100 and blocking the passage of foreign substances having a diameter of more than a centimeter level a first inlet fan unit 3300 for forcibly introducing livestock contaminated air that has passed through the foreign matter filtering unit 3200 according to a corresponding control signal a warming concentration chamber 3400 for introducing and concentrating livestock contaminated air passing through the first inlet fan unit 3300 and maintaining a constant temperature according to a corresponding control signal an exhaust duct part 3500 for discharging the livestock polluted air of the warming concentration chamber 3400 to the advanced oxidation filter ball reaction part 4000 may include"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_159", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process aop"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_135", "text": "thus the input stream may preferably be heated to above the oxidation reaction ignition temperature without substantial heat exchange with an external source of heat that is without substantial heat exchange with other fluids via a heat exchanger fired heater or the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a process for the supercritical water oxidation of an organic waste material comprising a feeding a pressurized aqueous mixture of said waste material and an oxidant source to a center reaction zone of a platelet tube reactor which is supported within an outer shell and whose outer surface defines together with an inner surface of said shell an annular space a wall of said platelet tube being provided with fluid passages which permit the flow of fluid from said annular space into said center reaction zone through a plurality of apertures b igniting a fuel at an inlet of said reaction zone to increase the temperature of said pressurized aqueous mixture c feeding water heated and pressurized to at least supercritical conditions externally of said reactor to at least one point along said annular space surrounding said platelet tube reactor wherein the resulting pressure in said annular space is higher than the pressure in the center reaction zone within said platelet tube such that said supercritical water flows from said annular space through said fluid passages in the wall of said platelet tube and into said center reaction zone through said plurality of apertures forming a thin film of supercritical water over substantially the entire inner surface of said platelet tube and heating said mixture to supercritical reaction temperature and d reacting said organic waste with said oxidant in said reaction zone"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "claim_15", "text": "a process for the supercritical water oxidation of an organic waste material comprising a feeding a pressurized aqueous mixture containing said waste material and an oxidant source at ambient temperature to a center reaction zone of a platelet tube reactor which is supported within an outer shell and whose outer surface defines together with an inner surface of said shell an annular space a wall of said platelet tube being provided with fluid passages which permit the flow of fluid from said annular space into said center reaction zone through a plurality of apertures b igniting a fuel at an inlet of said reaction zone to increase the temperature of said pressurized aqueous mixture c feeding water heated and pressurized to at least supercritical conditions externally of said reactor to multiple locations along said annular space surrounding said platelet tube reactor wherein the resulting pressure in said annular space is higher than the pressure in the center reaction zone within said platelet tube such that said supercritical water flows from said annular space through said fluid passages in the wall of said platelet tube and into said center reaction zone through said plurality of apertures forming a thin film of supercritical water over substantially the entire inner surface of said platelet tube and heating said mixture to supercritical reaction temperature and d reacting said organic waste with said oxidant in said reaction zone at a temperature of from about 1100 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "claim_21", "text": "a process for the oxidation of an organic waste material comprising a feeding a pressurized aqueous mixture of water and said waste material to a center zone of a platelet tube reactor which is supported within an outer shell and whose outer surface defines together with an inner surface of said shell an annular space a wall of said platelet tube being provided with fluid passages which permit the flow of fluid from said annular space into said center zone through a plurality of apertures b igniting a fuel at an inlet of said reaction zone to increase the temperature of said pressurized aqueous mixture c feeding water heated and pressurized to at least supercritical conditions externally of said reactor to at least one point along said annular space surrounding said platelet tube reactor wherein the resulting pressure in said annular space is higher than the pressure in the center zone within said platelet tube such that said supercritical water flows from said annular space through said fluid passages in the wall of said platelet tube and into said center zone through said plurality of apertures forming a thin film of supercritical water over substantially the entire inner surface of said platelet tube and heating said mixture to supercritical temperature d separating organic components from inorganic components of said waste material while at supercritical conditions and e oxidizing said separated organic components outside of said platelet tube reactor"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "5 252 224 discloses a supercritical water oxidation process in which the reaction mixture is passed through the reactor at a velocity sufficient to prevent settling of a substantial portion of the solid particles from the reaction mixture"}, {"pat_id": "US-6030587-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pressurized reactor for supercritical water oxidation comprising a pressure vessel for containing a fluid and capable of operating in excess of a supercritical temperature and a supercritical pressure of said fluid said vessel further comprising a shell and a cap portion said portions fitting together to enclose an interior space said portions having interior and exterior surfaces and a common longitudinal axis said interior space having a center point an oxidizer said oxidizer mixed with said fluid an electrical heating means a hollow protuberance located in at least one of said portions said protuberance formed along said common axis and projecting into said interior space said protuberance having an end closed to said interior surface and an end open to said exterior surface said protuberance receives said electrical heating means said electrical heating means heats said fluid in a first zone surrounding said interior center point and means for cooling said vessel exterior surface thereby cooling said interior surface and creating a second zone in said fluid along said interior surfaces wherein said fluid exists in a subcritical state said heating means and said cooling means creating a density gradient in said fluid and thereby cause a steady state convective circulation to form in said fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100735544-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "concentration of the high concentration of organic wastewater in the high temperature aerobic digestion tank 1a is 2.5 5 of the suitable solids if the concentration of the solid is too low the conditions that can be activated because the lack of energy sources for high temperature aerobic microorganisms it has a problem of generating insufficient heat of oxidation to form"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102688285-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the environmental factor is a sensing value sensed by the sensor constituting the sensor unit 4 and includes ph temperature dissolved oxygen do oxidation reduction potential orp sludge concentration sludge generation amount water quality and flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "this drop in ph gives immediate indication of the effectiveness of the cavitation nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "US-3876536-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a pressure between 150 and 4 000 psig so that a reduction of between 30 and 70 percent in chemical oxygen demand is obtained separating the gaseous liquid and solid phases from said oxidation and biologically oxidizing the liquid phase in an aeration contact tank containing a biomass suitable to effect biological oxidation of the organic solutes present in said liquid phase the improvement which comprises maintaining powdered activated carbon in the aeration contact tank in an amount sufficient to enhance the biooxidation and substantially reduce the odor and color of said liquid phase carrying out the biological oxidation until excess biomass builds up and the activated carbon becomes spent transferring a mixture of the excess biomass and spent carbon to a wet oxidation reactor and oxidizing said mixture under conditions similar to those used for wet air oxidation of the raw sewage sludge or night soil so as to regenerate the powdered activated carbon for further use in the biological oxidation step and at the same time disposing of the excess biomass"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore there is an urgent need to introduce a structure that can effectively absorb such heat deformation to protect the gravity wet oxidation reactor.the present invention created to solve the above problems is to protect the gravity wet oxidation reactor by effectively absorbing the heat deformation according to the temperature inside the gravity pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100983829-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition since the energy is generated during the co 2 generation process and offsets the energy absorption by the reduction reaction of anaerobic microorganisms heating energy required to increase the temperature of the methane fermentation tank can be reduced and organic acid fermentation since the co 2 generated by the co 2 generation and oxidation of aerobic microorganisms get up at the same time the higher the methane generation efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "US-6350376-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a further purpose of the present invention is to perform control for optimal temperature through adjustment of the flow rate of the heat exchange water to accomplish lower flow rate and lower pressure of the heat exchange water so as to reduce installation space and vibration due to the pump and to achieve a heat exchange system that minimizes cost increase"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101739419-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a constant temperature system for leachate and wastewater treatment plants installed in a nitrification tank in a leachate treatment plant including a tiller a flow control tank a mixing tank a nitrification tank a settling tank a thickening tank a fenton oxidation treatment tank or a reverse osmosis treatment tank a plurality of nitrification vessels buried in the ground and purifying and discharging the supplied leachate from the outside and having a plurality of chambers partitioned by a plurality of partition walls for setting the movement path of the leachate therein at least one agitator disposed on the bottom surface of the nitrification tank to mix the leachate while rotating a first heat pump disposed in an upper part of the nitrification tank on the ground to heat the nitrification tank and heat exchanging the first chamber leachate and the heat exchanged refrigerant disposed in front of the nitrification tank in the direction in which the leachate flows 3 heat pump a fourth heat pump to a sixth heat pump arranged in parallel with the first heat pump to the third heat pump and arranged in the rear along the direction in which the leachate of the nitrification tank flows and the heat exchanged refrigerant is heat a first heat exchanger connected to the first heat pump to a third heat pump and disposed in the first chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a second heat exchanger connected to the fourth heat pump to the sixth heat pump and disposed in the second chamber and performing heat exchange with the leachate a first circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the first heat exchange unit a second circulation pump for circulating the refrigerant in the second heat exchange unit a preliminary circulation pump interposed between the first circulation pump and the second circulation pump and capable of temporarily operating corresponding to the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump a three way valve connected between any one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump and selectively supplying the heat exchanged refrigerant to the first chamber or the second chamber a sensor unit provided on the three way valve for sensing the temperature or pressure of the refrigerant flowing into the three way valve a first heat pump to a sixth heat pump a first circulation pump and a second circulation pump and a control unit controlling the temperature of the leachate in the nitrification tank to a set range by controlling the agitator an expansion tank provided to compensate for a pressure of the heat exchanged refrigerant supplied through the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump and an air blower unit for supplying air supplied from the outside to the periphery of the agitator in the nitrification tank the air blower unit includes an air flow path for introducing outside air into the vicinity of the agitator a compressor for forcibly supplying external air through the air flow path and a nozzle provided at an end portion of the air flow path for discharging air toward the agitator and wherein the agitator includes a housing fixed to the bottom of the nitrification tank and passing through the inside in a vertical direction a propeller for rotating the inside of the housing to mix the leachate a driving motor for driving the propeller and a guide arm provided on the outer circumferential surface of the housing so as to be guided through the air passage when installed wherein the control unit controls the at least one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump to selectively operate the heat pumps when the temperature of the nitrification tank reaches the set temperature by receiving the data of the sensor unit the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump operates first and controls the heat pumps to operate after the set time has elapsed wherein the nitrification tank includes a plurality of ventilation doors formed with openings communicating with the outside at upper portions of the chambers and selectively opening and closing the openings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100762919-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "as such by filling the contact media 136 in the influent stable contact chamber 131 the influent may be performed very stably regardless of the low concentration or the high concentration and is also very effective in coping with changes in winter temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the second temperature being greater than the first temperature after the primary stream has been injected into said front port of the elongate reaction chamber and has been allowed to travel toward the back end of said elongate reaction chamber during use a first injection side port downstream in the elongate reaction chamber located at such distance from the front port that 90 100 of oxidant injected by the automatic from injection control system in the front port is reacted with the organic matter by the time it reaches said injection side port during use an automatic side injection control system adapted to inject during use an amount of cooling water per unit time and an amount of oxidant per unit time through said first injection side port in a manner that the amount of oxidant injected through the first injection side port is effective to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a predetermined amount in the primary stream and the amount of the cooling water injected through the first injection side port is in proportion to the amount of the oxidant injected such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially counterbalances at least a portion of any heat of oxidation released n 1 following injection side ports each of the n 1 port ports being at such distance from the front port that 90 100 of the oxidant injected in all ports upstream of each n 1 side injection port is reacted with the organic matter by the time it reaches said injection side port during use and wherein the automatic side injection control system is adapted to inject an amount of cooling water per unit time and an amount of oxidant per unit time through each of said n 1 side injection ports during use in a manner that the amount of oxidant injected in each n 1 side injection port is effective to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a predetermined amount in the primary stream during use and the amount of the cooling water injected in each n 1 side injection port is in proportion to the amount of the oxidant injected such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially counterbalances at least a portion of any heat of oxidation released during use and such that the automatic side injection control system selectively controls the temperature of the stream in the range of 750 1200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "claim_21", "text": "during use the heating system being connected such that the stream flows from the heating system to the reaction chamber during use a conduit connected to introduce oxidant into the stream at or before the front portion of the reaction chamber during use an oxidant injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the oxidant injection port being connected to introduce oxidant into the reaction chamber during use a cooling water injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the water injection port being connected to introduce cooling water during use into the reaction chamber and an automatic controller adapted to control the amount of cooling water and oxidant introduced into the reaction chamber during use the amount of oxidant introduced being controlled to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a selected amount during use and the amount of cooling water introduced being controlled in proportion to the amount of oxidant introduced such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially i counterbalances at least part of the heat of oxidation released by the reaction of the oxidant with the organic matter and ii selectively controls the temperature of the stream in the range of 750 1200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "claim_60", "text": "during use the heating system being connected such that the stream flows from the heating system to the reaction chamber during use a conduit connected to introduce oxidant into the stream at or before the front portion of the reaction chamber during use a first oxidant injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the first oxidant injection port being connected to introduce oxidant into the reaction chamber during use a cooling water injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the cooling water injection port being connected at about the same location or downstream of the first oxidant injection port and the cooling water injection port being connected to introduce cooling water during use into the reaction chamber a second oxidant injection port connected downstream of the cooling water injection port the second oxidant injection port being connected to introduce oxidant into the reaction chamber during use a controller adapted to control the amount of oxidant introduced into the reaction chamber during use the mount of oxidant introduced being controlled to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a selected amount during use and a temperature control system adapted to control the temperature of the stream during use the temperature control system being adapted to control the temperature of the stream by varying the amount of cooling water introduced as a function of the oxidant introduced such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially i counterbalances at least part of the heat of oxidation released by the reaction of the oxidant with the organic matter and ii selectively controls the temperature of the stream in the range of 750 1200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "para_142", "text": "some corrections may be made for heat losses in order to inject the proper amount of water so that the temperature is maintained at or around a desired plateau value"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "para_155", "text": "some corrections may be made for heat losses in order to inject the proper amount of water so that the temperature is maintained at or around a desired plateau value"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "para_156", "text": "some corrections may be made for heat losses in order