emical sewage treatment for ship that can minimize the sludge generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-5106513-A", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "while supercritical water oxidation requires a thicker walled vessel due to higher operating pressure the less dense process stream in supercritical temperature water oxidation necessitates a larger vessel to achieve a comparable residence time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100232360-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "the present invention is an anaerobic tank anoxic tank aerobic tank sedimentation tank sludge in order to improve the point that the conventional technique is different in performance and inefficient in order to remove residual nitrogen and phosphorus after treating organic wastewater providing a novel system that properly connects thickeners sludge storage tanks and dehydrators and simultaneously removes nitrogen and phosphorus biologically eliminating the problem of releasing nitrogen into nitrogen gas and eluting phosphorus and promoting the self oxidation of excess sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452663-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "flow control tank 1 anaerobic tank 2 for removing phosphorus in the water to be treated flowing in from the flow rate control tank 1 an anaerobic tank 3 for removing nitrate nitrogen in the treated water flowing in from the anaerobic tank 2 an aerobic tank 4 for nitrifying nitrogen by aeration of air into the water to be treated introduced from the anoxic tank 3 a fenton oxidation unit 10 for fenton oxidation treatment of the water to be treated flowing in from the aerobic tank 4 a sedimentation tank 5 for separating the water to be treated from the fenton oxidation unit 10 into a supernatant and sludge a high temperature sterilization unit 20 for high temperature sterilization of the water to be treated by heat exchange a floating filtration tank 1000 having an inlet 1010 into which the target water is introduced a floating filtration device 1020 mounted on the target water inlet space 1040 and a 