gned to measure one or more of the ph value of the water the oxidation reduction potential of the water water temperature and combinations thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102013032-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "on the other hand the rear end of the flow rate adjustment tank 100 may be provided with a pre treatment device 400 for weakening the cell membrane wall strength of the organic material constituting the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-7404899-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "6 200 466 describes a reactor system for decontamination of water by photolytic oxidation utilizing near blackbody radiation the system comprising 1 a reaction chamber defining an internal space with an inlet and an outlet and 2 a broadband radiator for generating radiant energy with wavelengths between about 150 nm and about 3 um the broadband radiator disposed within the reaction chamber such that a sufficient dosage of broadband radiation irradiates the contaminants and or the oxidant within the internal space of the reaction chamber thereby causing photolytic oxidation of the contaminants by direct action of the radiation on the contaminants to break chemical bonds by sustaining a free radical chain reaction of oxidizing components thus breaking down the contaminants by way of atomic abstraction of the components of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-7404899-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "6 117 335 describes a reactor system for decontamination of water by photolytic oxidation utilizing near blackbody radiation the system comprising 1 a reaction chamber defining an internal space with an inlet and an outlet and 2 a broadband radiator for generating radiant energy with wavelengths between 150 nm and about 3 \u03bcm the broadband radiator disposed within the reaction chamber such that a sufficient dosage of broadband radiation irradiates the contaminants and or the oxidant within the internal space of the reaction chamber thereby causing photolytic oxidation of the contaminants by way of atomic abstraction of the components of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102735412-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the sensors may include for example a ph sensor an oxidation reduction potential orp sensor a chlorine sensor a temperature sensor etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "at supercritical conditions no liquid water phase is present to be vaporized to steam to remove heat from the reactor vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "after subcritical wet oxidation treatment the oxidation mixture exits the reactor vessel 20 via a conduit 22 and is heated by a heater 24 to supercritical water temperatures in excess of 374 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "additional oxidant such as oxygen gas air or chemical oxidant such as hydrogen peroxide or ozone may optionally be added via a conduit 26 to the oxidation mixture prior to the mixture entering the heater 24 or after heating the oxidation mixture to supercritical water temperatures via a conduit 26"}, {"pat_id": "US-11738314-B2", "para_id": "para_158", "text": "supercritical water oxidation reactions while also utilizing radial thermal gradients and the concentration of fuel along a central axis of the inner vessel s to protect the metal outer vessel from chemical and or oxidation attack due to the high temperature high pressure reactions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200330905-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the treatment efficiency of the aeration tank 4 is affected by the design operation conditions such as the load of organic matter the aeration time the air amount and the conditions of the growing environment such as the water temperature and ph"}, {"pat_id": "US-5055180-A", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "thus an uninsulated tank will normally last for a much longer period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325646-B2", "para_id": "para_358", "text": "the efc according to any embodiment may further include an oxidation reduction potential sensor a ph sensor a chlorine sensor a conductivity sensor a flow rate sensor a temperature sensor or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325646-B2", "para_id": "para_367", "text": "the efc according to any embodiment may further include an oxidation reduction potential sensor a ph sensor a chlorine sensor a conductivity sensor a flow rate sensor a temperature sensor or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-5468350-A", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the toc which has become ions by the oxidation decomposition in evaporation container 2 is removed by ion exchange resin filling polisher 8 or a reverse osmosis membrane"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the low concentration wastewater which is a dehydrated filtrate is sent to the low concentration wastewater collecting tank 300 when the low concentration wastewater and the leachate discharged from the fermentation tank 503 in the composting step are introduced into the low concentration wastewater collection tank 300 the primary water is subjected to the magnetization treatment and the static pressure treatment the treated water is supplied to the primary aeration tank 310 and air is supplied from the blower 422 to the primary settling tank 311 so that the settled solids are supplied to the primary settling tank 312 activated humic substance pellet minerals containing active minerals and minus ions are collected by the primary transfer pump 313 when they reach the central cone of the lower part of the primary settling tank 311 a primary microorganism culture tank 314 in which a primary bioreactor 315 filled with minerals or ceramics packings 316 emitting radiant minerals or ceramics and radiating far infrared rays and negative ions is installed and the primary aeration tank 310 the surplus sludge produced is separated into a high temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of high concentration wastewater a biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage a secondary aeration tank 414 in the low concentration wastewater secondary biological treatment stage and a secondary microorganism culture tank the sludge which has been settled in the primary settling tank 310 is supplied to the primary microorganism culture tank 314 by the primary transfer pump 313 and supplied to the primary microorganism culture tank 314 the air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the primary bioreactor 315 and the lower portion of the primary microorganism culture tank 314 to supply the wastewater while the aeration is performed to convert the polyphenol compounds into metabolites corrosive microorganisms that convert water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors humic substances precursors or corrosive substances humic substances and microorganisms that are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms are excreted by the corrosion reaction and then sent to the aeration tank 310 where the primary biological wastewater treatment the entire system is induced to become wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and microorganisms that are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms the solids are precipitated in the first settling tank 311 and the overflowed the first biologically treated water which is the overflow is treated with the first biological treatment stage of the low concentration wastewater sent to the first biological treatment tank 400 when the primary biological treatment water is supplied to the primary biological treatment water storage tank 400 electrolytic oxidation treatment electron beam treatment eelectron beam treatment or electrolytic oxidation treatment and electronic pretreatment are performed to remove the biodegradable organic matter contained in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the settled solids are supplied to the secondary settling tank 416 by the central cone cone it is possible to deposit active erosion material pellets minerals containing active minerals minerals or ceramics that emit negative ions and ultraviolet rays that emit far infrared rays and negative ions by the secondary transfer pump 417 the excess sludge is returned to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 and the secondary aeration tank 414 in which the secondary bioreactor 419 filled with the mineral or ceramics packing 420 is loaded and the excess sludge discharged is discharged temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater and the biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage together with the excess sludge to be discharged to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 sludge precipitated in the secondary settling tank 415 is supplied to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the secondary bioreactor 419 and the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 a corrosive microorganism which transforms water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors or corrosive substances by providing a polyphenol compound as a metabolite by supplying a wastewater and microbes in symbiotic relationships and sent to the secondary aeration tank 414 to induce the whole of the secondary biological wastewater treatment system to be subjected to the wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and the microorganisms which are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms and the secondary settling tank 415 the second biologically treated water which is the overflowing water is the second biological treatment step of the low concentration wastewater sent to the final biological treatment water tank 421 the secondary biologically treated water is subjected to sterilization treatment by a combination of at least one of oxidizing agent oxidizing agent ultraviolet ray irradiation electrolytic oxidation or electron beam irradiation and then subjected to sand filtration to remove suspended solids a final treatment step of the wastewater discharging the treated water when the dehydrated cake dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process is supplied to the mixer 500 a moisture adjuster and a soil conditioner are injected into the mixer mixer 501 while stirring to adjust the water content to 60 to 65 wt and fed to a fermentation tank 503 which is opened and straightened by the fermentation tank feed conveyor 502 and then flipped to the fermentation tank mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 30 to 50 days"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5224799-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in daily life and organic wastewater treatment wastewater treatment is effectively performed by making the most of the action of various useful microorganisms and creating an environment in which the microorganisms are easily active in the treatment water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102810409-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a high concentration wastewater treatment device which sprays a high temperature flame on the water surface in a concentration tank to evaporate the water surface after filtering the concentrate in an ro membrane filtration device cools the evaporated water vapor in a wet scrubber and discharges it as condensate so that foreign substances can be removed by oxidation combustion and are chemically stabilized so that they can easily coagulate and precipitate with a coagulant and dehydrate the precipitated sludge to form a cake so that it can be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102810409-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to the present invention the concentrate filtered in the ro membrane filtration device is sprayed onto the water surface in a concentration tank by high temperature flames to evaporate the water surface the evaporated water vapor is cooled in a wet scrubber and discharged as condensate so that foreign substances can be removed by oxidation combustion and thus are chemically stabilized so that they easily coagulate and precipitate with a coagulant and the precipitated sludge is dehydrated and turned into a cake for treatment thereby improving the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "US-5591415-A", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "fourth because the adverse effects of pressure and temperature have been distributed and mostly separated so that the pressure acts mainly on the pressure vessel and the temperature acts mainly on the reactor considerably higher temperatures and pressures may be safely utilized as compared to those which may be safely applied in the case of conventional reactors"}, {"pat_id": "US-5591415-A", "para_id": "para_166", "text": "because two phase feeds can be converted to higher temperature single phase feed in the upward extension 912 this embodiment of the invention serves to also minimize preheating requirements thereby facilitating operating cost and equipment investment reduction"}, {"pat_id": "US-12264089-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "adding to be treated cyanide containing wastewater into a cyanide primary treatment tank and performing a cyanide primary treatment on the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater in the cyanide primary treatment tank to obtain primary treated wastewater wherein a process of the cyanide primary treatment comprises under a stirring condition adding alkali liquor into the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater to adjust a power of hydrogen ph value of the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater to a first preset alkaline range and adding a sodium hypochlorite solution into the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater simultaneously to adjust an oxidation reduction potential orp of the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater to obtain a first mixture and allowing the first mixture to react at room temperature for a period of time and retain for a period of time to thereby obtain the primary treated wastewater and the primary treated wastewater comprises a remaining amount of chlorine"}, {"pat_id": "US-12264089-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "adding to be treated cyanide containing wastewater into a treatment tank and performing a cyanide primary treatment on the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater in the treatment tank to obtain wastewater after cyanide primary treatment also referred to as primary treated wastewater where a process of the cyanide primary treatment includes under a stirring condition adding alkali liquor into the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater to adjust a ph value of the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater to a first preset alkaline range and adding a sodium hypochlorite solution into the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater simultaneously to adjust an oxidation reduction potential orp of the to be treated cyanide containing wastewater to obtain a first mixture and allowing the first mixture to react at room temperature for a period of time and retain also referred to as hold for a period of time to thereby obtain the wastewater after cyanide primary treatment and chlorine is remained in the wastewater after cyanide primary treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102328962-B1", "para_id": "claim_25", "text": "a structure in which the guide rod is coupled a structure in which a pressure discharge device for discharging the pressure generated inside the rotary processing vessel is configured on one side of the rotating processing vessel a structure in which a measuring device configured to measure the internal temperature and internal pressure of the rotating processing vessel is coupled to the other side of the rotating processing vessel a structure in which a heating device configured to heat or cool the fluid material molecules filled in the inside of the rotary processing vessel is coupled to one end of the rotating processing vessel in the inside of the rotary processing container a fragrance emitting member composed of plants such as cypress oak juniper or animal such as musk or silicate obsidian germanium elvan chungite ore mud ball ocher ball tourmanium ball sericite biotite muscovite ball alumina ball illite ball tourmanium mineral material such as alkali ball plant material and material catalysis inducing material consisting of animal material compared to the total capacity of the rotary processing vessel 100wt a structure in which a magnification of 5wt to 50wt was added the inner wall of the rotary processing vessel is composed of wood stone cement or plastic based material to prevent material oxidation and material catalysis between the rotating processing vessel and the inner wall the osmotic pressure action and the condensation phenomenon while the rotating processing vessel is in contact with the fluid material molecules filled in the rotating processing vessel by the material catalysis and the material molecule contacting action features a nature friendly eco friendly material molecule separation and processing machine that inserts a barrier film that exhibits adiabatic action while blocking the deformation of the basic properties of the fluid material molecules inserted into the inside of the rotary processing vessel by the action of gravity using a nature friendly material molecule separation and processing machine that separates and extracts fluid material molecules with light specific gravity and fluid material molecules with heavy specific gravity combined with polluted fluid material molecules an eco friendly material molecule separation and processing machine applied to an eco friendly method that separates and extracts fluid substance molecules and fluid substance molecules with light specific gravity or purifies polluted water generated in aquaculture or fish farms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452662-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "flow control tank 1 anaerobic tank 2 for removing phosphorus in the water to be treated flowing in from the flow rate control tank 1 an anaerobic tank 3 for removing nitrate nitrogen in the treated water flowing in from the anaerobic tank 2 an aerobic tank 4 for nitrifying nitrogen by aeration of air into the water to be treated introduced from the anoxic tank 3 a fenton oxidation unit 10 for fenton oxidation treatment of the water to be treated flowing in from the aerobic tank 4 a sedimentation tank 5 for separating the water to be treated from the fenton oxidation unit 10 into a supernatant and sludge a high temperature sterilization unit 20 for high temperature sterilization of the water to be treated by heat exchange a flotation filtration tank 1000 having an inlet 1010 into which the wtbt is introduced a flotation filtration device 1020 mounted on the wtbt inlet space 1040 and a discharge part 1030 from which the wtbt is discharged and circulation guide part 40 for guiding the water to be treated in the inlet space 1040 of the flotation filtration tank 1000 to the flotation filtration device 1020 the fenton oxidation unit 10 a reaction tank 100 having a reaction space therein a wastewater supply unit 200 provided to supply wastewater fenton oxide supply unit 300 provided to supply the fenton oxide a main supply unit 400 provided to supply the wastewater and fenton oxide supplied from the wastewater supply unit 200 and the fenton oxide supply unit 300 to the reactor 100 the crystals 500 are located in a large amount in the reaction space 110 of the reaction tank 100 and are provided to attach the sludge generated in the reaction process while flowing in the wastewater supplied from the main supply unit 400 a treated water discharge unit 600 provided to discharge the treated water treated in the reaction tank 100 a sediment discharge unit 700 provided for discharging precipitated sludge among sludge generated in the reaction process in the reaction tank 100 a circulation unit 800 provided to circulate a portion of the treated water treated in the reaction space unit 110 to the main supply unit 400 and and a fenton filter membrane 900 provided to prevent the crystals 500 of the reaction space 110 from being discharged to the treated water discharge unit 600 the circulation unit 800 a circulation pipe 810 having an inlet end connected to the reactor 100 and an outlet end connected to the main supply unit 400 the circulation pump 820 is for supplying a portion of the treated water to the lower end of the reaction space 110 through the circulation pipe 810 and is supplied to the lower end of the reaction space 110 by the main supply unit 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452662-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "at least one oxygen supply unit is mounted in the vertical direction inside the guide partition wall and the oxygen supply unit is composed of an oxygen supply pipe and an oxygen supply nozzle to remove the descending floating filter media and contaminants contained in the water to be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452662-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in the present invention the configuration of the device except for the fenton oxidation unit 10 the high temperature sterilization unit 20 the floating filtration tank 1000 and the circulation guide unit 40 may be used as it is known"}, {"pat_id": "US-10501355-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the wastewater undergoes a catalytic oxidation reaction in the system in which the macromolecular hard to degrade organic materials are converted into small molecules and thereby is removed"}]</data>
