, "continue", "bypass", "be", "conduct", "alarm", "suppress", "view", "elapse", "warm", "pasteurize", "expose", "stem", "combine", "get", "apply", "contaminate", "confirm", "refrigerate", "rise", "preheat", "reach", "trigger", "aerate", "engage", "display", "extinguish", "jet", "dump", "refer", "increase", "achieve", "soften", "maximize", "invent", "regenerate", "pour", "disclose", "circulate", "melt", "notify", "pipe", "will", "restore", "provide", "wrap", "pulse", "contain", "mention", "space", "alleviate", "proceed", "compare", "withdraw", "enhance", "arrange", "leak", "repeat", "vaporize", "reuse", "calculate", "process", "transform", "fight", "limit", "regard", "release", "bring", "do", "settle", "create", "facilitate", "lock", "free", "understand", "bury", "deleteaccorde", "exceed", "consider", "slide", "judge", "impact", "run", "end", "insert", "direct", "sag", "seat", "cover", "show", "might", "omit", "appreciate", "configure", "bond", "overheat", "cool", "derive", "start", "fit", "conceive", "enable", "collide", "guide", "perform", "act", "thereto", "consist", "want", "pulverize", "open", "instruct", "house", "sublime", "mean", "reenergize", "atomize", "supply", "use", "predetermine", "desalinate", "cut", "estimate", "associate", "break", "involve", "buffer", "tube", "initiate", "draw", "invoke", "shrink", "stagnate", "extend", "control", "transmit", "case", "need", "monitor", "expend", "exist", "terminate", "collect", "subcoole", "instal", "bleed"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5979490-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "to prevent the water from freezing within an in ground water delivery assembly the underground supply sections and internal valve mechanisms are buried to a sufficient depth to keep the water out of the above ground portion of the assembly"}, {"pat_id": "US-4283211-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "or thereabove or brackish water sea water or other saline water or wastewater at or above its freezing point is brought into heat exchange contact with the liquid phase condensate of a working fluid or refrigerant hereinafter usually termed working fluid having a boiling point significantly below the freezing point of water or of the saline water whereby the water is frozen and gives up its latent heat of fusion which is absorbed by the working fluid condensate as its latent heat of vaporization the working fluid condensate thereby being vaporized by that exchange of latent heats of phase transition at autogenic pressure and the vapor is superheated to approximately the temperature of the inlet water the superheated vapor is released in a turbine to create mechanical shaft power which by conventional mechanical and electrical means is converted to electric power"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "rather than install thermal protection or risk the freezing and rupture of water pipes residents may simply leave their outdoor valves open to a bleeding or dripping level the temperature of household water continuously flowing through to the outdoor valves is usually sufficient to prevent freezing of the valve and associated plumbing"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention provides a simple design for a mechanically actuated temperature responsive valve that efficiently utilizes the volumetric expansion of freezing water to cause water from an outdoor tap to flow through discharge ports"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "thus as water in reservoir 142 freezes its expanding volume lifts piston 130 unseating valve head 132 and opening a fluid path between conduit 110 and exhaust ports 120 through which water is continuously discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-4932429-A", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "when water begins to flow through in the screw stopper 1 water from the duct which is comparatively warm flows into the water pipe valve and thus it enables to raise the water s temperature and prevent water in the water pipe valve from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100912781-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "seventh since the heating wire is provided on the outer surface of the body of the inlet and the dehydration unit it is possible to prevent the viscosity rise and freezing of the slurry due to the temperature drop and thus can be used to operate even in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200337587-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "such a conventional water meter as the tap water in the lower and upper casing is frozen due to the outside temperature dropped below freezing in the protective container during the winter the meter reading unit embedded in the lower and upper casing is frozen and broken so that the water meter is replaced or there was a problem such as not only to bear the economic burden of the repair but also to suffer the inconvenience"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200337587-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the freeze prevention water meter is a meter body having an inlet and an outlet so that water supplied from a predetermined water supply source can flow in and out and has a receiving portion in communication with each of the inlet and outlet meter reading flow rate of the water flowing out of the outlet a metering member which is accommodated in the receiving portion so as to be able to be inserted into the inlet portion so as to heat the water flowing into and out of the meter body to a predetermined temperature and is drawn out to the outlet portion via the bottom side of the receiving portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200337587-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "it not only prevents the damage caused by freezing but also prevents freezing without using power to reduce the economic burden of the user and prevents the occurrence of safety accidents and mechanical failures due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-12337259-B2", "para_id": "para_1210", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump bottom of the container 139 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365041-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "60 and a valve 30 connected by dc 12v to control whether water is discharged by being involved in the opening and closing of the water outlet and a heating element 40 wound around the water supply pipe and generating heat according to external temperature changes to prevent freezing and bursting of the water supply pipe in the water pipe including and a cover body 50 that protects from external factors by receiving a part of the water outlet pipe the water supply pipe and the heating element inside the valve 30 is a dc 12v solenoid valve is installed in the boundary section of the bent shape where the water outlet pipe starts from the water supply pipe prevents water from remaining in the outlet pipe when locked and protrudes to the upper surface of the outlet pipe with the end bent downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_i