rcumferential surface of the flow path tube 74 in contact with the ion exchange resin 64 a temperature sensor for detecting the temperature t of the softening means 60 that changes according to the season for example winter 110 is attached to the inner circumferential surface of the flow path tube 74 to prevent freezing of the softening means 60 according to the temperature t of the softening means 60 detected by the temperature sensor 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175854-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "according to the softening apparatus and the control method of the washing machine according to the present invention as described above by mounting a heater and a temperature sensor in the softening means to detect whether the softening means is frozen and when the softening means is frozen in order to prevent freezing of the softening means even in winter by driving the heater to thaw the softening means it is possible to prevent freezing of the softening means and deterioration of softening performance and to take prompt measures according to the freezing of the softening means"}, {"pat_id": "US-4205698-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "this device operates on the principle of bringing relatively warmer line water up to the valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101286956-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to prevent the freezing of the pipe conventionally the insulation is wrapped in the pipe the heating wire is wrapped in the outside of the pump or the heater is installed in the pump room to install the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0008176-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "since the water is drawn off at the water temperature prevailing in the receptacle the addition of that water to the flow through the heat exchanger in which the waste water gives off heat does not result in any cooling of this flow with the above mentioned concomitant disadvantages and risks of freezing in the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101225602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by implementing t