x with the water meter installed or by installing a heat insulating material in the lid installed on the upper surface of the water meter protection box to prevent the freezing point below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200301700-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and the purpose of the present invention is to prevent the water meter from freezing by heating the bottom of the water meter when the outside temperature decreases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200301700-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the same effect is generated even when combined with each other and tightly fixed and thus the process of supplying power to the heater is the same as the above embodiment and thus a detailed description thereof will be omitted.according to the present invention as described above even if the outside temperature is lowered the temperature inside the water meter box drops below zero so that the heater warms the bottom of the water meter and prevents the water meter from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4857185-A", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "this will provide higher temperature of the water to keep it from freezing in winter and also assist the treatment process for better performances the process thus becoming highly energy efficient"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 1 the controller 130 when the temperature data obtained from the temperature detection unit 120 drops below 6 degrees celsius the on off valve driver 150 is operated to open the on off valve 140 by a predetermined angle an automatic dripping device for preventing freezing characterized in that when the temperature data obtained from the temperature detection unit 120 rises above 6 degrees celsius the on off valve drive unit 150 is operated to block the on off valve 140"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in one embodiment of the present invention the automatic water fall device for preventing freezing is mounted inside the main body and after receiving power from the outside and storing it therein when the power supplied from the outside is cut off the power stored therein a power supply unit capable of charging and discharging providing a temperature detection unit a control unit and an on off valve driving unit a power supply unit warming unit mounted in a structure surrounding an outer circumferential surface of the power supply unit and a wireless communication module mounted inside the main body capable of performing wireless communication with an operator s smart device and transmitting data obtained from the control unit to the operator wherein the control unit further includes from the temperature detection unit in real time the detected temperature data and state data of the on off valve drive unit may be transmitted to an operator through a wireless communication module and the on off valve drive unit may be controlled according to a control signal received from the operator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "by doing so it is possible to provide an automatic dripping device for preventing freezing that includes a configuration capable of effectively preventing freezing while minimizing the amount of dripping water by controlling the flow rate of the fluid gradually as the freezing temperature of the fluid approaches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition according to the automatic dripping device for preventing freezing and bursting of the present invention it is provided with an on off valve coupling part a rotation drive part a heat supply part and an on off valve warming part that perform specific roles thereby preventing the occurrence of malfunction of the on off valve due to a sharp drop in temperature during operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the automatic dripping device 100 for freezing prevention according to the present embodiment may open and close the on off valve 140 by a specific angle according to the temperature data obtained from the temperature detector 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this case according to the present embodiment the on off valve driving unit 150 is operated according to the temperature data obtained from the temperature detection unit 120 to open or block the on off valve 140 and the on off valve 140 the flow rate of the fluid can be controlled to increase gradually as the freezing temperature of the fluid approaches thereby minimizing the amount of dripping water and effectively preventing freezing at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "the power supply unit 170 may provide power stored therein to the temperature detection unit 120 the control unit 130 and the opening closing valve driving unit when the power supplied from the outside to the automatic dripping device 100 for preventing freezing is cut off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "and an automatic dripping device for preventing freezing that can transmit state data of the on off valve drive unit 150 to an operator through a wireless communication module 173 and control the on off valve drive unit 150 according to a control signal received from the operator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "is possible and such variations fall within the protection scope of the present invention.10 piping entering the object to be frozen or bursting or piping exiting from the object 20 external power 100 automatic dripping device for freezing prevention 110 body part 111 opening and closing lid 112 power indicator lamp 113 operation indicator lamp 114 storage space 120 temperature detection unit 130 control unit 131 external power input terminal 132 transformer 133 relay 140 on off valve 150 on off valve driving unit 150e emergency operation button 151 opening and closing valve coupling pa