pening the automatic discharge valve 50 when the temperature is reached by setting the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356118-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention is to actively solve all the problems that the conventional ground water upper protection hole contained and when the temperature of the water passing through the water pipe reaches a set temperature the automatic discharge valve is opened to open the water inside the water pipe it is an object of the present invention to prevent the freezing of the water pipe in advance by discharging it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356118-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "by discharging to prevent the freezing of the water pipe 20 in advance as well as the characteristic of the continuous water supply is made without interruption"}, {"pat_id": "US-6338364-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "as additional ice forms between the plug and the closed valve the ice runs out of room to expand thus causing the pipe to burst at it weakest point"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in colder environments existing exterior collection and storage tanks may crack or break when the temperature drops below freezing and the water in the tank turns to ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the microprocessor monitors the water temperature in storage tank and the temperature of the heat sink and activates the solar circulation pump to cause the heat sink to deliver heat to the storage tank when the possibility of freezing exists in order to delay the need to dump water from the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "if at step 116 the program determines that the water utilization system is calling for water then the program follows the yes branch to step 124 where the pump is activated and the water in the current storage tank is directed by means of the diverter valve to the primary outlet and therefore to the water utilization system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an automatic liquid flow control unit adapted to be attached to a liquid line to enable liquid to trickle therethrough in order to avoid liquid freeze up said unit comprising a rigid conduit means having an inlet including threaded fastening means for attaching said inlet to said liquid line an electrical conduit a solenoid actuated pilot valve mounted to said conduit means downstream of said inlet and being in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough said valve including an electric solenoid connected to said electric circuit to be actuable to open said valve to a predetermined trickling mode wherein liquid trickles through said conduit means and temperature sensitive switch means mounted against an outer surface of said conduit upstream of said valve and downstream of said fastening means and arranged for sensing the temperature of said outer surface and being electrically connected to said electrical conduit and said solenoid for actuating said solenoid to open said valve to said liquid trickling mode in response to the sensed temperature approaching the freezing temperature of the liquid said valve including a manual bleed valve means for actuating said pilot valve independently of said temperature sensitive switch means to establish a flow rate greater than said trickling mode"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "an automatic liquid flow control unit adapted to be attached to an externally threaded spigot to enable liquid to trickle therethrough in order to avoid liquid freeze up said unit comprising rigid conduit means having a horizontal portion and an upwardly inclined inlet portion which includes internally threaded fastening means for attaching said inlet to said externally threaded spigot an electric circuit a solenoid actuated pilot valve mounted to said horizontal portion of said conduit means downstream of said inlet and being in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough said valve including an electric solenoid connected to said electric circuit to be actuable to open said valve to a predetermined trickling mode wherein liquid trickles through said conduit means and temperature sensitive switch means mounted against an outer surface of said horizontal portion of said conduit upstream of said valve for sensing the temperature of said outer surface and being electrically connected to said electrical circuit and said solenoid for actuating said solenoid to open said valve to said liquid trickling mode in response to the sensed temperature approaching the freezing temperature of the liquid said valve including manual bleed valve means for actuating said pilot valve independently of said temperature sensing switch means to establish a flow rate greater than said trickling mode"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in many dwellings especially those without basements there is no interior shut off valve within the dwelling to prevent such bursting"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "furthermore each of those devices are actuated in response to ambient air temperature and thus will serve to trickle water when the air temperature is near the freezing temperature of water even though the temperature of the water in the conduit may be at a higher temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a solenoid actuated valve is mounted to the conduit downstream of the inlet and is in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "since the actuation of the unit depends upon the water temperature within the conduit the unit will only operate to trickle water when there exists a real danger that freezing may occur thus minimizing water waste"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302629-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it is about a water meter to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302629-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "thus the present invention is devised to solve the conventional problems as described above the purpose is to reduce the pressure in the winter when the temperature is lowered in the water flowing into the inside of the meter the pressure according to the expansion of the volume the present invention provides a water meter provided with a buffer unit to absorb naturally thereby preventing freezing of the meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200375794-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "conventionally in order to prevent freezing of the water meter a case covering the outer shell of the water meter is formed and a heating line is built in the case or on one side of the number counter in the water meter for heating while sensing the temperature of water in the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200375794-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "by stopping the heating operation of the heater 5 to heat the heat meter so that the water meter 1 does not freeze to prevent freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the heating system to prevent freezing of the pipe for fire extinguishing water in the tunnel a power control panel for controlling heating power a three phase heating cable installed on the outer circumferential surface along the main pipe drawn out from the power control panel and disposed in the longitudinal direction of the tunnel a power supply wire drawn out from the power control panel and wired in parallel with the main pipe a wire tray installed in parallel with the main pipe and housing the electric power supply wires a single phase heating cable installed in a branch pipe branched from the main pipe and branched from the electric power supply wire to receive heating power and it includes first and second temperature sensors that are disposed on one side of the main pipe and one side of the branch pipe located at the exit or inlet side of the tunnel to obtain first temperature information and second temperature information the power control panel is to control the output of the heating power for each of the three phase heating cable for the three phase heating cable and the single phase heating cable according to the first and second temperature information to prevent freezing of the pipe for fire extinguishing water in the tunnel dual heating system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "dual heating system to prevent freezing of receiving piping"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the problem to be solved by the present invention is a heating system for preventing freezing of pipes for extinguishing water in a tunnel comprising a power control panel for controlling heating power a three phase heating cable installed on the outer circumferential surface along the main pipe drawn out from the power control panel and disposed in the longitudinal direction of the tunnel a power supply wire drawn out from the power control panel and wired in parallel with the main pipe a wire tray installed parallel to the main piping and receiving electric power supply wires a single phase heating cable installed in a branch pipe branched from the main pipe and branched from a power supply wire to receive heating power and first and second temperature sensors arranged on one side of the main pipe and on one side of the branch pipe positioned at the exit or inlet side of the tunnel to obtain first temperature information and second temperature information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition efficient power control is possible by arranging temperature sensors in different main pipes and branch pipes among the pipes of fire extinguishing water in the tunnel to adjust the output according to the temperature information and to selectively increase the output according to the temperature difference.1 is a view showing a state in which an embodiment of the dual heating system for preventing freezing of pipes for fire extinguishing water in a tunnel according to the present invention is applied to a tunnel"}, {"pat_id": "US-10898826-B2", "para_id": "para_773", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump bottom of the container 139 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102480228-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in other words when severe freezing is expected due to a large amount of snowfall or a rapid drop in temperature only salt water which is the original solution is sprayed so that the snow melts or thaws quickly and when the amount of snowfall is less than expected or the temperature is low it is sprayed in a state where a certain amount of water is mixed with salt water which is a stock solution so that sufficient spray can be made while reducing the amount of salt water used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102480228-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "this is to prevent the water stored in the rainwater storage tank 400 from freezing due to a temperature change in the winter season by maintaining a buried state while allowing rainwater to be easily collected"}, {"pat_id": "US-5553637-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the second chamber 31 has a primary inlet 34 connected at 35 to the outlet 11 via the supply line section 13a subjected to freezing temperature i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238623-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a drop in temperature or pressure in the zone may prevent rapid freezing of residual moisture or air itself in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-5059228-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101494087-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "also the lid 120 isolates the space 10 inside the frame 100 to prevent inflow of outside air at a low temperature thereby further lowering the possibility of freezing the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101494087-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "this may be advantageous in preventing freezing of the water meter 320 and the connecting piping"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101494087-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "after the water meter 320 is replaced or the meter reading is completed the operator can remove the meter reading unit 300 from the temporary fixing unit 150 and move the meter reading unit 300 downward to place it on the support unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in doing so pressure relief in the system at a temperature above the freezing point of water generates fluid flow from the well and or pressure tank or other source thereby preventing freeze up"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "when fluid 40 which is typically not water based in chamber 42 reaches a point it will contract as it loses heat and changes phase from a liquid to a solid at the freezing point of the fluid and will cause piston 38 biased open by the spring 44 to retract from seat 34"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "above the freezing point of water will open and allow relatively warmer water from the tank 304 to enter the trough to prevent ice buildup when the air temperature is cool"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the cap which may be self tapping is then threaded in with tool 31 until the o ring 22 contacts the inner walls of the fluid chamber"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2824249-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "by adopting such a structure the connector itself also generates heat so that the t shaped joint can be sufficiently heated and the effect of preventing freezing becomes more remarkable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102428233-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "an object of the present invention as described above is installed in a tunnel to prevent freezing of the fire extinguishing water in the tunnel comprising a water supply unit including a water supply pipe installed in the tunnel heating means mounted along the outer peripheral surface of the water supply pipe an outdoor temperature sensor mounted on one side of the water supply pipe located at the entrance or exit of the tunnel among the water supply pipes to sense the outside temperature a power saving control unit that receives outdoor temperature information corresponding to the outdoor temperature and transmits an output signal for each section corresponding to the received outdoor temperature information and it can be achieved by providing a power saving type tunnel fire extinguishing water freeze prevention device comprising a power controller that receives the transmitted output signal for each section and proportionally outputs the heating power applied to the heating means in response to the received output signal for each section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102428233-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "1 an embodiment of the present invention s energy saving tunnel fire extinguishing water freeze prevention device is installed in the tunnel t to prevent the tunnel fire water freezing and includes a water supply pipe installed in the tunnel"}, {"pat_id": "US-4838039-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "direct contact heat transfer requires less temperature difference between the vaporizing refrigerant and freezing solution than does indirect heat transfer systems to achieve the same energy transfer due to the elimination of the heat exchanger surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101627819-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent freezing clothes cloths clothes etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water valve for preventing freezing of a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe by discharging water little by little as the stem holder operates and a waterway is partially opened when the temperature is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in the case of a water valve located outdoors it is difficult to use the water pipe or the tap water inside the water valve due to the freezing temperature in winter and the volume expansion of the frozen tap water causes the water pipe or the connection parts of the water pipe to deteriorate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of tap water conventionally a method of warming the water valve and the water pipe by wrapping the surroundings of the water valve and the water pipe with a heat insulating material has been most widely used but the effect is insufficient when the temperature drops significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition a method of preventing freezing and bursting due to a decrease in temperature in winter has been disclosed by winding a heating wire spirally around a water valve or water pipe applying power thereto and maintaining the water valve or water pipe at a constant temperature due to heat generated from the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200315853-Y1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "in this embodiment the band heaters 80 and 81 are attached to the drain holes 43 and 83 so that the water is automatically heated to prevent freezing when the water is cold below a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101528163-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this water meter is exposed to the outside for easy access to check the amount of water meter so when the outside temperature goes down to freezing in winter the water meter breaks down due to the frozen wave and sometimes the function is lost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "therefore when the temperature drops such as in the winter when the inside of the valve body is closed by the opening closing ball the remaining water inside the flow path freezes and the volume of ice expands causing a problem that inevitably causes freezing and rupture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "therefore when the temperature drops such as in the winter freezing due to residual water inside the flow path is inevitable and when freezing occurs the entire water angle valve must be replaced which inevitably results in excessive costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100422855-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it is possible to prevent corrosion of various parts constituting the boiler or causing environmental pollution by acidic condensate and to prevent freezing of condensate storage container in winter and to prevent back pressure or excessive condensate figure of the evacuation chamber formed separately from the water discharge chamber at the time of occurrence to the invention so as to automatically discharged through the hole to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the air nozzle 20 is provided integrally with the injection pipe 21 and at the same time one or more are fixed so that the supplied air is sprayed so that water can circulate in the storage tank 80 and at the end of the injection pipe 21 a fitting 22 is provided so that one touch coupling with the air supply hose 23 is possible and the fitting 22 is installed on the side surface 12 of the main body 10 and the inner receiving space of the main body 10 11 is filled with ant