 determination unit determines that the detected temperature and humidity exceed the set value the control unit 70 may a cover for preventing freezing of a water meter characterized in that it transmits an alarm signal or text message to the meter manager s mobile phone 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091015-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the freeze prevention device for a water meter attached to the side of the water meter to prevent freezing of the water meter a first body having a fastening guide groove formed on one surface a heating element inserted into a heating element insertion groove formed on one surface of the first body a second body in which a fastening guide protrusion formed on one surface is inserted into the fastening guide groove to be combined with one surface of the first body and the other surface is in contact with the outer peripheral surface of the water meter a waterproof gasket disposed on the outer side of the heating element insertion groove and formed in a rectangular ring shape rechargeable battery pack for supplying dc power to the heating element a failure display unit that is connected to the heating element or a power line that provides power to the heating element and is disposed outside the freeze prevention device for the water meter to indicate whether the heating element has failed and it includes an operation switching module for measuring the temperature of the outside air automatically switching the operation of the heating element according to the measured temperature value and adjusting the power supply amount from the rechargeable battery pack to the heating element according to the temperature value the second body a square shaped waterproof gasket insertion groove into which the waterproof gasket is inserted on one surface fixing guide portions formed to protrude on both ends in the longitudinal direction of the second body and it is formed in each of the fixing guide portion and includes a first fixing hole and a second fixing hole to which the fixing portion formed by a spring is fastened the first body inserting a plurality of bolts formed on the other surface of the first body to facilitate replacement of the heating element in a state where the contact surface of the second body water meter is attached to the side surface of the water meter and the fixing part is fastened to surround the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7343863-B2", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "this warms the road surface of the road 30 from the inside and as a result it is possible to prevent snow from accumulating on the road surface and from freezing the road surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302638-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however the conventional water meter protection tube is manufactured by installing a heat insulating material to prevent freezing of water taps and water meters in winter but in the cold districts where the outside temperature is below 20 c the protection tube structure applied with such a heat insulating material structure does not show any effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "a floating frame held on the surface by the buoyant body a stretch bending tube supported on the floating frame and extending to a vertical lower portion and having a lower end positioned close to a bottom surface a pumping unit for pumping up the low level water of the water through the expansion and contraction tube in a state of being installed on the floating frame a battery for supplying power to the pumping unit and low level water jetting means for jetting water pumped by the pumping section a second sensor part for sensing the temperature of the surface layer water is mounted on the floating frame a second sensor part for sensing the temperature of the surface layer water is mounted on the floating frame the floating frame includes a cooling unit installed inside the housing and operated by receiving power from the battery the cooling unit cooling the low level water pumped by the pumping unit a pumping unit and a purge control unit for operating the freezing unit and the heating unit based on the water temperature information transmitted from the first sensor unit and the second sensor unit the freezing portion includes a cold water induction pipe for introducing water cooled by the freezing portion is connected to the cold water induction pipe and the cold water induction pipe is provided with a plurality of cold water nozzles for ejecting water passing through the cold water induction pipe the heating unit includes and a hot water induction pipe extending toward the bottom surface is connected to the bottom surface side of the water heat exchanger for guiding the water heated by the heating unit to the bottom surface side and a plurality of hot water nozzles for spraying water into the water tank a rotating ring for connecting the water circulating device and mixing the water between the water circulating devices the rotating ring being able to rotate and maintain a horizontal state in a state where the expansion and contraction tube of each water circulating device is wrapped a support portion mounted on the expansion and contraction tube and rotatably supporting the rotary ring at a lower portion of the rotary ring a rotating ring driving unit for rotating the rotating ring at a constant speed a circulation line for circulating the rotary ring of the one side water circulation device and the rotary ring of the other side water circulation device and a cutting block circulating along the circulation line while being fixed to the circulation line and dividing the water in front of the circulation line so as to create upflow and downflow wherein the rotary ring is a pulley shaped member having a constant diameter and has an inward gear on its inward face wherein the rotary ring driving section includes an underwater motor fixed to the expansion and bellows pipe and a drive gear fixed to a drive shaft of the underwater motor and meshing with the inward gear the support portion includes a height holding holder fixed to a lower portion of the rotary ring a plurality of support arms fixed to the height holding holder and extending to a bottom surface of the rotary ring and having roller bearings at extension ends thereof and a bearing roller which is mounted on a roller bearing of the rotary ring and contacts the bottom surface of the rotary ring and rolls when the rotary ring rotates in the circulation line horizontal rods extending in a direction orthogonal to the longitudinal direction of the circulation line and having coupling grooves are fixed at predetermined intervals the cutting block is a block shaped member having an upper inclined surface and a lower inclined surface that divides the water in the forward direction of the cutting block into an upper portion and a lower portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "the purging control unit 47 operates the freezing unit 43 and the heating unit 45 on the basis of the temperature information transmitted through the first sensor unit 33 and the second sensor unit 35 determine how many degrees the cooling or heating temperature should be adjusted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302628-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water meter and more particularly when the temperature is lowered in the winter when water introduced into the meter is frozen the buffer member is configured to naturally absorb the pressure due to the expansion of the volume it is about a water meter that prevents the meter from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302628-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "thus the present invention is devised to solve the conventional problems as described above the purpose is to reduce the pressure in the winter when the temperature is lowered in the water flowing into the inside of the meter the pressure according to the expansion of the volume the present invention provides a water meter that is configured to naturally absorb the shock absorbing member to prevent freezing of the meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 by measuring the temperature of the water by the temperature sensor 5 in the water pipe p2 when the temperature is less than the set temperature the inlet valve 7 and the outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time to prevent freezing by circulation of water secondary water purification equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide a secondary water purification apparatus designed to prevent freezing by using a temperature sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "and the flow sensor to prevent the freezing of the filter and the device by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature sensor 5 located in the water pipe p2 below a set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "manufacturing cost and management of secondary water purification equipment designed to prevent freezing by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature of the water is measured without the heat insulator and auxiliary materials such as heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100999749-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "this means through the temperature sensor to automatically adjust the operation of the heating wire to prevent the freezing of the water pipes and sewage pipes it is possible to prevent the freezing and sewage pipes freeze accidentally by the administrator the outside of the ceiling finish panel by attaching a display lamp on the screen it can be checked visually"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101159544-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition as a simple method for preventing freezing the configuration generates heat energy in the water pipe so that the outdoor water pipe does not freeze in winter and is equipped with a temperature sensor in the water pipe to prevent freezing of the water pipe and then detects the temperature in the water pipe all winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101628749-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a steam freezing apparatus for generating steam at a high temperature for melting piping such as a frozen water pipe or a sewer and the pump is driven to reflect the presence of residual water to remove the residual water thereby preventing the pump from being burned due to continuous pump driving at the time of stopping the water supply and reliably preventing the freezing caused by the residual water in winter and a method of controlling the pump drive thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430463-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "conventional water meter is to be installed in the thermal insulation case to prevent freezing in winter but there is a limit to the thermal insulation capacity of the thermal insulation case and if water is left inside the meter it is frozen when the temperature drops so it cannot be completely prevented"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5838066-Y2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a solenoid rod is provided so that it can be pushed out and retracted by a second solenoid coil and a pressure switch mechanism that is activated when the water pressure in the water pressure chamber falls below a specified level is connected to the water pressure chamber through a thin tube thereby injecting water into the freezing prone area of the water pipe at approximately zero temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101861841-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "such a water meter has a protective box due to a problem of breakage or freezing due to external impact and temperature difference due to the season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101756200-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the communication check module 71 pumps a certain percentage of water into the tank in the morning lunch evening so as to block the number of steps during the rf network check time and the communication check module 71 is used to prevent freezing of the winter water pipe the temperature sensor s39 is attached to the groundwater protecting apparatus 2 and the temperature is lower than the temperature set by the temperature detecting module 73 the motor is repeatedly operated at a predetermined time interval to forcibly start the water and the water in the water pipe is moved the power check module 72 allows the surveillance camera s34 to photograph the monitoring camera s34 only at the moment when the guard means 25 is opened and closed in the groundwater monitoring system and the leakage check module 75 detects the leakage of the water from the occlusion portion 222 it is possible to check the leakage by comparing the sound at the normal time and the sound with the sound sensor in the event of leakage and the leakage position of the water pipe through the pressure sensor of the pipe can be grasped when water is reduced to a certain level or less through a level sensor using an angle sensor at a time when water below a fixed value is used in order to estimate the water leakage of the water supply pipe using a specific time in order to check water shortage phenomenon when water is depleted data is collected by dividing the water depletion time and recovery time by using an electrode and if the motor is not operated for a certain period of time the controller 3 controls the reservoir 4 to charge the reservoir 4 with a certain amount of chlorine so that the management server 7 installs an electrode at a specific point on the end of the reservoir tank accumulate along the curve points"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100896597-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the circulation pump 23 is installed to be discharged to the cooler inner cylinder 22 to be circulated again and the bottom of the cooler inner cylinder 22 senses the cooling temperature of the coolant to be cooled and unnecessarily compresses the compressor on the freezing cycle 30 it is preferable that the temperature sensor 21 is installed to prevent the lamp from operating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722480-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "recently in order to prevent the water meter from freezing due to a sudden drop in temperature the internal air is directly inserted into the water meter storage box 100 or the water meter protection tube 200 so that external air is directly connected to the water meter 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101285291-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time the filtration filter device is wrapped through the outer space of the filter case so as to be discharged through the nozzle hole of the cap coupled to the rear end of the filter case is filtered through the inner space without freezing in the winter season the first heating coil may be further controlled by a controller to selectively generate heat periodically for a predetermined time depending on the surface temperature of the filter case"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the water supply control device of claim 1 wherein further comprising a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value wireless automatic water level control system further comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "water supply control device according to an additional aspect of the present invention further comprises a temperature sensor for sensing the outside temperature the pump control unit is the freezing wave to prevent the freezing of the water supply pipe by intermittently driving the pump when the outside temperature detected by the temperature sensor is less than the reference value it further comprises a prevention drive"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "that is when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270 the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 in the water supply line by installing a temperature sensor electrically connected to the control unit in the winter when the temperature of the water passing through the water supply line falls below a certain temperature by sending a signal to the control unit causes the control unit is installed at one end of the water supply line and the control unit and by operating the electrically connected circulation pump the water supply circulating in the water supply line characterized in that to prevent the freezing of the water supply line due to the freezing of the water flowing in the water supply line in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "another object of the present invention is to install a temperature sensor in the water supply line to detect when the temperature of the water flowing in the water supply line falls below an appropriate temperature to operate the circulation pump installed at one end of the water supply line thereby operating the water in the water supply line the purpose is to provide a drinking fountain that circulates to prevent freezing of the water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition in the water supply line by installing a temperature sensor electrically connected to the control unit in the winter when the temperature of the water passing through the water supply line falls below a certain temperature by sending a signal to the control unit to be installed at one end of the water supply line by operating the circulation pump electrically connected to the control unit the water inside the water supply line is circulated to prevent freezing of the water supply line due to freezing of water flowing in the water supply line during the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "by sending a signal to the circulation pump 90 is operated to prevent the freezing of the water supply line 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "when the water flowing in the water supply line 20 falls below a predetermined temperature the control unit 40 by receiving a signal from the water in the water supply line 20 is to circulate by preventing the freezing of the water supply line 20 due to the freezing of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "by circulating the water in the water supply line by as well as saving water as well as the effect of freezing prevention at the same time the operation of the present invention with reference to the accompanying drawings as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080704-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080704-A", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "therefore t2 t1 ef is the freezing point depression t1 ef t1 is the driving force needed in conducting the multiple phase transformation t3 t2 is the temperature differential needed to accomplish the desired heat coupling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200335080-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however the conventional water meter protection tube is manufactured by installing a heat insulating material to prevent freezing of water taps and water meters in winter but in the cold districts where the outside air temperature is below 20 c there is a problem that the protection tube structure using such a heat insulating material does not show any effect"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the system comprises a water pipe including a water stop valve a pipe connected with the water pipe through a first electromagnetic valve and a second electromagnetic valve the system allowing the first valve to close temporarily while said second valve is held open in order to drain water from the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as the ambient temperature has dropped to about 5 c or below the first valve is heated by a heater in which it is housed thereby preventing its freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200360698-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however since the temperature difference between the ground and the atmosphere is not large and the protective casing 104 is installed close to the ground the temperature inside the protective casing 104 and the temperature of the atmosphere become similar resulting in a problem of freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200360698-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the heat absorbing plate 6 is in contact with the lower portion of the meter 10 to transmit the geothermal heat transmitted by the heat pipe 5 to the meter 10 to prevent freezing of the meter 10.as described above according to the present invention it is possible to prevent the freezing of the meter by preventing the temperature drop of the meter by using geothermal heat at the bottom of the ground and it is not necessary to use a separate heat insulator and thermal insulation material to secure the space inside the protection tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an apparatus for preventing the water in a water supply pipe upstream of the apparatus from freezing comprising sample chamber means filled with water and exposed to the environment the water in said sample chamber means freezing when the environmental temperature goes below freezing drain means for receiving water from the water supply pipe in one portion thereof and for discharging it to the environment from another portion thereof means closing off said drain means when the water in said sample chamber means is not frozen piston like means for operating on said closing means to open said drain means in response to the water in said sample chamber means freezing means delivering water from the water supply pipe to said drain means when said drain means is open said delivery means including a holding tank means having said drain means and said closing means located therein thermal isolating means including a first heat sink between said holding tank means and said sample chamber means wherein said piston like operating means extends through said thermal isolating means between said sample chamber means and said holding tank wherein in operation the lower end of the piston moves within said sample chamber means in response to the water therein freezing which in turn forces the upper end of the piston against said closing means thereby opening said drain means wherein a flow of water through the water supply pipe and out said drain means to the environment is maintained as long as the water in said sample chamber means is frozen such a water flow tending to prevent water in the water supply pipe upstream of the apparatus from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "water in the holding tank as well as water from the water supply system moving through connecting pipe 17 hose 23 and channel 26 in filler tube 24 flows into the common opening 30 in the pedestal drain element and then out drain pipe 31 thus maintaining a flow of water in the water supply system upstream of the apparatus preventing freezing of the water in the upstream portion of the system thereby"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "as the ambient temperature rises slightly above freezing the ice in the apparatus begins to melt however it does not melt immediately thereby shutting off the drain opening 30"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "the lower end of the exterior thaw tube 32 thus thaws quickly and also freezes quickly which provides a fast refreezing of the apparatus and reopening of the drain opening 30 should the ambient temperature after only a short period of thaw again go below freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430524-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "therefore the object of the present invention is to provide a self heating function to maintain the water meter main body at a certain temperature even in winter to prevent frost condensation or condensation on the outside surface of the water meter main body in winter in particular it is to provide a water coil built in water meter to prevent winter freezing accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430524-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "thus in the electrothermal coil built in water meter 1 according to the present invention is supplied with power from the battery 501 installed in the battery installation 50 in order to prevent the occurrence of freezing accidents in the winter when the cold wave continues as described above by inserting the heat generating means 20 into the heat generating means built in box 30 to be mounted on the lower surface of the water meter body 10 to maintain the water meter body 10 above a certain temperature to prevent freezing accidents in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430524-Y1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "thus frost or condensation forms on the outer surface of the water meter main body 10 due to cold weather in winter simply and easily without waste of unnecessary resources"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100942717-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "insulation material 10ac is filled in the separation space formed between the first plate 10aa and the second plate 10ab can be used in the form of urethane the winter of the water tank 10 by the temperature drop outside such as it prevents freezing of rainwater stored inside to prevent the collection tank 10 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200398138-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "as the drainage hole penetrated to the outside is opened the drinking water remaining inside the barrel is discharged to the outside to prevent freezing of the tap water due to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0139294-Y1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "at this time the gas refrigerant gas condensed while passing through the condenser 80 is phase reduced into a high pressure liquid refrigerant gas at a temperature slightly higher than room temperature which is the ambient temperature of the cold hot water purifier and decompressed by passing through a capillary tube not shown"}, {"pat_id": "US-10422112-B2", "para_id": "para_230", "text": "in these cases while the apparatus 10 functions to produce water ice the refrigerating fluid coming from the condenser 310 is deviated into the second condenser 321 so as to heat the vector fluid in the storage tank 328"}, {"pat_id": "US-5318059-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the water temperature within certain pipes within the dwelling may fall below freezing despite the use of a temperature sensitive valve unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5318059-A", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "as noted earlier even in moderate climates the outside temperature may occasionally be expected to fall below freezing whereby water at the outside faucet might freeze thereby presenting the risk of a pipe burst which can produce damage to the pipe and dwelling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102320839-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the prior art provides a freeze prevention heating system for a water meter box using a carbon fiber heating element to prevent freezing of a water pipe and a water meter and is an effective technology to prevent freezing because the heat generation time is preserved for a long time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102320839-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "according to the present invention consisting of the above described configuration the temperature sensor or the timer sensor accurately grasps the external temperature situation and fundamentally blocks the freezing of the water supply pipe by operating the heating wire built into the water supply pipe and the heating wire as it operates based on the renewable energy produced by solar panels it not only has an excellent level of energy efficiency but also has the effect of contributing to nature conservation as a nature friendly technology"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102320839-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "above all in the present invention freezing is actively prevented due to the operation of the heating wire installed in the water pipe and in particular the heating wire utilizes the electric power charged from the solar panel to reduce operating costs and a temperature sensor and a timing sensor it should be noted that as various convenient functions are additionally provided based on the control unit etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_813", "text": "fourth regarding the detailed explanation of low temperature use although it can be used at temperatures down to 10 care must be taken to prevent solidification or freezing of moisture in the drain 301 and if freezing is a concern use it by installing an air dryer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404540-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the installation work of the heating wire w is performed by winding the heating wire w around the water pipe t and the water meter m and applying power from the power supply unit p the generated heat source can maintain the water pipe t and the water meter m at a constant temperature to prevent the water meter m from freezing due to a decrease in temperature during the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404540-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "when there is a risk of freezing of the water meter m due to a drop in winter temperature and a rapid drop in the temperature of the tap water the temperature of the heating wire w can be detected from the temperature information detected by the temperature sensor 100 and the flow rate information detected by the flow sensor 200 or not"}, {"pat_id": "US-7497228-B2", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "because the temperature control valve measured a higher temperature it would remain closed and not allow warmer water from below ground to replace the freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387977-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the wastewater treatment apparatus using the underwater micro generator generator to prevent the drug and the air is sucked together in the drug suction pipe to prevent the drug remaining in the drug suction pipe and to simultaneously effect the stirring and flotation separation of the drug a first level sensor for sensing the level of the medicine drug storage unit for storing the drug a medicine pump for allowing the medicine storage unit to suck the medicine into the medicine suction pipe a protective box protecting the medicine and the medicine storage unit a heater located inside the protective box for preventing freezing of the protective box a temperature sensor controlling the operation of the heater a reaction flotation tank for causing a reaction by mixing the chemicals with the wastewater collec