ted to the sprinkler water supply pipe and has a partition 201 having an outer diameter smaller than the inner diameter of the body 1 the outer peripheral surface of the partition 201 to seal the upper end of the body 1 a water pipe coupling part 2 having an upper plate 202 having a predetermined thickness and coupled to an upper end of the body 1 a fire valve 3 received below the upper plate 202 between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 a fire prevention shape memory alloy spring 21 coupled to the lower side of the upper plate 202 and accommodated between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 and coupled to the fire valve 3 a freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 having an upper end coupled to the partition 201 a stopper 221 coupled to a lower end of the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring 22 it is coupled to the lower end of the body 1 to receive the stopper 221 the top is open and comprises a freeze proof coupling body 4 having a water discharge pipe 401 at the bottom the lower end of the body 1 is formed with a freeze protection hole 102 at room temperature through the fire valve 3 and the stopper 221 to form a sealed structure the fire proof shape memory alloy spring 21 is predetermined the water is injected through the water injection port 101 by compressing at the fire temperature of the fire valve 3 and the freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 is tensioned at a predetermined freezing temperature to freeze proof hole 102 and it provides a sprinkler with a freeze protection structure characterized in that the water flows through the water discharge pipe 401"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102064947-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a sprinkler comprising a body 1 having a cylindrical shape and having an open top and having at least one water jet 101 on a side surface thereof it is connected to the sprinkler water supply pipe and has a partition 201 having an outer diameter smaller than the inner diameter of the body 1 the outer peripheral surface of the partition 201 to seal the upper end of the body 1 a water pipe coupling part 2 having an upper plate 202 having a predetermined thickness and coupled to an upper end of the body 1 a fire valve 3 received below the upper plate 202 between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 a fire prevention shape memory alloy spring 21 coupled to the lower side of the upper plate 202 and accommodated between the inner circumferential surface of the body 1 and the outer circumferential surface of the partition wall 201 and coupled to the fire valve 3 it is coupled to the lower end of the body 1 the freeze proof coupling body 4 having an upper portion and a water discharge pipe 401 in the lower portion a freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 coupled to one side of the freeze proof coupling body 4 a stopper 221 accommodated inside the freeze protection assembly 4 and coupled to the freeze protection shape memory alloy spring 22 the lower end of the body 1 is formed with a freeze protection hole 102 at room temperature through the fire valve 3 and the stopper 221 to form a sealed structure the fire proof shape memory alloy spring 21 is predetermined the water is injected through the water injection port 101 by being compressed at the fire temperature of the fire valve 3 and the freeze proof shape memory alloy spring 22 is compressed at a predetermined freezing temperature to freeze proof hole 102 and water can flow through the water discharge pipe 401"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7151025-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after reacting for 0 hours the reacted reaction solution enters the filter cylinder 122 through the discharge pipe 115 and is filtered and washed with deionized water in order to obtain modified chitosan among them the ratio of the amount of glutamic acid dimethyl sulfoxide and concentrated sulfuric acid used is 1 g 10 0 ml 0.25 0.3 ml and the mass ratio of chitosan and glutamic acid is 2 1 step and step 2 using the drive mechanism 3 the modified chitosan prepared in step 1 is put into the electroplating wastewater in the stirring reaction chamber 2 through the material outlet 1222 and p h is adjusted to 2 to 8 the temperature in the stirring reaction chamber 2 is adjusted to 10 to 50 c by the heating tube 27 and at the same time the stirring rod 21 is rotated to 120 to 150 rpm by the driving mechanism 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200190678-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "conventionally in order to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes in an apartment water tanker or a water meter protection container many schiropols are built in the water meter and water pipes to prevent freezing in cold weather or cold regions falling below a certain temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11095960-B2", "para_id": "para_107", "text": "55 degrees fahrenheit to maintain the internal water lines from suffering from freezing pipe conditions that can result in a burst pipe s"}, {"pat_id": "US-11095960-B2", "para_id": "para_128", "text": "furthermore be communicating with a home router the water meter and leak detection system 10 126 200 can communicate with intelligent thermostats sending a signal to turn on the residential or corporation heat to a temperature that will inhibit freezing water in the residential and corporation interior water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240028-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "another important aspect of the bi metallic disk is that after the predetermined temperature of for example 36 has been reached and the disk has warped to break the electrical contact of the switch the disk will maintain the warped shape until manually re set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "the heater 16 then raises the temperature in the water tank 10 under the control of the controller 64 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100328970-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the outer circumferential surface of the hopper tank 101 the apparatus for discharging the contaminants characterized in that the constant temperature wire coil 111 is attached to prevent freezing of the contaminants in the hopper tank 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100328970-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the circumferential surface of the hopper tank is characterized in that a constant temperature wire coil is attached to prevent freezing of the contaminants in the hopper tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100751233-B1", "para_id": "para_108", "text": "when the temperature is below the set temperature it is repeated periodically for a predetermined period of time to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101239253-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "on the other hand the conventional water meter is a method to prevent the freezing in winter when the temperature is low and when the inside of the outer shell is frozen the bottom of the counter and the impeller housing are designed to relieve the expansion pressure in order to prevent the freezing of the device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102561600-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition a sensor for detecting the internal temperature of the hydrant and a heating wire for supplying heat are provided inside the hydrant housing to keep the inside of the hydrant warm thereby exhibiting an advantageous effect of protecting the hydrant from freezing in winter.1 is a view of a replacement process of an antifreeze hydrant according to the prior art 2 and 3 are views of an automatic heating antifreeze hydrant according to an embodiment of the present invention 4 and 5 show only some configurations to show the operating principle of the automatic heating antifreeze hydrant according to the present invention figure 6 is an internal heating component using a hot wire of the antifreeze hydrant according to the present invention 7 is a coupling structure of the lower end of the middle pipe which is a part of the antifreeze hydrant according to the present invention 8 and 9 are the coupling structure of the upper end of the intermediate pipe which is a part of the non freezing hydrant according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102561600-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in the present invention a heating wire is disposed inside the housing to supply heat in order to prevent freezing before water supply during a cold wave in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385568-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in this case in the case of groundwater after the operation of the temperature sensor 80 that detects the freezing temperature due to the characteristics of the groundwater the water temperature 0 or more it is preferable to have a timer to stop the continuous operation"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3706683-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0064 5 the first second and third short wire cords are power cords but instead the first second and third short wire cords themselves are self temperature controlled tropics t since the shape joint can be heated sufficiently by the connector itself the effect of preventing freezing becomes more remarkable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430457-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the conventional technique is to install a heating wire in the shape of caps on the outside of the water meter and to arrange a sensor to heat it when the temperature is below a certain temperature to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "internal temperature sensing means for sensing the internal temperature cold water temperature sensing means for sensing the cold water temperature of the cold water tank the internal temperature detected by the internal temperature sensing means and the cold water temperature detected by the cold water temperature sensing means the four way valve for controlling the four way valve to prevent the freezing of the cold water tank by changing the flow path through which the refrigerant is circulated according to the control of the control means and the control means for controlling the overall operation by determining whether the cold water tank is frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "under the control of the drive means and the control means the temperature of the cold water tank is raised to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "however in this conventional method since the refrigerant circulates only according to the freezing cycle for cooling the purified water when the indoor temperature especially in winter of the product installation place is low and the freezing point or the cold water temperature is a freezing condition there is a problem that the cold water tank is frozen the user can not take the purified water as well as reduce the reliability of the product"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the present invention has been made to solve the above problems an object of the present invention is to determine the freezing of the cold water tank according to the changing product internal temperature and cold water temperature to determine the freezing of the cold water tank even in the winter at low room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "four way valve driving means for driving control of the four way valve to prevent freezing of the cold water tank it is characterized in that the compressor driving means for controlling the drive to increase the temperature of the cold water tank according to the control to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "accordingly in the evaporation tube 43 when the low temperature low pressure free refrigerant depressurized in the capillary tube 125 evaporates while passing through several pipes the purified water in the cold water tank 7 is cooled and evaporated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "the control means 110 determines whether the cold water temperature tc detected by the cold water temperature detecting means 112 is equal to or lower than the cold water setting temperature tcs set by the temperature setting switch 105 and thus the cold water temperature tc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "in the case of the occurrence condition since the cold water temperature tc falls gradually in step s16 the cold water temperature tc that is lowered is sensed by the cold water temperature detecting means 112 and the detected cold water temperature tc is transmitted to the control means 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "therefore in step s18 the internal temperature tr sensed by the internal temperature detecting means 116 is set in the control means 110 and the internal temperature trs the inside of the product where the freezing phenomenon occurs in the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "as a result of the determination in step s18 when the internal temperature tr is not equal to or below the freezing internal temperature trs no the indoor temperature where the cold hot water purifier is installed and the cold water temperature tc of the cold water tank 7 are the normal temperature condition illuminator returns to the step s15 and repeats the operation of the step s15 or less"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "on the other hand when the determination result in the step s18 when the internal temperature tr is less than the internal temperature trs of the freezing generation yes it is determined that the cold water tank 7 is frozen and the flow advances to step s19 to control means 110 outputs a control signal for controlling the four way valve 123 to the four way valve driving means 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_99", "text": "if tc is not equal to or higher than the cold water set temperature tcs no it is determined that the freezing of the cold water tank 7 is not completely removed and the flow returns to the step s21 where the fan motor under the compressor 35 while driving 39 the operation of step s21 and below is repeated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "as a result of the discrimination in step s23 when the cold water temperature tc is equal to or higher than the cold water set temperature tcs yes it is determined that the freezing of the cold water tank 97 is completely removed and the flow advances to step s24 to control means 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "as a result of the determination in step s16 when the cold water temperature tc is equal to or lower than the freezing generation temperature tcd yes it is determined that the cold water tank 7 is frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "it is possible to take cold water at a desired temperature under any temperature condition and have an excellent effect of satisfying a user s reliability of a product"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101290447-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the freeze prevention water meter equipped with a conventional airbag configured as described above is the airbag absorbs the freezing expansion force of the tap water introduced into the shaft of the impeller and the fine gap on the upper side of the airbag housing when freezing of tap water occurs due to the temperature drop in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101290447-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "if it is carried out if the freeze expansive force of the tap water is generated by the fall of the ambient temperature in the winter it is easily delivered to the airbag 430 through the freeze expansion force inlet 11 and is absorbed to prevent freezing damage of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194148-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "edo has the effect of preventing the freezing of the chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194148-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "if the temperature is lowered the outdoor temperature may not directly affect the water tank thus delaying the freezing time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a closed cylinder portion 100 coupled to the lower side of the groundwater protection part a piezoelectric tube 210 installed at one side to prevent the groundwater from expanding due to internal pressure generated when the groundwater rises is coupled to one side of the piezoelectric pipe the other side is coupled to the plate check valve sand filter 220 for filtering the sand contained in the groundwater plate check valve 230 is coupled to one side of the sand filter the other side is coupled to the meter to prevent the groundwater filtered by the sand filter backflow a meter 240 coupled to one side of the plate check valve and the other side coupled to a pressure gauge a pressure gauge 250 coupled to one side of the meter and coupled to a three way valve on the other side a three way valve 260 coupled to the pressure gauge to form a flow path in the direction of the emergency water supply pipe 600 or the water supply pipe 700 an underground water level protection hole 200 including an underground water level protection column 270 formed along an inner circumference to prevent freezing waves it is configured to include and the controller 500 for supplying power to the underground water protection unit if the temperature is below the set temperature the controller 500 a temperature sensor 510 for detecting the ambient temperature a temperature setting unit 520 for setting a reference temperature for supplying power to the ground water protection protection vessel a memory unit 530 for storing the reference temperature set by the temperature setting unit a power supply unit 540 for supplying power to the ground water protection protection line a temperature comparison unit 550 for comparing the temperature sensed by the temperature sensor with the reference temperature stored in the memory unit a power supply signal transmitter 560 for transmitting a power supply signal to a power supply unit when the temperature compared by the temperature comparison unit is less than a reference temperature freezing prevention comprising a central control unit 570 for controlling the signal flow between the temperature sensor the temperature setting unit the memory unit the power supply unit the temperature comparison unit the power supply signal transmission unit and groundwater upper protection device capable of underwater discharge sterilization treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition by installing a heating wire to prevent freezing waves in the underground water protection unit and by configuring a controller to supply power according to the temperature it is possible to automatically control according to temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "in addition by installing a heating wire to prevent freezing waves in the underground water protection unit and by configuring a controller to supply power according to the temperature it is possible to automatically control according to temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the freezing prevention device which is installed in the piping 2 of water supply and is configured to prevent the freezing of the said piping 2 an installation hole 11 formed at an upper portion thereof a drainage hole 12 formed at a lower portion thereof and a hollow body 10 to which the pipe 2 is fastened to both sides an expansion projection part 20 provided in the installation hole 11 to receive a volume expanding material 3 that expands in volume as the temperature decreases and downwardly protrudes into the main body 10 by the expansion a drain opening and closing part 30 provided to be opened and closed in the drain hole 12 into the main body 10 conversion connection portion 40 for connecting the expansion protrusion 20 and the drainage opening and closing part 30 into the interior of the main body 10 to convert the downward projection of the expansion projection 20 to the upward movement of the drainage opening and closing part 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "preventing freezing by flowing tap water as described above is a waste of tap water is generated badly because the water must continue to flow while the temperature is falling there is a problem that the inconvenience to use by always operating the valve manually"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in order to solve the above problems a heating freeze protection device has been proposed which installs a separate heater around the valve and the pipe to prevent freezing by heating the pipe when the ambient temperature drops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101214677-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "such a conventional water meter as the tap water in the lower and upper casing is frozen due to the outside temperature dropped below freezing in the protective container during the winter the meter reading unit embedded in the lower and upper casing is frozen and broken so that the water meter is replaced or there was a problem such as not only to bear the economic burden of the repair but also to suffer the inconvenience"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101214677-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the second support 250 may not only prevent the water meter 10 itself from freezing or freezing due to winter outdoor temperature but also may be made of transparent glass so that the number of the display unit 220 can be easily read"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101214677-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "therefore when using the freeze delay water meter 10 according to the present invention the double window by the vacuum cap 240 the first support 230 and the second support 240 the vacuum space 243 is formed therein the effect is that even if the temperature of the outside air in winter is lowered it is possible to prevent the tap water from freezing in advance or delay the freezing rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in the case of a freeze prevention module equipped with such a temperature type automatic valve the temperature is measured to prevent freezing through heat transfer but if the module is exposed to sub zero weather for a long time abnormal operation may be executed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200452318-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the heating element is a planar or linear heating element.the present invention for achieving the above object the heat insulating material is installed inside the cover of the tap water meter box having a check hole the heating element is installed inside the heat insulating material the temperature sensor is installed on the heating element to sense the current temperature and characterized in that it comprises a height adjustment port for adjusting the installation height of the heating element.the present invention as described above has the effect of preventing the freezing in winter by removing the cover of the existing water metering box and installing a cover having a heating element and heat insulator or installing a water metering device box in which the heating element is installed on one side of the inner side in the new building in addition even when installed in the ground by applying power to the heating element to generate heat there is an effect that can prevent the freezing of the water supply meter box from the freezing in winter.1 is a view showing a first embodiment of the present invention 2 is an enlarged view of the heating element of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200452318-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "since it is applied heat is generated from the heating element 6 to prevent freezing of the meter and the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102061131-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the metal heater 110 is installed to be in contact with the pipe 10 under the heat insulating material 11 surrounding the pipe 10 and supplies power to the metal heater 110 to generate heat to prevent freezing of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102061131-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when an operation command of the heater 110 is issued the metal heater controller 130 supplies power to the metal heater 110 based on this and the metal heater 110 generates heat to prevent freezing of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200371082-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in other words the heat insulating material 6 is simply configured to be inserted into the inner wall surface of the protective container 2 so that the meter 3 is inevitably formed between the heat insulating material 6 so in case of severe effects there was a disadvantage in that reliability was greatly reduced.accordingly the present invention is to fundamentally solve the conventional problems as described above when the water meter freezes or freezes in cold weather by protecting the meter to be insulated by using geothermal heat in the ground in a protective container accommodating the water meter the purpose of the present invention is to provide a freezing freeze protection device for water meters to prevent water in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-9238904-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the temperature sensing device detects the temperature of the fluid within the flushing device 100 measuring for freezing conditions and triggers the freeze control valve 710 to open under predetermined temperatures such as freezing condition temperatures to prevent freezing of the fluid within the flushing device 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "by the temperature sensor and the power is supplied to the power storage unit 20 thereby preventing freezing of the main body 1 and the tube 70"}, {"pat_id": "US-8065905-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "where the effective amount is sufficient to reduce an amount of bulk water and or an amount of residual water in the pipeline below desired amounts and to depress a freezing point temperature of the composition to a temperature below an operating temperature of the pipeline where operating temperature is below the freezing point of pure water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8065905-B2", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "a system for use in conditioning and or pressure testing pipelines comprising an aqueous composition comprising an effective amount of a metal ion formate salt where the aqueous composition fills a pipeline or portion thereof where the pipeline or portion thereof is pressurized to a pressure between about 1.25 to about 1.5 times an operating pressure of the pipeline where the effective amount is sufficient to reduce an amount of bulk water and or an amount of residual water in the pipeline below desired amounts and or to depress a freezing point of the aqueous composition to a temperature below an operating temperature of a pipeline to be conditioned or tested where the operating temperature of the pipeline is below the freezing point of pure water and where the aqueous composition is directly discharged into the environment without further processing or treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-8065905-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the present invention relates to a method and a use of an aqueous metal ion formate salt composition for reducing a residual water film on an interior of a pipeline during pipeline dewatering operations which may involve the use of a pig or a plurality of pigs for pipeline pressure testing operations for freezing pointing suppression for sub freezing temperature pipeline testing operations i.e"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5838064-Y2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "conventional water meter cabinets that stand above the ground cannot be expected to have the antifreeze effect of geothermal heat compared to those that are buried above ground so even if the surrounding area is protected with insulation material the insulation material itself cannot be expected to generate heat"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177676-Y1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "when the cover is equipped with the function of sealing and thermal insulation at the same time when the temperature suddenly dropped due to the strength reinforcement by the reinforcement plate 2 or reinforcement core 21 to be purchased during the molding of the lid by external force or impact even if a shock is applied to the protective container 50 or the lid 1 or 20 of the water meter the damage or damage is eliminated and the dripped temperature does not flow into the water meter protector 50 so that the thermal insulation case 51 therein the water meter 52 installed in the thermal insulation case 51 can be freed from freezing.therefore the present invention as described above forms a number of support holes provided with a screw hole at the bottom while inserting a molded reinforcing plate provided with upper and lower reinforcement protrusions or forming a primary molded reinforcing core when manufacturing a lid of a water meter protection container and a screw"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2923642-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "in addition ground laying pipeline 1 by using a power source stored in a battery by a solar cell as a power source 61 for the defrosting function and the anti freezing function it is possible to contribute to energy saving and to be used in for example a mountain area where it is difficult to secure the power source"}, {"pat_id": "US-7043934-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the ice maker can be identical or similar to those used in refrigerator freezers although is should have its own evaporator for freezing purposes and should have an expansion device that controls the temperature levels so that ice making is possible or may be a flake ice maker or other such device as known in the art"}, {"pat_id": "US-12017929-B2", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the following components are installed in the refrigerant circulation loop 4 valves 33 to 37 to reverse refrigerant streams in cooling and heating components 8 and 9 during alternating modes of water freezing and ice melting the temperature control valve 38 to adjust the refrigerant temperature increase or decrease according to the system operating algorithm and valves 39 and 40 to control refrigerant pressure at the inlet and the outlet of the compressor 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0385568 2003.05.15 designated by reservoir control system registered and filed by the present applicant the groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432779-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "by blocking the external cold air double triple to maintain the underground temperature inside the protective casing 1 to prevent the rapid descent to below zero to prevent freezing of the water meter 2"}, {"pat_id": "US-5103653-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for providing a supply of purified ice and a supply of purified liquid water from a source of unpurified liquid water said method comprising the steps of a cooling selected areas of at least one ice forming surface to a temperature below the freezing temperature of water b directing a water stream of the unpurified liquid water over said selected areas to form ice at said selected areas while washing impurities away from the formed ice with said stream c increasing the temperature at said selected areas at various times to remove said ice from said ice forming surface d collecting the ice removed in step c in a bin e warming a portion of said bin at selected times to melt some of the ice therein into purified liquid water f collecting in a container the purified liquid water derived in step e wherein step a includes conducting thermal energy to at least one evaporator passage from said selected areas of said ice forming surface wherein said evaporator passage is part of a continuous refrigerant flow path for refrigerant fluid said flow path including a compressor a condenser a metering device and the evaporator passage wherein step a includes energizing said compressor and wherein said method further comprises the steps of g sensing the amount of collected ice in said bin h sensing the amount of collected purified liquid water in said container i in response to both the amount of said collected ice in said bin exceeding a first predetermined amount and the amount of said collected purified liquid water in said container exceeding a second predetermined amount deenergizing said compressor and j following step i re energizing said compressor whenever either or both of the following occurs 1 the amount of collected ice in said bin falls below the first predetermined amount and 2 the amount of collected purified liquid water in said container falls below the second predetermined amount and wherein step e includes the steps of passing a flow of fluid heated by the ambient environment along the underside of said bin in response to the amount of collected purified water in said container being below the said second predetermined amount and causing said fluid to be cooled by said passing and then conducting said fluid in the cooled condition downward in a convective flow through a conduit to a location having at least a temperature of the ambient environment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145007-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "water remaining inside the floating tube is automatically drained to the outside through the drain hole which prevents the freezing and freezing of water at low temperature in winter because there is no water remaining in the floating tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100245825-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the same members are denoted by the same reference numerals as described above and the heat exchange means is a cylinder in which a certain amount of groundwater is introduced and stored while being buried in the ground at a depth not affected by the freezing depth of the ground that is the temperature of the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101363635-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "7 the control box 50 controls the heating wire 30 for dissipating heat to prevent the water pipe 1 from freezing due to low temperature thereby freezing the water pipe 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266383-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "it prevents water meter from freezing even during the cold winter season and it saves much manpower and time due to reconstruction.when it is used for a long time the protection box is cracked or damaged due to earth pressure or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-8105488-B2", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "submerged combustion heaters or other heat sources may be used to raise water temperature as desired such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4031800-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "however depending on the environmental temperature and fluctuations in the composition of the wastewater even if the operating conditions are the same the icing speed when colliding with the supercooling plate is fast and icing may occur on the supercooling plate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4031800-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the cooling energy required to reduce the pressure to the maximum the load on the supercooled water production heat exchanger increases and the running cost increases can be maintained to prevent clogging freezing in the piping"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101915532-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a fire water supply pipe disposed at a ceiling portion of the room for supplying fire water with sprinklers installed in the ceiling portion a fire fighting water supply unit for supplying fire fighting water to the fire fighting water supply pipe when a fire occurs a temperature measuring unit for measuring temperature values at a plurality of positions of the fire water supply pipe a heating unit disposed inside the fire water supply pipe and heating the inside of the fire water supply pipe according to supply of external power and a temperature value reaching a pre determined freeze thaw temperature is selected and a temperature value reaching the selected freeze thaw temperature is set as a freeze wave expected temperature value and a control unit for heating the heating unit to a heating temperature set by using the heating unit at a position corresponding to the expected value of the freezing wave among a plurality of positions of the heating unit the temperature measuring unit includes and temperature sensors for measuring a temperature value at a plurality of positions of the fire water supply pipe the heating unit includes a guide pipe disposed inside the fire water supply pipe a plurality of heating points formed at a plurality of positions of the guide pipe and a power supply unit for separately supplying power to the plurality of heating points to achieve a heating temperature of each of the plurality of heating points wherein the power supply unit is driven under the control of the control unit the positions of the plurality of heating points are the same as the positions of the temperature sensors the guide pipe may include a hollow tube formed of a flexible tube at the plurality of outer circumferential positions of the guide pipe support rods extending a predetermined length along the outer side are formed at the ends of the support rods rolling members are formed wherein the rolling members are arranged to roll along the inner circumference of the fire water supply pipe at a plurality of inner circumferential positions of the fire water supply pipe wherein a seating groove on which the rolling members are mounted is formed the guide pipe may include and is inserted and moved inside the fire water supply pipe wherein the rolling members are respectively seated in the seating grooves to determine a placement position fire fighting water supply facility with frost protection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "prevents freezing the control unit is further provided with a sticking prevention function when the operation time of the discharge pump is stopped for a specific time or more the discharge pump is operated for a specific time at a specific period to prevent sewage from sticking to the storage tank or the discharge pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in a preferred embodiment of the present invention the control unit is further provided with a temperature sensor for sensing the temperature of the storage tank so that when the temperature of the storage tank is less than a specific temperature the freezing wave for operating the discharge pump for a specific time period predetermined prevention may be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "thus when the temperature of the storage tank 100 is below a certain temperature the freezing prevention function operates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "at this time the temperature sensor 270 is to monitor whether the sewage stored in the storage tank 100 freezes it will be common that the sensing unit is installed in the storage tank 100 and connected to the control unit 250 if necessary the sensing unit may be installed around the outside of the storage tank 100 or provided in a control box provided with a pcb so that the freezing prevention function may operate according to the ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "freeze protection function can achieve the purpose enough to prevent the freezing of the sewage the sewage contains a lot of impurities or foreign matter and storage tank 100 is also mainly installed in places where the temperature does not easily drop even in the winter such as underground therefore it is possible to prevent freeze by flowing sewage with only one minute of operation per hour"}, {"pat_id": "US-6003780-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "while these above described freezeproof valve mechanisms function to permit fountain operation on a year round basis there still exists an ongoing need for further improvements particularly with respect to eliminating undesirable failure modes"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5910493-Y2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "3 the electric heating coil c is connected to a circulation pump p installed in the heating and hot water supply pipe 1 to prevent it from freezing and its manual switch sw"}, {"pat_id": "US-8147117-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the present invention provides a means for mixing drinking water stored in large storage tanks preventing thermal stratification of the water to reduce risk of freezing by generating large mixing bubbles toward the bottom of the tank causing mixing of layers of water in the tank through turbulence created as the bubbles rise through the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4181577-A", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "when initiating the heat pump cycle load must be available in the form of heat to allow refrigerant pressures to build and settle at desire heat pump capacities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045455-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however this method has a problem that can not effectively prevent the decay of the water due to the green algae occurring during the summer and also in the winter to empty the water of the pond to freeze and prevent freezing of the water to become a pond of ugly landscape facilities there is this.the present invention has been made to actively solve the above problems and after pumping ground water 100m underground through a jet pump to maintain an average temperature of 22 in the summer and 12 in the winter the purpose is to provide artificial ecological mooring pond using groundwater geothermal heat that is configured to circulate with the supply to the pond.as a means for achieving the above described technical problem the present invention after forming a core ball groove having a depth of 100m underground through boring work and accommodates a jet pump for supplying water to the inside of the core ball groove and then through the jet pump the discharged water is discharged into the pond through the water supply pipe and the water accumulated in the pond is purified through the uv sterilizer and the filter connected to the purified water pump and the purified water discharge line and then discharged to the external pipe housed inside the protective pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-5013344-A", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a system for providing purified ice and purified water from a source of unpurified water comprising a continuous refrigerant flow path including a compressor an evaporator condenser means and a metering device an ice forming surface means responsive to energization of said compressor for cooling selected areas of said ice forming surface to a temperature below the freezing temperature of water by conducting thermal energy to said evaporator from said selected areas means for issuing a stream of the unpurified water over said selected areas to form ice at said selected areas while washing impurities away from the formed ice with said stream means for increasing the temperature at said selected areas at various times to remove said ice from said ice forming surface a bin for collecting ice removed from said ice forming surface heating means for warming a portion of said bin at selected times to melt some of the ice collected therein into purified liquid water container means for collecting the purified liquid water formed by melting the ice in said bin bin sensor means for sensing the amount of ice collected in said bin container sensor means for sensing the amount of purified liquid water collected in said container control means responsive to both said bin sensor means and said container means for de energizing said compressor when the amount of said collected ice in said bin exceeds a first predetermined amount and when the amount of said collected purified liquid water in said container exceeds a second predetermined amount said control means further including means for reenergizing said compressor in response to either or both of the following conditions 1 the amount of collected ice in said bin falling below the first predetermined amount and 2 the amount of collected purified liquid water in said container falling below the second predetermined amount wherein said condenser means in said refrigerant flow path includes first and second condensers disposed in said respective parallel and alternatively conductive first and second path sections said second condenser being disposed at the underside of said bin to heat collected ice at the bottom of said bin means for utilizing rejected heat from said second condenser to melt ice in said bin at a temperature of approximately 32 f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391660-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "for example in a steam freezing apparatus including a heater for supplying heat a heating pipe coupled to the heater a pump for supplying water a connection pipe for connecting the heating pipe and the pump and a control unit the controller may preheat the heater for a predetermined elapsed time from the start of operation and preheat the connection pipe to the reference temperature when the measured temperature of the connection pipe is lower than a preset reference temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391660-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as another example in a steam freezing apparatus including a heater for supplying heat a heating pipe coupled to the heater a pump for supplying water a connection pipe for connecting the heating pipe and the pump and a control unit when the measured temperature of the heating tube outlet side is lower than a predetermined reference temperature the heater is preheated until the temperature of the heating tube outlet side reaches the reference temperature and when the measured temperature of the connection tube reaches a predetermined reference if the temperature is lower than the temperature the connection pipe may be preheated to the reference temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water freeze prevention device for a water utilizing device that is periodically exposed to water freezing temperatures said water freeze prevention device comprising a first valve for regulating water flow through a first pipe leading from a water inlet device to a water utilization device an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said first valve back and forth between a closed position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and an open position associated with a second mode of operation of said water freeze prevention device a second valve for draining water from a portion of the first pipe located between the first valve and the water utilization device an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said second valve back and forth between an open position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and a closed position associated with a second mode of operation of said water freeze prevention device a third valve for draining water from the water utilization device an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said third valve back and forth between an open position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and a closed position associated with a second mode of operation of said water freeze prevention device temperature setting device for invoking the first mode of operation and the second mode of operation of said first second and third valves a temperature sensing device capable of detecting a preset adjustable temperature that invokes appropriate operation of said valve actuators and an electrical current sending device capable of driving said valve actuators based upon electrical signals transduced from said preset adjustable temperature whereby said water utilizing device is either completely winterized or completely charged with water such that without electrical power the first valve will be in the closed position to prevent water from entering said water utilizing device and the second and third valves will be in the open position to allow water to drain from said water utilizing device to provide freeze protection in the case of a electrical power outage during freezing conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "a water freeze prevention device for an evaporative cooler that is periodically exposed to water freezing temperatures said water freeze prevention device comprising a first valve for regulating water flow through a first pipe leading from a water inlet device to the evaporative cooler an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said first valve back and forth between a closed position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and an open position associated with a second mode of operation of said device a second valve for draining water from a portion of the first pipe located between the first valve and the evaporative cooler an electrically drive valve actuator capable of moving said second valve back and forth between an open position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and a closed position associated with a second mode of operation of said device a third valve for draining water from the evaporative cooler an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said third valve back and forth between an open position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and a closed position associated with a second mode of operation of said device a temperature setting device for invoking the first mode of operation and the second mode of operation of said first second and third valves a temperature sensing device capable of detecting a preset adjustable temperature that invokes appropriate operation of said valve actuators and an electrical current sending device capable of driving said valve actuators based upon electrical signals transduced from said preset adjustable temperature whereby said evaporative cooler is either completely winterized or completely charged with water such that without electrical power the first valve will be in the closed position to prevent water from entering said evaporative cooler and the second and third valves will be in the open position to allow water to drain from said evaporative cooler to provide freeze protection in the case of a electrical power outage during freezing conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "an evaporative cooler and its associated piping system and certain freezing temperature exposed portions of applicant s device are drained and thus winterized"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "indeed in some particularly preferred embodiments of this invention the third valve may be attached to a water utilization device that is located out of doors and therefore exposed to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102154031-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition by providing a heater tube on the inner wall of the body protection element of the intermittent device the open or closed operating space of the intermittent device is always maintained at room temperature to prevent freezing thereby improving the maintenance and management of facilities and product quality.1 is a view showing a partial excerpt of a deodorizing pipe of an odor prevention facility in a terminal treatment plant to which an automatic condensate drainage device of the present invention is applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200407066-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "by maintaining the airtight as described above in the case of the winter season when the external temperature is low by increasing the heat insulating power of the water meter protective tube 51 can have the advantage of eliminating the fear of freezing.the present invention as described above is made of frp material with sufficient rigidity and the water meter protective container cover is formed with airtight means to maintain airtightness while preventing damage and deformation while preventing the air flow inside and outside of the protective container"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432778-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the present invention was created to solve the problems of the prior art it is possible to block the external cold air double triple in a double triple configuration of the water meter protection pail a lot of external cold air between the lid and the protective pail it prevents water meter from freezing even during the cold winter season and it saves a lot of manpower and time due to reconstruction.in case of long term use the protection box is cracked or damaged due to earth pressure or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554870-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "1 and 2 the conventional water meter freeze protection device the outer wall 3 in front of the water meter 2 installed in the water supply pipe 1 for measuring the water consumption of the consumer such as a home or a shopping mall the meter management door 4 for hinge opening and closing at the time of measuring the water consumption is rotatably hinged by the hinge member 5 the heat insulating member 9 for blocking heat transfer in the rear of the meter management door 4 is built in to prevent freezing of the water meter 2 but in this way only by incorporating the insulation member 9 in the rear of the conventional meter management door 4 effectively prevents the freezing phenomenon that occurs in winter there are many problems such as the leakage caused by the freeze because it can not be and the cost is required because the water meter must be replaced.accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems it is to solve the freezing phenomenon that occurs in the winter when the air temperature drops below zero in the section where the water meter is installed to measure the water consumption of the consumer such as home or shopping mall it is an object of the present invention to provide a water meter freeze protection device that can effectively prevent the leakage caused by freezing in advance as well as reduce the cost of water meter replacement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554870-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to completely prevent the occurrence of an accident in advance.as described above the present invention can effectively prevent the freezing phenomenon generated in the winter when the atmospheric temperature drops below zero in the section where the water meter for measuring the water consumption of the consumer such as a home or a shopping mall is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-1012