 the water supply pipe 113 the microprocessor 151 detects the temperature of the water supply pipe 113 through the water supply pipe temperature sensor 125 the steam heating element 140 is heated by the heater power switch 152 so as to reach the set heating temperature corresponding to the detected temperature of the water supply pipe 113 the steam heating element 140 is heated step by step so that the water supply pipe 113 is gradually heated to prevent a sudden increase in the vaporization pressure due to the rapid overheating of the water supply pipe 113"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "according to the present invention regardless of whether or not the steam generating operation is instructed in a state in which power is input to the steam defrosting apparatus the steam heating element is preheated to prepare for steam generation and the freezing of its own water supply pipe is steadily and quickly thawed in winter thereby preventing the steam heating element from overheating due to insufficient water supply or water supply failure by controlling the steam heating element in response to occurrence of abnormality in the supply water during steam generation the steam heating element is prevented from being overheated by controlling the heating of the steam heating element so as not to reach the overheated state in case of shortage or water supply failure thereby preventing the interruption of the steam freezing operation due to overheating.100 a steam cracker 110 pump 113 a water supply pipe 120 water sensor 125 a water supply pipe temperature sensor 130 steam heating element temperature sensor 140 steam heating element 150 the control unit 151 a microprocessor 152 heater power switching part 153 a pump power switching unit 154 control power supply 160 power switch 165 the transformer 170 a steam generating switch 180 display portion"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "valve 44 at an outlet of deuterium separation container 30 is connected via a conduit 48 to an inlet of a tank 50 which forms a part of an irradiation unit 52"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "after valve 44 has been open for a sufficiently long interval to permit the essentially deuterium free water from separator 28 to flow into tank 50 timer 62 or microprocessor 18 activates cooling element 56 to reduce the temperature of the water sample to the freezing point 32 f"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3706682-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0069 7 the first second and third short line cords are power cords but instead the first second and third short line cords themselves are self temperature controlled tropics t since the shape joint can be heated sufficiently by the connector itself the effect of preventing freezing becomes more remarkable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100643176-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "it is configured to prevent the phenomenon from occurring and to prevent freezing and condensation due to the temperature difference between the temperature inside the sensor unit 52 and the sample when measuring the sample in a low temperature state"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "liquid sulphur not flowing but still in a molten state requiring flow to resume and plugged in which portions of the pipeline have experienced sulphur solidification perhaps with formation of voids which forms one or more plugs within the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "using the latent heat signatures associated with phase changes of a process fluid in this case sulphur to identify solidification or melting of the process fluid at locations along a pipeline is not dependent on a particular melting or freezing temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "for example curves in the pipeline may tend to accumulate more solidified process fluid compared to straight sections of the pipeline and anchor points along the pipeline may accumulate more solidified process fluid as a result of heat transfer to the anchors supporting the pipeline which may drop the temperature of the anchor points below the freezing point of the process fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing prevention device for a water meter installed between a water inlet pipe and a water outlet pipe to prevent a water meter for measuring a flow rate of water passing through the water pipe from being frozen a housing installed in the water pipe and having an inlet through which water flows into the inside and a drain through which the incoming water is discharged to the outside a temperature responsive member installed in the housing and contracting or expanding according to a change in temperature and contracting below a predetermined threshold temperature a fixture having the temperature sensitive member installed therein and fixed to the housing and and a moving body provided inside the temperature sensitive member and opening and closing the inlet while being moved in accordance with contraction or expansion of the temperature sensitive member wherein the inlet port is provided with an internal inflow pipe inserted into the water outlet pipe and extending to the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "thus even if the water meter is warmed up the water meter is frozen and damaged if the temperature is greatly lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in embodiments of the present invention tap water flows automatically so that the water meter can not be frozen when the water reaches a temperature at which the water inside the water meter can be frozen even if the user does not use tap water thereby preventing freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "and a freezing prevention unit installed in the metering body and opening the bypass unit formed in the metering body while the internal temperature sensitive member shrinks when the temperature falls below a predetermined threshold temperature to discharge the water inside the metering body to the outside a freezing prevention water meter may be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a freezing prevention device for a water meter which is installed between a water inlet pipe and a water outlet pipe to prevent a water meter for measuring a flow rate of water passing through the water pipe from being frozen a housing having an inlet through which water is introduced and a drain through which the incoming water is discharged a temperature sensitive member installed in the housing and contracting or expanding according to a temperature change a fixture having the temperature sensitive member installed therein and fixed to the housing and a moving body provided with the temperature sensitive member therein and opening and closing the inlet while being moved in accordance with contraction or expansion of the temperature sensitive member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "while the present invention has been described in connection with what is presently considered to be preferred embodiments it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed embodiments but on the contrary it is to be understood that the invention is not limited thereto.10 water inlet pipe 20 water outlet pipe 30 el storage 100 weighing main body 110 bypass unit 200 freeze prevention unit 210 case 300 freezing prevention device 310 housing 211 311 inlet 212 312 drain hole 313 internal inlet pipe 220 320 temperature sensitive member 230 330 240 340 moving body 250 350 elastic member 260 360 rubber member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "that is in the safety valve device 100 according to the present embodiment in winter water in the faucet 10 is discharged to the outside to prevent freezing of water before the water falls below the freezing point of the water is heated to a predetermined temperature or higher the water is discharged to the outside so that the user does not get burned by hot water when using tap water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "therefore water passing through the first inlet 111 is relatively low in temperature immediately before freezing hereinafter referred to as quot low temperature water quot for convenience hereinafter referred to as quot hot water quot for convenience"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5841246-Y2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "time until freezing buried type 7 hours 06 minutes conventional exposed type 5 hours 89 minutes invented exposed type 8 hours 28 minutes notes average wind speed 47jg 9 outside temperature 18.11 as mentioned above the present invention makes it easier to install above ground water meters makes them relatively inexpensive improves the cold resistance of water pipes and stop valves that can cause freeze damage and eliminates the need for conventional underground water meters"}, {"pat_id": "US-7403839-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "such sensors 12 can be hard wired into the electrical supply of the structure or battery operated but are preferably hard wired and include a battery backup in the event of a power failure a condition where flooding is more likely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102697803-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "as a result of the air introduced in this way tap water contained in the water pipe is quickly introduced to the outside through the outlet hole thereby preventing freezing of the water pipe even in winter when the temperature suddenly drops.figure 1 is a perspective view of a freeze protection device according to one embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101136250-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the remaining water is automatically drained to the outside through the drainage hole which prevents freezing due to the absence of water remaining in the floating tube and opens the valve by turning the handle in reverse to open the part connected to the water pipe while blocking the drainage hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention relates to a heating device for preventing the water quality improvement and freezing of the water tank 1 installed outdoors that is on the roof for fire extinguishing more specifically the inside of the water tank 1 in the form of a float when floated in water above or below a certain temperature the water inside the water tank 1 is heated to inhibit microbial sterilization as well as proliferation and to prevent freezing so that the water tank 1 and the pipe are corroded by the microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "to prevent freezing by convection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "or more the water in the water tank 1 is heated and sterilized at low temperature thereby suppressing the growth of microorganisms in winter when the temperature is 4 c or less it is characterized in that the water in the water tank 1 is heated to prevent freezing due to the phenomenon of heat treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "is installed outside the water tank 1 to control the operation of the heater member 20 when the temperature of the water in the water tank 1 is 30 or more or 4 or less by operating the heater member 20 when the temperature of the water in the water tank 1 by the above described water temperature sensor 23 in the summer season is 30 or more by operating the heater member 20 to pasteurize the temperature of the water in the water tank 1 in winter when 4 or less to operate the heater member 20 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "or less after it is determined to be winter and thus heats the water inside the water tank 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "or lower the water tank 1 the heater member 20 is operated to maintain the temperature of the water inside 4 6 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "after checking only the temperature of the water inside the water tank 1 to determine the operation of the heater member 20 as the temperature inside the water tank 1 or less than 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "in addition although the external temperature of the winter season is measured by the external temperature sensor but may be lower than the temperature actually measured by obstacles or other factors such as wind the controller 30 of the present invention has an external temperature of 4 when the temperature of the water inside the water tank 1 becomes 4 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_171", "text": "furthermore be communicating with a home router the water meter and leak detection system 10 126 200 can communicate with intelligent thermostats sending a signal to turn on the residential or corporation heat to a temperature that will inhibit freezing water in the residential and corporation interior water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102366732-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "furthermore the heat exchanger may include a refrigerant pipe through which a refrigerant object flows and a freezing chamber in which the inside is maintained at a constant temperature by the refrigerant pipe and the air transferred from the air storage tank is cooled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 1 or 2 the freeze protector a housing having an accommodation space formed therein an inlet portion formed on one side and a drainage portion formed on the other side and a water pipe device for preventing freezing comprising a temperature sensitive member accommodated in the housing and provided to open and close the drainage part while changing in length according to temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "another method for preventing the water pipe from freezing is to prevent the water pipe from freezing by artificially opening a water valve to continuously drain the water when it is expected that the water contained in the water pipe will freeze due to low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore since the freeze preventer operates normally below the freezing temperature and the tap water is smoothly drained the entire water pipe can be protected from freezing or bursting.1 is a block diagram showing a water pipe device for preventing freezing according to a first embodiment of the present invention 2 is a block diagram showing a water pipe device for preventing freezing according to a second embodiment of the present invention figure 3 is an enlarged view of the a portion of figure 1 figure 4 is an enlarged view of the b portion of figure 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the configuration of the present invention for achieving the above object the motor pump for supplying the raw water is supplied to the storage tank remotely through the pipe and installed in the intake well and the inner upper side of the storage tank to sense the water level of the storage tank an ultrasonic sensor installed in the outer circumferential surface to prevent freezing a temperature sensing sensor installed inside the storage tank to measure a temperature in the storage tank and installed outside the storage tank and measured from the ultrasonic sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "on the other hand the ultrasonic sensor 30 is not frozen even in winter as it is installed in the storage tank 20 but there is room for freezing when the temperature is drastically lowered so as to prevent this ultrasonic sensor as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "on the other hand when the winter temperature is lowered below the set temperature the heater 32 is operated to prevent the ultrasonic sensor from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387639-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it is formed thicker so that it can be mounted blocking the inflow and transmission of cold ground temperature and allowing the underground geothermal heat to flow in and keeping it warm thus preventing freezing of water meters etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387639-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in particular since the plurality of absorption holes 5 5 5 of the bottom surface side 7 of the water meter protection tube 1 and the lower side heat insulating material 6 were formed in the same manner the water meter protection tube 1 inside together with the upper insulation 6 not only prevents the cold temperature from being transmitted but also allows the geothermal heat to flow in warmer than the ground temperature during the winter season so that the temperature inside the water meter protector 1 is similar to the geothermal heat in order to maintain the water supply it is possible to act to prevent freezing of the water meter 3 and the like and in the rainy season the water inside the water meter protection tube 1 can be easily discharged.as described above the present invention is simple in construction by preventing deformation of the rim of the water meter protector to form a lid well by forming a tapered reinforcement 9 on the round inclined surface of the side portion and the bottom surface in order to facilitate the purchase storage and loading and to form a plurality of absorbent holes in the bottom surface and the bottom insulation of the water meter protection container and to block the cold temperature transfer inside the water meter protection container with a thick formed upper side insulation material"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387639-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "on the other hand warm geothermal heat is introduced in the winter season so that the temperature inside the water meter protector can maintain a temperature similar to that of the geothermal temperature thereby preventing freezing of water meters and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101640581-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore the liquid flowing in the closed channel does not freeze in the flowing state but when the freezing temperature is reached in the state where the flow is stopped the liquid is phase changed from the liquid to solid by freezing and volume expansion occurs if the increase can not be accommodated in the pipeline or equipment the frost will occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101640581-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "summary of the invention the present invention has been conceived to solve the above described problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a liquid filling chamber which is capable of opening an opening closing member connected to a main pipe by an expansion action so that the liquid in the main piping always flows thereby preventing the freezing of the main piping and the occurrence of freezing of the main piping even if the temperature falls below the freezing temperature in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101640581-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to the present invention configured as described above the opening and closing member connected to the main pipe is opened by the expansion action generated when the liquid filled in the liquid filling chamber falls to the freezing temperature and is frozen thereby continuously discharging the liquid of the main pipe to the outside it is possible to prevent the freezing of the main pipe and the occurrence of the freezing of the main pipe even if the temperature of the liquid falls below the freezing temperature in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100670676-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition since the synthetic resin reinforcement cover 3 protects and reinforces the upper side of the upper styropole 2 it acts to block the transmission of the cold temperature outside easily such as a water meter installed inside the water meter protector it will also keep warm to prevent freezing.as described above the present invention is simple in construction the adhesive material or assembly so that the reinforcement cover and the upper styropol and the metering cap and styropole which is a synthetic resin material can be easily fixed and combined without a separate article or assembly parts it saves a lot of parts and assembly time it is easy to use the metering cap prevents damage and damage of the upper styropole and blocks the cold outside temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681403-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition in order to solve the problem that the water of the body is frozen and the ceramic insulator is broken if the outside air temperature in winter falls below freezing for a long time without using active water according to one embodiment of the present invention when the controller senses the sub zero temperature by the temperature sensor after the power supply of the supply pump is shut off and the sub zero temperature elapses for a certain time for example 1 hour the drain valve is opened it is possible to prevent the occurrence of the problem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681403-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention as described later after the supply pump 72 for supplying water to the active water supply apparatus 100 is shut off the controller 70 is controlled by the temperature sensor 73 when the freezing temperature is sensed and the freezing temperature passes the predetermined time the drain valve 71 is opened to discharge the water in the body 10 to the outside thereby preventing the freezing of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372345-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if you install the water meter outside the building as described above there is an advantage that the meter reading staff can easily read and the privacy is not infringed during the metering process but it is installed outdoors in the winter season where the freezing is low due to the low outside temperature this will provide a cause for freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3206862-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the temperature inside the main body case 1 rises due to the heat generated by the electrolytic bath 2 and the heat generated by the transformer 13 and this heats the electrolytic bath 2 and the pipe 3 disposed inside the main body case 1 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3206862-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "this time one chamber 2a side of the electrolytic cell 2 serves as a cathode to generate alkaline ionized water and the other chamber 2b side serves as an anode to generate acidic ionized water thereby being neutralized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100728827-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "or less detected by a temperature sensor installed inside the pipe to prevent freezing of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100728827-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "only when the flow does not flow to the heating device 10 by supplying power to the pipe pipe 100 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "in some example embodiments the temperature sensor 115 may be used to prevent pipes from freezing and the pressure sensor 115 may be used to prevent pipes from bursting"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "in some example embodiments the system may receive weather data and if there is prediction of sub zero temperatures in the forecast the system may automatically turn on the main valve to allow water to flow through the pipes thereby preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "when the temperature drops the system opens the main valve and allows the water to flow thus preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200230541-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "due to this problem the supply of tap water is interrupted during the winter and the tap water has to be supplied after melting the tap with hot water or heat.if the temperature drops too much the water meter freezes due to the freezing of the water meter due to rapid freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200230541-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "only when it goes below zero use the tap water as necessary to prevent freezing by freezing as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-8667978-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in the illustrative example control panel and indicators 28 includes led indicators 32 as follows a monitor indicator which indicates the monitoring system is active an away indicator which indicates the water system is shut off a seismic alarm indicator which indicates that seismic sensor 27 has been triggered a low high temperature alarm indicator which indicates that temperature sensor 23 has detected extreme heat or a near freezing condition a slow leak alarm which indicates that the back pressure pressure drop rate is between the low and high level thresholds a water flow alarm which indicated that the rate of pressure drop has exceeded the upper threshold and a humidity alarm that indicates that the humidity has exceeded a threshold when building 10 is unoccupied or that a profile has been exceeded when the household is in use"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101782407-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a regeneration wastewater treatment apparatus comprising a low temperature crystallization tank 40 for cooling the regenerated wastewater filtered by the strong acid filtering apparatus 30 to a low temperature so as not to be frozen through a low temperature cooling unit 70 to precipitate as colorless particulate crystals of a hydrazine salt a low temperature cooling unit 70 composed of an evaporator 71 and a condenser 72 for cooling the regeneration wastewater of the low temperature crystallization tank 40 but not freezing the recovered wastewater cooled at a low temperature in the low temperature crystallization tank 40 is transported to the vacuum evaporation crystallization tank 100 through the regeneration waste water transfer pipe 81 by the acid pump 21 a primary condensing tank 80 for primarily condensing water by cooling and condensing water vapor by heat exchange with high temperature steam generated from the condensing tank 80 the crystals are removed from the low temperature crystallization tank 40 and the remaining regenerated waste water filtrate is vacuum evaporated by indirect heating through a heating device 110 and a vacuum state by a vacuum pump to precipitate white powdery crystals of a nitrogen compound a vacuum evaporation crystallization tank 100 composed of a closed type adiabatic reaction tank a secondary condensing tank 120 for re condensing water vapor that is not condensed in the primary condensing tank 80 and is discharged and discharged through the cooling condensing device 130 a cooling condenser 130 for cooling water in the secondary condensing tank 120 to coagulate through heat exchange with the refrigerant to form condensed water a vacuum pump 140 for generating a vacuum of 0.2 atm in the vacuum evaporation and crystallization tank 100 to lower the evaporation temperature of the regenerated wastewater to 60 c the condensed water produced in the primary condensing tank 80 and the secondary condensing tank 120 is periodically opened to open the drain valve 90 and stored in the condensed water storage tank 150 through the condensate transfer pipe 91 which is characterized by low temperature and high vacuum evaporation concentration crystallization"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101782407-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "the wastewater is then stored in a low temperature chiller 70 at a temperature of 2 c or less to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432780-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it relates to a water meter protection tank to increase the temperature blocking force to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432780-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the present invention was created to solve the problems of the prior art described above the water meter protective casing is a double structure and having an air layer therebetween to keep the inside temperature of the protective casing while blocking the external cool air to double the average year its purpose is to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes in colder winter seasons or colder regions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101801033-B1", "para_id": "para_150", "text": "the heating device 50 installed in the buoy body 23 of the object internet buffer 20c and the sensor body 21 of the object internet water quality sensor 20a the holder body 22 of the object internet holder 20b is used to prevent freezing of the reaction solution even in a subzero temperature and to prevent condensation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321205-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bellows type frozen preventive tools and the applicable water gauge and heatexchanger the present invention relates to a freeze protection device which prevents freezing due to a volume change when a liquid fluid flowing into a water meter a heat exchanger and various pipes has a lowered ambient temperature to a subzero region or when the fluid is frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321205-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "tex