he temperature of the water in the water pipe to discharge the water in the water pipe only until a certain temperature it is possible to save the amount of water discharged to prevent freezing it has an effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the valve 13 and the temperature detection sensor 12 which are installed in the flowing water pipe and opened closed to discharge the water flowing in the water pipe are inputted and analyzed and analyze the information and determine the freezing time of the water in the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the temperature detection sensor 12 may be installed in a water pipe adjacent to the meter 11 that is in an area of the water pipe where the freezing may occur most easily due to exposure to the outside air thereby detecting the temperature of water in the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "the controller 14 may be provided with information on the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor 12 and determine the freezing time of the water in the water pipe by grasping the temperature change of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the control unit 14 uses the phenomenon that the temperature rise before the freezing of the water in the water pipe the temperature of the water in the water pipe is less than 3 and continuously lowered to a preset reference temperature range for a preset reference time interval when it rises it is determined that the freezing time has arrived and outputs a control signal for opening the valve 13 to the valve 13 whereby the valve 13 is opened to discharge water to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "for example when the temperature of the water in the water pipe does not rise even after a preset time has elapsed since the control unit 14 opened the valve 13 for freezi