device and more particularly to a water meter freeze protection device that can maintain a constant temperature at room temperature to prevent freezing of the water meter pipe in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415979-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "as the water pipes or water meters are frozen in the cold weather of the winter as described above the cost of replacing tap water and broken water meters that are wasted due to the drainage of unnecessary drinking water is increasing.therefore the present invention was devised in view of the same problems as the prior art and an object thereof is to provide a water meter freezing prevention apparatus capable of maintaining a constant temperature at room temperature to prevent freezing of the water meter pipe in winter"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236382-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in any of the vacuum freezing processes described an aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200487219-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in this water meter 10 tap water is allowed to pass through the water meter so that when the air temperature falls below freezing in winter tap water passing through the water meter is frozen and thus the water meter 10 is frequently frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200487219-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention the apparatus further includes a flow rate measuring means 70 provided inside the housing 11 for measuring the flow rate of tap water passing through the inside of the housing 11 receives the signal of the flow rate measuring means 70 and when the flow rate of the tap water passing through the interior of the housing 11 is equal to or higher than a predetermined speed the flow rate of the water in the water flow meter is reduced.th