471-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as the solenoid valve 22 is operated as described above to flow out the fluid in the stopped state until the frozen fluid melts preventing the fluid from freezing due to the fluid flow inside the pipeline of the water pipe 11 and at the same time it will thaw the frozen fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the solenoid valve 122 is opened to drain the fluid in the stopped state until the frozen fluid melts thereby preventing the fluid from freezing due to the fluid flow generated inside the pipeline of the fluid transport pipe 110 and at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the solenoid valve 122 is opened to drain the fluid in the stopped state until the frozen fluid melts thereby preventing the fluid from freezing due to the fluid flow generated inside the pipeline of the fluid transport pipe 110 and at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "at this time since the inner diameter of the inlet pipe 311 is smaller than the inner diameter of the fluid transport pipe 110 the pressure increase inside the installation pipe 312 occurs first"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "it is configured to operate the solenoid valve installed in the pipeline connected to the member to discharge the fluid introduced into the fluid receiving member thereby preventing the damage of the fluid receiving member that is freezing due to the increase in pressure generated by the freezing of the product lifespan this has the effect of extending and increasing consumer confidence in the product"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at least one temperature sensor installed at two or more different locations in the room a heater a fan blowing the air heated by the heater and a freeze protection device of a hot air heater including a power supply as a freeze protection method performed to pre