cles 330 for water purification by water pressure by opening and closing the lower portion of the water purification body wow a branch pipe 400 connected so that the drinking water treated while passing through the purified water pipe 300 may be supplied to a storage tank or a user and an ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 fixed to the side of the branch pipe 400 to check the turbidity of water and provide information to the controller 700 wow a flow rate sensor 600 fixed to the side of the branch pipe 400 to check the flow rate of water and provide information to the controller 700 wow the supply pump 100 and the temperature sensor 340 the heating wire 350 the solenoid valve 370 the ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 and the flow rate sensor 600 are signal connected to control the supply pump 100 according to the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at one side of the vertical pipe 310 a temperature sensor 340 that checks the temperature inside the water purification pipe 300 at any time and provides information to the controller 700 is installed and a controller receiving information from the temperature sensor 340 in accordance with the operation control of 700 a heating wire 350 that operates to prevent freezing is installed but the vertical pipe 310 and the water purification guide pipe 320 in which the heating wire 350 is installed become a pipe through which water passes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in addition in winter the controller 700 controls the operation to operate the heating wire 350 according to the value measured by the temperature sensor 340 to prevent freezing and the flow rate sensor 600 checks the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200498205-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition in the winter if the permeated water that seeps into the pavement layer of the bridge deck is not drained quickly and remains it freezes due to the low temperature causing freezing and rupture of the pavement layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-11471899-B1", "para_id": "para_170", "text": "of course these approaches are exemplary and in other embodiments heating devices or other approaches may be utilized for purposes of assuring that the system is not subject to becoming inoperable due to freezing of liquid therein"}, {"pat_id": "US-6237620-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this expense can be considerable when it is realized that the pipes constituting the plumbing system for conveyance of water throughout the vehicle boat yacht cottage or lodge may proceed in relatively inaccessible regions which may require removal of a structural component of the mobile home boat yacht cottage or lodge in order to provide access to the freeze damaged length of pipe or the particular fitting adversely affected by the freezing temperature in the winter months"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "for this reason a separate thermal insulation material may be installed at the part where the water meter is installed but when the external temperature is very low there is a problem that such thermal insulation material cannot prevent freezing of the meter.document 1 registration utility model publication no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "fifth the color of the water meter is not simply changed based on the outside temperature where the water meter is installed but based on the temperature of the tap water passing through the water meter it is possible to inform the possibility of freezing thereby further enhancing the reliability of freezing prediction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "fifth by not simply changing the color based on the outside temperature at which the water meter is installed but by notifying the possibility of freezing based on the temperature of the tap water passing through the water meter there is an effect to further increase the reliability of freezing wave prediction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654101-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in more detail a bypass pipe for freeze and burst prevention is connected between the suction pipe and the discharge pipe so that the temperature detected by the temperature sensor in winter is lowered below the set temperature if there is no water flow because the user does not use water the pump is driven so that the pressure of the discharge pipe is higher than the opening pressure of the relief valve and water circulates through the bypass pipe to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654101-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore the purpose of the present invention is to connect a bypass pipe for freeze prevention between the suction pipe and the discharge pipe so that in the winter if the temperature detected by the temperature sensor falls below the set temperature and there is no water flow because the user does not use water the pump is driven so that the pressure of the discharge pipe is higher than the opening pressure of the relief valve allowing water to circulate through the bypass pipe thereby providing a freeze prevention water supply pressurization device and a control method thereof that can prevent freezing in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "on the other hand in the case of using a heating wire there is a concern of excessive use of energy a fire occurrence problem due to overheating and a loss of thermal insulation function due to breakage of the heating wire.the present invention was devised to improve such a conventional problem and it is configured to determine whether the intake pump is operated not only by the internal level of the water tank but also by the outside temperature detected by the temperature sensor so that water of water temperature higher than the outside temperature in winter is it is an object of the present invention to provide a freeze proof intermittent tap water to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe by heat 