se a first temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the mixed solution flowing through the antifreeze hose a heater for heating the mixed solution stored in the antifreeze tank to a predetermined temperature a temperature controller for adjusting the temperature of the mixed solution and the temperature information of the mixed solution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit while the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to heat the mixed solution heating control unit including water tank for storing water a selection unit which selects any one of the mixed solution or water stored in the antifreeze tank or the water tank in response to a control signal of the control unit and transmits it to the circulation pump and a second temperature sensor for measuring the ambient temperature of the pipe for transferring the liquid further comprising the control unit supplies the water supplied from the water tank to the circulation pump through the selection unit when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a set temperature and when the external temperature information measured by the second temperature sensor is lower than the set temperature the water supplied from the antifreeze tank is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "such a temporary measure has difficulty in preventing freezing of the water meter and water pipe due to the thermal insulation problem when the external temperature is very low below 5 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the present invention according to one aspect for achieving the above object is an antifreeze tank in which a mixture of antifreeze and water is stored in a predetermined ratio antifreeze hose installed along the pipe for transferring the liquid to transfer the liquid a circulation pump for supplying and circulating the mixed solution into the antifreeze hose a first temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the mixed solution flowing through the antifreeze hose a heater for heating the mixed solution stored in the antifreeze tank to a predetermined temperature a temperature controller for adjusting the temperature of the mixed solution and while the temperature information of the mixed solution measured through the first temperature sensor is output and displayed in real time through the display unit the heater is driven in response to the temperature information of the mixed solution and the temperature set through the temperature controller to drive the mixed solution it provides a system for preventing freezing and freezing of piping for liquid transport characterized in that it comprises a control unit for heating the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102346405-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the supplied water may be supplied to the circulation pump and when the temperature is lower than a set temperature the mixed liquid supplied from the antifreeze tank may be supplied to the circulation pump.as described above according to the system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipe for liquid transport according to the present invention an antifreeze hose through which antifreeze mixture heated to a predetermined temperature flows along the pipe for liquid transport is installed and the antifreeze flowing through the antifreeze hose it is possible to prevent freezing and freezing of the liquid transport pipe in winter by transferring the heat source of the liquid to the liquid transport pipe.1 is a view showing a system for preventing freezing and freezing of pipes for liquid transport according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101517040-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "however according to the conventional techniques as described above the ground water is discharged from the inside of the tunnel and the emergency water supply pipe 300 and the discharge pipe 400 constituted in the prior art of the former and the discharge pipe 139 when the ambient temperature falls below freezing in the cold winter season due to the closed state of the inside of the pipe when the valve is closed by the opening and closing valve 139a which is caused by the flow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101517040-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in order to prevent the freezing of the water pipe exposed to the ground it is necessary to open the valve of the water pipe slightly to always circulate the water to the water pipe or to install a heat radiator to raise the temperature of the water pipe i was doing"}, {"pat_id": "US-7128081-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "operating the peltier heat pump at this constant temperature avoids repetitive thermal stresses that can occur when a device is required to cycle up and down to achieve heating and cooling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302626-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water meter and more particularly to a freeze proof water meter to accommodate the air into the water meter to prevent freezing caused by a sudden drop in temperature in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302626-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the purpose is to provide a freeze proof water meter to accommodate the air into the water meter to prevent freezing caused by a sudden drop in temperature during the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302626-Y1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "will be accommodated and the appropriate freeze protection will be achieved accordingly.as described above the present invention accommodates air into the water meter to prevent freezing caused by a sudden drop in temperature in winter and thus it is easy to prevent freezing with a simple structure and is easy to manufacture and requires a separate heater"}, {"pat_id": "US-12522516-B2", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the primary pump 130a is thus used to enable the sample collection to occur within a desired temperature range provided within the interior space preventing the intake liquid from freezing or being overheated by the exterior conditions i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "a freeze protection valve assembly comprising a valve housing having a flow channel with an inflow end an outflow end and an opening in the housing to said flow channel a control valve mounted within said flow channel said control valve having a valve stem which carries a valve stop said valve stop being normally biased in a position which is closed but which valve stem and valve stop is movable to an open position in response to pressure exerted upon said valve stem a control lever extending through said opening in the housing of said channel adjacent the valve stem of said control lever a resilient member having an opening defined therethrough which resilient member seals said opening through the housing to said channel and which said resilient member has said control lever mounted therethrough to complete the sealing of said opening through the housing of said channel and which said resilient member also provides a fulcrum for pivoting of said lever and a thermally responsive member positioned and adapted to operatively engage one end of said control lever when the temperature of said thermally responsive member approaches the freezing point of water whereby said lever is pivoted at said resilient member to bring its opposed end into engagement with said valve stem to thereby open said valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "outlet opening 57 is similarly designed to receive a fitting that is connectable for example to a drain system all of which are not shown"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "it is therefore seen that the present invention provides a simple device for activating a fluid valve in response to a thermal and spec