 conduits 98"}, {"pat_id": "US-12127513-B2", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "in another embodiment an electrical pump may be used to transfer this water out of the tanks and into a hose or pipe for attachment to a shower laundry room kitchen or other locations where warm hot water is desired"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200340234-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the pressure is always maintained at high pressure and thus the internal temperature of the water tank is also maintained at a high temperature of 130 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-4798239-A", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the two anti freezing valves 15 and 16 effectively protect the meter against freezing by virtue of the transfer of heat from soil zones where the collectors 10 are buried to the valves 15 and 16 flanking the meter thereby preventing the freezing of the water circulating from the valve 15 to the valve 16 even in the case of a substantially negative temperature of the adjacent atmosphere"}, {"pat_id": "US-11998860-B2", "para_id": "para_1116", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the produced water or wastewater temperature in the sump bottom of the container 139 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101882879-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as an embodiment of the present invention a device for preventing freezing temperature sensor contact relay may be further included in the upper casing 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-4456024-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "to prevent freezing of water in a conventional residential water supply system the above described valve would be constructed and adjusted to open when the water temperature dropped to or slightly below the freezing temperature for example around 30 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-4456024-A", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "ambient temperatures below freezing but of insufficient duration to reduce the water temperature to the freezing point will no