ith the heat sink 70 is installed to radiate heat to the inside of the main body 10 to prevent freezing due to cold"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101508672-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a medicine dispensing apparatus for dispensing medicine formed by injecting medicine into water supplied to a water supply pipe the apparatus comprising a main body a medicine supply pipe 30 which is installed inside the main body and is for supplying medicines in a medicine storage tank provided in the medicine storage tank to the water supply pipe one side connected to the medicine storage tank and the other side connected to the water supply pipe a chemical supply pump provided with the chemical supply pump a motor interlocked with the medicine dispensing pump and adjusting a dose of the medicine by adjusting a rotation speed a control unit electrically connected to the motor to control the driving and rotating speed of the motor and a pressure sensor for sensing a pressure inside the medicine inlet pipe and electrically connected to the motor so that the medicine is supplied to the medicine inlet pipe only when water flows inside the water supply pipe the pipe is provided with a branch connecting member at one end for facilitating installation in the water supply pipe a heat radiating plate is installed inside the main body a temperature sensor interlocked with the heat radiating plate is further installed and a heating wire is installed on the medicine inlet pipe to prevent freezing of the medicine a side wall of the main body is connected to a first medicine inlet pipe connected to a medicine storage tank and supplying medicines to the inside of the main body and a second medicine inlet pipe connected to a water supply pipe for supplying medicines to the water supply pipe and a hose connecting the two connection ports"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101508672-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the medicine dispensing apparatus according to the present invention is provided with a heat dissipating plate 70 inside the main body 10 to prevent the freezing due to heavy snow or cold in the winter and a temperature for sensing the temperature inside a sensor 71 is further installed"}, {"pat_id": "US-8117998-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "as described above according to a hot water supplying system of the invention since a water tank storing a predetermined amount of water is provided with the hot water supplying system and water stored in the water tank and remaining in the pipelines is preheated even when the hot water is not used it is possible to supply hot water heated to a set temperature in the shortest time whenever a user wants to use the hot water and to prevent the pipelines from freezing and bursting in the winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261190-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a water meter protection box for preventing freezing of a weighing container which is embedded in a basement and filled with a resin foam therein comprising an inner cylinder having an inner groove to seat the water pipe of the metering hopper on an outer surface thereof a height adjustment means for adjusting the height of the inner cylinder in accordance with a height of the outer cylinder to correspond to the inner groove and including a metering chamber an outer cylinder and a heat insulating material interposed between the inner passage and the outer tube to block the outside air to maintain the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-5816288-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "temperature variations especially low temperatures below freezing can cause the screens to frost over and become damaged thus allowing an entrance to the storage tank for insects and other undesired elements"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100918589-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "or in order to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes in the past a large amount of foamed polystyrene styrofoam is built into a single walled protective case but the freezing of water meters and water pipes is prevented in cold weather or cold regions falling below a certain temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100518072-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in winter when it is desired to prevent freezing of the water meter m power is always supplied to the heating wire 2h penetrated through the inlet pipe 1c of the main body 1 by an appropriate supply means"}, {"pat_id": "US-4282070-A", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "anti freeze material added to lower the freezing temperature for increased refrigerating capability the medium may be rerouted at least in part through an additional heat exchanger 46 to be brought up to the temperature of the entering feed from source 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hot wire control apparatus for controlling power supply to a hot wire installed in close contact with a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe a temperature sensor for sensing an external temperature a relay for switching the supply of external power to the hot wire heater a power supply to the hot wire is provided when the external temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is lower than a first temperature and a power supply is not supplied to the hot wire when the external temperature is equal to or higher than a second temperature higher than the first temperature a control unit a first display unit for turning on the lamp when power is normally supplied from the external power source to the control unit a second display unit for turning on the lamp when the control unit is operating normally when power is supplied to the hot line a third display unit indicating that power is supplied to the hot wire without any abnormality and and a case enclosing the relay the first display unit the second display unit the third display unit and the control unit the control unit wherein the timer counts a pulse signal using the timer when the power is supplied to the hot wire and controls the relay to stop power supply to the hot wire if the power is supplied to the hot wire for a first time or longer counts a pulse signal by using the timer when the power is cut off and controls the relay when the pulse signal is counted for a second time different from the first time to supply power to the hot wire again when the external temperature becomes lower than a preset third temperature at which the freeze wave can occur the power supply to the hot wire is continuously supplied independently of the timer wherein the case is waterproof and has a hole in which the first display unit the second display unit and the third display unit are installed the waterproof is maintained by providing a rubber hook to the hole wherein the first display unit is turned on and the second display unit and the third display unit are turned off when the external temperature is higher than the second temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore when using the bimetallic controlled frost protector a power of about 38 w to 76 w per household is leaked for 24 hours every day for about 5 months november march during winter there is a problem in that the electric charge is lost.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in an effort to solve the problems of the conventional freezing prevention apparatus having a bimetallic sensor control system the present invention provides a water pipe heating line control device for preventing the freezing of the water pipe by increasing the efficiency of energy consumption by increasing the efficiency of energy consumption"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a hot water line controller for controlling the supply of power to a hot wire installed in close contact with a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe a temperature sensor for sensing and a power supply unit for supplying power to the hot wire when the external temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is lower than a first temperature and supplying power to the hot wire when the external temperature is equal to or higher than a second temperature higher than the first temperature wherein the control unit interrupts the power supply to the hot wire when the power supply to the hot wire is continued for a first time or more and the power supply is cut off at a temperature lower than the second temperature and the power source is supplied again to the hot wire if it continues for 2 hours or more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "for example when the first temperature is set to 2 deg c and the first temperature is set to 4 deg c when the external temperature sensed by the temperature sensor 210 becomes 2 deg c power is supplied to the heat line installed in the water pipe to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102466363-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "since the outside air temperature drops below freezing in winter proper insulation must be accompanied to prevent freezing and bursting of the water meter and the water pipe connected to the water meter and an open configuration must be taken to allow meter reading of usage even in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102466363-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in general when the outside temperature drops below freezing such as in winter the water flowing inside the main body of the water meter freezes and expands and the expansion force may cause a freeze phenomenon that damages the glass cover of the meter or damages the meter itself"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing process for obtaining pure water from salt water comprising feeding salt water to a vertically arranged elongated closed tank to establish a column of salt water therein the level of which is above the feed point continuously cooling a body of mercury externally of said tank and injecting said mercury in the form of finely atomized particles into the upper portion of said liquid column withdrawing said mercury from the bottom of said tank and recirculating said mercury through said liquid column to maintain the column at a temperature which is subcooled with respect to the salt water infeed so that the infeed has ice crystals formed therein due to contact with the subcooled column permitting the ice crystals to accumulate and form a solid block of ice in the upper portion of said tank above the level of mercury injection moving said block of ice upwardly in said tank by hydraulic pressure of incoming salt water and melting the upper portion of said block of ice by indirect heat exchange with the salt water feed prior to entry of said feed into said column and withdrawing pure water from the upper portion of the tank between the top of said tank and the top of said ice block and withdrawing concentrated salt water and precipitated salts collected above the mercury from the lower portion of said tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200371057-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water meter to prevent freezing particularly the material of the transparent plate body on which the upper glass surface and the dial of the water meter which are easily damaged in winter season are transparent but strong in impact resistance and cold resistance and slightly elastic it is replaced with a material that has a high temperature and reinforces a well damaged part in the water meter so that the amount of water contained is reduced and the volume of the expanded ice is reduced thereby preventing freezing of the entire water meter and the diffusion and disappearance of glycerin"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101978152-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "also the lid 120 isolates the space 10 inside the frame 100 to prevent inflow of outside air at a low temperature thereby further lowering the possibility of freezing the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101978152-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "this may be advantageous in preventing freezing of the water meter 320 and the connecting piping"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101978152-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "after the water meter 320 is replaced or the meter reading is completed the operator can remove the meter reading unit 300 from the temporary fixing unit 150 and move the meter reading unit 300 downward to place it on the support unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "US-11596874-B2", "para_id": "para_136", "text": "system 100 includes air blower 106 that bubbles ambient air 110 through standing water 112 in tank 102 in this non limiting example the bubbling is accomplished via air stone 108"}, {"pat_id": "US-11054295-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "elevated temperatures can be an indication of bacteria growth in water networks and temperatures that are too low can lead to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-10167205-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "this step puts the droplet at a temperature below its freezing point but leaves it free of ice crystals thus ensuring the same starting conditions for all experiments"}, {"pat_id": "US-10167205-B1", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "the height of the chamber and the vertical speed of the droplet produce the residence time for the transition of the warm wastewater droplet to the point where it explosively separates into the concentrated eutectic liquid solution droplet and fragments of fresh ice fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-10167205-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "air is introduced into the chamber via an annulus duct around the chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-10167205-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "at 35 occurring in the middle of the chamber 27 the purified ice fragments sweep upward into the spiraling cold air stream while the heavier liquid core continues to fall to the bottom of the chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200299813-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "therefore the heat discharged from the condenser 2c is blown by the blower 3 to the evaporation chamber 1b through the blower opening 2w and the internal temperature of the evaporation chamber 1b is raised to about 35 40 degreec"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the pipe adjacent the location of the thermal sensor drops below freezing the sensor is actuated and completes an electrical circuit from a power source to a solenoid actuated valve to thereby cause it to open and allow water to trickle from the water supply pipe through an existing water outlet fixture and down its adjacent and pre existing drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing the sensor is de actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid actuated valve and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "with the circuit thus closed solenoid actuated valve 66 will open and allow water to pass through from conduit 65 to faucet 22 via conduit 67"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "that is upon such a rise in temperature contact arm 51 of thermal switch 50 opens to interrupt the electrical circuit conveying electricity between power source 70 and solenoid actuate valve 66 and thereby cause valve 66 to close in a manner well known in the art"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102625034-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a joint that installs a heating wire in a pipe for supplying fire water but prevents it from sagging to one side due to its own weight and maintains the installation state stably even after a long period of time preventing freezing or freezing due to cold waves etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "discontinuance of dental services in case of malfunction or exhaustion of water in the single pressure storage tank 2 9 in order to prevent the occurrence of a separate simple auxiliary metal or plastic material inside the device the tank 2 14 is installed and in case of emergency the tank cap 2 14 1 is opened and the user can be used to pour the graft in addition a small load is provided at the inlet of the pipe 3 9 to which the water of the unit chair to which each is connected is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the built in electronic temperature controller 2 15 of the pcb board 2 1 detects this and supplies the electric heater of the hot water tank 2 2 and 2 3 the supply pipe of the unit chair 3 9 by operating the circulation pump 2 21 the temperature of the system main body 2 rises due to electrical heat dissipation thereby preventing the freezing of the system.the present invention is devised to solve the problems of the prior art as described above the object of the present invention is that the purified water is circulated by the circulation pump 2 21 without staying in one place attached to the scale or various sludge it is blocked by the cartridge filter 2 13 and can be treated as water warmed at the same temperature as the body temperature of the human body by the electric heater 2 3 and the temperature control device 2 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature falls below the freezing point the built in electronic temperature control device 2 15 of the pcb board 2 1 detects it and the hot water tank 2 by operating the heater 2 3 and the warm water circulation device 2 21 of 2 the temperature inside the system is increased due to electric heat dissipation thereby preventing the freezing of the system at the source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102819243-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the fire extinguishing water in the fire extinguishing water tank 20 is circulated along the fire extinguishing pipe 10 to prevent freezing or bursting"}, {"pat_id": "US-5927099-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "because icemakers make ice by spraying water onto electrically chilled freezer plates a substantial amount of water is lost during each freezing cycle by failing to freeze before reaching the bottom of the freezer plates and exiting into the drain yet a considerable amount of energy is expended in lowering the temperature of this lost water as well as of the water that does freeze"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "freeze protection system of flush toilet freezing burst prevention system for water closet the present invention relates to a freeze protection system of a flush toilet and more particularly by detecting a change in temperature in a water supply pipe line of a flush toilet an electric valve is automatically opened and closed according to an electrical signal thereby allowing a certain amount of water to flow into the flush toilet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe the water supply valve was opened slightly so that the water flow was always maintained in the water supply pipe so that water was always circulated in the water supply pipe or a separate heat radiator was installed to increase the temperature of the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "by doing so while minimizing power consumption water pipes are prevented from freezing and water supply is controlled to save water.1 is a conceptual diagram schematically showing a freeze protection system of the flush toilet according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention detects the temperature sensor 13 to prevent freezing of the connection pipe passing through the inside of the flush toilet 10 and when the temperature falls below the set temperature the controller c controls a predetermined time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the temperature sensor 13 may be set to operate at a temperature for example 5 to 10 at which the freezing wave is expected in winter and the controller c may measure the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the controller c is a circulation pump p and the first opening and closing valve to prevent freezing of the water supply line 11 connected to the flush toilet 10 in accordance with the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 13 pneumatic or electric signals are controlled to actuate v\u2081 and second open close valves v\u2082"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "thus the controller c opens the first opening closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention can be operated to prevent the freezing in winter by wrapping a heating wire not shown in all the connection pipes to make the water supply including the water supply pipe and the water discharge pipe in particular the temperature sensor when the heating wire is preferentially operated by the control of the controller c according to the temperature value measured in 13 so that the heating wire is organically interlocked with the freeze protection system of the flush toilet of the present invention and the heating wire is not operated due to a short circuit of the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102075865-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in addition the heating device is further mounted on the water meter inside the main body of the protector to sense the temperature inside the main body of the winter protector to warm the water meter thereby preventing the freezing of the water meter and improving the safety of the product.1 is an exploded perspective view of the water meter protector of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101207999-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102587945-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "additionally it is possible to prevent freezing of the air valve 90 in a convenient and effective manner by configuring the heating element 44 solar cell 55 temperature sensor signal transmitter and control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-4370865-A", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "when the ice drops the ice making plate 2 will experience an abrupt increase in temperature which is sensed by an ice drop or removal sensing thermostat th3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101568929-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "such a water meter has a protective box due to a problem of breakage or freezing due to external impact and temperature difference due to the season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the heater 16 then raises the temperature in the water tank 10 under the control of the controller 64 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-7527736-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "submerged combustion heaters or other heat sources may be used to raise water temperature as desired such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101239699-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus when freezing occurs in the water meter the entire water meter the work of replacing it is in progress"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in certain embodiments data from this flow meter is transmitted via a low power wireless transmitter to a gateway and hub assembly"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200384179-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as described above according to the present invention by wrapping the inner cylinder 20 with the upper insulating material 40 and the outer insulating material 50 and by inserting the outer cylinder 30 can be preserved as much as possible the geothermal heat introduced into the inner cylinder 20 it is possible to prevent freezing of the water pipe and the water meter by keeping the temperature inside the protection container at room temperature even in cold weather and by combining the reinforcing flange 70 on the upper edge of the outer cylinder 30 even if the protection container is buried in the ground by being able to withstand the load sufficiently there is an effect that can prevent the breakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-4954151-A", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the compressor 11 must also operate for a period of time to remove heat from the water before freezing begins"}, {"pat_id": "US-4954151-A", "para_id": "para_115", "text": "in an alternative embodiment a temperature measuring device is used to measure the rate of change of temperature of the water as it is cooled prior to freezing and from this measurement the capacity of the heat pump can be determined"}, {"pat_id": "US-4635668-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "apparatus for automatically controlling flow in a water line to avoid freeze damage comprising a temperature sensor adapted for connection to the water line the water line a normally closed valve adapted for connection to a housing control circuit means within said housing and responsive to said temperature sensor for continuously monitoring the temperature of water in the line and selectively opening and closing said valve to allow increased periodic flow in the water line with decreasing water temperature and indicator means associated with said housing and connected to said control circuit means for indicating the temperature proximity of water in the line to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430528-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "conventional water meter protection box is installed in the water meter inside of the water meter in the water meter to prevent the water meter from freezing in winter but the water meter is stuck in the water meter when the temperature drops rapidly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore the present invention by simply installing the device around the water pipe and connecting only the power supply the sensor detects that the temperature drops to sub zero temperatures and heats the heating sheet to prevent freezing phenomenon that the water pipe freezes or freezes in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the sensor operates to supply electric current to the electric line surrounding the water pipe to heat the water pipe to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "after that when the temperature rises to the image the temperature sensor 5 detects this and the circuit board 4 operates to stop the supply of electricity to the heating sheet thereby eliminating the consumption of electricity"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5313597-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "one aspect of the present invention includes a heater wire inserted into a heater guide tube provided along a pipe for water supply and or hot water supply a power supply line for supplying power to the heater wire and a heater guide tube together with the heater wire and a control unit for controlling the switching element for turning on and off the power supplied to the heater line via the power supply line and the switching element based on the detected temperature of the pipe temperature sensor"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5313597-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "therefore the control unit inside the control box 60 can detect the resistance value of the thermistor 71 or a change in the resistance value via the lead wire sensor wire 36 and can detect the temperature of the environment where the thermistor 71 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5313597-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore each antifreeze heater 20 is independently a heater based on the conditions of each of the tubes 12a to 12e and 13a to 13c with the heat insulating material and the outside temperature and the inside temperature detected by the sensor of each antifreeze heater 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the warm air device that is installed on the ceiling or wall of the interior of the toilet through a built in case to supply hot air to prevent freezing of water pipes a heater installed in the case to generate heat for freezing of water pipes a fan installed in the case adjacent to the heater to supply heat from the heater to the room a temperature sensor installed in the case and detecting an indoor temperature used as data for determining whether the heater and the fan are operated it is built in the case so as to be connected to the heater the fan and the temperature sensor the operation of the heater and fan based on the room temperature from the temperature sensor when the power is supplied or when the operation is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is installed in the ceiling or wall of the interior of the toilet through a built in case in the warm air device for supplying hot air to prevent the freezing of water pipes etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is a process to prevent the freezing of water pipes by controlling the operation of 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200362784-Y1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "that is when the second set temperature is set to the control unit 50 at 8 c and the third set temperature to 12 c the room 50 is detected from the temperature sensor 40 in the state in which the operation is stopped the operation of the heater 20 and the fan 30 is controlled such that the temperature is between 8 c and 12 c to prevent freezing of water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102313735-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the coil heater 221 is a coil heater made of a silicon material and is installed to surround the wastewater supply pipe 220 thereby preventing the water inside the wastewater supply pipe 220 from freezing in winter when the temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5851260-Y2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "an anti freeze valve 2 low temperature valve connected to piping 1 is used to prevent freezing by lowering the water temperature to a temperature equal to or close to that of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101595915-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "according to the present invention since the steam is generated at high speed at the time of starting the speed of the thawing operation is improved and the start is terminated to prevent the damage of the self components at the time of termination of the operation.100 a steam cracker 110 pump 113 a water supply pipe 130 steam heating element temperature sensor 140 steam heating element 150 the control unit 151 a microprocessor 152 heater power switching part 153 a pump power switching unit 154 control power supply 160 power switch 165 the transformer 170 a steam generating switch 180 display portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101873877-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "when the measured temperature of the temperature sensor is lower than a predetermined reference value heat is generated through the heating element to prevent the water meter from being frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101873877-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "if the control device can communicate via the iot chip and the water meter is an electronic meter remote meter reading meter reading at a remote location can be implemented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100966852-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it has a configuration in which a pressure relief valve is installed to be discharged to the outside to close the exhaust port.as described above according to the freeze protection device of the water pipe of the present invention by operating the hydraulic cylinder with a small amount of water flowing out according to the external temperature change and the force of the water the freeze with the water discharged through the operation of the cylinder effectively also by replacing the capacity of the hydraulic cylinder only it is possible to secure as much water as possible to prevent freezing at any water pipe size or water pressure and more precisely by controlling the amount of discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100689108-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "0 385 568 2003.05.15 titled reservoir control system which is filed and filed by the present applicant has a groundwater level detection unit for detecting the water level of the intake well a motor driving part controlling a driving of the motor for pumping the ground water a controller for controlling the groundwater level sensor and the motor driver a first power supply unit supplying power to the respective parts a water tank level sensing unit for sensing the level of the storage means for storing the raw water a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of raw water of the water tank an rf transmitter for converting the water tank water level detection signal and the temperature signal into a radio signal and transmitting the radio signal the rf transmitter the water tank level sensor and the second power supply for supplying power to the temperature sensor and the rf receiver for receiving a signal to the rf transmitter and transmits to the control unit the groundwater level sensor and the water tank level detection the above problem is solved by easily measuring the water level of the water tank by the conduction of power by the negative and preventing the damage of the device due to freezing in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100251489-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in case of direct heating if the water inside the vertical pipe header and pipe connecting the collector and heat storage tank freezes due to the temperature drop in winter the device will absorb the volume expansion caused by the freezing of water and the increase of the internal pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in claim 1 the above flow control tank a wheel washing facility including a heater to maintain the water temperature above a certain level to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to one embodiment the flow control tank may include a heater to maintain a water temperature above a certain level to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "5 the flow control tank 30 may include a heater 60 to maintain the water temperature above a certain level to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255061-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "d2 the smart water meter has a heat supply unit for supplying heat to the water meter installed in the water pipe and the management server controls the smart water meter to cause the water supply unit to determine if there is a risk of freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255061-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "power may be supplied to the heating wire 140 to raise the temperature of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255061-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "step s505 in this case as in the above described step s404 the management server 800 combines the outside temperature information received from the meteorological server 90 with the temperature information of the water of the water pipe received from the smart water meter thereby freezing hazards"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_197", "text": "however the salinity of salt water industrial brine 202 that enters freezing desalination cell unit enclosure 271 via salt water industrial brine inlet 275 also has influence on the freezing process the higher the salt concentration the lower the necessary freezing temperature to be accomplished"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_197", "text": "by using a salinity sensor for salt water industrial brine 202 and a temperature sensor not specifically shown in figures throughout this patent inside freezing desalination cell unit enclosure 271 the freezing process can be automatically controlled via a computer microprocessor control system"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_203", "text": "in each specialized freezing desalination ellipsoidal tank 310 due to upwards action of acoustic pressure shock waves 10 desalinated ice 281 accumulates at the top of specialized freezing desalination ellipsoidal tank 310 from where desalinated ice 281 is pushed or vacuumed through ice collection pipe 247 towards ice melting system heat exchanger 298 where the ice crystals are melt in a solution although still having low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_215", "text": "if it does not pass the necessary decontamination level partially decontaminated water 353 is sent back via return pipe for insufficient decontaminated water 354 to specialized freezing separation ellipsoidal tank for tritiated water heavy water 350 for further freezing decontamination process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200407276-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "compressor for compressing the refrigerant into a gaseous form of high temperature and high pressure a refrigerant pipe formed of a thin tube to form the high temperature high pressure gas type refrigerant in a medium temperature high pressure gas liquid mixed state and the low temperature low pressure refrigerant in the medium temperature high pressure gas liquid mixed state a freezing unit including an evaporator which absorbs heat while surrounding the gas cold water tank for supplying the purified cold water required for the water tank of the small vending machine cold water tank for maintaining the water supplied by the freezing unit cold purified cold water introduced from the outside connected to the cold water tank and the water tank water supply and the cold water tank a water supply unit including a water supply hose supplied to a water tank water supply and at least one water supply valve positioned to be connected to the cold water tank to supply the cold water stored in the cold water tank to the small vending machine at the request of the small vending machine and and a case unit configured to surround the freezing unit and the water supply unit a water tank water supply fixing support for supporting the water tank water supply unit a power supply for supplying electrical energy necessary for the freezing unit and the water supply unit and a controller for controlling the freezing unit and the water supply unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200407276-Y1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "a refrigerating unit including an evaporator which absorbs surrounding heat while subliming the refrigerant in a high pressure gas liquid mixed state into a gas of low temperature and low pressure cold water tank for supplying the purified cold water required for the water tank of the small vending machine cold water tank for maintaining the water supplied by the freezing unit cold purified cold water introduced from the outside connected to the cold water tank and the water tank water supply and the cold water tank a water supply unit including a water supply hose supplied to a water tank water supply and at least one water supply valve positioned to be connected to the cold water tank to supply the cold water stored in the cold water tank to the small vending machine at the request of the small vending machine and a case part configured to surround the freezing part and the water supply part a water tank water supply fixing support for supporting the water tank water supply a power supply for supplying electrical energy necessary for the freezing part and the water supply part and a controller for controlling the freezing part and the water supply part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210318-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "can be maintained to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468890-Y1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "therefore the user can adjust the temperature controller 32 so that the water w heating temperature in the steam tank 10 can be arbitrarily set to be heated whereby the water w appropriately according to the freezing state of the freezing pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804115-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "therefore when the temperature around the water tank is lowered in the winter season the water supplied to the water tank maintains the temperature of the image according to the driving signal supplied from the control box 92 and the power source and it is possible to prevent the water tank from being deformed or broken by freezing the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368217-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition according to the present invention when embedding the detection conduit 52 between the water supply pipe 50 and the support 10 the surface close to the support 10 is maintained by the thermal insulation means 20 the surface of the ground which is greatly affected by the atmospheric temperature it prevents freezing by heat insulation without losing heat and also transmits geothermal heat to the internal space 11 of the support 10 to compensate for insufficient heat insulation effect of the thermal insulation materials 21 and 22 and internal space"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337708-B2", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the green energy water manufacturing device according to claim 4 wherein the hydroxide ions that are separated by the ion separation device are conducted through a venturi tube that is connected to the ion separation device into the ion emulsification device the ultrasonic wave emission source of the ion emulsification device emitting ultrasonic waves to the hydroxide ions to cause emulsification and thus fast dissolution of the hydroxide ions into water to thereby form high concentration alkaline green energy water the water conducted into the venturi tube being cooled by a water cooling device to have temperature of the water controlled within a range between freezing point and room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337708-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the hydroxide ions that are separated by the ion separation device are conducted through a venturi tube that is connected to the ion separation device into the ion emulsification device and the ultrasonic wave emission source of the ion emulsification device emits ultrasonic waves to the hydroxide ions to cause emulsification and thus fast dissolution of the hydroxide ions into water to thereby form high concentration alkaline green energy water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337708-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "above the freezing point in order to increase the half life period of the hydrogen ions and make the ions fast dissolving in the cold water to form high concentration acidulous green energy water 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101997339-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "when the flow rate in the pipe is stopped the power supplied to the heater is cut off and the operation power of the heater is limited in proportion to the temperature signal inputted through the temperature sensor if the system is for the purpose that to maximize electrical efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "US-12231085-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the moisture collection layer 40 may additionally and or alternatively prevent the energy dissipating receiver 20 from cracking and or freezing such as during circumstances when there are large temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the site at which the air seal is located is selected so that said seal lies on a level in the drain where freezing would not normally occur because water flowing through the pipes connected to the drain maintains said location at a temperature somewhat above freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "another important aspect of the bi metallic disk is that after the predetermined temperature of for example 36 has been reached and the disk has warped to break the electrical contact of the switch the disk will maintain the warped shape until manually re set"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569861-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for suppressing freezing and bursting of water facilities including water pipes and water meters a disposition step of arranging a phase change material pcm outside the water facility to suppress external exposure of the water facility prior to the placement step a crushing step of adding the phase change material to water and pulverizing the phase change material a shell forming step of forming a capsule by adding a synthetic resin to a mixture of the water and the phase change material and a separation of separating the capsule from the mixture further comprising an encapsulation step comprising the step the phase change material is a paraffin type the phase change material is undecane dodecane tridecane tetradecane pentadecane hexadecane hexadecane heptadecane octadecane nonadecane and eicosane the encapsulating step further comprises a step of maintaining the mixture at room temperature for a predetermined time prior to the separating step prior to the placement step further comprising a filling step of filling the capsule inside the pouch and sealing the pouch the placement step is a wrapping step of wrapping the water pipe with the pouch filled with the capsule inside the water meter is accommodated in the inner space of the water meter box the disposing step includes an installation step of disposing the pouch filled with the capsule between an inner surface of the water meter box forming the inner space and the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569861-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "due to freezing of water facilities by suppressing freezing of water facilities in the winter season have1 is a schematic flowchart of a method for suppressing freezing and bursting of a water facility according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569861-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the freezing occurrence time of the water pipe wp was confirmed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the second zion area 152 of the freezing prediction zion sheet 150 a second information transmission cover 152a is formed in a basic color in the third zion area 153 of the freezing prediction zion sheet 150 a third information transmission cover 153a is formed in a basic color the second zion area 152 is changed to a second color except for the second information transmission sign 152a when the second set temperature is lower than or equal to the second color while the second information transmission sign 152a is displayed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore if the temperature outside of the cold weather winter season plummets there is a risk that the water meter will freeze"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "fifth instead of simply changing the color based on the outside temperature at which the water meter is installed it is appropriate to increase the reliability of freeze prediction by making it possible to inform the possibility of freezing based on the temperature of tap water passing through the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "fifth rather than simply changing the color based on the outside temperature at which the water meter is installed it is possible to increase the reliability of freeze prediction even more by allowing the possibility of freezing to be based on the temperature of tap water passing through the water meter.1 is an external view of a water meter 100 equipped with a prediction sheet for freezing waves according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "according to this since the color does not change based on the outside air temperature at which the water meter is installed the temperature of the tap water passing through the water meter is measured and thus there is an advantage of making the prediction of the possibility of freezing more reliable"}, {"pat_id": "US-9605904-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the processor may calculate the dew point for the primary air flow based on the at least one environmental condition sensed by the at least one sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101464954-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the inside of the casing is frozen an elastic sheet and an elastic pad are provided on the bottom surface of the counter and the bottom surface of the impeller housing so as to relieve the expansion pressure however since the buffering action is performed only by the material of the elastic sheet and the elastic pad the expansion pressure due to the freezing can not be sufficiently mitigated and the number of parts increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101504545-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "on the other hand by installing a temperature sensor to prevent freezing of the water purification equipment in case of installation in the winter or cold weather areas it is possible to prevent damage to facilities by freezing membranes and system protection devices for mobile water treatment devices bars are untested"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101369585-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as a result when the temperature decreases the water existing inside the main body of the water meter freezes and the volume expands and the pressure increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101369585-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in recent years the temperature drop sharply occurs especially due to the abnormal temperature and this causes the water meter freezing frequency to increase significantly"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0738408-Y2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore while suppressing the waste of tap water as much as possible as a device that prevents freezing with no maintenance cost a faucet as seen in kaisho 62 156445an electric valve is installed in the bypass pipe that connects the upstream side of therutotomoni a temperature sensor thatdetect the outside air temperatureis provided the outside airwhen the temperature reaches around 0 c the electric power is applied at a constant cycle.the water in the water pipe is intermittently opened by opening the valve for a short time.a device that discharges water from the bypass pipe to the outsideis proposed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194416-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "another object of the present invention is to maintain the temperature of the fluid through the housing provided in the first double pipe the second double pipe the valve meets each other and to prevent the freezing of the water pipe to prevent freezing of the water pipe in winter to provide a structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541137-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "the control unit 500 may apply a driving signal to the fan 100 when the temperature of the ballast water w sensed by the sensor unit 300 becomes lower than a preset freezing point of the ballast water w"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541137-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "3 when the temperature of the ballast water w sensed by the sensor unit 300 becomes higher than the freezing point of the preset ballast water w the control unit 500 outputs a drive stop signal can be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100960607-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "since the outside air temperature drops to below zero in winter it must be accompanied with proper insulation to prevent freezing of the water meter and the water pipe connected to the water meter and a configuration that can be opened to read the amount of usage in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702920-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "because of the lack of material cases of freezing and freezing of the meter often occurred resulting in failure to maintain proper function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102263501-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present disclosure relates to a water meter freeze protection cover and more particularly to a water meter freeze protection cover for preventing the water meter from freezing due to a decrease in external temperature in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102263501-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in a situation where the external temperature is lowered such as in winter the water flowing inside the main body of the water meter freezes and expands so the freezing force may damage the glass cover of the totalizer or damage the totalizer itself"}, {"pat_id": "US-11976446-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "empirical testing has determined that modest power on the order of five watts will produce a temperature differential of thirty degrees fahrenheit or more in the spigot body which is sufficient to prevent freezing at temperatures of zero degrees fahrenheit or less"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101432240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the inside of the casing is frozen an elastic sheet and an elastic pad are provided on the bottom surface of the counter and the bottom surface of the impeller housing so as to relieve the expansion pressure however since the buffering action is performed only by the material of the elastic sheet and the elastic pad the expansion pressure due to the freezing can not be sufficiently mitigated and the number of parts increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008089-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "use cloth old clothes or cloth to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008089-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in addition according to the wireless communication terminal system and a method of driving the built in smart metering based temperature sensor according to the present invention the management server transmits the status information of the water meter to the user terminal according to the temperature information of the water supply pipe transmitted from the wireless communication terminal therefore the effect that the user can prevent the freezing of the water pipe in advance is also obtained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100513311-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "water meter protection container is a device to prevent the water meter from freezing or being damaged by external impact in the winter when the temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "US-7510656-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "submerged combustion heaters or other heat sources may be used to raise water temperature as desired such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102131865-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in order to prevent freezing from freezing the valve control shaft and the cooling air transmitted from the water exposure pipe are basically blocked to prevent freezing due to the cold in winter resulting in a reflux of the reflux with a cold air blocking water distribution engine having an insulating layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "during this freezing process water molecules crystallize to form a lattice structure which allows the ice layer 60 to float on top of the water 10 while rejecting salt organic compounds minerals or other impurities into the water 10 beneath the layer of ice 60"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "water meter 300a 300b 300c and 400 may analyze air temperature and allow a user to view whether an attic basement or well house may be nearing freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101423708-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in the conventional water meter due to the icing of the inside of the winter casing having a low temperature frequent occurrence of freezing accidents occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101423708-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "by providing the pads the expansion pressure is relieved by the buffering action of the elastic sheet and the elastic pad thereby preventing the water meter from being damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101423708-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "10 0926266.the present invention relates to a water meter which is capable of reducing the expansion pressure caused by the freezing of the interior of a winter casing having a low temperature in a prior art water meter thereby remarkably decreasing the functionality and durability of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101423708-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition the elastic cover 50 is a function of preventing the frost accident of the water meter by relieving the inflation pressure due to the freezing of the inside of the winter casing 10 having a low temperature as shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101423708-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "thus when the inside of the winter casing having a low temperature is frozen the expansion pressure due to freezing is sufficiently mitigated thereby preventing the accident of the water meter from being frozen"}, {"pat_id": "US-10410501-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the water use and water energy use can use non invasive flow and temperature sensors for monitoring and thus no cutting into the water pipe is necessary"}, {"pat_id": "US-5538031-A", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "this procedure fills the pipes with antifreeze thereby preventing freezing of fluid within the pipes when the outdoor temperature falls below thirty two degrees fahrenheit or zero degrees celsius"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "10 is extended to the outside through the through hole 21a and the waterproof clamp 20 to prevent the water flowing through the fire water supply pipe 3 a backflow pipe 30 having both ends connected to the front and rear ends of the fire water supply pipe 30 so as to communicate with the front and rear ends of the installation position of the heater 10 a pump 40 connected to the backflow pipe 30 so that water flowing through the firefighting water supply pipe 3 flows back through the backflow pipe 30 the waterproof clamp 20 is formed in a semi circular shape the through hole 21a is formed the inner peripheral surface is provided with a waterproof portion 21 having a packing 21b for blocking the periphery of the through hole 4 and the bolt 22 combination with the waterproof portion 21 is composed of a semi circular fixing portion 23 for fixing the waterproof portion 21 to the circumferential surface of the fire water supply pipe 3 the power supply system rechargeable battery 50 is applied to the charge is connected to the heater 10 and the auxiliary heater 10 to supply power a control unit 60 for controlling charging and discharging of the rechargeable battery 50 and operations of the heater 10 and the pump 40 a water temperature sensor 70 around the heater 10 and fixedly installed on an inner circumferential surface of the fire water supply pipe 3 so as to be positioned at a circumference of the heater 10 it includes a detection sensor 80 for detecting the operation of the fire fighting equipment connected to the fire water supply pipe 3 the control unit 60 receives the signals of the water temperature sensor 70 and the sensor 80 to prevent the water heater 10 from freezing only water around the heater 10 when the water temperature is lower than the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "do not freeze only the surrounding water to prevent freezing of the fire water supply pipe 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101029692-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the remaining water inside the inside is discharged to the ground through the discharge hole 130 to prevent freezing even if the outside air temperature is low"}]</data>
</edge>
