e 41 and is installed so that the stirring blade 41 is introduced into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 through the upper portion of the sludge drying tank 10 thereby stirring sludge or wastewater containing the sludge that has flowed into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 and the sludge drying tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714293-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "according to one aspect of the present invention a steam heat sludge drying device is provided which is applied to a sludge drying and treatment system and recovers steam heat generated in a water treatment process using high heat to dry sludge with the steam heat the steam heat sludge drying device comprising a sludge drying tank 10 a steam jacket 20 which is installed to form a steam passage continuously connected to the outside of the sludge drying tank 10 and which is composed of a side jacket shell 20a covering a side of the sludge drying tank 10 and a bottom jacket shell 20b covering the bottom of the sludge drying tank 10 a sludge inlet 11 which is installed on one side of the upper end of the sludge drying tank 10 and into which sludge or wastewater including sludge flows in a sludge outlet 12 formed in a lower tank exposure area where the side jacket shell 20a is omitted among areas adjacent to the lower end of the sludge drying tank 10 a sludge outlet opening closing unit 30 comprising a closer 32 for blocking the sludge outlet 32 and a hydraulic cylinder 34 for opening and closing the sludge outlet 12 by moving the closer 32 between a position for blocking the sludge outlet 12 and a position for opening the sludge outlet 12 a steam inlet 21 formed on the upper portion of the side jacket shell 20a to allow steam to flow into the steam passage a condensate outlet 22 formed on the bottom jacket shell 20b to allow condensate in which steam is condensed to be discharged an agitator 40 including a stirring blade 41 and a motor 42 for rotating the stirring blade 41 and installed such that the stirring blade 41 is introduced into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 through the upper part of the sludge drying tank 10 thereby stirring sludge or wastewater containing the sludge that has flowed into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 a plurality of support columns 52 that extend downward from the bottom surface of the sludge drying tank 10 and are watertightly welded into a plurality of joining holes formed in the bottom jacket shell 20b a side fixing structure 54 that secures the side jacket shell 20a and the sludge drying tank 10 in a spaced state a manhole 14 formed at the upper part of the sludge drying tank 10 to allow a worker to enter the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 a manhole cover 60 installed to block the manhole 14 a viewing window 15 installed on one side of the upper portion of the sludge drying tank 10 a lighting window 16 installed adjacent to the viewing window 15 to allow the transmission of light irradiated from a lighting device a steam passage temperature sensor 71 installed on the side jacket shell 20a to measure in real time the temperature of steam flowing into the steam passage a steam passage pressure sensor 72 installed on the side jacket shell 20a to measure in real time the pressure of the steam passage a condensate temperature sensor 73 installed on the bottom jacket shell 20b to measure the temperature of condensate a tank temperature sensor 74 installed on the upper portion of the sludge drying tank 10 to measure in real time the internal temperature of the sludge drying tank 10 a tank pressure sensor 75 installed on the upper portion of the sludge drying tank 10 to measure in real time the internal pressure of the sludge drying tank 10 and it includes a controller 5 that controls the operation of the steam heat sludge dryer 1 by using data transmitted from the steam passage temperature sensor 71 the steam passage pressure sensor 72 the condensate temperature sensor 73 the tank temperature sensor 74 and the tank pressure sensor 75"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714293-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "it further includes a side fixing structure 54 formed to guide steam from a steam inlet to a condensate outlet while fixing a shell 20a and a sludge drying tank 10 in a spaced state a manhole 14 formed on the top of the sludge drying tank 10 to allow a worker to enter the inside of the sludge drying tank 10 a cover body 61 joined by a fastener to block the manhole 14 a manhole cover 60 including the cover body 61 and a hot air blower 90 installed in the cover body 61 to blow high temperature hot air into the inside of the sludge drying tank 10 through the manhole 14"}, {"pat_id": "US-8075652-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the compressor chamber 3 is completely separated from the mixing chamber 2 by bottom panel 9 for preventing hot air penetration from compressor chamber 3 into the air mixing chamber 2 which can result in changes of predetermined temperature regimes of the condenser and evaporator"}, {"pat_id": "US-8075652-B2", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "as a result of heat exchange the air mixture is heated and evacuated outside and the vapor of the refrigerant transforms into liquid and then passes through the temperature regulating valve trv 24"}, {"pat_id": "US-8075652-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "thus the water generation purification and its pumping to the tank of water dispensing block continues"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687400-B1", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "in this way by collecting and accumulating the temperature difference between the inside temperature and the outside temperature in real time to build big data it is possible to predict the time to block odor by analyzing the time and conditions of high concentration odor occurrence"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "steam tracing as in a pipeline of fuel oil the liquid will be expanded or contracted according to the change in liquid temperature and consequently the pressure within the block will be increased or decreased"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "however when there is a change in the liquid temperature the amount of leakage must be calculated from the rate of passing the liquid to or from the block taking into account a volume change due to a change in the liquid temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "however if the liquid temperature of the block 1 decreases the liquid is supplied to the block through the means for measuring the flow rate in an amount of the liquid corresponding to the reduction in the liquid volume due to the decrease in the liquid temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498578-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "depending on the quality of raw water the first block 1 may be omitted"}, {"pat_id": "US-4351651-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "as the temperature of the exiting air increases the curl of strips 60 increases to thus more and more block the flow of air between the top and bottom portions of exit pipe 24 to thus provide a fluid restriction and cause a longer transit and residence time to air passing through cold air exchanger 16 of the present system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101030980-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "figure 1 shows a block diagram of a conventional water quality multi item measuring device of water purification equipment the signal detected from a plurality of sensors s1 s5 for measuring temperature ph turbidity residual chlorine concentration and electrical conductivity respectively is transferred to the main control unit 7 through the sensor transducers 1 to 5 and the analog signal lines 6 and the ad conversion unit inside the main control unit 7 transmits the analog signal inputted through the analog signal lines 6 8 converts the signal into a digital signal and processes the signal in the main control unit 7 to make digital data and the main control unit 7 displays these data via the lcd display unit 9 and simultaneously communicates with rs 232c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101030980-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "figure 2 shows the overall block diagram of the water quality multi item measuring device 20 according to the present invention as shown in figure 2 temperature ph turbidity residual chlorine concentration and electrical conductivity in the water treatment plant and the reservoir of the water purification plant in order to measure the items of water quality such as the measured number of samples to be supplied to each sensor measuring sensor unit 21 for measuring each water quality items and each signal measured by the measuring sensor unit and the respective sensors and the digital sensor converts the digital data into digital data using the calibration factor stored for each sensor and transmits the signal to the main control unit 23 via the sensor interbase unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 1