tially for a hot water pipe p"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "oxygen management block an oxygen control block for generating an oxygen supply control signal corresponding to the measured dissolved oxygen concentration when the measured dissolved oxygen concentration is less than the preset discharge allowable dissolved oxygen concentration oxygen supply means for supplying pressurized air to a predetermined depth position based on the oxygen supply control signal a green algae management block that monitors whether the measured surface layer water temperature the middle layer water temperature and the lower layer water temperature are outside the preset allowable temperature difference range and instructs a corresponding green algae alarm when the preset allowable temperature difference is out of range an alarm generation block for generating a green algae generation alarm for alarming that green algae is generated by an increase in nutrients caused by a conductive phenomenon in which the surface layer and the lower layer are mixed based on the commanded green algae alarm and sending the green algae generation alarm to the management means the management means for operating each winch installed in each of the plurality of winch machine rooms when the floodgate opening request signal is received to open the corresponding movable walkway gates and visually generating a green algae alarm when the green algae generation alarm is received"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_252", "text": "the water temperature algae concentration and organic pollutant concentration may be selectively delivered to the oxygen control block 404 and the algae management block 410"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_253", "text": "to this end the sensor block 402 as shown in figure 5 for example dissolved oxygen sensor 501 water temperature sensor 502 chlorophyll a sensor 503 water temperature weak layer sensor 504 orp oxidation reduction potential ec sensor 505 electric conductivity ec sensor 506 toc sensor 507 ss sensor 508 na sensor 509 cod sensor 510 tp sensor 511 tn sensor 512 flow sensor 513 ph sensor 514 turbidity sensor 515 light intensity sensor 516 alkalinity sensor 517 nh 4 n sensor 518 po 4 the p sensor 519 the cl sensor 520 the fe 2 sensor 521 the air temperature sensor 522 the residence time sensor 523 the water level sensor 524 and the like may be included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_257", "text": "the measurement may be continuously performed according to a set cycle and then transferred to the oxygen management block 404"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_276", "text": "next the green algae management block 410 compares the water temperature difference between the surface layer water temperature the middle layer water temperature and the lower layer water temperature measured by the water temperature sensor and the preset allowable water temperature difference range and the water temperature surface layer water temperature when the middle layer water temperature and the lower layer water temperature difference is determined to be out of the preset allowable temperature difference range the alarm generation block 412 may provide a function of instructing a corresponding green algae alarm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384971-B1", "para_id": "para_295", "text": "here algae related sensors may include for example chlorophyll a sensor 503 ss sensor 508 turbidity sensor 506 and the like and organic contaminant related sensors may include for example water temperature medicine layer sensor 504 orp and the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-7160469-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "another possible variation is creating conditions of some under pressure in the area surrounding the cylinder for example by appropriate pump or bellows and or increasing the temperature in order to even further reduce the amount of air that is around during the fast fluctuation process so that even larger droplets can evaporate more quickly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439863-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore in the conventional washing machine generating apparatus 200 of the washing machine the washing rate is lowered in the winter when low temperature tap water is supplied while a part of the electrolyte that is not dissolved is collected around the drain hole 101 to block drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102812276-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "although the preferred embodiments of the present invention have been described in detail above the scope of the present invention is not limited thereto and various modifications and improvements made by those skilled in the art using the basic concept of the present invention defined in the following claims also fall within the scope of the present invention.g1 landfill layer g2 cover layer 1 leachate recovery section 11 leachate plate 111 leachate channel 12 blocking member 13 leachate drain 2 leachate purification unit 21 leachate inlet line 22 purification unit 211 purification body 211a 1st body 211b 1st purification space 211c 2nd body 211d 2nd purification space 222 ceramic filter 223 1st activated carbon layer 224 2nd activated carbon layer 225 zeolite layer 226 silica sand layer 227 compartment filter 23 purification storage 231 storage space 24 natural stone 25 heating section 3 landfill gas recovery section 31 gas pipe 311 through hole 32 flow pipe 33 landfill gas purification unit 34 storage tank 35 landfill gas pump 36 control valve 4 high temperature sterilization unit 41 steam generator 42 storage unit connection line 43 steam line 44 steam pump 5 uv sterilization section 51 substrate section 52 uv ray generation unit 6 dust suppression unit 61 spray line 62 drum 63 spraying unit 64 supply pipe 65 spray pump 7 wheel washing unit 71 tunnel section 711 car wash area 711a entrance 711b exit 72 lower wash section 73 side wash section 74 rear wash section 741 hinge block 742 shaft 743 drive motor 744 spray pipe 744a vertical pipe 744b horizontal pipe 75 front wash section 76 wash water supply storage unit 77 sterilization wash unit 78 dry car wash unit 79 car wash water recovery unit 8 pedestrian safety section 8a pedestrian safety passage 81 outer structure 811 entrance 82 frame section 821 pedestrian passage 83 roof 84 blocking 85 1st rail section 86 2nd rail section 87 frame drive unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5646863-A", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "to reduce the effect of organic contamination on the electrode surfaces an absorptive stripping voltage combined with a unique voltage is applied to measuring cell working electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102061131-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rectangular heating element for dissipating heat in accordance with the supply of power a rectangular heating element housing in which an electric cable connection hole is formed at one side and the bottom surface is concave so as to have a predetermined curvature while the heating element is inserted and wrapped therein an upper cover having an upper surface having a curved flat shape having a predetermined curvature and a lower surface protruding integrally formed with an insertion groove for fitting and coupling an upper end of the heating element housing a lower cover coupled to a lower portion of the upper cover to surround the heating element housing and having a through hole formed at a bottom thereof so that the heating element housing is partially exposed a thermal pad provided in a space between the upper cover and the heating element housing to block heat exchange with the outside a bimetal provided in an inner space of the heating element housing to automatically block a temperature rise of the heating element a heat transfer pad further coupled to a bottom surface of the heat generator housing to expand a heat transfer area of the heat generator housing or to be contacted along a curved surface of the pipe and the electrical cable connection hole of the heating element housing is provided in pairs one side of the connection hole includes a power member is drawn into the housing and the other connection hole includes a lamp member drawn out of the housing to indicate the operating state of the heating element strip connecting holes for connecting the strip of the pipe band is further formed at both edges of the upper cover the lamp member has a structure in which the lamp is coupled to the end of the bellows type cable having a predetermined length the heat transfer pad has a rectangular flexible metal belt structure as a whole pads are integrally formed at regular intervals on both left and right sides of the body portion constituting the center line of the metal belt structure and connecting strips of pipe bands to the end of the pad portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161642-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "pump 4 a sterilizing filter 9 for sterilizing bacteria contained in the filtered purified water while passing through the filter a display setting unit 11 for displaying temperature and operating conditions and a cold water storage tank 14 the cold water temperature sensor 14 for measuring the purified water temperature of the hot water the hot water temperature sensor 15 for measuring the purified water temperature of the hot water storage tank 12 and the purified water temperature stored in the hot water storage tank 12 are raised"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100421172-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a wastewater treatment apparatus capable of storing and treating waste a hot air spraying unit in which a plurality of micropores are formed along an end circumferential surface of the hot air guide tube so as to finely spray hot air into the wastewater stored in the evaporative concentration tank to activate contact with the wastewater a sludge flow preventing plate which is horizontally disposed at a predetermined interval from a lower circumference of the lower end of the sludge flow preventing drum and a bottom surface of the evaporation concentration tank to block the settled sludge from floating and by forcibly circulating the heated wastewater in the evaporation condenser to be introduced again to the upper portion and then sprayed downward to preheat the wastewater supplied from the wastewater storage tank to prevent the deterioration of the hot air guide tube and at the time of heating the wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_441", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may receive a sump temperature value and a low pressure vapor temperature value in block 7274"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_460", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_465", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may in block 7392 receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_524", "text": "if in block 6878 the sump temperature value is either greater than the target or greater than the minimum sump temperature threshold the sump adjuster pid output may be set to zero in block 6882"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_525", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from for example a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_571", "text": "as shown in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_571", "text": "and the delta between the source or sump temperature and desired temperature may be used to calculate the power required in block 6596"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_574", "text": "any pre existing fluid in the bearing feed conduit may be purged and the conduit may be brought up to the temperature of the purified water in block 6574"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_575", "text": "if in block 6578 the temperature indicated by the bearing feed flow sensor 6562 drops beyond a predefined value an error may be generated in block 6580"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_575", "text": "if in block 6578 temperature does not drop below this value operation may continue in block 6582 as the data indicates flow in the bearing feed conduit is as expected"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_584", "text": "in block 7528 the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_591", "text": "in block 7832 the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor s 6082a d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_594", "text": "in some embodiments the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_595", "text": "in some embodiments if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a d are less than the threshold the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_598", "text": "if in block 7604 flow of source water into the system 6000 exists the temperature of the source water may be obtained from a source water temperature sensor 6036 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_600", "text": "obtaining the temperature of the water source in block 7652 may include reading an output from one or more sensor such as a source water temperature sensor 6036 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_603", "text": "in block 6718 a delta between the target temperature and the temperature indicated by the electronics temperature sensor may be input to a pid loop run by the controller 6034"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_604", "text": "if in block 6724 the sensor data indicates that the current temperature of the electronics housing is greater than a high temperature limit the target temperature value may be set to a low temperature limit in block 6726"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_604", "text": "if instead in block 6728 the sensor data indicates that the current temperature of the electronics housing is less than the low temperature limit the target temperature value may be set to the high temperature limit in block 6730"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_608", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_609", "text": "if in block 8016 the system 6000 is not in a production start up state in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_609", "text": "in block 8022 the blowdown temperature target may be fed to a blowdown temperature control loop along with a current perhaps low pass filtered value of the temperature of blowdown exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may use the output from the blowdown temperature control loop as the extra source valve command value in block 8024"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "if the measured temperature value exceeds the reference temperature value this is an emergency situation in which a fire may soon occur"}, {"pat_id": "US-4940549-A", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "or at least to some elevated temperature prior to introduction to a stage i treatment tank 18 as shown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266383-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "it prevents water meter from freezing even during the cold winter season and it saves much manpower and time due to reconstruction.when it is used for a long time the protection box is cracked or damaged due to earth pressure or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100458619-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the non excavation overall repair method of supplying the impregnating tube to the inside of the molding apparatus and supplying compressed air or water to harden and cure the impregnated tube in the pipeline with hot water supplied by expanding the impregnated tube in the pipeline installing a forming end 50 having a forming hole 52 at one end of the tube 40 mixing the fast curable unsaturated resin with f a and materials with the impeller device 70 impregnating the tube 40 into the mixed quick curable unsaturated resin and f a and material installing a wholesaler device 60 to block the conduit 2 of the manhole 1 to prevent excessive extension of the impregnation tube 40 after connecting the forming end 50 to the impregnating tube 40 the impregnating tube 40 in the forming apparatus 10 by bending 90 toward the conduit 2 in the inside of the manhole 91 and injecting air to reverse insert step non excavation pipeline repair method using a molding end and a bottom wholesale characterized in that it comprises the step of lining in the pipe line 2 by supplying a water temperature of 85 to the reverse insert impregnated tube 40"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4031800-B2", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in the present invention the supercooling release means 3 may be a conventional supercooling release plate formed in a plate shape a block having a plane on which supercooled wastewater collides or other shapes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100339649-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in other words the water meter 7 exposed to the outside is covered with a heat insulating member 5 6 and a cover 2 3 and covered with a lid 4 to block the cold air and temperature of the outside to maintain the heat retention it is to prevent the malfunction or breakage of the instrument of the water meter 7 installed in 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0168514-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "it recovers energy from the discharged water and covers it with a glass greenhouse to keep it warm and at the same time it uses solar heat to minimize the maintenance cost in winter while maintaining the optimal temperature for trees to grow in the glass greenhouse"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100529024-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the purification filter unit 43 is provided in such a way that the titanium dioxide block 44 forming a plurality of through holes alternately with an ultraviolet lamp 45 such as a uv fluorescent lamp thereby providing internal air according to the operation of the exhaust fan 46"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102549174-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "depending on the quality of raw water the first block 1 may be omitted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255667-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in addition during the summer when the air temperature is high the light blocking pad 51 is closed to prevent the internal temperature of the reaction tank 10 and the temperature of the sewage or waste water from being excessively high to block sunlight from penetrating into the internal space of the housing 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100776387-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "a reinforcing member 230 through which the installation hole 233 on which the 240 is seated is provided is provided and is attached to the upper surface of the unit block 110 while being in close contact with the upper surface of the reinforcing member 230 to guide drainage of water 240 is provided and the polyethylene sheet 250 is provided to prevent the leakage of water by seating on the upper surface of the reinforcing member 230 to accommodate the seat 210 while the drain 240 is opened the polyethylene sheet 250 to prevent flow caused by shrinkage forces that occur as the temperature changes in water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432778-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the present invention was created to solve the problems of the prior art it is possible to block the external cold air double triple in a double triple configuration of the water meter protection pail a lot of external cold air between the lid and the protective pail it prevents water meter from freezing even during the cold winter season and it saves a lot of manpower and time due to reconstruction.in case of long term use the protection box is cracked or damaged due to earth pressure or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100468450-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "which is the maximum operating temperature of the membrane system may be used"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_441", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may receive a sump temperature value and a low pressure vapor temperature value in block 7274"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_460", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_465", "text": "otherwise the controller 6034 may in block 7392 receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_523", "text": "if in block 6878 the sump temperature value is either greater than the target or greater than the minimum sump temperature threshold the sump adjuster pid output may be set to zero in block 6882"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_524", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from for example a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_570", "text": "as shown in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_570", "text": "and the delta between the source or sump temperature and desired temperature may be used to calculate the power required in block 6596"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_573", "text": "any pre existing fluid in the bearing feed conduit may be purged and the conduit may be brought up to the temperature of the purified water in block 6574"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_574", "text": "if in block 6578 the temperature indicated by the bearing feed flow sensor 6562 drops beyond a predefined value an error may be generated in block 6580"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_574", "text": "if in block 6578 temperature does not drop below this value operation may continue in block 6582 as the data indicates flow in the bearing feed conduit is as expected"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_583", "text": "in block 7528 the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_590", "text": "in block 7832 the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor s 6082a d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_593", "text": "in some embodiments the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_594", "text": "in some embodiments if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a d are less than the threshold the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_597", "text": "if in block 7604 flow of source water into the system 6000 exists the temperature of the source water may be obtained from a source water temperature sensor 6036 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_599", "text": "obtaining the temperature of the water source in block 7652 may include reading an output from one or more sensor such as a source water temperature sensor 6036 see e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_602", "text": "in block 6718 a delta between the target temperature and the temperature indicated by the electronics temperature sensor may be input to a pid loop run by the controller 6034"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_603", "text": "if in block 6724 the sensor data indicates that the current temperature of the electronics housing is greater than a high temperature limit the target temperature value may be set to a low temperature limit in block 6726"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_603", "text": "if instead in block 6728 the sensor data indicates that the current temperature of the electronics housing is less than the low temperature limit the target temperature value may be set to the high temperature limit in block 6730"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_607", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_608", "text": "if in block 8016 the system 6000 is not in a production start up state in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_608", "text": "in block 8022 the blowdown temperature target may be fed to a blowdown temperature control loop along with a current perhaps low pass filtered value of the temperature of blowdown exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_609", "text": "for example the controller 6034 may use the output from the blowdown temperature control loop as the extra source valve command value in block 8024"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972396-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a lid formed of a rim shaped lower end portion an inclined rim shaped stop portion of upper and lower light beams extending from an upper portion of the lower portion and a roof completely covering the upper portion of the interrupted portion it is configured to include in the center of the ceiling inside the cover a support roller via a wire rope connecting the winch device and the protective cover is installed around the side of the floating means the concrete block and weight installed in the water pulleys passing through the connecting rope to connect is characterized in that it is installed in a plurality of equal intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972396-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a lid formed of a rim shaped lower end portion an inclined rim shaped stop portion of upper and lower light beams extending from an upper portion of the lower portion and a roof completely covering the upper portion of the interrupted portion it is configured to include in the center of the ceiling inside the cover a support roller via a wire rope connecting the winch device and the protective cover is installed around the side of the floating means the concrete block and weight installed in the water pulleys passing through the connecting rope to connect is characterized in that it is installed in a plurality of equal intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177518-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "34 and the water supply connection pipe 29 is configured to be screwed to connect without welding can not only block the penetration of harmful substances to the human body due to welding but also to form a simple structure for assembly work.as described above according to the water tank for cold and warm water purifier according to the embodiment of the present invention after forming a flange to the outside at the portion where the upper cylinder and the lower cylinder is in contact the inner space is formed by welding the upper cylinder the temperature sensor fitting hole and the cold water discharge port formed on the upper surface of the upper surface of the sensor are combined with the temperature sensor and the outflow pipe by the screw projections"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101993404-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition the curing process can be performed at the optimum temperature and pressure conditions and immediate action can be taken in the pressure and temperature changes inside the tube liner thereby obtaining a high quality curing tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101862825-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition according to another embodiment of the present invention a sodium hypochlorite generation system based on normal temperature control of liquid phase dechlorination and backflow prevention of chlorine injection has an inverse number in response to shortage of water supply pressure due to chlorine injection through the vacuum pressure of the injector this prevents chlorine and water from being corroded.fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948131-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "moreover in some embodiments the control sub system 50 may determine fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 based on sensor data determined by a fluid temperature annulus sensor 54 process block 118"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102602389-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should include not only the above embodiments but also other variously modified embodiments according to the technical spirit of the invention described in the claims below.10 body 11 protruding end 11a 1st pass 11b second pass 11c third pass 12 1st peduncle 13 printed circuit board 20 water tank 21 exterior wall 22 inner wall 23 insulation 24 receptor 25 second peduncle 30 connection information board 31 1st wit home 32 2nd wit home 33 self adhering member 40 temperature sensor 50 sterilization lamp 60 water level sensor 70 cooling means 71 thermoelectric element 72 cooling rod 73 water cooler 73a water block 73b first connection hose 73c second connection hose 73d radiator 73e circulation pump 73f cooling fan 80 water fountain 81 water nozzle 82 water level control ball 83 auxiliary water nozzle 90 water supply means 91 proximity sensor 92 water pump 93 water hose 100 height adjustable 110 recovery stand 111 recovery plate 111a drain hole 111b 1st hose passage hole 112 noise reduction hopper 112a second hose passage hole 113 filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674459-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "8 is a view showing an embodiment in which the turbulence generator according to the present invention is formed in the internal space of the injection nozzle body to generate a turbulent flow rate in the internal space based on the hot water pressure or the cold water pressure supplied from the high pressure water pump 9 is a view showing an embodiment in which a high pressure water pump according to the present invention generates pressure for transferring high pressure hot water or cold water for washing sewage water pipe while receiving power from a power transmission part for a pump fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main block having a first inlet and a second inlet each having a different flow path on one side thereof and a second outlet formed on the other side a temperature responsive member installed at one side to open and close the first inlet and vary in length while expanding or contracting according to a temperature change a first elastic member for applying an elastic force to the temperature sensitive member in a direction to close the first inlet a connecting rod protruding from the other side of the temperature sensitive member a setting block connected to the connecting rod at least one end of which is arranged to open and close the second inlet and a water inlet through which water flows and a second elastic member installed in the setting block and providing an elastic force in a direction of closing the flow path of the second inlet and a safety valve device having a function of discharging hot water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a main block having a first inlet and a second inlet each having a different flow path on one side thereof and a second outlet formed on the other side a temperature sensitive member installed on one side of the first inlet so as to open or close the first inlet and change its length while expanding or contracting with a change in temperature a first elastic member for applying an elastic force to the temperature sensitive member in a direction to close the first inlet a connecting rod protruding from the other side of the temperature sensitive member a moving block movably installed on the second inlet side flow path and formed with a water passage through which water flows in the second inlet a second elastic member for providing an elastic force to the moving block in a direction toward the outlet a catching part having water pipes through which the water passes when both ends of the catching part are caught by the catching jaws of the moving block and are spaced apart from the moving block a low temperature setting adjuster coupled to an end of the connecting rod and rotatably screwed to the latch to adjust a compression amount of the temperature sensitive member a high temperature setting adjuster rotatably installed on an inner circumferential surface of the main block to adjust a height of the main block and support the movable block to set a position of the movable block and a third elastic member provided at the latching portion the latching portion providing an elastic force in a direction to close the channel portion of the moving block and a safety valve device having a function of discharging hot water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention there is provided a portable terminal comprising a main block having a first inlet and a second inlet each having a different flow path on one side thereof and a second outlet formed on the other side a temperature responsive member installed at one side to open and close the first inlet and vary in length while expanding or contracting according to a temperature change a first elastic member for applying an elastic force to the temperature sensitive member in a direction to close the first inlet a connecting rod protruding from the other side of the temperature sensitive member and a setting block connected to the connecting rod at least one end of which is arranged to open and close the second inlet and in which a water pipe through which water flows is provided can be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the temperature sensing member and the setting block may be provided with sealing members for enhancing the sealing force between the first inlet and the second inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a portable terminal comprising a main block having a first inlet and a second inlet each having a different flow path on one side thereof and a water outlet formed on the other side a temperature sensitive member installed on one side of the first inlet so as to open or close the first inlet and change its length while expanding or contracting with a change in temperature a first elastic member for applying an elastic force to the temperature sensitive member in a direction to close the first inlet a connecting rod protruding from the other side of the temperature sensitive member a moving block movably installed on the second inlet side flow path and formed with a water passage through which water flows in the second inlet a second elastic member for providing an elastic force to the moving block in a direction toward the outlet a catching part having water pipes through which the water passes when both ends of the catching part are caught by the catching jaws of the moving block and are spaced apart from the moving block a low temperature setting adjuster coupled to an end of the connecting rod and rotatably screwed to the latch to adjust a compression amount of the temperature sensitive member and a high temperature setting adjuster rotatably installed on an inner circumferential surface of the main block to adjust a height of the movable block and to set the position of the movable block by supporting the movable block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the temperature sensing member and the moving block may be respectively provided with sealing members for enhancing the sealing force between the first inlet and the engaging portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "when the water of the faucet 10 or the water pipe is relatively low in temperature as in the winter season the water can be introduced into the main block 110 through the first water inlet 111 or may be introduced into the main block 110 through the second inlet 112 if the water in the water pipe is relatively hot"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "here the temperature sensing member 120 and the setting block 150 may be provided with a sealing member s for improving the sealing force with respect to the first inlet 111 and the second inlet 112 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "the sealing member s may be made of a rubber material and may be formed when the temperature sensing member 120 blocks the first inlet 111 or when the setting block 150 blocks the second inlet 112 it is possible to prevent water from being wasted by leakage by increasing the sealing force so that water does not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "at this time the temperature sensing member 220 and the moving block 250 may be provided with a sealing member s for improving the sealing force with respect to the first inlet 211 and the catching portion 270 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the temperature sensing member 220 may be provided with a sealing member s at one side thereof which is in contact with the first inlet 211 and may be provided at a portion of the moving block 250 which contacts the latching portion 270 a sealing member s may be provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "as a result the sensing unit 270 is separated from the moving block 250 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "5 the high temperature setting adjuster 290 may be adjusted to adjust the position of the movable block 250 to a predetermined amount in the direction of expansion expansion of the temperature sensitive member 220 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4882021-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "for this reason the heat of rainwater stored in the rainwater tank 16 moves to the tap water flowing through the tap water pipe 14 via the tap water pipe 14"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4882021-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "for this reason the heat of rainwater stored in the rainwater tank 16 moves to the liquid flowing through the liquid feeding pipe 46 via the liquid feeding pipe 46"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the conventional valve actuation systems are divided into three types pneumatic hydraulic and electrical systems in term of power systems they are relatively mature for conventional applications the conventional most fail open and or fail closed actuations are powered by springs as spring returns without monitoring devices but for some challenging applications or server services like fast pressure protection less than one or two seconds or remote pipelines or pumping stations or compression stations and subsea drilling and production offshore platform operation and subsea drilling and production or safety protections the conventional valve actuation system just cannot meet the challenges the first is the speech for isolating or releasing time is life and money for each accident the second is reliable power source availability without electricity how the modem computer driven control system would works the third is safety issue for most cylinder assembly joint they are equipped with long external bolts for containing pressure the bolts are under constantly corrosion and tension either above water or underwater the corrosion and creep can cause the cylinder assembly to fall apart and can kill the operators on the other hand for the actuation power supply the gas over oil actuators is the current solution the gas over oil actuator has a pneumatic hydraulic electric actuation combining system and is very expansive and larger and less reliable some of them conventional valve actuation system powered by natural gas cause some environment issues while the conventional valve actuation system used for subsea applications are equipped by other type of gas over oil actuators for safety valves or bop applications in fact the bop is just other type of block valve this system is powered by a group pressurized nitrogen bottles finally the actuator installation is other issue most valve is need to equipped with actuator to operate but one time consuming process is to adjust a position between the valve shaft and the joint flanges in short those systems are inefficient unreliable and expensive for example a 3000 psi pressurized bottle nitrogen on the land would become less than 1500 psi gas due to the deep water pressure and the deep water temperature and the actuation system is not reliable what if there was a deadman s switch in the bop actuation system the deepwater horizon accident could be avoided"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "this hybrid pressure protection system combines relief and block functions in one unit and not only release overpressure fluid into lower pressure zone but also isolate overpressure fluid from normal pressures zone with novel thermal actuators and simple normal open and normal closed valves this system greatly reduce total executing time and increase reliability with at least two redundancies the block subsystem has a normal open standard pressure class valve integrated with the thermal actuation system and has the isolating time less than 2 second without damaging seat and shaft seal packing the releasing subsystem has a normal closed standard pressure class valve integrated with the thermal actuation system and has the releasing time less than 2 second without damaging seat and shaft seal packing the system with redundancy feature for the valves and the actuators include at least two pressure sensing devices combination of blocking and relief at the same time greatly reduce the system cost and has the highest level of system reliability over all prior arts or existing products"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the control chamber assembly is the brain of the system in this invention it combines all control elements pre set condition sensing and judgment seamlessly as one unit at the highest level of adaptability and controllability for most control applications like the level control as the sense piston move up and down as a liquid level increase or decrease in the sensing cavity or temperature control as a temperate change in the sensing cavity the piston can move up and down or motion control and so on the control chamber assembly is based on two human brain function with two systems high level of control of the cerebrum system and a low level control of the cerebellum system at the cerebrum system the control chamber can make decision either to release restore or block the line pressure and acts with or without electric signal or power and with a self feedback function from the line pressure while at the cerebellum system it check the set pressure in the activity cavity against the line pressure in the sensing cavity with the center shutter valve safety valve the pressure sensor as redundant devices at the low level of control the valve functions become simpler and is no longer to define a block valve or relief valve just simple normal closed and normal open valves it integrates this pressure protection system at the lightest level of reliability simplicity and lowest level of barrier over all exiting pressure systems in the market or in research and over all prior arts while electronic sensor digital control wireless communication devices still can be added on this system to communicate with other devices or human through buses like profit bus foundation bus or wireless communication the control chamber system can be used for both linear or rotary actuation system and subsea bop or valve or tree well flow or pressure controls so there is no block or release but release block actuator only single control chamber system it not only increase integrity of protection system but also simplify the valve design and selection and eliminate the partial stroke testing by switching functions between normally open positions to normally closed in the two valves with full stroke test and increase the reliability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102354834-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "or it can be installed in an area where the air is polluted and can sterilize various viruses and bacteria in water or air and remove odors using a photocatalytic hydroxyl generator and install an underground buried water tank to minimize changes in external temperature it has the effect of supplying clear tap water by precipitating foreign substances such as red tap water or sand using a screen by forming a filtration device in the1 is a block diagram of the present inventors rainwater river water purification livestock house environmental pollution facility odor removal and virus sterilization complex system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102366732-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition when delivering purified water from a single water supply unit to a plurality of water tanks it can be delivered while maintaining a low temperature through the cooling unit thereby minimizing the distance limitation between the water supply unit and the water tank and using a single water supply unit it is possible to supply purified low temperature water to the dog s tank which has the effect of saving the operating cost of the farm.1 is a cross sectional view of a conventional aquaculture farm pollution prevention device 2 is a configuration diagram of a high temperature and red tide disaster prevention system in a farm according to an embodiment of the present invention 3 is a block diagram of the air supply pipe of the present invention 4 is a block diagram of a cooling unit of the present invention 5 is a cross sectional view of a heat exchanger of the present invention 6 is a cross sectional view of the air pipe of the present invention 7 is a connection diagram of a control unit of the present invention 8 is a configuration diagram of a high temperature and red tide disaster prevention system for a farm according to another embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore since the freeze preventer operates normally below the freezing temperature and the tap water is smoothly drained the entire water pipe can be protected from freezing or bursting.1 is a block diagram showing a water pipe device for preventing freezing according to a first embodiment of the present invention 2 is a block diagram showing a water pipe device for preventing freezing according to a second embodiment of the present invention figure 3 is an enlarged view of the a portion of figure 1 figure 4 is an enlarged view of the b portion of figure 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387639-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in particular since the plurality of absorption holes 5 5 5 of the bottom surface side 7 of the water meter protection tube 1 and the lower side heat insulating material 6 were formed in the same manner the water meter protection tube 1 inside together with the upper insulation 6 not only prevents the cold temperature from being transmitted but also allows the geothermal heat to flow in warmer than the ground temperature during the winter season so that the temperature inside the water meter protector 1 is similar to the geothermal heat in order to maintain the water supply it is possible to act to prevent freezing of the water meter 3 and the like and in the rainy season the water inside the water meter protection tube 1 can be easily discharged.as described above the present invention is simple in construction by preventing deformation of the rim of the water meter protector to form a lid well by forming a tapered reinforcement 9 on the round inclined surface of the side portion and the bottom surface in order to facilitate the purchase storage and loading and to form a plurality of absorbent holes in the bottom surface and the bottom insulation of the water meter protection container and to block the cold temperature transfer inside the water meter protection container with a thick formed upper side insulation material"}, {"pat_id": "US-11505478-B2", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "1 is a block diagram illustrating elements of an exemplary computing device in which embodiments of the present disclosure may be implemented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102355027-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an outer housing 10 having a frame structure having a predetermined size the inner housing 20 is installed inside the outer housing 10 the upper surface is opened to accommodate the object to be treated therein a stirring unit 30 installed horizontally inside the inner housing 20 to stir the object to be treated a driving unit 40 installed on an outer side of the inner housing 20 to rotate the stirring unit 30 a heating unit 50 installed along the inner bottom surface of the inner housing 20 to heat the inner housing 20 an air exhaust unit 60 installed on one upper side of the inner housing 20 to discharge the air of the inner housing 20 to the outside an air supply unit 70 installed inside the outer housing 10 to supply compressed air into the inner housing 20 and a controller 80 installed on one side of the outer housing 10 to control the operation of the driving unit 40 the heating unit 50 the air exhaust unit 60 and the air supply unit 70 including the stirring unit 30 a rotating shaft 31 installed to horizontally cross the inner housing 20 a plurality of fixing clamps 32 installed at predetermined intervals on the rotating shaft 31 a mounting table 33 of a predetermined length installed on the plurality of fixing clamps 32 a main stirring blade 34 installed on the mounting table 33 including the mounting base 33 is it is arranged so as to be spaced apart from another adjacent installation table 33 by 90 the main stirring blade 34 is two or more are installed so as to connect the ends of the three adjacent installation tables 33 in an arc shape to space them 180 apart in the fixing clamp 32 auxiliary stirring blades 35 of a predetermined length are installed at intervals of 90 from the mounting table 33 so that the object to be treated is stirred between the rotation shaft 31 and the main stirring blades 34 the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is the tip of the three auxiliary stirring blades 35 is connected and formed in an arc shape in the opposite direction to the main stirring blade 34 the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is the tip is installed to be inclined at a predetermined angle a to one side with respect to the fixing clamp 32 and the tip of the auxiliary stirring blade 35 is positioned in the space between the pair of installation tables 33 the heating unit 50 a rectangular shaped body 51 with an open upper surface a heater 52 installed on one side of the main body 51 and installed to have a predetermined length in a horizontal direction including in the body 51 a temperature sensor 53 for detecting the temperature of the thermal medium stored therein and an inlet and outlet pipe 54 for supplying heat medium oil to the inside of the body 51 or discharging the inside heat medium oil to the outside is provided the heating unit 50 it is installed horizontally along the middle part of the bottom surface of the inner housing 20 and is integrally fixed by welding the air exhaust unit 60 it is configured so that the air and moisture inside the inner housing 20 are discharged together the air supply unit 70 compressor 71 for generating compressed air a flow path 72 connected to the compressor 71 and a plurality of injection nozzles connected to the flow path 72 and supplying compressed air to the inside of the inner housing 20 including between the injection nozzle and the flow path 72 food characterized in that a check valve 73 is installed to allow compressed air to be discharged toward the inner housing 20 and to block moisture inside the inner housing 20 from being discharged through the flow path 72"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100670676-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition since the synthetic resin reinforcement cover 3 protects and reinforces the upper side of the upper styropole 2 it acts to block the transmission of the cold temperature outside easily such as a water meter installed inside the water meter protector it will also keep warm to prevent freezing.as described above the present invention is simple in construction the adhesive material or assembly so that the reinforcement cover and the upper styropol and the metering cap and styropole which is a synthetic resin material can be easily fixed and combined without a separate article or assembly parts it saves a lot of parts and assembly time it is easy to use the metering cap prevents damage and damage of the upper styropole and blocks the cold outside temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629806-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "during installation the winch not shown is used to pull the liner assembly 20 into the pipeline p via a winch cable 84 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131549-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in addition the collection of condensate on the surface of the condensate collecting plate 80 to maintain a lower state than the temperature of the convection to collect the condensate which is formed on both sides of the condensate collecting plate 80 while inclined similarly downward the cross section is provided in a shape so as to flow down but the lower side thereof is provided with a \uc751\ucd95 type condensate guide 75 to match the length of the condensate collecting plate 80 and then the condensate guide 75 the lower side of the is connected to the induction pipe 92 to be connected in accordance with the upper edge of the support wall 55 of the reservoir 66 formed in the block 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280209-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention is a static electricity generating element 100 for generating an electrostatic field the heat insulation tube 200 is inserted into the static electricity generating element 100 to block the internal and external temperature transfer water is introduced into the heat insulation tube 200 closing element 300 to prevent it from being the housing 400 is inserted into the heat insulating tube 200 and the closing element 300 and one side is coupled to the housing 400 and the other side is connected to the tube housing 450 the electrostatic generating element 100 is assembled in the order of the carbon cylinder 120 zinc tube 140 the carbon cylinder 120 in the pipe 150 is provided with a screw portion on the outer circumference the one side of the carbon cylinder 120 is a honeycomb structure formed with a through hole 122 therein the screw portion 121 is formed on the outer periphery is assembled with the finishing element 300 the other side having the expansion portion 125 the inner periphery is provided with a screw portion 121 is assembled to the pipe 150 the finishing element 300 is one side the threaded portion 301 is provided on the periphery and assembled with the carbon cylinder 120 and the other side is formed with the inclined surface 302 and the heat insulation pipe 200 is formed with a fine nap on the surface thereof to generate the static electricity generating element 100 and the closing element 300 is inserted and the housing connector 450 has an extension portion 455 on one side of which a screw portion 451 is provided on the inner circumference to be assembled with the housing 400 and a screw portion on the outer circumference to assemble with the tubular body"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low temperature and high pressure deep water environments and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101284178-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "reduce the temperature of the purified sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 1 the controller may be configured to block the open valve when the temperature of the water detected by the temperature detection sensor is greater than or equal to the first reference temperature after the preset opening time has elapsed since the valve is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1 the controller may block the open valve when the temperature of the water detected by the temperature detection sensor is greater than or equal to a preset third reference temperature after the preset opening time after the valve is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in particular the controller may block the open valve when the temperature of the water detected by the temperature detection sensor is greater than or equal to the first reference temperature after the preset opening time has elapsed after opening the valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "as another example the controller 14 may receive the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor unit 11 and block the valve 13 when the temperature of the water in the water pipe rises above a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102592787-B1", "para_id": "para_151", "text": "likewise the dissolution time may be determined differently depending on the temperature flow rate etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637212-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "on the other hand when the suction disk 40 is horizontally conveyed in the front rear left and right directions in the reaction tank 20 the corner round members 22 provided at the vertical corners 21 of the reaction tank 20 are slightly since the suction force of the suction disk 40 reaches the corner of the reaction vessel 20 because it has the curved surface 22a having a large diameter it helps to solve the suction blind spot.20 reactor 21 vertical corner 22 corner round member 22a curved surface 23 supersonic 23a sleep 24 sludge 24a surface 30 diffraction disk 31 end plate 32 ejection hole 33 branch pipe 34 downward cylindrical wall 36 first burring portion 37 47 kyonggi tube 39 air pipe 39a reinforcing rib 40 suction disk 41 elbow 42 inlet 44 upward cylindrical wall 46 side inlet 48 forming section 49 exhaust pipe 50 separating disk 52 54 notch 56 second burring portion 60 three dimensional transfer mechanism 62 moving frame 62a 62b vertical beam 62c upper cross beam 62d lower cross beam 64 forward backward feed mechanism 64a 64b connecting plate 66 left and right feed mechanism 66a connecting plate 68 shanghai song instrument 68a support plate 68b reinforcing plate g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 lm guide b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 lm block t1 t2 front and back padding t3 left and right padding t4 shanghai plywood r1 r2 reinforced plate e1 e2 side fixing plate u1 u2 u3 u4 bearing block l1 l2 l3 l4 feed screw m1 m2 m3 m4 servo motor d1 d2 d3 d4 rotary encoders c1 c2 c3 c4 coupling k1 k2 k3 k4 brackets n1 n2 n3 n4 nuts t4a cutting section 70 control section 71 72 73 74 motor driving part 75 heater 76 blower 80 temperature sensor p1 first pump p2 second pump s1 level sensor s2 depth sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100685017-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "in addition the aberration unit 30 for circulating the internal air so as to reduce the temperature difference of the internal space p in which the power supply unit 10 is accommodated through the inlet channel 4 one end of which is connected to the vertical channel 4a"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0752203-Y2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the unit body 1 includes a power supply circuit 4 a differential amplification circuit 5 a gain adjustment circuit 6 a schmitt circuit 7 a trigger circuit 8 and a switching circuit 9 on a substrate 14 housed in a casing 11 and the temperature sensor 2 described above is used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101338951-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "to prevent damage to the sensor the exhaust air was cooled through a condenser to condense the vapor before reaching the gas analyzer"}, {"pat_id": "US-5470460-A", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "screen 25 is installed so as to direct the coarse particles into canal 26 while allowing passage therethrough of the cyanide containing effluent and smaller suspended particles through passage 2 into the bioreactor tank 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-12043992-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the meter data may include readings from temperature sensors at the windings of the transformer"}, {"pat_id": "US-12043992-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "5 where short circuit alerts in conjunction with over temperature alerts may indicate a fire short circuit alerts with the absence of over temperature alerts tamper alerts or other alerts would indicate a flood rather than another type of event e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a method of monitoring and controlling a low carbon permeable ecological structure consisting of a plurality of corrosion resistant piles a plurality of horizontal framing frames in the form of spacers an ecological block for water purification and an ecological block for fishes and fishes first the low carbon permeable ecological installed at a predetermined position of the structure 100 receives the detected data from a plurality of sensors 210 to detect the conductivity water quality water temperature or quantity of river water by wire or wireless"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "in addition the disclosed embodiments include a system and method for improving the accuracy of a rod measurement by utilizing filler material to increase the surface area within the volume of an inlet block for keeping the fluid temperature constant during the pressure decay"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "in each case the material used to form the inlet block may be selected based on the operating conditions of the mass flow controller taking into account such considerations as operating temperature composition of gas or fluid and flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "it is noted that changes of the temperature of a compressible gas in the modified inlet block 444 may cause the gas to expand or contract and thereby result in unwanted variances in the flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature the increased surface area or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "this heat exchanger interface will help in keeping the temperature of the fluid in the modified inlet block 444 constant during the pressure decay thereby improving the accuracy of the rate of decay measurement by avoiding fluctuations in the rate that may have otherwise been cause by fluctuations in the temperature of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3774668-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "next at block 806 a functionality check of the tank temperature sensor 744 and a board temperature sensor not shown is run to determine if the sensors are operating properly within an acceptable temperature difference e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3774668-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "12 c and then as shown at block 808 the tank temperature is checked without water to determine if it exceeds a desired threshold e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "in other words in such embodiments fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40 for example via one or more external fluid conduits 62 such as a hose process block 98"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "additionally or alternatively determining the one or more fluid parameters associated with the fluid in the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 may include determining fluid temperature present within the tubing annulus 25 for example via an upstream fluid temperature sensor 58a process block 120"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "nevertheless in some such embodiments the predetermined duration threshold may be adaptively adjustable for example based at least in part on fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a controller ensures that a siphon filling programme is activated after a certain time period and uses a temperature sensor to determine the temperature in the area of the siphon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106221-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the heat insulating material 20 is seated and inserted on the upper side of the inner water meter 1 of the protective tube 10 to block the cold outside and maintain the temperature to prevent freezing of the water meter 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200408786-Y1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "on the other hand if the groundwater in the water collection pipe 122 is filled with groundwater in the conditions of low outside temperature such as winter season the groundwater may freeze and freeze so the ground water inside the water collection pipe 122 is lowered to a temperature that can freeze the state of figure 4a in order to operate the handle 134 to lower the opening and closing hole 132 as shown in figure 4b to block the distribution holes 131a 132a while opening the drain pipe 124"}, {"pat_id": "US-9370746-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "therefore when a pressure pump that delivers supply water to the ro membrane module is operated at a constant operating pressure a water volume of produced pe