ecting rod and rotatably screwed to the engaging portion and a second elastic member provided between the latching part and the main block and providing an elastic force in a direction in which the latching part is caught by the latching jaw"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention there is provided a portable terminal comprising a main block having a receiving space formed therein and having an inlet and an outlet formed on one side and the other side respectively so as to communicate with the receiving space a temperature sensitive member having one side embedded in the accommodation space for opening and closing the inlet and varying in length while expanding or contracting according to a temperature change a first elastic member provided between the temperature sensitive member and the main block to provide an elastic force to the temperature sensitive member in a direction closing the inlet port a connecting rod protruding from the other side of the temperature sensitive member a catching portion formed at the both ends of the catching jaw formed in the receiving space and having a water passage through which water flows and a setting adjusting unit coupled to an end of the connecting rod and rotatably screwed to the latching unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the flange 122 may be provided on an outer circumferential surface of the temperature sensitive member 120 so that the first elastic member 130 can be easily coupled to the temperature sensitive member 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "while the present invention has been described in connection with what is presently considered to be preferred embodiments it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed embodiments but on the contrary it is to be understood that the invention is not limited thereto.10 faucet 100 freeze prevention device 110 main block 111 accommodation space 111a jaw 112 inlet 113 outlet 114 cover part 120 temperature responsive member 121 sealing member 130 first elastic member 140 connecting rod 150 latching part 151 160 setting adjusting unit 161 bearing 170 second elastic member"}, {"pat_id": "US-11623178-B2", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "at block 720 the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11623178-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "if so the method 700 proceeds to block 740 where the controller 180 activates the auxiliary condenser 14 to expel heat from the water recovery system 10 and reduce the temperature of the one or more internal condenser coils 48 and then the method 700 proceeds to block 745"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101764073-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the heat insulating material 20 is placed between the lid 11 and the water meter 1 inside the protective barrel 10 to prevent the water meter 1 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "1b gases may be fed into the ionization chamber 44 via a gas conduit 33"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_106", "text": "via the ion source block the surfaces of conduit 150 are thus preferably maintained at temperature greater than the set point of pid 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101284179-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "reduce the temperature of the purified sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102370139-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "according to one aspect of the present invention in the strainer for spatially separating both the reaction tank for removing contaminants in the incoming wastewater and the treatment water tank for storing the treated water from which the contaminants have been removed through the reaction tank the strainer block and the strainer block are formed the first nozzle socket and the fastening structure are formed to improve the fastening force with the strainer block including the nozzle disposed in the nozzle hole and the step with the fastening structure formed on each surface the first nozzle socket on one side and the first nozzle socket on the other side it provides a strainer comprising the first nozzle socket and the strainer block and a second nozzle socket that is fastened to the nozzle on the other side and has improved fastening force.as described above according to one aspect of the present invention the temperature of the cooling water can be lowered by heat exchanging the cooling water to cool the data center with the outside while minimizing power consumption and the temperature rise due to the heat exchange with the cooling water is actively used for water treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "here q is the quantity m 3 h of the supplied constant m 3 h q 1 is the amount m 3 h of the same time period constant for the same date of the previous year and \u03b1 is the weight value for the day and \u03b2 is a weighted value for temperature correction of temperature deviation for the same date analysis of a constant increase decrease pattern of a constant due to one year temperature change in a water supply block \u03b4 is the weighted value for climate change automatically calculating the exponent value taking into account changes in the number of consecutive days and constants such as a clear day or rainfall day and \u03b5 is a large scale consumer in the waterworks block or a large water meter the number of installers and the weighted value according to the type of industry using tap water usage pattern analysis data at a specific time"}, {"pat_id": "US-12188689-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the local controller 40 may also transmit the tb measurement of the temperature sensor 32 to the load manager 48 and the index si may be computed by the load manager 48 to decide if it may interrupt or not the water heater during a power demand management request"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261190-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a water meter protection box for preventing freezing of a weighing container which is embedded in a basement and filled with a resin foam therein comprising an inner cylinder having an inner groove to seat the water pipe of the metering hopper on an outer surface thereof a height adjustment means for adjusting the height of the inner cylinder in accordance with a height of the outer cylinder to correspond to the inner groove and including a metering chamber an outer cylinder and a heat insulating material interposed between the inner passage and the outer tube to block the outside air to maintain the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3131661-B2", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "is divided into a plurality of monitoring blocks and the convection of the entire water area is determined based on the flow velocity water temperature and inflow outflow information into from each monitoring block"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3131661-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also lake water sea water river water the target water area such as dam water is divided into a plurality of monitoring blocks and the convection of the entire water area is calculated based on the flow velocity water temperature and inflow outflow information to and from each monitoring block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101703283-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "one embodiment of the configuration of the water pipe heat line control device according to the present invention is a heat line control device for controlling the supply of power to a hot line installed in close contact with a water pipe to prevent the water pipe from being frozen and includes a temperature sensor 210 and a controller 200"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing process for obtaining pure water from salt water comprising feeding salt water to a vertically arranged elongated closed tank to establish a column of salt water therein the level of which is above the feed point continuously cooling a body of mercury externally of said tank and injecting said mercury in the form of finely atomized particles into the upper portion of said liquid column withdrawing said mercury from the bottom of said tank and recirculating said mercury through said liquid column to maintain the column at a temperature which is subcooled with respect to the salt water infeed so that the infeed has ice crystals formed therein due to contact with the subcooled column permitting the ice crystals to accumulate and form a solid block of ice in the upper portion of said tank above the level of mercury injection moving said block of ice upwardly in said tank by hydraulic pressure of incoming salt water and melting the upper portion of said block of ice by indirect heat exchange with the salt water feed prior to entry of said feed into said column and withdrawing pure water from the upper portion of the tank between the top of said tank and the top of said ice block and withdrawing concentrated salt water and precipitated salts collected above the mercury from the lower portion of said tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035713-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the electronics 120 may include elements configured to receive information from the actuator m 107 temperature sensor t pressure sensor p and the like process and or store the information therein and communicate the information to a remote location via the radio module 130"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the built in electronic temperature controller 2 15 of the pcb board 2 1 detects this and supplies the electric heater of the hot water tank 2 2 and 2 3 the supply pipe of the unit chair 3 9 by operating the circulation pump 2 21 the temperature of the system main body 2 rises due to electrical heat dissipation thereby preventing the freezing of the system.the present invention is devised to solve the problems of the prior art as described above the object of the present invention is that the purified water is circulated by the circulation pump 2 21 without staying in one place attached to the scale or various sludge it is blocked by the cartridge filter 2 13 and can be treated as water warmed at the same temperature as the body temperature of the human body by the electric heater 2 3 and the temperature control device 2 15"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0088468-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "during the heat pump operation the extraction of the ice water suspension may continuously take place as well as a corresponding supply of fresh water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4808290-A", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "if pool water stops flowing through metal conduit 46 while electrical power continues to be supplied to field wiring block 366 then after approximately five minutes the temperature of metal bar 384 and thermostatic switch 386 rises above the aforementioned predetermined temperature and themostatic switch 386 opens"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "by doing so while minimizing power consumption water pipes are prevented from freezing and water supply is controlled to save water.1 is a conceptual diagram schematically showing a freeze protection system of the flush toilet according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102461368-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in addition according to another embodiment of the present invention the structure of the superheated steam forming boiler module that forms the thermal steam can take a stable structure that can minimize damage due to heat while effectively generating high temperature steam thereby reducing the working time"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4407420-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "that is since the water distribution amount on a rainy day is affected by rain the rainy day correction means 82 removes the rainy day correction coefficient to handle it as a clear day and use it as a calculated value of the average fluctuation pattern"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11229143-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore the high temperature first working liquid 51 passing through the first fluid pipeline 191 in adjacency to the first liquid inlet 11 can more effectively quickly and uniformly contact and mix with the agent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102033592-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention by appropriately selecting the temperature for each section to accurately detect the effective chlorine concentration accurately calculate the effective use time while adjusting the input amount of sodium hypochlorite aqueous solution to have a set residual chlorine concentration hypochlorous acid sodium aqueous solution can also be used as long as the time limit so that sodium hypochlorite aqueous solution can be appropriately used without waste.1 is a view showing the configuration of the use state and integrated water supply management system installed in a simple tap water intelligent intelligent chlorine input device 100 according to a first embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101583008-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "1 the bimetal 23 or 23 the heater power is directly applied to the steam generating part 20 and the power is not applied to the bimetal 23 or 23 so that the bimetal 23 or 23 can not function as a temperature sensor accordingly the bimetal 23 or 23 can not block the input of the heater power when the steam generating part 20 overheats and thus the steam thawing device can not be operated safely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a synthetic resin structure having a network structure including a plurality of pores and a water permeable base layer block comprising a porous concrete composition accommodated in the plurality of pores of the synthetic resin structure a water pocket block positioned on the permeable base layer block a water collecting tank configured to store water collected through the water permeable base layer block a sprinkler pipe positioned under the permeable base block and configured to sprinkle water stored in the water collecting tank under the permeable base block at least one sensor unit configured to measure at least one of a surface temperature and humidity of the water pocket block a water supply pump operating to supply water stored in the water collecting tank to the sprinkling pipe a communication unit configured to receive public data on one or more of weather population and vehicles of an installation area of the permeable base block from an external server and an automatic watering system using a water permeable base layer block comprising a control unit configured to control an operation of the water supply pump by further using the public data together with at least one of the surface temperature and the humidity measured by the sensor unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the automatic sprinkling system using the permeable base block according to an embodiment further includes a communication unit configured to receive public data on one or more of weather population and vehicles of an installation area of the permeable base block from an external server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "weather data api application programming interface based data to predict the road temperature and to reduce the road temperature by utilizing the latent heat of vaporization by permeating rainwater and tap water back to the lower part of the road in proportion to the predicted temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "for example the controller 130 may operate the water supply pump 140 when the current state determined through sensor data is dry compared to a set state and or the temperature is high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "in an embodiment the control unit 130 of the watering system may calculate a temperature predicted value of the installation area eg road of the permeable base block based on the acquired sensor data and or public data s3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "the water supplied to the sprinkler pipe is permeable back to the top due to the permeability of the permeable base block and serves to lower the road temperature by the latent heat of vaporization"}, {"pat_id": "US-4954151-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "vaporization of the refrigerant within the evaporator 17 absorbs heat through the freeze plate 19 from water and ice 21 in the water vessel 23 and the refrigerant temperature is essentially established by the expander 15 which may include a conventional capillary or expansion valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101758303-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "when t3 approaches t3set pumps 14 and 72 begin as shown in control action block 432 and return to 410 via control steps 433 434 and 480"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4964402-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "5 the communication unit 27 that transmits receives data to from the center facility 2 side and the operating device side such as the drive current value of the pump 4 are provided on the board provided inside"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4964402-B2", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "it is a whole block diagram of the management system of a water treatment facility.it is a schematic diagram of a manhole pump facility.it is a front view in a control box.it is a front view of a controller.it is a block diagram of a controller.it is a flowchart figure of an automatic drainage process.it is a timing chart figure which shows the drive timing of the pump by a reverse drive means.it is a block diagram of a monitoring control server.it is a facility condition screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an operating current history management screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is a pump daily report screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an alarm management screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an alarm detail screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an apparatus operation condition display screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.4 pump 6 controller 7 monitoring control server management device 13 internet communication line 14 manhole water tank 17 control box 18 water level sensor 19 temperature sensor temperature detection means 22 pump breaker 27 communication unit communication means 30 breaker sensor 33 automatic calling means 38 packet charging communication network communication network 39 information display means 51 operating current management screen 63 alarm details screen 64 device status display screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564334-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the drug feeder may include a stock solution reservoir in which the liquid polymer is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100898189-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "51 is connected to the output terminal of the signal transmission unit 51 through the drive 53 in accordance with the output information of the water level sensor 11 the oxygen sensor 12 and the temperature sensor 13 the first to sixth solenoid valves 21 22 23 24 25 26 and the hot and cold water coolers 5 6 and the first pump a micro process unit hereinafter referred to as mpu 54 that controls 31 is connected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100898189-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "figure 2b is a block diagram of the control system of the live fish tank according to the present invention the water level sensor 11 oxygen sensor 12 temperature sensor 13 salinity sensor 14 and turbidity sensor 15 is connected to a signal transmission unit 51 for focusing and transmitting the output signal of each sensor and the output level of the signal transmission unit 51 through the drive 53 through the level sensor 11 and oxygen detection first to eighth solenoid valves for adjusting oxygen hot cold water supplementary water supply and salinity according to the output information of the sensor 12 the temperature sensor 13 the salinity sensor 14 and the turbidity sensor 15 21 22 23 24 25 26 27 28 and hot cold water 5 6 and the first and second pumps 31 32 the controlling mpu 54 is connected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102030301-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the back plate 208 may have a terminal block not shown or other type of electrical connections for removably connecting the electronic brick 206 to the back plate 208"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101938119-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "by adopting the heater channel the heat insulating layer and the frp layer which are provided so as to cover the inner circumferential surface of the microbial reaction tank it is possible to block the cold heat transmitted from the ground during the cold season and to increase the temperature of the sewage introduced into the microbial reaction tank it is possible to maximize the treatment efficiency by microorganisms.1 is a view for explaining a configuration of a large capacity wastewater treatment apparatus according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11738314-B2", "para_id": "para_161", "text": "at block 1330 the method 1300 includes driving a hydroelectric system with the released pressurized water and at block 1340 refilling the vessel with water recovered from water used to drive the hydroelectric drive system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904534-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition it is possible to precisely control the temperature of the cold hot water and to compensate for the change in the ph concentration due to the temperature change of the drinking water thereby supplying the drinking water having a constant ph concentration.1 is a block diagram showing a cold warm water purifier according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101166906-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "through the present invention by maintaining the temperature of the digester and the concentration tank in the distributed urban organic waste recycling facility installed in the central heating complex by using hot water or heating circulating water in the central heating complex the variation of urban organic inflow and outflow it is possible to increase the efficiency of digesters in distributed urban organic waste recycling facilities which are difficult to maintain constant temperature because they are installed large and small digesters"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101739467-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in order to prevent this an ice seed chest ice seachest is installed in the seawater inflow section so as to block the inflow of iceberg when the seawater is inhaled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101474298-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "a valve controller 2100 may be provided to check the condition and selectively block the supply of fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008089-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "1 is a diagram illustrating an example of a system for monitoring a state of underground facilities using a manhole cover based on a low power wide area network lpwan 2 is a block diagram of a wireless communication terminal system incorporating a smart metering based temperature sensor according to the present invention 3 is a block diagram for explaining the configuration of the wireless communication terminal shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "after a block of ice is formed the temperature of the insulation chamber may be increased to melt the surfaces of the block of ice that contact the internal wall of the tank in order to facilitate vertical movement of the block of ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "4 feed water 10a is then pumped into the tank 20 to raise the block of ice 60a above at least one wall of the tank 20 and a mechanical device such as a push rod 70 or moveable arm is used to remove the block of ice 60a from the tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "after the block of ice 60a is formed the temperature of the internal walls 26 may be increased to facilitate vertical movement of the block of ice 60a by pumping a higher temperature fluid 80a not shown through the insulation intake pipe 34 and purging or removing the lower temperature fluid 80 through an insulation exhaust pipe 36"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101361104-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition facilities such as the cooling unit heat exchanger pump valve of the water treatment unit and the heat treatment unit are provided separately from the machine room it is arranged to be protected from the outside.as described above the present invention constitutes a purification treatment part of a predetermined water body of a physical treatment method of increasing dissolved oxygen do while maintaining a constant surface temperature of water in a predetermined water area using geothermal heat exchange and nanobubbles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 is a conventional temperature and humidity control system using a spray nozzle is connected to each of the plurality of water distribution supply unit 10 and the plurality of water distribution supply unit 10 provided along the longitudinal direction of the house h house a plurality of spray nozzles 20 spraying mist therein a distributor 30 connected to each of the plurality of water distribution supply units 10 to distribute water to each of the plurality of water distribution supply units 10 drive pump 40 for supplying water to the distributor 30 side the water tank 50 is connected to the drive pump 40 to store the water supplied to the distributor 30 by the drive pump 40 and a first valve 41 interposed between the driving pump 40 and the distributor 30 to supply or block the water supplied to the distributor 30 the distributor 30 and the water tank 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition another effect of the present invention is to feed back the temperature and humidity of the spraying location by controlling the supply amount of the sterilizing spray liquid supplied to the spray line has the effect of minimizing energy consumption.1 is a configuration diagram of a temperature and humidity control system using a conventional spray nozzle figure 2 is a block diagram of a first embodiment of the present invention nano fog spray system 3 is a configuration diagram of a first embodiment of the present invention nano fog spray system figure 4 is a block diagram of a nano fog spray system using the present invention hypochlorous acid figure 5 is a configuration diagram of a second embodiment of the nano fog spraying system using the present hypochlorous acid water 6 is a detailed block diagram of a controller unit applied to the present invention 7 is a detailed configuration diagram of the second controller unit applied to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "6 the controller unit 130 applied to the present invention controls the raw water pump which may be configured in the raw water supply line to supply the raw water to the raw water supply unit and to control the on and off of the filtered water supply valve 109"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "it is equipped with a compressor to allow drainage even in a building without drainage on the floor.it can be drained by air pressure.electric ball valves and strainers do not block or block pumps and pipes due to foreign substances such as hair even when water is circulated in the electrolysis tank"}]</data>
