  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a blocking network 21 is formed in the center to prevent the blockage 21 so that the sewage water 1 can flow from the top to the bottom and a vertical pipe communicating vertically with the lower part of the blocking network 21 the sewage 1 is introduced into the inlet space 11 of the main body 10 through 22"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however scaling up to a high throughput commercial volume system in a small laboratory system is a problem associated with achieving and maintaining high pressure in a large extraction vessel to provide constant pressure and temperature while maintaining constant throughput raw materials"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "due to the high temperature some of the apiin was degraded"}, {"pat_id": "US-8857473-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the flexible hose is pushed through the compression fitting towards the frozen blockage and emits a stream of water under pressure from the pump that erodes and eliminates the frozen blockage and return water is pushed from the blockage back to the return fitting and through the return hose to the container thereby providing a closed loop system"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4521319-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in this case it is possible to set the iron phosphate so as to be in a dissolved state by adjusting the ph but there is a possibility that precipitation may occur little by little in the piping or the like due to the rise in temperature or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687400-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "meanwhile unlike the spray nozzle of the cooled hexagonal water spray unit 300 which operates normally by measuring the surrounding temperature of the cooled hexagonal water spray unit 300 through the first temperature measurement sensor 410 and the second temperature measurement sensor 420 it is possible to identify and replace the spray nozzle that does not spray cooling hexagonal water due to blockage or other malfunctions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100461568-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition the reaction heat is generated due to the excessive input of the raw material causing the temperature rise of the reactor as well as the problem that the color is changed in the manufactured product.accordingly in the present invention by installing a distillation tank between the stripper and the recycling tank for treating methylamine wastewater to improve the above problems by removing the carbon dioxide and its derivatives in the low boiling organic matter through low temperature distillation of the low boiling organic matter separated from the stripper the purpose of the present invention is to provide a low boiling point organic matter recovery and purification method that eliminates the cause of salt generation when reusing the low boiling point organic matter solves the color problem of the recycled raw material and reuses the low boiling point organic material that has been incinerated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100625882-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "however if the temperature of the wall surface is lower than the precipitation temperature of the inorganic material even if the growth starts on the wall surface the precipitated inorganic material starts to melt again weakening the adhesion of the inorganic material and thus the growth of the inorganic material is limited in the present invention as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102808335-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the second aspect of the present invention is a method for treating a cleaning waste liquid discharged from a process for manufacturing an electrode of a lithium ion secondary battery by a processing device wherein the cleaning waste liquid is a suspension of a solid component an electrode material and a cleaning liquid and the processing device comprises a stirring means for stirring the cleaning waste liquid introduced from the electrode manufacturing process a feed line for drawing the cleaning waste liquid from the stirring means and an evaporation and separation means for supplying the cleaning waste liquid through the feed line and further evaporating the cleaning liquid in the cleaning waste liquid to separate the solid component and in the processing method the cleaning waste liquid is stirred by the stirring means the solid component is dispersed and the cleaning waste liquid is supplied to the evaporation and separation means thereby evaporating the cleaning liquid in the cleaning waste liquid in the evaporation and separation means to separate the solid component.according to the present invention since the washing waste liquid is supplied to the evaporation separation means in a state where the solid component is dispersed the blockage of the path or device by the solid component can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "also the air cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920177-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the membrane separation tank is converted and the phosphorus substance is ingested and removed by the microorganism a membrane unit fixed to the membrane separation tank by a membrane frame device a backwashing device connected to one side of the separation membrane unit to inject backwashing liquid into the separation membrane when the pressure rises above the pressure set in the separation membrane to prevent blockage of the separation membrane a treatment water storage tank connected to one side of the treatment water line flowing out through the membrane unit to receive and store the treatment water a suction pump connected to the treatment water storage tank to suck the treatment water a primary heat exchanger connected to the suction pump to heat cool the treated water forcibly introduced by the suction pump to a set temperature a circulation pump for circulating the treated water passing through the primary heat exchanger a heat pump connected with the circulation pump to absorb heat from the treated water and to exchange heat and then return the heat treated treated water to the treated water storage tank a heating and cooling device connected to the heat pump so as to exchange heat with the working liquid via the heat pump it provides an immersion type membrane separation apparatus and an air conditioning apparatus using the apparatus comprising a cooling and heating circulation pump for circulating the working liquid of the cooling and heating mechanism to continuously flow into the heat pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102911115-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "specifically the second water quality analysis step s5 may include a second blockage phenomenon detection step s51 for detecting a blockage phenomenon of the member 40 through the second sensor unit 70 and a pretreatment completion inspection step s52 for measuring do nitrate ammonia ph temperature water depth and pressure of the pretreated wastewater through the first sensor unit 60"}, {"pat_id": "US-5746254-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the water escape openings 25 are formed to be elongate in the vertical direction in order to preclude blockage by ice build up within the connector 10 if water accumulates and freezes within the downstream conduit section 15 right up to the connector 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "different conditions such as temperature pressure flow rate gas liquid ratio and chemical additives in the pipeline cause different formation time formation rate formation position and formation amount of hydrate in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "thus the forwardly directed stream from the nozzle 19 is particularly useful in creating an initial opening through a blockage caused by most materials"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the water heater system of claim 7 wherein the condensate collector 390 includes a drain 398 and wherein the controller 142 is further configured to determine a drain blockage of the drain 398 based on a comparison between a temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 and a temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418 when the water heater is in the heating mode optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller 142 when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "the method of claim 12 wherein the condensate collector 390 further includes a drain 398 configured to receive the condensate the method further comprising determining a drain blockage of the drain 398 by the controller 142 based on a comparison between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 and the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418 when the water heater 10 is in the heating mode optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller 142 when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the controller 142 concludes that the cause of the stagnation is a blockage somewhere in the drain assembly 90 e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the controller 142 may be configured to query the first second and third temperature sensors 114 118 122 during specific time periods of the day when determining a drain blockage or a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "for example when determining a drain blockage the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and second temperature sensors 114 118 during morning hours when it is most likely the user will require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "alternatively the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "in particular when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "thus the invention provides among other things a water heater 10 including a control system 38 338 configured to detect an error in the water heater 10 such as a leakage or a drain blockage by utilizing and or comparing temperature readings of condensate flue gases and outside atmosphere during specific operating modes of the water heater 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3274541-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as described above the substance judging device 14 and the computer device 20 are composed of the plankton measuring device 10 the water quality measuring device 11 and the toxic substance monitoring device 12 from the water intake source 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-5776333-A", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "also the air cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger 18"}]</data>
</edge>
