", "reinforce", "appear", "add", "go", "relate", "revolve", "twist", "output", "handle", "grab", "expect", "set", "give", "stack", "authenticate", "form", "represent", "save", "spray", "build", "screw", "conclude", "depend", "compress", "mix", "correct", "push", "pack", "wait", "join", "deteriorate", "evaluate", "support", "turn", "penetrate", "undergo", "diagnose", "discover", "moisture", "dissolve", "hoist", "bridge", "move", "interpose", "progress", "locate", "read", "adopt", "reduce", "plug", "query", "may", "deplete", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "drip", "mimic", "net", "spot", "obtain", "must", "endure", "absorb", "shield", "define", "charge", "predict", "know", "transport", "finish", "heat", "galvanize", "laminate", "waste", "continue", "be", "conduct", "print", "elapse", "embody", "warm", "expose", "combine", "get", "apply", "drill", "contaminate", "confirm", "weld", "reach", "extract", "display", "substitute", "extinguish", "sld", "achieve", "dump", "increase", "refer", "circulate", "fuse", "will", "restore", "provide", "wrap", "contain", "mention", "uncoil", "ship", "clamp", "compare", "scale", "arrange", "leak", "size", "calculate", "limit", "regard", "repair", "release", "oil", "do", "settle", "create", "facilitate", "cure", "bury", "pipeline", "exceed", "consider", "baffle", "judge", "weave", "end", "insert", "spawn", "seat", "box", "cover", "show", "find", "configure", "bond", "cool", "derive", "start", "fit", "telescope", "enable", "guide", "act", "perform", "consist", "thereto", "open", "mean", "side", "supply", "use", "predetermine", "propeller", "cut", "estimate", "associate", "draw", "extend", "control", "transmit", "case", "need", "monitor", "expend", "elevate", "collect", "instal", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-8658095-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the conventional means for reducing oxygen corrosion in hot water systems is to remove most of the molecular dissolved oxygen by mechanical and chemical means"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "6 in the same manner as the temperature sensor 110a it is possible to detect that leakage occurs when the humidity value becomes higher than the second detection signal of the neighboring sensing unit 100 because the humidity becomes higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "if only the temperature sensor 110a is applied if the temperature of the soil is lowered due to reasons other than leakage in order to compensate for this it is possible to compare the temperature and humidity sensing values together"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102239966-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a pump that supplies external water to the inlet of the steam generating pipe a water supply hose that connects the external water to the pump a steam discharge hose that discharges the steam supplied from the outlet of the steam generating pipe to the outside of the housing and the operation of the heater and the pump it comprises a control unit for controlling the the pedestal consists of a front plate and a rear plate bent in a vertical state and the front plate has a display unit indicating temperature and error code while screwing one side of the cover to the rim a steam amount control lever a steam switch a residual water removal switch and a socket for connecting the steam discharge hose is mounted the rear plate is made by perforating the entrance while screwing the other side of the cover to the edge portion the lower end is screwed inside the doorway formed on the rear plate of the pedestal and both sides are screwed to the cover and a socket connecting the earth leakage circuit breaker and water supply hose is mounted and the power supply line is connected so that it can flow into the inside and the accessories can be stored an inner plate providing a storage space is provided a spray gun having a nozzle connected to the front end of the steam discharge hose to inject steam is provided a plurality of drainage holes are drilled in lower corners of the front plate and the rear plate of the pedestal so that moisture can be discharged to the outside a plurality of first vents are formed on the upper side of the inner plate to discharge heat inside the housing while preventing the inflow of moisture scattered from the outside and a plurality of second vents are formed on one side of the cover to be mounted on the pedestal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200337587-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "it not only prevents the damage caused by freezing but also prevents freezing without using power to reduce the economic burden of the user and prevents the occurrence of safety accidents and mechanical failures due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "control the heating element 40 based on the information provided by 64 but the plug 61 receiving ac 220v power from the outside and after converting the supplied ac 220v power into dc 12v the valve 30 a converter 62 supplied to and an earth leakage breaker 63 integrally coupled with a plug to cut off power in the event of an earth leakage accident in the heating element 40 the temperature sensor 64 installed in the water supply pipe detects the temperature of the water supply pipe transmits the detected information to the controller box 60 and the controller box analyzes the detected information to determine the prediction of freezing and bursting including those operated by current supply when judged to be at risk of freezing as the water supply pipe 10 further surrounds the insulator 41 around the heating element 40 wound in a spiral shape a filter 70 made of a micron mesh network is installed in the setting area while preventing loss of warmth caused by the heating element"}, {"pat_id": "EP-4034718-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "another advantage is that it is capable of monitoring anomalies at the end point abnormal vibration possible water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-4205698-A", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "nonetheless the present invention is considered to teach considerable improvement over the teachings of this prior art in that it allows the ambient temperature to control whether or not the valve is open without regard to a localized temperature increase from warm water being dripped out past the mechanism"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_480", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at this time the middle layer water and the lower layer water is lower than the temperature of the surface water due to the difference in density to cool the water stored in the intake tower to form a low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021938-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "night minimum flow rate detection method to reduce gas flow gas injection type to find out leaked gas after filling the gas inside the pipe and the radar detection to find the leak by using the temperature of the leak point is lower than the leak point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4819721-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "while the pressure is maintained the resin is cured to form a relatively hard tight fitting rigid pipe lining which effectively seals any cracks and repairs any pipe or joint deterioration to prevent further leakage either into or out of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4802665-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a measurement mechanism that includes measurement means that outputs measurement data collected by automatic management and a transmission mechanism that transmits the measurement data a measurement database in which the measurement data is recorded and an observation by an administrator of the water treatment plant an observation database in which the obtained observation data is recorded a storage means including an operation database in which diagnosis data for diagnosing the operation status of the water treatment plant is stored and the measurement data and the observation data are diagnostic means for diagnosing the operation status of the water treatment plant and outputting the diagnosis result in comparison with the diagnostic data a portable computer comprising observation data input means for inputting the observation data observation data transmission means for transmitting the observation data to the storage means and display means for displaying the diagnosis result output from the diagnosis means a terminal and a position display tag attached to at least one of the water treatment device and the pipe and having position information and the portable terminal further includes a reading means for reading the position information of the position display tag the observation data is the liquid color and coloring degree the presence and degree of water leakage in the pipe the presence and degree of abnormal noise the presence and absence of abnormal odor the degree and type the temperature of the pipe water treatment equipment and pump the position information read by the reading means is recorded in the observation database and the diagnosis means includes the position information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "vacuum apparatus for evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means an air compressor for injecting high pressure compressed air into a sealed conduit detecting unit for detecting the pressure and temperature changes in the test tank connected to the vacuum device and the air compression device and connected to the interior of the conduit a controller which controls the driving of the vacuum apparatus and the air compressor and determines whether there is a leakage based on a result detected by the sensing unit it includes a supply device for supplying power and power to each device from the power take off device of the vehicle when the vehicle is mounted or to supply each device the power produced by the generator when mounted on the vehicle to be movable with the vehicle the supply device includes a noise blocking circuit for blocking the noise of the power supplied to each device the power cable connected to the front and rear ends of the noise blocking circuit is provided with a twisted cable to block the noise by increasing the capacitance by twisting the wire the controller is installed inside the main body that forms the appearance and executes the program stored in the storage to control the operation of each device a central processing unit and a printed circuit board for determining a leakage test result according to the detection signal of the detection unit a plurality of operation switches provided on one side of the main body and receiving an operation for controlling driving of each device it is provided on the other side of the main body and includes a plurality of connection ports electrically connected to each device the operation switch is provided with a power switch a vacuum pump provided in the vacuum device a vacuum valve first to fifth switches electrically connected to the compressor and the compressor valve provided in the air compressor the connection port is provided with the vacuum pump and the vacuum valve the compressor and the compressor valve the vent valve for releasing the pressure in the test tank and the first to seventh ports respectively connected to the sensing unit the supply device the first to fifth switches can be set to manual and automatic modes and operation off the cable connecting the sensing unit and the controller is a leakage inspection apparatus of the conduit facility characterized in that provided with a shielded cable shielded to reduce noise"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "authenticating permissions for c conducting a vacuum test or a pressurization test by evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means using a vacuum means or injecting high pressure compressed air into the conduit facility based on the test mode setting state step d detecting changes in pressure and temperature inside the test tank connected to the conduit using a detector and e using the control unit to determine whether the conduit is leaked based on the result detected by the detection unit the leakage inspection method of the conduit facility characterized in that in the step a the supply device cuts off the noise of the power supplied to each device by using a noise blocking circuit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in order to achieve the object as described above the leak test apparatus of the conduit facility according to the present invention is a vacuum device for evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means high pressure compressed air in the sealed conduit facility a sensing unit for detecting pressure and temperature changes in the test tank connected to the injecting air compressor the vacuum device and the air compressor and connected to the inside of the conduit facility and controlling the driving of the vacuum device and the air compressor the controller is configured to determine whether or not leakage based on a result detected by the detector and to supply power and power to each device from a power take off device of a vehicle when the vehicle is mounted or to be produced by a generator when a vehicle is mounted to be movable with a vehicle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "it is possible to determine whether or not leakage of conduit facilities"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3520440-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "