tions of the reinforcement tube and connected to the distal end of the reinforcement tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bollard type water leakage inspection panel protection devicethe present invention relates to a bollard type hot water leakage meter panel guard in particular the inlet and exhaust ports formed on the lower and upper sides of the housing to form a ventilation flow path between the inside and outside of the hot water leakage meter panel guard the moisture inside the hot water leakage meter panel guard and a bollard type hot water leak inspection panel protector which is capable of naturally drying moisture and is suitable to prevent internal condensation by maintaining uniform temperature inside and outside of the warm water leakage inspection panel protector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in addition as a result of the formation of a ventilation flow path between the inside and the outside of the hot water leak inspection panel guard by the configuration of the inlet port 130 and the exhaust port 150 at the lower side and the upper side respectively the exhaust port formed at the upper side of the hot air heated by summer solar heat by natural discharge through the 150 there is an advantage that can prevent the abnormal phenomenon of the hot water leakage metering panel circuit due to the high temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101131-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "due to this stress the inner circumferential surface of the water pipe becomes seriously damaged such as peeling peeling or cracking and the expansion joint which is a stretch joint is damaged due to elastic deformation due to a temperature difference and leaks are caused by this"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101756200-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the communication check module 71 pumps a certain percentage of water into the tank in the morning lunch evening so as to block the number of steps during the rf network check time and the communication check module 71 is used to prevent freezing of the winter water pipe the temperature sensor s39 is attached to the groundwater protecting apparatus 2 and the temperature is lower than the temperature set by the temperature detecting module 73 the motor is repeatedly operated at a predetermined time interval to forcibly start the water and the water in the water pipe is moved the power check module 72 allows the surveillance camera s34 to photograph the monitoring camera s34 only at the moment when the guard means 25 is opened and closed in the groundwater monitoring system and the leakage check module 75 detects the leakage of the water from the occlusion portion 222 it is possible to check the leakage by comparing the sound at the normal time and the sound with the sound sensor in the event of leakage and the leakage position of the water pipe through the pressure sensor of the pipe can be grasped when water is reduced to a certain level or less through a level sensor using an angle sensor at a time when water below a fixed value is used in order to estimate the water leakage of the water supply pipe using a specific time in order to check water shortage phenomenon when water is depleted data is collected by dividing the water depletion time and recovery time by using an electrode and if the motor is not operated for a certain period of time the controller 3 controls the reservoir 4 to charge the reservoir 4 with a certain amount of chlorine so that the management server 7 installs an electrode at a specific point on the end of the reservoir tank accumulate along the curve points"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101012226-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional partition wall has a problem that the shrinkage phenomenon occurs in the winter the lifting phenomenon occurs on the mating surface to cause leakage and the breakage of the partition wall due to expansion in summer.the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the object of the present invention not only can adjust the height of the main body according to the change of rainwater and sewage but also a plurality of the main body by fixing a single reinforcing beam and coupling force and by increasing the stiffness of the body to prevent distortion of the body due to water pressure and further provided with a support beam in the body to improve the durability and to adjust the length of the body in accordance with temperature changes to prevent damage to the body to provide sewage and storm divider assemblies for sewage pipes with"}, {"pat_id": "US-12510435-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "wherein the monitoring unit configured to monitor the state of the conduit unit by at least one of detecting a leakage occurrence at the conduit unit determining a temperature at the conduit unit determining a pressure at the conduit unit determining a flow rate at the inside of the conduit unit or determining a ph value of the fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-12510435-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "according to an embodiment the monitoring unit is configured to monitor the state or condition of the conduit unit by at least one of detecting a leakage occurrence at the conduit unit determining a temperature at the conduit unit determining a pressure at the conduit unit determining a flow rate of the fluid at the inside of the conduit unit and determining a ph value of the fluid inside the conduit unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-4630676-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the resin is then cured to form a relatively hard tight fitting rigid pipe lining which effectively seals any cracks and repairs any pipe or joint deterioration to prevent further leakage either into or out of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-6243483-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "using these sensors temperature and ph anomalies may be used to detect leakage along the pipeline 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604858-B2", "para_id": "para_480", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435698-Y1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "as described above according to the waterproofing device of the concrete reservoir according to the present invention in the concrete reservoir tank so that the polyethylene sheet is lining construction on the inner wall surface having a waterproof function water leakage due to damage of the polyethylene sheet the concrete reservoir condensate due to the temperature difference between the inside and outside or the outside water through the fill in the state in which the concrete reservoir is buried so that the water generated between the polyethylene sheet and the inner wall surface of the concrete reservoir to collect to either side as a result the water does not accumulate between the inner wall of the concrete reservoir and the polyethylene sheet thereby preventing corrosion of the concrete structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101910492-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion external shock temperature etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this invention relates to a method and a system for detecting a leakage from a liquid transporting pipeline and more particularly to a method and a system for minimizing a pressure change due to a temperature change of a liquid within a blocked pipeline containing the liquid to be transported and detecting a leakage of the liquid from the blocked pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "however when there is a change in the liquid temperature the amount of leakage must be calculated from the rate of passing the liquid to or from the block taking into account a volume change due to a change in the liquid temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "however in the case of larger and longer pipeline an amount of the liquid to be passed through a flow rate meter will be increased owing to an increase in volume change due to a change in the liquid temperature in the pipeline and the sensitivity of the flow rate meter is lowered for a small amount of leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "said 10 km or to wait for the leakage detection until the temperature of the pipeline has reached the ambient one for reducing the effect of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "however if the liquid temperature of the block 1 decreases the liquid is supplied to the block through the means for measuring the flow rate in an amount of the liquid corresponding to the reduction in the liquid volume due to the decrease in the liquid temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "since the time constant of the pipeline is 70.5 hours the pipeline does not so simply undergo temperature change thus during the 10 minutes the pipeline undergoes decrease in temperature by about 0.2 c and the temperature may be regarded as substantially 50 c at t 0"}, {"pat_id": "US-9732911-B2", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "the integrated pipeline protection system as claimed in claim 1 wherein the combinational arrangement of the nanosensor the electronic circuitry and microchips is configured to measure at least one real time data to regularly monitor general parameters of the pipeline and predict future leakage to enable preventive maintenance of the pipeline at that location the real time data relating to estimated future leakage of the pipeline comprising corrosion in the pipeline strain created by internal expending force of fluid in the pipeline condition of peripheral interface of the pipeline changes in temperature pressure humidity shocks vibrations toxic gases along with the position along the pipeline"}, 