tation c in other words the change due to leak appears only in the leak occurrence section as a virtual leak flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-8069676-B2", "para_id": "para_388", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920963-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the sealing material 60 is a protective layer for preventing the leakage preventing structure from being deteriorated due to expansion or contraction or deterioration of the structural material due to temperature change and is preferably finished with an elastic material sealant in consideration of the behavior of the joint 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102669555-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition for example in the case of concrete forming a drainage channel there is a risk of water leakage occurring at the connection area and when rainwater or sewage flows in or leaks the concrete cracks due to deterioration or changes in the volume of moisture due to temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5027325-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "measure the abnormal information signals inside or below the underground pipes in the underground structure or structure by fluctuation of the detection signal from the normal state and within the specific distance section set by the analysis of the measurement signal a method was adopted to detect the signs of disaster accidents caused by ground depression ground subsidence radioactivity leakage or abnormal temperature rise in a specific distance section and to identify the site of occurrence and predict it in advance"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3633342-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "some tests can detect a leak but require a second test to determine the location of the leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102514544-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an electronic device for controlling a sewage treatment plant memory and a processor connected to the memory including the processor receiving the water level measurement value from the water level sensor installed in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant where the sewage first flows when the water level measurement value is equal to or less than a preset first reference water level stopping the operation of the motor pump located in the water tank of the sewage treatment plant when the water level measurement value exceeds the first reference water level and is less than or equal to a second reference water level set higher than the first reference water level operating the motor pump at a predetermined first strength when the water level measurement value exceeds the second reference water level the motor pump is operated at a preset second intensity higher than the first intensity and a warning message is sent to a manager terminal used by the manager of the sewage treatment plant the processor determining a first correlation between each other based on the amount of sewage inflow per unit time by hour the number of residents by hour in the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant and the regional characteristic information of the unit area through the first correlation a first expected sewage inflow per unit time at an expected future time is determined based on the number of real time residents of the unit area corresponding to the sewage treatment plant at the current time and regional characteristic information of the unit area when the first expected sewage inflow amount is less than or equal to the preset critical sewage inflow amount the first reference water level and the second reference water level are lowered by a preset first height when the first expected sewage inflow exceeds the predetermined critical sewage inflow the first reference water level and the second reference water level are raised by a predetermined second height the expected future time point is a time point at which a reference elapsed time required to discharge sewage from the second reference water level to the first reference water level elapses when the motor pump is operated at the first intensity from the present time the first height and the second height correspond to a total amount of sewage that can be introduced according to a difference inflow corresponding to a difference between the first expected sewage inflow and the critical sewage inflow during the reference elapsed time the processor determining a second correlation between each other based on the number of residents per hour in the unit area regional characteristic information of the unit area and power consumption per hour in the unit area through the second correlation the real time number of residents is determined based on the real time power consumption of the unit area where the sewage treatment plant is located extracting precipitation per unit time based on the weather forecast of the unit area generating a second expected sewage inflow based on the amount of precipitation the area of the unit area and the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the second expected sewage inflow is added to the first expected sewage inflow the second expected sewage inflow amount is calculated by the following equation esi2 expected sewage inflow means the second expected sewage inflow a area means the area of the unit area p precipitation means the precipitation nostp number of sewage treatment plant means the number of sewage treatment plants included in the unit area the processor derive a third correlation between the water level change of the sewage treatment plant tank the power consumption of the motor pump and the water pressure of the water flowing inside the water outlet pipe connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank based on the third correlation the measured water level change measured in the sewage treatment plant tank and the measured power consumption of the motor pump are connected to the direction in which water is discharged from the sewage treatment plant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425726-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "receiving tank automatic control system capable of real time monitoring characterized in that consisting of a communication unit 36 for receiving and transmitting to the display unit 32"}, {"pat_id": "US-10005001-B2", "para_id": "para_391", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "US-4579640-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "an electrostatic water treatment apparatus comprising a cylindrical shell adapted to hold water under pressure said shell having end closures and a water inlet and outlet an electrode assembly extending into said shell and forming with said shell an annular passageway through which water is adapted to flow between said inlet and outlet said electrode assembly comprising a an elongated cylindrical electrode b end closure cap members for said electrode at least one of said end caps having cylindrical side walls with an inner portion thereof telescoping within said cylindrical electrode and an outer shoulder portion thereof extending axially outwardly beyond the end of the electrode c a continuous coating of silicone adhesive covering the exterior of the electrode and the outer shoulder portion of the end cap d a thin impervious insulating sleeve overlying the silicone adhesive coating and also covering the exterior of the electrode and the outer shoulder portion of the end cap and e ring clamp means surrounding said outer shoulder portion of the end cap and securely clamping the insulating sleeve and silicone adhesive coating thereto thereby permitting rapid expansion and contraction of the assembly due to sudden temperature changes while preventing leakage of water into the interior of the electrode or between the electrode and the insulating sleeve"}, {"pat_id": "US-11002699-B2", "para_id": "para_478", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "US-5062442-A", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "apparatus for monitoring a fluid conduit system for leakage points comprising a main valve having a housing that includes an inlet an outlet and a valve seat interposed between the inlet and outlet and a valve member in the housing operable between an open and a closed position for controlling fluid flow through the main valve seat and volumetric flow meter shunt means for defining a shunt flow path that opens to the inlet and outlet bridging the valve seat and controlling the opening of the valve member as a function of the flow volume in the shunt path and maintaining the main valve member closed until the volume in the shunt path exceeds a predetermined value the shunt means including a flow meter having a first shunt section a valve actuating element having a second shunt section that includes a shunt valve the shunt valve having a valve seat and a closure member for closing and opening the fluid flow path through the shunt valve seat an actuating element for controlling the opening and closing of the closure member and control means for controlling the actuating element the control means being connected to the flow meter and the actuating element and including an integrator that intermittently integrates the flow through the first shunt section a measuring section having laminar flow therethrough a first heat source for heating fluid flowing through the measuring section detecting means for detecting the temperature of the fluid prior to heating by the heat source and evaluating means for determining the flow volume from the temperature detected by the detecting means and the amount of heat given off by the heat source the detecting means including first and second temperature sensors the sensors respectively comprising first and second thin layer metal foil resistors adapted for having a constant voltage applied thereto with the first resistor being downstream of the second resistor and defining the first heat source and the second resistor serving to determine the temperature of the fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-5062442-A", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "apparatus for monitoring a fluid conduit system for leakage points comprising a main valve having a housing that includes an inlet an outlet and a valve seat interposed between the inlet and outlet and a valve member in the housing operable between an open and a closed position for controlling fluid flow through the valve seat and volumetric flow meter shunt means for defining a shunt flow path that opens to the inlet and outlet bridging the valve seat and controlling the opening of the valve member as a function of the flow volume in the shunt path and maintaining the main valve member closed until the volume in the shunt path exceeds a predetermined value the shunt means including a measuring section having laminar flow therethrough a first heat source for heating fluid flowing through the measuring section detecting means for detecting the temperature of the fluid prior to heating by the heat source and evaluating means for determining the flow volume from the temperature detected by the detecting means and the amount of heat given off by the heat source the detecting means including first and second temperature sensors the sensors respectively comprising first and second thin layer metal foil resistors adapted for having a constant voltage applied thereto with the first resistor being downstream of the second resistor and defining the first heat source and the second resistor serving to determine the temperature of the fluid the measuring section comprising a bent pipe section having an exterior surface the temperatures sensors being mechanically and thermally connected to the pipe bend exterior surface and being at a predetermined spacing along the pipe section from one another"}, {"pat_id": "US-5062442-A", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "apparatus for monitoring a fluid conduit system for leakage points comprising a main valve having a housing that includes an inlet an outlet and a valve seat interposed between the inlet and outlet and a valve member in the housing operable between an open and a closed position for controlling fluid flow through the valve seat and volumetric flow meter shunt means for defining a shunt flow path that opens to the inlet and outlet bridging the valve seat and controlling the opening of the valve member as a function of the flow volume in the shunt path and maintaining the main valve member closed until the volume in the shunt path exceeds a predetermined value the shunt means including a measuring section having laminar flow therethrough a first heat source for heating fluid flowing through the measuring section detecting means for detecting the temperature of the fluid prior to heating by the heat source and evaluating means for determining the flow volume from the temperature detected by the detecting means and the amount of heat given off by the heat source the detecting means including first and second temperature sensors the sensors respectively comprising first and second thin layer metal foil resistors adapted for having a constant voltage applied thereto with the first resistor being downstream of the second resistor and defining the first heat source and the second resistor serving to determine the temperature of the fluid the upstream temperature sensor being an electric resistance that is about 10 times as great as that of the downstream resistor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100776387-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "a reinforcing member 230 through which the installation hole 233 on which the 240 is seated is provided is provided and is attached to the upper surface of the unit block 110 while being in close contact with the upper surface of the reinforcing member 230 to guide drainage of water 240 is provided and the polyethylene sheet 250 is provided to prevent the leakage of water by seating on the upper surface of the reinforcing member 230 to accommodate the seat 210 while the drain 240 is opened the polyethylene sheet 250 to prevent flow caused by shrinkage forces that occur as the temperature changes in water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554870-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "1 and 2 the conventional water meter freeze protection device the outer wall 3 in front of the water meter 2 installed in the water supply pipe 1 for measuring the water consumption of the consumer such as a home or a shopping mall the meter management door 4 for hinge opening and closing at the time of measuring the water consumption is rotatably hinged by the hinge member 5 the heat insulating member 9 for blocking heat transfer in the rear of the meter management door 4 is built in to prevent freezing of the water meter 2 but in this way only by incorporating the insulation member 9 in the rear of the conventional meter management door 4 effectively prevents the freezing phenomenon that occurs in winter there are many problems such as the leakage caused by the freeze because it can not be and the cost is required because the water meter must be replaced.accordingly the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems it is to solve the freezing phenomenon that occurs in the winter when the air temperature drops below zero in the section where the water meter is installed to measure the water consumption of the consumer such as home or shopping mall it is an object of the present invention to provide a water meter freeze protection device that can effectively prevent the leakage caused by freezing in advance as well as reduce the cost of water meter replacement"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3652115-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "lastly it helps act as a thermal insulator and therefore decreases the thermal leakage in undesired directions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "the sealing member s may be made of a rubber material and may be formed when the temperature sensing member 120 blocks the first inlet 111 or when the setting block 150 blocks the second inlet 112 it is possible to prevent water from being wasted by leakage by increasing the sealing force so that water does not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold hot water supply device 100 and may include for example a water level sensor 612 cold water hot water temperature sensors 624 and 634 wire or the like sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640 660 a water leakage sensor 670 one or more overflow sensors 690 can do"}, {"pat_id": "US-7403839-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "such sensors 12 can be hard wired into the electrical supply of the structure or battery operated but are preferably hard wired and include a battery backup in the event of a power failure a condition where flooding is more likely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468179-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is difficult to find a sensor on the market that can detect leakage while enduring high temperature particularly in a very high temperature pipe.accordingly the present invention has an object to provide a leak detection device that can withstand high temperatures and can stably detect leakage.leakage detection device according to an embodiment of the present invention a plurality of heat shields made of an insulating material and a pair of through holes formed in parallel the plurality of heat shields in series through a pair of through holes of the heat shield and a sensing unit connected to the wire and connected to the wire to measure a resistance change due to the energization caused by the fluid leaked from the pipe.as described above according to the present invention the wire is formed to penetrate into the heat shield made of insulating material thereby preventing heat conduction to the leak detection device so that the leak can be stably detected for a long time in a pipe where a high temperature fluid flows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is such a water tank is contaminated with water quality because the temperature of the stored water is increased due to the high external temperature of the summer and the water quality is contaminated and the contaminated water is not suitable for extinguishing corrosion mic microbially induced corrosion is progressed causing leakage and other defects which causes a problem of inadequate supply of extinguishing water in case of fire"}, {"pat_id": "US-5044824-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "while the pressure is maintained the resin is cured to form a relatively hard tight fitting rigid pipe lining which effectively seals any cracks and repairs any pipe or joint deterioration to prevent further leakage either into or out of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-11826681-B2", "para_id": "para_373", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "therefore if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200436180-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "this method is not only cumbersome for construction and difficult to work with but also takes a long time and causes a lot of leakage due to weakening of adhesive force and poor soldering and the soldering part due to ground subsidence and uplift or external impact due to seasonal temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the method further includes monitoring by a controller a rate of temperature change detected by a first temperature sensor positioned to sense a temperature of the condensate within a condensate collector of the exhaust assembly"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the o ring 170 is configured to inhibit leakage of a condensate stream e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the controller 142 thus concludes at 250 that there is leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the controller 142 thus concludes at 250 that there is a leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "for example should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c one f to three f between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "if during the standby mode the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 114 are different than different leakage rates may be indicated to the controller"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the controller 142 may be configured to query the first second and third temperature sensors 114 118 122 during specific time periods of the day when determining a drain blockage or a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "in particular the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "the leakage temperature limit 690a may be proximate the maximum temperature limit 685a of the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "although the leaked water may lose some heat during the wait period 695 while accumulating in the drain pipe 394 this is not significant enough to prevent the change in state of the temperature reading from the negative rate of change to the positive rate or change or to prevent the increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "9 11 only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the controller thus concludes at 550 that there is leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "thus the invention provides among other things a water heater 10 including a control system 38 338 configured to detect an error in the water heater 10 such as a leakage or a drain blockage by utilizing and or comparing temperature readings of condensate flue gases and outside atmosphere during specific operating modes of the water heater 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100444623-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "however if the precision construction is not made the watertightness is lost so much care is required during construction and even if the precision construction is performed the elevation of the ground due to the external conditions that is the temperature change and the external impact according to the season if sinking occurs the soldering parts are damaged and water tightness is degraded which leads to a problem of leakage of sewage and in some cases development of a hole or a connection socket of a manhole"}, {"pat_id": "EP-4190981-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "this is because when the temperature on the supply line drops below a limit value there is an increasing risk of icing which in turn increases the risk of leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the sealing member 121 may be made of a rubber material so that when the temperature sensing member 120 closes the inlet 112 it is possible to prevent water from being wasted by leakage by increasing the sealing force so that water does not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drain device with double bodythe present invention relates to a drain having a dual structure and more particularly having a drain and the outer cylinder and the inner cylinder to prevent the leakage of sewage having a hot temperature of the waste collected in the drain after installation of the drain and sewage into cement or mortar it not only prevents water leakage due to absorption but also prevents leakage of water leakage and leakage by the outer cylinder even if a gap of the inner cylinder occurs as well as filtering wastes such as food waste by a plurality of strainers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "there is a problem in that leakage occurs due to absorption of sewage leaked into the cement or mortar buried"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "a waste filtration passage having a plurality of first filtration holes in the first filtration to filter the wastes contained in the filthy water flowing through the effluent inlet holes a first filtration panel fitted to the first fitting support and positioned in a longitudinal direction with respect to the inner cylinder and provided with a plurality of second filtration holes at a bottom thereof to filter out filthy water and wastes from the waste filtration tank secondly a second filtration panel fitted to the second fitting support and positioned longitudinally with respect to the inner cylinder and having a plurality of third filtration holes in the center to filter out filthy water and wastes from the first filtration panel in a third filter it is made.the present invention is provided with an outer cylinder embedded in cement or mortar and the inner cylinder to be inserted into the inside of the outer cylinder but because the inner cylinder and the outer cylinder are provided in a state separated from each other the hot sewage temperature flowing into the inner cylinder side is the outer cylinder by preventing the transfer to the side it is possible to prevent the external cylinder from generating heat deformation gap due to hot temperature and also to prevent the leakage of water leaked from the inner cylinder by being absorbed by cement or mortar"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion external shock temperature etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-12265759-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the daily construction process of heating pipelines there will be problems such as pipeline leakage but generally the pipeline is tested manually on a regular basis to ensure the normal operation of the pipeline or after receiving complaints from users it may be because individual users can t receive the heating or the heating temperature is too low so the pipeline detection will be carried out"}, {"pat_id": "US-9671068-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "example of the parameter associated with the pipeline 200 may include all the relevant parameters that are capable of determining any leakage future leakage or any attempt of theft in the pipeline 200 such as corrosion in the pipeline 200 strain created by internal expending force of fluid in the pipeline 200 condition of peripheral interface of the pipelines 200 changes in temperature pressure humidity shocks vibrations and toxic gases along with the position along the pipeline 200 etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9671068-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "the real time data relating to estimated future leakage and regular monitoring of the pipeline 200 may include but not limiting to corrosion in the pipeline strain created by internal expending force of fluid in the pipeline 200 condition of peripheral interface of the pipeline 200 changes in temperature pressure humidity shocks vibrations toxic gases along with the position along the pipeline 200 and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101978152-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if a wave is generated in the meter section the water can not be used in the building waste of water due to leakage can occur and the meter may be damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102593825-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "the control unit 300 may include a display unit 310 that generates an alarm signal or shows the water leakage situation to the user visually and visually and provides electrical signals to the three way heat source supply valve the flow control valve for controlling the hot water temperature and the water supply and blocking valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-9254221-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "because the role of the heating pipe the temperature of the liquid in the pipeline will be elevated and it has an advantage of comfortable and healthy to dispose the pipeline on the pad it can prevent the leakage and obtains higher safety"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102099550-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "as a method to prevent water leakage in buildings there is a method of installing a drain drainage pipe a pipe that guides rainwater on a pipe bridge to the surface and frequent contact and temperature of moisture in the periphery of the inlet side where the drain is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "however the coupling by bearing is possible in a fermentation device operated at room temperature and normal pressure but there is room for problems such as leakage and deformation due to thermal expansion in a drying device supplied with high temperature and high pressure dry air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262046-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "1 and 2 the present inventors electric power control system 120 includes a power supply unit 10 for supplying electricity to the electric power control system a filter unit 20 for filtering water and contaminants that are flowing into the inlet formed at one side of the electrolytic cell in the state in which electricity is supplied to the power supply and moving to the supply pipe a flow rate or flow rate part 30 for measuring the amount and flow rate of water when the water passing through the filter part flows through the supply pipe through a flow meter or a flow rate meter a temperature sensor unit 40 for measuring a temperature of water passing through the flow rate or flow rate through a temperature sensor in order to generate the concentration of germicidal ions through the electrolysis of the water passing through the flow rate or flow rate a mesh type electrode having a plurality of perforated shapes is laminated or used within a range that does not affect the flow rate of water or a lattice electrode portion 50 to increase the sterilization concentration by reducing the flow rate of water passing through the electrode by causing a phenomenon in the electrode and the electrode stacked in the form an electric leakage blocking unit 50 1 which blocks or prevents an electric leakage phenomenon due to residual electricity remaining in the electrode unit or water even when the electric power is supplied from the power source or when the electric power is cut off a current sensor unit 60 for sensing an amount of current supplied to the electrode of the electrode unit with a current sensor and monitoring water quality of the supply water a voltage sensor unit 70 for inferring electric conductivity or total dissolved solids tds by measuring the supply voltage supplied to the power supply unit a direct current power generator 80 for generating direct current power according to the electrical conductivity or total dissolved solids tds value inferred by the voltage sensor the amount of power required by controlling the flow rate or flow rate the current sensor unit the voltage sensor unit and the dc power generating unit to read the electrical conductivity of the water and the tds value and the electrical resistance value according to the water flow rate flow rate and temperature change an electrical control unit 90 for generating control a wired or wireless communication unit 100 supporting communication by transmitting information of the electric resistance value obtained from the electric control unit to an external terminal or a computer by wire or wirelessly a display unit 110 which displays a state of operation by the electric control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 1 the control unit drives the temperature sensor at regular intervals the heat pipe leakage monitoring device characterized in that to cut off the power at the remaining time except the driving time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the mounting table is provided with a plurality of temperature sensors 120 for monitoring whether leakage occurs in the heat pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_378", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "however since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside the temperature sensor often malfunctions and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as a result the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100957704-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the openings 130 are formed and the openings 130 are bonded to each other by heat sealing thereby preventing loss of adhesion due to temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-5150989-A", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "while the pressure is maintained the resin is cured to form a relatively hard tight fitting rigid pipe lining which effectively seals any cracks and repairs any pipe or joint deterioration to prevent further leakage either into or out of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101626616-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water leakage measuring apparatus for a water supply pipe including a plurality of water pipes connected by at least one joint pipe a peltier element formed into a plurality of pieces and fastened to at least a part of the outside of the plurality of water pipes a battery for storing electricity produced by the peltier device a plurality of pressure sensors inserted in the holes formed in the at least one coupling pipe and sensing a first pressure of each of the plurality of water pipes a data memory for storing preset standard pressure values a controller for comparing the standard pressure value with the first pressure to determine whether the plurality of water pipes are leaking and and a radio signal processing unit for sending a message informing whether or not the leakage occurs to the outside under the control of the control unit wherein the peltier element produces the electricity using a temperature change of at least a part of the plurality of water pipes the plurality of pressure sensors the data memory the control unit and the wireless signal processing unit are driven using electricity stored in the battery wherein determining that the leaked water is leaked when the second pressure which is at least part of the first pressure is lower than the standard pressure value determining a second water pipe corresponding to the second pressure among the plurality of water pipes wherein the radio signal processing unit controls the second pressure and the information for identifying the second water pipe to be sent to the outside together"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101626616-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a leakage measurement method for a water supply pipe including a plurality of water pipes connected by at least one coupling pipe a first step in which a peltier element formed of a plurality of pieces and coupled to at least a part of the outside of the plurality of water pipes produces electricity a second step of storing electricity produced by the peltier device through a battery a third step wherein the data memory stores a preset standard pressure value a fourth step of sensing a first pressure of each of the plurality of water pipes by a plurality of pressure sensors inserted into holes formed in the at least one joint pipe a fifth step of the control unit comparing the standard pressure value and the first pressure to determine whether the plurality of water pipes are leaked or not and and a sixth step in which the wireless signal processing unit sends out a message informing whether or not the leak is caused to the outside according to the control of the control unit in the first step the peltier element produces the electricity using a temperature change of at least a part of the plurality of water pipes the plurality of pressure sensors the data memory the control unit and the wireless signal processing unit are driven using electricity stored in the battery in the fifth step determining a leakage if the second pressure that is at least part of the first pressure is lower than the standard pressure value and and determining a second water pipe corresponding to the second pressure among the plurality of water pipes and the sixth step of sending out the second pressure and information for identifying the second water pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101626616-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the water supply pipe leakage measuring apparatus according to the present invention stores electricity from the peltier element 10 as the battery 35 of the control module 30 due to the temperature difference between the inside and the outside of the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102722253-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "in order for the gas sensor 270 to operate a membrane hole through which gas can pass may be formed in the lower part of the housing portion 100 although not shown in the drawing"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "tm ti h ti to cp \u03c1 \u03b4 wherein ti is a temperature of fluid in the pipeline and the unit is k h is a convection heat transfer coefficient of steam and a thermal insulation layer 6 in the pipeline and the unit is w m2 k cp is a specific heat capacity of steam and the unit is j kg k \u03c1 is a steam density and the unit is kg m3 \u03b4 is a wall thickness of the pipeline namely a distance by which steam flows out from the inside of the pipeline via a leakage hole to the outer wall of the pipeline in unit time and the unit is m s \u03b4 mt\u03c1 a wherein m is a mass flow of steam namely a fluid mass of the fluid that passes through an effective cross section of a closed pipeline in unit time and the unit is kg s t is a unit time namely 1 s and a is the area of the leakage hole and the unit is m2 a corresponding relationship between a steam pressure and a temperature in the heating pipeline is obtained by an antoine empirical formula or by looking up a table of steam pressure and temperature enthalpy values as shown in a formula 7 below ln p 9.3876 3826.36t 45.47 7 wherein p is the steam pressure and the unit is mpa t is the steam temperature and the unit is k a value p calculated by substituting tm as the steam temperature into the formula 7 is the pipeline leakage transient pressure pm corresponding to the pipeline leakage transient steam temperature tm in step 3 the process of positioning a leakage location by the plc according to a pressure gradient method is specifically as follows firstly a pressure gradient p x leftbracketingbar u upstream of a leakage point and a pressure gradient p x leftbracketingbar d downstream of the leakage point are calculated p x leftbracketingbar u p 1 pmx 8 p x leftbracketingbar d pm p 2l s x 9 wherein l is a distance from a pressure sensor within a region of the leakage point to a temperature sensor downstream thereof and the unit is m s is a distance from a temperature sensor within the region of the leakage point to a pressure sensor downstream thereof and the unit is m x is a distance from the location of the leakage point to a pressure sensor upstream within the region of the leakage point and the unit is m x represents a gradient direction dot over p 1 is a pressure value detected by the pressure sensor upstream of the leakage point and the unit is mpa dot over p 2 is a pressure value detected by a pressure sensor downstream of the leakage point and the unit is mpa and pm is the pipeline leakage transient pressure and the unit is mpa it is known from a formula for conservation of momentum within a steam pipeline p x leftbracketingbar u f \u03c1 u22 d 10 p x leftbracketingbar d f \u03c1 u22 d wherein f is a friction coefficient u is a flow velocity of steam and the unit is m s \u03c1 is a steam density and the unit is kg m3 d is a pipeline diameter and the unit is m the aperture of a leakage hole is less than the pipeline diameter and a pipeline length and the variation of friction coefficients of two adjacent sides of the leakage hole within a short distance are ignored in the case of pipeline leakage no phenomena of obvious free outflow and flow reduction of steam occur because of the presence of the thermal insulation layer 6 and therefore pressure gradients upstream and downstream of the leakage point are approximately the same and after being stabilized the pressures restore an original pressure distribution along the pipeline it can be obtained from simultaneous equations 8 10 that x l s p 1 pm p 1 p 2 since the arrangement locations of the sensors are known the location of the leakage point can be positioned accurately according to a calculated value x and in step 3 in the process of positioning the location of the leakage point a correction coefficient \u03be is introduced and the value x is corrected by a method of using temperatures to correct pressures wherein the correction coefficient is represented by a formula below \u03be 2 tmt 1 t 2 a corrected new value x is x l s p 1 pm p 1 p 2 \u03be wherein tm is the pipeline leakage transient steam temperature and the unit is k dot over t 1 is a temperature value detected by the temperature sensor upstream of the leakage point and the unit is k and dot over t 2 is a temperature value detected by the temperature sensor downstream of the leakage point and the unit is k"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "an identification system for implementing the pipeline potential safety hazard intelligent identification method integrating power frequencies pressures and temperatures according to claim 1 comprising temperature sensors pressure sensors an iot electricity meter a plc an iot dtu a communication cable and a remote server wherein the pressure sensors and the temperature sensors are arranged on a heating pipeline and the iot electricity meter is located in a device pump unit distribution box at the starting end of the heating pipeline and collects the frequency variation of a heating supply pump in real time the plc communicates with the temperature sensors the pressure sensors the iot electricity meter and the iot dtu receives temperature values pressure values and frequency values collected in real time performs operation analysis outputs early warning signals and positions a leakage point and the iot dtu is in signal connection with the remote server via a mobile network and the remote server processes and stores all data of the monitoring system"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "by integrating on site pressure sensing and temperature sensing operating state monitoring on the heating pipelines and pipeline leakage analysis and early warning are realized without adding sensing devices"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in view of the disadvantages in the prior art the present invention provides a heating pipeline operating state monitoring system and method integrating pressure sensing and temperature sensing which solve the problems of high economical costs and low field applicability of traditional pipeline leakage monitoring"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the monitoring system comprises temperature sensors pressure sensors an internet of things iot electricity meter a plc an iot dtu a communication cable and a remote server the pressure sensors and the temperature sensors are arranged on a heating pipeline the iot electricity meter is located in a device pump unit distribution box at the starting end of the heating pipeline and collects a frequency variation of a heating supply pump in real time the plc communicates with the temperature sensors the pressure sensors the iot electricity meter and the iot dtu receives temperature values pressure values and frequency values collected in real time performs operation analysis outputs early warning signals and positions a leakage point and the iot dtu is in signal connection with the remote server via a mobile network and the remote server processes and stores all data of the monitoring system"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "2 performing energy analysis on fluid at the leakage location of the pipeline to obtain the leakage transient temperature taking a temperature variation as guidance for solving the pressure gradient positioning the leakage point of the heating pipeline improving positioning accuracy performing logical operation via the plc by the algorithm finding the leakage in time and outputting early warning signals"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "since the heating pipeline is long a temperature sensor is arranged within a certain distance downstream of the pressure sensor according to a common construction method and the heating pipeline needs a unit division to facilitate monitoring analysis"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "wherein \u03c6h is the capacity of convective heat exchange between the fluid and the inner wall of the pipeline and the unit is w \u03c6e is the heat capacity of heat conduction between the inner wall of the pipeline and the outer wall of the pipeline and the unit is w \u03c6h is the heat capacity of heat conduction between the outer wall of the pipeline and the environment and the unit is w h is a convection heat transfer coefficient of steam and the unit is w m2 k d is a diameter of the pipeline and the unit is m \u03b4 is a wall thickness of the pipeline namely a distance by which steam flows out from the inside of the pipeline via the leakage hole to the outer wall of the pipeline in unit time and the unit is m s \u03b4 is the thickness of the thermal insulation layer 6 and the unit is m l is a length between pipe sections and the unit is mm \u03bb is a thermal conduction coefficient of a pipeline material and the unit is w m k \u03bb is a thermal conduction coefficient of a thermal insulation material and the unit is w m k twn is the temperature of the inner wall of the pipeline in the case of no leakage and the unit is k ton is the temperature of the outer wall of the pipeline in the case of no leakage and the unit is k and te is the temperature of the outer surface of the thermal insulation layer 6 an approximation of an environment temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_95", "text": "since a heat flow \u03c6 in each heat transfer process remains unchanged that is \u03c6h \u03c6c \u03c6v\u03c6 ton can be obtained from simultaneous equations 2 4 at the moment of leakage the temperature of the inner surface of the thermal insulation layer 6 is the temperature of the outer wall of the pipeline without leakage that is ton tol and thus the variation of the transient heat capacity of steam at the moment of leakage can be obtained by substituting tol into the formula 1 \u03b4q"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "and the variation of the temperature in the pipeline is less affected by an external environment the process of solving the transient pressure by the leakage transient temperature is specifically as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_131", "text": "when leakage occurs in the pipeline a negative pressure at the leakage hole propagates inside the pipeline in the form of pressure waves because collection analysis of the pressure sensors on the pressure waves are mature and the variation of the transient temperature at the leakage point can be hardly embodied by data collected by the temperature sensors a pipeline leakage early warning is realized by setting a pressure threshold value"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "when an on off event happens to the heating supply pump unit at the starting end of the pipeline a great gradient variation of the pressure in the pipeline may be caused which can cause a false leakage early warning easily therefore the plc collects data from the pressure sensors and the temperature sensors to form a pressure dataset p1 p2 p3 p4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100836904-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it consists of a drive 22 for driving the unit 23 the display unit 23 is a filter loss amount display unit 24 for displaying the loss of each filter 5 stored by the wired terminal 70 connected from the outside in percentage and when the filter 5 is replaced filter replacement display section 25 in which the lamp is selectively flashed when the lamp is reached the water level level display section 26 in which the lamp is selectively lit according to the water level level of the water tank 6 and the driving of the pump 3 and it consists of a drive display unit 27 the lamp is turned on when the water leakage and a water temperature display unit 28 for displaying cold and hot water the output terminal of the mpu 21 is installed on one side of the facet 8a is connected to the facet lamp 9 for providing a refreshing feeling when the water is discharged the water level sensor 30 is installed in the water tank 6 at the input end of the mpu 21 and senses the water level in four stages and the water leakage sensor is installed on the bottom surface of the case 1 to detect water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101066393-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "and the heater 10 is extended to the outside through the through hole 4 formed in the fire water supply pipe 3 in the state installed inside the fire water supply pipe 3 the waterproof clamp 20 installed in the fire water supply pipe 3 since water is used to prevent leakage there is an advantage that the installation and maintenance of the heater 10 is very easy"}]</data>
</edge>
