"discard", "add", "suffer", "sample", "relate", "mislay", "force", "handle", "comply", "expect", "balance", "set", "stack", "evaporate", "form", "concentrate", "spray", "save", "chill", "depend", "weaken", "mix", "pack", "mitigate", "assemble", "wait", "step", "evaluate", "effectuate", "neutralize", "fall", "dissolve", "submerge", "move", "oxidize", "ionize", "progress", "simplify", "recycle", "locate", "reduce", "dehydrate", "may", "sand", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "mimic", "design", "isolate", "obtain", "must", "propose", "deposit", "absorb", "evaporator", "define", "transfer", "construct", "antifoame", "charge", "could", "predict", "know", "transport", "favor", "heat", "avoid", "fail", "shape", "select", "be", "suppress", "expose", "combine", "get", "apply", "contaminate", "confirm", "preweighe", "rise", "grout", "preheat", "reach", "extract", "extinguish", "achieve", "increase", "agglomerate", "maximize", "assembly", "disclose", "circulate", "melt", "will", "provide", "contain", "mention", "compare", "load", "arrange", "leak", "alter", "calculate", "transform", "limit", "repair", "release", "do", "prove", "settle", "create", "facilitate", "lock", "bury", "exceed", "consider", "inflow", "insert", "direct", "cover", "show", "configure", "fabricate", "cool", "derive", "fit", "enable", "particle", "collide", "perform", "act", "consist", "thereto", "power", "open", "mean", "side", "supply", "use", "cut", "estimate", "associate", "break", "draw", "stagnate", "control", "transmit", "monitor", "expend", "elevate", "exist", "collect", "instal"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-8658095-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the conventional means for reducing oxygen corrosion in hot water systems is to remove most of the molecular dissolved oxygen by mechanical and chemical means"}, {"pat_id": "US-8658095-B2", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the tube functions to provide support for noble metal band 26c band and may include any corrosion resistant material such as stainless steel of any suitable composition aluminum other metals and plastics and combinations thereof"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6765582-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "further since the water to be treated 6 supplied from the nozzle 35 to the discharge unit 2 flows down while being in contact with the circular pipe 4 the water to be treated 6 functions as substantial cooling water and the temperature of the circular pipe 4 rises due to the discharge 9"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101247110-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "pressure and temperature generated when the micro bubbles are destroyed can cause a corrosion state in the reaction chamber 41 so the reaction chamber 41 is connected to both ends by a flange 44 so that the structure can be replaced immediately in case of serious damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-4619819-A", "para_id": "para_99", "text": "high quality phosphorus must be burned in the unit to prevent corrosion of the stainless steel"}, {"pat_id": "US-6926878-B2", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "to near boiling but temperatures above room temperature tend to produce faster reaction time"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_435", "text": "5 5a the sump assembly 500 may be made from material that is corrosion and high temperature resistant"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_435", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures moisture and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_456", "text": "7 the lower flange 704 and upper flange 712 may be manufactured out of any material having sufficient structural strength and corrosion and temperature resistant properties"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_480", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "US-8741100-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "while various different high alloys offer answers in regard to corrosion and temperature resistance the costs of the vessels and the appurtenances fabricated from them are generally quite high"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "bethridge on ca transferred to the inflowing solvent before entering the thus heat exchanger 925 preheated the water and reduced the energy requirements of the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100735544-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "a chemical treatment method using an antifoaming agent has a problem of lowering oxygen transfer efficiency due to residual silicone and other chemicals in the antifoaming agent.the present invention has been made in view of this point and install a straight or radial air supply means on the bottom of the high temperature aerobic digestion reaction tank and supply air to the blower while supplying wastewater to the internal circulation pump to supply air from the discharge nozzle of the air supply means and wastewater are mixed and discharged to form conditions for activating high temperature aerobic microorganisms through the complete mixing of the wastewater in the high temperature aerobic digestion reactor and oxygen transfer through air supply thereby increasing the decomposition efficiency of organic matter and the purpose is to remove the pathogenic microorganisms and e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100554692-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "at this time the middle layer water and the lower layer water is lower than the temperature of 