ion line 11 can be efficiently detected by arranging the ut sensor 32 suitable for the wall thickness measurement"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6763630-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "in some embodiments the ut sensor 32 may be located on the inlet side of the condenser 5 see fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-5676802-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "and therefore serious corrosion occurs at the tower top and in the piping connected to the cooler and condenser"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a method of monitoring and controlling a low carbon permeable ecological structure consisting of a plurality of corrosion resistant piles a plurality of horizontal framing frames in the form of spacers an ecological block for water purification and an ecological block for fishes and fishes first the low carbon permeable ecological installed at a predetermined position of the structure 100 receives the detected data from a plurality of sensors 210 to detect the conductivity water quality water temperature or quantity of river water by wire or wireless"}, {"pat_id": "US-5450765-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "examples of such applications are 1 pig signaling devices that is devices used to signal the passage of a pig apparatus through the pipeline 2 corrosion probes that is devices to detect and or measure the rate of corrosion occurring in the pipeline 3 analysis of the contents flowing through the pipeline such as the amount of water contained in petroleum products or the specific gravity of the products 4 the temperature of the fluid or gas flowing through the pipeline 5 the pressure within the pipeline 6 fluid or gas flow rates and 7 benchmark systems which may include frequency channels that can be sold to in line inspection companies"}, {"pat_id": "US-11713258-B2", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the first segment can comprise the rough or coarse filters which should filter solid contaminates at least 2 millimeters in length and up to 10 millimeters in length depending on the amounts of suspended solids amounts of aquatic life if any water temperature and system operational conditions and other requirements"}, {"pat_id": "US-11713258-B2", "para_id": "para_152", "text": "in another embodiment a pressure device such as a vacuum pump can be used to reduce the pressure inside the heat exchanger to lower the temperature of thermal distillation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "5 to 5a the sump assembly 500 may be made of a material that is resistant to corrosion and high temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "7 the bottom flange 704 and the top flange 712 may be made of any material having sufficient structural strength corrosion resistance and temperature resistance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "in another embodiment the sump 1302 may be made of any other material having sufficient corrosion resistance and high temperature resistance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100739855-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "this effectively eliminates c 14 nuclides in the targeted mixed bed waste resins without the use of acid solutions and high temperature oxidation treatments which contribute to the decay of the device and large amounts of other cationic radionuclides and the addition of waste resins via vitrification"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101087340-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the main equipment composition of the secondary cooling system of the performance factory is used for casting and equipment cooling in the continuous casting process and the high temperature coolant discharged through the scale pit hot water bath and filter and scale which is a high temperature corrosion product of the casting and oils such as inorganic salts and roller greases are removed cooled to the standard level of cooling water while passing through a water tank and then recycled to the continuous casting process water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970306-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to form a negative electrode or a positive electrode separately so that the negative electrode or the positive electrode can be replaced individually during replacement due to corrosion breakage respectively.in order to achieve the above object the present invention is a sensor for measuring the temperature or hydrogen ion concentration such as constant sewage is coupled to the holder the amount of residual chlorine in which a negative electrode and a positive electrode is formed on one side of the holder a device for measuring the amount of residual chlorine in the indicator by measuring the amount of residual chlorine contained in the measured water by galvanic cell electrolysis by combining the measuring sensor separately"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "temperature sensors traditionally used within the industry are of resistive temperature detector rtd type and are typically configured with a stainless steel dome to prevent malfunction due to corrosion and water ingress issues"}, {"pat_id": "US-5961837-A", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "all the tests hereinafter described were performed using the static corrosion test sct technique in which a preweighed corrosion coupon was set in a beaker containing the test water and a stirrer set a 2500 rpm temperature was controlled via a vertex set at 50 c"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5699445-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent these obstacles various water treatment chemicals such as a corrosion inhibitor a scale inhibitor and a slime adhesion inhibitor are added to the circulating water in the open circulation cooling water system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4199407-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-8967186-B2", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "the controller also communicates with a locally visible station status indication via a separate connection 86 on the sensor station"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102473332-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the ammonia recovery apparatus using a distillation column composed of a pall ring the ammonia recovery device includes a sedimentation tank or a wastewater tank in which wastewater is stored a microfilter for removing suspended solids solids or heavy metals with a size of 5 \u03bcm to 10 \u03bcm contained in the waste water stored in the settling tank or the waste water tank a preheater for preheating the wastewater removed in the suspended matter solid matter or heavy metal in the microfilter using the high temperature liquid at the bottom of the steam stripper including a steam stripper for receiving wastewater preheated in the preheater and heating it with steam wherein the steam stripper passes the preheated wastewater through a pall ring heated with steam using an inner filler in which pall rings are stacked thereby passing a small amount of ammonia"}, {"pat_id": "US-4204914-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-10189721-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "many freshwater applications suffer degraded performance due to buildup of scale bacteria and corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion external shock temperature etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9671068-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "example of the parameter associated with the pipeline 200 may include all the relevant parameters that are capable of determining any leakage future leakage or any attempt of theft in the pipeline 200 such as corrosion in the pipeline 200 strain created by internal expending force of fluid in the pipeline 200 condition of peripheral interface of the pipelines 200 changes in temperature pressure humidity shocks vibrations and toxic gases along with the position along the pipeline 200 etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9671068-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the parameter that may be monitored include but not limiting to corrosion in the pipeline 200 strain created by internal expending force of fluid in the pipeline 200 condition of peripheral interface of the pipeline 200 changes in temperature pressure humidity shocks vibrations and toxic gases along with the position along the pipeline 200 etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-9671068-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "the real time data relating to estimated future leakage and regular monitoring of the pipeline 200 may include but not limiting to corrosion in the pipeline strain created by internal expending force of fluid in the pipeline 200 condition of peripheral interface of the pipeline 200 changes in temperature pressure humidity shocks vibrations toxic gases along with the position along the pipeline 200 and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100426050-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "since the acidity of the condensate is about ph2.8 ph3.5 the acid condensate if it comes in contact with the components constituting the component there is a risk of corrosion and if such acid condensate is discharged to the sewer as it may cause environmental pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100393921-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the advanced treatment process of the waste water by the corrosion reaction of the present invention to achieve the above object is introduced into the flow control tank and the concentrated supernatant is conveyed through the return pipe to remove odor and antagonize pathogens"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100393921-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "in addition the treated water is returned from the unheated tank through the pipe 41 to the un anaerobic tank 3 at the front end thereby further