f the piping divided into three quarters after flowing out from the sea water box one side of the piping through which the cooler s seawater flows a side of a pipeline through which seawater flows in and out of a cooler a side of a pipeline through which seawater flows into the condenser and a pipeline through which seawater flows out from the condenser and one side of the one side of the piping through which the seawater flows out from the condenser and one side of the piping leading to the sea water electrolysis device out of which the seawater flows out from the condenser the seawater electrolytic apparatus includes an analysis component for analyzing the degree of seawater seafood and bacteria capture a determination component for measuring and determining the concentration of hypochlorous acid produced by the power supply of the power supply a control arrangement for regulating the intensity of the received electric power a generating structure for generating hypochlorous acid an inlet through which seawater flows and an outlet through which seawater is discharged in order to determine the concentration of hypochlorous acid the ph and temperature of seawater are measured simultaneously d a seawater inflow step to inflow external seawater the seawater flowing in the seawater inflow step flows along the piping a pumping step of pumping the seawater flowing in the seawater inflow step so as to flow along the pipeline supplying a current to the pipeline through which the seawater flows in the seawater flow stage using a power supply device a step of collecting the flowing seawater when the seawater flowing through the seawater box flows through the pipeline after the seawater flow step a step performed after the seawater collection step the hypochlorous acid measurement step of measuring hypochlorous acid contained in the collected seawater based on the measurement result of the hypochlorous acid measurement step a current adjustment step of adjusting the current supplied in the seawater electrolytic apparatus so that the hypochlorous acid concentration of the seawater discharged from the seawater electrolytic apparatus does not exceed the environmental standard of 0.2 ppm a seawater discharge step of discharging the seawater into which the concentration of hypochlorous acid has been converted according to the current regulation through the current regulating step from the seawater electrolytic apparatus and the seawater is completely discharged to the outside of the hull or the like after the seawater flow step the pumping step the method potential supply step and the seawater discharge step of the seawater electrolytic device is performed wherein the cooling is performed in the course of the step of cooling the marine plant cooling water line"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a method of inhibiting corrosion at least a part of the cooling target device group is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between the cooling water passing through the steel pipe and the cooling target device and the temperature of the cooling water after heat exchange becomes high"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in the type cooling facility at least a part of the group of cooled devices is indirectly cooled via a heat exchanger between the cooling water passing through the steel pipe and the cooled device and the cooling water after heat exchange is corrosion of the steel pipe after the indirect cooling and after the indirect cooling is included in the high heat load device or the first cooler after the high heat load device in which the water temperature becomes high"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "this is a method for inhibiting corrosion of a cooling system wherein at least a part of the group of devices to be cooled is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between cooling water passing through a steel pipe and the device to be cooled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "this is a method for inhibiting corrosion of a cooling system wherein at least a part of the group of devices to be cooled is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between cooling water passing through a steel pipe and the device to be cooled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "this is a method for inhibiting corrosion of a cooling system wherein at least a part of the group of devices to be cooled is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between cooling water passing through a steel pipe and the device to be cooled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "this is a method for inhibiting corrosion of a cooling system wherein at least a part of the group of devices to be cooled is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between cooling water passing through a steel pipe and the device to be cooled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "this is a method for inhibiting corrosion of a cooling system wherein at least a part of the group of devices to be cooled is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between cooling water passing through a steel pipe and the device to be cooled"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "thereby supply of the dissolved oxygen in the inner surface of the cooling water pipe 23 and the skid pipe 8a in the high heat load device 12a can be suppressed and the corrosion rate can be further reduced"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "thereby there exists a problem that the water flow distance until cooling water returns to the water treatment facility 1 from the elevated water tank 4 and the length of the part which performs heat exchange inside a skid pipe become long"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "therefore the corrosion rate of the skid pipe can be reduced by suppressing the temperature of the cooling water from increasing inside the skid pipe and suppressing the supply of dissolved oxygen"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "and at least a part of the group of devices to be cooled is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between the cooling water passing through the steel pipe and the device to be cooled a high heat load device in which the temperature of the cooling water after heat exchange becomes high is included"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "the following examples evaluated the effect of cooling water temperature on the corrosion rate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "as a result it was confirmed that both the corrosion prevention effect and the pipe clogging prevention effect can be achieved if the langeria index is in the range of 0.3 to 0.3.description of symbols 1 water treatment equipment 2 1st cooler 3 water pump 4 elevated water tank 5 mill cooling equipment 6 descaling equipment 7 furnace body 8 skid pipe 8b skid pipe 8b skid rail 8c refractory heat insulation 9 second cooler 10 pressurizer 11 circulating water type cooling equipment 12 cooled device group 12a high heat load device 13 circulating water treatment plant 14 water temperature measuring unit 15 cooling condition adjusting unit 16 flow rate measuring unit 17 flow rate adjusting unit 18 dechlorination device 21 furnace wall 22 water cooling jacket 23 cooling water piping"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5047535-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "1 is a partially broken perspective view schematically showing a conventional boiling water light water reactor having some features according to an embodiment of the present invention.1 is a schematic diagram illustrating a jet pump having several features according to an embodiment of the present invention.1 is a partially broken perspective view schematically illustrating a turbine having several features according to an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a flowchart illustrating one method for reducing stress corrosion cracking of components exposed to high temperature water in a high temperature water system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention.6 is a graph showing the effect of dissolved zinc on the crack growth rate of sensitized alloy 600.it is a graph showing the relationship between stress corrosion crack length and time showing the effect of zinc in reducing the crack growth rate of 316ss in high temperature water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100806134-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "it is composed of a double wall having a minimum temperature difference between the ground and the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent condensation inside the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent corrosion of the valve facility 110 disposed in the valve chamber structure 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101619674-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore it is important to clarify the characteristics of the corrosion behavior inside the pipeline through experiments in order to increase the safety of the co2 transfer process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101619674-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition according to the present invention it is possible to empirically simulate changes in the internal conditions of the pipeline such as concentration flow rate and temperature of the carbon dioxide mixture including the impurities and it has the effect of foreseeing and reducing negative influence factors of corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101619674-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "therefore according to the present invention by experimentally simulating changes in the internal conditions of the pipeline such as concentration flow rate and temperature of the carbon dioxide mixture including impurities it is possible to determine how the characteristics of the internal corrosion behavior of the pipeline during carbon dioxide long it has the effect of knowing the receipt and by doing so it predicts and reduces the negative influence factors of corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938463-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition the electrolytic treatment method is to crush manure and the like and to pass them through the electrode plate with a narrow gap between each other so that the decomposition and oxidation occurs by electricity not only is not easy to crush but also generated during electrolysis of seawater due to the strong oxidizing power of hypochlorous acid hclo 3 corrosion of the structure is easy and the treated water may contain excessive hypochlorous acid which may cause secondary pollution.the present invention was created in order to solve the above problems the object of the present invention is the wastewater by purifying various wastewater including manure generated in the vessel through four steps of microbial decomposition precipitation adsorption filtration and biodegradation disinfection it has good treatment capacity and it is easy to utilize the space of vessels where various equipments are concentrated and it is easy to maintain and adapt to load change or temperature change of waste water and also biochemical sewage treatment for ship that can minimize the sludge generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-4203806-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7443008-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore according to the above described embodiment flow accelerated corrosion can be effectively suppressed while employing relatively inexpensive components made of carbon steel in equipment where flow accelerated corrosion may occur"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7443008-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore according to the above described embodiment flow accelerated corrosion can be effectively suppressed while employing relatively inexpensive components made of carbon steel in equipment where flow accelerated corrosion may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100756497-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a vertical cylindrical body provided with a raw water inlet for introducing raw water into the lower part a heat transfer sheet made of carbon fiber installed at a lower end of the main body which is a lower portion of the raw water inlet so that raw water is heated to supply steam to the upper portion an aluminum sacrificial anode made of aluminum and installed above the raw water inlet of the main body to prevent corrosion by raw water introduced by applying an electric current an s shaped combustion tube which is installed from the lower part of the main body to the upper part and is installed to be in contact with the raw water introduced from the raw water inlet a burner installed at an upper end of the combustion tube to change steam into superheated steam a demister installed at an upper end of the main body to remove moisture contained in the heated superheated steam from the burner coil type is connected to the demister is supplied to remove the moisture and is in communication with the upper end of the combustion tube the superheated steam heated by the burner to remove the moisture to the superheated steam having a supercritical temperature it includes an inner cylinder of the high temperature oxidation unit is provided with an air inlet for oxidizing superheated steam having a supercritical temperature at high temperature a fan for moving superheated steam having a supercritical temperature to an inner cylinder end of the high temperature oxidation unit a condenser connected to the high temperature oxidation unit and installed at a lower side of the combustion tube and condensing superheated steam supplied from the high temperature oxidation unit to form water induction pipe connected to the condenser to induce superheated steam to the cooling coil cooling coil for cooling the high temperature oxidized pure water by heat exchange with the superheated steam flowing into the induction pipe a plate installed between the condenser and the cooling coil to prevent heat exchange between the condenser and the cooling coil a pure water storage tank installed at a lower end of the main body and connected to the cooling coil to store pure water which is cooled and a superheated steam heated from the lower end of the cooling coil and the upper part of the demister to the demister and a vacuum pump leading to the cooling coil through a high temperature oxidation unit and a condenser characterized in that consisting of the raw water inlet is a pure water production apparatus characterized in that the supply of heated raw water circulated through the cooling coil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100756497-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the pure water production apparatus of the present invention is a vertical cylindrical body having a raw water inlet for introducing the raw water to the bottom a heat transfer sheet made of carbon fiber installed at a lower portion of the main body which is a lower portion of the raw water inlet and allowing raw water to be heated to supply steam to the upper portion an aluminum sacrificial anode made of aluminum and installed above the raw water inlet of the main body to prevent corrosion by raw water introduced by applying an electric current an s shaped combustion tube which is installed from the lower part of the main body to the upper part and is installed to be in contact with the raw water introduced from the raw water inlet a burner installed at an upper end of the combustion tube to change steam into superheated steam a demister installed at an upper end of the main body to remove moisture contained in the heated superheated steam from the burner connected to the demister is supplied with steam to remove moisture and installed to communicate with the upper end of the combustion tube heated by the burner to remove the superheated steam with supercritical temperature to the superheated steam having an air inlet is provided with a high temperature oxidation unit for high temperature oxidation of the superheated steam having a supercritical temperature a condenser connected to the high temperature oxidation unit and installed at a lower side of the combustion tube to condense superheated steam supplied from the high temperature oxidation unit to form water a cooling coil connected to the condenser and heat exchanged with the raw water flowing into the main body to cool the high temperature oxidized pure water a plate installed between the condenser and the cooling coil to prevent heat exchange between the condenser and the cooling coil and a pure water storage tank installed at a lower end of the main body and connected to the cooling coil to store the pure water which is cooled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100756497-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "as shown the pure water manufacturing apparatus according to the present invention is a vertical cylindrical body 10 is provided with a raw water inlet 11 the heat transfer sheet 12 of the carbon fiber is installed on the bottom of the raw water inlet 11 the superheated steam of the aluminum sacrificial anode 20 to prevent corrosion by raw water the s shaped combustion tube 30 is installed from the lower portion of the main body 10 to the upper portion and the steam converted by the heat transfer sheet 12 burner 40 to be converted into a furnace a demister 50 for removing moisture contained in superheated steam and an air inlet 61 which is heated by the burner 40 to provide high temperature oxidation to superheat the superheated steam"}, {"pat_id": "US-7951298-B2", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "the reason the real time orp numbers rose so dramatically at the fw heater exit was most likely because of the corrosion that had occurred in the fw heater itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a contaminant separator for removing coarse and or fine contaminants contained in organic sewage an oxygen free liquid corrosion tank and an aerobic liquid corrosion tank connected to a rear end of the contaminant separator wherein the organic oxygen injected liquid containing the organic sewage is circulated between the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank and the aerobic liquid corrosion tank and the organic injected from the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank denitrification of nox n nitrogenous nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen of the circulating fluid circulated from the aerobic liquid corrosion tank using filthy water as a carbon source and residual circulating fluid circulated from the anoxic liquid corrosion tank in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank a liquid corrosion tank for oxidizing nh 4 n ammonia nitrogen to no x n nitrogen nitrogen or nitrous nitrogen by removing organics a temperature control device installed in the liquid corrosion tank to reduce an elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank it is connected to the rear end of the liquid corrosion tank to concentrate the liquid corrosion solution conveyed from the liquid corrosion tank to separate the concentrated sludge and the desorption liquid the concentration of the sludge in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank to measure the concentration of the concentrated sludge when lower than a predetermined reference concentration mlss control apparatus for returning to the aerobic liquid corrosion tank and conveying the desorption liquid to the anoxic liquid corrosion tank when the concentration is higher than the reference concentration a dehydrator connected to a rear end of the mlss controller for dehydrating by inputting an organic flocculant into the concentrated sludge a solid liquid separator connected to the rear end of the dehydrator and agglomerated by adding an inorganic coagulant and an organic coagulant to the dewatered desorption solution then flocculating or settling sludge and transferring the treated water to a neutralization tank an ozone processor connected to a rear end of the solid liquid separator and performing ozonation treatment of the treated water using ozone and a filter connected to the rear end of the ozone treatment unit for filtration and discharge of suspended solids increased after the ozone oxidation treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "the method of claim 8 shatterproof device connected to the rear end of the exhaust fan and configured to prevent the scattering of liquid and diffusion of odors by introducing the high temperature humid air stagnated in the upper layer in the liquid corrosion tank and the heat exchanged air dis