stagnated in the upper layer in the liquid corrosion tank and the heat exchanged air discharged from the cooling tank it may further include"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "on the other hand the liquid corrosion tank is equipped with a multi purpose temperature control device can reduce the liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion liquid rises due to the exothermic reaction in the process of removing organic matter and nitrogen in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the temperature control device 100 according to the present embodiment may be applied to the liquid corrosion tank 120 in the wastewater treatment facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "the temperature control device 100 may be selectively installed in the aerobic tank 121 in the liquid corrosion tank 120"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_333", "text": "5 5a the sump assembly 500 may be made from material that is corrosion and high temperature resistant"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_333", "text": "a corrosion resistant material is preferred because the sump is exposed to high temperatures moisture and corrosive source water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_354", "text": "7 the lower flange 704 and upper flange 712 may be manufactured out of any material having sufficient structural strength and corrosion and temperature resistant properties"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_378", "text": "in alternate embodiments other materials may be used with preference that those materials have the properties of high temperature resistance corrosion resistance do not absorb water and have sufficient structural strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358103-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the flexible conduit tube is wavy so it is very easy to draw wires and is not subject to temperature changes so there is no need for relaxation mea