nism culture tank the sludge which has been settled in the primary settling tank 310 is supplied to the primary microorganism culture tank 314 by the primary transfer pump 313 and supplied to the primary microorganism culture tank 314 the air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the primary bioreactor 315 and the lower portion of the primary microorganism culture tank 314 to supply the wastewater while the aeration is performed to convert the polyphenol compounds into metabolites corrosive microorganisms that convert water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors humic substances precursors or corrosive substances humic substances and microorganisms that are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms are excreted by the corrosion reaction and then sent to the aeration tank 310 where the primary biological wastewater treatment the entire system is induced to become wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and microorganisms that are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms the solids are precipitated in the first settling tank 311 and the overflowed the first biologically treated water which is the overflow is treated with the first biological treatment stage of the low concentration wastewater sent to the first biological treatment tank 400 when the primary biological treatment water is supplied to the primary biological treatment water storage tank 400 electrolytic oxidation treatment electron beam treatment eelectron beam treatment or electrolytic oxidation treatment and electronic pretreatment are performed to remove the biodegradable organic matter contained in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the settled solids are supplied to the secondary settling tank 416 by the central cone cone it is possible to deposit active erosion material pellets minerals containing active minerals minerals or ceramics that emit negative ions and ultraviolet rays that emit far infrared rays and negative ions by the secondary transfer pump 417 the excess sludge is returned to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 and the secondary aeration tank 414 in which the secondary bioreactor 419 filled with the mineral or ceramics packing 420 is loaded and the excess sludge discharged is discharged temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater and the biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage together with the excess sludge to be discharged to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 sludge precipitated in the secondary settling tank 415 is supplied to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the secondary bioreactor 419 and the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 a corrosive microorganism which transforms water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors or corrosive substances by providing a polyphenol compound as a metabolite by supplying a wastewater and microbes in symbiotic relationships and sent to the secondary aeration tank 414 to induce the whole of the secondary biological wastewater treatment system to be subjected to the wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and the microorganisms which are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms and the secondary settling tank 415 the second biologically treated water which is the overflowing water is the second biological treatment step of the low concentration wastewater sent to the final biological treatment water tank 421 the secondary biologically treated water is subjected to sterilization treatment by a combination of at least one of oxidizing agent oxidizing agent ultraviolet ray irradiation electrolytic oxidation or electron beam irradiation and then subjected to sand filtration to remove suspended solids a final treatment step of the wastewater discharging the treated water when the dehydrated cake dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process is supplied to the mixer 500 a moisture adjuster and a soil conditioner are injected into the mixer mixer 501 while stirring to adjust the water content to 60 to 65 wt and fed to a fermentation tank 503 which is opened and straightened by the fermentation tank feed conveyor 502 and then flipped to the fermentation tank mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 30 to 50 days"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3635942-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the system comprises a main control device with which it connects the power unit of the control system used for power supply the heating unit used to increase the temperature the cooling unit to be used to decrease the temperature the water pump unit used to pump the water out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "meanwhile when the chamber 10 is buried in the ground condensation is generated in the wall plate 12 due to a temperature difference between the pipe and the underground and such condensation occurs along the wall plate 12 of the chamber 10 and the bottom plate 13 it becomes a factor of failure due to corrosion of various valves and measuring instruments"}, {"pat_id": "US-4343683-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100408926-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "chemical resistance is especially suitable for sewage or gas and it does not leak due to ion dissolution and has a favorable effect on maintenance"}]</data>
