  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100357289-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "therefore the wastewater that has passed through the settled land is subjected to filtration or centrifugation as in method 2 or 3 when the suspended solids contamination concentration is 500mg l to 1000mg l and to the centrifugation process to remove the suspended matter when 1000mg l or more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aeration tank for aerating the treated water so that aerobic microorganisms propagate in the treated water by the supplied oxygen to form floes a measurement unit for measuring and monitoring a treatment state by sampling a predetermined amount of the treated water being treated in the aeration tank a suction unit connected to one or more of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water from each of the aeration tanks and supplying the collected water to the measuring unit a discharge unit connecting the measurement unit and the aeration tank so that the treated water measured by the measurement unit is discharged back to the aeration tank and a central processing unit that receives the measurement data measured by the measurement unit analyzes the measurement data and controls the measurement unit the suction unit and the discharge unit the suction part one or more aeration tank connection pipes connected to each of the aeration tanks one end of which is disposed so as to be submerged in each of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water in each aeration tank and a scoring point control unit installed at the bottom of the aeration tank connection pipe installed to be drawn into the lower part of the aeration tank connection pipe or drawn out to the outside and to adjust the depth inserted into the aeration tank the measuring unit a measuring tank accommodating the treated water supplied through the inlet and having a washing water inlet through which washing water flows a spray nozzle installed at the washing water inlet inside the measuring tank to inject washing water into the measuring tank an angle adjusting unit rotatably installed at an end of the spray nozzle and adjusting a spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle a rotating inner tube installed on an inner circumferential surface of the measuring tank and having a plurality of through holes a rotary driving unit installed to be connected to the rotating inner tube to transmit power to the rotating inner tube and to rotate the rotating inner tube inside the measuring tank to form a vortex inside the measuring tank a washing state confirmation unit installed inside the measuring tank to photograph the inside of the measuring tank the control unit of the central processing unit analyzes the degree of contamination of the measurement tank through the image of the inside of the measurement tank captured by the washing state confirmation unit and analyzes whether or not cleaning of the inside of the measurement tank is necessary or a part requiring cleaning when the control unit confirms a position requiring washing the spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle is adjusted as the angle adjuster rotates a washing unit for cleaning the inside of the measurement tank by spraying washing water into the measurement tank after the treated water measured in the measurement tank is discharged to the aeration tank through the discharge unit and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting the freeze protection unit a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe a heating unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction part the treated water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part and when the temperature sensed by the temperature sensing unit is equal to or less than a predetermined temperature a temperature control unit for adjusting the heating temperature of the heating unit so that the treated water or washing water inside the pipe does not freeze"}, {"pat_id": "US-4957624-A", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "an arrangement for purifying water comprising receiving means having a confined space for receiving a liquid said receiving means including means for introducing a predetermined finite amount of impure water to be purified into said receiving means said receiving means further including holding means for accumulating and holding the partially purified water in the form of a body of water therein means for filtering the water prior to being introduced into said holding means to obtain partially purified water means for heating at least some of the partially purified water to a temperature to and about the boiling point thereof means for returning the partially purified heated water to said filtering means which in turn filters and returns the water passing through said filter means to said holding means to begin a new heating and filtration cycle with attendant further purification of the partially purified water said heating means being maintained activated until the degree of contamination of such water has dropped below a predetermined level said receiving and holding means including a vessel having an upper region receiving said filtering means and a lower region for holding the body of water and a perforated lid removably supported on said upper region said vessel having an outlet at said lower region thereof wherein said heating means includes an external heater situated at the exterior of said vessel and communicating with said vessel outlet and wherein said returning means includes a riser tube communicating with said heater and having an outlet end for directing steam generated by said heater and slugs of water entrained by such steam and jointly rising in said riser tube generally toward said filtering means"}, {"pat_id": "US-4957624-A", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an arrangement for purifying water comprising receiving means having a confined space for receiving a liquid said receiving means including means for introducing a predetermined finite amount of impure water to be purified into said receiving means said receiving means further including holding means for accumulating and holding the partially purified water in the form of a body of water therein means for filtering the water prior to being introduced into said holding means to obtain partially purified water means for heating at least some of the partially purified water to a temperature to and about the boiling point thereof means for returning the partially purified heated water to said filtering means which in turn filters and returns the water passing through said filter means to said holding means to begin a new heating and filtration cycle with attendant further purification of the partially purified water said heating means being maintained activated until the degree of contamination of such water has dropped below a predetermined level said receiving and holding means including a vessel having an upper region receiving said filtering means and a lower region for holding the body of water and a perforated lid removably supported on said upper region said circulating means including a riser tube extending upwardly from said heating means and having an outlet end for directing steam generated by said heating means and slugs of water entrained by such steam moving through said riser tube generally toward said filtering means a holding cup received in said upper region of said vessel and including a portion into which said introducing means and the outlet end of said riser tube are directed and a main portion accommodating said filtering means in such a manner that water flowing from the outlet end of said riser tube enters said filtering means from below to flow upwardly through said filtering means and is discharged from an upper region of said filtering means to spill over a rim of the holding cup and proceed toward said holding means"}, {"pat_id": "US-4957624-A", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "an arrangement for purifying water comprising receiving means having a confined space for receiving a liquid said receiving means including means for introducing a predetermined finite amount of impure water to be purified into said receiving means said receiving means further including holding means for accumulating and holding the partially purified water in the form of a body of water therein means for filtering the water prior to being introduced into said holding means to obtain partially purified water means for heating at least some of the partially purified water to a temperature to and about the boiling point thereof means for returning the partially purified heated water to said filtering means which in turn filters and returns the water passing through said filter means to said holding means to begin a new heating and filtration cycle with attendant further purification of the partially purified water said heating means being maintained activated until the degree of contamination of such water has dropped below a predetermined level and means for selectively interrupting the flow of purified water of the body to said filtering means subsequent tot he completion of the purifying operation with attendant rise in the temperature of the water of the body to its boiling point and by continued heating convert a portion of such water into steam wherein said receiving means has at least one discharge opening situated above said body of water for the discharge of the thus generated steam therethrough out of said vessel and further comprising means for condensing the thus discharged steam received from said vessel into water and for collecting the condensed water in a collecting space for eventual use"}, {"pat_id": "US-4957624-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "then the heating means may advantageously include an electric resistance heater so situated in the accumulation chamber as to be fully immersed in the body of water and the circulating means may include a steam collecting bell disposed upwardly of the heater for collecting steam generated by the heater and a riser tube extending from the steam collecting bell toward the filtering means for conducting the collected steam together with water slugs entrained thereby to the filtering means"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "the washing tub 210 may further include a washing tub contamination measuring sensor for measuring the degree of contamination of the washing liquid and transmitting the measurement result to the controller 59"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3319944-B2", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "according to the present invention as described above when the photographing means is housed in a camera case having a transparent monitoring window on the lower surface and the light shielding hood is placed on the water surface together with the lighting means since it is arranged at a certain distance from the water surface in the space above the water surface in the light blocking hood determined by the float mounting position the photographing means the lighting means and the monitoring window of the camera case are connected to the water in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "determining whether the preset threshold value is exceeded and 1 when the controller 200 determines that the sum of the influence value a2 due to the water temperature and the influence value a4 due to the membrane contamination is greater than the preset limit value the water treatment system using a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition after the step k l the control unit 200 is the influence value a4 due to the membrane contamination is less than a predetermined reference the influence value a2 and the membrane contamination due to the water temperature determining whether the sum of the influence values a4 is greater than the preset limit value and l1 when the controller 200 determines that the sum of the influence value a2 due to the water temperature and the influence value a4 due to the membrane fouling is greater than the preset limit value the water treatment using a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "next the control unit 200 calculates the influence value a4 due to membrane contamination in a predetermined manner by using the calculated pretreatment filter the water temperature and the influence values a1 a2 a3 due to the osmotic pressure and the initial expected pump operation rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "after that in a process in which a temperature control process using a heat exchanger or steam is added if it is determined that the sum of the influence value a2 due to the water temperature and the influence value a4 due to the membrane contamination exceeds the preset limit value further adjusting the temperature of the water treatment system using a conditioning process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the air nozzle 20 is provided integrally with the injection pipe 21 and at the same time one or more are fixed so that the supplied air is sprayed so that water can circulate in the storage tank 80 and at the end of the injection pipe 21 a fitting 22 is provided so that one touch coupling with the air supply hose 23 is possible and the fitting 22 is installed on the side surface 12 of the main body 10 and the inner receiving space of the main body 10 11 is filled with anti pollution means 30 in which elvan quartz loess balls activated carbon and charcoal are mixed to prevent contamination or deterioration of stored water and a perforated groove 41 at the upper end thereof to prevent separation the formed cover plate 40 is coupled and fixed to the main body while on one side of the edge of the main body 10 a heating wire 50 for preventing freezing and a temperature at which the inside temperature is sensed to transmit a signal to the controller 70 one or more water pollution prevention units d having the sensor 60 installed and fixed are disposed on the bottom of the storage tank and fixing the water pollution prevention units installed and fixed in series or parallel when the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe passes through the filter and is stored as water in the storage tank the stored water is contamination prevention means 30 by spraying air from the air nozzle 20 of the water pollution prevention unit d and sprayed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "21 and one or more are fixed at the same time and a fitting 22 is provided at the end of the injection pipe 21 so that it can be one touch coupled with the air supply hose 23 the fitting 22 is the body it is installed on the side surface 12 of the 10 and the internal receiving space 11 of the main body 10 contains a mixture of elvan quartz loess balls activated carbon and charcoal so as to prevent contamination or deterioration of the stored water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "it is installed and the internal receiving space 11 of the main body 10 is filled with elvan stone quartz loess ball activated carbon and anti pollution means 30 mixed with charcoal so as to prevent contamination or deterioration of the stored water and the at the upper end a cover plate 40 having a perforated groove 41 formed thereon to prevent separation is fixed to the main body while on one side of the edge of the main body 10 a heating wire 50 for freezing prevention and an internal temperature one or more water pollution prevention units d installed and fixed with a temperature sensor 60 that detects and transmits a signal to the controller 70 are disposed on the bottom of the storage tank but are installed and fixed in series or in parallel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "21 and one or more are fixed at the same time and a fitting 22 is provided at the end of the injection pipe 21 so that it can be one touch coupled with the air supply hose 23 the fitting 22 is the body it is installed on the side surface 12 of the 10 and the internal receiving space 11 of the main body 10 contains a mixture of elvan quartz loess balls activated carbon and charcoal so as to prevent contamination or deterioration of the stored water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102026864-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the technical problem to be achieved by the present invention in the reinforcement using a lining panel of a stainless steel material in the interior of the conventional concrete water tank as described above the expansion and contraction action occurs in the material of the lining panel by the water pressure and the internal temperature of the lining panel preventing the damage and coating the outer surface of the structure consisting of lining panels to prevent contamination of water from oxides and contaminants that are likely to be generated by by products during construction and additionally using a grouting agent to damage the damaged parts of conventional concrete the lining panel can be repaired and coated on the lining panel using a stainless coating agent to prevent rust and corrosion of the plate due to contact with water for a long time as a damaged part of the surface of the lining panel generated during bending welding and the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-9749792-B2", "para_id": "para_115", "text": "because the present invention water use and water energy monitoring apparatus can be used in situations where the source of water comes for a well or non commercial operation and furthermore where the commercial operations water treatments plants are under pressure to provide more water supplies or where problems breakdowns or accidental situations can cause contamination of the water source the present invention can be fitted with display parameters of and provide warning for numerous mineral elements and biological contaminates"}, {"pat_id": "US-7726138-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "for an atmospheric water recovery method and means for obtaining potable water from atmospheric air in which cold deep seawater is pumped through a heat exchanger that reacts with humid air to produce condensate potable water that is collected in a tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100378569-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "therefore it is necessary to control temperature appropriately by cooling to maintain mid temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100785044-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 wherein the air supply facility 3 is installed by modifying the existing air supply facility 3 to prevent contamination of the submerged membrane 10 in the aerobic tank 9 and to maintain dissolved oxygen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102732710-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "as described above the electrode of the ph sensor 1330 must be free of contamination and may require periodic renewal and correction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_487", "text": "16 the gear pump 326 of the conventional underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment has the advantages of being compact lightweight and inexpensive and can withstand harsh operating conditions contamination by dust rise in oil temperature overload so it is particularly suitable for hydraulic drive in construction machinery industrial vehicles agricultural machinery etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-8496832-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "we have found that passing the water vapor through the fritted membrane in combination with the adsorption and aeration steps acts to exclude any residual volatile chemicals and even acts to reduce residual bacterial contamination with much greater efficiency than a conventional distillation process"}, {"pat_id": "US-5259203-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "thus the water being used as the refrigerant is periodically mixed with the condensed water subjecting it to contamination and making the consumption of the water questionable"}, {"pat_id": "US-5646863-A", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "to reduce the effect of organic contamination on the electrode surfaces an absorptive stripping voltage combined with a unique voltage is applied to measuring cell working electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "according to claim 1 the raw water inlet pipe is attached to one side before the raw water is injected into the virus sterilization device is attached to the contaminant sensor to determine the degree of contamination to prevent the inflow and inflow of raw water to the raw water inlet valve the virus sterilization device is the location where the raw water inflow distributing large particles by distributing large screens distributing raw water to virus sterilizers plural uv lamps or uvleds are installed inside virus sterilizers and ozone injection hoses installed outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the raw water inlet pipe 10 is attached to one side before the raw water is injected into the virus sterilization device 16 is attached to the contaminant sensor 12 to determine the degree of contamination to prevent the inflow and inflow of raw water to the raw water inlet valve 14 in addition the virus sterilization device 20 installs a distribution screen 22 at a position where raw water is introduced to filter foreign matter having large particles distributes and supplies the raw water into the virus sterilization device 20 and a virus sterilization device 20 a plurality of uv lamps or uvleds 24 are installed therein and ozone is introduced through an ozone injection hose 28 from an ozone generator 26 installed outside to sterilize viruses and a virus sterilizer 20 it provides a water supply system for supplying fish farm facilities capable of controlling water temperature and virus sterilization of raw water passing through the virus sensor 16 and then measuring the virus through the filtration device 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101716466-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation sensor 18 installed in a drainage passage 213 of the solar cell module 21 to measure the amount of precipitation water collected in the solar cell module 21 an opening and closing unit 225 connected at both ends to the drainage passage 213 and connected to an elastic string 281 for detecting the amount of precipitation by the precipitation sensor 18 to determine the opening and closing level of the collecting tube 221 a collecting connection unit 12 connected to the drainage passage 213 for collecting the precipitation a control server 11 for controlling the operation of the opening closing means installed in the collection connection unit 12 based on the information transmitted from the precipitation sensor 18 a storage unit 15 in which the precipitation is stored a detection unit 16 for detecting the state of water stored in the storage unit 15 and and a branch unit 14 operated by the control server 11 based on the information transmitted from the detection unit 16 the storage unit 15 is installed under the solar cell module and is shielded by the solar cell module"}, {"pat_id": "US-8038881-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the on line sensors 140 are used to measure and feed the control unit information on multiple parameters such as tph nitrogen dissolved oxygen toc and temperature listed in table 1 below anticipate inlet fluctuations in conjunction with the controller that has been specifically designed for predefined flow rates and identify contamination type as well as level of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101928816-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "s10 transmitting a measured value from the first temperature sensor and the conductivity sensor to the control unit by draining a large amount of cooling water and supplying new raw water to replace the cooling water s20 of calculating the electric conductivity calculated value from the measured value received in step s20 and when the electric conductivity calculated value is equal to or more than the first reference electric conductivity s30 and the step of calculating the electric conductivity calculated in the step s20 s40 of opening the drain valve when the quasi electroconductivity is exceeded measuring the value of the total dissolved solids of the cooling water accommodated in the cooling tower at the first and second points of view through the tds meter calculating a tds increase rate from a value obtained by the first and second pressure sensors s50 determining whether the tds increase rate exceeds a preset reference tds increase rate s51 s60 and when the difference between the two pressure values received in the step s60 exceeds the reference pressure difference range through the control unit the discharge valve is opened to discharge foreign matter s07"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101962825-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an extraction well a water permeation reaction wall of a sand layer a biochar layer or a biochar alginate bead layer formed on the outer periphery of the extraction well a siphon pipeline installed outwardly from the inside of the extraction well an activated charcoal and a zero valent iron powder mixed powder filter disposed in the middle of the siphon pipeline for filtering odor and ground chlorinated organic compounds and a real time pollution degree measuring device connected to the extraction well wherein the contaminated groundwater passes through the permeable reaction wall of the sand layer the bio char layer or the bio char alginate bead layer to remove organic pollutants and heavy metal pollutants the present invention relates to a method for purifying harmful groundwater which is capable of continuously pumping purified groundwater in a well by means of a siphon hydraulic power and to purify odorous components and chlorinated organic compounds contained in the pumped the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the pollutant contamination degree of the extraction well is automatically measured in real time to monitor contamination and when the pollution degree is higher than the reference value the water permeation reaction wall of the sand layer repair the biochar of the biochar layer of the permeable reaction wall is filled with wood byproducts in an electric furnace under an oxygen free anaerobic condition and subjected to pyrolysis reaction in a temperature range of 300 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-6773588-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "thus in some climes where the municipal water temperature is particularly cool and an ro is used as the purification unit it may be desirable to add a simple heater at the upstream end of the modular manifold and such a preheater module is also shown as head 13y in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "groundwater contamination prevention structure 1 1 is built in the space inside the combined structure to combine and directly connected to each other and sealed to each other structural structure 1 1 1 is installed inside the underground rock well inside the casing 4 4 to prevent the groundwater contamination by itself and to automatically drain and drain the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "it maintains the same level of water that is inflowed by itself and automatically intakes and pumps while preventing groundwater contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and at the same time automatically takes in and pumps the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837105-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "therefore according to the embodiment of the present invention it is possible to prevent the external air from flowing into the internal space 51c of the pdf panel 50 through the foam insulating material 60 to prevent condensation caused by the temperature difference the internal contamination degree of the pdf panel water tank 1 equipped with the system can be lowered and the effect of reinforcing the interior of the pdf panel 50 can be expected"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7396654-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "q h f t hin f t cin f f here f is an influence coefficient due to contamination of the heater 2 and the degree of contamination of the heater 2 is determined by the detected values from the flow meter 91 temperature detector 92 steam thermometer 94 and temperature detector 96"}, {"pat_id": "US-6562205-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "thus the high temperature ultrapure water produced by the apparatus of the invention is found suitable for cleaning wafers in the semiconductor fabrication process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100397313-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "in table 4 than room temperature for a severe high temperature metal ion contamination the degree of fe ions are eluted only 1 10 10 atoms cm 2 or less can not be accepted in a semiconductor fabrication process that is not a problem and thus high temperature ultra pure water produced according to the present invention it can be seen that the high temperature ultrapure water produced by the device is suitable for the wafer cleaning of the semiconductor manufacturing process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102545607-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the method of claim 10 livestock wastewater treatment action characterized in that it further comprises a microorganism collection and dormancy process s90 of collecting and storing the filtered microorganisms in a low temperature container to prevent contamination and then introducing them into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed of movement and dormant treatment cultivation method of asrobacter crystallopoietes strain to improve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102545607-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "to prevent contamination and then put into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed for example a movement speed of 2 m sec to dormant microorganism collection and dormancy process s90 is preferably further included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102545607-B1", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "to prevent contamination and then put into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed for example 2m sec for dormant treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102623682-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a temperature sensor not shown that detects contamination of tap water and a water quality sensor not shown may be installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102313700-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "of tap water flowing along the pipeline and wirelessly transmit the level to the water quality monitor or the water quality monitoring central control room it is related to the valve for monitoring and controlling the water quality of the water supply pipe that cuts off the supply to the household and determines the discharge of the sewage when it exceeds the standard value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101610599-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "further the high temperature water treatment apparatus according to the present invention has an effect of minimizing an increase in the differential pressure of the separation membrane thereby reducing the frequency of chemical cleaning due to membrane contamination and prolonging the life of the separation membrane.1 is a conceptual diagram of an advanced water treatment apparatus using a dissolved air floating apparatus and a submerged membrane separation tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100935446-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the high temperature 800 1 100 is isolated from the combustion chamber 102 by the metal heating tube 101 to prevent contamination of gas or air flow through the combustion chamber 102 the combustion chamber 102 is completely burned by high temperature the gas or air flow is introduced into the third dust collector 28 through the exhaust pipe 104 collected and cleaned and then discharged into the stack 29"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433871-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the control device may include the degree of contamination of raw water or treated water measured by the sensing device internal and external temperature of the water treatment unit internal and external humidity of the water treatment unit and a pump that analyzes the amount of sunlight irradiated to the water treatment device in real time and is installed in front of the first water quality detection device to supply raw water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10590011-B2", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "this is due to the fact that the temperature of the external environment is lower than the temperature at the surface of the wall 12 inside the chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the conventional automatic chlorine injection system as described above and the problem to be solved by the present invention is to provide an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a water tank of a public building which can store a large amount of chlorine in the automatic chlorine injection device and timely inject and replenish it and also prevent deterioration of the chlorine solution due to changes in the surrounding temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to solve the above mentioned problem the automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a water tank of a public building according to the present invention comprises a main storage tank storing a predetermined amount of chlorine solution inside one or more auxiliary storage tanks installed on one side of the main storage tank and replenishing the chlorine solution to the main storage tank a cooling device installed in the main storage tank and cooling the chlorine solution stored in the main storage tank and the auxiliary storage tank to maintain the same at a predetermined temperature a quantitative pump installed inside or outside the main storage tank and quantitatively discharging the chlorine solution stored inside the main storage tank and it includes a control device installed on one side of the main storage tank and controlling the operation of the cooling device and the quantitative pump wherein the control device detects the water level of tap water stored inside the reservoir to calculate the real time storage capacity of the tap water measures the chlorine concentration of the tap water and determines the chlorine injection time and injection amount based on the change in tap water usage according to the day of the week and time thereby operating the quantitative pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention provides an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a public building water tank which stores a large amount of chlorine in an automatic chlorine injection device and enables timely injection and replenishment and also prevents deterioration of chlorine solution due to changes in ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3497806-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "to prevent the measurement accuracy from deteriorating due to contamination of these pipes and water quality detector while controlling the water temperature of the inflow water flowing into the water purification plant and sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359693-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as such the direct cooling water purifier 1 has an excellent cooling effect by directly cooling the purified water but has a problem in safety because the purified water is immediately contaminated when the refrigerant leaks from the evaporator.the present invention is designed to solve the problems of the prior art as described above has excellent thermal efficiency to supply a large amount of purified cold and hot water and has a double tube evaporator to solve the contamination problem by the refrigerant the purpose of the present invention is to provide a large capacity cold hot water purifier using a circulation pump for water purification tank to maintain an even temperature distribution"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7009733-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "it occupies a large area of the digested structure avoids problems such as energy consumption due to the heat insulation system of the structure reduces operating costs and at the same time avoids the addition of the chemicals of the present invention and secondary contamination from the source"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the pet water dispenser may also include an illumination assembly having a lighting device a water level sensor a water temperature sensor a proximity sensor a contamination level sensor a thermoelectric element or device and a sterilizing filter e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the wireless power transmitter 72 and the wireless power receiver 73 may exchange information such as state condition or coupling information of the docking station 71 water tank 10 and or the inner assembly 100 power usage information battery charging information of the battery b battery output voltage current information control information or information from various sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200186594-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of upper and lower cases 1 2 having an o ring 3 in the coupling portion to achieve a predetermined size and shape and waterproof and the lower case 2 is suction of water to perform a buoyancy control function the ballast 16 is provided with discharge ports 9a and 9b and the piston 7a is moved up and down by forward and reverse rotation of the dc motor 5a above the ballast 16 to obtain diving and buoyancy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the contamination index calculating unit 343 calculates the contamination index of the membrane filtration tank 320 by using a pressure gauge p for measuring the inter membrane pressure difference kpa a viscometer c for measuring the viscosity of the raw water that has been pretreated q for measuring the flow rate of the filtrate and may include a calculator not shown for calculating the contamination index fi according to equation 1 by applying each measured value additionally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "at this time the determination unit 346 may determine that the chemical cleaning is performed when the temperature of the raw water is equal to or higher than the reference temperature the current time is included in the reference time zone or the date is included"}, {"pat_id": "US-9494480-B2", "para_id": "para_112", "text": "because the present invention water use and water energy monitoring apparatus can be used in situations where the source of water comes for a well or non commercial operation and furthermore where the commercial operations water treatments plants are under pressure to provide more water supplies or where problems breakdowns or accidental situations can cause contamination of the water source the present invention can be fitted with display parameters of and provide warning for numerous mineral elements and biological contaminates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100217951-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "when the heater 25 is operated by the temperature sensor 15 mounted on the fermentation vessel 70 to keep the temperature constant and to promote the fermentation the fermentation is more easily performed when the enzyme is added.according to the present invention as described above the food waste residue fermentation and wastewater treatment device of the present invention is a device for disinfecting food waste removing water from a centrifuge fermenting the remaining semi dry food waste it is an extremely useful invention in the environmental industry because it has an effect of preventing contamination of soil and water quality by enabling fermentation and sewage treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972507-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "by circulating a portion of the treated water the concentration reaction time is shortened and the concentration reaction while the heating temperature of the treated water is maintained the treated water of the concentrated reaction tank is introduced into the heat exchanger again so that the heated treated water of the acid wastewater flowing in contact with the outside of the coiled inner tube into which the acidic wastewater is introduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102172981-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "to measure the water quality of multi sampling samples collected from multiple series by using a sensor it is easy to maintain while reducing the installation cost of the sensor and it is possible to reduce the deviation of the measured value due to sensor contamination and measurement consistency by measuring the multi sampling sample with the same measuring instrument sensor at one measurement location"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101504545-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the water treatment apparatus according to the present invention comprises a water collecting tank 10 in which raw water is introduced and stored a pretreatment means 20 30 for low turbidity and tacticity which is installed at the downstream end of the water collecting tank 10 and whose operation is controlled according to the turbidity of raw water an automatic backwash filter 40 supplied with the treated water of the preliminary treatment means 20 and 30 for the low turbidity or tackiness and a water treatment device 40 for receiving the treated water of the automatic backwashing filter 40 a brackish water and sea water membrane 50 60 for controlling the operation according to the dissolved water concentration of the treated water to separate the dissolved ionic material of the raw water and use it as a purified water a membrane cleaning device cip 70 for cleaning the membranes 50 and 60 to prevent secondary contamination due to microorganisms or external contaminants in the treated water treated in the membranes 50 and 60 and chlorine disinfection or ultraviolet disinfection uv sterilizing means 80 a treatment water tank 90 for storing sterilized treated water in the sterilization means 80 and supplying purified water to the sterilization means 80 a mineralsetron connected to the treated water tank 90 for supplying the minerals removed from the membranes 50 and 60 tds turbidity and temperature measurement values of the supply means 95 and the water collecting tank 10 to measure the total dissolved solids tds turbidity and temperature of the water collecting tank 10 50 60 to drive the water purification apparatus in accordance with the raw water conditions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130731-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an automatic cleaning unit for cleaning the foreign matter attached wherein the uv treatment unit uv lamp unit for irradiating the ultraviolet light to the filtered water in the filtering unit a washing unit for removing the foreign matter attached to the ultraviolet lamp unit and the ultraviolet ray uv intensity meter for measuring the intensity of ultraviolet light from the lamp and on temperature for measuring the temperature inside the body including a sensor it can prevent secondary pollution due to by products prevent contamination of tanks efficient and easy to maintain sterilization effect and product miniaturization and an integrated water treatment device using an ultraviolet lamp"}]</data>
