e pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-10029923-B2", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "as the fresh water collected in the liquid pools 25a to 25d is collected by condensing the steam gasified from the heated raw water temperature of the fresh water is higher than raw water thus heat is transferred from the fresh water to the raw water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100375819-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "since there are many parts the mechanical failure frequency is high and the drying temperature is difficult to control and thus the drying sludge having the desired moisture content cannot be obtained.the present invention has been made to improve the problems of the conventional drying apparatus by mixing a predetermined amount of dry sludge already dried in the dehydration sludge having a high moisture content by putting into the dryer \u2460 reducing the sludge drying treatment time in the dryer \u2461 it is an object of the present invention to maximize the daily throughput of the sludge and to provide a sludge drying apparatus that can adjust the water content of the sludge to the user s intended level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101367947-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hopper in which collected food waste is stored a primary sorting mill for receiving and crushing food waste from the hopper and sorting out various foreign matters a fine grinding machine for finely crushing the food waste which is sorted and supplied from the primary sorting mill a primary fermenter which receives the food wastes crushed and supplied from the fine crusher and indirectly heats them with low temperature steam in a vacuum under reduced pressure to discharge moisture and primary fermentation and drying of the water wastes a secondary fermenter which receives fermented products discharged from the primary fermenter and discharged from the primary fermenter and indirectly heats them with low temperature steam in a reduced pressure vacuum to ferment the dried fermented product to produce fermented feed a secondary sorting mill for pulverizing fermented feed discharged from the secondary fermenter and sorting various foreign substances by magnetic force a condensation tank configured to receive water discharged from the primary fermenter and condense it using a heat exchanger a coagulation tank for coagulating by administering a coagulant to the condensed water supplied from the condensation tank a high speed sedimentation tank for sedimenting the sludge discharged from the coagulation tank at high speed to separate the supernatant and the sludge activated carbon tank for filtering the supernatant discharged from the high speed precipitater using activated carbon a reverse osmosis membrane tank for discharging the filtered water discharged from the activated carbon tank using a reverse osmosis membrane a concentration tank for concentrating the sludge discharged from the high speed settler and a system for producing fermented feed fermented compost or liquid fertilizer using food waste characterized by dehydrating sludge discharged from the thickening tank to produce fermented compost and discharging the fermented compost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101367947-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a hopper in which collected food waste is stored a primary sorting mill for receiving and crushing food waste from the hopper and sorting out various foreign matters a fine grinding machine for finely crushing the food waste which is sorted and supplied from the primary sorting mill a primary fermenter which receives the food wastes crushed and supplied from the fine crusher and indirectly heats them with low temperature steam in a vacuum under reduced pressure to discharge moisture and primary fermentation and drying of the water wastes a secondary fermenter which receives fermented products discharged from the primary fermenter and discharged from the primary fermenter and indirectly heats them with low temperature steam in a reduced pressure vacuum to ferment the dried fermented product to produce fermented feed a secondary sorting mill for pulverizing fermented feed discharged from the secondary fermenter and sorting various foreign substances by magnetic force a condensation tank configured to receive water discharged from the primary fermenter and condense it using a heat exchanger a coagulation tank for coagulating by administering a coagulant to the condensed water supplied from the condensation tank a high speed sedimentation tank for sedimenting the sludge discharged from the coagulation tank at high speed to separate the supernatant and the sludge activated carbon tank for filtering the supernatant discharged from the high speed precipitater using activated carbon a reverse osmosis membrane tank for discharging the filtered water discharged from the activated carbon tank using a reverse osmosis membrane a concentration tank for concentrating the sludge discharged from the high speed settler and a dehydrator for producing fermentation compost by dewatering the sludge discharged from the thickening tank and discharging the fermentation compost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273956-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to provide a powder containing minerals and a method for preparing the same which can reduce the purification cost.in order to achieve the above object the preparation method of the powder containing minerals of the present invention includes 6 to 10 parts by weight of persimmon leaves 6 to 10 parts by weight of oak leaves 6 to 10 parts by weight of larvae leaves 4 to 7 parts by weight of melon 4 to 7 parts by weight of pineapple 4 to 7 parts by weight of mango 4 to 7 parts by weight of persimmon 4 to 7 parts by weight of banana 20 to 30 parts by weight of water 18 to 32 parts by weight of brown sugar in a stirrer mixing process a primary fermentation aging process of storing the mixed solution mixed in the grinding mixing process in a fermentation vessel and fermenting and fermenting at a temperature of 18 to 22 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100665251-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "among the harmful substances transported the dust is collected by the dust filtration unit and released to the outside and some dust and the volatile organic compound gas is a part of the heat source sent to the combustor from the heat exchanger to the chamber in order to prevent dust from coal filtration and harmful substance transfer step s114 and harmful substances transferred to the chamber to the chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200168715-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore after crushing a predetermined amount of food waste and sewage sludge it is crushed to about 5 mm and when food waste and sewage sludge raw materials having a water content of about 80 85 are introduced into the tank aerobic thermophilic microorganisms are added thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100701887-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the present invention having the above configuration is configured to operate using the waste heat hot steam generated in the incinerator the connection pipes 211a 211b provided on the rotary shaft 22 of the crushing impeller 21 the steam supply pipe and the steam discharge pipe not shown are hermetically connected and installed to allow hot steam to be discharged via the rotating shaft 22 and the paddle 210 and the connection port of the heating tank 35 37 and the drainage port 38 is also connected to the steam supply pipe and the steam discharge pipe not shown in an airtight manner so that the hot steam can be discharged via the heating zone 36 the drying chamber 30 air blowing pipe not shown for supplying high temperature air via a heat exchanger not shown to the drying barrel 31 of it is configured and used to be injected into the crushing chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200194241-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sump collecting and storing waste water a ph adjusting tank connected to the water collecting tank by a pipe incorporating a stirrer and neutralizing by administering acid and or alkali to the wastewater a homogenization tank connected to the ph adjusting tank and installed inside the stirrer so as to face the impeller of the stirrer and homogenizing the crushing of the neutralized wastewater phase and particles of water an emulsion zone tank connected to the homogeneous tank and laminated with a plurality of magnetic plates at equal intervals but arranged to face the same polarity so as to emulsify the homogenized properties by magnetic force ultrasonic tank connected to the emulsion zone tank and the ultrasonic generator is installed on both sides of the inner zone to be crushed finely pulverize the emulsion zone finely to maximize the oxidized surface area a centrifugation tank connected to the ultrasonic tank and piped through two cyclone units sequentially disposed and centrifuged and oxidized with the purified o 2 and 0 3 while passing down the micronized contaminants and discharging contaminants downward far infrared wave at a predetermined temperature is connected to the centrifugation tank and separated into a plurality of rooms and the far infrared generating minerals and heaters are disposed inside each room and the properties introduced from the centrifugation tank are moved to the upper or lower portion of each room"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200194241-Y1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the technical constitution of the present invention for achieving the above object is a homogenization tank for crushing the neutralized wastewater phase and homogenizing the particles of water an emulsion zone tank for emulsifying the homogenized properties by magnetic force and the emulsified properties ultrasonic tank that maximizes oxidized surface area by pulverizing centrifuged with centrifuged and oxidized with o\u2082 and 0\u2083 plasmad while passing the micronized form and contaminants are discharged to the bottom aging tanks that further refine the particles of water by far infrared waves at a predetermined temperature while moving the constellations to the upper or lower portions of each room and the oxidizing and polymer coagulants are administered to the micronized phases supplied from the aging tanks so that they react and aggregate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569861-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for suppressing freezing and bursting of water facilities including water pipes and water meters a disposition step of arranging a phase change material pcm outside the water facility to suppress external exposure of the water facility prior to the placement step a crushing step of adding the phase change material to water and pulverizing the phase change material a shell forming step of forming a capsule by adding a synthetic resin to a mixture of the water and the phase change material and a separation of separating the capsule from the mixture further comprising an encapsulation step comprising the step the phase change material is a paraffin type the phase change material is undecane dodecane tridecane tetradecane pentadecane hexadecane hexadecane heptadecane octadecane nonadecane and eicosane the encapsulating step further comprises a step of maintaining the mixture at room temperature for a predetermined time prior to the separating step prior to the placement step further comprising a filling step of filling the capsule inside the pouch and sealing the pouch the placement step is a wrapping step of wrapping the water pipe with the pouch filled with the capsule inside the water meter is accommodated in the inner space of the water meter box the disposing step includes an installation step of disposing the pouch filled with the capsule between an inner surface of the water meter box forming the inner space and the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101467204-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the air at room temperature is sent to the cooling exchanger 8 in the means for producing the dry air through the air inlet 9 where the water is condensed and separated and then the heat exchanger 6 and is heated in the heat exchanger to become unsaturated dry air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100850033-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the organic matter thus pulverized is transferred to the at least one sterilization transfer screw 9 of the sterilization tank 10 by the first transfer screw 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100850033-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the pulverized material thus pulverized is introduced into the sound sterilization tank 10 by the first transfer screw 7 and then the temperature of steam injected by the steam injection tube 9 is 120 c and 2.5 kg cm 2 pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the storage tank 41 for collecting odors 72 a stirrer 51 which is charged for the fermentation and decomposition treatment of the food waste a to be evenly supplied and stirred by the stirring blade 511 together with the microorganism and the wood chip 512 a nozzle 52 for spraying washing water b at a predetermined temperature for washing to prevent anaerobically progressing due to the saccharide enzyme microorganism carcass and the like and to provide aerobic condition a driving motor 54 for rotating the agitation blade 511 of the wooden chip and a driving motor 54 for driving the agitation blade 511 the nozzle 52 the oxygen generator 53 a liquid phase fermentation decomposition unit 50 including a control unit 55 that is electrically connected to the motor 54 and controls it a sedimentation tank 61 for precipitating and separating the effluent c obtained by the liquid fermentation decomposition treatment so as to separate and collect the effluent c as waste water d and solid matter e or a centrifugal separator 62 for rotating and separating the effluent c 60 the separated and collected wastewater d is purified by chemical biological and physical treatments to separate the solid e the solid e1 the nitrogen n and the phosphorus p a purification treatment unit 70 having an adjustment tank 72 an anaerobic tank 73 an anoxic tank 74 an aerobic tank 75 a biological sedimentation tank 76 and a filtration tank 77 the collected and collected solid matter e microbial solids e1 and meat fish and cereal shaped material f for the balance of insufficient nutrient balance are added through the automatic weighing hopper 81 0.0 gt c lt rti gt for 20 to 60 minutes a feed fermentation unit 90 which is charged with the sterilized humidified mixed feed and fermented in the fermenter 91 for 2 to 5 days to produce a functional feed g a feed dryer 100 for feeding the functional feed g and drying in the dryer 101 a feedstock storage tank 1104 for storing the dried functional food g a descendant 1101 for loading the feedstock into the delivery vehicle 1103 to supply the feedstock to the feedstock in a nonpackaged state or in a packed state and a feed packing section 110 having a feed packing machine 1102 for feeding the feed in units of a unit of weight wherein the functional feed and the liquid fertilizer lt rti gt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the 