  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102056088-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "breakage of the filler 14 may occur due to high temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101861841-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "such a water meter has a protective box due to a problem of breakage or freezing due to external impact and temperature difference due to the season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101012226-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional partition wall has a problem that the shrinkage phenomenon occurs in the winter the lifting phenomenon occurs on the mating surface to cause leakage and the breakage of the partition wall due to expansion in summer.the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the object of the present invention not only can adjust the height of the main body according to the change of rainwater and sewage but also a plurality of the main body by fixing a single reinforcing beam and coupling force and by increasing the stiffness of the body to prevent distortion of the body due to water pressure and further provided with a support beam in the body to improve the durability and to adjust the length of the body in accordance with temperature changes to prevent damage to the body to provide sewage and storm divider assemblies for sewage pipes with"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101785632-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in general a telescopic tube or expansion joint is formed by forming a space in which a connected portion can flow without detaching or a portion of a resiliently deformed portion in which a tube is shrunk or elongated in a longitudinal direction due to a change in environment such as temperature thereby preventing breakage due to expansion and contraction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101832706-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "therefore according to the embodiment of the present invention it is possible to easily solve the expansion contraction phenomenon of the support column 20 due to the temperature change through the air circulation hole 21 that is for example it is possible to prevent deformation or breakage of the waterproof type earthquake resistant dry pad 1 for a water tank due to a change in ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101725313-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "as a result the groundwater sprinkling system for reducing the internal temperature of a building having a sloped window according to the present invention reduces energy by utilizing the ground water drained around the building shields the radiant heat by sprinkling groundwater on the sloped window of the building it is possible to reduce the internal temperature of the building and thus to create a comfortable indoor environment and to save the cooling cost and to utilize the existing well facilities and to add the r through the reverse osmosis treatment it is possible to reduce the hardness and evaporation residue of the ground water to prevent piping scale and valve breakage and it is possible to continuously reuse the r o filter with citric acid by adding cip equipment"}, {"pat_id": "US-9273801-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "this limits the movement expansion and contraction due to temperature changes of the pipe in area of service connection 8 thus preventing breakage or leaks in the service line not shown attached to service connection 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition by installing a heating wire to prevent freezing waves in the underground water protection unit and by configuring a controller to supply power according to the temperature it is possible to automatically control according to temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "in addition by installing a heating wire to prevent freezing waves in the underground water protection unit and by configuring a controller to supply power according to the temperature it is possible to automatically control according to temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161642-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "therefore when a backflow occurs from the hot water storage tank 12 due to the breakage of the check valve 13 the temperature of the cold water of the cold water storage tank 10 is increased to be higher than the minimum cooling temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100339649-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "in other words the water meter 7 exposed to the outside is covered with a heat insulating member 5 6 and a cover 2 3 and covered with a lid 4 to block the cold air and temperature of the outside to maintain the heat retention it is to prevent the malfunction or breakage of the instrument of the water meter 7 installed in 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101824260-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "by controlling the operation of the reactor 100 based on the temperature measured by the temperature measuring device 170 breakage of the apparatus due to overheating can be effectively prevented.100 ultraviolet reactor 121 seawater inlet 120 body 122 sea water outlet 160 ultraviolet lamp 170 temperature measuring device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "first the offshore plant 100 according to the prior art resumes the operation of transferring marine resources and as the temperature of the marine resources is rapidly lowered due to the row thompson effect the pipeline 130 is damaged due to temperature drop there is a problem that there is a risk of breakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "summary of the invention the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a multiple pressure regulator for an offshore plant which can reduce the risk of damage or breakage of a pipeline due to a rapid temperature drop in the process of transferring marine resources"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "accordingly the multiple pressure regulating device 1 for an offshore plant according to the present invention can reduce the risk of damage or breakage of the pipeline 40 due to a temperature drop the effect of increasing the durability of the line 40 can be obtained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "accordingly in the multi pressure regulating apparatus 1 for a marine plant according to the present invention when the marine resources discharged from the transfer unit 30 are transferred to the resource treatment facility 20 a pressure drop and a temperature drop occur rapidly it is possible to reduce the risk of damage or breakage of the pipeline 40 as well as to prevent a decrease in the amount of water transferred to the marine resources due to the deposit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "accordingly in the multiple pressure regulating apparatus 1 for an offshore plant according to the present invention when the marine resources discharged from the transfer unit 30 are transferred to the resource treatment facility 20 a pressure drop and a temperature drop occur rapidly it is possible to reduce the risk of damage or breakage of the pipeline 40 as well as to prevent a reduction in the amount of water transferred to the marine resources due to the deposit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and an object of the present invention is to accurately check the water level by sensing the water level and temperature in the storage tank through the water level sensor and the temperature sensor to send to the storage tank remote water level management can effectively control the quantity and use the water level sensor as an ultrasonic sensor to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and to prevent the water level from being incorrectly detected due to breakage or malfunction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100477145-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition even if precision construction is performed if the soil is raised and settled due to external conditions that is seasonal temperature changes and external shocks the soldering parts are damaged and watertightness is deteriorated"}, {"pat_id": "US-4510026-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the current was cut off to avoid further increase of the temperature which would have resulted in breakage of the plastic cylinders after which a negative pressure was applied to the system with an ejector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "on the other hand in the case of using a heating wire there is a concern of excessive use of energy a fire occurrence problem due to overheating and a loss of thermal insulation function due to breakage of the heating wire.the present invention was devised to improve such a conventional problem and it is configured to determine whether the intake pump is operated not only by the internal level of the water tank but also by the outside temperature detected by the temperature sensor so that water of water temperature higher than the outside temperature in winter is it is an object of the present invention to provide a freeze proof intermittent tap water to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe by heat exchange occurring in the process along the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970306-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to form a negative electrode or a positive electrode separately so that the negative electrode or the positive electrode can be replaced individually during replacement due to corrosion breakage respectively.in order to achieve the above object the present invention is a sensor for measuring the temperature or hydrogen ion concentration such as constant sewage is coupled to the holder the amount of residual chlorine in which a negative electrode and a positive electrode is formed on one side of the holder a device for measuring the amount of residual chlorine in the indicator by measuring the amount of residual chlorine contained in the measured water by galvanic cell electrolysis by combining the measuring sensor separately"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5738390-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "in addition when applying to the activated sludge treatment method of the mbr method membrane separation method it is desirable to take appropriate measures so that the membrane breakage phenomenon due to the addition of powdered activated carbon does not occur in a short time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200327278-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "according to the cold and hot water ionizer of the present invention it is possible to prevent the rise in water temperature during the pressurized transportation that occurs when the purified water is supplied to the electrolytic means by using a pump and the electrolytic means is operated according to the water shock phenomenon during the pump start pump stop"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413252-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in other words due to the change of temperature and external impacts depending on the season and the impact of the uplift and settlement of the ground the mortar inlet is easily damaged and water tightness is degraded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624111-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "however the water meter as described above freezes the volume of water contained in the main body when the external air temperature drops below zero while the supply of tap water is stopped in the winter and the water contained in the main body is not flowing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101568929-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "such a water meter has a protective box due to a problem of breakage or freezing due to external impact and temperature difference due to the season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200384179-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as described above according to the present invention by wrapping the inner cylinder 20 with the upper insulating material 40 and the outer insulating material 50 and by inserting the outer cylinder 30 can be preserved as much as possible the geothermal heat introduced into the inner cylinder 20 it is possible to prevent freezing of the water pipe and the water meter by keeping the temperature inside the protection container at room temperature even in cold weather and by combining the reinforcing flange 70 on the upper edge of the outer cylinder 30 even if the protection container is buried in the ground by being able to withstand the load sufficiently there is an effect that can prevent the breakage"}]</data>
</edge>
