  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101021938-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "night minimum flow rate detection method to reduce gas flow gas injection type to find out leaked gas after filling the gas inside the pipe and the radar detection to find the leak by using the temperature of the leak point is lower than the leak point"}, {"pat_id": "US-6338364-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "as additional ice forms between the plug and the closed valve the ice runs out of room to expand thus causing the pipe to burst at it weakest point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "authenticating permissions for c conducting a vacuum test or a pressurization test by evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means using a vacuum means or injecting high pressure compressed air into the conduit facility based on the test mode setting state step d detecting changes in pressure and temperature inside the test tank connected to the conduit using a detector and e using the control unit to determine whether the conduit is leaked based on the result detected by the detection unit the leakage inspection method of the conduit facility characterized in that in the step a the supply device cuts off the noise of the power supplied to each device by using a noise blocking circuit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in order to achieve the object as described above the leak test apparatus of the conduit facility according to the present invention is a vacuum device for evacuating the interior of the conduit facility sealed by the sealing means high pressure compressed air in the sealed conduit facility a sensing unit for detecting pressure and temperature changes in the test tank connected to the injecting air compressor the vacuum device and the air compressor and connected to the inside of the conduit facility and controlling the driving of the vacuum device and the air compressor the controller is configured to determine whether or not leakage based on a result detected by the detector and to supply power and power to each device from a power take off device of a vehicle when the vehicle is mounted or to be produced by a generator when a vehicle is mounted to be movable with a vehicle"}, {"pat_id": "US-5736059-A", "para_id": "para_159", "text": "vent 13 allows for rising convection currents to leak out of duct 6 should a batch of hot wastewater produce a hot upper layer from say a draining dishwasher at 140 f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bollard type water leakage inspection panel protection devicethe present invention relates to a bollard type hot water leakage meter panel guard in particular the inlet and exhaust ports formed on the lower and upper sides of the housing to form a ventilation flow path between the inside and outside of the hot water leakage meter panel guard the moisture inside the hot water leakage meter panel guard and a bollard type hot water leak inspection panel protector which is capable of naturally drying moisture and is suitable to prevent internal condensation by maintaining uniform temperature inside and outside of the warm water leakage inspection panel protector"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "it can be dried naturally and there is no temperature difference between the inside and outside of the hot water leak detector panel protector that is the temperature inside and outside is kept uniform to prevent internal condensation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "it can be dried naturally and there is no temperature difference between the inside and outside of the hot water leak inspection panel protector that is the temperature inside and outside is kept uniform thereby preventing internal condensation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "by configuring the inlet port 130 and the exhaust port 150 on the lower side and the upper side of the housing 110 as described above it is possible to more smoothly form the ventilation flow path between the inside and outside of the hot water leak inspection panel guard and as a result the moisture and moisture can be dried naturally and there is no temperature difference between the inside and the outside of the hot water leak reading panel protector that is the temperature inside and outside is kept uniform thereby preventing internal condensation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in addition as a result of the formation of a ventilation flow path between the inside and the outside of the hot water leak inspection panel guard by the configuration of the inlet port 130 and the exhaust port 150 at the lower side and the upper side respectively the exhaust port formed at the upper side of the hot air heated by summer solar heat by natural discharge through the 150 there is an advantage that can prevent the abnormal phenomenon of the hot water leakage metering panel circuit due to the high temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-12111007-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "the system can thus effectively improve the chance of leak prediction and detection and determine leaking position accurately including tiny or pinhole leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101467038-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the controller 240 controls the boiler the water supply control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve not shown and the heating control valve 140 so as to operate at a set temperature of the boiler drive time and the hot water 130 and the recovery regulating valve 140 and generates a control signal by setting the reference value of the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 160 170 180 and the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 the hot water supply pipe sensor 161 the hot water discharge pipe sensor 162 the heating water inlet pipe sensor 171 and the heating water supply pipe sensor 151 160 170 180 the change in the sensed pressure value from the heating water discharge pipe sensor 172 the recovery inlet pipe sensor 181 and the recovered discharge pipe sensor 182 is sensed or when the leakage from the water leak sensor 190 is sensed the water control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve 130 and the recovery control valve 140 are shut off"}, {"pat_id": "US-11953161-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "pipeline leaks and spills can cause serious and potentially dangerous problems"}, {"pat_id": "US-11953161-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "as discussed above pipeline leaks and spills can cause serious and potentially dangerous problems"}, {"pat_id": "US-11774044-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "a vertical comparison time sequence allows the hydrogen concentration curve at each evacuation pipe to be derived over time and a horizontal comparison sensor position allows the specific leak position of the pipeline to be determined"}, {"pat_id": "EP-4071454-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this acoustic leak detection works very well in practice however it is difficult to determine the exact location of the leak"}, {"pat_id": "EP-4071454-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "there the speed of sound in water is measured to determine the temperature of the water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-4071454-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "as a result the water temperature in the section 20 of the residential pipe 17 rises"}, {"pat_id": "US-8403000-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "tank heat leak has a dramatic effect on the pressure temperature and density relationships of the lng thus making it very difficult to control the fuel tank pressure and maintain consistent fuel quality for delivery to the engine"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H07103960-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "however the leakage position is detected from the ratio of the mass imbalance magnitudes of the adjacent sections before and after the leakage occurrence section"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H07103960-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "g leakage flow rate g b g c p b at valve station b pressure p c pressure at valve station c p pressure at leak point l bc pipeline length between valve station b and valve station c in other words the change due to leak appears only in the leak occurrence section as a virtual leak flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the method may further include determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected the method may include marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected the method includes marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "6 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold water temperature test is performed to identify a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "7 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold water temperature test is performed to identify a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the system can also be used to identify which pipe to replace based on a change in temperature of a pipe entering the ground point a from a specific first manifold and a pipe exiting the ground point b from a specific second manifold whereby the pipelines of the manifolds marked at point a and point b connect to the inlet and outlet respectively of the specific portion of underground pipe where the leak is located"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in the method described herein in order to detect accurately the underground leaking pipe 126 as well as to identify point a 170 and point b 172 the user 102 has to perform a series of tests involving time based temperature testing of the pipelines 114 of the manifolds 112 and a narrowing down process to pinpoint point a 170 and point b 172"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "this can help the user 102 eliminate time temperature testing and the process of elimination test for identifying which fixtures are connected to which distribution lines 118 of which manifolds 112 and track where the pipelines 114 are directed to"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "infrared cameras and thermometers are an example of temperature testing equipment 144 that may also be used to find warm spots which when dealing with a leak 154 on the hot side and can give the user 102 a general vicinity of where the leak 154 is located which can allow the user 102 to start with a manifold 112 nearby thereby saving time and providing accuracy that the tested manifold 112 is likely close to point a 170 and point b 172"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "no time temperature testing is necessary because pipes 114 should not feel hot on their own if no fixture is turned on requiring hot water to flow through the pipes 114"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_102", "text": "if there is a temperature change after a heating element 132 is applied to the pipelines 114 of the tested manifold 112 the pipes 114 which should be hot after the heating element 132 was applied will begin to become noticeably cold or cooler to the touch or as detected by temperature testing equipment 144 due to the presence of cold water moving or being pulled towards the leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "conversely if a hot water manifold 112 is being tested and a cooling element 134 is applied then the temperature change means that the tested pipelines 114 which were cooled by the cooling element 134 begin to heat up due to the presence of moving hot water moving towards the leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "as noted above because the user 102 knows that in this controlled testing environment the fixtures 122 are turned off then there should be no active source causing the water to flow through the pipelines 114 of the tested manifold 112 and yet the fact that there is a noticeable temperature change after the user 102 either heats the pipelines 114 of a cold water manifold 112 or cools the pipelines 114 of a hot water manifold 112 which indicates that water is flowing towards the leak 154 anyway and is carrying cold water or hot water towards the leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_112", "text": "thus the user 102 can more closely confirm if the leak 154 is on the hot or cold side using such a test on the hot water heater 110"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_116", "text": "generally speaking a process of elimination test may include 1 determining whether the leak is on the a cold side or a hot side 2 identifying a first test manifold 112 and identifying a first fixture 122 associated with that first test manifold 112 3 changing the temperature of the pipelines 114 of the first test manifold 112 i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "5 shows an example of a decision tree or flowchart 500 for testing a hot water manifold 112 to detect and identify a leak on the property 104 which may begin at step 502"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_138", "text": "6 and the manifold 112 is before the leak 154 then both pipelines 114 would cool down after the heating element 132 is utilized to heat the pipelines 114a 114b and the fixture 122 is off because cool water is flowing through the pipelines 114a 114b to get to the leak 154 and the user 102 can detect that change in temperature the cooling of heated pipelines 114a 114b using touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_140", "text": "so after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154 to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118 the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_145", "text": "by performing time based temperature checks the user 102 may determine that pipeline 114c has water flowing down towards the leak 154 at the main water entrance 108 to the property 104 and through pipeline 114c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_147", "text": "8a the pipelines 114d 114e will both slowly cool down which indicates to the user 102 that the leak 154 is past this manifold 112b because the pipelines 114d 114e did not stay hot"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_155", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a 114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_165", "text": "because of this process of elimination and testing of each fixture 122 s distribution lines 118 pipelines 114a 114c from cold water manifold 112a and where the water goes the user knows that the leak 154 is past pipeline 114c from the initial temperature check and that pipeline 114c brings water to the half bath vanity sink 842 the half bath toilet 840 and hose bib 1 810 and hose bib 2 812"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_166", "text": "as noted above the process of elimination test requires the user to locate a pipeline 114 that leads to a leak 154 by performing an initial temperature test and then identify all the distribution lines 118 for any manifolds 112 of connected fixtures 112 that have water going to and from via the distribution lines 118 of the manifolds 112 and through the connected underground portions of the pipeline 114"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_168", "text": "accordingly the user 102 can temperature test the pipelines 114 of all of the manifolds 112 for the half bath vanity sink 842 the half bath toilet 840 hose bib 1 810 and hose bib 2 812 to see if the leak 154 is before or after each manifold 112 of each fixture 112 and to identify point a 170 and point b 172"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_169", "text": "the user 102 may perform a temperature test on pipelines 114d 114e to see if the leak 154 is past this manifold 112b or before this manifold 112b"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_170", "text": "accordingly the user may perform a temperature test on pipelines 114f 114g 114h to see if the leak 154 is past this manifold 112c as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_173", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks the user 102 tries to determine 1 if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2 which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline s 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3 which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_175", "text": "after performing this initial temperature test the user 102 knows that pipeline 114c is a distribution line 118 and is most likely the pipeline 114 leading to the leak 154 because of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_176", "text": "the user may perform a temperature test by cooling down the pipelines 114d 114e and 114f of manifold 112b using any type of cooling element 134 including but not limited to ice cubes cold towels or other cooling elements"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_209", "text": "11 18 because the hot water will be leaking out through the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 containing an underground leak 154 which will make the surrounding area around the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 and floors above the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 noticeably warmer via touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_210", "text": "accordingly as the hot water returns through the underground cold water pipeline 114 from the crossover valve 184 and or supply lines 120 the user 102 should be able to detect and sense either using touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144 that the floor of a particular location on the property 104 is noticeably warmer because the hot water will leak out through the underground cold water pipeline 114 making the floors and surrounding area located above the location of the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 noticeably hotter as the pump 180 pumps the hot water in the loop created with the underground hot water pipelines 114 and the underground cold water pipelines 114"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_212", "text": "it may be that the user 102 finds that the floor to be marked corresponding to the underground leaking cold water pipeline 114 is in the same room areas as the installed crossover valve and test fixture 182 however it may also be true that the floor that will have a noticeable increase in temperature is located elsewhere on the property 104 and not proximate to the crossover valve 184 and installed test fixture 182"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_213", "text": "at step 1612 if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected the user 102 may safely assume and determine that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_218", "text": "at step 1626 if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected the method may include visibly marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property 104 as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak 154 for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_226", "text": "at step 1714 if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_230", "text": "at step 1728 if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected the method includes marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property 104 as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_241", "text": "at step 1814 if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 126 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_243", "text": "at step 1828 if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected the method 1800 includes marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property 104 as the area of the property 104 to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3633342-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "some tests can detect a leak but require a second test to determine the location of the leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in or leak into the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5333487-B2", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a water softening device for producing soft water by softening raw water in a cation exchange resin bed tower a reverse osmosis membrane separation device for separating soft water produced by the hard water softening device into permeated water and concentrated water by a reverse osmosis membrane module an electrodeionization module an ion exchange resin mixed bed tower or a cation exchange resin single bed tower for deionizing the permeated water obtained by the reverse osmosis membrane separator a softening process for producing soft water by passing raw water in a downward flow through a cation exchange resin bed having a depth of 300 to 1500 mm housed in the cation exchange resin bed tower a first regeneration process for regenerating the entire cation exchange resin bed by generating a downward flow of the regenerated liquid by collecting at the bottom while distributing liquid to the top of the bed and regenerating after the first regeneration process a second regeneration process for regenerating a part of the cation exchange resin bed by generating an ascending flow of the regeneration liquid by collecting the liquid at the middle while distributing the liquid to the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed valve means switchable to in the second regeneration process the amount of regeneration liquid that provides a regeneration level of 1 to 6 eq lr is supplied to a hardness leak prevention bed whose depth is set to 100 mm with the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed as a base point"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5333487-B2", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a water softening device for producing soft water by softening raw water in a cation exchange resin bed tower a first reverse osmosis membrane separation device for separating soft water produced by the hard water softening device into permeated water and concentrated water by a first reverse osmosis membrane module a second reverse osmosis membrane separation device for further separating the permeated water obtained by the first reverse osmosis membrane separation device into permeated water and concentrated water by a second reverse osmosis membrane module a softening process for producing soft water by passing raw water in a downward flow through a cation exchange resin bed having a depth of 300 to 1500 mm housed in the cation exchange resin bed tower a first regeneration process for regenerating the entire cation exchange resin bed by generating a downward flow of the regenerated liquid by collecting at the bottom while distributing liquid to the top of the bed and regenerating after the first regeneration process a second regeneration process for regenerating a part of the cation exchange resin bed by generating an ascending flow of the regeneration liquid by collecting the liquid at the middle while distributing the liquid to the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed valve means switchable to in the second regeneration process the amount of regeneration liquid that provides a regeneration level of 1 to 6 eq lr is supplied to a hardness leak prevention bed whose depth is set to 100 mm with the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed as a base point"}, {"pat_id": "US-5062442-A", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in a preferred embodiment the evaluating means comprise a resistance measuring circuit which measures the actual resistance of the temperature sensors and a microprocessor connected thereto by way of an a d converter for calculating the volumetric flow"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5333486-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "a water softening device for producing soft water by softening raw water in a cation exchange resin bed tower a reverse osmosis membrane separation device for separating soft water produced by the hard water softening device into permeated water and concentrated water by a reverse osmosis membrane module a softening process for producing soft water by passing raw water in a downward flow through a cation exchange resin bed having a depth of 300 to 1500 mm housed in the cation exchange resin bed tower a first regeneration process for regenerating the entire cation exchange resin bed by generating a downward flow of the regenerated liquid by collecting at the bottom while distributing liquid to the top of the bed and regenerating after the first regeneration process a second regeneration process for regenerating a part of the cation exchange resin bed by generating an ascending flow of the regeneration liquid by collecting the liquid at the middle while distributing the liquid to the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed valve means switchable to in the second regeneration process the amount of regeneration liquid that provides a regeneration level of 1 to 6 eq lr is supplied to a hardness leak prevention bed whose depth is set to 100 mm with the bottom of the cation exchange resin bed as a base point"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "this drop in temperature may mimic the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "the sealing member s may be made of a rubber material and may be formed when the temperature sensing member 120 blocks the first inlet 111 or when the setting block 150 blocks the second inlet 112 it is possible to prevent water from being wasted by leakage by increasing the sealing force so that water does not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "for example the error state data includes an error state open or short for the hot water temperature sensor 634 or the cold water temperature sensor 624 a leak state such as cold hot water there may be a state in which the lamp 633 is heated for more than the threshold time during heating of the heater 633 a state in which the evaporator 623 is operated for more than the threshold time at the time of heating"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "the operational innovation features are long waiting solutions and include 1 the cylinder joint method with a rigid joint between the font plate assembly and the cylinder assembly with the novel locking device and a flexible joint between the back plate assembly and the cylinder assembly with the back step the rigid front joint with the eccentric plug assembly and radial locking setscrew provide simple and antic corrosion robust locking mechanism since the bolts are defined as a pressure container part in the pressure vessel standards around the world according to navy and major marine structures specifications all vital bolts should be made out of inconel alloy in order to prevent catastrophic failure due to corrosion where the seat water corrosion is a major problem moreover this requirements not only greatly increase cost for the marine projects but also create compatibility problem with surrounding parts like washer nuts and welding areas thanks to those novel joint method there is no bolts on the cylinder assembly as pressure containing part parts even with setscrews so the feature provides a redundant locking function moreover there is no tension bolts in the rigid joint and the flexible joint so even temperature change would not affect the joint seal with the back step while the cylinder assembly with thermal expansion would not affect joint seal as well meanwhile they are easy to assembly and disassembly and can stand for high cycle operations like high cycle relief application without retightening bolts and increase reliability and reduce the cost as a result the linear drive assembly eliminate any joint leak or break due to those thermal expanding the back joint with axial freedom successfully solves the creep issue for most pipelines and offshore applications 2 the porting system most external tubing on the conventional actuator are constructed like spaghetti and can easily be hit and damaged corroded and mislaid out but this porting system with two porting systems a and b not only reduce tubing leak by accident hit during the operation and transportation and reduce the pollution if the naturel gases are used for actuation power supply but also simplify porting tubing layout the composite tubing a b not only solve the corrosion issues but also balances load on the piston assembly the nonmetal end of the tubing a can be secured with the front plate assembly for seals and joint and an open end connected with cavity a the tubing a can be secured with front plate assembly to additional external outlet outside the front plate assembly for accelerating or decelerating open or closed speeds with multiple fluid pads for fast closing or opening less one second without damaging valve seat and stem packing by operating step opening or closing three or two ports at the beginning and one or two ports at the closed position or vice versa in offshore platform where the working space is very limited so the internal tubing not only provides safe and secure flow line but also have the shortest flow line and provide a multiple flow line for each piston which not only have more flexible control with multiple fluid pad assemblies so for quick closing operation at beginning three flow lines can be opened and in the end only one flow control is set to open and reduce the impact force on the seat or packing of valves 3 the relative position adjustment is a great feature for most operators in the field the conventional positions adjustment is based on a absolution positions change between 0 90 degree while the relative position adjustment mechanism separating from the conventional absolute position adjustment is other disrupt innovation in this invention for most operators in the field a correct closed position of closure members like disc ball or plug is critical for all rotary valve even 0.5 degree off can cause leak but 99 of stem position adjustments are about the stem relative position to the joint flanges bolt holes with no need to alter a factor set range 0 90 0.5 degree only 1 of the actuation adjustments is an absolute adjustment between 0 90 5 or 10 degree the relative positions adjustments on the rotatable interface plates is a simple solution to 99 problems for further position security anti loosening washers or semi permanent adhesive may be added with the bolts after setting a correct position moreover the high friction structures with the setscrews is designed to secure the adjusted position as a redundancy for 1 problems the factory set 90 5 can be solved at the factory it along saves 60 time in most rotary actuations installation moreover the top and bottom flange assembly can be interchangeable so without changing the design or installing the cylinder assembly the direction of rotations of actuator can changed from clockwise to anticlockwise or for any valve connection without body change especially in field repairs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468179-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is difficult to find a sensor on the market that can detect leakage while enduring high temperature particularly in a very high temperature pipe.accordingly the present invention has an object to provide a leak detection device that can withstand high temperatures and can stably detect leakage.leakage detection device according to an embodiment of the present invention a plurality of heat shields made of an insulating material and a pair of through holes formed in parallel the plurality of heat shields in series through a pair of through holes of the heat shield and a sensing unit connected to the wire and connected to the wire to measure a resistance change due to the energization caused by the fluid leaked from the pipe.as described above according to the present invention the wire is formed to penetrate into the heat shield made of insulating material thereby preventing heat conduction to the leak detection device so that the leak can be stably detected for a long time in a pipe where a high temperature fluid flows"}, {"pat_id": "US-6970808-B2", "para_id": "para_129", "text": "a flow simulator 820 which is connected to the flow monitor 815 and the pipe gate simulator 810 does a preliminary simulation based on new models developed for flow in pipeline systems to predict pressure points and velocity points under steady and unsteady state conditions throughout the line of the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "the first set of data that is collected may include one or more of the water temperature the water pressure a zero flow rate before and after a water consumption event for example"}, {"pat_id": "US-8667978-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in the illustrative example control panel and indicators 28 includes led indicators 32 as follows a monitor indicator which indicates the monitoring system is active an away indicator which indicates the water system is shut off a seismic alarm indicator which indicates that seismic sensor 27 has been triggered a low high temperature alarm indicator which indicates that temperature sensor 23 has detected extreme heat or a near freezing condition a slow leak alarm which indicates that the back pressure pressure drop rate is between the low and high level thresholds a water flow alarm which indicated that the rate of pressure drop has exceeded the upper threshold and a humidity alarm that indicates that the humidity has exceeded a threshold when building 10 is unoccupied or that a profile has been exceeded when the household is in use"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a fluid accommodating member in which fluid freezing at a low temperature and increasing in volume thereof is accommodated therein one side has an open cylindrical shape the outer circumferential surface is formed with a male screw to be screwable the middle portion of the inner receiving space is formed with a locking projection protruding to a predetermined height the other end of the outer member formed with a female screw and the inner diameter is inserted into the inner receiving space of the outer member has a cylindrical shape that is moved in the longitudinal direction and the o ring is mounted on one end thereof and the inner diameter reduced to be slidable through the locking jaw from the middle region to the other end the stepped surface is formed and the inner end of the stepped surface is formed with a male screw the male screw of the inner member is fastened to the locking jaw to prevent the inner member is separated from the outside of the outer member the inner receiving space of the outer member is fastened to the stopper and the female screw formed on the other end of the outer member a ground member having a rod shape protruding from the inner surface of the inner member and a ground terminal to which the other end surface of the inner member is temporarily in contact with the inner member to generate a detection signal and one side surface of the inner member"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "the water from the municipal water system 128 has a temperature that varies relatively slowly since they are typically delivered via pipes which are buried underground"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "9 11 only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "further since any slight increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 at the end of the wait period 695 might indicate that there is a leak the controller may be able to detect even smaller leaks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080118-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "third the connection structure between the manhole and the sewer pipe of the present invention is due to the phenomenon that the inner wall surface of the manhole is contracted or expanded due to seasonal factors for example outside air temperature during use of the manhole and in the outer circumferential surface of the exponential socket and the manhole even if a gap is generated between the inner circumferential surface of the connection hole of the wall a leak can be prevented through an index ring installed at a corresponding portion between the exponential socket and the inner wall of the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "US-10180414-B2", "para_id": "para_110", "text": "for example the sensor assembly may include one or more piezoelectric sensors acoustic sensors acoustic transducers hydrophones pressure sensors pressure transducers temperature sensors accelerometers flow sensors chlorine sensors leak detectors vibration sensors or other types of sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413252-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in other words due to the change of temperature and external impacts depending on the season and the impact of the uplift and settlement of the ground the mortar inlet is easily damaged and water tightness is degraded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the sealing member 121 may be made of a rubber material so that when the temperature sensing member 120 closes the inlet 112 it is possible to prevent water from being wasted by leakage by increasing the sealing force so that water does not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "due to the elastic force of the first elastic member 130 the inlet 112 is closed by the temperature sensitive member 120 and water does not leak before the temperature responsive member 120 contracts"}, {"pat_id": "US-11354748-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "for example a slight change in the rate of water flow into a faucet may indicate a water leak whereas a similar change in rate of water flow through a water main may be part of normal fluctuations in household water usage"}, {"pat_id": "US-12050157-B2", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "the information may include for example the current water flow past water flow status of the automatic shut off valve status of whether a leak is detected home or away mode status and water temperature current and past temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102736709-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "therefore when the temperature control storage pipe 201 and the cooling water storage pipe 211 of the present invention are installed while extending in the longitudinal direction they are first wrapped with a rubber socket and then secondly wrapped with a coupling band so that each temperature control storage pipe 201 and each cooling water storage pipe 211 are connected and extend along the longitudinal direction"}, {"pat_id": "US-9983092-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "paulson s process and apparatus 24 use acoustic monitoring to indicate possible leak locations the pipeline is also monitored for temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10275402-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "thus embodiments described herein may provide a system for pipeline leak detection that may include a distributed acoustic sensing component an edge processing unit responsible for extracting features from the acoustic raw data which will be suitable for data fusion a data network to transfer data to a control station a scada system for gathering pressure temperature and flow data and or an ild system for estimating leak probabilities based on pressure temperature and or flow data and a signal processing unit which processes and fuses the data from the acoustic and ild systems to generate leak alarms"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "as another example prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the smart water valve can include a housing unit that uses various sensors for monitoring water flowing into the property from the main pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "for example the processor 206 may communicate in a bidirectional manner with each of the transceiver 202 physical input module 204 electronically actuated ball valve 208 flow sensor 210 temperature sensor 212 and leak sensor 214"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "in some implementations the flow sensor 210 the temperature sensor 212 and leak sensor 214 may be contained within the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "for example the processor 206 can receive sensor data from the flow sensor 210 the temperature sensor 212 and the leak sensor 214"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "for example the smart water valve 126 can determine that the temperature of the water leak of 60 degrees f matches the temperature of water consumed by the toilet of 177 degrees c 62 degrees f"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "in some examples the smart water valve 126 can determine that temperature of the water leak matches the temperature of the particular water consuming device based on the temperatures matching within a threshold variance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "10 since there is little influence by high temperature and high pressure inside there is an advantage in that the sealing is reliable and the replacement cycle is long"}, {"pat_id": "US-11359989-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "memory which when all combined enable the detection of a leak increase the accuracy of locating the leak and reduce the occurrence of an erroneous leak identification that is common when traditional rarefaction leak detection techniques are used"}, {"pat_id": "US-11359989-B2", "para_id": "para_231", "text": "further the fluid properties of the pipeline may be continuously measured using the pressure sensing means e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in certain embodiments data from this flow meter is transmitted via a low power wireless transmitter to a gateway and hub assembly"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the leak sensor may or may not have temperature and motion tamper detecting capabilities inside the sensor s housing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "daily averages of temperature and pressure measurements are shared on a twelve hour basis by leak sensor 20 and water control unit 30 via the gateway 40"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948132-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "a hydrophone may offer significant advantages over a piezoelectric element which when mounted to a structure like a fire hydrant will sense incidental acceleration from leak sound waves traveling through the water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-9109349-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "because first electronic valve 12 is shut no additional water is permitted to enter from connection line 22 into structure 70 until system 10 is reset thus significantly reducing the volume of damaging water capable of escaping connection line 22 or other tributary within structure 70 during a leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102313735-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the coil heater 221 is a coil heater made of a silicon material and is installed to surround the wastewater supply pipe 220 thereby preventing the water inside the wastewater supply pipe 220 from freezing in winter when the temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "US-9690303-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "because first electronic valve 12 is shut no additional water is permitted to enter from connection line 22 into structure 70 until system 10 is reset thus significantly reducing the volume of damaging water capable of escaping connection line 22 or other tributary within structure 70 during a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-10508966-B2", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "the presence of the leak on the consumer side means that there is a constant flow of water from the water main through the external stop tap and hence a constant heating effect and therefore the average temperature of the baseline is greater than compared to the first and second sites illustrated by figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-10508966-B2", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "9 illustrates a fourth site having at least one significant leak on the consumer side such as a constantly running tap or a break in the supply pipe and for which several water flow causing events occur during the 24 hour period for example an occupied dwelling"}, {"pat_id": "US-10508966-B2", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "therefore the average temperature of the baseline is greater and the variation in temperature is lesser than compared to the first and second sites illustrated by figs"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2749860-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in a further embodiment an additional sensor system can be provided on the base part namely for sound measurement for the purpose of leak detection and or for recording the quantitative water supply via the hydrant and or for the detection of water parameters such as pressure ph hardness turbidity and temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101626616-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a leakage measurement method for a water supply pipe including a plurality of water pipes connected by at least one coupling pipe a first step in which a peltier element formed of a plurality of pieces and coupled to at least a part of the outside of the plurality of water pipes produces electricity a second step of storing electricity produced by the peltier device through a battery a third step wherein the data memory stores a preset standard pressure value a fourth step of sensing a first pressure of each of the plurality of water pipes by a plurality of pressure sensors inserted into holes formed in the at least one joint pipe a fifth step of the control unit comparing the standard pressure value and the first pressure to determine whether the plurality of water pipes are leaked or not and and a sixth step in which the wireless signal processing unit sends out a message informing whether or not the leak is caused to the outside according to the control of the control unit in the first step the peltier element produces the electricity using a temperature change of at least a part of the plurality of water pipes the plurality of pressure sensors the data memory the control unit and the wireless signal processing unit are driven using electricity stored in the battery in the fifth step determining a leakage if the second pressure that is at least part of the first pressure is lower than the standard pressure value and and determining a second water pipe corresponding to the second pressure among the plurality of water pipes and the sixth step of sending out the second pressure and information for identifying the second water pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "moreover the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak for incipient freeze condition and thus the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-11053668-B1", "para_id": "para_154", "text": "as an example determining the leak height may include fitting the acquired pressure data to an equation of the form pressure c 1 time where c is a constant"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "2a 5b may be a smart meter system and provide advantages over conventional water meters including but not limited to water flow monitoring water flow metering leak detection alert notifications that may be based on leak identification cost efficiency volume and or run time freeze warnings that may be based on monitoring water temperature and or air temperature humidity monitoring pressure monitoring to prevent low pressures and over pressuring leak tracing by utilizing pressure sensors remote control operation including opening and or closing valves remotely battery operated units provided to be long lasting and for use in hard to reach places zigbee radio communication for long range and obstruction interference minimization and a wi fi to zigbee hub to provide ease of connectivity to home networks and longer range access to meters"}, {"pat_id": "US-5591415-A", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "furthermore in conventional hot wall design the pressure vessel wall runs at substantially higher temperature and is consequently much more susceptible to corrosive attack and vessel failure in the event a liner leak occurs"}, {"pat_id": "US-6834556-B2", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "for example base sensors may include chemical detectors and weather sensors that indicate the air temperature wind speed wind direction precipitation sunlight levels humidity barometric pressure or other environmental properties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100408926-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "chemical resistance is especially suitable for sewage or gas and it does not leak due to ion dissolution and has a favorable effect on maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "in such a configuration a sensor such as a temperature sensor may be included to determine the source of a particular leak among one of a plurality of fluid sources"}]</data>
</edge>
