  <data key="d6">["manage", "place", "make", "happen", "apply", "preheat", "connect", "trigger", "carry", "display", "fasten", "achieve", "increase", "prepare", "secure", "have", "minimize", "send", "fix", "retain", "can", "relate", "fuse", "pump", "provide", "contain", "desire", "cast", "prevent", "oxygenate", "feed", "correspond", "advance", "form", "eliminate", "crush", "seal", "overflow", "action", "build", "suspend", "pass", "occur", "couple", "repair", "pressurize", "bring", "automate", "support", "disinfect", "dissolve", "integrate", "allow", "protrude", "run", "result", "illuminate", "locate", "lead", "recycle", "remove", "reduce", "may", "activate", "discharge", "cool", "detect", "fit", "obtain", "separate", "include", "perform", "dispose", "thereto", "enter", "expand", "open", "block", "supply", "use", "raise", "sensor", "exchange", "transport", "require", "close", "heat", "maintain", "install", "improve", "control", "shape", "be", "generate", "instal", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11795088-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an automated mobile low power consumption with a hybrid power capacity wastewater treatment facility comprising one or more raw wastewater feeding pipelines 1 that carry raw wastewater directly from a wastewater generation source to one or more rough solid crushing pumping pit 2 comprising a first electrical submersible pump 3 actioned by a level sensor 4 wherein the first electrical submersible pump 3 with a stainless steel solid crushing impeller 5 allows to generate a homogenous substance which is then pumped through a flexible hose with quick coupling 6 to a biological reactor 7 for removing suspended or dissolved organic material in the homogenous mixture through an aerobic system comprising a second electrical submersible pump 8 that oxygenates the wastewater and the wastewater treatment contained in the biological reactor 7 up to 6.0 mg l of the dissolved oxygen by means of an eductor or aerator 9 which is triggered by a programmable logic controller 10 that is located in a control panel 32 and in order to automate the function of the facility detects readings of the process conditions through a dissolved oxygen sensor 11 and a suspended solids sensor 12 to control the generation of biological sludge and microorganisms which are used for the organic matter degradation a mixture resulting from the biological reactor 7 which passes overflowing through a communication pipeline 13 including a screen 14 to allow the passage of water to a sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 in which the separation of a liquid phase and a solid phase occurs by sedimentation filtration flotation and precipitation in which the liquid phase is water while in the solid phase is sludge the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 has a third electrical submersible pump 16 that allows a recirculation of the biological sludge to the biological reactor 7 managed by the programmable logic controller 10 the liquid phase resulting from the sedimentation and sludge separation tank 15 enters overflowing through a communication channel 17 including a screen 18 to allow the passage of water through a disinfection tank 19 that has an automated supply system of sodium chloride 20 for the elimination of pathogen and bacteria present in water the disinfection tank 19 comprises a ph sensor 23 the suspended solids sensor 12 a chlorine sensor 24 and a temperature sensor 25 the disinfection tank 19 further comprises a screen system 21 to prevent the passage of solids to a filtration tank 27 and an electric valve 37 to eliminate solid materials passed to the disinfection tank disinfected water from the disinfection tank 19 is pumped by a fourth electrical submersible pump 22 to a connection hose 26 that is connected with the filtration tank which contains gravel 28 of different granulometries activated carbon 29 garnet 30 and silica sand 31 with which the water treatment is achieved furthermore the facility has a photovoltaic feeding system made up of a package of solar panels 33 for energy generation through solar energy with a storage battery bank 34 of the energy obtained during the day and for continuous use during the night in which the energy generation is managed by a local charge controller that is located in the control panel 32 being part of the programmable logic controller 10 that performs the energy displacement to the storage battery bank 34 for storage and to provide during the night while there is no energy generation so that the system maintains continuous operation the local charge controller also allows the connection of an alternate source of energy and at the same time the local charge controller sends information related to voltage current and consumption to the programmable logic controller 10 for displaying dynamic graphs in the control panel 32 and sends the information to remote access sites the facility has a night lighting system 35 comprising at least two lamp towers that illuminate the totality of the area used by the facility and nearby surroundings the lamp towers are fed by the package of solar panels 33 and the storage battery bank 34 the lamp towers have high resolution digital cameras 36 that allow to have photographs frame by frame from certain time periods or live video of everything that is happening around the facility and with a visual monitoring finally the facility has a series of anchors 38 to transport and mount in a platform 39 that is integrated with the photovoltaic feeding system and the night lighting system 35"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1565408-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "after the lower layer 23 has thus been heated to the desired temperature the pump 7 can be activated for pumping water from the pit 4 through the heat exchanger to the evaporator"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1565408-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "the water present in the pit 4 is already preheated by the residual heat from the condensed water so that the temperature of the water being supplied to the heat exchanger 5 may be higher already than that of the seawater being supplied to the pit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit wherein the softening of the repair pipe comprises fixing the position of the steam injection hose by connecting the steam injection hose to the middle of the length of the fixing wire connected at both ends to a pair of connection rings provided in the protective guard maintenance method of conduit using guards and insulation case"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit the step of pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe may include passing the other end of the traction wire having one end connected to the sealing cap through a pair of connection rings provided on the protection guard and a step of press fitting and fixing the end portion of the maintenance pipe to the end portion of the maintenance pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit the step of cooling the maintenance pipe may include the steps of fixing the other end of the traction wire one end of which is connected to the sealing cap press fitted to both ends of the maintenance pipe to a pair of connection rings provided on the protection guard a method of repairing and installing a conduit using a protective guard and an insulating case installed in a work area the method comprising the step of minimizing shrinkage deformation of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit wherein the heating plate has a support structure connected to an upper end of a heating plate body that generates heat when power is applied thereto and a hook ring provided at an upper portion of the support structure and connected to a hook of the crane portion the heat insulating case includes a thermostat having an opening that is opened upward to allow the heating plate to advance and retreat and an opening portion that is opened by the supporting structure is closed and the thermostat has a fixing portion corresponding to the connection hole formed in the fixing plate wherein the securing member is detachably fixed to the earth retaining plate by a fastening member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit wherein the heating plate has a support structure connected to an upper end of a heating plate body that generates heat when power is applied thereto and a hook ring provided at an upper portion of the support structure and connected to a hook of the crane portion wherein the heat insulating case includes a thermostat which is formed on both sides of the thermostat to have a long hole corresponding to a protruding member provided at both ends of the supporting structure and is coupled with the supporting structure and a side cover that seals the long hole wherein the protection guard and the heat insulating case are installed in the work area"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the heat insulating case into contact with the end portion of the repair pipe protruding from the conduit after fixing the connection flange to the end of the conduit the present invention provides a method of repairing and installing a conduit using a protective guards and a heat insulating case provided in the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "2 it is possible to reduce the time required to heat the fused heat plate to a predetermined temperature by heating the fused heat plate used for heat welding of the maintenance pipe to a high temperature in the internal space of the heat sealed case which is blocked from the external environment since it is possible to prevent contact with the operator it is possible to reduce the time required for heat generation thereby improving work productivity and preventing burn incidents of the operator.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102724384-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of apartments 33 are installed in the space between a plant factory 41 and another plant factory 41 and the road surface of the access road 15 and the rooftop of the apartment 33 are installed at the same height the upper part of the rooftop of the apartment 33 and the rooftop of the plant factory 41 are connected to each other to install a hollow plate shaped building an emergency shelter 09 and a cultivation space for plants 11 are installed on the upper surface of the hollow plate building and a building formation part in which led lighting 07 is installed on the upper part of the cultivation space a number of water tanks 29 are installed in the outer underground area outside the outer perimeter of the pit a wastewater tank 96 and a sewage tank 97 are installed in a location larger than the installation diameter of the water tank 29 and deeper than the depth of the bottom surface of the pit a water generator 23 is installed on the ground surface with a larger installation diameter than the water tank 29 and a dome outer installation section in which graphene ropes 21 are installed in a net shape on the water generator 23 installed on the opposite side of the water generator 23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101087340-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the main equipment composition of the secondary cooling system of the performance factory is used for casting and equipment cooling in the continuous casting process and the high temperature coolant discharged through the scale pit hot water bath and filter and scale which is a high temperature corrosion product of the casting and oils such as inorganic salts and roller greases are removed cooled to the standard level of cooling water while passing through a water tank and then recycled to the continuous casting process water"}, {"pat_id": "US-7105095-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "the lithium ion electrode is therefore preferably placed directly in a cooling water pit cooling water tank or cooling water piping of the cooling water system"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035713-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "1 in some embodiments a pressure sensor p a temperature sensor t and the like may fit into the standard water meter pit i.e"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6819735-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the cold water in the pit 44 is supplied to the refrigerator main body 21 via the pump 45 and the pipe 46 and heats are exchanged to raise the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-6846407-B2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "running the water through this many times can increase the reheat temperature up to 100 to 110 degrees fahrenheit"}]</data>
</edge>
