  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101505028-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "thereby the object to be cleaned 1 is firstly cleaned by high pressure air bubbling through the lower spray nozzle 233 by driving the spray pump 235 in a state of being immersed in the cleaning liquid in the cleaning tank 210 the spray nozzle 233 is driven by the spray pump 235 to discharge the cleaning solution through the upper spray nozzle 233 before being lifted from the cleaning tank 210 by the driving of the cleaning lifting driver 225 the washing liquid is circulated through the upper spray nozzle 233 by the clean wash water accommodated in the regenerating wash fluid reservoir 240 by the driving of the regenerating wash fluid circulating pump 245 and the steam supply pipe 117 the drying and residual washing liquid is removed by the high temperature steam supplied from the waste water regeneration apparatus 100 and sprayed through the upper spray nozzle 233 and then discharged to the outside of the cleaning loading unit 220 or the cleaning quality of the object to be cleaned 1 can be further improved without consuming energy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aerobic digestion tank 100 in which organic matter contained in waste water is oxidatively decomposed by activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms and an air nozzle provided at an inner lower portion of the aerobic digestion tank 100 to discharge air providing a lifting force for circulating the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the aerobic digester in which the organic matter contained in the waste water is oxidatively decomposed due to the activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms and the air nozzle which is provided in the inner lower portion of the aerobic digester to provide the lifting force for circulating the waste water is vertically upward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the self heating high temperature aerobic digestion apparatus for wastewater treatment according to the present invention is an aerobic digestion tank 100 in which organic matter contained in wastewater is oxidatively decomposed by activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms and the aerobic digestion tank 100 according to figs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102912417-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the hot air drying unit is characterized by including a body part having an inlet hopper for introducing sludge through the sludge discharge unit storing the sludge and discharging it to the sludge transfer unit through an outlet a transfer screw member rotatably provided on the body part and transferring the sludge through a spiral blade a power unit provided at an end of the transfer screw member to provide driving force and a hot air supply unit provided around the periphery of the body part to supply hot air to heat and dry the sludge stored in the body part.the sludge drying device of a sewage treatment plant according to the present invention compresses sludge stored in a sludge storage tank at high pressure to discharge moisture as much as possible thereby primarily lowering the moisture content and secondarily drying the discharged sludge by mixing it while applying high temperature hot air thereby lowering the moisture content of the sludge as much as possible and enabling recycling.figure 1 is a configuration diagram of a sludge drying device of a sewage treatment plant according to one embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102900862-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "through energy self sufficiency and remote control using solar energy the device comprising a water quality improvement device including a warm upper layer inlet located in a warm upper layer among water depths a density current diffusion portion located in a temperature gradient layer and a stagnant lower layer inlet portion located in a stagnant lower layer and further including a driving motor for rotating an impeller located in the density current diffusion portion a lift device located on the upper part of the water quality improvement device and lifting and lowering the water quality improvement device so that the water surface is buoyant by buoyancy while the density current diffusion portion is located in the temperature gradient layer it is characterized by including a solar power generation panel installed on the upper surface of the lift device to generate power using solar energy and supply power to the lift device and the driving motor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102900862-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "according to the disclosed technology the water quality improvement device is raised and lowered by a certain length in the vertical direction according to the water depth position of the temperature gradient layer according to the season so that the density current diffusion unit is always located in the temperature gradient layer thereby improving the efficiency of water quality improvement according to the density current diffusion and the driving motor of the impeller for introducing water from the warm upper layer and water from the stagnant lower layer and discharging them in the transverse direction of the temperature gradient layer to diffuse the density current and the lift device for raising and lowering the water quality improvement device are each supplied with power charged by solar energy thereby achieving energy independence and accordingly there is no need to connect a separate external power source which ultimately resolves the difficulty of the facility and the distribution state of the temperature gradient layer in water depth the state of the mixed effluent in the temperature gradient layer discharging in the transverse direction and the lifting state of the lift device can be monitored in real time and since such operation is possible through wireless remote control the operating efficiency of the water quality improvement device for water quality improvement is greatly improved"}, {"pat_id": "US-4383892-A", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in an apparatus for lifting evaporating and storing of water on a cyclic basic a vacuum chamber located at an elevation above a body of poluted water and having a double connection to the body of water and operating on fluxuations in pressure in the vacuum chamber to keep the concentration of polutants low with means in one connection assisting the flow of water into the vacuum chamber and means in the other connection assisting the return flow to the body of water the elevation of the vacuum chamber above the body of water being greater than water can be lifted by a vacuum as water without boiling it ejector means connected to the vacuum chamber above the boiling level to create the vacuum and direct the resulting vapor through a check valve to a condenser where the vapor is converted to distilled water means directing part of the distilled water through another check valve to where it is confined in the heating system and heated to a high temperature and pressure while confined between the last check valve and the ejector relief valve until it is released by it s own internal pressure with a blast that is directed into the ejector where it creates the vacuum in the vacuum chamber to start another cycle excess distilled water is stored"}, {"pat_id": "US-5306397-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "this is compensated by an automatically controlled pumping off of the brine with the lifting pump for the brine 13 and by subsequent refilling of the evaporation chamber 5 with new de aerated seawater via the tube 12"}, {"pat_id": "US-11518666-B2", "para_id": "para_438", "text": "by the lifting of the lifting cover 210 and the water ejection nozzle 240 water may be ejected from a position adjacent to the water receiving container"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101012226-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional partition wall has a problem that the shrinkage phenomenon occurs in the winter the lifting phenomenon occurs on the mating surface to cause leakage and the breakage of the partition wall due to expansion in summer.the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the object of the present invention not only can adjust the height of the main body according to the change of rainwater and sewage but also a plurality of the main body by fixing a single reinforcing beam and coupling force and by increasing the stiffness of the body to prevent distortion of the body due to water pressure and further provided with a support beam in the body to improve the durability and to adjust the length of the body in accordance with temperature changes to prevent damage to the body to provide sewage and storm divider assemblies for sewage pipes with"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238165-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "it belongs to the scope of rights.1 drinking water supply device 10 main body 11 settling space 12 lower space 13 first door 13a hole 14 second door 20 container 21 discharge pipe 30 detection unit 31 controller 32 sensor 33 supporter 40 temperature control unit 41 cooling unit 411 refrigerant pipe 412 refrigerant unit 42 heating unit 421 heating tube 422 heat generating unit 50 direct part 51 solenoid valve 60 drain tray 61 drain pipe 62 container 70 storage 71 storage body 72 cover 73 sterilizer 81 82 83 lifting device 811 screw 812 drive motor 813 lifting bar 831 link unit 831a 831b and 831c link member 832 drive part 832a link screw 832b link motor 832c link block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 g