  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the housing and o ring seals tend to wear over time due to salt penetration because the multiple chambers and housing sections are connected via a plurality of nuts and bolts"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035484-B2", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "practically however it is very difficult to reduce the cross section to zero due to production tolerances on the valve bore and the valve bodies and dimensional changes in operation due to temperature influences and or wear"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_403", "text": "13 the main problem during the operation of the pump of the conventional underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is that if the temperature rises due to the heat of the liquid being handled or the frictional heat of the wetted surface the material may wear out or corrode or the packing may stick so in order to suppress this the following basic methods are used to have cooling and lubrication functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 re