  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102267401-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "and the storage water water pollution prevention system s using the water pollution prevention unit of the storage water is a filter 100 with a built in fine filter to remove various foreign substances contained in the rainwater collected through the rainwater pipe and the filter a storage tank 80 for storing and storing rainwater flowing through and a means for preventing pollution of the water stored in the storage tank by spraying the water stored in the storage tank with air according to a selected time period d of the water pollution prevention unit d 30 to circulate inside the storage tank while supplying air to prevent contamination or deterioration of water due to long term storage and the compressor 90 driven under the control of the controller 70 and the water pollution prevention unit a temperature sensor 60 that is fixed to one side of d and provides information to the controller 70 by periodically checking the temperature of the water and the controller 70 according to the temperature value measured by the temperature sensor 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100891996-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a reactor for treating high concentration organic matter in the influent with microorganisms an acid pipe receiving air from a blower installed outside the reactor to make fine air bubbles an activity checking tank installed inside the reaction tank to check activity of the microorganism a heat exchanger installed outside the reaction tank to prevent a temperature increase of the waste water due to metabolic heat of microorganisms in the reaction tank a settling tank receiving the treated wastewater from the reaction tank to precipitate the microbial sludge and returning it to the reaction tank and discharging the supernatant water and pc control device for observing and controlling the measuring instrument of the reaction tank and the activity confirmation tank the diffuser is aeration reactor for a high concentration organic wastewater treatment including an acoustic resonance acid engine in order to increase the oxygen transfer rate to the microorganisms in the reactor and reduce the power cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100891996-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "a high concentration organic waste water treatment aeration device of the present invention the reaction tank for treating the high concentration organic material in the influent with a microorganism an acid pipe receiving air from a blower installed outside the reactor to make fine air bubbles an activity checking tank installed inside the reaction tank to check activity of the microorganism a heat exchanger installed outside the reaction tank to prevent a temperature increase of the waste water due to metabolic heat of microorganisms in the reaction tank a settling tank receiving the treated wastewater from the reaction tank to precipitate the microbial sludge and returning it to the reaction tank and discharging the supernatant water and a pc control device for observing and controlling the measuring instruments of the reaction tank and the activity checking tank wherein the diffuser includes an acoustic resonance engine for increasing oxygen transfer rate to the microorganisms in the reactor and reducing power cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101628749-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "when the user turns off the steam generating switch 170 to terminate the steam generation while the steam generating body 140 generates steam the controller 150 controls the heater power supply to the steam heating element 140 the temperature of the steam heating element 140 is measured by the steam heating element temperature sensor 130 and the driving of the pump 110 is stopped when the temperature measurement value of the measured steam heating element 140 is lower than the set temperature if the temperature measurement value of the measured steam heating element 140 is not lower than the set temperature the pump 110 is driven to circulate water through the water supply pipe 113 the pump 110 is driven to supply water to the steam heating element 140 while detecting the supply water of the supply pipe 113 and checking whether the supply water is circulated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "on the other hand the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260 it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recogni