spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time the method may include checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_116", "text": "using the time based temperature test or checking for larger sized singular pipelines 114 6 identifying a second fixture 122 7 performing another time temperature test on the pipelines of the first test manifold 112 to determine if the distribution lines 118 of the first test manifold cools down or heats up at a slower rate than the other as the distribution line 118 from the first test manifold 112 whereby the one that cools down or heats up quickly i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_225", "text": "at step 1712 after turning on the recirculation pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_241", "text": "at step 1812 the method includes checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104 after turning on the pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102458731-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition the concentration of the neutralizing agent may change frequently depending on external environmental factors such as ambient temperature and solvent evaporation but the conventional neutralizing device has a problem in that it cannot be checked frequently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101327389-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "that is by checking the condensate and curing temperature throughout the construction by the moisture sensor and the temperature sensor it is possible to contribute to the quality improvement by checking the uniform curing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a steam melting apparatus a steam heating element for heating water supplied through the water supply pipe to generate steam a pump for introducing water into the water supply pipe a water supply pipe temperature sensor for detecting the temperature of the water supply pipe a steam heating element temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the steam heating element a water detection sensor for detecting water in the water supply pipe a steam generating switch for instructing steam generation according to manual operation a display unit for displaying various conditions related to preheating thawing and steam generation in the state of receiving the power supply the freezing of the water supply pipe is checked through the water supply pipe temperature sensor the heater power is applied to the steam heating element to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe and while the steam is generated according to the instruction of the steam generation switch a controller for notifying the user of a water supply abnormality state by checking a water supply abnormality state of the water supply pipe through the sensor and controlling the steam heating element in response to the water supply abnormality state to prevent overheating of the steam heating element a power switch for switching the input of the ac power source by manual operation and a transforming unit for converting a voltage of a power source applied through the power switch and supplying the converted voltage to the control unit as a control power source to use the control unit as its own circuit driving power source and a power supply for operating the heater and a power supply for operating the pump are supplied to the control unit through the power switch"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to achieve the above mentioned object the present invention provides a steam generator comprising a steam heating element for generating water by heating water supplied through a water supply pipe a pump for introducing water into the water supply pipe a water supply pipe temperature sensor for detecting the temperature of the water supply pipe a steam heating element temperature sensor for measuring a temperature of the steam heating element a water detection sensor for detecting water in the water supply pipe a steam generating switch for instructing steam generation according to manual operation a display unit for displaying various conditions related to preheating thawing and steam generation in the state of receiving the power supply the freezing of the water supply pipe is checked through the water supply pipe temperature sensor the heater power is applied to the steam heating element to defrost the freezing of the water supply pipe and while the steam is generated according to the instruction of the steam generation switch a controller for notifying the user of a water supply abnormality state by checking a water supply abnormality state of the water supply pipe through the sensor and controlling the steam heating element in response to the water supply abnormality state to prevent overheating of the steam heating element a power switch for switching the input of the ac power source by manual operation and a transforming unit for converting a voltage of a power source applied through the power switch and supplying the converted voltage to the control unit as a control power source to use the control unit as its own circuit driving power source and a power source for operating the heater and a power source for driving the pump are supplied to the control unit through the power switch"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "after checking only the temperature of the water inside the water tank 1 to determine the operation of the heater member 20 as the temperature inside the water tank 1 or less than 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101295851-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "deleteaccording to the remote water level management device configured as described above by accurately checking the water level through the water level and temperature detection in the storage tank can effectively control the motor pump it is possible to minimize the power waste due to unnecessary driving ultrasonic by using the sensor it is possible to accurately detect the water level regardless of the season and freezing and it is possible to detect the malfunction and breakage of the motor pump controller thereby enabling effective water level management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200336269-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in order to determine the temperature of the purified water through the temperature sensing unit 80 for detecting this and the water supplied through the temperature sensing unit 80 so that users can selectively use alkaline water or acidic ionized water"}, {"pat_id": "US-9010356-B2", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "the controller also communicates with a locally visible station status indication via a separate connection 86 on the sensor station"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485678-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "monitoring real time measurement results such as pressure and temperature of the compressor dew point of the air dryer cooling water temperature of the water cooler ozone pollution concentration around the equipment ozone generation amount etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102261819-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the simulation and prediction unit uses turbidity and alkalinity as main factors during rainfall among the factors of the inflow flow rate of raw water hydrogen ion concentration turbidity alkalinity electrical conductivity and water temperature and hydrogen ion concentration and the mixed paper drug injection derivation unit 1310 that derives the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper with the water temperature as the main factor the raw water inflow of the flocculated paper and the settling basin the g value of the flocculated paper water temperature turbidity and the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper through the visualized interface image a flocculation paper settling cell sludge management unit 1320 that establishes a plan detects changes in the sludge interface through a sensor and corrects the sludge by checking the degree of agglomeration through light intensity detection and the number of loss head filtration duration and filtered water the filter paper management unit 1330 that establishes a plan for autonomous backwashing through turbidity information the advanced treatment management unit 1340 that performs accident and failure prediction through the status information of the ozone generating device and the maintenance of the water level of the purified water and optimum chlorine it is preferable to provide a purified water disinfection ability management unit 1350 for deriving the contact time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the pipe 310 and the vertical pipe 310 are installed in the upper and lower positions respectively to guide water to be purified while passing water in the upper and lower zigzag directions and a net 331 form a temperature sensor 340 for providing information to the controller 700 by frequently checking the temperature inside the water purification natural mineral particles 330 and the water purification tube 300 which are contained in a bag of and filled in the vertical tube 310 and the in accordance with the operation control of the controller 700 that received the information from the temperature sensor 340 the heating wire 350 that operates to prevent freezing and the water purification tube 300 prevents foreign substances from flowing into the interior and at the same time natural mineral particles for water purification the vertical pipe 310 according to the operation control of the airtight cover 360 for cleaning 330 and the controller 700 installed under the vertical pipe 310 to receive information from the ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 a water purification tube 300 including an electromagnetic valve 370 for individually washing the natural mineral particles 330 for water purification by water pressure by opening and closing the lower portion of the water purification body wow a branch pipe 400 connected so that the drinking water treated while passing through the purified water pipe 300 may be supplied to a storage tank or a user and an ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 fixed to the side of the branch pipe 400 to check the turbidity of water and provide information to the controller 700 wow a flow rate sensor 600 fixed to the side of the branch pipe 400 to check the flow rate of water and provide information to the controller 700 wow the supply pump 100 and the temperature sensor 340 the heating wire 350 the solenoid valve 370 the ultrasonic turbidimeter 500 and the flow rate sensor 600 are signal connected to control the supply pump 100 according to the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102243293-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the supply pump 100 is connected the other side is a water supply pipe 200 connected to the water purification pipe 300 and the water supply pipe 200 and the water supply pipe 200 are connected and fixed to facilitate passage and the inside is for water purification at the same time as the natural mineral particles 330 are filled a plurality of vertical pipes 310 arranged in a vertical direction so that water can be passed through zigzag 3 to 5 times or more and at the upper and lower positions of the sides of the vertical pipe 310 respectively a water purification guide pipe 320 that is installed and guides water to be purified while passing through the upper and lower zigzag directions and a natural mineral particle 330 for water purification that is contained in a bag in the form of a net 331 and filled in the vertical pipe 310 wow according to the operation control of the temperature sensor 340 which provides information to the controller 700 by checking the temperature inside the water purification tube 300 from time to time and the controller 700 receiving the information from the temperature sensor 340"}, {"pat_id": "US-8967186-B2", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "the controller also communicates with a locally visible station status indication via a separate connection 86 on the sensor station"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102111311-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "storing the stirring time of each food reducer the number of openings and closings of the input port and the input amount monitoring the condition of the food reducer calculating and controlling the rpm of the motor by referring to the temperature information of the temperature sensor according to the stirring time the number of openings and closings of the input port and the amount of input on the control board controlling the heating tank heating wire and shoot valve checking whether it is in an optimal control state transmitting the current status information and a solution to the manager when the control status is not optimal remotely monitoring the food reducer by the control board confirming that a specific event has occurred in the control board and transmitting each device data to a data management relay management server to manage users and points the control board controlling a motor a heating tank a heating wire and a shoot valve through a food reducer control board and a waste water management control board checking whether the control board has a problem including the step of transmitting a message to the control board for dispatch to the site for the problem occurrence the control board includes a food reducer control board for controlling a food reducer and a waste water management control board for managing waste water through a waste water quality sensor and a waste water flow measurement sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102111311-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention comprises the steps of storing the stirring time of each food reducer the number of opening and closing of the input port and the input amount monitoring the condition of the food reducer calculating and controlling the rpm of the motor by referring to the temperature information of the temperature sensor according to the stirring time the number of openings and closings of the input port and the amount of input on the control board controlling the heating tank heating wire and shoot valve checking whether it is in an optimal control state if it is not the optimal control state the step of transmitting the current state information and a solution to the manager"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100301389-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition the dilution air valve 15 for preventing the temperature rise due to the overload of the blower 50 by introducing dilution air into any one of the rear end and the front end of the water separator 40 at the front end of the blower 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100756437-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a checking the internal state and determining the maintenance position by a camera entering the conduit b removing deposits and deposited deposits attached to the interior of the conduit c impregnating a liquid two component thermosetting resin mixed with a two component resin cured at room temperature to a fiber sheet made of synthetic fibers d attaching the order sheet to the outer surface of the fibrous sheet and applying the two component thermosetting resin to the thixotropic order sheet e placing the expansion member into a repair position by winding the repair member on which the fiber sheet and the order sheet are stacked on the outer surface of the expansion member and entering the expansion member into the conduit f supplying compressed air into the expansion member to expand the expansion member by volume expansion to make surface contact with the outer surface of the order sheet on the inner wall of the conduit and press for a predetermined time g curing the thermosetting resin of the repairing material by a heat source provided inside the expansion member to integrate the repairing material on the inner wall of the conduit and h drawing out the retracted expansion member from the conduit to the outside so as to be separated from the conduit integrated into the conduit in the thermosetting conduit repair method comprising a step d is uneven to expand the area in contact with the outer surface while inflating with the expansion member when the expansion member is expanded on the outer surface of the order sheet before attaching the order sheet to the fiber sheet thermosetting type conduit repair method characterized in that it further comprises the step of forming a plurality in parallel to the longitudinal direction of the expansion member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102221358-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "6 shows the sequence of the steam injector operating according to the present invention in which steam and a heated fluid are introduced into the steam injector s100 heating and moving the heated fluid s200 and a preset pressure control unit the step of checking whether the pressure is reached s300 and the step of sequentially opening the nozzle 121 while the elastic part 110 is retracted when the predetermined pressure is reached s400 and the step of spraying the steam with increased pressure to the nozzle s500 and the step s600 of increasing the efficiency of the steam injector due to a high temperature and high pressure effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100906654-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a display unit for displaying an external storage device for storing the dangerous situation data output from the controller a controller including a response device unit for checking movement and internal temperature and transmitting a check result to the controller and an external transmission unit for transmitting the water quality analysis result data and the location information output by the controller to the water quality management server it is configured to float in small reservoirs and reclaimed freshwater lake water including and measure the water quality and current location of the small reservoirs and reclaimed freshwater lakes in real time and the measured current position information and movement information and water quality measurement signal automatic water quality measuring device for transmitting wirelessly and receive and analyze the water quality measurement signal transmitted from the water quality automatic telemetry device and store it in the built db and the unspecified number of users who have made an online connection through the data communication network are provided with the analysis results stored in the db for small reservoirs and a water quality management server for checking the water quality state management information of reclaimed freshwater lake agricultural water and the position and movement of the automatic water quality measuring device in real time small water reservoir and reclaimed freshwater lake remote water quality automatic observation system characterized in that made including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714895-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide a non excavation complete water and sewage repair method which can shorten the work time by automatically controlling and performing construction work through a controller of a wireless control member thereby eliminating the inconvenience of having to manually operate a steam supply valve while checking a thermometer and a pressure gauge one by one in the past and which can precisely measure the temperature and pressure of steam for hardening a tube to secure data according to the work conditions thereby enabling more precise work to be performed"}]</data>
