r 892 tire roller 893 tractor 894 trailer 895 ram 896 lead 897 coolant cooling 898 pile 899 helmet 900 fuel pump 901 cam 902 fuel tank 903 starting device 904 boom front pin 905 cad work 906 adapter 907 fish finder sonar 908 drilling machine for crude oil 909 manganese nodule 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-8496832-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "we have found that passing the water vapor through the fritted membrane in combination with the adsorption and aeration steps acts to exclude any residual volatile chemicals and even acts to reduce residual bacterial contamination with much greater efficiency than a conventional distillation process"}, {"pat_id": "US-8650892-B2", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a system for providing ice and drinkable hot and cold water created from purified potable water derived from an atmosphere said system comprising a housing having an air inlet port and an air exhaust port a refrigerant compressor at least one multi way solenoid operated refrigerant control valve a controller for monitoring and for controlling said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve and other electrical subsystems within the system an evaporator wherein said evaporator has fins for maximizing surface area contact and heat transfer with ambient air wherein said fins are coated with non toxic anti corrosion materials that comply with applicable regulatory food standards for paint or a ptfe protective layer said coating promoting rapid collection of condensate water and wherein said evaporator can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive chilled refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to chill air passing across said evaporator fins and wherein said evaporator can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive hot refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to defrost said evaporator fins an anti static anti mold air filter wherein said anti static anti mold air filter is installed upstream of said evaporator a condenser for the system s refrigeration cycle a fan or blower wherein said fan or blower circulates ambient air from said air inlet port through said anti static anti mold air filter across said evaporator said condenser then out said air exhaust port a collector with highly polished surfaces a preliminary filter to remove any smell of condensate water and ammonia wherein said preliminary filter is comprised of activated carbon or zeolite a condensate collection tank wherein said highly polished surfaces of said collector facilitate gravity flow of condensate water into said condensate collection tank and wherein said condensate collection tank is equipped with a water level detector said water level detector and controller causing said evaporator to stop receiving chilled refrigerant at a predetermined high level setpoint at least one water pump a particle filter for filtering particles to protect an intake of said at least one water pump a water purification filtration assembly to filter out bacteria viruses and heavy metals as well as to remove unwanted smells comprising at least one activated carbon filter at least one reverse osmosis filter wherein said reverse osmosis filter has an aperture of less than or equal to 0.0001 \u03bcm and wherein said reverse osmosis filter can be back flushed such that a waste water can be directed to said collector via a three way valve that is controlled by a waste water proportion controller at least one zeolite filter wherein said at least one water pump pumps condensate water from said condensate collection tank through said water purification assembly a purified water collection tank for collecting purified water wherein said purified water collection tank is equipped with a water level detector said water level detector and controller causing said at least one water pump to stop pumping new purified water into said purified water collection tank at a predetermined high level setpoint a cooling loop disposed within said purified water collection tank wherein said cooling loop can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to cool said purified water and wherein a temperature of said purified water in the purified water collection tank is maintained within a temperature range of 2 15 celsius a sterilization system for killing biological material and viruses within said purified water collection tank comprising an ultra violet light device and sterilization chamber said ultra violet light device having an effective sterilization rate of at least 99.99 using a wavelength in a range of 253 255 nm a hot water tank that receives purified water from said purified water collection tank through gravity drain wherein said hot water tank contains an electrical heating element wherein the purified water within said hot water tank is within a range of 50 95 celsius as controlled by said controller and wherein to provide hot potable water for a user said hot potable water can be pumped by a hot water pump through an electrically operated valve and an output filter to a common outlet header a common outlet valve disposed at said common outlet header that can be positioned to allow a user to obtain an output of hot or cold purified water from the system an ice maker the ice maker comprising an inlet to a vessel the inlet provided with purified water a vessel for containing the purified water during cooling at least one cooling loop adjacent to the vessel and an ice dispenser thereby allowing a user to obtain an output of ice or hot or cold purified water from the system"}, {"pat_id": "US-8650892-B2", "para_id": "claim_28", "text": "a method for making a system for providing ice and drinkable water derived from an atmosphere said method comprising the steps of providing a housing having an air inlet port and an air exhaust port providing a refrigerant compressor providing at least one multi way solenoid operated refrigerant control valve providing a controller for monitoring and for controlling said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve and other electrical subsystems within the system providing an evaporator wherein said evaporator has fins for maximizing surface area contact and heat transfer with ambient air wherein said fins are coated with non toxic anti corrosion materials that comply with applicable regulatory food standards for paint or a ptfe protective layer said coating promoting rapid collection of condensate water and wherein said evaporator can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive chilled refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to chill air passing across said evaporator fins and wherein said evaporator can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive hot refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to defrost said evaporator fins providing an anti static anti mold air filter wherein said anti static anti mold air filter is installed upstream of said evaporator providing a condenser for the system s refrigeration cycle providing a fan or blower wherein said fan or blower circulates ambient air from said air inlet port through said anti static anti mold air filter across said evaporator said condenser then out said air exhaust port providing a collector with highly polished surfaces providing a preliminary filter to remove any smell of condensate water and ammonia wherein said preliminary filter is comprised of activated carbon or zeolite providing a condensate collection tank wherein said highly polished surfaces of said collector facilitate gravity flow of condensate water into said condensate collection tank and wherein said condensate collection tank is equipped with a water level detector said water level detector and controller causing said evaporator to stop receiving chilled refrigerant at a predetermined high level setpoint providing at least one water pump providing a particle filter for filtering particles to protect an intake of said at least one water pump providing a water purification filtration assembly to filter out bacteria viruses and heavy metals as well as to remove unwanted smells comprising at least one activated carbon filter at least one reverse osmosis filter wherein said reverse osmosis filter has an aperture of less than or equal to 0.0001 \u03bcm and wherein said reverse osmosis filter can be back flushed such that a waste water can be directed to said collector via a three way valve that is controlled by a waste water proportion controller at least one zeolite filter wherein said at least one water pump pumps condensate water from said condensate collection tank through said water purification assembly providing a purified water collection tank for collecting purified water wherein said purified water collection tank is equipped with a water level detector said water level detector and controller causing said at least one water pump to stop pumping new purified water into said purified water collection tank at a predetermined high level setpoint providing a cooling loop disposed within said purified water collection tank wherein said cooling loop can be configured by said at least one solenoid operated refrigerant control valve to receive refrigerant as pumped from said refrigerant compressor to cool said purified water and wherein a temperature of said purified water in the purified water collection tank is maintained within a temperature range of 2 15 celsius providing a sterilization system for killing biological material and viruses within said purified water collection tank comprising an ultra violet light device and sterilization chamber said ultra violet light device having an effective sterilization rate of at least 99.99 using a wavelength in a range of 253 255 nm providing a hot water tank that receives purified water from said purified water collection tank through gravity drain wherein said hot water tank contains an electrical heating element wherein the purified water within said hot water tank is within a range of 50 95 celsius as controlled by said controller and wherein to provide hot potable water for a user said hot potable water can be pumped by a hot water pump through an electrically operated valve and an output filter to a common outlet header providing a common outlet valve disposed at said common outlet header that can be positioned to allow a user to obtain an output of hot or cold purified water from the system and providing an ice maker comprising an inlet to a vessel the inlet provided with purified water a vessel for containing the purified water during cooling at least one cooling loop adjacent to the vessel and an ice dispenser having an ice release mechanism thereby providing a method for making a system for producing air extracted purified water and ice the purified water being thereby available for a user to extract via said common outlet valve and the ice being available for a user to extract through said ice release mechanism"}, {"pat_id": "US-5460732-A", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "a process for preventing corrosion to the materials of construction of a nickel based alloy or ferrous based alloy wet oxidation system treating raw caustic wastewaters at elevated temperature and pressure comprising the steps a establishing a flow of clean water and oxygen containing gas through said wet oxidation system b adding a caustic wastewater to said system at a point within a reactor vessel or at a point as far upstream of said reactor vessel as a process heat exchanger to produce an oxidized gas liquid mixture c separating said oxidized gas liquid mixture into an oxidized liquid phase effluent and a gaseous phase effluent d measuring the carbon dioxide content of said gaseous phase effluent to establish a baseline carbon dioxide content value while the ph of said system liquid effluent remains at 7 or above and e adding sufficient alkalinity to said raw caustic wastewater to maintain said system liquid effluent ph at 7 or above upon the carbon dioxide content of said gaseous phase effluent exceeding said baseline value by a selected proportion thereby preventing excessive corrosion to the material of construction of said wet oxidation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a closed cylinder portion 100 coupled to the lower side of the groundwater protection part a piezoelectric tube 210 installed at one side to prevent the groundwater from expanding due to internal pressure generated when the groundwater rises is coupled to one side of the piezoelectric pipe the other side is coupled to the plate check valve sand filter 220 for filtering the sand contained in the groundwater plate check valve 230 is coupled to one side of the sand filter the other side is coupled to the meter to prevent the groundwater filtered by the sand filter backflow a meter 240 coupled to one side of the plate check valve and the other side coupled to a pressure gauge a pressure gauge 250 coupled to one side of the meter and coupled to a three way valve on the other side a three way valve 260 coupled to the pressure gauge to form a flow path in the direction of the emergency water supply pipe 600 or the water supply pipe 700 an underground water level protection hole 200 including an underground water level protection column 270 formed along an inner circumference to prevent freezing waves it is configured to include and the controller 500 for supplying power to the underground water protection unit if the temperature is below the set temperature the controller 500 a temperature sensor 510 for detecting the ambient temperature a temperature setting unit 520 for setting a reference temperature for supplying power to the ground water protection protection vessel a memory unit 530 for storing the reference temperature set by the temperature setting unit a power supply unit 540 for supplying power to the ground water protection protection line a temperature comparison unit 550 for comparing the temperature sensed by the temperature sensor with the reference temperature stored in the memory unit a power supply signal transmitter 560 for transmitting a power supply signal to a power supply unit when the temperature compared by the temperature comparison unit is less than a reference temperature freezing prevention comprising a central control unit 570 for controlling the signal flow between the temperature sensor the temperature setting unit the memory unit the power supply unit the temperature comparison unit the power supply signal transmission unit and groundwater upper protection device capable of underwater discharge sterilization treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "under a pressure not less than a saturated steam pressure at said heating temperature while simultaneously applying a shearing force of 0.01 mpa to 20 mpa to said water containing combustible solid"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "under a pressure not less than a saturated steam pressure at said heating temperature while applying a shearing force of 0.01 mpa to 20 mpa to said water containing combustible solid"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the treatment was conducted for an hour with the pressure temperature and shearing force inside the vessel kept at the aforesaid values to remove the water from the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the treatment was conducted for an hour with the pressure temperature and shearing force inside the vessel kept at the aforesaid values to remove the water from the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0513186-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "while supercritical water oxidation requires a thicker walled vessel due to higher operating pressure the less dense process stream in supercritical temperature water oxidation necessitates a larger vessel to achieve a comparable residence time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101163512-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the organic substance drying method of drying a hydrous organic substance a first step of heating the hydrous organic material to hydrolyze it into a liquid liquid organic material a second step of heating the liquid organic material by heating the liquid organic material and using the heat generated in the process of condensing the vaporized water vapor while condensing the vaporized water vapor and a third step of performing the second step to concentrate the liquid organic material into a concentrated organic material the first step is the step of supplying the water containing organic matter to the decomposition tank 130 by supplying steam to the decomposition tank 130 to heat the temperature of the water containing organic matter 180 c 250 c a hydrolysis step of hydrolyzing the liquid organic matter and a step of heat exchanging the hydrolyzed high temperature liquid organic material with a low temperature hydrous organic material to be hydrolyzed the second step is the step of supplying the liquid organic matter into the internal space of the evaporator 80 the step of supplying water vapor discharged from the internal space of the evaporator 80 to the steam compressor 87 the steam compressor 87 compresses the steam to high temperature steam according to the steam pressure curve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273956-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to provide a powder containing minerals and a method for preparing the same which can reduce the purification cost.in order to achieve the above object the preparation method of the powder containing minerals of the present invention includes 6 to 10 parts by weight of persimmon leaves 6 to 10 parts by weight of oak leaves 6 to 10 parts by weight of larvae leaves 4 to 7 parts by weight of melon 4 to 7 parts by weight of pineapple 4 to 7 parts by weight of mango 4 to 7 parts by weight of persimmon 4 to 7 parts by weight of banana 20 to 30 parts by weight of water 18 to 32 parts by weight of brown sugar in a stirrer mixing process a primary fermentation aging process of storing the mixed solution mixed in the grinding mixing process in a fermentation vessel and fermenting and fermenting at a temperature of 18 to 22 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-6977047-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "carbon fines are replaced when they become ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0595858-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "there are several problems with this arrangement 1 the temperature gradient from the top to the bottom of the vessel reactor is a source of heat loss and can significantly reduce the potential for recovering useful energy 2 the hot brine is very corrosive and depressurization of such a brine through a valve is problematic 3 the flow pattern in the vessel reactor does not ensure complete oxidation of organic matter so that a second stage reactor is usually required to further oxidize the fluid effluent from the vessel reactor and 4 the brine may likewise contain unoxidized or partially oxidized products and may require special disposal if it is deemed hazardous"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236974-A", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "this equipment may also be designed in other ways for example with the waste vapor inlets and mixing chamber at the top and waste vapor outlet at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101595809-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the nanotubular photocatalyst immobilized on the titanium support is rotated by itself at this time the photocatalyst may be washed by washing a conductive metal support such as titanium with a detergent oxidizing the titanium mesh surface as an anode by using a copper or iron coil or a foil as a counter electrode in a mixed electrolyte of ammonium fluoride nh4f water h2o and ethylene glycol c2h6o2 treating at 400 to 500 c while supplying oxygen per unit surface area of the support to be oxidized in an amount of 350 to 450 ml per minute in a furnace capable of controlling the atmospheric gas and the treatment temperature a step of storing an aqueous solution of hexavalent chromium bisphenol a and a hydrogen ion concentration which are necessary for the reaction of the photocatalyst 15 in the water tank 2 and a step of supplying an aqueous solution stored in the water tank 2 to the outflow pipe and the inflow pipe wherein the photocatalyst 15 reacts with ultraviolet rays from the light source unit 7 toward the photocatalytic reaction vessel 1 through a reduction reaction of hexavalent chromium and oxidation of bisphenol a are carried out at the same time at this time in the step of moving the aqueous solution stored in the water tank 2 toward the photoreactor 1 the rotational speed and the hydration residence time of the rotating means hrt the rotation speed of the rotating shaft 13 to which the photocatalyst 15 is attached increases as the supply flow rate from the water tank 2 increases and the supply flow rate decreases hrt tend to be opposite the optimum retention time for the photocatalyst 15 and the contaminant to react on the surface is obtained lt rti the light source unit 7 for irradiating ultraviolet rays to the photoreactor 1 is applied with solar light 72 and is irradiated with the solar light 72 to form a single reduction of hexavalent chromium and a single reduction of hexavalent chromium and bisphenol a oxidation is treated simultaneously the photocatalytic reaction of the hexavalent chromium with the treatment of hexavalent chromium according to the presence or absence of water of bisphenol a in the photoreducer 1 is carried out by controlling the hydrogen ion concentration ph chromium and bisphenol a at the same time by adjusting the hydrogen ion concentration ph under the same irradiation condition of the sunlight 72 the present invention relates to a method for producing a titanium supported on a solar irradiated titanium support which is capable of controlling the simultaneous treatment efficiency of hexavalent chromium and bisphenol a wherein the simultaneous treatment efficiency is higher than that in the neutral condition by adjusting the hydrogen ion concentration ph improvement of treatment efficiency of hexavalent chromium and simultaneous removal of hexavalent chromium and environmental hormone by water treatment system with self rotating immobilized nanotube photocatalyst"}, {"pat_id": "US-4123340-A", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the thus treated waste water is preneutralized to a ph of 5.2 in a vessel 4 by the addition of sodium hydroxide solution"}, {"pat_id": "US-4123340-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the thus treated waste water is conducted into vessel 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12 the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor leaving salts dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0177912-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore the degradation of the treated water quality is frequently caused by the decrease of the activity of the reactive microorganisms due to the change of the temperature and the organic factors of the various factors and when the treated water quality deteriorates in order to form reaction conditions such as anaerobic anaerobic aerobic and sedimentation which are essential to maintain the biological circulation altitude treatment a plurality of independent reaction tanks having separate structures are installed the main reaction conditions of each independent reaction vessel anaerobic primary settling tank anaerobic tank anaerobic tank anaerobic tank anaerobic tank final settling tank due to the large amount of pollutant circulation by removing the organic substances and nutrients by eliminating the organic substances and nutrients"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200202134-Y1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "a microbial growth tank that supplies sufficient oxygen while passing and supplies bead abrasion powder 5a containing a lot of proliferating microorganisms 8a to the purification sedimentation basin 13 .microorganisms multiply in the sedimentation basins and aeration tanks of existing wastewater treatment plants and the appropriate oxygen concentration and the appropriate 