  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5386206-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "that is the operator first remove the lid 52 from the standpipe 50 pulled by grasping the handle 33 of the mud sump vessel 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101669813-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the apparatus is formed into a rectangular box shape extending in forward and backward directions the upper part of the front surface is formed with an inflow port through which rainwater collects and an upper part of the rear surface is formed with an outlet for discharging rainwater filtered for recycling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "if foreign matters and dirt accumulate in the waste collection container 4 while being used in this way the rainwater inlet network 2 installed on the rainwater drainage tank 1 on the road as in the prior art is removed and the waste collection vessel installed in the waste collection container base 3 is removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101529143-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "an initial quality treatment device for preventing floatation of a work according to the present invention is an enclosure having an open upper part which is an excellent inflow part to which an excellent inflow pipe 11 and a manhole cover 13 coupled to an upper portion of the manhole 10 to form a manhole 10 for discharging the rainwater from the outside and discharging the rainwater from which the rainwater is removed and a cylindrical vortex forming part 21 located in the inside of the manhole body 10 and formed so as to penetrate through the vortex forming part 21 to face the inside surface and connected to the inlet part of the manhole 10 and a fine through hole 23 formed on the surface of the vortex forming portion 21 to block the vortex and allow the vortex to pass therethrough to form an inflowing vortex a vortex bath 20 an early stage sewage treatment system for preventing injury of a conventional sludge containing a sludge preventing member 30 for preventing a sludge from rising comprising one end being fixed to the sludge sludge preventing member 30 wherein the float prevention member 30 includes a fixing member 40 fixed to the upper portion of the vortex bath 20 or the upper portion of the manhole 10 and the outer circumferential surface is spaced apart from the inner surface of the vortex tank 20 by a predetermined distance and is formed into a conical shape inclined downward a plurality of through holes 32 formed to be smaller in diameter than the fine through holes 23 of the vortex vessel 20 and extending from the bottom of the vessel barrier plate 31 to the bottom surface and a support base 33 made of a metal rod for maintaining the height of the support base the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654689-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in rainwater basins having a water quality improvement function and a malodor removal function a filter block installed in the rainwater vessel housing a purifying agent embedded in the filter block which removes odors removes heavy metals and calcium chloride a rainwater cover cover member coupled to an upper portion of the filter block and a filter block assembly in which an inflow opening for inflow of inflow water is vertically penetrated and a filter block is installed at an edge portion wherein the filter block assembly includes a filter assembly formed in a rectangular shape and having the filter block installed at an edge portion thereof and a seating protrusion formed at an edge portion to be seated on the rainwater receiver housing wherein the filter block is formed of a cylindrical body formed in a structure having a receiving space for receiving the purifying agent therein and having a plurality of through holes drilled on the surface thereof and having an inclined surface or a curved surface portion so that foreign substances contained in the inflow water are not accumulated and a support member installed on the cover and coupled to the filter assembly characterized by comprising a block body formed of a cylindrical or polygonal cylinder a pair of covers provided at both ends of the block body rain gutters with removal function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599839-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "for example the valve may automatically release the gas cartridge pressure upon swelling of the support wall in contact with water such as in a life raft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 1002809 has a main body having an inlet pipe and a discharge pipe a contaminant collecting part provided inside the body and collecting floating contaminants and water soluble contaminants in the initial rainwater flowing through the inflow pipe a sedimentation tank in which the initial stormwater that has passed through the clogging trapping unit is stored a swirling screen for filtering precipitable contaminants in the initial storm that are stored in the settling tank and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside the swirl screen includes an inlet through which the initial storm flows an external vessel through which the sediment is discharged and an inner vessel which is installed in the outer vessel to be separated from the outer vessel and has a lower portion communicating with the outer vessel and a side of which is provided with a flow pipe for supplying an initial storm with the filtration tank an initial stormwater is discharged from the sedimentation tank to the filtration tank due to a difference in water level between the sedimentation tank and the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101867483-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to the present invention there is provided an initial outflow eliminating rainwater disposal apparatus using a rotary screening vessel wherein the initial outflow initial contaminant having a high degree of contamination is excluded through the structure of the screen when the screen is applied through the second filtration when the screen is applied to supply water of high quality and to prevent the water shortage phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730411-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thus the inner surface of the cleaning screen can be reliably cleaned particularly the bottom end of the inner circumferential surface where the foreign matter is most frequently caught it is possible to further improve the self cleaning ability.1 is a block diagram schematically showing a conventional wastewater treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "US-12338143-B2", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the collection of rainwater is of particular interest because it is naturally distilled and because ocean air has fewer atmospheric contaminants as compared to air over populated areas"}, {"pat_id": "US-12338143-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "in one embodiment a method of collecting water is disclosed comprising modifying a waterborne vessel for the purposes of collecting rainwater wherein the vessel comprises a plurality of storage compartments a retractable cover a plurality of collectors and an onboard microfiltration system collecting rainwater providing a porous filter cover to the storage compartments to protect the collected rainwater from contamination applying a retractable non porous cover over the collected rainwater so as to prevent evaporation and providing a plumbing medium so as to filter the collected rainwater through a microfiltration system prior to being offloaded"}, {"pat_id": "US-11096458-B1", "para_id": "para_446", "text": "a five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail comprises a central sail intersector central sail supporting ribs central sail rib raising arms an adjustable water and leaf separating leaf filtering central sail attached to the central sail supporting ribs for functioning as a water diverting device to predeterminately redirect the flow of water functioning as a leaf filtering device to filter leaves from rain water when used upside down functioning as a water collector to collect rain water when used upside down functioning as a wind blocker to block wind functioning as a privacy screen to provide privacy functioning as an awning to angledly block rain and sun beams functioning as a canopy to vertically block rain and sun beams functioning as a wind redirector to redirect wind in and out of sail and functioning as a sail steering wind powered device to steer the sail in multiple different directions a ring sail rib intersector primary automatically centered and reinforced ribs for resisting bending and warping due to heavy winds providing reinforced infrastructure for a sail when used on a wind powered land vehicle providing reinforced infrastructure for an emergency rainwater collecting device on a marine vessel and providing reinforced infrastructure for a shade canopy secondary automatically centered and reinforced ribs for resisting bending and warping due to heavy winds providing reinforced infrastructure for a sail when used on a wind powered land vehicle providing reinforced infrastructure for an emergency rainwater collecting device on a marine vessel and providing reinforced infrastructure for a shade canopy multi rib connecting automatically centered and reinforced adjustable cores inserted into and screwed to the primary automatically centered and reinforced ribs and the secondary automatically centered and reinforced ribs the multi rib connecting automatically centered and reinforced adjustable cores for allowing manufacturers to shorten long ribs into the primary automatically centered and reinforced ribs and the secondary automatically centered and reinforced ribs to reduce the length and volume of the shipping package of the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail in a shipping container to save money from expensive shipping costs and securely and reinforcingly connecting the primary automatically centered and reinforced ribs to the secondary automatically centered and reinforced ribs to provide strength and structure to the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail rib length adjusting holes drilled into the primary automatically centered and reinforced ribs the secondary automatically centered and reinforced ribs and the multi rib connecting automatically centered and reinforced adjustable cores a ring sail arm intersector ring sail rib raising arms foldably attached to the ring sail arm intersector an adjustable water collecting wind blocking privacy screen ring sail attached to the primary automatically centered and reinforced ribs and the secondary automatically centered and reinforced ribs the adjustable water collecting wind blocking privacy screen ring sail for functioning as an emergency rainwater collector on a marine vessel functioning as a water collector to collect rainwater when used upside down functioning as a sail on a wind powered land vehicle functioning as a wind blocker to block wind functioning as a privacy screen to provide privacy functioning as an awning to angledly block rain and sun beams functioning as a canopy to vertically block rain and sun beams functioning as a water diverting device to predeterminately redirect the flow of water functioning as a leaf filtering device to filter leaves from rain water when used upside down functioning as a wind redirector to redirect wind in and out of sail and functioning as a wind resistor to protect users an upper post attached to the central sail intersector the ring sail arm intersector slidably attached to the upper post a lower post and a multi angled multi surface mountable multi plate connecting reversible stackable base attached to the lower post for stackably connecting multiple the multi angled multi surface mountable multi plate connecting reversible stackable bases together securing the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail at the base of a wall securely wedging the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a step recess built into a truck bumper corner or an rv bumper corner without need for bolting securely wedging the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail into a tailgate gap without need for bolting securely wedging the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a balcony railing without need for bolting securely wedging the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a railing of a watercraft without need for bolting securely attaching the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a tow hitch securely attaching the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a utility hole of a truck bed without need for bolting securely attaching the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a wind powered land vehicle to act as a sail and securely attaching the five device in one water and leaf separating leaf filtering water collecting wind blocking wind redirecting marine yacht land yacht balcony bumper and trailer hitch mountable sail to a column table wall fence bumper balcony or patio"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101763341-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the unit box 20 may be made of one material selected from concrete acrylic resin polyethylene resin polypropylene resin polychlorinated resin frp iron and stainless steel in the case of the unit box 20 of the present invention gravity or power must be mobilized to move the sediment deposited under the unit box 20 out of the rainwater storage vessel 100 by using the pull line 50 to remove the sediment on the water surface therefore it is preferable to use a material that has a low specific gravity and does not break down from an external impact"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218344-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to prevent the re injury of the sediment which is a disadvantage of the swirl method by applying the anti floating means the filtration tank equipped with the filtration means is separately installed to separate the vortex and the laminar flow forming tank capable of forming the laminar flow"}]</data>
