  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-1575875-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "disinfection metal removal and oil water emulsion splitting occurs and contaminants are removed by vacuuming floated material from the surface and removing bottom sediments via the sloped bottom of the vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes for collecting only contaminants generated during the filtration process and sludge from the second storage tank which are formed in the filtration tank and a backwash water drain pump configured to discharge contaminants and sludges introduced into the inside of the backwash drainage storage tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "US-7520993-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in an exemplary embodiment the system for treating an aqueous liquid containing dissolved minerals and dissolved hydrocarbons comprises passing the aqueous liquid or a waste water feed stream through a warm lime softener wherein the warm lime softener or warm lime softening system comprises a lime silo a sodium carbonate silo and a caustic storage tank in fluid communication with a lime and soda precipitation softener vessel which is in fluid communication with a sludge storage tank wherein contacting the waste water feed stream with lime and sodium carbonate in the lime and soda precipitation softener vessel produces a particulate suspension that settles to produce a sludge part of which may be recycled back to the lime and soda precipitation softener vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100451543-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "a at this time by the supply of dissolved oxygen the reaction vessel 40 within the micro organisms active in addition reduces the waste water of cod and bod filtered through an organic substance oxidation process and the nitrification of nitrogen becomes actively made nh 3 to supply produced by n0 2 n no 3 n and denitrified in the next precipitation step s42 and discharge step s5 to remove nitrogen n"}, {"pat_id": "US-4076615-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "adjusting to the ph of the treated influent waste water stream to cause precipitation of the alum as aluminum hydroxide 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938463-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition the electrolytic treatment method is to crush manure and the like and to pass them through the electrode plate with a narrow gap between each other so that the decomposition and oxidation occurs by electricity not only is not easy to crush but also generated during electrolysis of seawater due to the strong oxidizing power of hypochlorous acid hclo 3 corrosion of the structure is easy and the treated water may contain excessive hypochlorous acid which may cause secondary pollution.the present invention was created in order to solve the above problems the object of the present invention is the wastewater by purifying various wastewater including manure generated in the vessel through four steps of microbial decomposition precipitation adsorption filtration and biodegradation disinfection it has good treatment capacity and it is easy to utilize the space of vessels where various equipments are concentrated and it is easy to maintain and adapt to load change or temperature change of waste water and also biochemical sewage treatment for ship that can minimize the sludge generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-4445935-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "during this addition the oxidation reduction potential of the combined solution may be continually monitored by employing a conventional high impedance voltmeter"}, {"pat_id": "US-5340468-A", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "a system adapted for regulating the addition of lime to reduce water alkalinity comprising a treatment vessel having 1 a mixing zone wherein a stream of untreated water is mixed with lime and 2 a flocculation zone that receives said mixture of water and lime from said mixing zone and allows precipitation of the resulting insoluble salts a first sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said stream of untreated water entering said mixing zone a second sensor operable for measuring the conductivity of said water in said flocculation zone pump means for adding said lime to said untreated water in said mixing zone and a controller operable for regulating said pump means by periodically sampling said conductivities measured by said first sensor and said second sensor computing the ratio of said conductivities for each sample computing the slope of said conductivity ratio and determining the minimum value of said conductivity ratio said controller being operable for regulating said pump means so that sufficient lime is added to said water to pass through said minimum conductivity ratio and further turning said pump means off when said ratio exceeds a predetermined maximum set point and said slope is positive and turning said pump means on when said ratio falls below a predetermined minimum set point and said slope is negative"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the vessel 311 the three annular movable partition plates 312 evenly installed vertically inside the annular closed chamber 310 and the rotating mechanism 31 installed in the center of the annular closed chamber 310 to rotate and drive the annular movable partition plate 312"}, {"pat_id": "US-8685252-B2", "para_id": "para_197", "text": "while such high recovery in conventional membrane systems can lead to scaling embodiments of the present invention avoid this problem by the open channel membrane spacing and the use of vibration to suspend particles that can result from precipitation of the concentrated dissolved solids"}]</data>
</edge>
