 bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-11014837-B2", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "specifically the present embodiments relate to a technology for providing an energy self contained oceanic drone on which an ocean survey and monitoring complex sensor is mounted using a polymer electrolyte fuel cell and a solar cell based on new renewable energy complexly"}, {"pat_id": "US-11014837-B2", "para_id": "para_102", "text": "furthermore hydrogen production efficiency can be enhanced and a maintenance and management cost for the water electrolysis system can be reduced because water electrolysis treatment is performed based on two types of seawater and fresh water through advanced water treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102051029-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the contaminant sensor 12 prevents the inflow of contaminated water by closing the raw water inlet valve 14 when oil leakage or rapid deterioration of water by a vessel occurs in the sea shore or river and the virus sterilization device 20 by removing harmful bacteria such as norovirus vibrio bacteria and cholera bacteria water is evenly introduced into the virus sterilizer 20 through the distribution screen 22 to remove the bacteria by contacting the raw water to the uv lamp or uvled 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100440889-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to increase the efficiency of adhering microorganisms contained in the contaminants of influent water flowing through the gills a grid type nonwoven fabric fiber netting material is installed on a fixed frame and a plurality of the fixed frames are superimposed to be spaced apart from each other a contact oxidation vessel in which a sludge port is formed at the bottom for discharging the precipitated sludge from the contact material bubble generating means provided on one side of the contact oxidation vessel and generating bubbles for performing lateral aeration a sedimentation tank installed at one side of the contact oxidation tank to precipitate residual contaminants contained in the influent water that has passed through the contact oxidation tank and a sludge tank that is connected to a lower portion of the sludge port of the contact oxidation tank and generates a sludge settled to a lower portion of the contact oxidation tank and the sludge tank wherein the contaminated river water treatment apparatus comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101070807-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hull having a contaminant floatation space of an appeal a river and an ocean hereinafter referred to as an hoso having a structure having an open lower portion at an inner portion thereof a bubble injecting body positioned in an appeal below a predetermined depth from the bottom of the hull while being supported on one side of the hull with respect to the contaminant floating space to provide a bubble in the direction of the contaminant floating space a bubble supply device provided in the hull to provide bubbles to the bubble injector a coagulant injector positioned above the bubble injector and injecting a coagulant together with the bubble injector toward the contaminant floating space a coagulant supply device provided in the hull and providing a coagulant to the coagulant injector a contaminant collecting unit positioned at an opposite side of the bubble injector with respect to the contaminant floating space and collecting contaminants floating into the contaminant floating space algae removal vessel system for improving the water quality characterized in that the hull provided with a pollutant treatment unit for processing the pollutants collected in the pollutant collection unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218344-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to prevent the re injury of the sediment which is a disadvantage of the swirl method by applying the anti floating means the filtration tank equipped with the filtration means is separately installed to separate the vortex and the laminar flow forming tank capable of forming the laminar flow"}]</data>
</edge>
