ed water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1355734-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "the active water generator 1 is therefore preferably tuned to improve the breakup of the clusters and such tuning can advantageously be accomplished by varying the modulation frequency and bias voltage while viewing the output of a orp meter measuring oxidation reduction potential of one of the processed water streams exiting the vessel 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-7291314-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the active water generator 1 is therefore preferably tuned to improve the breakup of the clusters and such tuning can advantageously be accomplished by varying the modulation frequency and bias voltage while viewing the output of a orp meter measuring oxidation reduction potential of one of the processed water streams exiting the vessel 10"}]</data>
