  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-6030587-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pressurized reactor for supercritical water oxidation comprising a pressure vessel for containing a fluid and capable of operating in excess of a supercritical temperature and a supercritical pressure of said fluid said vessel further comprising a shell and a cap portion said portions fitting together to enclose an interior space said portions having interior and exterior surfaces and a common longitudinal axis said interior space having a center point an oxidizer said oxidizer mixed with said fluid an electrical heating means a hollow protuberance located in at least one of said portions said protuberance formed along said common axis and projecting into said interior space said protuberance having an end closed to said interior surface and an end open to said exterior surface said protuberance receives said electrical heating means said electrical heating means heats said fluid in a first zone surrounding said interior center point and means for cooling said vessel exterior surface thereby cooling said interior surface and creating a second zone in said fluid along said interior surfaces wherein said fluid exists in a subcritical state said heating means and said cooling means creating a density gradient in said fluid and thereby cause a steady state convective circulation to form in said fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "US-11738314-B2", "para_id": "para_143", "text": "the radial temperature gradient caused by the cyclonic rotation within the liquid 922 and the incoming water flowing in the water jacket space 928 can result in a temperature at inner walls 921 of the outer vessel 901 that is sufficiently low to mitigate against corrosion of the inner wall by high temperature reactions occurring within the chamber 900 and also can permit walls of the outer vessel 901 to be relatively thin compared to conventional high temperature high pressure reaction vessels"}]</data>
