tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101587697-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "1 to 3 the apparatus for producing hydrogen water according to the present invention comprises a closed container 230 having an open close valve 220 operated by a knitting machine 210 a static pressure maintaining unit 200 for maintaining the water level and a hydrogen generating chamber 320 supplied with raw water purified by the static pressure holding unit 200 is formed of a closed vessel 340 formed by bifurcating the ion exchange membrane 330 between the oxygen generating chamber 310 supplied with the raw water an electrolysis unit 300 having a cathode plate 311 in the oxygen generating chamber and an anode plate 321 in the hydrogen generating chamber 320 to perform electrolysis according to power supply a fluid pump 400 for supplying raw water and hydrogen from the hydrogen generation chamber 320 of the electrolysis unit 300 and feeding the raw water and hydrogen a filter unit 500 including a filter 510 connected to the fluid pump 400 to receive raw water and hydrogen to remove foreign matter and ozone a dissolution part 600 having a nozzle 610 to supply raw water and hydrogen from the filter part 500 and inject the raw water into the raw water the fluid pump 400 is provided in the piping after the dissolved portion 600 so that the fluid pump 400 is driven in accordance with detection of the supply of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4992181-A", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "a method for treating water removed from the ground to reduce the content of noxious sulfur containing impurities therein before the water is supplied to an associated water system said method comprising the steps of spraying the water to be treated in the upper portion of a closed standpipe which has an inlet for the water to be treated and an outlet through which water can flow to the associated water system the inlet and the outlet of the standpipe being so positioned that air which becomes disassociated from water can collect in the upper portion of the standpipe controlling the spraying of water in the upper portion of the closed standpipe to maintain a superatmospheric therein to pressurize the associated water system entraining air with the water before it is sprayed in the standpipe said last named step being carried out in a vessel in which the ground water is sprayed upwardly maintaining the water level in the standpipe that is required to enable the flow of water therefrom to the associated water system containing the ground water before it is delivered to the associated water system with a catalyst for the oxidation of sulfur and sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions and controlling the time of contact between the ground water and the catalyst the amount of air entrained with the water sprayed in the vessel and the amount of air entrained with the water sprayed in the standpipe so that entrained air separates from the water and forms an air pocket inside the standpipe and there is a substantially complete oxidation of sulfur and sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions"}, {"pat_id": "US-4992181-A", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the method comprises the steps of spraying the water to be treated in the upper portion of a standpipe upon demand from an associated water system to cause a flow of water from within the standpipe through a bed of a catalyst for the oxidation of sulfur containing moieties to sulfate anions and from the catalyst bed to the associated water system entraining air with the water sprayed in the standpipe and maintaining the water level in the standpipe that is required to enable the flow of water and entrained air therefrom to pass through the catalyst bed and to the associated water system"}, {"pat_id": "US-6171480-B1", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "therefore the diameter of contact chamber is an important factor because as it increases the distance traveled in each complete circle increases and the volume of water that can be stripped increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730411-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thus the inner surface of the cleaning screen can be reliably cleaned particularly the bottom end of the inner circumferential surface where the foreign matter is most frequently caught it is possible to further improve the self cleaning ability.1 is a block diagram schematically showing a conventional wastewater treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101851689-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a screen net which is immersed in the treated water in a reaction tank having an open upper part and has a mesh structure and passes through the treated water to be filtered and is arranged in a direction perpendicular to the flowing direction of the treated water a screen portion disposed on the left side and the right side a contaminant remover installed in the reaction tank so as to circulate the contaminants to remove contaminants generated in the reaction tank a distillation unit installed at a lower portion of the reaction tank and supplying air to the treated water from a lower portion of the reaction tank and and a control unit for receiving the water level information of the treated water from a water level sensor for sensing the water level of the treated water and controlling the operation of the debris remover in accordance with the level of the treated water the contaminant a transporting conveyor for circulating and moving the inside and outside of the reaction tank a collecting removing unit being coupled to the transporting conveying unit and a conveying roller unit disposed adjacent to the conveying conveyor and connected to the driving unit to move the conveying conveyor by rotation and a driving unit connected to the conveying unit to move the conveying unit and controlled to be driven by the control unit wherein a concave shaped collecting part is formed to collect contaminants deposited on the bottom of the reaction tank and connected to the conveying conveyor so as to move along the bottom surface of the reaction tank and to circulate the inside and the outside of the reaction tank according to the movement of the conveying conveyor and a collecting removing unit for discharging and removing the contaminants collected by the collecting unit while moving the conveying conveyor a part of which is annularly immersed in the reaction tank and disposed adjacent to the bottom and side surfaces of the reaction tank so as not to interfere with the flow of the treated water to reduce the screening effect the collecting wherein the collecting unit is located on the bottom surface of the reaction vessel so as to observe the moving direction while being immersed in the reaction tank a collecting body for collecting contaminants and a separation preventing part formed at both ends of the collecting part body to prevent separation of the contaminants collected in the collecting part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306263-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "the height of the coagulant layer obtained through experiments and calculations and the amount of coagulant input correspond to the degree of contamination of the wash water and are stored in the operation unit of the washing machine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102385106-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in the seawater desalination system according to an embodiment of the present invention the reaction vessel has a water supply port connected to the water tank on one side a drain port provided at a position lower than the water level supplied to the other side and the methane tank on the lower side it may include a gas inlet connected to and a gas outlet provided on the upper surface or one side of the upper surface.according to the hydrogen production apparatus using plasma discharge of the present invention and the seawater desalination system including the same it is possible to maximize the amount of hydrogen generated in a short time by using pulse plasma discharge in the hydrogen production apparatus and the produced hydrogen is supplied to the fuel cell the generated power can be supplied to the high pressure pump to operate the seawater desalination system.1 is a schematic diagram showing a seawater desalination system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand the quantitative waste water is discharged quantitatively and discharged into the aeration tank 50 equipped with the oxygen supply nozzle 57 by the water level difference through the first wear 31 via the flow rate control anoxic tank 40 the coarse sewage flows through the weir 35 into the sedimentation filtration tank 20 in which the sludge s is precipitated in a downward upward flow by the induction pipe 93 in the sedimentation filtration tank 20 and the treated supernatant is the discharge vessel"}]</data>
</edge>
