  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}]</data>
