  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10982416-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention has a fully automatic system combined with a high pressure water supply pump station a low pressure water circulation pump station and a private water tank at the local area with an automation control panel that has the pressure modulating and autonomous monitoring functionality to manage water pressure limitation constraints and allow water to flow between different water pressure zones and integrate them into a single homogenous water distribution system for user with both the water directly from city water main and the water from a private water tank to remedy local water flow deficiencies in a reliable way with a sufficient capacity for all kinds of situations especially under an emergency condition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "multi function water storage system and method for reducing the contamination by initial rain and preventing a city from flooding the present invention relates to a multi functional next generation storage system and storage method that can be easily applied to urban areas and can be used to control the initial excellent pollution load caused by rainfall to prevent urban flooding and to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "US-5770057-A", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "since this last situation is rather rare it is accepted by most city regulations although there is still some macroparticulate contamination of the water body at the downstream end of main conduit 14b because these regulations do not require the extreme water overflows to be completely screened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377605-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention has an advantageous effect of enabling a quick response by directly detecting the contamination leakage by a sensor directly installed in the field.1 is a diagram showing a state in which in the water treatment instrumentation control system for a smart city of the present invention a pair of sensors for water quality inspection are installed at regular intervals symmetrically left and right at the edges of a tributary p and a main stream m"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102156126-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "in the present invention when the wastewater flows into the wastewater inlet 101 through the discharge pipe p of a wastewater discharge source such as an industry or a livestock industry as described above the wastewater inlet passage before supplying it to the treatment facility 102 part of the wastewater flowing from 101 is continuously acquired and the wastewater purified through a multi stage cyclone device is supplied to the water quality tms 170 and various sensors provided inside the water quality tms 170 not shown city measures this and provides information on contamination of wastewater"}]</data>
</edge>
