r balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "initial flow rate and flow rate information measured by the smart meter 30 water quality information measured by the first sensor device 40 and the second sensor device 50 and the consumer 90 measured by the water pressure sensor 70 is provided immediately before the flow rate and flow rate information or water pressure information leak detection sensor 60 the connection node terminal 400 for collecting the leakage information measured by wired or wireless communication method and an integrated control server 600 in the ict integrated monitoring water management system for building a smart water city that includes the integrated control server 600 ict integrated monitoring for building a smart water city water management and maintenance of the block where the water management system 1 is installed analysis of the flow rate in the block prediction and flow of abnormal signs and operating and monitoring the network through constant monitoring of water pressure in order to build a smart water city corresponding to the scada system the flow rate flow rate water quality and water pressure information on the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 are connected to each sensor by wired wireless communication from the connected node terminal 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the ict integrated monitoring water management system for building a smart water city according to an embodiment of the present invention includes initial flow rate and flow rate information measured by the smart meter 30 and a first sensor unit 40 and the water quality information measured by the second sensor unit 50 the flow rate and flow rate information or water pressure information immediately before being provided to the consumer 90 measured by the water pressure sensor 70 the leak detection sensor 60 connection node terminal 400 for collecting the leakage information measured in by wired or wireless communication method and an integrated control server 600 which is a central control monitoring system that performs integrated management and monitoring after receiving all measurement information collected by the access node terminal 400 through the network 500 it characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101293190-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the data transmission unit that transmits to the server configures the field equipment to enable intelligent leakage monitoring of water and sewage pipes in large areas such as u city"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200176500-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition in order to solve the above problems by covering the rubber plate or plywood in the water collector as a temporary measure to prevent the leakage of odor if left for a long time to leave the rubber plate or plywood road surface during sudden heavy rain or heavy rain due to poor drainage some of the city centers were flooded resulting in frequent disasters such as enormous property damage.the present invention was devised to solve the above problems and it is possible to simultaneously prevent backflow of road water due to odors and heavy rains caused by domestic waste and wastewater thereby protecting the environment and improving the quality of life of residents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377605-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention has an advantageous effect of enabling a quick response by directly detecting the contamination leakage by a sensor directly installed in the field.1 is a diagram showing a state in which in the water treatment instrumentation control system for a smart city of the present invention a pair of sensors for water quality inspection are installed at regular intervals symmetrically left and right at the edges of a tributary p and a main stream m"}]</data>
