e microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to reduce the risk of local flooding due to heavy rain in the city center while reducing the necessity of excavation and replacement of existing sewerage or storm drainage in the urban roads thereby reducing social costs such as traffic congestion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101738905-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the water collecting boundary block according to the present invention since the water stored in the space portion is continuously supplied to the ground through the drain hole it is possible to prevent the desertification of the city and the damage of the trees"}, {"pat_id": "US-9127448-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "because the device operates by gravity the catch basin is typically positioned at a locally minimum elevation in the road segment or city block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "20 0433333 installed on the top of the casing casing developed for waterworks to block the inflow of external pollutants to make waterproof to prevent the inflow of rainwater into the inside of the city when submerged can be cleaned with a simple method when cleaning with compressed air of the number of wells for an antifouling structure is disclosed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016232-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of heavy rain urban sewage pipe control method the clogged sewage pipe is to be connected to the main pipe with a large diameter directly through the emergency pipe or to control the existing sewage pipe to the shortest distance by dividing a certain area of the city into a block to prevent the sewage flowing into a certain area the sewage pipe exiting from a certain area is controlled to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or connected to the shortest distance the sensor is a speed sensor to measure the flow rate of rainwater to calculate the flow rate of each sewage pipe and if the flow rate reaches the dangerous water level is to send an alarm signal to the smartphone of the manager in advance a meter is installed in each sewage pipe installed in the city and if the controller receiving the signal of the meter is judged that no sewage flows in the sewage pipe it is determined that some pipes of the sewage pipes are blocked and the manager through the communication unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101253532-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition the present invention is to solve the problem that it is difficult to determine the situation whether the rainwater runoff is a problem or if the rainfall is an excess of capacity if the rainfall is sustained urban flooding occurs in the city by installing and remotely monitoring the sewage section it is possible to prevent the flooding of the city more effectively by remotely controlling the floodgate of the drainage pumping station as well as the initial storm drain.1 is an exemplary view showing the current state of domestic sewage treatment facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200440231-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "summarizing the contents of the spoken sidewalk block a voting space that is an empty space is formed inside the sidewalk block so that the visually impaired person taps with a walking stick while walking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101994814-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention the control unit 150 controls the first hydraulic cylinder 112 and the second hydraulic cylinder 122 of the first and second driving units 110 and 120 and detects the operation of the piston through the sensor to determine whether to open or close the water level door 200 and the water gate 700.the system for preventing backflow of seawater and river water in a sewer system of coastal cities and lowlands according to the present invention is characterized in that a river or sea flows backward by controlling a sluice passage and a sluice gate formed between a sewer pipe and a sluice outlet to flow river water or seawater into a sewer pipe there is an effect that can be prevented.1 is an exemplary view of a conventional sewage system 2 is a perspective view of a movable backflow prevention system for seawater and river water in a sewer system of a coastal city and a lowland according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016233-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the blocked sewage pipe is to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or to be connected to the shortest distance by dividing a certain area of the city into a block to prevent the sewage flowing into a certain area the sewage pipe exiting from a certain area is controlled to be directly connected to the main pipe with a large diameter or connected to the shortest distance the sensor is a speed sensor to measure the flow rate of rainwater to calculate the flow rate of each sewage pipe and when the flow rate reaches the dangerous water level is to send an alarm signal to the smartphone of the manager in advance each sewage pipe installed in the city is provided with a meter reading and the control unit receiving the signal of the meter if it is determined that the sewage does not flow in the sewage pipe it is determined that some of the sewage pipes are blocked the manager through the communication unit since the smartphone sends a signal that a problem has occurred the smartphone receives a signal and shows the location of the pipe on which the problem occurred and the administrator moves to the location shown on the screen of the smartphone to clean the pipe endoscope to penetrate through the smart phone outputs a screen on which a flow rate is above a dangerous water level or a blocked pipe and when the application installed in the smart phone is executed a main screen is output and the main screen flows sewage from the city"}, {"pat_id": "US-10005682-B1", "para_id": "para_250", "text": "one or both of the primary and secondary flow paths can optionally comprise a flow meter or a ph meter or both"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750392-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the inner bottom surface of the manhole is formed in an arc shape so as to smoothly rotate when the backflow prevention plate 30 is rotated by the pressure of the sewage and the backflow prevention plate 30 is rotated according to the water level of the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "initial flow rate and flow rate information measured by the smart meter 30 water quality information measured by the first sensor device 40 and the second sensor device 50 and the consumer 90 measured by the water pressure sensor 70 is provided immediately before the flow rate and flow rate information or water pressure information leak detection sensor 60 the connection node terminal 400 for collecting the leakage information measured by wired or wireless communication method and an integrated control server 600 in the ict integrated monitoring water management system for building a smart water city that includes the integrated control server 600 ict integrated monitoring for building a smart water city water management and maintenance of the block where the water management system 1 is installed analysis of the flow rate in the block prediction and flow of abnormal signs and operating and monitoring the network through constant monitoring of water pressure in order to build a smart water city corresponding to the scada system the flow rate flow rate water quality and water pressure information on the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 are connected to each sensor by wired wireless communication from the connected node terminal 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if at least one or more of the parameters constituting the water quality measured by the formed second sensor unit 50 does not match a preset criterion control not only to control the turbidity drain valve 300 but also to discharge the turbid water water pressure measured by the water pressure detection sensor 70 among the flow rate control valve 80 and the water pressure detection sensor 70 sequentially formed between the turbid water drain valve 300 and the consumer 90 is outside the preset water pressure range if not by controlling the flow rate control valve 80 to maintain the flow rate and flow rate to be maintained in a preset water pressure range the administrator mobile terminal accessible through the network 500 for the database 630 800 provides a real time monitoring and monitoring module 621 that provides a function to support decision making ict integrated monitoring for smart water city construction send and receive to receive the location and property information of natural and artificial objects existing on the surface and underground and ground spaces of the water management system 1 from the big data server 700 through the network 500 after controlling the unit 610 the received information is matched and generated based on gis information based on the water pipe of the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for smart water city construction and then through the network 500 by controlling the transmitter receiver 610 to transmit to the manager mobile terminal 800 the manager can directly control the water supply network block and facility information db as well as support various planning and decision making and industrial activities in connection with the manager s work"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to support disaster response biofilm management energy management and water pipe network investigation diagnosis simulation data for leak progress rate for a preset water pipe which is a gis based facility for waterworks is generated and a network for the generated simulation data 500 through the indirect evaluation of the facilities of the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for smart water city construction through transmission to the manager s mobile terminal 800 as well as to predict the current state of the facilities indirectly among the influence factors that can be obtained factors with high influence are selected and calculated through an algorithm and each block and facility pipe network operation module supporting decision making tasks including washing rehabilitation replacement and search of water pipes by controlling the transmitting and receiving unit 610 to transmit the ranking to the manager mobile terminal 800 through the network 500 622 and simulate the information in the tap water network stored in the database 630 using hydraulic algorithms and generate simulation results for flow rate water pressure water quality and flow rate to analyze the water flow rate and water leak rate in the block and predict the leak point and flow rate provides an analysis program for monitoring water pressure and monitoring leaks to the manager s mobile terminal 800 through the network 500 but it is a web system that allows administrators to easily access the network through information sharing to secure the network operation and monitoring system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "accordingly in order to supply water to hilly areas and to cultivate forests by pumping groundwater flowing underground as a water vein with electricity generated from renewable energy in the ground that is drying up due to climate change adjacent to the city center 84 the invention comprises a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 forming the afforestation block 30 a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to allow for the planting of landscaping trees 46 by protruding a moving gap 42 provided between a separate outer wall 32 in the rear wall 31 and afforestation blocks 30 30 assembled in a stack so that the moving gaps 42 are connected to each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101799853-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the present invention also provides a water circulation system for a city that can protect a natural ecosystem as well as a person by restoring a water circulation system in a city where water circulation is difficult due to road pavement sidewalk block and the like and a roadside protection trench used in the system there is"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161569-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore the float bowel 63 will follow the water level to move up and down causing the water stop cock 65 to stop at or release from the stub tube 52"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore it is virtually impossible to install a decompression valve in a jurisdiction block where a manhole structure is mainly installed in a road network where city traffic is frequent"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the city culvert structure according to the present invention is characterized in that drainage can be guided irrespective of a road gradient by using a block body having the same shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "induce the rainwater guided to the ground is conveyed through the conveying pipe member filtering rainwater conveyed through the conveying pipe member through a filtration unit storing the filtered rainwater in a storage tank pumping the stored rainwater through at least one of river water maintenance water irrigation canal water vegetation water around the river and waterfront park landscaping fountain supplying the necessary power to the filtration unit and the pumping means by at least one of a photovoltaic device or a wind turbine wherein a portion of the rainwater is permeable in the step of inducing rainwater through the permeable sidewalk block"}]</data>
