  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-6912890-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "many city codes prohibit any such blockage or restriction in the plumbing line thus if one forgets to remove the erhardt device before covering over the plumbing line with drywall the resulting structure is in violation of the city code"}, {"pat_id": "US-11326977-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the local water company conducts leakage management by continuously monitoring and analyzing the night flow of the dma"}, {"pat_id": "US-4815492-A", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "according to still further features of my invention the flapper valve if it should be corroded or clogged with protein accumulations allowing waste fluid to leak there through whereupon the means for activating the pump can be caused to operate and to turn the pump on and discharge the leaked fluid from a flood back into the city sewer line to prevent sewage from leaking into the building"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the application can be configured to determine if there is a leak in a fluid system in the building by comparing the fluid data obtained from at least one sensor device of the plurality of sensor devices to evaluation data associated with various events and conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_156", "text": "for example a short refill every certain time may indicate a medium leak while a longer refill more than x may mean there is a potential future leak while a much longer refill time than x can indicate a major leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water leakage safe diagnosis system in sewage wastewater and leachate treatment plantsthe present invention relates to a leak safety diagnosis device for sewage wastewater and leachate treatment plant and more particularly to protect the pipe from external influences while increasing the coupling force and sealing force of the joint portion where the pipe and the pipe contact each other and to prevent the leakage of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-12315357-B2", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "the incidents 404 may include a roof leak a foundation leak a wall leak or a window leak for example"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201943-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the sewage pipe for rainwater according to the present invention has a leak hole 20 formed on the upper circumferential surface thereof so that a part of the rainwater penetrates into the ground 2 to prevent disasters and to supply water to roadside trees installed in the city"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102275063-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "this is because it is difficult to determine whether there is a leak unless there is a change in the leaking part because it must be used to determine whether there is a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in 1988 piper alpha platform fire accident killed 167 people and costed 3.4 billion because of removing the pump a s pressure safety valve in 1999 a pressure relief valve failed on a 16 inch gasoline pipeline operated by the olympic pipe line company in bellingham wash"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the system includes a water meter inline to a main water valve wherein the water meter is configured to provide water usage data to a collector unit and an irrigation system configured to receive weather data city requirements for water use and soil moisture levels and provide a water consumption data from different regions to the collector unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "initial flow rate and flow rate information measured by the smart meter 30 water quality information measured by the first sensor device 40 and the second sensor device 50 and the consumer 90 measured by the water pressure sensor 70 is provided immediately before the flow rate and flow rate information or water pressure information leak detection sensor 60 the connection node terminal 400 for collecting the leakage information measured by wired or wireless communication method and an integrated control server 600 in the ict integrated monitoring water management system for building a smart water city that includes the integrated control server 600 ict integrated monitoring for building a smart water city water management and maintenance of the block where the water management system 1 is installed analysis of the flow rate in the block prediction and flow of abnormal signs and operating and monitoring the network through constant monitoring of water pressure in order to build a smart water city corresponding to the scada system the flow rate flow rate water quality and water pressure information on the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 are connected to each sensor by wired wireless communication from the connected node terminal 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to support disaster response biofilm management energy management and water pipe network investigation diagnosis simulation data for leak progress rate for a preset water pipe which is a gis based facility for waterworks is generated and a network for the generated simulation data 500 through the indirect evaluation of the facilities of the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for smart water city construction through transmission to the manager s mobile terminal 800 as well as to predict the current state of the facilities indirectly among the influence factors that can be obtained factors with high influence are selected and calculated through an algorithm and each block and facility pipe network operation module supporting decision making tasks including washing rehabilitation replacement and search of water pipes by controlling the transmitting and receiving unit 610 to transmit the ranking to the manager mobile terminal 800 through the network 500 622 and simulate the information in the tap water network stored in the database 630 using hydraulic algorithms and generate simulation results for flow rate water pressure water quality and flow rate to analyze the water flow rate and water leak rate in the block and predict the leak point and flow rate provides an analysis program for monitoring water pressure and monitoring leaks to the manager s mobile terminal 800 through the network 500 but it is a web system that allows administrators to easily access the network through information sharing to secure the network operation and monitoring system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "to this end the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is a system that manages each of the grid type waterworks network formed in the downtown area and the waterworks network formed in the outskirts of the city as an integrated system to manage the network"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102336715-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "this is because it is difficult to determine whether there is a leak unless there is a change in the leaking part because it must be used to determine whether there is a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "while this may not point to the exact location of the leak this data combined with a geo spatial map will allow cities to gather insight into a potential section sub section or branch of the city plumbing that could be leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "water meter 300a 300b 300c and 400 may further provide notifications to a user of a potential leak and may connect to a city network by utilizing one or more communication networks including but not limited to wi fi cellular networks or other ami radio connection through a hub universal serial bus usb port"}]</data>
</edge>
