  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200426198-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is formed in a hollow block shape of the concrete material the body portion having an inlet 11 and outlet 12 different in size from the front and rear a first filter plate member 2 made of a pitched concrete material installed in a plate shape at an inlet 11 of the body portion 1 a second filter plate member 3 made of water permeable concrete which is installed in a plate shape at an outlet 12 of the body portion 1 boundary block having a water quality purification function of the stream characterized in that consisting of a plurality of contact media 4 installed vertically in the interior of the front inlet 11 of the first filter plate portion 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100616387-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore the river water enters through the upstream end and enters the vegetation space portion 14 while rotating the rotary sieve 20 so that purification occurs at the root of the aquatic plant 40"}, {"pat_id": "US-4418549-A", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "as the temperature of the exiting air increases the curl of strips 60 increases to thus more and more block the flow of air between the top and bottom portions of exit pipe 24 to thus provide a fluid restriction and cause a longer transit and residence time to air passing through cold air exchanger 16 of the present system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4619819-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101494221-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the slope of the bottom surface 15 may have a downward slope in the longitudinal direction toward the downstream side of the stream or may have a downward slope in the transverse direction to one side of the stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562303-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 1221646 a base plate fixed to the bottom surface of a small stream a sensor housing fixed at an eccentric position on the base plate and having a cross sectional area of the inlet through which water is introduced is larger than the cross sectional area of the outlet through which water is discharged a water quality sensor installed on one side wall of the sensor housing to detect the quality of water passing through the sensor housing and a screen unit fixed to the circumference of the base plate to block the inflow of foreign substances other than water through the front rear left right and upper sides of the water quality sensor it is possible to monitor water quality by installing it in a place with a low water depth such as a small river a water quality monitoring device for a small stream has been proposed to improve the safety and durability of the water quality monitoring device by using a screen unit and a sensor housing to protect the water quality sensor in two layers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "US-4451277-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-4537615-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-11008737-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "hot air is blown across the ambient air stream 130 and circulated via an air blower 109 absorbing moisture from the ambient air stream and concentrating the humidity of the air in the first chamber 108"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210549-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the guide groove 111 is disposed to be spaced apart from each other the body portion 110 is installed across the river and integrally formed at both ends of the body portion 110 the floating material collected and collected floating material g g is a water barrier structure 100 having a collection box 120 having a space formed therein to be drawn out to the outside forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210549-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the main body 110 is a unit block made of concrete material which is installed in place of a huge dam in order to effectively use water resources in a small river and a plurality of units may be installed along the stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101400074-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "further the present invention has an effect of improving the safety of the entire system including a display unit for monitoring and displaying the oxidant concentration at each of a plurality of points in the main stream pipe.1 is a block diagram of a ballast water treatment system in accordance with an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-4351651-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "as the temperature of the exiting air increases the curl of strips 60 increases to thus more and more block the flow of air between the top and bottom portions of exit pipe 24 to thus provide a fluid restriction and cause a longer transit and residence time to air passing through cold air exchanger 16 of the present system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 an actuator housing for operating a water gate to one side and the other side of the foundation concrete a hydrologic actuator disposed inside the actuator housing an operating hinge connecting one side and the other side of the operating device a lower support pipe configured in the middle of the actuating hinge a front sluice plate disposed at an upper end of the lower support pipe a hydrostatically reinforced guide plate support disposed in a trapezoidal shape at an upper end of the front sluice plate a front stream water inlet control block installed between the hydrostatically reinforced guide plate support a lower support pipe configured at a lower end of the front river water inlet control block on the one side and the other side while adjusting the front stream water inlet control block up and dow