2320-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "with the siphon passage plate 20 is formed on the lower surface of the connection block 30 while preventing the siphon passage plate 20 connected to the connection block 30 from sagging toward the bottom of the river a plurality of stoppers 33 protruding from the lower end of the connecting rod 30 so as to generate the action of forming the low level water discharging passage 21 while being automatically raised by the weight of the connecting rod 30 the stream water passing through the siphon passage 21 generates a vortex action and an aeration action is generated so that the polluted river water is naturally cleaned and purified and at the same time the operation of the movable waterborne door plate 10 the siphon passage plate 20 is provided at the rear surface thereof with a sidewall of the siphon passage plate 20 so as to generate a gravity dispersion action that originally cuts off the action of trapped river water in the upper portion of the movable waterborne door plate 10 constitutes a horizontal vortical plate 38 and a vertical vortical plate 39 the automatic folding type siphon passage 21 and the automatic folding drainage backflow preventing plate 16 are automatically brought into close contact with the lower end portion of the base concrete 100 by their respective weights when the movable protection gate plate 10 is conducted the automatic folding type siphon passage 21 which functions to increase the cross section of the river during the flood and the river water flowing from the upstream of the river are discharged over the movable flood gate plate 10 and a function of the automatic folding drainage backflow prevention plate 16 which functions to push the sand gravels passing through the prevention plate 16 and stacked on the rear side stream of the movable water security door plate 10 to the downstream portion of the river using the moving water control system for purging it is recommended to discharge the clean