frame or by opening and closing by the weight 22 of the upper coupled to the hinge 14 to block the odor rising from the drain and to block the backflow sewage but backflow when the sewer bursts or pops out from a weak place when blocked it is often better to discharge back to the road than to block when the sewer overflows due to heavy rain so it is not always good to prevent backflow of sewage.the present invention has been devised to solve the problems caused by the deodorization and insect repellent device of the conventional sewer as described above is normally closed to not send the sewage to the river to prevent odors or pests coming out to flow the sewage into the river if the water level in the stream is lower than the sewage level the sewage on the road will flow to the river and the dregs can be caught on top of it preventing foreign matter from entering the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "9 the front water gate 40 is rotated by the water pressure generated by the elevated water level and is interlocked with the angle adjuster 53 of the good interlocking portion 50 the link section 60 is interlocked and the rotating plate 30 is rotated to reduce the outflow cross section of the grating 20 to block the inflow of rainwater into the fine powder chamber 2 so that a large amount of rainwater naturally flows out into the discharge stream soils inherent in stormwater are also naturally released into the discharge stream thereby blocking the introduction of the soil from the storm sewer thereby preventing the sediment from accumulating on the sewer sewer pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101736967-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in the ecological restoration scenario the treated water sewage treated by the sewage treatment unit and the water taken a first scenario in which the obtained integer is used as a treatment water for ecological restoration a second scenario in which the wastewater treatment water having improved water quality within a certain range by the sewage treatment section and the water harvested by the intake treatment section are used as the treatment water for ecological restoration a third scenario in which the treated water sewage treated by the sewage treatment unit and the withdrawal constant whose water quality is improved within a certain range by the intake treatment unit are used as the ecological restoration treatment water and a fourth scenario in which sewage treatment water having improved water quality within a certain range by the sewage treatment section and water intake water having improved water quality within a certain range by the intake treatment section are used as the treatment water for ecological restoration .as described above the present invention maximizes the restoration effect of the ecosystem to be restored improves the habitat environment of the ecosystem in the water space it can be expected to have an effect of efficiently managing the water space in ecological and environmentally friendly manner.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "additionally the filtered seawater may be provided to treatment block 260 wherein a variable speed high pressure pump 212 pushes the filtered seawater through to membrane 214 whereby a concentrate is created on the high pressure side of the membrane 214 and a permeate stream is created on the low pressure side of the membrane 214"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "by controlling the pump 212 that pumps water into the membrane block 214 and or a concentrate line valve 223 thereby changing the quality of the outputted permeate stream for subsequent batches of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "additionally this process may continue for as many treatment blocks 260 as there are in the treatment system 200 until a final permeate stream optionally having untreated filtered seawater water blended therein is produced from a final membrane pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_146", "text": "9 seawater treatment system 900 may include a treatment block 960 that may process and treat water from a water intake system 901 and produce a permeate stream and a concentrate stream or multiple streams"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_147", "text": "for example in one or more embodiments water taken in by the water intake system 901 may be treated in the treatment block 960 to produce a product water stream having a specific salinity and or hardness"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_147", "text": "as shown the product stream may be discharged from the treatment block 960 into a blending point or an injection water reservoir 992"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_150", "text": "subsequently the water intake system 901 and the treatment block 960 may be controlled or manipulated and the quantity and quality of water taken into the treatment block 960 and discharged from the treatment block 960 as the product stream into the injection water reservoir 992 may be controlled"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_152", "text": "subsequently calculations may be made in view of the information about the produced water obtained by the sensors 993a 993b and the water intake system 901 and treatment block 960 may react or be controlled or manipulated to produce water in the product stream in a specific quantity and water quality such that combining the product stream with the produced water in the injection water reservoir 992 results in a dischargeable water stream of a predetermined water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102418387-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is common to block the bicycle paths trails and trails with a lid so as not to cause harm or discomfort to users using the trails"}, {"pat_id": "US-10464021-B2", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "the one or more sensors 160 can be configured to the presence absence or concentration of one or more markers in the feed stream 112 the feed concentrate 116 the draw stream 122 the diluted draw stream 126 or the ro permeate 156 via one or more of uv visible spectroscopy fluorimetry conductivity or a fluoride selective electrode probe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434028-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition it is possible to suppress the load and delay that may occur according to the operation change of the management means for such verification and to optimize the installation and operation state through an active response to the external environment.the present invention provides a water pipe connection system of a prefabricated water intake tower for water intake and a method for installing the same comprising the steps of manufacturing a water pipe connection system the manufactured water pipe connection system is inspected at the inspection site and the water pipe connection system is installed at the installation site wherein the water pipe connection system is managed by monitoring facilities disposed at the inspection site and the installation site respectively the handling situation of the water pipe connection system and the surrounding environment the water pipe connection system includes an excavation hole 10 penetrating in an up stream direction at a predetermined position of the dam body 100 installed to block and confine water a water intake pipe connection system of a prefabricated water intake tower for water intake including a discharge pipe 20 having one end connected to the lower part of the water intake tower body 200 built in a prefabricated manner in the water in the reservoir and the other end extending toward the excavation hole 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 in the water blocking device of the buoyancy type clapboard block to prevent flooding and overburden of rivers including the flexible water blocking plate 80 made of the member 90 is installed the floating matter removal module 100 for removing the floating matter floating in the river when the water barrier block 60 is raised and lowered includes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by the center of gravity 140 to move toward the hinge shaft 125 125a of the opening and closing cover 121 121a by rotating upward to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the crate 10 in the dry stream when the rainwater does not flow in the waterways while stably catching foreign substances mixed in the rainwater opening and closing cover 121 121a by the weight 140 to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10 to prevent foreign substances such as cigarette butts or vinyl to enter the drain 1 in addition the uneven protrusions 112 and 113 of the body 110 and the uneven protrusions 124 and 124a of the opening and closing cover 121 and 121a are inserted into the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101773568-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in the ecological restoration scenario the treated water sewage treated by the sewage treatment unit and the water taken a first scenario in which the obtained integer is used as a treatment water for ecological restoration a second scenario in which the wastewater treatment water having improved water quality within a certain range by the sewage treatment section and the water harvested by the intake treatment section are used as the treatment water for ecological restoration a third scenario in which the treated water sewage treated by the sewage treatment unit and the withdrawal constant whose water quality is improved within a certain range by the intake treatment unit are used as the ecological restoration treatment water and a fourth scenario in which sewage treatment water having improved water quality within a certain range by the sewage treatment section and water intake water having improved water quality within a certain range by the intake treatment section are used as the treatment water for ecological restoration .as described above the present invention maximizes the restoration effect of the ecosystem to be restored improves the habitat environment of the ecosystem in the water space it can be expected to have an effect of efficiently managing the water space in ecological and environmentally friendly manner.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101591318-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the water rich stream 9 exiting the phase separator 8 as an effluent is also cooled with a heat exchanger 11 to cause the residual solute to re dissolve and produce a single phase cooled water rich stream 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101591318-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "the water rich stream 222 exiting the phase separator 218 as the effluent is cooled with the water rich heat exchanger 210 to cause the residual solute to re dissolve and produce a single phase cooled water rich stream 226"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage outlet odor prevention device to guide the stream while opening a box frame 10 installed at an end of the sewage pipe 1 at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber 3 and seated on an outer circumference of the opened sewage discharge port 2 a primary blocking door 20 connected to the upper hinge part 11 at the upper end of the box frame 10 to block the sewage discharge port 2 to block odor a plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 which are connected to the primary blocking door 20 and block odor while being opened and closed according to water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced during rain hinge connecting portion 40 for opening and closing the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 in accordance with the water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced in rainy weather by being connected to the upper side of the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30"}, {"pat_id": "US-10494284-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "2 system when a user opens the faucet to collect purified water the stored water is pumped by a feed pump through the carbon block filters and subsequently through the reverse osmosis ro membranes and thereby dispensed on demand"}, {"pat_id": "US-6420185-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "on line monitoring can then begin by shifting the four way selector valve 182 to block the flow of the zero stream 184 and allow the flow of concentrate stream 116 to the analyzer 122 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101921821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 to the sewage water collection line 2 and discharges a large amount of rainwater flowing into the continuous rainwater to the river smoothly a rectangular outer frame 10 which is formed in a box shape to be seated on an upper portion of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 to block malodors and opens to the front and rear to guide sewage an inner frame 20 detachably attached to the inside of the outer frame 10 by a drawer a wall like opening closing gate 30 connected to the upper side of the inner frame 20 by a hinge portion 31 so as to be opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced the sewage water supply system according to the present invention is characterized in that the sewage water supply pipe 2 is connected to the opening closing water gate 30 40 the flow rate regulator 40 includes a center shaft 41a at the lower end of the inner frame 20 and is rotated upward and downward to adjust the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while guiding the soil contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate center shaft 41a of the rotary plate 41 so that the rotary plate 41 and a link portion 42 for rotating the link member in a non the upper portion of the link portion 42 is engaged with the first link pin 42a at the upper end of the upper side of the interchange gate 30 and the lower end of the link portion 42 is inserted when the interchange gate 30 is opened by inserting the second link pin 42b an upper link 42c for transmitting the rotational force to the lower link 42e and a sliding hole 42d having an elongated shape for sliding the second link pin 42b of the upper link 42c on the upper side and a lower link 42e whose lower side is coupled to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 41a of the rotary plate 41 and is coupled together with the upper link 42c so that the opening and closing gate 30 is opened and the rotating plate 41 is rotated in synchronization with the rotating force generated when the rotating plate 41 is rotated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit an inflow tank through which rainwater flows from the transport pipe member a filtering part installed in the inflow tank and the rainwater flowing upward from the lower part and filtered by the fluidized bed filter medium and it is installed on the upper portion of the filtration unit and includes a back washing unit for back washing the fluidized bed medium the filter unit includes an upper filter net and a lower filter net installed between the fluidized bed media and an upper portion of the lower filter net is provided with an air inlet to disturb the fluidized media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit a precipitation tank into which rainwater flows from the transfer pipe member a filtration tank communicating with an upper portion of the precipitation tank to receive rainwater from the precipitation tank a dewatering plate fixed to the inner wall of the lower portion of the filtration tank in a horizontal direction a fluidized bed medium loaded on the dewatering plate to filter rainwater a buoyancy weight plate installed in the horizontal direction on the fluidized bed upper part and lowered by buoyancy according to the water level and compressing and dehydrating the fluidized bed medium by the weight when lowered a washing nozzle installed on the buoyancy weight plate to wash the fluidized bed media a washing water storage tank connected to the filtered water discharge valve installed at the lower portion of the filtration tank to store rainwater and supply supernatant water to the storage unit and a pump for supplying rainwater stored in the wash water reservoir to the wash nozzle stream type water flow circulation system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method according to claim 1 or 2 the permeable sidewalk block unit each box shaped reservoir formed in the box shape is connected to each other to be installed on the ground and to form an excellent storage space therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "induce the rainwater guided to the ground is conveyed through the conveying pipe member filtering rainwater conveyed through the conveying pipe member through a filtration unit storing the filtered rainwater in a storage tank pumping the stored rainwater through at least one of river water maintenance water irrigation canal water vegetation water around the river and waterfront park landscaping fountain supplying the necessary power to the filtration unit and the pumping means by at least one of a photovoltaic device or a wind turbine wherein a portion of the rainwater is permeable in the step of inducing rainwater through the permeable sidewalk block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "1 and 2 the stream water flow circulation system according to the present invention is a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river the permeable walkway block unit 100 forming a walkway for pedestrians to pass through an irrigation canal 101 installed in parallel with the water permeable sidewalk block unit 100 and having a communication path 101a capable of receiving rainwater from the water permeable sidewalk block unit 100 a conveying pipe member 200 for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit 100 a filtration unit 300 for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path 101a of the irrigation canal 101 and the transfer pipe member 200 and embedding it under the ground a storage unit 400 provided to receive and receive the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit 300 and pumping means 500 for supplying water from the storage unit 400 upstream of the stream or irrigation canal 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "as will be described below the permeable sidewalk block unit 100 may be configured alone without the permeable block member 120 and is intended to be expressed in terms of this"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "para_204", "text": "in addition the storage of rainwater in the storage tank secures the amount of storage during the feng shui season and can also be utilized as the maintenance water for river maintenance or irrigation during the dry season thereby increasing the water resource circulation rate and maintaining the river ecological environment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "pumped and transported to the sludge dehydrator 50 using a pump and when the transportation is completed open the closed blocking gate 23 and close the blocking gate 23 on the top of the other sedimentation tank to prevent the inflow of river water pumping and transporting the sludge dewatering device 50 and then dewatering and purifying the moisture contained in the journey is discharged back to the reservoir 11 characterized in that the stream water purification by sedimentation and dredging"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the present invention by installing a sedimentation basin is divided into a predetermined size in the sewer and coriander site sedimented pollutants and sludge flowing along the stream to block the flow of the stream compartmentally and then easily sediment first to protect the water quality of rivers and lakes second to prevent the destruction of aquatic ecosystems due to the inflow of soils and sands third to prevent aesthetic and sanitary defects due to sedimentation of soil and journey during rainfall and flooding fourthly the dredging operation is very effective and economical compared to the existing method is to provide a stream water purification apparatus by precipitation and dredging and its method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object to form a coriander site on both sides of the sewer and formed in the central longitudinal direction to form embankment on both sides of the coriander site to let the river water flowing through the river flows through the stream in the river the sewer and coriander site has a block size to the river flow inflow to the side of the river inflow to the side of the river flows into a predetermined size so as not to affect the water flow capacity of the river so that the dredging of the journey to facilitate a housing having a bottom surface on which river water is discharged and having a plurality of sedimentation tanks divided by a sedimentation basin divider in a direction parallel to the reservoir in the center of the sedimentation basin so as to control the river water during the dredging operation a front end of the enclosure that is a sedimentation inlet flow path with a head protruding from the center connected to the sedimentation basin divider having a jaw and a groove at the bottom and an upper rod hook groove at the top the prefabricated movable blocking gate installed in the blocking gate installation unit is achieved by installing a sedimentation basin consisting of several prefabricated clasp plates that are miniaturized for easy transportation and an upper hook rod to support the prefabricated clasp plates"}, {"pat_id": "US-10294654-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a mounting bracket for attaching the bar screen to the at least one wall or at least one inlet pipe below a mouth of the at least one inlet pipe so as to catch and remove unwanted debris from an incoming stream of fluid including debris wherein the mounting bracket includes at least one block and at least one bar extending out from the at least one block the at least one block providing alignment and mounting for the bar screen wherein the bar screen and the mounting bracket has a quick connect disconnect configuration to couple them together"}, {"pat_id": "US-10294654-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a mounting bracket attaching the screen basket to at least one wall or the at least one inlet pipe below a mouth of the at least one inlet pipe so as to catch and remove unwanted debris from an incoming stream of fluid including debris wherein the mounting bracket includes at least one mounting block wherein the screen basket and mounting bracket includes a quick connect disconnect configuration for mounting the screen basket to the mounting bracket and the at least one mounting block extending longitudinal along a center axis of the at least one inlet pipe and outward laterally relative to the mounting bracket perpendicular to the center axis of the at least one inlet pipe"}]</data>
