  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100757461-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in general the wastewater and sewage discharged from the home to the stream are purified through the wastewater treatment device to clean up the wastewater and sewage and then discharged to the river to prevent contamination of the stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "para_602", "text": "contaminated stream water which has a small specific gravity in addition to the outlet of the sluice is placed in a state where it is absolutely impossible to move to the downstream of the river due to the material pushing action and the material bundling action"}, {"pat_id": "US-4787980-A", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "controlling contamination in the sampling lines or piping because intermittent sluffing of contaminants will change the characteristic and quality of the water arriving at the multiplexer analytical instruments and or points of use"}, {"pat_id": "US-8852437-B2", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "although the disinfectant d is primarily added for condition control and its reduction of concentration is measured the disinfecting effect of the added disinfectant can be additionally utilized to continue the production cycle in case of an only minimal contamination in the product stream for example if a minor error has occurred at an individual membrane or only possibly existing weak growth has been entrained"}, {"pat_id": "US-8852437-B2", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "this is because a rough change means a significant membrane fracture or module error or else a detachment of a nest of microorganisms or germs up to then not detectable and requires immediate counter measures"}, {"pat_id": "US-9493370-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "due to the unpredictable nature of these variables there may be a considerable time lag between introduction of treatment chemicals into the wastewater stream and acceptable effluent contamination levels at the outlet of the daf"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224234-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "according to the initial rainwater storage system using the storage tank of the present invention the sewage and the initial rainwater on the sewage that is installed in a number of small rivers at a certain distance is collected and collected but the sewage is directly directed to the sewage terminal treatment plant through the sewer drainage rainwater is collected in the storage tanks buried in the main stream of the main stream and discharged for a long time below the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant after rainy weather to prevent contamination of small rivers and main streams and there is no need to add more facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224234-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "as shown in figures 1 to 6 the present invention provides a settling basin 82 and the settling chamber 50 to prevent soil from entering the interior of the storage tank 30 while a certain distance to the small river 60 selected and collected sewage and initial excellent on the sewage 80 installed a number of sewage the sewage is directed directly to the sewage end treatment plant through the drainage house the initial excellent is buried in the sewage site 72 of the main stream 70 it collects in the old storage tank 30 and discharges it for a long time below the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant after rainy weather and prevents contamination of small rivers and mainstream streams 70 and adds sewage end treatment facilities"}, {"pat_id": "US-12012339-B2", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "temperatures in the main circulation stream 106 can range from 150 to 300 degrees fahrenheit which is sufficient to destroy all pathogens that were introduced into the system 1 via the biologically contamination water stream 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134148-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in order to prevent soil contamination the bottom of the pond is installed with a pe water repellent film and the boundary baffle of each filtration tank is interwoven with wood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102088362-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the upper sprinkling method of the inlet chute 51 has a problem that it is difficult to fully utilize the water spraying effect such as the effect of directly piercing the dewatering hole 521 and the separation effect of the fine sludge and the heat utilization is lowered even when heated hot water is used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101577939-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 2007 0083441the present invention solves these problems of conventional methods and simultaneously cleanses polluted river water generated from a point pollution source and a nonpoint pollution source more efficiently by using natural forces and at the same time it is an object of the present inventionin the present invention in order to prevent the river water stored in the drought season automatically from running out the width of the siphon passage formed inside the movable waterproof door is wide the middle is slightly bent and the upper part is wide the water stream that is stored in the iron is prevented from escaping thereby forming a low level water discharge passage in which the fishing rod is naturally formed at the same time as the fishing rod so that the sea water is formed naturally so as to discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101896514-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional disinfecting apparatus for disinfecting the vehicle has a disadvantage that the disinfectant flowing down after disinfection of the vehicle flows into the stream indiscriminately and becomes a main cause of environmental pollution.the present invention has been made to solve the above problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a freezing prevention tank having a heater for heating a heating medium between chemical tanks to prevent freezing of the mixed disinfectant and the waste water treatment means for purifying the waste water after disinfection and discharging the waste water to collect the wastewater and purifying the wastewater to prevent water contamination in advance and a wastewater treatment unit for uniformly generating the concentration of the mixed disinfectant by providing an aeration unit for mixing the disinfectant and the water to breathe a disinfection heat ray into the lower part of the ice disinfecting system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100729863-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the present invention relates to a sludge removal and sewage treatment apparatus and method of the dredged soil and in particular the sediment and sediment deposited on the bottom of the river or reservoir using a dredger or pumpable device without draining the water of the stream or reservoir inhalation separation and purification of pollutants it is possible to carry out work while preserving and to selectively dredge only the parts that require dredging and to perform dredging to separate the gravel or sand contained in dredging soil for recycling purposes and to clean the stream the present invention relates to a sludge removal and sewage water treatment apparatus and method for dredged soil which can be re introduced into a reservoir or reservoir to prevent secondary contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173850-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "according to the present invention in treating livestock waste water the solid matter and the urine waste water are separated and the solid matter is effective to be recycled as an organic fertilizer and the urine waste water as water is disinfected to prevent contamination of the stream and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "para_252", "text": "however if the water is confined by using the top discharge type water storage method such as the conduction type water gate and the rubber dam the particles of the incompletely decomposed materials in the course of the material friction action are separated from the viscous force contained in the fine particles water quality contamination of river water becomes more and more intense due to the material combination between pollutant molecules and clean water molecules due to the viscous force and magnetic force contained in the fine particles this is because the specific gravity of the stream water becomes heavier than the specific gravity of the water molecules through the process of continuously generating the material binding actions which further increases the pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in this process when the clogging phenomenon is confirmed in the filter medium 140 the contamination adhered to the filter medium 140 is removed by supplying the compressed air through the air blowing pipe 144 thereby improving the filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032253-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in general wastewater and sewage generated in industrial facilities or homes are purified by a wastewater treatment device and discharged into the river to prevent contamination of the stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6241510-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "furthermore the present invention creates a vacuum inside the filter and at the same time creates a vacuum break to prevent the filter body from being damaged and by mixing air into the conventional sand sand fluidization technology using a water stream the filter sand is turbulent and the filter sand is separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102089609-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "natural purification may be performed in the course of the process of separating and discharging high contamination water but by installing the purification tank 190 in the inlet 120 as described above the water separated and discharged from the complementary upper stream is described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042731-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "it is installed to provide a water intake space therein the water reservoir body to separate and receive only the groundwater flows through the bottom of the stream filtered water without interfering with the contamination of the external surface water a well lid body for sealing an open upper surface of the well body to separate and block the inside of the well body from the air layer on the water surface it is installed inside the well body and the upper surface is inserted deeper than the bottom of the well body main body across the sand gravel layer of the river bottom in a state spaced apart from the well cover body the groundwater is a water intake pipe in which a plurality of fine water intake holes are formed on the lower side thereof so that the water can be taken into the water intake space inside the main body one end extends to the center of the intake space through the well cover body and the other end is installed to protrude to the top of the well cover body and discharges the groundwater taken into the intake space through the intake pipe to the water supply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the spring engaging groove 440 is coupled to one side of the wear plate driving spring 300 the wear plate operating spring 600 when the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater is small or there is no inflow of sewage and stormwater the weir plate 200 is rotated at an angle of inclination at all times at least one side of the wear plate 200 and one side and the other side of the sewage line 10 are formed on the left side and the right side of the center of the wear plate 200 so as to be rotated by the elastic force of the wear plate 600 respectively the pressure of the sewage and the storm that the wear plate 200 is rotated is adjusted by using the wear plate driving spring 300 and the driving spring adjusting nut 400 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be rotated or fixed when the inflow amount of the sewage and the storm is small it is possible to block and minimize the inflow of sewage and to prevent the inflow of sewage and stormwater by effectively opening and closing the ware plate 200 to prevent the contamination of the stream and the upper surface of the wear plate 200 is configured to be wider than the lower surface of the lower surface of the wear plate 200 when the wear plate 200 is rotated due to inflow of sewage and storm and the sewage and stormwater are completely prevented from flowing into the sewage pipe 10 by the upper surface and the frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9409110-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "1 as 130a 130b and 130c are operable to send and receive signals from the controller not shown to initiate flow of the process stream through side stream inlet 122 as fluid in the process stream is pumped through the cooling system by pump 126"}, {"pat_id": "US-4144722-A", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "depending upon the contamination of the atmosphere or environment under which the air conditioning system must operate it may be desirable to include in the system a further filtering arrangement such as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101285813-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "provided a cause of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741836-B1", "para_id": "para_290", "text": "however if the water is confined by using the top discharge type water storage method such as the conduction type water gate and the rubber dam the particles of the incompletely decomposed materials in the course of the material friction action are separated from the viscous force contained in the fine particles water quality contamination of river water becomes more and more intense due to the material combination between pollutant molecules and clean water molecules due to the viscous force and magnetic force contained in the fine particles this is because the specific gravity of the stream water becomes heavier than the specific gravity of the water molecules through the process of continuously generating the material binding actions which further increases the pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "economic losses to construct sewage terminal treatment plant can be saved.the stream runoff procurement apparatus and method thereof according to the present invention always allow a certain amount of streams to flow through the river to survive the ecosystem of the stream and furthermore the contamination of the pipeline is prevented in advance so that the groundwater due to the corrosion and breakage of the sewer pipe is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the sewage stored in the at least one cso storage tank 102 may be discharged directly to the discharge stream 105 through the discharge unit 140 if the concentrated heavy rain is discharged sewage amount at this time the discharge unit 140 further includes an initial excellent water treatment unit 145 for preventing discharge of wastes swept away by rainwater into the stream thereby preventing csos that is untreated sewage from contaminating the river by preventing minimum river contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "in addition the sewage stored in the at least one cso storage tank 102 may be discharged directly to the discharge stream 105 through the discharge unit 140 if the concentrated heavy rain is discharged sewage amount at this time the discharge unit 140 further includes an initial excellent water treatment unit 145 for preventing discharge of wastes swept away by rainwater into the streams thereby preventing csos that is untreated sewage and contaminating the rivers by preventing minimum river contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067632-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "of the reservoir or river prevents turbid water diffusion that prevents contamination of the reservoir or stream so that it is economically appropriately blocked before it spreads inward so that only clean water from which the soil and contaminants have been removed from the turbid water flows into the reservoir or stream to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-11407653-B2", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "this sensor can indicate possible contamination via bacteria colonies that have greater potential to be present in water with higher levels of turbidity or indicate other potential contaminants ranging from lead to various ions e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100532247-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "that is as the air is supplied to the water side of the river through the air nozzle 610 of the air supply means foreign matter to sink in the river is floated to the water side which can easily remove the float and prevent contamination of the river by the foreign matter"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2196438-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "method for the contamination dependent dynamic adjustment of the nitrification and denitrification phases in further biological waste water treatment in a main stream process by contamination dependent control for a cascade like basin arrangement with upstream denitrification with at least one continuously operating nitrification zone using at least one ventilation device wherein the oxygen input of the ventilation device is depending on contamination selectively supplied to individual basins or basin sections by real time evaluation of procedural and energetically relevant parameters and thus an intermittent operation of individual basins or basin sections in alternation is achieved characterized in that the oxygen input at least of one continuously running ventilation device preferably a turbo blower is supplied to individual basins or basin sections by a control unit using fuzzy pattern technology on the basis of the parameter characteristics classifiers"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "to limit contamination of the receiving flows and streams by untreated combined sewage the diverted flow may enter the receiving stream by direct overflow only when the soil percentage of the water to be discharged has been reduced to a level such that there is no further risk of appreciable contamination of the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the sedimentation paper 400 is provided with a path of at least several hundred meters or more and is formed in the form of a stream using a terrain thereby minimizing contamination"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0549733-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "teflon causes mechanical degradation with the degradation by products many of which being too small to filter with state of the art filtration equipment entering the chemical process stream further the rapid action of the pump usually greater than 60 cycle per minute creates massive impulse in the system with a resulting pulsed flow which forces particles through filters thus rendering the filters ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "US-5730879-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a process for conditioning recirculating evaporative cooling water in a cooling system of the type including a source of make up water an evaporative cooling unit and a heat exchanger piped together in a circulating line and including a makeup water line and a bleedoff line said process being useful to reduce the amount of make up water required during the operation of the system and to prevent essentially scale corrosion and micro biological contamination said process comprising determining the ph of saturation of the recirculated evaporative cooling water in the cooling water system passing a controlled volume of the recirculated evaporative cooling water through a strong cation exchange media positioned in a side stream from said circulating line in an amount sufficient to maintain the ph of the recirculated evaporative cooling water within a positive 0.4 above and a negative 0.4 below the ph of saturation monitoring the corrosion potential to provide a measurement which determines an amount of corrosion inhibitor to be added adding a corrosion inhibiter to the cooling water in response to the measurement obtained by monitoring the corrosion potential of this cooling water monitoring the oxidizing chemical levels in the circulating line to provide a measurement which determines the activation of a generator to produce a controlled level of oxidizing agents and generating oxidizing agents in the cooling water in response to the measurement obtained by monitoring the oxidizing chemical levels of the cooling water in the circulating line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042852-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "therefore if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the pollution is further increased by the material decomposition and material binding action so that the water stored in the reservoir always maintains the full water level while the water that flows upstream from the upstream frequent discharge through the phone is the best way to prevent the contamination of the river water and also by using the method of discharging the water in the reservoir through the cyphon constituted in the sluice the substances contained in the water are combined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042852-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "actions increase water contamination but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200422043-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "it is possible to carry out work while preserving and to selectively dredge only the parts that require dredging and to perform dredging to separate the gravel or sand contained in dredging soil for recycling purposes and to clean the stream the present invention relates to a sludge removal and sewage water treatment device of dredged soil which can be re introduced into a reservoir or reservoir to prevent secondary contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the first object of the present invention due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rain the initial rainwater that has not been purified to exceed the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage terminal treatment plant is discharged to the stream it is to provide an initial excellent storage processing system using a storage tank to prevent the contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102224305-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore the contamination detection sensor 50 is configured to sense all or part of the factor and continuously transmits real time sensing information for each factor or when a value equal to or greater than a threshold set for a specific factor is sensed the corresponding sensing information it can be configured to send out only"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102224305-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "the management unit 150 may set an opening time of the on off valve 40 and an opening closing control period of the on off valve 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102224305-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "the system 100 of the present invention uses a siphon principle to circulate water while discharging water and sludge from the compensation stream to the downstream but it is also significant in separating and discharging the water in a specific section with high contamination in the compensation stream before diffusion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101489530-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "this river is equipped with a sensor to measure the electrical conductivity of water to determine the degree of contamination of the flowing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_307", "text": "actions increase water contamination but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-6420185-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the silica standard stream 174 is thus continuously added into the feed stream 144 having a known flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-6420185-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "zero contamination level water to qualify the analyzer 122 because it is cleaner than the upw being tested"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377605-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention has an advantageous effect of enabling a quick response by directly detecting the contamination leakage by a sensor directly installed in the field.1 is a diagram showing a state in which in the water treatment instrumentation control system for a smart city of the present invention a pair of sensors for water quality inspection are installed at regular intervals symmetrically left and right at the edges of a tributary p and a main stream m"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604863-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "alternatively sensors can be placed upstream to detect the level of contamination of the wastewater stream before it enters the confined chamber and the processor can predictively determine the correct number of cycles needed to treat the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102207359-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "water plants pumped by the high pressure dredging pump 52 are filtered and discharged to the original stream after being quickly removed or if the risk of contamination is predicted due to turbidity or high bod it is preferable to send it to the coagulation tank of the plant to purify the original stream and then send it to the original stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-8262914-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "due to the unpredictable nature of these variables there may be a considerable time lag between introduction of treatment chemicals into the wastewater stream and acceptable effluent contamination levels at the outlet of the daf"}]</data>
