e material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which a lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "US-4969393-A", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the entire sidewall of the bellows 23 may but need not be deformable as long as the deformability of the bellows suffices to ensure that the upper portion 23a can close the switch 24 when warranted in view of the condition of the supply 33 of softening agent therein"}, {"pat_id": "US-8430115-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the water source 7 may be anything that is able to supply a steady stream of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10358363-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "wastewater means water from a manufacturing process municipal waste or other waters which are required to be treated prior to discharge to a receiving stream lake or other water way"}, {"pat_id": "US-4823826-A", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "stinger 4 is in sealing relationship with elbow 20 to prevent leakage of water from pipeline 2"}, {"pat_id": "US-6998054-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "if the user is inclined to destroy the ammonium on site the column can be regenerated with hydrochloric acid and the regenerant waste treated in an electrolytric chamber under the influence of dc current to change the chlorides to hypochlorite which then reacts with the ammonia to eventually convert it to nitrogen gas through the mono di and tri chloramine reaction process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101562757-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "it is possible to provide a non point pollution abatement facility capable of preventing the discharge water pump from being damaged due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0063236-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "while one partial stream x flows into the bottom trough 5 arranged below the reaction column 7 through an inflow tube 17 the other partial stream y is first fed through an inflow tube 18 penetrating the outer wall 8 into the cathode trough 1"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the o ring 170 is configured to inhibit leakage of a condensate stream e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101740507-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "patent document 2 discloses a conventional oral washing machine valve that controls the amount of oral wash water flowing in the mouth washer and controls the flow of oral wash water when not in use the water flow control unit and the spray nozzle for spraying the thin and strong water stream are performed so as to prevent the splashing of the spray nozzle by the water pressure during use of the mouth washer and to prevent leakage phenomenon by installing double sealing member for preventing water leakage the present invention relates to a mouth washer"}, {"pat_id": "US-5938900-A", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "rubber seal 404 meshes with the slot to preclude water leakage from the housing 104"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102595204-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an air treatment device includes an air flow generator arranged to produce an air flow through the air treatment device a moisture or water vapor source arranged to introduce water vapor into the air stream a body surrounding both the air flow generator and the moisture source when in use and providing water to the moisture source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377605-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention has an advantageous effect of enabling a quick response by directly detecting the contamination leakage by a sensor directly installed in the field.1 is a diagram showing a state in which in the water treatment instrumentation control system for a smart city of the present invention a pair of sensors for water quality inspection are installed at regular intervals symmetrically left and right at the edges of a tributary p and a main stream m"}]</data>
