  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "after installing foundation concrete 800 at one end of a cross section structure of a river or stream and constructing a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 on the upper end of the foundation concrete 800 an inflow pipe 1110 and a lower discharge pipe 1120 are connected to discharge water stored in the lower end of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 and an inflow control valve 1170 is connected to adjust the inflow amount and an upper and lower raising and lowering device 5810 is connected to adjust the pipe in the upper and lower direction according to the inflow level of river water that changes frequently and a rising discharge pipe 101 a falling discharge pipe 103 a right angled falling pipe 202 a water storage tank 201 a discharge amount control unit 203 a right angled falling pipe 202 and in a method of producing electricity by using the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 equipped with a power generation unit 33 a structure in which a water storage tank 8000 and a water purification promotion storage tank 11111 are constructed by dredging to a depth 20 to 600 times deeper than the surface 9000 of the soil layer constituting a river or stream and then the foundation concrete 800 is poured on the surface 9000 constituting a river or stream and the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 are constructed on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 and the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 is constructed to store river water on the upper part of the foundation concrete 800 the inflow pipe 1110 and the lower discharge pipe 1120 a structure in which an intermediate storage water inflow line 501 is formed to pump the stored water stored inside the upstream side of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 toward the rear side starting from the internal ground surface 9000 in the upstream direction of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 penetrating the middle part of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 to the rear part a structure in which a lower movement line 1919 is connected to the end of the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 to move the power generation water introduced through the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 downward a structure in which an entrance 1332 used for inspecting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224234-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 1 the storage tank 30 is formed with a discharge port 31 for discharging the initial excellent water the manual water gate 40 is separately managed and installed to be gradually inclined in the water running direction to increase the storage capacity of the storage tank 30 in order to connect the third connecting pipe 32 to the secondary collector pipe 71 the water gate installation pipe 35 in communication with the outlet 31 is further extended the sluice installation conduit 35 is further formed with a guide groove 311 to slidably engage the manual hydrogate 40 for cracking the initial excellent of the storage tank 30 the manual water gate 40 is slidingly coupled to the guide groove 311 the initial use using the storage tank is lifted and opened by the lifting lever 45 exposed to the cilantro site 72 of the main stream 70 excellent storage handling system"}, {"pat_id": "US-5306397-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "this is compensated by an automatically controlled pumping off of the brine with the lifting pump for the brine 13 and by subsequent refilling of the evaporation chamber 5 with new de aerated seawater via the tube 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101983371-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "at the same time the tree branches it is a natural friendly environment that cleans polluted river water by creating a large artificial rain farm for artificial rainwater storage which is composed of large scale rainwater reservoirs which acts to prevent the pollution of the river environment by pulverizing the quality and garbage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_172", "text": "as described above the manhole having a multi structure according to the present invention when the sewage contaminated into the rainwater inlet space or the initial rainwater is usually introduced through the lifting floating means provided in the manhole this is discharged into the sewage inlet space which is purified at the sewage treatment plant and discharged to the stream to prevent the pollution of the stream.when clean rainwater flows into the rainwater inlet space it passes through the storm drain and discharges into the stream to protect the river ecosystem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102751616-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the above wheel frame is connected by a lifting member so that the underwater position can be adjusted it is formed at the open end of the above bucket body and includes a flange shaped edge portion that can be supported by the above turnover bar the above flange shaped rim portion is formed so that the turnover bar can be supported in contact with the flange shaped rim portion and the bucket body to prevent the bucket module that has passed the top dead center from being reversely rotated due to a reverse load generated from the water flow generating portion"}, {"pat_id": "US-12157091-B2", "para_id": "para_236", "text": "the method comprises providing a pressure retarded osmosis pro module comprising 1 an enclosure comprising a semi permeable membrane with a first side and a second side opposite the first side with foulant located on at least the second side 2 a raw saline solution having an osmotic pressure por at a gauge pressure pgr for entering the first side of the semi permeable membrane and 3 a fluid stream having a gauge pressure pgp and an osmotic pressure pop for entering the second side of the semi permeable membrane and periodically changing the balance of pressures from functioning as the pro to functioning as reverse osmosis ro by creating a net driving pressure that is opposite to the pro thereby inducing the ro process to create backward flow towards the second side of the semi permeable membrane thereby lifting the foulant and enhancing evacuation of the foulant"}, {"pat_id": "US-9873069-B2", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "1 the wastewater via the intake 1 has streamed through the separating screen 6 and reaches the bulky material free region 3b as well as the connection line 4 and finally the pump 5 now a reversal of the flow path such as is highlighted by the arrows for the flow of the wastewater which are indicated in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781790-B1", "para_id": "para_99", "text": "at this time the earth and sand mixed with rainwater can be easily removed while piled up inside the overflow prevention jaw 112 and the clear rainwater overflowing the overflow prevention jaw 112 is a stream through the discharge portion 13 of the combined sewer pipe 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960002267-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to circulate and purify the water in the water tank through the lifting tank while ozone is dropped into the air stream and the air flow flows upward from the bottom of the tank for lifting the water in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741836-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the multifunctional movable guard gate which is constructed to dredge the river and to be driven by the fixed support and actuator cylinders is combined with the foundation concrete to be combined with the side wall to save the river ecosystem and at the same time in the eco friendly construction method which combines the integrated control system and the remote control system that operate the opening and closing operations in a comprehensive manner to purify polluted river water while reviving the river ecosystem after dredging the entire width of the stream the foundation of the river is provided with foundation concrete an exponential wall body is formed on one side and the other side surface of the foundation concrete and an elevating guide wall is formed on an end surface of the exponential wall so as to project laterally the upper and lower operation guides for vertically moving up or down the multi purpose movable function gate are coupled to the elevating guide wall in a u shape a lower end of the cylinder rod is coupled to an upper end of the lifting guide wall the cylinder rod is mechanically coupled to the upper and lower operation cylinders the upper and lower operating cylinders are fixedly engaged with a cylinder support which serves to act as a support when the upper and lower operation guides are operated up and down a fixed support for fixing the artificial multi function movable security gate is fixedly connected to one side and the other side of the upper and lower operation guides the lower end of the actuating device cylinder which is formed inside the universal multifunctional movable retainer and the upper end of the operating device cylinder is connected to the upper end of the double acting multifunctional movable storage tank in a whitish manner so as to store or discharge the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "para_81", "text": "for example when 100 of the river water flows down from the upstream of the river 98 of the river water is discharged through the double discharge water gate 713 and the remaining 2 of the river water is discharged through the double discharge pipe 715 and at the same time the organic substance material molecules having a specific gravity are moved smoothly while the clean stream water having a specific gravity floats naturally to the upper layer portion of the purifying box 7000 by a material pushing action of pushing light substance molecules of a specific gravity and is pushed out of the purge box 7000 while being naturally contained in the lifting gang 711 coupled to the purge box 712"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}]</data>
