  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-6358407-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "a first filtration zone is thereby formed of a layer composed of coagulated contaminant suspended solids which have formed into larger flocculent particles and reached the determined point of height in the vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "a substantially contaminant free water stream is introduced into the system via conduit 213"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_104", "text": "a substantially contaminant free water stream is preferably introduced into the system via conduit 309"}, {"pat_id": "US-11780746-B2", "para_id": "para_156", "text": "the first waste stream 12 can comprise a foamate having a first pfas concentration"}, {"pat_id": "US-9493370-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "due to the unpredictable nature of these variables there may be a considerable time lag between introduction of treatment chemicals into the wastewater stream and acceptable effluent contamination levels at the outlet of the daf"}, {"pat_id": "US-9493370-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "referring now to the drawing figures and in accordance with a one embodiment of the present invention a system 10 and method of treating a wastewater stream 1 to produce an effluent stream 2 having a contaminant concentration below a predetermined threshold comprises a wastewater treatment facility 20 having a storage or dissolved air filtration tank daf 30 a wastewater inlet 40 for providing contaminated wastewater to tank 30 and an effluent outlet 50 for withdrawing treated wastewater 1 from tank 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200432978-Y1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "therefore the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 in addition to being discharged to 122 the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100251344-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the stream purification method may further include transferring the sludge water to the reactor to perform a purification process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for treating wastewater containing solids biological oxygen demanding compounds and biologically tolerant compounds or biologically inhibitory compounds separating the solids and biological oxygen demanding compounds from the wastewater feed using a primary separation process to provide a water phase comprising solid phase and wastewater wherein the solid phase comprises an initial level of pathogen irradiating the solid phase to reduce the level of the pathogen the wastewater comprising the biologically resistant compound or the biologically inhibitory compound is mixed with the adsorbent material in the mixing means for a sufficient time for the adsorption of the biologically resistant compound or biologically inhibitory compound from the wastewater onto the adsorbent material producing a mixture of wastewater and an adsorbent material adsorbed by a biologically tolerant compound or biologically inhibitory compound characterized in that the adsorbent material is characterized by adsorption capacity for a biologically tolerant or biologically inhibitory compound and a microorganism attached to the adsorbent material capable of decomposing an inorganic contaminant wherein the combined adsorbent material characteristic contributes to the biological regeneration of the adsorbent material separating and removing at least 90 of said adsorption treated wastewater from said mixture of said adsorbed treated wastewater and said adsorbent material with which said biologically resistant compound or biologically inhibitory compound adsorbed treating the adsorbed material adsorbed with the biologically resistant compound or the biologically inhibitory compound and the remaining 10 or less of the adsorbed treated wastewater to a biological regenerative reactor containing the microorganism treated wastewater for a period of time sufficient to cause the microorganisms in the biological regeneration reactor to biologically act on at least a portion of the biocompatible compound or biological inhibitory compound on the adsorbent material maintaining in a suspension of said biological regeneration reactor to produce a biologically regenerated adsorbent material and a biologically treated water effluent releasing the biologically treated water effluent from the biological regeneration reactor removing solids from the biological regenerator water effluent using a solid separation apparatus selected from the group consisting of a membrane operating system a clarifier a settler and a combination comprising at least one of a membrane operating system a clarifier or a settler wherein the biological effluent stream is passed through a sub system for separating the adsorbent material in the biological regenerative reactor downstream of the biological regenerative reactor to separate the effluent of the biological re introducing into the device and and recycling the biologically regenerated adsorbent material to the mixing means"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "for example in the effluent stream the sensor may indicate whether the concentration of a contaminant such as a biologically tolerant compound a biologically inhibitory compound and or a compound that is generally resistant to biodegradation has reached a predetermined value or trend value or trend so that the controller can be stimulated to perform some action upstream downstream from or at the sensor from the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102088362-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the upper sprinkling method of the inlet chute 51 has a problem that it is difficult to fully utilize the water spraying effect such as the effect of directly piercing the dewatering hole 521 and the separation effect of the fine sludge and the heat utilization is lowered even when heated hot water is used"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0436666-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "that liquid may be disposed of in a variety of appropriate ways so long as disposal is accomplished with limited release of the contained contaminant compounds"}, {"pat_id": "US-8585892-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "effluent wastewater w is introduced into a set 300 of sumps and filters that are configured in series because microbial reduction of ammonia in an influent stream is a multi stage process"}, {"pat_id": "US-8388833-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "effluent wastewater w is introduced into a set 300 of sumps and filters that are configured in series because microbial reduction of ammonia in an influent stream is a multi stage process"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604157-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the extraction mechanism 100 functions to remove contaminants such as water and solid particulates from a pumped gaseous stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floating bucket for collecting suspended solids a fourth floating material collection conveyor for transporting the collected particulate matter and the ultra fine particles in the rear portion of the floating material collection rotating bucket fine particles rising from the rear portion of the fourth floating material collection conveyor to the upper portion of the river water a fourth contaminant screw feeder configured to collect and collect sex contaminants and ultra fine magnetic contaminants to push and transport the contaminants to the outside of the river water processing box and combine the rotor and the rotor support a fifth floating material collection conveyor for transporting and collecting the collected particulate matter and 