  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for automatically degassing a downflow biological water treatment filter having various levels an influent flow into the top of the filter and an effluent flow from the base of the filter a stopping the outflow to prevent drainage of the filter comprising a backwash system b flushing gas trapped from the filter by introducing a back flow of water into the base of the filter c automatically checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow d draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level e continually flushing the filter to release the trapped gas from the filter f stopping the backwash stream and the backwash waste stream if present resuming the outflow to restart the filter and g maintaining influent flow during steps a through f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "maintaining an outflow from the top of each filter during the process b stopping the inflow to the base of the filter selected to be degassed to prevent backwash backflow to the other filter c directing backwash water flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g stopping the inflow to the base of the filter selected to be degassed to prevent backwash backflow to the other filter h directing a backwash stream to the base of the selected filter to flush the trapped gas from the filter i stopping the backwash and backwash wastewater if any present in the filter selected in step b resuming the inflow to the base of the filter in step b and reactivating the filter in step b j continuously degassing the other selected filter by repeating steps b to i while continuing with step a k flushing the finally selected filter l if present stopping the backwash flow to the finally selected filter and m resuming the inflow to the base of the finally selected filter to reactivate the finally selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300 connected to the unit and capable of checking and operating managing measurement data of the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360 for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420 for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers for water supply and sewage treatment by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430 for storing measured data of quantity and water quality of each region and state information and manager information of each unit receiving the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote location the transmission unit for transmitting the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the sewage treatment automatic control unit or integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine 410 wow water quality management remote control system comprising a control system unit 400 consisting of a mobile communication terminal text transmission unit 440 for generating a short text message"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}]</data>
