wastewater stream to travel from an inlet 210 at a bottom of said electrochemical cell to an outlet 220 in a top of said electrochemical cell wherein said electrochemical cell also includes a first and second electrical headers 260 270 wherein each of said conductive plates 250 255 is in electrical communication with either said first or said second header 260 270"}, {"pat_id": "US-10876085-B2", "para_id": "para_95", "text": "a region 24 for generating cavitation may consist of elements such as a twisted plate 26 to form a spiral element to tighten the flow of liquid and a work piece in the form of a cylinder 28 with a central channel 29 having a constriction and expansion of the passage section of the fluid flow for inception of cavitation"}, {"pat_id": "US-9682872-B2", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "2 or any other type of mixing device may be provided between inlet 40 and tank 30 to mix wastewater 1 with treatment chemicals prior to its introduction into tank 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0128277-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "a screen device connected to the upper side of the aeration tank 1 through a pipe removes and collects a relatively small contaminant discharged from the raw wastewater and lifts it to the ground thereby increasing the device protection and processing efficiency in a subsequent process"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325645-B2", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the use of the flow director 48 is considered advantageous at least because the flow pattern caused by the flow direction 48 on the continuous fluid stream ls creates a longer dwell time on the continuous fluid stream ls to travel through the insert 40"}, {"pat_id": "US-8226832-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the side stream thereby created can be used to introduce any additive such as for example a corrosion inhibitor into the flow of source water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173309-B1", "para_id": "para_238", "text": "the apparatus 580 further allows the water flows w1 and w2 to flow repeatedly in the circulation path formed by connecting the external annular flow path 585a to the suction side of the first pump 1p via the pipeline p"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134037-B1", "para_id": "para_112", "text": "laminar flow peeling is caused from the inner wall surface to generate a cavitation action thereby facilitating ultrafineness of organic matter and sludge in the drainage that is destruction of cell membranes of microorganisms in sludge and ultrafineness of the cytoplasm"}, {"pat_id": "US-6752926-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "oxygen is depleted in the bioreactor due to biochemical oxidation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435493-Y1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "therefore the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 in addition to being discharged to 122 the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-7678235-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "while the capacity of any system to remove contaminants from inlet water is to some extent a function of the total impurity levels in the inlet water systems of the invention are particularly well suited to remove a plurality of different contaminants of widely different types from a single feed stream producing water that is comparable to distilled water and is in some cases comparable to ultrapure water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11401171-B2", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "3a and 3b before during or after flowing into the portion 325 of the holding tank 280 via the inlet 285 the treated slop feed stream undergoes dissolved air flotation daf which is a process by which suspended solids oil and or other contaminants are removed from the treated slop feed stream via air bubble flotation"}, {"pat_id": "US-10464021-B2", "para_id": "para_106", "text": "outlets and inlets designed to remove and replace draw stream or diluted draw stream or pasteurization distillation advanced oxidation system membrane filtration such as nf or uf absorption of the contaminants or destruction or inoculation of the contaminants by exposure to oxidants uv high pressure temperature or any similar methods and associated equipment operably coupled thereto between the outlet of the first side and the inlet of the first side such as prior to or after an ro element"}, {"pat_id": "US-10464021-B2", "para_id": "para_112", "text": "the ro permeate may be potable water and the ro concentrate may be at least partially regenerated draw stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-4405349-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "some of the inlet feed stream desirably first cooled to just above the freezing point of the feed stream in a heat exchanger is cooled by the ice crystals to form additional ice in the warm concentrator thereby increasing the efficiency of the system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4405349-A", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "so that when they combine with the inlet feed stream which is only slightly above the freezing point of water in the warm concentrator the feed stream becomes further cooled and more ice is thereby formed thus increasing the efficiency of the system"}, {"pat_id": "US-10156321-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the method recognizes that impurities in the carbon dioxide stream change the phase behavior and fluid transport properties of the carbon dioxide effluent and that a variation of contaminant levels in the flow stream under an identical inlet pressure and temperature scenario may lead to the formation of two phase flow within the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-9850152-B2", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "water will also absorb ir and the temperature will be raised a factor which will again shifts the equilibrium more towards the caco3 precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "US-4168231-A", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "here the dirty water whirls at high velocity creating a central vortex in the separator from top to bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 in the water blocking device of the buoyancy type clapboard block to prevent flooding and overburden of rivers including the flexible water blocking plate 80 made of the member 90 is installed the floating matter removal module 100 for removing the floating matter floating in the river when the water barrier block 60 is raised and lowered includes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1866487-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "advantageously the computing part according to a further development comprise a floating element so that it is moved upwards by a rising water level and thereby releases the previously retained in the lower vorsperrenposition solids for effective discharge of solids over the outflow surge again"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by the center of gravity 140 to move toward the hinge shaft 125 125a of the opening and closing cover 121 121a by rotating upward to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the crate 10 in the dry stream when the rainwater does not flow in the waterways while stably catching foreign substances mixed in the rainwater opening and closing cover 121 121a by the weight 140 to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10 to prevent foreign substances such as cigarette butts or vinyl to enter the drain 1 in addition the uneven protrusions 112 and 113 of the body 110 and the uneven protrusions 124 and 124a of the opening and closing cover 121 and 121a are inserted into the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082127-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "consisting of a salinity meter installed on the ballast water inlet pipe to measure salinity of the ballast water introduced a chemical tank supplying a sterilant to the ballast water inlet pipe through a metering pump a physical treatment device installed on the main transport pipe to kill remove and damage the zooplankton and the underwater microorganisms by physical impact using the flow rate and pressure of ballast water it is connected to the outlet of the physical processing device the positive electrode plate and the negative electrode plate is installed alternately therein the variable rectifier capable of controlling the voltage and current according to the flow rate of the incoming fluid the flow rate inside the pipe and the salt concentration of seawater an electrolysis device that receives power and generates residual chlorine to perform sterilization treatment on microorganisms in water a tro sensor connected to the outlet of the electrolysis device and measuring the concentration of the oxidant and on the basis of the salinometer measurement value or the measured value of the tro sensor including a control device for controlling the inflow into the ballast water inlet pipe the inflow into the ballast water transport pipe the chemical input amount or the amount of power supplied from the rectifier when the salinity of ballast water measured by the salinity meter is 0 to 8 psu the sterilant is supplied to the ballast water inlet pipe through the chemical tank and the ballast water supplied with the sterilizer is either front or rear of the physical pretreatment device"}, {"pat_id": "US-6383361-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "for example oxygen water mixture 69 including make up water preferably enters tank 82 through inlet 86 at an angle sufficient to cause the mixture 69 to impinge against wall 87"}, {"pat_id": "US-10377649-B2", "para_id": "para_193", "text": "this fermentation process can be applied using microbes to stabilize the hydrogen sulfide to elemental sulfur or to sulfuric acid generally a less desirous end product because of issues associated with corrosion due to low ph"}, {"pat_id": "US-8404121-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "to separate solids from a waste stream comprises several steps for example a providing a separation vessel comprising i a fluid inlet ii a solids outlet comprising an overflow conduit having a height hw measured from a base portion of the separation vessel and iii a fluid outlet at a first position between the base portion and hw b feeding an aerated inlet mixture to the separation vessel via the fluid inlet at a flowrate qi the aerated inlet mixture comprising i a fluid ii a solid contaminant and iii an aerating gas c separating the inlet mixture in the separation vessel into i an upper float layer comprising aerated solids and being located at a second position and ii a lower clarified layer comprising a clarified fluid and being located at a third position the second position being relatively further away from the base portion of the separation vessel than the third position d withdrawing the upper float layer from the separation vessel via the overflow conduit and e withdrawing the lower clarified layer from the separation vessel via the fluid outlet at a selected flowrate qo"}, {"pat_id": "US-7531087-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in one embodiment devices such as emaciators and screens not shown are provided to chop or otherwise divide up and filter the solids in the material to be carried from the community or neighborhood sewage system prior to entry into inlet 12 such that only pulverized entrained solids are contained in the influent stream moved by fill pump 14 or circulation pump 28"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356690-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a stream type water flow circulation system installed around the river a permeable sidewalk block unit forming a sidewalk through which pedestrians pass an irrigation canal provided in parallel with the permeable sidewalk block unit and having a communication path capable of receiving rainwater from the permeable sidewalk block unit a conveying pipe member for conveying rainwater penetrating downward through the water permeable sidewalk block unit a filtration unit for filtering rainwater coming through the communication path of the irrigation canal and the transfer pipe member and being installed under the ground a storage unit provided to receive and store the rainwater filtered by the filtration unit and a pump for supplying water from the storage unit upstream of the stream or irrigation canal the filtration unit an inflow tank through which rainwater flows from the transport pipe member a filtering part installed in the inflow tank and the rainwater flowing upward from the lower part and filtered by the fluidized bed filter medium and it is installed on the upper portion of the filtration unit and includes a back washing unit for back washing the fluidized bed medium the filter unit includes an upper filter net and a lower filter net installed between the fluidized bed media and an upper portion of the lower filter net is provided with an air inlet to disturb the fluidized media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-8262914-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "referring now to the drawing figures and in accordance with a one embodiment of the present invention a system 10 and method of treating a wastewater stream 1 to produce an effluent stream 2 having a contaminant concentration below a predetermined threshold comprises a wastewater treatment facility 20 having a storage or dissolved air filtration tank daf 30 a wastewater inlet 40 for providing contaminated wastewater to tank 30 and an effluent outlet 50 for withdrawing treated wastewater 1 from tank 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object to form a coriander site on both sides of the sewer and formed in the central longitudinal direction to form embankment on both sides of the coriander site to let the river water flowing through the river flows through the stream in the river the sewer and coriander site has a block size to the river flow inflow to the side of the river inflow to the side of the river flows into a predetermined size so as not to affect the water flow capacity of the river so that the dredging of the journey to facilitate a housing having a bottom surface on which river water is discharged and having a plurality of sedimentation tanks divided by a sedimentation basin divider in a direction parallel to the reservoir in the center of the sedimentation basin so as to control the river water during the dredging operation a front end of the enclosure that is a sedimentation inlet flow path with a head protruding from the center connected to the sedimentation basin divider having a jaw and a groove at the bottom and an upper rod hook groove at the top the prefabricated movable blocking gate installed in the blocking gate installation unit is achieved by installing a sedimentation basin consisting of several prefabricated clasp plates that are miniaturized for easy transportation and an upper hook rod to support the prefabricated clasp plates"}, {"pat_id": "US-10294654-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a mounting bracket for attaching the bar screen to the at least one wall or at least one inlet pipe below a mouth of the at least one inlet pipe so as to catch and remove unwanted debris from an incoming stream of fluid including debris wherein the mounting bracket includes at least one block and at least one bar extending out from the at least one block the at least one block providing alignment and mounting for the bar screen wherein the bar screen and the mounting bracket has a quick connect disconnect configuration to couple them together"}, {"pat_id": "US-10294654-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a mounting bracket attaching the screen basket to at least one wall or the at least one inlet pipe below a mouth of the at least one inlet pipe so as to catch and remove unwanted debris from an incoming stream of fluid including debris wherein the mounting bracket includes at least one mounting block wherein the screen basket and mounting bracket includes a quick connect disconnect configuration for mounting the screen basket to the mounting bracket and the at least one mounting block extending longitudinal along a center axis of the at least one inlet pipe and outward laterally relative to the mounting bracket perpendicular to the center axis of the at least one inlet pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300 connected to the unit and capable of checking and operating managing measurement data of the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360 for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420 for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers for water supply and sewage treatment by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430 for storing measured data of quantity and water quality of each region and state information and manager information of each unit receiving the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote location the transmission unit for transmitting the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the sewage treatment automatic control unit or integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine 410 wow water quality management remote control system comprising a control system unit 400 consisting of a mobile communication terminal text transmission unit 440 for generating a short text message"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}]</data>
