  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200426198-Y1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in order to achieve the object of the present invention is formed of a hollow block of a concrete material the body portion having an inlet and an outlet having different sizes in front and rear a first filter plate member made of a pitched concrete material installed in a plate shape at an inlet of the body part a second filter plate member made of water permeable concrete which is installed in a plate shape at an outlet of the body portion a boundary block having a water quality purification function of a river is provided comprising a plurality of contact media installed vertically inside the front inlet of the first filter plate part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a structure in which a rainwater discharge blocking wall 990 is configured to fail to flow into the interior of the rainwater collection channel 999 combined with the stairs through the rainwater inlet 998 the upper position of the combined rainwater collecting channel 999 is a structure configured to be equal to the upper surface portion 980 of the land a structure in which a floor covering material 880 composed of rocks is installed at a lower end of the waterway wall 100 so that water swimmers or swimmers can play or swim in water with confidence at the lower end of the combined rainwater collection channel 999 a rainwater or contaminants contaminated with rivers or rivers or reservoirs or dams while constructing a stepped artificial reef 890 where organisms amphibians or fish can be easily inhabited"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "after the above mentioned river embankment 100 is maintained the river is deeply dredged a water barrier is formed on the dredged riverbed and then the above mentioned foundation concrete 800 is installed inside the water barrier and then a partition 999 for generating a siphon effect is formed on the upper part of the above mentioned foundation concrete 800 to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity to the center of the lower part while preferentially discharging clean river water with a heavy specific gravity and a front inlet 91 is formed on the front part of the lower part and a rear outlet 92 is formed on the rear part of the lower part and an eco friendly movable dam 9999 for preventing green algae occurrence that combines an electric power generation unit 7777 that produces eco friendly electricity using hydraulic power is installed on the rear part of the above mentioned rear outlet 92"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101102443-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present application as a means for solving the above problems as a water treatment method for obtaining purified water suitable for drinking water or industrial water for the target water selected from the treated water selected from river river water ground water wastewater treatment plant after pretreatment of the water to be treated in a sulphate denitrification tank or an ultrasonic electrolysis tank an ozone containing water is made and supplied to a high precision filtration tank to remove residual contaminants while passing through the filter bed of the biofilm separation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714328-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after deeply dredging the upstream and downstream portions by blocking the above mentioned river the above mentioned river embankment 100 on one side and the other side of the above mentioned river is obliquely prepared the above mentioned concrete 111 is installed on the riverbed and on the sides of the bottom of one side of the bank and the other side of the bank a fish habitat facility 112 is constructed using rocks or bank structures so that amphibians benthic animals or fish can easily inhabit it and then various bank structures 113 are stored inside the above mentioned fish habitat facility 112 so that fish can easily inhabit it a structure comprising an eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is configured as a dam reservoir lake or estuary structure configured to hold water in the upper part of the above concrete 111 a structure in which a bottom water rising passage 7777 is formed by combining a bottom inlet 311 that acts to discharge heavy bottom water between one side and the other side of the front part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae occurrence and a bottom water rising passage 7777 is formed by a structure in which the bottom part is narrow and the upper part is formed by a gradually wider inclined plate 322 a structure in which an air inlet 321 for preventing gravity generation is formed in the upper part of the above mentioned low level water rising passage 7777 to prevent low level water which automatically rises by the action of gravity and siphon action from being discharged in the downstream direction of the river when it reaches a certain water level a structure in which a material friction and material explosion generating unit 889 is combined to generate electricity by separating the light gravity river water and the heavy gravity river water into upper and lower parts through the gravity material friction and material explosion generated between the light gravity river water and the light gravity river water thereby causing the polluted river water with a light specific gravity to float to the upper part while simultaneously automatically separating the clean river water with a heavy specific gravity to the lower part and simultaneously discharging it in the downstream direction of the river through the lower inlet 311 and the bottom water rising passage 7777 a structure in which the lower layer water rising passage 7777 and the upper part power generation water movement passage 211 formed on the rear part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae occurrence are each formed with a plurality of upper discharge ports 151 a structure in which an exhaust emission control valve 163 is combined at one end of the upper exhaust port 151 a structure in which an induction pipe 152 for generating gravitational acceleration caused by the action of gravity is formed at the lower part of the rear portion of the upper discharge port 151 a structure in which a gravity acceleration generating unit 911 is formed in the upper part of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 with a height that is 10 to 1 000 times wider and a volume that is larger than the thickness area and volume ratio of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 a structure in which an air inlet 158 is formed at the upper part of the above mentioned gravity acceleration generating unit 911 a structure in which dual control valves 161 162 are respectively formed in the upper and lower parts of the induction pipe 152 for generating the above mentioned gravitational acceleration effect to control the discharge amount of river water the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae which is connected to an electric power generation unit 331 that generates electricity at the lower end of the above mentioned gravitational acceleration generating induction pipe 152 is installed in a river a reservoir a dam a lake or an estuary to hold water and then the double control valve 162 is closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714328-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "after the river embankment 100 is repaired the river 2001 is deeply dredged and a water barrier is formed on the dredged riverbed and then a concrete 111 foundation is installed inside the water barrier and an eco friendly movable weir 8888 for preventing green algae which consists of a structure of a lower horizontal support and an upper horizontal support on the top of the foundation concrete is installed or the river is blocked to form a dam reservoir or lake or an eco friendly movable weir 8888 for preventing green algae which consists of a structure of an estuary dam is installed to block the water and then a low level water inlet 311 and a low level water discharge rising passage 7777 are formed inside the eco friendly movable weir for preventing green algae and then an automatic control system a surveillance camera and a remote control system 1000 are combined and configured in the river embankment 100 and combined with a power generation system to produce electricity and purify polluted river water which is an eco friendly and natural method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714328-B1", "para_id": "claim_28", "text": "after installing sheet piles in a river to block the water the river embankment 100 is maintained the river 2001 is deeply dredged a water barrier is formed on the dredged riverbed and a concrete 111 foundation is installed inside the water barrier and an eco friendly movable weir 8888 for preventing green algae which consists of a structure of a lower horizontal support and an upper horizontal support on the top of the foundation concrete is installed or the river is blocked to form a dam reservoir or lake or an eco friendly movable weir 8888 for preventing green algae which consists of a structure of an estuary dam is installed to block the water and then a low level water inlet 311 and a low level water rising passage 7777 for discharging low level water are formed inside the eco friendly movable weir for preventing green algae thereby generating electricity and purifying polluted river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101788811-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an activated carbon filtration unit in which raw water sucked from an emergency water feeder or a river or a river side is subjected to filtration treatment with a large particle while foreign substances are filtered through the sand and filtered water filtered by the sand filtration unit is re a filter cloth for holding a filter medium between the filter plates stacked in multiple means so that small foreign substances contained in the filtered water are filtered by the filter medium coated with the filter cloth while being supplied with the filtered water filtered by the activated carbon filter unit is provided a pressurized filter portion connected to a third raw milk feed inlet for feeding raw water to one side of the filter plate and connected to the other side of the third filtered water discharge pipe through which the filtered water is discharged from the filter plate and the filter cloth a membrane filter in which filtered water filtered by the filter is sucked and highly filtered to fine foreign matters a modular water production system comprising a part a filtration data storage unit for presetting and storing a state value of a water quality to be filtered by the modular water production system and a limit pressure value inside the operation unit a state of the water quality filtered by the modular water production system a water quality measurement data comparing unit for storing the data and a pressure measurement data verifying unit for checking and storing the filtration state by measuring the pressure inside each of the actuating units a water quality measurement monitoring unit a failure confirmation monitoring unit for checking the operation state of each operation unit of the modular water production system to check for a failure a system general status data storage unit in which the installation location and related information of the modular water production system are stored a water quality status data storage unit for storing information on the status of the water quality and the water quality status and quantity on the site a central control unit including an operating unit data storage unit for storing a value of a proper pressure value and a proper filtering throughput in each operating unit a system data transmitting and receiving unit for wirelessly transmitting measured data and data confirmed by the fault checking and monitoring unit to the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit and receiving a signal of a central control unit a central data transmitting and receiving unit provided in the central control unit for receiving data transmitted through the system data transmitting and receiving unit and transmitting an instruction command to the modular water producing system and when the water quality measurement value measured by the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit is out of the range of a predetermined set value or when a malfunction of each of the operating units occurs and the malfunction confirmation monitoring unit confirms it and an emergency monitoring control unit for generating an emergency signal in the central control unit when the water quality and pressure data measured and transmitted from the water quality monitoring and monitoring unit is out of the predetermined water quality and pressure data range wherein the control unit controls the operation of each of the actuating units of the modular water production system to automatically perform backwashing by operating each valve of the modular water production system to stop the supply of raw water and a washing automatic control unit is additionally provided to the water supply unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562303-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 1221646 a base plate fixed to the bottom surface of a small stream a sensor housing fixed at an eccentric position on the base plate and having a cross sectional area of the inlet through which water is introduced is larger than the cross sectional area of the outlet through which water is discharged a water quality sensor installed on one side wall of the sensor housing to detect the quality of water passing through the sensor housing and a screen unit fixed to the circumference of the base plate to block the inflow of foreign substances other than water through the front rear left right and upper sides of the water quality sensor it is possible to monitor water quality by installing it in a place with a low water depth such as a small river a water quality monitoring device for a small stream has been proposed to improve the safety and durability of the water quality monitoring device by using a screen unit and a sensor housing to protect the water quality sensor in two layers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046833-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heavy water purification tank in the form of a tank for purifying water by decolorization and odor removal of the water purified by the microbial purification tank a circulating tank having a chemical material inlet for chemical treatment at an upper portion thereof and a pumping means for circulating discharged water by pumping the stored heavy water in the lower portion the circulating tank being loaded with the purified heavy water purified by the heavy water septic tank and discharged according to the use of the heavy water including the sedimentation sedimentation tank has a sludge separation space in which the lower portion is inclined the upper portion is formed in an open tank shape and sludge and manure and foreign substances are loaded at the lower portion in the center along the slope and the water of the upper portion overflows when a predetermined amount or more is loaded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101694827-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention relates to an initial good treatment apparatus capable of effectively preventing contaminants mixed with an initial storm due to contamination of a river lake by effectively treating contamination mixed with the initial rainwater by a pretreatment tank and a filtration tank an inlet pipe for guiding the initial storm of the gut pipe to the pretreatment tank and an inlet pipe connected to the filtration tank of the main body the main body is located at the same depth as the gutter tube and the inlet tube is formed higher than the outlet tube at the position of the water head and the initial gutter inside the main body is moved by the water head difference quot an early stormwater treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100616402-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an extension 30 in which the hole 32 is drilled a plurality of inlet pipes 40 each having a truncated cone shape inserted into and fixed to the through holes 180 of the main body 10 and a horizontal portion 51 a vertical portion 52 protruding from an upper center of the horizontal portion 51 and having an upper portion open to form a space therein and installed horizontally in an inner space of the vertical portion 52 it is provided with a plurality of partition walls 53 the water purifying plants are planted in the space of the vertical portion 52 is inserted into the iron cross sectional insertion grooves 14 15 a plurality of longitudinally long iron \u51f8 \u578b section planting table 50 bubble generation block of the river suitable for ecological environment including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101221721-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "by preventing the inflow of the river has the effect of preventing the contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initi