inwater flows into the space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 is formed a continuous inflow inlet 410 is formed between the upper cap 300 and the housing 200 to connect the space between the inflow port 100 and the housing 200 with the inner space of the housing 200 a lower cap 400 and and a first initial storm inflow port 210 formed in the housing 200 and connecting a space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 to an internal space of the housing 200 an inner tube 500 inserted into the housing 200 and formed in a tubular shape having openings at both ends thereof one end connected to the lower cap 400 and the other end protruding outside the housing 200 further comprising the first initial stormwater inlet 210 connects a space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 and a space between the housing 200 and the internal pipe 500 the inner cap 500 may be formed in the inner cap 500 so as to prevent the outer cap 500 from flowing back to the space between the housing 200 and the inner cap 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101398010-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a reservoir installed on the lower side of the gutter a connection pipe connecting the storm water pipe and the storage tank a storage tank installed in the connection pipe for controlling the stormwater flowing into the storage tank through the connection pipe a first sensor installed on the upstream side of the connection pipe among the gross conduits and measuring a contamination degree and a quantity of the ozone flowing into the gutter tube a second sensor installed inside the storage tank for measuring a contamination level and a water level of the storm water filled in the storage tank a discharge pump installed in the storage tank for sucking the rainwater in the storage tank and discharging the rainwater to the outside and a control unit for opening and closing the storage tank gates in accordance with an initial stormwater inflow signal and an initial wastewater termination signal of the first sensor and driving the discharge pump according to the high water level signal or the contamination signal of the second sensor the storage tank gates a connection pipe interlocking part installed to be rotatable at an inlet of the connection pipe and interrupting the connection pipe while rotating and an excellent pipe shut off part slidably installed in the connection pipe cut off part and slid in a state where the connection pipe cut off part is opened to cut off the excellent pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "in addition the reinforcing part 148 is installed close to the rotational center of the odor blocking plate 143 but may be installed at a space away from the backflow permitting plate 145 to the left as long as it is within a range that does not block the backflow permitting hole 144 .100"}, {"pat_id": "US-5232307-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hydraulic diverter for receiving water including storm water comprising a first flush flow having a relatively high concentration of pollutants and a sustained flow which is relatively free of pullutants said diverter comprising an inlet a first outlet section and a second outlet section each of said outlet sections connected to receive storm water from said inlet for discharging storm water from said diverter said diverter having two operational states and having means for utilizing energy of the storm water to change operational states such that first flow is discharged through said first outlet section in a first operational state and sustained flow is discharged through said second outlet section in a second operational state wherein said water received by said diverter additionally comprises a nuisance flow having a relatively high concentration of pullutants wherein said diverter is configured to discharge nuisance flow through said first outlet section in said first operational state and wherein each of said outlet sections comprises an articulated tube said articulated tubes being disposed in a guide block"}, {"pat_id": "US-7846327-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floatable skimmer positioned in said housing chamber between the inlet and outlet of said housing chamber said skimmer being movably mounted in a skimmer track and having floatation thereon mounted to raise and lower said skimmer with the rise and fall of storm water in said filter box to thereby block floatable debris from passing through said filter box said floating skimmer having top and bottom edges said bottom edge defining a variable channel opening thereunder for the passage of water thereunder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "at this time the rainwater that is filtered through the first storage block 10 and a plurality of storage blocks 10 adjacent to each other repeatedly is introduced into the storage space s connected to each other via the above described downstream guide pipe 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100799651-B1", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "as shown in figure 6 the cartridge which is the main part of the purification treatment apparatus to be purified again sewage after the contaminant removal device provided on the inlet side of the overflow water and storm water discharge treatment apparatus according to the present invention is provided with only the main cartridge 620 in addition the main cartridge 620 and the auxiliary cartridge 630 may be included"}, {"pat_id": "US-8034236-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in this storm water filter box a pair of baffles 36 are mounted along the bottom for capturing sand gravel or non floatable trash but it should be clear that these baffles may or may not be included within the filter box 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
