  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-4283211-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "or thereabove or brackish water sea water or other saline water or wastewater at or above its freezing point is brought into heat exchange contact with the liquid phase condensate of a working fluid or refrigerant hereinafter usually termed working fluid having a boiling point significantly below the freezing point of water or of the saline water whereby the water is frozen and gives up its latent heat of fusion which is absorbed by the working fluid condensate as its latent heat of vaporization the working fluid condensate thereby being vaporized by that exchange of latent heats of phase transition at autogenic pressure and the vapor is superheated to approximately the temperature of the inlet water the superheated vapor is released in a turbine to create mechanical shaft power which by conventional mechanical and electrical means is converted to electric power"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a blocking network 21 is formed in the center to prevent the blockage 21 so that the sewage water 1 can flow from the top to the bottom and a vertical pipe communicating vertically with the lower part of the blocking network 21 the sewage 1 is introduced into the inlet space 11 of the main body 10 through 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100912781-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "seventh since the heating wire is provided on the outer surface of the body of the inlet and the dehydration unit it is possible to prevent the viscosity rise and freezing of the slurry due to the temperature drop and thus can be used to operate even in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102239966-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a pump that supplies external water to the inlet of the steam generating pipe a water supply hose that connects the external water to the pump a steam discharge hose that discharges the steam supplied from the outlet of the steam generating pipe to the outside of the housing and the operation of the heater and the pump it comprises a control unit for controlling the the pedestal consists of a front plate and a rear plate bent in a vertical state and the front plate has a display unit indicating temperature and error code while screwing one side of the cover to the rim a steam amount control lever a steam switch a residual water removal switch and a socket for connecting the steam discharge hose is mounted the rear plate is made by perforating the entrance while screwing the other side of the cover to the edge portion the lower end is screwed inside the doorway formed on the rear plate of the pedestal and both sides are screwed to the cover and a socket connecting the earth leakage circuit breaker and water supply hose is mounted and the power supply line is connected so that it can flow into the inside and the accessories can be stored an inner plate providing a storage space is provided a spray gun having a nozzle connected to the front end of the steam discharge hose to inject steam is provided a plurality of drainage holes are drilled in lower corners of the front plate and the rear plate of the pedestal so that moisture can be discharged to the outside a plurality of first vents are formed on the upper side of the inner plate to discharge heat inside the housing while preventing the inflow of moisture scattered from the outside and a plurality of second vents are formed on one side of the cover to be mounted on the pedestal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200337587-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the freeze prevention water meter is a meter body having an inlet and an outlet so that water supplied from a predetermined water supply source can flow in and out and has a receiving portion in communication with each of the inlet and outlet meter reading flow rate of the water flowing out of the outlet a metering member which is accommodated in the receiving portion so as to be able to be inserted into the inlet portion so as to heat the water flowing into and out of the meter body to a predetermined temperature and is drawn out to the outlet portion via the bottom side of the receiving portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101776914-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the handle 26 and the screw engagement portion 27 are provided on the inside of the steam hose 29 and an auxiliary convex portion 28 is inserted into the lower portion of the screw coupling portion 27 so that the screw coupling portion 27 is inserted into the auxiliary block portion 28 and the lower part of the airtight packing 24 is brought into close contact with the convex part 23 so that the inner circumferential surface of the airtight packing 24 is directed toward the steam hose 29 airtight means 20 which expands and seals the circumferential surface of the steam hose 29 to prevent the steam inside the steam generator 12 and the tube t from leaking to the outside a discharge pipe 41 is inserted into a front surface of the tube t inverted into the inside of the pipe and the automatic pressure member 42 is coupled to the upper portion of the discharge pipe 41 a temperature and pressure control unit 43 is installed in the temperature and pressure control unit 43 and an automatic valve 44 is provided under the temperature and pressure control unit 43 to automatically discharge the internal pressure of the tube t to the outside an automatic pressure regulating device 40 having a first outlet 45 formed at a lower end of the automatic valve 44 and a second outlet 46 formed at a side of the automatic valve 44 and a condensate storage chamber 51 is formed at the end of the recovery line 47"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100357289-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in the center of the crystal growth tank 2 is a central axis in which two blade propeller stirrers 2 1 are connected to the upper power source 7 and rotated to increase the mixing and heat transfer efficiency while the ice crystals grow to a sufficient size 7 1 fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101893417-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in one example the control device receives the incoming water quality value and the flow rate value from the first sensor derives the influent load receives the outflow water quality value from the second sensor receives the temperature value from the third sensor a data portion for data wise the water quality by temperature a driving unit for driving the valve to introduce the water into the pre treatment tank and the bioreactor the real time influent load value is derived from the real time influent water quality value and the real time flow value from the first sensor and the real time runoff water quality value is derived from the derived real time influent load and the real the real time recirculated water load value is obtained from the fourth sensor by receiving the real time recirculated water quality value and the real time flow rate value from the fourth sensor and the real real time flow rate value is received and a real time connection load is derived and when the real time reflux water load and real time connection water load exceeds the above mentioned additional connection water load and additional reflux water load the valve is driven to the pre so that the real time counter current load and the real time connection water load are set to the above characterized in that it comprises a load by driving the valve and can be linked or less wake analysis unit such that flowing into the bioreactor through the raw water inlet line.as described above according to the system of the present invention in the continuous treatment of the wastewater it is possible to automatically determine whether or not the pre treatment of the reflux water and the connection water is performed by the sensing basis thereby reducing the cost required for the pretreatment and improving the treatment efficiency of the pretreatment it is possible to improve the treatment efficiency of the whole system by preventing the load of the bioreactor.1 is a block diagram illustrating a system of the present invention 2 is a schematic view showing an example of a bioreactor which is a constitution of the present invention 3 is a block diagram showing a detailed configuration of a control apparatus which is a constitution of the present invention figures 4a and 4b are operational state diagrams of the system of the present invention 5 is a schematic view showing an example of a pretreatment tank which is a constituent of the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the air discharge pipe 60 is a high temperature and high pressure aerobic digestion tank characterized in that to return the carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms to the inlet water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "on the other hand the air discharge pipe 60 is to return the carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms to the inlet water storage tank not shown to prevent the outflow of bubbles or odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100722407-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "on the other hand carbon dioxide generated as a result of the oxidation reaction of the over supplied air and high temperature aerobic microorganisms are returned to the inlet water storage tank not shown through the air discharge pipe 60 to prevent the outflow of bubbles or odors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101435107-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "the main feature is that the shape of the inlet pipe and the outlet pipe of the cooling block and the heating block are mutually changed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a purified water tank unit 1000 for introducing purified water to remove foreign substances and supplying a fixed quantity by driving a metering pump an advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 that electrolyzes the purified water supplied from the purified water tank unit 1000 by the operation of a bdd electrode and generates oh groups hydrogen peroxide and ozone to generate radical water in the advanced oxidation process livestock air inlet chamber unit 3000 for forcibly introducing livestock polluted air generated from livestock facilities and containing total hydrocarbons and concentrating it while maintaining a constant temperature radical water is introduced from the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 and livestock polluted air is introduced from the livestock air inlet chamber 3000 to cause an advanced oxidation process reaction sterilize the virus with ultraviolet rays and photocatalytic reaction with a filter ball advanced oxidation filter ball reaction unit 4000 to cause total hydrocarbon reduction system in the advanced oxidation process of environmental pollution around livestock facilities including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3 the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 is a purified water inlet 2100 for receiving purified water flowing in a fixed amount from the purified water tank unit 1000 a housing part 2200 connecting the purified water inlet 2100 to one side of the lower end and storing purified water flowing in from the purified water inlet 2100 in an external cavity 2210 a purified water heating unit 2300 that is fixedly installed in a coil shape in a portion of the external cavity 2210 in which the purified water is stored in the housing 2200 and heats the purified water according to a corresponding control signal a temperature sensor unit 2400 that is fixedly installed on the other side of the outer cavity of the housing unit 2200 and detects the temperature of purified water according to a corresponding control signal a water filter unit 2500 that is fixedly installed in a part of the inner space of the housing 2200 divides the outer cavity 2210 and the inner cavity 2520 removes foreign substances contained in purified water passes it and introduces it into the inner cavity 2520 while being installed in the central position of the internal cavity 2520 of the water purification filter unit 2500 it is fixed at the top in a sealed state and electrolyzes purified water according to the corresponding control signal so that oh groups and hydrogen peroxide are generated to generate radical water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the total hydrocarbon reduction system for the advanced oxidation process of the environmental pollution around the livestock facility of the present invention devised to achieve the above object includes a purified water tank unit 1000 for introducing purified water removing foreign substances and supplying a fixed quantity by driving a metering pump an advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 that electrolyzes the purified water supplied from the purified water tank unit 1000 by the operation of a bdd electrode and generates oh groups hydrogen peroxide and ozone to generate radical water in the advanced oxidation process livestock air inlet chamber unit 3000 for forcibly introducing livestock polluted air generated from livestock facilities and containing total hydrocarbons and concentrating it while maintaining a constant temperature radical water is introduced from the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 and livestock polluted air is introduced from the livestock air inlet chamber 3000 to cause an advanced oxidation process reaction sterilize the virus with ultraviolet rays and photocatalytic reaction with a filter ball advanced oxidation filter ball reaction unit 4000 that causes may include"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the advanced oxidation process radical water generator 2000 includes a purified water inlet 2100 for receiving purified water flowing in a fixed amount from the purified water tank unit 1000 a housing part 2200 connecting the purified water inlet 2100 to one side of the lower end and storing purified water flowing in from the purified water inlet 2100 in an external cavity 2210 a purified water heating unit 2300 that is fixedly installed in a coil shape in a portion of the external cavity 2210 in which the purified water is stored in the housing 2200 and heats the purified water according to a corresponding control signal a temperature sensor unit 2400 that is fixedly installed on the other side of the outer cavity of the housing unit 2200 and detects the temperature of purified water according to a corresponding control signal a water filter unit 2500 that is fixedly installed in a part of the inner space of the housing 2200 divides the outer cavity 2210 and the inner cavity 2520 removes foreign substances contained in purified water passes it and introduces it into the inner cavity 2520 while being installed in the central position of the internal cavity 2520 of the water purification filter unit 2500 it is fixed at the top in a sealed state and electrolyzes purified water according to the corresponding control signal so that oh groups and hydrogen peroxide are generated to generate radical water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the livestock air inlet chamber unit 3000 is an air inlet duct 3100 that introduces livestock contaminated air from the bottom surface of the livestock facility and has a funnel shaped cross section a foreign material filtering unit 3200 included in the livestock polluted air introduced from the air inlet duct 3100 and blocking the passage of foreign substances having a diameter of more than a centimeter level a first inlet fan unit 3300 for forcibly introducing livestock contaminated air that has passed through the foreign matter filtering unit 3200 according to a corresponding control signal a warming concentration chamber 3400 for introducing and concentrating livestock contaminated air passing through the first inlet fan unit 3300 and maintaining a constant temperature according to a corresponding control signal an exhaust duct part 3500 for discharging the livestock polluted air of the warming concentration chamber 3400 to the advanced oxidation filter ball reaction part 4000 may include"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a process for the supercritical water oxidation of an organic waste material comprising a feeding a pressurized aqueous mixture of said waste material and an oxidant source to a center reaction zone of a platelet tube reactor which is supported within an outer shell and whose outer surface defines together with an inner surface of said shell an annular space a wall of said platelet tube being provided with fluid passages which permit the flow of fluid from said annular space into said center reaction zone through a plurality of apertures b igniting a fuel at an inlet of said reaction zone to increase the temperature of said pressurized aqueous mixture c feeding water heated and pressurized to at least supercritical conditions externally of said reactor to at least one point along said annular space surrounding said platelet tube reactor wherein the resulting pressure in said annular space is higher than the pressure in the center reaction zone within said platelet tube such that said supercritical water flows from said annular space through said fluid passages in the wall of said platelet tube and into said center reaction zone through said plurality of apertures forming a thin film of supercritical water over substantially the entire inner surface of said platelet tube and heating said mixture to supercritical reaction temperature and d reacting said organic waste with said oxidant in said reaction zone"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "claim_15", "text": "a process for the supercritical water oxidation of an organic waste material comprising a feeding a pressurized aqueous mixture containing said waste material and an oxidant source at ambient temperature to a center reaction zone of a platelet tube reactor which is supported within an outer shell and whose outer surface defines together with an inner surface of said shell an annular space a wall of said platelet tube being provided with fluid passages which permit the flow of fluid from said annular space into said center reaction zone through a plurality of apertures b igniting a fuel at an inlet of said reaction zone to increase the temperature of said pressurized aqueous mixture c feeding water heated and pressurized to at least supercritical conditions externally of said reactor to multiple locations along said annular space surrounding said platelet tube reactor wherein the resulting pressure in said annular space is higher than the pressure in the center reaction zone within said platelet tube such that said supercritical water flows from said annular space through said fluid passages in the wall of said platelet tube and into said center reaction zone through said plurality of apertures forming a thin film of supercritical water over substantially the entire inner surface of said platelet tube and heating said mixture to supercritical reaction temperature and d reacting said organic waste with said oxidant in said reaction zone at a temperature of from about 1100 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571423-A", "para_id": "claim_21", "text": "a process for the oxidation of an organic waste material comprising a feeding a pressurized aqueous mixture of water and said waste material to a center zone of a platelet tube reactor which is supported within an outer shell and whose outer surface defines together with an inner surface of said shell an annular space a wall of said platelet tube being provided with fluid passages which permit the flow of fluid from said annular space into said center zone through a plurality of apertures b igniting a fuel at an inlet of said reaction zone to increase the temperature of said pressurized aqueous mixture c feeding water heated and pressurized to at least supercritical conditions externally of said reactor to at least one point along said annular space surrounding said platelet tube reactor wherein the resulting pressure in said annular space is higher than the pressure in the center zone within said platelet tube such that said supercritical water flows from said annular space through said fluid passages in the wall of said platelet tube and into said center zone through said plurality of apertures forming a thin film of supercritical water over substantially the entire inner surface of said platelet tube and heating said mixture to supercritical temperature d separating organic components from inorganic components of said waste material while at supercritical conditions and e oxidizing said separated organic components outside of said platelet tube reactor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aeration tank for aerating the treated water so that aerobic microorganisms propagate in the treated water by the supplied oxygen to form floes a measurement unit for measuring and monitoring a treatment state by sampling a predetermined amount of the treated water being treated in the aeration tank a suction unit connected to one or more of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water from each of the aeration tanks and supplying the collected water to the measuring unit a discharge unit connecting the measurement unit and the aeration tank so that the treated water measured by the measurement unit is discharged back to the aeration tank and a central processing unit that receives the measurement data measured by the measurement unit analyzes the measurement data and controls the measurement unit the suction unit and the discharge unit the suction part one or more aeration tank connection pipes connected to each of the aeration tanks one end of which is disposed so as to be submerged in each of the aeration tanks and capable of collecting treated water in each aeration tank and a scoring point control unit installed at the bottom of the aeration tank connection pipe installed to be drawn into the lower part of the aeration tank connection pipe or drawn out to the outside and to adjust the depth inserted into the aeration tank the measuring unit a measuring tank accommodating the treated water supplied through the inlet and having a washing water inlet through which washing water flows a spray nozzle installed at the washing water inlet inside the measuring tank to inject washing water into the measuring tank an angle adjusting unit rotatably installed at an end of the spray nozzle and adjusting a spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle a rotating inner tube installed on an inner circumferential surface of the measuring tank and having a plurality of through holes a rotary driving unit installed to be connected to the rotating inner tube to transmit power to the rotating inner tube and to rotate the rotating inner tube inside the measuring tank to form a vortex inside the measuring tank a washing state confirmation unit installed inside the measuring tank to photograph the inside of the measuring tank the control unit of the central processing unit analyzes the degree of contamination of the measurement tank through the image of the inside of the measurement tank captured by the washing state confirmation unit and analyzes whether or not cleaning of the inside of the measurement tank is necessary or a part requiring cleaning when the control unit confirms a position requiring washing the spray angle of the washing water sprayed through the spray nozzle is adjusted as the angle adjuster rotates a washing unit for cleaning the inside of the measurement tank by spraying washing water into the measurement tank after the treated water measured in the measurement tank is discharged to the aeration tank through the discharge unit and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting the freeze protection unit a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe a heating unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction part the treated water supply pipe of the suction part and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part and when the temperature sensed by the temperature sensing unit is equal to or less than a predetermined temperature a temperature control unit for adjusting the heating temperature of the heating unit so that the treated water or washing water inside the pipe does not freeze"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "decreasing the throat diameter will increase the pressure differential across the throat and increase the length of the stream that is cavitating"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the controller 88 could be equally effective in a case of a fixed nozzle cavitation system wherein a number of inputs to the controller 88 from inlet pressure 90 outlet pressure 92 vacuum 99 temperature 101 and flow 102 produce signals to pump 18 and valve 96 to control cavitation to provide an optimum process"}, {"pat_id": "US-8398733-B2", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the compressor chamber 3 is completely separated from the mixing chamber 2 by bottom panel 9 for preventing hot air penetration from compressor chamber 3 into the air mixing chamber 2 which can result in changes of predetermined temperature regimes of the condenser and evaporator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200470242-Y1", "para_id": "