ate greater than said trickling mode"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a solenoid actuated valve is mounted to the conduit downstream of the inlet and is in a normally closed state to prevent the passage of liquid therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102912417-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the hot air drying unit is characterized by including a body part having an inlet hopper for introducing sludge through the sludge discharge unit storing the sludge and discharging it to the sludge transfer unit through an outlet a transfer screw member rotatably provided on the body part and transferring the sludge through a spiral blade a power unit provided at an end of the transfer screw member to provide driving force and a hot air supply unit provided around the periphery of the body part to supply hot air to heat and dry the sludge stored in the body part.the sludge drying device of a sewage treatment plant according to the present invention compresses sludge stored in a sludge storage tank at high pressure to discharge moisture as much as possible thereby primarily lowering the moisture content and secondarily drying the discharged sludge by mixing it while applying high temperature hot air thereby lowering the moisture content of the sludge as much as possible and enabling recycling.figure 1 is a configuration diagram of a sludge drying device of a sewage treatment plant according to one embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200375794-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "by stopping the heating operation of the heater 5 to heat the heat meter so that the water meter 1 does not freeze to prevent freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the heating system to prevent freezing of the pipe for fire extinguishing water in the tunnel a power control panel for controlling heating power a three phase heating cable installed on the outer circumferential surface along the main pipe drawn out from the power control panel and disposed in the longitudinal direction of the tunnel a power supply wire drawn out from the power control panel and wired in parallel with the main pipe a wire tray installed in parallel with the main pipe and housing the electric power supply wires a single phase heating cable installed in a branch pipe branched from the main pipe and branched from the electric power supply wire to receive heating power and it includes first and second temperature sensors that are disposed on one side of the main pipe and one side of the branch pipe located at the exit or inlet side of the tunnel to obtain first temperature information and second temperature information the power control panel is to control the output of the heating power for each of the three phase heating cable for the three phase heating cable and the single phase heating cable according to the first and second temperature information to prevent freezing of the pipe for fire extinguishing water in the tunnel dual heating system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "dual heating system to prevent freezing of receiving piping"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102109022-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the problem to be solved by the present invention is a heating system for preventing freezing of pipes for extinguishing water in a tunnel comprising a power control panel for controlling heating power a three phase heating cable installed on the outer circumferential surface along the main pipe drawn out from the power control panel and disposed in the longitudinal direction of the tunnel a power supply wire drawn out from the power control panel and wired in parallel with the main pipe a wire tray installed parallel to the main piping and receiving electric power supply wires a single phase heating cable installed in a branch pipe branched from the main pipe and branched from a power supply wire to receive heating power and first and second temperature sensors arrange