of the raw water inlet and allowing raw water to be heated to supply steam to the upper portion an aluminum sacrificial anode made of aluminum and installed above the raw water inlet of the main body to prevent corrosion by raw water introduced by applying an electric current an s shaped combustion tube which is installed from the lower part of the main body to the upper part and is installed to be in contact with the raw water introduced from the raw water inlet a burner installed at an upper end of the combustion tube to change steam into superheated steam a demister installed at an upper end of the main body to remove moisture contained in the heated superheated steam from the burner connected to the demister is supplied with steam to remove moisture and installed to communicate with the upper end of the combustion tube heated by the burner to remove the superheated steam with supercritical temperature to the superheated steam having an air inlet is provided with a high temperature oxidation unit for high temperature oxidation of the superheated steam having a supercritical temperature a condenser connected to the high temperature oxidation unit and installed at a lower side of the combustion tube to condense superheated steam supplied from the high temperature oxidation unit to form water a cooling coil connected to the condenser and heat exchanged with the raw water flowing into the main body to cool the high temperature oxidized pure water a plate installed between the condenser and the cooling coil to prevent heat exchange between the condenser and the cooling coil and a pure water storage tank installed at a lower end of the main body and connected to the cooling coil to store the pure water which is cooled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100756497-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "as shown the pure water manufacturing apparatus according to the present invention is a vertical cylindrical body 10 is provided with a raw water inlet 11 the heat transfer sheet 12 of the carbon fiber is installed on the bottom of the raw water inlet 11 the superheated steam of the aluminum sacrificial anode 20 to prevent corrosion by raw water the s shaped combustion tube 30 is installed from the lower portion of the main body 10 to the upper portion and the steam converted by the heat transfer sheet 12 burner 40 to be converted into a furnace a demister 50 for removing moisture contained in superheated steam and an air inlet 61 which is heated by the burner 40 to provide high temperature oxidation to superheat the superheated steam"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972507-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "by circulating a portion of the treated water the concentration reaction time is shortened and the concentration reaction while the heating temperature of the treated water is maintained the treated water of the concentrated reaction tank is introduced into the heat exchanger again so that the heated treated water of the acid wastewater flowing in contact with the outside of the coiled inner tube into which the acidic wastewater is introduced"}, {"pat_id": "US-10156321-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the method recognizes that impurities in the carbon dioxide stream change the phase behavior and fluid transport properties of the carbon dioxide effluent and that a variation of contaminant levels in the flow stream under an identical inlet pressure and temperature scenario may lead to the formation of two phase flow within the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11229143-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore the high temperature first working liquid 51 passing through the first fluid pipeline 191 in adjacency to the first liquid inlet 11 can more effectively quickly and uniformly contact and mix with the agent"}, {"pat_id": "US-7951298-B2", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "the reason the real time orp numbers rose so dramatically at the fw heater exit was most likely because of the corrosion that had occurred in the fw heater itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100718246-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 the inlet means a winch positioned in the other manhole to insert the folded liner located in the manhole on one side into the buried pipe a wire connected at one end to the winch and at the other end to a liner and mobile device that can move along the inside of the buried pipe to connect the wire connected to the winch to the liner deformation tube insertion method for preventing deformation due to temperature changes including"}, {"pat_id": "US-7713399-B2", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "the process preferably starts with spent caustic at a moderate temperature from the storage tank that can require pre heating or cooling to reach a preferred 25 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-9850152-B2", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "water will also absorb ir and the temperature will be raised a factor which will again shifts the equilibrium more towards the caco3 precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101758303-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the method or process may include moving the hydrolyzed sludge to the bottom of the heat exchanger to provide sludge to sludge heat transfer to efficiently heat the sludge into which the hydrolyzed sludge has been introduced or dehydrated and moving the sludge upward through the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100966852-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it has a configuration in which a pressure relief valve is installed to be discharged to the outside to close the exhaust port.as described above according to the freeze protection device of the water pipe of the present invention by operating the hydraulic cylinder with a small amount of water flowing out according to the external temperature change and the force of the water the freeze with the water discharged through the operation of the cylinder effectively also by replacing the capacity of the hydraulic cylinder only it is possible to secure as much water as possible to prevent freezing at any water pipe size or water pressure and more precisely by controlling the amount of discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_197", "text": "however the salinity of salt water industrial brine 202 that enters freezing desalination cell unit enclosure 271 via salt water industrial brine inlet 275 also has influence on the freezing process the higher the salt concentration the lower the necessary freezing temperature to be accomplished"}, {"pat_id": "US-7404899-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "6 200 466 describes a reactor system for decontamination of water by photolytic oxidation utilizing near blackbody radiation the system comprising 1 a reaction chamber defining an internal space with an inlet and an outlet and 2 a broadband radiator for generating radiant energy with wavelengths between about 150 nm and about 3 um the broadband radiator disposed within the reaction chamber such that a sufficient dosage of broadband radiation irradiates the contaminants and or the oxidant within the internal space of the reaction chamber thereby causing photolytic oxidation of the contaminants by direct action of the radiation on the contaminants to break chemical bonds by sustaining a free radical chain reaction of oxidizing components thus breaking down the contaminants by way of atomic abstraction of the components of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-7404899-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "6 117 335 describes a reactor system for decontamination of water by photolytic oxidation utilizing near blackbody radiation the system comprising 1 a reaction chamber defining an internal space with an inlet and an outlet and 2 a broadband radiator for generating radiant energy with wavelengths between 150 nm and about 3 \u03bcm the broadband radiator disposed within the reaction chamber such that a sufficient dosage of broadband radiation irradiates the contaminants and or the oxidant within the internal space of the reaction chamber thereby causing photolytic oxidation of the contaminants by way of atomic abstraction of the components of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102030301-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the back plate 208 may have a terminal block not shown or other type of electrical connections for removably connecting the electronic brick 206 to the back plate 208"}, {"pat_id": "US-9718717-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "therefore the dimensions of the reactor will have to be relatively large in order to carry out in a first phase the heating at carbonization temperature then in a second phase the carbonization"}, {"pat_id": "US-9718717-B2", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "by measuring q flow rate t inlet t outlet for one of the two fluids and dt that is to say a calculation between the inlet and outlet temperatures of each product k is deduced therefrom which if it decreases is a sign of fouling which is also measured in other terms by the fact that it is necessary to raise the temperature of the oil in order to reach the same final temperature that is to say to increase the dt in order to have the same q since k decreases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100342599-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "during the ultrasonic sterilization a heat jacket 25 for circulating a cooling water was attached to the outside of the sterilization reactor in order to remove the generated heat because heat is generated due to the cavitation phenomenon of ultrasonic waves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102651073-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a first suction blower an ultraviolet light source that decomposes volatile organic compounds vocs in the air by irradiating ultraviolet rays to the air passing through the blower a titanium dioxide net that decomposes voc contained in the air passing through the blower again a first plasma reactor that creates ozone water by passing some of the air that has passed through the titanium dioxide net generating ozone using atmospheric pressure plasma and introducing it into the water of the water tank a water electrolysis device that supplies power to the anode and cathode submerged in water of the water tank to cause electrolysis to generate oxygen and hydrogen a hydrogen collector that collects hydrogen generated from the cathode a second plasma reactor that generates hydrogen ions using atmospheric pressure plasma from hydrogen supplied through a first connection pipe connected to the hydrogen collector a second suction blower that sucks hydrogen ions through a second connection pipe connected to the second plasma reactor and introduces them into the water of the water tank and a display that controls the fresh air supply and displays power supply temperature humidity dust amount and oxygen amount"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101467204-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the air at room temperature is sent to the cooling exchanger 8 in the means for producing the dry air through the air inlet 9 where the water is condensed and separated and then the heat exchanger 6 and is heated in the heat exchanger to become unsaturated dry air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130731-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an automatic cleaning unit for cleaning the foreign matter attached wherein the uv treatment unit uv lamp unit for irradiating the ultraviolet light to the filtered water in the filtering unit a washing unit for removing the foreign matter attached to the ultraviolet lamp unit and the ultraviolet ray uv intensity meter for measuring the intensity of ultraviolet light from the lamp and on temperature for measuring the temperature inside the body including a sensor it can prevent secondary pollution due to by products prevent contamination of tanks efficient and easy to maintain sterilization effect and product miniaturization and an integrated water treatment device using an ultraviolet lamp"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6679439-B2", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "monitoring of water permeability coefficient in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the storage tank 41 for collecting odors 72 a stirrer 51 which is charged for the fermentation and decomposition treatment of the food waste a to be evenly supplied and stirred by the stirring blade 511 together with the microorganism and the wood chip 512 a nozzle 52 for spraying washing water b at a predetermined temperature for washing to prevent anaerobically progressing due to the saccharide enzyme microorganism carcass and the like and to provide aerobic condition a driving motor 54 for rotating the agitation blade 511 of the wooden chip and a driving motor 54 for driving the agitation blade 511 the nozzle 52 the oxygen generator 53 a liquid phase fermentation decomposition unit 50 including a control unit 55 that is electrically connected to the motor 54 and controls it a sedimentation tank 61 for precipitating and separating the effluent c obtained by the liquid fermentation decomposition treatment so as to separate and collect the effluent c as waste water d and solid matter e or a centrifugal separator 62 for rotating and separating the effluent c 60 the separated and collected wastewater d is purified by chemical biological and physical treatments to separate the solid e the solid e1 the nitrogen n and the phosphorus p a purification treatment unit 70 having an adjustment tank 72 an anaerobic tank 73 an anoxic tank 74 an aerobic tank 75 a biological sedimentation tank 76 and a filtration tank 77 the collected and collected solid matter e microbial solids e1 and meat fish and cereal shaped material f for the balance of insufficient nutrient balance are added through the automatic weighing hopper 81 0.0 gt c lt rti gt for 20 to 60 minutes a feed fermentation unit 90 which is charged with the sterilized humidified mixed feed and fermented in the fermenter 91 for 2 to 5 days to produce a functional feed g a feed dryer 100 for feeding the functional feed g and drying in the dryer 101 a feedstock storage tank 1104 for storing the dried functional food g a descendant 1101 for loading the feedstock into the delivery vehicle 1103 to supply the feedstock to the feedstock in a nonpackaged state or in a packed state and a feed packing section 110 having a feed packing machine 1102 for feeding the feed in units of a unit of weight wherein the functional feed and the liquid fertilizer lt rti gt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "from the food waste a fed into the casing 311 having an inlet and an outlet formed therein a crushing section 30 a storage tank 41 for continuously feeding a predetermined amount of the selected food waste a while storing the selected food waste a a second hood 41 disposed above the storage tank 41 for collecting odors 72 a stirrer 51 which is charged for the fermentation and decomposition treatment of the food waste a to be evenly supplied and stirred by the stirring blade 511 together with the microorganism and the wood chip 512 a nozzle 52 for spraying washing water b at a predetermined temperature for washing to prevent anaerobically progressing due to the saccharide enzyme microorganism carcass and the like and to provide aerobic condition a driving motor 54 for rotating the agitation blade 511 of the wooden chip and a driving motor 54 for driving the agitation blade 511 the nozzle 52 the oxygen generator 53 a liquid phase fermentation decomposition unit 50 including a control unit 55 that is electrically connected to the motor 54 and controls it a sedimentation tank 61 for precipitating and separating the effluent c obtained by the liquid fermentation decomposition treatment so as to separate and collect the effluent c as waste water d and solid matter e or a centrifugal separator 62 for rotating and separating the effluent c 60 the separated and collected wastewater d is purified by chemical biological and physical treatments to separate the solid e the solid e1 the nitrogen n and the phosphorus p a purification treatment unit 70 having an adjustment tank 72 an anaerobic tank 73 an anoxic tank 74 an aerobic tank 75 a biological sedimentation tank 76 and a filtration tank 77 the collected and collected solid matter e microbial solids e1 and meat fish and cereal shaped material f for the balance of insufficient nutrient balance are added through the automatic weighing hopper 81 0.0 gt c lt rti gt for 20 to 60 minutes a feed fermentation unit 90 which is charged with the sterilized humidified mixed feed and fermented in the fermenter 91 for 2 to 5 days to produce a functional feed g a feed dryer 100 for feeding the functional feed g and drying in the dryer 101 a feedstock storage tank 1104 for storing the dried functional food g a descendant 1101 for loading the feedstock into the delivery vehicle 1103 to supply the feedstock to the feedstock in a nonpackaged state or in a packed state and a feed packing section 110 having a feed packing machine 1102 for feeding the feed in units of a unit of weight wherein the functional feed and the liquid fertilizer the object of which is achieved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519079-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "the scope of the present invention is defined by the appended claims rather than the detailed description and all changes or modifications derived from the meaning and scope of the claims and their equivalents are to be construed as being included within the scope of the present invention do.100 variable operation part 110 pollutant selection unit 120 measurement part flow rate temperature electrical conductivity monitoring 130 model prediction control unit 131 model input unit 132 first numerical analysis operation section 133 second numerical analysis operation section 134 model output section 140 141 operation pressure error calculating section 142 150 variable operation control unit 210 inlet water storage tank 220 standard processing process execution unit 230 first transfer pipe 240 control valve 250 water treatment membrane nanofilter or reverse osmosis filter 260 pressurizing pump 270 second transfer pipe 280 final treated water storage tank 300 contaminant database"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102452662-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "flow control tank 1 anaerobic tank 2 for removing phosphorus in the water to be treated flowing in from the flow rate control tank 1 an anaerobic tank 3 for removing nitrate nitrogen in the treated water flowing in from the anaerobic tank 2 an aerobic tank 4 for nitrifying nitrogen by aeration of air into the water to be treated introduced from the anoxic tank 3 a fenton oxidation unit 10 for fenton oxidation treatment of the water to be treated flowing in from the aerobic tank 4 a sedimentation tank 5 for separating the water to be treated from the fenton oxidation unit 10 into a supernatant and sludge a high temperature sterilization unit 20 for high temperature sterilization of the water to be treated by heat exchange a flotation filtration tank 1000 having an inlet 1010 into which the wtbt is introduced a flotation filtration device 1020 mounted on the wtbt inlet space 1040 and a discharge part 1030 from which the wtbt is discharged and circulation guide part 40 for guiding the water to be treated in the inlet space 1040 of the flotation filtration tank 1000 to the flotation filtration device 1020 the fenton oxidation unit 10 a reaction tank 100 having a reaction space therein a wastewater supply unit 200 provided to supply wastewater fenton oxide supply unit 300 provided to supply the fenton oxide a main supply unit 400 provided to supply the wastewater and fenton oxide supplied from the wastewater supply unit 200 and the fenton oxide supply unit 300 to the reactor 100 the crystals 500 are located in a large amount in the reaction space 110 of the reaction tank 100 and are provided to attach the sludge generated in the reaction process while flowing in the wastewater supplied from the main supply unit 400 a treated water discharge unit 600 provided to discharge the treated water treated in the reaction tank 100 a sediment discharge unit 700 provided for discharging precipitated sludge among sludge generated in the reaction process in the reaction tank 100 a circulation unit 800 provided to circulate a portion of the treated water treated in the reaction space unit 110 to the main supply unit 400 and and a fenton filter membrane 900 provided to prevent the crystals 500 of the reaction space 110 from being discharged to the treated water discharge unit 600 the circulation unit 800 a circulation pipe 810 having an inlet end connected to the reactor 100 and an outlet end connected to the main supply unit 400 the circulation pump 820 is for supplying a portion of the treated water to the lower end of the reaction space 110 through the circulation pipe 810 and is supplied to the lower end of the reaction space 110 by the main supply unit 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100557743-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "a protective container formed with a heat insulating layer solidified by filling a stirred ocher mortar with a mixture of an aqueous solution of a curing agent was formed while being buried while accommodating a water meter thereby increasing the insulation and heat storage performance and the strength and durability of the structure caused by changes in earth pressure and temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100557743-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a protective container formed with a heat insulating layer solidified by filling a stirred ocher mortar with a mixture of an aqueous solution of a curing agent was formed while being buried while accommodating a water meter thereby increasing the insulation and heat storage performance and the strength and durability of the structure caused by changes in earth pressure and temperature it can prevent deformation"}]</data>
