  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drainage tank that has a function to prevent the inflow of pests etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133174-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in the untreated water inlet line 20 may be provided with a transfer pump 60 for pumping and supplying untreated water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101560279-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage tank for mixing storages of fresh water and fresh water a main body 100 on which a fine flow path 200 is formed the top side of which is flown out and and is formed as a lower settled space relative to the clearance passage 200 so as to be formed on the clearance passage 200 and to deposit only the initial clearance of the clearance moving in the clearance passage 200 an initial fine precipitation tank 300 the upper part of the bleed passage 200 is opened a baffle wall 400 is formed around the baffle 200 so as to prevent escape of the baffle introduced onto the baffle 200 one side of the escape prevention wall 400 is connected to the end of the roof 500 so that the storm that flows along the slope of the roof 500 of the house can be introduced into the clearance passage 200 the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the main flow path 110 lt rti gt the downflow channel is formed along the flow direction of the stormwater a first space 121 and a second space 122 that divides the inner space of the main body 100 into a first space 121 and a second space 122 123 are formed on the partition wall 120 the overflow passage 123 is formed at a predetermined distance from the lower surface of the main body 100 the storm inlet 110 is formed on the storeroom 200 where the first space 121 is located and a fresh water inlet 140 formed in the second space 122 and into which fresh water flows into the second space 122 and a mixed water outlet 150 formed in the second space 122 and mixed with water mixed with fresh water and fresh water stored in the second space 122 to be discharged to the outside of the main body 100 the mixed water outlet 150 is formed below the fresh water inlet 140 when the water level of the mixed water is lower than the position of the fresh water inlet 140 the fresh water inlet 140 is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "thus it is composed of one set including a control panel that moves the sewage in the sewage tank along the sewage discharge path and discharges it through the sewage discharge pipe one set of sewage treatment equipment is installed one or more depending on the installation area the air supply path includes an air supply pipe installed between the air storage tank and the first end of the three way valve and an air inlet pipe installed between the second end of the three way valve and the sewage tank the control panel operates the compressor to supply the air in the air storage tank to the sewage tank through the air supply pipe the first and second ends of the three way valve and the air inlet pipe a regulator set is installed in the air supply pipe the regulator set includes a regulator for discharging air from the air storage tank to a preset pressure it further comprises at least one of a filter for removing moisture and impurities contained in the air from the air storage tank and an oil removal unit for removing oil contained in the air from the air storage tank the sewage auxiliary tank is installed in the sewage inflow path to remove the bubbles inside the sewage auxiliary tank to prevent the operation of the sewage treatment device due to the inflow of bubbles into the sewage tank when the control panel receives a notification of reaching the lowest water level from the water level sensor it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete it is counted after the operation of discharging the sewage from the sewage tank is performed and when a preset time elapses it is determined that the sewage discharge is complete when the discharge of sewage in the sewage tank is completed the knife valve installed on the sewage inflow path is controlled to be in an open state to open the sewage inflow path so that the sewage is moved to the sewage tank through the sewage inflow path and the three way valve of the air inlet and outlet installed on the air supply path is controlled so that the second end of the three way valve on the sewage tank side and the third end of the air discharge pipe are in an open state and the first end of the air storage tank side control to be closed to move the air in the sewage tank along the air discharge path and discharge it through the air discharge pipe after receiving the notification of reaching the highest water level and performing the operation of discharging wastewater when the notification of reaching the lowest water level is not notified from the water level sensor even after a predetermined time has elapsed after receiving the notification of the notification of reaching the highest water level a warning message to a preset terminal sewage treatment device characterized in that for transmitting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837300-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel portion for guiding water to move in a predetermined direction an infiltration inducing pipe portion penetrating through the bottom surface of the water channel portion and communicating with an underground aquifer below the impermeable layer in the ground layer a filtering unit installed at a connection portion between the infiltration induction pipe and the water channel unit and composed of several layers for removing foreign matter from water flowing into the underground aquifer and having a lower porosity toward the lower layer and and an opening closing part for selectively shielding the infiltration induction tube part the water a sediment guiding part having a guide protrud