or of the level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171325-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "on the other hand the present invention detects the water level difference between the water inlet ip and the water outlet op into which the sewage and waste water flows and when the water level is higher than the set water level the rapid lifting and removing process according to the rpm control of the drive motor 1 is automatically controlled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321349-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as in the conventional case it is possible to detect the amount of water introduced through the inlet by using a flow meter but the flow meter has a high price and the zero point is inaccurate due to corrosion and breakage causing problems in performance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309643-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the bad smell source sucked by operating the blower 2 in the operation panel 15 is inside the first carrier storage chamber 5 1 via the vacancy 4 1 in order to facilitate the flow of air through the inlet 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is higher than the minimum value opening the three way valve so that the water of the second tank is supplied through the downpipe and connected to the supply pipe and preventing the water of the first tank from being supplied to the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is higher than the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe purified in the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joined from the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joined including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so that the charge level of the battery is lower than the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is below the minimum value turning on the three way valve to connect the other discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is above the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe passes through the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joins the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joins including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 if the charge level of the battery is below the minimum value the above energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system is a greenhouse having a rainwater receiver a first tank at the bottom connected to the rainwater receiver through a collection pipe and a second tank at the top of the first tank wherein the discharge pipe of the first tank is connected to a water pump and an ascending pipe extends upward from the water pump and communicates with the inlet of the second tank so that rainwater stored in the first tank is supplied to the second tank above by the operation of the water pump and a descending pipe which is a discharge pipe of the second tank extends downward to near the ground and near the first tank an inlet port is connected to another discharge pipe 10a of the first tank and the descending pipe of the second tank and an outlet port is connected to a supply pipe connected to a supply pipe that extends into the greenhouse and supplies water to plants inside the greenhouse and a three way valve is installed and a branch pipe branches off from the upstream of the supply pipe and is connected to a sterilizing water generator via a quantitative pump and the outlet of the sterilizing water generator is it is connected to a merging pipe and the merging pipe joins the supply pipe at a position downstream from the branch pipe so that the sterilizing water generator manufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080805-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "meanwhile the high concentration overflow water storage tank 220 is provided at the front end of the low concentration overflow water storage tank 230 and the reason for placing the location of the high concentration overflow water inlet 211 below the low concentration overflow water inlet 212 may be due to a high contaminant concentration of the initial overflow water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101915884-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the driving unit 231 is driven at the upper portion and a lifting type water gate 230 vertically lifted and lowered according to the measured water level of the water level meter 300 the watertight housing 210 allows the water to be dewatered to the height of the watertight housing 210 at the ultraviolet sterilizer 100 at a normal time in the control unit 400 when the discharge water level corresponding to the height below the height of the water gate housing 210 is detected in the measurement of the ultrasonic level meter 300 the water gate 230 is completely accommodated in the water receiving groove 211 and when the discharged water level above the height of the water gate housing 210 is sensed the water gate 230 is elevated to a height corresponding to the discharged water level to reduce the flow rate of discharged water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959915-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore since the inlet 113a is installed spaced apart from the bottom of the wetland 10 the wetland 10 can always maintain a constant water level to function as the wetland 10 and also the water of the wetland 10 when this is drained the sediment deposited on the bottom of the wetland 10 can be prevented from being sucked toward the inlet 113a side as well as the habitat of the fish by amber and gravel and reverse contact oxidation by amber and gravel it is possible to purify 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102713396-B1", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "fourth by forming the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit evaporator 2 1 2 and the circulation water between the salt separation tank 5 1 and the salt separation unit concentrated water circulating water ejector 7 1 2 and controlling the residence time of the concentrated water flowing out of the concentrated water tank 15 1 supercooling and the formation of fine ice seed water in the salt separation tank 5 1 were promoted thereby reinforcing the formation and growth of the brine water containing organic and inorganic substances contained in the influent into an ice slurry"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "air sludge deposited on the wall and the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration portion contact oxidation tank and the precipitation contact oxidation tank transfer to the sludge storage tank through the shaft but one side of the sludge storage tank and the supernatant water storage tank partitioned by the operation of the full width bank installed in the inlet distribution tank and the outflow storage tank and prevented from being closed by the sludge while being discharged from the inside of the contact oxidation tank at least one selected from the group consisting of an acid pipe for supplying dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to water and crushed stone having a porosity of 30 to 40 or plastic having a porosity of 80 or more in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and the settling part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the inlet 1 has a circular or rectangular shape as a part for collecting the polluted river water and sewage the effluent from the sewage treatment facility to flow into the contact oxidation tank and has a movable bank in the inlet distribution tank 2 18 weir is installed and the flow rate in the inlet distribution tank 2 is kept constant by adjusting the water level using the movable bank 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100977056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this case even if there is an error the manager does not immediately check this and because it is confirmed in the process of checking the control panel there is a problem in pumping operation.the present invention solves the problem of installing the case by welding on the upper casing of the well while alleviating the water shock phenomenon in which the pressure rises or falls due to the rapid flow rate changes inside the pump pipe and also pumping pressure it solves the problem of inadequate disinfection of groundwater by supplying chlorine from outside when the set value is reached and the control panel checks the change of internal pressure of the pump along with the water level of the well in the meantime if an abnormality occurs in the groundwater pumping the manager is immediately notified to take action.the present invention inserts the packing cap on the upper side of the out casing the outer side of the case is fitted to the outside of the packing cap while the inner side of the case is supported by the upper portion of the packing cap the case the wire inlet and pump pipe connector while fixing the cover to the upper side the inside of the case to install a flexible pipe connected to the pump and the water shock protector and a pressure valve the flexible pipe is a meter installed in the meter case through the meter connector and ground water passing through the meter is discharged after being mixed with the chlorine of the quantity supplied from the chlorine injector and the ground water pump and the chlorine pump by detecting the water level of the well and the water pressure and the amount of chlorine control the operation and notify the administrator wirelessly when an error occurs it will be written by providing the urban"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100523856-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "an integrated automatic control unit 300a connected to the apparatus unit and the automatic sewage treatment unit to check manipulate and manage the measurement data of the water tank and the sewage treatment plant an integrated display unit 360a for displaying the measured data measured by the respective sensor units so as to be distinguishable monitoring and control unit 420a for monitoring and controlling the pollution state of rivers and rivers supplying water supply and sewage by connecting the integrated automatic control unit distributed in various areas through a network a database unit 430a for storing measurement data of the obtained quantity and quality of each region state information of each part and administrator information receives the measurement data of the quantity and water quality of each area from a remote place and transmits the control signal of the monitoring control unit to the water tank automatic control unit the sewage treatment automatic control unit or the integrated automatic control unit and transmits to the external linkage engine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100984372-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "rain gutters 20 including a rain box 40 communicating with the first outlet hole 21b of the rain gutter through a connecting pipe 30 to store rainwater flowing into the rain gutter it includes a rooftop excellent induction pipe 2 for leading the rainwater collected on the roof of the building around the road to the rain gutter the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar in the driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility comprising an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge a sleeve 51 having the same size as the thickness of the bottom of the rain gutter main body and inserted into an insertion hole formed in the bottom of the rain gutter main body a perforated pipe 50 inserted into the sleeve so as to communicate with the inside of the rain gutter and installed by a filling material filled in the bottom of the rain gutter and penetrating the rainwater stored in the rain gutter into the ground a valve installed at an inlet side of the hole tube to adjust an opening degree of the hole tube driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility characterized in that it comprises a filter 52 is attached to the filter mounting portion 21c formed concave at the bottom of the rain gutter to remove the foreign matter from the rainwater flowing into the hole"}]</data>
