  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drainage tank that has a function to prevent the inflow of pests etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object in a drainage tank configured to introduce and discharge sewage such as rain and sewage of daily life and to prevent the discharge of odors generated therein or the introduction of mice and pests accommodating sewage inside a main body having an inlet space an upper inlet part having an open upper part to introduce wastewater a side inlet part for introducing wastewater on one side and a discharge part for discharging the wastewater accommodated in the inflow space on the other side a blocking means having a blocking net seated on the main body to block foreign substances in the sewage and a vertical pipe for introducing the sewage into the inflow space and a moving pipe that moves up and down according to the level of sewage in the inflow space on the vertical pipe to block odors or prevent rats and pests from entering and is formed integrally or separately on the moving pipe to generate buoyancy according to the level of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275853-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "it may further include a chamber 1000 having.according to the present invention only the initial excellent water can be separated and efficiently treated to fine contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in rainy weather sewage such as soil fallen leaves and vinyl flows into the sewers indiscriminately but there is no separate facility to prevent them.these dirts block the flow of rainwater by blocking the inflow of the rain gutters or the inlet of the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101229485-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "to quickly drain without it being not cause any inconvenience caused to traffic and flooded with traffic accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101230730-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "according to the present invention as described above while planting vegetation on the side of the vegetation soil while water is continuously supplied to the vegetation through the water storage unit and the water supply surface rain water in the water storage unit through the water supply path formed in rain water by allowing heavy water to be filled such as eco friendly and continuous supply of moisture to the vegetation without additional management work it is very easy to maintain and manage the vegetation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178211-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "to quickly drain without it being not cause any inconvenience caused to traffic and flooded with traffic accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "a drainage inlet 411 may be formed on the upper surface of the contaminant removal device 49"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "the rainwater on the road surface 1 flows through the inlet port 411 and falls to the upper side of the water permeable filter agent 493 to remove the contaminants adhering to the lower side of the screen net 492 and the water permeable filter agent 493 the drainage of the rainwater can be smoothly performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102768687-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of adjustment tanks 1 including a first adjustment tank a plurality of second adjustment tanks and a third adjustment tank each adjustment tank including an inlet valve 11 for controlling the opening and closing of an inlet port through which sewage flows in and an outlet valve 12 for controlling the opening and closing of an outlet port through which sewage flows out a chimney valve 2 for controlling the communication between adjacent control units a control unit 4 that controls the above inlet valve outlet valve and flue valve and a distribution unit 5 that distributes sewage flowing out from the above plurality of adjustment tanks to a sewage treatment facility and or a simple treatment facility including the above control unit controls the communication valve so that all of the plurality of adjustment tanks are connected in normal times when sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility does not flow in and when sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility flows in due to rain the communication valve is controlled so that the third adjustment tank is not connected to the remaining adjustment tanks and as the amount of sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility increases the number of second adjustment tanks that are not connected to the first adjustment tank but are connected to the third adjustment tank increases and the communication valve is controlled so that the number of second adjustment tanks that are not connected to the first adjustment tank but are connected to the third adjustment tank increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102768687-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the above control unit is a contaminant removal device characterized in that when sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility is introduced due to all adjustment tanks or rain the control unit controls the activated sludge supply unit and the coagulant supply unit so that the activated sludge and coagulant are supplied only to the third adjustment tank and the second adjustment tank connected to the third adjustment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100837429-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the hinge portion 18 is provided with a protruding bent portion 19 formed in the inlet portion of the arm hinge piece 16a provided on one side thinner than the thickness of the arm hinge piece 16a and provided on the other side 16b is the other end is blocked in the state in which the fixing pin 17 is penetrated through the female hinge piece 16a 16b and the hydraulic hinge piece 7 by bending the protruding bent portion 19 to the inside the odor prevention device for rain gutter collection well characterized in that the through inserted fixing pin 17 is separated to the outside to prevent the hinge portion 18 from being separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100837429-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "covered on the top to prevent separation in the assembled state the upper plate has a plurality of inlet holes perforated at regular intervals and the inclined plate welded inclined inwardly on both sides of the lower surface of the upper cover plate each of the inclined plates is provided with a movable plate which is opened and closed at a predetermined angle by rain or sewage loads and both side surfaces of the inclined plate are integrally welded with inverted triangular side screening plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100837429-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "covered on the top to prevent separation in the assembled state the upper plate has a plurality of inlet holes perforated at regular intervals and the inclined plate welded inclined inwardly on both sides of the lower surface of the upper cover plate each of the inclined plates is provided with a movable plate which is opened and closed at a predetermined angle by rain or sewage loads and both side surfaces of the inclined plate are integrally welded with inverted triangular side screening plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100837429-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "covered on the top to prevent separation in the assembled state the upper plate has a plurality of inlet holes perforated at regular intervals and the inclined plate welded inclined inwardly on both sides of the lower surface of the upper cover plate each of the inclined plates is provided with a movable plate which is opened and closed at a predetermined angle by rain or sewage loads and both side surfaces of the inclined plate are integrally welded with inverted triangular side screening plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100837429-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "5 is fixed to the lower support plate 2 the lower portion is in the shape of a rectangular shaped lid is covered in the upper portion of the lower support plate 2 is to prevent the separation in the assembled state and the upper plate 12 upper cover plate 11 having two inlet holes 23 perforated at predetermined intervals and an inclined plate 25a welded downwardly inwardly to both sides of the upper surface plate 12 of the upper cover plate 11 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "the upper plate 60 is installed on the upper end of the block 50 but by using the own weight of the upper plate 60 the upper tank 60 is seated and fixed on the upper end of the uppermost connecting block 50 thereby closing the vertical water tank 1a is formed s240 and finally the rain inlet pipe 64 is coupled to the inlet pipe coupling hole 61 formed in the upper plate 60 and then in the same position as the ground as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in the bollard type hot water leak detection panel protector according to an embodiment of the present invention the rain rain water of the intake port 130 to prevent the inflow into the housing 110 through the inlet 130 the inlet port 140 formed in the housing 110 to cover the inlet port 130 at the upper side and the rainwater can be prevented from being introduced into the housing 110 through the exhaust port 150"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "the upper plate 60 is installed on the upper end of the block 50 but by using the own weight of the upper plate 60 the upper tank 60 is seated and fixed on the upper end of the uppermost connecting block 50 thereby closing the vertical water tank 1a is formed s240 and finally the rain inlet pipe 64 is coupled to the inlet pipe coupling hole 61 formed in the upper plate 60 and then in the same position as the ground as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100916003-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "however the existing sewage odor prevention device as described above is to block some of the water flow area of the rain gutter inlet to reduce the original function of collecting rainwater on the road surface flowing to the sewer pipe and also produced uniformly in the factory there was a problem that it is difficult to use publicly in the field where rain gutters of different sizes and shapes are used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060724-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the sewage on the ground may be introduced into the rainwater toil chamber 100 by being led to the upper inlet 110 by the water barrier 102 after the contaminants are removed by the contaminant screen 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "at this time the rain inlet 32 may be formed in the upper plate 30 as described above but formed on the upper end of the outer wall block 20 that is the outer wall according to the rain storage tank 1 of the present invention buried underground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101221721-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "by preventing the inflow of the river has the effect of preventing the contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switc