cting duct 30 connected to a circumference of the main collecting box in fluid communication with the main collecting box and collecting rainwater to guide the inside of the main collecting box it is installed in the auxiliary inlet formed in the upper portion of the auxiliary water collecting duct includes an auxiliary grating 40 for opening and closing the auxiliary inlet the auxiliary grating may be installed to be rotatable in the rectangular frame through the rotary shaft 42a while being arranged in line with the rectangular frame 41 and the rectangular frame installed in communication with the auxiliary inlet formed on the upper portion of the auxiliary collecting duct"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101051778-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "here the rain permeable layer 240 and the base layer 260 is made of a material having voids during filling such as sand so that when the foreign material blocking member 270 is not provided inlet 130 and outlet 140 may be blocked for example by sand first or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101051778-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "as described above the storm storage block 100 is formed in a smaller number than the inlet opening 130 and has a discharge port 140 for discharging the amount of rain that is less than the amount of rain that flows into the body 110 each unit cell rainwater may be temporarily stored inside c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this configuration although it consumes electrical energy and requires installation of a separate sensor motor and controller the initial rainwater inlet 61 of the initial rainwater storage unit 60 is clogged with contaminants or the initial rainwater storage unit even if the initial rainfall is not stored due to breakage of 60 the storm guide unit 50 may be driven as a driving source based on the information detected from the sensor thereby storing the storm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 having an upper inlet 11 and a sewage inlet 12 for introducing rain or sewage into the inside of the above mentioned ground 1 and having an outlet 13 for discharging the introduced rain or sewage the upper plate 21 is installed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 and has a plurality of through holes 21a for rain or sewage to be introduced so as to be adjustable to block the inflow or discharge of foul odors caused by rain or sewage the lower plate 22 is formed with a discharge groove 22a and a foul odor blocking groove 22b intersectingly while being in close contact with the lower part of the upper plate 21 a central hole 23 penetrating the center of the upper plate 21 a long hole 24 penetrating the center of the lower plate 22 and a fastening bolt 25a that penetrates the central hole 23 of the upper plate 21 and the long hole 24 of the lower plate 22 and fastens with a nut 25b so as to align the discharge groove 22a or the foul odor blocking groove 22b of the lower plate 22 from the through hole 21a of the upper plate 21 to prevent the discharge or discharge of rain or sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in the first paragraph the above main body 10 is characterized by having a filter net 14 further provided inside to filter and remove foreign substances that have entered through the upper inlet 11 and the sewage inlet 12 and is a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage without foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage and allowing smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves the present invention relates to a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage free from foreign substances such as fallen leaves and more specifically to a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage which flows into the upper inlet of the manhole while preventing and blocking foul odors leaking out from inside naturally collecting foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet thereby preventing blockage and preventing pedestrians from falling when the grating comes off while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage free from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of the manhole can be controlled while blocking bad odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and pedestrians can be prevented from falling when the grating comes off while the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage can be controlled while allowing smooth inflow of sewage away from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole can be controlled while preventing and blocking foul odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling accidents that may occur when the grating is detached is provided.figure 1 is a cross sectional view showing a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage water from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain and sewage water according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the grating part 20 is configured to be installed on the upper inlet 11 formed on the upper part of the main body 10 and to allow rain or sewage to flow in as desired while preventing foul odors from the lower part from leaking out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the blockage prevention means 30 is formed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 so that foreign substances such as fallen leaves accumulate on the grating part 20 and prevent rain or sewage from passing through the grating part 20 and is configured so that foreign substances such as fallen leaves naturally slide and allow the inflow of rain or sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole while blocking and preventing foul odors flowing out from inside and naturally collects foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet thereby preventing blockage and provides the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling when the grating detaches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102694540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 having an upper inlet 11 and a sewage inlet 12 for introducing rain or sewage into the above ground and an outlet 13 for discharging the introduced rain or sewage a grating 20 formed through a penetration to remove foreign substances such as fallen leaves contained in rain or sewage by being placed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 an odor blocking means 30 comprising a first inclined plate 31 and a second inclined plate 32 formed at the upper and lower portions corresponding to each other while being inclined so that rain or sewage flowing into the interior of the main body 10 can be discharged downward while rain or sewage flowing in from the upper inlet 11 can be discharged downward and a rotating plate 34 formed at each end of the first inclined plate 31 and the second inclined plate 32 can be rotated through a hinge 33 at the upper portion to block odors rising along with opening due to the load of rain or sewage the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 are provided with a catch net a to prevent pests such as cockroaches and rats from entering the inside while being installed on the sewage inlet 12 and the discharge pipe 13 of the above body 10 and respectively inserted to induce or discharge rain or sewage a fixing member 43 inserted on the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 to prevent detachment a packing 44 to prevent the outflow of rain or sewage and fixing means 45a 45b 45c to fix the inlet pipe 41 the discharge pipe 42 and the catch net 43 to each other and the fixing means 45a 45b 45c are provided with a plurality of catch protrusions 46 protruding in the opposite direction from the outer surface of the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 and a plurality of catch protrusions 46 protruding in the opposite direction from the direction of inflow into the inside of the sewage inlet 12 and the discharge pipe 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100529500-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "during the summer season large scale stormwater generated from sidewalks and roadways is drained through a vertical drainage pipe connected to the storm drain on the roadway in the drainage treatment method of the road characterized in that the rainwater is drained by a method of naturally falling during the drainage treatment through the vertical drainage pipe in the driveway 200 when a large amount of rain is generated due to heavy rain the rainwater collected through the rain receiver 210 is drained through the vertical drainage pipe 230 as it is the rainwater is penetrated through the drainage hole 112 of the permeable sidewalk block 110 of the sidewalk 100 and the rainwater that penetrates through the sand layer 120 is gradually inclined to block the barrier film collecting rainwater through 130 while collecting the rainwater generated in the sidewalk 100 in contact with the vertical drainage pipe 230 and through the drainage hole 142 of the rainwater inlet hole 140 seated on the seating portion 162 formed on both inner upper sides"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water filter in particular a rain water filter for a cistern with a housing 1 in which a sieve 9 is arranged which divides the housing 1 into a dirty water chamber and a clean water chamber wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet 12 for the filtered water with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon 17 into the dirty water outlet wherein in the lower part of the housing 1 of the water filter a siphon chamber 15 is formed which connects with the dirty water outlet via an overflow edge 16 and which has an outer opening 14 and that for forming the siphon 17 in the siphon chamber 15 a region between the overflow edge 16 and the outer opening 14 is separated by means of a partition wall 18 wherein the lower edge of the partition wall 18 is situated below the outer opening 14 and below the overflow edge 16 and wherein a dirty water outlet pipe 13 which forms the dirty water outlet runs through the siphon chamber 15 and has an opening forming the overflow edge 16 inside the siphon chamber 15 which is situated on the upper side of a horizontally extending portion of the dirty water outlet pipe 13 characterized in that the housing 1 has an upper part 2 in the form of a cylinder that is closed on the lower side by a bottom 5 wherein the bottom 5 has a passage 6 to which the dirty water outlet pipe 13 is connected and that the housing has a lower part 3 which contains the siphon chamber 15 and has the form of a pot which is connected with its open side to the bottom 5 and that the dirty water outlet pipe 13 runs in a bend through the siphon chamber this bend leading to a portion of the lateral wall of the lower part 3 and extending through this portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100984372-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "rain gutters 20 including a rain box 40 communicating with the first outlet hole 21b of the rain gutter through a connecting pipe 30 to store rainwater flowing into the rain gutter it includes a rooftop excellent induction pipe 2 for leading the rainwater collected on the roof of the building around the road to the rain gutter the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar in the driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility comprising an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge a sleeve 51 having the same size as the thickness of the bottom of the rain gutter main body and inserted into an insertion hole formed in the bottom of the rain gutter main body a perforated pipe 50 inserted into the sleeve so as to communicate with the inside of the rain gutter and installed by a filling material filled in the bottom of the rain gutter and penetrating the rainwater stored in the rain gutter into the ground a valve installed at an inlet side of the hole tube to adjust an opening degree of the hole tube driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility characterized in that it comprises a filter 52 is attached to the filter mounting portion 21c formed concave at the bottom of the rain gutter to remove the foreign matter from the rainwater flowing into the hole"}]</data>
