  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102091573-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a structure in which a rainwater discharge blocking wall 990 is configured to fail to flow into the interior of the rainwater collection channel 999 combined with the stairs through the rainwater inlet 998 the upper position of the combined rainwater collecting channel 999 is a structure configured to be equal to the upper surface portion 980 of the land a structure in which a floor covering material 880 composed of rocks is installed at a lower end of the waterway wall 100 so that water swimmers or swimmers can play or swim in water with confidence at the lower end of the combined rainwater collection channel 999 a rainwater or contaminants contaminated with rivers or rivers or reservoirs or dams while constructing a stepped artificial reef 890 where organisms amphibians or fish can be easily inhabited"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837300-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel portion for guiding water to move in a predetermined direction an infiltration inducing pipe portion penetrating through the bottom surface of the water channel portion and communicating with an underground aquifer below the impermeable layer in the ground layer a filtering unit installed at a connection portion between the infiltration induction pipe and the water channel unit and composed of several layers for removing foreign matter from water flowing into the underground aquifer and having a lower porosity toward the lower layer and and an opening closing part for selectively shielding the infiltration induction tube part the water a sediment guiding part having a guide protruding from the bottom surface of the water channel part and a settling groove formed between the guide and the guide an induction intrusion section having an inclined surface inclined upward in the moving direction of the water on the bottom surface of the water channel part and an inlet port formed on the opposite vertical surface and and a water film portion for controlling the amount and movement of water moving along the water channel portion the infiltration induction pipe portion may include an induction pipe connected to the induction pier at the upper end and connected to the underground aquifer below a flow rate measuring unit installed at an upper side of the guide pipe to measure an amount of water moving along the guide pipe and a water level control valve provided below the flow rate measuring unit and passing through the induction pipe the water level control valve includes a cylindrical body through which upper and lower parts pass a first inlet connected to an upper portion of the induction pipe a second inlet connected to a lower portion of the induction pipe and a buoyant body selectively shielding the first inlet and the second inlet while moving up and down along the body the opening a high level sensor installed at a relatively high position in the infiltration induction pipe a low water level sensor installed at a relatively low position in the permeation guide pipe a door unit provided at a relatively higher position than the high level sensing sensor to selectively shield the induction pipe and a control unit for receiving the signal of the high level sensing sensor and the low level sensing sensor and the signal of the flow rate measurement unit and controlling the door unit when the signal of the high level sensing sensor is received the control part shields the door part so as to prevent the water in the waterway part from flowing into the underground aquifer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6885661-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "1 a waterway sediment removing device for removing sediments in a waterway which is steered by a user via a steering handle and has a traveling portion having at least one front wheel and at least two rear wheels and the traveling portion"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6885661-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "as a result the accumulated sediment adhering between the side surfaces of the plurality of moving blades and being lifted is scraped off by each of the fixed blades and falls to the transport portion through the inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101127810-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1 the upper part of the inlet well 110 protrudes a certain height from the bottom surface of the waterway 10 and the upper end face of the inlet well 110 forms an inclined surface having a higher sidewall in the direction in which water is introduced to prevent inflow of soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102442307-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 1796648 there is a device for supplying water to farmland by automatically lifting and lowering the water supply control plate that opens and closes the inlet of the fixed plate fixed to the inner surface of the wall of the waterway through the lifting drive"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101221659-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the height adjustable channel using the connector and the adjustment bolt of the present invention the opening is formed in the upper a plurality of concrete channel blocks formed in the channel along the longitudinal direction while communicating with the opening a waterway assembled and assembled along the longitudinal direction the bracket mounting groove being formed at one side and the other side of both sidewalls of 