long the flow direction of the stormwater a first space 121 and a second space 122 that divides the inner space of the main body 100 into a first space 121 and a second space 122 123 are formed on the partition wall 120 the overflow passage 123 is formed at a predetermined distance from the lower surface of the main body 100 the storm inlet 110 is formed on the storeroom 200 where the first space 121 is located and a fresh water inlet 140 formed in the second space 122 and into which fresh water flows into the second space 122 and a mixed water outlet 150 formed in the second space 122 and mixed with water mixed with fresh water and fresh water stored in the second space 122 to be discharged to the outside of the main body 100 the mixed water outlet 150 is formed below the fresh water inlet 140 when the water level of the mixed water is lower than the position of the fresh water inlet 140 the fresh water inlet 140 is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a soil cement layer formed to a predetermined thickness on the bottom surface and an inner surface of the underground space formed by digging the ground of the outer side of the building to a predetermined depth and the soil cement layer formed on the bottom surface of the underground space portion a sand layer formed at a height an activated carbon layer formed at a predetermined height above the sand layer a gravel layer formed at a predetermined height above the activated carbon layer and an opening in the underground space seated horizontally on an upper surface of the gravel layer a fire fighting water supply tank having a shielding plate to shield the a first hollow rainwater inlet pipe inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank by vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and having one end inserted into the through hole formed in the boundary stone perpendicular to the outer wall of the building a hollow second rainwater inlet pipe that is installed as an inlet and has one end connected to the eaves gutter that collects rainwater falling to the roof of the building and the other end vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank vertically penetrating the shielding plate of the fire water supply tank and vertically buried in the fire water supply tank with the upper end exposed to the outside an inner space is provided an opening is formed in the center of the upper surface and a plurality of water collecting holes are formed on the lower outer surface the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the a hollow water intake unit introduced into the inner space through a water collecting hole one end is connected to an opening formed in the water intake unit so that fire water collected in the inner space of the water intake unit is supplied and the other end is connected to an opening formed in the steel pipe pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "this is to take in the fire water that has been purified by the fire water supply tank 500 and stored in the sand layer 520 while passing through the layers 520 in turn and vertically penetrates the shielding plate 550 of the fire water water supply tank 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text":