y storing the storm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101450993-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "therefore when the liquid composition changes with the progress of the electrolytic reaction and a sufficient flow rate can not be ensured the reaction conditions may be different on the inlet side and on the outlet side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101321349-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "as in the conventional case it is possible to detect the amount of water introduced through the inlet by using a flow meter but the flow meter has a high price and the zero point is inaccurate due to corrosion and breakage causing problems in performance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102704480-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as a rainwater irrigation method using an energy self sufficient eco friendly greenhouse system the above method a step for determining whether it is irrigation time if it is irrigation time detecting the minimum value of the water level of the second tank and if it is higher than the minimum value opening the three way valve so that the water of the second tank is supplied through the downpipe and connected to the supply pipe and preventing the water of the first tank from being supplied to the supply pipe a step for checking the charge level of the battery and if the current charge level is higher than the predetermined minimum value turning on the metering pump and turning on the sterilizing water generator 24 so that a certain amount of water coming out through the outlet port of the three way valve is branched from the upstream of the supply pipe through the branch pipe purified in the sterilizing water generator 24 and then joined from the downstream of the supply pipe through the joining pipe and a step for stopping the bypass process in which a certain amount of the supply water is branched and joined including the sterilizing component by turning off the metering pump and turning off the sterilizing water generator 24 so that the charge level of the battery is lower than the minimum