nufactures and supplies water with a sterilizing function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however especially in the rainy season or in the fall foreign substances such as fallen leaves can block the inlet making it difficult to drain which can easily lead to flooding and human casualties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the water tank 1 includes a groundwater inlet pipe 51 installed in one of the storage blocks 100 disposed on the uppermost layer and supplied with the extracted groundwater 52 wherein the groundwater inlet pipe and the stormwater intake pipe are connected to an excellent connection portion formed on the upper side of the storage block to induce rainwater inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the water tank 1 includes a groundwater inlet pipe 51 installed in one of the storage blocks 100 arranged on the uppermost layer and supplied with the extracted groundwater 52 and the groundwater inlet pipe and the rainwater inlet pipe are connected to a plurality of excellent connection portions formed on the upper side of the storage block thereby inducing the entry of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "5 the water tank 1 of the present invention includes a groundwater inlet pipe 51 installed in one of the storage blocks 100 disposed on the uppermost layer and supplied with extracted groundwater and the rainwater inlet pipe and the rainwater inlet pipe are connected to the rainwater connection portion 11 formed on the upper side of the storage block to induce the rainwater to be drawn in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218752-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in addition the inlet part 21 may change the porosity and permeability coefficient according to the particle size of the aggregate used and when the porosity and the permeability coefficient are increased foreign matter may be included in the rainwater