iltration layer 70 located between the cover 40 and the distribution plate 50 is formed so as to penetrate the side 24 of the case 20 to the outside to guide the initial superiority exceeding the design capacity to the existing storm pipe further includes a pass pipe 23 the inner space 66 of the filter container 60 is filled with a filter medium including a wood chip chip processed by chipping the thin thin material filtration and adsorption capacity of non point pollutants and zeolite activated carbon for supplying nutrition to vegetation the filtration layer 70 is composed of a first filtration layer 72 composed of small particles such as sand and a second filtration layer 74 composed of crushed stone having a larger particle size than the first filtration layer 72"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100684923-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is made in the form of a box the inlet 10 is formed on one side is introduced into the sewage and the outlet 20 for discharging the sewage to the sewage treatment plant is formed on the other side the outlet 20 is a buoy type shut off valve 30 in the sewage rainwater sewage chamber is installed on the sewer inlet 40 formed around the inlet 10 the wear 50 and the rough wood screen 60 the sewage stored in the rainwater toil 50 outside the ware 50 catches contaminants through the rough wood screen 60 and inside the rainwater toil scum and sediment to reduce the intrusion water inlet screen 10 70 to form to form an earth and sand lamination space portion 80 is the earth and sand is laminated on one side of the bottom surface of the superior soil chamber 100 the inclined surface s so that the earth and sand into the earth and sand lamination space portion 80 excellent sewage sills characterized in that formed 81"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101866141-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flow regulating tank for storing effluent treated and discharged in the sewage treatment plant a reaction tank connected to the flow rate adjusting tank and having an inlet reaction tank and an oxidation tank communicated with each other an ultra fine bubble generating unit for generating ultra bubbles after supplying ozone to the process water introduced from the flow rate adjusting tank or the inflow reaction tank and supplying the bubbles to a lower region of the oxidation reaction tank the treatment water treated in the oxidation reaction tank flows through an advection tube provided in a region below the water surface of the oxidation reaction tank and contacts with the foamed filter material for inducing the contact reaction of the hydrophilicized polymer material by the ozone a reaction tank and a treatment water tank into which the treated water treated in the contact reaction tank flows wherein the inlet reaction tank and the oxidation reaction tank are separated from each other through a partition wall the partition wall is spaced apart from the bottom surface of the reaction tank to form a spacing space and through the passage provided by the spacing space a pressure is generated in the lower direction of the oxidation reaction tank by the flow of the treatment water which is reversely circulated in the oxidation reaction tank and flows into the lower region of the oxidation reaction tank by the pressure in the lower direction the rate of rise of minute bubbles in the water is delayed and the rate of dissolution of the minute bubbles is increased and the treatment water in which the residence time in the oxidation reaction tank is increased due to the delay of the floatation rate is passed through the advection tube is introduced into the contact reaction tank wherein the foamed filter medium is disposed at a middle portion of the contact reaction tank the treated water is introduced into the upper portion of the contact reaction tank and flows in the lower direction and passes through the foamed filter medium further comprising an air supply unit for supplying air to the lower portion of the foamed filter medium to induce the floating of the sludge deposited on the foamed filter medium when the foamed filter medium is occluded by the sludge wherein the treatment tank is provided with an advection pipe having an a shaped structure at one side of the upper part of the contact reaction tank and treatment water staying in the contact reaction tank lower region passing through the foamed filter medium in the contact reaction tank through the admission pipe and a rainwater reservoir for storing incoming rainwater and further comprising an inflow control unit for allowing the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank to flow into the inflow reaction tank or the treatment water tank depending on the degree of contamination"}]</data>
