  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101560279-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water storage tank for mixing storages of fresh water and fresh water a main body 100 on which a fine flow path 200 is formed the top side of which is flown out and and is formed as a lower settled space relative to the clearance passage 200 so as to be formed on the clearance passage 200 and to deposit only the initial clearance of the clearance moving in the clearance passage 200 an initial fine precipitation tank 300 the upper part of the bleed passage 200 is opened a baffle wall 400 is formed around the baffle 200 so as to prevent escape of the baffle introduced onto the baffle 200 one side of the escape prevention wall 400 is connected to the end of the roof 500 so that the storm that flows along the slope of the roof 500 of the house can be introduced into the clearance passage 200 the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the bottom portion of the main flow path 110 lt rti gt the downflow channel is formed along the flow direction of the stormwater a first space 121 and a second space 122 that divides the inner space of the main body 100 into a first space 121 and a second space 122 123 are formed on the partition wall 120 the overflow passage 123 is formed at a predetermined distance from the lower surface of the main body 100 the storm inlet 110 is formed on the storeroom 200 where the first space 121 is located and a fresh water inlet 140 formed in the second space 122 and into which fresh water flows into the second space 122 and a mixed water outlet 150 formed in the second space 122 and mixed with water mixed with fresh water and fresh water stored in the second space 122 to be discharged to the outside of the main body 100 the mixed water outlet 150 is formed below the fresh water inlet 140 when the water level of the mixed water is lower than the position of the fresh water inlet 140 the fresh water inlet 140 is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102286640-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a soil cement layer formed to a predetermined thickness on the bottom surface and an inner surface of the underground space formed by digging the ground of the outer side of the building to a predetermined depth and the soil cement layer formed on the bottom surface of the underground space portion a sand layer formed at a height an activated carbon layer formed at a predetermined height above the sand layer a gravel layer formed at a predetermined height above the activated carbon layer and an opening in the underground space seated horizontally on an upper surface of the gravel layer a fire fighting water supply tank having a shielding plate to shield the a first hollow rainwater inlet pipe inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank by vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and having one end inserted into the through hole formed in the boundary stone perpendicular to the outer wall of the building a hollow second rainwater inlet pipe that is installed as an inlet and has one end connected to the eaves gutter that collects rainwater falling to the roof of the building and the other end vertically penetrating the shield plate of the firefighting water supply tank and inserted into the gravel layer of the firefighting water supply tank vertically penetrating the shielding plate of the fire water supply tank and vertically buried in the fire water supply tank with the upper end exposed to the outside an inner space is provided an opening is formed in the center of the upper surface and a plurality of water collecting holes are formed on the lower outer surface the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the a hollow water intake unit introduced into the inner space through a water collecting hole one end is connected to an opening formed in the water intake unit so that fire water collected in the inner space of the water intake unit is supplied and the other end is connected to an opening formed in the steel pipe pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the non point contaminant removing device 10 may be rainwater collected from a roof of a building in addition to the above mentioned sump well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to provide a block for wind and photovoltaic power generation in a road or building it is installed in accordance with the width and length of the roof to be installed in the photovoltaic power generation plate 25 provided with a photovoltaic generator 58 induction pipe for rainwater induction around the outer side of the lower portion 24 formed in the upper and lower directions to the guide wall 28 and the guide groove 29 to the lower portion 24 is formed to be inclined in both directions from the side portion 22 in the power generation block 20 provided with 35 protruding from both side edges of the solar light collecting plate 25 on one side from the upper portion 22 to form a side wall 31 to the upper side in accordance with the inclination rotating shafts 45 are connected to each other and installed between the side walls 31 and the rotating shafts 45 are provided with a rotating drum 44 on the outer surface of the rotating drum 44 is inclined to rotate the rotary blade 43 at equal intervals to the outer side of the rotary blade 43 is provided with an outer wall body 33 for connecting between the side walls 31 the cross section of the outer wall body 33 is provided with an inlet 21 of the inverse trumpet shape and an inlet 21 of the other side to the upper side of the guide wall 28 the fixing bar 49 for supporting downward from the edge of the outer wall body 33 to the upper side of the guide wall 28 water storage block for solar power generation is configured to be inclined with a guide net 29 fixed to the induction pipe 35 for the rainwater induction groove 29"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102812276-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "although the preferred embodiments of the present invention have been described in detail above the scope of the present invention is not limited thereto and various modifications and improvements made by those skilled in the art using the basic concept of the present invention defined in the following claims also fall within the scope of the present invention.g1 landfill layer g2 cover layer 1 leachate recovery section 11 leachate plate 111 leachate channel 12 blocking member 13 leachate drain 2 leachate purification unit 21 leachate inlet line 22 purification unit 211 purification body 211a 1st body 211b 1st purification space 211c 2nd body 211d 2nd purification space 222 ceramic filter 223 1st activated carbon layer 224 2nd activated carbon layer 225 zeolite layer 226 silica sand layer 227 compartment filter 23 purification storage 231 storage space 24 natural stone 25 heating section 3 landfill gas recovery section 31 gas pipe 311 through hole 32 flow pipe 33 landfill gas purification unit 34 storage tank 35 landfill gas pump 36 control valve 4 high temperature sterilization unit 41 steam generator 42 storage unit connection line 43 steam line 44 steam pump 5 uv sterilization section 51 substrate section 52 uv ray generation unit 6 dust suppression unit 61 spray line 62 drum 63 spraying unit 64 supply pipe 65 spray pump 7 wheel washing unit 71 tunnel section 711 car wash area 711a entrance 711b exit 72 lower wash section 73 side wash section 74 rear wash section 741 hinge block 742 shaft 743 drive motor 744 spray pipe 744a vertical pipe 744b horizontal pipe 75 front wash section 76 wash water supply storage unit 77 sterilization wash unit 78 dry car wash unit 79 car wash water recovery unit 8 pedestrian safety section 8a pedestrian safety passage 81 outer structure 811 entrance 82 frame section 821 pedestrian passage 83 roof 84 blocking 85 1st rail section 86 2nd rail section 87 frame drive unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102368680-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408175-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a light shielding hemispherical mining film 20 installed on the ground so that sunlight can be incident on a livestock field 21 formed in the ground the greenhouse 10 is provided with a solar cell module 12 installed on the roof 11 so as to be able to produce electric power by incident solar light a livestock field 21 and a barn 30 which is addressed to the livestock field 21 so that the livestock can use the livestock field 21 and solar light can be incident on the livestock field 21 the livestock manure that is formed in the lower part of the barn 30 and is collected in the barn 30 is used for fermentation of methane to be used as a fermentation broth of a compost or to be used for liquefaction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408175-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "it is therefore to be understood that the appended claims are intended to cover such modifications and changes as fall within the true scope of the invention.10 greenhouse 11 roof 111 slope 12 solar cell module 20 mining membrane 21 cattle field 30 housing 31 duct 311 perforated plate 40 ventilation part 41 frame 42 inlet 43 outlet 50 filter purifier 51 chamber 52 biofilter 53 diffusion plate 531 through hole 54 exhaust fan 60 manure processing unit 61 contaminant removing tank 62 63 methane production tank 64 filtrate tank 70 collecting tube 80 cogeneration generator 81 gas storage tank 90 excellent water collecting tank 91 water pipe h p hot water pipe m mesh mesh 100 combined animal husbandry system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102015918-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in this case a filter or a strainer may be installed in the inlet 12a to block foreign substances from flowing from the inclined surface 11a of the roof 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684272-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rainwater storage bin with a structure where the bottom and sides are closed and the top is open forming a rainwater storage space inside to collect and store rainwater a cover plate that is installed to cover and seal the upper surface of the rainwater storage box has a plurality of rainwater inlet holes formed through it to guide rainwater to the rainwater storage space and has a plurality of wick exposure holes through which a wick is installed it consists of a wick installed through the wick exposure hole to absorb rainwater stored in the rainwater storage space and guide it to the upper surface of the cover plate after covering the rainwater storage box with a cover plate and installing a wick vegetation is planted on the cover plate and installed on the roof of the building to realize rooftop greening and improve the urban heat island the wick is made of non woven fabric and is manufactured by impregnating it with a treatment solution and drying it to increase antibacterial properties heat insulation adhesion fixation and anti contamination properties the treatment solution contains 5.5 by weight of hydroxyproline 4.5 by weight of triclosan 3.5 by weight of sodium methylsiliconate 3.0 by weight of sodium orthosilicate a green roof module responsive to heat reduction requirements characterized by 2.5 by weight of prostaglandin and the remainder being polyurethane resin"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100984372-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "rain gutters 20 including a rain box 40 communicating with the first outlet hole 21b of the rain gutter through a connecting pipe 30 to store rainwater flowing into the rain gutter it includes a rooftop excellent induction pipe 2 for leading the rainwater collected on the roof of the building around the road to the rain gutter the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar in the driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility comprising an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge a sleeve 51 having the same size as the thickness of the bottom of the rain gutter main body and inserted into an insertion hole formed in the bottom of the rain gutter main body a perforated pipe 50 inserted into the sleeve so as to communicate with the inside of the rain gutter and installed by a filling material filled in the bottom of the rain gutter and penetrating the rainwater stored in the rain gutter into the ground a valve installed at an inlet side of the hole tube to adjust an opening degree of the hole tube driveway side rainwater storage and infiltration facility characterized in that it comprises a filter 52 is attached to the filter mounting portion 21c formed concave at the bottom of the rain gutter to remove the foreign matter from the rainwater flowing into the hole"}]</data>
