 fresh water inlet 140 the fresh water inlet 140 is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101495675-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "2 and 7 the first filtration body 1 is formed in a net shape at the inlet 7 so as to collect large contaminants introduced into the void through the inlet 7 of the pretreatment tank 2 the contaminant collecting net 15 is installed on the left vertical wall 6 of the pretreatment tank 2 and the upper wall of the pretreatment tank in a detachable manner"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101669813-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the apparatus is formed into a rectangular box shape extending in forward and backward directions the upper part of the front surface is formed with an inflow port through which rainwater collects and an upper part of the rear surface is formed with an outlet for discharging rainwater filtered for recycling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the storm recycling method is mounted on the road surface to block the inflow of large solids by storm inflow grating a solids removing step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating to remove the medium solids flowing into the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits the rainwater flowing from the lower trench conduit flows into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand the storm recycling method the step of mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block the inflow of large solids to the storm inflow grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall flowing from the lower trench conduit 60 consists of the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "4 since the wastewater treatment apparatus of the present invention is provided with a filter medium for removing contaminants only in the treatment tank and the inlet portion is configured to be open at the upper end and empty inside the sediment of the sediment portion under the inlet portion of the storm receiver if the state can be confirmed and a deposit deposits a fixed amount it can be removed by aspirating this deposit via a suction pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826790-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "at the upper part a sloping induction plate is installed at the tip of the first drainage guide plate a second settling filtration tank for blocking inflow of fine contaminants accompanied by the storm and having a filter net installed on the downflow channel formed by the lower part of the precipitation inducing plate and the first drainage guide plate to remove the dissolved fine contaminants a second rim hole formed in the upper portion of the first drainage guide plate of the secondary settling filtration tank and having a second rim hole and a second rim hole formed in the second rim of the second settling filtration tank the second partition wall is provided with a drain plate for partitioning the space with the second settling filtration tank and discharging the rainwater having an inclined surface at the inlet side and flowing into the second rinse hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101694827-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention relates to an initial good treatment apparatus capable of effectively preventing contaminants mixed with an initial storm due to contamination of a river lake by effectively treating contamination mixed with the initial rainwater by a pretreatment tank and a filtration tank an inlet pipe for guiding the initial storm of the gut pipe to the pretreatment tank and an inlet pipe connected to the filtration tank of the main body the main body is located at the same depth as the gutter tube and the inlet tube is formed higher than the outlet tube at the position of the water head and the initial gutter inside the main body is moved by the water head difference quot an early stormwater treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "US-7922916-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "inlet filters range from filter socks or tubes to gravel filled bags that are designed to impede flow into curb inlets thus allowing sediment and debris to collect in front of the device and not enter the storm drainage system through the curb inlet"}, {"pat_id": "US-7922916-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as the inlet devices become ineffective or the collected sediment and debris clog the inlet the primary function of the curb inlet is inhibited and the storm water that is intended to enter the curb inlet can cause street flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that 