ay be formed in the upper plate 30 as described above but formed on the upper end of the outer wall block 20 that is the outer wall according to the rain storage tank 1 of the present invention buried underground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101357244-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the door panel 330 for selectively opening closing the waterway 101 the drive unit 340 for rotating the door panel 330 and the drive unit 340 respectively are provided at the 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654689-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "in the present application the terms comprises or having and the like are used to specify that there is a feature a number a step an operation an element a component or a combination thereof described in the specification but do not preclude the presence or addition of one or more other features integers steps operations elements components or combinations thereof.1 filter block 11 11 block body 111 distribution hole 12 12 cover 13 13 support member 131 132 separation preventing protrusion 133 fastening plate 2 rainwater drain cover member 4 filter block assembly 41 filter assembly part 411 stone publication 412 connecting plate 413 fitting groove 42 seat rest portion 5 rain storm housing 51 seating jaw 52 drain passage h inlet opening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the contaminant collecting tank 13 is formed of a rectangular tube body 13a which is enclosed by a vertical wall on the side of the storm inflow port 12 of the pretreatment tank 1 and which has a lower portion closed and an upper portion thereof opened a contaminant collecting net 13c for collecting large sized contaminants contained in the stormwater is provided on the end side of the storm inlet 12 and a pretreatment water having the contaminants removed from the vertical wall of the rectangular watertight vessel 13 and the water retention tank 14 is provided at one side of the rectangular tube body 13a so as to prevent the large contaminants from being removed from the contaminant collecting tank 13 through the through hole 13b of the cylinder 13a so as to be discharged in the tangential direction of the outer diameter of the water separator 14"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "2 in order to reduce the resistance to the flow of the initial storm that flows into the plates 121 and 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 1002809 has a main body having an inlet pipe and a discharge pipe a contaminant collecting part provided inside the body and collecting floating contaminants and water soluble contaminants in the initial rainwater flowing through the inflow pipe a sedimentation tank in which the initial stormwater that has passed through the clogging trapping unit is stored a swirling screen for filtering precipitable contaminants in