ra_id": "para_91", "text": "since a leakage in the leaking transporting pipeline section 1201 has been detected the multiway valve 801 of the left wind turbine 110 closes the second valve inlet b and directs the electrolyzed gas from the electrolyzer unit 111 and or from the storage tank 901 via the first valve inlet a into the transporting pipeline 131"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a slope 62 formed over a wide area for the purpose of creating grassland and forest a road 63 formed with a slope 67 at the edge so as to penetrate the slope 62 a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 to prevent the slope 67 from sinking and a vegetation block 30 formed with a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to plant landscaping trees 46 in a protruding manner an assembly block 30 30 assembled in a layered structure and a slope 67 formed in an arid or hilly area where a renewable energy generation device 100 formed with solar and wind power generation devices 60 68 is built near a field 74 or a grassland or forest management area on the slope in a slope 62 in which a plurality of afforestation blocks 30 are stacked on a slope 67 equipped to be planted in the above mentioned vegetation zone 33 a water tank 71 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 of the afforestation blocks 30 30 assembled in the above mentioned stacked structure a vegetation zone 33 33 equipped with a vegetation wall 34 for planting landscaping trees 46 by protruding while a water supply hole 44 is perforated in the front wall 31 a moving gap 42 provided between a separate outer wall 32 in the rear wall 31 and afforestation blocks 30 30 are assembled in a stacked manner so that the moving gaps 42 are connected to each other an installation structure in a hilly area where a renewable energy power generation device for grassland and forest creation can be installed which is provided by assembling an assembly block 30 equipped with a vegetation wall 34 that is fixed to the outer section c of the vegetation block 30 connected to a water supply inlet 44 from a water tank 71 to support the lower section of the vegetation zone 33 33 while being assembled into the lower section of the above mentioned afforestation block 30 30 thereby preventing rainwater from collapsing due to subsidence on a slope 67"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "therefore the purpose of this invention is to provide power and equipment for collection in an economical and environmentally friendly manner by providing a renewable energy power generation device which is the main component of the present invention and a suction pump suction pipe and storage facility connected thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102435204-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "when it reaches the top an overflow pipe that discharges the treated water located at the top to the outside of the measuring tank 2 is installed the oxygen supply means 5 is a main pipe 51 and blowing means 52 installed on the inlet side of the main pipe 51 to blow wind into the main pipe 51 branch pipe 53 branching at least two from the main pipe 51 each outlet communicating with each bioreactor 1 and an opening rate adjusting means 54 installed on the branch pipe 53 to adjust the opening rate inside the branch pipe 53 the blowing means 52 includes a blower 521 blower for blowing wind into the main pipe 51 and an rpm adjusting means 522 for adjusting the amount of oxygen flowing into the main pipe 51 by adjusting the number of revolutions per unit time of the blower 521 in the measuring tank 2 the dissolved oxygen concentration sensing means 4 ph sensing means 21 mlss sensing means 22 orp sensing means 23 temperature according to the control signal of the control unit 6 a cleaning means 27 for cleaning the contaminants attached to the surface of the sensing means 24 is additionally mounted the washing means 27 uses antifoam water as washing water to remove contaminants in the upper and lower portions of the vortex prevention wall fitting groove 28 a female side sine wave groove 29a processed in the form of a sine wave is processed the upper and lower portions of both ends of the vortex prevention wall 26 are processed in the form of a sine wave and a sine wave groove 29b on the male side engaged with the sine wave groove 29a on the female side is processed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102435204-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the dissolved oxygen concentration sensing means 4 in the measuring tank 2 the ph sensing means 21 the mlss sensing means 22 the orp sensing means 23 and the temperature sensing means 24 are included in the measurement tank 2 it is installed at an angle of 35 to 75 degrees from the horizontal plane to accurately measure the water quality of the treated water sample and to remove the suspended substances on the surface naturally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569729-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a work line 10 provided with a water storage tank 22 for water treatment at the water surface 11 a frame 21 fixed to be projected to both sides of the work line 10 a steam jet pipe 12 having a jet port 33 provided to be submerged in the water surface 11 while being fixed a solar cell module 20 which is obliquely projected upwardly symmetrically on the side of the solar cell module 20 at both sides of the frame 21 a guide groove 28 projecting from both sides of the guide groove 29 so that the guide groove 29 is formed in the guide groove 29 a gap section spaced from the upper side of the guide groove 29 on both sides an outlet 19 provided as a wall 18 and a shielding film 37 protruded to the lower side of the water vapor distribution plate 12 at both side ends of the solar power generation plate 20 section 40 an induction part 23 protruding from the upper side of the water storage tank 22 to the lower side of the discharge port 19 and a low pressure section 40 separated from the upper end of the induction part 23 by a moving distance a movement section 47 and a condensation section 54 to be formed a water jetted from the moving interval a is discharged to the upper side of the water storage tank 22 through the water discharge port 19 and a condensing water condensing device provided in the water storage tank so as to flow into the guide part protruding from the water storage tank side walls 31 formed by protrusions of a blocking film 37 fixed to both side ends of the solar cell plate 20 a rotating shaft 42 passing between the side walls 31 a rotary drum 44 provided on the rotary shaft 42 a rotary vane 43 projecting at a plurality of intervals on the outer side surface of the rotary drum 44 an outer wall body 33 connected to the side wall 31 provided on the outer side of the rotary vane 43 a fixing wall 49 provided at both ends of the outer wall body 33 to support the upper side of the solar power generation plate 20 downward and an inlet 21 formed at both sides of the fixed wall a rotary drum 44 for reinforcing the rotational force by the wind force guided to the power generation plate 20 and rain water to the water storage tank 22 by the conveyance pipe 35 passing through the lower side of the solar power generation plate 20 wherein the condenser is configured to store the condensed water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101780266-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "as described above the method of reducing the amount of sludge of a wastewater dehydrating sludge using the jar drum type sludge reducing apparatus and the jar drum type sludge reducing apparatus in which the blades of the present invention are installed is characterized in that the high temperature fermenting microorganism ty em and a ceramic ball serving as a swelling fire can be supplied to facilitate the reduction of dehydrated sludge by smooth supply of temperature and oxygen and the high temperature heat and moisture inside the drum type drum body can be supplied to the blowing air pressure and the high temperature heat and moisture gathered on the upper part of the drum type drum body by the convection phenomenon can be recovered by a hot air blower and reused thereby saving energy.1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404152-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "the screening crushing unit 32 is provided with a casing 321 having an inlet and an outlet for blowing wind while mixing food waste into the casing 321 thereby separating contaminants such as light vinyl plastic and plastic products and crushing the remaining food waste and a hammer 322 mounted thereon"}]</data>
