  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101893417-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in one example the control device receives the incoming water quality value and the flow rate value from the first sensor derives the influent load receives the outflow water quality value from the second sensor receives the temperature value from the third sensor a data portion for data wise the water quality by temperature a driving unit for driving the valve to introduce the water into the pre treatment tank and the bioreactor the real time influent load value is derived from the real time influent water quality value and the real time flow value from the first sensor and the real time runoff water quality value is derived from the derived real time influent load and the real the real time recirculated water load value is obtained from the fourth sensor by receiving the real time recirculated water quality value and the real time flow rate value from the fourth sensor and the real real time flow rate value is received and a real time connection load is derived and when the real time reflux water load and real time connection water load exceeds the above mentioned additional connection water load and additional reflux water load the valve is driven to the pre so that the real time counter current load and the real time connection water load are set to the above characterized in that it comprises a load by driving the valve and can be linked or less wake analysis unit such that flowing into the bioreactor through the raw water inlet line.as described above according to the system of the present invention in the continuous treatment of the wastewater it is possible to automatically determine whether or not the pre treatment of the reflux water and the connection water is performed by the sensing basis thereby reducing the cost required for the pretreatment and improving the treatment efficiency of the pretreatment it is possible to improve the treatment efficiency of the whole system by preventing the load of the bioreactor.1 is a block diagram illustrating a system of the present invention 2 is a schematic view showing an example of a bioreactor which is a constitution of the present invention 3 is a block diagram showing a detailed configuration of a control apparatus which is a constitution of the present invention figures 4a and 4b are operational state diagrams of the system of the present invention 5 is a schematic view showing an example of a pretreatment tank which is a constituent of the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426715-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank and the initial excellent effluent which has been filtered by the stencil strainer flows into the storage tank and stores the initial excellent effluent while storing the initial excellent effluent"}, {"pat_id": "US-7238281-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the placement of first baffle 34 within inner chamber 20 reduces the turbulence of the water flowing into inner chamber 20 and directs oil and floatables to the center of passage 40 thereby enhancing the effectiveness of absorbent adsorbent material 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a solid separator 232 and a solid separator 232 a first processing unit 230 including an oil water separator 234 and a solids separator 232 formed under the enclosing hollow shape to separate outflow water and oil components and a sedimentation tank 238 for storing solids a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation storage tank 410 in which contaminants included in the effluent are precipitated is formed and fine pollutants and effluent are purified a second processing unit 240 provided with a microfiltration wall 440 to a cartridge porous filter 282 in which a third inlet hole 206 into which the effluent treated by the second processing unit 240 is introduced is formed and a plurality of refinery holes 510 are formed on the outer periphery to finally purify the effluent the inlet and outlet member 284 provided in the cartridge porous filter 282 and having a plurality of inlet and outlet holes 520 on the outer periphery the cartridge porous filter 282 and the inlet member 284 are fixed to a fixing part 288 and a third processing unit 250 including a filter support member 286 connected to the fixing unit 288 a storage tank 280 for storing effluent treated with non point pollutants by the third processing unit 250 and a drainage system in which a discharge line 260 is formed to discharge the effluent treated with non point pollutants and an effluent pipe 214 through which the effluent is waterproofed is formed on one side of the storage tank 280"}, {"pat_id": "US-10941535-B2", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "the above uses for the stormwater runoff and erosion control devices of the present disclosure are not intended to be limiting but are just examples of the multitude of ways in which storm water control carpets or blankets wattles also called dimensional tubes and compact drainage filters according to the present disclosure may be used in combination with retaining walls bioswales concrete barriers gross solids removal devices gsrds filtering vaults gabions drainage inlet filters and other best management practices to prevent erosion and minimize contamination of watersheds due to stormwater runoff"}, {"pat_id": "US-6093314-A", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "instead the runoff pools at the entrance to the drain inlet and beyond creating a potentially hazardous situation for motorists pedestrians and others"}, {"pat_id": "US-5366322-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "because the compartments are concentrically arranged water which manages to leak from a particular compartment for example by passing beneath the flexible compartment wall may only pass into an adjacent compartment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100791422-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "an object of the present invention is a tank having a hollow inside the inlet formed on the upper surface the storage tank and the narrowing storage tank formed by partitioning the inner space of the lower side of the inlet by the partition wall respectively the narrow surface on the upper surface of the storage tank a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the artificial wetland consisting of inflow culvert wetland space and outflow culvert the rainfall outflow and normal base flow from the inflow culvert into the inflow water is treated and then discharged to the outflow culvert a first connection between the inlet culvert and a wetland space such that an inflow consisting of a normal base flow including nitrogen and organic substances and a portion of the rainfall runoff of a design rainfall output wqv flows into the wetland space from the inlet culvert wetland intake channel deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the artificial wetland which can simultaneously process the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow of the present invention consists of an inflow culvert a wetland space and an outflow culvert the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow from the inflow culvert in the artificial wetland discharged and discharged to the effluent effluent after discharge into the effluent effluent the inflow water consisting of the normal base flow and the rainfall rainfall part of the design rainfall output wqv including nitrogen and organic matter from the inlet culvert a first wetland intake channel connected between the inlet culvert and a wetland space to be introduced into the wetland space deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1522525-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the pit used here consists of a settling pit which is connected via an inlet to a filter shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300414-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition it is equipped with an inlet line for introducing raw water and an external carbon source into the anoxic tank and by automatically adjusting the inflow of raw water and external carbon source the denitrification efficiency of the anaerobic tank can be improved operating costs can be reduced and the amount of external carbon source can be reduced this can be reduced to prevent further contamination by runoff"}, {"pat_id": "US-9427706-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "a portion of the input water prior to the inlet at 80 is directed to the bottom inlet of the lifting column 76 as indicated 88"}, {"pat_id": "US-10336544-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the water source may comprise either a surface storage facility or a surface water collection facility which collects water runoff and delivers the water through a piping system to an aquifer which is typically at an elevation below the elevation of the water source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102247357-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "as a result water pollution is prevented and land use efficiency is improved by reducing non point pollutants in surface water such as rainfall runoff by using a landscaping space in which vegetation is planted without installing a facility for reducing non point pollutants in a separate space"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6549343-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "that is by connecting the weather forecast to the internet of things iot platform of the electronic automatic shut off groundwater automatic inlet valve 12 inflow of runoff groundwater in summer when urban floods frequently occur due to continuous rainfall or heavy rain"}]</data>
</edge>
