oom hoist rope 888k front drum 888l rear drum 888m parallel weights 889 macadam roller 890 tandem roller 891 tamping roller 892 tire roller 893 tractor 894 trailer 895 ram 896 lead 897 coolant cooling 898 pile 899 helmet 900 fuel pump 901 cam 902 fuel tank 903 starting device 904 boom front pin 905 cad work 906 adapter 907 fish finder sonar 908 drilling machine for crude oil 909 manganese nodule 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-10435880-B1", "para_id": "para_218", "text": "the storm water management system 100 can be sealed to prevent the accumulated storm water from entering infiltrating the underlying surface 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "it is possible to prevent flooding or flood damage as much as possible by going down to the infiltration water or evaporating to the atmosphere and to prevent the groundwater depletion by the infiltration water going to the ground soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a plurality of downflow biological water treatment filters having various levels inflows entering the top of the filter and outflows flowing out of the bottom of the filter a maintaining an inflow to each filter inlet while all filters selected to be degassed are degassed b stopping the outflow from the filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the selected filter including the backwash system c directing backwash water flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the selected filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the level of the selected filter reaches a flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g next stopping the outflow from the selected filter and then introducing backwash water to the selected filter h stopping the backwash and backwash wastewater in the selected filter if present and resuming the outflow from the filter of step b to reactivate the filter of step b i degassing the remaining selected filters by repeating steps b through h continuously with step a j flushing the finally selected filter k stopping the backwash flow into the finally selected filter and l resuming the outflow from the finally selected filter to reactivate the finally selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_19", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a plurality of downflow biological water treatment filters each filter having a variable level an inflow into the top of the filter and an outflow from the base of the filter the filter comprising a locking the outlet valve from the first filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the filter b opening the backwash fresh water valve of the selected first filter c starting the backwash pump d automatically checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level f flushing the selected first filter to release the trapped gas from the filter g next closing the outlet valve from the selected filter and then opening the backwash fresh water valve to the selected filter h closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the selected first filter i opening the outlet valve from the selected first filter j repeat steps d to i successively for each additional filter where the next successive filter in steps d to g of the previous order is a subsequent step d a first filter selected from f k flushing the last selected filter l turning off the backwash water pump m opening the outlet valve from the finally selected filter n closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the finally selected filter and o maintaining the inlet valve open in steps a to n"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the degassing method comprises the steps of a maintaining the inflow to each inlet of each filter while all the filters selected for degassing are degassed b stopping the outflow from the filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the selected filter comprising the backwash system c directing the backwash flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the selected filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater if the selected filter level is flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g next stopping the outflow from the selected filter and directing the backwash flow to the next selected filter h stopping the backwash and the backwash wastewater in the selected filter and resuming the outflow from the filter of step b to reactivate the filter of step b and i successively repeating steps b to h to degas other selected filters while continuing with step a j flushing the finally selected filter k discontinuing the backwash flow to the finally selected filter and l resuming the outflow from the last selected filter to reactivate the last selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole structure in particular by installing a buoyancy blocking device to block the inlet by the buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom of the rainwater inlet of the manhole while performing the original function of the rainwater on the road concentrated guerrillas it is related to the structure of the manhole backflow prevention system of the road which is designed to block the inflow of the manhole in case of the backflow of sewage due to heavy rain or flood thereby preventing flooding damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the present invention by installing a buoyancy blocking device 130 is operated by buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet 113 of the manhole 110 to block the inlet 113 the rainwater from the original while performing the function of the guerrilla torrential rain flooding due to the backflow of sewage due to the flood effect is to be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "to prevent the possible torque perpendicular to the flow direction 10 the forced plates 32 engage laterally in the guide slot 12 of the abutment 30 and reduce the possible torque of the lifting platform 17 when lowering perpendicular to the flow direction 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 deep dredging of the river having a large length maintenance and construction of the embankment of the dredged river so that it does not collapse using the civil engineering material after installing the foundation concrete on the bottom and side of the river the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algal bloom for both ado and hydroelectric power generation is installed in a multi level step in the upper part to store a large amount of river water to produce eco friendly electricity while polluted after installing an eco friendly artificial fish farm combined rainwater storage tank at the inlet of rivers rivers dams and reservoirs which acts to purify river water naturally and at the same time to prevent flood damage the embankment is equipped with the automatic control system and the monitoring using an eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algal blooms for both a fishway and hydroelectric power generation which is configured by combining a camera and the remote control system a large amount of river water is stored to prevent flood damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "a main body formed in a hexahedral shape and extending a certain length from side to side a first front cover and a second front cover which are installed to be spaced apart from each other on the left and right sides of the front part of the main body so as to form an inlet through which water flows into the central side of the open front part of the main body a first opening closing door and a second opening closing door installed on the main body behind the first front cover and the second front cover and movably installed along the left and right directions of the main body to open and close the inlet a door driving unit for moving the first and second opening and closing doors a control unit that operates the door driving unit by an operator s or manager s manipulation or automatically operates the door driving unit according to a set pattern and a blocking screen installed on the main body corresponding to the inlet side behind the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door to block the inflow of foreign substances into the main body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101685359-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flat valve that is installed in a manhole to block reverse flow of odors and insects and to introduce sewage and stormwater a bracket provided opposite to the inner side surface of the inlet of the manhole and having a latching groove and and a valve body connected to the brackets and fitted in the latching grooves wherein the valve body includes a fixed panel having a lower portion at both ends thereof fitted into the engaging grooves a valve panel installed on both sides of the fixed panel so as to be hinged to open or close the inlet a sealing pad formed along an edge of the valve panel a t shaped supporter having a column formed at a central upper portion of the fixed panel and a support bar formed at an upper portion of the column and elastic springs connecting both ends of the support bar and the valve panel one end of the fixed panel is pinned and fixed to one of the brackets since both ends of the fixed panel are fixed to the brackets without being fixed to the brackets only one end of the fixed panel is pinned so that when the sewage due to the flood flows backward the valve body rotates around the pin to open the inlet through the inlet of the manhole wherein a through hole is formed in the bracket and a connection hole is formed in the fixing panel so as to penetrate through the fixing panel and are connected to each other by fins"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
