  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101669813-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the apparatus is formed into a rectangular box shape extending in forward and backward directions the upper part of the front surface is formed with an inflow port through which rainwater collects and an upper part of the rear surface is formed with an outlet for discharging rainwater filtered for recycling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of recycling rainwater the rainwater recycling method includes mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block inflow of large solids into the rainwater inlet grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall recycled from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 storm water recycling method comprising the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand the storm recycling method the step of mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block the inflow of large solids to the storm inflow grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall flowing from the lower trench conduit 60 consists of the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the non point pollutant removal device 10 is for removing contaminants such as fallen leaves scattered on the ground in the early stage of rainfall and a nonpoint pollutant removal device having a known structure may be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101501179-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "especially it is difficult to secure the site because it requires a separate site to install the contact tank and it is difficult to select the site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100922895-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore there is a need for a nonpoint source removal method that can remove nonpoint pollutants such as soil and other suspended solids contained in rainfall effluents entering fractionated or combined pipelines when they pass through stormwater inlets.an object of the present invention devised to solve the above problems is to remove the non point source material contained in the rainfall effluent in the upper part of the rainwater inlet in the structural management method for the treatment of non point source and the existing rainwater removal function the present invention provides an excellent filtration apparatus for nonpoint pollutant management to prevent inflow of nonpoint pollutants into conduits and streams by applying a porous elastic pavement to be kept intact"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "2 in order to reduce the resistance to the flow of the initial storm that flows into the plates 121 and 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a solid separator 232 and a solid separator 232 a first processing unit 230 including an oil water separator 234 and a solids separator 232 formed under the enclosing hollow shape to separate outflow water and oil components and a sedimentation tank 238 for storing solids a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation storage tank 410 in which contaminants included in the effluent are precipitated is formed and fine pollutants and effluent are purified a second processing unit 240 provided with a microfiltration wall 440 to a cartridge porous filter 282 in which a third inlet hole 206 into which the effluent treated by the second processing unit 240 is introduced is formed and a plurality of refinery holes 510 are formed on the outer periphery to finally purify the effluent the inlet and outlet member 284 provided in the cartridge porous filter 282 and having a plurality of inlet and outlet holes 520 on the outer periphery the cartridge porous filter 282 and the inlet member 284 are fixed to a fixing part 288 and a third processing unit 250 including a filter support member 286 connected to the fixing unit 288 a storage tank 280 for storing effluent treated with non point pollutants by the third processing unit 250 and a drainage system in which a discharge line 260 is formed to discharge the effluent treated with non point pollutants and an effluent pipe 214 through which the effluent is waterproofed is formed on one side of the storage tank 280"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "6d when rainwater flows into the first accommodation chamber 11a through the inlet pipe 13 in a state where the rainfall is greatly increased due to heavy rain or the like some rainwater may cause the protrusion 50 to fall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a body 10 provided with a collecting part 11 therein it is constructed between the road and the sidewalk including one or more inlet 12 and the permeable hole 13 formed on opposite sides of the body the inflow hole 12 is formed at the same height as the road surface of the road on one side facing the road side of the body so that the initial rainfall and contaminants flowing along the road surface of the body flows into the catchment of the body the perforation hole 13 is lower than the inlet hole on the other side of the body so that the initial rainfall and the contaminants introduced into the catchment unit is permeated to the bottom of the walkway to induce purification of the contaminants formed at the same height the body is a block body 10 2 provided with a hollow water collecting part 11 an inflow hole 12 and a permeation hole 13 which are open to the upper part therein so as to be detachable on an upper portion of the block body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the cover 10 2 is coupled to the water collecting unit 11 of the block body of the water hole so that the initial rainfall and contaminants introduced through the inlet hole 12 is directed to the water hole 13 side the boundary rainfall initial rainfall purification block characterized in that the opposite bottom portion is formed in a curved shape downward toward the hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 3 wherein the upper side is rotatably coupled to the body or the block body through the hinge and the lower side is configured to be rotatable only to the collecting portion side through the blocking jaw formed in the periphery of the inlet hole and a grill for adjusting the passage area of the inflow hole while rotating by the initial rainfall purification block for combined use"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "boundary combined initial rainfall purification block according to the present invention the body is provided with a collecting portion therein including the at least one inlet hole and the permeable hole formed on the opposite side of the body is installed between the road and the sidewalk the inlet hole flows along the road surface of the initial rainfall and contaminants flow into the catch portion of the body it is formed at the same height as the road surface of the road on one side toward the road side of the body and the permeable hole so that the initial rainfall and the contaminants introduced into the water collecting unit is permeated to the bottom of the sidewalk to induce the purification of the contaminants it is characterized in that formed on the other side of the body is lower than the inlet hole and the same height as the bottom of the water collecting portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "this embodiment is to prevent the blockage of the sewage system by the contaminants by pitching the initial rainfall flowing along the road surface to the lower floor of the sidewalk to prevent the blockage of the sewage system by the contaminants the rapid inflow of the initial rainfall and congestion along the road surface without congestion importantly from this point of view as shown in figure 4 the road side of the body 10 is formed with an inclined guide portion 14 for quickly leading the initial rainfall and contaminants of the road road surface into the inlet hole 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the dirt on the road surface is removed from the road by the initial rainfall so that the road surface is free of the dirt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the artificial wetland consisting of inflow culvert wetland space and outflow culvert the rainfall outflow and normal base flow from the inflow culvert into the inflow water is treated and then discharged to the outflow culvert a first connection between the inlet culvert and a wetland space such that an inflow consisting of a normal base flow including nitrogen and organic substances and a portion of the rainfall runoff of a design rainfall output wqv flows into the wetland space from the inlet culvert wetland intake channel deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the artificial wetland which can simultaneously process the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow of the present invention consists of an inflow culvert a wetland space and an outflow culvert the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow from the inflow culvert in the artificial wetland discharged and discharged to the effluent effluent after discharge into the effluent effluent the inflow water consisting of the normal base flow and the rainfall rainfall part of the design rainfall output wqv including nitrogen and organic matter from the inlet culvert a first wetland intake channel connected between the inlet culvert and a wetland space to be introduced into the wetland space deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a treatment structure provided in a substantially empty box shape and divided into a pretreatment tank a filtration tank and a backwash tank from one side to the other by first and second sidewalls having vertical insides a screen means installed in the pretreatment tank to filter suspended matter and garbage in the rainfall effluent flowing into the pretreatment tank and a filtration means installed in the filtration tank to precipitate heavy non point pollutants in the pretreatment water flowing into the filtration tank and adsorb and filter light non point pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 0894022 april 10 2009 in the treatment of non point pollutants contained in the initial rainfall effluent waterproofing the effluent purified in the non point pollutant treatment apparatus the variable wear is formed to protrude upwards to the inside so that the initial rainfall outflow water flows in the rain pipe is formed on one side a gripping portion is formed at an upper end and a screen is formed on an outer surface thereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1522525-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the pit used here consists of a settling pit which is connected via an inlet to a filter shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200391152-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the rainwater flowing down from the inclined surface does not pass through the filtering basket 6 but flows out through the bypass hole 44a of the support plate 44 to reach the drain hole 2a thereby ensuring a water free flow without disturbing the drainage of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "and part of the circulating water through the circulating water supply pipe 61 through the circulating water supply pipe 61 is sent to the buried contact medium storage facility 70 and the circulating water introduced into the void contact medium storage facility is purified while passing through the pore medium is distributed and collected the facility 80 is moved to the distribution collection basin 81 and is supplied from the collection basin 81 to the pond 30 formed at the bottom of the reservoir so that the water in the pond is always kept purified while the pond 30 water overflowed to the free fall into the overflow wear room 31 this operation is to be re introduced to the filtration purification 40 of the repeatedly formed through the air outlet pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "1 to 6 to separate the initial rainfall effluent and to form a rainwater toil chamber 11 having a settling function the rainwater toil chamber 11 is an inlet pipe 12 rainwater discharge pipe 13 and tea collection rainwater collection facility 10 having a storage facility inlet pipe 14 and the settling space 15 connected to the reservoir so that rainwater flows into the reservoir while having a function and the screen facility 16 to block the inflow of contaminants into the reservoir the rainwater collection facility in the rainwater collection facility 11 the storage facility 20 through which the rainwater flows into the reservoir through the reservoir inlet pipe 14 and installed on the bottom of the reservoir to produce a water change pipe and the overflow wear room on one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "it moves to the distribution collection basin 81 which is a collecting facility 80 and supplies it to the pond 30 formed at the bottom of the reservoir from the sump 81 so that the water in the pond is always kept purified water while the pond 30 water overflowed to the free fall into the overflow wear room 31 this operation is to be re introduced to the filtration purification 40 of the repeatedly formed through the air outlet pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100712051-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "when this structure is adopted the number of the rainwater introduced through the rainfall water filter inflow passage a does not directly collide with the dirt accumulated on the bottom of the dirt absorption preform 240 but once it collides with the dirt inducing part 250 is introduced into the bottom surface of the filter cartridge 220 and the other part flows into the sludge sedimentation part 240 through the sludge inlet port 251 to deposit sediments thereby enabling more efficient purification"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101129908-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first opening and closing part installed in a first primary conduit buried in the ground of the sewer to inflow only sewage and initial rainwater a second opening and closing portion installed in a second collecting conduit buried in the ground of a sewer the second opening being closed by a relatively larger initial rainfall than the first opening and closing portion and the storage tank is connected to the first and second secondary conduits so as to increase the amount of initial excellent water flowing through the first opening and closing opening and closing portion inside the storage tank is installed foreign matter removal means for filtering foreign matter introduced during the initial rain the first opening and closing part and the second opening and closing part is an opening and closing plate formed with an inlet an inlet prevention plate fixed to the bottom of the opening and closing plate to block the inlet and a spring cylinder connected to the opening and closing plate by an initial excellent water pressure including and the second opening and closing part is connected to the first opening and closing part through an interlocking means so that the first opening and closing part may be opened simultaneously"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "6d when rainwater flows into the first accommodation chamber 11a through the inlet pipe 13 in a state where the rainfall is greatly increased due to heavy rain or the like some rainwater may cause the protrusion 50 to fall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", 