presence of the facultative microbes that were added in large concentration and grown through replacement of the piping wall biomass"}, {"pat_id": "US-6338595-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the base section 14 is provided with openings 17 and knockouts 18 which may be removed in sufficient number so as to permit the passage of volumes of water that are less than or at maximum not in excess of the flow of water during the average occasion rainfall experienced in the area of installation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101058919-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this collection device is designed to automatically collect and remove only the rainwater so that the initial rain which contains various pollutants in the early days of rain does not mix with the relatively clean rainwater afterwards"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2901149-B1", "para_id": "para_175", "text": "this is because heavy rainfall conditions could dilute the incoming food source creating a low our and therefore a false toxicity reading"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101725047-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "2016 0081535 includes a first inlet inlet through which an initial rainfall 10 containing rain which flows along a road surface 50 a first filtration layer 110 formed on an upper portion of the first filtration layer 110 to allow the initial void 10 to be filtered and a second filtration layer 110 disposed on a lower portion of the first filtration layer 110 to pass through the first filtration layer 110 a second filtration layer 120 for further filtering the filtration water 20 formed at the upper portion of the second filtration port 20 through which the filtration water 20 flows and flowing through the second inlet port 104 a first filtering layer 130 formed in the filter frame 130 so that the first filtering layer 130 and the second filtering layer 130 can be disposed or separated from the ground 50 while being accommodated in the filtering layer 110 and 120 a reverse flow blocking hole 140 is formed to form a space between the first filtration layer 110 and the second filtration layer 120 to prevent the reverse flow of the initial clearance 10 the first filtration layer 110 is connected to the inside of the filtration part 100 and the filtration frame 130 and supplies air to the reverse flow blocking hole 140 from the outside of the paper surface 50 an air supply part 200 for removing contaminants adhering to the lower surface of the filter frame 130 through pneumatic pressure and a second filtering layer 110 formed outside the side surface of the filter frame 130 to be connected to the backflow blocking hole 140 a bypass portion 300 for preventing the filtered water 20 flowing into the reverse flow blocking hole 140 from flowing back to the lower portion of the first filtration layer 110 and a bypass portion 300 for preventing the reverse flow blocking hole 140 the filtered water 20 that is connected to the outer surface of the filtration frame 130 and the lower portion of the second filtration layer 120 and passes through the first and second filtration layers 110 and 120 is discharged to the sewer pipe 70 and a drainage unit 400 for allowing the waste water to be treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "in this configuration although it consumes electrical energy and requires installation of a separate sensor motor and controller the initial rainwater inlet 61 of the initial rainwater storage unit 60 is clogged with contaminants or the initial rainwater storage unit even if the initial rainfall is not stored due to breakage of 60 the storm guide unit 50 may be driven as a driving source based on the information detected from the sensor thereby storing the storm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102247357-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "as a result water pollution is prevented and land use efficiency is improved by reducing non point pollutants in surface water such as rainfall runoff by using a landscaping space in which vegetation is planted without installing a