he system of the present invention has the advantage of effectively reducing the excess sludge generated in the biological reactor to the discharged water quality thereby improving the treatment efficiency of the entire system.1 is a schematic diagram illustrating a system of the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-10703650-B2", "para_id": "para_133", "text": "concentration polarization results of accumulation of dissolved salt at the membrane surface creating relatively high localized osmotic gradient reducing osmotically driven normal permeate diffusion and hinders membrane flux"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100578050-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "when the pit shaped jaw is aligned with the height of the inlet and the outlet similar to the gradient of the lower bed the inlet may form a small waterfall by the slope of the lower bed and the outlet may be similar to the height of the lower bed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100578050-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the aerator may be in the form of an air jet or diffuser such as a porous plate or disc type"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the dirt on the road surface is removed from the road by the initial rainfall so that the road surface is free of the dirt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102423221-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "as an example the input space further includes a distribution block that is installed to protrude toward the top while crossing the center of the inlet to separate and partition the space and the bottom surfaces of both spaces partitioned by the distribution block are it is characterized in that a downward inclination gradient is formed toward each incision hole"}, {"pat_id": "US-7285216-B2", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "in the interface zone 48 which is thus located immediately below the surface of the water 46 in the reactor 10 biological oxidation of sulphides to elemental sulphur across the steep redox potential typically about 150 mv that exists across the interface zone 48 occurs with elemental sulphur forming as a floating biofilm not shown on the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605553-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore in order to solve the above problems a trap structure is formed inside a conventional sewage receiving device and a ventilation cap having a vent hole a spherical lightweight check ball a funnel shaped gradient ring a trapping pipe and a semi circular container a trap structure in which the parts are assembled in sequence is assembled and it is normally assembled and installed at the inlet of the sewage collecting device to prevent backflow of odors and pests through the sewage accumulated on the check ball and trap part which normally block the gradient ring as the sewage flows through the purpose of the drain is to be easily made by the rise of the check ball and the discharge of air through the vent"}]</data>
