  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200480951-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "technical field 0001 the present invention relates to a grating device having a clogging alarm and an odor blocking function the present invention relates to a grating device having a clogging alarm and a malodor shielding function and more particularly to a grating device having an opening and closing plate for opening and closing a sewage inlet so that various insects or the like may come in from the sewer in addition when the upper part of the grating is clogged with various kinds of garbage and the rainwater and the sewage can not be discharged it is possible to promptly notify the management office of the flooding damage and the opening closing angle to a grating device having a clogging alarm and an odor blocking function which can improve durability by preventing an unreasonable external force from acting on the grill"}, {"pat_id": "US-7922916-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as the inlet devices become ineffective or the collected sediment and debris clog the inlet the primary function of the curb inlet is inhibited and the storm water that is intended to enter the curb inlet can cause street flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 an actuator housing for operating a water gate to one side and the other side of the foundation concrete a hydrologic actuator disposed inside the actuator housing an operating hinge connecting one side and the other side of the operating device a lower support pipe configured in the middle of the actuating hinge a front sluice plate disposed at an upper end of the lower support pipe a hydrostatically reinforced guide plate support disposed in a trapezoidal shape at an upper end of the front sluice plate a front stream water inlet control block installed between the hydrostatically reinforced guide plate support a lower support pipe configured at a lower end of the front river water inlet control block on the one side and the other side while adjusting the front stream water inlet control block up and down the river water inlet control cylinder for opening and closing the lower portion of the river water inlet is configured in the lower front portion of the front sluice plate a rear hydroplate hingedly coupled by a rear hydrologic hinge a hydroelectric aberration configured to form a u shaped hydroelectric aberration housing at a lower end of the rear hydrological plate and coupled to a generator in a hydroelectric aberration housing and a power generation aberration protection cover that protects the power generation aberration when the water gate is opened at the time of flooding on the top of the power generation aberration wherein the front hydrology plate and the hydraulic pressure reinforced guide plate at the lower end of the front lower portion of the river water inlet the upper part of the river water outlet is formed in the form of a larger than the top of the water discharge at the same time at the upper end of the front hydrostatic plate and the pressure reinforced guide plate support to discharge the river water while generating a strong water pressure toward the upper layer of the water gate eco friendly power generation system combined with nature friendly water purifier in the form of a child"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an influent distribution tank for measuring influent flow rate and toc ss and ec water quality and analyzing the flow rate and water quality data to classify and transport the influent into the high concentration medium concentration low concentration storage tank according to the pollutant content receiving the initial high concentration influent and temporarily storing it the high concentration influent is directly connected to the sewage treatment plant and discharged and a high concentration storage tank having an internal washing facility a medium concentration tank configured to temporarily receive and discharge the inflow water when it is difficult to direct discharge at a time when the high concentration tank is full a low concentration storage tank receiving and temporarily storing low concentration influent water in which the contaminant concentration of the influent water falls below a predetermined level and discharging it and receiving water discharged from the medium low concentration storage tank after a simple treatment and through the disinfection process the water discharge below the legal water quality concentration is a simple treatment facility that can be used as a wash water and deodorizing water in the discharge or wash water storage tank corresponding to the water quality flow rate of the influent water is discharged to the sewage treatment plant after a temporary storage through a high concentration storage tank and the outflow water below the legal water concentration discharged from the medium low concentration storage tank is discharged or washed water storage tank after disinfection treatment it can be used as washing water and deodorizing water in the inside the inflow water distribution tank is equipped with sensors for measuring the water quality of the toc ss and ec therein to measure the flow rate and water quality data analyze the measurement data in the control computer and then the high concentration it is configured to automatically open and close the sluice of the channel connected to the medium low concentration storage tank to classify and transfer the influent to any one of the high medium low concentration storage tank to classify and store the inflow by the flow rate and the water quality data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "therefore in the non power source immersion prevention system of the present invention the opening and closing valve 300 is automatically opened by the access port 200 that ascends and descends by the water level when the flooding occurs in the manhole and the water is flooded in the manhole by the suction force generated through the ejector 500 water can be rapidly discharged to the outside through the suction pipe 400 to prevent corrosion or breakdown of the facility by flooding and it is possible to immediately cope with the flooding by the person without any operation the installation cost is reduced as compared with the drainage method using the conventional pump and the pause time is set during the operation by the amount of water flowing into and discharged from the water collection container 630 provided at the upper portion of the water inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 installed at the inlet of the primary sedimentation tank 1 into which the sewage flows and the suspended matter generated on the water surface of the incoming sewage is led to the suspended debris removal device installed at the downstream of the inflow portion to prevent clogging of the flowing sewage an apparatus for crushing and flooding suspended matters of a primary clarifier a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier 1 to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "therefore the development of the float shattering and anti rust prevention device of the primary sedimentation tank using the acidifier to smooth the flow of the suspended solids through the float remover without the solidification of the suspended solids in the process of moving the sewage from the inlet of the primary sedimentation tank to the suspension .summary of the invention the present invention has been made in order to solve the above mentioned problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a flotage removing device which prevents flotation from stagnating and hardening in the process of moving sewage from an inflow part of a primary clarifier to a flotage removing device the present invention provides an apparatus for preventing flocculation and flooding of a primary clarifier using an acidifier to smooth the flow of the flocculant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides an apparatus for preventing floatation and flooding of a primary clarifier using an acidifier the apparatus comprising an inlet to a first settling tank through which sewage is introduced an apparatus for crushing and preventing floatation of a primary clarifier using an acidifier to prevent clogging of sewage flowing into a sludge removal device installed at a rear end of a site comprising a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "US-8691091-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "by performing an air release cycle prior to a backwash cycle the release of air may be controlled to prevent the air charge from rushing out to the drain during backwash thereby preventing noise rattling flooding and loss of filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "it is possible to prevent flooding or flood damage as much as possible by going down to the infiltration water or evaporating to the atmosphere and to prevent the groundwater depletion by the infiltration water going to the ground soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole structure in particular by installing a buoyancy blocking device to block the inlet by the buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom of the rainwater inlet of the manhole while performing the original function of the rainwater on the road concentrated guerrillas it is related to the structure of the manhole backflow prevention system of the road which is designed to block the inflow of the manhole in case of the backflow of sewage due to heavy rain or flood thereby preventing flooding damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the present invention by installing a buoyancy blocking device 130 is operated by buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet 113 of the manhole 110 to block the inlet 113 the rainwater from the original while performing the function of the guerrilla torrential rain flooding due to the backflow of sewage due to the flood effect is to be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 as a water blocking device of a buoyancy type water blocking block to prevent flooding and over wave of a river including a flexible water plate 80 made of it is a configuration in which the member 90 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 in the water blocking device of the buoyancy type clapboard block to prevent flooding and overburden of rivers including the flexible water blocking plate 80 made of the member 90 is installed the floating matter removal module 100 for removing the floating matter floating in the river when the water barrier block 60 is raised and lowered includes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is installed on the drain around the road the front part and the lower part are opened respectively and the upper surface part the left surface part the right surface part and the rear part are formed in a closed hexahedron shape respectively and a main body extending a certain length left and right a first front cover and a second front cover which are installed to be spaced apart from each other on the left and right sides of the front part of the main body so as to form an inlet through which water flows into the central side of the open front part of the main body a first opening closing door and a second opening closing door installed on the main body behind the first front cover and the second front cover and movably installed along the left and right directions of the main body to open and close the inlet a door driving unit for moving the first and second opening and closing doors a control unit that operates the door driving unit by an operator s or manager s manipulation or automatically operates the door driving unit according to a set pattern a blocking screen installed on the main body corresponding to the inlet side behind the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door to block foreign substances from entering the main body the lower surface of the main body includes a plurality of bottom frames arranged to form a square shape and a bottom plate installed to close the space between the bottom frames and having a discharge port for discharging water to a drain on one side the upper surface portion of the main body includes a plurality of ceiling frames disposed parallel to the lower surface portion and arranged to form a square shape on the upper portion of the lower surface portion and a ceiling plate installed to close a space between the ceiling frames the left side the right side and the rear portion each have a plurality of side frames having one end connected to the floor frame and the other end coupled to the ceiling frame to support the ceiling frame with respect to the floor frame including a side plate installed to close the space between the side frame and the ceiling frame the upper and lower ends of the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door are inserted into each of the floor frame and the ceiling frame on the front side to a certain depth to prevent movement of the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101841645-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the diameter of the water hole 311 formed in the block housing 30 is smaller than the diameter of the inlet hole 21 formed in the press plate 20 the number of the holes 311 is formed in the block housing 30 in a smaller number than the number of the inlet holes 21 formed in the press plate 20 so that the gap between the inlet holes 21 of the block housing 30 is discharged to the permeable hole 311 in a state of being filled with water thereby preventing flooding or flooding due to abrupt discharge"}, {"pat_id": "US-8221618-B2", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "during high flow events flooding or thunderstorms water may pass over inlet device 703 through mesh screen 804 and flow downstream to prevent the filtration system from backing up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however especially in the rainy season or in the fall foreign substances such as fallen leaves can block the inlet making it difficult to drain which can easily lead to flooding and human casualties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632740-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and and an anaerobic stage in which phosphorus is discharged to the outside through a discharge port of denitrification and deodorization together with microorganisms by using a microorganism to remove phosphorus from the suspended matter of the sewage which has undergone the preparation step the air lifting unit includes an inlet pipe through which the activated sludge is introduced through a lower part of the inlet pipe an air supply pipe provided in the shape of a double pipe passing through the inside of the inflow pipe and having a nozzle formed at its end to provide a passage through which air is supplied into the inflow pipe and a circular spray plate installed at a part of the other end of the air supply pipe and disposed to block the activated sludge sprayed through the inflow pipe and disperse to the upper portion of the media media the reaction step comprises a sewage floatation step of flooding the sewage having undergone the anaerobic step to the top of the denitrification tank and the deodorization tank using the inflow pipe a sewage blowing step of blowing the sewage floated to the upper part of the denitrifying and desorbing unit through the sewage flooding step to the upper part of the media filter using the air supply pipe a sewage spraying step in which the sewage discharged through the sewage spraying step is sprayed onto the spraying plate to be sprayed to the upper portion of the media filter medium simultaneous treatment of the aerobic degassing process in which sewage water having been subjected to the sewage sprinkling step is passed through the mediare media and the exposure time is delayed in the atmosphere to simultaneously perform aerobic and degassing of sewage and further comprising the step of supplying oxygen to the wastewater contained in the denitrification and deodorization unit through the aerobic deaeration simultaneous treatment step using the anaerobic unit using the aerobic unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632740-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in addition the reaction step may include a denitrification and deodorization process in which an inlet port through which sewage flows is formed and the activated sludge is accommodated therein to precipitate contaminants of the sewage into the activated sludge an air supply pipe provided in the form of a double pipe penetrating the inside of the inflow pipe and having a nozzle at its end to provide a passage through which air is supplied into the inflow pipe and a circular spray plate installed at a part of the other end of the air supply pipe and arranged to block the activated sludge sprayed through the inlet pipe and disperse into an upper part of the denitrifying and desorbing furnace and injecting the activated sludge into the upper part by using air pressure and an air lifting unit disposed on the top of the denitrifying and degassing unit for delaying the air exposure time of the activated sludge discharged through the air lifting unit in a state where the air lifting unit passes through the air lifting unit a plurality of medial filter media on the bottom surface of the denitrification tank and the deodorizing tank and an acidifier unit for supplying oxygen into the inside of the denitrification tank and the deodorizing tank an anaerobic stage in which phosphorus is discharged to the outside through a discharge port of denitrification and deodorization together with microorganisms by using microorganisms to remove phosphorus from the suspended solids of the sewage which have undergone the high liquid preparation stage a sewage floatation step of floating the waste water to an upper part of the denitrification tank and the deodorization tank using a pipe a sewage blowing step of blowing the sewage floated to the upper part of the denitrifying and desorbing unit through the sewage flooding step to the upper part of the media filter using the air supply pipe a sewage spraying step in which the sewage discharged through the sewage spraying step is sprayed onto the spraying plate to be sprayed to the upper portion of the media filter medium simultaneous treatment of the aerobic degassing process in which sewage water having been subjected to the sewage sprinkling step is passed through the mediare media and the exposure time is delayed in the atmosphere to simultaneously perform aerobic and degassing of sewage and an aerobic step of supplying oxygen to the sewage contained in the denitrification and deodorization process through the aerobic deaeration simultaneous treatment step using the anaerobic unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101937611-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore in the sewage odor removal system of the present invention the supply water flowing into the spraying housing moves downward through the upper discharge hole of the adjustment inlet so as to dissolve and store the stored medicine and at the same time since the supply water is discharged by adjusting the gap between the drain pipe 112a and the drain pipe 112a it is possible to sufficiently dissolve the chemicals and to discharge them and also it is possible to safely and accurately sense the return pipe line condition by protecting the detection sensor and to prevent flooding of the sensing sensor to prevent contamination and damage and to selectively maintain deodorization direction sterilization or a mixture of these as needed to maintain the state of the best sewage line it is effective"}]</data>
</edge>
