  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200426198-Y1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in order to achieve the object of the present invention is formed of a hollow block of a concrete material the body portion having an inlet and an outlet having different sizes in front and rear a first filter plate member made of a pitched concrete material installed in a plate shape at an inlet of the body part a second filter plate member made of water permeable concrete which is installed in a plate shape at an outlet of the body portion a boundary block having a water quality purification function of a river is provided comprising a plurality of contact media installed vertically inside the front inlet of the first filter plate part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in addition when it is determined that the wastewater treatment capacity information is obtained by communicating with the wastewater treatment capacity management terminal configured in the wastewater treatment facility 210 to determine whether the treatment capacity limit is reached at the time of initial discharge by delaying the opening of the water gate or valve 500 for a connection and sewage treatment plant connection by a predetermined time the effect of preventing the processing capacity limit can be prevented in advance.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a siphon action generating partition 999 is formed in the center of the lower part of the upper part of the above foundation concrete 800 to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity while preferentially discharging clean river water with a heavy specific gravity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "after the above mentioned river embankment 100 is maintained the river is deeply dredged a water barrier is formed on the dredged riverbed and then the above mentioned foundation concrete 800 is installed inside the water barrier and then a partition 999 for generating a siphon effect is formed on the upper part of the above mentioned foundation concrete 800 to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity to the center of the lower part while preferentially discharging clean river water with a heavy specific gravity and a front inlet 91 is formed on the front part of the lower part and a rear outlet 92 is formed on the rear part of the lower part and an eco friendly movable dam 9999 for preventing green algae occurrence that combines an electric power generation unit 7777 that produces eco friendly electricity using hydraulic power is installed on the rear part of the above mentioned rear outlet 92"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100616387-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore the river water enters through the upstream end and enters the vegetation space portion 14 while rotating the rotary sieve 20 so that purification occurs at the root of the aquatic plant 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method of manufacturing a shore block installed in a waterfront area such as a lake a dam a river slope and a bank a filling purified water sludge containing organic matter and having a particle size of 5 \ud0c6 or less in a filling groove embedded in a side plate having a predetermined thickness b drying the side plates by filling the mortar so that the upper part of the crushed stones is exposed after a plurality of crushed stone of different sizes are disposed adjacent to the purified sludge and precipitated c arranging the side surface of the side plate so that the filling surface faces inward and assembling the form frame by connecting the top plate and the bottom plate to the side plate d pouring a mortar having 6 to 15 by weight of water 65 to 80 by weight of crushed stone and 10 to 25 by weight of cement into the internal space of the mold and curing the mortar and e removing the dried sludge after removing the mold thereby protruding the crushed stone"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a revetment block installed on a slope of a lake a dam reservoir a river or a trench the present invention relates to an eco friendly revetment block capable of supporting the growth and activity of water creatures by supplying oxygen in water by surface collision as well as purification of water produced and contacted thereby"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "it is preferable that the upper portion of the soil 113 is filled with sand and gravel 114 to prevent the soil 113 filled in the soil receiving groove 111a from being lost due to the water level fluctuation as well as an optimum natural condition for scattering aquatic insects and fish in the aquatic space 112a can be formed as described later"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "therefore the shore protection block of the present invention can be installed in a lake a dam reservoir slope a river or a ditch to provide a space where various aquatic plants aquatic insects and fish can coexist along with water purification.10 top plate 11 vertical plate 12 soil seating plate 20 bottom plate 30 31 side plate 32 40 purified water sludge 50 crushed stone 60 mortar 70 mold 80 slope 100 shore block 110 body portion 111 upper surface 111a soil receiving groove 112 lower surface 112a aquatic space 113 soil 114 sand and gravel 115 aquatic plant 120 surface part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow er