on tanks divided by a sedimentation basin divider in a direction parallel to the reservoir in the center of the sedimentation basin so as to control the river water during the dredging operation a front end of the enclosure that is a sedimentation inlet flow path with a head protruding from the center connected to the sedimentation basin divider having a jaw and a groove at the bottom and an upper rod hook groove at the top the prefabricated movable blocking gate installed in the blocking gate installation unit is achieved by installing a sedimentation basin consisting of several prefabricated clasp plates that are miniaturized for easy transportation and an upper hook rod to support the prefabricated clasp plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the dewatered degreased liquid collected in the lower collecting part 56 through the discharge hole and collected in the lower collecting part 56 is discharged back to the water reservoir 11 through the degreasing solution discharge pipe 54 while the overflowed sump is an inlet 53"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "it protects the quality of rivers and lakes prevents the destruction of aquatic ecosystems due to the inflow of sediments and streams and also prevents the reduction of runoff cross sectional area"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218344-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to prevent the re injury of the sediment which is a disadvantage of the swirl method by applying the anti floating means the filtration tank equipped with the filtration means is separately installed to separate the vortex and the laminar flow forming tank capable of forming the laminar flow"}]</data>
