g nozzle 300 installed at an inner upper end of the measurement water storage tank 200 to diffuse and spray clean washing water to clean the inside of the measurement water storage tank 200 a washing water inlet line 340 having a washing water automatic valve 310 and an nozzle automatic valve 320 for automatically controlling the opening and closing operation to supply the washing water to the cleaning nozzle 300 a controller 400 for automatically controlling each automatic valve by an electrical signal in the automatic measurement of water pollution for monitoring the water pollution consisting of cleaning of the washing water inflow line 340 between the first measurement water line 110 that is opened and closed controlled by the first automatic valve 130 and the second measurement water line 120 that is opened and controlled by the second automatic valve 140"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102455510-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "accordingly it can be seen that the administrator can remotely control the valve control unit 160 to control the amount of discharge by controlling the opening and closing of the solenoid type electric valve 150 thereby preventing river contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "therefore the water in the rainwater inlet space 12 filled with only clear rainwater may prevent contamination of the river even if it flows into the river through the rainwater discharge unit 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "therefore the water in the rainwater inlet space 12 filled with only clear rainwater may prevent contamination of the river even if it flows into the river through the rainwater discharge unit 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_171", "text": "therefore the water in the rainwater inlet space 12 filled with only clear rainwater may prevent contamination of the river even if it flows into the river through the rainwater discharge unit 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "para_252", "text": "however if the water is confined by using the top discharge type water storage method such as the conduction type water gate and the rubber dam the particles of the incompletely decomposed materials in the course of the material friction action are separated from the viscous force contained in the fine particles water quality contamination of river water becomes more and more intense due to the material combination between pollutant molecules and clean water molecules due to the viscous force and magnetic force contained in the fine particles this is because the specific gravity of the stream water becomes heavier than the specific gravity of the water molecules through the process of continuously generating the material binding actions which further increases the pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869158-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "rainwater flowing into the rainwater discharge pipe 140 by the above process is to discharge to the river or lake to prevent contamination of the river or lake and groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101579303-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 2007 0083441the present invention solves these problems of conventional methods and simultaneously cleanses polluted river water generated from a point pollution source and a nonpoint pollution source more efficiently by using natural forces and at the same time the present invention also provides a multifunctional movable water gate for water purification in the present invention in order to prevent the river water stored in the drought season automatically from running out the width of the siphon passage formed inside the movable waterproof door is wide the middle is slightly bent and the upper part is wide it is natural that the fish that restore the natural ecosystem constituted to discharge the river water which is stored in the iron is constituted so as to constitute the low water discharge passage which is formed naturally at the same time as the fish friendly operation method that cleans contaminated river water using multifunctional movable water gate that functions as a rope operated water purification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032253-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in general wastewater and sewage generated in industrial facilities or homes are purified by a wastewater treatment device and discharged into the river to prevent contamination of the stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101724155-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a rainwater purification plant the present invention relates to rainwater purification and water supply facilities for trees and more particularly to a rainwater purification and water supply facility for trees which comprises a sidewalk covered with concrete and asphalt a rainwater flowing along a sidewalk and a road surface it is introduced into the reservoir soil and supplied to the foundation soil again through many wicks to prevent contamination of the river or ground water prevent flooding due to heavy rainfall improve the urban aesthetics and prevent the trees from dry the present invention relates to a rainwater purification and water supply facility for trees"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102451025-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "it provided a cause of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101380889-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the sewage treatment system is a device to reduce contamination of rivers by discharging untreated sewage cso s overflowed from sewage wells of a combined sewer system to a river watershed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102209197-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the frequent discharge method is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and if the water in the storage space is discharged through the lower part of the sluice gate it is caused by a substance binding action that combines substances contained in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "in addition regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042731-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the lower end is installed to be inserted below the first sand gravel layer of the bottom of the river and the upper end is installed up and down across the river so as to be exposed above the maximum water surface of the river thereby providing a water intake space therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042731-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "it is installed to provide a water intake space therein the water reservoir body to separate and receive only the groundwater flows through the bottom of the stream filtered water without interfering with the contamination of the external surface water a well lid body for sealing an open upper surface of the well body to separate and block the inside of the well body from the air layer on the water surface it is installed inside the well body and the upper surface is inserted deeper than the bottom of the well body main body across the sand gravel layer of the river bottom in a state spaced apart from the well cover body the groundwater is a water intake pipe in which a plurality of fine water intake holes are formed on the lower side thereof so that the water can be taken into the water intake space inside the main body one end extends to the center of the intake space through the well cover body and the other end is installed to protrude to the top of the well cover body and discharges the groundwater taken into the intake space through the intake pipe to the water supply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "according to the present invention configured as described above by using the stone and red earth finish the appearance of the blow beam can reduce the objection to the beam as an artificial structure can be harmonized with the natural environment of the river as well as on the outer surface of the blow beam depending on the vegetation of aquatic plants can provide river purification and fish habitat there is an advantage to prevent the contamination of river water with the free movement of fish by opening and closing the water intake"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101682161-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "first a certain volume of space is provided in a measurement chamber provided with a measurement sensor and water supplied from a water source such as a ground water intake point and a river or a lake can be stored in this space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101468197-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "therefore the water stored in the water storage space is always kept at the high water level it is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and it is also possible to discharge water from the water reservoir through the lower part of the water gate it causes the pollutants such as accumulated sludge to be discharged and at the same time causes the material acceleration phenomenon the material incidence phenomenon the material decomposition effect the substance floating phenomenon etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100803745-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore when the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the contamination is further increased by the material decomposition and material binding action so that the lower end of the rubber dam or the siphon passage coupled with the rubber dam constitutes the water gate the method of discharging only the influent that flows through the bottom of the siphon or the hydrologic gate is the best way to prevent the contamination of the river water and to purify the contaminated water and also to discharge the water in the reservoir space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the first object of the present invention is to prevent contamination of the valley channel by overflowing the partition wall during rainy weather and also to sewage initial rainwater and valley water excellent sewage and valleys using a storage tank that can be discharged to the river and prevented from being discharged to the river by the initial rainwater that has not been purified due to the initial rainfall that is supercharged during rainy weather exceeding the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the initial rainwater storage system for sewage and valley water separation using the storage tank according to the present invention by overflowing the dividing wall during rainy weather to prevent contamination of the valley waterway and also to sewage initial rainfall and valley water rainwater on the other hand due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rainy weather the initial rainwater that has not been purified by the excess of the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant is discharged to the river to prevent the river from being polluted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101363621-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "therefore if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time the contamination is further increased by the material decomposition action and the material binding action so that the water stored in the reservoir always maintains the full water level and the water coming from the upstream through the lower part of the water gate the method of frequent discharge is the best way to prevent the contamination of river water and also by using the method of discharging the water in the reservoir through the lower part of the sluice the material binding action of the substances contained in the water it discharges pollutants such as aggregated sewage sludge and at the same time it accelerates the material acceleration material scavenging material decomposition material flotation and naturally cleans the polluted water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741836-B1", "para_id": "para_290", "text": "however if the water is confined by using the top discharge type water storage method such as the conduction type water gate and the rubber dam the particles of the incompletely decomposed materials in the course of the material friction action are separated from the viscous force contained in the fine particles water quality contamination of river water becomes more and more intense due to the material combination between pollutant molecules and clean water molecules due to the viscous force and magnetic force contained in the fine particles this is because the specific gravity of the stream water becomes heavier than the specific gravity of the water molecules through the process of continuously generating the material binding actions which further increases the pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741836-B1", "para_id": "para_424", "text": "therefore the water stored in the water storage space is always kept at the high water level it is the best way to prevent contamination of river water and it is also possible to discharge water from the water reservoir through the lower part of the water gate it causes the pollutants such as accumulated sludge to be discharged and at the same time causes the material acceleration phenomenon the material incidence phenomenon the material decomposition effect the substance floating phenomenon etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "in this way by continuously supplying river water to rivers a certain amount of running water always flows during the dry season so that the ecosystem of the river can survive and the urban environment is greatly improved and in terms of sewer pipes as the solids content and chemical oxygen demand are lowered corrosion and breakage of pipelines can be prevented in advance and through this groundwater contamination due to leakage of contaminated water air pollution due to odor and miniaturized sewage treatment plant can be miniaturized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "economic losses to construct sewage terminal treatment plant can be saved.the stream runoff procurement apparatus and method thereof according to the present invention always allow a certain amount of streams to flow through the river to survive the ecosystem of the stream and furthermore the contamination of the pipeline is prevented in advance so that the groundwater due to the corrosion and breakage of the sewer pipe is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "US-11142470-B2", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "preliminary tests were conducted to validate the sample and analysis method as well as to verify contamination levels prior to performing the disinfection procedures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the sewage stored in the at least one cso storage tank 102 may be discharged directly to the discharge stream 105 through the discharge unit 140 if the concentrated heavy rain is discharged sewage amount at this time the discharge unit 140 further includes an initial excellent water treatment unit 145 for preventing discharge of wastes swept away by rainwater into the