mple the second soil inflow preventing apparatus 12 and the second river inflow adjusting apparatus 22 may be provided with a storage tank inflow channel of the river water quality purification facility by the inter contact oxidation method and a device disclosed in the drainage channel opening closing system 10 0299334 can be used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "an influent distribution step of reducing the energy of river water lake water or effluent flowing into the water purification apparatus through a flow distribution tank and evenly distributing it to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step of biologically purifying the inflow water having passed through the precipitation step into the contact oxidation tank having the microbial contact material installed therein river water that combines modular wetland infrastructure and modular catalytic oxidation and filtration facilities including a 4th purification step that finally removes fine sludge and suspended solids that were not filtered through the contact oxidation tank through a filter tank equipped with filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "the method according to claim 7 or 8 if the influent flows directly to the sedimentation tank through the water level control pipe of the modular wetland based facility due to the increase in inflow flow rate the screen material installed in the sump is not provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "however in korea s river water and lake water where the concentration of organic and suspended substances is high and the water quality changes severely with seasons the contact area of effective effective microorganisms is greatly reduced because microorganisms and suspended substances are excessively attached to the surface of microbial contact materials"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a contact oxidation tank in which contact materials such as gravel waste concrete and waste tires are embedded to precipitate adsorb and biologically oxidize organic matter and suspended matter in the river water that has passed through the primary storage tank and purify through the contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "therefore the inflow path into which the river water flows into the primary storage tank is always lower than the river water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the river water to be treated which has passed through the pretreatment unit 10 flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 is purified in the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 and then passes through the discharge tank 40 to be discharged into a river or lake thereby performing the functions of water quality purification and management during normal times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "for example when rainfall continues for more than 1 hour and river flooding is expected a movable dam can be installed in the river and when the movable dam is covered all the holes or valves flowing into or out of the facility are automatically blocked thereby protecting the facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "the ecological block 130 for water purification in the low carbon permeable ecological structure 100 may be formed along the plurality of horizontal frames 120 to construct the dam or beam structure into a permeable stream through which river water passes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101189554-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "it is preferable in that it can enable the oxidation process by a photocatalyst with respect to waste water.the present invention can efficiently remove the hardly decomposable organic matter from the discharged water discharged to the river by means of the above described solution to reduce the pollution of the drinking water source can be recycled as well as water.1 is a conceptual diagram of an advanced water treatment apparatus of this embodiment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101189554-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "by the above described highly purified water treatment device and method the photocatalyst is circulated between the raw water tank and the separation membrane thereby making it possible to oxidize the hardly decomposable organic substance by the photocatalyst to the maximum thereby discharging the hardly decomposable organic substance into the river at low cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100440889-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to increase the efficiency of adhering microorganisms contained in the contaminants of influent water flowing through the gills a grid type nonwoven fabric fiber netting material is installed on a fixed frame and a plurality of the fixed frames are superimposed to be spaced apart from each other a contact oxidation vessel in which a sludge port is formed at the bottom for discharging the precipitated sludge from the contact material bubble generating means provided on one side of the contact oxidation vessel and generating bubbles for performing lateral aeration a sedimentation tank installed at one side of the contact oxidation tank to precipitate residual contaminants contained in the influent water that has passed through the contact oxidation tank and a sludge tank that is connected to a lower portion of the sludge port of the contact oxidation tank and generates a sludge settled to a lower portion of the contact oxidation tank and the sludge tank wherein the contaminated river water treatment apparatus comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101091864-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 0637607 invention new city ecological park artificial waterway water circulation system accordingly the technical problem of the present invention is to solve such a conventional problem and an object of the present invention is to install an artificial water channel around a river thereby increasing the oxidation efficiency by increasing the inflow path of natural oxidized water thereby treating riverside filtration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828913-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the wastewater thus taken in flows into the oxidation electrode tank 121 and the seawater flows into the reduction electrode tank 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101638519-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "specifically the present invention can be applied to a case where the water quality of a water body such as a river a lake a reservoir and a sea area deteriorates due to monitoring of a pollution source or when a precaution is required due to concern about worsening of water quality and ecological environment n and phosphorus p adsorption and degradation degradation of organic matter by the generation of ultrasonic waves degradation of organic matter by ultrasound it is composed of dissolved oxygen by microbubbles floating separation and oxidation oxidative decomposition by microorganisms adhering to artificial herbaceous plants photo oxidation and adsorption of contaminants by photo oxidizer the present invention is directed to a water quality management system and a method of operating the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200285740-Y1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "ss 78mg \u2113 is treated economically and conveniently and the sewage of sewage pipes is treated using the gravel contact oxidation tank using the gravel layer filtration and charcoal biofilm filtration purification method which is a natural purification method that does not require additional site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200285740-Y1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "therefore in order to prevent obstruction by fine suspended matter and environmental microorganisms the lower sludge discharge facility 24 is installed at the lower part of the gravel contact oxidation facility 11 and the charcoal biofilm filtration tank 13 and is excessive by the diffuser 21 device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102219449-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore various methods have been proposed to purify the stored water and the conventional water purification methods include gravel contact oxidation method reverse contact oxidation method sewage treatment plant water purification method and chlorine input purification method but they are consistently expensive and expensive"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187983-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore various methods have been proposed to purify the stored water and the conventional water purification methods include gravel contact oxidation method reverse contact oxidation method sewage treatment plant water purification method and chlorine input purification method but they are consistently expensive and expensive"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101167038-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however iron or manganese in ionic form under anaerobic conditions in underground river filtration is oxidized in contact with air in the intake well but gradually forms a sediment but as a result it accumulates in the well and the inner wall of the pump resulting in well efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of inflow distribution tank aeration part contact oxidation tank sediment part contact oxidation tank outflow storage tank sludge storage tank and acid pipe and by applying contact oxidation method using contact media in the aeration part and precipitation contact oxidation tank polluted river water and sewage in the apparatus for treating sewage installed on one side of the inflow distribution tank to adjust the level of the treated water flowing from the inlet each movable bank for adjusting the level of the treated water installed and installed on one side of the outlet storage tank perforated perforated walls 7 15 of area formed in the interface between the inlet distribution tank and the aeration contacting tank the interface between the aeration contacting tank and the sludge hopper and the interface between the precipitation contacting oxidation tank and the outflow reservoir a supernatant water storage tank which is formed by trapping the sludge hopper formed in the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration contacting oxidation tank and the precipitation contacting oxidation tank to the sludge storage tank through an air lift and partitioned by an operation full width bank on one side of the sludge storage tank an diffuser installed in the inflow distribution tank and the outflow storage tank to supply dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to the inside of the contact oxidation tank and the treated water discharged while being prevented from being closed by sludge and contact oxidation method further comprises at least one contact medium selected from the group consisting of crushed stone of 30 to 40 of porosity or plastic of 80 or more of porosity in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and precipitation part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "80mg l or less is used for the sewage treatment and the diffuser is installed at the bottom of the contact oxidation tank to remove aeration and sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a contact oxidation tank in which contact materials such as gravel waste concrete and waste tire are embedded to precipitate adsorb and biologically oxidatively decompose organic matter and suspended matter in the river water that has passed through the storage tank and the purified river water that has passed through the contact oxidation tank it is composed of a secondary storage tank for intake and discharge and an acid pipe is installed under the contact oxidation tank to facilitate contact oxidation and sludge discharge of the pollutant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to achieve the above object as well as other objects that can be easily expressed the present invention applies a contact oxidation method to increase the contact surface of the deeper contaminated river water and sewage or sewage and the contact media to reduce the contamination concentration but as crushed stone"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "air sludge deposited on the wall and the trapezoidal sludge hopper formed between the aeration portion contact oxidation tank and the precipitation contact oxidation tank transfer to the sludge storage tank through the shaft but one side of the sludge storage tank and the supernatant water storage tank partitioned by the operation of the full width bank installed in the inlet distribution tank and the outflow storage tank and prevented from being closed by the sludge while being discharged from the inside of the contact oxidation tank at least one selected from the group consisting of an acid pipe for supplying dissolved oxygen at all times or intermittently to water and crushed stone having a porosity of 30 to 40 or plastic having a porosity of 80 or more in the aeration part contact oxidation tank and the settling part contact oxidation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "precipitate contact oxidation tank 4 sludge hopper 5 to collect precipitated sludge outflow reservoir 10 to collect treated effluents outlet 11 to dispose of treated water and precipitation contact oxidation 4 it consists of a sludge storage tank 13 for sedimentation by storing the sludge precipitated in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the inlet 1 has a circular or rectangular shape as a part for collecting the polluted river water and sewage the effluent from the sewage treatment facility to flow into the contact oxidation tank and has a movable bank in the inlet distribution tank 2 18 weir is installed and the flow rate in the inlet distribution tank 2 is kept constant by adjusting the water level using the movable bank 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "by installing the acid pipe 11 in the lower portion of the outflow storage tank 10 by supplying oxygen to recover the dissolved oxygen to discharge to the river to remove the adverse effects of the river ecosystem"}]</data>
