", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "first referring to figure 3a the river filtration vertical collection well cleaning device according to the present invention is a general crane or drilling machine drilling equipment 11 a pipe attached to one side of the drilling equipment 11 and having a space therein a rod 12 having a shape and a brush 13 attached to an end of the rod 12 and cleaning the strainer 3 while lifting up and down along the rod 12 may be included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100430034-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the wastewater and the sludge supplied from the flow rate control tank are smoothly supplied with a predetermined amount of wastewater without clogging while the user visually confirms the flow rate and the sludge sludge by means of the flow rate and sludge sludge adjusting means while the user visually confirm the sludge sludge and a sludge regeneration step of regulating the flow rate of the sludge a microbial propagation means mbbr distributed in a range of 30 to 70 of the volume of the microorganism propagation tank so as to more efficiently adsorb and decompose harmful substances contained in the wastewater supplied to the microorganism propagation tank in the flow rate and return sludge control step a microbial growth step for maximizing the growth of microorganisms a sedimentation tank supplying step of supplying the treated water to the sedimentation tank wherein the harmful substances contained in the wastewater generated by the microorganism propagated by the microorganism growing step are more efficiently treated by the microorganisms by physical adsorption and biochemical methods a float and a settling sludge removing step for primarily removing suspended solids such as ss contained in the treated water supplied to the settling tank in the settling tank supplying step and removing the settled sludge the upper porous plate of the filtering means mcf is moved to the bottom dead center by the lifting member so that the suspended substances contained in the floated water separated in the float and the settling sludge removal step are secondarily removed and converted into clean water a supernatant inflow step for introducing the supernatant into the main body of the filtering means mcf a discharge step of passing the high water introduced in the high water inflow step through the filtering member to filter foreign substances contained in the high water and discharging the converted clean water to the outside of the filtering means mcf after discharging the clean water in the discharging step the upper perforated plate is moved to the top dead center so as to desorb the suspended matters contained in the filtering member and the washing water and air are introduced into the inside of the main body through the washing water inlet and backwash air inlet and a desorption step of desorbing suspended matters attached to the filtering member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101581252-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "thus the greeneye collecting apparatus according to the present invention can be efficiently and efficiently applied to a small river a reservoir it is possible to process the greenhouse by applying the control data set by the external server in real time and the greenhouse can be collected and dehydrated while driving the self generated power through the sunlight as the power source so that the ecological environment for the water quality can be efficiently improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the plate like door 27 is installed to open and close the waterway while being coupled by the door lifting member 27 penetrating through the upper center of the upper portion of the door 27 and spaced apart from the front and rear of the door 27 to face each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the door is coupled to and lifted through a pair of door frames having a shape in which lower portions are respectively inserted into and fixed to a pair of intake door walls formed integrally with the support block and a door lifting member penetrating through an upper center of the door frame"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "door plate 26 which is a shape is coupled to the plate through the door lifting member 27 passing through the center of the upper end of the door frame 26 the plate like door 27 is installed to open and close the waterway and the front and rear of the door 27 is formed so as to face each other the aeration generating plate 22 is fixed to both sides of the intake door wall 21 the aeration generating plate 22 is a constant a plurality of drains 23 are penetrated at intervals to discharge the river water and generate aeration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "therefore when the water level of the river and the like to increase the water level by the blowing beam 10 blocking the river and secure the required quantity the door lifting member 27 rotates the door 26 installed in the water intake door 20 and the door 26 is lowered to the bottom of the intake door 20 to reduce the amount of river water discharged through the intake door 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741836-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the multifunctional movable guard gate which is constructed to dredge the river and to be driven by the fixed support and actuator cylinders is combined with the foundation concrete to be combined with the side wall to save the river ecosystem and at the same time in the eco friendly construction method which combines the integrated control system and the remote control system that operate the opening and closing operations in a comprehensive manner to purify polluted river water while reviving the river ecosystem after dredging the entire width of the stream the foundation of the river is provided with foundation concrete an exponential wall body is formed on one side and the other side surface of the foundation concrete and an elevating guide wall is formed on an end surface of the exponential wall so as to project laterally the upper and lower operation guides for vertically moving up or down the multi purpose movable function gate are coupled to the elevating guide wall in a u shape a lower end of the cylinder rod is coupled to an upper end of the lifting guide wall the cylinder rod is mechanically coupled to the upper and lower operation cylinders the upper and lower operating cylinders are fixedly engaged with a cylinder support which serves to act as a support when the upper and lower operation guides are operated up and down a fixed support for fixing the artificial multi function movable security gate is fixedly connected to one side and the other side of the upper and lower operation guides the lower end of the actuating device cylinder which is formed inside the universal multifunctional movable retainer and the upper end of the operating device cylinder is connected to the upper end of the double acting multifunctional movable storage tank in a whitish manner so as to store or discharge the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101293413-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the buoyancy body 22 and the wire 23 which connects the water gate 21 and the buoyancy body 22 so that the buoyancy gate 21 can be opened and closed in conjunction with the lifting and lowering of the buoyancy body 22 and it is composed of a pulley 24 installed on the inner ceiling of the storage tank 10 so as to support the wire 23 the natural freshwater of the river water introduced into the storage tank 10 and the river water stored in the storage tank 10 it is preferable that it is comprised so that it may drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101931526-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "therefore the rotary damper r for removing various contaminants and suspended matters as described above is constructed such that no clearance is generated from the frame 100 or the rake 500 during the up and down movement of the lifting main screen 300 so that t