916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "a multi cross mill crusher 130 for processing the particulate contaminant molecules contained in the contaminated river water into fine ultrafine magnetic material molecules by crushing them and then striking them the rotary bucket 212 the contaminant injection remover 215 the submersible pump 216 the connecting pipe 214 the support 213 is formed on the rear surface of the tertiary contaminant screw feeder 108 particulate matter a floating material collection rotating bucket 109 for collecting and transporting floating material molecules floating on the water while collecting the ultra fine particles having a low specific gravity a fourth suspended solids collecting conveyor 110 which conveys particulate matters and ultra low specific gravity particles collected on the rear portion of the suspended solids collecting rotation bucket 109 it is composed by combining the rotary body 204 and the rotary support 303 on the rear portion of the conveyor 112 for collecting the suspended solids and collects particulate contaminants and ultra fine magnetic impurities that rise to the upper layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100686885-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "that is according to the fourth embodiment of the present invention even when the water gate 30 is closed the lower layer water of the storage space may be introduced through the inlet 61 and be discharged on the principle of siphon through the outlet 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102207360-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a first motor and a suction hopper mounted in front of the body to suck the sediment a discharge pipe connected in communication with the suction hopper to send the sucked sediment to the outside and installed inside the suction hopper to crush the sediment an underwater cleaning robot comprising a crushing screw and a second motor for driving the crushing screw and a hydraulic pressure generating device mounted on the body and configured to drive the first and second motors using hydraulic pressure and control remotely the technology is also presented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100983257-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "in addition as shown in figures 4 to 6 along the inner circumferential surface of the tip of the nozzle outlet 13 the crushing projection to collide with the air bubbles injected with the river water to crush the air bubbles into finer particles bar 17 is formed to protrude at regular intervals the crushing projection 17 is also not limited to the shape or number shown in the drawings of course can be installed in various forms and number"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894569-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "1 the water treatment apparatus according to the present invention includes an inflow water storage tank 10 for receiving and storing ground water and river water an ozone supply unit 20 for supplying ozone an ozone mixer 30 for mixing the ozone with the ozone and discharging it as mixed water while removing the contaminants contained in the influent water and an ozone bubble crusher 30 for supplying the mixed water discharged from the ozone mixer 30 50 for receiving and storing the treated water treated in the ozone bubbler crushing part 40 and discharging the treated ozone while removing the residual ozone contained in the treated water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_452", "text": "to maintain state therefore a space is generated between the sluice gate 30 and the housing 20 so that the lower layer water of the reservoir can be discharged through the space and foreign substances such as sedimentary sludge deposited on the bottom of the river are generated by the action"}]</data>
