e 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101504881-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "further in the present invention the floating screen and the movable screen connected thereto are installed in front of the orifice so that the movable screen covers the orifice for a predetermined time during which the water level in the rainfall chamber rises during rains thereby temporarily filtering the foreign substances over the fence it is possible to temporarily block or reduce the inflow of foreign matter into the sewage treatment plant through the connection pipe at the time of bar and rainfall.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "however if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100375130-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the past there was a poverty that caused social controversy such as untreated and discharged to the terminal treatment discharge pipe in the untreated state contaminating the water quality of the water supply source or adversely affect the biological growth in the water.the present invention has been invented to prevent the above closed end of the present invention is to be installed in the initial sedimentation tank cold dust chamber to the front end inlet of the body having a fastening flange portion is attached to the hinge portion formed on the upper surface of the body disc it is installed to be opened and closed by means of the connecting pipe through the fastener is installed on the left and right sides of the upper connecting portion between the supports connected to the shaft of the hinge portion the fitting section of the connecting pipe through the support between the buckle is installed in the early stage of rain when a large amount of rainwater flows in at this time as the floats fastened to the left and right connectors and the floats fastened to the disks the disks in the open open state move downwards to the support point to block the inlet formed at the tip of the body"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0627530-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the passage channel 58 formed due to the hollow curvature in the bottom of the float the cross section of which is enlarged downwards through the trough shape of the chamber bottom 30 serves for an unimpeded outflow of rain or mixed water as long as the outflow quantity does not need to be throttled for example in the case of a mixed water sewerage system twice the dry weather outflow quantity does not exceed"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080805-A", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the water in the well might have a low ph due to surrounding soil conditions the effects of acid rain or due to oxidation of anion portions of the original iron compounds"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "at least one sensor device can expediently be provided in order to determine the degree of contamination of the retaining elements"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "in the event that the rain overflow basin 1 is busy or there is a blockage in the area of the retaining element 8 the water can thus flow from the basin chamber 5 to the basin overflow 7 via the emergency overflow 16 without being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "however if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_191", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275666-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "contained in the rain water is first filtered by the grating cover 3 but those passing through the sedimentation chamber 9 formed at the bottom of the sump 1 after the accumulation the discharge pipe 2 has a structure that is discharged through the drain pipe 2 thereby becoming a main factor to block the drain pipe 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "that is when rainwater c flows in through the opened discharge port 120 the rainwater c flows into the rainwater receiving chamber 420 and the second buoyancy body 410 seals the rainwater receiving chamber 420 with the buoyancy of the rainwater c thereby blocking the fluid inflow into the casing 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100795399-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "2001919900000 2000.05.31 rainwater sediment in the combined sewage system was excellent in preventing sand inflow and contaminant inflow but the sewage was stagnated at the bottom of rainwater sewage chamber causing odor occurrence there was no problem of collecting only the amount of sewage so that there was a problem that excessive sewage flowed into the tea house and the sewage treatment plant in rainy weather.the technical problem to be achieved by the present invention is to prevent the inflow of sand and contaminants into the collecting pipe to prevent the odor caused by decay by the absence of stagnation of sewage and to provide an improved stormwater to collect only the planned sewage during rain will be"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the rainy soil chamber of patent document 4 is a buoy that adjusts the degree of opening of the connecting pipe according to the increase in flow rate in the connection pipe connecting the rain soil chamber and the drain pipe so that it can collect as much as the design capacity regardless of the increase in flow rate due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at the end of the sewer pipe 1 the sewage discharge port 2 is normally closed to guide the sewage to the sewage treatment plant through the rainwater discharge chamber 3 to block the discharge of odors and to increase the amount of sewage into rainwater that flows during rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage outlet odor prevention device to guide the stream while opening a box frame 10 installed at an end of the sewage pipe 1 at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber 3 and seated on an outer circumference of the opened sewage discharge port 2 a primary blocking door 20 connected to the upper hinge part 11 at the upper end of the box frame 10 to block the sewage discharge port 2 to block odor a plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 which are connected to the primary blocking door 20 and block odor while being opened and closed according to water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced during rain hinge connecting portion 40 for opening and closing the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 in accordance with the water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced in rainy weather by being connected to the upper side of the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the sewage discharge odor blocking device of the present invention for achieving the above object is normally blocked at the distal end of the sewage pipe to block the discharge of odor and discharge of odors and when rain rains in large quantities when the rain flows to open the sewage to guide the river a discharge opening odor blocking device comprising a box frame installed at an upper end discharge port of a sewer pipe at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber and seated at an outer circumference of an open sewage discharge port a primary blocking door connected to the upper end of the box frame to block odors by closing the sewage discharge outlets in usual times a second blocking door connected to the first blocking door to block the odor by blocking the sewage discharge outlet it is characterized by consisting of a hinge connecting portion to be connected to the upper side of the secondary barrier door to be separated from each other in order to open and close the plurality of blocking doors in order to correspond to the water level in accordance with the water level and water pressure of the rain flowing in large quantities in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water filter in particular a rain water filter for a cistern with a housing 1 in which a sieve 9 is arranged which divides the housing 1 into a dirty water chamber and a clean water chamber wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet 12 for the filtered water with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon 17 into the dirty water outlet wherein in the lower part of the housing 1 of the water filter a siphon chamber 15 is formed which connects with the dirty water outlet via an overflow edge 16 and which has an outer opening 14 and that for forming the siphon 17 in the siphon chamber 15 a region between the overflow edge 16 and the outer opening 14 is separated by means of a partition wall 18 wherein the lower edge of the partition wall 18 is situated below the outer opening 14 and below the overflow edge 16 and wherein a dirty water outlet pipe 13 which forms the dirty water outlet runs through the siphon chamber 15 and has an opening forming the overflow edge 16 inside the siphon chamber 15 which is situated on the upper side of a horizontally extending portion of the dirty water outlet pipe 13 characterized in that the housing 1 has an upper part 2 in the form of a cylinder that is closed on the lower side by a bottom 5 wherein the bottom 5 has a passage 6 to which the dirty water outlet pipe 13 is connected and that the housing has a lower part 3 which contains the siphon chamber 15 and has the form of a pot which is connected with its open side to the bottom 5 and that the dirty water outlet pipe 13 runs in a bend through the siphon chamber this bend leading to a portion of the lateral wall of the lower part 3 and extending through this portion"}]</data>
