h", "pack", "join", "support", "effectuate", "penetrate", "fall", "dissolve", "hoist", "move", "oxidize", "locate", "reduce", "plug", "may", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "net", "spot", "obtain", "deposit", "evaporator", "transfer", "construct", "charge", "finish", "heat", "avoid", "galvanize", "drain", "dose", "shape", "continue", "bypass", "be", "suppress", "inch", "warm", "combine", "apply", "drill", "weld", "rise", "reach", "assume", "aerate", "extract", "display", "sld", "dump", "refer", "increase", "achieve", "soften", "maximize", "contemplate", "leach", "retain", "circulate", "notify", "provide", "wrap", "contain", "mention", "space", "uncoil", "ship", "proceed", "scale", "escape", "enhance", "arrange", "leak", "vaporize", "size", "calculate", "process", "limit", "release", "migrate", "oil", "do", "settle", "create", "facilitate", "align", "exceed", "baffle", "disinfect", "weave", "direct", "spawn", "seat", "box", "cover", "show", "equalize", "bifurcate", "configure", "overheat", "cool", "derive", "start", "fit", "enable", "guide", "perform", "act", "thereto", "occlude", "consist", "open", "mean", "supply", "use", "propeller", "cut", "draw", "extend", "control", "transmit", "case", "need", "monitor", "elevate", "groove", "collect", "instal", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101089024-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "this is because the cavitation phenomenon is prevented when the non suction single stage volute pump is used and pumping suction may occur even at low tide so durability and pumping efficiency are excellent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177665-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "air discharge valves 23 and 26 for discharging air to the outside to prevent the cavitation of the chamber when the temperature rises or falls beyond the highest or lowest point a water transmission system 24 which transmits to the control unit 10 and a water level meter 25 to measure the water level in accordance with the movement of the float 28 to the control unit 10 characterized in that it comprises a shock absorber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177665-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the air discharge valve 23 for discharging air to the outside to prevent the cavitation of the chamber when the water level is further dropped beyond the lowest point and is located at the top to measure the pressure in the air chamber 17 to control the a pressure transmitter 24 for delivering to the unit 10 a water gauge 25 for measuring the water level and delivering it to the control unit 10 and positioned at the top to allow cavitation of the chamber when the water level rises further past the highest point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102654788-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "electrolysis in the electrolytic chamber is performed efficiently to increase the concentration of dissolved hydrogen while suppressing damage to the diaphragm"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-7013909-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the vacuum valve controller 100 thus constructed operates as follows when the water level of sewage in the sewage pit 1 increases and the pressure in the pressure sensor pipe 2 increases the pressure is transmitted via the pipe 33 to the first chamber 17 of the vacuum valve controller 100"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "as a result contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "a certain water level difference in this case indicates a reduced flow of water between the pelvic chamber 5 and the storage space 10 via the retaining elements 11 wherein contamination of the retaining elements 11 can be concluded"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0418572-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "by increasing the water level 34a and the pressure generated thereby a vertical flow of the purified water in the space between the walls of the inner pot 42 and the pot like extension 41 is then promoted from top to bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also when the water level rises the retractable watershed wall prevents the backwash of the river water to prevent flooding damage and the impoundment collection box having a filter net for filtering the contaminants contained in the sewage and storm seats is installed so that the contaminants do not flow into the wells and an odor chamber connected to the ceiling of the sewage pipe at an upper portion of the open the curtain can be installed to block the malodor generated in the sewer line and to move the sewer line along the moving rail to the left and right sides of the sewer line to conveniently remove and remove the contaminant lifting device connected with the wire have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654508-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the precipitation inducing grooves 511 are formed so as to be curved downwardly inclined so as to reach one upper end portion the precipitation inducing groove 511 is formed at a predetermined distance from the upper end of one side of the swash plate 510 and the upper end of one side of the lower flat plate portion toward the other side upper end portion of the lower flat plate portion and curved downward and a plurality of depressions are formed in an inclined shape"}, {"pat_id": "US-9078419-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "the bubbles eventually burst while suspended above as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "however in case the water in the filter chamber rises over a water level of the overflow weir 37 placed at the filtrate outflow chamber 36 the injected oxidation air cannot rise over the water surface of the filter chamber but can be moved to the outflow side due to the air pressure by the water head difference with the outflow side"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "then the backwashing water is transferred from the collecting chamber 24 to the filter chamber through the conveyance pipe 235 connected to the underdrain block 23 and the pressure equalizing chamber 232 and the collecting orifices 231 thereby flowing upward in the filter medium 22"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "further as a result of spraying the air laden water into tank 33 the entrained air and any residual non oxidized gases in the water such as h2 s methane natural gas or the like are separated from the water resulting in a water column 55 in the bottom of tank 33 and an air and gas column 56 in the top of tank 33"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974535-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "also as described above the time point at which the initial rainwater drain valve v1 is closed closed can be closed only for a time period in which the water level precipitation amount is maintained on the high water level of the flowmeter chamber 112c when the rainwater is not continuously detected the initial rainwater exclusion valve v1 is closed closed to prevent contamination of the body portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore it is possible to block the supply of river water or seawater backflowing to the stormwater chamber 110 to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604858-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition the present invention is provided with a pressure automatic replenishment device to replenish the pressure but it is only possible to replenish a small amount of pressure for a limited time only when the water supply is provided through the pumping pipe to completely fill the leaked pressure completely it is not possible to do this but even if it is assumed that the normal positive pumping is very effective.the present invention is to actively solve all the problems in the groundwater supply apparatus of the above described prior invention and when the disk interlocking up and down with the mouth according to the change in water level reaches the minimum water level automatically the flow path of the water cylinder by closing the air pressure to prevent leakage to the outside and when the water supply to the water cylinder is started by the water supply pressure acting on the upper side of the disk forcibly moved upwards to open the flow path to smoothly supply water to the pressurized water tank it is to be an object of the invention.the present invention is to provide an air pressure leakage blocking device on the lower side of the pressurized water tank as a means for solving the above problems the air pressure leakage blocking device is connected to the water supply pipe to one side of the water chamber the other side of the water chamber a shaft guide holder is installed at the center of the flow path of the water supply cylinder formed on the upper part and a disk shaft is installed at the upper and lower sides of the shaft guide holder respectively and a disk is provided at the cover bracket radially installed on the outer circumferential surface of the water cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6779430-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an internal or water level adjusting mechanism which is installed outside the tank the water level control mechanism the degradation accumulated amount of the treated water in the storage tank is allowed to overflow exceeds a predetermined level constant the water level of the decomposition storage tank while maintaining the level the water level in the food waste disposer is the same as the water level in the decomposition storage tank in conjunction with this water level and exceeds the perforated plate and is one of the stirring mechanisms in the stirring chamber"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6779430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an internal or water level adjusting mechanism which is installed outside the tank the water level control mechanism the degradation accumulated amount of the treated water in the storage tank is allowed to overflow exceeds a predetermined level constant the water level of the decomposition storage tank while maintaining the level the water level in the food waste disposer is the same as the water level in the decomposition storage tank in conjunction with this water level and exceeds the perforated plate and is one of the stirring mechanisms in the stirring chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-970007651-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "filtration tank 20 for primary filtering the wash water drained from the air purifier 1 and the lower portion of the filtration tank 20 the upper part of the filtration filter 21 of the filtration tank 20 and the storage tank 30 communicates with the connecting pipe 15 and is divided into left and right sides by a filter 31 installed at an oblique plate and the external water supply pipe 13 is connected to receive secondary filtration and external water supply and the water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-7340879-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the system maintains a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling in the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h thermocouple and compensation wire 103i temperature measurement contact 103j thermocouple 103k compensation contact 103l compensation wire 103m reference contact 103n type of thermocouple 103o no protection tube 103p protection tube 103q high temperature object 103r protection tube there is 103s sis type 103t temperature measuring termi