ess the secondary settling tank 440 rectifies the flow rate as a final flocculation floc and flows the treated water separated from the flow rate rectifier 441 for dividing the treated water and sludge into the disinfecting discharge tank 510 which is the next process"}, {"pat_id": "US-12017929-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the control and monitoring tool comprises the control panel with microprocessor and control boards connected with it control valves and water level sensors"}, {"pat_id": "US-7238281-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the placement of first baffle 34 within inner chamber 20 reduces the turbulence of the water flowing into inner chamber 20 and directs oil and floatables to the center of passage 40 thereby enhancing the effectiveness of absorbent adsorbent material 42"}, {"pat_id": "US-10005001-B2", "para_id": "para_522", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as a result since the water supplied to the surface of the second pole chamber side of the diaphragm decreases there is a risk that the diaphragm may be damaged by overheating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "if the electrolytic water generator continues to be used while the second feed water passage or the second outlet is blocked the second outlet is immediately filled with the gas generated in the second electrode chamber and the water level in the second outlet is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "as a result electrolysis in the electrolytic chamber 40 is stopped and further decrease in the water level in the second outlet 13 is suppressed so that damage to the diaphragm 43 can be suppressed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794732-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "when electrolysis proceeds in this state the water in the second pole chamber