he activated carbon is removed thereby backwashing the activated carbon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101630395-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the control unit 100 receives data on the operation state of the air compressor 30 and the air discharger 40 transmitted from the detection circuit unit 50 and the real time pressure value and the water level transmitted from the pressure sensor 10 a real time water level value transmitted from the sensor 20 is calculated by an operation state analysis algorithm and a water shock is prevented by determining whether the water shock equipment is operating normally according to the operation result in the control unit 100 when the water level rises during a periodic change that does not follow the pressure change by applying the analysis algorithm the compressed air leaks due to the breakage of the air supply line portion wherein the water hammer is a water hammer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200366648-Y1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "an increase in rainwater from the sewer pipe p to the first accommodation chamber 13a through the inlet pipe 14 for example 4q flows in a clockwise direction along the water level in which the float 21 of the flow regulating opening 20 rises as the water level of the first accommodation chamber 13a rises as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-6171480-B1", "para_id": "para_162", "text": "in this embodiment the top of the drying tube is fitted with a venturi 44 that assists escaping air to carry the foam to a reservoir outside the system"}, {"pat_id": "US-6171480-B1", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "therefore the diameter of contact chamber is an important factor because as it increases the distance traveled in each complete circle increases and the volume of water that can be stripped increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102201560-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "40 and including a control unit 50 for controlling the chemical solution injection means 40 by the flow rate of the groundwater supply pipe 30 and the water level i