ibute medicines supplied from the pumping unit 200 300 comprising a leakage detection switch 370 is provided to detect chemicals leaked to the barrier wall 400 while forming a barrier wall 400 to collect chemicals leaking into a proper space on the floor where the medicine dispensing tank 300 is located and a medicine insertion visual identification unit 340 provided at a lower portion of the housing 310 in which the distal end of the medicine inlet pipe 320 is located so as to identify the inflow situation of the medicine with the naked eye the chemical injection detecting means 350 disposed directly below the water ejector 312 formed at the upper end of the front surface of each distribution chamber 311 formed at the rear portion of the housing 310 when the float switch 353 is vertically provided in the auxiliary water tank 352 provided in the support body 351 and the float 353a descends below the appropriate water level wherein the control unit is configured to notify that the inflow is stopped and to monitor the infusion of the medicine in the water supply chemical supply system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4808290-A", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "as mentioned above contaminants such as calcium and magnesium within anode chamber 52 can combine with hydroxyl ions that back migrate from the catholyte into the anolyte to form chlorates that can reduce the concentration of the brine such contaminates can also form deposits upon the anode side of the ion permeable membrane which deposits can lead to a plugging of the membrane and a corresponding reduction in the efficiency of the chlorinator"}, {"pat_id": "US-5059287-A", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a method for improving the efficiency of a distiller comprising the steps of a horizontally disposing a heating element between about one sixteenth and one half inch below a desired water level in a chamber for vaporizing water the heating element being spaced from the chamber s water containing sides by at least three quarters