43-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the bad smell source sucked by operating the blower 2 in the operation panel 15 is inside the first carrier storage chamber 5 1 via the vacancy 4 1 in order to facilitate the flow of air through the inlet 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the sewage discharge odor blocking device of the present invention for achieving the above object is normally blocked at the distal end of the sewage pipe to block the discharge of odor and discharge of odors and when rain rains in large quantities when the rain flows to open the sewage to guide the river a discharge opening odor blocking device comprising a box frame installed at an upper end discharge port of a sewer pipe at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber and seated at an outer circumference of an open sewage discharge port a primary blocking door connected to the upper end of the box frame to block odors by closing the sewage discharge outlets in usual times a second blocking door connected to the first blocking door to block the odor by blocking the sewage discharge outlet it is characterized by consisting of a hinge connecting portion to be connected to the upper side of the secondary barrier door to be separated from each other in order to open and close the plurality of blocking doors in order to correspond to the water level in accordance with the water level and water pressure of the rain flowing in large quantities in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the inflow chamber may further include a water level sensor installed penetrating inward from an upper surface of the inflow chamber so as to sense the water level inside the inflow chamber to control the operation of the contaminant treatment unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in other words the water level detector 12 is to operate the contaminant processing unit 40 only when the waste water reaches a constant level in the inflow chamber 10 to prevent unnecessary waste of power"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258669-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "1 and 2 since it may not always be consistently aligned on the cutout 106 the upper and lower lengths of the intergranular corrosion prevention protective cover 110a may cover the level formed above or below the level cutout 106"}, {"pat_id": "US-4582610-A", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thus the present invention generally contemplates providing spray holes in the well pipe at a location below the top of the well and above the average static water level in the well spraying and aerating a fractional portion of the well water pumped through the well pipe and permitting the fractional portion of well water to fall back down the well and checking the backflow of water in the well pipe from the building above the spray holes when pumping of water in the well pipe stops"}]</data>
