  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "ordinarily because of the imperfect seal between between piston 230 and interior wall 240 water filling reservoir 242 via aperture 250 is free to migrate into air chamber 258 the buildup of water is limited however by the presence of displaced air"}, {"pat_id": "US-4619819-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a nozzle comprising an inlet body having an inlet opening therethrough said inlet body having means for connection a pressurized stream of contaminated water thereto in communication with said inlet opening a throat body lying adjacent to and connected to said inlet body said throat body having an opening therethrough said throat body opening being in alignment with said inlet opening a resilient throat member attached to said throat body said resilient throat member lying in said opening through said throat body so that said throat member defines a nozzle throat a fluid pressure port in said throat body said fluid pressure port being connected between said throat member and said throat body so that pressurizing said port pressurizes said throat member to resiliently distend said throat member to reduce throat area therethrough an outlet body lying adjacent to and connected to said throat body said outlet body having an outlet opening therethrough in line with said throat opening said outlet opening being formed by a tapered expansion wall defining an expansion chamber therein said wall being shaped to expand contaminated water passing through said throat to maintain optimum cavitation in the water as it moves through the length of said expansion chamber and means for sensing conditions in the contaminated water stream at the inlet and outlet of said nozzle and control means for controlling the pressure in said port to control nozzle area said sensor means being connected to said control means wherein said control means varies the nozzle throat to optimize cavitation conditions in response to the sensed conditions in said inlet and outlet of said nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "US-8376254-B2", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "certain embodiments of the present invention provide a spray assembly 15 for use in an automatic well washer that can reduce and or eliminate the occurrence of blockage from accumulation of solid matter in a fluid stream used to wash the well vault or tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224234-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "as shown in figures 1 to 6 the present invention provides a settling basin 82 and the settling chamber 50 to prevent soil from entering the interior of the storage tank 30 while a certain distance to the small river 60 selected and collected sewage and initial excellent on the sewage 80 installed a number of sewage the sewage is directed directly to the sewage end treatment plant through the drainage house the initial excellent is buried in the sewage site 72 of the main stream 70 it collects in the old storage tank 30 and discharges it for a long time below the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant after rainy weather and prevents contamination of small rivers and mainstream streams 70 and adds sewage end treatment facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200432978-Y1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "therefore the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 in addition to being discharged to 122 the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-4451277-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the second temperature being greater than the first temperature after the primary stream has been injected into said front port of the elongate reaction chamber and has been allowed to travel toward the back end of said elongate reaction chamber during use a first injection side port downstream in the elongate reaction chamber located at such distance from the front port that 90 100 of oxidant injected by the automatic from injection control system in the front port is reacted with the organic matter by the time it reaches said injection side port during use an automatic side injection control system adapted to inject during use an amount of cooling water per unit time and an amount of oxidant per unit time through said first injection side port in a manner that the amount of oxidant injected through the first injection side port is effective to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a predetermined amount in the primary stream and the amount of the cooling water injected through the first injection side port is in proportion to the amount of the oxidant injected such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially counterbalances at least a portion of any heat of oxidation released n 1 following injection side ports each of the n 1 port ports being at such distance from the front port that 90 100 of the oxidant injected in all ports upstream of each n 1 side injection port is reacted with the organic matter by the time it reaches said injection side port during use and wherein the automatic side injection control system is adapted to inject an amount of cooling water per unit time and an amount of oxidant per unit time through each of said n 1 side injection ports during use in a manner that the amount of oxidant injected in each n 1 side injection port is effective to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a predetermined amount in the primary stream during use and the amount of the cooling water injected in each n 1 side injection port is in proportion to the amount of the oxidant injected such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially counterbalances at least a portion of any heat of oxidation released during use and such that the automatic side injection control system selectively controls the temperature of the stream in the range of 750 1200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "claim_21", "text": "during use the heating system being connected such that the stream flows from the heating system to the reaction chamber during use a conduit connected to introduce oxidant into the stream at or before the front portion of the reaction chamber during use an oxidant injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the oxidant injection port being connected to introduce oxidant into the reaction chamber during use a cooling water injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the water injection port being connected to introduce cooling water during use into the reaction chamber and an automatic controller adapted to control the amount of cooling water and oxidant introduced into the reaction chamber during use the amount of oxidant introduced being controlled to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a selected amount during use and the amount of cooling water introduced being controlled in proportion to the amount of oxidant introduced such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially i counterbalances at least part of the heat of oxidation released by the reaction of the oxidant with the organic matter and ii selectively controls the temperature of the stream in the range of 750 1200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-5582715-A", "para_id": "claim_60", "text": "during use the heating system being connected such that the stream flows from the heating system to the reaction chamber during use a conduit connected to introduce oxidant into the stream at or before the front portion of the reaction chamber during use a first oxidant injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the first oxidant injection port being connected to introduce oxidant into the reaction chamber during use a cooling water injection port connected to the reaction chamber downstream of the front portion of the reaction chamber the cooling water injection port being connected at about the same location or downstream of the first oxidant injection port and the cooling water injection port being connected to introduce cooling water during use into the reaction chamber a second oxidant injection port connected downstream of the cooling water injection port the second oxidant injection port being connected to introduce oxidant into the reaction chamber during use a controller adapted to control the amount of oxidant introduced into the reaction chamber during use the mount of oxidant introduced being controlled to reduce the content of organic matter in the stream by a selected amount during use and a temperature control system adapted to control the temperature of the stream during use the temperature control system being adapted to control the temperature of the stream by varying the amount of cooling water introduced as a function of the oxidant introduced such that heat absorbed by the cooling water substantially i counterbalances at least part of the heat of oxidation released by the reaction of the oxidant with the organic matter and ii selectively controls the temperature of the stream in the range of 750 1200 f"}, {"pat_id": "US-4537615-A", "para_id": "para_355", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0377131-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "another partial stream of the used catholyte from the cathode chamber 78 is transported via the line 91 and the metering pump 95 into a storage container 112 from which the used catholyte which has been given a basic ph value by the electrolysis reaction is available for the neutralization of the swimming pool water stands"}, {"pat_id": "US-11008737-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "hot air is blown across the ambient air stream 130 and circulated via an air blower 109 absorbing moisture from the ambient air stream and concentrating the humidity of the air in the first chamber 108"}, {"pat_id": "US-5306397-A", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "this is compensated by an automatically controlled pumping off of the brine with the lifting pump for the brine 13 and by subsequent refilling of the evaporation chamber 5 with new de aerated seawater via the tube 12"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0436666-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "that liquid may be disposed of in a variety of appropriate ways so long as disposal is accomplished with limited release of the contained contaminant compounds"}, {"pat_id": "US-6398194-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the total diameters of all the water distribution tubes 3 cannot exceed the diameter of the output pipe 13 to maintain the magnitude of pressure with the water distribution tubes 3 capable of withstanding the high water pressure from the output pipe 13 and conveying the supplied water to cavitation housings 4 the cavitation housings 4 are installed to the ends of the water distribution tubes 3 and are t shaped tubular fixtures having formed inside a spray guide element 41 inclined in the direction of water flow the said guide element 41 causes a slight reduction of the inner diameter thereby deflecting the flow of water downward to generate turbulence with the intake opening of a fresh air supply tube 5 situated immediately over this point which is approximately one third the distance away from the nearest end of the fixture where an annular projection along the inner diameter in conjunction with the spray guide element 41 changes the width of the original diameter reducing a section of the inner diameter and thereby forming a mixture chamber 44 in between a rear pressure constrictive opening 42 and a front pressure constrictive opening 43 near the spray nozzle 45 at the anterior such that when pressurized water flows forcefully out of the water distribution tube 3 the reduced flow volume effected by the rear pressure constrictive opening 42 results in an impedance that causes an instant raising of the water pressure and consequent increase in the momentum of the water surging through the smaller constrictive opening at which time the flow passes by the connector opening of the fresh air supply tube 5 with the frictional action inducing air through the interior of the said tube and into the mixture chamber 44 where the air and water are swirled against each other to produce a cavitated wash that continues to stream after eddying through the front constrictive opening 43 to emerge from the spray nozzle 45 into the greater body of water of the pond"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604858-B2", "para_id": "para_610", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759677-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in some embodiments the apparatus may further comprise two or more aerators wherein at least one aerator may be used to introduce air bubbles into the untreated water stream entering the evaporation chamber and at least one other aerator may be used to allow excess air or other gases to exit the evaporation chamber to maintain equilibrium and avoid a buildup of pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759677-B2", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the introduction of air bubbles into the untreated water stream will increase the surface area of contact between the heated air in the evaporation chamber and the untreated water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759677-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the portion of untreated water that does not evaporate is transported back into untreated water chamber 104 via recirculation reservoir 108"}, {"pat_id": "US-7340879-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the system maintains a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling in the system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4514366-A", "para_id": "para_304", "text": "prior to filling the tank a gelled clay was put in"}, {"pat_id": "US-5190728-A", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "a fouling monitor for continuously measuring chemical and biological fouling in a commercial water system having a main stream of the water wherein the biological and chemical fouling is due to the process of fouling deposits said monitor comprising means for taking a slip stream of water from the main stream of the water a dissolved oxygen probe for measuring dissolved oxygen levels said probe having a sensing head said sensing head having a roughened surface for enhancing the attachment of fouling deposits means for continuously supplying air to the slip stream means for selectively supplying nutrient to the slip stream means for mixing the air and nutrient in the slip stream a chamber in which the sensing head of the dissolved oxygen probe is received to expose the head to the slip stream mixture and means for recording the output of the probe whereby the probe continuously measures fouling and the addition of nutrient differentiates between chemical and biological fouling"}, {"pat_id": "US-5190728-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "as above explained the system may be for example a white water source to a paper making machine where it is important to control biological fouling in order to make quality paper"}, {"pat_id": "US-8069676-B2", "para_id": "para_518", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0070989-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "such fouling or freeze up can occur when a solution becomes supersaturated"}, {"pat_id": "US-10118835-B2", "para_id": "para_107", "text": "typically input water is pretreated to prevent clogging and fouling of the evaporation chambers due to settling of the sediment inherent in the input water stream as well as to reduce the scaling of the chamber walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-10005001-B2", "para_id": "para_522", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in this process when the clogging phenomenon is confirmed in the filter medium 140 the contamination adhered to the filter medium 140 is removed by supplying the compressed air through the air blowing pipe 144 thereby improving the filtration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101316313-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "one end is exposed to the upstream side of the valley channel 10 so that the fish can go upstream and the other end is partially buried to expose the wall surface of the drop beam 11 and the blockage of the fish 12 and a gravel trap 13 installed upstream of the fishery 12 so as to form a fishery that can inhabit the fish and a first superior soil chamber 21 formed downstream of the fishery 12"}, {"pat_id": "US-11002699-B2", "para_id": "para_608", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100757303-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole type body each having a sewage inlet pipe and an outlet pipe for guiding sewage of the sewer pipe to the sewage treatment plant through the first accommodation chamber the second accommodation chamber which is in communication with the first accommodation chamber among the accommodation chambers and the third accommodation chamber which is isolated from the first accommodation chamber are installed inside the body so as to communicate with each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100757303-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "a manhole type body installed with a sewage inlet pipe and an outlet pipe respectively in contact with the first accommodation room of any one of the rooms to guide the sewage of the sewer pipe to the sewage treatment plant through the first accommodation room the second accommodation chamber which is in communication with the first accommodation chamber among the accommodation chambers and the third accommodation chamber which is isolated from the first accommodation chamber are installed inside the body so as to communicate with each other"}, {"pat_id": "US-11840469-B2", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "when the contaminated water stream comprises a water oil mixture the components passing out through the first outlet the partially purified water stream may consist predominantly of water and any dissolved substances and depending on the extent of separation some oil and the components passing out of the second outlet the contaminant stream may consist predominantly of oil but with some water and dissolved substances being present"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318395-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in some embodiments the apparatus may further comprise two or more aerators wherein at least one aerator may be used to introduce air bubbles into the untreated water stream entering the evaporation chamber and at least one other aerator may be used to allow excess air or other gases to exit the evaporation chamber to maintain equilibrium and avoid a buildup of pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318395-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the introduction of air bubbles into the untreated water stream will increase the surface area of contact between the heated air in the evaporation chamber and the untreated water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318395-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the portion of untreated water that does not evaporate is transported back into untreated water chamber 104 via recirculation reservoir 108"}, {"pat_id": "US-5395522-A", "para_id": "para_108", "text": "water is admitted through an inlet port 80 flows through reaction chamber 46 in which organics in the water stream are oxidized and or ionized by exposure to uv while juxtaposed to a photocatalytic surface and exits through a plurality of exit ports 82"}, {"pat_id": "US-5395522-A", "para_id": "para_109", "text": "to provide a flow path through chamber 46 ensuring relatively dispersed flow and uniform residence time of the water within the chamber 46 so as to ensure uniform oxidation and or ionization of organics in the water stream electrodes 84 and 86 may be formed of sheet material curved as shown to provide semicircular baffles"}, {"pat_id": "US-11826681-B2", "para_id": "para_503", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-6998054-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "if the user is inclined to destroy the ammonium on site the column can be regenerated with hydrochloric acid and the regenerant waste treated in an electrolytric chamber under the influence of dc current to change the chlorides to hypochlorite which then reacts with the ammonia to eventually convert it to nitrogen gas through the mono di and tri chloramine reaction process"}, {"pat_id": "US-4539119-A", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "first sulfur dioxide absorption chamber 28 at ambient temperatures must remove nearly all of the sulfur dioxide present in the flue gas stream so that the sulfur dioxide discharged to the atmosphere via line 28b will meet the current federal and state air pollution standards"}, {"pat_id": "US-8992851-B2", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "an outlet or discharge port of the pump 5 is connected to and in fluid communication with an outflow conduit such as outlet pipe 9 which may lead to a settling storage tank or pond not shown for the treated water or in the alternative which may lead directly to a discharge location for the treated water depending on the particular circumstances of the treatment process"}, {"pat_id": "US-8992851-B2", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "most of the organic compounds in the wastewater are oxidized in the pump chamber 26 but some oxidation may take place in the outflow pipe 34 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-8992851-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the reactor chamber was connected to thus just upstream from the suction nozzle of a centrifugal pump having a 7 horsepower electric motor driving an open type impeller within a circular pump casing at a rate of 3400 revolutions per minute rpm"}, {"pat_id": "US-8992851-B2", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "the fenton s catalyst and the hydrogen peroxide are thereby combined in the recirculation conduit 160 which functions as a reaction chamber in which the fenton s catalyst and the hydrogen peroxide react to yield hydroxyl free radicals that are mixed with the water stream flowing in the recirculation conduit and expelled back into the main wastewater stream of the inflow pipe 112 and into the pump chamber 126 where the hydroxyl free radicals are available for the oxidation of the organic compounds under the agitation action of impeller 124"}, {"pat_id": "US-6171480-B1", "para_id": "para_162", "text": "in this embodiment the top of the drying tube is fitted with a venturi 44 that assists escaping air to carry the foam to a reservoir outside the system"}, {"pat_id": "US-9611160-B2", "para_id": "para_139", "text": "dilution with a rinsing water stream 52 can help reduce the cod level of the combined steam to below a predetermined target such as 2000 mg l prior to further treatment wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "9 the front water gate 40 is rotated by the water pressure generated by the elevated water level and is interlocked with the angle adjuster 53 of the good interlocking portion 50 the link section 60 is interlocked and the rotating plate 30 is rotated to reduce the outflow cross section of the grating 20 to block the inflow of rainwater into the fine powder chamber 2 so that a large amount of rainwater naturally flows out into the discharge stream soils inherent in stormwater are also naturally released into the discharge stream thereby blocking the introduction of the soil from the storm sewer thereby preventing the sediment from accumulating on the sewer sewer pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-5938900-A", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "rubber seal 404 meshes with the slot to preclude water leakage from the housing 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325645-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "this exemplary embodiment or another exemplary embodiment may further provide a pressurized chamber defined by the housing wherein the pressurized chamber is configured to hold a continuous sonic optimization fluid to allow the transducer to generate cavitation in the continuous sonic optimization fluid stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-12325645-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "this exemplary embodiment or another exemplary embodiment may further provide that the at least one solids dissociation apparatus further comprises at least one fluid passage defined by the at least one insert wherein the at least one fluid passage is adapted to isolated the continuous fluid stream inside of the at least one insert from the pressurized chamber and remote from the transducer to allow for cavitation inside of the at least one fluid passage via the traveling sonic wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435493-Y1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "therefore the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 in addition to being discharged to 122 the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-10167205-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "at 35 occurring in the middle of the chamber 27 the purified ice fragments sweep upward into the spiraling cold air stream while the heavier liquid core continues to fall to the bottom of the chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-10376807-B2", "para_id": "para_108", "text": "typically input water is pretreated to prevent clogging and fouling of the evaporation chambers due to settling of the sediment inherent in the input water stream as well as to reduce the scaling of the chamber walls"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 in the water blocking device of the buoyancy type clapboard block to prevent flooding and overburden of rivers including the flexible water blocking plate 80 made of the member 90 is installed the floating matter removal module 100 for removing the floating matter floating in the river when the water barrier block 60 is raised and lowered includes"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_508", "text": "35 in alternate embodiments the apparatus may maintain a constant blowdown water flow to prevent scaling and other accumulation in the apparatus as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-8980091-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "an effluent stream from the aeration basin is introduced into a membrane bioreactor to separate the solid content therefrom and thereby to produce activated sludge as a retentate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage outlet odor prevention device to guide the stream while opening a box frame 10 installed at an end of the sewage pipe 1 at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber 3 and seated on an outer circumference of the opened sewage discharge port 2 a primary blocking door 20 connected to the upper hinge part 11 at the upper end of the box frame 10 to block the sewage discharge port 2 to block odor a plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 which are connected to the primary blocking door 20 and block odor while being opened and closed according to water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced during rain hinge connecting portion 40 for opening and closing the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 in accordance with the water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced in rainy weather by being connected to the upper side of the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604863-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "alternatively sensors can be placed upstream to detect the level of contamination of the wastewater stream before it enters the confined chamber and the processor can predictively determine the correct number of cycles needed to treat the water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4076617-A", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "otherwise the gaseous bubbles of ozone and oxygen will dampen the acoustic energy and tend to prevent the necessary cavitation of the waste solids"}, {"pat_id": "US-5591415-A", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "actually it becomes critical to have the oxidation started in the premixing chamber in order to prevent unreacted products from exiting the reactor as it will be explained hereinbelow"}, {"pat_id": "US-5591415-A", "para_id": "para_166", "text": "because two phase feeds can be converted to higher temperature single phase feed in the upward extension 912 this embodiment of the invention serves to also minimize preheating requirements thereby facilitating operating cost and equipment investment reduction"}]</data>
</edge>
