 way valve a first heat pump to a sixth heat pump a first circulation pump and a second circulation pump and a control unit controlling the temperature of the leachate in the nitrification tank to a set range by controlling the agitator an expansion tank provided to compensate for a pressure of the heat exchanged refrigerant supplied through the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump and an air blower unit for supplying air supplied from the outside to the periphery of the agitator in the nitrification tank the air blower unit includes an air flow path for introducing outside air into the vicinity of the agitator a compressor for forcibly supplying external air through the air flow path and a nozzle provided at an end portion of the air flow path for discharging air toward the agitator and wherein the agitator includes a housing fixed to the bottom of the nitrification tank and passing through the inside in a vertical direction a propeller for rotating the inside of the housing to mix the leachate a driving motor for driving the propeller and a guide arm provided on the outer circumferential surface of the housing so as to be guided through the air passage when installed wherein the control unit controls the at least one of the first heat pump to the sixth heat pump to selectively operate the heat pumps when the temperature of the nitrification tank reaches the set temperature by receiving the data of the sensor unit the first circulation pump or the second circulation pump operates first and controls the heat pumps to operate after the set time has elapsed wherein the nitrification tank includes a plurality of ventilation doors formed with openings communicating with the outside at upper portions of the chambers and selectively opening and closing the openings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100762919-B1", "para_id": "para_121", "text": "as such by filling the contact media 136 in the influent stable contact chamber 131 the influent may be performed very stably re