g a predetermined space a cylindrical swirl flow induction separator for inducing the precipitates contained in the rainwater to be precipitated by gravity while inducing swirl flows of the rainwater provided in the chamber a float storage tank provided on the swirl flow induction separator for storing the suspended matter filtered by the swirl flow induction separator a wear provided on an outer wall of the swirl flow induction separator the teeth having an uneven shape repeatedly arranged to uniformly control the flow rate of the treated water to be moved and it comprises a swirl flow guide plate provided in a spiral form on the inner wall of the swirl flow induction separator a space between an edge portion of the chamber and the swirl flow induction separator and having four channel regions for equally distributing the swirl flow down flow in the swirl flow induction separator and directing the vertical upward flow the initial water treatment apparatus using the four channels characterized in that the treated water filled in the two channel areas are moved to the inner space of the weir at an equal flow rate through the weir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185905-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "however when the gate 51 is not normally opened due to corrosion of the rotating shaft 53 or interference with foreign matter the level sensor 54 maintains a state in which it is in contact with the compression spring 80"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200166989-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is characterized in that it consists of a packing part to be in close contact with the frame when the water is discharged to prevent the water is discharged to the outside or water is introduced from the outside the frame and the door part are reinforced with corrosion resistance by using a non metallic material and the hinge part is formed to be able to open and close in a rotatable state in a state where the door part is fixed and coupled to the frame at a corresponding position on the upper side thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102548347-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole 100 provided around roads or buildings for drainage of rainwater with a manhole cover 120 detachably assembled on the upper surface and having a drain 101 of a predetermined caliber on the bottom a chamber housing 110 provided in a pot bellied shape at the lower end of the drain 101 of the manhole 100 as the center and having a discharge port 102 and a connection flange 140 on the bottom surface a sewage pipe 200 having a flange 210 and an inlet 211 coupled to the connection flange 140 of the chamber housing 110 in a state buried in the ground at a predetermined depth so that rainwater flows through the manhole 100 it is installed inside the chamber housing 110 and when rainwater flows into the manhole 100 the outlet 102 is opened and when the water in the sewage pipe 200 flows backward it rises by buoyancy and blocks the drain 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102548347-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention is provided around roads or buildings for drainage of rainwater and a manhole cover is detachably assembled on the upper surface and a drain hole of a predetermined caliber is provided on the bottom a chamber housing provided in a pot bellied shape at the bottom of the manhole centering on the drain hole and having a discharge port and a connection flange on the bottom surface a sewage pipe buried at a predetermined depth in the ground provided with a flange coupled to a connection flange of the chamber housing and an inlet through which rainwater flows through a manhole it is installed inside the chamber housing opens the outlet when rainwater flows into the manhole and rises when the water in the sewage pipe flows backward to block the drain consists of"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102548347-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "therefore it is possible to effectively prevent the rainwater of the sewage pipe 200 from flowing back into the manhole 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "9 the front water gate 40 is rotated by the water pressure generated by the elevated water level and is interlocked with the angle adjuster 53 of the good interlocking portion 50 the link section 60 is interlocked and the rotating plate 30 is rotated to reduce the outflow cross section of the grating 20 to block the inflow of rainwater into the fine powder chamber 2 so that a large amount of rainwater naturally flows out into the discharge stream soils inherent in stormwater are also naturally released into the discharge stream thereby blocking the introduction of the soil from the storm sewer thereby preventing the sediment from accumulating on the sewer sewer pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "since the discharge port 120 is communicated with the inside of the casing 100 via the connecting port 423 at the top of the rainwater collecting chamber 420 the second buoyancy body 410 can block the fluid inflow through the discharge port 120 by sealing the connecting port 423 with the buoyancy of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "that is when rainwater c flows in through the opened discharge port 120 the rainwater c flows into the rainwater receiving chamber 420 and the second buoyancy body 410 seals the rainwater receiving chamber 420 with the buoyancy of the rainwater c thereby blocking the fluid inflow into the casing 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "therefore it should be understood that the embodiments described above are exemplary in all respects and not restrictive.1 ground type odor treatment device 21 rainwater catcher 21a grating 22 water pipe 23 road 24 curbstone 25 press block 26 connecting pipe 100 casing 110 inlet 120 exhaust port 130 cover 130a anti slip surface 200 odor treatment material receiving section 200a odor treatment material 201 access hole 210 inlet 220 outlet 230 s