rding to it is installed to correspond to the main rotation opening and closing plate 31 and is connected by a connecting means 4 provided on the outside of the rotating shaft 32a provided to be moved up and down through the movement fixing means 5 sewage inflow control device provided in the stormwater chamber characterized in that consisting of the auxiliary rotation opening and closing plate 32 to guide or block to the stormwater chamber 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100774588-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "therefore water is dispersed and dropped by the guide plate 33 while the sewage falls in the middle of the main rotation opening and closing plate 31 to prevent breakage of the main rotation opening and closing plate 31 during long time use"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101132846-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "rotating shaft 2 coupled across the inside of the frame 1 along the transverse direction of the and the opening and closing plate is installed in the rotating shaft 2 opening and closing the sewage inlet hole 711 according to the amount of sewage 3 and the horizontal holding stopper 4 coupled to the other side of the frame 1 to control the closed state of the opening and closing plate 3 and the opening stopper to control the opening angle of the opening and closing plate 3 in the rainwater and rainwater inflow prevention device of rainwater soil consisting of 5 the frame 1 is coupled to a single rotating shaft 2 is accompanied with a plurality of opening and closing plate 3 for opening and closing the sewage inlet hole 711 according to the amount of sewage in the inner center of the frame 1 is connected in the longitudinal direction to partition each opening and closing plate 3 and is provided with a support frame 11 to prevent the sag of the rotating shaft 2 the open stopper 5 is disposed transversely across the other lower portion of the opening and closing plate 3 and is elevated by the height adjusting means 6 coupled to both upper surfaces of the frame 1 to open and close the opening plate 3"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0346256-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an apparatus for in situ repairing of rainwater and sewage pipework which is too narrow to be inspected internally by the pressurised injection of a plugging product by means of a pump the plugging product being brought to an injection chamber by feed means the apparatus comprising a front module having a hook system at its front end and a rear module having sealing means characterised in that each module 1 2 has arms 3 5 movable from an inoperative position into an operative position by hydraulic means 4 6 connected to a hydraulic pump 8 disposed at ground level so that the front module 1 acts as a clearer and guide to facilitate the passage of the rear module 2 the same having interchangeable sealing means 9 at each of its two ends to bound with the pipe 7 an injection chamber 10 in the rear module 20 itself so as to minimise losses of plugging product the same being fed into the chamber 10 through a tube 11 connected to the pump 12 at ground level and extending into the chamber 10 and also into the walls of the pipe 7 not only between the arms 5 of the rear module 2 but also through the arms 5 the same being formed with perforations 23 the arms 5 therefore maintaining the plugging product after the postioning thereof it being possible to adapt the apparatus to various pipe diameters by virtue of the interchangeability of the sealing means 9 and by virtue of means 42 on the arms 3 5 of each module 1 2 for the attachment of plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102037006-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the floating body is coupled to the lower side of the support so that the float when the seal is high the other side of the support and the link is upward along the floating body and the one side and the adjusting plate are lowered to close the inflow pipe horizontal part.when the water is low the support and the other side of the link are lowered along the floating body by opening the horizontal part of the inlet pipe as the throttle is raised control device to block the odor by adjusting the inflow by the opening and closing according to the height of the water characterized in that the opening and closing according to the height of the water to block the odor while keeping the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "the opening and closing member 55 coupled with the lifting rod 51 is coupled to the upper storage chamber 35 when the lifting rod 51 moves upward to block the discharge port 39 to prevent the discharge of the rainwater to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100977492-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "4 the fixed block 18 may not be provided when the storm soil chamber 3 is narrow and the frame 10 is supported over the storm soil chamber 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100977492-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "therefore it is possible to adjust the interval between the opening and closing plate 30 and the sewage inlet plate 20 it is possible to adjust the amount of sewage 1 containing the earth and sand flowing into the rainwater chamber 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100795399-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "2001919900000 2000.05.31 rainwater sediment in the combined sewage system was excellent in preventing sand inflow and contaminant inflow but the sewage was stagnated at the bottom of rainwater sewage ch