oor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4377451-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore in such an aerobic sewage purification apparatus in particular when an abnormality occurs in the blower the inside of the septic tank cannot be maintained in a normal aerobic condition the purification function is lowered and untreated water from the septic tank to the river is discharged and becomes environmental pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101682161-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "first a certain volume of space is provided in a measurement chamber provided with a measurement sensor and water supplied from a water source such as a ground water intake point and a river or a lake can be stored in this space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "the manhole 200 is configured to discharge contaminants through the discharge pipe 2 and the induction apparatus 100 is configured to discharge contaminants to the river in the contaminant discharge chamber 12 and may include a recovery pipe 260 so that contaminants discarded in the induction apparatus 100 can be collected and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore it is possible to block the supply of river water or seawater backflowing to the stormwater chamber 110 to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101293413-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the buoyancy body 22 and the wire 23 which connects the water gate 21 and the buoyancy body 22 so that the buoyancy gate 21 can be opened and closed in conjunction with the lifting and lowering of the buoyancy body 22 and it is composed of a pulley 24 installed on the inner ceiling of the storage tank 10 so as to support the wire 23 the natural freshwater of the river water introduced into the storage tank 10 and the river water stored in the storage tank 10 it is preferable that it is comprised so that it may drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101577682-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a filtration apparatus for filtering foreign matter in a sample in ground water river water or seawater a tubular type filtration chamber communicating with a connection pipe through which the sample is supplied to form a path for moving the sample and discharging the filtered water filtered by the foreign substance to the discharge port while providing a filtration space of the sample introduced into the inlet and and a filtration member for filtering the foreign substance of the sample while providing the discharge port to the discharge port while shielding the discharge port in a state of being built in the filtration chamber so as to be able to communicate therewith wherein the filter member comprises a mesh network which is formed in a cylindrical shape having openings on both sides and which is fixed to the filtration chamber while receiving the discharge port through one opening and is formed of a mesh body to filter the foreign substances of the sample and supply filtered filtrate to the discharge port a mesh network shielding plate fixed to the mesh network to shield the other opening of the mesh network while guiding the sample introduced into the inlet of the filtration chamber to the mesh network and and a mesh network coupler for releasably securing the mesh network to the filtration chamber the filtration device comprises and a sample guide provided in a part of the filtration member or a part of the filtration chamber to guide the sample introduced into the inlet of the filtration chamber to the mesh network the sample guide and a branch protrusion protruding conically from the mesh screen shield plate to branch the sample radially while facing the sample introduced into the inlet port"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101577682-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "the method according to claim 1 said filtration chamber comprising a chamber main body formed at one end of the inlet port and connected to the connection pipe to provide a filtration space of the sample and to open at the other end to detachably receive the mesh network and and a chamber cover having a discharge port formed therein for shielding the opening of the chamber body so as to be openable and closable the chamber cover being connected to the connection pipe and a part of the mesh network coupler being provided to detachably fix the mesh network"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101577682-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a filtration apparatus for inspecting a sample of groundwater river water or seawater the apparatus comprising a filtration apparatus for filtering foreign matter in groundwater river water a filtration chamber of a tubular type which is provided to allow the passage of the sample to flow and to provide the filtration space of the sample introduced into the inlet port and to discharge the filtered water filtered by the foreign substance to the outlet port and a filtration member for filtering the foreign substance of the sample while shielding the discharge port in a state of being built in the filtration chamber so as to communicate with the discharge port wherein the filtration member is formed into a cylindrical shape having openings on both sides thereof a mesh network fixed to the filtration chamber while receiving the discharge port through an opening the mesh network being made of a mesh body to filter the foreign substances of the sample and supply filtered filtrate to the discharge port a mesh network shielding plate fixed to the mesh network to shield the other opening of the mesh network while guiding the sample introduced into the inlet of the filtration chamber to the mesh network and a mesh network coupler for detachably securing the mesh network to the filtration chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100555594-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "the apparatus provided in the chamber 200 is prevented from contacting with water and when external air is introduced into the apparatus chamber later the apparatus is discharged to the air inlet 201 thereby preventing corrosion of the apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 made of a flexible water plate 80 in the order device of the buoyancy type clapboard block to prevent overflow and overburden of rivers including on the upper side of the fixing plate 70 the giyeok shaped cover members 90 respectively installed to protect the flexible water blocking plate 80 are installed it includes a floating matter removal module 100 for removing the floating matter floating in the river when the water blocking block 60 goes up and down the floating matter removal module 100 a pair of pinion gears 110 that are rotatably installed on the guide structure 54 and are installed at regular intervals on both sides based on the guide groove 53 a rack gear 120 formed on an outer circumferential surface of the water barrier block 60 to rotate the pinion gear 110 by meshing with the pinion gear 110 when the water barrier block 60 is raised and lowered a pair of arms 130 coupled to the center of the pinion gear 110 to rotate together with the rotation of the pinion gear 110 a connecting shaft 140 connecting the pair of arms 130 to each other a mesh network member 150 installed on the arm 130 to filter the floating matter floating in the river by rotating the connecting shaft and a rotation motor 160 for rotating the mesh member 150 at a predetermined angle with respect to the arm 130 to rotate the mesh member 150 to remove the floating matter filtered by the mesh member 150"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 as a water blocking device of a buoyancy type water blocking block to prevent flooding and over wave of a river including a flexible water plate 80 made of it is a configuration in which the member 90 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 the horizontal portion of the water barrier block 60 from the upper side of the buoyancy chamber 51 so as to prevent the water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side by being compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal portion 62 62 a pressing portion 81 compressed on the upper surface and a fixing plate portion 82 extending from the pressing portion 81 and fixed to the lower end of the fixing plate 70 on both upper surfaces of the buoyancy chamber 51 in the water blocking device of the buoyancy type clapboard block to prevent flooding and overburden of rivers including the flexible water blocking plate 80 made of the member 90 is installed the floating matter removal module 100 for removing the floating matter floating in the river when the water barrier block 60 is raised and lowered includes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102295330-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "a vertical part 61 and a water barrier block 60 comprising a horizontal portion 62 protruding in the horizontal direction on both sides at the lower end of the vertical portion 61 a plurality of bolts 99 on both sides of the upper surface of the buoyancy chamber 51 are fixedly installed via a fixing plate 70 in the width direction of the river and when the water block 60 rises the vertical part of the water block 60 61 it is made of a flexible water blocking plate 80 that is compressed on both sides and the upper surfaces of both sides of the horizontal part 62 to prevent water flowing into the buoyancy chamber 51 from passing to the embankment side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the rainy soil chamber of patent document 4 is a buoy that adjusts the degree of opening of the connecting pipe according to the increase in flow rate in the connection pipe connecting the rain soil chamber and the drain pipe so that it can collect as much as the design capacity regardless of the increase in flow rate due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the sewage discharge odor blocking device of the present invention for achieving the above object is normally blocked at the distal end of the sewage pipe to block the discharge of odor and discharge of odors and when rain rains in large quantities when the rain flows to open the sewage to guide the river a discharge opening odor blocking device comprising a box frame installed at an upper end discharge port of a sewer pipe at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber and seated at an outer circumference of an open sewage discharge port a primary blocking door connected to the upper end of the box frame to block odors by closing the sewage discharge outlets in usual times a second blocking door connected to the first blocking door to block the odor by blocking the sewage discharge outlet it is characterized by consisting of a hinge connecting portion to be connected to the upper side of the secondary barrier door to be separated from each other in order to open and close the plurality of blocking doors in order to correspond to the water level in accordance with the water level and water pressure of the rain flowing in large quantities in rainy weather"}]</data>
