  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100454362-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "and an anaerobic oxygen free aerobic step for causing an organic oxidation reaction opening the barrier wall and maintaining the entire reaction chamber in aerobic state for the first time in the state of integrating the first and second reaction chambers to dephosphate excess intake organic matter oxidation reaction and denitrification gas generated in the previous anoxic stage excess sludge a total exhalation excess sludge discharge step of opening the outlet to discharge excess sludge ingested with phosphorus the variable barrier wall is characterized by consisting of the entire anoxic precipitation discharge step of discharging the supernatant by opening the treated water outlet after the sludge for a predetermined time by switching the entire reaction chamber to an anoxic state in the open wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654508-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the precipitation inducing grooves 511 are formed so as to be curved downwardly inclined so as to reach one upper end portion the precipitation inducing groove 511 is formed at a predetermined distance from the upper end of one side of the swash plate 510 and the upper end of one side of the lower flat plate portion toward the other side upper end portion of the lower flat plate portion and curved downward and a plurality of depressions are formed in an inclined shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101833173-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a supply pipe for supplying a branch pipe which is split at one side of the supply pipe a solenoid valve for shielding the branch pipe a drug reservoir containing a chlorine liquid a chemical liquid conduit connected to the chemical reservoir for introducing the chlorine liquid into the branch pipe a metering pump for injecting the chlorine liquid into the chemical liquid transfer conduit a merging pipe formed in a y shape and mixing raw water introduced through a supply pipe with treated water in which a chlorine liquid flowing through the chemical liquid transfer pipe and a part of the raw water flowing through the branch pipe are mixed a controller for controlling the solenoid valve and the metering pump the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water flowing from the measurement branch pipe is set to a value obtained by subtracting the concentration of the residual chlorine contained in the dilution water from the measurement branch pipe and a residual chlorine measuring unit including a residual chlorine measuring sensor for measuring the residual chlorine and a zinc ionizing electrode for removing anions contained in the introduced dilution water wherein a plurality of partition walls are provided between the zinc ionizing electrode and the residual chlorine measuring sensor and a display window is provided on one side of the controller and the measurement is made from the current chlorine measuring unit to measure the concentration of the foreign matter in the precipitation chamber the information of the residual chlorine is displayed on the display window of the controller and the opening closing sensor provided in the water supply and the controller drives the solenoid valve and the metering pump at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0126558-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in order to smoothly induce sediment residue a recovery hole 41 is formed at the bottom of the sedimentation chamber 40 composed of the inclined surface so as to drop the sedimentation debris into the decay chamber 20 in the recovery hole 41"}, {"pat_id": "US-10654738-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in processes for the precipitation of solids in a fluidized bed reaction chamber despite the presence of the fluidized bed with its abrasive effect to reduce deposits forming on the reaction chamber in a wall certain portions in the reaction chamber may not be optimally circulated thus allowing the deposit of salts on the walls for instance at the inlet of the reaction chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974535-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "also as described above the time point at which the initial rainwater drain valve v1 is closed closed can be closed only for a time period in which the water level precipitation amount is maintained on the high water level of the flowmeter chamber 112c when the rainwater is not continuously detected the initial rainwater exclusion valve v1 is closed closed to prevent contamination of the body portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100403183-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "a highly concentrated precipitation tank for filtration oxidation and decomposition to remove biochemical oxygen demand bod and suspended solids ss the high concentration sedimentation filtration chamber 2 400b in the rear is formed through the high concentration filtration chamber b and the upper portion the outlet is formed in the upper end of the rear side the disinfection tank 510 is built in the outlet side to filter and purified filthy water from the disinfection tank 510 it consists of a discharge tank 500 which is discharged after contact by sterilization is a basic feature of the technical configuration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472947-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the first coagulation stir motor 320a and the second coagulation stir motor 320b rotate 60 times per minute to prevent breakage of the large coagulation floc generated by contact with the polymer coagulant and the first coagulation stir shaft 322a and a second agglomeration stirring shaft 322b are provided with a plurality of first agglomeration stirring blades 324a and a second agglomeration stirring blade 324b"}, {"pat_id": "US-8002974-B2", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "it is noted that inclusion of an intermediate chamber 34 at the lower right side of pretreatment apparatus 10a and upstream from inlet 16b of stormwater management apparatus 10b is desirable to the ph buffering reaction as well as to precipitate and complex formation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in the filtration chamber 13 a precipitation filter 21 is installed to remove suspended matter and rust contained in raw water of tap water flowing from the tap water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420441-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "hydrocarbons and carbonates produced in colloidal form adsorb and lead to coagulation and precipitation of lead chromium and other heavy metal ions in seawater to remove heavy metals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101004287-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the filtration chamber is formed in the center and the precipitation chamber and the aggregation chamber is provided with a main body formed sequentially on the outside of the filtration chamber the agglomeration chamber is it is formed to be supplied to the bottom of the settling chamber through the vertical flow path is formed in the outer side of the settling chamber formed through the inlet formed in the upper portion flowing downwards a plurality of baffle plates in the agglomeration chamber the plurality of obstruction plates being spaced apart from each other in the vertical direction to move along the passage formed in a zigzag shape a lifting wire having one end fixed to the baffle plate positioned at the lowest end and fixed to a fixing unit installed at the upper portion of the main body through a through hole formed in the baffle plate positioned at an upper portion thereof and and a weight member connected to a lower portion of the baffle plate positioned at the lowest end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175904-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in the filtration chamber 13 a precipitation filter 21 is installed to remove suspended matter and rust contained in raw water such as tap water flowing from the tap water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200160370-Y1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the filter 100 to facilitate the filter 100 the filtration chamber 230 for filtering the waste water fermented by the filter device 100 through the contact medium and the contact filter 240 of the filter chamber 230 the precipitation chamber 220 is formed to receive the filtrate purify the sedimentation action and discharge it in a clean state and at the same time the precipitated debris may fall into the decay chamber 250"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a plurality of annular movable partitions installed evenly up and down a rotation mechanism installed in the center of the annular closed chamber to rotate and drive the annular movable partition plate and an annular movable partition installed on the inner wall of the annular closed chamber"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "2 in the present invention a discharge hole is installed in the annular movable partition plate a discharge unit is installed below the discharge hole and the annular movable partition plate rotates to effectively clog the pipe due to organic salt precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7083442-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the vessel 311 the three annular movable partition plates 312 evenly installed vertically inside the annular closed chamber 310 and the rotating mechanism 31 installed in the center of the annular closed chamber 310 to rotate and drive the annular movable partition plate 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420116-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in order to achieve the object of the present invention as described above an integrated contaminant processing apparatus according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention has an inlet formed on one side the inlet chamber is formed to open the other side a precipitation chamber installed at an open portion of the inflow chamber having a discharge port formed on the other side a overflowware installed on the inner side corresponding to the discharge port and a sedimentation hopper formed to be inclined at a lower portion thereof a coarse contaminant processing unit having a fixed screen mounted inclined inside the inflow chamber corresponding to the inlet and filtering coarse contaminants it is installed inclined to the inner side of the inlet chamber to the rear side of the fixed screen and having a vibration damping main body having a wedge bar screen a chain having a plurality of rakes for lifting the impurities caught in the wedge bar screen and a chain drive unit for driving the chain a miscellaneous matter processing unit comprising a a settling discharge unit for discharging sand settled to the inner lower portion of the settling chamber to the outside it is characterized by including"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7345713-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "14 alternately clockwise and counterclockwise the bending rocking plate 211 is rotated at each angle along the reaction plate 210 and the oxidizing agent is sprayed onto the reaction plate through each firing hole 2110 at this time the oxidizing agent sufficiently contacts and reacts with the filler bag 2101 on the outer wall of the reaction plate 210 to produce a liquid containing strong oxidizing sulfuric acid radicals which accumulates in the mixing chamber 21 s3 if it is necessary to treat the wastewater in the complex destruction chamber 20 the second suction pump 3 the liquid containing strongly oxidizing sulfuric acid radicals in the mixing chamber 21 is sucked up into each spray plate 342 through the mixing chamber 44 and uniformly sprayed onto the waste water from each spray port 3420 dissociating the metal ions from the complex state at the same time"}]</data>
