  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100238498-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the weight of the flute 286 must be made to overcome the vacuum pressure temporarily applied to the upper surface 292 so that the flute 286 can be lowered in response to the fall of the sewage level in the sump pit 154"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101955319-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "in particular the hydraulic block 620 includes a main chamber 622 which is filled with hydraulic pressure and is rotatably assembled in a state where the drive spur gear 640 and the idle gear 650 are gear engaged with each other a buffer chamber 626 having a spherical internal space at an interval from the main chamber 622 and a passing chamber 624 for connecting the main chamber 622 and the buffer chamber 626 in the vertical direction are formed"}, {"pat_id": "US-12318731-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the loading force may be attributable to normal mechanical springs or hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100727599-B1", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "in other words when the first buckle 7 is raised by buoyancy during full water to block the second orifice 19a the blocking diaphragm 24 and the blocking rib by the blocking diaphragm 24 constituting the booster 200 the first diaphragm 22 and the first support plate 21 are lowered by the hydraulic pressure concentrated in the second chamber and the third chamber while the flow path between the first and second chambers is blocked thereby immersing in the water more deeply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101227166-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "connected via a hose h to the connecting pipe 21 of the pipe pipe flange 20 installed at one end and the water flowing through the water inlet 31 through the water outlet 32 pipe line 1 1 a manifold 30 to be delivered to it a pump 40 which is operated by being supplied with power and is connected to the inlet 31 of the manifold 30 to continuously supply water block piping line hydraulic test integrated system including a pressure measuring device 50 installed between the outlet 32 and the hose h of the manifold 30 to measure the water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "therefore the first passage 851a is opened and closed by the ball valve 855a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565159-B1", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "the drive motor 44a operates the hydraulic pump 42a and the hydraulic pump 42a includes the first and second piston pumps 30a and 31a the drive motor 29a of the introduction device 20a and the first and second hydraulic pumps 42a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200166989-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is characterized in that it consists of a packing part to be in close contact with the frame when the water is discharged to prevent the water is discharged to the outside or water is introduced from the outside the frame and the door part are reinforced with corrosion resistance by using a non metallic material and the hinge part is formed to be able to open and close in a rotatable state in a state where the door part is fixed and coupled to the frame at a corresponding position on the upper side thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-5147530-A", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "9 water flow through the channel 131 is blocked and the water in bore 126 can only move through water drive line 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in addition the present invention has the effect of preventing the malfunction in advance by providing a pressure preventing means for enclosing the third opening and closing plate to prevent the third opening and closing plate is not opened by the water pressure in the storage tank even if the buoyancy chamber level is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "on the other hand when the operation of the submersible motor pump 4 is stopped there is no further groundwater flow in the water supply pipe 10 the water pressure applied to the piston valve 40 is released and the piston valve 40 is the elastic member 60 the groundwater remaining in various well facilities such as the groundwater meter 6 the hydraulic pressure gauge 8 the branching pipe 7 for the ground water by automatically opening the drainage passage 52 while moving upwards as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101068780-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "because the confidentiality is maintained by the sewage is smoothly discharged in the process there is no risk of opening more than necessary to prevent the leakage of odor or various harmful insects"}]</data>
</edge>
