  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101008852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage pipe installed with the switchgear to discharge the clear rainwater to the pipeline and collect only the initial rainwater and the sewage into the rainwater discharge chamber a pair of fixing brackets fixed to both sides of an exposed cross section of the sewage pipe a first tube welded to the front lower surface of each fixing bracket a shielding plate shaped to correspond to the shape of the exposed cross sectional size of the sewage pipe a second pipe body welded to both sides of the upper surface of the shielding plate and and a hinge shaft inserted between the first pipe and the second pipe so that the screen plate is hinged to an upper portion of the exposed end of the sewage pipe so as to open and close the open exposed cross section of the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "US-11738314-B2", "para_id": "para_143", "text": "the radial temperature gradient caused by the cyclonic rotation within the liquid 922 and the incoming water flowing in the water jacket space 928 can result in a temperature at inner walls 921 of the outer vessel 901 that is sufficiently low to mitigate against corrosion of the inner wall by high temperature reactions occurring within the chamber 900 and also can permit walls of the outer vessel 901 to be relatively thin compared to conventional high temperature high pressure reaction vessels"}]</data>
</edge>
