  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "therefore the solid matter such as the earth and sand can flow smoothly to the connecting pipe 21 along the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101357244-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the door panel 330 for selectively opening closing the waterway 101 the drive unit 340 for rotating the door panel 330 and the drive unit 340 respectively are provided at the 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "as a method of separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water by using green energy such as sunlight or hydropower a producing power through the solar power generation unit 1510 and supplying power to the power supply unit 140 to supply electricity through the electrode 130 s210 b temporarily storing the purified seawater in the storage tank 110 and first electrolyzing the electrode 130 through the electrode 130 s220 c performing second electrolysis through the electrode 130 in the waterway 120 while flowing the first electrolyzed seawater from the reservoir 110 s230 d injecting the caustic soda containing water electrolyzed through the step c into the inlet through the jet port 1601 and simultaneously heating the same through the evaporation chamber 1610 to generate steam s240 e receiving steam heated in the evaporation chamber 1610 through a moving duct 1615 to generate a steam turbine generator 1620 s250 and f collecting the concentrated caustic soda heated through the evaporation chamber 1610 through the drainage port 1603 in step d and generating and remaining the steam turbine generator 1620 in step e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "on the other hand the method of separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water using the green energy according to another aspect of the present invention for achieving the above object a to produce power by itself through the solar power generation unit 1510 supplying power to the power supply unit 140 and supplying electricity through the electrode 130 s210 b temporarily storing the purified seawater in the storage tank 110 and first electrolyzing the electrode 130 through the electrode 130 s220 c performing second electrolysis through the electrode 130 in the waterway 120 while flowing the first electrolyzed seawater from the reservoir 110 s230 d injecting the caustic soda containing water electrolyzed through the step c into the inlet through the jet port 1601 and simultaneously heating the same through the evaporation chamber 1610 to generate steam s240 e receiving steam heated in the evaporation chamber 1610 through a moving duct 1615 to generate a steam turbine generator 1620 s250 and f collecting the concentrated caustic soda heated through the evaporation chamber 1610 through the drain 1160 in step d and generating the steam turbine generator 1620 in step e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101015621-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "electrode plate fixing bolts for fixing the other end of the electrode plate to the other end of the electrolytic chamber of the main body housing and on the opposite surface of the main body housing to form an electrolytic chamber but formed in the other direction with the inlet sterilization water generation module consisting of a cover housing is formed with an outlet for the discharge of the disinfected sterilized water installed on the water inlet of the inlet water flowing into the disinfectant disinfection water generating module is a positive pressure valve and the sterilization disinfection water to detect the pressure drop is made based on the set pressure inside the waterway tube to operate the sterilization disinfection water generation module static pressure flow rate detection means comprising a flow rate detection sensor for detecting the flow rate inside the water pipe of the inflow water flowing into the module and stopping the flow of the flow rate to stop the operation of the sterilizing disinfection water generating module a filter installed at one side of the water pipe to filter foreign substances contained in influent water flowing into the sterilizing disinfection water generating module supplying power to the disinfectant disinfectant generating module while supplying a positive power and a negative power to the electrolytic reaction to remove the chloride attached to the electrode plate but the chloride generated during electrolysis is applied to the electrode plate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "therefore the solid matter such as the earth and sand can flow smoothly to the connecting pipe 21 along the waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101070989-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the treated water of the four waterway regions 170 is transferred to the treated water outflow inducing unit 190 via the wear 180 and the treated water is disposed at one side of the chamber 110 in the treated water outflow inducing unit 190"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "according to claim 1 the freeze prevention means 34 includes a chamber 341 fixed to be exposed to the water jet 31 and stored therein a freeze prevention valve 342 coupled to the bypass pipe 33 and the chamber 341 and a connecting pipe 343 connecting the anti freeze valve 342 to each other and an operating bar built in the connecting pipe 343 to partially open the anti freeze valve 342 according to the increase in the volume of the operating water 344 an artificial waterway having a water supply for freezing prevention characterized in that it consists of"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100787919-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "therefore it is preferable that the crushed stone outflow prevention part 60 for preventing the crushed stone oil chamber is installed at both ends in the longitudinal direction of the water pipe"}]</data>
</edge>
