and block odor while being opened and closed according to water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced during rain hinge connecting portion 40 for opening and closing the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30 in accordance with the water pressure generated by a large amount of rain introduced in rainy weather by being connected to the upper side of the plurality of secondary blocking doors 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the sewage discharge odor blocking device of the present invention for achieving the above object is normally blocked at the distal end of the sewage pipe to block the discharge of odor and discharge of odors and when rain rains in large quantities when the rain flows to open the sewage to guide the river a discharge opening odor blocking device comprising a box frame installed at an upper end discharge port of a sewer pipe at an upper portion of the rainwater discharge chamber and seated at an outer circumference of an open sewage discharge port a primary blocking door connected to the upper end of the box frame to block odors by closing the sewage discharge outlets in usual times a second blocking door connected to the first blocking door to block the odor by blocking the sewage discharge outlet it is characterized by consisting of a hinge connecting portion to be connected to the upper side of the secondary barrier door to be separated from each other in order to open and close the plurality of blocking doors in order to correspond to the water level in accordance with the water level and water pressure of the rain flowing in large quantities in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 having an upper inlet 11 and a sewage inlet 12 for introducing rain or sewage into the inside of the above mentioned ground 1 and having an outlet 13 for discharging the introduced rain or sewage the upper plate 21 is installed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 and has a plurality of through holes 21a for rain or sewage to be introduced so as to be adjustable to block the inflow or discharge of foul odors caused by rain or sewage the lower plate 22 is formed with a discharge groove 22a and a foul odor blocking groove 22b intersectingly while being in close contact with the lower part of the upper plate 21 a central hole 23 penetrating the center of the upper plate 21 a long hole 24 penetrating the center of the lower plate 22 and a fastening bolt 25a that penetrates the central hole 23 of the upper plate 21 and the long hole 24 of the lower plate 22 and fastens with a nut 25b so as to align the discharge groove 22a or the foul odor blocking groove 22b of the lower plate 22 from the through hole 21a of the upper plate 21 to prevent the discharge or discharge of rain or sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a grating portion 20 having a control means 25 for controlling odor blocking and a odor blocking groove 22b protruding on the inner surface so as to indicate the matching position of the through hole 21a of the upper plate 21 and the discharge groove 22a or the odor blocking groove 22b of the lower plate 22 while having a fixing portion 26 for preventing misalignment of the upper plate 21 and the lower plate 22 and having either a first elastic protrusion 27a having a protrusion 27c that exerts elasticity by means of a spring 27b and a second elastic protrusion 28a having a piece 28b that exerts elasticity an anti clogging means 30 formed on the grating part 20 to prevent foreign substances such as fallen leaves from outside from slipping and blocking the inflow of rain or sewage and a manhole characterized by including a fall prevention part 40 that is installed at the lower part of the grating part 20 of the main body 10 and prevents a nearby pedestrian 2 from falling when the grating part 20 is displaced capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage and allowing smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves the present invention relates to a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage free from foreign substances such as fallen leaves and more specifically to a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage which flows into the upper inlet of the manhole while preventing and blocking foul odors leaking out from inside naturally collecting foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet thereby preventing blockage and preventing pedestrians from falling when the grating comes off while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage free from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of the manhole can be controlled while blocking bad odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and pedestrians can be prevented from falling when the grating comes off while the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage can be controlled while allowing smooth inflow of sewage away from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole can be controlled while preventing and blocking foul odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling accidents that may occur when the grating is detached is provided.figure 1 is a cross sectional view showing a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage water from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain and sewage water according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figure 2 is a cross sectional view showing a pedestrian protection situation of a manhole that allows smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling and blocking the inflow and outflow of rain and sewage according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 3a to 3c are perspective views sequentially showing the operating state of the grating part of a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage according to the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figure 4 is a cross sectional view showing a grating section of a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage according to one embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 5a to 5d are cross sectional views sequentially showing the operating state of a grating section of a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage according to another embodiment of the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 6a and 6b are side views sequentially showing the operating state of the grating section of a manhole that allows the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while 