  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a square grating frame formed on one side of the road surface edge a fixed grating that is detachably mounted on one side of the above grating frame and in which the grating plate and the support bar are formed into a grating structure a sub frame formed by dividing the fixed grating and forming a drainage passage with the upper and lower surfaces open a lifting grating comprising left and right side walls in the shape of the letter l formed in opposition and a grid plate and a support bar formed in a grid structure upward between the left and right side walls and which is liftably connected to the sub frame to secure the drainage passage when raised a locking means is provided for fixing the elevating grating by raising it to a set height from the subframe to secure the drainage passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "according to the grating for a rainwater drainage ditch capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention according to the embodiment of the present specification as described above in normal times when it does not rain or when the amount of rainfall is small the elevating grating 50 that is connected to a rectangular sub frame 40 so as to be able to be lifted up and down is lowered to the initial position by pulling down the lifting pieces 140 180 formed on the left and right side walls thereof along the guide rails 120 170 formed on the inner surface of the sub frame 110 corresponding to the lifting pieces thereby maintaining the same height as the fixed grating 60 that is secured to one side of the grating frame 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102047325-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a storage tank 20 into which rainwater flows into the road rain gutter 10 buoyancy material 30 is installed in the storage tank 20 a sensor 40 installed inside the storage tank 20 consists of including when the buoyancy material 30 is raised by the excellent buoyancy introduced into the storage tank 20 is in contact with the sensor 40 the waterproof door 100 is automatically operated a guide 50 is further installed at the bottom of the sensor 40 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement along the guide 50 one side 53 of the guide 50 is attached to the inner wall of the storage tank 20 and the other side of the guide 50 is formed with a projection 55 the buoyancy material 30 is characterized in that the lifting and lowering movement by the buoyancy while being bitten by the projection 55 the storage tank movable structure using buoyancy characterized in that the water level control material 70 is installed in the storage tank 20 to adjust the waterproof door movable water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200469392-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3b 4b is formed so that the locking blades 3c 4c of the noise prevention pads to be hooked to the lower end 1n 2n of the connecting groove of the basic drain plate 1 and the closing drain plate 2 and finish that is connected to the noise prevention pad 3 by installing the connection nut 6 where the circular square or polygonal hole 2q of the finishing drainage plate 2 installed on the angle 30 installed in the trench structure drainage channel is located insert the hole 2q of the drain plate 2 into the connecting bolt 6 then fix the fixing bolt 5 to the connecting nut 6 and then the basic drain plate 1 vertically female guide bar 11 link 12 formed in the shape of the connecting groove 10 of the side that is not formed in the locking jaw 13 is pushed in accordance with the locking step 23 of the finishing drain plate 2 horizontally it is a sump and trench drain cover device which is basically connected by lifting method and the basic drain plate 1 is continuously connected in the same way as necessary and the end part is connected by installing the finishing drain plate 2 again.the present invention has the top plate 1b 2b is connected to each other by the expansion pad application is formed in a straight line and can form a variety of drain holes 9 the appearance is beautiful and the top plate 1b 2b square alternatively diamond shaped protrusions 1f 2f are formed to prevent slippage and expansion grooves are formed on the support 1h 2h to withstand high loads and drain plates can be connected without additional tools"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a road surface 12 formed by packing asphalt or concrete and a collecting unit 10 installed on both sides of the road surface 12 to collect rainwater and a rainwater collecting unit 20 connected to the collecting unit 10 in a road structure provided with an excellent discharge pipe 20 for discharging to a sewer a housing 32 formed with an opening 34 on the upper side and inserted into the road surface 12 a lifting block 30 mounted on the housing 32 such that the upper end of the lifting block 30 can be lifted up and down and the rack gear 31 is extended downward a spring 40 connected to a lower side of the elevating block 30 to press the elevating block 30 upward a pinion gear 50 meshing with the rack gear 31 a drive shaft 60 rotatably shaft connected to the pinion gear 50 and connected to the pinion gear 50 through a ratchet 61 and positively rotated only when the rack gear 31 is lowered a rotation limiting device 70 coupled to the drive shaft 60 to restrict the drive shaft 60 to rotate only in the normal rotation direction a housing 81 formed in a cylindrical shape and having a through hole 81a through which the drive shaft 60 is rotatably inserted is formed on one side of the center axis and a housing 81 having a central end 82a and an outer end 82b the center end 82a is connected to the driving shaft 60 extending to the inside of the housing 81 and the outside end 82b is fixed to the inner circumferential surface of the housing 81 and a rotation shaft 83 coupled to the outer side of the housing 81 so as to be coaxial with the drive shaft 60 so as to rotate together with the housing 81"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "2 2007 road structure for easy waste disposal summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above described problems in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a rainwater garden at an adjacent location of a road to prevent flooding or subsidence the present invention provides a road structure having a multifunctional drainage line of a road surface that can enhance drainage efficiency and utilize collected watercolor as a multipurpose by forced drainage of water.in order to achieve the above mentioned object the present invention provides a road surface 12 comprising asphalt or concrete pavements a collecting fixture 10 installed on both sides of the road surface 12 to collect rainwater and a storm drain pipe 20 connected to the storm sewer 10 and discharging collected stormwater to the sewer a housing 32 formed with an opening 34 on the upper side and inserted into the road surface 12 a lifting block 30 mounted on the housing 32 such that the upper end of the lifting block 30 can be lifted up and down and the rack gear 31 is extended downward a spring 40 connected to a lower side of the elevating block 30 to press the elevating block 30 upward a pinion gear 50 meshing with the rack gear 31 a drive shaft 60 rotatably shaft connected to the pinion gear 50 and connected to the pinion gear 50 through a ratchet 61 and positively rotated only when the rack gear 31 is lowered a rotation limiting device 70 coupled to the drive shaft 60 to restrict the drive shaft 60 to rotate only in the normal rotation direction a housing 81 formed in a cylindrical shape and having a through hole 81a through which the drive shaft 60 is rotatably inserted is formed on one side of the center axis and a housing 81 having a central end 82a and an outer end 82b the center end 82a is connected to the driving shaft 60 extending to the inside of the housing 81 and the outside end 82b is fixed to the inner circumferential surface of the housing 81 and a rotation shaft 83 coupled to the outer side of the housing 81 so as to be coaxial with the drive shaft 60 so as to rotate together with the housing 81"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100885534-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 includes a valve means 24 for guiding discharge through the outlet the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar rainfall reduction facility characterized in that it comprises an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge according to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101170324-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "then in order to prevent the floating garbage b which is swept away by the rain water w while filling the lifting fork 50 from the fork receiving chamber 25 the floating garbage introduced from the concrete drainage passage 24 it is necessary to temporarily block b in the middle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101983371-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "at the same time the tree branches it is a natural friendly environment that cleans polluted river water by creating a large artificial rain farm for artificial rainwater storage which is composed of large scale rainwater reservoirs which acts to prevent the pollution of the river environment by pulverizing the quality and garbage"}, {"p