the switchgear according to claim 3 wherein the switch is connected to the connecting rod while floating in the rainwater in the opening and closing plate 42a for opening and closing the residual water outlet 14a the connecting table 42b connected to the opening and closing plate and the immersion tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200466978-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3 wherein the rain inlet opening and closing unit rainfall inlet opening and closing cover that can open and close the rainwater inlet hole while moving along the rainwater storage tube it is connected to the rain inlet opening and closing cover and includes a lifting member which is lifted in accordance with the water level of rain when the rainwater level rises the elevating member is raised in accordance with the rainwater level and thus the rainwater inflow opening closing cover is raised to open the rainwater inflow hole when the rainwater level is low the elevating member is lowered according to the rainwater level the rainwater inlet hole opening and closing cover is lowered to close the rainwater inlet hole characterized in that the rainwater storage device using a digging hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100611047-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "as a result the lifting brackets are provided on the bottom of the cover at the end of the operating lever which has a support bracket and a basket having a basket that can be rotated by converting the water pressure due to the drop of rainwater flowing into the rotational force"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100611047-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "by opening the inlet of rain gutters it is possible to facilitate the inflow of rainwater due to the increase of the water passage area as well as to reduce the adsorption rate of foreign substances to the cover and to automatically drop when the rainwater inflow decreases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200333114-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "contrary to the operation both of the divided objects 10 and 10 are immersed to an appropriate depth to reduce the length.as described above the present invention is configured to adjust the length appropriately to the specification of the rain gutter to which the dredging container is applied so that it can be easily and widely applied to the rain gutters of various standards thereby greatly expanding the scope of the application"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a box type rainwater storage unit 10 embedded in an edge of a road or road and storing rainwater therein an excellent storage tank body 21 having an upper portion formed therein and having at least one long hole shaped rectifying hole 21a communicating with the rain storage unit and having a first discharge hole 21b formed at one side thereof the rain gutter part 22 is formed to protrude in the upper portion and arranged in line with the road surface and the opening is formed toward the upper portion the grating 23 is installed in the upper opening of the rain gutter part the plate is made of the first inside the rainwater tank body a rainwater storage tank 20 including a baffle 24 that is formed at a predetermined interval from one discharge hole and forms a overflow portion 24b between the ceiling portions of the rainwater storage tank main body it is connected to the first outlet hole 21b of the rainwater storage tank through the connection pipe 30 includes a sewage box 40 for storing the rainwater discharged from the rainwater storage tank the rainwater storage tank has a container seating portion 21c formed in a groove shape at a bottom portion of the rainwater storage body corresponding to the lower portion of the rainwater gutter part and has a tubular structure with an open top and a lifting hook 27a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method according to claim 4 wherein the valve means the lifting port 25a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rainwater storage tank body the transfer means for transmitting the lifting of the float the lifting force of the float through the transfer means receiving transmission includes an opening and closing plate 25d for opening and closing the second outlet hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 25b to move up and down with the buckle both sides of the lifting bar and the opening and closing plate is fixed road side opening characterized in that between the two sides is rotatably coupled to the baffle through a hinge to open and close the opening and closing the driving plate while rotating under the guide of the hinge according to the lifting of the elevating rod 25c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "rain gutters formed with an opening toward the upper portion grating which is installed in the upper opening of the rain gutters consisting of a plate shaped between the ceiling of the rainwater reservoir main body while being set at a predetermined distance from the first outlet hole inside the rainwater reservoir body an excellent storage tank including a baffle forming a overflow portion at the top a sewage box connected to the first outlet hole of the rainwater storage tank through a connecting pipe to store rainwater discharged from the rainwater storage tank wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a bottom of the rainwater storage tank body corresponding to a lower portion of the rainwater reservoir a container seating portion formed in a groove shape in the portion the upper structure is provided with a lifting hook and is characterized in that it comprises a container which is collected in the container seating portion to collect the contaminants introduced to the rainwater reservoir body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a reservoir which is buried in a drainage passage in a basement of a road the upper surface of which is open to the surface of the road and which is empty inside and which has bottom drains and side drains on the bottom and sides thereof a grating provided with an opening closing portion covering the open upper surface of the storage container to control rainwater and foreign substances into the storage container and it is connected to the opening and closing portion of the grating in a state arranged in the reservoir and buoyancy body for opening and closing the opening and closing while being elevated in accordance with the flow rate of the rain in the reservoir the grating the outer frame seated on the upper edge of the reservoir and the center portion penetrated a plurality of fixed gratings fixedly disposed at the central through hole of the outer frame and spaced apart at regular intervals along the length direction respectively and having an excellent inlet hole the opening and closing portion is disposed between each of the fixed grate and made up of a plurality of lifting grate for opening and closing the gap between the fixed grate while lifting up and down according to the lifting of the buoyancy body and a connecting frame one end of which is connected to each bottom surface of the plurality of lifting bars and the other end of which is connected to the buoyancy body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater drainage for roads apparatus for draining of rain water for road the present invention relates to a rainwater drainage system for roads and more particularly between a plurality of stationary grates provided with rainwater inlet holes in the grating and each of the fixed grates while being lifted up and down according to the lifting of the buoyant body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "opening and closing part made up of a plurality of lifting grate to open and close when small rain occurs the opening and closing part is closed state rainwater inlet through the rain inlet hole to prevent the inflow of foreign matters and in case of many rain the opening and closing part is opened so that a large amount of rainwater can be quickly flowed into the reservoir and discharged to the drainage so that it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather situation of the road and also to prevent leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside and of foreign substances in the drainage can be cracked down get the effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "when a certain load when a certain amount of rain is filled into the reservoir is applied to the lifting plate 41a the weight 41b opposite to the opening and closing plate 41a is lifted upward while the opening and closing plate 41a is axially rotated downward while the the bottom drain 11 is opened to drain the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "as described above the rainwater drainage device for a road according to an embodiment of the present invention is disposed between a plurality of fixed grate provided with rainwater inlet for grating and each of the fixed grate while being lifted up and down according to the lifting of the buoyant body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "provides an opening and closing part consisting of a plurality of lifting grate to open and close the gap between the opening and closing when there is little rain the opening and closing part is sealed in the rain state through the rain inlet hole only rainwater flows into the storage container below and other foreign matters are blocked in case of occurrence the opening and closing part is opened so that a large amount of rainwater can be quickly introduced into the storage container and discharged to the drainage channel so that it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather condition of the road and also the leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-11505962-B2", "para_id": "para_234", "text": "a method of manufacturing and using a five device in one water collect