l the initial excellent pollution load caused by rainfall to prevent urban flooding and to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank 1 according to at least one of the preceding claims characterized in that at least one sensor device 18a 18b is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining elements 8 22 is derived from the measurement data of the sensor device 18a 18b preferably from the measurement data of two sensor devices 18a 18b"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "at least one sensor device can expediently be provided in order to determine the degree of contamination of the retaining elements"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the initial rainwater storage system for sewage and valley water separation using the storage tank according to the present invention by overflowing the dividing wall during rainy weather to prevent contamination of the valley waterway and also to sewage initial rainfall and valley water rainwater on the other hand due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rainy weather the initial rainwater that has not been purified by the excess of the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant is discharged to the river to prevent the river from being polluted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384724-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the present invention during rain the initial rainwater containing non point pollutants introduced into the manhole can be drained to the sewage treatment plant through sewage pipes to reduce the contamination of the rivers by the non point pollutants as well as inflow after the initial rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 