  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100908323-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "an object of the present invention is to fasten the first pipe coupling and the second pipe coupling of the connecting portion for connecting the sewage receiver and the rain pipe to the face to face to minimize the overall height of the first pipe coupling and the second pipe coupling second the present invention provides a sewage receiver that can bury a pipe connected to a pipe coupling deeper from the ground to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank the water tank is not affected by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust and in particular the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346424-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the gravel bottom penetration facility installed at the bottom of the storage tank should be more than 10 13 mm per hour considering the infiltration rate of the lower layer soil and should be installed in the area where the function is not degraded by freezing in winter.the present invention is to solve the problems as described above the object is to provide a storage and permeation interlocking device of rainwater effluent which can easily adjust the size and shape and excellent workability by using a plastic cell as a pillar of the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130757-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in addition in the present invention between the rainwater discharge pipe 120 and the sewage inflow pipe 130 the heat insulating layer 150a 150b 150c in which the heat insulating material 152a 154b 152c is embedded is further configured to communicate with the atmosphere it is possible to prevent the cold air of the winter season from being delivered to the lower portion from the sump a can be delivered to the sewage inflow pipe 130 to prevent the sewage freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-9765508-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the hewitt invention is a device to collect and dispense roof rain water comprising a container to collect water having an opening a pump to drive the water out of the container a debris disposal mechanism a sensor to measure the water level wherein the pump is activated at a specific water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449313-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "there is a limit to solve the problem as described above.the present invention is designed to solve the problems caused by the above mentioned pain the purpose of the present invention is first can not effectively regulate the use of water drawn into their farmland by drilling a hole in the barrel arbitrarily but artificially in order to prevent the necessity of drilling by installing a drain valve that can be opened and closed at the bottom of the barrel and the manufacturing process of the barrel it is possible to prevent the barrel from being punctured by inducing water to the surrounding farmland through the drain valve in the farming season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432779-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "it is effective to maintain a constant double triple triple structure to be able to block the external cold air it is a very useful invention that has the effect of preventing the freezing of water meters and water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130759-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to prevent the sewage flowing into the sewage inlet pipe and freeze the sewage inflow pipe and by presenting a thermal insulation box that can be installed in the sewage inlet pipe the sewage trapped in the trap can be prevented from freezing and the sewage backflow is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101351825-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "in order to prevent the rainwater from easily evaporating during the rain or to prevent the catchment unit 120 from freezing or freezing by lowering the temperature the inlet opening and closing part 125 is for example the opening and closing slide 125a sliding over the inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261190-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "0173850 water meter protector accordingly it is an object of the present invention to fundamentally solve the above mentioned conventional problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a double structure in which moisture or moisture penetration into the inside is completely blocked thereby preventing the resin foam from freezing or buoyancy and to provide a structure of a water meter protector which can be mounted regardless of the height at which the water meter can be inserted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200422219-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "on the other hand the water meter box is basically required to combine thermal insulation to prevent freezing and also requires a stable waterproof structure that can block the inflow of rain water etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200422219-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "also in winter the soaked rain water freezes becoming the main cause of freezing of water meters.the object of the present invention devised to solve the above problems by providing a rubber packing larger than the diameter of the cover on the bottom of the cover the rubber packing is in close contact between the outer diameter of the cover and the inner diameter of the upper end of the enclosure stable waterproof it is to provide a water meter box configured to make the action"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100878252-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the drain trap for draining the dirt and rain water flowing through the gratings in the catchment on both sides of the road the drain trap 1 and the frame 2 configured to be inserted into the catch port 15 one side is fixed to the frame 2 and the other side is less affected by relaxation and contraction so that the inner wall is composed of partitions 4 having a certain height in the form of irregularities 5 on the inner wall to withstand freezing winter water it is configured to be able to fresh water the lower portion of the sump 3 is configured with a stopper 7 to open and close the drain hole 6 to drain the fresh water when cleaning a drain passage 14 formed between the partition wall 4 and the frame 2 as a passage through which the water flowing in the sump 3 flows through the partition 4 to the sewer the sump 3 is fixed to the other side of the frame 2 which is not fixed to be configured at a predetermined angle downward to the central side of the sump 3 the lower end side is composed of a diaphragm 9 facing in the lower direction a derivative 8 configured to form a space 13 between the inner wall of the sump 3 and the diaphragm 9 fixed to the frame 2 a trapping net 10 configured between the inner wall of the frame 2 and the diaphragm 9 in the space 13 to collect foreign substances induced by the derivative 8 chemical injection into the side wall of the diaphragm 9 in contact with the lower side of the collecting network 10 is a drug d is built in the form that can easily penetrate and melt by water w contained in the sump 3 device 12 is configured the drug injection device 12 is regularly filled with the amount of medicine d necessary for the cleaning of the grating 16 and the trapping network 10 in which garbage and foreign matter collected the medicine d filled in the chemical injection device 12 is a drain trap of the catchment characterized in that the appropriate drug d that can be used to cope with the surrounding environment to neutralize the main contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "characterized in that in order to reduce the risk of freezing of the system special means 5 are mounted in at least some of the drains 1 or other inlets which are so located that the flow of air therethrough can be heavy said means 5 being arranged to reduce such heavy flow of air in both directions through the respective drain but not to prevent some ventilation of the system and designed to permit a small flow of water to pass directly therethrough without appreciable gathering of water in said means and to be automatically opened when required to permit a greater flow of water to pass"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "characterized by providing special means in at least some of the drains and other inlets which are so located that the flow of air therethrough can be heavy and designing said means to reduce such heavy flow of air in both directions through the respective drain but not to prevent some ventilation of the system and to permit a small flow of water to pass directly therethrough without appreciable gathering of water in said means and to be automatically opened when required to permit a greater flow of water to pass"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in regions of extreme cold the rain water drains often freeze resulting in great expense in thawing of the drains and creating difficulties and costs as a result of flooding due for example to the melting of large quantities of snow"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the site at which the air seal is located is selected so that said seal lies on a level in the drain where freezing would not normally occur because water flowing through the pipes connected to the drain maintains said location at a temperature somewhat above freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102263501-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "since the water meter is generally installed outside the building it may be provided with a waterproofing material 210 to prevent the freezing prevention function of the cover from being deteriorated by snow rain or high humidity"}]</data>
</edge>
