  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "conveniently an emergency overflow 15 may be provided in the region of the retaining wall 8 as needed which serves to relieve the pressure of the pelvic chamber 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101136508-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "miscellaneous goods such as vinyl are accumulated excessively and sewage it is a defect that the rainwater overflows or reflows easily even in small rainfall due to the blockage and it loses the function of the drainage channel and debris such as fallen leaves accumulated in the rain gutter structure is destroyed causing severe odor or surrounding sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200181883-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "it is designed to prevent clogging of gravel layer by blocking pipes of solids garbage gravel sand contained in rainwater.the present invention forms a plurality of through holes 2 in the rain pipe 1 and each through hole 2 is provided with a penetrating hole 3 having a filter 6 foreign matter contained in the rainwater rubble 14 by preventing the inflow into the water by preventing the blockage of the permeable ground rubble to improve the excellent water permeation function to prevent the overflow of the river and also to easily combine the coupling case 5 to the fixed case 4 it can be easy to install the filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100772481-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "therefore when penetrating through the permeable sheet and into the ground on the outside the penetration ability due to the blockage of the pores does not decrease"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100749128-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "filter bag 80 is provided in the frame 71 of the filter to filter the foreign matter contained in the rainwater flowing into the sump 20 by removing the foreign matter contained in the rainwater it is possible to provide a sewage line structure for sludge removal to prevent sewer pipe blockage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102634268-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "in other words by further improving the separation efficiency of foreign substances in the main manhole 110 itself it is possible to reduce loads such as pipe blockage at the rear end"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "in the event that the rain overflow basin 1 is busy or there is a blockage in the area of the retaining element 8 the water can thus flow from the basin chamber 5 to the basin overflow 7 via the emergency overflow 16 without being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275666-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the present invention can effectively block various kinds of contaminants such as soil and leaves by installing a separate strainer inside the sump thereby preventing the blockage of the drain pipe in advance and at the same time improving the drainage efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "if the blockage was such that the full opening of the throttle element caused by this means that the blockage cannot be removed for example because the object causing the blockage such as wood diaper ball or the like is larger than the clear flow cross section of the drain pipe at the level of throttle element or upstream of it the throttle element opens completely but the blockage is not removed"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "if both yes signals are present at the and gate 41 at the same time then there is a blockage in the drain pipe 13 because otherwise the flow through the drain pipe 13 would be significantly greater at such high water levels and there will therefore be a fault message indicating this blockage reports and or triggered a security process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in the first paragraph the above main body 10 is characterized by having a filter net 14 further provided inside to filter and remove foreign substances that have entered through the upper inlet 11 and the sewage inlet 12 and is a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage without foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the first paragraph the above mentioned blockage prevention means 30 is characterized by having a protrusion 31 formed on the upper part of the grating 20 so that foreign substances such as fallen leaves can slide a plurality of perforations 32 through which rain or sewage flowing into the protrusion 31 can flow and a collecting groove 33 through which foreign substances such as fallen leaves sliding between the protrusions 31 can gather which is a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage and allowing smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves the present invention relates to a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage free from foreign substances such as fallen leaves and more specifically to a manhole capable of controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage which flows into the upper inlet of the manhole while preventing and blocking foul odors leaking out from inside naturally collecting foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet thereby preventing blockage and preventing pedestrians from falling when the grating comes off while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage free from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of the manhole can be controlled while blocking bad odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and pedestrians can be prevented from falling when the grating comes off while the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage can be controlled while allowing smooth inflow of sewage away from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole can be controlled while preventing and blocking foul odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling accidents that may occur when the grating is detached is provided.figure 1 is a cross sectional view showing a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage water from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain and sewage water according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 3a to 3c are perspective views sequentially showing the operating state of the grating part of a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage according to the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 5a to 5d are cross sectional views sequentially showing the operating state of a grating section of a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage according to another embodiment of the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the blockage prevention means 30 is formed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 so that foreign substances such as fallen leaves accumulate on the grating part 20 and prevent rain or sewage from passing through the grating part 20 and is configured so that foreign substances such as fallen leaves naturally slide and allow the inflow of rain or sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole while blocking and preventing foul odors flowing out from inside and naturally collects foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet thereby preventing blockage and provides the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling when the grating detaches"}]</data>
</edge>
