the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed consists of the tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction the unit block 211 includes a top and bottom assembly 2111 installed at a bottom and a top thereof a basic assembly 2112 installed at a middle of the top and bottom assembly 2111 and a top and bottom assembly 2111 and a base assembly 2112"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system includes a first step which is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of a part where the sedimentation tank and the storage tank are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank and laying a sheet on a foundation bottom on which basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block to form the storage assembly a fifth step of installing a water repellent sheet and a protective sheet on the side surface of the storage assembly and a protective sheet on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank a sixth step of connecting the pipe to the storage tank to prevent damage to the sheet or the storage assembly a seventh step of installing the sedimentation tank the inspection cleaning manhole and the inspection manhole of the storage tank an eighth step of connecting the pipe between the rainwater inlet conduit and the sedimentation tank the pipe between the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and the pipe between the storage tank and the discharge conduit so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank to the storage tank a ninth step of filling back the excavated part remaining after the installation of the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and voltage the tenth step is to clean up the rainwater storage system and plant it if necessary"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the first embodiment includes a first step of ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the part where the sedimentation tank 1 and the storage tank 2 are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and placing a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed in order to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 are laid in the side surface of the storage assembly 21 and the protective sheet 23 is placed in the upper surface to protect the upper portion thereby completing the storage tank 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the second embodiment is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed steps a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed it consists of a tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102006970-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition the filtered rain water can be recycled into the landscape water and in particular a portion of the water is guided to the outside through the water containing member formed inside the perforated pipe of the drop pipe thereby supplying the moisture required for vegetation growth to prevent death on the other hand it is possible to properly maintain the moisture in the ground by preventing the phenomenon of excessive leakage of water by the water containing member has the effect of preventing the growth of the vegetation and root rot due to soil moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4997312-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system leakage into the sewer line through manholes leakage into the sewer line through manholes where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101028522-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "one preferred embodiment of the bridge installation catch port 1 according to the present invention as shown in figure 1 the catchment main body 10 is installed in the drain hole is in communication with the top and bottom of the bridge and the catchment main body 10 it is disposed on the circumferential surface of the water collecting body 10 and comprises a leakage preventing unit 20 to prevent the rain water penetrates downward between the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200480536-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the bellows sleeve is inserted into the connecting tube and the space between the bellows is closed thereby preventing the joint parts of the bellows sleeve and the connecting tube from being damaged and there is a fixed and leakage free effect"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system where there is water leakage into the sewer line through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "thereby the rainwater drained from the lower connecting pipe can be guided to the inside of the gutter and leakage from the connecting portion between the lower connecting pipe and the gutter can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2599727-Y2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "description of the related art normally water leakage due to rain leakage rain blowing or the like in an existing building indoors or at a work site of a building under construction or groundwater in an underground building occurs not only at the ceiling of the building but also at the joint between the pillar and the ceiling"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2599727-Y2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to prevent such water leakage a rain gutter as a drainage channel should be newly installed around the pillar or a vinyl sheet copper plate steel plate etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080118-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional technique described above has a problem in that leakage of the sewage is serious because it is difficult to cope with shrinkage expansion caused by torsion of the sewer pipe or seasonal factors.the present invention has been made to solve the various problems according to the prior art described above an object of the present invention is to facilitate the coupling between the above mentioned water outlet socket and sewage pipe while allowing the sewage pipe to be connected to the manhole using the water outlet socket the sewage pipe can be precisely combined and to provide a new structure of the manhole and the sewer pipe to prevent the external earth and sand inflow and leakage of internal sewage or rain water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081354-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "chemical spill blocking system according to the present invention for achieving the above object is arranged to surround the storage tank spaced apart from the storage tank in which the chemical is stored and extends a predetermined height upward from the ground from the storage tank a protective part including a protective wall for forming a storage space around the storage tank to prevent leakage of the leaked chemicals a discharge unit for discharging the chemicals contained in the protection unit to the wastewater treatment plant and discharge the rainwater to the rainwater furnace a detection unit for detecting whether the rain or rain is contained in the protection unit a main control unit selectively controlling the operation of the discharge unit according to the information detected by the detection unit a hydrologic unit installed in the rainwater passage to open and close the rainwater passage and an auxiliary control unit for controlling the operation of the hydrologic unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100801684-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage pipe sewer pipe comprising a sewage pipe 1 having at least one manhole 11 and rainwater pipe 2 installed separately from the sewage pipe 1 and provided with at least one manhole 21 a detection means 3 provided with a plurality in one side of the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 and a turbidimeter which is a sensor for detecting a false contact and leakage of the pipe on the discharge side of the rain pipe 2 is provided with a collecting conduit 4 including at least one inlet hole 41 the inlet hole 41 is a soil inflow prevention device to prevent the soil from entering the conduit 4 5 classification means provided with a sensing means characterized in that it comprises a manhole 6 is provided between the sewage pipe 1 and the rain pipe 2 used to connect the sewage pipe 1 and rain pipe 2 at the same time sewerage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the present invention is another object to provide a block structure of the wall block the index plate and the prefabricated rainwater storage tank to effectively prevent the leakage of stored rain while combining the wall block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the index plate may serve as a shock absorber against the shock that may occur when engaging the uneven portion of the wall block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "by opening a large amount of rainwater into the reservoir quickly and allowing it to be discharged into the drain it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather conditions of the road and also to prevent leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside and the introduction of foreign substances into the drain can be controlled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "opening and closing part made up of a plurality of lifting grate to open and close when small rain occurs the opening and closing part is closed state rainwater inlet through the rain inlet hole to prevent the inflow of foreign matters and in case of many rain the opening and closing part is opened so that a large amount of rainwater can be quickly flowed into the reservoir and discharged to the drainage so that it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather situation of the road and also to prevent leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside and of foreign substances in the drainage can be cracked down get the effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326602-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "provides an opening and closing part consisting of a plurality of lifting grate to open and close the gap between the opening and closing when there is little rain the opening and closing part is sealed in the rain state through the rain inlet hole only rainwater flows into the storage container below and other foreign matters are blocked in case of occurrence the opening and closing part is opened so that a large amount of rainwater can be quickly introduced into the storage container and discharged to the drainage channel so that it is possible to respond quickly to the rainy weather condition of the road and also the leakage of odors from the underground drainage to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200352056-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the connector used at the time of the branch of the sewer pipe the sewer pipe 100 is coupled to the connection hole 110 the connector protection ring 200 is coupled to the structure that can prevent the leakage of sewage as much as possible the connector protection ring 200 has a fastening portion 210 horizontally formed on one side the fastener 230 is coupled to the fastening portion 210 the leakage preventing rubber ring 220 is attached to the inside is connected to the other side of the pipe joint 240 is formed the fixed rubber ring 260 is coupled to both sides of the connector protection ring 200 is firmly fixed to the sewer pipe 100 while the connection pipe 300 is bolted to the connection pipe connection 240 of the connector protection ring 200 the connection pipe 300 is a bolt portion 310 is formed at the bottom and the fixing bolt 330 is coupled to the top the leakage preventing rubber ring 320 is attached to the inside the connection pipe 400 is at the top combined the connection pipe 400 the bolt installation groove 410 is formed in the lower portion the fold portion 440 is formed in the middle portion the sewer pipe connector is characterized in that the rain pipe 500 is coupled to the upper portion of the connection pipe 400 to collect the rainwater to be transferred to the sewer pipe 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "in this example if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation but that there are water levels above a threshold the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "however since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside the temperature sensor often malfunctions and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as a result the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically the present invention relates to a safety manhole cover for preventing rainwater trapping with a catch preventing part and a slope to prevent safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage during rainy weather and to prevent accidents caused by footing when a pedestrian is walking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "there was a problem that causes an electric shock accident.in order to solve these problems the present invention prevents safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage in rainy weather and safety manholes for preventing rainwater swelling with a catch preventing part and an inclined part to prevent accidents caused by footfalls when pedestrians walk"}]</data>
</edge>
