  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101736743-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage sludge tank for a sewage sludge sewage treatment system comprising a pretreatment tank in which flocs are formed and the pollutants are settled while overflowing a filtration tank in which contaminants are filtered by a filtration unit including a floating filter medium between filtration nets formed at upper and lower portions after inflow of contaminant removed water via the pretreatment tank and a washing filtration water tank through which the purified water flows through the filtration tank and then flows out through the outlet port"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "a drainage inlet 411 may be formed on the upper surface of the contaminant removal device 49"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "the rainwater on the road surface 1 flows through the inlet port 411 and falls to the upper side of the water permeable filter agent 493 to remove the contaminants adhering to the lower side of the screen net 492 and the water permeable filter agent 493 the drainage of the rainwater can be smoothly performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102768687-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of adjustment tanks 1 including a first adjustment tank a plurality of second adjustment tanks and a third adjustment tank each adjustment tank including an inlet valve 11 for controlling the opening and closing of an inlet port through which sewage flows in and an outlet valve 12 for controlling the opening and closing of an outlet port through which sewage flows out a chimney valve 2 for controlling the communication between adjacent control units a control unit 4 that controls the above inlet valve outlet valve and flue valve and a distribution unit 5 that distributes sewage flowing out from the above plurality of adjustment tanks to a sewage treatment facility and or a simple treatment facility including the above control unit controls the communication valve so that all of the plurality of adjustment tanks are connected in normal times when sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility does not flow in and when sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility flows in due to rain the communication valve is controlled so that the third adjustment tank is not connected to the remaining adjustment tanks and as the amount of sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility increases the number of second adjustment tanks that are not connected to the first adjustment tank but are connected to the third adjustment tank increases and the communication valve is controlled so that the number of second adjustment tanks that are not connected to the first adjustment tank but are connected to the third adjustment tank increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102768687-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the above control unit is a contaminant removal device characterized in that when sewage exceeding the design capacity q of the sewage treatment facility is introduced due to all adjustment tanks or rain the control unit controls the activated sludge supply unit and the coagulant supply unit so that the activated sludge and coagulant are supplied only to the third adjustment tank and the second adjustment tank connected to the third adjustment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "it is possible to prevent the end of the waste.as described above the present invention is a device for treating a nonpoint source of pollution caused by an initial rainfall and can be immediately installed in an existing storm conduit 12 and particularly a coarse contaminant such as soil stones and leaves is a contaminant treatment tank 13 is treated preferentially the fine contaminants such as sand or mud is moved to the sediment storage unit 14 by the rotational centrifugal force through the rainwater movement port 16 provided to be eccentric with one side and the rainwater flow prevention plate installed at the bottom 18 and the concave portion 17 to prevent the backflow and settled in the lower part after removing the very fine sludge through the fibrous filtrate of carbide with rainwater can further extend the service life of the filter medium on the other hand it is possible to selectively process only the initial rainfall of high concentration by the amount of change in flow rate and in particular it is provided with two stages of filtration to increase the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100635485-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it has been discharged and has become a major contaminant in rivers and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the initial rainwater collecting weir is the same as the initial upper water level of the upper weir the initial rainwater is filled in the initial rainwater storage tank while the initial rainwater is transferred to the initial rainwater storage tank through the contaminant blocking pipe rainwater filtration and collection device excluding the initial excellent after the rain reaches the upper end of the water level to perform the function of overflowing the rainwater to the top"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060724-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the sewage on the ground may be introduced into the rainwater toil chamber 100 by being led to the upper inlet 110 by the water barrier 102 after the contaminants are removed by the contaminant screen 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1 non contaminant purification device characterized in that it further comprises a filtration tank connected to the rain pipe and the rainwater flowing through the flow passage of the rain pipe flows to remove foreign substances piggybacked in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200370542-Y1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "it has been discharged and has become a major contaminant in rivers and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101662794-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "when the flow rate of the rainwater in the trough 20 is increased due to a large amount of rainfall the rainwater passes through the drain hole 22 and a large contaminant such as a part of leaves that can be accumulated on the bus stop roof 10 is discharged directly to the drain port 22 without passing through the catch 21"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200351729-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "as water flows over the floor as it is there is a problem that causes not only obstacles to traffic flow due to heavy rain and snow in winter but also causes for causing vehicle accidents and safety accidents.the present invention in view of the above mentioned problems the present invention the sewage removal network to handle the clogging caused by the foreign matter in the rain gutter drain of the bridge to ensure the drainage treatment of the top of the bridge thereby resulting in vehicle accidents and safety the present invention relates to a decontamination facility inside a bridge rain gutter to prevent accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102779569-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rain water inlet device with contaminant removal functionthe present invention relates to a rainwater collecting device having a contaminant removing function and more specifically to a rainwater collecting device having a contaminant removing function for preventing clogging of an internal passage due to foreign substances thereby enabling rainwater to drain more smoothly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101865757-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a manhole body having a lid formed by spacing a plurality of penetrating holes communicating with the ground for natural discharge of rainwater and at least the upper end thereof from the bottom of the manhole body is arranged at a height corresponding to the inflow pipe and divides the inside thereof into two chambers and in order to induce deceleration of the flow velocity of the rainwater flowing from the inflow pipe to the outflow pipe there is disclosed a rainwater storage and manhole facility apparatus including a partition wall provided with a distribution hole for communicating compartments.1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826482-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to accomplish the above objects there is provided a vertical channel rain water filtration apparatus comprising a vertical water channel type rainwater filtration apparatus having a collecting pipe through which rainwater flows upwardly and a drain pipe for discharging contaminants downward a vertical pipe case having an expansion part having a diameter relatively larger than that of the water collecting pipe and the drain pipe a funnel shaped funnel pipe communicating with the water collecting pipe and disposed on the upper side of the expanding unit so that the rainwater flowing downward is in surface contact with the swirl like shape due to the acceleration due to the gravity and the turning force and a mesh screen provided on the upper side of the expansion unit for separating the rainwater falling from the funnel pipe and the rainwater and the rainwater through the collision caused by the dropping of the rainwater and a rainwater collecting part having a rainwater collecting compartment for collecting separated rainwater and having a rainwater outlet formed at one side of the rainwater collecting compartment and a contaminant discharge path through which the contaminants separated to the outside of the inclined surface of the mesh screen are discharged thereby discharging the contaminants to the contaminant discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "when the rainwater stored in the sedimentation tank 110 is stagnated due to the contaminant 120 being blocked by the contaminants the primary infiltration pond 130 may contain floating contaminants mixed in the rainwater that overflows the sedimentation tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "as shown the primary penetrating paper 130 is positioned side by side with the settling tank 110 to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "non point source contaminant treatment system and method of first rain the present invention relates to an initial rainfall non point source treatment system to separate the initial rainwater containing a large amount of non point source during the rainfall to discharge to the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101089297-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is installed in the rain gutter the upper portion is formed so as to open the outlet is formed on the side is spaced apart from the inner wall of the rain gutter spaced at a predetermined distance installed and detachable to separate the inner space of the cylinder up and down at a set distance from the upper end excellent in that a plurality of holes are formed in the outer circumferential surface and the inlet has a step at the bottom in the cylindrical shape of the upper and lower openings in the center portion induction plate an impregnation trap network installed at the step of the inlet of the rainwater guide plate to be seated on the stepped portion to collect the contaminants falling into the rainwater flowing through the inlet and as a contaminant separating means installed between the rainwater guide plate and the contaminant collecting network the rainwater flowing from the rainwater guide plate does not flow directly into the hole on the outer circumferential surface of the rainwater guide plate so that the contaminants mixed in the rainwater fall into the trap of trapping dust with the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to rain or the like the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100795399-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "2001919900000 2000.05.31 rainwater sediment in the combined sewage system was excellent in preventing sand inflow and contaminant inflow but the sewage was stagnated at the bottom of rainwater sewage chamber causing odor occurrence there was no problem of collecting only the amount of sewage so that there was a problem that excessive sewage flowed into the tea house and the sewage treatment plant in rainy weather.the technical problem to be achieved by the present invention is to prevent the inflow of sand and contaminants into the collecting pipe to prevent the odor caused by decay by the absence of stagnation of sewage and to provide an improved stormwater to collect only the planned sewage during rain will be"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "together with and an inflow control gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at an upstream portion of the purifier box constructed upstream of the multifunctional watercourse constituting a double discharge regulating gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at a downstream portion of the purge box a structure in which a double air duct coupled to the regulating water gate is formed at the lower end of the double discharge adjusting water gate a dust collector is configured to lift up a large contaminant at an upstream portion of the purifier box the structure of the vibration damper includes a first screen installed at an inclined position with respect to inflow water and a damper main body for filtering contaminants such as inflow water through a first screen and a second screen the rolling chains being configured to be continuously rotated by a driving force of a first driving poly that is belt coupled with a driving motor along a plurality of sprocket wheels formed opposite to both sides of the main body of the vibration damper a first driven poly configured on the other side of a rotational axis associated with said first driven poly a large lifting rake pin coupled with the rolling chain so as to lift large contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain not shown so as to prevent the pins from being separated from one side and the other of the outer surface of the pin a transverse coupling plate formed between the rolling chain and one side of the large lifting rake coupled with the pin a plurality of large lifting rakes formed between the transverse coupling plates a third screen having a plurality of water discharging holes for filtering small sized contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain wherein the upper end of the third screen is coupled to the plate member to form a curved surface up to the upper end of the upper sprocket wheel a first upper and lower guide rails which are combined with the large lifting rake and act to assist the rectilinear motion of the rolling chain while preventing the pin which is simultaneously engaged with the rolling chain from being sagged by the weight of the obstacle lower guide rails third and lower guide rails and fourth and lower guide rails are disposed between one side of the pin and the other side by the four upper and lower guide rails structure a hitting rake for hitting and removing the impurities contained in the large lifting rake wherein the driving rake is joined to one side and the other side of the driving rake case by a white bond a structure coupled to a second driven poly on one side of the white paper the second driven pulley which rotates the pulley in the reverse direction a first driven pulley axially coupled to the driving motor and a rotary belt coupled to the driving pulley wherein the pulley is rotated counterclockwise to remove contaminants trapped between the large lifting rakes a discharge conveyor installed at a rear side of the main body of the damper to receive the dirt falling and discharge it to the outside an air pump operative to float light contaminants having a specific gravity introduced into the inside of the purifier box the air discharge pipe coupled to the air pump is installed in the inside of the purifier box to float the organic matter material molecules of light specific gravity contained in the rainwater or river water flowing into the purifier box to the upper end of the purifier box a conveyor belt to which a binding plate and a lifting barrel for pouring and removing lightweight contaminants introduced into the inside of the purifier box are coupled a structure in which the coupling plate and the lifting bristle are combined with a white paper a structure in which a plurality of holes are formed in the lower end of the lifting bar a structure in which a nonwoven fabric is installed on the bottom of the lifting jacket and then the nonwoven fabric is fixed to the lifting jacket using an engaging member having a plurality of water discharging holes formed at an upper end of the non woven fabric the conveyor belt is coupled with a plurality of roller motors not shown to rotate the conveyor belt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a structure that is coupled to a conveyance belt for conveying contaminants to the outside on the rear side of the lifting bar the underwater pump connected to the conveyor belt constitutes a submerged pump at the lower end of the purifier box to remove the particulate contaminants remaining in the inside of the lifting jacket when lifting the particulate contaminants floating on the upper end of the booster box a pipeline coupled with the submersible pump an underwater pump for completely removing fine contaminants introduced into the purifier box by using a water injection nozzle formed at an end of a pipe connected to the pipeline and a discharge control valve coupled to a discharge control valve for controlling discharge of light organic matter molecules floating at the upper end of the purifier box at a downstream portion of the purifier box the process of cleansing polluted river water or contaminated rainwater using a river water or rain water purification system configured to purify polluted river water and contaminated rainwater by separate discharge is characterized in that the multifunctional water gate configured to store the river water to store river water or rainwater and to open the inflow adjusting gate constructed in the purifying box to inflow river water or rainwater into the inside of the purifying box and the air discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a catchment facility 100 for collecting rainwater in a catchment area a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100 a natural vegetation decomposing tank 300 installed at a downstream side of the contaminant separating tank 200 and for treating non point pollutants discharged with rainwater discharged from the contaminant separating tank 200 a first storage tank 400 installed at a downstream side of the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 having a membrane filtration tank 500 for storing the treated water treated in the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 a second storage tank 600 installed at a downstream side of the first storage tank 400 for storing the treated water treated by the membrane filtration unit 500 and it is composed of a transmission and distribution facility 700 for supplying the treated water treated in the second storage tank 600 to reuse water it is installed in the rear of the water collecting facility 100 and further comprises an initial rain water treatment tank 120 for separately treating the initial rain water falling in the initial rain flowing from the water collecting facility 100 the initial rainwater treatment tank 120 cylindrical rotating portion 121 for discharging the particulate matter contained in the initial rain water to the bottom by the centrifugal force while the initial rain water flows in a tangential direction it is installed on the downstream side of the cylindrical rotating part 121 and precipitates the fine particulate matter in the treated water treated by the cylindrical rotating part 121 the inclined coupled to the bottom of the porous flat plate 131 formed with a plurality of perforations and its lower end eco friendly hybrid rainwater recycling system including an initial rainwater treatment tank comprising a solid liquid separator 124 having a solid liquid separation plate 125"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "eco friendly hybrid rainwater recycling system including the initial rainwater treatment tank of the present invention the water collecting facility 100 for collecting rainwater in the catchment target area a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100 a natural vegetation decomposing tank 300 installed at a downstream side of the contaminant separating tank 200 and for treating non point pollutants discharged with rainwater discharged from the contaminant separating tank 200 a first storage tank 400 installed at a downstream side of the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 having a membrane filtration tank 500 for storing the treated water treated in the natural vegetation digestion tank 300 a second storage tank 600 installed at a downstream side of the first storage tank 400 for storing the treated water treated by the membrane filtration unit 500 and a water supply and drainage system 700 for supplying the treated water treated in the second storage tank 600 to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as a result deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20 the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40"}]</data>
