49-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "however if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599839-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "for example the valve may automatically release the gas cartridge pressure upon swelling of the support wall in contact with water such as in a life raft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102097635-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in the rainwater storage device a storage means 10 for allowing rainwater to flow in temporarily stored and then discharged filtering means 20 for filtering contaminants through the rainwater from the storage means 10 a storage tank 30a formed at a position separate from the filtering means 20 and connected to the filtering means 20 to store rainwater from which foreign matter has been removed it includes a pump 40a for discharging the stored rainwater installed in the storage tank 30a outside the storage tank 30a the storage means 10 a manhole 130 through which initial rainwater flows a sedimentation tank 140 connected to the manhole 130 and the wear 131 and through which a large amount of rainwater flows it has a distribution tank 150 for supplying rain water from the sedimentation tank 140 the filtering means 20 it includes a second filter 220 disposed horizontally the second filter 220 rainwater storage device using a mineral wool filter comprising a through portion 260a is formed in the horizontal direction can be filtered while moving in the horizontal direction rainwater is drained to the bottom contacting the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "however if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 0894022 april 10 2009 in the treatment of non point pollutants contained in the initial rainfall effluent waterproofing the effluent purified in the non point pollutant treatment apparatus the variable wear is formed to protrude upwards to the inside so that the initial rainfall outflow water flows in the rain pipe is formed on one side a gripping portion is formed at an upper end and a screen is formed on an outer surface thereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the rainy soil chamber of patent document 4 is a buoy that adjusts the degree of opening of the connecting pipe according to the increase in flow rate in the connection pipe connecting the rain soil chamber and the drain pipe so that it can collect as much as the design capacity regardless of the increase in flow rate due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101964855-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the fine dust and contaminants in the roadway 114 may be generated by the exhaust gas of the vehicle c the tire wear of the vehicle c and the asphalt wear of the roadway 114 and the like"}]</data>
