  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100242042-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "therefore it is considered that it will be easy to construct a small wastewater treatment plant of small to medium size population of 5 000 to 50 000 people .as described above by treating wastewater using the intermittent long term aeration process of the present invention an efficient wastewater treatment method is provided which is economical and can be treated without bypass of wastewater during flooding as well as during rainy and dry seasons"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080805-A", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the water in the well might have a low ph due to surrounding soil conditions the effects of acid rain or due to oxidation of anion portions of the original iron compounds"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the river water to be treated which has passed through the pretreatment unit 10 flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 is purified in the biological contact oxidation treatment unit 30 and then passes through the discharge tank 40 to be discharged into a river or lake thereby performing the functions of water quality purification and management during normal times"}]</data>
</edge>
