916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "check manhole 26 is formed at the upper end of the storage tank 2 the construction method of the rainwater storage system a includes a first step of ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 and the storage tank 2 is installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and placing a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed in order to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 are laid in the side surface of the storage assembly 21 and the protective sheet 23 is placed in the upper surface to protect the upper portion thereby completing the storage tank 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "check manhole 26 is formed at the upper end of the storage tank 2 the construction method of the rainwater storage system a comprises a first step of ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed consists of the tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction the unit block 211 includes a top and bottom assembly 2111 installed at a bottom and a top thereof a basic assembly 2112 installed at a middle of the top and bottom assembly 2111 and a top and bottom assembly 2111 and a base assembly 2112"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system includes a first step which is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of a part where the sedimentation tank and the storage tank are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank and laying a sheet on a foundation bottom on which basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block to form the storage assembly a fifth step of installing a water repellent sheet and a protective sheet on the side surface of the storage assembly and a protective sheet on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank a sixth step of connecting the pipe to the storage tank to prevent damage to the sheet or the storage assembly a seventh step of installing the sedimentation tank the inspection cleaning manhole and the inspection manhole of the storage tank an eighth step of connecting the pipe between the rainwater inlet conduit and the sedimentation tank the pipe between the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and the pipe between the storage tank and the discharge conduit so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank to the storage tank a ninth step of filling back the excavated part remaining after the installation of the sedimentation tank and the storage tank and voltage the tenth step is to clean up the rainwater storage system and plant it if necessary"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the first embodiment includes a first step of ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the part where the sedimentation tank 1 and the storage tank 2 are installed a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and placing a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed in order to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 are laid in the side surface of the storage assembly 21 and the protective sheet 23 is placed in the upper surface to protect the upper portion thereby completing the storage tank 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_85", "text": "the construction method of the rainwater storage system a according to the second embodiment is a ground excavation step of excavating the ground of the portion where the sedimentation tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge portion 3 is installed steps a second step of laying a foundation crushing to select the excavated ground spread the crushed stone evenly and lay the sand for flatness adjustment thereon a third step of protecting the storage tank 2 and laying a sheet on the foundation bottom on which the basic crushed stone is installed to block the inflow of groundwater or leakage of stored rainwater from the outside to the storage tank 2 a fourth step of assembling a unit block 211 to form the storage assembly 21 a fifth step of laying the order sheet 22 and the protective sheet 23 for waterproofing on the side surface of the storage assembly 21 the protective sheet 23 on the upper surface to protect the upper surface portion to complete the storage tank wow a sixth step of connecting a pipe to the storage tank 2 to prevent damage to a sheet or a connection portion with the storage assembly 21 a seventh step of installing the inspection tank 1 the orifice discharge unit 3 and the inspection cleaning manhole 25 and the inspection manhole 26 of the storage tank 2 piping between the rainwater inlet pipe 13 and the sedimentation tank 1 so that rain water flows from the sedimentation tank 1 to the storage tank 2 and discharges to the discharge conduit 5 the sedimentation tank 1 and an eighth step of connecting the pipe with the storage tank 2 the pipe between the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 and the pipe between the orifice discharge part 3 and the discharge conduit 5 a ninth step of backfilling and energizing the remaining excavated part after the immersion tank 1 the storage tank 2 and the orifice discharge part 3 are installed it consists of a tenth step to clean up the rainwater storage system a and planting as needed to finish the construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102702375-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention was created to solve the above mentioned problems and needs and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a method for manufacturing a sewage prevention and odor blocking permeable grating that increases water permeability by using eco friendly cork and easily drains water even during heavy rain or monsoon rain while preventing sewage from flowing in and blocking odors.in order to achieve the above object a method for manufacturing a dirt prevention and odor blocking water permeable grating according to an embodiment of the present invention comprises an outer frame forming a frame to be installed on the upper part of a rainwater drain or a drain an inner frame forming a plurality of square spaces by intersecting a plurality of horizontal and vertical bars in a grid shape inside the outer frame and a water permeable block filling the square spaces formed in the inner frame the method comprising a a preparatory step of preparing the outer frame and the inner frame and cork b a crushing step of crushing the cork into a size of 6 to 9 mm c a coating step of immersing the crushed cork in a waterproof coating solution and taking it out in a state where the coating solution has been applied d a drying step of drying the waterproof coated cork at 70 to 80 c using a vibrating device b a mixing step of mixing the dried cork with a binder and c a pressing step of pressing the mixed cork into the square space at 80 to 90 c using a heat roller"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052944-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a container shaped sand container that is disposed on the ground and accommodates water evaporating sand the upper side being opened a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container a cleaning wastewater spraying device for spraying the cleaning wastewater stored in the cleaning wastewater storage tank to the water evaporation sand stored in the sand storage unit a washing waste water recirculation mechanism that recirculates excess washing waste water flowing down through the gaps between the particles of water evaporating sand contained in the sand containing portion to the washing waste water storage tank the soil purification method includes while spraying cleaning wastewater from the cleaning wastewater spraying device on the water evaporation sand accommodated in the sand container the water of the cleaning wastewater adhering to the water evaporation sand is evaporated into the air to remove it from the sandbox introducing the water evaporating sand in which the chelating agent is accumulated for a predetermined period of time in the sand containing unit into the classifying unit and recovering the chelating agent accumulated in the water evaporating sand a method for soil purification wherein a part of the sand discharged from the classification unit is used as water evaporation sand stored in the sand storage unit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rainwater supply unit that supplies the rinse water and a chelating agent recovery unit that recovers the chelating agent from the cleaning wastewater discharged from the chelating agent removal unit the chelating agent removing unit has a sand rinsing device that sprays or jets rinsing water on the sand separated by the classifying unit to remove the chelating agent held in the sand the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank for receiving and storing cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the sand rinsing device a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052947-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a chelating agent recovery unit the chelating agent recovery unit a cleaning wastewater storage tank that receives and stores cleaning wastewater containing a chelating agent discharged from the filtration unit a perforated plate disposed in the ground disposed in a space formed by a peripheral wall a bottom wall coupled to the lower end of the peripheral wall and the peripheral wall and the bottom wall and allows cleaning wastewater to pass but not sand a container shaped sand container having an open upper side for containing water evaporating sand on the perforated plate in its internal space a roof disposed above the sand container and preventing rain water from dropping into the sand container it is disposed adjacent to the outer surface of the peripheral wall of the sand container and its internal space communicates with the internal space of the sand container via a communication hole formed in the peripheral wall below the perforated plate"}]</data>
