  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the filter unit includes a first vertical plate extending a predetermined length from the lower surface of the deck directly below the lower end of the deck equipped with an assembly step is inserted into the assembly groove is inserted into the assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck it includes a first filtration plate which is replaceably mounted in the mounting hole formed in the lower end of the first vertical plate immersed in the rainwater of the storage space to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater a second vertical plate extending at a predetermined length from the lower surface of the deck to a lower portion of the deck by inserting an assembled jaw into the upper end of the lower surface of the deck and being inserted and assembled in an assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction a lower point of contact with the upper end of the overflow bulkhead provided at a lower level than the outer wall of the concrete bottom layer so as to be replaced with an opening formed in an opening formed therein to remove the nonpoint source of pollution contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow bulkhead including 2 filtration editions the first vertical plate and the second vertical plate is made of a plate body having an assembling jaw on the upper end to be inserted and assembled in the assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck the permeable concrete bottom layer comprises a deck walkway rainwater storage device for the filtering space characterized in that it comprises at least one overflow plate having a relatively lower height than the outer wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the second vertical plate extending a certain length directly below the lower surface of the deck and relative to the permeable concrete bottom layer of the reservoir portion than the outer wall and a second filtration plate installed to be replaceable in an opening formed in an opening formed at a lower end in contact with an upper end of the overflow partition which is provided at a low height to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow partition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "multifunctional storage system to reduce initial rain pollution and prevent urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-10364563-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "typically a drywell would comprise an open pit or a container optionally filled with loose aggregate material such as gravel or loose stones into which the surface water is directed either by a grate on the top surface wherein the top surface of the drywell is generally flush or slightly below the ground level or from a pipe which may be connected to the source of surface water such as rain water from a downspout and which permits the discharge of the water into the drywell"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4983069-A", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "typically a drywell would comprise an open pit or a container optionally filled with loose aggregate material such as gravel or loose stones into which the surface water is directed either by a grate on the top surface wherein the top surface of the drywell is generally flush or slightly below the ground level or from a pipe which may be connected to the source of surface water such as rain water from a downspout and which permits the discharge of the water into the drywell"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200167090-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "these sewer feet are drainage systems that allow water to flow down the road in the event of heavy snow or rain"}]</data>
