  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "4 517 207 registered on may 28 2010 entitled structure for reservoir penetration of storm water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of recycling rainwater the rainwater recycling method includes mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block inflow of large solids into the rainwater inlet grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall recycled from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 storm water recycling method comprising the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101010048-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "and a support 7 installed to support the filter assembly below the multistage stacked filter 2 and to ensure an excellent inflow space between the multistage stacked filter 2 and the perforated pipe 3 the backflow prevention hole 5 is installed to wrap around the upper end and comprises a multi directional backwash filter 6 is filled with the filter medium m therein the multi stage stacked type filter 2 is made by assembling a plurality of blocked filter medium 200 the blocked media filling frame 200 is a hexahedron the filter medium m is filled in the frame and the lower surface of the frame forms a mesh structure to allow passage of rainwater the lower edge of the media filling frame 200 is provided with a leg 200b for adjusting the coupling height and stack height between the media filling frame 200 the upper edge of the filter medium filling frame 200 is provided with a coupling groove 200c is inserted into the leg 200b the multi directional backwash filter 5 is formed to form a mesh structure the upper side is provided with a lid of the mesh structure to be opened and closed for the exchange of media the upper end of the backflow prevention hole 5 installed to protrude above the upper surface of the multi stage stacked filter 2 the mesh m to block the inflow of the media in order to prevent the filter medium m enters into the backflow prevention hole 5 storm water treatment device characterized in that the structure"}, {"pat_id": "US-4923330-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "to separate such silt from the water it was typical to employ a settling chamber which would hopefully permit an appropriate quantity of the storm water to stand a sufficient length of time to permit silt particles to settle out of the water prior to its being discharged to the surrounding soil"}, {"pat_id": "US-5958226-A", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "however gravel leaves and other debris accumulate on top of the cartridges and block water flow so that a worker must reach in and dig them out by hand which is slow and time consuming"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101770268-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "4 517 207 registered on may 28 2010 entitled structure for reservoir penetration of storm water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248173-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "patent registration 10 0582121 excellent storage tank patent registration 10 0938223 assembly type excellent storage tank patent 10 1118263 excellent storage tank and pre construction method using precast concrete block patent 10 1013235 method of manufacturing excellent storage tank the present invention is a prefabricated rainwater storage tank column and the bottom and top of the columnar block and the prefabricated block for easy to carry out the vertical assembly process was a high difficulty in the process of building an excellent storage tank by pc block assembly the purpose is to provide a bottom column beam coupling structure of the prefabricated rainwater storage tank combined with a simple and stable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101993772-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "here the catch forming block 140 may be detachably fixed to the side plate 110 by bolting or integrally fixed by welding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582121-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the bottom plate has a storage block formed with a coupling portion to be integral with the base surface and and a top block having a rectangular plate shape and end of which is mounted on the top plate stepped portion of the storage block to be coplanar with the top plate of the storage block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582121-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the upper block 30 has a rectangular plate shape having a predetermined thickness and is formed on the stepped portion 15 of the upper plate 11 of the storage block 10 to be coplanar with the upper plate of the storage block"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101722458-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "with this configuration when the waste water and the stormwater are introduced into the inlet port 100m the slide panel 30m is bent downward due to the self weight of the waste water and the storm water and the waste water and the storm water penetrate through the fixed frame 31m the inflow port 100m is closed by the elasticity of the cut off panel 33m in case there is no inflow of wastewater and stormwater and it is possible to block the malodor flowing backward and to prevent the inhabitants living in the inside from flowing out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "second step s2 of seating the excellent storage tank block b consisting of the connecting member 30 to the cut bottom surface the third step s3 of inserting the fastener 40 into the seating groove 21a of the rainwater storage tank blocks b arranged in a multi row species and fixed through the fastening means the fourth step s4 of placing the finishing panel 60 on the outer circumferential surface of the rainwater tank block b and fixing it via the fastening means the fifth step s5 of forming a waterproof layer by applying a waterproofing material to the peripheral surface of the rainwater storage block b in which the finishing panel 60 is installed rainfall storage tank characterized in that it comprises a sixth step s6 after the soil is covered with the top surface of the storm water storage block b having a waterproof layer is chopped or pour concrete into the top surface of the soil after soil cover excellent storage tank construction method using blocks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "and in the case of the lower block body 10 is connected to each other via a fastening means long bolt and nut as shown in the enlarged view of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178358-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "provides a sewer type sewer pipe without cross piping in the conduit characterized in that consisting of a cover 50 to block the inside and outside of the sewage conduit to three channels.the present invention can be smoothly transported without disturbing the flow of sewage or rainwater because there is no pipe exposed or traversed in storm water or sewage it is easy to maintain the maintenance of the sewage pipe and reduce the cost of maintenance.1 is an exemplary view showing a configuration of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition according to the storage tank operating system and operating method through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention it is possible to effectively cope with a disaster such as a flood caused by a sudden sudden change in the flow rate due to a heavy rain or a local rainfall.1 is a view illustrating a storage tank operating system to which a storage tank operating system is applied through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "the sewage odor blocking device 140 includes a body 141 forming a storm water receiving space 142 while maintaining a predetermined position below the manhole cover 120 and inclined from the lower side of the body 141"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "in addition the reinforcing part 148 is installed close to the rotational center of the odor blocking plate 143 but may be installed at a space away from the backflow permitting plate 145 to the left as long as it is within a range that does not block the backflow permitting hole 144 .100"}, {"pat_id": "US-5232307-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a hydraulic diverter for receiving water including storm water comprising a first flush flow having a relatively high concentration of pollutants and a sustained flow which is relatively free of pullutants said diverter comprising an inlet a first outlet section and a second outlet section each of said outlet sections connected to receive storm water from said inlet for discharging storm water from said diverter said diverter having two operational states and having means for utilizing energy of the storm water to change operational states such that first flow is discharged through said first outlet section in a first operational state and sustained flow is discharged through said second outlet section in a second operational state wherein said water received by said diverter additionally comprises a nuisance flow having a relatively high concentration of pullutants wherein said diverter is configured to discharge nuisance flow through said first outlet section in said first operational state and wherein each of said outlet sections comprises an articulated tube said articulated tubes being disposed in a guide block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "is protruded is provided so as to be spaced apart from the bottom of the road side catch port 10 the horizontal catch plate 94 is adjusted to the height according to the water level flowing through the road side catch port 10 by the buoyancy body 92 and the coarse coarse collusion through lower rainwater downflow horizontal collecting plate 94 it is characterized in that it is provided to be filtered through the water filtration network 96 .according to the above configuration and operation the present invention is to embed the storage tank in the bottom of the flower bed formed between the road and the sidewalk to quickly absorb and collect rainwater flowing along the road during rainy weather and to supply the rainwater stored in the storage tank to the lower flower bed it helps to drown landscaping water and in particular contaminants contained in rainwater can be easily filtered and recycled into water resources including road cooling water road washing water and digestive water to contribute to water shortage.1 is a block diagram showing the stormwater storage system as a whole for vegetation infiltration according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-7846327-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floatable skimmer positioned in said housing chamber between the inlet and outlet of said housing chamber said skimmer being movably mounted in a skimmer track and having floatation thereon mounted to raise and lower said skimmer with the rise and fall of storm water in said filter box to thereby block floatable debris from passing through said filter box said floating skimmer having top and bottom edges said bottom edge defining a variable channel opening thereunder for the passage of water thereunder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "at this time the rainwater that is filtered through the first storage block 10 and a plurality of storage blocks 10 adjacent to each other repeatedly is introduced into the storage space s connected to each other via the above described downstream guide pipe 16"}, {"pat_id": "US-8034236-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in this storm water filter box a pair of baffles 36 are mounted along the bottom for capturing sand gravel or non floatable trash but it should be clear that these baffles may or may not be included within the filter box 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
