  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "the water quality meter 143 may be arranged to measure the water quality of the sewage flowing into the upper inlet 111 of the storm water chamber 110 through the contaminant screen 103"}, {"pat_id": "US-8808497-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "water and other fluids often accumulate various contaminants and it is often desirable or necessary to separate the fluid from the contaminant to meet various purity targets or reduce the volume of liquid within an open reservoir which may be necessary for practical legal or other reasons"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "and a contaminant treatment means 500 provided between the first compartment member 300 and the second compartment member 400 to remove contaminants from the influent water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition between the second compartment member 400 and the storm water receiving tank 100 is further provided with a contaminant filtration adsorption means 700 filled with a filter medium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "here the storm drainage treatment apparatus according to the present invention may not have a passage for guiding the inflow of water to the upper side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the contaminant material desorbed from the filtering unit 220 and the sludge separated from the stormwater so that the filtered effluent can be prevented from flowing into the filtration means 220 while passing through the filtration means 220"}, {"pat_id": "US-7780855-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "these two factors combined would result in greater total contaminants being brought to the separator tank during peak flows"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "the water quality meter 143 may be arranged to measure the water quality of the sewage flowing into the upper inlet 111 of the storm water chamber 110 through the contaminant screen 103"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101822469-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a tubular housing 200 inserted into a drain port 100 for drainage of storm water and having openings at both ends thereof an upper cap 300 having an inlet port 310 through which the rainwater flows into the space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 is formed a continuous inflow inlet 410 is formed between the upper cap 300 and the housing 200 to connect the space between the inflow port 100 and the housing 200 with the inner space of the housing 200 a lower cap 400 and and a first initial storm inflow port 210 formed in the housing 200 and connecting a space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 to an internal space of the housing 200 an inner tube 500 inserted into the housing 200 and formed in a tubular shape having openings at both ends thereof one end connected to the lower cap 400 and the other end protruding outside the housing 200 further comprising the first initial stormwater inlet 210 connects a space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 and a space between the housing 200 and the internal pipe 500 the inner cap 500 may be formed in the inner cap 500 so as to prevent the outer cap 500 from flowing back to the space between the housing 200 and the inner cap 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100799651-B1", "para_id": "para_100", "text": "as shown in figure 6 the cartridge which is the main part of the purification treatment apparatus to be purified again sewage after the contaminant removal device provided on the inlet side of the overflow water and storm water discharge treatment apparatus according to the present invention is provided with only the main cartridge 620 in addition the main cartridge 620 and the auxiliary cartridge 630 may be included"}]</data>
</edge>
