  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while allowing it to flow to one side of the upper portion eco friendly rainwater management system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "it is configured to be made as a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while being possible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "it is configured to be made as a storage tank to be supplied to the outside through the pump and the water supply pipe while allowing it to flow to one side of the upper portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "therefore by the rainwater collecting well 10 of the present invention the initial rainwater is discharged through the drain pipe 11 and the rainwater having a low degree of contamination can be discharged through the collecting pipe 16 to store more clean rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "in claim 1 or 2 a grating for a rainwater drainage system capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention characterized in that the upper surfaces of the fixed grating and the elevating grating are formed in a block like gently curved shape so that sediments including cigarette butts and fallen leaves accumulating on the upper surface of the grating are pushed along the gently curved surface of the upper surface of the grating by the current of water and are induced to quickly drain downward through the rainwater drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in claim 1 or 2 a grating for a rainwater drain capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention characterized in that the support rods forming the grating in the form of a grid structure of the above mentioned fixed grating and the lifting grating are formed below the upper surface of the grid plate thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "2 to 5 the support bar 60b forming the grating in the form of a grid structure of the fixed grating 60 and the lifting grating 50 described above is formed below the upper surface of the grid plate 60a thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "2 3 and 5 the upper surfaces of the fixed grating 60 and the elevating grating 50 described above are formed in a block like gently curved shape so that sediments including cigarette butts and fallen leaves accumulating on the upper surface of the grating are pushed along the gently curved surface of the upper surface of the grating by the current of water and are induced to quickly drain downward through a rainwater drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "at this time since the upper surfaces of the fixed grating 60 and the lifting grating 50 described above are formed in a block like gently curved shape and the support rod 60b forming the grating in a grid like shape is formed to be positioned lower than the upper surface of the grid plate 60a it is possible to minimize the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating and it is possible to induce the various sediments to be pushed along the gently curved upper surface of the grating by the current of water and to flow down through the rainwater drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_97", "text": "due to this the fixed grating 60 and the lifting grating 50 cover the opening of the rainwater drain thereby maintaining the original function of the rainwater drain grating which is to prevent the wheels of a vehicle or the legs of a pedestrian from falling into the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275853-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore as described above since the initial rainwater does not have a relatively large flow rate the water level in the drainage passage 10 is low thereby bypassing the main body portion 100 and the sustained rainwater bypasses the main body portion 100 because of the large flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2696007-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the installation of the rainwater catcher can be made comfortable even by inexperienced do it yourselfers when the pipe housing is indirectly connected to the catching bucket via a plugged locking connection with plugging direction oriented substantially in the direction of the axis of the drain opening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200203779-Y1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "if the soldering parts are damaged to reduce the watertightness causing a problem of leakage of sewage or rainwater and in severe cases the main drain pipe hole or the connection socket 18 may develop to breakage.the present invention was devised to solve all the problems of the related art and its purpose is to provide a connection socket with its own cushion so that the airtightness can be maintained without a separate packing or soldering when joining and there is no partial damage even by external impact"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102027469-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in being installed in bridge and draining storm of bridge the top plate collecting part may be embedded in the top plate of the bridge and the rainwater of the top plate may be introduced into a protection catcher located at one side of the upper catchment part and connected vertically to the upper catchment part and buried in a protection wall of the bridge and a protective catchment space into which sewage of the upper plate is introduced a line drain connected to the upper plate collecting part and communicating with the upper plate collecting part and embedded in the upper plate a discharge pipe connected to the protection catchment unit and in communication with the protection catchment space and penetrating the protection wall the display unit is disposed in the upper collecting portion and may be erected if rainwater is accumulated in the upper collecting space of the upper collecting portion and the rainwater is not drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular in addition to the heavy rainfall due to the rainy season and typhoons the recent changes in global weather patterns caused by el nino and la nia have caused local and local concentration rainfall frequently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide water pipe body fitted into the above drain and having an open upper portion to receive the above rainwater a grating member that is fitted and fixed to the upper part of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain permeation guide holes formed on the side wall of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain a shielding control panel positioned inside the guide water channel body to open or close the above pitching guide holes a lifting and transporting guide means provided in the above guide waterway body and for lifting and transporting the shielding control panel and in a road drainage device for preventing water retention on a road surface the device is composed of a filter net member that is fitted and fixed into the water permeation guide hole formed in the guide water channel body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain block formed to protrude downward a media plate formed in a mat shape having a predetermined size such that the drain blocks are stacked at a predetermined thickness on the stacked upper portion a gravel layer filled with a predetermined thickness on an upper portion of the media plate and a cover layer in which the soil is filled with a predetermined thickness to an upper portion of the gravel layer direct drainage rainwater treatment reservoir of the flat site characterized in that the configuration is made including"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "on the body formed in the form of a square plate to be installed in a plurality of stacked in the basement space drain passages are formed at regular intervals while an assembly protrusion protruding a certain height toward the upper portion is formed on the upper circumference of the drain passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147512-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "direct drainage of the flat site to facilitate the drainage of the flat site where rapid drainage is required in the first place while allowing the stored rainwater to be used as water as well as facilitating the maintenance and management of the facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101229485-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "to quickly drain without it being not cause any inconvenience caused to traffic and flooded with traffic accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the collecting basin 20 to block backflow and the collecting basin for dividing and filtering the soil sand and cigarette butts and rubbish mixed with rainwater or sewage so as to maintain a predetermined distance from the bottom and the side of the inside of the sump 20 in the rain gutter drain provided with 30 the sump 20 is of the upper and lower strait shape having a seating jaw 22b formed at the top edge of the entrance 22a to hang inside the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 of the manhole cover 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the simple manhole of the rain gutter drain according to the present invention the manhole cover 40 fixed to the upper end step surface 14 of the opening 12 of the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 and the manhole 10 mounted to a predetermined height inside to block the backflow of the sewage and backflow of odor and is installed to maintain a certain distance from the bottom and sides of the inside of the sump 20 the sand mixed in rainwater or sewage in the rain gutter sewer having a collecting cabinet 30 for dividing and filtering cigarette butts and garbage respectively the collecting well has a seating jaw at the upper edge of the entrance so as to be suspended inside the manhole through the support frame of the manhole cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102802400-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however since the drainage hole formed on the upper surface of the rainwater pipe block of the conventional road curb stone is formed horizontally to the road surface and covered with a metal grid not only is it difficult to drain the water quickly but the width of the road that can be used by vehicles is narrowed and when the road curb stone is damaged due to a vehicle accident the entire block that comprises the road curb stone and drainage pipe must be replaced and at night especially during heavy rain the positions of the road curb stone and the road cannot be clearly identified which poses a risk of accident"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101189539-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however if the wastes flowing with the sewage flow into the tea house or if more earth and sand are introduced into the tea house due to many rainwater garbage and soil will accumulate in the tea house which will block or drain the tea house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the non point pollutant removal device 10 is for removing contaminants such as fallen leaves scattered on the ground in the early stage of rainfall and a nonpoint pollutant removal device having a known structure may be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the non point contaminant removing device 10 may be rainwater collected from a roof of a building in addition to the above mentioned sump well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-1013702