ained by a method of naturally falling during the drainage treatment through the vertical drainage pipe in the driveway 200 when a large amount of rain is generated due to heavy rain the rainwater collected through the rain receiver 210 is drained through the vertical drainage pipe 230 as it is the rainwater is penetrated through the drainage hole 112 of the permeable sidewalk block 110 of the sidewalk 100 and the rainwater that penetrates through the sand layer 120 is gradually inclined to block the barrier film collecting rainwater through 130 while collecting the rainwater generated in the sidewalk 100 in contact with the vertical drainage pipe 230 and through the drainage hole 142 of the rainwater inlet hole 140 seated on the seating portion 162 formed on both inner upper sides"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100529500-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "on the other hand rainwater through the permeable sidewalk block 110 of the sidewalk 100 is collected to the sidewalk drain 160 along the blocking membrane 130 the permeable aggregate 150 is stored in the sidewalk drain 160 as a result rainwater is slowly transferred to the vertical drainage pipe 230 through the drainage connection pipe 170 and at this time the sidewall drainage port 160 and the drainage connection pipe 170 are coupled to the pitching net n"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100529500-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in addition even when the amount of rainwater generated in the sidewalk 100 is a large amount the rainwater generated in the sidewalk drain 160 may flow back to the upper portion through the sand layer 120 so that the rainwater overflows into the roadway 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "according to claim 1 wherein the upper edge of the support block 10 is formed with a stepped jaw 11a on which the support plate 32 is seated while at the same time both sides of the inclined surface 12a toward the flow path of the central portion is formed to drain the odor and backflow preven