  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "ordinarily because of the imperfect seal between between piston 230 and interior wall 240 water filling reservoir 242 via aperture 250 is free to migrate into air chamber 258 the buildup of water is limited however by the presence of displaced air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100834924-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "via conduit to a drain not shown to receive filtered water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4787980-A", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "controlling contamination in the sampling lines or piping because intermittent sluffing of contaminants will change the characteristic and quality of the water arriving at the multiplexer analytical instruments and or points of use"}, {"pat_id": "US-4018682-A", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "whereby the water fraction of the mixture forms small snow like crystals thus separating the water from the clay and silt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-5871648-A", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "the vessel drain opens to remove all contaminant via the sludge discharge stream 50"}, {"pat_id": "US-6916427-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "pre treating helps to improve the primary reactor s 7 efficiency allowing for an increase of fluent flow through the system by initiating the reduction and flocculation of dissolved and suspended particles in the fluent stream prior to entering the primary reactor 7"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the waste water stream will inherently include a higher concentration of contaminant ions than the feed water and will therefore have a higher conductivity"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0070989-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "such fouling or freeze up can occur when a solution becomes supersaturated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338818-Y1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "first the rainwater drainage sump according to the present invention is installed rainwater drainage sump in a public facility the initial rainwater generated in the early stage is drained to the bottom drain formed in the main body of the wear or orifice type rainy rainfall by restraining the drainage caused by the increase a certain amount of rainwater is stored in public facilities and the remaining rainwater due to the increase of rainwater flows to the upper drain of the sump for reducing the drainage of rainwater to be drained thereby suppressing the drainage of the drainage well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100578050-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the pump is not basically used for the inflow or outflow of the stream water of the pit type tank but pipes connected to the pump may be installed to drain water during maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "US-5965027-A", "para_id": "para_129", "text": "the vessel drain opens to remove all contaminant via the sludge discharge stream 50"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0063236-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "while one partial stream x flows into the bottom trough 5 arranged below the reaction column 7 through an inflow tube 17 the other partial stream y is first fed through an inflow tube 18 penetrating the outer wall 8 into the cathode trough 1"}, {"pat_id": "US-9611160-B2", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "the first diluted steam could be a rinsing stream and could be combined with the treated stream either prior to their combined discharge to a drain or prior to the carbonator if present and or any further treatment section present or of the concentrated stream after the anodic oxidation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the soil removed by the soil damper 100 is picked up through the obstacle receiver 8 and the impurity conveying conveyor not shown and then transported to the outside.1 tributary cloth 2 waterway entrance 3 waterway 4 drainage pumping station 5 drain pump 5a winch motor 6 hydrograph 7 main stream 8 container receiver 9 waterway exit 10a upper fixed frame part 10b lower movable frame part 11 connecting shaft 13 roller guide rail 13a upper guide rail 13b lower guide rail 14 roller chain 15 blocking plate 16a drive sprocket 16b lower guide roller 17 roller chain drive motor 21 pulling wire take up roller 22 pull wire 23 drive sprocket 24 take up roller 25 chain 26 winding roller drive motor 27 28 support block 29 limit switch 30 control unit 31 internal level sensor 40 auxiliary screen member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100936376-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "it can be closed at both ends of the auxiliary frame or by opening and closing by the weight 22 of the upper coupled to the hinge 14 to block the odor rising from the drain and to block the backflow sewage but backflow when the sewer bursts or pops out from a weak place when blocked it is often better to discharge back to the road than to block when the sewer overflows due to heavy rain so it is not always good to prevent backflow of sewage.the present invention has been devised to solve the problems caused by the deodorization and insect repellent device of the conventional sewer as described above is normally closed to not send the sewage to the river to prevent odors or pests coming out to flow the sewage into the river if the water level in the stream is lower than the sewage level the sewage on the road will flow to the river and the dregs can be caught on top of it preventing foreign matter from entering the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102067925-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is contained in the range of sec or less it is formed so that intensity may fall in the range of 4 mpa or more and 5 mpa or less the cover 314 includes two composition layers having different porosities of the base 110 the drainage path 312 the rain pipe 320 and the sewer 330 may include two composition layers having different porosities from the base 110"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "if the blockage was such that the full opening of the throttle element caused by this means that the blockage cannot be removed for example because the object causing the blockage such as wood diaper ball or the like is larger than the clear flow cross section of the drain pipe at the level of throttle element or upstream of it the throttle element opens completely but the blockage is not removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102418387-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is common to block the bicycle paths trails and trails with a lid so as not to cause harm or discomfort to users using the trails"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by the center of gravity 140 to move toward the hinge shaft 125 125a of the opening and closing cover 121 121a by rotating upward to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the crate 10 in the dry stream when the rainwater does not flow in the waterways while stably catching foreign substances mixed in the rainwater opening and closing cover 121 121a by the weight 140 to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10 to prevent foreign substances such as cigarette butts or vinyl to enter the drain 1 in addition the uneven protrusions 112 and 113 of the body 110 and the uneven protrusions 124 and 124a of the opening and closing cover 121 and 121a are inserted into the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102660526-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pool built to a predetermined depth on the banks of a stream or river a balancing tank connected to the pool by an overflow pipe and a drainage pipe to store water discharged from the pool a filtration device connected to the balancing tank and the supply pipe to filter the water in the balancing tank and connected to the pool and the water supply pipe to supply the filtered water to the pool and it includes a piping control manhole built between the pool and the balancing tank to control the overflow pipe drain pipe and water supply pipe to prevent contaminants from the pool from flowing into the balancing tank the piping control manhole is a first contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the overflow pipe a second contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the drainage pipe a third pollutant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the water supply pipe a first pollutant discharge pipe and a first pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle portion of the front overflow pipe of the first pollutant penetration blocking valve a second pollutant discharge pipe and a second pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the drainage pipe in front of the second pollutant penetration blocking valve a water damage recovery system for a swimming pool comprising a third pollutant discharge pipe and a third pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the water supply pipe in front of the third pollutant penetration blocking valve"}]</data>
</edge>
