ge flow of the rainwater drained from the moving port 54 the moving section 59 and the passage port 57 provided to drain water naturally for the drainage path 52 and the vegetation block is reinforced the present invention provides a separate pressurizing device for promoting the drainage of rainwater from a ferry or a drain pipe provided for the purpose of preventing damages caused by flooding with surrounding slopes due to heavy rain or flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the assembled rainwater storage tank 10 according to the present invention having the above described structure can be installed rapidly and firmly to meet the capacity suitable for the building at low cost and can use rainwater as drinking water for drinking water and emergency drinking water it is possible to prevent flood control in the rainy season and typhoon as well as to surely prevent pollution by contaminated initial rainwater by eliminating a large but early power without extra power.10 assembly type stormwater tank 20 water storage tank tower 21 lower block 22 water quality observation block 23 upper block 24 capacity adjustment block 30 drain pipe assembly 31 first drain pipe 32 opening and closing means 33 second drain pipe 34 filter pipe 40 water supply pipe 50 water pump 60 advanced water purification device 70 fountain hose 80 sterilization device 90 water storage tank 100 building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131549-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "in addition the support wall 55 to form the reservoir 66 is connected to the supply pipe 67 is connected to the induction pipe 92 one side of the partition wall 62 formed in the reservoir 66 by providing a drain 70 in the reservoir the reservoir 66 of the block 50 is filled with excess water that is excessively filled by the occurrence of flood or heavy rain etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "it is possible to prevent flooding or flood damage as much as possible by going down to the infiltration water or evaporating to the atmosphere and to prevent the groundwater depletion by the infiltration water going to the ground soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the flood diffusion prevention system of a building structure that is installed in a multi story building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to leakage from spreading to the elevating facility space a drainage passage formed on the floor of the common space for each floor in the building structure a drainage trench installed on the upper portion of the drainage passage to shield the drainage passage and a plurality of drainage holes for draining the inflowing water into the drainage passage a drain module connected to and configured to include a pipe for discharging the water to the outside a flood detection sensor installed in the drainage module to detect whether water has flowed in a water supply shutoff valve installed in a water supply line of the building structure to block water supply by a control signal and a flood signal received from the flood detection sensor a control unit for transmitting the control signal to the water supply shut off valve so as to be blocked and it is installed in front of the opening closing door of the elevator installed in the building structure and is raised to a preset height from the floor and includes a blocking module to prevent water from flowing into the elevator when submerged the blocking module is a blocking member installed in front of the opening closing door to open or shield the front lower part of the opening closing door according to the elevation an elevating wire having one end coupled to the upper portion of the blocking member to elevate the blocking member and the flooding prevention system of a building structure characterized in that it is connected to the other end of the elevating wire and configured to include a wire driving unit for elevating and lowering the elevating wire in conjunction with the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention provides a system for preventing the spread of water in a building structure that is installed in a multi storey building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to a leak from spreading to an elevating facility space the it is installed on the upper part of the drain to shield the drain and includes a drain trench having a plurality of drain holes through which the inflowing water is drained into the drain and a piping part connected to the drain to drain the water to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the installation height of the flood detection sensor 210 is installed at a certain height from the bottom of the drain 101 not the bottom of the drain 101 so that it can be determined that flooding has occurred due to water leakage not living water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "by allowing only the drain hole 111 to pass through and to improve the drainage effect by opening both the drain hole 111 and the through holes 112 and 112a when a water leak occurs it is possible to prevent the spread of flood damage due to water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "and a cap 198 connected to the hinge 190 of the fixed frame 125 provided at the end of the branch pipe 121.the present invention provides a stable drainage of rainwater by providing a stable removal of rainwater or flood caused by heavy rainfall as described above while checking the clogging caused by sedimentation that accumulates while moving in a drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "a main body formed in a hexahedral shape and extending a certain length from side to side a first front cover and a second front cover which are installed to be spaced apart from each other on the left and right sides of the front part of the main body so as to form an inlet through which water flows into the central side of the open front part of the main body a first opening closing door and a second opening closing door installed on the main body behind the first front cover and the second front cover and movably installed along the left and right directions of the main body to open and close the inlet a door driving unit for moving the first and second opening and closing doors a control unit that operates the door driving unit by an operator s or manager s manipulation or automatically operates the door driving unit according to a set pattern and a blocking screen installed on the main body corresponding to the inlet side behind the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door to block the inflow of foreign substances into the main body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681132-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention provides a method of installing a water level plate that can block a connection pipe of a water intake tunnel while being easily installed and capable of withstanding water pressure and is capable of installing an already manufactured device in a water intake tunnel without producing water the present invention provides a method for replacing a water gate using a shutoff device for water gate maintenance of a water intake tower for replacing a water gate"}, {"pat_id": "US-5004014-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in these structures if a water pipe ruptures and the rupture goes undetected as can occur when one is asleep or during a holiday or weekend not only will the floor where the rupture occurred flood but the water will also drain to lower floors"}]</data>
</edge>
