  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100522326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "limestone drain for sedimentation and removal of sludge contained in the runoff flowing out of the pit during mountainous highway construction a storage tank for storing the treated water discharged from the limestone drain but discharged when a predetermined amount is introduced in consideration of the case where a large amount of groundwater flows out due to rainy season or hydrogeological site conditions aquifer and a reaction tank for removing heavy metals contained in the acid drainage by mixing red mud powder with the discharge water discharged from the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200340109-Y1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "limestone drain for sedimentation and removal of sludge contained in the runoff flowing out of the pit during mountainous highway construction a storage tank for storing the treated water discharged from the limestone drain but discharged when a predetermined amount is introduced in consideration of the case where a large amount of groundwater flows out due to rainy season or hydrogeological site conditions aquifer and a reaction tank that mixes red mud powder with effluent discharged from the storage tank and treats acidic drainage on the basis of drinking water quality standards"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426715-Y1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank and the initial excellent effluent which has been filtered by the stencil strainer flows into the storage tank and stores the initial excellent effluent while storing the initial excellent effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674110-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes and modifications may be made without departing from the scope of the present invention.1 rainwater catcher 2 3 by drain pipe 4 infiltration ball 10 penetration ditch 10a infiltration ditch inflow section 11 perforated fan for flow equalization 12 shovel rake 12a contamination 13 flooding bumps 14 drainage filter fiber 15 observation 15a 15b plug 20 pretreatment tank 20a pretreatment tank inflow section 21 sand pack 22 stagnant water outlet 30 runoff water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in vegetation reservoirs for preventing pollution and creating a healthy urban environment a reservoir for storing rainfall runoff on the surface of the ground a vegetation filtration reservoir located at a lower portion of the reservoir and having a height of 25 to 60 cm including humus soil and sand at least one es filtration layer located below the vegetation filtration reservoir a collecting part located below the es filtration layer and having a storage part including a first gravel layer and a second gravel layer and a permeate part disposed in a lower part of the storage part and including a third gravel layer and a sand layer a pouring pipe disposed in the infiltration portion and being buried in the pouring portion to collect rainwater flowing out from the pouring portion an outlet pipe connected to the pipe a drain pipe provided in the vegetation filtration reservoir and a water pipe for collecting the water collected in the pipe pipe upward a bypass pipe connected to the drain port for bypassing the rainwater flowing out of the storage compartment of the storage compartment a second accommodating portion having a first accommodating portion having an inflow port into which the rainwater effluent flows an outlet provided with a screen for removing foreign matter in the rainwater inflow water flowing from the first accommodating portion and a vertical partition wall arranged so as to be communicated with each other an es expanded shale filter medium is disposed at a boundary between the vegetation filtration reservoir and the original soil and a bottom surface of the bottom of the water outlet is at least 30 cm away from the bottom of the bottom of the water outlet the vegetation filtration reservoir includes fly ash within 5 of the volume of the vegetation filtration reservoir wherein an aerobic condition layer is formed on the upper part of the basin of the drain hole and an anaerobic anaerobic condition layer is formed on the lower part of the basin of the drain hole to prevent pollution and to provide a healthy urban environment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "and a bypass pipe for bypassing and discharging rainfall runoff exceeding the storage capacity of the storage unit wherein the drain can be connected to the bypass pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in the non point pollution backwash automation system that treats non point pollutants generated by precipitation including a pre treatment tank and a screen tank formed with a partition wall therebetween the pre treatment tank is connected to a pipe at the bottom of the partition wall at a predetermined height inside and overflows an advection pipe for supplying the raw water accommodated therein to the screen tank a drain door provided at the bottom of the bulkhead to open and close only in the direction of the pretreatment tank from the screen tank to discharge all remaining water in the screen tank to the pretreatment tank it is provided on the floor and consists of a drain pump for pumping the residual water accommodated in the pre treatment tank and the screen tank has a perforated panel to filter out foreign substances while the raw water flowing into the lower part through the advection pipe moves upstream"}, {"pat_id": "US-7182874-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "10 a high flow condition is illustrated where the runoff volume exceeds the capacity of the separators and spills over the top of second weir 36 effectively bypassing both separators and proceeds untreated into the free space on the outlet side of baffle 28 and then into the outlet drain pipe where it can be combined with the flows from other vortex separator treatment units prior to ultimate discharge into the environment"}, {"pat_id": "US-10364563-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "soil composition therefore is a controlling factor in the leaching process i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-6093314-A", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "instead the runoff pools at the entrance to the drain inlet and beyond creating a potentially hazardous situation for motorists pedestrians and others"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100791422-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "an object of the present invention is a tank having a hollow inside the inlet formed on the upper surface the storage tank and the narrowing storage tank formed by partitioning the inner space of the lower side of the inlet by the partition wall respectively the narrow surface on the upper surface of the storage tank a scoop screening net installed at an inclined side of the crop storage tank to filter the scouring material and rolling the filtered scoop into the scoop storage tank an opening closing door formed at the side surface of the scoop storage tank and settled on the bottom of the storage tank in order to remove the sediment it has an opening and closing valve and a sediment discharge port formed at the bottom of the algae tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-7341400-B2", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the pavement 4 may be permeable block paving where individual blocks 26 are supported on a particulate bedding layer such as gravel 28 that allows water to pass between the blocks 26"}, {"pat_id": "US-6334953-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the flaps enable excess water from the runoff water flow to drain from the filter bag as the filter bag becomes filled with silt and other debris to prevent a back up or blockage of runoff water within the discharge pipe of the storm water discharge system"}]</data>
