  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a square grating frame formed on one side of the road surface edge a fixed grating that is detachably mounted on one side of the above grating frame and in which the grating plate and the support bar are formed into a grating structure a sub frame formed by dividing the fixed grating and forming a drainage passage with the upper and lower surfaces open a lifting grating comprising left and right side walls in the shape of the letter l formed in opposition and a grid plate and a support bar formed in a grid structure upward between the left and right side walls and which is liftably connected to the sub frame to secure the drainage passage when raised a locking means is provided for fixing the elevating grating by raising it to a set height from the subframe to secure the drainage passage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4602939-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the elbow body e prevents corrosion and dust accumulation and contamination due to the wind and rain of the elbow and serves as an installation base for laying the sensor unit s which is an accessory device and the overflow water that has passed through the elbow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular in addition to the heavy rainfall due to the rainy season and typhoons the recent changes in global weather patterns caused by el nino and la nia have caused local and local concentration rainfall frequently"}, {"pat_id": "US-10422139-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "thus certain exemplary embodiments can provide purposeful rapid dehydration of the system and or at least some of its assemblies in order to ready itself for the next storm event"}, {"pat_id": "US-10422139-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "thus certain exemplary embodiments can provide purposeful rapid dehydration of the system and or at least some of its assemblies in order to ready itself for the next storm event"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101229485-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "to quickly drain without it being not cause any inconvenience caused to traffic and flooded with traffic accidents"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4180947-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "0013 by attaching a sealing member that keeps the airtightness in contact with the other end of the shielding member the shielding property between the frame body and the shielding member is increased so that unnecessary items such as fallen leaves dust and earth and sand that become clogged with drainage grooves are removed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4180947-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the shielding property between the frame body and the shielding member is enhanced and it is possible to avoid the entry of unnecessary materials such as fallen leaves and dust that become the cause of clogging of the drainage groove into the drainage groove"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the collecting basin 20 to block backflow and the collecting basin for dividing and filtering the soil sand and cigarette butts and rubbish mixed with rainwater or sewage so as to maintain a predetermined distance from the bottom and the side of the inside of the sump 20 in the rain gutter drain provided with 30 the sump 20 is of the upper and lower strait shape having a seating jaw 22b formed at the top edge of the entrance 22a to hang inside the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 of the manhole cover 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the simple manhole of the rain gutter drain according to the present invention the manhole cover 40 fixed to the upper end step surface 14 of the opening 12 of the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 and the manhole 10 mounted to a predetermined height inside to block the backflow of the sewage and backflow of odor and is installed to maintain a certain distance from the bottom and sides of the inside of the sump 20 the sand mixed in rainwater or sewage in the rain gutter sewer hav