in a diagonal direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101433517-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "preferably at least one filter member selected from a nonwoven fabric an ocher block a cement block and a soil may be further provided on the upper surface of the drain hole of the foreign matter filtering barrel to filter foreign matter in the rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102702375-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention was created to solve the above mentioned problems and needs and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a method for manufacturing a sewage prevention and odor blocking permeable grating that increases water permeability by using eco friendly cork and easily drains water even during heavy rain or monsoon rain while preventing sewage from flowing in and blocking odors.in order to achieve the above object a method for manufacturing a dirt prevention and odor blocking water permeable grating according to an embodiment of the present invention comprises an outer frame forming a frame to be installed on the upper part of a rainwater drain or a drain an inner frame forming a plurality of square spaces by intersecting a plurality of horizontal and vertical bars in a grid shape inside the outer frame and a water permeable block filling the square spaces formed in the inner frame the method comprising a a preparatory step of preparing the outer frame and the inner frame and cork b a crushing step of crushing the cork into a size of 6 to 9 mm c a coating step of immersing the crushed cork in a waterproof coating solution and taking it out in a state where the coating solution has been applied d a drying step of drying the waterproof coated cork at 70 to 80 c using a vibrating device b a mixing step of mixing the dried cork with a binder and c a pressing step of pressing the mixed cork into the square space at 80 to 90 c using a heat roller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101124941-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "rather it acts as a path for pests such as mosquitoes and to prevent this rain blocks are installed to prevent odor and pest backflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "therefore in the case of the first case of the rain preventing rain purification block 100 combined only as in the case of the former the catching portion 11 of the boundary preparatory initial rainfall purification block 100 is connected in fluid communication with each other the longitudinal direction of the catching portion 11"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101662794-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "when the flow rate of the rainwater in the trough 20 is increased due to a large amount of rainfall the rainwater passes through the drain hole 22 and a large contaminant such as a part of leaves that can be accumulated on the bus stop roof 10 is discharged directly to the drain port 22 without passing through the catch 21"}, {"pat_id": "US-4997312-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "