 system capable of drainage installed between the sidewalks and the driveway the wheels of the vehicle are removed to serve as a boundary between the sidewalks and the roadway to drain the rainwater on the roadway and to prevent the vehicle from rushing to the sidewalk due to the collision with the car"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the upper one side of the circular or rectangular tube has a shape that is open in the longitudinal direction to provide a space for preventing the crossing over the boundary block the drain is formed on the lower side and both ends are connected to other water pipes a concave convex portion is formed in the open end surface wherein a binding groove is formed in a longitudinal direction and the open upper side is installed so that the other side is directed toward the roadway side and an upper portion of the waterway tube installed at the same height as the ground surface of the sidewalk it is a plate having a shape of a memory device with a round cross section so as to cover the open portion in the longitudinal direction of the water pipe a binding piece is inserted into the binding groove at both ends in the longitudinal direction but the binding piece is bent in two stages in the longitudinal direction so that a step with the outer surface of the water channel does not occur and the binding groove is formed at the end of the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "is inserted into and combined with the water pipe one side of the lower inner side is coupled to the upper hinge to open only to the inside so that in the rain when the water accumulated on the road is opened inward to drain through the water pipe usually keeps the closed state odor is leaked to the outside and a plurality of rectangular openings and exits are formed to prevent the inflow of the reverse flow through the water pipe to the roadway by absorbing the impact force to protect the occupants the wheels of the vehicle to fall into the water pipe to prevent the entry of the vehicle side to increase the friction by bringing the bottom of the vehicle in contact with the ground the wheel rides on the open top of the water pipe curb plates made of plastic or metal that are broken or bent in a collision with a vehicle to prevent it from rushing into the sidewalk a circular fume pipe embedded in a lower portion of the water pipe to provide a rainwater moving path flowing through the drain hole of the water pipe and connecting pipes are installed at a plurality of water pipes in order to connect the drain pipe of the water pipe and the fume pipe a boundary block system for sidewalks capable of draining and shock absorbing characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "consisting of the grating the grating serves to prevent the foreign matter mixed in the rain water is introduced into the drain hole so that the drain pipe is not blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by the center of gravity 140 to move toward the hinge shaft 125 125a of the opening and closing cover 121 121a by rotating upward to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the crate 10 in the dry stream when the rainwater does not flow in the waterways while stably catching foreign substances mixed in the rainwater opening and closing cover 121 121a by the weight 140 to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10 to prevent foreign substances such as cigarette butts or vinyl to enter the drain 1 in addition the uneven protrusions 112 and 113 of the body 110 and the uneven protrusions 124 and 124a of the opening and closing cover 121 and 121a are inserted into the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the rainy soil chamber of patent document 4 is a buoy that adjusts the degree of opening of the connecting pipe according to the increase in flow rate in the connection pipe connecting the rain soil chamber and the drain pipe so that it can collect as much as the design capacity regardless of the increase in flow rate due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "US-8617390-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "embodiments can also include a second pressure gradient system in fluid communication with the treatment tank where the second pressure gradient system acts on head space in the treatment tank to create a pressure gradient serving to transport head space gases towards the leaching field which may also be referred to as a drain field downstream of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "characterized in that in order to reduce the risk of freezing of the system special means 5 are mounted in at least some of the drains 1 or other inlets which are so located that the flow of air therethrough can be heavy said means 5 being arranged to reduce such heavy flow of air in both directions through the respective drain but not to prevent some ventilation of the system and designed to permit a small flow of water to pass directly therethrough without appreciable gathering of water in said means and to be automatically opened when required to permit a greater flow of water to pass"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "characterized by providing special means in at least some of the drains and other inlets which are so located that the flow of air therethrough can be heavy and designing said means to reduce such heavy flow of air in both directions through the respective drain but not to prevent some ventilation of the system and to permit a small flow of water to pass directly therethrough without appreciable gathering of water in said means and to be automatically opened when required to permit a greater flow of water to pass"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in regions of extreme cold the rain water drains often freeze resulting in great expense in thawing of the drains and creating difficulties and costs as a result of flooding due for example to the melting of large quantities of snow"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the site at which the air seal is located is selected so that said seal lies on a level in the drain where freezing would not normally occur because water flowing through the pipes connected to the drain maintains said location at a temperature somewhat above freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101128069-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main collection box 10 having a concrete structure with an open top and inducing drainage of road surface water into sewage and sewage systems a plurality of grill bars 21 arranged at regular intervals to form a frame having a plurality of inflow holes 22 the main grating 20 installed on an upper portion of the main collecting box an auxiliary collecting duct 30 connected to a circumference of the main collecting box in fluid communication with the main collecting box and collecting rainwater to guide the inside of the main collecting box it is installed in the auxiliary inlet formed in the upper portion of the auxiliary water collecting duct includes an auxiliary grating 40 for opening and closing the auxiliary inlet the auxiliary grating may be installed to be rotatable in the rectangular frame through the rotary shaft 42a while being arranged in line with the rectangular frame 41 and the rectangular frame installed in communication with the auxiliary inlet formed on the upper portion of the auxiliary collecting duct"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a grating seating end having a u shaped cross section and a predetermined thickness and length and configured to be connected adjacently and having a stepped stepped in a predetermined depth and length direction from the upper end of both sides to seat and fix the grating thereon a drainage passage formed in a longitudinal direction and integrally forming a u shaped cross sectional shape from the grating seating end so as to drain rainwater or wastewater therein an embossed portion protruding from one end and being inserted and fixed to the engraved portion directed to the other end connected adjacently a polymer concrete precast drain trench comprising a concave formed at the other end and a concave portion formed at the one end of the adjacent connected to be inserted and fixed wherein the polymer concrete precast drain trench is a coarse aggregate having a size of 5 mm to 20 mm 30 to 50 parts by weight 15 to 25 parts by weight of fine aggregate of 1.2 mm to 5 mm size 5 to 10 parts by weight of blast furnace slag 5 to 10 parts by weight of fly ash 2 to 7 parts by weight of silica fume 0.1 to 5 parts by weight of water reducing agent an inorganic binder containing 5 to 10 parts by weight of water unsaturated polyester resin 8 10 parts by weight 5 10 parts by weight stone powder used as a reinforcing filler for the unsaturated polyester resin 1 to 2 parts by weight of a hardener added to cure the unsaturated polyester resin part including 1.5 to 3 parts by weight of a shrinkage reducing agent added to prevent cracking due to shrinkage of polymer concrete and 1 to 2 parts by weight of a crosslinking agent silane added to increase chemical adhesion of polymer concrete an organic binder composed of reinforcing fiber material containing 3 to 5 parts by weight of steel fiber added to improve the tensile strength and elastic modulus of polymer concrete it is cured by pouring a polymer concrete mortar composition containing inside the mold the u shaped cross section a porous filter for neutralizing and or purifying pollutants in sewage is provided on the inner surface of the drainage channel formed in a shape and formed in the longitudinal direction by alkalizing acid rain in the rainwater flowing into the drainage channel the porous filter for neutralizing the acid rain by alkalizing the acid rain contains 60 by weight of a porous filler containing bentonite powder porous feldspar powder pearlite powder and kaolinite powder in the same weight ratio 20 by weight of sodium hydroxide alkalizing agent and 20 by weight of lime powder"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the porous filter that neutralizes acid rain and or purifies pollutants on the inner surface of the drainage passage formed in the u shaped cross sectional shape and formed in the longitudinal direction is attached to and detached from the insertion groove formed in a plurality of the inner surface of the drainage passage formed in the u shaped cross sectional shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "a grating seating end formed therein a drainage passage formed in a longitudinal direction and integrally forming a u shaped cross sectional shape from the grating seating end so as to drain rainwater or wastewater therein an embossed portion protruding from one end and being inserted and fixed to the engraved portion directed to the other end connected to each other a trench body block comprising a concave formed at the other end and a concave portion formed at one end of the one end to be connected adjacently wherein the trench body block includes 30 to 50 parts by weight of a coarse aggregate having a size of 5 mm to 20 mm 1.2mm to 5mm fine aggregate 15 to 25 parts by weight blast furnace slag 5 to 10 parts by weight fly ash 5 to 10 parts by weight silica fume 2 to 7 parts by weight water reducing agent 0.1 to 5 parts by weight water 5 to 10 parts by weight an inorganic binder containing unsaturated polyester resin 8 10 parts by weight 5 10 parts by weight stone powder used as a reinforcing filler for the unsaturated polyester resin 1 to 2 parts by weight of a curing agent added to cure the unsaturated polyester resin part including 1.5 to 3 parts by weight of a shrinkage reducing agent added to prevent cracking due to shrinkage of polymer concrete and 1 to 2 parts by weight of a crosslinking agent silane added to increase chemical adhesion of polymer concrete an organic binder composed of reinforcing fiber material containing 3 to 5 parts by weight of steel fiber added to improve the tensile strength and elastic modulus of polymer concrete it is cured by pouring a polymer concrete mortar composition containing inside the mold the u shaped cross section an industrial by product equipped with a porous filter for neutralizing and or purifying pollutants in sewage by alkalizing acid rain in the rainwater flowing into the drainage channel and reducing non point pollution polymer concrete precast drain trench is used as a solution to the problem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the present invention is configured to be connected adjacent to each other having a u shaped cross section and a predetermined thickness and length and a grating seating end having a stepped stepped in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends to seat and fix the grating on the upper portion a drainage passage formed in a longitudinal direction and integrally forming a u shaped cross sectional shape from the grating seating end so as to drain rainwater or wastewater therein an embossed portion protruding from one end and being inserted and fixed to the engraved portion directed to the other end connected to each other a trench body block comprising a concave formed at the other end and a concave portion formed at one end of the one end to be connected adjacently wherein the trench body block includes 30 to 50 parts by weight of a coarse aggregate having a size of 5 mm to 20 mm 1.2mm to 5mm fine aggregate 15 to 25 parts by weight blast furnace slag 5 to 10 parts by weight fly ash 5 to 10 parts by weight silica fume 2 to 7 parts by weight water reducing agent 0.1 to 5 parts by weight water 5 to 10 parts by weight an inorganic binder containing unsaturated polyester resin 8 10 parts by weight 5 10 parts by weight stone powder used as a reinforcing filler for the unsaturated polyester resin 1 to 2 parts by weight of a curing agent added to cure the unsaturated polyester resin part including 1.5 to 3 parts by weight of a shrinkage reducing agent added to prevent cracking due to shrinkage of polymer concrete and 1 to 2 parts by weight of a crosslinking agent silane added to increase chemical adhesion of polymer concrete an organic binding material composed of reinforcing fiber material containing 3 to 5 parts by weight of steel fiber added to improve the tensile strength and elastic modulus of polymer concrete it is cured by pouring a polymer concrete mortar composition containing inside the mold the u shaped cross section an industrial by product equipped with a porous filter for neutralizing and or purifying pollutants in sewage by alkalizing acid rain in the rainwater flowing into the drainage channel and reducing non point pollution polymer concrete precast drainage trench is a feature of the technology configuration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039711-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in addition the present invention is easy to clean the rain fall and garbage in rain compared to the grating for the metal drainage it is possible to manage the drainage by lifting only the desired part without lifting the whole like grating for the conventional metal drainage improve workability due to maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "partitioning means for partitioning the maintenance tank and the treatment tank the upper part being blocked and the lower part being in communication first filtration means detachably located in the treatment tank and configured to filter adsorb and remove contaminants contained in road surface drainage that rises from a lower portion of the treatment tank to an upper side and it is installed on the upper side of the rain catcher the maintenance tank and the treatment tank to have a size covering the entire area thereof an auxiliary shield plate for shielding the upper opening of the treatment tank is provided on one side of the bottom surface the road drain drain lid formed at a predetermined position with an open passage for forcing flow into the inner space road drainage treatment device having an excellent receiving function including a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715225-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "therefore the buoyancy may be generated buoyancy but the drain box 10 is opened in the rain box 10 can be treated to the outside as the rainwater is collected in the drain box 10 as shown in figure 5a and 5b and as the rainwater collected in the drain box 10 is intended to flow backward the rainwater rises in the direction of the arrow so that the substructure 50 and the shielding plate 60 are lifted to the upper side together by the shielding plate 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100529500-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "during the summer season large scale stormwater generated from sidewalks and roadways is drained through a vertical drainage pipe connected to the storm drain on the roadway in the drainage treatment method of the road characterized in that the rainwater is drained by a method of naturally falling during the drainage treatment through the vertical drainage pipe in the driveway 200 when a large amount of rain is generated due to heavy rain the rainwater collected through the rain receiver 210 is drained through the vertical drainage pipe 230 as it is the rainwater is penetrated through the drainage hole 112 of the permeable sidewalk block 110 of the sidewalk 100 and the rainwater that penetrates through the sand layer 120 is gradually inclined to block the barrier film collecting rainwater through 130 while collecting the rainwater generated in the sidewalk 100 in contact with the vertical drainage pipe 230 and through the drainage hole 142 of the rainwater inlet hole 140 seated on the seating portion 162 formed on both inner upper sides"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100710632-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore in order to prevent the backflow of the odor the vinyl bag may be covered on the grating of the drain but in case of sudden rain the plastic bag may block the drain of the rainwater which may prevent the rainwater from draining and cause a safety accident due to the rainwater"}]</data>
