  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101275853-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "in particular the partition wall 20 when the water level in the drain 10 is lower than the predetermined water level as shown in figure 2 the right the waste water bypasses the main body portion 100 as shown in figure 5 drain 10 if the water level in the above is above the predetermined water level the right the sewage may be formed so that the water flows through the drainage path 10 by overflowing the partition wall 20 without bypassing the main body portion 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275853-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore as described above since the initial rainwater does not have a relatively large flow rate the water level in the drainage passage 10 is low thereby bypassing the main body portion 100 and the sustained rainwater bypasses the main body portion 100 because of the large flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "simultaneously therewith the battery operated audible alarm which is electrically connected to a water sensor on the conduit senses the rising water and makes a circuit thus causing the alarm to sound to notify the building occupant"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "float 11 lifts due to a rising water level in sump pit 50 thus causing float arm 14 to disengage rollers 16 16 as it rotates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the automatic dripping device for preventing freezing may include a falling water providing pipe installed to communicate with the falling water storage tank and to supply the falling water stored in the falling water storage tank to a user a water level detection and alarm unit installed in the fall water storage tank detecting the level of the fluid stored in the fall water storage tank and alerting an operator through an alarm member when the detected level exceeds a preset range and a falling water drain pipe installed to communicate with the falling water providing pipe and discharging the falling water from the falling water providing pipe to the outside when an alarm is generated by the alarm member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the automatic dripping device for preventing freezing of the present invention the falling water stored in the falling water storage tank can be re supplyed to the user by providing a falling water providing pipe a water level detection and alarm unit and a falling water drain pipe that perform specific roles it is possible to prevent the waste of water and the capacity of the water stored in the water storage tank can be adjusted within a safe range thereby providing an automatic water fall device for preventing freezing that can prevent an accident in which water overflows in the water storage tank during operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "is possible and such variations fall within the protection scope of the present invention.10 piping entering the object to be frozen or bursting or piping exiting from the object 20 external power 100 automatic dripping device for freezing prevention 110 body part 111 opening and closing lid 112 power indicator lamp 113 operation indicator lamp 114 storage space 120 temperature detection unit 130 control unit 131 external power input terminal 132 transformer 133 relay 140 on off valve 150 on off valve driving unit 150e emergency operation button 151 opening and closing valve coupling part 152 rotary drive unit 153 heat supply unit 154 opening and closing valve warming part 161 additional mounting piping 161a extension pipe 162 additionally installed on off valve 163 falling water storage tank 164 falling water flow rate detection unit 165 falling water supply pipe 166 water level detection and alarm unit 167 water drain pipe 171 power supply unit 172 power supply part warming part 173 wireless communication module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101491882-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "47 a body 31 having a space 46 is provided an opening closing ball 48 for closing and opening the water supply port 43 by buoyancy is introduced into the space 46 when water flows in or out a shock absorber 49 is provided below the open close ball 48 to provide a shock absorbing action when the open close ball 48 falls an upper lid 42 having a water supply inlet 41 is installed on the upper side of the body 47 wherein a lower cover 50 for closing the space 46 is provided below the body 47 to prevent the opening closing ball 48 and the shock absorber 49 from being separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673081-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it includes a shield plate forming a plate shape and connected to the end of the support rope wound or unwound on the winding shaft a lower end of the shielding plate includes a stopper protruding to have a space toward the deposit receiving container 120 and an insertion hole into which the stopper is inserted is formed on an upper surface of the base to which the lower end of the shielding plate abuts the insertion hole is closed by being covered with a locking block plate which is rotatably fixed around the shaft and the shaft is positioned at the deposit container of the insertion hole and one end of the locking block plate closes the insertion hole and the other end is positioned around the shaft"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673081-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "buoyancy member which is located on the surface of the sewage in the drain pipe and moves up and down according to the water level change of the sewage a support that is fixed horizontally along the buoyancy member and the drain pipe and the receiving groove while being fixed to the end of the support a sluice member disposed in front of and having a plurality of water passages a guide line formed on an upper portion of the drain pipe and forming a groove line in an up and down direction and disposed on an upper surface of the support and movably engaged with the guide line so that the buoyancy member a sluice platform with a guide bar guiding the lifting direction of the support and the sluice along the shanghai east of the and"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502305-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to operate a warning alarm when the unwanted water due to the closing of the main water supply valve and to enter the inspection state to prevent damage due to leakage of the product and the space in which the product is installed in the case of the ion water purifier with the reservoir the alarm sounds together with the alarm and at the same time the water level of the reservoir is automatically forced by the automatic drain valve and in the case of the reservoir type the alarm and the warning sound operate quickly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100502305-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in addition the present invention operates a warning alarm at the time of undesired intake due to poor closing of the main water supply valve and enters the inspection state to prevent damage due to water leakage in the product and the space where the product is installed due to water overflow in case of the attached ion water purifier the alarm sounds with alarm and the water level of the reservoir is automatically forced by the automatic drain valve at the same time as the alarm"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "then the backwashing water is transferred from the collecting chamber 24 to the filter chamber through the conveyance pipe 235 connected to the underdrain block 23 and the pressure equalizing chamber 232 and the collecting orifices 231 thereby flowing upward in the filter medium 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101974535-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "also as described above the time point at which the initial rainwater drain valve v1 is closed closed can be closed only for a time period in which the water level precipitation amount is maintained on the high water level of the flowmeter chamber 112c when the rainwater is not continuously detected the initial rainwater exclusion valve v1 is closed closed to prevent contamination of the body portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100807744-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "that is while the drain 133 is closed by the shield plate 151 the movement of sewage is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100807744-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "4 b likewise when the water level in the sewer 20 is increased due to the increase of sewage the lifting stopper 130 is also raised while the locking stand 183 is fitted into the locking groove 132"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2678581-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "therefore the structure of the water level adjusting basin 9 includes a basin body 9a and a water level adjusting pipe portion 9b provided in the basin body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100466336-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thereby increasing the amount of distilled water condensed water filled in the evaporator brine heater 1 thereby raising the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-970007651-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "filtration tank 20 for primary filtering the wash water drained from the air purifier 1 and the lower portion of the filtration tank 20 the upper part of the filtration filter 21 of the filtration tank 20 and the storage tank 30 communicates with the connecting pipe 15 and is divided into left and right sides by a filter 31 installed at an oblique plate and the external water supply pipe 13 is connected to receive secondary filtration and external water supply and the water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in an embodiment the groundwater softening system further includes a first water level sensor installed inside the first tank and a second water level sensor installed inside the second tank wherein the control device includes groundwater stored in a tank having a higher water level among the first tank and the second tank may be selectively discharged through the drain pipe based on the measured values of the first water level sensor and the second water level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102433439-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in an embodiment the groundwater softening system further includes a first water level sensor installed inside the first tank and a second water level sensor installed inside the second tank wherein the control device includes groundwater stored in a tank having a higher water level among the first tank and the second tank may be selectively discharged through the drain pipe based on the measured values of the first water level sensor and the second water level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_533", "text": "the above mentioned firefighter nozzle 10 is connected to multiple pipe nozzles 10 at a distance of 1 meter or 3 meters using a flexible hose 190 for forest fire prevention or indoors or outdoors of a building and a flexible high pressure hose 190 used in the event of an internal fire is formed by a hydraulic press with wire and rubber and a cloth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h thermocouple and compensation wire 103i temperature measurement contact 103j thermocouple 103k compensation contact 103l compensation wire 103m reference contact 103n type of thermocouple 103o no protection tube 103p protection tube 103q high temperature object 103r protection tube there is 103s sis type 103t temperature measuring terminal 103u temperature measuring contact 103v stainless steel metal sheath 103w platinum temperature measuring resistance body with protective tube 103x mica 103y platinum wire 103z magnetism 104 level or pressure switch 104a diaphragm type pressure switch 104b pneumatic sensor pressure switch 105 flow meter for checking discharge amount 106 motor control module 107 weight for valve switch oper