  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "with valve 10 closed no further water will be permitted to pass from drain pipe 53 into sump pit 50 thereby preventing basement 61 from flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178211-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the present invention is to block the upper surface of the drain cover due to foreign matters or in particular even when a large amount of water in a moment of heavy rain or heavy rains can be drained smoothly without clogging with foreign matter so that the water around the drain cover it not only prevents seizing but also provides excellent effects to prevent flooding and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "2 2007 road structure for easy waste disposal summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above described problems in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a rainwater garden at an adjacent location of a road to prevent flooding or subsidence the present invention provides a road structure having a multifunctional drainage line of a road surface that can enhance drainage efficiency and utilize collected watercolor as a multipurpose by forced drainage of water.in order to achieve the above mentioned object the present invention provides a road surface 12 comprising asphalt or concrete pavements a collecting fixture 10 installed on both sides of the road surface 12 to collect rainwater and a storm drain pipe 20 connected to the storm sewer 10 and discharging collected stormwater to the sewer a housing 32 formed with an opening 34 on the upper side and inserted into the road surface 12 a lifting block 30 mounted on the housing 32 such that the upper end of the lifting block 30 can be lifted up and down and the rack gear 31 is extended downward a spring 40 connected to a lower side of the elevating block 30 to press the elevating block 30 upward a pinion gear 50 meshing with the rack gear 31 a drive shaft 60 rotatably shaft connected to the pinion gear 50 and connected to the pinion gear 50 through a ratchet 61 and positively rotated only when the rack gear 31 is lowered a rotation limiting device 70 coupled to the drive shaft 60 to restrict the drive shaft 60 to rotate only in the normal rotation direction a housing 81 formed in a cylindrical shape and having a through hole 81a through which the drive shaft 60 is rotatably inserted is formed on one side of the center axis and a housing 81 having a central end 82a and an outer end 82b the center end 82a is connected to the driving shaft 60 extending to the inside of the housing 81 and the outside end 82b is fixed to the inner circumferential surface of the housing 81 and a rotation shaft 83 coupled to the outer side of the housing 81 so as to be coaxial with the drive shaft 60 so as to rotate together with the housing 81"}, {"pat_id": "US-9771712-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "a sump pump connects directly to the sewer drain pipe using a drain pipe coupler or is located adjacent thereto within the tank where overflow from the drain triggers the sump pump to discharge fluid and sewage into an outlet pipe and out of the basement to prevent flooding and contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101955319-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 1673966 november 26 2016 manhole drainage and ventilation system in underground distribution line summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above described problems in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to solve the above mentioned problems it is possible to prevent secondary electric safety accidents caused by external damage such as an earthquake inside the underground pipe due to an external force such as an earthquake or the like the main purpose of this system is to provide an improved drainage system of underground distribution line to prevent flooding and to prevent electric accidents caused by flooding.a base plate 20 installed on an inner bottom surface of the underground pipe 10 a base plate 20 mounted on the base plate 20 and a plurality of underground distribution lines l which are seated on the shelves 24 and which are arranged in the vertical direction at the center of the shelves 24 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "that is in the present invention the drainage flow of the rainwater drained from the moving port 54 the moving section 59 and the passage port 57 provided to drain water naturally for the drainage path 52 and the vegetation block is reinforced the present invention provides a separate pressurizing device for promoting the drainage of rainwater from a ferry or a drain pipe provided for the purpose of preventing damages caused by flooding with surrounding slopes due to heavy rain or flood"}, {"pat_id": "US-10422119-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "if this occurs the water may still be able to pass through the openings 42 in the corners to prevent water from backing up or flooding over into other areas because the drain is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "US-10422119-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "if this occurs the water may still be able to pass through the openings 42 in the center to prevent water from backing up or flooding over into other areas because the material 34 over the drain 44 is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674110-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes and modifications may be made without departing from the scope of the present invention.1 rainwater catcher 2 3 by drain pipe 4 infiltration ball 10 penetration ditch 10a infiltration ditch inflow section 11 perforated fan for flow equalization 12 shovel rake 12a contamination 13 flooding bumps 14 drainage filter fiber 15 observation 15a 15b plug 20 pretreatment tank 20a pretreatment tank inflow section 21 sand pack 22 stagnant water outlet 30 runoff water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373478-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drain device of manholethe present invention relates to a non power drainage device of the manhole and more specifically to detect the inundation through the water level sensing buoy in the presence of the manhole inside and operate the ejector installed in the connection pipe line and the manhole pipe with a non powered water in the manhole the present invention relates to a non powered drainage device of a manhole that is quickly discharged to the outside to prevent corrosion and breakdown of facilities due to flooding inside the manhole and to maintain a clean state"}, {"pat_id": "US-8691091-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the rapid air escape may also cause the filter media to jump vertically inside the filter tank causing it to be lost through the drain line and possibly causing plugging of the drain and flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-8691091-B2", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "by performing an air release cycle prior to a backwash cycle the release of air may be controlled to prevent the air charge from rushing out to the drain during backwash thereby preventing noise rattling flooding and loss of filter media"}, {"pat_id": "US-10753077-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "if this occurs the water may still be able to pass through the openings 42 in the corners to prevent water from backing up or flooding over into other areas because the drain is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "US-10753077-B2", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "if this occurs the water may still be able to pass through the openings 42 in the center to prevent water from backing up or flooding over into other areas because the material 34 over the drain 44 is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200427026-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the precipitate washed with water from the inclined bottom 13a flows into the sewage treatment plant through the drain pipe 17 together with the washing water.as described above according to the present invention by automating the water washing process of the sediment deposited in the storage tank to facilitate the maintenance of the storage tank and to wash the sediment deposited in the storage tank using the water head difference the siphon structure of the large volume of wash water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937200-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however in the case of the levee structure water can be simply discharged to the other side of the levee to prevent the collapse and flooding of the levee but in the case of the float floating on the water source a net is generally formed at one end of the drain pipe to prevent the inflow of the levee"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100519106-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the phenomenon occurs and there is a problem that the flooding damage occurs in the lowlands.accordingly the present invention is to solve the above problems the backflow of the drain to prevent the rainwater backflow through the drain cover to prevent the backflow through the backflow prevention device that can block the drainage the object is to provide a prevention device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100519106-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "according to the present invention backflow prevention device configured as described above it is possible to block the occurrence of flooding damage by preventing the rainwater backflow through the drain cover through the backflow prevention device that can block the drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-6270661-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "if this happens especially in cases where the groundsoil provides less than ideal drainage it can lead to incomplete or improper treatment of the water backing up flooding etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "it is possible to prevent flooding or flood damage as much as possible by going down to the infiltration water or evaporating to the atmosphere and to prevent the groundwater depletion by the infiltration water going to the ground soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102814353-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the present invention is to solve the above problems and the object is to form a relatively large rainwater inflow hole in a drain cover through which waste such as leaves can pass thereby preventing clogging of the rainwater inflow hole by the waste and resulting flooding and at the same time to form a hole cover at the lower part of the drain cover to block waste from entering thereby blocking waste such as leaves that normally pass through from entering drain pipes and below and also to prevent various safety accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102814353-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention forms a relatively large rainwater inflow hole in a drain cover through which waste such as leaves can pass thereby preventing clogging of the rainwater inflow hole by the waste and resulting flooding and at the same time by forming a hole cover at the lower part of the drain cover to block the inflow of waste such as leaves thereby preventing waste such as leaves that normally pass through from entering drain pipes and below and also has the effect of preventing various safety accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102814353-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "that is the present invention forms a relatively large rainwater inflow hole h through which waste such as leaves can pass in a drain cover 100 thereby preventing clogging of the rainwater inflow hole h by the waste and resulting flooding while also forming a hole cover 200 at the lower part of the drain cover 100 to block waste from entering thereby blocking waste such as leaves that normally pass through from entering the drain pipe or lower and also preventing various safety accidents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345691-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in the above embodiment when the flow rate increases there is a limit value in the pipeline and when the pressure rises reverse flow of sewage occurs to prevent flooding damage at the upstream site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063307-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "not only burnout occurred but there was a problem of property damage due to flooding due to drainage.the present invention is to solve the above problems the air is compressed in the inside of the air pressure tank by the suction force of the drain pump during the drainage process was compressed in the air pressure tank when the water in the drain pipe back flow after the completion of drainage as the air expands it supports the check valve for preventing the backflow to prevent water hammer and at the same time to discharge the end of the drain pipe to constitute a water collecting tank drainage device equipped with a water hammer prevention air pressure tank to remove the foreign matter caught in the filter net of the drain pump biodegradation that is sucked together with water by suction power of the drainage pump when the drainage pump is installed by installing a vacuum netting connecting socket to which the vacuum gauge is connected to the suction end of the drainage pump and a plurality of foreign matter crushing blades are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187840-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it includes a rainwater management block that allows rainwater to be stored in rainwater storage blocks and a rainwater management block that opens a drain valve to allow rainwater to penetrate into the infiltration facility after a rainfall has passed and discharges stored rainwater depending on the situation to prevent flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the flood diffusion prevention system of a building structure that is installed in a multi story building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to leakage from spreading to the elevating facility space a drainage passage formed on the floor of the common space for each floor in the building structure a drainage trench installed on the upper portion of the drainage passage to shield the drainage passage and a plurality of drainage holes for draining the inflowing water into the drainage passage a drain module connected to and configured to include a pipe for discharging the water to the outside a flood detection sensor installed in the drainage module to detect whether water has flowed in a water supply shutoff valve installed in a water supply line of the building structure to block water supply by a control signal and a flood signal received from the flood detection sensor a control unit for transmitting the control signal to the water supply shut off valve so as to be blocked and it is installed in front of the opening closing door of the elevator installed in the building structure and is raised to a preset height from the floor and includes a blocking module to prevent water from flowing into the elevator when submerged the blocking module is a blocking member installed in front of the opening closing door to open or shield the front lower part of the opening closing door according to the elevation an elevating wire having one end coupled to the upper portion of the blocking member to elevate the blocking member and the flooding prevention system of a building structure characterized in that it is connected to the other end of the elevating wire and configured to include a wire driving unit for elevating and lowering the elevating wire in conjunction with the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention provides a system for preventing the spread of water in a building structure that is installed in a multi storey building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to a leak from spreading to an elevating facility space the it is installed on the upper part of the drain to shield the drain and includes a drain trench having a plurality of drain holes through which the inflowing water is drained into the drain and a piping part connected to the drain to drain the water to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "it is possible to effectively prevent the inflow into the lowering facility space thereby preventing flooding of the elevating facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the installation height of the flood detection sensor 210 is installed at a certain height from the bottom of the drain 101 not the bottom of the drain 101 so that it can be determined that flooding has occurred due to water leakage not living water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "and a cap 198 connected to the hinge 190 of the fixed frame 125 provided at the end of the branch pipe 121.the present invention provides a stable drainage of rainwater by providing a stable removal of rainwater or flood caused by heavy rainfall as described above while checking the clogging caused by sedimentation that accumulates while moving in a drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-4180094-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the drain cover 12 is placed over a drain 14 in the floor 16 to prevent water backing up in the sewage system from flooding into the building in which the drain 14 is located"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is installed on the drain around the road the front part and the lower part are opened respectively and the upper surface part the left surface part the right surface part and the rear part are formed in a closed hexahedron shape respectively and a main body extending a certain length left and right a first front cover and a second front cover which are installed to be spaced apart from each other on the left and right sides of the front part of the main body so as to form an inlet through which water flows into the central side of the open front part of the main body a first opening closing door and a second opening closing door installed on the main body behind the first front cover and the second front cover and movably installed along the left and right directions of the main body to open and close the inlet a door driving unit for moving the first and second opening and closing doors a control unit that operates the door driving unit by an operator s or manager s manipulation or automatically operates the door driving unit according to a set pattern a blocking screen installed on the main body corresponding to the inlet side behind the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door to block foreign substances from entering the main body the lower surface of the main body includes a plurality of bottom frames arranged to form a square shape and a bottom plate installed to close the space between the bottom frames and having a discharge port for discharging water to a drain on one side the upper surface portion of the main body includes a plurality of ceiling frames disposed parallel to the lower surface portion and arranged to form a square shape on the upper portion of the lower surface portion and a ceiling plate installed to close a space between the ceiling frames the left side the right side and the rear portion each have a plurality of side frames having one end connected to the floor frame and the other end coupled to the ceiling frame to support the ceiling frame with respect to the floor frame including a side plate installed to close the space between the side frame and the ceiling frame the upper and lower ends of the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door are inserted into each of the floor frame and the ceiling frame on the front side to a certain depth to prevent movement of the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in addition the present invention can prevent foreign matter such as floating debris of a certain size or more contained in sewage such as rainwater or sewage from entering the drain preventing clogging of the drain and flooding due to backflow and removing and cleaning foreign matter such as filtered floating debris"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in regions of extreme cold the rain water drains often freeze resulting in great expense in thawing of the drains and creating difficulties and costs as a result of flooding due for example to the melting of large quantities of snow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however especially in the rainy season or in the fall foreign substances such as fallen leaves can block the inlet making it difficult to drain which can easily lead to flooding and human casualties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101937611-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore in the sewage odor removal system of the present invention the supply water flowing into the spraying housing moves downward through the upper discharge hole of the adjustment inlet so as to dissolve and store the stored medicine and at the same time since the supply water is discharged by adjusting the gap between the drain pipe 112a and the drain pipe 112a it is possible to sufficiently dissolve the chemicals and to discharge them and also it is possible to safely and accurately sense the return pipe line condition by protecting the detection sensor and to prevent flooding of the sensing sensor to prevent contamination and damage and to selectively maintain deodorization direction sterilization or a mixture of these as needed to maintain the state of the best sewage line it is effective"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "for instance flooding of laundry rooms is such a common occurrence that many housing codes now require washing machines to be positioned within catch basins"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}]</data>
</edge>
