"have", "minimize", "accommodate", "discard", "reinforce", "go", "relate", "modify", "revolve", "exit", "force", "handle", "comply", "grab", "expect", "set", "evaporate", "form", "concentrate", "save", "spray", "build", "conclude", "chill", "depend", "weaken", "mix", "push", "pack", "steam", "join", "deteriorate", "turn", "effectuate", "penetrate", "undergo", "fall", "hoist", "dissolve", "move", "ionize", "locate", "read", "reduce", "plug", "query", "may", "communicate", "discharge", "store", "design", "seep", "net", "spot", "obtain", "must", "exhaust", "permeate", "absorb", "condition", "evaporator", "define", "charge", "transport", "finish", "favor", "heat", "galvanize", "lie", "drain", "fail", "shape", "select", "trickle", "continue", "bypass", "be", "print", "link", "warm", "expose", "combine", "apply", "drill", "weld", "rise", "preheat", "reach", "extract", "sld", "dump", "refer", "achieve", "increase", "soften", "maximize", "pour", "regenerate", "disclose", "melt", "circulate", "will", "restore", "provide", "wrap", "contain", "space", "uncoil", "ship", "compare", "scale", "leak", "size", "calculate", "limit", "regard", "silt", "oil", "do", "settle", "create", "facilitate", "understand", "bury", "exceed", "consider", "baffle", "disinfect", "run", "weave", "insert", "direct", "spawn", "seat", "box", "cover", "show", "configure", "match", "cool", "derive", "start", "fit", "guide", "act", "perform", "thereto", "consist", "open", "mean", "supply", "sanitize", "use", "propeller", "cut", "associate", "break", "tube", "initiate", "draw", "invoke", "stagnate", "extend", "control", "case", "transmit", "need", "monitor", "expend", "exist", "collect", "instal", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102678075-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide plate 24 formed with 24a it includes a water circulation means a provided in the lower cultivation unit 19b to push the water inside the lower cultivation unit 19b forward the water circulation means a is a guide rod 51 provided inside the lower cultivation portion 19b to extend laterally a slide block 52 laterally slideably coupled to the guide rod 51 a plurality of blades 53 extending in the front and rear directions and rotatably coupled to the front of the slide block 52 laterally within a certain angle a floating aquatic weed production system comprising a reciprocating drive means 54 connected to the slide block 52 to cause the slide block 52 to reciprocate laterally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102678075-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a floating aquatic weed production system is provided comprising a plurality of blades 53 and a reciprocating drive means 54 connected to the slide block 52 to cause the slide block 52 to reciprocate laterally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "110 170 wall 120 water tank 121 drain pipe 125 screw 126 drive motor 127 freezing prevention spring 128 water temperature sensor 129 controller 130 180 spacer 140 heater 147 temperature sensor 150 opening and closing door 160 support leg"}, {"pat_id": "US-4018682-A", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "whereby the water fraction of the mixture forms small snow like crystals thus separating the water from the clay and silt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "is possible and such variations fall within the protection scope of the present invention.10 piping entering the object to be frozen or bursting or piping exiting from the object 20 external power 100 automatic dripping device for freezing prevention 110 body part 111 opening and closing lid 112 power indicator lamp 113 operation indicator lamp 114 storage space 120 temperature detection unit 130 control unit 131 external power input terminal 132 transformer 133 relay 140 on off valve 150 on off valve driving unit 150e emergency operation button 151 opening and closing valve coupling part 152 rotary drive unit 153 heat supply unit 154 opening and closing valve warming part 161 additional mounting piping 161a extension pipe 162 additionally installed on off valve 163 falling water storage tank 164 falling water flow rate detection unit 165 falling water supply pipe 166 water level detection and alarm unit 167 water drain pipe 171 power supply unit 172 power supply part warming part 173 wireless communication module"}, {"pat_id": "US-5553637-A", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the second chamber 31 has a primary inlet 34 connected at 35 to the outlet 11 via the supply line section 13a subjected to freezing temperature i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "as a result it is possible to prevent unnecessary power consumption in the feed pump for supplying water to the filtration membrane portion and to maintain the flow rate on the surface of the filtration membrane to prevent the filtration membrane from clogging due to fouling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200315853-Y1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "in this embodiment the band heaters 80 and 81 are attached to the drain holes 43 and 83 so that the water is automatically heated to prevent freezing when the water is cold below a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-7566400-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the conditioning of the wastewater and solids via oxidation reduction reactions thus form self adhering solids shedding water upon drying and disinfected wastewater with high plant nutrients at the point where the odor reduction and color changes of the conditioned solids and liquids occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238165-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "it belongs to the scope of rights.1 drinking water supply device 10 main body 11 settling space 12 lower space 13 first door 13a hole 14 second door 20 container 21 discharge pipe 30 detection unit 31 controller 32 sensor 33 supporter 40 temperature control unit 41 cooling unit 411 refrigerant pipe 412 refrigerant unit 42 heating unit 421 heating tube 422 heat generating unit 50 direct part 51 solenoid valve 60 drain tray 61 drain pipe 62 container 70 storage 71 storage body 72 cover 73 sterilizer 81 82 83 lifting device 811 screw 812 drive motor 813 lifting bar 831 link unit 831a 831b and 831c link member 832 drive part 832a link screw 832b link motor 832c link block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example in one winter a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the system comprises a water pipe including a water stop valve a pipe connected with the water pipe through a first electromagnetic valve and a second electromagnetic valve the system allowing the first valve to close temporarily while said second valve is held open in order to drain water from the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an apparatus for preventing the water in a water supply pipe upstream of the apparatus from freezing comprising sample chamber means filled with water and exposed to the environment the water in said sample chamber means freezing when the environmental temperature goes below freezing drain means for receiving water from the water supply pipe in one portion thereof and for discharging it to the environment from another portion thereof means closing off said drain means when the water in said sample chamber means is not frozen piston like means for operating on said closing means to open said drain means in response to the water in said sample chamber means freezing means delivering water from the water supply pipe to said drain means when said drain means is open said delivery means including a holding tank means having said drain means and said closing means located therein thermal isolating means including a first heat sink between said holding tank means and said sample chamber means wherein said piston like operating means extends through said thermal isolating means between said sample chamber means and said holding tank wherein in operation the lower end of the piston moves within said sample chamber means in response to the water therein freezing which in turn forces the upper end of the piston against said closing means thereby opening said drain means wherein a flow of water through the water supply pipe and out said drain means to the environment is maintained as long as the water in said sample chamber means is frozen such a water flow tending to prevent water in the water supply pipe upstream of the apparatus from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "water in the holding tank as well as water from the water supply system moving through connecting pipe 17 hose 23 and channel 26 in filler tube 24 flows into the common opening 30 in the pedestal drain element and then out drain pipe 31 thus maintaining a flow of water in the water supply system upstream of the apparatus preventing freezing of the water in the upstream portion of the system thereby"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "as the ambient temperature rises slightly above freezing the ice in the apparatus begins to melt however it does not melt immediately thereby shutting off the drain opening 30"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "the lower end of the exterior thaw tube 32 thus thaws quickly and also freezes quickly which provides a fast refreezing of the apparatus and reopening of the drain opening 30 should the ambient temperature after only a short period of thaw again go below freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_813", "text": "fourth regarding the detailed explanation of low temperature use although it can be used at temperatures down to 10 care must be taken to prevent solidification or freezing of moisture in the drain 301 and if freezing is a concern use it by installing an air dryer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h therm