 be in the closed position to prevent water from entering said water utilizing device and the second and third valves will be in the open position to allow water to drain from said water utilizing device to provide freeze protection in the case of a electrical power outage during freezing conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "a water freeze prevention device for an evaporative cooler that is periodically exposed to water freezing temperatures said water freeze prevention device comprising a first valve for regulating water flow through a first pipe leading from a water inlet device to the evaporative cooler an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said first valve back and forth between a closed position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and an open position associated with a second mode of operation of said device a second valve for draining water from a portion of the first pipe located between the first valve and the evaporative cooler an electrically drive valve actuator capable of moving said second valve back and forth between an open position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and a closed position associated with a second mode of operation of said device a third valve for draining water from the evaporative cooler an electrically driven valve actuator capable of moving said third valve back and forth between an open position associated with a first mode of operation of the water freeze prevention device and a closed position associated with a second mode of operation of said device a temperature setting device for invoking the first mode of operation and the second mode of operation of said first second and third valves a temperature sensing device capable of detecting a preset adjustable temperature that invokes appropriate operation of said valve actuators and an electrical current sending device capable of driving said valve actuators based upon electrical signals transduced from said preset adjustable temperature whereby said evaporative cooler is either completely winterized or completely charged with water such that without electrical power the first valve will be in the closed position to prevent water from entering said evaporative cooler and the second and third valves will be in the open position to allow water to drain from said evaporative cooler to provide freeze protection in the case of a electrical power outage during freezing conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "an evaporative cooler and its associated piping system and certain freezing temperature exposed portions of applicant s device are drained and thus winterized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102154031-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition by providing a heater tube on the inner wall of the body protection element of the intermittent device the open or closed operating space of the intermittent device is always maintained at room temperature to prevent freezing thereby improving the maintenance and management of facilities and product quality.1 is a view showing a partial excerpt of a deodorizing pipe of an odor prevention facility in a terminal treatment plant to which an automatic condensate drainage device of the present invention is applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "groundwater contamination prevention structure 1 1 is built in the space inside the combined structure to combine and directly connected to each other and sealed to each other structural structure 1 1 1 is installed inside the underground rock well inside the casing 4 4 to prevent the groundwater contamination by itself and to automatically drain and drain the water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4213830-A", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "the low temperature evaporation of the waste water drain flows which become more and more concentrated further prevents the danger of corrosion damage and of incrustation since both phenomena are favored by elevated temperatures and concentrations"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S6015800-Y2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "this is to prevent freezing inside the water meter body"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S6015800-Y2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "since the water dispenser is allowed to flow through the water dispenser damage to the dispenser body due to freezing of water accumulated inside the dispenser body can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102602389-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should include not only the above embodiments but also other variously modified embodiments according to the technical spirit of the invention described in the claims below.10 body 11 protruding end 11a 1st pass 11b second pass 11c third pass 12 1st peduncle 13 printed circuit board 20 water tank 21 exterior wall 22 inner wall 23 insulation 24 receptor 25 second peduncle 30 connection information board 31 1st wit home 32 2nd wit home 33 self adhering member 40 temperature sensor 50 sterilization lamp 60 water level sensor 70 cooling means 71 thermoelectric element 72 cooling rod 73 water cooler 73a water block 73b first connection hose 73c second connection hose 73d radiator 73e circulation pump 73f cooling fan 80 water fountain 81 water nozzle 82 water level control ball 83 auxiliary water nozzle 90 water supply means 91 proximity sensor 92 water pump 93 water hose 100 height adjustable 110 recovery stand 111 recovery plate 111a drain hole 111b 1st hose passage hole 112 noise reduction hopper 112a second hose passage hole 113 filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a freezing prevention device for a water meter installed between a water inlet pipe and a water outlet pipe to prevent a water meter for measuring a flow rate of water passing through the water pipe from being frozen a housing installed in the water pipe and having an inlet through which water flows into the inside and a drain through which the incoming water is discharged to the outside a temperature responsive member installed in the housing and contracting or expanding according to a change in temperature and contracting below a predetermined threshold temperature a fixture having the temperature sensitive member installed therein and fixed to the housing and and a moving body provided inside the temperature sensitive member and opening and closing the inlet while being moved in accordance with contraction or expansion of the temperature sensitive member wherein the inlet port is provided with an internal inflow pipe inserted into the water outlet pipe and extending to the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention there is provided a freezing prevention device for a water meter which is installed between a water inlet pipe and a water outlet pipe to prevent a water meter for measuring a flow rate of water passing through the water pipe from being frozen a housing having an inlet through which water is introduced and a drain through which the incoming water is discharged a temperature sensitive member installed in the housing and contracting or expanding according to a temperature change a fixture having the temperature sensitive member installed therein and fixed to the housing and a moving body provided with the temperature sensitive member therein and opening and closing the inlet while being moved in accordance with contraction or expansion of the temperature sensitive member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "while the present invention has been described in connection with what is presently considered to be preferred embodiments it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed embodiments but on the contrary it is to be understood that the invention is not limited thereto.10 water inlet pipe 20 water outlet pipe 30 el storage 100 weighing main body 110 bypass unit 200 freeze prevention unit 210 case 300 freezing prevention device 310 housing 211 311 inlet 212 312 drain hole 313 internal inlet pipe 220 320 temperature sensitive member 230 330 240 340 moving body 250 350 elastic member 260 360 rubber member"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_171", "text": "furthermore be communicating with a home router the water meter and leak detection system 10 126 200 can communicate with intelligent thermostats sending a signal to turn on the residential or corporation heat to a temperature that will inhibit freezing water in the residential and corporation interior water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "another method for preventing the water pipe from freezing is to prevent the water pipe from freezing by artificially opening a water valve to continuously drain the water when it is expected that the water contained in the water pipe will freeze due to low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore since the freeze preventer operates normally below the freezing temperature and the tap water is smoothly drained the entire water pipe can be protected from freezing or bursting.1 is a block diagram showing a water pipe device for preventing freezing according to a first embodiment of the present invention 2 is a block diagram showing a water pipe device for preventing freezing according to a second embodiment of the present invention figure 3 is an enlarged view of the a portion of figure 1 figure 4 is an enlarged view of the b portion of figure 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681403-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition in order to solve the problem that the water of the body is frozen and the ceramic insulator is broken if the outside air temperature in winter falls below freezing for a long time without using active water according to one embodiment of the present invention when