tals are removed from the low temperature crystallization tank 40 and the remaining regenerated waste water filtrate is vacuum evaporated by indirect heating through a heating device 110 and a vacuum state by a vacuum pump to precipitate white powdery crystals of a nitrogen compound a vacuum evaporation crystallization tank 100 composed of a closed type adiabatic reaction tank a secondary condensing tank 120 for re condensing water vapor that is not condensed in the primary condensing tank 80 and is discharged and discharged through the cooling condensing device 130 a cooling condenser 130 for cooling water in the secondary condensing tank 120 to coagulate through heat exchange with the refrigerant to form condensed water a vacuum pump 140 for generating a vacuum of 0.2 atm in the vacuum evaporation and crystallization tank 100 to lower the evaporation temperature of the regenerated wastewater to 60 c the condensed water produced in the primary condensing tank 80 and the secondary condensing tank 120 is periodically opened to open the drain valve 90 and stored in the condensed water storage tank 150 through the condensate transfer pipe 91 which is characterized by low temperature and high vacuum evaporation concentration crystallization"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226160-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an exhaust valve 11 open to exhaust the high temperature and high pressure steam of the first reactor 10 for the exhaust gas drain valve 22 which is closed to inject the high temperature and high pressure steam in the first reactor 10 into the second reactor 20 while the exhaust valve is opened and the exhaust valve 21 which is opened steam of high temperature and high pressure in addition to the second reactor 20 in which the sample introduced into the second reactor 20 is preheated by the steam of high temperature and high pressure exhausted from the first reactor introduced through the open exhaust valve 21"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text"