d to drain the fluid in the stopped state until the frozen fluid melts thereby preventing the fluid from freezing due to the fluid flow generated inside the pipeline of the fluid transport pipe 110 and at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584471-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the solenoid valve 122 is opened to drain the fluid in the stopped state until the frozen fluid melts thereby preventing the fluid from freezing due to the fluid flow generated inside the pipeline of the fluid transport pipe 110 and at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "US-5555747-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a directional freeze crystallization system comprising a a crystallizer means consisting of a heat exchanger b a vessel for containing liquid to be purified c a cooling means for conveying a heat transfer fluid to said heat exchanger said heat transfer fluid being at a temperature less than the freezing point of said liquid to be purified d a filling means for conveying said liquid to be purified into said vessel e a draining means for conveying unfrozen liquid from said vessel f a heating means for melting ice frozen on said heat exchanger g a transfer means for conveying melted ice from said vessel h an accumulator connected by a fluid conduit to said vessel i a quantity sensor to determine the volume of unfrozen liquid in said accumulator j a state sensor to determine the absence of frozen liquid in said vessel j control means for repeatedly sequentially actuating said filling means cooling means draining means heating means and transfer means responsive to said quantity sensor and said state sensor to fill said vessel with liquid to be purified freeze a fraction of said liquid to be purified adjacent to said heat exchanger drain the unfrozen fraction of said liquid to be purified melt the frozen fraction of said liquid to be purified and convey the melted fraction from said vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a water meter and more particularly to a freeze proof water meter having a drain portion for discharging water in accordance with the temperature drop in the lower portion of the water meter to prevent freezing caused by the temperature drop in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "an object of the present invention is to provide a freeze prevention type water meter having a drain portion for discharging water in response to a temperature drop in the lower part of the water meter to prevent freezing caused by a temperature drop in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "therefore the water meter is discharged to the outside of the water filled in the outer shell 100 by the drain portion 1 provided to the lower portion of the outer shell 100 and is restored to its original state when returning to the normal temperature by preventing the water from being discharged freezes generated by freezing the filled water are prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "as described above the present invention includes a drain portion for discharging water at the lower part of the water meter according to the temperature drop so as to prevent freezing caused by the temperature drop in winter the freeze is easily prevented according to the change in temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200498205-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition in the winter if the permeated water that seeps into the pavement layer of the bridge deck is not drained quickly and remains it freezes due to the low temperature causing freezing and rupture of the pavement layer"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the water heater system of claim 7 wherein the condensate collector 390 includes a drain 398 and wherein the controller 142 is further configured to determine a drain blockage of the drain 398 based on a comparison between a temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 and a temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418 when the water heater is in the heating mode optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller 142 when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "the method of claim 12 wherein the condensate collector 390 further includes a drain 398 configured to receive the condensate the method further comprising determining a drain blockage of the drain 398 by the controller 142 based on a comparison between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 and the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418 when the water heater 10 is in the heating mode optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller 142 when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor 418"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "the controller 142 concludes that the cause of the stagnation is a blockage somewhere in the drain assembly 90 e.g"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the controller 142 thus concludes at 250 that there is leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the controller 142 thus concludes at 250 that there is a leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the controller 142 may be configured to query the first second and third temperature sensors 114 118 122 during specific time periods of the day when determining a drain blockage or a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "for example when determining a drain blockage the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and second temperature sensors 114 118 during morning hours when it is most likely the user will require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "although the leaked water may lose some heat during the wait period 695 while accumulating in the drain pipe 394 this is not significant enough to prevent the change in state of the temperature reading from the negative rate of change to the positive rate or change or to prevent the increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "alternatively the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "in particular when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the controller thus concludes at 550 that there is leakage i.e"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_80", "text": "thus the invention provides among other things a water heater 10 including a control system 38 338 configured to detect an error in the water heater 10 such as a leakage or a drain blockage by utilizing and or comparing temperature readings of condensate flue gases and outside atmosphere during specific operating modes of the water heater 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_248", "text": "there may also be a drain line not shown for when the system is shut down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970306-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to form a negative electrode or a positive electrode separately so that the negative electrode or the positive electrode can be replaced individually during replacement due to corrosion breakage respectively.in order to achieve the above object the present invention is a sensor for measuring the temperature or hydrogen ion concentration such as constant sewage is coupled to the holder the amount of residual chlorine in which a negative electrode and a positive electrode is formed on one side of the holder a device for measuring the amount of residual chlorine in the indicator by measuring the amount of residual chlorine contained in the measured water by galvanic cell electrolysis by combining the measuring sensor separately"}, {"pat_id": "US-4230530-A", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "decreasing the time between cycles of water overflow will of course produce a cooler temperature for the condenser and for the output of the distiller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200408786-Y1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "on the other hand if the groundwater in the water collection pipe 122 is filled with groundwater in the conditions of low outside temperature such as winter season the groundwater may freeze and freeze so the ground water inside the water collection pipe 122 is lowered to a temperature that can freeze the state of figure 4a in order to operate the handle 134 to lower the opening and closing hole 132 as shown in figure 4b to block the distribution holes 131a 132a while opening the drain pipe 124"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "outlet opening 57 is similarly designed to receive a fitting that is connectable for example to a drain system all of which are not shown"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "it is therefore seen that the present invention provides a simple device for activating a fluid valve in response to a thermal and specifically to a freezing change in temperature without the requirement for external power or human intervention"}, {"pat_id": "US-4922233-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "monitoring systems presently used to monitor the condition of a drain valve and employing differential temperature sensors are ineffective or insufficient for a number of reasons"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "calcium chloride which is used for snow removal does not flow quickly into the drainage channel and may penetrate into the road surface resulting in a problem of weakening the durability of ascon"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3497806-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "to prevent the measurement accuracy from deteriorating due to contamination of these pipes and water quality detector while controlling the water temperature of the inflow water flowing into the water purification plant and sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413252-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in other words due to the change of temperature and external impacts depending on the season and the impact of the uplift and settlement of the ground the mortar inlet is easily damaged and water tightness is degraded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102018905-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in the sewage sludge treatment method using an alkane based solvent for extracting and treating organic matter from sewage sludge using a multi stage separation reactor an organic material separating step of separating an alkane based solvent into the sewage sludge into the multi stage separation reactor to separate the microorganisms and organic sludge attached to the solvent from the outermost water present in the outside of the microorganism s110 and organic matter concentration step s120 to diffuse the non polar solvent into the inside of the microorganisms to induce cell membrane destruction of the microorganisms by swelling and to drain out the crystal water remaining inside the microorganisms by cell membrane destruction to the outside s120 but the solvent introduced in the organic material separation step s110 is a solvent present in a liquid state at atmospheric pressure and room temperature in the alkane based solvent the microorganism and organic sludge attached to the solvent is the upper side of the water by a solvent whose specific gravity is less than 1 suspended in water and separated from water the sewage sludge introduced in the organic material separation step s110 of the chemical treatment tank 10 the aerobic tank 20 the sedimentation tank 30 the concentration tank 40 and the dehydration device 50 are installed in sequence in the sewage treatment plant sewage sludge finished in the aeration tank 20 the settling tank 30 or the concentration tank 40 further comprising a pretreatment step s110 p for the solvent input the pretreatment step s110 p may include a concentration detection step of detecting a concentration of mixed liquor suspended solids mlss which is a mixed solution average suspended solids concentration for the sewage sludge and an input amount detecting step of determining an input amount of the introduced solvent according to the detected mlss concentration further comprising a concentration adjusting step of diluting the mlss concentration of the sewage sludge to less than 5 000 ppm wherein the organic material any one or more of the outermost water separated in the separation step s110 or the crystallized water separated in the organic matter concentration step s120 is re introduced into the sewage sludge to maintain the mlss concentration of the sewage sludge at a system optimum value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drain device with double bodythe present invention relates to a drain having a dual structure and more particularly having a drain and the outer cylinder and the inner cylinder to prevent the leakage of sewage having a hot temperature of the waste collected in the drain after installation of the drain and sewage into cement or mortar it not only prevents water leakage due to absorption but also prevents leakage of water leakage and leakage by the outer cylinder even if a gap of the inner cylinder occurs as well as filtering wastes such as food waste by a plurality of strainers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "there is a problem in that leakage occurs due to absorption of sewage leaked into the cement or mortar buried"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "15 2002 the present invention provides a drainage outlet with an inner cylinder and an outer cylinder to minimize heat transfer of the hot temperature of the waste and the inner cylinder is spaced from the outer cylinder so that the heat transfer of the outer cylinder is not performed so that the gap due to thermal deformation of the outer cylinder is achieved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "a waste filtration passage having a plurality of first filtration holes in the first filtration to filter the wastes contained in the filthy water flowing through the effluent inlet holes a first filtration panel fitted to the first fitting support and positioned in a longitudinal direction with respect to the inner cylinder and provided with a plurality of second filtration holes at a bottom thereof to filter out filthy water and wastes from the waste filtration tank secondly a second filtration panel fitted to the second fitting support and positioned longitudinally with respect to the inner cylinder and having a plurality of third filtration holes in the center to filter out filthy water and wastes from the first filtration panel in a third filter it is made.the present invention is provided with an outer cylinder embedded in cement or mortar and the inner cylinder to be inserted into the inside of the outer cylinder but because the inner cylinder and the outer cylinder are provided in a state separated from each other the hot sewage temperature flowing into the inner cylinder side is the outer cylinder by preventing the transfer to the side it is possible to prevent the external cylinder from generating heat deformation gap due to hot temperature and also to prevent the leakage of water leaked from the inner cylinder by being absorbed by cement or mortar"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102797750-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a first tank 1100 softening tank equipped with a level sensor 1110 capable of detecting the lowest and highest water levels as well as the supply of raw water a first channel q1 installed to be able to send the fluid discharged to the lower part of the first tank softening tank a circulation pump 1200 installed at a predetermined position of the first channel a cooling device 1300 installed at a predetermined position of the circulation pump to be able to cool the temperature of the fluid passing through the circulation pump a second channel q2 installed to be able to send the fluid passing through the cooling device at high pressure a reverse osmosis membrane high pressure pump 1400 installed at a predetermined position of the second channel and a reverse osmosis membrane 1500 ro membrane or a second tank 1700 ro produced water storage tank having a reverse osmosis membrane ro membrane or ro membrane and a third channel q3 for discharging the product water produced in the reverse osmosis membrane a reverse osmosis membrane produced water supply valve 1600 installed at a predetermined position of the third channel a level sensor 1710 installed at an end of the third channel for storing the product water and detecting the lowest and highest water levels and capable of discharging the product water downward a fourth channel q4 through which concentrated water is discharged from the reverse osmosis membrane ro membrane or ro membrane and a concentrated water drain valve 1810 and a concentrated water recovery valve 1820 installed in the fourth channel for discharging the concentrated water as waste water or supplying it to the first tank softening water tank and a connection between the concentrated water valve and the first tank softening water tank in a concentrated wastewater reduction device of an ro system which comprises a concentrated water recovery path q5 connected internally a produced water recovery path q6 branched from a third path located between the reverse osmosis membrane and the reverse osmosis membrane produced water supply valve and connected to the inside of the first tank softening water tank and equipped with a produced water circulation valve 1900 and a control unit s connected to control the level sensors of the first and second tanks and the pumps valves and electrical components installed in each path a first electrical conductivity sensor 1001 installed at a predetermined position of the third flow path q3 installed between the reverse osmosis membrane product water supply valve 1600 and the product water circulation valve 1900 and the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 so as to detect the electrical conductivity of the fluid passing through the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 and send it to the control unit s a second electrical conductivity sensor 1002 installed between the cooling device 1300 and the reverse osmosis membrane high pressure pump 1400 to detect the electrical conductivity of the fluid being transported through the second channel q2 and send it to the control unit s and when a fluid having an electrical conductivity higher than a certain value flows through the second channel q2 the control unit s blocks the concentrated water recovery valve 1820 installed in the concentrated water recovery channel q5 and opens the concentrated water drain valve 1810 to prevent the fluid having an electrical conductivity higher than the set value from being continuously supplied to the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 thereby preventing the failure of the reverse osmosis membrane 1500 and extending its lifespan"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "in order to prevent the water stagnant in the water pipe 3 from freezing when the temperature detected by the temperature sensor 5 falls below the set temperature detected by the temperature sensor 5 during the idle period of the boiler 1 by the valve control unit 13 of the controller 10 the electromagnetic valve 3 is opened and at the same time the electromagnetic valve 7a is automatically closed through the valve control unit 13 and the pump 6 provided in the boiler 1 is operated to the inside through the water pipe 3 the supplied water is discharged by bypassing the drain pipe 4c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "during the idle period of the boiler 1 the electromagnetic valve 3 is automatically opened and closed according to the external temperature sensed through the temperature sensor 5 to discharge the water stagnated in the water pipe 2 to the outside through the drain pipe 4c to the outside of the water pipe by allowing water to flow at regular intervals through 2 it is possible to prevent the water meter and water pipe from being frozen by increasing the freezing point freezing point of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "when the outside temperature drops below freezing the water system must be drained to prevent damage to the pipes tanks water fixture s and other plumbing components"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "for some rv units 4 the r value in regards to temperature may be too low to maintain an interior environment 206 temperature needed when plugged into and using only external electrical power system without running the furnace and consuming limited on board fuel"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_269", "text": "insulated adequately to prevent excessive heat loss especially when the rv unit is operating only from the on board fuel and battery to save on lp gas and battery drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the pipe adjacent the location of the thermal sensor drops below freezing the sensor is actuated and completes an electrical circuit from a power source to a solenoid actuated valve to thereby cause it to open and allow water to trickle from the water supply pipe through an existing water outlet fixture and down its adjacent and pre existing drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102099550-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "as a method to prevent water leakage in buildings there is a method of installing a drain drainage pipe a pipe that guides rainwater on a pipe bridge to the surface and frequent contact and temperature of moisture in the periphery of the inlet side where the drain is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "discontinuance of dental services in case of malfunction or exhaustion of water in the single pressure storage tank 2 9 in order to prevent the occurrence of a separate simple auxiliary metal or plastic material inside the device the tank 2 14 is installed and in case of emergency the tank cap 2 14 1 is opened and the user can be used to pour the graft in addition a small load is provided at the inlet of the pipe 3 9 to which the water of the unit chair to which each is connected is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "US-5927099-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "because icemakers make ice by spraying water onto electrically chilled freezer plates a substantial amount of water is lost during each freezing cycle by failing to freeze before reaching the bottom of the freezer plates and exiting into the drain yet a considerable amount of energy is expended in lowering the temperature of this lost water as well as of the water that does freeze"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102075865-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in addition the heating device is further mounted on the water meter inside the main body of the protector to sense the temperature inside the main body of the winter protector to warm the water meter thereby preventing the freezing of the water meter and improving the safety of the product.1 is an exploded perspective view of the water meter protector of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-10376807-B2", "para_id": "para_170", "text": "for controlling input water pre heating energy management including solar and wind power generation controlling the temperature at various stages to maintain safe temperatures to prevent mold formation provide a graphical user interface via a handheld device wired wireless and be able to log all system operations self maintenance monitor the quality of the input drain and product water several times per unit of time detect when the efficiency of the system is going down possibly caused by scaling and thereby initiating a self flush cleaning cycle and monitoring the system temperature on a continuing basis to ensure that the system operates in a safe temperature zone and does not become a breeding ground for dangerous bacteria mold by controlling the electric heater to self sanitize the system periodically"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the site at which the air seal is located is selected so that said seal lies on a level in the drain where freezing would not normally occur because water flowing through the pipes connected to the drain maintains said location at a temperature somewhat above freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100926077-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in addition the shower mode is more convenient because it provides the cold hot soft water and the cold hot water of the optimum temperature based on the user s body temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100926077-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "subsequently looking at the plurality of pipe lines w1 to w14 provided in the water softener according to the present invention by connecting the external cold hot water pipes to the first valve assembly 350 to remove the cold hot raw water of the cold hot water pipes the first valve assembly 1 by connecting the first and second raw water supply lines w1 w2 to the first valve assembly 350 and the first valve assembly 350 to the first and second soft water tanks 710 720"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "during this freezing process water molecules crystallize to form a lattice structure which allows the ice layer 60 to float on top of the water 10 while rejecting salt organic compounds minerals or other impurities into the water 10 beneath the layer of ice 60"}, {"pat_id": "US-10099943-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "4 feed water 10a is then pumped into the tank 20 to raise the block of ice 60a above at least one wall of the tank 20 and a mechanical device such as a push rod 70 or moveable arm is used to remove the block of ice 60a from the tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101090211-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a water pressure control encoder switch for adjusting the intensity of the water output the temperature of the water ph concentration the operation button to receive the output time the water level sensor for measuring the water level an input unit configured of a temperature sensor measuring a temperature of water a pump for raising the water to the shampoo ware a heater for heating the water to a temperature set by the operation button an electrolysis tank for ionizing the water and performing electrolysis to match the ph concentration input to the operation button ac power is supplied to the shampoo ware the auxiliary tank equipped with a heater an electrolysis tank a drain box for collecting sewage a solenoid opened and closed to control the flow of water between a water supply tank into which water is input and the solenoid a pump a compressor and a heater"}, {"pat_id": "US-10501355-B2", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "the wastewater undergoes a catalytic oxidation reaction in the system in which the macromolecular hard to degrade organic materials are converted into small molecules and thereby is removed"}]</data>
</edge>
