  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular in addition to the heavy rainfall due to the rainy season and typhoons the recent changes in global weather patterns caused by el nino and la nia have caused local and local concentration rainfall frequently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the non point pollutant removal device 10 is for removing contaminants such as fallen leaves scattered on the ground in the early stage of rainfall and a nonpoint pollutant removal device having a known structure may be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100925049-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore an object of the present invention for solving the problems as described above is formed in the u trench trench length drain groove portion on the surface of the surface block used for paving the road at intervals of 3 10cm drainage distance is excellent water is accumulated in the drainage process or water flows on the road surface because the rainfall is drained to the lower part of the road at the same time through the drain grooves of individual blocks installed on the entire road without having to flow into long separate rain gutters or sides"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519076-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "the present invention is intended to provide a device for storing rainwater generated by intensive rainfall or the like on a sloping slope of a slope so that drainage can be facilitated effectively so that a floodwater suddenly blowing due to heavy rain or the like is provided as a separate drain pipe and provides a separate crushing structure to facilitate the drainage of the drainage which is entrained with soil floats and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the filter unit includes a first vertical plate extending a predetermined length from the lower surface of the deck directly below the lower end of the deck equipped with an assembly step is inserted into the assembly groove is inserted into the assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck it includes a first filtration plate which is replaceably mounted in the mounting hole formed in the lower end of the first vertical plate immersed in the rainwater of the storage space to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater a second vertical plate extending at a predetermined length from the lower surface of the deck to a lower portion of the deck by inserting an assembled jaw into the upper end of the lower surface of the deck and being inserted and assembled in an assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction a lower point of contact with the upper end of the overflow bulkhead provided at a lower level than the outer wall of the concrete bottom layer so as to be replaced with an opening formed in an opening formed therein to remove the nonpoint source of pollution contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow bulkhead including 2 filtration editions the first vertical plate and the second vertical plate is made of a plate body having an assembling jaw on the upper end to be inserted and assembled in the assembly groove recessed in the longitudinal direction on the lower surface of the deck the permeable concrete bottom layer comprises a deck walkway rainwater storage device for the filtering space characterized in that it comprises at least one overflow plate having a relatively lower height than the outer wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the second vertical plate extending a certain length directly below the lower surface of the deck and relative to the permeable concrete bottom layer of the reservoir portion than the outer wall and a second filtration plate installed to be replaceable in an opening formed in an opening formed at a lower end in contact with an upper end of the overflow partition which is provided at a low height to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow partition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "it was provided to prevent the collapse and to provide stable drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101303849-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "after being purified while passing through the purification treatment means built in the space is discharged to the inner space of the drain pipe through the drain hole of the drain pipe and then descends along the drain pipe is discharged to the outside through the discharge hole of the housing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4523875-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the porous reservoirs provide a system of open passages for ducting water to the footer drain line system and for providing regions where water may temporarily accumulate harmlessly in a situation of heavy rainfall or backup of the storm drain line which serves the building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338818-Y1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "first the rainwater drainage sump according to the present invention is installed rainwater drainage sump in a public facility the initial rainwater generated in the early stage is drained to the bottom drain formed in the main body of the wear or orifice type rainy rainfall by restraining the drainage caused by the increase a certain amount of rainwater is stored in public facilities and the remaining rainwater due to the increase of rainwater flows to the upper drain of the sump for reducing the drainage of rainwater to be drained thereby suppressing the drainage of the drainage well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in vegetation reservoirs for preventing pollution and creating a healthy urban environment a reservoir for storing rainfall runoff on the surface of the ground a vegetation filtration reservoir located at a lower portion of the reservoir and having a height of 25 to 60 cm including humus soil and sand at least one es filtration layer located below the vegetation filtration reservoir a collecting part located below the es filtration layer and having a storage part including a first gravel layer and a second gravel layer and a permeate part disposed in a lower part of the storage part and including a third gravel layer and a sand layer a pouring pipe disposed in the infiltration portion and being buried in the pouring portion to collect rainwater flowing out from the pouring portion an outlet pipe connected to the pipe a drain pipe provided in the vegetation filtration reservoir and a water pipe for collecting the water collected in the pipe pipe upward a bypass pipe connected to the drain port for bypassing the rainwater flowing out of the storage compartment of the storage compartment a second accommodating portion having a first accommodating portion having an inflow port into which the rainwater effluent flows an outlet provided with a screen for removing foreign matter in the rainwater inflow water flowing from the first accommodating portion and a vertical partition wall arranged so as to be communicated with each other an es expanded shale filter medium is disposed at a boundary between the vegetation filtration reservoir and the original soil and a bottom surface of the bottom of the water outlet is at least 30 cm away from the bottom of the bottom of the water outlet the vegetation filtration reservoir includes fly ash within 5 of the volume of the vegetation filtration reservoir wherein an aerobic condition layer is formed on the upper part of the basin of the drain hole and an anaerobic anaerobic condition layer is formed on the lower part of the basin of the drain hole to prevent pollution and to provide a healthy urban environment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "and a bypass pipe for bypassing and discharging rainfall runoff exceeding the storage capacity of the storage unit wherein the drain can be connected to the bypass pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in the non point pollution backwash automation system that treats non point pollutants generated by precipitation including a pre treatment tank and a screen tank formed with a partition wall therebetween the pre treatment tank is connected to a pipe at the bottom of the partition wall at a predetermined height inside and overflows an advection pipe for supplying the raw water accommodated therein to the screen tank a drain door provided at the bottom of the bulkhead to open and close only in the direction of the pretreatment tank from the screen tank to discharge all remaining water in the screen tank to the pretreatment tank it is provided on the floor and consists of a drain pump for pumping the residual water accommodated in the pre treatment tank and the screen tank has a perforated panel to filter out foreign substances while the raw water flowing into the lower part through the advection pipe moves upstream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "6d when rainwater flows into the first accommodation chamber 11a through the inlet pipe 13 in a state where the rainfall is greatly increased due to heavy rain or the like some rainwater may cause the protrusion 50 to fall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "therefore in the case of the first case of the rain preventing rain purification block 100 combined only as in the case of the former the catching portion 11 of the boundary preparatory initial rainfall purification block 100 is connected in fluid communication with each other the longitudinal direction of the catching portion 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101662794-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "when the flow rate of the rainwater in the trough 20 is increased due to a large amount of rainfall the rainwater passes through the drain hole 22 and a large contaminant such as a part of leaves that can be accumulated on the bus stop roof 10 is discharged directly to the drain port 22 without passing through the catch 21"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2598696-B1", "para_id": "para_279", "text": "for example in the event of a heavy rainfall where road water or water from the pavement may leak into the one or more open topped utility channels 20 the level of water can be eased by transferring the water from the one or more open topped utility channels 20 to the storm water drain 360 via the utility channel drainage pipe 380"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200391152-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the rainwater flowing down from the inclined surface does not pass through the filtering basket 6 but flows out through the bypass hole 44a of the support plate 44 to reach the drain hole 2a thereby ensuring a water free flow without disturbing the drainage of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "US-5069693-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the cooling of the air increases its density thus adding gravity boost to the air flow induced by the downstream air pump at the exhaust and filtering zone"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "6d when rainwater flows into the first accommodation chamber 11a through the inlet pipe 13 in a state where the rainfall is greatly increased due to heavy rain or the like some rainwater may cause the protrusion 50 to fall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187840-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it includes a rainwater management block that allows rainwater to be stored in rainwater storage blocks and a rainwater management block that opens a drain valve to allow rainwater to penetrate into the infiltration facility after a rainfall has passed and discharges stored rainwater depending on the situation to prevent flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102418387-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is common to block the bicycle paths trails and trails with a lid so as not to cause harm or discomfort to users using the trails"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "and a cap 198 connected to the hinge 190 of the fixed frame 125 provided at the end of the branch pipe 121.the present invention provides a stable drainage of rainwater by providing a stable removal of rainwater or flood caused by heavy rainfall as described above while checking the clogging caused by sedimentation that accumulates while moving in a drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the first method is to install water gates valves and movable wear to control the discharge amount at the outlet and open these facilities at normal times to drain the reservoir water and then close the water gate to settle down after a certain period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060765-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore when heavy rain pours within a short time the other manhole of the concrete pipeline 110 is opened to drain the rainwater to the river the composite storage tank is temporarily stored in the river through the open manhole after temporarily storing the rainwater by doing so the quantity of rainwater flowing into the river can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the rainy soil chamber of patent document 4 is a buoy that adjusts the degree of opening of the connecting pipe according to the increase in flow rate in the connection pipe connecting the rain soil chamber and the drain pipe so that it can collect as much as the design capacity regardless of the increase in flow rate due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "when the rainfall exceeding the amount of the storm receiver 20 as shown by the arrow in the drawing drainage exceeding the amount of the storm receiver 20 is the upper surface and the lid 60 of the first partition wall 50 it flows through the passage 81 formed between and passes through the maintenance tank 30 it is stored in the common storage area formed by communicating the lower portion of the maintenance tank 30 and the lower portion of the treatment tank 40 in turn sedimentary particulate matter with a high specific gravity is precipitated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "then after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20 it is re introduced into the maintenance tank 30 the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100930723-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the manhole structure in the present invention discharges the inflow water into the ground or drainage layers while collecting and storing the inflow water through the porous block of the infiltration tank and rainfall or a lot of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}]</data>
