  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100815578-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "3 pour secondary bottom concrete bc2 to the drainage channel 5 to the position and finally waterproof the inner surface of the drain trench 1 and then drain the drainage 5 apply mortar m while giving a gradient to the bottom and finally finish glazing 6 on the angle 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101260798-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the airtightness in the deodorization pipe is firmly maintained to prevent the inflow of outside air and thus to provide the automatic condensate drainage device of the end treatment plant odor prevention equipment to prevent the freezing of winter and improve the performance of the facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216269-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "now when an earthquake occurs by breaking away from the conventional manhole design and construction method it is desperately required to improve so as not to cause stress concentration torsion damage and grade defects in the inlet and drain hole joints.there is korean patent registration no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100758560-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the gradient precast trench structure block 100 located in the outer body of the block 100 when the block 100 is combined with another block 100 to form a trench structure the outside of the block 100 to prevent the inflow of dirt from the outside a stage 170 formed to secure the cover over the body a base portion 180 positioned at both lower ends of the outer body of the block 100 to increase the bondability with the cement placed on the floor where the block 100 is to be installed and fixed to install the block 100 a u shaped drainage portion 120 that performs a wastewater treatment so as not to leave residues and residual water at the bottom of the drainage path a drain pipe 160 for discharging wastewater flowing out of the drain 120 to a septic tank a drain pipe connection part 150 formed in an elliptic intaglio on one side of the bottom of the block 100 to discharge wastewater flowing out of the drain part 120 of the block 100 to the drain pipe 160 an embossed 191 formed on one side of the outer body of the block 100 to facilitate connection of the block 100 with another block 100 an intaglio 192 formed on an outer body of the block 100 on an opposite side of the embossment 191 and formed to facilitate connection between the block 100 and a counterpart block in combination with the embossment 191 it is coupled to the lower grooves on both sides of the connection portion of the block 100 100 through the attachment screw 210 and after the coupling of the block 100 and another block 100 in a trench structure to prevent shaking and bending a connection part 200 formed to easily install the trench structure wherein a connection part 200 supporting the block 100 when the trench structure is formed using the connection part 200 is formed on a bottom surface thereof the block 100 is modularized into 1m to 3m using the connection part 200 to connect two or more blocks 100 to form a trench structure and then embedded in cement installed at the installation location to shake the trench structure"}, {"pat_id": "US-6916427-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "pre treating helps to improve the primary reactor s 7 efficiency allowing for an increase of fluent flow through the system by initiating the reduction and flocculation of dissolved and suspended particles in the fluent stream prior to entering the primary reactor 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a u shaped buried aqueduct made of resin material which is installed to be buried between the edge of the road and the ground or in the ground of the central separator and flows rainwater on a road surface such as a road into a sewer or underground a locking flange formed integrally with an upper opening side edge of the u shaped buried water pipe and forming a locking jaw at an end thereof square side insertion holes formed on outer peripheral surfaces of the buried water pipe facing each other and opposed to each other rti gt a horizontal retaining rod coupled to the side insertion holes of the squares facing each other on the outer circumferential surface of the buried water pipe to prevent gradient deformation of the buried water pipe and a cover channel forming a drainage groove and a drainage groove to which a top surface of the buried aqueduct is formed while both ends are coupled to each other on the locking flange to prevent separation by the locking step and a drain grating is coupled to an upper surface thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "u shaped buried water pipe a locking flange formed integrally with an upper opening side edge of the u shaped buried water pipe and forming a locking jaw at an end thereof square side insertion holes formed on outer peripheral surfaces of the buried water pipe facing each other and opposed to each other it includes and the horizontal maintenance bar to prevent the gradient deformation of the buried waterway pipe while being coupled to prevent rotation in the lateral insertion hole of the square facing each other on the outer circumferential surface of the buried waterway pipe and a cover channel forming a drainage groove and a drainage groove to which a top surface of the buried aqueduct is formed while both ends are coupled to each other on the locking flange to prevent separation by the locking step and a drain grating is coupled to an upper surface thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101026854-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as the bottom plate construction method for the prefabricated water tank placing and curing concrete in a formwork constructed to a size that can support the water tank to form a first base chipping the first base surface and forming a joint in the same shape as the water tank arranging and assembling the base frame to the first base surface in accordance with the joint seating an angle bent to be in close contact with the inner surface of the base frame and the first base surface coupling a fixing bolt having a support member embedded in the concrete of the second base to each fastening hole of the angle and the base frame is supported so as not to be pushed by hydraulic pressure and fastening the fixing support by fastening the fixing nut to the fixing bolt making a step fixing the angle fixed by the fastening support with a set bolt to a first base seating a drain portion of the same block as a drain box and a pipe for guiding drainage of water on an upper surface of the first foundation inside the base frame placing and curing concrete so as to be gradient in the direction of the drain portion in the base frame on which the drain portion is seated to form a second foundation separating a block of the drain portion in the second foundation and installing a plurality of polyethylene sheets so that the ends overlap the upper surface of the second foundation fixing the drain box and the polyethylene sheet by heat fusion in a state in which the drain box of the drain portion is seated on the second base from which the block is separated and a plurality of fastener mounting steps mounted on a second base to prevent the flow of the polyethylene sheet by contraction so as to fix the polyethylene sheet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102331873-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "it is drained through a drain hole but since the green belt is installed between the road and the sidewalk it can become an obstacle in the drainage of rainwater on the side of the sidewalk when it rains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "lt rti gt as described above the present invention is configured to combine the support member for horizontal maintenance to the side channel channel made of a resin material thereby maintaining a constant gradient while preventing the left and right width deformation of the side channel channel made of resin material regardless of the external environment the flow of water can be made smoothly in particular it can be expected that the effect of making the drainage grating steady state.figure 1 is an exploded view showing the structure of the resin material side opening water pipe as an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102678778-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a body having a box shape with an installation space inside a mounting hole formed through the side and a cylindrical flange extending from the upper surface a manhole cover that is detachably coupled to the flange to open and close the installation space in communication with the inside of the flange and it includes a guide sleeve mounted on the mounting hole to guide the cable to the installation space an installation ring is formed on the upper and side surfaces of the body and a fixing groove is formed on the side of the body recessed to a certain depth along the circumferential direction of the side a drainage channel extends downward on the inner lower surface of the body and an inclined gradient is formed on the inner lower surface of the body toward the drainage channel a manhole installed at the lower part of the installation space and filtering foreign substances contained in the water flowing into the installation space and then intermittently discharging the purified water toward the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200333387-Y1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "in addition the outer side of the upper surface of the culvert box is formed as a single gradient it is possible to drain the contaminants dropped to the upper surface of the culvert box to the outside to prevent contamination of water flowing along the culvert box"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a cover seating end formed of a material and formed in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends of the trench body block in order to mount and fix the cover on the upper portion of the trench body block a drainag