support fixing bracket includes a lower support portion for supporting lower ends of both ends of the adjacently connected trench body block both side support portions formed in a shape bent at a predetermined height at both ends of the lower support portion in the upper direction to surround both end side portions of the trench body block and a drainage level control member for adjusting the drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by integrally extending from both ends of the lower supporter in an outward direction of the both side supporters wherein the drainage level control member includes the lower supporter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "an extension piece extending from a ball nut integrally formed with the extension piece and having a screw therein a ball screw coupled to the ball nut and rotated forward and backward to adjust a drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut polymer concrete precast drainage using industrial by products with enhanced drainage gradient and level adjustment including and a support member that supports forward and reverse rotation while preventing sinking of the ball screw under the ball screw"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "3 the polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products in which the drainage gradient and level of the present invention are easily adjusted and the pollutant purification function is enhanced a plurality of trench body blocks 100 connected to each other having a cross section and a predetermined length in the connection portion where the plurality of trench body blocks 100 are adjacently connected connection support fixing brackets 200 for fixing and coupling while supporting the lower ends of both ends of the trench body blocks 100 connected adjacently however the trench body block 100 is formed of a polymer concrete material and a cover formed in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends 110 in order to mount and fix the cover on the top of the trench body block 100 a seating end 120 and a drainage passage 130 formed in a longitudinal direction in the inner center of the trench body block and integrally formed in a u shaped cross sectional shape from the cover seating end 120 to drain rainwater or sewage an embossed portion 140 formed at one end of the trench body block 100 and configured to secure a connection connection with the other end of the trench body block 100 to be adjacently connected and a concave portion 150 formed at the other end of the trench body block 100 and configured to fix the connection in correspondence with the raised portion 140 of the trench body block 100 connected to each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the drainage level control member 230 includes an extension piece 231 extending from the lower support part 210 a ball nut 232 formed integrally with the extension piece 231 and having a screw therein a ball screw 233 coupled to the ball nut 232 and rotated forward and backward to adjust the drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut 232 it is configured to include a support member 234 supporting the forward and reverse rotation while preventing the sinking of the ball screw under the ball screw 233"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products with enhanced drainage gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function of the present invention constituted as described above facilitates drainage gradient and level adjustment during drainage trench construction this prevents water leakage at the connecting part between the connected drain trenches and has a very excellent effect of purifying pollutants that cause foul odors and decay rainwater or wastewater accumulated by the stagnant soil or residue inside the trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605553-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore in order to solve the above problems a trap structure is formed inside a conventional sewage receiving device and a ventilation cap having a vent hole a spherical lightweight check ball a funnel shaped gradient ring a trapping pipe and a semi circular container a trap structure in which the parts are assembled in sequence is assembled and it is normally assembled and installed at the inlet of the sewage collecting device to prevent backflow of odors and pests through the sewage accumulated on the check ball and trap part which normally block the gradient ring as the sewage flows through the purpose of the drain is to be easily made by the rise of the check ball and the discharge of air through the vent"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "as described above the street drain structure according to the present invention can guide drainage regardless of the road gradient by using blocks of the same shape"}, {"pat_id": "US-8617390-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "embodiments can also include a second pressure gradient system in fluid communication with the treatment tank where the second pressure gradient system acts on head space in the treatment tank to create a pressure gradient serving to transport head space gases towards the leaching field which may also be referred to as a drain field downstream of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106330-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 1 tilt detection sensor 40 is provided on the circumference of the main body 10 to detect the gradient change of the main body 10 leakage detection means 50 provided on the outer circumference of the body 10 to detect water leakage from the body 10 a sewage detection sensor 60 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to detect when sewage is supplied through the water supply pipe 14 a flow rate measurement means 70 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to measure the flow rate of sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 further comprising a washing means 80 for washing the flow rate measuring means 70 using the discharged water discharged to the drain pipe 15 the leak detection means 50 it is formed in a cylindrical shape extending in the front rear direction and having an opening 51a formed on one surface and the collecting case 51 provided so that the opening 51a is in close contact with the circumferential surface of the main body 10 it is provided inside the catchment case 51 and includes a leak detection sensor 52 for detecting the collected waste water inside the catchment case 51 the flow rate measurement means 70 a support bracket 71 provided inside the water supply pipe 14 an impeller 72 rotatably coupled to the support bracket 71 and rotated by sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 it is connected to the impeller 72 and includes a rotation sensor 73 for measuring the rotational speed of the impeller 72 the cleaning means 80 a water storage tank 81 connected to the drain pipe 15 through a connection pipe 81a to store a portion of the discharged water discharged through the drain pipe 15 an injection nozzle 82 provided to face the impeller 72 inside the water supply pipe 14 and connected to the water storage tank 81 through a supply pipe 82a it includes a water supply pump 83 provided in the middle of the supply pipe 82a the management server a receives the signals of the tilt detection sensor 40 the leak detection means 50 the sewage detection sensor 60 and the flow rate measurement means 70 the slope of the main body 10 is set it is changed to a reference value or more or the sewage detection means 50 detects the sewage or the sewage detection sensor 60 the sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 is sensed to the flow rate measuring means 70 when it is detected that the signal of the sewage measured by the dropping below a preset speed a warning signal or a message is transmitted to the portable terminal b if the rotation of the impeller 72 is not detected by the rotation detection sensor 73 in the state in which water passing through the drain pipe 15 is sensed by the sewage detection sensor 60 the water feed pump 83 is operated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106330-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to another feature of the present invention it is provided on the circumference of the main body 10 is provided with a tilt sensor 40 for detecting the gradient change of the main body 10 and is provided on the outer circumference of the main body 10 leakage detection means 50 for detecting leaks generated in the body 10 and a sewage detection sensor 60 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to detect when sewage is supplied through the water supply pipe 14 and the water supply pipe 14 is provided in the flow rate measuring means 70 for measuring the flow rate of sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 and the discharge water discharged to the drain pipe 15 to wash the flow rate measuring means 70 further comprising a washing means 80 the leak detecting means 50 is formed in a cylindrical shape extending in the front rear direction and an opening 51a is formed on one surface so that the opening 51a is attached to the circumferential surface of the main body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0758560 registration date september 7 2007 in the gradient precast trench structure block 100 when a trench structure is formed by combining the block 100 with another block 100 by being located on the outer body of the block 100 the outside of the block 100 is step 170 formed to fix the cover on the upper body base portions 180 located at the lower ends of both sides of the outer body of the block 100 in order to increase the bonding property with the cement placed on the floor where the block 100 is to be installed and fixed to install and fix the block 100 a u shaped drain unit 120 that performs erroneous drainage treatment so as not to leave residue and residual water at the bottom of the drainage channel a drain pipe 160 for discharging the wastewater flowing from the drain 120 to a septic tank a drain pipe connection unit 150 for discharging wastewater flowing from the drain unit 120 of the block 100 to the drain pipe 160 by being formed in an oval shaped intaglio on one side of the bottom of the block 100 a relief 191 formed on one side of the outer body of the block 100 to facilitate connection between the block 100 and another block 100 an intaglio 192 that is located on the outer body of the block 100 on the opposite side of the embossed 191 and is combined with the embossed 191 to facilitate connection of the block 100 and the counter block it is coupled to the lower grooves on both sides of the connection portion of the block 100 100 through the attachment screw 210 and prevents shaking and bending after combining the block 100 and another block 100 in a trench structure"}]</data>
