  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a guide water pipe body fitted into the above drain and having an open upper portion to receive the above rainwater a grating member that is fitted and fixed to the upper part of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain permeation guide holes formed on the side wall of the guide water pipe body connected to the above drain a shielding control panel positioned inside the guide water channel body to open or close the above pitching guide holes a lifting and transporting guide means provided in the above guide waterway body and for lifting and transporting the shielding control panel and in a road drainage device for preventing water retention on a road surface the device is composed of a filter net member that is fitted and fixed into the water permeation guide hole formed in the guide water channel body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101473166-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "when the contaminant flows into the conveyance pipe 51 through the discharge hole 12 and the inflow portion 514 the conveyance drive unit is operated to perform the operation of the impurity removing unit 5 having the above the conveyance shaft 53 rotates in one direction and the conveyance plate 52 surrounding the conveyance shaft 53 moves in the right direction of the waterway 1 as the conveyance shaft 53 rotates the contaminants introduced into the pipe 51 are pushed toward the lower discharge portion 512 and the compressed and separated water is discharged to the drain 513a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268810-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain 10 and a height adjustment ring 20 coupled to the drain 10 and including an eccentric hole 21 whose central side is eccentric to one side compared to the central side of the height adjustment ring 20 a water pipe 30 seated on the drain 10 by being coupled to the height adjustment ring 20 protective frames 40 50 for protecting the waterway tube 30 from external force applied from the upper direction of the waterway tube 30 seated on the drainage passage 10 the drain 10 is it includes a u shaped inner space 10a as a predetermined block shape in the inner space 10a the coupling portion 11 to which the height adjustment ring 20 is coupled is configured to protrude along the inner wall of the curved region and the coupling groove 12 is formed in the coupling portion 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101415953-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "technical solution in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a frame structure comprising a frame having a lower end immersed in a water passage through which water flows and an upper end extending outwardly from a waterway a screen which is provided on a chain belt which is spanned by sprocket wheels of the spindle drums and the driven drums and moves according to rotation of the spindle drums and the driven drums and a drain pipe formed at the lower end of the frame for discharging the water blocked by the shielding portion to the side of the driven drum wherein the water flow is not affected by the damper"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102200910-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a drain pipe including a drain pipe upper plate a drain pipe lower plate disposed below the drain pipe upper plate and a holder mounted on an opening provided on the drain pipe upper plate by checking the flow of drainage in real time or periodically through the opening and closing of the top surface it is possible to determine whether the drainage pipe is clogged and whether the drainage pipe is repaired or not and find a countermeasure for the construction of the drainage pipe and repair of the defect and compare the situation and emergency measures in advance a drainage inspection port for checking the flowing state of the drainage passing through the designated location among the drainage pipes while watching and and a collecting well for collecting drainage flowing through the drain pipe and discharging the large capacity drainage collected by the collecting water to a downstream waterway and the drain pipe top plate includes a water vein pipe connected to the opening to prevent the soil material or contaminants separated from the pavement material existing on the road or ground from entering the drain pipe and a permeate guide pipe that supports left and right sides of the lower side of the water vein pipe it is manufactured as a facility having an inverted y shape and the lower plate of the drain pipe using one material selected from concrete metal nonferrous metal synthetic resin and plastic it is manufactured in a shape of a shape and a u shape and has a plurality of third drainage holes perforated on both left and right sides or bottom and a water permeable pad is attached to the left and right sides or bottom and is connected to the top of the drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102200910-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "a drainage inspection port for checking the flowing state of the drainage passing through the designated location among the drainage pipes while watching and a water collecting well collecting drainage flowing through the drain pipe and discharging the large capacity drainage collected by the collecting water to a downstream waterway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102559283-B1", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "the method of claim 16 wherein the step s350 sensing the sludge level through a sludge level sensor s351 the limit switch box for sludge drain is connected to various contacts of the solenoid valve for sludge drain and drives and controls the solenoid valve for sludge drain according to the control signal of the smart control unit s352 the solenoid valve for sludge drain is driven according to the signal of the limit switch box for sludge drain to supply or block air transmitted to the actuator for sludge drain s353 the actuator unit for sludge drain is driven by the solenoid valve for sludge drain and the main valve for sludge drain is directly driven to turn on and off the flow of the waterway on the waterway s354 the main valve for sludge drain is driven according to the drive of the actuator unit for sludge drain and the flow of the waterway is turned on and off s355"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449313-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically it prevents freezing and perforation due to freezing in winter when there is little agricultural water flow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for purifying contaminated river water by providing a support structure on both sides of a river to form a water channel therebetween and installing a water gate between the both side support structures to open and close the water channel and a plurality of support rods supporting the watershed are slidably slidable with respect to the watershed respectively in the middle of the drainage side of the watershed and between the support rods and the bottom of the waterway and a lifting cylinder capable of lifting and lowering the water gate is provided in the support base and a guide hole is formed in the longitudinal direction of the support base on a surface of the support base opposed to the water gate and between the rod and the drain side of the water inlet a fixing rod and the lifting cylinder is lifted upwardly in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder in the closed state of the watercourse so that the weight of the watercount which is stored in the watercounting space is clean the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 further comprising the steps of discharging the lower layer water first to purify contaminated river water thereby inducing a substance separation action caused by the action of gravity while purifying the contaminated river water with clean river water the shape of the hydrograph plate 80 is continuously bent in the shape of w in the transverse direction and bonded to the fixed bar 32 the vertical supports 90 and 91 which are continuously arranged in the form of a triangle vertically laid out on the lower surface and the upper surface of the water gate plate 80 to prevent warpage of the water gate plate 80 from 30 cm to 1 m together with zooming at intervals of and an index member not shown is coupled to the horizontal and vertical directions of the water gate plate 80 the water leveling plate 80 and the vertical supports 90 and 91 are combined to form a hybrid type opening closing member of a double layer structure having a flat plate shape the cylinder head according to any one of claims 1 to 5 wherein the cylinder head 51 of the lifting cylinder 50 is driven in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder 50 the water level plate 80 is lowered in accordance with the operation to shut off the discharge of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a method for purifying contaminated river water by providing a support structure on both sides of a river to form a water channel therebetween and installing a water gate between the both side support structures to open and close the water channel and a plurality of support rods supporting the watershed are slidably slidable with respect to the watershed respectively in the middle of the drainage side of the watershed and between the support rods and the bottom of the waterway and a lifting cylinder capable of lifting and lowering the water gate is provided in the support base and a guide hole is formed in the longitudinal direction of the support base on a surface of the support base opposed to the water gate and between the rod and the drain side of the water inlet a fixing rod and the lifting cylinder is lifted upwardly in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder in the closed state of the watercourse so that the weight of the watercount which is stored in the watercounting space is clean the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 further comprising the steps of discharging the lower layer water first to purify contaminated river water thereby inducing a substance separation action caused by the action of gravity while purifying the contaminated river water with clean river water the shape of the hydrograph plate 800 is continuously bent in the shape of a semicircle in the transverse direction and is coupled to the fixed bar 32 the vertical supports 900 and 901 which are continuously arranged in a semicircular plate are vertically arranged on the lower surface and the upper surface of the hydrograph plate 800 to prevent the hydrograph plate 800 from being bent combined with zooming and an index member not shown is coupled to the horizontal and vertical directions of the hydrograph plate 800 the hydrograph plate 800 and the vertical supports 900 and 901 are combined to form a hybrid type opening closing member of a double layer structure having a flat plate shape the cylinder head according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the cylinder head 51 of the lifting cylinder 40 is driven in accordance with the driving of the lifting cylinder 40 the water level plate 800 is lowered in accordance with the operation to shut off the discharge of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102601272-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "it forms a side screening wall 101 and a drain 102a that discharges the filtered water filtered through the screen structure 200 and on the inner surface a gasket covers both ends of the screen structure 200 to prevent the inflow of impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101134495-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "on the other hand the method of separating the seawater into caustic soda and fresh water using the green energy according to another aspect of the present invention for achieving the above object a to produce power by itself through the solar power generation unit 1510 supplying power to the power supply unit 140 and supplying electricity through the electrode 130 s210 b temporarily storing the purified seawater in the storage tank 110 and first electrolyzing the electrode 130 through the electrode 130 s220 c performing second electrolysis through the electrode 130 in the waterway 120 while flowing the first electrolyzed seawater from the reservoir 110 s230 d injecting the caustic soda containing water electrolyzed through the step c into the inlet through the jet port 1601 and simultaneously heating the same through the evaporation chamber 1610 to generate steam s240 e receiving steam heated in the evaporation chamber 1610 through a moving duct 1615 to generate a steam turbine generator 1620 s250 and f collecting the concentrated caustic soda heated through the evaporation chamber 1610 through the drain 1160 in step d and generating the steam turbine generator 1620 in step e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100555055-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the discharged water passing through the fiber filtration filter coated with the photocatalyst is sterilized while passing through the ultraviolet treatment device c provided in the pipeline or waterway type"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100732805-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the plate like door 27 is installed to open and close the waterway while being coupled by the door lifting member 27 penetrating through the upper center of the upper portion of the door 27 and spaced apart from the front and rear of the door 27 to face each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-940000292-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "in addition after the water supply is made when the faucet 25 is locked water still remains in the faucet tube 24 and at this time by locking the adjustment knob 17 forward the valve support pipe 14 is also moved to the front at the same time the on off valve disc 16 coupled to the front end to block the inlet hole 3a between the inner plate 3 no water supply in the faucet tube 24 water remaining in the faucet pipe 24 in the space portion 9a through the space generated between the front end wall of the packing support ring 9 and the on off valve disc 16 while the on off valve disc 16 is moved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the anti icing system installed inside the sidewalk canal of an underpass a body part which is installed on the floor according to the width of the side channel water pipe and includes a lower frame to which the electric heating wire can be mounted and a column or plate to which a sensor can be attached to either side or one wall side of the water channel pipe can be erected a temperature sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the water pipe to measure the surrounding temperature to derive a temperature measurement value a humidity sensor attached to a pillar or plate positioned on one or both walls of the main body or connected to the main body and installed at separate locations on one or both walls of the waterway pipe to measure the surrounding humidity to derive a humidity measurement value a flow measurement device attached to the inner wall of the drain pipe located at the lower end of the side channel waterway and measuring the amount of water flowing from the side channel channel through the drain pipe to the collection well to derive a flow rate a heating wire mounted inside the lower frame of the main body to prevent freezing of the side channel and a control unit controlling driving of the heating wire using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor anti icing system comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as such road culverts installed on underground passageways or local roads with side gut water pipes solve these problems because minimal vehicle passage in the underpass may be impossible and traffic safety problems may occur due to the accumulation of ice in the side hole waterway due to freezing of the drain pipe during the cold winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102058301-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "round water pipe circular drain ditch the present invention relates to a circular waterway pipe installed along the roadside and the waterway side to drain the rainwater smoothly more specifically the pipe made of synthetic resin material is installed in close contact with the inner channel of the circular waterway tube made of concrete material it relates to a circular waterway pipe that allows rainwater to flow through a pipe made of synthetic resin material without directly contacting the inner surface of the inner waterway thereby reducing corrosion of the circular waterway pipe and suppressing the occurrence of odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "it is to be made easily through and in particular to make the drainage grating solid state while providing a reinforcement of the assembled circular waterway tube of resin material and its construction method to strengthen the connection with the peripheral finish such as the sidewalk block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "u shaped buried water pipe a locking flange formed integrally with an upper opening side edge of the u shaped buried water pipe and forming a locking jaw at an end thereof square side insertion holes formed on outer peripheral surfaces of the buried water pipe facing each other and opposed to each other it includes and the horizontal maintenance bar to prevent the gradient deformation of the buried waterway pipe while being coupled to prevent rotation in the lateral insertion hole of the square facing each other on the outer circumferential surface of the buried waterway pipe and a cover channel forming a drainage groove and a drainage groove to which a top surface of the buried aqueduct is formed while both ends are coupled to each other on the locking flange to prevent separation by the locking step and a drain grating is coupled to an upper surface thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "while supporting the marble structure 50 the drainage grating 200 or the marble structure 50 can always maintain the same height as the sidewalk block 300 which is a peripheral finish for a long time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to block the water contaminants flowing into the drain pump station 4 along the water channel 3 from the distribution tent 1 from the screen member and to remove the obstructed substances from the screen member by the rake mechanism and an upper fixed frame portion 10a disposed at a lower end of the upper fixed frame portion 10a so as to be pivotable about a connecting shaft 11 and having a maximum rising position for opening the water channel 3 a lower movable frame portion 10b having a lower end connected to the auxiliary screen member 40 and a lower movable frame portion 10b connected to the connecting shaft 11 and a rake mechanism driving means for driving a rake mechanism for removing the contaminants caught in the screen member one of the rake mechanism driving means is supported by a drive sprocket 16a provided in the upper fixed frame portion 10a and the lower end is supported by a lower guide roller 16b provided at a lower end of the lower movable frame portion 10b and a roller chain drive motor 17 for driving the drive sprocket 16a wherein the endless roller chain 14 the drainage pump station 4 and the outer main stream 7 are communicated with each other through a water passage outlet 9 and the water passage outlet 9 is selectively connected to the water pump 6 by a winch motor 5a and the drain pump 4 is provided with a drain pump 4 that ascends and descends by the winch motor 5a an internal water level measuring sensor 31 and an external water level measuring sensor 32 for measuring the internal water level l and the external water level h which are the water level of the main stream and the main stream 7 respectively the controller 30 receives the internal level l provided by the internal level measuring sensor 31 and the external level l provided by the external level measuring sensor 32 and outputs the internal level l and the external level h further comprising a turning operation mechanism for turning the lower movable frame part 10b in accordance with the change and a control part 30 for providing an operation control signal to the water gate opening and closing and drainage pump lifting winch motor 5a the control unit 30 when the water level l measured by the water level measuring sensor 31 is lower than the water level h measured by the water level measuring sensor 32 the water level gate 6 closes the waterway outlet 9 the winch motor 5a is controlled so that the drain pump 5 descends into the drain pump station 4 and the control signal for controlling the winch motor 5a is transmitted to the winding roller drive motor 26 so that the lower movable frame portion 10b is lowered to the maximum lowering position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the soil removed by the soil damper 100 is picked up through the obstacle receiver 8 and the impurity conveying conveyor not shown and then transported to the outside.1 tributary cloth 2 waterway entrance 3 waterway 4 drainage pumping station 5 drain pump 5a winch motor 6 hydrograph 7 main stream 8 container receiver 9 waterway exit 10a upper fixed frame part 10b lower movable frame part 11 connecting shaft 13 roller guide rail 13a upper guide rail 13b lower guide rail 14 roller chain 15 blocking plate 16a drive sprocket 16b lower guide roller 17 roller chain drive motor 21 pulling wire take up roller 22 pull wire 23 drive sprocket 24 take up roller 25 chain 26 winding roller drive motor 27 28 support block 29 limit switch 30 control unit 31 internal level sensor 40 auxiliary screen member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101070989-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "the treated water of the four waterway regions 170 is transferred to the treated water outflow inducing unit 190 via the wear 180 and the treated water is disposed at one side of the chamber 110 in the treated water outflow inducing unit 190"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "resin sided waterway pipe to prevent deformation in width direction and construction method water conduit the present invention relates to a side channel water pipe water collecting well of the resin material e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "1 to 6 the resin material side waterway pipe to prevent the deformation in the width direction according to an embodiment of the present invention is installed between the edge of the road and the sidewalk or the lower outer side of the central separator to drain rainwater flowing on the road surface such as road the horizontal holding rod 30 is coupled to the side opening channel 10 of the resin material of the upper opening type to be introduced into the base and the vertical supporting rod 40 is coupled to the horizontal holding rod 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water supply pipe 32a exposed at the upper end a solenoid valve sv1 coupled to the water supply pipe 32a to control water and a solenoid valve sv1 interposed therebetween on both sides to supply water to the water supply pipe 32a it is configured to include a bypass pipe 33 for bypassing and a freeze prevention means 34 coupled to the bypass pipe 33 to bypass the water in the water supply pipe 32a in a small amount to prevent freezing in winter a three way solenoid valve sv2 is further coupled to the water supply pipe 32a which selectively controls the bypassed water and supplies it to the inner space 31a of the water spray stand 31 or the stone water tank 2 artificial waterway with water supply for freeze protection"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102448193-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "according to the characteristics for achieving the object as described above the first invention relates to an artificial waterway having a water supply unit for preventing freezing for this purpose a stone waterway a water supply unit installed in the inner center of the stone water tank to supply water and a plurality of landscaping stones radially arranged to have different sizes and height differences around the stone water tank the bottom surface is inclined toward the stone waterway and the water supply unit includes a water jet having an internal space communicating with a drain pipe buried underground a water supply pipe exposed to the top of the water jet across the internal space from the ground and the water supply pipe a solenoid valve coupled to the to regulate water a bypass pipe with both sides extending to the water supply pipe with the solenoid valve interposed therebetween to bypass the water and a small amount of water in the water supply pipe to bypass the circulation in winter to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S592439-Y2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a bypass waterway is provided with the other end connected to a waterway downstream of the check valve and the equipment water stop valve is closed to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101509202-B1", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "the present invention may however be embodied in many different forms and should not be construed as limited to the embodiments set forth herein rather it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed embodiments but on the contrary .2 modification of a waterway type house 10 collecting container 10a collecting space 11 top surface 12 connection pipe 20 cover 22 surface water inflow hole 24 infiltration inflow hole 30 guard plate 32 anchor 40 grating 50 inlet ball cover 50a drain board 50b 50c grill type cover 62 foundation concrete 64 110 112 wire mesh 120 concrete support layer 130 sand layer 140 packing block 200 excellent main building 210 excellent connector 220 excellent manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the upper one side of the circular or rectangular tube has a shape that is open in the longitudinal direction to provide a space for preventing the crossing over the boundary block the drain is formed on the lower side and both ends are connected to other water pipes a concave convex portion is formed in the open end surface wherein a binding groove is formed in a longitudinal direction and the open upper side is installed so that the other side is directed toward the roadway side and an upper portion of the waterway tube installed at the same height as the ground surface of the sidewalk it is a plate having a shape of a memory device with a round cross section so as to cover the open portion in the longitudinal direction of the water pipe a binding piece is inserted into the binding groove at both ends in the longitudinal direction but the binding piece is bent in two stages in the longitudinal direction so that a step with the outer surface of the water channel does not occur and the binding groove is formed at the end of the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention is a boundary block system capable of drainage the upper one side of the tube has a shape that is open in the longitudinal direction the lower side is formed with a drain hole the binding groove is open at both open ends a waterway tube formed in a direction and a plate member having a shape of a cross section so as to cover a portion open in the longitudinal direction of the waterway tube and both ends are formed with a binding piece to be inserted into the binding groove the upper side is formed inside one lower end the curbstone plate is hinged coupled to the opening and closing is formed so as to open only to the inside and a fume pipe that is buried in the bottom of the water pipe to provide a rainwater flow path flowing through the water outlet of the water pipe and the water drain pipe and the it characterized in that it comprises a connecting pipe for connecting the fume pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "the pipe 40 may be installed.therefore the present invention allows the cross section to act as a boundary stone by combining the curbstone plate and the waterway pipe of the memory shape and by installing a connecting pipe and a fume pipe at the bottom to facilitate the drainage to effectively drain the rainwater accumulated on the road side in rainy weather it can be prevent the backflow and can block the odor generated in the drainage can absorb the impact force to promote the safety of the occupants and easy to restore the original due to the damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "consisting of the grating the grating serves to prevent the foreign matter mixed in the rain water is introduced into the drain hole so that the drain pipe is not blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181401-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "by the center of gravity 140 to move toward the hinge shaft 125 125a of the opening and closing cover 121 121a by rotating upward to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the crate 10 in the dry stream when the rainwater does not flow in the waterways while stably catching foreign substances mixed in the rainwater opening and closing cover 121 121a by the weight 140 to block the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10 to prevent foreign substances such as cigarette butts or vinyl to enter the drain 1 in addition the uneven protrusions 112 and 113 of the body 110 and the uneven protrusions 124 and 124a of the opening and closing cover 121 and 121a are inserted into the rainwater inlet 11 of the grating 10"}]</data>
