  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10422139-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "thus certain exemplary embodiments can provide purposeful rapid dehydration of the system and or at least some of its assemblies in order to ready itself for the next storm event"}, {"pat_id": "US-10422139-B1", "para_id": "para_105", "text": "thus certain exemplary embodiments can provide purposeful rapid dehydration of the system and or at least some of its assemblies in order to ready itself for the next storm event"}, {"pat_id": "US-8602687-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "most existing pumping stations in low elevation areas especially in costal lands rely on storm water being collected and transported via canals and or waterways at or below sea levels and ground elevations with many such canals lined with elevated levees and or floodwalls extending above ground level elevations"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-9624658-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "7 shows a side view of a storm water drain filter secured to a wall of a pit via a cantilever bracket"}, {"pat_id": "US-9624658-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "17 the u shaped hoops 45 may include slots 46 to receive the bag side attachment elements 9 so as to prevent them catching on the side of the pit during removal of the filter bag and frame during maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "US-9624658-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "once a filter system is installed by one of the above methods rubber seal and or mastic and foam tape such as boa tape may be applied attached between the top of the storm water drain filter and the pit opening to provide seal between the storm water drain filter system 1 and the pit 17"}, {"pat_id": "US-5958226-A", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "however gravel leaves and other debris accumulate on top of the cartridges and block water flow so that a worker must reach in and dig them out by hand which is slow and time consuming"}, {"pat_id": "US-5322629-A", "para_id": "para_185", "text": "the reduction in flow with time is believed to be due to the swelling of organics and inorganic oxides in the compost as they combine with water molecules"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200479774-Y1", "para_id": "para_87", "text": "as a result as the removed relatively pure storm can be stored the deterioration of the water quality due to the decay of the impurities contained in the stormwater can be minimized in the storage of the storm water"}, {"pat_id": "US-6093314-A", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "instead the runoff pools at the entrance to the drain inlet and beyond creating a potentially hazardous situation for motorists pedestrians and others"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1951964-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is a well known fact that when storm water and waste water are pumped there are greater or lesser problems of sedimentation of sand and sludge blocking of pumps because of elongated objects and accretion of grease in pumping stations for water and waste water drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102684805-B1", "para_id": "para_125", "text": "100 solids separation unit 110 solids separation chamber 120 rainwater supply department 130 first rainwater supply pipe 140 solids discharge unit 150 second storm water supply pipe 200 storm water supply tank 204 floating material receiving part 206 floating material discharge part 208 rainwater runoff member 210 floating matter suppression panel 212 floating matter inflow space 214 floating matter suppression space part 220 floating material discharge device 222 discharge support housing 222a operation guide groove 224 discharge driving means 226 discharge scraper 228 discharge brush 230 discharge switch device 232 first open and close driving member 234 driving rod 236 opening and closing rail member 238 opening closing panel 240 sealed frame 250 floating matter inflow guide 260 floating matter discharge space part 300 flocculation tank 302 front flocculation tank 304 rear flocculation tank 306 stormwater storage unit 308 condensation unit 310 rainwater supply member 312 first rainwater passing panel 314 fixed panel 316 rainwater inlet hole 320 split frame 322 storm water passage section 330 second rainwater passing panel 340 panel cleaning member 342 lifting guide 344 cleaning brush 346 cleaning driving member 350 stirring member 352 stirring driving means 360 drug input unit 362 chemical discharge pipe 370 first supply pump 380 force feed pump 500 filtration tank 502 sedimentation space 504 treated water inlet 510 separation panel 520 removal panel 530 treated water passage panel 540 first filtration member 550 second filtration member 560 second supply pump 570 water level detection sensor 600 sump 602 treated water storage space 604 treated water collection unit 606 drain hole 610 treated water drain pipe 612 drain valve 620 sump opening and closing device 622 drain opening and closing body 624 enclosed main body 626 elevating rail 628 sealing protrusion 630 second opening and closing driving member 640 sealing flange 642 rail guide groove 644 protrusion insertion groove 650 third filtration member 700 drive control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2598696-B1", "para_id": "para_279", "text": "for example in the event of a heavy rainfall where road water or water from the pavement may leak into the one or more open topped utility channels 20 the level of water can be eased by transferring the water from the one or more open topped utility channels 20 to the storm water drain 360 via the utility channel drainage pipe 380"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101822469-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a tubular housing 200 inserted into a drain port 100 for drainage of storm water and having openings at both ends thereof an upper cap 300 having an inlet port 310 through which the rainwater flows into the space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 is formed a continuous inflow inlet 410 is formed between the upper cap 300 and the housing 200 to connect the space between the inflow port 100 and the housing 200 with the inner space of the housing 200 a lower cap 400 and and a first initial storm inflow port 210 formed in the housing 200 and connecting a space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 to an internal space of the housing 200 an inner tube 500 inserted into the housing 200 and formed in a tubular shape having openings at both ends thereof one end connected to the lower cap 400 and the other end protruding outside the housing 200 further comprising the first initial stormwater inlet 210 connects a space between the drain port 100 and the housing 200 and a space between the housing 200 and the internal pipe 500 the inner cap 500 may be formed in the inner cap 500 so as to prevent the outer cap 500 from flowing back to the space between the housing 200 and the inner cap 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "the sewage odor blocking device 140 includes a body 141 forming a storm water receiving space 142 while maintaining a predetermined position below the manhole cover 120 and inclined from the lower side of the body 141"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "is protruded is provided so as to be spaced apart from the bottom of the road side catch port 10 the horizontal catch plate 94 is adjusted to the height according to the water level flowing through the road side catch port 10 by the buoyancy body 92 and the coarse coarse collusion through lower rainwater downflow horizontal collecting plate 94 it is characterized in that it is provided to be filtered through the water filtration network 96 .according to the above configuration and operation the present invention is to embed the storage tank in the bottom of the flower bed formed between the road and the sidewalk to quickly absorb and collect rainwater flowing along the road during rainy weather and to supply the rainwater stored in the storage tank to the lower flower bed it helps to drown landscaping water and in particular contaminants contained in rainwater can be easily filtered and recycled into water resources including road cooling water road washing water and digestive water to contribute to water shortage.1 is a block diagram showing the stormwater storage system as a whole for vegetation infiltration according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "US-6334953-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the flaps enable excess water from the runoff water flow to drain from the filter bag as the filter bag becomes filled with silt and other debris to prevent a back up or blockage of runoff water within the discharge pipe of the storm water discharge system"}, {"pat_id": "US-11186980-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "according to one exemplary embodiment there is provided a method of removing sediment from fluid flow within a storm water drain pit comprising deflecting flow entering the pit towards the side walls of the pit by one or more deflectors so as to reduce the energy of the fluid flow and promote settling of sediment within the catch pit"}]</data>
</edge>
