  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-8602687-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "most existing pumping stations in low elevation areas especially in costal lands rely on storm water being collected and transported via canals and or waterways at or below sea levels and ground elevations with many such canals lined with elevated levees and or floodwalls extending above ground level elevations"}, {"pat_id": "US-4096877-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "addition of reduced pressure backflow preventers to prevent contamination of the supply main further complicates such systems and adds substantially to installation costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an upstream side main water supply pipe 101 connected to a water supply source and provided with a water supply pump 130 a downstream side main water supply pipe 102 connected to the upstream side main water supply pipe 101 through a main on off valve 110 a sprinkler bridge 200 branched from the downstream main supply pipe 102 and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and a sprinkler head 300 installed at a lower end of the sprinkler double pipe 200 first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the main opening closing valve 110 respectively further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flow meters 510 520 respectively installed at an inlet end and an outlet end of the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 a drain pipe 600 connected to the sprinkler bridge pipe 200 through the three way valve 610 and provided with a drain pipe meter 620 between the second sprinkler bridge pipe flow meter 520 and the sprinkler head 300 lt rti the main on off valve 110 includes a valve body 111 connected to the upstream main supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 a valve cap 112 covering the upper portion of the valve body 111 a valve seat 116 formed in the valve body 111 an opening closing plate 117 installed in the valve body 111 to open and close the valve seat 116 a lifting and lowering rod 118 coupled to an upper end of the nut 117 and a nut box 119 screwed to the lifting and lowering rod 118 and an opening and closing drive means 120 for rotating the nut box 119 including the valve cap 112 includes an elevation guide portion 113 for vertically supporting the elevating and lowering rod 118 a rotation support portion 114 for rotatably supporting the nut box 119 and a reinforcing connecting portion 115 connecting the portion 113 and the rotation supporting portion 114 the opening and closing drive means 120 includes a drive motor 123 mounted on a motor mount 122 fixed to a support plate 121 integrally formed with the rotary support 114 and a driven gear 126 coupled to an upper end of the nut box 119 and engaged with the driving gear 125 the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 and the first and second sprinkler pipe flowmeters 410 and 420 are controlled by controlling the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 according to the detection signals of the water discharge pipes 510 and 520 and the discharge pipe flow meter 620 and a control means 700 the control means 700 includes a fire detector 710 installed on the building an input unit 720 for inputting the normal mode and the test mode a main opening closing valve sensor 730 for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve 110 the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and the 3 way valve 610 according to the fire detection signal of the fire detector 710 and the input signal of the input unit 720 the flow rate of the refrigerant is detected on the upstream side in accordance with the sensing signals of the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 the first and second sprinkler pipe flow meters 510 and 520 the drain pipe flow meter 620 it is possible to judge the abnormality of the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main water supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 to determine an abnormality position display command and an alarm command a control unit 740 for outputting a command to display the degree of opening of the main on off valve 110 a valve driver 750 for sending a driving signal to the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 and the three way valve 610 according to a control command of the controller 740 a display unit 760 for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the controller 740 and an alarm unit 770 for outputting an alarm according to an alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "sensing switch.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided an air conditioning system comprising an upstream main water supply pipe connected to a water supply source and having a water supply pump a downstream main water supply pipe connected to the upstream main water supply pipe through a main on a sprinkler multistage pipe branched from the downstream main supply pipe and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve first and second main water supply flowmeters respectively installed at the inflow end and the outflow end of the main opening closing valve and a sprinkler head installed at the lower end of the sprinkler multi branch pipe the sprinkler system according to claim 1 further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flowmeters installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the sprinkler opening closing valve respectively and connected to the sprinkler multi wherein the main on off valve includes a valve body connected to the upstream main supply pipe and the downstream main supply pipe a valve cap covering the upper portion of the valve body a lifting screw rod coupled to an upper end of the opening closing plate a nut box screwed to the lifting lowering rod and an opening closing drive means for rotating the nut box wherein the valve cap supports the lifting lowering rod so as to be movable up and down a rotation support portion for rotatably supporting the nut box and a reinforcing connection portion for connecting the elevation guide portion and the rotation support portion wherein the opening and closing drive means is fixed to the support plate integrally formed with the rotation support portion a drive gear fixed to a motor shaft of the drive motor and a driven gear coupled to an upper end of the nut box and engaged with the drive gear a sprinkler opening closing valve a three way valve and an upstream side main water supply pipe and a downstream side main water supply pipe in accordance with detection signals of the first and second main water supply flowmeters first and second sprinkler multi and a control means for judging the presence or absence of abnormality of the multi branch pipe and the drain pipe and outputting an alarm wherein the control means is installed in the building and smoke detectors an input unit for inputting a normal mode and a test mode a main opening closing valve sensor for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve a sparkler opening closing valve and a 3 way valve according to a fire detection signal of the fire detector and an input signal of an input unit and outputs control commands to the first and second main water supply flow meters the first and second it is possible to determine the abnormality of the upstream main supply pipe downstream main supply pipe sprinkler discharge pipe and drain pipe according to the detection signal of the sprinkler flow meter drain pipe flow meter and main opening closing valve detector a controller for outputting a command for displaying the degree of opening of the main opening closing valve according to a detection signal of the detector a valve driving unit for sending a driving signal to the main opening closing valve the sprinkler opening closing valve and the three way valve according to a control command of the control unit a display unit for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the control unit and an alarm unit for outputting an alarm in response to an alarm command of the control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102393706-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "there is a difficulty in performing the original function of the flotation jeon due to freezing and if the operation of the flotation jeon is not smooth in this way there is a problem in that the flotation jeon buried underground by excavating a standing pipe must be replaced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the flood diffusion prevention system of a building structure that is installed in a multi story building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to leakage from spreading to the elevating facility space a drainage passage formed on the floor of the common space for each floor in the building structure a drainage trench installed on the upper portion of the drainage passage to shield the drainage passage and a plurality of drainage holes for draining the inflowing water into the drainage passage a drain module connected to and configured to include a pipe for discharging the water to the outside a flood detection sensor installed in the drainage module to detect whether water has flowed in a water supply shutoff valve installed in a water supply line of the building structure to block water supply by a control signal and a flood signal received from the flood detection sensor a control unit for transmitting the control signal to the water supply shut off valve so as to be blocked and it is installed in front of the opening closing door of the elevator installed in the building structure and is raised to a preset height from the floor and includes a blocking module to prevent water from flowing into the elevator when submerged the blocking module is a blocking member installed in front of the opening closing door to open or shield the front lower part of the opening closing door according to the elevation an elevating wire having one end coupled to the upper portion of the blocking member to elevate the blocking member and the flooding prevention system of a building structure characterized in that it is connected to the other end of the elevating wire and configured to include a wire driving unit for elevating and lowering the elevating wire in conjunction with the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "US-9855518-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "a screen box sbx assembly in accordance with the present invention comprises an ultrafine screen a screen frame of flat plate and hollow tubing that incorporates air scouring at the lowest elevation of the screen the frame being sealed to prevent liquids and solids from bypassing the screen so all must pass through the screen a flexible discharge hose that may have swivel joints or may extend and compress in an accordion fashion to minimize forces on the screened decanter guiderails to define the vertical and horizontal movement of the invention a lifting device to raise and lower the invention in the liquid at controlled descent speed and multiple rise rates an effluent flow manifold with openings to allow liquid to flow to the screen from below the screen a deflector plate with drain ports an encoder to position the screen box in the tank to measure headloss and to insure the appropriate amount of screen is in contact with the wastewater a protective maintenance hood to backwash disinfect and thaw the screen controls sensors actuated valves modulating valve flow meter and in some cases a filtrate pump if required by the existing hydraulic gradient"}]</data>
</edge>
