  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101957444-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "seventh it is possible to purify the river lake pond fountain eighth it is possible to increase dissolved oxygen and reuse water treatment in cage farms and freshwater farms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101017356-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a metal plate material which is elastically bent and inserted into an inner circumference of the drain pipe a diameter adjusting means coupled to both ends of the metal sheet so that the metal sheet can be inserted into a drain pipe having various sizes by adjusting a diameter of a banded metal sheet a first shielding film coupled to an upper end of the metal plate so as to be in close contact with an exposed end surface of the drain pipe and partially closing an upper end of the drain pipe and odor reduction in the drain pipe to reduce the odor prevent the backflow of the river water second odor membrane hinged to the lower portion of the first screen so that the sewage is discharged by water pressure device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101017356-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at the same time the sewage flowing through the inside of the drain pipe is configured to be automatically discharged by water pressure and to prevent the backflow of river water during rainy weather while painting the pattern and text on the front of the screen to block the open drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101017356-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a first shielding film coupled to the first closing portion of the drain pipe and a second shielding membrane hinged to the lower portion of the first shielding membrane to reduce odors in the drain pipe to prevent backflow of river water and to discharge wastewater by water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101017356-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in addition since the second shielding film 50 is in close contact with the exposed end surface of the drain pipe 200 through the packing 70 it is possible to prevent the river water flowing back through the drain pipe 200 during rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark