  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the non point contaminant removing device 10 may be rainwater collected from a roof of a building in addition to the above mentioned sump well"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system where there is water leakage into the sewer line through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9157227-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in sanitary sewer system where there is a water leakage into the sewer system through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof down spout connections are made to the system which normally should carry only the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machines drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102812276-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "although the preferred embodiments of the present invention have been described in detail above the scope of the present invention is not limited thereto and various modifications and improvements made by those skilled in the art using the basic concept of the present invention defined in the following claims also fall within the scope of the present invention.g1 landfill layer g2 cover layer 1 leachate recovery section 11 leachate plate 111 leachate channel 12 blocking member 13 leachate drain 2 leachate purification unit 21 leachate inlet line 22 purification unit 211 purification body 211a 1st body 211b 1st purification space 211c 2nd body 211d 2nd purification space 222 ceramic filter 223 1st activated carbon layer 224 2nd activated carbon layer 225 zeolite layer 226 silica sand layer 227 compartment filter 23 purification storage 231 storage space 24 natural stone 25 heating section 3 landfill gas recovery section 31 gas pipe 311 through hole 32 flow pipe 33 landfill gas purification unit 34 storage tank 35 landfill gas pump 36 control valve 4 high temperature sterilization unit 41 steam generator 42 storage unit connection line 43 steam line 44 steam pump 5 uv sterilization section 51 substrate section 52 uv ray generation unit 6 dust suppression unit 61 spray line 62 drum 63 spraying unit 64 supply pipe 65 spray pump 7 wheel washing unit 71 tunnel section 711 car wash area 711a entrance 711b exit 72 lower wash section 73 side wash section 74 rear wash section 741 hinge block 742 shaft 743 drive motor 744 spray pipe 744a vertical pipe 744b horizontal pipe 75 front wash section 76 wash water supply storage unit 77 sterilization wash unit 78 dry car wash unit 79 car wash water recovery unit 8 pedestrian safety section 8a pedestrian safety passage 81 outer structure 811 entrance 82 frame section 821 pedestrian passage 83 roof 84 blocking 85 1st rail section 86 2nd rail section 87 frame drive unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102368680-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the fire water supply tank through the first rainwater inlet pipe and the second rainwater inlet pipe is purified while passing through the gravel layer the activated carbon layer and the sand layer in turn and the fire water collected in the sand layer is the house"}, {"pat_id": "US-4523875-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "moreover in the presence of a very significant downpour some of the debris may be transported from place to place in a drain line and may tend to collect at a common location causing a blockage of the entire system"}, {"pat_id": "US-5538043-A", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "similarly use of the invention may permit intermittently seasonally used or occupied appliances and dwellings to remain unheated during inclement weather where continuous heating may ordinarily is required to guard against line freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11465071-B2", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "more specifically the frame members 44 are attached to or integral with each other in a substantially open manner which results in most or preferably all of the sides of the frame 20 being open spaces that will not block or at least block as little as possible any movement and subsequent contact by the moisture laden air 14 against the condensation surfaces 28 30 the condensation panels 18 and the exiting of dried air 38 away from of the condensation panels 18 that comprise the apparatus 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101662794-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "when the flow rate of the rainwater in the trough 20 is increased due to a large amount of rainfall the rainwater passes through the drain hole 22 and a large contaminant such as a part of leaves that can be accumulated on the bus stop roof 10 is discharged directly to the drain port 22 without passing through the catch 21"}, {"pat_id": "US-4997312-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system leakage into the sewer line through manholes leakage into the sewer line through manholes where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system where there is water leakage into the sewer line through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "US-6009906-A", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "similarly use of the invention may permit intermittently seasonally used or occupied appliances and dwellings to remain unheated during inclement weather where continuous heating may ordinarily is required to guard against line freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1960608-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "via a feed line 4 a waste water is introduced into the container 2 and conveyed via a drain line 5 in the form of a pressure line via a backflow level 6 to drain from there into a sewer system 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "characterized in that in order to reduce the risk of freezing of the system special means 5 are mounted in at least some of the drains 1 or other inlets which are so located that the flow of air therethrough can be heavy said means 5 being arranged to reduce such heavy flow of air in both directions through the respective drain but not to prevent some ventilation of the system and designed to permit a small flow of water to pass directly therethrough without appreciable gathering of water in said means and to be automatically opened when required to permit a greater flow of water to pass"}, {"pat_id": "US-4486122-A", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "characterized by providing special means in at least some of the drains and other inlets which are so located that the flow of air therethrough can be heavy and designing said means to reduce such heavy flow of air in both directions through the respective drain but not to prevent some ventilation of the system and to permit a small flow of water to pass directly therethrough without appreciable gathering of water in said means and to be automatically opened when required to permit a greater flow of water to pass"}]</data>
