edia 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes for collecting only contaminants generated during the filtration process and sludge from the second storage tank which are formed in the filtration tank and a backwash water drain pump configured to discharge contaminants and sludges introduced into the inside of the backwash drainage storage tank and spraying compressed air to the contaminants adsorbed on the filter medium means a water washing unit that performs secondary backwashing while washing the filter unit using the effluent water when the air washing unit is completed and an air cleaning unit that performs driving of the air washing unit and the water washing unit a backwash control unit for controlling the backwashing when the inflow loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor for checking the amount of contaminants including sludge flowing into the main tank and the inflow amount of backwash water and sending the backwash water level sensor to the backwash control unit and a backwashing and discharging pump for discharging the effluent and allowing the backwashing of the effluent upon backwashing to be performed and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the effluent when the water level reaches a certain level and a water supply line connected to the water discharge line so as to perform backwashing of the filter medium means and a water supply line for supplying the water to the water washing unit side in a reverse flow direction"}, {"pat