 alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200404651-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to test the hydraulic pressure of the pipe install a pvc plug for the hydraulic pressure in the hole of the water pipe and perform the hydraulic pressure test.if there is any abnormality or leakage in the pipe unplug the plug drain the water repair it and then wrap the teflon seal to prevent leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "64 a disk valve 66 for opening and closing the water passage 61a of the valve housing 61 is selectively installed while moving up and down and is elastic between the disk valve 66 and the elastic member support frame 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200406578-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an independent manhole having an upper surface with a predetermined volume of space and embedded at the edge of the road to expose the upper surface a plurality of water outlet holes are formed in a circumferential surface thereof and the water pipes are buried in the basement layer made of earth and sand supporting the road while communicating with the space of the independent manhole a drain pipe communicating with the space of the independent manhole and the space of another adjacent manhole and a wall having a double sided tubular shape and fixed to a space between the space of the free standing manhole and the drain pipe a wall having an opening formed to block an open side of the guide and having a cutout formed in a predetermined width and rotatable with the fixed base"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200406578-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "a wall having a double sided tubular shape and fixed to a space between the space of the free standing manhole and the drain pipe a wall having an opening formed to block an open side of the guide and having a cutout formed in a predetermined width and rotatable with the fixed base"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101026854-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as the bottom plate construction method for the prefabricated water tank placing and curing concrete in a formwork constructed to a size that can support the water tank to form a first base chipping the first base surface and forming a joint in the same shape as the water tank arranging and assembling the base frame to the first base surface in accordance with the joint seating an angle bent to be in close contact with the inner surface of the base frame and the first base surface coupling a fixing bolt having a support member embedded in the concrete of the second base to each fastening hole of the angle and the base frame is supported so as not to be pushed by hydraulic pressure and fastening the fixing support by fastening the fixing nut to the fixing bolt making a step fixing the angle fixed by the fastening support with a set bolt to a first base seating a drain portion of the same block as a drain box and a pipe for guiding drainage of water on an upper surface of the first foundation inside the base frame placing and curing concrete so as to be gradient in the direction of the drain portion in the base frame on which the drain portion is seated to form a second foundation separating a block of the drain portion in the second foundation and installing a plurality of polyethylene sheets so that the ends overlap the upper surface of the second foundation fixing the drain box and the polyethylene sheet by heat fusion in a state in which the drain box of the drain portion is seated on the second base from which the block is separated and a plurality of fastener mounting steps mounted on a second base to prevent the flow of the polyethylene sheet by contraction so as to fix the polyethylene sheet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "meanwhile the dry fire extinguishing system according to the present invention can be designed to prevent corrosion due to water remaining inside the pipe after a hydraulic pressure test and water leakage due to valve leakage by installing a dry air facility or an air compressor equipped with a heater that supplies dry air and also to install a drain cock at the lowest part of a branch pipe and a cross pipe to discharge and dry water remaining in the pipe by dry air or compressed air thereby blocking corrosion due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102794119-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "according to one embodiment in order to prevent corrosion caused by the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe after discharging the mixed extinguishing water according to a hydraulic pressure test or fire detection the dry extinguishing system may install at least one drain cock not shown in each of the cross pipe 5 and the branch pipe 6 to discharge the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101759711-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "0563988summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above circumstances and an object of the present invention is to provide a shredding unit in which a plurality of blades are radially provided and new towing elements for replacement are connected successively the sewage pipe is crushed and the new sewer pipe is automatically replaced in succession while being moved using a wire driven as a pulling unit that intermittently pulls together with union and release the present invention provides a sewer pipe replacement device which can reduce the unit cost and replace the sewer pipe can shorten the construction period and reduce the cost.summary of the invention it is an object of the present invention to provide a replacement apparatus for a non drilling sewage pipe in which an old or damaged synthetic resin drain pipe buried in the ground for drainage of sewage or wastewater is replaced with a new one a crushing unit provided with a number of blades radially in a conical body and provided with new traction elements for replacement and a pair of upper and lower actuators arranged in parallel on the base and reciprocating forward and backward using hydraulic pressure a pulling unit having first and second gripping elements which are mounted on each of the fixed and movable stages and which are tied and released in a reciprocating manner depending on whether a frictional force acts or not wherein the first gripping element is adapted to move forward and backward in the reciprocating motion of the traction unit and the second gripping element is repeatedly held to maintain the position of the wire pulled back while the wire is retracted the wire is intermittently moved and the old sewing pipe is crushed by using the crushing unit so that replacement work can be performed easily"}, {"pat_id": "US-4946574-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "after the electrolysis is completed the electrolyzed water from said electrolytic cell 12 is divided into alkaline water 101 and acidic water 102 wherein said acidic water 102 is directly drained out since it cannot be used for drinking while said alkaline water flows into an ultraviolet sterilizing tank 15 to be sterilized therein before flowing out therefrom to be used for drinking purposes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "meanwhile the dry fire extinguishing system according to the present invention can be designed to prevent corrosion due to water remaining inside the pipe after a hydraulic pressure test and water leakage due to valve leakage by installing a dry air facility or an air compressor equipped with a heater that supplies dry air and also to install a drain cock at the lowest part of a branch pipe and a cross pipe to discharge and dry water remaining in the pipe by dry air or compressed air thereby blocking corrosion due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "at this time in order to reliably remove the remaining water in the pipe the dry fire extinguishing system can open the drain cock not shown and inject air dried by a drying facility not shown into the entire pipe 4 5 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822595-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "according to one embodiment in order to prevent corrosion caused by the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe after discharging the mixed extinguishing water according to a hydraulic pressure test or fire detection the dry extinguishing system may install at least one drain cock not shown in each of the cross pipe 5 and the branch pipe 6 to discharge the extinguishing water remaining inside the pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in configuring the odor prevention device 110 to prevent the odor coming up from the ground the odor prevention device 110 includes a prevention body 112 having a seating flange 111 upward to be seated on the bottom surface of the manhole cover 105 the prevention body 112 and the first vertical portion 113 protrudes downward from the mounting flange 111 an inclined portion 114 formed to have a width narrowed inward from an end of the first vertical portion 113 a second vertical portion 115 projecting downward from the end of the inclined portion 114 a plurality of water passages 116 formed to drain a small amount of rainwater to the inclined portion 114 a discharge hole 117 formed to be opened between the second vertical portions 115 to discharge a large amount of rain and garbage deformed by the hydraulic pressure of the sewage to the water hole 116 while being drained down and after completion of drainage to return to the original state to prevent the odor coming up through the water hole 116 fixing the blocking plate 118 of a material having elasticity and excellent return force the discharge hole 117 is a sewer manhole odor prevention device characterized in that it comprises a rotating plate 120 installed so as to block the odor coming up while draining the rain and waste of the opposite"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "70 is opened and the effluent is collected into the sump 100 while the current groundwater level is lower than the set ground level the effluent water due to the closing pressure of the water level control device 40 70 in the water level control device of the sump well configured to block the collection of water so that the current ground level is lower than the set ground level it is possible to reduce the number of continuous water block and pumping the water level control device 40 70 one end is connected to the collecting pipe 10 and the inlet pipes 22 52 84 provided with hydraulic pressure gauges 21 51 81 for checking the water pressure of the effluent and the inlet pipe 22 52 84 the drain pipe 23 53 85 and the main pipe 24 54 87 connected to the drain pipe 23 53 85 the inlet pipe 22 52 84 is provided with locking ends 25 52a 82 on the upper inner circumferential surface and a cover for preventing foreign matter from penetrating the upper ends of the main tubes 24 54 and 87 body parts 20 50 and 80 fastened to open and close 27 55 and 86 installed inside the body parts 20 50 80 the eluent water flowing into the inlet pipes 22 52 84 is opened and is drained to the drain pipes 23 53 85"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913996-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "the body portion 50 is connected to the water collecting pipe 10 the hydraulic pressure gauge 51 for checking the water pressure of the effluent is installed the inlet pipe 52 is formed with a locking end 52a at the end of the discharge water is discharged a drain pipe 53 having a slide hinge 53a formed inside the upper end and draining the effluent in the opposite direction of the inflow pipe 52 and a main pipe 54 connected to the drain pipe 53 the upper end of the main pipe 54 located between the drain pipe 53 and the inlet pipe 52 is configured to be fastened to open and close the cover 55 to prevent foreign substances from penetrating"}]</data>
