  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200318223-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a discharge mechanism having a plurality of ribs formed at regular intervals along the curved surface on a curved seating plate curved surface having a predetermined curvature and having a drain pipe through the top surface of the seating plate sewage fume pipe is mounted on the upper surface of the rib is spaced apart from the seating plate at a predetermined distance and provided with a plurality of fasteners that are bonded to the anchor an anchor bar having one or more catching portions the anchor bar having a plurality of discharge holes formed on a circumferential surface thereof and being inserted into a corrugated pipe filled with gel like concrete inwardly while being inserted into the ground a wire interconnecting the fixture and the anchor landfill erosion prevention structure of the sewer pipe for sewage due to leakage characterized in that consisting of"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200318936-Y1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "reference numeral 52 denotes a fastener to which the anchor 50 and the wire 60 are interconnected.according to the present invention as described above while the rainwater penetrated to the ground is blocked by the seating plate so as not to flow into the ground directly supporting the water pipe while the rainwater guided to both edges by the wings of the seating plate is since it is discharged from a long distance by a drain pipe of a predetermined length ground erosion and collapse by rainwater are minimized and it is tightly connected through anchors and wires having excellent fixing force so that the warpage and bending of the water pipe due to partial ground collapse are possible"}]</data>
