85 hydraulic crane 885a piston motor 886 tower crane 886a names of each part of the guy derrick structure 886b guy derrick 886c main 886d boom 886e boom foil 886f turnbuckle 886g sling 886h triangular derrick 886i main 886j boom 886k boom foil 886l rack 887 drag crane 887a structure of drag crane 887b hoist cable 887c dump cable 887d bucket 887e lower boom 887f retroflex cable 887g cable roller 887h boom cable 887i cable roller 887j boom hoist cable 887k cable drum 887l cable drum 887m parallel weight 888 crane with clamshell attachment 888a holding line 888b opening line 888c clamshell bucket 888d upper frame 888e lower frame 888f rack line 888g rope guide 888h boom tendon 888i bridle 888j boom hoist rope 888k front drum 888l rear drum 888m parallel weights 889 macadam roller 890 tandem roller 891 tamping roller 892 tire roller 893 tractor 894 trailer 895 ram 896 lead 897 coolant cooling 898 pile 899 helmet 900 fuel pump 901 cam 902 fuel tank 903 starting device 904 boom front pin 905 cad work 906 adapter 907 fish finder sonar 908 drilling machine for crude oil 909 manganese nodule 910 scoop net 911 suction collecting machine 912 seabed mineral mining robot 913 periscope 914 rubber balloon 915 wire rope chain 916 double structure pipeline automatic pneumatic valve transport device 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101738905-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the water collecting boundary block according to the present invention since the water stored in the space portion is continuously supplied to the ground through the drain hole it is possible to prevent the desertification of the city and the damage of the trees"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750392-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the inner bottom surface of the manhole is formed in an arc shape so as to smoothly rotate when the backflow prevention plate 30 is rotated by the pressure of the sewage and the backflow prevention plate 30 is rotated according to the water level of the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if at least one or more of the parameters constituting the water quality measured by the formed second sensor unit 50 does not match a preset criterion control not only to control the turbidity drain valve 300 but also to discharge the turbid water water pressure measured by the water pressure detection sensor 70 among the flow rate control valve 80 and the water pressure detection sensor 70 sequentially formed between the turbid water drain valve 300 and the consumer 90 is outside the preset water pressure range if not by controlling the flow rate control valve 80 to maintain the flow rate and flow rate to be maintained in a preset water pressure range the administrator mobile terminal accessible through the network 500 for the database 630 800 provides a real time monitoring and monitoring module 621 that provides a function to support decision making ict integrated monitoring for smart water city construction send and receive to receive the location and property information of natural and artificial objects existing on the surface and underground and ground spaces of the water management system 1 from the big data server 700 through the network 500 after controlling the unit 610 the received information is matched and generated based on gis information based on the water pipe of the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for smart water city construction and then through the network 500 by controlling the transmitter receiver 610 to transmit to the manager mobile terminal 800 the manager can directly control the water supply network block and facility information db as well as support various planning and decision making and industrial activities in connection with the manager s work"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "referring to figure 1 ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is the intake station 10 ground water 20 smart meter 30 the first sensor unit 40 the second sensor device unit 50 leak detection sensor 60 water pressure sensor 70 flow control valve 80 consumer 90 water purification plant 100 rechlorination injection facility 200 turbidity drain valve 300 a connection node terminal 400 a network 500 an integrated control server 600 and a big data server 700 and a manager mobile terminal 800"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101625-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "to this end the ict integrated monitoring water management system 1 for the construction of a smart water city is a system that manages each of the grid type waterworks network formed in the downtown area and the waterworks network formed in the outskirts of the city as an integrated system to manage the network"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101799853-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the present invention also provides a water circulation system for a city that can protect a natural ecosystem as well as a person by restoring a water circulation system in a city where water circulation is difficult due to road pavement sidewalk block and the like and a roadside protection trench used in the system there is"}]</data>
</edge>
