  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102714328-B1", "para_id": "para_445", "text": "the reason is that when the eco friendly movable weir for preventing green algae constructed according to the present invention is installed in a river with a structure of a dam reservoir lake or estuary and a structure of an eco friendly movable weir for preventing green algae 8888 that operates up and down to block a large amount of water green algae will not be generated by various reactions that occur naturally in the polluted river water and instead the polluted river water will be naturally purified into clean river water with a heavy specific gravity and at the same time the polluted river water will be naturally revived by preferentially discharging the clean bottom water with a heavy specific gravity thereby producing eco friendly electricity that is friendly to nature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a structure in which the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir frame 830 and white paper 88 are combined to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity on top of the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir 8888 is formed a structure in which a plurality of bolt units 919 for siphon plate joining are connected to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a nature friendly environmentally friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water by using an eco friendly movable weir for preventing green algae which is configured by combining a siphon plate 929 that acts to preferentially discharge polluted river water with a light specific gravity to the upper part of the siphon plate joining bolt unit 919 formed on the upper part of the eco friendly movable weir frame 830 for preventing green algae and forming a siphon passage 833 for discharging bottom water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "in any one of the clauses selected from clauses 1 and 2 a structure in which an eco friendly movable dam frame 830 for preventing green algae is combined with a white paper 88 to block the inflow of light weight polluted river water to the upper part of a rubber dam type movable dam 8118 that is either installed on the upper part of the above mentioned foundation concrete 800 or is newly installed a structure in which a plurality of bolt units 919 for siphon plate joining are connected to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a nature friendly environmentally friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water by using an eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae which is formed by combining a siphon plate 929 that acts to preferentially discharge polluted river water with a light specific gravity to the upper part of the siphon plate joining bolt unit 919 formed at the upper part of the eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae 8888 for preventing green algae and forming a siphon passage 833 for discharging bottom water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a structure in which the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir frame 830 and white paper 88 are combined to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity on top of the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir 8888 is formed a structure in which a shaped siphon action generating assembly partition 836 is sequentially fixed to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a structure in which the power generation water discharge pipe 3151 is constructed at an angle along the slope of the downstream part of the river starting from the lower part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth a structure in which an upward discharge pipe 3150 is formed in an l shape at a height that is 5 to 20 lower than the height of the lower part of the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is formed in the upstream part of the river at the end of the above mentioned power generation water discharge pipe 3151 a structure in which a terminal discharge pipe 3152 is formed in a t shape at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 3150 a structure in which an air exhaust unit 381 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a plurality of power generation water final pipes 262 each having a different thickness are connected around the end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a control unit 266 configured to control the discharge amount is connected to the upper part of the final power generation water pipe 262 a structure in which an upper storage tank 259 is connected to a lower discharge unit 256 configured in a different form with each storage capacity to store power generation water and discharge it to the lower part at the lower part of the above mentioned power generation water final pipeline 262 a structure in which a hydroelectric power generation unit 335 configured to generate electricity by hydraulic power is combined at the lower end of the above mentioned lower discharge unit 256 a nature friendly eco friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water using an eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae growth that is characterized by generating hydroelectric power by using an eco friendly movable dam that acts to prevent green algae growth"}, {"pat_id": "US-7585409-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "it will also be appreciated that gac filters are non polar in nature so they have the greatest affinity for other non polar substances and as a result are most effective in the removal of a variety of organic contaminates including trihalomethanes pesticides herbicides and polyaromatic hydrocarbons"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 an actuator housing for operating a water gate to one side and the other side of the foundation concrete a hydrologic actuator disposed inside the actuator housing an operating hinge connecting one side and the other side of the operating device a lower support pipe configured in the middle of the actuating hinge a front sluice plate disposed at an upper end of the lower support pipe a hydrostatically reinforced guide plate support disposed in a trapezoidal shape at an upper end of the front sluice plate a front stream water inlet control block installed between the hydrostatically reinforced guide plate support a lower support pipe configured at a lower end of the front river water inlet control block on the one side and the other side while adjusting the front stream water inlet control block up and down the river water inlet control cylinder for opening and closing the lower portion of the river water inlet is configured in the lower front portion of the front sluice plate a rear hydroplate hingedly coupled by a rear hydrologic hinge a hydroelectric aberration configured to form a u shaped hydroelectric aberration housing at a lower end of the rear hydrological plate and coupled to a generator in a hydroelectric aberration housing and a power generation aberration protection cover that protects the power generation aberration when the water gate is opened at the time of flooding on the top of the power generation aberration wherein the front hydrology plate and the hydraulic pressure reinforced guide plate at the lower end of the front lower portion of the river water inlet the upper part of the river water outlet is formed in the form of a larger than the top of the water discharge at the same time at the upper end of the front hydrostatic plate and the pressure reinforced guide plate support to discharge the river water while generating a strong water pressure toward the upper layer of the water gate eco friendly power generation system combined with nature friendly water purifier in the form of a child"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102083441-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "when the ozone is circulated as described above it is effective to recirculate the discharged ozone to the inflow side by contacting the water in the ozone reaction tank at the outflow side.the method for treating wastewater containing an organic solvent according to the present invention comprises a thermal treatment step and a forced oxidation treatment step for the treatment of a wastewater containing a high concentration of hardly decomposable organic solvent and the wastewater containing the organic solvent is preheated while passing through a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_139", "text": "2 the water permeable block 300 is a porous block capable of absorbing water eg rainwater generated in nature and even if it rains where the water permeable block 300 is disposed the water permeable block 300 the surface is porous so it absorbs rainwater and does not leave moisture on the surface of the permeable block 300 thereby preventing the user from sliding due to moisture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_144", "text": "water generated in nature such as rainwater and fog may be collected through the smart water collection system 10 of the present invention and specifically the first storage tank 140 of the tree type water collection facility 100 the bench type water collection system it may be temporarily collected through the second storage tank 220 of the facility 200 and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "US-10648165-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the system further includes a mechanism for controlling the tension in the elongated yieldably deformable support cable and thereby controlling the resistance that is offered by the system to the flow of fluid through the fluid flow channel and the entry of objects into the storm drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-10352505-B2", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "the extrapolated moving average steps are calibrated due to the dynamic nature of the subject process in light of signal noise valve seepage etc"}]</data>
