  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100834924-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the screen assembly for a composite sewage overflow dam of the present invention separates solids from a large ratio of fluid being transported and is disposed along the flood dam side during use to block interrupt the overflowing heavy rain water and to remove solids such as large wastes in turbid and dirty water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "in claim 1 or 2 a grating for a rainwater drainage system capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention characterized in that the upper surfaces of the fixed grating and the elevating grating are formed in a block like gently curved shape so that sediments including cigarette butts and fallen leaves accumulating on the upper surface of the grating are pushed along the gently curved surface of the upper surface of the grating by the current of water and are induced to quickly drain downward through the rainwater drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition it is possible to minimize the initial excellent water remaining in the water channel does not cause water pooling the remaining water does not decay there is an effect of reducing the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100636832-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "more specifically when the water level of the reservoir rises to a high level due to a failure of the existing water level control valve it is discharged through the overflow water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "US-4797028-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "various methods have been used in an attempt to prevent beavers from blocking the inlet of flood control risers in water reservoirs and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101501179-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "especially it is difficult to secure the site because it requires a separate site to install the contact tank and it is difficult to select the site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment 811 the above flood control equipment 811 is the hull position movement construction machinery control equipment 811a the marine hydroelectric power generation control equipment 811b the power transmission control equipment 811c the harmful red tide prevention control equipment 811d the disaster prevention control equipment 811e the fishery spawning control equipment 811f and the dam water gate control control equipment 811g are each individually equipped and the floating dock device of the flood control equipment is connected to the inside of the flood control equipment body 1 to prevent flooding of the underground passage the floating dock device of the above flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding connected to the ocean tunnel traffic device 941 and the ocean hydroelectric power plant the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment has a length of 800 mm a diameter of 300 mm a portable lug connecting pin connection shaft for the inner and outer walls of each tank of the main tank and the outer block tank and a thickness of the steel plate of the portable lug is 150 mm and the pin connecting shaft is inserted into the portable lug to be connected and the processing hole of the connecting pin connecting shaft has a diameter of 30 mm and the portable lug pin has a length and a pin body diameter of 500 2 10 mm and is disassembled and combined with a nut at the threaded position processed into the end portion of the pin connecting shaft inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding the double structure block tank transported by the tugboat is a barge hull on the top of the holding tank assembled by a band jig mounted on a semi submersible work vessel with a length and width of 600 m and a height and steel plate thickness of 800 m and 40 m and 18 mm and the barge hull on the bottom of the holding tank has a pipe bridge at each of the four corners in the length and width of 15 m and a diameter and thickness of \u03c015 m and a length of 24 mm and a thickness of 1 km forming a double structure block tank inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment the size of the external block tank which is composed of the perimeter of the main tank and the inner block tank is individually combined to form a small sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 600 m a length of 800 m a height of 800 m a height of 600 m a medium sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 2 m a length of 3.2 m and a height of 2 m and a large sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 10 m a length of 10 m and a height of 10 m and the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment while operating according to the sea depth the portable lug pin is installed by fastening the bolt nut in the machined hole of the lug connecting shaft and at the same time the pin is bent to prevent the lug pin from coming off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helicopter station 619 and a thermal power plant 626 are equipped with satellite launch pads 643 and mooring towers 644 and space rocket launch pads to detect climate abnormalities and equipment for detecting the weather movement status of the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention flood control equipment to detect climate abnormalities in order to prioritize emergency rescue the flood control equipment in the flooded area is always equipped with several air compressors 80 connected to rescue tubes 130 and ropes 131 at the accident site and before the underground passage is flooded the flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment to prevent flooding by installing a water tank for rescue and flood control in the flooded area so that people can board the tubes 130 and be rescued by rescue workers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for underground passage flood prevention is configured to supply power to each pump using the marine hydroelectric power generator 213 facilities to prevent underground passage flooding in the above underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment the hydraulic power generator 213 is installed a device 218 for pushing a rotary shaft under an upper rotary shaft 217 is positioned and a stator coil 219 a stator frame 220 and a central stator 221 are positioned at the bottom of the device 218 for pushing the rotary shaft and an electric wire 71 is inserted into the gap of the central stator 221 and a fan 195 is positioned at the bottom of the central stator 221 and a braking device ring 223 a brake jack 224 and a low speed rotary shaft 225 are positioned at the bottom of the fan 195 and a low speed cooler 222 is positioned at the bottom of the low speed rotary shaft 225 and a rotating electromagnet rotor coil formed along the circumference of the rotary shaft 198 and an armature coil for a non rotating coil generator installed along the circumference of the rotor coil and a lower end of the rotary shaft 198 the conventional marine hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment which is provided with several waterwheels and turbines 267 for setting up positions turbine rotating shafts 227 casings 141 vane pumps guide vanes 142 and impellers 228 supplies power to each pump of the hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment to prevent underground passage flooding and is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flooding prevention and flood control equipment the vertical multi stage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the above underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is as follows according to the control block diagram and the vertical multi stage pump operation method of the bf model the pump power 272 and the control power 273 are separated and distinguished and the emergency operation sequence circuit 274 of the control power 273 is connected to the dc power spray supply circuit 275 and the m c drive signal contact output circuit 279 and the output circuit terminal and then the m c switch contact of the pump power 272 and the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the contacts that enable each pump to be operated in emergency mode and at the same time the dc power supply circuit 275 of the control power 273 provides the input setting of the diac switch setting circuit 277 and the switch input circuit 58 to the micro control unit 276 and at the same time the led display circuit 278 and the drive signal contact output circuit 279 outputs a signal and the motor overload signal input circuit 280 is installed so that the circuit contacts of the unit 276 and the pump power supply 272 tip are connected to the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the inverter operation data input output circuit 281 is formed as a circuit for mutual input and output between the inverter 47 circuit and the micro control unit 276 and the discharge pressure transmitter 284 is connected to the pressure detection circuit 282 and then the circuit 282 is input set to the unit 276 and then the suction discharge pressure switch 285 is connected to the external status input circuit 283 and then the input circuit 283 is input set to the micro control unit 276"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in addition in the case of dam type power plants it is often unavoidable to avoid significant head fluctuations due to imbalances between rainfall and water usage and such power plants are sometimes called variable head power plants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_545", "text": "the flood control equipment configured inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment is configured to prevent the dispatch of conventional forest fire fighting equipment such as transport equipment and to achieve zero disaster by using a plurality of nozzle holes of the pipe nozzles inside the pipe nozzle body for fire prevention and disaster prevention measures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1061", "text": "and the outline of the vibratory hammer is that it drives or pulls out work by vibration force and the vibration frequency is more than 500 times per minute and the standard indication is indicated by the motor output kw and driving force ton and the drop hammer lifts a metal block with a wire rope and drops it on the head of a pile to drive the pile with the impact force and among the basic construction machines it is suitable when you want to reduce the equipment cost and operating cost under the same conditions for small scale construction from a long distance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1116", "text": "in addition the present invention uses hydroelectric power generation facilities that convert the potential energy of water stored in various dam water facilities according to the mountainous terrain of a mountain range into kinetic energy to generate hydroelectric power thereby solving the problem of environmental pollution by using water resource fuel as an alternative to expensive oil and coal fuels for thermal power generation and provides underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment that is continuously developed in parallel with the fishway tunnel devices that replace the existing dam gates of rivers and streams to block the inflow of salt water into water intake facilities and reinstall various fishway tunnel devices in the middle of rivers and middle dams and underwater weirs so that marine organisms can move to rivers and fish and shellfish can freely spawn in stable areas such as streams in valleys and the forestation project that improves the geological level of the river bottom to restore the natural ecosystem order and balance and maximizes ecosystem restoration activities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1120", "text": "the present invention as a technical idea for achieving the above purpose is in the underground flood prevention and flood control equipment the above flood control equipment 811 is the hull position movement construction machinery control equipment 811a the marine hydroelectric power generation control equipment 811b the power transmission control equipment 811c the harmful red tide prevention control equipment 811d the disaster prevention control equipment 811e the fishery spawning control equipment 811f and the dam water gate control control equipment 811g are each individually equipped and the floating dock device of the flood control equipment is connected to the inside of the flood control equipment body 1 to prevent flooding of the underground passage the floating dock device of the above flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding connected to the ocean tunnel traffic device 941 and the ocean hydroelectric power plant the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment has a length of 800 mm a diameter of 300 mm a portable lug connecting pin connection shaft for the inner and outer walls of each tank of the main tank and the outer block tank and a thickness of the steel plate of the portable lug is 150 mm and the pin connecting shaft is inserted into the portable lug to be connected and the processing hole of the connecting pin connecting shaft has a diameter of 30 mm and the portable lug pin has a length and a pin body diameter of 500 2 10 mm and is disassembled and combined with a nut at the threaded position processed into the end portion of the pin connecting shaft inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding the double structure block tank transported by the tugboat is a barge hull on the top of the holding tank assembled by a band jig mounted on a semi submersible work vessel with a length and width of 600 m and a height and steel plate thickness of 800 m and 40 m and 18 mm and the barge hull on the bottom of the holding tank has a pipe bridge at each of the four corners in the length and width of 15 m and a diameter and thickness of \u03c015 m and a length of 24 mm and a thickness of 1 km forming a double structure block tank inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment the size of the external block tank which is composed of the perimeter of the main tank and the inner block tank is individually combined to form a small sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 600 m a length of 800 m a height of 800 m a height of 600 m a medium sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 2 m a length of 3.2 m and a height of 2 m and a large sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 10 m a length of 10 m and a height of 10 m and the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment while operating according to the sea depth the portable lug pin is installed by fastening the bolt nut in the machined hole of the lug connecting shaft and at the same time the pin is bent to prevent the lug pin from coming off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1120", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helicopter station 619 and a thermal power plant 626 are equipped with satellite launch pads 643 and mooring towers 644 and space rocket launch pads to detect climate abnormalities and equipment for detecting the weather movement status of the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention flood control equipment to detect climate abnormalities in order to prioritize emergency rescue the flood control equipment in the flooded area is always equipped with several air compressors 80 connected to rescue tubes 130 and ropes 131 at the accident site and before the underground passage is flooded the flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment to prevent flooding by installing a water tank for rescue and flood control in the flooded area so that people can board the tubes 130 and be rescued by rescue workers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1127", "text": "the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for underground passage flood prevention is configured to supply power to each pump using the marine hydroelectric power generator 213 facilities to prevent underground passage flooding in the above underground passage flood prevention and flood control equip