evice 917 core drill 918 bio pipe skid 919 rubber tire 920 burner boom 921 harmful red tide microorganism 922 pollution free natural gas 923 air nozzle 924 mineral gathering trough 925 updraft 926 downdraft 927 yellow dust fine dust 928 piers bridge columns 929 fish farms 930 chemicals 931 cement 932 nets for securing fishery resources 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "that is in the present invention the drainage flow of the rainwater drained from the moving port 54 the moving section 59 and the passage port 57 provided to drain water naturally for the drainage path 52 and the vegetation block is reinforced the present invention provides a separate pressurizing device for promoting the drainage of rainwater from a ferry or a drain pipe provided for the purpose of preventing damages caused by flooding with surrounding slopes due to heavy rain or flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101811192-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "2003 063287 since the structure that drives the gate is complicated it is easy to catch foreign matter and it is possible to prevent the foreign matter from floating in the guide groove formed on the side of the gate of the foreign material floating in the upstream of the flood there is a structural problem that the flood damage will be caused by the action that the foreign substances that are caught in the water supply channel block the water channel and increase the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the assembled rainwater storage tank 10 according to the present invention having the above described structure can be installed rapidly and firmly to meet the capacity suitable for the building at low cost and can use rainwater as drinking water for drinking water and emergency drinking water it is possible to prevent flood control in the rainy season and typhoon as well as to surely prevent pollution by contaminated initial rainwater by eliminating a large but early power without extra power.10 assembly type stormwater tank 20 water storage tank tower 21 lower block 22 water quality observation block 23 upper block 24 capacity adjustment block 30 drain pipe assembly 31 first drain pipe 32 opening and closing means 33 second drain pipe 34 filter pipe 40 water supply pipe 50 water pump 60 advanced water purification device 70 fountain hose 80 sterilization device 90 water storage tank 100 building"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7117022-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "it may also be implemented in a mixed format with a partial hardware module that implements a part of hardware elements.brief description of the drawings it is a block diagram which shows the inland water flooding analysis apparatus which concerns on embodiment 1 of this invention.fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101502320-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "with the siphon passage plate 20 is formed on the lower surface of the connection block 30 while preventing the siphon passage plate 20 connected to the connection block 30 from sagging toward the bottom of the river a plurality of stoppers 33 protruding from the lower end of the connecting rod 30 so as to generate the action of forming the low level water discharging passage 21 while being automatically raised by the weight of the connecting rod 30 the stream water passing through the siphon passage 21 generates a vortex action and an aeration action is generated so that the polluted river water is naturally cleaned and purified and at the same time the operation of the movable waterborne door plate 10 the siphon passage plate 20 is provided at the rear surface thereof with a sidewall of the siphon passage plate 20 so as to generate a gravity dispersion action that originally cuts off the action of trapped river water in the upper portion of the movable waterborne door plate 10 constitutes a horizontal vortical plate 38 and a vertical vortical plate 39 the automatic folding type siphon passage 21 and the automatic folding drainage backflow preventing plate 16 are automatically brought into close contact with the lower end portion of the base concrete 100 by their respective weights when the movable protection gate plate 10 is conducted the automatic folding type siphon passage 21 which functions to increase the cross section of the river during the flood and the river water flowing from the upstream of the river are discharged over the movable flood gate plate 10 and a function of the automatic folding drainage backflow prevention plate 16 which functions to push the sand gravels passing through the prevention plate 16 and stacked on the rear side stream of the movable water security door plate 10 to the downstream portion of the river using the moving water control system for purging it is recommended to discharge the clean river water flowing through the bottom of the river due to heavy weight it prevents pollution by preventing gravity from discharging all of the river water stored in drought condition and enhances water flow area of river water to prevent flood damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131549-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "in addition the support wall 55 to form the reservoir 66 is connected to the supply pipe 67 is connected to the induction pipe 92 one side of the partition wall 62 formed in the reservoir 66 by providing a drain 70 in the reservoir the reservoir 66 of the block 50 is filled with excess water that is excessively filled by the occurrence of flood or heavy rain etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "it is possible to prevent flooding or flood damage as much as possible by going down to the infiltration water or evaporating to the atmosphere and to prevent the groundwater depletion by the infiltration water going to the ground soil"}, {"pat_id": "US-12043992-B2", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "5 where short circuit alerts in conjunction with over temperature alerts may indicate a fire short circuit alerts with the absence of over temperature alerts tamper alerts or other alerts would indicate a flood rather than another type of event e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277227-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition according to the storage tank operating system and operating method through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention it is possible to effectively cope with a disaster such as a flood caused by a sudden sudden change in the flow rate due to a heavy rain or a local rainfall.1 is a view illustrating a storage tank operating system to which a storage tank operating system is applied through real time control according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-10640941-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "further due to the opening of the flood discharge holes on the dam floating objects in the flood may block the flood discharge holes which in turn causes the flood to flow over the dam causing greater environmental damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole structure in particular by installing a buoyancy blocking device to block the inlet by the buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom of the rainwater inlet of the manhole while performing the original function of the rainwater on the road concentrated guerrillas it is related to the structure of the manhole backflow prevention system of the road which is designed to block the inflow of the manhole in case of the backflow of sewage due to heavy rain or flood thereby preventing flooding damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the present invention by installing a buoyancy blocking device 130 is operated by buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet 113 of the manhole 110 to block the inlet 113 the rainwater from the original while performing the function of the guerrilla torrential rain flooding due to the backflow of sewage due to the flood effect is to be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "4 this water softener 30 includes a cylindrical water softener body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center it includes a support cylinder 39 fixed to the bottom of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the flood diffusion prevention system of a building structure that is installed in a multi story building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to leakage from spreading to the elevating facility space a drainage passage formed on the floor of the common space for each floor in the building structure a drainage trench installed on the upper portion of the drainage passage to shield the drainage passage and a plurality of drainage holes for draining the inflowing water into the drainage passage a drain module connected to and configured to include a pipe for discharging the water to the outside a flood detection sensor installed in the drainage module to detect whether water has flowed in a water supply shutoff valve installed in a water supply line of the building structure to block water supply by a control signal and a flood signal received from the flood detection sensor a control unit for transmitting the control signal to the water supply shut off valve so as to be blocked and it is installed in front of the opening closing door of the elevator installed in the building structure and is raised to a preset height from the floor and includes a blocking module to prevent water from flowing into the elevator when submerged the blocking module is a blocking member installed in front of the opening closing door to open or shield the front lower part of the opening closing door according to the elevation an elevating wire having one end coupled to the upper portion of the blocking member to elevate the blocking member and the flooding prevention system of a building structure characterized in that it is connected to the other end of the elevating wire and configured to include a wire driving unit for elevating and lowering the elevating wire in conjunction with the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the present invention provides a system for preventing the spread of water in a building structure that is installed in a multi storey building structure and prevents the water flowing in due to a leak from spreading to an elevating facility space the it is installed on the upper part of the drain to shield the drain and includes a drain trench having a plurality of drain holes through which the inflowing water is drained into the drain and a piping part connected to the drain to drain the water to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a sewage odor blocking device and more particularly it is located under the manhole cover to block the bad smell of sewage and a backflow permitting hole is provided on one side to selectively allow backflow in the event of a flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "according to the present invention it is located on the lower side of the manhole cover to block odors and at the same time provide a backflow permitting hole on one side to selectively allow backflow in case of a flood thereby preventing damage to the manhole due to water pressure in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102711665-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the purpose of the present invention is to provide a multifunctional ecological block equipped with a water collection and infiltration function and a construction method thereof which includes a water channel a retention section provided at the rear of the water channel section and an inspection port provided on the side of the water channel section thereby reducing the discharge of pollutants flowing out with rainwater to prevent water pollution delaying rainwater from concentrating on rainwater pipes to prevent flood damage and improving groundwater depletion by securing a space through which rainwater can continuously infiltrate the lower soil layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102569525-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "a main body formed in a hexahedral shape and extending a certain length from side to side a first front cover and a second front cover which are installed to be spaced apart from each other on the left and right sides of the front part of the main body so as to form an inlet through which water flows into the central side of the open front part of the main body a first opening closing door and a second opening closing door installed on the main body behind the first front cover and the second front cover and movably installed along the left and right directions of the main body to open and close the inlet a door driving unit for moving the first and second opening and closing doors a control unit that operates the door driving unit by an operator s or manager s manipulation or automatically operates the door driving unit according to a set pattern and a blocking screen installed on the main body corresponding to the inlet side behind the first opening and closing door and the second opening and closing door to block the inflow of foreign substances into the main body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681132-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention provides a method of installing a water level plate that can block a connection pipe of a water intake tunnel while being easily installed and capable of withstanding water pressure and is capable of installing an already manufactured device in a water intake tunnel without producing water the present invention provides a method for replacing a water gate using a shutoff device for water gate maintenance of a water intake tower for replacing a water gate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101685359-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flat valve that is installed in a manhole to block reverse flow of odors and insects and to introduce sewage and stormwater a bracket provided opposite to the inner side surface of the inlet of the manhole and having a latching groove and and a valve body connected to the brackets and fitted in the latching grooves wherein the valve body includes a fixed panel having a lower portion at both ends thereof fitted into the engaging grooves a valve panel installed on both sides of the fixed panel so as to be hinged to open or close the inlet a sealing pad formed along an edge of the valve panel a t shaped supporter having a column formed at a central upper portion of the fixed panel and a support bar formed at an upper portion of the column and elastic springs connecting both ends of the support bar and the valve panel one end of the fixed panel is pinned and fixed to one of the brackets since both ends of the fixed panel are fixed to the brackets without being fixed to the brackets only one end of the fixed panel is pinned so that when the sewage due to the flood flows backward the valve body rotates around the pin to open the inlet through the inlet of the manhole wherein a through hole is formed in the bracket and a connection hole is formed in the fixing panel so as to penetrate through the fixing panel and are connected to each other by fins"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952192-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is connected to the connection pipe from one side of the sump of the sewage in order to reduce or delay the flow rate of the flood flowing into the river during the flooding storm water collector rainwater inlet tank flowing through a penetration well formed in the ground below the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet a first cylindrical tube having a cylindrical shape penetrating into the penetrating well so as to form a space between the sidewalls of the penetrating well and having a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a second cylindrical hole having a cylindrical shape which is inserted into the first oil hole and has a nonwoven fabric for filtering foreign matters on the outside thereof and has a plurality of through holes formed at its periphery a filtration layer filled with aggregate in a space between the penetrating well and the first perforated tube and a filter net fastened to block an upper end of the first oil pipe wherein the rainwater is discharged through the outlet of the sump well at a normal flow rate and the rainwater introduced into the rainwater inflow tank through the connecting pipe at an abnormal flow rate is formed in the first flow pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to purify rainwater collected in a storage tank and to provide it as a landscape water and a living water thereby preventing a water shortage phenomenon and a nonpoint pollution reduction high initial stormwater is stored in the reservoir and purified rainwater is discharged at the end of rainfall or gradually penetrated into the underground to prevent flood maintain groundwater level at a certain level to prevent ground stabilization and river pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "2008 0067603 discloses a odor blocking device and rainwater backflow device for sewer manholes that continuously block the occurrence of odor generated in the manhole of the sewer and also cope sensitively with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "there was a problem of not being able to.the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above the object of the present invention is to ensure the maximum amount of water through the rain unit to the discharge pipe side through the drainage unit seated in the cover to ensure the maximum amount of water it is to provide a facility for preventing the smell and backflow of road rainwater receivers that can reliably block the outflow of odor due to wastewater and also effectively cope with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
