  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in claim 1 or 2 a grating for a rainwater drain capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention characterized in that the support rods forming the grating in the form of a grid structure of the above mentioned fixed grating and the lifting grating are formed below the upper surface of the grid plate thereby minimizing the accumulation of various sediments such as cigarette butts and fallen leaves around the rainwater drain on the grating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "according to the grating for a rainwater drainage ditch capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention according to the embodiment of the present specification as described above in normal times when it does not rain or when the amount of rainfall is small the elevating grating 50 that is connected to a rectangular sub frame 40 so as to be able to be lifted up and down is lowered to the initial position by pulling down the lifting pieces 140 180 formed on the left and right side walls thereof along the guide rails 120 170 formed on the inner surface of the sub frame 110 corresponding to the lifting pieces thereby maintaining the same height as the fixed grating 60 that is secured to one side of the grating frame 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire hose 9 and a fire nozzle frame 11 and a hook 13 i