ing platform 17 the flood pumping systems 14 and the associated pressure pipes 6 which are not shown here are for example offset with respect to the axis of rotation 5 to highlight the planning challenge for efficient training"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "figure 6 turns off the cut aa figure 8 in which the flood pumping station 15 consisting of the lifting platform 17 with the installed flood pumping systems 14 and the cantilevered pressure pipes 6 is in rest position 23 and thus represents the h\u00f6henkote at the top position of the lifting platform 17 in this state according to the invention a complete outflow in the flow direction 10 of the sewer 19 to the receiving water 29 with lowered discharge control system 9 and inflow water layers below the accumulation target 27 is made possible"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in this case it is clear that according to the invention here is the flood case in which the top edge 21 of the relief control system 9 always nachgesteuert above the high water mark 13 or an underlying high water level 16 which in turn was above the maximum storage target 27 of the sewer 19 is located so that further the congestion target 27 of the sewer system 19 exceeding zulaufwassermengen can be pumped by the flood pumping systems 14 in the receiving water 29"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "to prevent the possible torque perpendicular to the flow direction 10 the forced plates 32 engage laterally in the guide slot 12 of the abutment 30 and reduce the possible torque of the lifting platform 17 when lowering perpendicular to the flow direction 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a structure that is coupled to a conveyance belt for conveying contaminants to the outside on the rear side of the lifting bar the underwater pump connected to the conveyor belt constitutes a submerged pump at the lower end of the purifier box to remove the particulate contaminants remaining in the inside of the lifting jacket when lifting the particulate contaminants floating on the upper end of the booster box a pipeline coupled with the submersible pump an underwater pump for completely removing fine contaminants introduced into the purifier box by using a water injection nozzle formed at an end of a pipe connected to the pipeline and a discharge control valve coupled to a discharge control valve for controlling discharge of light organic matter molecules floating at the upper end of the purifier box at a downstream portion of the purifier box the process of cleansing polluted river water or contaminated rainwater using a river water or rain water purification system configured to purify polluted river water and contaminated rainwater by separate discharge is characterized in that the multifunctional water gate configured to store the river water to store river water or rainwater and to open the inflow adjusting gate constructed in the purifying box to inflow river water or rainwater into the inside of the purifying box and the air discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}]</data>
