  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_487", "text": "16 the gear pump 326 of the conventional underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment has the advantages of being compact lightweight and inexpensive and can withstand harsh operating conditions contamination by dust rise in oil temperature overload so it is particularly suitable for hydraulic drive in construction machinery industrial vehicles agricultural machinery etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101699031-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to the water treatment apparatus of the present invention the particulate pollutants contained in the silt treatment water flowing into the flow rate adjusting tank through the run off grooves formed in the flood wall defining the sediment tank and the flow rate adjusting tank are filtered by the filter the flow of the silt treated water flowing into the flow rate adjusting tank via the needle bed is more directional than that of the conventional method so that it has some effect of preventing the settling of the contamination source by the turbulence"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484939-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in the present invention when the building is downward the wastewater pipe is folded by the joints folded in multiple stages and when the building is raised by the buoyancy the wastewater pipe is expanded together with the joint it is possible to minimize the exposure of the various hoses supplied and discharged to the outside to avoid damage to the aesthetics and to prevent the hoses exposed to the outside from being lost by the river at a high flow rate it is possible to prevent problems such as wastewater leaking and contamination of the surroundings and to prevent the administrator from having to dispatch the hose and the wires separately by hand when the flood and the flood alert sound"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101903469-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition in the summer season muddy water and pollutants are directly introduced into the interior of the tunnel through the casing due to flood so that the contamination of the groundwater is further increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102853309-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "according to the invention of a water intake contamination prevention facility utilizing a variable tidal current barrier and its operation method even when the water volume and velocity of a river fluctuate rapidly during a sudden typhoon or flood the facility can be automatically maintained thereby ensuring the safety of the facility and the water intake facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
