op sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a method for automatically degassing a downflow biological water treatment filter having various levels an influent flow into the top of the filter and an effluent flow from the base of the filter a stopping the outflow to prevent drainage of the filter comprising a backwash system b flushing gas trapped from the filter by introducing a back flow of water into the base of the filter c automatically checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow d draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level e continually flushing the filter to release the trapped gas from the filter f stopping the backwash stream and the backwash waste stream if present resuming the outflow to restart the filter and g maintaining influent flow during steps a through f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a plurality of downflow biological water treatment filters having various levels inflows entering the top of the filter and outflows flowing out of the bottom of the filter a maintaining an inflow to each filter inlet while all filters selected to be degassed are degassed b stopping the outflow from the filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the selected filter including the backwash system c directing backwash water flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the selected filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the level of the selected filter reaches a flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g next stopping the outflow from the selected filter and then introducing backwash water to the selected filter h stopping the backwash and backwash wastewater in the selected filter if present and resuming the outflow from the filter of step b to reactivate the filter of step b i degassing the remaining selected filters by repeating steps b through h continuously with step a j flushing the finally selected filter k stopping the backwash flow into the finally selected filter and l resuming the outflow from the finally selected filter to reactivate the finally selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a number of upstream biological filters in a water treatment system having an inflow into the filter an outflow from the filter and a backwash system a maintaining the outflow from the top of each filter while degassing all filters selected to be degassed b stopping the inflow to the base of the filter selected to be degassed to prevent backwash backflow to the other filter c directing backwash water flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g stopping the inflow to the base of the filter selected to be degassed to prevent backwash backflow to the other filter h then inducing a backwash flow to the base of the selected filter to flush the trapped gas from the filter i stopping the backwash and backwash wastewater if present in the filter selected in step b and resuming the inflow to the base of the filter of step b to reactivate the filter of step b j continuing step a while continuing to repeat steps b to i to degas other selected filters k flushing the finally selected filter l stopping backwash and backwash wastewater if present into the finally selected filter and m resuming the inflow to the base of the finally selected filter to reactivate the finally selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "claim_19", "text": "a method of automatically degassing a plurality of downflow biological water treatment filters each filter having a variable level an inflow into the top of the filter and an outflow from the base of the filter the filter comprising a locking the outlet valve from the first filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the filter b opening the backwash fresh water valve of the selected first filter c starting the backwash pump d automatically checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level f flushing the selected first filter to release the trapped gas from the filter g next closing the outlet valve from the selected filter and then opening the backwash fresh water valve to the selected filter h closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the selected first filter i opening the outlet valve from the selected first filter j repeat steps d to i successively for each additional filter where the next successive filter in steps d to g of the previous order is a subsequent step d a first filter selected from f k flushing the last selected filter l turning off the backwash water pump m opening the outlet valve from the finally selected filter n closing the backwash fresh water valve and the backwash wastewater valve to the finally selected filter and o maintaining the inlet valve open in steps a to n"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the degassing method comprises the steps of a maintaining the inflow to each inlet of each filter while all the filters selected for degassing are degassed b stopping the outflow from the filter selected for degassing to prevent drainage of the selected filter comprising the backwash system c directing the backwash flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the selected filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater if the selected filter level is flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g next stopping the outflow from the selected filter and directing the backwash flow to the next selected filter h stopping the backwash and the backwash wastewater in the selected filter and resuming the outflow from the filter of step b to reactivate the filter of step b and i successively repeating steps b to h to degas other selected filters while continuing with step a j flushing the finally selected filter k discontinuing the backwash flow to the finally selected filter and l resuming the outflow from the last selected filter to reactivate the last selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869204-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "maintaining an outflow from the top of each filter during the process b stopping the inflow to the base of the filter selected to be degassed to prevent backwash backflow to the other filter c directing backwash water flow to the base of the filter selected in step b to flush the gas trapped from the filter d checking the filter level to see if the filter will overflow e draining backwash wastewater when the filter level reaches the flood level f continuously flushing the filter selected in step b until the trapped gas is released from the filter g stopping the inflow to the base of the filter selected to be degassed to prevent backwash backflow to the other filter h directing a backwash stream to the base of the selected filter to flush the trapped gas from the filter i stopping the backwash and backwash wastewater if any present in the filter selected in step b resuming the inflow to the base of the filter in step b and reactivating the filter in step b j continuously degassing the other selected filter by repeating steps b to i while continuing with step a k flushing the finally selected filter l if present stopping the backwash flow to the finally selected filter and m resuming the inflow to the base of the finally selected filter to reactivate the finally selected filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "and a cap 198 connected to the hinge 190 of the fixed frame 125 provided at the end of the branch pipe 121.the present invention provides a stable drainage of rainwater by providing a stable removal of rainwater or flood caused by heavy rainfall as described above while checking the clogging caused by sedimentation that accumulates while moving in a drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101681132-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the present invention provides a method of installing a water level plate that can block a connection pipe of a water intake tunnel while being easily installed and capable of withstanding water pressure and is capable of installing an already manufactured device in a water intake tunnel without producing water the present invention provides a method for replacing a water gate using a shutoff device for water gate maintenance of a water intake tower for replacing a water gate"}]</data>
