  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102714962-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however conventional separators have a problem in that when the amount of sewage and foreign substances contained in the sewage flowing into the drainage pumping station during a flood increases excessively the separator is damaged or overturned and broken due to foreign substances caught in the separator and water pressure caused by increased sewage and there is a problem in that the driving part that drives the rake to collect the caught foreign substances is subject to excessive load resulting in damage to the driving part or breakage of the rake"}]</data>
