  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5386206-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "that is the operator first remove the lid 52 from the standpipe 50 pulled by grasping the handle 33 of the mud sump vessel 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706162-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "a odor blocking tube formed of a synthetic resin material having a cylindrical shape having a narrow bottom and widening toward the top and having a ring shaped weight added to the bottom a circular flange having a plurality of first bolt holes and coupled to an upper surface of the malodor blocking tube and a second bolt hole corresponding to the first bolt hole thereof so as to be coupled to the circular flange and a fastening ring inserted into an inner circumferential surface of the manhole cover wherein the odor blocking tube comprises a plurality of supports having the same curvature is further attached to the inner side and the upper side of the upper side discharges rainwater flowing through the manhole cover and the elastic valve is fixed to the support to block the sewage of the main body backflow"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4334422-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "and the upper edge of the mud reservoir 5 inserted in the mud reservoir 4 is locked by the locking protrusion 16 of the anti lifting ring 15 to prevent the mud reservoir 5 from floating"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4334422-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "when the mud reservoir 5 is taken in and out the locking protrusion 16 of the anti lifting ring 15 is elastically deformed appropriately and the flange portion 12 of the mud reservoir 5 is the retaining protrusion 16 can be easily climbed over and when the mud pool container 5 is about to float up due to rainwater or the like accumulated inside the main body 3 the retaining protrusion 16 causes the mud reservoir container to rise"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259156-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "the present invention relates to the fabrication of rainwater storage tanks having the ability to store rai