e of the road and the ground or in the ground of the central separator and flows rainwater on a road surface such as a road into a sewer or underground a locking flange formed integrally with an upper opening side edge of the u shaped buried water pipe and forming a locking jaw at an end thereof square side insertion holes formed on outer peripheral surfaces of the buried water pipe facing each other and opposed to each other rti gt a horizontal retaining rod coupled to the side insertion holes of the squares facing each other on the outer circumferential surface of the buried water pipe to prevent gradient deformation of the buried water pipe and a cover channel forming a drainage groove and a drainage groove to which a top surface of the buried aqueduct is formed while both ends are coupled to each other on the locking flange to prevent separation by the locking step and a drain grating is coupled to an upper surface thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102548347-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole 100 provided around roads or buildings for drainage of rainwater with a manhole cover 120 detachably assembled on the upper surface and having a drain 101 of a predetermined caliber on the bottom a chamber housing 110 provided in a pot bellied shape at the lower end of the drain 101 of the manhole 100 as the center and having a discharge port 102 and a connection flange 140 on the bottom surface a sewage pipe 200 having a flange 210 and an inlet 211 coupled to the connection flange 140 of the chamber housing 110 in a state buried in the ground at a predetermined depth so that rainwater flows through the manhole 100 it is installed inside the chamber housing 110 and when rainwater flows into the manhole 100 the outlet 102 is opened and when the water in the sewage pipe 200 flows backward it rises by buoyancy and blocks the drain 101"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102548347-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention is provided around roads or buildings for drainage of rainwater and a manhole cover is detachably assembled on the upper surface and a drain hole of a predetermined caliber is provided on the bottom a chamber housing provided in a pot bellied shape at the bottom of the manhole centering on the drain hole and having a discharge port and a connection flange on the bottom surface a sewage pipe buried at a predetermined depth in the ground provided with a flange coupled to a connection flange of the chamber housing and an inlet through which rainwater flows through a manhole it is installed inside the chamber housing opens the outlet when rainwater flows into the manhole and rises when the water in the sewage pipe flows backward to block the drain consists of"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pair of vertical support bars are installed to be coupled to each other so that the side channel can be continuously installed at a predetermined height from the bottom surface the locking flange is prevented from being separated by the locking jaw portion while preventing the deformation in the width direction characterized in that the g shaped grating mounting frame is configured to be coupled by a fastening member the edge portion of the drainage creasing is applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101386144-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "when the lifting flange 23 protrudes from the main body foreign matter contained in rainwater or sewage is caught thereby preventing the flow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "to block the odor flowing back from the sewer and when the amount of rain water is relatively large the rotary drainage guide plate rotates downward to filter the filth by the strainer while smoothing the inflow of rain water odor countercurrent blocking function and dirt sewer rain gutter with manure function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "including a rod and one side is fixedly coupled to both ends of the hinge shaft and the other side is composed of second connecting rods respectively coupled to both side plates of the strainer the strainer is the main weight of the rotating drainage plate if the amount of rainwater flowing into the opening is relatively small by limiting the rotation of the rotary drainage guide plate by the self load of the strainer to close the drain hole to block the odor flowing back from the sewer rain water when the amount of is relatively large the rotation drainage guide plate rotates downward to facilitate the inflow of rain water while the manure the present invention provides a sewer rain gutter having a bad smell counter current blocking function and a dirt filtering function for filtering dirt by a net"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "a drain pipe 115 connecting the inlet pipe 110 and the drain pipe 128 with the fixed flange 125 is used as the accumulation pipe 124 and the accumulation pipe 124 is provided with a drain pipe an inspection sensor 116 for measuring an increase in the weight of the deposition pipe 124 by generating a signal according to a deposition weight of the deposited deposit 122 by forming a part 130 of the deposition pipe 124 the fixed flange 125 is separated from the fixed state by the signal of the driving shaft 116 and the wheels 147 are mounted so as to be easily removed along with the movement of the separated accumulation pipe 124 145"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102758462-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole body 3 having an upper opening formed at the top that can be opened and closed by means of an upper cover 2 and having an inlet and an outlet formed at the bottom respectively to which an inlet pipe 100 and an outlet pipe 200 for introducing sewage or rainwater are respectively connected a cover pipe 5 made of metal material and having a support step 51 formed on the inner surface to support the upper cover 2 while being supported and having a support flange 52 formed integrally in the outer surface of the lower surface in an outward direction in a manhole 1 which includes a fixed pipe 7 disposed at the lower portion of the cover pipe 5 made of metal or synthetic resin as a material and having upper and lower penetrations to allow sewage water to pass through the outer circumference of which is closely fitted to the inner surface of the upper opening h of the manhole body 3 and which is provided with a fall prevention structure 71 on the inner circumference to support and receive a pedestrian in the event of a fall and a fixed flange 72 formed to extend outward on the upper outer circumference and a height adjustment means 6 configured to adjust the height of the cover pipe 5 through filling mortar 64 the above manhole body 3 is it comprises an upper assembly block 31 having the upper opening h formed at the upper side and the open lower side a lower assembly block 32 having the inlet and outlet holes respectively formed at the lower side and having upper and lower parts penetrated an intermediate assembly block 33 vertically stacked between the upper assembly block 31 and the lower assembly block 32 and having upper and lower parts penetrated and a bottom assembly block 34 vertically stacked below the lower assembly block 32 and having an open upper side on the upper surface of the above floor assembly block 34 the upper and lower surfaces of the above lower assembly block 32 the upper and lower surfaces of the above intermediate assembly block 33 and the lower surface of the above upper assembly block 31 the connecting projections 41 and connecting grooves 42 are formed in a ring shape and are fitted and connected to each other the above mentioned binding protrusion 41 and the above mentioned binding groove 42 are it is composed of two sets of inner and outer diameters that are different and arranged with a gap between them centered on the center of the above manhole body 3 on the lower surface of the lower assembly block 32 the lower surface of the intermediate assembly block 33 and the lower surface of the upper assembly block 31 the upper part of the guide rod 43 having a vertical length is fixed in place on the upper surface of the above floor assembly block 34 the upper surface of the above lower assembly block 32 and the upper surface of the above middle assembly block 33 each guide receiving groove 44 is formed to accommodate the guide rod 43 by fitting the lower portion thereof between the above fixed flange 72 and the manhole body 3 when the above filling mortar 64 is formed it is embedded inside with the manhole body 3 placed in the facility space formed underground anchor screw rods 61 embedded in the edge of the upper opening h of the manhole body 3 sequentially penetrate the fixed flange 72 and the support flange 52 the above fixed flange 72 is supported by a lower support nut 62 that is screw connected to the anchor screw rod 61 on its bottom surface and the above supported flange 52 is fixed by an upper fixing nut 63 that is screw connected to the anchor screw rod 61 on its top surface so that the cover pipe 5 and the above fixed pipe 7 are arranged while forming a gap at the edge of the upper opening h of the manhole body 3 a manhole characterized in that the filling mortar 64 is injected and filled between the fixed flange 72 and the manhole body 3 and cured and an elastic spring structure 8 is embedded inside the filling mortar 64 to elastically offset the shock vibration load applied from the upper portion of the cover pipe 5 between the fixed flange 72 and the manhole body 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in configuring the odor prevention device 110 to prevent the odor coming up from the ground the odor prevention device 110 includes a prevention body 112 having a seating flange 111 upward to be seated on the bottom surface of the manhole cover 105 the prevention body 112 and the first vertical portion 113 protrudes downward from the mounting flange 111 an inclined portion 114 formed to have a width narrowed inward from an end of the first vertical portion 113 a second vertical portion 115 projecting downward from the end of the inclined portion 114 a plurality of water passages 116 formed to drain a small amount of rainwater to the inclined portion 114 a discharge hole 117 formed to be opened between the second vertical portions 115 to discharge a large amount of rain and garbage deformed by the hydraulic pressure of the sewage to the water hole 116 while being drained down and after completion of drainage to return to the original state to prevent the odor coming up through the water hole 116 fixing the blocking plate 118 of a material having elasticity and excellent return force the discharge hole 117 is a sewer manhole odor prevention device characterized in that it comprises a rotating plate 120 installed so as to block the odor coming up while draining the rain and waste of the opposite"}]</data>
