  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101247110-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "pressure and temperature generated when the micro bubbles are destroyed can cause a corrosion state in the reaction chamber 41 so the reaction chamber 41 is connected to both ends by a flange 44 so that the structure can be replaced immediately in case of serious damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-10759676-B2", "para_id": "para_456", "text": "7 the lower flange 704 and upper flange 712 may be manufactured out of any material having sufficient structural strength and corrosion and temperature resistant properties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100956077-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "therefore the size of the separation space 8 is calculated in consideration of the expansion ratio of the lining material 3 from the length of the pipeline 1 in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604858-B2", "para_id": "para_456", "text": "7 the lower flange 704 and upper flange 712 may be manufactured out of any material having sufficient structural strength and corrosion and temperature resistant properties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714293-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "sludge drying tank 10 a steam jacket 20 installed to form a steam passage continuously passing through the outside of the sludge drying tank 10 and consisting of a side jacket shell 20a covering the side of the sludge drying tank 10 and a bottom jacket shell 20b covering the bottom of the sludge drying tank 10 a sludge inlet 11 installed on the upper side of the above sludge drying tank 10 into which sludge or waste water containing sludge flows in a sludge outlet 12 formed in the lower tank exposure area where the side jacket shell 20a is omitted among the areas adjacent to the bottom of the sludge drying tank 10 a sludge outlet opening closing unit 30 comprising a closer 32 that blocks the sludge outlet 12 and a hydraulic cylinder 34 that opens and closes the sludge outlet 12 by moving the closer 32 between a position where the sludge outlet 12 is blocked and a position where the sludge outlet 12 is opened a steam inlet 21 formed on the upper part of the side jacket shell 20a to allow steam to flow into the steam passage a condensate outlet 22 formed in the above bottom jacket shell 20b to discharge condensate in which steam is condensed an agitator 40 including a stirring blade 41 and a motor 42 that rotates the stirring blade 41 and installed so that the stirring blade 41 is introduced into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 through the upper part of the sludge drying tank 10 thereby stirring sludge or wastewater containing the sludge introduced into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 a plurality of support columns 52 extending downward from the bottom surface of the sludge drying tank 10 and fitted into a plurality of joining holes formed in the bottom jacket shell 20b and watertightly welded a side fixing structure 54 that fixes the side jacket shell 20a and the sludge drying tank 10 in a spaced state a manhole 14 formed at the top of the sludge drying tank 10 to allow workers to enter the inside of the sludge drying tank 10 a manhole cover 60 installed to block the above manhole 14 a viewing window 15 installed on the upper side of the above sludge drying tank 10 a lighting window 16 installed adjacent to the above viewing window 15 to allow the transmission of light emitted from the lighting device a steam passage temperature sensor 71 installed on the above side jacket shell 20a to measure the temperature of steam flowing into the steam passage in real time a steam passage pressure sensor 72 installed on the above side jacket shell 20a to measure the pressure of the steam passage in real time a condensate temperature sensor 73 installed in the above bottom jacket shell 20b to measure the condensate temperature a tank temperature sensor 74 installed at the top of the sludge drying tank 10 to measure the internal temperature of the sludge drying tank 10 in real time a tank pressure sensor 75 installed on the top of the sludge drying tank 10 to measure the internal pressure of the sludge drying tank 10 in real time and it includes a controller 5 that controls the operation of the steam heat sludge dryer 1 by using data transmitted from the steam passage temperature sensor 71 the steam passage pressure sensor 72 the condensate temperature sensor 73 the tank temperature sensor 74 and the tank pressure sensor 75"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714293-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "at least one of the first sludge dryer 1a the second sludge dryer 1b and the third sludge dryer 1c is installed to form a steam passage continuously connected to the outside of the sludge drying tank 10 and a steam jacket 20 composed of a side jacket shell 20a covering the side of the sludge drying tank 10 and a bottom jacket shell 20b covering the bottom of the sludge drying tank 10 a sludge inlet 11 installed on one side of the upper portion of the sludge drying tank 10 and into which sludge or wastewater including sludge flows in a sludge outlet 12 formed in a lower tank exposed area where the side jacket shell 20a is omitted among areas adjacent to the lower portion of the sludge drying tank 10 a closure 32 for blocking the sludge outlet 12 and the closure 32 a sludge outlet opening closing unit 30 composed of a hydraulic cylinder 34 that opens and closes the sludge outlet 12 by moving between a position where the sludge outlet 12 is blocked and a position where the sludge outlet 12 is opened a steam inlet 21 formed on the upper portion of the side jacket shell 20a to allow steam to flow into the steam passage a condensate outlet 22 formed on the bottom jacket shell 20b to discharge condensate in which steam is condensed an agitator 40 including a stirring blade 41 and a motor 42 that rotates the stirring blade 41 and is installed so that the stirring blade 41 is introduced into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 through the upper portion of the sludge drying tank 10 thereby stirring sludge or wastewater containing the sludge that has flowed into the interior of the sludge drying tank 10 and the sludge drying tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102714293-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "it further includes a side fixing structure 54 formed to guide steam from a steam inlet to a condensate outlet while fixing a shell 20a and a sludge drying tank 10 in a spaced state a manhole 14 formed on the top of the sludge drying tank 10 to allow a worker to enter the inside of the sludge drying tank 10 a cover body 61 joined by a fastener to block the manhole 14 a manhole cover 60 including the cover body 61 and a hot air blower 90 installed in the cover body 61 to blow high temperature hot air into the inside of the sludge drying tank 10 through the manhole 14"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_417", "text": "sixth thoroughly check and confirm whether there is any gas leakage from the valve or flange joint and tight surface of the piping system whether there is any abnormality in power consumption and whether there is any abnormality in the operation of automatic devices and monitoring devices"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark 