the sealing cap through a pair of connection rings provided on the protection guard and a step of press fitting and fixing the end portion of the maintenance pipe to the end portion of the maintenance pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit the step of cooling the maintenance pipe may include the steps of fixing the other end of the traction wire one end of which is connected to the sealing cap press fitted to both ends of the maintenance pipe to a pair of connection rings provided on the protection guard a method of repairing and installing a conduit using a protective guard and an insulating case installed in a work area the method comprising the step of minimizing shrinkage deformation of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit wherein the heating plate has a support structure connected to an upper end of a heating plate body that generates heat when power is applied thereto and a hook ring provided at an upper portion of the support structure and connected to a hook of the crane portion the heat insulating case includes a thermostat having an opening that is opened upward to allow the heating plate to advance and retreat and an opening portion that is opened by the supporting structure is closed and the thermostat has a fixing portion corresponding to the connection hole formed in the fixing plate wherein the securing member is detachably fixed to the earth retaining plate by a fastening member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit wherein the heating plate has a support structure connected to an upper end of a heating plate body that generates heat when power is applied thereto and a hook ring provided at an upper portion of the support structure and connected to a hook of the crane portion wherein the heat insulating case includes a thermostat which is formed on both sides of the thermostat to have a long hole corresponding to a protruding member provided at both ends of the supporting structure and is coupled with the supporting structure and a side cover that seals the long hole wherein the protection guard and the heat insulating case are installed in the work area"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the heat insulating case into contact with the end portion of the repair pipe protruding from the conduit after fixing the connection flange to the end of the conduit the present invention provides a method of repairing and installing a conduit using a protective guards and a heat insulating case provided in the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "2 it is possible to reduce the time required to heat the fused heat plate to a predetermined temperature by heating the fused heat plate used for heat welding of the maintenance pipe to a high temperature in the internal space of the heat sealed case which is blocked from the external environment since it is possible to prevent contact with the operator it is possible to reduce the time required for heat generation thereby improving work productivity and preventing burn incidents of the operator.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "7 the bottom flange 704 and the top flange 712 may be made of any material having sufficient structural strength corrosion resistance and temperature resistance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the flange 122 may be provided on an outer circumferential surface of the temperature sensitive member 120 so that the first elastic member 130 can be easily coupled to the temperature sensitive member 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200384179-Y1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "as described above according to the present invention by wrapping the inner cylinder 20 with the upper insulating material 40 and the outer insulating material 50 and by inserting the outer cylinder 30 can be preserved as much as possible the geothermal heat introduced into the inner cylinder 20 it is possible to prevent freezing of the water pipe and the water meter by keeping the temperature inside the protection container at room temperature even in cold weather and by combining the reinforcing flange 70 on the upper edge of the outer cylinder 30 even if the protection container is buried in the ground by being able to withstand the load sufficiently there is an effect that can prevent the breakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-11884555-B2", "para_id": "para_354", "text": "7 the lower flange 704 and upper flange 712 may be manufactured out of any material having sufficient structural strength and corrosion and temperature resistant properties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102561408-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in the case of the mixing tank 11 similar to the cooling tank 4 by using a pvc 100a standard water pipe and firmly welding or bonding the joint between the flange portion provided at both ends and the pvc pipe it is desirable to prevent oxygen and its mixed air from leaking to the outside while preventing damage from external impact or temperature difference between inside and outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-10633265-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a device for the filtration of water in containers comprising an electrolysis cartridge with electrified plates and an automation device which act synergistically the device including at least three metal rectangular plates on the electrolysis cartridge each of the rectangular plates includes one end having a groove that forms a folded terminal at least one interleaved plate placed between the at least three rectangular metal plates the at least one interleaved plate is placed equidistantly between the plates with terminals the at least three metal rectangular plates and the interleaved plates are placed inside a casing having threaded ends and with an inner walls having a pair of grooved insulating plates with channels disposed towards a center of the casing each channel of each one of the grooved insulation plate coincides in arrangement and size with respect to the channel of the opposing grooved insulation plate in such a way that the plates and the interleaved plates are inserted into each pair of the channels of the insulation plates an innermost end of each insulation plate includes a stop to detain the advance of the plates and at the opposite end of each insulation plate includes a lock having a t shape having at least one groove wherein if one of the grooves is at a crossing point of the lines forming it and that said groove coincides in size and shape to accommodate the fold of the extension being in the at least one of the metal rectangular plates on an opposite section from where the groove is located the lock has a fold having a form of a square u to be supported on the edge of the insulation plate in which the lock is placed and that the insulation plate has an groove to ensure a correct positioning of the lock when the lock is placed in the groove a cross section that forms the t shape presses the plates avoiding that they travel in the channels at the same time the fold has a flange that when closing the cartridge is arranged on the inside of a first lid causing the closure a lid includes a first cylindrical section attached to a surrounding plate which at an end of which is attached to the cylindrical section has a stop which engages in a notch at the edge of the casing toward the center of the lid on the side where the stop is located there is a second cylindrical section which supports a gasket which performs an airtight seal between the casing and the lid the casing and the lid are secured by a threaded ring in its internal section and grooved by its outer face whose thread is engaged in the casing since the latter has the counterpart of the thread of the ring on the outside of the casing immediately after the ring a surrounding casing is placed which contacts the terminals of the plates in such a way that by employing as many conventional cables attached to the terminals as are inserted into a insulating casing submerged in epoxy resin which protects them the opposite end is attached to a conventional automation control box in order to electrify the plates inside the housing at the opposite end of the casing a second cap is screwed with the same characteristics as the first cap however the automation device comprises a t connection in the cross section of a plug that seals are inserted and has a hole centered through which is a stem forming a single piece with a blade positioned inside the connection the opposite end of said rod activates a flow sensor which is conventionally connected to a pcb electronic board and in the same way the card is connected to a temperature sensor which is placed in the t connection on one side of the stem said sensor measures the temperature of the water flow through the t connection at the same time the water passage activates the stem and the previous measurements are sent to a logical processing unit to automate the process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100408926-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "chemical resistance is especially suitable for sewage or gas and it does not leak due to ion dissolution and has a favorable effect on maintenance"}]</data>
