rces 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100375130-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the past there was a poverty that caused social controversy such as untreated and discharged to the terminal treatment discharge pipe in the untreated state contaminating the water quality of the water supply source or adversely affect the biological growth in the water.the present invention has been invented to prevent the above closed end of the present invention is to be installed in the initial sedimentation tank cold dust chamber to the front end inlet of the body having a fastening flange portion is attached to the hinge portion formed on the upper surface of the body disc it is installed to be opened and closed by means of the connecting pipe through the fastener is installed on the left and right sides of the upper connecting portion between the supports connected to the shaft of the hinge portion the fitting section of the connecting pipe through the support between the buckle is installed in the early stage of rain when a large amount of rainwater flows in at this time as the floats fastened to the left and right connectors and the floats fastened to the disks the disks in the open open state move downwards to the support point to block the inlet formed at the tip of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101758362-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rain gutters 100 installed between the gutters and the roadway and having a gut hole 110 and a mounting jaw 120 formed along the edge of the gutting hole 110 210 formed in the shape of an opened top box and embedded in the ground through the fixing hole 110 and a flange part a vertical part 230 bent upward from an edge of the flange part 220 and a drain hole 240 formed at one side of the superior receiving main body 210 and connected to the drain hole 240 200 having a drain pipe 250 for transferring the stormwater to a sewer pipe buried in the ground a flange 320 formed on an upper edge of the inner tube main body 310 and hooked on the flange 220 an inner cylinder 300 having an upright bent portion formed at an edge of the outer cylinder 200 and having a vertical portion 330 which is in close contact with the inner surface of the vertical portion 230 of the cylinder 200 a support shaft 400 fixed to the front and rear walls of the inner cylinder 300 a cylindrical shaft portion 510 inserted into the inner cylinder 300 and rotatably supported by the support shaft 400 a bucket portion 520 integrally formed on the downstream side of the cylindrical shaft portion 510 a blocking member 500 provided with a count weight portion 530 integrally formed on the upstream side of the shaft portion 510 a stopper 600 provided inside the inner cylinder 300 to prevent the blocking member 500 from turning to the dead point by more than 90 degrees a first engaging member 700 coupled to a downstream side of an inner wall surface of the inner cylinder 300 and having a top surface edge of the bucket part 520 engaged a second latching member 800 coupled to an upper side of the inner wall surface of the inner cylinder 300 and having a bottom edge of the count weight portion 530 engaged on an upper surface thereof and a rectangular frame portion 910 which is seated on the flange portion 320 of the inner cylinder 300 and whose outer wall surface is in close contact with the inner surface of the vertical portion 330 of the inner cylinder 300 and a superior receiving lid 900 provided with a lattice portion 920 formed in a substantially rectangular shape the support shaft 400 is inserted into the shaft hole 410 formed in the front and rear walls of the inner cylinder 300 and the sealant is injected between both ends of the support shaft 400 and the shaft hole 410 the bucket part 520 of the blocking member 500 includes a concave part 522 formed concavely on the upstream side and a bottom part 523 formed of an inclined part 523 formed upwardly inclined from the downstream side end of the concave part 522 a front and rear wall body 524 vertically formed at the front and rear ends of the bottom portion 521 and a locking protrusion 525 protruding in the downstream direction from the inclined portion 523 and a latching jaw 526 protruding in the front rear direction the count weight portion 530 is formed in a rectangular plate shape a weight 531 is embedded in the count weight portion 530 the weight w2 of the count weight portion 530 is heavier than the weight w1 of the bucket portion 520 with respect to the cylindrical shaft portion 510 the support shaft 400 and the cylindrical shaft portion 510 which are rotation points of the bucket portion 520 of the blocking member 500 and the count weight portion 530 are installed at positions displaced toward the count weight portion 530 520 is increased the first latching member 700 includes a latching portion 710 to which the latching jaw portion 525 is caught and a latching portion 720 to which the latching jaw portion 526 is caught the second latching member 800 includes a latching portion 810 for latching the lower surface of the upstream end portion of the counting weight portion 530 and a latching portion 820 for latching the front and rear ends of the counting portion 530 lt rti gt wherein the first latching member 700 and the second latching member 800 are integrally formed in the inner cylinder 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192911-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the present invention has the advantage that the maintenance work for the removal of the contaminant is easy because the contaminants introduced with rainwater is quickly transferred to the main drain pipe without being stuck or blocked in the branch drain pipe as the drainage speed of the rainwater container is improved.1 is a front view showing the structure of the rain canister in accordance with the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "to block the odor flowing back from the sewer and when the amount of rain water is relatively large the rotary drainage guide plate rotates downward to filter the filth by the strainer while smoothing the inflow of rain water odor countercurrent blocking function and dirt sewer rain gutter with manure function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "including a rod and one side is fixedly coupled to both ends of the hinge shaft and the other side is composed of second connecting rods respectively coupled to both side plates of the strainer the strainer is the main weight of the rotating drainage plate if the amount of rainwater flowing into the opening is relatively small by limiting the rotation of the rotary drainage guide plate by the self load of the strainer to close the drain hole to block the odor flowing back from the sewer rain water when the amount of is relatively large the rotation drainage guide plate rotates downward to facilitate the inflow of rain water while the manure the present invention provides a sewer rain gutter having a bad smell counter current blocking function and a dirt filtering function for filtering dirt by a net"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in configuring the odor prevention device 110 to prevent the odor coming up from the ground the odor prevention device 110 includes a prevention body 112 having a seating flange 111 upward to be seated on the bottom surface of the manhole cover 105 the prevention body 112 and the first vertical portion 113 protrudes downward from the mounting flange 111 an inclined portion 114 formed to have a width narrowed inward from an end of the first vertical portion 113 a second vertical portion 115 projecting downward from the end of the inclined portion 114 a plurality of water passages 116 formed to drain a small amount of rainwater to the inclined portion 114 a discharge hole 117 formed to be opened between the second vertical portions 115 to discharge a large amount of rain and garbage deformed by the hydraulic pressure of the sewage to the water hole 116 while being drained down and after completion of drainage to return to the original state to prevent the odor coming up through the water hole 116 fixing the blocking plate 118 of a material having elasticity and excellent return force the discharge hole 117 is a sewer manhole odor prevention device characterized in that it comprises a rotating plate 120 installed so as to block the odor coming up while draining the rain and waste of the opposite"}]</data>
