 is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment inside the main body 1 of the above mentioned flood control equipment after the rescue workers complete the rescue a plurality of high performance submersible pumps 36 are installed in each power pump i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100437577-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the underground equipment is flooded inside the underground structure due to water leakage which causes a decrease in the function of the underground equipment the flooding of the cable connection material causes the shortening of the life and the failure and the leakage of the manhole during the inspection due to the excessive drainage work time there is a problem to reduce the work efficiency .the present invention has been invented in view of the above mentioned problems and prevents leakage by inserting a plurality of sealing wings formed with a plurality of sealing wings inside the duct preventing the failure of cable connection material and improving the efficiency of structure maintenance installation and it is easy to dismantle store and transport and it can be reused which can reduce the cost and the purpose is to prevent leaks more completely by fixing the escape opening prevention device with a tightening bolt on the existing flange part"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "4 this water softener 30 includes a cylindrical water softener body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center it includes a support cylinder 39 fixed to the bottom of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g"}]</data>
