ement housing in which an electric cable connection hole is formed at one side and the bottom surface is concave so as to have a predetermined curvature while the heating element is inserted and wrapped therein an upper cover having an upper surface having a curved flat shape having a predetermined curvature and a lower surface protruding integrally formed with an insertion groove for fitting and coupling an upper end of the heating element housing a lower cover coupled to a lower portion of the upper cover to surround the heating element housing and having a through hole formed at a bottom thereof so that the heating element housing is partially exposed a thermal pad provided in a space between the upper cover and the heating element housing to block heat exchange with the outside a bimetal provided in an inner space of the heating element housing to automatically block a temperature rise of the heating element a heat transfer pad further coupled to a bottom surface of the heat generator housing to expand a heat transfer area of the heat generator housing or to be contacted along a curved surface of the pipe and the electrical cable connection hole of the heating element housing is provided in pairs one side of the connection hole includes a power member is drawn into the housing and the other connection hole includes a lamp member drawn out of the housing to indicate the operating state of the heating element strip connecting holes for connecting the strip of the pipe band is further formed at both edges of the upper cover the lamp member has a structure in which the lamp is coupled to the end of the bellows type cable having a predetermined length the heat transfer pad has a rectangular flexible metal belt structure as a whole pads are integrally formed at regular intervals on both left and right sides of the body portion constituting the center line of the metal belt structure and connecting strips of pipe bands to the end of the pad portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200177518-Y1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "34 and the water supply connection pipe 29 is configured to be screwed to connect without welding can not only block the penetration of harmful substances to the human body due to welding but also to form a simple structure for assembly work.as described above according to the water tank for cold and warm water purifier according to the embodiment of the present invention after forming a flange to the outside at the portion where the upper cylinder and the lower cylinder is in contact the inner space is formed by welding the upper cylinder the temperature sensor fitting hole and the cold water discharge port formed on the upper surface of the upper surface of the sensor are combined with the temperature sensor and the outflow pipe by the screw projections"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5841246-Y2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "time until freezing buried type 7 hours 06 minutes conventional exposed type 5 hours 89 minutes invented exposed type 8 hours 28 minutes notes average wind speed 47jg 9 outside temperature 18.11 as mentioned above the present invention makes it easier to install above ground water meters makes them relatively inexpensive improves the cold resistance of water pipes and stop valves that can cause freeze damage and eliminates the need for conventional underground water meters"}, {"pat_id": "US-5044824-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "while the pressure is maintained the resin is cured to form a relatively hard tight fitting rigid pipe lining which effectively seals any cracks and repairs any pipe or joint deterioration to prevent further leakage either into or out of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101746200-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "a first step of preparing a housing made of a binary alloy of copper and tin the surface of which is coated with a corrosion inhibitor a second step of manufacturing a plurality of zinc assemblies a third step of installing a plurality of fluororesin members in the housing and the zinc assembly between the fluororesin members and and a fourth step of installing a cap and a rotary flange at upper and lower ends of the housing in the first step a melt casting step of charging a copper alloy and a tin into a crucible to produce a molten copper alloy a gas discharging step of extracting and discharging the gas from the molten copper alloy a casting molding step of casting the cast copper alloy by injecting the copper alloy molten metal from which the gas is discharged into the casting mold and and a corrosion inhibitor coating step of coating the surface of the casting with a corrosion inhibitor the second step comprises a jig seating step of placing a truncated conical jig having a hollow portion in a vacuum chamber on a support plate a zinc burning step of burning solid zinc into liquid zinc in the vacuum chamber a zinc injection step of injecting the liquid zinc into the jig a zinc cooling step of cooling the liquid zinc in the vacuum chamber at room temperature a zinc ingot obtaining step of separating the jig from the support plate to obtain a truncated cone shaped zinc ingot an ingot first processing step of vertically cutting an inclined surface of the zinc ingot to form a columnar zinc ingot a fluid inlet formed with a cylindrical groove on an upper surface and a lower surface of the zinc ingot and having a fluid inlet and a rim portion a fluid passing portion through which the fluid passes and a fluid outlet an ingot second processing step of dividing the zinc ingot into parts and an ingot third processing step of forming a fitting groove in a rim portion formed in the fluid inflow portion and forming a fitting rim in a rim portion formed in the fluid outflow portion at a position rotated at a constant angle in the circumferential direction so as to be disposed to be shifted from the fitting groove step forming a plurality of flow channels through which the fluid flows in the fluid through part to form a zinc plate and the plurality of zinc plates are combined in a state where the flow channels included in the respective zinc plates are arranged to be shifted from each other by fitting the fitting grooves and the tabs respectively formed in the fluid inlet and the fluid outlet of the different zinc plates wherein the copper tin alloy is a zinc iron zinc alloy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101746200-B1", "para_id": "claim_17", "text": "a first step of preparing a housing made of a binary alloy of copper and tin the surface of which is coated with a corrosion inhibitor a second step of manufacturing a plurality of zinc assemblies a third step of installing a plurality of fluororesin members in a housing having a surface coated with a corrosion inhibitor and the zinc assembly between the fluororesin members and and a fourth step of installing a cap and a rotary flange at upper and lower ends of the housing in the first step a melt casting step of charging a copper alloy and a tin into a crucible to produce a molten copper alloy a gas discharging step of extracting and discharging the gas from the molten copper alloy a casting molding step of casting the cast copper alloy by injecting the copper alloy molten metal from which the gas is discharged into the casting mold and and a corrosion inhibitor coating step of coating the surface of the casting with a corrosion inhibitor the second step comprises a step of baking the solid zinc into liquid zinc in a vacuum chamber a zinc injection step of injecting the liquid zinc into a molding die of a molding member connected to a cover member and a hinge in the vacuum chamber a zinc cover step of placing the cover member on the forming member and covering the forming frame a zinc cooling step of cooling the liquid zinc in the vacuum chamber at room temperature a zinc ingot obtaining step of obtaining a zinc ingot by separating cold zinc from the mold an ingot first processing step of cutting the zinc ingot to form a cylindrical ingot of zinc a fluid inlet formed with a cylindrical groove on an upper surface and a lower surface of the zinc ingot and having a fluid inlet and a rim portion a fluid passing portion through which the fluid passes and a fluid outlet an ingot second processing step of dividing the zinc ingot into parts and an ingot third processing step of forming a fitting groove in a rim portion formed in the fluid inflow portion and forming a fitting rim in a rim portion formed in the fluid outflow portion at a position rotated at a constant angle in the circumferential direction so as to be disposed to be shifted from the fitting groove step forming a plurality of flow channels through which the fluid flows in the fluid through part to form a zinc plate and the plurality of zinc plates are combined in a state where the flow channels included in the respective zinc plates are arranged to be shifted from each other by fitting the fitting grooves and the tabs respectively formed in the fluid inlet and the fluid outlet of the different zinc plates zinc plate bonding step wherein the corrosion inhibiting ion water treatment apparatus comprises a copper tin alloy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101746200-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the first step includes a melt casting step of charging copper and tin into a crucible to produce a molten copper alloy a gas discharging step of extracting and discharging the gas from the molten copper alloy a casting molding step of casting the cast copper alloy by injecting the copper alloy molten metal from which the gas is discharged into the casting mold and a corrosion inhibitor coating step of coating the surface of the casting with a corrosion inhibitor wherein the second step comprises the steps of placing a jig in a frustum shape having a hollow portion in a vacuum chamber on a support plate a zinc burning step of burning solid zinc into liquid zinc in the vacuum chamber a zinc injection step of injecting the liquid zinc into the jig a zinc cooling step of cooling the liquid zinc in the vacuum chamber at room temperature a zinc ingot obtaining step of separating the jig from the support plate to obtain a truncated cone shaped zinc ingot an ingot first processing step of vertically cutting an inclined surface of the zinc ingot to form a columnar zinc ingot a fluid inlet formed with a cylindrical groove on an upper surface and a lower surface of the zinc ingot and having a fluid inlet and a rim portion a fluid passing portion through which the fluid passes and a fluid outlet an ingot second processing step of dividing the zinc ingot into parts and an ingot third processing step of forming a fitting groove in a rim portion formed in the fluid inflow portion and forming a fitting rim in a rim portion formed in the fluid outflow portion at a position rotated at a constant angle in the circumferential direction so as to be disposed to be shifted from the fitting groove step forming a plurality of flow channels through which the fluid flows in the fluid through part to form a zinc plate and a plurality of zinc plates coupled to each other in a state where the flow channels included in the respective zinc plates are arranged to be shifted from each other by fitting the fitting grooves and the tabs respectively formed in the fluid inlet and the fluid outlet of the different zinc plates and a zinc plate bonding step in which the copper tin alloy is used to manufacture a corrosion inhibiting ion water treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101746200-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the present invention also provides a method for manufacturing a copper alloy comprising the steps of preparing a housing made of a binary alloy of copper and tin the surface of which is coated with a corrosion inhibitor a second step of manufacturing a plurality of zinc assemblies a third step of installing a plurality of fluororesin members in a housing having a surface coated with a corrosion inhibitor and the zinc assembly between the fluororesin members and a fourth step of in