flow channels included in the respective zinc plates are arranged to be shifted from each other by fitting the fitting grooves and the tabs respectively formed in the fluid inlet and the fluid outlet of the different zinc plates and a zinc plate bonding step in which the copper tin alloy is used to manufacture a corrosion inhibiting ion water treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101957713-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "then steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe through the steam inlet at a secondary pressure and steam is supplied to the inside of the maintenance pipe pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe so as to be tightly fixed cooling the repair pipe closely fixed to the inner surface of the conduit to separate the sealing cap from both ends of the repair pipe preparing a warming case for disposing a fusing heat plate that generates heat when power is applied in an inner space and preheating the fusing heat plate to be heated to a predetermined temperature inside the warming case and and a step of thermally fusing the repair pipe to the connection flange by bringing the fusing heat plate separated from the thermal insulation case into contact with the end of the repair pipe protruded from the conduit the step of pressurizing and expanding the maintenance pipe may include passing the other end of the traction wire having one end connected to the sealing cap through a pair of connection rings provided on the protection guard and a step of press fitting and fixing the end portion of the maintenance pipe to the end portion of the maintenance pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in the present invention the composite panel 10 can be firmly assembled by fitting the composite panel 10 to the skeleton constituting each component panel of the large tank so that the connection part of the composite panel 10 is caused by internal deformation pressure due to bending deformation or temperature change"}, {"pat_i