ng portion between the supports connected to the shaft of the hinge portion the fitting section of the connecting pipe through the support between the buckle is installed in the early stage of rain when a large amount of rainwater flows in at this time as the floats fastened to the left and right connectors and the floats fastened to the disks the disks in the open open state move downwards to the support point to block the inlet formed at the tip of the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102772254-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "are discharged downward as is thereby preventing water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "20 0433333 installed on the top of the casing casing developed for waterworks to block the inflow of external pollutants to make waterproof to prevent the inflow of rainwater into the inside of the city when submerged can be cleaned with a simple method when cleaning with compressed air of the number of wells for an antifouling structure is disclosed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902536-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a rainwater receiver connected to a sewage main pipe by a connection pipe a rainwater collecting body having a rainwater inlet at an upper portion and a rainwater outlet at a lower side of the rainwater outlet and a bellows coupling portion embedded in an inner portion of the rainwater outlet and a flange part extending from the cylindrical body and having a coupling part formed at a rear end thereof and a flange part coupled to the coupling part wherein the cylindrical body and the wrinkle portion are configured to be smaller than the inner diameter of the rainwater outlet and the flange portion is configured to be larger than the inner diameter of the rainwater outlet wherein the bellows is inserted into the rainwater outlet the flange portion is configured to be coupled to the bellows coupling portion in a bolt fastening manner the bellows an insertion body formed in a disk shape and embedded in the inner side of the rainwater outlet and having a plurality of bolt holes at predetermined intervals along the circumference a nut inserted into a front end portion of the bolt through hole a flange seating part formed on a rear surface of the coupling body so as to be exposed to the inside of the rainwater receiver main body the flange part being seated and connected to a rear end of the bolt through hole and a plurality of protruding fins extending integrally forward from the coupling body and spaced apart from each other along the circumference of the coupling body a packing material is formed on a front surface of the flange portion to prevent leakage between the flange portion and the coupling body when the flange portion and the coupling body are coupled the bellows coupling part is integrally formed on a rear surface of the coupling body along a circumferential direction and includes a friction protrusion for improving frictional force between the flange part and the coupling body when the coupling body and the coupling body are coupled to each other in addition wherein the flange portion is configured to be coupled to the coupling body by being inserted into the bolt through hole through the flange portion and being fastened to the nut while the flange portion is seated on the flange seating portion wherein the flange seating portion is formed between a protruding ring integrally protruding rearward from the rear surface of the coupling body and a rear surface of the coupling body wherein the friction protrusions are formed in an arc shape so as to connect a plurality of neighboring through holes among the plurality of bolt through holes the upper end of the cylindrical body is longer than the lower end the flange portion a plurality of first bolt holes are formed through the circumference of the disc a plurality of fitting protrusions are formed on the front surface of the disc and a step is formed on the inner side of the disc to accommodate the coupling piece in a circumferential direction rear flange and a plurality of second bolt holes are formed along the circumferential direction and a fitting hole is formed in the fitting hole the packing flange being formed on the front surface of the front flange rti gt wherein the flange portion is attached to the flange portion by an adhesive in a state where the coupling piece is seated on the stepped portion and the fitting flange is engaged with the fitting flange so that the front flange and the rear flange are combined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902536-B1", "para_id": "claim_9", "text": "a rainwater collecting body having a rainwater inlet at an upper portion and a rainwater outlet at a lower side of the rainwater outlet and a bellows coupling portion embedded in an inner portion of the rainwater outlet and a bellows extending from the cylindrical body and having a coupling part formed at a rear end thereof and a flange part coupled to the coupling part the method comprising the steps of connecting the connection pipes to the sewage main pipe inserting the rear end connection pipe into the rainwater receiver main body through the rainwater outlet port and then retracting and connecting the rear end connection pipe to the fitting portion of the connection pipe with the connection pipe connected to the sewage main pipe inserting the bellows into the rainwater receiver main body through the rainwater inflow port and inserting the bellows through the rainwater outlet port into the rainwater receiver main body and inserting the cylindrical body into the reheater end connection pipe to connect the bellows and connecting and fixing mortar to the space formed between the cylindrical body and the wrinkle part and the rainwater outflow port after fixing the flange part to the bellows coupling part by the bolt fastening method the bellows an insertion body formed in a disk shape and embedded in the inner side of the rainwater outlet and having a plurality of bolt holes at predetermined intervals along the circumference a nut inserted into a front end portion of the bolt through hole a flange seating part formed on a rear surface of the coupling body so as to be exposed to the inside of the rainwater receiver main body the flange part being seated and connected to a rear end of the bolt through hole and a plurality of protruding fins extending integrally forward from the coupling body and spaced apart from each other along the circumference of the coupling body a packing material is formed on a front surface of the flange portion to prevent leakage between the flange portion and the coupling body when the flange portion and the coupling body are coupled the bellows coupling part is integrally formed on a rear surface of the coupling body along a circumferential direction and includes a friction protrusion for improving frictional force between the flange part and the coupling body when the coupling body and the coupling body are coupled to each other in addition wherein the flange portion is configured to be coupled to the coupling body by being inserted into the bolt through hole through the flange portion and being fastened to the nut while the flange portion is seated on the flange seating portion wherein the flange seating portion is formed between a protruding ring integrally protruding rearward from the rear surface of the coupling body and a rear surface of the coupling body wherein the friction protrusions are formed in an arc shape so as to connect between a plurality of adjacent through holes of the plurality of bolt through holes the upper end of the cylindrical body is longer than the lower end the flange portion a plurality of first bolt holes are formed through the circumference of the disc a plurality of fitting protrusions are formed on the front surface of the disc and a step is formed on the inner side of the disc to accommodate the coupling piece in a circumferential direction rear flange and a plurality of second bolt holes are formed along the circumferential direction and a fitting hole is formed in the fitting hole the packing flange being formed on the front surface of the front flange rti gt wherein the flange portion is attached to the flange portion by an adhesive in a state where the coupling piece is seated on the stepped portion and the fitting flange is engaged with the fitting flange so that the front flange and the rear flange are combined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "by fitting the top plates together to form a sealed rainwater reservoir the purpose is to reduce the overall weight according to the reduction of the cross sectional area of the block itself compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure formed by the column integrally formed by the column"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "rainwater storage tank with a storage block of the weight reduction structure for the present invention in the rainwater storage tank to be buried underground to temporarily store rainwater to discharge when necessary both sides are closed and both sides are the upper and lower sides while the opening is formed openings are formed in each of the four sides of the outer wall block structure in which the outer wall is formed by using the outer wall block of the open hexahedral structure and the storage block of the hexahedral structure having the upper and lower sides is installed and the opening of the outer wall block and the storage block are at the same time a separate block connection member is coupled to each one edge portion of the outer wall block and the storage block in contact with each other to form a connection between the blocks and each of the outer wall block and the storage block interconnected by the block connection member by fitting the top plate on the top and forming a sealed rainwater reservoir compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure in which the plate and the lower plate are integrally formed by the pillar there is an excellent effect of reducing the overall weight by reducing the cross sectional area of the block itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100729127-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "in addition since the connection of the drain pipe 40 and the water collecting pipe 10 is fixed to the fitting groove 13 formed at the other end of the water collecting pipe 10 the effect of preventing leakage of rainwater and sewage through the seam portion"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5343029-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "therefore it is possible to prevent the display tag 1 from being placed at a low position so as to block the upper portion of the bucket body 22 and prevent the display tag 1 from obstructing the flow of rainwater in the rainwater 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624009-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "after fitting to one end of the fitting pipe 90 to be fitted one end of the coupling pipe 90 is fitted into the coupling portion 70 the long bolt 50 is fastened by tightening the long bolt 50 to the long bolt hole 43 by zooming it is in close contact with the outer circumferential surface of the connecting pipe 90 and the connecting portion 70 is made more securely watertight.each of the semi circular arc type connecting members configured as described above is more firmly fixed by the use of the assembled assembly device and the long bolts that cause tension thereby preventing the inflow of external soil or foreign matter and leakage of internal sewage or rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101841998-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of horizontal support frames mounted on the upper surface of the u shaped drainage installed on the road side spaced apart from each other a side frame installed at both ends of the horizontal support frame and a plurality of drain holes through which water is discharged and a drain frame installed between the transverse support frames and discharging water a first fixed bracket fixed to a lower surface of one end of the lateral support frame a second fixed bracket fixed to the lower surface on the other end side of the transverse support frame a connection support rod fixedly installed to connect the first fixed bracket and the second fixed bracket to each other a plate like elastic member fixedly mounted on an upper surface of the connection support rod and having an elastic force a drainage hole formed in the drainage frame to block or open the drainage hole so as to allow the rainwater to fall into the drainage passage or to prevent the odor from escaping to the outside wherein the horizontal support frame is provided at a central portion formed at the center in the longitudinal direction of the grating body portion and at outer side edges of the two drainage frames formed outside the widthwise portion of the center portion the downwardly bent portions of the downwardly bent portions formed by bending downward from both sides of the lateral support frame provided at the center portion are formed in a lowered height of the downward bent portion formed by bending downward from both sides of the lateral support frame is shorter the backflow prevention plate is supported at an end portion of a downwardly bent portion of the horizontal support frame having one end portion at the center and the other end is supported at an end portion of a downwardly bent portion of the horizontal support frame provided at the outer peripheral side portions of the drainage frame and is inclined downwardly from the central portion toward the magnetic field portion wherein the backflow prevention plate is provided with a pivot shaft at one end side so as to be inserted into the first and second fixed brackets and a fitting hole in which the coaxial shaft is fitted is formed the first and second fixed brackets are formed such that the height of the outline grooves formed at the central portion is shorter than the height of the outline grooves formed at the edge portions a grating structure provided with a malodor backflow prevention plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102758462-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole body 3 having an upper opening formed at the top that can be opened and closed by means of an upper cover 2 and having an inlet and an outlet formed at the bottom respectively to which an inlet pipe 100 and an outlet pipe 200 for introducing sewage or rainwater are respectively connected a cover pipe 5 made of metal material and having a support step 51 formed on the inner surface to support the upper cover 2 while being supported and having a support flange 52 formed integrally in the outer surface of the lower surface in an outward direction in a manhole 1 which includes a fixed pipe 7 disposed at the lower portion of the cover pipe 5 made of metal or synthetic resin as a material and having upper and lower penetrations to allow sewage water to pass through the outer circumference of which is closely fitted to the inner surface of the upper opening h of the manhole body 3 and which is provided with a fall prevention structure 71 on the inner circumference to support and receive a pedestrian in the event of a fall and a fixed flange 72 formed to extend outward on the upper outer circumference and a height adjustment means 6 configured to adjust the height of the cover pipe 5 through filling mortar 64 the above manhole body 3 is it comprises an upper assembly block 31 having the upper opening h formed at the upper side and the open lower side a lower assembly block 32 having the inlet and outlet holes respectively formed at the lower side and having upper and lower parts penetrated an intermediate assembly block 33 vertically stacked between the upper assembly block 31 and the lower assembly block 32 and having upper and lower parts penetrated and a bottom assembly block 34 vertically stacked below the lower assembly block 32 and having an open upper side on the upper surface of the above floor assembly block 34 the upper and lower surfaces of the above lower assembly block 32 the upper and lower surfaces of the above intermediate assembly block 33 and the lower surface of the above upper assembly block 31 the connecting projections 41 and connecting grooves 42 are formed in a ring shape and are fitted and connected to each other the above mentioned binding protrusion 41 and the above mentioned binding groove 42 are it is composed of two sets of inner and outer diameters that are different and arranged with a gap between them centered on the center of the above manhole body 3 on the lower surface of the lower assembly block 32 the lower surface of the intermediate assembly block 33 and the lower surface of the upper assembly block 31 the upper part of the guide rod 43 having a vertical length is fixed in place on the upper surface of the above floor assembly block 34 the upper surface of the above lower assembly block 32 and the upper surface of the above middle assembly block 33 each guide receiving groove 44 is formed to accommodate the guide rod 43 by fitting the lower portion thereof between the above fixed flange 72 and the manhole body 3 when the above filling mortar 64 is formed it is embedded inside with the manhole body 3 placed in the facility space formed underground anchor screw rods 61 embedded in the edge of the upper opening h of the manhole body 3 sequentially penetrate the fixed flange 72 and the support flange 52 the above fixed flange 72 is supported by a lower support nut 62 that is screw connected to the anchor screw rod 61 on its bottom surface and the above supported flange 52 is fixed by an upper fixing nut 63 that is screw connected to the anchor screw rod 61 on its top surface so that the cover pipe 5 and the above fixed pipe 7 are arranged while forming a gap at the edge of the upper opening h of the manhole body 3 a manhole characterized in that the filling mortar 64 is injected and filled between the fixed flange 72 and the manhole body 3 and cured and an elastic spring structure 8 is embedded inside the filling mortar 64 to elastically offset the shock vibration load applied from the upper portion of the cover pipe 5 between the fixed flange 72 and the manhole body 3"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4360658-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "2 for the purpose of conveyance.it is a partial cross section figure which shows another tip shape of the support body of the frame skeleton block of this invention.it is a top view which shows the outer periphery fitting part and outer periphery fitting receiving part which were provided in the frame skeleton block of this invention.it is sectional drawing which shows the conventional water storage facilities such as a common rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4360658-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "1 the skeleton block 4 shown in this embodiment includes a base 41 having a flat plate shape and a substantially square shape hereinafter simply referred to as a square and one diagonal of two diagonal lines on the base 41"}]</data>
