  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102882673-B1", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "according to the grating for a rainwater drainage ditch capable of variably adjusting the drainage area for flood prevention according to the embodiment of the present specification as described above in normal times when it does not rain or when the amount of rainfall is small the elevating grating 50 that is connected to a rectangular sub frame 40 so as to be able to be lifted up and down is lowered to the initial position by pulling down the lifting pieces 140 180 formed on the left and right side walls thereof along the guide rails 120 170 formed on the inner surface of the sub frame 110 corresponding to the lifting pieces thereby maintaining the same height as the fixed grating 60 that is secured to one side of the grating frame 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171293-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "at this time since the amount of water is small so that you do not have to worry about inflow of the earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking the sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing the cross sectional area of the drainage pipe and preventing the burnout of the sewage terminal treatment plant while reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100885534-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 includes a valve means 24 for guiding discharge through the outlet the valve means the buckle 24a to rise and fall according to the rain water level stored in the rain gutter main body a transmission means for transmitting the lifting of the float receiving the lifting force of the float through the transmission means the second it includes an opening and closing plate 24d for opening and closing the outflow hole the transmission means is connected to the buckle lifting bar 24b to move up and down with the ball both sides are rotatably coupled between the two sides while the lifting rod and the opening and closing plate is hinged to the baffle to lift the lifting bar rainfall reduction facility characterized in that it comprises an opening and closing rod 24c for opening and closing the opening and closing plate while rotating under the guidance of the hinge according to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "at this time since the amount of water is small so that you do not have to worry about inflow of the earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking the sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing the cross sectional area of the drainage pipe and preventing the burnout of the sewage terminal treatment plant while reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101604772-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in the lower part of the base frame section a support frame section fixed to the ground and rotatably supporting the base frame section and a tilt adjusting section for lifting one side of the base frame section are further provided which is an element of the hydrological cycle for the target sample under constant rainfall conditions it is possible to easily measure the hydrological quantity by calculating the underflow discharge and groundwater discharge and it is possible to carry out the detailed test and verification that reflects the watershed characteristics by considering the watershed slope and the upstream outflow of the watershed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a treatment structure provided in a substantially empty box shape and divided into a pretreatment tank a filtration tank and a backwash tank from one side to the other by first and second sidewalls having vertical insides a screen means installed in the pretreatment tank to filter suspended matter and garbage in the rainfall effluent flowing into the pretreatment tank and a filtration means installed in the filtration tank to precipitate heavy non point pollutants in the pretreatment water flowing into the filtration tank and adsorb and filter light non point pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200466978-Y1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3 wherein the rain inlet opening and closing unit rainfall inlet opening and closing cover that can open and close the rainwater inlet hole while moving along the rainwater storage tube it is connected to the rain inlet opening and closing cover and includes a lifting member which is lifted in accordance with the water level of rain when the rainwater level rises the elevating member is raised in accordance with the rainwater level and thus the rainwater inflow opening closing cover is raised to open the rainwater inflow hole when the rainwater level is low the elevating member is lowered according to the rainwater level the rainwater inlet hole opening and closing cover is lowered to close the rainwater inlet hole characterized in that the rainwater storage device using a digging hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200234791-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in this case the amount is small so when you do not have to worry about the inflow of earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing cross sectional area reduction of the drainage pipe and burning of the pump in the sewage treatment plant and reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4637561-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition the inner lid is equipped with a pressure relief mechanism and a rainwater dropping mechanism so that it is hardly affected by water increase during abnormal rainfall such as typhoons and therefore damage due to lifting of the manhole cover is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4637561-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "in addition it is hardly affected by water increase during abnormal rainfall such as a typhoon and therefore damage due to lifting of the manhole cover 6 is prevented so that a normal state can always be maintained"}]</data>
</edge>
