  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in particular in addition to the heavy rainfall due to the rainy season and typhoons the recent changes in global weather patterns caused by el nino and la nia have caused local and local concentration rainfall frequently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "treatment facility for early rainfall using water retention and its methodthe present invention relates to an excellent treatment facility utilizing a disaster reservoir and a method of forming the same and more specifically to remove impurities in the initial rainwater and to settle the foreign matters to prevent the entry of foreign substances and debris into the reservoir and rivers it induces infiltration and natural purification to maintain the supply of groundwater smoothly and at the same time separates rainwater flowing into the initial rainfall and rainfall discharges or fresh water and minimizes the amount of rainwater remaining in the reservoir to corrupt or pest the present invention relates to a rainwater treatment facility and a method of forming the rainwater that can block breeding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "in the method of recycling rainwater the rainwater recycling method includes mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block inflow of large solids into the rainwater inlet grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall recycled from the upper lower trench conduit 50 60 storm water recycling method comprising the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "on the other hand the storm recycling method the step of mounting on the surface of the road 8 to block the inflow of large solids to the storm inflow grating 10 a solids removal step installed on the bottom of the rainwater inlet grating 10 to remove the medium solids introduced with the rainwater a porous filtration screen step of removing fine solids in the rainwater that has undergone the solids removal step a rainwater storage step of storing rainwater introduced through the porous filtration step a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater rainfall flowing from the lower trench conduit 60 consists of the step of introducing into the groundwater layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6132141-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "3 is an example of a sewer rainwater switching type storage facility according to the present invention and is a diagram in the case of allowing overflow discharge to a river in the middle of rainfall.fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 it is installed to open and close on the upper surface of the treatment tank when the amount of rainfall exceeding the processing capacity the inner lid to block the top of the treatment tank to induce the rainfall to flow into the discharge box road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function further comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in this case the headquarters is a control center that is provided with a main computer server that receives the processing status information such as initial rainwater inflow and outflow by the communication device 70 and issues a command thereby providing comprehensive operation management and monitoring functions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781302-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "therefore the present invention stores the initial rainwater containing a large number of non point pollutants in urban areas with high pollution during rainfall and stored in the initial rainwater excellent storage 10 to enable the deposition of sand particles generated at this time such as branches and plastic bags when water level is measured by sensor detection while blocking the inflow of floating garbage the rainwater inflow switch is automatically adjusted to block the inflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938853-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however the sewage blocking block for sewer is made of pe so that the material is easy to move inside the conduit and is easily assembled but the construction is easy but in the case of the pe block if strong water pressure acts during heavy rain or rainfall the pe block due to the strength or durability of the water pressure can not withstand the damage of the installed pe block the connection between the pe block may be a problem that the coupling part or the whole by the fastening protrusion is lost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101501179-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "especially it is difficult to secure the site because it requires a separate site to install the contact tank and it is difficult to select the site"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102257819-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water purification biofilm unit is further installed at the discharge end ex wherein the water purification biofilm unit includes a dam dam installed to block drainage by blocking a portion of the discharge end ex a purification groove hom formed in a predetermined depth at a predetermined interval in a part of the length of the dam dam a pair of vertical frames ver standing and fixed at both ends of the width center of the dam dam a horizontal frame hoz connecting and fixing the upper end of the vertical frame ver a double shaft winch wic fixed on the horizontal frame hoz to be positioned directly above each purification groove hom a drum dr fixed to both shafts of the winch wic and wound around a wire wr in the integrated management system for automatic monitoring of sewage pipes having a net shaped biofilm purification tank 1000 in which an end of the wire wr is fixed inserted into the purification groove hom and filled with a purification ball therein the biofilm cleaning container 1000 includes a pair of side frames 1100 an upper frame 1200 assembled and fixed to an upper end of the side frame 1100 and a tip of the side frame 1100 and the upper frame 1200 and a front frame 1300 and a rear frame 1400 respectively assembled at the rear end the side frame 1100 the upper frame 1200 the front frame 1300 and the rear frame 1400 are fixed with a wire mesh net w to the rectangular frame f so that water flowing along the river can escape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "manual valve operation method is unrealistic because the manager must operate the valve in the early stage of rainfall and it has the disadvantage of high cost and difficulty of maintenance such as failure when using devices such as flow meters and sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100925049-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore an object of the present invention for solving the problems as described above is formed in the u trench trench length drain groove portion on the surface of the surface block used for paving the road at intervals of 3 10cm drainage distance is excellent water is accumulated in the drainage process or water flows on the road surface because the rainfall is drained to the lower part of the road at the same time through the drain grooves of individual blocks installed on the entire road without having to flow into long separate rain gutters or sides"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure integrally formed by it has an excellent effect such as reducing the cross sectional area of the block itself to thereby reduce the overall weight"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in addition in the case of dam type power plants it is often unavoidable to avoid significant head fluctuations due to imbalances between rainfall and water usage and such power plants are sometimes called variable head power plants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226649-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the control unit may further include changing to the constant priority supply mode when the water level of the rainwater storage tank is lower than the reference value in the rainwater priority supply operation mode.smart system according to an embodiment of the present invention can efficiently supply water by using a constant and rain water it is possible to save a constant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101504881-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "further in the present invention the floating screen and the movable screen connected thereto are installed in front of the orifice so that the movable screen covers the orifice for a predetermined time during which the water level in the rainfall chamber rises during rains thereby temporarily filtering the foreign substances over the fence it is possible to temporarily block or reduce the inflow of foreign matter into the sewage treatment plant through the connection pipe at the time of bar and rainfall.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101644965-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the river water inflow section includes a first river water inflow control apparatus and a second river inflow comprising the element introduced into the pretreatment unit is pretreated and then flows out to the storage unit f the water quality purification unit g or treated water pits the water quality purification unit g includes a first stage water purification unit that receives the river water or the rainwater effluent from the storage unit to purify and discharge the river water or the rainwater effluent from the storage unit and a water purification unit that receives the river water or rainwater discharged from the first a second stage water purification unit inflow control unit and a treated water foot inflow control unit wherein at least one of a fixed phase media and a fluid phase media is filled in the first stage water purification unit and the second stage water purification unit in the case of rainfall the second stage water purification unit inflow control unit is closed the treated water inflow control unit is opened and the first and second soil inflow prevention devices are opened to open the rainwater inflow the first river water inflow control device and the second river water inflow control device are closed so that the river water inflow part b does not receive the river water in the non wastewater treatment the second stage water purification unit inflow control unit is opened the treated water inflow control unit is closed the first soil inflow prevention device and the second earth inflow prevention device are closed to block the rainwater inflow water inflow part a and the first river water inflow control device and the second river inflow control device are closed does not enter the inflow section b at the end of the rainfall the first soil inflow prevention device and the second soil inflow prevention device are closed to block the rainwater inflow water inflow part a and the first river water inflow control device and the second river inflow control device so that the river water inflow part b does not receive the river water wherein the first stage water purification unit is filled with a stationary phase material and a fluid phase filter material wherein the second stage water purification unit is filled with a stationary phase filter medium the preprocessing section includes a needlepoint portion c a screen portion d and a dispensing portion e the distribution section e distributes the raw water treated by the settling section and the screen section d to the storage section f the water quality purification section g or the treated water feet the dispensing unit distributes the raw water flowing out of the pre treatment unit to the storage unit f at the time of rainfall distributes the raw water discharged from the pre treatment unit to the water quality purification unit g the dispensing unit e includes a dispensing tank for introducing and storing the raw water treated by the settling unit and the screen unit d a measuring unit for measuring the quality of the raw water and a raw water source for the water quality purification unit g a water purification unit inflow control unit for controlling inflow and a storage unit inflow control unit for controlling the inflow of raw water into the storage unit f wherein the water quality purification unit inflow control unit and the storage unit inflow control unit are respectively closed when the water quality of the raw water measured by the measurement unit is a water quality capable of being discharged to the river is discharged through a bypass pipe not the storage section characterized in that when the quantity of raw water measured by the measuring section exceeds the treatment capacity of the water quality purification section or the storage section the excess quantity is discharged through the bypass pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when the wind is blown the odor preventing curtain is opened and the odor is generated.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned disadvantages of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a non powered flow rate control device for preventing malodorous flow which comprises a flow rate control device which is detachably attached to a distal end portion of a sewer pipe and it is possible to collect all the high initial initial storms generated at the beginning of the sewage or rainfall that flow in the usual way into the sewage subtraction channel and the rain that flows in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall it is possible to prevent the overflowing of the stormwater by reducing the outflow section of the sewage and to naturally induce the slurry moving along with the storm into the river to prevent the accumulation of the slurry on the sewage drainage pipe which is in close contact with the inner side wall surfaces of the flow rate regulating device while being rotated up and down odor proof packing is installed on the wall to block off odors generated in the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101192404-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition according to the water source protection and non point source reduction control system using the green dam according to the present invention by controlling the discharge valve by remote control from the central control unit to freely regulate the discharge size of the outlet the green dam is secured after the rainfall rainwater can be continuously discharged and in the dry season the size of the outlet can be further narrowed to obtain the effect of preventing the dryness of the river as the water always flows or is absorbed by the aquifer.1 is a side cross sectional view showing the structure of a conventional treatment facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101253532-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition the present invention is to solve the problem that it is difficult to determine the situation whether the rainwater runoff is a problem or if the rainfall is an excess of capacity if the rainfall is sustained urban flooding occurs in the city by installing and remotely monitoring the sewage section it is possible to prevent the flooding of the city more effectively by remotely controlling the floodgate of the drainage pumping station as well as the initial storm drain.1 is an exemplary view showing the current state of domestic sewage treatment facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "2 in order to reduce the resistance to the flow of the initial storm that flows into the plates 121 and 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the past rainfall data of the river basin and the operation history data of the pump are output to the water level prediction device 1 via the database interface 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101763664-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "as described above since the entrance of the manhole block is usually exposed on the road the wastewater of the road may flow into the manhole block at the time of rainfall and the sewage flowing in the sewer pipe may flow into the manhole block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a body 10 provided with a collecting part 11 therein it is constructed between the road and the sidewalk including one or more inlet 12 and the permeable hole 13 formed on opposite sides of the body the inflow hole 12 is formed at the same height as the road surface of the road on one side facing the road side of the body so that the initial rainfall and contaminants flowing along the road surface of the body flows into the catchment of the body the perforation hole 13 is lower than the inlet hole on the other side of the body so that the initial rainfall and the contaminants introduced into the catchment unit is permeated to the bottom of the walkway to induce purification of the contaminants formed at the same height the body is a block body 10 2 provided with a hollow water collecting part 11 an inflow hole 12 and a permeation