nderground to prevent flood maintain groundwater level at a certain level to prevent ground stabilization and river pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100298244-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in order to solve the above problems the present invention by installing a sedimentation basin is divided into a predetermined size in the sewer and coriander site sedimented pollutants and sludge flowing along the stream to block the flow of the stream compartmentally and then easily sediment first to protect the water quality of rivers and lakes second to prevent the destruction of aquatic ecosystems due to the inflow of soils and sands third to prevent aesthetic and sanitary defects due to sedimentation of soil and journey during rainfall and flooding fourthly the dredging operation is very effective and economical compared to the existing method is to provide a stream water purification apparatus by precipitation and dredging and its method"}]</data>
