  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100744631-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "hydrologic control unit for adjusting the connected via the plurality of chlorine ion meter and wired and wireless communication means and stores the concentration data received from the chlorine ion meter and to identify the variation in the water quality compared to the comparative chlorine ion concentration data stored in the database and stores the result a main server for outputting and transmitting to a remote place and a management server connected to the main server through a wired wireless communication means and controlling the operation of the water level or the sewage treatment plant of the reservoir into which the initial rainwater flows in accordance with the change in the water quality of the initial rainwater transmitted from the main server"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "in addition regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101346104-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the second vertical plate extending a certain length directly below the lower surface of the deck and relative to the permeable concrete bottom layer of the reservoir portion than the outer wall and a second filtration plate installed to be replaceable in an opening formed in an opening formed at a lower end in contact with an upper end of the overflow partition which is provided at a low height to remove the non point pollutant contained in the rainwater that overflows the overflow partition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "multi function water storage system and method for reducing the contamination by initial rain and preventing a city from flooding the present invention relates to a multi functional next generation storage system and storage method that can be easily applied to urban areas and can be used to control the initial excellent pollution load caused by rainfall to prevent urban flooding and to reuse water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102006970-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "as described above the rainwater storage type double side channel canal of the present invention by removing the non point source of rainwater in accordance with the dual filtering structure to prevent contamination of soil and groundwater the accumulation of rainwater by the double channel structure of the u shaped structure by smoothing and discharging it is possible to reduce peak discharge during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101724155-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a rainwater purification plant the present invention relates to rainwater purification and water supply facilities for trees and more particularly to a rainwater purification and water supply facility for trees which comprises a sidewalk covered with concrete and asphalt a rainwater flowing along a sidewalk and a road surface it is introduced into the reservoir soil and supplied to the foundation soil again through many wicks to prevent contamination of the river or ground water prevent flooding due to heavy rainfall improve the urban aesthetics and prevent the trees from dry the present invention relates to a rainwater purification and water supply facility for trees"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_86", "text": "in addition regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the first object of the present invention is to prevent contamination of the valley channel by overflowing the partition wall during rainy weather and also to sewage initial rainwater and valley water excellent sewage and valleys using a storage tank that can be discharged to the river and prevented from being discharged to the river by the initial rainwater that has not been purified due to the initial rainfall that is supercharged during rainy weather exceeding the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224277-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the initial rainwater storage system for sewage and valley water separation using the storage tank according to the present invention by overflowing the dividing wall during rainy weather to prevent contamination of the valley waterway and also to sewage initial rainfall and valley water rainwater on the other hand due to the initial rain that is supercharged during rainy weather the initial rainwater that has not been purified by the excess of the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant is discharged to the river to prevent the river from being polluted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the control unit provided in the terminal box can receive the rainfall information measured by the rainfall measurement sensor to control the initial rainfall non point pollution source system characterized in that for controlling the operation of the valve drive motor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "the present invention provides a method for separating and discharging a nonpoint source from initial rainfall a rainfall measurement step s1 in which the rainfall measurement sensor 200 measures rainfall a closing switch operation step s2 of operating a switch to close the pollution separation pipe 140 when the rainfall measured in the rainfall measurement step reaches the pollution separation pipe closing rainfall amount the closing signal generated in the closing switch operation step is transmitted to the control unit 310 and the control unit 310 receives the closing signal to drive the valve driving motor 142 through the electric valve 141 pollution separation pipe 140 s3 to separate the contaminant pipe closing step after the contamination separation pipe opening step is closed the control unit after the pollution separation pipe opening setting time set by the manager through the input unit 330 provided in the terminal box 300 has elapsed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 power generation unit 11 solar module 20 support 100 rainboard 110 first settling tank 120 second settling tank 130 valve box 140 contamination separation pipe 141 electric valve 142 valve drive motor 143 backflow prevention trap 144 gas backflow prevention albo 150 suspended solids filter 160 steel grating 200 rainfall sensor 210 rain gauge case 211 rain gauge bottom 212 lever 213 coupling member 220 bucket 221 bucket pillar 222 bucket pillar support 223 lever 224 weight 225 magnet 226 switch 227 lever pin 230 water inlet 240 filter medium 300 terminal box 310 control unit 320 charging unit 330 input unit 340 timer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101450430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "1 to 3 rainfall runoff on roads and other road surfaces is introduced into an existing waterway through an induction waterway and a separate flow distribution structure a pretreatment tank and various abatement facilities are installed in the existing waterway it can be seen that the initial effluent is introduced into the abatement facility and the rainwater effluent from which the non point pollutant is removed through the abatement facility is reintroduced into the existing canal thereby removing the nonpoint contamination of the initial effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416507-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition through the pollutant source management method that installs pollutant treatment device near pollutant source such as impervious area it manages the whole basin equally and removes from the existing rainwater pipe end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416507-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as described above the rainfall runoff treated by the action of the soil filter bed layer 50 and the plant 80 is collected into the hole drainage pipe 30 through the hole of the hole drainage pipe 30 and is transferred to the public water and the hole drainage pipe the treated rainfall runoff that did not penetrate 30 penetrates into the existing soil through the soil membrane 70 at the bottom of the soil media layer 50 thereby preventing contamination of public waters and groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101038336-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "by dispersing rainwater it is possible to prevent flooding of roads and low lying houses and to help counter flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}]</data>
</edge>
