  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101179577-B1", "para_id": "para_76", "text": "a margin can be provided and the amount of rainwater remaining in the waterway can be minimized so that water pooling does not occur and the remaining rainwater can be decayed or reduce the occurrence of odor and block the reproduction of pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100633532-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "the amount of sewage flowing through the rainwater and sewage inlets 23 may not exceed the weir 40 and the rainfall may be small even in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100633532-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "in rainy weather with heavy rainfall rainwater and sewage flowing through the rainwater and sewage inlets 23 of the manhole 10 increase and the wear 40 formed inside the manhole 10 by the flow rate of the rainwater and sewage increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the case of rainwater storms installed upstream the rainwater is collected at least 10 times the maximum amount of sewage during rainfall and thus the sewage flowing into rainwater stormwater installed downstream of the sewage flows in excess amount"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition due to excessive wear height and river water backflow the domestic sewer pipeline system is over planned in the upstream pipeline so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338818-Y1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "first the rainwater drainage sump according to the present invention is installed rainwater drainage sump in a public facility the initial rainwater generated in the early stage is drained to the bottom drain formed in the main body of the wear or orifice type rainy rainfall by restraining the drainage caused by the increase a certain amount of rainwater is stored in public facilities and the remaining rainwater due to the increase of rainwater flows to the upper drain of the sump for reducing the drainage of rainwater to be drained thereby suppressing the drainage of the drainage well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown therein is provided with a vortex induction pipe 120 is coupled to the inlet pipe 110 in which the raw water is introduced to induce vortex one side the lower portion of the vortex induction pipe is equipped with a removable screen net 130 it is formed in contact with the first filtration tank 100 the first filtration tank is communicated through the first transfer pipe 210 provided on the upper surface of the contact the inside is floated upward by the introduced filtered water contained in the filtered water the second filtration tank 200 is provided with a plurality of filtration filters 220 for adsorbing or coagulating sedimentation of various foreign matter and the second transport pipe 310 formed in contact with the second filtration tank 200 the upper portion of the contact surface kite through the third filter tank 300 is discharged to the discharge pipe 330 provided on one side by adjusting the flow rate of the filtered water discharged through the second transport pipe 310 and the foreign matter is provided therein is provided with a filter layer 320 therein non point source removal device is known which is characterized in that it is configured to include but in the case of the non point source removal device as described above the effect is due to the problem of site security required during the installation and inconvenience of maintenance and management after installation of the treatment facility it is insignificant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a solid separator 232 and a solid separator 232 a first processing unit 230 including an oil water separator 234 and a solids separator 232 formed under the enclosing hollow shape to separate outflow water and oil components and a sedimentation tank 238 for storing solids a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation storage tank 410 in which contaminants included in the effluent are precipitated is formed and fine pollutants and effluent are purified a second processing unit 240 provided with a microfiltration wall 440 to a cartridge porous filter 282 in which a third inlet hole 206 into which the effluent treated by the second processing unit 240 is introduced is formed and a plurality of refinery holes 510 are formed on the outer periphery to finally purify the effluent the inlet and outlet member 284 provided in the cartridge porous filter 282 and having a plurality of inlet and outlet holes 520 on the outer periphery the cartridge porous filter 282 and the inlet member 284 are fixed to a fixing part 288 and a third processing unit 250 including a filter support member 286 connected to the fixing unit 288 a storage tank 280 for storing effluent treated with non point pollutants by the third processing unit 250 and a drainage system in which a discharge line 260 is formed to discharge the effluent treated with non point pollutants and an effluent pipe 214 through which the effluent is waterproofed is formed on one side of the storage tank 280"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the case of rainwater storms installed upstream the rainwater is collected at least 10 times the maximum amount of sewage during rainfall and thus the sewage flowing into rainwater stormwater installed downstream of the sewage flows in excess amount"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition due to excessive wear height and river water backflow the domestic sewer pipeline system is over planned in the upstream pipeline so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "10 0894022 april 10 2009 in the treatment of non point pollutants contained in the initial rainfall effluent waterproofing the effluent purified in the non point pollutant treatment apparatus the variable wear is formed to protrude upwards to the inside so that the initial rainfall outflow water flows in the rain pipe is formed on one side a gripping portion is formed at an upper end and a screen is formed on an outer surface thereof and a solid separator separating the initial rainfall and the solids through the inflow pipe to separate the effluent and the solids and formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "and part of the circulating water through the circulating water supply pipe 61 through the circulating water supply pipe 61 is sent to the buried contact medium storage facility 70 and the circulating water introduced into the void contact medium storage facility is purified while passing through the pore medium is distributed and collected the facility 80 is moved to the distribution collection basin 81 and is supplied from the collection basin 81 to the pond 30 formed at the bottom of the reservoir so that the water in the pond is always kept purified while the pond 30 water overflowed to the free fall into the overflow wear room 31 this operation is to be re introduced to the filtration purification 40 of the repeatedly formed through the air outlet pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "1 to 6 to separate the initial rainfall effluent and to form a rainwater toil chamber 11 having a settling function the rainwater toil chamber 11 is an inlet pipe 12 rainwater discharge pipe 13 and tea collection rainwater collection facility 10 having a storage facility inlet pipe 14 and the settling space 15 connected to the reservoir so that rainwater flows into the reservoir while having a function and the screen facility 16 to block the inflow of contaminants into the reservoir the rainwater collection facility in the rainwater collection facility 11 the storage facility 20 through which the rainwater flows into the reservoir through the reservoir inlet pipe 14 and installed on the bottom of the reservoir to produce a water change pipe and the overflow wear room on one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100601908-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "it moves to the distribution collection basin 81 which is a collecting facility 80 and supplies it to the pond 30 formed at the bottom of the reservoir from the sump 81 so that the water in the pond is always kept purified water while the pond 30 water overflowed to the free fall into the overflow wear room 31 this operation is to be re introduced to the filtration purification 40 of the repeatedly formed through the air outlet pipe 32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "rainfall conduit installed at least one or more monthly wear inherently so that rainwater flows from the predetermined watershed in rainy weather is separated into the initial rainfall and the continuous runoff a connection pipe connected to the rainwater conduit so that the initial rainwater flows in and a screen for filtering the suspended solids contained in the initial rainwater and filtering rainwater when rainwater exceeding an allowable capacity flows through the connection pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "the first method is to install water gates valves and movable wear to control the discharge amount at the outlet and open these facilities at normal times to drain the reservoir water and then close the water gate to settle down after a certain period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wear type rainwater chute device characterized in that to prevent the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the wear 100 and the sluice gate 400 are hingedly coupled to one side of the front side of the wear 100 so that the other side is closed when either side is opened and the other end of the interlocking bar 120 is a sluice gate it is pin coupled to the center of the 400 the sluice gate 400 is made of a circular shape the sluice gate 400 is a wear type characterized in that the slide or rolling motion is made along the bottom of the sewage pipe 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "the rainy soil chamber of patent document 4 is a buoy that adjusts the degree of opening of the connecting pipe according to the increase in flow rate in the connection pipe connecting the rain soil chamber and the drain pipe so that it can collect as much as the design capacity regardless of the increase in flow rate due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it can be done and because it consists of installing a wear and a sluice gate at the top of a sewage pipe not an orifice type that requires civil engineering work there is a useful effect to simplify the installation work"}]</data>
