h is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the artificial wetland which can simultaneously process the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow of the present invention consists of an inflow culvert a wetland space and an outflow culvert the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow from the inflow culvert in the artificial wetland discharged and discharged to the effluent effluent after discharge into the effluent effluent the inflow water consisting of the normal base flow and the rainfall rainfall part of the design rainfall output wqv including nitrogen and organic matter from the inlet culvert a first wetland intake channel connected between the inlet culvert and a wetland space to be introduced into the wetland space deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "meanwhile when it rains rains the rainwater flows into the pretreatment unit as the water to be treated but the first passage is closed the second passage is open the introduced water to be treated passes through the pretreatment unit and flows into the non point pollutant filtration unit through the second passage to remove non point pollutants and the water to be treated from which the non point pollutants have been removed flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit through the third passage to be purified and discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "for example when rainfall continues for more than 1 hour and river flooding is expected a movable dam can be installed in the river and when the movable dam is covered all the holes or valves flowing into or out of the facility are automatically blocked thereby protecting the facility"}]</data>
</edge>
