  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102009623-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "eighth the fine dust detection sensor rainfall detection sensor road surface detection sensor cctv to detect the dust state of the road outside the injector is equipped with the effect that can remove the dust completely by spraying when checking the site situation in real time have.1 is a schematic diagram showing a clean rod watering system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "US-4523875-A", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the porous reservoirs provide a system of open passages for ducting water to the footer drain line system and for providing regions where water may temporarily accumulate harmlessly in a situation of heavy rainfall or backup of the storm drain line which serves the building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of the initial rainfall of 2.5 mm hr the inflow of rainwater into the first storage vessel 112 through the rainwater inflow conduit 104 is performed and the rainwater overflowing after the initial rainfall is discharged to the side of the existing rainwater pipe a first storage vessel 112 connected to the first storage vessel 112 to perform primary precipitation through an induction runflow section 102 constituted by a discharge pipe 106 a second storage vessel 114 having an excellent supply hole 118 formed therein for supplying the only an upper portion of the stormwater to the filtration vessel 210 side and a second storage vessel 114 for dividing the first and second storage vessels 112 and 114 a partition wall 116 formed with a storm drainage hole 115 through which the initial stormwater is moved and a filter member 116 formed in the storm drainage hole 118 and storm drainage hole 115 to remove foreign matter contained in the initial stormwater and the second storage vessel 114 140 for supplying only the rainwater located in the upper part of the lagoon rainwater to the filtration treatment tank and a water level sensor for detecting the water level of the water tank caused by the filtration resistance of the filter medium means a pre processing unit including a lossy head sensor 120 for sensing a loss head according to the amount of water the effluent outlet hole 212 for discharging the filtered effluent is connected to a filtration tank 210 formed at a position lower than the height of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 a sludge hopper 230 configured to guide the sludge contained in the storm introduced into the filtration tank from the second storage vessel 114 to the backwash drainage storage tank 310 side of a backwash processing unit 300 to be described later a first filter medium unit 222 made of polyvinyl alcohol pva and a second filter medium unit 224 made of polyurethane pu which are embedded in the filtration tank 210 and the first and second filtering means 222 and 224 are installed at a ratio of 7 3 and a filter cover 380 having a flow space formed therein for filtration of the float according to the inflow amount of the storm with a filtration line speed of 18 to 20 m h a filtration treatment section 200 including filter medium means 220 capable of high speed filtration with a filtration rate of 10 m 3 m 2 day or more with a volume of 15 l m 3 the upper and lower flow spaces of the filter means 220 are disposed inside the filtration tank 210 so as to surround the circumferential surface of the backwash drainage storage tank 310 the upper mesh network 384 and the lower mesh network 382 are formed at upper and lower portions of the filter media frame 382 and through which pollutants including sewage sludge and backwash water pass the air cleaning unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 are positioned on the upper and lower portions of the upper and lower mesh nets 284 and 286 to backwash the filtering unit 220 380 the filtration tank 210 is installed inside the filtration tank 210 and stops the inflow of filtered effluent from the filtration means 220 and removes contaminants generated during the filtration process and only excellent sludges flowing from the second storage tank 114 a backwash drainage reservoir 310 having a plurality of reverse osmosis inflow holes 312 for collecting ozone and a backwash drain pump 320 which is formed inside the backwash drainage storage tank 310 and connected to the discharge line 322 for sucking inflow pollutants and sludge into the sewage treatment plant or the designated wastewater treatment facility including so that the air filtering means 220 is rotated by the swirling phenomenon by injecting the compressed air into the contaminants adsorbed on the filter means 220 and the contaminants are separated by the impact pressure generated at this time a water washing unit 340 for performing secondary backwashing while washing the filter media 220 using the effluent when driving of the air washing unit 330 is completed a backwashing control unit 350 for controlling the driving of the washing unit 330 and the water washing unit 340 to control the backwashing when the loss head is 80 mm or more and a backwash level sensor 360 for checking the amount of inflow of contaminants and reverse water contained in the backwash water level sensor 360 to the backwash control unit 350"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102261819-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the simulation and prediction unit uses turbidity and alkalinity as main factors during rainfall among the factors of the inflow flow rate of raw water hydrogen ion concentration turbidity alkalinity electrical conductivity and water temperature and hydrogen ion concentration and the mixed paper drug injection derivation unit 1310 that derives the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper with the water temperature as the main factor the raw water inflow of the flocculated paper and the settling basin the g value of the flocculated paper water temperature turbidity and the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper through the visualized interface image a flocculation paper settling cell sludge management unit 1320 that establishes a plan detects changes in the sludge interface through a sensor and corrects the sludge by checking the degree of agglomeration through light intensity detection and the number of loss head filtration duration and filtered water the filter paper management unit 1330 that establishes a plan for autonomous backwashing through turbidity information the advanced treatment management unit 1340 that performs accident and failure prediction through the status information of the ozone generating device and the maintenance of the water level of the purified water and optimum chlorine it is preferable to provide a purified water disinfection ability management unit 1350 for deriving the contact time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102340325-B1", "para_id": "para_77", "text": "in addition in the present invention it is possible to provide an iot based drinking water storage tank management platform service through real time water quality information monitoring an analysis algorithm exceeding the standard value and big data related to season rainfall and water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408976-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "and a cap 198 connected to the hinge 190 of the fixed frame 125 provided at the end of the branch pipe 121.the present invention provides a stable drainage of rainwater by providing a stable removal of rainwater or flood caused by heavy rainfall as described above while checking the clogging caused by sedimentation that accumulates while moving in a drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2901149-B1", "para_id": "para_175", "text": "this is because heavy rainfall conditions could dilute the incoming food source creating a low our and therefore a false toxicity reading"}, {"pat_id": "KR-910009261-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "the method of claim 12 wherein the rainfall prediction step includes receiving time series rainfall distribution data to calculate a center point where each set of rainfall overlaps checking whether the center point moves according to a predetermined rule and calculating the position of the center point before the predetermined time from the present by calculating the average value and the variance of the position of the center point in the past when moving according to the predetermined rule or when the center point moves without the predetermined rule the rainfall increase decrease rate acquisition step of acquiring the increase decrease rate of rainfall from the local mean of the region and the position where the latest rainfall distribution at the current calculation time does not fluctuate within a predetermined period and the latest rainfall distribution is limited by the calculated center point"}]</data>
