  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a peripheral wall 110 forming a square frame a partition wall 120 formed in the shape of a \u5341 shape to partition the inside of the peripheral wall 110 and a joint wall 130 formed so that each side extends from the corner portion 111 of the peripheral wall 110 and forms a vertical angle with the corner portion 111 it is configured to include and at each end of the joint wall 130 a plurality of block units 100 in which longitudinal recessed parts 131 and convex parts 132 are formed alternately are arranged sequentially in four horizontal directions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the prefabricated rainwater infiltration storage tank 200 provided by the present invention is an underground structure built overall in a square shape and a plurality of the block units 100 are arranged in succession in four horizontal directions and adjacent block units it is constructed by arranging the recessed portion 131 and the convex portion 132 of the joint wall 130 to engage and combine"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102644552-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the prefabricated rainwater infiltration storage tank 200 may be disposed on the peripheral walls of the block units 100a and 100b forming the outer line of the structure without the joint wall 130 being formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200499204-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "however there was a problem that a step inevitably occurred inside the expansion pipe section which could lead to leakage of sewage or rainwater.the present invention was created to solve the above mentioned problems and the purpose of the present invention is to provide a rubber ring for watertightness and step removal by being inserted into a part where polyethylene pe double walled pipes or multi walled pipes having an expansion section formed at one end are connected to each other so that the double walled pipes or multi walled pipes can be connected to each other without a separate joint pipe and by eliminating the step created inside the expansion section the leakage of sewage water and the intrusion of unknown water can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200368643-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is an object of the present invention to provide a resin reinforced joint structure to prevent the inflow and leakage of internal sewage and rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102380491-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the above mentioned joint method the joint method using the color ring is not used for sewage pipes including rainwater pipes because it is difficult to fill the mortar and there is a concern about groundwater contamination and subsidence due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277086-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "6 is a finish block 14 installed on the outer surface during installation of the rainwater storage tank 1 according to the present invention by minimizing the production process by producing the same side and upper portion in the same shape both ends of the finish block 14 there is a bolt connection groove 110 is formed in each pillar block 10 11 12 so that the speech is possible as shown in figure 6c side view the upper portion of the recess 120 the lower portion of the iron portion 130 which is intended to improve construction and watertightness"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101874284-B1", "para_id": "para_82", "text": "in addition the present invention has the effect that when the upper block and the lower drain pipe are joined the joint frame using concrete is formed so that even when the load transferred to the lower drain pipe is increased due to the rainwater flowing through the drain hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "thirdly there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "in addition it functions as a support and prevents deformation of the shape due to external force thereby enabling removal of foreign substances mixed in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100590407-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "therefore the joint is not used for sewage pipes including rainwater pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102914824-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "at this time packing to prevent leakage is configured to be placed between the inner diameter of the joint pipe and the outer diameter of the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200480536-Y1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the bellows sleeve is inserted into the connecting tube and the space between the bellows is closed thereby preventing the joint parts of the bellows sleeve and the connecting tube from being damaged and there is a fixed and leakage free effect"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102110404-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "right angle soft joints connected at right angles connection joints connecting up down while being straight and right angled and closed cast iron panels coupled to the upper part of the side wall cast iron panel and closed connections connecting the finished cast iron panel and the side wall cast iron panel by constructing a cast iron panel assembly composed of a joint the plastic assembly block body is laid and stacked to constitute a rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "2528179 prior document 2 a lower manhole block 10 having a closed bottom an open top and a drainage port 11 formed on the side so that a drain pipe 1 is connected an intermediate manhole block 20 that is laminated and assembled in at least one layer on the lower manhole block 10 and is provided so that the upper and lower portions are open an upper manhole block 30 that is laminated and assembled on the intermediate manhole block 20 is open at the upper and lower portions and has a trench 31 installed at the upper portion a joint portion 40 that connects the corresponding assembly surfaces of the lower manhole block 10 the intermediate manhole block 20 and the upper manhole block 30 with a positive and negative structure an airtight packing 50 that is installed between the joint portions 40 and is provided so as to block water leakage and absorb vibration and an odor trap 60 provided to block odors flowing back through the drain and a variable odor trap 80 is provided between the lower manhole block 10 and the middle manhole block 20 and the variable odor trap 80 is an elastic membrane 81 that divides the space of the lower manhole block 10 and the middle manhole block 20 in a state where the edge thereof is engaged with the joint portion 40 that connects the lower manhole block 10 and the middle manhole block 20 in a positive and negative structure a ring plate 83 that is installed in the center of the elastic membrane 81 and through which a drainage hole 82 for draining rainwater passes a conical weight 84 that is provided to open and close the drainage hole 82 while moving downward from the upper portion of the elastic membrane 81 and a roller 85 that has one end connected to the ring plate 83 and the other end installed in the trench 31"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "the surface joint 410 and the water pocket 420 have slip resistance and help to improve walking stability and at the same time they form a flow path through which rainwater and foreign substances on the water pocket block 400 can flow thereby improving the drainage function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102191037-B1", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "the surface joint 410 is formed by partially recessing the surface of the water pocket block 400 and may have one or a plurality of linear shapes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200352056-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the present invention is to achieve the above object the present invention is coupled to the connection hole of the sewer pipe is composed of a structure that can prevent the leakage of the sewage as much as possible while the connector protection ring is one side cut off the fastening part is formed horizontally the fastening part is coupled to the fastening part the leak proof rubber ring is attached to the inside the joint pipe connection part is formed on the other side and the circular fixed rubber ring is coupled to both sides so that the connector protection ring is firm it is fixed to the sewer pipe the connection pipe is connected to the joint pipe joint of the connector protection ring while the connection pipe is formed with a bolt portion at the bottom and the fixed bolt is coupled to the upper leak proof rubber ring inside is attached the connection pipe is coupled to the upper portion the connection pipe the bolt installation groove is formed in the lower portion the pleat portion is formed in the middle portion the connection pipe is excellent in the upper it is combined to provide a sewer pipe connector characterized in that the rainwater is collected and transferred to the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100734227-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "if the above mentioned injection tube 12 and the exhaust pipe 13 is removed in the cured state the joining is completed and the state is more robust and watertight.the resin reinforcement method of the manhole junction of the present invention as described above and the joint structure using the same as well as the joint of the manhole and the sewer pipe more tightly as well as the watertight joint of the manhole and sewage pipe to allow the external soil or foreign matter inflow and internal sewage and rainwater it is effective to prevent this leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101287038-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if water leaks occur at the joint connecting the pipe and the manhole sphere in the sewage or rainwater manhole three dimensional deformation of the manhole and the pipe due to settlement or movement of soil and cracks will occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 1030605 discloses a flat rectangular plate having a rectangular horizontal plate having a coupling groove at the center or both sides of the diagonal portion one lower end being coupled to the coupling groove of the plastic shaped support block to be coupled with the cast iron panel and the rectangular parallelepiped cast iron panel the straight connection joint for connecting the cast iron panels in parallel the right angle joint for connecting at right angles a cast iron panel assembly constituted by a joint joint connecting the upper and lower ends of the cast iron panel and connected to each other while being connected to each other a finishing cast iron panel coupled to an upper portion of the side wall cast iron panel and a finishing connection joint connecting the finishing cast iron panel and the side wall cast iron panel a rainwater storage tank is constructed by laying and laminating a sieve on the bottom of the rainwater storage tank group is a rainwater storage tank configured for worker access passage by assembling the cast iron panel assembly"}]</data>
