  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100798219-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in general sewer pipes buried beneath underground roads are likely to have an uneven settlement due to the vibration or impact load of heavy vehicles passing through the roads and during flooding the cavities gradually expand due to the scour of backfill material in sewer pipe joints"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100838923-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "due to the phenomenon aging progresses and as industrial zones such as industrial complexes expand toxic wastewater and wastewater flow into sewage pipes and corrosion is accelerated and during flooding the cavity is gradually enlarged due to the scour of sewage pipe joints"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helicopter station 619 and a thermal power plant 626 are equipped with satellite launch pads 643 and mooring towers 644 and space rocket launch pads to detect climate abnormalities and equipment for detecting the weather movement status of the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention flood control equipment to detect climate abnormalities in order to prioritize emergency rescue the flood control equipment in the flooded area is always equipped with several air compressors 80 connected to rescue tubes 130 and ropes 131 at the accident site and before the underground passage is flooded the flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment to prevent flooding by installing a water tank for rescue and flood control in the flooded area so that people can board the tubes 130 and be rescued by rescue workers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1120", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helic