north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102859794-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "1 a drain trap according to the prior art includes a drain trap sleeve 1 that is buried in an indoor floor and has an overflow pipe 1a that protrudes upward in the center of the floor a base panel 10 that is buried in an indoor floor and is positioned in the upper center of the drain trap sleeve 1 and has a joint formed in the center of a space that is recessed to collect water a sealing cap 20 that is installed to cover the upper part of the overflow pipe 1a of the drain trap sleeve 1 to block an unpleasant odor that rises through the overflow pipe 1a of the drain trap sleeve 1 while maintaining a water level at a certain level from the inner bottom of the drain trap sleeve 1 an upper strainer 30 that is formed to cover the upper part of the base panel 10 and filter out foreign substances and the upper part is installed in the joint of the base panel 10 and is composed of an inner filter 40 that filters out foreign substances such as hair from water passing through the upper filter 30 while guiding downward water to drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032930-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "install the haunch reinforcement respectively on the left and right of the partition fixed with the fixing bolt in the part facing the partition and the inner blade of the haunch reinforcement and the part of the frp tank and the outer wing of the haunch reinforcement after fixing the haunch reinforcement material to the partition wall haunch surface f al tank by molding laminated resin and glass chopped strand mat to a thickness of 4mm or more so that the fixing bolt is not in contact with the sewage in order to prevent deformation due to the water level difference between the tanks comprising a steel reinforcing ring is installed on the inner rim of the frp tank to reinforce the strength of the frp tank when the steel reinforcing ring is configured sanding is performed on the inside of the frp tank before bonding to prevent separation of the frp material and laminated to have a thickness of 4 mm or more using a glass chopped strand mat"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032930-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "4 two or more rectangular 40 50 mm steel reinforcing rods 26 are installed in the partition wall 22 in the vertical direction to prevent deformation due to the water level difference between the tanks"}, {"pat_id": "US-7383157-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the system of claim 1 wherein said aged pipe evaluation factor data includes at least one among a sewer based buried area a road a buried year a damage state a soil condition an inner corrosion degree a basic construction method a soil condition a pipe diameter a joint method the number of divides a underground water level an i i ratio and a pipe flow speed state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804115-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plurality of side panels connected in series to form side surfaces of the water tank a top panel connected to a side surface of the water tank and connected in series so as to form an upper surface of the water tank a bottom panel connected to a bottom of the water tank so as to close the bottom of the side panel and and a reinforcing portion that maintains a gap between the side panels facing each other so as to prevent deformation of the water tank and a gap between the top panel and the bottom panel which are arranged to face each other the joint portion formed between the plurality of bottom panels is formed to protrude to the outside of the water tank further comprising a freezing prevention unit for preventing freezing of water to be dewatered in the water tank and providing thermal energy to the water surface of the fresh water to enable freezing of water frozen from the water surface to be more effectively prevented the above a control box installed on the upper panel a guide rod inserted into the water tank from the control box a moving block slidably installed in the vertical direction along the guide bar and having a support extending laterally a heater installed in the support for suppressing freezing by providing thermal energy to water and a buoyant body mounted on the support for lifting the support block and the moving block along the water level and flowing along the water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200194172-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "with the increase the flange is placed upright and upside down with the conventional upper and lower body upside down flange joining is easier to join"}]</data>
