  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in addition when it is determined that the wastewater treatment capacity information is obtained by communicating with the wastewater treatment capacity management terminal configured in the wastewater treatment facility 210 to determine whether the treatment capacity limit is reached at the time of initial discharge by delaying the opening of the water gate or valve 500 for a connection and sewage treatment plant connection by a predetermined time the effect of preventing the processing capacity limit can be prevented in advance.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "as described above the pc structural type manhole 300 is provided with a water gate or valve 500 for a connection pipe of a wastewater treatment plant which is a water gate or valve for discharging an initial storm water to a wastewater treatment plant or a valve 600 for a river connection which is a water gate or a valve for performing opening and closing of the water gate or valve and constitutes an opening and closing device 550 or 650 for opening and closing the water gate by controlling according to the control signal of the configured rtu it is possible to prevent manhole accidents efficiently and to manage the initial storm including contamination source in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102855051-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however it is difficult to identify trash inside the manhole by manpower and if the trash is not cleaned in a timely manner the trash can block the river connection pipe connecting the manhole to the river and as a result the mixed water of sewage and rainwater cannot be discharged into the river so the inside of the manhole becomes filled with the mixed water of sewage and rainwater and the mixed water of sewage and rainwater flows back upstream of the manhole causing urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102855051-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "therefore before the garbage goes over the separation wall 200 and overflows to the second area the first outlet pipe 500 inside the interception manhole 100 when the amount of garbage accumulated in an area exceeds the standard when the garbage goes over the separation wall 200 and flows into the second area the garbage disposal alarm information is immediately provided to the collection manhole management company for garbage disposal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore non point pollution is reduced by using an accessory manhole and an rtu the accidental runoff water is supplied to the sewage pipe without being sent to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping