a fixed frame which is inserted into the bracket frame so as to be hooked on the engaging jaw barrier rib panels installed inside the fixed frame with a predetermined gap therebetween a blocking panel the fixing walls are formed at opposite side walls of the fixing frame to be spaced apart from each other by a predetermined distance so as to be detachably inserted into the fixing walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384724-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the present invention during rain the initial rainwater containing non point pollutants introduced into the manhole can be drained to the sewage treatment plant through sewage pipes to reduce the contamination of the rivers by the non point pollutants as well as inflow after the initial rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in an initial high boiling point contamination treatment system 100 connected to the end of the conduit or the river water from which the polluted water is discharged to provide pollution excellence and selectively supply only the initial nonpoint pollution excellence a reservoir 200 for storing initial boiling impurity contamination provided to the water collection channel 130 of the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants a siphon pipe 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the water level of the reservoir 200 becomes equal to or higher than the height of the highest part in the reversed u shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889975-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the storeroom 100 may include a grating seating surface 121 formed in a boundary area between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 wherein the grating 200 comprises a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insert tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 formed in a grid shape inside the grating frame 210 to block rainwater into the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter the grating frame 210 is formed to protrude at a predetermined interval in an area contacting the grating seating surface 121 so that the soil introduced into the grating frame 210 from the grating insertion tube 120 and the grating frame 210 is separated from the grinding frame 210 and a plurality of the soil inflow teeth 240 for inflowing into the interior of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889974-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent storage tank 100 which is embedded in the inside of the ground and receives stormwater introduced from the ground a grating 200 rotatably coupled to the upper surface of the superior storage tank 100 for introducing the stormwater into the storage tank and blocking the foreign material a dirt collecting box 400 provided in the superior storage tank 100 for filtering dirt contained in the rainwater and a collection box support 300 provided at an upper portion of the superior storage container 100 and supporting the dirt collection box 400 the storm reservoir 100 a reservoir body 110 in which the storm is stored a grating insert tube 120 formed on the upper portion of the reservoir body 110 and coupled to the grating 200 and a grating seating surface 121 formed on the boundary region between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 so as to be stepped inwardly in a predetermined area so that the grating 200 is seated and supported the grating 200 a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insertion tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 disposed in the grating frame 210 at predetermined intervals in the longitudinal direction and having irregularities formed on the upper surface thereof to block rainwater from the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter a plurality of reinforcing frames 230 arranged in the grating frame 210 in a lateral direction at regular intervals a plurality of protrusions protruding from the ground at a predetermined interval in the lower portion of the outer reinforcing frame 230a to allow the gravel to flow into the gap between the grating insert tube 120 and the grating frame 210 and includes a soil inflow tooth 240 the height of the earth inflow tooth 240 and the height of the outer reinforcement frame 230a may be greater than the height of the reinforcement frame 230 located inside the outer reinforcement frame 230a and the reinforcing frame 230 is formed at the same height as the reinforcing frame 230"}]</data>
