g into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and pedestrians can be prevented from falling when the grating comes off while the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage can be controlled while allowing smooth inflow of sewage away from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole can be controlled while preventing and blocking foul odors flowing out from the inside and foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet are naturally collected to prevent blockage and the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling accidents that may occur when the grating is detached is provided.figure 1 is a cross sectional view showing a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage water from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain and sewage water according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figure 2 is a cross sectional view showing a pedestrian protection situation of a manhole that allows smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling and blocking the inflow and outflow of rain and sewage according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 3a to 3c are perspective views sequentially showing the operating state of the grating part of a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage according to the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figure 4 is a cross sectional view showing a grating section of a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage according to one embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 5a to 5d are cross sectional views sequentially showing the operating state of a grating section of a manhole that can control the inflow and blockage of rain or sewage according to another embodiment of the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figures 6a and 6b are side views sequentially showing the operating state of the grating section of a manhole that allows the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage according to a modified example of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figure 7 is a cross sectional view showing a grating section of a manhole that allows for the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves while controlling the inflow and blocking of rain or sewage according to another modified example of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "figure 8 is a perspective view showing a fall prevention part of a manhole that can control and block the inflow and outflow of rain or sewage according to the present invention while allowing the smooth inflow of sewage from foreign substances such as fallen leaves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "flowing into the upper inlet of a manhole while blocking and preventing foul odors flowing out from inside and naturally collects foreign substances such as fallen leaves that can block the entrance when flowing into the upper inlet thereby preventing blockage and provides the effect of preventing pedestrians from falling when the grating detaches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102694540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a main body 10 having an upper inlet 11 and a sewage inlet 12 for introducing rain or sewage into the above ground and an outlet 13 for discharging the introduced rain or sewage a grating 20 formed through a penetration to remove foreign substances such as fallen leaves contained in rain or sewage by being placed on the upper inlet 11 of the main body 10 an odor blocking means 30 comprising a first inclined plate 31 and a second inclined plate 32 formed at the upper and lower portions corresponding to each other while being inclined so that rain or sewage flowing into the interior of the main body 10 can be discharged downward while rain or sewage flowing in from the upper inlet 11 can be discharged downward and a rotating plate 34 formed at each end of the first inclined plate 31 and the second inclined plate 32 can be rotated through a hinge 33 at the upper portion to block odors rising along with opening due to the load of rain or sewage the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 are provided with a catch net a to prevent pests such as cockroaches and rats from entering the inside while being installed on the sewage inlet 12 and the discharge pipe 13 of the above body 10 and respectively inserted to induce or discharge rain or sewage a fixing member 43 inserted on the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 to prevent detachment a packing 44 to prevent the outflow of rain or sewage and fixing means 45a 45b 45c to fix the inlet pipe 41 the discharge pipe 42 and the catch net 43 to each other and the fixing means 45a 45b 45c are provided with a plurality of catch protrusions 46 protruding in the opposite direction from the outer surface of the inlet pipe 41 and the discharge pipe 42 and a plurality of catch protrusions 46 protruding in the opposite direction from the direction of inflow into the inside of the sewage inlet 12 and the discharge pipe 13"}]</data>
