ltered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060765-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore when heavy rain pours within a short time the other manhole of the concrete pipeline 110 is opened to drain the rainwater to the river the composite storage tank is temporarily stored in the river through the open manhole after temporarily storing the rainwater by doing so the quantity of rainwater flowing into the river can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in configuring the odor prevention device 110 to prevent the odor coming up from the ground the odor prevention device 110 includes a prevention body 112 having a seating flange 111 upward to be seated on the bottom surface of the manhole cover 105 the prevention body 112 and the first vertical portion 113 protrudes downward from the mounting flange 111 an inclined portion 114 formed to have a width narrowed inward from an end of the first vertical portion 113 a second vertical portion 115 projecting downward from the end of the inclined portion 114 a plurality of water passages 116 formed to drain a small amount of rainwater to the inclined portion 114 a discharge hole 117 formed to be opened between the second vertical portions 115 to discharge a large amount of rain and garbage deformed by the hydraulic pressure of the sewage to the water hole 116 while being drained down and after completion of drainage to return to the original state to prevent the odor coming up through the water hole 116 fixing the blocking plate 118 of a material having elasticity and excellent return force the discharge hole 117 is a sewer manhole odor prevention device characterized in that it comprises a rotating plate 120 installed so as to block the odor coming up while draining the rain and waste of the opposite"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "formed to discharge a large amount of rainwater and waste and a block and a rotating plate installed to be fixed or mounted in the water hole and the discharge hole to discharge the sewage and waste and to prevent odors coming up the garbage can be discharged quickly eliminating the fear of flooding and preventing odors from the manhole from rising to the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102387766-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention is to solve the above problems and it is installed in the grouting manhole to block the limited drainage of rainwater as well as the communication path with the sewage pipe to the outside so it is easy to install in all existing manhole structures and the installation cost it is an object of the present invention to provide an odor prevention device for sewage pipes that can minimize the odor and increase the efficiency of blocking odors around the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102387766-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "according to the odor prevention device for a sewage pipe according to the present invention it is elastically installed in an existing or new grouting manhole and since it blocks the communication path with the sewage pipe with a limited drainage function of rainwater it is easy to install in response to manholes of various structures while the installation work is simple the facility cost is greatly reduced and the manhole s own drainage function is maintained while preventing contamination of the surrounding area due to bad odors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102387766-B1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "corresponding to the manhole it is easy to install and easy to install and it is possible to significantly reduce the cost of equipment and to prevent contamination of the surroundings due to odor while maintaining the drainage function of the manhole itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101772474-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole portion including a manhole provided at a predetermined position of an inner space through which the upper and lower portions penetrate and a manhole tube through which sewage flows and flows out to the outside an upper body for filtering sewage introduced into the manhole an upper surface of the upper body is protected and a gap is formed in the longitudinal direction to allow rainwater to flow into the semicircular rainwater support a top plate made of a plate having a predetermined thickness a hinge shaft formed at a center of gravity of a side surface of the upper plate for left and right swing motion of the upper plate the rainwater is introduced through the rainwater induction passage connected to the inlet and the inlet and swung to the lower portion with the weight so that the upper surface of the upper panel a semicircular rainwater pedestal for lifting the foreign matter entrance preventing network connected to the lower portion of the upper plate by exposing the foreign matter entrance network at an angle from the ground surface by the hinge axis a rainwater guiding path installed between the foreign matter entry preventing network and the semicircular rainwater support in the foreign matter entry preventing network and guided to the semicircular rainwater pedestal by the rainwater entering the foreign matter entrance preventing network a foreign matter entry preventing network including a protruding stop member which prevents foreign matter from entering the inside when the upper plate is swung at a predetermined angle from the ground surface and allows only rainwater to flow in a lower body coupled to the upper body in an empty shape a lower body fixed to a manhole of the manhole a lower body supporting the upper body for swinging left and right and guiding the rainwater introduced from the upper body to the manhole passage a hinge hole formed in the lower body portion into which the hinge shaft is inserted the hinge hole into which the hinge shaft is inserted a stop member formed at one end of the foreign object entry preventing network and an intermediate stopping guide groove guiding the stopping member in the up and down direction and having one end blocked so that the stopping member protruding from the lower end of the foreign substance entry preventing network is stopped when the foreign substance entry preventing network is exposed to the upper side by a predetermined angle or more manhole equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101772474-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a manhole unit including a manhole provided at a predetermined position of an inner space through which upper and lower portions pass and a manhole tube through which sewage flows to flow out to the outside an upper body for filtering sewage introduced into the manhole an upper surface of the upper body is protected and a gap is formed in the longitudinal direction to allow rainwater to flow into the semicircular rainwater support a top plate made of a plate having a predetermined thickness a hinge shaft formed at a center of gravity of a side surface of the upper plate for left and right swing motion of the upper plate the rainwater is introduced through the rainwater induction passage connected to the inlet and the inlet and swung to the lower portion with the weight so that the upper surface of the upper panel a semicircular rainwater pedestal for lifting the foreign matter entrance preventing network connected to the lower portion of the upper plate by exposing the foreign matter entrance network at an angle from the ground surface by the hinge axis a rainwater guiding path installed between the foreign matter entry preventing network and the semicircular rainwater support in the foreign matter entry preventing network and guided to the semicircular rainwater pedestal by the rainwater entering the foreign matter entrance preventing network a foreign matter entry preventing network including a protruding stop member which prevents foreign matter from entering the inside when the upper plate is swung at a predetermined angle from the ground surface and allows only rainwater to flow in a lower body coupled to the upper body in an empty shape a lower body fixed to a manhole of the manhole a lower body supporting the upper body for swinging left and right and guiding the rainwater introduced from the upper body to the manhole passage a hinge hole formed in the lower body portion into which the hinge shaft is inserted the hinge hole into which the hinge shaft is inserted a stop member formed at one end of the foreign object entry preventing network and an intermediate stop guiding groove guiding the stop member in the up and down direction and having one end blocked so that the stop member protruding from the lower end of the foreign substance entry preventing network is stopped when the foreign substance entry preventing network is exposed to the upper side by a predetermined angle or more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101198688-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition the present invention can significantly increase the water purification ability by supplying oxygen by generating a vortex in the rainwater or waste water flowing by the first and second stepped protrusion formed on the bottom of the zeolite concrete"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically the present invention relates to a safety manhole cover for preventing rainwater trapping with a catch preventing part and a slope to prevent safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage during rainy weather and to prevent accidents caused by footing when a pedestrian is walking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "there was a problem that causes an electric shock accident.in order to solve these problems the present invention prevents safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage in rainy weather and safety manholes for preventing rainwater swelling with a catch preventing part and an inclined part to prevent accidents caused by footfalls when pedestrians walk"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102190972-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a plate formed in a plate shape so as to be seated on an upper portion of the sewer manhole and having a through hole in the center a drain pipe connected to the through hole downward of the plate bent laterally from the lower side and having a shape in which an end is cut diagonally and including a shielding film hinged to the end of the drain pipe and opened by rainwater or sewage discharged from the drain pipe or closed by a load the drain pipe an upper pipe connected to be orthogonal to the plate and it includes a lower pipe connected in a direction of 75 to 85 degrees to the lower end of the upper pipe an end of the lower pipe is connected to the shielding film and when the shielding film is opened a gait net is provided for spreading so that the space between the lower pipe and the shielding film is covered and filtering foreign substances an elastic body connected to the gait net is provided on the inner upper end of the lower pipe the elastic body expands when the shielding film is opened and contracts when closed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102190972-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to achieve the above object a odor blocking device for a sewer according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention includes a plate formed in a plate shape so as to be seated on an upper portion of a sewer manhole and a through hole formed in the center a drain pipe connected to the through hole downward of the plate bent laterally from the lower side and having a shape in which an end is cut diagonally and a shielding film hinged to the end of the drain pipe and opened by rainwater or sewage discharged from the drain pipe or closed by a load"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100981985-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore in the present invention the air distribution hole 12a penetrated in the vertical direction to extend from one end of the manhole cover 12 to the lower end of the heat insulating material 122 is provided in the groundwater layer of the manhole cover 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "block the discharge to the outside of the flow induction manhole 20 through 110"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4637561-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition the inner lid is equipped with a pressure relief mechanism and a rainwater dropping mechanism so that it is hardly affected by water increase during abnormal rainfall such as typhoons and therefore damage due to lifting of the manhole cover is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100734227-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "if the above mentioned injection tube 12 and the exhaust pipe 13 is removed in the cured state the joining is completed and the state is more robust and watertight.the resin reinforcement method of the manhole junction of the present invention as described above and the joint structure using the same as well as the joint of the manhole and the sewer pipe more tightly as well as the watertight joint of the manhole and sewage pipe to allow the external soil or foreign matter inflow and internal sewage and rainwater it is effective to prevent this leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101287038-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if water leaks occur at the joint connecting the pipe and the manhole sphere in the sewage or rainwater manhole three dimensional deformation of the manhole and the pipe due to settlement or movement of soil and cracks will occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102309597-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "functional sewage odor blocking device for manholesthe present invention relates to a functional sewage odor blocking device for a manhole and more particularly a sewage odor that can efficiently block odors in a manhole while easily discharging external rainwater and domestic water by a combination structure of a slope assembly and an odor blocking assembly it s about blocking devices"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however especially in the rainy season or in the fall foreign substances such as fallen leaves can block the inlet making it difficult to drain which can easily lead to flooding and human casualties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894740-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "these excellent manholes have a hollowed rectangular shape with the lower part closed and the upper part formed with an inlet port"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101894740-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "according to the present invention various foreign substances and harmful components contained in the rainwater can be filtered by the filtration unit provided in the water hole of the manhole main body thereby contributing to prevention of contamination of the groundwater and removal of foreign matter is facilitated by the replacement structure of the filtration unit and has a useful effect of securing convenience of cleaning and maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "2008 0067603 discloses a odor blocking device and rainwater backflow device for sewer manholes that continuously block the occurrence of odor generated in the manhole of the sewer and also cope sensitively with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101907012-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "as described above in the detachable manhole multi screen system of the present invention a multi stage screen is installed in a manhole so as to prevent clogging of a drain pipe by filtering contaminants that are floated or swept away by rainwater or wastewater it is possible to separate and collect various sizes of impurities introduced together with the wastewater to block the inflow of the manholes into the drain hole thereby preventing the manholes and the drain holes from being clogged by the obstacles and easily removing and collecting the filtered contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889974-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent storage tank 100 which is embedded in the inside of the ground and receives stormwater introduced from the ground a grating 200 rotatably coupled to the upper surface of the superior storage tank 100 for introducing the stormwater into the storage tank and blocking the foreign material a dirt collecting box 400 provided in the superior storage tank 100 for filtering dirt contained in the rainwater and a collection box support 300 provided at an upper portion of the superior storage container 100 and supporting the dirt collection box 400 the storm reservoir 100 a reservoir body 110 in which the storm is stored a grating insert tube 120 formed on the upper portion of the reservoir body 110 and coupled to the grating 200 and a grating seating surface 121 formed on the boundary region between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 so as to be stepped inwardly in a predetermined area so that the grating 200 is seated and supported the grating 200 a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insertion tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 disposed in the grating frame 210 at predetermined intervals in the longitudinal direction and having irregularities formed on the upper surface thereof to block rainwater from the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter a plurality of reinforcing frames 230 arranged in the grating frame 210 in a lateral direction at regular intervals a plurality of protrusions protruding from the ground at a predetermined interval in the lower portion of the outer reinforcing frame 230a to allow the gravel to flow into the gap between the grating insert tube 120 and the grating frame 210 and includes a soil inflow tooth 240 the height of the earth inflow tooth 240 and the height of the outer reinforcement frame 230a may be greater than the height of the reinforcement frame 230 located inside the outer reinforcement frame 230a and the reinforcing frame 230 is formed at the same height as the reinforcing frame 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416889-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "therefore the rainwater and sewage that did not flow into the upper portion of the trench cover 31 are diverted to the manhole 20 through the boundary block so that the rainwater and sewage that do not flow through the trench cover 31 flow into other adjacent areas"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the device installed in the large sewer or the catchment inlet of the rainwater manhole to block backflow of various odors and insects the base bottom plate 4 and the base bottom plate 4 having a rectangular long plate shape side vertical plates 5a and 5b integrally attached to both ends of the left and right sides and the front and rear and the top is open but the base seating plate in the outward direction on the upper end of the side vertical plates 5a 5b 6a 6b is formed integrally projecting to the base portion 2 to be fastened to the engaging jaw 7 of the sump 3 and to the open front and rear of the base portion 2 the left assembly fastener 10 and the right assembly fastener 11 each of which is to be assembled and symmetrical in shape respectively wherein the left assembly fastener 10 and the right assembly fastener 11 are respectively inclined downward at one side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "a device inserted into a large sewer or a rainwater inlet of a rainwater manhole to block backflow of various odors and bugs the base bottom plate 4 being horizontally positioned in a rectangular long plate shape and provided with the base"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "quot the base portion to form a shape the assembly portion is to be assembled to each of the open front and rear surfaces of the base portion and the sewage inlet is formed in the part assembled to abut the base portion it is attached to the sewage inlet of the odor prevention device which is configured to block backflow of odor from the inside of the sump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "is attached to the assembly hook 9 and the sewage inlet 16 of the assembly hook 9 to prevent odors from the inside of the sump 3 from being reversed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420604-Y1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "in accordance with the diameter of the inlet portion of the sump 3 provided in the usual large sewer or rainwater manhole assembly fasten the assembly fasteners 9 on the front and rear surfaces of the base part 2 formed in the shape respectively the inclined plate of the left fasteners 10 and the right fasteners 11 constituting the assembly fasteners 9 in the state where the side bracket 15 and the bottom plate side bracket 19 are brought into contact with each other they are integrally assembled by spot fastening or by means of a rivet or a piece of nail or by spot welding"}]</data>
