igned to block the inflow of the manhole in case of the backflow of sewage due to heavy rain or flood thereby preventing flooding damage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "the present invention by installing a buoyancy blocking device 130 is operated by buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet 113 of the manhole 110 to block the inlet 113 the rainwater from the original while performing the function of the guerrilla torrential rain flooding due to the backflow of sewage due to the flood effect is to be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a sewage odor blocking device and more particularly it is located under the manhole cover to block the bad smell of sewage and a backflow permitting hole is provided on one side to selectively allow backflow in the event of a flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200495876-Y1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "according to the present invention it is located on the lower side of the manhole cover to block odors and at the same time provide a backflow permitting hole on one side to selectively allow backflow in case of a flood thereby preventing damage to the manhole due to water pressure in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101685359-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a flat valve that is installed in a manhole to block reverse flow of odors and insects and to introduce sewage and stormwater a bracket provided opposite to the inner side surface of the inlet of the manhole and having a latching groove and and a valve body connected to the brackets and fitted in the latching grooves wherein the valve body includes a fixed panel having a lower portion at both ends thereof fitted into the engaging grooves a valve panel installed on both sides of the fixed panel so as to be hinged to open or close the inlet a sealing pad formed along an edge of the valve panel a t shaped supporter having a column formed at a central upper portion of the fixed panel and a support bar formed at an upper portion of the column and elastic springs connecting both ends of the support bar and the valve panel one end of the fixed panel is pinned and fixed to one of the brackets since both ends of the fixed panel are fixed to the brackets without being fixed to the brackets only one end of the fixed panel is pinned so that when the sewage due to the flood flows backward the valve body rotates around the pin to open the inlet through the inlet of the manhole wherein a through hole is formed in the bracket and a connection hole is formed in the fixing panel so as to penetrate through the fixing panel and are connected to each other by fins"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "2008 0067603 discloses a odor blocking device and rainwater backflow device for sewer manholes that continuously block the occurrence of odor generated in the manhole of the sewer and also cope sensitively with the backflow caused by the rainy season flood"}]</data>
</edge>
