", "act", "include", "operate", "perform", "consist", "dispose", "open", "block", "expand", "enter", "blow", "mean", "insulate", "supply", "absorb", "use", "shield", "transfer", "raise", "propeller", "stop", "construct", "mold", "charge", "disperse", "asphyxiate", "cut", "straighten", "smooth", "throttle", "ascend", "sense", "finish", "identify", "close", "draw", "rotate", "classify", "galvanize", "maintain", "install", "improve", "control", "laminate", "case", "transmit", "register", "monitor", "characterize", "shape", "elevate", "inhale", "input", "keep", "bypass", "be", "age", "rack", "generate", "adjust", "flood", "collect", "instal", "bleed", "mark"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "connect with the test tube of the tester and check the water level of the test tube for a certain time to determine whether the leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101704960-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole inserted in the ground to block the odor coming out to the outside 10 having an inlet space 12 through which a manhole cover 1 or a rainwater inlet frame 2 10 the rainwater and the wastewater discharged from the main body 10 10 are discharged while the rainwater and the wastewater flowing into the inflow space 12 of the main body 10 a of the water tank 21 in a state of being integrally fused with the inside of the main body 10 10 and the water level a which is provided with a cleaning means 26 for selectively removing the foreign matter in the lower direction by selectively using either the a blocking portion 23 or the rotation blocking portion 24 20 the main body 10 is inserted into the main body 10 so that the upper portion of the main body 10 is inserted and stacked so that the height of the main body 10 30 having a support base 31 with a mounting groove 32 so that the upper part of another body 10 is inserted and stacked while supporting a pressure externally integrally in the interior of the body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706162-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "first the odor blocking tube 110 is formed of a synthetic resin material in the form of a cylindrical shape of the lower end is narrower and wider toward the upper end a ring shaped weight 111 is installed on the lower edge the weight 111 is the manhole body 10 it has a length that can be located below the minimum water level of the sewage flowing inside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100654756-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "when the amount of sewage flowing into the collecting manhole that is when the water level changes the elevating member blocks all of the drainage holes of the fixing plate thereby preventing the sewage from flowing back to the road through the collecting manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time the modular wetland infrastructure is preferably provided with a maintenance manhole for managing the contact oxidation tank installed at the bottom of the wetland infrastructure and the inflow water collected in the facility due to the increase of inflow flow rate it is desirable to have a water level control pipe that directly delivers water to the contact oxidation tank at the bottom of the modular wetland infrastructure and a bypass channel that bypasses the influent when the water level control is impossible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "the modular wetland infrastructure 300 maintenance to be connected to the lower contact oxidation tank 500 to maintain the contact oxidation tank 500 located in the lower portion of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 manhole 330 and if the water level of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to precipitation exceeds a certain level in order to protect the wetland by transferring the influent directly to the sedimentation tank 400 modular wetland infrastructure 300 it is preferable to have a water level control pipe 340 is installed at the bottom of the through water connection with the drainage layer connected to the settling tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "10 0850307 registration date july 29 2008 sewer pipe maintenance monitoring system remotely monitors the inside of the sewer pipe by image and monitors the sewage flow rate data measured by the flow meter sensor in conjunction with the image it relates to a sewage pipe maintenance monitoring system capable of remotely monitoring and managing sewage pipes based on accurate information by supplementing errors in flow data and a flowmeter sensor installed in a sewer pipe to measure the flow rate and water level of sewage an underwater camera installed inside the manhole to take an image of the inside of the sewer pipe an on site control panel that receives the flow rate and water level of the flow meter sensor and the captured image of the underwater camera calculates the flow rate and processes the captured image according to the transmission format sewage related data and image data are collected from the field control panel through a communication network and flow velocity water level and flow data fluctuations are analyzed to determine whether ingress water inflow water leakage occurs and image data is output to the screen to analyze data and video data"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stirring device unit 800 having a blade 820 forcibly dispersing and stirring together with the sewage a water level sensor 900 for detecting that the water level of the sewage introduced into the manhole 100 rises above a predetermined height a pump 1000 for forcibly inhaling and discharging the mixture of the sewage and sludge s stirred by the stirring device 800 the first valve 500 and the second valve 600 are opened or closed at the same time respectively and received the displacement measured from the sludge detection unit 700 to determine whether there is deposition and flows into the interior by the water level sensor 900"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention the manhole 100 embedded in the ground e the inlet pipe 200 communicated to one side of the outer peripheral surface of the manhole 100 and the outflow pipe 300 communicated to the other side of the outer peripheral surface of the manhole 200 and a manhole cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the manhole 100 to block odors and backflows from being discharged to the outside a first valve 500 mounted on the distal outer circumferential surface of the inflow pipe 200 to adjust an inflow amount of sewage flowing into the manhole 100 a second valve 600 mounted on an outer circumferential surface of the outlet pipe 300 to adjust an amount of sewage flowing out of the manhole 100 sludge detection unit 700 is installed on the inner center bottom surface of the manhole 100 and rotates at a predetermined interval to detect the presence or absence of sludge s a plurality of stirrer units 800 installed on the inner bottom surface of the manhole 100 to stir sludge and s sewage introduced into the manhole a water level sensor 900 for detecting that the water level of the sewage introduced into the manhole 100 rises above a predetermined height a pump 1000 for forcibly inhaling and discharging the mixture of the sewage and sludge s stirred by the stirring device 800 the first valve 500 and the second valve 600 are opened or closed at the same time respectively and received the displacement measured from the sludge detection unit 700 to determine whether there is deposition and flows into the interior by the water level sensor 900"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air