cting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the above mentioned patent of the prior art the opening and closing plate is provided as a buoyancy body to increase the internal water level by the inflow of sewage so that the opening and closing plate rotates to block the manhole inlet to prevent backflow of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "a backflow prevention plate 70 which allows the upper and lower spaces to be blocked at the moment when the end is in close contact with the stopper 51 of the tubular body 50 while rotating at a predetermined angle according to the water level flowing into the manhole body 10 a lift adjusting device 80 consisting of a pair of links 82 rotatably coupled to both sides of an upper surface of the lifting block 81 which is capable of lifting up and down along the lifting shaft 61 consists of a high buoyancy buoyancy body 90 is provided to be able to be elevated in the axial direction of the lifting shaft 61 along the water level of the sewage flowing into the manhole body 10 through this configuration if the flow rate of sewage flowing into the manhole body is over a certain level due to the backflow prevention structure of the manhole connected to the sewer pipe the reverse flow of sewage is suppressed at the same time without being affected by the flowing water from the upper part at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "lifting floating means 4 consisting of a lower float 42 to prevent rainwater is discharged into the sewage inlet space 13 manhole having a multi structure characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "lifting floating means 4 consisting of a lower float 42 to prevent rainwater is discharged into the sewage inlet space 13 manhole having a multi structure characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "lifting floating means 4 consisting of a lower float 42 to prevent rainwater is discharged into the sewage inlet space 13 manhole having a multi structure characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "when the rainwater starts to flow into the rainwater inflow space is fixed through the connecting means at the bottom to keep the water passage to the lowered state so that the rainwater flows into the sewage inflow space when the water level of the sewage inflow space rises it characterized in that it comprises a lifting floating means consisting of a lower float to keep the water passage is blocked to prevent the rainwater is discharged into the sewage inlet space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_149", "text": "lifting floating means 4 consisting of a lower float 42 to prevent rainwater from entering the sewage inflow space 13 it includes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032930-B1", "para_id": "claim_10", "text": "install the haunch reinforcement respectively on the left and right of the partition fixed with the fixing bolt in the part facing the partition and the inner blade of the haunch reinforcement and the part of the frp tank and the outer wing of the haunch reinforcement after fixing the haunch reinforcement material to the partition wall haunch surface f al tank by molding laminated resin and glass chopped strand mat to a thickness of 4mm or more so that the fixing bolt is not in contact with the sewage in order to prevent deformation due to the water level difference between the tanks comprising a steel reinforcing ring is installed on the inner rim of the frp tank to reinforce the strength of the frp tank when the steel reinforcing ring is configured sanding is performed on the inside of the frp tank before bonding to prevent separation of the frp material and laminated to have a thickness of 4 mm or more using a glass chopped strand mat"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4441460-B2", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "2 the method for identifying the location of the water leak in the water channel 20 is that the at least the downstream end 21 of the target area 20 a of the water channel 20 is partitioned by a corner drop 31 as an example of a partition plate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "at this time the modular wetland infrastructure is preferably provided with a maintenance manhole for managing the contact oxidation tank installed at the bottom of the wetland infrastructure and the inflow water collected in the facility due to the increase of inflow flow rate if it is exceeded it is necessary to have a water level control pipe that directly transfers water to the contact oxidizing tank through a drainage layer installed therein and a bypass channel for bypassing the influent if the water level control is impossible"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the modular wetland infrastructure 300 maintenance to be connected to the lower contact oxidation tank 500 to maintain the contact oxidation tank 500 located in the lower portion of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 manhole 330 and if the water level of the modular wetland infrastructure 300 due to precipitation exceeds a certain level in order to protect the wetland by transferring the influent directly to the sedimentation tank 400 modular wetland infrastructure 300 it is preferable to have a water level control pipe 340 is installed at the bottom of the through water connection with the drainage layer connected to the settling tank 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373478-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drain device of manholethe present invention relates to a non power drainage device of the manhole and more specifically to detect the inundation through the water level sensing buoy in the presence of the manhole inside and operate the ejector installed in the connection pipe line and the manhole pipe with a non powered water in the manhole the present invention relates to a non powered drainage device of a manhole that is quickly discharged to the outside to prevent corrosion and breakdown of facilities due to flooding inside the manhole and to maintain a clean state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373478-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the present invention when a flooding occurs in a manhole the opening and closing valve is automatically opened by a buoy rising and falling by the water level to quickly discharge the flooded water in the manhole to the outside by the suction force generated through the ejector thereby preventing corrosion or failure of the facility due to the flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100331066-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the problems of the prior art as described above reducing the impermeable membrane for removing the overload in the capillary infiltration trench during the wastewater treatment process and reducing the concrete block and decay capacity for the manhole partition with improved economic efficiency in order to increase economic efficiency and function efficiency the level of water is kept constant so that the contact between soil surface and sewage is made closer which makes the treatment of soil microorganisms active and prepares for the increase of water level due to the change of wastewater load and quantity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102165890-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this invention has the effect of preventing malfunction or performance degradation due to flooding of various sensors or moisture exposed for a long time by forming an air pocket"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101911497-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "therefore in the non power source immersion prevention system of the present invention the opening and closing valve 300 is automatically opened by the access port 200 that ascends and descends by the water level when the flooding occurs in the manhole and the water is flooded in the manhole by the suction force generated through the ejector 500 water can be rapidly discharged to the outside through the suction pipe 400 to prevent corrosion or breakdown of the facility by flooding and it is possible to immediately cope with the flooding by the person without any operation the installation cost is reduced as compared with the drainage method using the conventional pump and the pause time is set during the operation by the amount of water flowing into and discharged from the water collection container 630 provided at the upper portion of the water inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101814741-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "10 1345691 registered on december 20 2013 sewer pipe flow meter accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a method of measuring a flow rate of a sewer pipe which can measure a more accurate flow rate by removing foreign matters mixed in sewage flowing through the sewage inlet pipe and measuring the water level and flow rate of the sewage in the sewage outlet pipe .according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewing machine comprising a floor net secured to a floor of a manhole body in a manhole including a manhole body having a sewage inlet pipe connected to an upstream side and a sewage outlet pipe connected to a downstream side a wall vertically coupled to an edge of the bottom net and having an upper end coinciding with a lower end of the sewer outlet pipe and a lower end of the sewer outlet pipe a filtration means including a partition net dividing the space into a space and a downstream space and passing through the sewage and a foreign substance and a filter net coupled to an upper end of the wall in the downstream space a water level meter for measuring the level of the sewage discharged through the sewage discharge pipe a water level measuring device installed at the upper end of the peripheral wall of the sewage discharge pipe a flow rate measuring unit for measuring a flow rate of the discharged sewage an input unit for inputting a flow rate measurement mode a flow rate calculation unit for calculating a flow rate of the sewage and a sectional area of the sewage calculated from the inner diameter and the water level of the sewage discharge pipe a memory unit for storing a flow rate measurement program and storing a unique number of the manhole a control unit for outputting a control command to the water level meter and the flow rate meter according to an input signal of the input unit a control unit for acquiring a flow rate value from a flow rate data table for each of the water level and flow rate according to the flow rate value by the flow rate measuring unit and outputting the flow rate value together with the unique number of the manhole as a flow rate display value and transmits the flow rate value by the flow velocity meter to the control unit and transmits the control command of the control unit to the water level meter and a flow rate measuring unit including a display unit for displaying a flow rate display value of the control unit wherein the sewage is introduced into the manhole body through the sewage inlet pipe a step of filtering the foreign matter by the partition net and the filter net in the sewage flowing into the manhole body a step of discharging the filtered sewage to the sewage outlet pipe the flow rate measurement control command of the control unit is transmitted through the communication unit and is received by the level meter and the flow meter and the level meter is connected to the outlet of the sewage outlet pipe measuring a water level and measuring the flow rate in the sewage outlet pipe the level value measured by the level gauge and the flow rate value measured by the flow rate meter are transmitted by the communication unit and received by the control unit obtaining a flow rate value corresponding to the received water level value and flow rate value from the flow rate data table for each of the water level and the flow rate of the memory unit and outputting the display flow rate value and displaying the displayed flow rate value output from the controller on the display unit.according to the method for measuring the flow rate of the sewage pipe of the present invention it is possible to remove foreign substances in the sewage flowing into the manhole through the sewage inlet pipe thereby allowing the sewage whose foreign substances have been removed to flow out through the sewage outlet pipe the flow rate of the sewage can be measured more accurately.1 to 7 show a preferred embodiment of a flow rate measuring method of a sewer pipe according to the present invention 1 is a perspective view of an apparatus for implementing a flow rate measurement method of a sewer pipe according to the present embodiment 2 is a longitudinal sectional view 3 is a partially cutaway perspective view 4 is a partially cutaway perspective view of the filtration means 5 is a partial cutaway exploded perspective view showing a water level measuring instrument a flow velocity measuring instrument a communication part and a protective cover 6 is a functional block diagram of the flow measuring means 7 is a flowchart showing a flow rate measurement method of a sewer pipe according to the present embodiment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102634268-B1", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "this is to control device failure due to pipe blockage by blocking the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582216-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "6 is a graph showing water level measurement data according to an embodiment of the present invention divided into a water level increase interval and a water level decrease interval"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100640012-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "equipped with a receiving groove located directly below the open passage the front top surface inclined toward the receiving groove relative to the direction in which the sewage flows and the rear wall is detachably seated in the receiving groove while the rear wall is a base having a sediment receiving container formed highly and buoyancy member which is located on the surface of the sewage in the drain pipe and moves up and down according to the change of the water level of the sewage a support fixed horizontally along the buoyancy member and the drain pipe and fixed to the end of the support of the receiving groove a guide line formed at the front and having a plurality of water passages a guide line formed at an upper portion of the drain pipe to form a groove line in an up and down direction and disposed on an upper surface of the support and movably engaged with the guide line a sluice platform having a guide bar for guiding the lifting direction of the support and the sluice along the shanghai east sludge removal type manhole in the drain pipe characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750392-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the inner bottom surface of the manhole is formed in an arc shape so as to smoothly rotate when the backflow prevention plate 30 is rotated by the pressure of the sewage and the backflow prevention plate 30 is rotated according to the water level of the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101573804-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the side plate 13 is formed by pivotally bending a plurality of unit plates 131 and the upper plate 14 is conically provided so that the water tank is entirely provided in a cylindrical shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101573804-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the water tank 10 according to claim 1 wherein the water tank 10 comprises a fixing pad 11 formed on the ground to a predetermined thickness a bottom plate 12 of stainless steel which is seated and fixed on the upper surface of the fixing pad a plurality of stainless steel unit plates 131 coupled vertically at the corners of the bottom plate a skeleton plate 132 made of aluminum and spaced apart from the outside of the unit plate a side plate 13 provided with a heat insulating material 133 made of synthetic resin filled in the side plate 13 a top plate 14 coupled to the top of the side plate and having a manhole 141 inside a drain pipe 151 for discharging the ground water contained in the water tank a drain pipe 152 for natural drainage when the water level rises above the water level a cleaning pipe a safety ladder 162 for lifting the worker to the upper portion of the upper plate and an outer ladder 161 for lifting the safety ladder 162 to the upper portion of the upper ladder are provided on the outer side of the inner ladder 154 and an exterior member 16 the fixing pads 11 are arranged on the ground at predetermined heights and intervals and are provided with a concrete block 112 and a metal base frame 113 seated on the concrete block the side plates 13 and the upper plate 14 are formed in a rectangular shape and a plurality of unit plates 131 provided with a pressure distribution portion 1311 protruding in a dome shape in a convex shape are connected to each other wherein the water tank is provided with a rectangular enclosure as a whole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102476350-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an upper cover fixed to the entrance of the sewer manhole at the lower side of the grating and having openings formed on the left and right sides of the central portion which is formed long in the front and rear directions by connecting the front and rear sides a pair of opening closing doors that open and close the opening of the top cover while rotating in an up and down direction around a pair of rotational shafts installed at the center of the top cover an actuator that provides a driving force so that the opening and closing door rotates to open and close the door includes the opening of the upper cover is blocked by the opening and closing door to block the odor of sewage and the upper cover by the opening and closing door open the opening of the to allow drainage of rainwater a rainwater inlet is formed locally at one point in the central portion of the upper cover a rainwater reservoir installed in a form surrounding the rainwater inlet at the lower part of the central portion of the upper cover to block sewage odor from leaking out through the rainwater inlet and storing rainwater flowing through the rainwater inlet and the rainwater reservoir a water level sensor installed inside the water tank to measure the water level is further included and when the water level measured by the water level sensor exceeds a predetermined value the opening and closing door is operated to open the opening of the upper cover and allow drainage of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007104-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a housing having a space formed therein and having a lower portion formed therethrough and fixedly fixed to an outlet upper wall of the manhole a gate for opening and closing the outlet of the manhole while lifting up and down into the housing a telescope type guard that is fixedly coupled to the upper end of the gate and is sealed to prevent foreign substances contained in the sewage from being penetrated and made of a plurality of stretchable guards a buoy having a buoyancy of a predetermined size and fixedly coupled to an upper portion of the telescope type guard and it is installed inside the telescope type guard and is connected so that a tension force is applied between the upper end of the gate and the lower end of the mouth and even when the mouth is raised or lowered when the water level of the sewage stored in the manhole rises or falls the gate is pulled by the tension force"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007104-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the present invention provides a housing having a space portion formed therein and a bottom portion formed therethrough the housing being fixed to an upper wall of the outlet of the manhole a gate for opening and closing the outlet of the manhole while lifting up and down into the housing a telescope type guard that is fixedly coupled to an upper end of the gate and has a sealed structure to prevent foreign substances contained in sewage from penetrating and is constructed with a plurality of stretchable guards a buoy having a buoyancy of a predetermined size and fixedly coupled to an upper portion of the telescope type guard and a tension force is inserted between the upper end of the gate and the lower end of the float and inserted into the telescope type guard and even when the float rises or falls when the water level of the sewage stored in the manhole rises or falls"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007104-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition even if the sewage increases due to an increase in the effect that the gate 30 blocks the outlet 5 due to an increase in the closing pressure due to the hydraulic pressure of the sewage the concave portion in front of the blocking block 32 of the gate 30 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102451236-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a blower installed at the entrance of the manhole of the square shape geor to supply outdoor air to the inside of the square shape machine a screen device that is installed at both sides of the rectangular shape at a predetermined distance to partition the working space and generates positive pressure while supplying external air through the blower inside the working space to block the inflow of polluted air and gas into the working space and and a water level sensing device installed outside the screen device to detect the water level in the rectangular shape and generate a warning sound and a warning light when the water level is higher than the reference water level the screen device is a pair of vertical frames the length of which is adjusted fixed to both sides of the inner surface of the square hyeonggeo an electric roll screen installed horizontally on the top of the vertical frame and provided with a first wireless communication module and air circulation and water level sensing system for construction of a square frame characterized in that it is installed on the outside of the vertical frame and consists of a shielding plate for shielding the air flow between the vertical frame and the square frame"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102451236-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a blower installed at the entrance of the manhole of the square shaped geode to supply outdoor air to the inside of the square shaped geode a screen device that is installed at both sides of the rectangular shape at a predetermined distance to partition the working space and generates positive pressure while supplying external air through the blower inside the working space to block the inflow of polluted air and gas into the working space and a water level sensing device installed on the outside of the screen device to sense the water level in the rectangular shape and generate a warning sound and a warning light when the water level is higher than the reference water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the water treatment system according to claim 4 wherein the water collection channel 130 a reservoir 200 for storing initial non point contamination excellent supplied from the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants an orifice for discharging the initial boiling point contamination stored in the reservoir 200 to the first discharge pipe 290 when the level of the reservoir 200 is equal to or higher than a predetermined water level h3 a reservoir outlet 250 having a reservoir 250 and and a first discharge conduit 290 for supplying an initial boiling impurity contamination through the orifice from the reservoir outlet 250 a flow rate reducing manhole 300 is connected to the other end of the first discharge pipe 290 a partition 310 is formed in the flow rate reducing manhole 300 to reduce the flow rate of the initial nonpoint contamination supplied from the first discharge pipe 290 and smooth the flow of the initial nonpoint contamination and a second discharge conduit 320 is connected to the flow rate reducing manhole 300 to supply an initial boiling impurity contamination to the sedimentation paper 400"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in an initial high boiling point contamination treatment system 100 connected to the end of the conduit or the river water from which the polluted water is discharged to provide pollution excellence and selectively supply only the initial nonpoint pollution excellence a reservoir 200 for storing initial boiling impurity contamination provided to the water collection channel 130 of the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants a siphon pipe 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the water level of the reservoir 200 becomes equal to or higher than the height of the highest part in the reversed u shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention selectively collects only the excellent initial non point pollution due to rainfall or the like at the point where the non point polluted water is discharged and selectively collects only the excellent non and provides a technical effect of providing an initial nonpoint contamination excellent treatment system that reduces waste and increases the efficiency of decontamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "thus until the water level from the bottom of the reservoir 200 reaches the height h4 of the highest part in the u shape reversed to the siphon channel 295 the initial sludge contamination and when the water level is equal to or higher than h4 the flow rate reduced manhole 300 is supplied with the excellent initial point contamination until the water level from the bottom surface of the reservoir 200 becomes h3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "when the water level of the reservoir 200 reaches the highest level in the u shape reversed to the siphon pipe 295 the initial non point contamination surplus is limited and the flow rate reducing manhole 300 discharges the initial non point contamination excellent supplied to the sedimentation paper 400 to proceed the secondary settlement and decomposition of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100528613-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a drain pipe body 11 having coupling grooves 113 of different lengths formed in the circumferential direction with the coupling grooves 113 circumferentially formed on the gentle slope 114 the speed reducing plate 12 having a plurality of different lengths is coupled to the coupling groove 113 of the drain pipe body 11 to reduce the flow rate of the sewage and the steel ring 15 is bonded to the lower portion of the drain induction pipe 115"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100528613-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "therefore the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above to form a flow rate reduction plate for reducing the rapid flow rate of the inflow water in the drain pipe body connected to the hinge bushing and the hinge shaft formed in the support block of the opening and closing forming the opening and closing member to be operated but is formed to be rotatable by forming a magnetic strip on the opening and closing member close to the steel ring formed in the bottom of the drainage induction pipe by magnetic force to prevent the back flow the water level has been due to the back flow in this case when the switching member is closed the led lamp formed in the drain pipe body emits light by contacting the switch to easily identify the state of the collecting manhole from the outside to provide a backflow prevention structure of the sewage pipe that prevents the backflow that serves as a countermeasure and disaster prevention the purpose is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore it is characterized by controlling and managing the operation of the pump by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal drainage reservoir water level of the manhole operating conditions of the pump inlet pressure and discharge pressure for each block reservoir customer and manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4964402-B2", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "it is a whole block diagram of the management system of a water treatment facility.it is a schematic diagram of a manhole pump facility.it is a front view in a control box.it is a front view of a controller.it is a block diagram of a controller.it is a flowchart figure of an automatic drainage process.it is a timing chart figure which shows the drive timing of the pump by a reverse drive means.it is a block diagram of a monitoring control server.it is a facility condition screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an operating current history management screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is a pump daily report screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an alarm management screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an alarm detail screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.it is an apparatus operation condition display screen figure displayed on the client terminal side.4 pump 6 controller 7 monitoring control server management device 13 internet communication line 14 manhole water tank 17 control box 18 water level sensor 19 temperature sensor temperature detection means 22 pump breaker 27 communication unit communication means 30 breaker sensor 33 automatic calling means 38 packet charging communication network communication network 39 information display means 51 operating current management screen 63 alarm details screen 64 device status display screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102744945-B1", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "9 shows a case where activated carbon parts 166 are installed at two intervals which means that a space 167 is formed between the upper and lower activated carbon parts 166 so that the odorous substances move slowly in the upper and lower activated carbon parts 166 and are adsorbed on the activated carbon and move quickly in the space 167 without resistance thereby shortening the time for removing the odor.100 manhole pump station 110 manhole pump station body 111 upper space 112 lower space 113 manhole 114 exhaust pipe 115 foothold 116 doorway 117 opening door 118 railing 119 ladder 120 inlet pipe unit 121 inlet pipe 122 inlet pipe 123 curved pipe 124 diffusion guide plate 130 pump 131 discharge pipe 140 opening closing opening 141 hinge pin 142 rotating cover 143 handle 144 cover holder 150 odor exhaust device 151 lower exhaust pipe 152 exhaust fan 153 exhaust hood 154 upper exhaust pipe 155 flexible corrugated pipe 156 corrugated pipe holder 157 detachable member 160 secondary odor remover 161 door 162 casing 163