  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101283731-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is connected to the dredging suction hose 2 to dredge the accumulated sediment in the pipeline through the manhole 3 and the hydraulic hose 4 that the hydraulic pressure for the operation of the cylinder flows in and out of the rear in the dredging robot 10 is provided with a cable 6 is connected to the control unit 5 so as to transmit and receive the dredging operation to the server in real time a rectangular frame 100 which is provided with a driving device inside and is moved back and forth caterpillar shaped transfer wheels 200 which are connected to both sides of the frame 100 to transfer the dredging robot 10 back and forth a bucket part 300 connected to the front surface of the frame 100 and moved up down left right and back and dredging the deposit to discharge the dredging suction hose 2 a plurality of pipe support members 400 installed on both sides of the frame 100 and foldable so as to be in close contact with side surfaces of the pipe line 1 so as not to flow when moving back and forth and left and right a monitoring device 500 installed at an upper portion of the frame 100 to check a state and a working condition of the pipeline 1 bucket type pipeline dredge robot characterized in that consisting of pocket portion 700 for receiving the deposits of solids dredged in the bucket portion 300 in the rear of the frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200406578-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an independent manhole having an upper surface with a predetermined volume of space and embedded at the edge of the road to expose the upper surface a plurality of water outlet holes are formed in a circumferential surface thereof and the water pipes are buried in the basement layer made of earth and sand supporting the road while communicating with the space of the independent manhole a drain pipe communicating with the space of the independent manhole and the space of another adjacent manhole and a wall having a double sided tubular shape and fixed to a space between the space of the free standing manhole and the drain pipe a wall having an opening formed to block an open side of the guide and having a cutout formed in a predetermined width and rotatable with the fixed base"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200406578-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "a wall having a double sided tubular shape and fixed to a space between the space of the free standing manhole and the drain pipe a wall having an opening formed to block an open side of the guide and having a cutout formed in a predetermined width and rotatable with the fixed base"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "sewage and rainwater is introduced and drained the manhole body is provided to open the upper portion a manhole cover coupled to the upper portion of the manhole body to allow the introduction of rainwater and it includes a backflow prevention unit is provided to block the backflow of sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body drained the backflow prevention unit an induction part coupled to the inside of the manhole body and having a hollow tube protruding from a lower surface in a central part to induce drainage and rainwater a backflow prevention buoy coupled to the hollow tube to prevent separation and provided to block the hollow tube by upward movement by water pressure when the sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body are drained a support portion coupled between the hollow tube and the backflow prevention buoy to support an upward movement of the backflow prevention buoy and to include a guide screwed to the hollow tube the backflow prevention buoy an upper body having a diameter smaller than the inner diameter of the hollow tube and a lower body disposed below the upper body so as to have a diameter larger than the inner diameter of the hollow tube to block the hollow tube by upward pressure to block the hollow tube part and it is coupled to the upper end of the upper body and when the blocking portion is a downward movement to allow the drainage of the sewage and rainwater after the upward movement by the hydraulic pressure includes a locking portion which is provided to be prevented from being separated from the surface of the support the support portion an inner support having a support hole for supporting the upper body therein to support the upward movement of the blocking unit and characterized in that it comprises an outer support connected to the inner support and a plurality of partitions to form a drainage passage connected to the hollow tube is disposed at regular intervals to have the same concentric circles on the outside of the inner support backflow prevention manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007104-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition even if the sewage increases due to an increase in the effect that the gate 30 blocks the outlet 5 due to an increase in the closing pressure due to the hydraulic pressure of the sewage the concave portion in front of the blocking block 32 of the gate 30 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007104-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition even if the sewage increases due to an increase in the effect that the gate 30 blocks the outlet 5 due to an increase in the closing pressure due to the hydraulic pressure of the sewage the concave portion in front of the blocking block 32 of the gate 30 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156757-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "double manhole cover with lifting structure linked type double manhole cover the present invention relates to a manhole cover installed in the manhole and more particularly by forming a double manhole cover formed in a double so as to be selectively opened and closed while interlocking with the hydraulic pressure inside the manhole the sewage in the manhole the double manhole cover which is selectively opened by water pressure controls the pressure inside the manhole to maintain a certain pressure below a certain pressure even if it flows backward so that the manhole cover is separated by the high water pressure inside the manhole or each connection part of the manhole and the pipe connected thereto"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156757-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the simple manhole cover is formed when the manhole cover is detached to the outside due to the high water pressure inside the manhole during the backflow of sewage due to torrential rain etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101156757-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole cover installed in the manhole and more particularly by forming a double manhole cover formed in a double so as to be selectively opened and closed while interlocking with the hydraulic pressure inside the manhole the sewage in the manhole the double manhole cover which is selectively opened by water pressure controls the pressure inside the manhole to maintain a certain pressure below a certain pressure even if it flows backward so that the manhole cover is separated by the high water pressure inside the manhole and it relates to a double manhole cover having a hinge type lifting structure characterized in that to prevent the fragile portion from being broken and to facilitate the locking of the double manhole cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306445-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the pipeline expansion device 1 includes an expander 11 for reshaping the deformation of the pipeline a a hydraulic electric pump 12 for generating hydraulic pressure to supply the expander 11 it is composed of a hydraulic line 13 for supplying the hydraulic pressure to the expander 11 and the hydraulic pressure is recovered to the hydraulic electric pump 12 the pipeline image photographing apparatus 2 includes a cctv camera 21 for inspecting the state inside the pipeline a and monitoring the rehabilitation work with the expander 11 it is composed of a rotating device unit 22 having a circumferential rotation device 221 to enable the cctv camera 21 to rotate in the circumferential direction and a vertical rotation device 222 to enable angle adjustment up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200450491-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in configuring the odor prevention device 110 to prevent the odor coming up from the ground the odor prevention device 110 includes a prevention body 112 having a seating flange 111 upward to be seated on the bottom surface of the manhole cover 105 the prevention body 112 and the first vertical portion 113 protrudes downward from the mounting flange 111 an inclined portion 114 formed to have a width narrowed inward from an end of the first vertical portion 113 a second vertical portion 115 projecting downward from the end of the inclined portion 114 a plurality of water passages 116 formed to drain a small amount of rainwater to the inclined portion 114 a discharge hole 117 formed to be opened between the second vertical portions 115 to discharge a large amount of rain and garbage deformed by the hydraulic pressure of the sewage to the water hole 116 while being drained down and after completion of drainage to return to the original state to prevent the odor coming up through the water hole 116 fixing the blocking plate 118 of a material having elasticity and excellent return force the discharge hole 117 is a sewer manhole odor prevention device characterized in that it comprises a rotating plate 120 installed so as to block the odor coming up while draining the rain and waste of the opposite"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101206997-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "making a step installing fixed tube guide means each having a predetermined shape at an inlet of the manhole and an inlet of the conduit installing a movable traction force attenuator for reducing the traction force of the traction winch between the front fixing portion of the first flexible tube and the wire of the traction winch towing the first flexible tube mounted on the flexible tube feeder equipped with the freezing facility in the state where the curable resin is impregnated into the predetermined section of the pipeline to be rehabilitated through the manhole using a towing winch inverting injecting the resin impregnated second flexible tube inside the first flexible tube pulled into the conduit using hydraulic pressure or air pressure to cause the resin impregnated portions of the first and second flexible tubes to adhere to each other by inverting the second flexible tube a heat source is supplied to the first and second flexible tubes having a state in which the second flexible tube is in close contact with the inner wall of the pipeline to harden and integrate the resin impregnated in the first and second flexible tubes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050751-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "foul smell isolation installation of manhole the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of the manhole and more particularly a plate in which an inlet hole is formed in the center portion to support the manhole cover to inflow the external fluid a reservoir formed in the lower end of the plate and the reservoir it is composed of a blocking film to seal the lower end is normally closed by gravity and magnetic material the blocking film automatically seals the lower end of the reservoir to smoothly block odors flowing back and forth from the water and sewage an open film is formed on the blocking film the open film is a blocking film by rotating to the contrary in rainy or rainy days the water and sewage pipes are flooded and opened to the backflowing fluid to discharge the fluid to the outside to prevent the opening of the manhole by hydraulic pressure thereby preventing personal injury blocking network is installed on the upper surface so that filtering out substances relate to the odor barrier device of a manhole which can prevent clogging of a phase by a foreign matter sewage or bad smell blocking device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the water pipe inspection device equipped with a valve 130 between the manhole 110 and the water connection pipe 120 the manhole 110 is formed in a cylindrical shape so that any one is not subjected to concentrated stress due to hydraulic pressure and a b shaped mounting groove 111 is formed around the upper opening 115 and has a disc shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10 0816410 registered on march 18 2008 more specifically the manhole is made of a cylindrical one of the manhole the present invention relates to a water conduit inspection device which can prevent stress concentration from occurring in a portion and that lifting shafts are disposed at both side ends of the opening closing partition to prevent the lifting shafts from being deformed by hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however the water supply pipe inspection device is disposed in the center of the opening and closing partition lifting shaft the lifting shaft may be deformed or damaged by the water pressure of the water passing through the water pipe the opening and closing partition is inoperable when the lifting shaft is deformed"}]</data>
