  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859661-B1", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "as described above the pc structural type manhole 300 is provided with a water gate or valve 500 for a connection pipe of a wastewater treatment plant which is a water gate or valve for discharging an initial storm water to a wastewater treatment plant or a valve 600 for a river connection which is a water gate or a valve for performing opening and closing of the water gate or valve and constitutes an opening and closing device 550 or 650 for opening and closing the water gate by controlling according to the control signal of the configured rtu it is possible to prevent manhole accidents efficiently and to manage the initial storm including contamination source in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101826790-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "at the upper part a sloping induction plate is installed at the tip of the first drainage guide plate a second settling filtration tank for blocking inflow of fine contaminants accompanied by the storm and having a filter net installed on the downflow channel formed by the lower part of the precipitation inducing plate and the first drainage guide plate to remove the dissolved fine contaminants a second rim hole formed in the upper portion of the first drainage guide plate of the secondary settling filtration tank and having a second rim hole and a second rim hole formed in the second rim of the second settling filtration tank the second partition wall is provided with a drain plate for partitioning the space with the second settling filtration tank and discharging the rainwater having an inclined surface at the inlet side and flowing into the second rinse hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101694827-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention relates to an initial good treatment apparatus capable of effectively preventing contaminants mixed with an initial storm due to contamination of a river lake by effectively treating contamination mixed with the initial rainwater by a pretreatment tank and a filtration tank an inlet pipe for guiding the initial storm of the gut pipe to the pretreatment tank and an inlet pipe connected to the filtration tank of the main body the main body is located at the same depth as the gutter tube and the inlet tube is formed higher than the outlet tube at the position of the water head and the initial gutter inside the main body is moved by the water head difference quot an early stormwater treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101968568-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stormwater catch type sewage treatment system having a nonpoint pollutant removal function a cartridge case into which a cartridge receiving groove into which a plurality of drain holes are perforated is inserted a filter cartridge inserted into the cartridge receiving groove a granular filter media contained in the filter cartridge a rainwater catch cover which is seated on the upper portion of the cartridge case and in which an inflow hole is formed and a plurality of opening and closing members that are mounted to close the drain hole and open at the inflow of the storm the cartridge case includes a case body protruding in an arc shape and pierced with the drain hole a seating frame protruding from the upper end of the case body a compartment protrusion protruding in the longitudinal direction at the center of the cartridge receiving recess and a cartridge binding portion formed on the inner surfaces of the front and rear side walls of the case body wherein the cartridge binding portion has a function of removing nonpoint contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the metering water guide 30 excludes a certain amount of initial storm the initial storm is inadequate to use due to a high degree of contamination due to various pollutants in the air and in the present invention a certain amount of initial storm is stored in the user storage 300 that is discharging to the discharge pipe 12 and some rainwater flowing into the catchment tank 10 is collected in the buoyancy chamber 15 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101840603-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "the smart watering method using the number of floors according to the preferred embodiment of the present invention having the above described structure is characterized in that a water pipe is connected or deep water is developed to extract water and a large amount of underwater pump is installed unlike the existing method which was charged for the installation fee and the production cost it extracts the number of storm floors from the first impervious layer penetrating into the basement and substitutes all the power required for extraction and watering from the natural resource power module it is possible to implement irrigation with a low cost and low budget and to contribute to environmental preservation by utilizing the number of floors with the possibility of contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore the present inventors install a sensor that can detect the concentration even if the height of the ware and the connecting pipe diameter are increased in order to prevent an overflow accident so that the amount of the sewage flowing into the collecting pipe according to the inflow of the sewage and the degree of contamination is appropriate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention can be centrally integrated management of each rainwater tortilla 20 connected to the conduit line for this purpose each rainwater tosoil 20 connected to the conduit line in 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101744938-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "when the measured degree of contamination of the initial stormwater is equal to or less than the set reference pollution value 1000 formed on one side of the initial storm drain pipe 600 to provide a closure signal to the first storm drain pipe 600 in this case the opening closing means 500 is not closed even when the closing signal due to the lapse of the set opening time is received from the rainwater detection control device 700 and is closed when receiving the closing signal from the pollution judgment means 1000 wherein said non point contaminated initial good treatment system comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the spring engaging groove 440 is coupled to one side of the wear plate driving spring 300 the wear plate operating spring 600 when the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater is small or there is no inflow of sewage and stormwater the weir plate 200 is rotated at an angle of inclination at all times at least one side of the wear plate 200 and one side and the other side of the sewage line 10 are formed on the left side and the right side of the center of the wear plate 200 so as to be rotated by the elastic force of the wear plate 600 respectively the pressure of the sewage and the storm that the wear plate 200 is rotated is adjusted by using the wear plate driving spring 300 and the driving spring adjusting nut 400 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be rotated or fixed when the inflow amount of the sewage and the storm is small it is possible to block and minimize the inflow of sewage and to prevent the inflow of sewage and stormwater by effectively opening and closing the ware plate 200 to prevent the contamination of the stream and the upper surface of the wear plate 200 is configured to be wider than the lower surface of the lower surface of the wear plate 200 when the wear plate 200 is rotated due to inflow of sewage and storm and the sewage and stormwater are completely prevented from flowing into the sewage pipe 10 by the upper surface and the frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand according to another embodiment of the present invention it is possible to centrally manage each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe line for this purpose in each rainwater toil 20 connected to the conduit pipe rainwater tosoil 20 is provided with a water level sensor 50 for measuring the amount of sewage flowing into and a sensing unit including an electrical conductivity or ss sensor 51 for detecting the degree of contamination the connection pipe 21 of each rainwater chamber 20 is provided with an opening and closing portion including a water gate 70 for opening and closing the orifice of the connection pipe 21 and a drive motor 71 for raising and lowering the water gate 70 the controller 60 receiving the signal of each sensing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "10 1604465 filed and patented by the applicant of the present application includes a collecting tank having an initial storm drainage chamber and a buoyancy chamber collecting stormwater a screen installed in the water collecting tank and filtering the foreign substances contained in the water flowing through the inlet of the water collecting tank an initial storm drain pipe for discharging stormwater and foreign matter collected in the initial storm drain chamber to the initial storm drain chamber after being supplied through the screen a clean water discharge pipe connected to the buoyancy chamber of the water collecting tank and guiding the stormwater collected in the buoyancy chamber to the storage unit for recycling a metering water guide installed in the water collecting tank and guiding part of the water flowing into the water collecting tank to the buoyancy chamber when the initial storm is discharged through the initial storm drain pipe by storing a predetermined amount of metering water by the metering water guide while guiding the storm introduced into t