is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101788120-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "according to the present invention the storm reservoir is capable of originally suppressing the inflow of the initial stormwater or the sewage selectively picking up only the peak flow rate in the stormwater storage and drainage system does not generate odor reduce administrative costs and effort by reducing.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100782992-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "582121 excellent storage tank is formed in each corner of the top plate and the bottom plate so that the opening is formed on the side of the cube respectively a plurality of nut settlement grooves are formed on the top and bottom of each column a storage block having a stepped portion formed on at least one side of the top plate and a joining portion formed integrally with the base surface on the bottom plate and an upper surface block having a rectangular plate shape and having an end mounted on the upper surface plate step portion of the storage block to form the same plane as the upper surface plate of the storage block wherein the storage blocks are repeatedly arranged in a straight line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101529143-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the float prevention member 30 is formed in a conical shape inclined so that the outer periphery thereof faces downward and a plurality of outflow holes 32 are formed on the surface to block the clogs and pass the storm surges"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the rainwater introduced into the storm reservoir is formed at the half point of the height of the slab 3 as described above so that the rainwater flowed into the storm reservoir is about 50 of the water into the basement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720398-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "it is possible to secure the strength and because the drain pipe is normally blocked by the odor backflow installed in the drain pipe it is possible to block the odor backflow from the sewage main pipe to the rainwater receiving side"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101277086-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition while the construction of the prior art has many problems in construction due to the dimensional deviation the present invention solved the construction problem by the dimensional deviation using a separate jig using the recess formed on the top of each pillar block it is characterized in that the stability is improved by preventing the fall or fall of the upper sphere during construction to solve the stability problems when assembling and installing the conventional rainwater storage tank and more economical by providing a rainwater storage tank that can be various construction depending on the limited space as an excellent storage tank it has not only satisfactory function but also stability and it is effective to improve long term durability by external wire speech method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "a storage block having a plurality of nut settling grooves formed at upper and lower portions of each column at least one side of the top plate having a stepped portion and a bottom portion of the bottom plate having a coupling portion integrally with the base surface it consists of a top block having a rectangular plate shape and the end is mounted on the top plate step of the storage block to form the same plane as the top plate of the storage block the storage block is repeatedly arranged in a straight line a plurality of the upper blocks are configured to be coupled between the storage blocks in a straight line to form a storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in the storm storage tank configured as described above the shape of the main block of the storm storage tank of patent registration no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "at this time the rain inlet 32 may be formed in the upper plate 30 as described above but formed on the upper end of the outer wall block 20 that is the outer wall according to the rain storage tank 1 of the present invention buried underground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "on the other hand the outer wall block 20 20a 20b of another embodiment applied to the storm storage tank 1 of the present invention one side is shown in figure 3 a is closed and the other side forms an opening 22 while the front and rear and the bottom is opened with a c shaped block body 20 as shown in figure 5 the overall shape is formed as a rectangular block body of the one or both ends of the a shape block bodies 20a and 20b having a structure in which the mounting protrusion 25 protrudes are installed to be mixed with each other and the outer wall block 20 having the structure a of fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "according to the present invention it is possible to reduce the risk of local flooding due to heavy rain in the city center while reducing the necessity of excavation and replacement of existing sewerage or storm drainage in the urban roads thereby reducing social costs such as traffic congestion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101615356-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "the method of claim 4 the settler flow rate attenuation apparatus comprises a flow attenuator having a trapezoidal shape in which an upper end of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe is disposed higher than an inner center of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe so that the sedimentation tank inflow pipe is inclined so as to block at least an outlet of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe a screen screen unit detachably coupled to a lower end of the flow velocity reduction unit and and a detailed screen unit connected to the bottom screen of the weft screen unit to have the same width as the weft screen unit and having a relatively small perforation compared to the weft screen unit when the flow rate is attenuated through the flow rate attenuating unit and the storm is introduced the contaminants contained in the storm are collected through the detailed screen unit and when the detailed screen unit is blocked the stormwater is supplied to the settling tank through the screen unit characterized by a nonpoint pollutant treatment system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101615356-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the sedimentation tank flow rate damping device has a trapezoidal shape having a trapezoidal shape in which the upper end of the sedimentation tank flow in pipe is disposed higher than the inner center of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe and is inclined so as to block at least half of the outlet of the sedimentation tank inflow pipe attenuator a screen screen unit detachably coupled to a lower end of the flow velocity reduction unit and a concave screen unit connected to the bottom screen of the weft screen unit to have the same width as the weft screen unit and having relatively small pores as compared with the weft screen unit the contaminants contained in the storm can be collected through the detail screen unit and when the detail screen unit is closed the stormwater can be supplied to the settling tank through the screen screen unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654689-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "in the present application the terms comprises or having and the like are used to specify that there is a feature a number a step an operation an element a component or a combination thereof described in the specification but do not preclude the presence or addition of one or more other features integers steps operations elements components or combinations thereof.1 filter block 11 11 block body 111 distribution hole 12 12 cover 13 13 support member 131 132 separation preventing protrusion 133 fastening plate 2 rainwater drain cover member 4 filter block assembly 41 filter assembly part 411 stone publication 412 connecting plate 413 fitting groove 42 seat rest portion 5 rain storm housing 51 seating jaw 52 drain passage h inlet opening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101468324-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "10 a the third open close board 40 of the present invention can be shut off passively so that even when the rain is over in the event of an emergency the river floods or exceeds the sewage treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant it is possible to block a multiple of the initial storm stored in the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 is a schematic view showing a flow rate control apparatus of a non dynamic flow rate control system according to the present invention a rectangular outer frame 6 which is seated on an upper part of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 and opens front and rear to open the lower part to block odors and to guide sewage and a flow control device 5 detachably mounted on the inner side of the outer frame 6 to control the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater to flow out to the sewage water collection pipe 2 the flow control device 5 includes an inner frame 10 detachably attached to the outer frame by a drawer a plate shaped rotary plate member 20 having a center shaft 21 at the lower end of the inner frame 10 and rotating up and down to guide the sewage contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream while controlling the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater wow the water flow control device 5 includes a water flow rotary shaft 31 rotatably mounted on the inside of the flow control device 5 and is fixed to the water flow rotary shaft 31 so as to be in close contact with both inner side walls of the flow control device 5 30 of a wall like shape opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 21 of the rotary plate member 20 so that the rotary plate member 20 is rotated in the non and a link portion 40 the outer frame 6 is seated at the distal end of the sewage pipe and an inner frame 10 is detachably attached to the inner side of the outer frame 6 by a drawer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when the wind is blown the odor preventing curtain is opened and the odor is generated.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned disadvantages of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a non powered flow rate control device for preventing malodorous flow which comprises a flow rate control device which is detachably attached to a distal end portion of a sewer pipe and it is possible to collect all the high initial initial storms generated at the beginning of the sewage or rainfall that flow in the usual way into the sewage subtraction channel and the rain that flows in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall it is possible to prevent the overflowing of the stormwater by reducing the outflow section of the sewage and to naturally induce the slurry moving along with the storm into the river to prevent the accumulation of the slurry on the sewage drainage pipe which is in close contact with the inner side wall surfaces of the flow rate regulating device while being rotated up and down odor proof packing is installed on the wall to block off odors generated in the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "to provide.according to the sewage pipe structure having the foreign matter filter net structure of the present invention the foreign matter mixed in the stormwater flowing along the sidewalk or the roadway is blocked by the foreign matter blocking portion and only the excellent storages are introduced into the storm receiving portion it is possible to minimize the flow resistance of the sewage and to minimize the generation of odor due to the corruption of the foreign matter by reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant and periodically removing the filtered foreign matter.1 to 7 show a preferred embodiment of a sewerage pipe structure having a foreign matter filtering network structure according to the present invention 1 and 2 are perspective views showing the installation state of a sewerage conduit structure having a trash filter network structure according to the present embodiment as seen from a side of a delivery side and a side view of a vehicle fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847553-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent filtration part 100 formed in a circular pipe shape penetrating the lower sidewall of the manhole 1 to filter out contaminants and suspended matters of excellent quality and at least one or more excellent penetration block boxes 200 each having a plate top plate 210 and a box shaped block main body 220 in which water permeable holes 201 are formed on the wall surface 20 for forming a reservoir space for storing stormwater flowing through the reservoir the superfiltration unit 100 a filtration tube 110 disposed at one side of the manhole 1 in the direction of a side wall of the manhole 1 in order to treat the contaminants and dirt that may flow into the lower portion of the manhole 1 a connection pipe 120 disposed outside the sidewall of the manhole 1 so as to communicate with the other side of the filtration cylinder 110 in order to inject the storm that passes through the filtration cylinder 110 into the storage vessel 20 and and a joint pipe 130 vertically penetrating the sidewall of the manhole 1 with an accommodation space for communicating the filtration cylinder 110 and the connection pipe 120 the filtering cylinder 110 and a plurality of upper filter banks 111a which are arranged at a predetermined interval and have a semicircular shape on the upper side of the width directional section with respect to the intermediate net 111a 111 having a filter body 111b and a filtering medium 112a disposed on the lower side of the widthwise end surface of the filtration outer casing 111 with respect to the intermediate mesh 111a and an inner filtration net 112b having a circular mesh at the longitudinal end thereof and a filtration inner tube 112 housed inside the filtration outer tube 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847553-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the prefabricated infiltration storage tank according to an embodiment of the present invention includes a superior filtration unit 100 formed in a circular tube shape penetrating a lower sidewall of a manhole 1 to filter out contaminants and suspended matters of excellent quality and at least one storm block unit 200 having a box shaped block body 220 and a plate like block top plate 210 having a water permeable hole 201 formed on a wall surface thereof and a reservoir 20 forming a reservoir space for storing the storm that flows through the reservoir 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847553-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "in addition the present invention has an effect of enhancing construction cost and productivity because a storage tank can be easily installed by using an excellent penetration block box that can be assembled by fastening a block top plate and a block body.1 is a schematic view showing a configuration of a prefabricated infiltration storage tank according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "2 in order to reduce the resistance to the flow of the initial storm that flows into the plates 121 and 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a storage block having a plurality of nut settling grooves formed at upper and lower portions of each pillar at least one side of the top plate having a stepped portion and a bottom portion of the bottom plate having a coupling portion integrally with the base surface it consists of a top block having a rectangular plate shape and the end is mounted on the top plate step of the storage block to form the same plane as the top plate of the storage block the storage block is repeatedly arranged in a straight line a plurality of the upper blocks are configured to be coupled between the storage blocks in a straight line to form a storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in the storm storage tank configured as described above the shape of the main block of the storm storage tank of patent registration no"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101770268-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "according to the present invention only a crush stone is installed at the lower end of the reservoir structure so as to penetrate not only the reservoir of the storm but also the stormwater and by implementing the water circulation system penetrating into the ground through the reservoir with the upper reservoir and the lower reservoir it is possible to keep reservoirs and infiltration for water circulation and thus to prevent flooding even in temporary s