umping of solids or food waste through the storm discharge pipe due to the lack of consciousness of the residents for the integrated rainwater catchment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "is protruded is provided so as to be spaced apart from the bottom of the road side catch port 10 the horizontal catch plate 94 is adjusted to the height according to the water level flowing through the road side catch port 10 by the buoyancy body 92 and the coarse coarse collusion through lower rainwater downflow horizontal collecting plate 94 it is characterized in that it is provided to be filtered through the water filtration network 96 .according to the above configuration and operation the present invention is to embed the storage tank in the bottom of the flower bed formed between the road and the sidewalk to quickly absorb and collect rainwater flowing along the road during rainy weather and to supply the rainwater stored in the storage tank to the lower flower bed it helps to drown landscaping water and in particular contaminants contained in rainwater can be easily filtered and recycled into water resources including road cooling water road washing water and digestive water to contribute to water shortage.1 is a block diagram showing the stormwater storage system as a whole for vegetation infiltration according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889975-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention the storeroom 100 may include a grating seating surface 121 formed in a boundary area between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 wherein the grating 200 comprises a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insert tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 formed in a grid shape inside the grating frame 210 to block rainwater into the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter the grating frame 210 is formed to protrude at a predetermined interval in an area contacting the grating seating surface 121 so that the soil introduced into the grating frame 210 from the grating insertion tube 120 and the grating frame 210 is separated from the grinding frame 210 and a plurality of the soil inflow teeth 240 for inflowing into the interior of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665326-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "the width of the lateral grooves 131 or the longitudinal grooves 132 may be equal to or greater than the diameter of the upper ends of the drain holes 135 a buffer space 134 may be formed in which an excellent light or the like is temporarily stored above the upper end of the drain hole 135"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665326-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "the width of the lateral grooves 131 or the longitudinal grooves 132 may be equal to or greater than the diameter of the upper ends of the drain holes 135 a buffer space 134 may be formed in which an excellent light or the like is temporarily stored above the upper end of the drain hole 135"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "therefore according to the present invention it is possible to efficiently use the storages stored in the road boundary block since the water is stored without discharging the water in the wet state immediately after the rain and the storm is drained to the ground when the ground is dry.1 is a perspective view showing a state in which a road boundary block according to an embodiment of the present invention is installed fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in order to prevent the foreign matter such as soil from flowing into the storm drain pipe 25 the storm drain pipe 25 may be inclined downward or the storm drain pipe 25 may be bent downward"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in addition rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "at this time the rainwater that is filtered through the first storage block 10 and a plurality of storage blocks 10 adjacent to each other repeatedly is introduced into the storage space s connected to each other via the above described downstream guide pipe 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676378-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "a stream type water circulation system comprising a water permeable press block unit for forming a walkway to which a pedestrian passes a communicating passage provided in parallel with the water permeable press block unit and capable of receiving rainwater from the water a conveyance pipe member for conveying rainwater infiltrated downward through the water permeable press block unit a filter for filtering the rainwater flowing through the communication channel of the irrigation channel and the conveyance pipe member a filtration unit a storage unit arranged to receive and store the filtered storm in the filtration unit and a pump for supplying the water to the upstream of the river or the irrigation water channel wherein the filtration unit is installed in the inflow tank in which the rainwater flows from the conveyance pipe member the rainwater flows upward from the lower part and a backwashing unit installed at an upper portion of the filtration unit and backwashing the fluidized media wherein the filtration unit has an upper sieve net and a lower sieve net installed between the fluidized media a stream type water circulation system in which an air inlet is provided at the upper part of the screen to disturb the fluid phase media by air during backwashing of the backwashing unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100988806-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "furthermore the present invention is possible to adjust the spacing between the construction of the holding member as the outer wall and the support member the upper plate and the lower plate is divided into the box shaped body block of the conventional hexahedral form it is possible to clean by a small equipment which is installed it is possible to reduce the number of holding members to facilitate the maintenance and to provide an excellent storm storage tank and construction method that can reduce the material cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100977492-B1", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "4 the fixed block 18 may not be provided when the storm soil chamber 3 is narrow and the frame 10 is supported over the storm soil chamber 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to the block type storm reservoir according to the present invention the corner block the side block and the inner block can be easily assembled to the base block and in particular in order to increase the height of the storage space the stacking of the blocks in multiple layers can be easily performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101051778-B1", "para_id": "para_79", "text": "as described above the storm storage block 100 is formed in a smaller number than the inlet opening 130 and has a discharge port 140 for discharging the amount of rain that is less than the amount of rain that flows into the body 110 each unit cell rainwater may be temporarily stored inside c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101921821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 to the sewage water collection line 2 and discharges a large amount of rainwater flowing into the continuous rainwater to the river smoothly a rectangular outer frame 10 which is formed in a box shape to be seated on an upper portion of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 to block malodors and opens to the front and rear to guide sewage an inner frame 20 detachably attached to the inside of the outer frame 10 by a drawer a wall like opening closing gate 30 connected to the upper side of the inner frame 20 by a hinge portion 31 so as to be opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced the sewage water supply system according to the present invention is characterized in that the sewage water supply pipe 2 is connected to the opening closing water gate 30 40 the flow rate regulator 40 includes a center shaft 41a at the lower end of the inner frame 20 and is rotated upward and downward to adjust the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while guiding the soil contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate center shaft 41a of the rotary plate 41 so that the rotary plate 41 and a link portion 42 for rotating the link member in a non the upper portion of the link portion 42 is engaged with the first link pin 42a at the upper end of the upper side of the interchange gate 30 and the lower end of the link portion 42 is inserted when the interchange gate 30 is opened by inserting the second link pin 42b an upper link 42c for transmitting the rotational force to the lower link 42e and a sliding hole 42d having an elongated shape for sliding the second link pin 42b of the upper link 42c on the upper side and a lower link 42e whose lower side is coupled to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 41a of the rotary plate 41 and is coupled together with the upper link 42c so that the opening and closing gate 30 is opened and the rotating plate 41 is rotated in synchronization with the rotating force generated when the rotating plate 41 is rotated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102075013-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the channel flow rate reduction apparatus for preventing river overflow according to an embodiment of the present invention has a shape corresponding to the channel and is fixed in position to be in close contact with the inner wall and the bottom surface of the channel a channel installation main body providing a first flow path flowing through the upper rainwater and sliding assembly in the direction intercepting the first flow path from the upper portion of the water channel installation body having a narrow flow cross sectional area than the first flow path at least one block assembly providing a second flow path to reduce storm flow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "10 1030605the present invention has been made to solve the above mentioned problems and it is an object of the present invention to prevent storm flooding by storing rainwater reduce load on a sewage treatment plant prevent urban heat island and replenish water resources the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a method of constructing a reservoir tank having a non point pollutant reduction type prefabricated reservoir block and a nonpoint source pollution reduction function using the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101927400-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the storage tank includes a nonpoint source pollution reduction device installed at one end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the storm reservoir tank to remove contaminants and non point pollutants contained in the rainwater flowing through the inlet and an upper water purification unit installed at the other end of the inner hollow ceiling portion of the stormwater storage tank to pumped stormwater stored in the stor age storage tank through the nonpoint pollutant reduction apparatus to highly purify the purified water a device the piping is installed at one end so as to be submerged in the stormwater in the storm reservoir and the other end has a high pressure spray nozzle at the end and is installed in the upper hollow portion of the storm reservoir an air supply device comprising an installed water supply pipe a pump mounted on the water supply pipe and pumping rainwater in an excellent storage tank and an air supply unit mounted on an exposed part of the water supply pipe and injecting air into the rainwater pumped into the water supply pipe the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention can be achieved by a storm water storage tank.the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention prevents or minimizes the flood damage in the event of heavy rainfall and has a non point pollution source reduction device an advanced water purification device and an air supply device it is stored in a reduced state and continuously supplies the air in the storm water to be stored for a long period of time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889974-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an excellent storage tank 100 which is embedded in the inside of the ground and receives stormwater introduced from the ground a grating 200 rotatably coupled to the upper surface of the superior storage tank 100 for introducing the stormwater into the storage tank and blocking the foreign material a dirt collecting box 400 provided in the superior storage tank 100 for filtering dirt contained in the rainwater and a collection box support 300 provided at an upper portion of the superior storage container 100 and supporting the dirt collection box 400 the storm reservoir 100 a reservoir body 110 in which the storm is stored a grating insert tube 120 formed on the upper portion of the reservoir body 110 and coupled to the grating 200 and a grating seating surface 121 formed on the boundary region between the storage tank main body 110 and the grating insert tube 120 so as to be stepped inwardly in a predetermined area so that the grating 200 is seated and supported the grating 200 a grating frame 210 rotatably coupled to the grating insertion tube 120 and seated on the grating seating surface 121 in a closed state a plurality of manhole saws 220 disposed in the grating frame 210 at predetermined intervals in the longitudinal direction and having irregularities formed on the upper surface thereof to block rainwater from the storm reservoir 100 and block foreign matter a plurality of reinforcing frames 230 arranged in the grating frame 210 in a lateral direction at regular intervals a plurality of protrusions protruding from the ground at a predetermined interval in the lower portion of the outer reinforcing frame 230a to allow the gravel to flow into the gap between the grating insert tube 120 and the grating frame 210 and includes a soil inflow tooth 240 the height of the earth inflow tooth 240 and the height of the outer reinforcement frame 230a may be greater than the height of the reinforcement frame 230 located inside the outer reinforcement frame 230a and the reinforcing frame 230 is formed at the same height as the reinforcing frame 230"}]</data>
</edge>
