  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101495675-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "2 and 7 the first filtration body 1 is formed in a net shape at the inlet 7 so as to collect large contaminants introduced into the void through the inlet 7 of the pretreatment tank 2 the contaminant collecting net 15 is installed on the left vertical wall 6 of the pretreatment tank 2 and the upper wall of the pretreatment tank in a detachable manner"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also when the water level rises the retractable watershed wall prevents the backwash of the river water to prevent flooding damage and the impoundment collection box having a filter net for filtering the contaminants contained in the sewage and storm seats is installed so that the contaminants do not flow into the wells and an odor chamber connected to the ceiling of the sewage pipe at an upper portion of the open the curtain can be installed to block the malodor generated in the sewer line and to move the sewer line along the moving rail to the left and right sides of the sewer line to conveniently remove and remove the contaminant lifting device connected with the wire have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "on the other hand it is possible to selectively treat only high initial rainfall by the change in flow rate and in particular to increase the treatment efficiency compared to the increase of the efficiency of filtration and to easily check from the outside by placing the differential pressure portion 23 in the center to measure the replacement cycle due to the clogging of the 1.2 filter medium which is a carbide embedded in the filtration unit due to the occurrence of overload it can prevent life shortening"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "even if a small amount of initial rainwater including a contaminant is moved to the storm drain 16 or even a large amount of stormwater moves the storm drain may not move directly toward the storm drain 12 without being purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "it is possible to prevent the end of the waste.as described above the present invention is a device for treating a nonpoint source of pollution caused by an initial rainfall and can be immediately installed in an existing storm conduit 12 and particularly a coarse contaminant such as soil stones and leaves is a contaminant treatment tank 13 is treated preferentially the fine contaminants such as sand or mud is moved to the sediment storage unit 14 by the rotational centrifugal force through the rainwater movement port 16 provided to be eccentric with one side and the rainwater flow prevention plate installed at the bottom 18 and the concave portion 17 to prevent the backflow and settled in the lower part after removing the very fine sludge through the fibrous filtrate of carbide with rainwater can further extend the service life of the filter medium on the other hand it is possible to selectively process only the initial rainfall of high concentration by the amount of change in flow rate and in particular it is provided with two stages of filtration to increase the treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637078-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a pretreatment tank which is made up of one concrete structure and in which an inlet of an initial storm is formed by partition walls partitioning the structure a filtration tank having a filtrate water outlet and a discharge tank having an outlet and a filter medium installed in the entirety of the filtration tank to filter pollutants contained in the initial rainwater discharged from the pre treatment tank through the filtration tank to the discharge tank wherein the hollow pipe tube has a predetermined length and an exhaust passage communicating with the pre treatment tank and the filtration tank the exhaust passage being formed in a hollow shape so that the upper portion is exposed from the filter medium over the entire length the upper portion of the filter material is exposed from the filter material to the inside of the filtration tank and the exposed portion is formed with an inlet hole for allowing the filter material washing water to flow into the discharge passage while the opposite end is installed in the partition wall 111b a filter media wash and contaminant discharge line configured to communicate with the filter material discharge outlet a filter material cleaning device installed under the filter material washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe to be buried in the filter material and spraying high pressure air or backwash water for washing the filter material and a filter medium washing water and contaminants which are installed outside the pretreatment tank and are washed by the filter material cleaning device and flowed into the pretreatment tank through the washing water and the contaminant discharge pipe and stagnant water accumulated in the water treatment tank and a stagnant water exclusion pump for removing the stagnant water when it is confirmed that stagnant water is present in the water treatment tank contaminants separated from the filter media and the filter media wash water used for the filter media are supplied to the discharge passage and the filtering water discharge port 135 having the reverse opening closing door 136 of the partition wall 111b to be forcedly sucked into the pretreatment tank and forcedly excluded to the outside by the congestion water exclusion pump the operation of the filter medium washing device is stopped and only the stagnant water exclusion pump is operated with the stagnant water of the water treatment tank to be operated until the complete removal of sediment deposited at the bottom of the tank has been confirmed initial treatment is a solid system of jing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pretreatment tank 1 having a contaminant collecting net collecting large contaminants from the inflowing storm a filtration tank 2 for supplying foreign substances pre processed to one side of the pretreatment tank and filtering foreign substances contained in the pretreatment water and a discharge tank 4 for collecting the filtered treated water to one side of the filtration tank 2 and discharging the filtered treated water to an external water storage tank a first impression manhole 3 is formed at the upper part of the pretreatment tank 1 to remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the pretreatment tank 1 may further include a dirt collecting tank 13 and a ditch water tank 14 therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101692678-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "the contaminant collecting tank 13 is formed of a rectangular tube body 13a which is enclosed by a vertical wall on the side of the storm inflow port 12 of the pretreatment tank 1 and which has a lower portion closed and an upper portion thereof opened a contaminant collecting net 13c for collecting large sized contaminants contained in the stormwater is provided on the end side of the storm inlet 12 and a pretreatment water having the contaminants removed from the vertical wall of the rectangular watertight vessel 13 and the water retention tank 14 is provided at one side of the rectangular tube body 13a so as to prevent the large contaminants from being removed from the contaminant collecting tank 13 through the through hole 13b of the cylinder 13a so as to be discharged in the tangential direction of the outer diameter of the water separator 14"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainwater purification section partition plate 225 and the contaminant separation slope screen 221 are arranged in opposite directions while sloping the contaminant separation slope screen 221 and the rainwater purification partition plate 225 are continuously connected to each other so that the contaminants and rainwater can be easily separated even in a narrow space by the contaminant separation slope screen 221 so that no pollutants accumulate in the city wherein the non point pollution reduction device is a non point pollution reduction device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 1002809 has a main body having an inlet pipe and a discharge pipe a contaminant collecting part provided inside the body and collecting floating contaminants and water soluble contaminants in the initial rainwater flowing through the inflow pipe a sedimentation tank in which the initial stormwater that has passed through the clogging trapping unit is stored a swirling screen for filtering precipitable contaminants in the initial storm that are stored in the settling tank and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside the swirl screen includes an inlet through which the initial storm flows an external vessel through which the sediment is discharged and an inner vessel which is installed in the outer vessel to be separated from the outer vessel and has a lower portion communicating with the outer vessel and a side of which is provided with a flow pipe for supplying an initial storm with the filtration tank an initial stormwater is discharged from the sedimentation tank to the filtration tank due to a difference in water level between the sedimentation tank and the filtration tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "here the storm drainage treatment apparatus according to the