to the space between the housing 200 and the inner cap 500"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the frequency and the run time of the combined water diversion and therefore the contaminant yielded to the receiving stream are reduced and there is a considerable reduction in the discharge of suspended substances into the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "6d when rainwater flows into the first accommodation chamber 11a through the inlet pipe 13 in a state where the rainfall is greatly increased due to heavy rain or the like some rainwater may cause the protrusion 50 to fall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101089297-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the present invention for achieving the above object is provided in the interior of the storm receiver only the upper portion is formed to be opened the outlet is formed on the side spaced apart from the inner wall of the storm receiver at a predetermined distance installed and detachable to separate the inner space of the cylinder up and down at a set distance from the upper end excellent in that a plurality of holes are formed in the outer circumferential surface and the inlet has a step at the bottom in the cylindrical shape of the upper and lower openings in the center portion induction plate an impregnation trap network installed at the step of the inlet of the rainwater guide plate to be seated on the stepped portion to collect the contaminants falling into the rainwater flowing through the inlet and as a contaminant separating means installed between the rainwater guide plate and the contaminant collecting network the rainwater flowing from the rainwater guide plate does not flow directly into the hole on the outer circumferential surface of the rainwater guide plate so that the contaminants mixed in the rainwater fall into the trap of trapping dust with the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "when the rainfall exceeding the amount of the storm receiver 20 as shown by the arrow in the drawing drainage exceeding the amount of the storm receiver 20 is the upper surface and the lid 60 of the first partition wall 50 it flows through the passage 81 formed between and passes through the maintenance tank 30 it is stored in the common storage area formed by communicating the lower portion of the maintenance tank 30 and the lower portion of the treatment tank 40 in turn sedimentary particulate matter with a high specific gravity is precipitated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as a result deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20 the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220901-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in addition the present invention can be washed by the non powered method of the natural freshwater and storage tank is completed compared to the existing method can reduce the cost of construction there is no fear of damage due to breakdown or power outage the use of stable storage facilities can handle pollution 1 is a plan view showing a natural freshwater storage system of the present invention"}]</data>
