  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the sewing machine according to the present invention is constructed such that one side and the other side of the sewing line are connected to one side of the sewing line and the other side of the sewing line and a wear plate operating spring 600 configured to elastically work such that the wear plate 200 returns to its original position as the wear plate 200 rotates in accordance with the inflow amount of the sewage in an automatic weir for use in a good toilette using an elastic action so that the wear plate 200 can return to its original position as the inflow amount is reduced in the frame 100 and is made of stainless steel material a shaft insertion groove on one side and the other side of the wear plate 200 so as to be engaged with the shaft 210 an anchor bolt coupling groove to be coupled to the upper side of the sewage pipe 10 and an anchor bolt 20 inserted and coupled to the anchor bolt coupling groove is connected to the upper side of the sewer line 10 the wear plate 200 the sewage and storm surge directly come into contact with the upper surface of the sewage and stormwater and the sewage and storm surge are rotated by the pressure applied to the upper surface of the warehouse plate 200 so that even if the pressure applied to the upper surface of the sewage and rainwater ware plate 200 is weak the upper surface is configured to be larger than the lower surface area a shaft coupling groove is formed on one side and the other side of the wear plate 200 so that the shaft 210 can be coupled to the wear plate 200 a fixing hinge 220 is formed on one surface and the other surface of the shaft coupling groove of the wear plate 200 for fixing the shaft 210 coupled to the wear plate 200 so as not to be detached from the wear plate 200 a shaft 210 and a spring coupling groove 211 are formed on one surface of the shaft 210 so as to be engaged with the wear plate drive spring 300 the drive spring adjusting nut 400 at least one bolt fixing groove 410 on the outer side so as to firmly fix the coupling state when the shaft 210 is engaged with the shaft 210 a fixing bolt 420 inserted into the bolt fixing groove 410 a spring insertion groove 430 is formed on one surface of the driving spring adjusting nut 400 so as to be engaged with the wear plate driving spring 300 and a shaft engaging groove 440 for engaging with the shaft 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the spring engaging groove 440 is coupled to one side of the wear plate driving spring 300 the wear plate operating spring 600 when the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater is small or there is no inflow of sewage and stormwater the weir plate 200 is rotated at an angle of inclination at all times at least one side of the wear plate 200 and one side and the other side of the sewage line 10 are formed on the left side and the right side of the center of the wear plate 200 so as to be rotated by the elastic force of the wear plate 600 respectively the pressure of the sewage and the storm that the wear plate 200 is rotated is adjusted by using the wear plate driving spring 300 and the driving spring adjusting nut 400 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be rotated or fixed when the inflow amount of the sewage and the storm is small it is possible to block and minimize the inflow of sewage and to prevent the inflow of sewage and stormwater by effectively opening and closing the ware plate 200 to prevent the contamination of the stream and the upper surface of the wear plate 200 is configured to be wider than the lower surface of the lower surface of the wear plate 200 when the wear plate 200 is rotated due to inflow of sewage and storm and the sewage and stormwater are completely prevented from flowing into the sewage pipe 10 by the upper surface and the frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "in other words so that the phenomenon that the wear plate 200 flows into the sewer pipe 10 when the wear plate 200 rotates due to inflow of sewage and storm is completely prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "at this time the storm conduit 10 may be provided with a plurality of overflow wear 11 12 13 if necessary the front side of each overflow wear 11 12 13 as a settlement 20 a gate is installed to allow initial rainwater to flow in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention can be installed at the end of a sewage pipe in contact with a river or coast while minimizing civil works and a wear type consisting of a conduction type ware and a sluice gate connecting the interlocking pipe connection to have a function of storm water and to have a function of preventing reverse flow of river or sea water"}]</data>
