control system 412 for controlling only the control water to be supplied to the rapid reaction tank 420 which is the next step the inlet of the rapid reaction tank 420 has a horizontal water flow control panel 422 having a reddish elbow type inlet 421 for rapid mixing of the treated water and the flocculant and the upper and lower portions in the body center an stirrer 423 to simultaneously perform upstream and downstream stirring a chemical input unit 424 for injecting a coagulant having an increased cohesive force on the rapid reaction tank 420 an outflow separation wall 425 for guiding the outflow water to a flocculation tank 430 which is the next step the flocculation tank 430 is a slow stirring device for coagulation 431 the final agglomerate is an outflow separation wall 433 for outflow to the secondary settling tank 440 which is the next process the secondary settling tank 440 rectifies the flow rate as a final flocculation floc and flows the treated water separated from the flow rate rectifier 441 for dividing the treated water and sludge into the disinfecting discharge tank 510 which is the next process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400040-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the first step of the water level transmitter measuring in real time whether the water level is maintained and the gate so that the level of the treated water in the treatment water tank is within a predetermined range when the level of the treated water in the treatment tank is out of a predetermined range in a second step of selectively opening and closing at least one of the valves and in the second step if the level of the treated water in the treatment water tank does not match within a predetermined range for a predetermined time the first and second flow rates operation of a backwash pump to backwash the membrane module by closing the control valve and ejecting the treated water in the treatment water tank from the casing outlet to the inlet and sludge outlet to reduce fouling of the membrane module we present a dynamic pressure control method of a membrane filtration advanced water purification apparatus characterized in that it consists of a third step of controlling the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in addition the rainwater flowing into the lid seat 5 flows into the inside of the water level protection box 1 and touches the water level valve 7 thereby causing the water level control valve 7 to corrode or generate rust the life of the wiping valve 7 is lowered.the present invention relates to a water level control apparatus for a water level control apparatus and a water level control apparatus for a water level control apparatus so that it can be automatically drained.in order to solve the above mentioned problems the present invention proposes a method of manufacturing a ladle type washing machine comprising the steps of forming an excellent collection groove along a circumferential direction around a bottom surface of a lid and a technique for penetrating and forming the through hole.according to the present invention even when the rainwater flows into the inside of the wedge shaped iron the rainwater is collected using the rainwater collecting grooves and then discharged automatically through the drainage path communicating with the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-7204930-B2", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "during the course of filtration an emergency such as a high level water sensor may be engaged the sensor then immediately sends from the plc a signal to set off the alarm 111 and alert the owners of the system that there is a high water level within the aeration tower 24"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101890574-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "the decanter apparatus 1000 may further include a power supply unit 1010 for supplying power to the decanter apparatus 1000 and the power supply unit 1010 may include a decanter lifting apparatus 1500 a check valve 1110 the control valve 1160 the water level check device 1800 the decanter pump 1700 and the motor operated valve 1600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172085-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "low quality high tds water may also be fed to solenoid or other control valve 162 along line 150 and connected to untreated water storage tank 168 along lines 164 and 166"}, {"pat_id": "US-9829150-B2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the first height adjustment screw 13 is threadably engaged to the first female threaded hole 12 in order to convert rotational motion of the first height adjustment screw 13 into translation motion of the lifter body 11 thus lifting or lowering the water level control valve 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200364573-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "more specifically when the water level of the reservoir rises to a high level due to a failure of the existing water level control valve the discharged through the overflow water discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200364573-Y1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "referring to the operation and effect of the present invention configured as described above the safety shut off device 10 of the present invention to detect the high water level of the reservoir 1 by the float float 6 to block the inlet pipe 2 can be installed and used together in the reservoir 1 provided with a water level control valve 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200364573-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "that is the safety shut off device 10 is obtained so as to prevent the occurrence of various accidents due to the water overflow of the reservoir 1 when the water level control valve 5 which frequently malfunctions is damaged"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3017891-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "next the circulating pump 4 is driven to apply pump pressure to the return pipe 9 via the hot water feed pipe 8 and the branch pipe 14 and at the same time time measurement is started by the water level change time measurement circuit 16 and this time is measured"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032302-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the spray control valve 122 is connected to the spray line 128 and the spray line and the spray line 128 to receive the spray solution from the feed control valve and to the spray nozzle and the spray solution supplied from the spray line the raw water is supplied to the raw water supply unit 102 by controlling the spray unit 120 including an air pump 129 which pumps the remaining spray liquid from the line and discharges it to the outside through a discharge control valve and a raw water pump that may be configured in the raw water supply line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100794198-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a sewage separation tank 20 capable of separating non organic non degradable foreign matter by receiving sewage and temporarily storage and decomposition of organic solids a conversion flow rate adjustment tank 30 for sharing the mutual conversion characteristics of the physical function flow rate control and the biological treatment function so that the characteristics of the water quality can be developed as an exhalation function primary contact aeration tank 40 which is the main treatment process to maintain the aerobic phase characteristics of the microorganism by maintaining the active range of the microorganism to the heavy load primary settling tank 50 for firstly separating the desorbed sludge secondary contact aeration tank 60 which is an auxiliary treatment process having an increase in the food chain and natural purification characteristics between the microorganisms by obtaining a function having a preliminary preliminary function by affording a specific surface area for attachment of organic matter and purified microorganisms secondary settling tank 70 for separating the sewage sludge secondary sludge storage tank 80 and the sludge collected in the first and second primary settling tank 50 70 and a discharge tank 90 for discharging the supernatant after disinfection under the boundary wall 22 of the contaminant separation tank 20 and the switching flow adjustment tank 30 an opening 23 for preventing the accumulation of organic matter based on the change in water level and the agitation of the switching flow adjustment tank 30 contact switching frames 31 41 61 disposed in the switching flow rate adjustment tank 30 the primary contact aeration tank 40 and the secondary contact aeration tank 60 upper and lower contact contact frames 31 41 61 and mesh fixing nets 33 43 63 in the purification processing apparatus having the contact support frame 31 41 61 having at least one diffuser 36 44 64 at the bottom the switching flow rate adjustment tank 30 side has a first stage air lift 35 for solving the factor of reducing the amount of transport due to the water level and increasing the efficiency of the flow rate adjustment the water tank 34 connected to the upper end of the first stage air lift 35 has two stages to transfer the quantity of raw water to the air float so that the transfer effort for the first contact aeration tank 40 which is a later process is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101127289-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "when the water level control valve 140 is open the water in the reservoir 150 is moved to the sterilization tank 160 to increase the level of the sterilization tank 160 and the water level is increased to detect the water level sensor 170"}]</data>
