weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 penetrating the middle part of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 to the rear part a structure in which a lower movement line 1919 is connected to the end of the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 to move the power generation water introduced through the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 downward a structure in which an entrance 1332 used for inspecting or repairing the lower movement line 1919 is combined with a locking device 1333 at the lower end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the rising discharge pipe 101 is connected to the end of the lower movement line 1919 a structure in which the upper and lowering device 5810 is combined to adjust the discharge water level in the upper and lower directions according to the amount of water stored inside the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or water storage device 1000 at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 101 a structure in which the upper part of the above mentioned up and down lifting device 5810 is connected to the lower part of the above mentioned dam reservoir lake and movable reservoir 8888 and the above mentioned down discharge pipe 103 for discharging the river water discharged upward through the above mentioned up and down discharge pipe 101 a structure in which an air discharge port 1331 for discharging air generated in the intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the rising discharge pipe 101 are combined at the upper end of the descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the right angled descending pipe 202 is formed at the lower end of the above descending discharge pipe 103 a structure in which the water storage tank 201 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 with a volume ratio 10 to 200 times larger than the structural volume ratio of the above mentioned right angled descending pipe 202 a structure in which a plurality of emission control units 203 are combined at the lower end of the above rectangular lowering pipe 202 to control the emission amount the lower part of the above rectangular descending pipe 202 is configured to be connected to the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above intermediate storage water inflow line 501 and the above lower moving line 1919 and the above rising discharge pipe 101 and the above falling discharge pipe 103 and the above water storage tank 201 and the above dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 which is configured to raise and discharge water through the above natural river water self purification action and the action of gravity and the action of gravity acceleration and the eco friendly method which purifies polluted river water and generates eco friendly hydroelectric power by preventing the occurrence of green algae thereby producing eco friendly electricity and at the same time exhibiting the function of an artificial fish farm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_137", "text": "a structure comprising a dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 that naturally purifies polluted river water in a valley of a river or stream located higher than the sea or a large river a structure in which the lower discharge passage 223 is formed at the lower end of the above dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the above water storage device 1000 a structure in which the inflow control valve 222 is formed at one end of the lower discharge passage 223 a structure in which a power generation water movement line 331 is connected using a round or square pipe or a round square or rectangular concrete pipe configured to prevent leakage to the outside at the other end of the lower discharge passage 223 after constructing the above power generation water transfer line 331 by crossing mountains and hills 221 a structure in which a v shaped rising discharge line 332 is formed at the end of the power generation water movement line 331 so that it is 1 to 10 lower than the horizontal state and the bottom height of the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 so that the power generation water discharged from the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or water storage device 1000 automatically falls downward by gravity over mountains and hills a structure in which a first acceleration discharge port 213 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at a high position above the dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or river water stored in the storage facility 1000 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the frictional action and explosive action of materials naturally occurring between the power generation water passing through the power generation water movement line 331 that is constructed over mountains and hills a structure in which a secondary acceleration discharge port 215 for gravitational acceleration action is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to discharge gaseous material molecules generated by the material friction and material explosion that occur naturally between the power generation water passing through the above mentioned power generation water movement line 331 and the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 to the outside at a position higher than the water level of the river water stored in the above mentioned dam reservoir lake movable weir 8888 or the above mentioned water storage device 1000 a structure in which the upper water tank 1503 is formed at the lower end of the above mentioned rising discharge line 332 a structure in which a lower discharge unit 1500 is formed at the lower part of the upper water tank 1503 a structure in which an emission control unit 203 is combined at the lower part of the above lower emission unit 1500 a structure in which the power generation unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102028873-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a floating bucket for collecting suspended solids a fourth floating material collection conveyor for transporting the collected particulate matter and the ultra fine particles in the rear portion of the floating material collection rotating bucket fine particles rising from the rear portion of the fourth floating material collection conveyor to the upper portion of the river water a fourth contaminant screw feeder configured to collect and collect sex contaminants and ultra fine magnetic contaminants to push and transport the contaminants to the outside of the river water processing box and combine the rotor and the rotor support a fifth floating material collection conveyor for transporting and collecting the collected particulate matter and the ultrafine particles on the rear part of the fourth contaminant screw feeder the suspended solids removing plate and the particulate collecting guide plate sequentially coupled with the rotating belt coupled to the rotating body a fifth suspended solids material collector in which the suspended particulate floating material plate which serves to prevent the collected suspended solids molecules from being separated from the outside of the rotating belt is combined and a water reservoir and a rainwater reservoir for connecting the lower end of the river water processing box and the river water discharge pipe by using a discharge control valve and storing the processed river water and at the end of the river water processing box from an upstream of the river"}, {"pat_id": "US-4268280-A", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "while heating the water w the steam s mixed with the water w is liquified and consequently the volume of the stream is abruptly reduced to less than about 1 2500 of the original volume and cavitation occurs in the water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a third aspect provides a system for simulating a leak in a pipeline the system comprising a pipeline a fluid supply operable to generate a fluid stream an inlet in fluid communication with the fluid supply so as to receive the fluid stream therefrom a control valve having a valve input a valve output and a control port the valve input being in fluid communication with the inlet so as to receive the fluid stream therefrom the control valve being operable to selectively permit or prevent communication of the fluid stream from the valve input to the valve output based on a control signal received at the control port a controller communicatively coupled to the control port and operable to provide the control signal to the control port an outlet in fluid communication with the valve output the outlet being fixed to the pipeline such that when the control valve permits communication of the fluid stream from the valve input to the valve output the fluid stream is output onto an outer surface of the pipeline such that a vibration is caused in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-4877519-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a waste water treatment system for high temperature hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream said system having a reactor constructed to operate at a sufficiently high temperature and pressure to effect hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream introduced to said reactor and a heat exchanger system with a means for flowing an influent waste water stream through said heat exchanger system prior to introduction to said reactor and a means for an effluent stream from said reactor through said heat exchanger system the improvement comprising said heat exchanger system having a first double pipe heat exchanger for said influent stream and a second double pipe heat exchanger for said effluent stream each of said double pipe heat exchangers having an inner tube which defines a tube side tube of the heat exchanger and an annular space between an outer tubular shell and said inner tube to define an annular space tube of the heat exchanger said first and second heat exchanger each having an inlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an inlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger a first conduit for delivering said influent stream to said tube side inlet of first heat exchanger a second conduit for delivering said effluent stream from said reactor to said tube side inlet of said second heat exchanger said first and second heat exchanger each having an outlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an outlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger means for circulating a heat exchange medium through said annular space inlets and outlets of said first and second heat exchangers to preheat said influent stream prior to introduction into said reactor where energy for preheating is extracted by said second heat exchanger from said effluent stream passing through said second heat exchanger to add heat energy to said heat exchange medium said first heat exchanger removing heat energy from said heat exchange medium to preheat said influent stream whereby influent and effluent streams pass through said tube side of each inner tube of said first and second heat exchangers to minimize clogging of said first and second heat exchanger said reactor comprising a closed vessel with an inlet and an outlet a third conduit extending from said tube side outlet of said first heat exchanger to said reactor inlet said second conduit being connected to said reactor outlet said reactor having a level control device located below said inlet to provide a liquid level in said reactor below said inlet to ensure that said inlet is above reacting liquid in said reactor said outlet located at a lower level in said reactor to define a downflow reactor zone said level control device comprising a control valve for controlling liquid flow in said reactor located below said inlet said liquid level sensor generating a signal to open fully said control valve when said liquid level sensor senses liquid means for fully closing said valve after sufficient liquid is drained from said reactor to drop reacting liquid level below said liquid level sensor to provide an intermittent flow of effluent to said second conduit"}, {"pat_id": "US-4877519-A", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "in a waste water treatment system for high temperature hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream said system having a reactor constructed to operate at a sufficiently high temperature and pressure to effect hydrolysis of cyanide in a waste water stream introduced to said reactor and a heat exchanger system with means for flowing an an influent waste water stream flowing through said heat exchanger system prior to introduction to said reactor and a means for flowing an effluent stream from said reactor through said heat exchanger system the improvement comprising said heat exchanger system having a first double pipe heat exchanger for said influent stream and a second double pipe heat exchanger for said effluent stream each of said double pipe heat exchangers having an inner tube which defines a tube side tube of the heat exchanger and an annular space between an outer tubular shell and said inner tube to define an annular space tube of the heat exchanger said first and second heat exchangers each having an inlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and inlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger a first conduit for delivering said influent stream to said tube side inlet of said first heat exchanger a second conduit for delivering said effluent stream from said reactor to said tube side inlet of said second heat exchanger said first and second heat exchangers each having an outlet for the tube side of said corresponding heat exchanger and an outlet for the annular space of the corresponding heat exchanger means for circulating a heat exchange medium through said annular space inlets and outlets of said first and second heat exchangers to preheat said influent stream prior to introduction into said reactor where energy for preheating is extracted by said second heat exchanger from said effluent stream passing through said second heat exchanger to add heat energy to said heat exchange medium said first heat exchanger removing heat energy from said heat exchange medium to preheat said influent stream whereby influent and effluent streams pass through said tube side of each inner tube of said first and second heat exchangers to minimize clogging of said first and second heat exchangers said reactor comprising a closed vessel with an inlet and an outlet a third conduit extending from said outlet of said first heat exchanger to said reactor inlet said second conduit being connected to said reactor outlet said reactor having a level control device located below said inlet to provide a liquid level in said reactor below said inlet to ensure that said inlet is above reacting liquid in said reactor said outlet is at a lower level in said reactor to define a downflow reactor zone said level control device comprising a control valve for controlling liquid flow in said second conduit and a liquid level sensor in said reactor located below said inlet said liquid level sensor generating a signal to open fully said control valve when said liquid level sensor senses liquid means for fully closing said valve after sufficient liquid is drained from said reactor to drop reacting liquid level below said liquid level sensor to provide an intermittent flow of effluent to said second conduit wherein said control valve is a ball valve with a fully open position and a fully closed position said fully open position of said ball valve avoiding clogging and abrasion of said ball valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-6855897-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "5 untreated water enters the apparatus via hose 24 and any solid particles in the water such as sand and gravel are removed by the filter 22 prior to entry of the water to the pump 21"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101435644-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the flow rate control valve 133 may be composed of a plurality of constant flow rate valves for supplying a predetermined flow rate to the electrolysis module 134"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102660526-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pool built to a predetermined depth on the banks of a stream or river a balancing tank connected to the pool by an overflow pipe and a drainage pipe to store water discharged from the pool a filtration device connected to the balancing tank and the supply pipe to filter the water in the balancing tank and connected to the pool and the water supply pipe to supply the filtered water to the pool and it includes a piping control manhole built between the pool and the balancing tank to control the overflow pipe drain pipe and water supply pipe to prevent contaminants from the pool from flowing into the balancing tank the piping control manhole is a first contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the overflow pipe a second contaminant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the drainage pipe a third pollutant penetration blocking valve installed in the middle part of the water supply pipe a first pollutant discharge pipe and a first pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle portion of the front overflow pipe of the first pollutant penetration blocking valve a second pollutant discharge pipe and a second pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the drainage pipe in front of the second pollutant penetration blocking valve a water damage recovery system for a swimming pool comprising a third pollutant discharge pipe and a third pollutant discharge pipe control valve installed in the middle of the water supply pipe in front of the third pollutant penetration blocking valve"}]</data>
