  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101837300-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water channel portion for guiding water to move in a predetermined direction an infiltration inducing pipe portion penetrating through the bottom surface of the water channel portion and communicating with an underground aquifer below the impermeable layer in the ground layer a filtering unit installed at a connection portion between the infiltration induction pipe and the water channel unit and composed of several layers for removing foreign matter from water flowing into the underground aquifer and having a lower porosity toward the lower layer and and an opening closing part for selectively shielding the infiltration induction tube part the water a sediment guiding part having a guide protruding from the bottom surface of the water channel part and a settling groove formed between the guide and the guide an induction intrusion section having an inclined surface inclined upward in the moving direction of the water on the bottom surface of the water channel part and an inlet port formed on the opposite vertical surface and and a water film portion for controlling the amount and movement of water moving along the water channel portion the infiltration induction pipe portion may include an induction pipe connected to the induction pier at the upper end and connected to the underground aquifer below a flow rate measuring unit installed at an upper side of the guide pipe to measure an amount of water moving along the guide pipe and a water level control valve provided below the flow rate measuring unit and passing through the induction pipe the water level control valve includes a cylindrical body through which upper and lower parts pass a first inlet connected to an upper portion of the induction pipe a second inlet connected to a lower portion of the induction pipe and a buoyant body selectively shielding the first inlet and the second inlet while moving up and down along the body the opening a high level sensor installed at a relatively high position in the infiltration induction pipe a low water level sensor installed at a relatively low position in the permeation guide pipe a door unit provided at a relatively higher position than the high level sensing sensor to selectively shield the induction pipe and a control unit for receiving the signal of the high level sensing sensor and the low level sensing sensor and the signal of the flow rate measurement unit and controlling the door unit when the signal of the high level sensing sensor is received the control part shields the door part so as to prevent the water in the waterway part from flowing into the underground aquifer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100698889-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in this case a defect occurs due to corrosion of the control valve 40 installed inside the manhole 10 and protected by the manhole and in case of emergency the control valve does not operate properly which may cause a great damage.the present invention is to solve the above mentioned conventional problems the groundwater to prevent the infiltration of the groundwater into the manhole through the improvement of the water film structure on the waterway entrance and exit side of the manhole the facility example inside the manhole that is protected by the manhole accordingly for example an object of the present invention is to provide a water supply manhole leak prevention facility that can prevent corrosion of control valves"}]</data>
