  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101776914-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the handle 26 and the screw engagement portion 27 are provided on the inside of the steam hose 29 and an auxiliary convex portion 28 is inserted into the lower portion of the screw coupling portion 27 so that the screw coupling portion 27 is inserted into the auxiliary block portion 28 and the lower part of the airtight packing 24 is brought into close contact with the convex part 23 so that the inner circumferential surface of the airtight packing 24 is directed toward the steam hose 29 airtight means 20 which expands and seals the circumferential surface of the steam hose 29 to prevent the steam inside the steam generator 12 and the tube t from leaking to the outside a discharge pipe 41 is inserted into a front surface of the tube t inverted into the inside of the pipe and the automatic pressure member 42 is coupled to the upper portion of the discharge pipe 41 a temperature and pressure control unit 43 is installed in the temperature and pressure control unit 43 and an automatic valve 44 is provided under the temperature and pressure control unit 43 to automatically discharge the internal pressure of the tube t to the outside an automatic pressure regulating device 40 having a first outlet 45 formed at a lower end of the automatic valve 44 and a second outlet 46 formed at a side of the automatic valve 44 and a condensate storage chamber 51 is formed at the end of the recovery line 47"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102480228-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in other words when severe freezing is expected due to a large amount of snowfall or a rapid drop in temperature only salt water which is the original solution is sprayed so that the snow melts or thaws quickly and when the amount of snowfall is less than expected or the temperature is low it is sprayed in a state where a certain amount of water is mixed with salt water which is a stock solution so that sufficient spray can be made while reducing the amount of salt water used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101467038-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the leakage detection control device 200 a time temperature setting unit 210 for setting the respective temperatures of the boiler drive time on off the hot water and the heating water a pressure sensor setting unit 220 for setting a reference pressure value to be compared with a pressure value sensed from each of the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 160 170 and 180 a valve control unit 230 for controlling opening and closing angles of the water supply control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve 130 and the recovery control valve 140 the water supply control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve 110 and the heating control valve 120 are operated to operate at a set temperature of the boiler drive time and the hot water the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 160 170 and 180 and the first to fourth pressure sensors 130 and 170"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101467038-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "the controller 240 controls the boiler the water supply control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve not shown and the heating control valve 140 so as to operate at a set temperature of the boiler drive time and the hot water 130 and the recovery regulating valve 140 and generates a control signal by setting the reference value of the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 160 170 180 and the first to fourth pressure sensors 150 the hot water supply pipe sensor 161 the hot water discharge pipe sensor 162 the heating water inlet pipe sensor 171 and the heating water supply pipe sensor 151 160 170 180 the change in the sensed pressure value from the heating water discharge pipe sensor 172 the recovery inlet pipe sensor 181 and the recovered discharge pipe sensor 182 is sensed or when the leakage from the water leak sensor 190 is sensed the water control valve 110 the hot water control valve 120 the heating control valve 130 and the recovery control valve 140 are shut off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a device capable of generating sodium hypochlorite saturated salt water tank receiving soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine the water level is controlled by a water gauge and a water supply valve a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank sodium hypochlorite generator having an automatic valve and a flow sensor characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "sodium hypochlorite generating device equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor according to the present invention to achieve the above object by supplying soft water from the water softener to dissolve the salt to make a saturated brine but by the water gauge and water supply valve a saturated brine tank in which the water level is controlled a brine water purification tank having a float valve for storing a saturated brine discharged from the saturated brine tank and maintaining a constant water level a brine flow rate control valve configured to control a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a brine flow meter which displays a flow rate of the brine discharged from the brine water level tank a venturi tube for mixing the brine discharged from the brine water tank and the soft water discharged from the soft water tank an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the brine flowing through the venturi tube to generate sodium hypochlorite a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank a softening tank for storing soft water discharged from the heat exchanger and having a temperature sensor for controlling the soft water and a heater for controlling the temperature of the soft water constantly a temperature sensor for automatic valve control measuring a temperature of soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank an automatic valve which bypasses the soft water supplied from the softener to the heat exchanger so that soft water discharged from the heat exchanger to the soft water tank can maintain a constant temperature a soft water supply solenoid valve for blocking soft water discharged from the soft water tank as necessary soft water flow rate control valve for adjusting the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank it characterized in that it comprises a soft water flow meter for displaying the flow rate of the soft water discharged from the soft water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h thermocouple and com