  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101181549-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the method according to claim 4 or 5 each of the first raw water supply module the second raw water supply module and the third raw water supply module an oil pressure measuring unit installed in the supply pipeline to measure oil pressure of raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder a flow rate control valve installed in the supply pipeline to regulate a flow rate of raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder a bypass pipeline branching from the supply pipeline and bypassing the raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder to the storage tank a bypass valve installed in the bypass pipeline to adjust a flow rate of raw water bypassed to the storage tank the pollution index predictor is configured to determine the hydraulic pressure of the raw water supplied to each of the filter membrane holders based on the hydraulic pressure measured by the hydraulic pressure measuring unit of each of the first raw water supply module the second raw water supply module and the third raw water supply module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100273822-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water pipe 14 of the water intake well 12 the water meter 14 for displaying the feed amount of the raw water control valve 15 for adjusting the discharge of raw water a check valve 16 for discharging raw water in the pipe 19 in only one direction a pressure gauge 26 displaying hydraulic pressure in the pipe 19 an air valve 25 for discharging air remaining in the pipe 19 or when raw water is pumped from the pumping means 18 and a reverse circulation line 27 for backflowing the remaining raw water in the pipe 19 to the pumping means 18 to prevent freezing when raw water is not being pumped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "64 a disk valve 66 for opening and closing the water passage 61a of the valve housing 61 is selectively installed while moving up and down and is elastic between the disk valve 66 and the elastic member support frame 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in addition the present invention is a technique for branching and installing the drainage branch pipe on one side of the water supply pipe connecting the drainage control valve to the bottom of the drainage branch pipe connecting the residual water drainage pipe to the bottom of the drainage control valve take a look.according to the present invention when the operation of the submersible motor pump is stopped automatically by the water pipe to prevent the water flow back to the water pipe and at the same time draining the water remaining in the pumping device in the upper ground water protective device to the outside cold water pumping device it provides the effect of preventing the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which is a component of the components in advance and greatly reduces the time and manpower associated with checking or replacing the groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge as well as providing convenience of post management after construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101874096-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in addition the analysis of the water supply pipe network can also determine the control time of the water control valve v2 by calculating the time during which the water pressure falls at the critical point c from the water control valve control point a at the reservoir control point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100565715-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in addition the hydraulic pressure supplied to the equipment side in excess of the proper hydraulic pressure promotes leakage of the connection part of the components forming the flow path thereby lowering the reliability of the product.if the leakage increases the entire component parts of the flow path including the control valve must be replaced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101847963-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition the analysis of the water supply pipe network can also determine the control time of the water control valve v2 by calculating the time during which the water pressure falls at the critical point c from the water control valve control point a at the reservoir control point"}, {"pat_id": "US-3871792-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pump system comprising a pump an electric motor in drive connection with said pump a service line a service valve in said service line a pressure switch in electric circuit with said motor and a control valve assembly comprising a valve housing having an input opening for flow connection thereto of said pump a discharge opening for flow connection to said service line and a main flow passageway interconnecting said input opening and said discharge opening a main valve spanning said main passageway means biasing said main valve toward closing position a first auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end with said main passageway on the downstream side of said main valve and terminating in an opening in said housing for hydraulic pressure connection to said pressure switch means coupling said pressure switch to said valve housing at said last opening a pilot valve assembly spanning said first auxiliary passageway and including a valve seat and a valve means normally biasing said pilot valve toward open condition and a second auxiliary passageway said second auxiliary passageway flow connecting at one end to said main passageway on the upstream side of said main valve and terminating at said pilot valve in pressure opposing relationship to said biasing means whereby development of hydraulic pressure against said valve in excess of any opposing pressure against said valve will close said valve and block said first auxiliary passageway"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101320409-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "even in the cold weather in winter it provides a useful effect to prevent the freezing of groundwater meter and hydraulic pressure gauge which are components of the well facilities"}]</data>
</edge>
