 unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "US-6423216-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "however in case the water in the filter chamber rises over a water level of the overflow weir 37 placed at the filtrate outflow chamber 36 the injected oxidation air cannot rise over the water surface of the filter chamber but can be moved to the outflow side due to the air pressure by the water head difference with the outflow side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the initial rainwater collecting weir is the same as the initial upper water level of the upper weir the initial rainwater is filled in the initial rainwater storage tank while the initial rainwater is transferred to the initial rainwater storage tank through the contaminant blocking pipe rainwater filtration and collection device excluding the initial excellent after the rain reaches the upper end of the water level to perform the function of overflowing the rainwater to the top"}, {"pat_id": "US-10184221-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "in the event of a leak of the impoundment area if the water level observed is falling relatively quickly and unrelated to the operation of the water control device for gate weir movement this could alert a user that the area needs to be checked for an impoundment leak such as the breach of a impoundment wall"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in the rainwater treatment facility according to the present invention in the case of a combined sewer system a lower weir having a height corresponding to the water level due to initial rainfall and a higher weir are provided in a part of the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "therefore it is possible to separately treat the highly polluted initial rainwater and the less polluted rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101604772-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "according to the present invention the phenomenon occurring when the lid technique is applied to the watershed the phenomenon such as erosion scouring and sedimentation occurring in the river due to the increase and decrease of the effluent the total amount of suspended substances contained in the generated effluent it is possible to easily carry out a phenomenon such as erosion and scouring of the surface soil analysis of the correlation between the degree of compaction and the increase or decrease in the amount of penetration and more reliable data can be secured"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 sand rinse device 62 coarse aggregate rinse device 63 washing waste water evaporation device 64 belt conveyor 65 sand supply device 66 rinse water spray device 67 cleaning waste water receiving tank 68 drive roller 68a shaft 69 driven roller 69a shaft 70 conveyor belt 71 support roller 72 guide plate 74 belt conveyor 75 coarse aggregate supply device 76 rinsing water spray device 77 cleaning waste water receiving tank 78 driving roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveyor belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 cleaning waste water discharge passage 84 cleaning waste water storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 91 side groove 9 washing wastewater supply device 93 washing wastewater return path 94 water level holding device 100 ground 101 bottom groove 102 communication hole 103 convex part 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 110 water tank 111 weir 112 washing wastewater supply pump 113 washing waste water supply pipe 116 frame structure 117 roof"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1892343-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "to prevent the possible torque perpendicular to the flow direction 10 the forced plates 32 engage laterally in the guide slot 12 of the abutment 30 and reduce the possible torque of the lifting platform 17 when lowering perpendicular to the flow direction 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wear type rainwater chute device characterized in that to prevent the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "as shown in the accompanying drawings in this embodiment the lower end of the sewage pipe 1 in contact with the river or the coast is hingedly coupled to the wear 100 erected or laid down and the sewage pipe in front of the wear 100 the vehicle collection pipe connection pipe 200 branched to the side of 1 the drive means 300 for rotating the wear 100 and the wear 100 are interlocked to open and close the entrance of the vehicle collection pipe connection pipe 200 sluice gate 400 sensors s1 s2 installed at the rear of the weir 100 to detect reverse flow of river water or seawater and the water level of ou water flowing down the sewage pipe by being installed in front of the weir 100 a control unit 500 that opens and closes the wear 100 and the sluice 400 in an interlocking manner by operating the driving means 300 by sensing a sensor s3 s4 for detecting a signal from the sensors s1 to s4"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052946-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 91 side groove 92 washing wastewater supply device 93 washing wastewater return path 94 water level holding device 100 ground 101 bottom groove 102 communication hole 103 projection 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 110 water tank 111 weir 112 washing wastewater supply pump 113 washing waste water supply pipe 116 frame structure 117 roof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "the inlet 1 has a circular or rectangular shape as a part for collecting the polluted river water and sewage the effluent from the sewage treatment facility to flow into the contact oxidation tank and has a movable bank in the inlet distribution tank 2 18 weir is installed and the flow rate in the inlet distribution tank 2 is kept constant by adjusting the water level using the movable bank 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "on the other hand the quantitative waste water is discharged quantitatively and discharged into the aeration tank 50 equipped with the oxygen supply nozzle 57 by the water level difference through the first wear 31 via the flow rate control anoxic tank 40 the coarse sewage flows through the weir 35 into the sedimentation filtration tank 20 in which the sludge s is precipitated in a downward upward flow by the induction pipe 93 in the sedimentation filtration tank 20 and the treated supernatant is the discharge vessel"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100348160-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "in addition the conventional internal conveying pipe and an anoxic tank conveying pump are removed to eliminate the blockage of the device and the pipe due to the sludge s deposition"}]<