 unit 33 is combined with the lower part of the lower discharge unit 1500 the thickness and size of the upper water tank 1503 are such that the power generation water discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500 is easily discharged to the power generation unit 33 configured in the lower direction at a high speed due to the action of gravity and when the size and total discharge area of the lower discharge unit 1500 are converted to a ratio of 100 the storage capacity of the upper water tank 1503 is configured to be 1 000 to 16 000 larger in size and larger in capacity so that the power generation water flowing in through the dam reservoir lake movable reservoir 8888 or the water storage device 1000 and the lower discharge passage 223 and the power generation water movement line 331 and the rising discharge line 332 is moved to the upper water tank 1503 and then discharged through the lower discharge unit 1500"}, {"pat_id": "US-6916427-B2", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "pre treating helps to improve the primary reactor s 7 efficiency allowing for an increase of fluent flow through the system by initiating the reduction and flocculation of dissolved and suspended particles in the fluent stream prior to entering the primary reactor 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the spring engaging groove 440 is coupled to one side of the wear plate driving spring 300 the wear plate operating spring 600 when the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater is small or there is no inflow of sewage and stormwater the weir plate 200 is rotated at an angle of inclination at all times at least one side of the wear plate 200 and one side and the other side of the sewage line 10 are formed on the left side and the right side of the center of the wear plate 200 so as to be rotated by the elastic force of the wear plate 600 respectively the pressure of the sewage and the storm that the wear plate 200 is rotated is adjusted by using the wear plate driving spring 300 and the driving spring adjusting nut 400 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be rotated or fixed when the inflow amount of the sewage and the storm is small it is possible to block and minimize the inflow of sewage and to prevent the inflow of sewage and stormwater by effectively opening and closing the ware plate 200 to prevent the contamination of the stream and the upper surface of the wear plate 200 is configured to be wider than the lower surface of the lower surface of the wear plate 200 when the wear plate 200 is rotated due to inflow of sewage and storm and the sewage and stormwater are completely prevented from flowing into the sewage pipe 10 by the upper surface and the frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101562757-B1", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "it is possible to provide a non point pollution abatement facility capable of preventing the discharge water pump from being damaged due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101562757-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "however when the water is discharged by the puncture smaller than the size of the sand particles the sand particles heavier than water can not escape by being caught by the perforated plate and can be returned to the filter medium layer by preventing the outflow of sand so that the cause of failure such as impeller wear and clogging of the drainage pump 117 to be described later can be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-5348664-A", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "because the measuring capability of the effluent redox probe 36 is resistant to fouling substances found in the wastewater the measuring electrode of the effluent redox probe is preferably submerged directly in the wastewater adjacent the effluent weir 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the frequency and the run time of the combined water diversion and therefore the contaminant yielded to the receiving stream are reduced and there is a considerable reduction in the discharge of suspended substances into the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102562679-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in any one selected from claims 1 and 2 a process of storing a large amount of river water by using an eco friendly movable weir 101 installed in the river or stream 2000 for preventing algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation structure a water reservoir 700 provided to store river water at a high place near the river or stream 2000 a structure in which a pump 33 is configured in the vicinity of the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal bloom for both fish and hydroelectric power generation a structure in which a pumping channel 701 is formed between the pump 33 and the water reservoir 700 a structure in which a drop channel 702 is formed between the water reservoir 700 and the river or stream 2000 after the pumped storage pump 703 is installed at the lower end of the falling waterway 702 river water is stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing algae for both fish and hydroelectric power generation during the day and then the fisheye and hydroelectric power at night the river water stored inside the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of combined algal bloom is pumped by using the pump 33 and the pumping waterway 701 to pump the opposite river water and stored in the water storage 700 and then the using the eco friendly movable weir 101 for preventing the occurrence of algal blooms which is configured to perform pumped power generation by using the pumped storage pump 703 of the falling waterway 702 stores a large amount of river water to generate pumped storage power at the same time it plays the role of a large rainwater storage tank that acts to prevent flood damage in advance and at the same time clean river water with a heavy specific gravity is constantly discharged through the bottom water discharge port 7777 for fishermen formed at the bottom to prevent algae from occurring electricity is produced using an eco friendly electricity system and a pumped storage power generation system that works to prevent green algae which is characterized by a nature friendly and eco friendly pumped storage power generation method that works to revive the natural ecosystem and at the same time naturally purify polluted river water at the same time it increases fishery resources by using naturally formed fisheries and at the same time acts as a large rainwater storage tank to prevent flood damage"}]</data>
