  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-4896542-A", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "sewers that carry wastewater from areas that experience severe storm water inflow problems typically operate under surcharged conditions during and immediately after rainfall events"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100633532-B1", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "the amount of sewage flowing through the rainwater and sewage inlets 23 may not exceed the weir 40 and the rainfall may be small even in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the case of rainwater storms installed upstream the rainwater is collected at least 10 times the maximum amount of sewage during rainfall and thus the sewage flowing into rainwater stormwater installed downstream of the sewage flows in excess amount"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in the rainwater treatment facility according to the present invention in the case of a combined sewer system a lower weir having a height corresponding to the water level due to initial rainfall and a higher weir are provided in a part of the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-RE36069-E", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "sewers that carry wastewater from areas that experience severe storm water inflow problems typically operate under surcharged conditions during and immediately after rainfall events"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in the case of rainwater storms installed upstream the rainwater is collected at least 10 times the maximum amount of sewage during rainfall and thus the sewage flowing into rainwater stormwater installed downstream of the sewage flows in excess amount"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101604772-B1", "para_id": "para_90", "text": "according to the present invention the phenomenon occurring when the lid technique is applied to the watershed the phenomenon such as erosion scouring and sedimentation occurring in the river due to the increase and decrease of the effluent the total amount of suspended substances contained in the generated effluent it is possible to easily carry out a phenomenon such as erosion and scouring of the surface soil analysis of the correlation between the degree of compaction and the increase or decrease in the amount of penetration and more reliable data can be secured"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wear type rainwater chute device characterized in that to prevent the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "we provide a wear type stormwater system to prevent reverse flow of river water or sea water by maintaining the state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102153821-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "it can be done and because it consists of installing a wear and a sluice gate at the top of a sewage pipe not an orifice type that requires civil engineering work there is a useful effect to simplify the installation work"}]</data>
</edge>
