ide of the wear plate 200 so that the shaft 210 can be coupled to the wear plate 200 a fixing hinge 220 is formed on one surface and the other surface of the shaft coupling groove of the wear plate 200 for fixing the shaft 210 coupled to the wear plate 200 so as not to be detached from the wear plate 200 a shaft 210 and a spring coupling groove 211 are formed on one surface of the shaft 210 so as to be engaged with the wear plate drive spring 300 the drive spring adjusting nut 400 at least one bolt fixing groove 410 on the outer side so as to firmly fix the coupling state when the shaft 210 is engaged with the shaft 210 a fixing bolt 420 inserted into the bolt fixing groove 410 a spring insertion groove 430 is formed on one surface of the driving spring adjusting nut 400 so as to be engaged with the wear plate driving spring 300 and a shaft engaging groove 440 for engaging with the shaft 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the spring engaging groove 440 is coupled to one side of the wear plate driving spring 300 the wear plate operating spring 600 when the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater is small or there is no inflow of sewage and stormwater the weir plate 200 is rotated at an angle of inclination at all times at least one side of the wear plate 200 and one side and the other side of the sewage line 10 are formed on the left side and the right side of the center of the wear plate 200 so as to be rotated by the elastic force of the wear plate 600 respectively the pressure of the sewage and the storm that the wear plate 200 is rotated is adjusted by using the wear plate driving spring 300 and the driving spring adjusting nut 400 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be adjusted so that the wear plate 200 can be rotated or fixed when the inflow amount of the sewage and the storm is small it is possible to block and minimize the inflow of sewage and to prevent the inflow of sewage and stormwater by effectively open