the property 104 as the area of the property 104 to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114"}, {"pat_id": "US-8065905-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "where the effective amount is sufficient to reduce an amount of bulk water and or an amount of residual water in the pipeline below desired amounts and to depress a freezing point temperature of the composition to a temperature below an operating temperature of the pipeline where operating temperature is below the freezing point of pure water"}, {"pat_id": "US-8065905-B2", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "a system for use in conditioning and or pressure testing pipelines comprising an aqueous composition comprising an effective amount of a metal ion formate salt where the aqueous composition fills a pipeline or portion thereof where the pipeline or portion thereof is pressurized to a pressure between about 1.25 to about 1.5 times an operating pressure of the pipeline where the effective amount is sufficient to reduce an amount of bulk water and or an amount of residual water in the pipeline below desired amounts and or to depress a freezing point of the aqueous composition to a temperature below an operating temperature of a pipeline to be conditioned or tested where the operating temperature of the pipeline is below the freezing point of pure water and where the aqueous composition is directly discharged into the environment without further processing or treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-8065905-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the present invention relates to a method and a use of an aqueous metal ion formate salt composition for reducing a residual water film on an interior of a pipeline during pipeline dewatering operations which may involve the use of a pig or a plurality of pigs for pipeline pressure testing operations for freezing pointing suppression for sub freezing temperature pipeline testing operations i.e"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2923642-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "in addition ground laying pipeline 1 by using a power source stored in a battery by a solar cell as a power source 61 for the defrosting function and the anti freezing function it is possible to contribute to energy saving and to be used in for example a mountain area where it is difficult to secure the power source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101327389-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "that is by checking the condensate and curing temperature throughout the construction by the moisture sensor and the temperature sensor it is possible to contribute to the quality improvement by checking the uniform curing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100458619-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the non excavation overall repair method of supplying the impregnating tube to the inside of the molding apparatus and supplying compressed air or water to harden and cure the impregnated tube in the pipeline with hot water supplied by expanding the impregnated tube in the pipeline installing a forming end 50 having a forming hole 52 at one end of the tube 40 mixing the fast curable unsaturated resin with f a and materials with the impeller device 70 impregnating the tube 40 into the mixed quick curable unsaturated resin and f a and material installing a wholesaler device 60 to block the conduit 2 of the manhole 1 to prevent excessive extension of the impregnation tube 40 after connecting the forming end 50 to the impregnating tube 40 the impregnating tube 40 in the forming apparatus 10 by bending 90 toward the conduit 2 in the inside of the manhole 91 and injecting air to reverse insert step non excavation pipeline repair method using a molding end and a bottom wholesale characterized in that it comprises the step of lining in the pipe line 2 by supplying a water temperature of 85 to the reverse insert impregnated tube 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101962825-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an extraction well a water permeation reaction wall of a sand layer a biochar layer or a biochar alginate bead layer formed on the outer periphery of the extraction well a siphon pipeline installed outwardly from the inside of the extraction well an activated charcoal and a zero valent iron powder mixed powder filter disposed in the middle of the siphon pipeline for filtering odor and ground chlorinated organic compounds and a real time pollution degree measuring device connected to the extraction well wherein the contaminated groundwater passes through the permeable reaction wall of the sand layer the bio char layer or the bio char alginate bead layer to remove organic pollutants and heavy metal pollutants the present invention relates to a method for purifying harmful groundwater which is capable of continuously pumping purified groundwater in a well by means of a siphon hydraulic power and to purify odorous components and chlorinated organic compounds contained in the pumped the method according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the pollutant contamination degree of the extraction well is automatically measured in real time to monitor contamination and when the pollution degree is higher than the reference value the water permeation reaction wall of the sand layer repair the biochar of the biochar layer of the permeable reaction wall is filled with wood byproducts in an electric furnace under an oxygen free anaerobic condition and subjected to pyrolysis reaction in a temperature range of 300 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-5651895-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the effort to remove arsenic compounds from the environment includes efforts to remove it from antifreeze that protects the radiators of engines used with large compressors in the natural gas processing and pipeline industry"}, {"pat_id": "US-5027842-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "in another aspect the invention relates to a system for commissioning pipelines which provides for lower amounts of product waste during the commissioning process to achieve reliable levels of product purity while reducing the possibility of pipeline damage due to the stress of subdesign temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "groundwater contamination prevention structure 1 1 is built in the space inside the combined structure to combine and directly connected to each other and sealed to each other structural structure 1 1 1 is installed inside the underground rock well inside the casing 4 4 to prevent the groundwater contamination by itself and to automatically drain and drain the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "it maintains the same level of water that is inflowed by itself and automatically intakes and pumps while preventing groundwater contamination"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "this drop in temperature may mimic the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "manually driven re melt programs can fail due to human error and the chances of failing to utilize safe reliable and repeatable re melting methods of solidified process fluid in the pipeline could result in a plant shutdown due to a pipeline rupture or damage from excessive movement of solidified process fluid and or pipe anchor failures"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "liquid sulphur not flowing but still in a molten state requiring flow to resume and plugged in which portions of the pipeline have experienced sulphur solidification perhaps with formation of voids which forms one or more plugs within the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "using the latent heat signatures associated with phase changes of a process fluid in this case sulphur to identify solidification or melting of the process fluid at locations along a pipeline is not dependent on a particular melting or freezing temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "for example curves in the pipeline may tend to accumulate more solidified process fluid compared to straight sections of the pipeline and anchor points along the pipeline may accumulate more solidified process fluid as a result of heat transfer to the anchors supporting the pipeline which may drop the temperature of the anchor points below the freezing point of the process fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "first the offshore plant 100 according to the prior art resumes the operation of transferring marine resources and as the temperature of the marine resources is rapidly lowered due to the row thompson effect the pipeline 130 is damaged due to temperature drop there is a problem that there is a risk of breakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "summary of the invention the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a multiple pressure regulator for an offshore plant which can reduce the risk of damage or breakage of a pipeline due to a rapid temperature drop in the process of transferring marine resources"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "accordingly the multiple pressure regulating device 1 for an offshore plant according to the present invention can reduce the risk of damage or breakage of the pipeline 40 due to a temperature drop the effect of increasing the durability of the line 40 can be obtained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "accordingly in the multi pressure regulating apparatus 1 for a marine plant according to 