ol arrangement for regulating the intensity of the received electric power a generating structure for generating hypochlorous acid an inlet through which seawater flows and an outlet through which seawater is discharged in order to determine the concentration of hypochlorous acid the ph and temperature of seawater are measured simultaneously d a seawater inflow step to inflow external seawater the seawater flowing in the seawater inflow step flows along the piping a pumping step of pumping the seawater flowing in the seawater inflow step so as to flow along the pipeline supplying a current to the pipeline through which the seawater flows in the seawater flow stage using a power supply device a step of collecting the flowing seawater when the seawater flowing through the seawater box flows through the pipeline after the seawater flow step a step performed after the seawater collection step the hypochlorous acid measurement step of measuring hypochlorous acid contained in the collected seawater based on the measurement result of the hypochlorous acid measurement step a current adjustment step of adjusting the current supplied in the seawater electrolytic apparatus so that the hypochlorous acid concentration of the seawater discharged from the seawater electrolytic apparatus does not exceed the environmental standard of 0.2 ppm a seawater discharge step of discharging the seawater into which the concentration of hypochlorous acid has been converted according to the current regulation through the current regulating step from the seawater electrolytic apparatus and the seawater is completely discharged to the outside of the hull or the like after the seawater flow step the pumping step the method potential supply step and the seawater discharge step of the seawater electrolytic device is performed wherein the cooling is performed in the course of the step of cooling the marine plant cooling water line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101619674-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefo