 be used to determine whether there is a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in 1988 piper alpha platform fire accident killed 167 people and costed 3.4 billion because of removing the pump a s pressure safety valve in 1999 a pressure relief valve failed on a 16 inch gasoline pipeline operated by the olympic pipe line company in bellingham wash"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102336715-B1", "para_id": "para_61", "text": "this is because it is difficult to determine whether there is a leak unless there is a change in the leaking part because it must be used to determine whether there is a leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "first the high initial initial rainfall that occurs at the time of sewage or rainfall inflowing into the city can be collected in the sewage subway pipeline through the sewage discharge section and the large amount of rainfall introduced into the large amount during rainfall is increased by the water pressure the opening of the sewage water discharge pipe is reduced by rotating the rotating plate by the linkage part and the link part linked with the open front water gate and the linkage part linked thereto to prevent the inflow of rainwater and soil to the sewage water supply pipe channel and discharging it to the discharge river it is possible to reduce the dredging cost by cutting off the earth and sand and it is possible to reduce the sewage treatment cost because it is possible to collect only the planned amount of sewage in the sewage subway pipeline as well as the breakage of the sewer pipeline and manhole due to the water pressure caused by the over can be prevented in advance"}]</data>
