  <data key="d6">["apply", "prevent", "collect", "penetrate", "rise", "supply", "reverse", "inhibit", "divide", "scour", "cope", "introduce", "base", "accord", "serve", "result", "require", "cause", "forget", "prepare", "induce", "last", "avoid", "remove", "cover", "have", "occur", "improve", "would", "reinforce", "may", "flow", "face", "can", "damage", "discharge", "be", "prohibit", "relate", "do", "describe", "instal", "create", "lose"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-6912890-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "many city codes prohibit any such blockage or restriction in the plumbing line thus if one forgets to remove the erhardt device before covering over the plumbing line with drywall the resulting structure is in violation of the city code"}, {"pat_id": "US-6912890-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "it is a further object of the invention that the leak testing device may serve as a permanent attachment to the test tee so that removal is not required thereby avoiding flooding of the foundation of the building or the area beneath the fluid based pipeline system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101955319-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "background of the invention field of the invention 0001 the present invention relates to a pipeline drainage system more particularly the present invention relates to a pipe drainage system for underground distribution lines and more particularly it relates to a distribution line installed in the ground it is possible to prevent secondary electric safety accidents caused by external damage such as an earthquake inside the underground pipe due to an external force such as an earthquake or the like to an underground distribution line with an improved drainage system to prevent flooding and prevent electric accidents due to flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013539-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "conventional sewage pipe repair method introduced to date as described above is not only has advantages and disadvantages according to the construction method but also is divided into the exponential method to index the leakage or flooding method and reinforcement method to reinforce the damaged pipeline conventionally the repair method has no method of preparing for such leaks and inundations due to the damage that may occur after the completion of repair of damaged pipelines"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201943-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "disasters such as flooding can be prevented and water can be supplied to street trees in urban areas where rainwater is not well supplied because it is covered with an impermeable layer such as asphalt or concrete.as described above according to the present invention since a leak hole is installed in a pipeline in which rainwater flows down a part of the rainwater can be penetrated into the ground so that disasters caused by flooding of rivers where rainwater collects can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014460-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the area where the sewage flows in the sewage pipe during flooding or the sewage of the downstream flows poorly and flows back upstream in particular the gap is not watertight and both sides of the seam of the sewer pipe due to the difference in head height due to the elevation difference between the upstream and the downstream water pressure is often applied through the gap between the outer surface and the concrete collar pipe which are installed to face each other so that the confluence of sewage and flooding may scour the backfill surface of the joint into the sewer pipe and it is lost in a loose state ultimately the upper ground of the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345691-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "in the above embodiment when the flow rate increases there is a limit value in the pipeline and when the pressure rises reverse flow of sewage occurs to prevent flooding damage at the upstream site"}, {"pat_id": "US-10458446-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "such soft reverse flow beneficially does not fully inhibit backflow which would create a shock wave that is harmful to the structures of the material flow conduit and to the pumping devices"}]</data>
</edge>
