  <data key="d6">["change", "mention", "see", "desire", "roll", "bury", "act", "perform", "work", "include", "join", "should", "combine", "purify", "apply", "consist", "prevent", "block", "give", "rise", "sink", "approximate", "assess", "connect", "use", "assume", "carry", "form", "advance", "construct", "look", "point", "know", "remain", "quantify", "allow", "achieve", "locate", "cause", "tilt", "limit", "pass", "have", "control", "depend", "vary", "affect", "would", "characterize", "may", "fix", "configure", "learn", "pollute", "contemplate", "shape", "continue", "can", "do", "discharge", "be", "store", "determine", "sample", "will", "start", "mistake", "generate"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5708211-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "because the consequences of a major oil line break are undesirable it is important to quantify the corrosivity of multiphase flow under varying conditions so effective corrosion control can be achieved"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1846689-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the diameter of the sensor unit should also be large enough so that the sensor unit can roll easily over small obstacles such as a discontinuity in the wall of the pipeline where two pipe sections join and so that the drag of the water will cause it to continue rolling onwards even when the pipe tilts uphill"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a structure in which the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir frame 830 and white paper 88 are combined to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity on top of the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir 8888 is formed a structure in which a shaped siphon action generating assembly partition 836 is sequentially fixed to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a structure in which the power generation water discharge pipe 3151 is constructed at an angle along the slope of the downstream part of the river starting from the lower part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth a structure in which an upward discharge pipe 3150 is formed in an l shape at a height that is 5 to 20 lower than the height of the lower part of the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is formed in the upstream part of the river at the end of the above mentioned power generation water discharge pipe 3151 a structure in which a terminal discharge pipe 3152 is formed in a t shape at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 3150 a structure in which an air exhaust unit 381 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a plurality of power generation water final pipes 262 each having a different thickness are connected around the end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a control unit 266 configured to control the discharge amount is connected to the upper part of the final power generation water pipe 262 a structure in which an upper storage tank 259 is connected to a lower discharge unit 256 configured in a different form with each storage capacity to store power generation water and discharge it to the lower part at the lower part of the above mentioned power generation water final pipeline 262 a structure in which a hydroelectric power generation unit 335 configured to generate electricity by hydraulic power is combined at the lower end of the above mentioned lower discharge unit 256 a nature friendly eco friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water using an eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae growth that is characterized by generating hydroelectric power by using an eco friendly movable dam that acts to prevent green algae growth"}, {"pat_id": "US-7941282-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "as known in the art these variations among pipeline construction geometry contents and nominal operating condition affect the extent and nature of corrosion and ablation of the pipeline walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-7941282-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "of course it is contemplated that a different calibration scheme may be applied depending on the particular measurement technologies and apparatus used in each case differences in the pipelines and the nature of the fluid carried whether a higher order calibration is desired and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102069616-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore the leakage measurement of underground buried water supply pipelines is buried over a very long distance due to the nature of the pipeline and also consists of small water supply pipelines connected to many branch points"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100714781-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "therefore the leakage measurement of underground buried drainage channel is buried over a very long distance due to the nature of the pipeline and because it consists of small pipelines connected to many branch points the strange symptom of the ground where the drainage pipes pass that is water leaks and rises into the air you can see it with the naked eye or a report by looking at the state where the ground is sunk"}, {"pat_id": "US-12091842-B2", "para_id": "para_261", "text": "this is mainly because of the nature of the transient pressure trace when a burst is located close to the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "US-5416724-A", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "because the gas carrying pipeline pressure and leak shape remain relatively constant the nature of the leak signal does not change and statistical stationarity can be assumed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore the leakage detection index le given by equation 7 below the smallest model of ak is the best approximating autoregressive model"}, {"pat_id": "US-11359989-B2", "para_id": "para_240", "text": "potential leak signal and may be mistaken by the pipeline leak detection apparatus as a leak events due to their transient nature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100935006-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "due to the nature of the pipeline construction that the engine should be advanced at a high speed the first work is performed up to the limit depth about 2m to allow the pit work to work without the masonry structure and then the construction of the masonry structure and the second pit work are performed simultaneously"}, {"pat_id": "US-11033648-B2", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "in order to learn more about the extent and nature of the damage and therefore to determine an appropriate treatment a user may sample the environmental conditions at various points along the pipeline by assessing properties that would be indicative of conditions suitable for biofilm formation including but not limited to a detection of certain bacterial species known to have a role in bacterial corrosion e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-10350653-B1", "para_id": "para_113", "text": "in order to learn more about the extent and nature of the damage and therefore to determine an appropriate treatment a user may sample the environmental conditions at various points along the pipeline by assessing properties that would be indicative of conditions suitable for biofilm formation including but not limited to a detection of certain bacterial species known to have a role in bacterial corrosion e.g"}]</data>
</edge>
