  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100523904-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "of course such changes will fall within the scope of the claims.the effect of the present invention can be expected by the configuration and action as described above even if the underground pipeline connecting the indoor drainage pipe and roof excellent pipe around the building vulnerable to the influence of sedimentation to the sewer manhole storm manhole and storm pipe the pipeline naturally rotates according to the settlement direction and the length of the pipeline is also increased by the amount of settlement which prevents damage and excessive deformation of underground pipelines ensuring durability reducing maintenance costs extending the life span and reducing the maintenance work around buildings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102100306-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step of the server storing the sub zone information determined to be in need of maintenance in the database the step of receiving and saving the operation history information and and storing the simulation data in connection with the gis data collecting and analyzing measurement data by the server displaying by the server a simulation object rdii parameter and a flow graph using a toolbox the server constructing and calibrating a model for each small area the server further includes performing model verification and simulation evaluation the step of the server building a model for each of the small areas constructing a pipe network for model building and collecting attribute data estimating the input value of the pipeline model calculating a dwf dry weather flow model input value comprising the step of calculating the input value of the simulation object rdii model the step of the server to calibrate each sub area dwf dry weather flow model calibration step wwf wet weather flow model correction step for the selected rainfall event before the server collects and analyzes measurement data inquiring by the server information about an existing zone in a database to divide the small zone selecting by the server an object that is inadequate compared to the sub zone criterion as an object to be divided into sub zones when the division target area is selected the server establishes the boundary of the small area using the boundary of the back road the river and the railway or the boundary of the administrative area while conforming to the area standard determining by the server the compatibility with the sub region criteria by extracting the stored sub region information determining that the boundary condition is met when the server is determined to be suitable for a small area standard if the server determines that the boundary condition is met further comprising the step of storing the set and stored sub zone information as the new divided sub zone information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 is a schematic view showing a flow rate control apparatus of a non dynamic flow rate control system according to the present invention a rectangular outer frame 6 which is seated on an upper part of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 and opens front and rear to open the lower part to block odors and to guide sewage and a flow control device 5 detachably mounted on the inner side of the outer frame 6 to control the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater to flow out to the sewage water collection pipe 2 the flow control device 5 includes an inner frame 10 detachably attached to the outer frame by a drawer a plate shaped rotary plate member 20 having a center shaft 21 at the lower end of the inner frame 10 and rotating up and down to guide the sewage contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream while controlling the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater wow the water flow control device 5 includes a water flow rotary shaft 31 rotatably mounted on the inside of the flow control device 5 and is fixed to the water flow rotary shaft 31 so as to be in close contact with both inner side walls of the flow control device 5 30 of a wall like shape opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 21 of the rotary plate member 20 so that the rotary plate member 20 is rotated in the non and a link portion 40 the outer frame 6 is seated at the distal end of the sewage pipe and an inner frame 10 is detachably attached to the inner side of the outer frame 6 by a drawer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a filtration tank provided with a filtration quartz for allowing the fine water to be filtered through a predetermined distance upward from a position spaced upward from the inner bottom the filtration tank is connected to the other side of the filtration tank via a backwash water tank transfer pipe at a central portion of one side facing the other central portion of the filtration tank and is filtered from the filtration tank through the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash tank where stormwater level is reached and is connected to a central portion of one side of the backwash water tank opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank through a discharge pipe to be introduced into the backwash water tank through the outlet pipe an effluent tank for discharging the filtered desulfur to the outside and bypassing the desulfurized effluent when the level of the desulfurized effluent storage tank is higher than a certain level through the bypass pipeline the sedimentation tank is disposed at a predetermined distance from the sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "a filtration tank provided with a filtration quaternion for allowing a rise in the height of the water to be filtered from a position spaced upward from the inner bottom by a predetermined distance upward the filtration tank is connected to the other side of the filtration tank via a backwash water tank transfer pipe at a central portion of one side facing the other central portion of the filtration tank and is filtered from the filtration tank through the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash tank where stormwater level is reached and is connected to a central portion of one side of the backwash water tank opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank through a discharge pipe to be introduced into the backwash water tank through the outlet pipe an effluent tank for discharging the filtered desulfur to the outside and bypassing the desulfurized effluent when the level of the desulfurized effluent storage tank is higher than a certain level through the bypass pipeline a bottom wastewater pipe disposed at a predetermined distance from the settling tank and connected to the transfer pipe from the inside of the settling tank selectively introducing the stagnant water of the settling tank and the backwash water is selectively supplied from the backwash water tank to the lower side of the filtration tank to backwash the filtration tank and the settling tank by the backwash water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101921821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 to the sewage water collection line 2 and discharges a large amount of rainwater flowing into the continuous rainwater to the river smoothly a rectangular outer frame 10 which is formed in a box shape to be seated on an upper portion of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 to block malodors and opens to the front and rear to guide sewage an inner frame 20 detachably attached to the inside of the outer frame 10 by a drawer a wall like opening closing gate 30 connected to the upper side of the inner frame 20 by a hinge portion 31 so as to be opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced the sewage water supply system according to the present invention is characterized in that the sewage water supply pipe 2 is connected to the opening closing water gate 30 40 the flow rate regulator 40 includes a center shaft 41a at the lower end of the inner frame 20 and is rotated upward and downward to adjust the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while guiding the soil contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate center shaft 41a of the rotary plate 41 so that the rotary plate 41 and a link portion 42 for rotating the link member in a non the upper portion of the link portion 42 is engaged with the first link pin 42a at the upper end of the upper side of the interchange gate 30 and the lower end of the link portion 42 is inserted when the interchange gate 30 is opened by inserting the second link pin 42b an upper link 42c for transmitting the rotational force to the lower link 42e and a sliding hole 42d having an elongated shape for sliding the second link pin 42b of the upper link 42c on the upper side and a lower link 42e whose lower side is coupled to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 41a of the rotary plate 41 and is coupled together with the upper link 42c so that the opening and closing gate 30 is opened and the rotating plate 41 is rotated in synchronization with the rotating force generated when the rotating plate 41 is rotated"}]</data>
