  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank and also if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "a temporary storage tank for chemicals having a cover installed on the unit one side is connected to the drug storage space of the drug temporary storage tank and the other side is connected to the connection pipe connected to the flocculation settler or the immersion well via the injector the drug discharge pipe is installed on the pipeline chemical discharge pump a discharge side bypass pipe bypassing the chemical discharge pipe and having a discharge side bypass valve in the middle a supply side bypass pipe bypassing the supply pipe and having a supply side bypass valve in the middle a control device electrically connected to the leak detection sensor a ph sensor a chemical discharge pump and a supply side shutoff valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272217-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition according to the present invention when the water level of the storage tank along the linearly located storage tank is more than a predetermined level by penetrating the overflowed rainwater has the effect of maximizing the penetration of the rainwater to increase the penetration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water level sensor 10 installed in a non contact manner separately a sensor board 20 for collecting and collecting water level values h of a set of water level sensors 10 installed by height at one of each position on the surface of the pipe p by wire a data collection device 30 that collects and collects the water level values h of the sensor boards 20 wired or wirelessly a sensor information controller 40 which is an mcu that receives the water level value h of the data collection device 30 and calculates a pipeline blockage state s an internet hub 50 that connects the sensor information control unit 40 with the local management control unit 60 or the remote management control unit 70 online a computer device that receives the water level value h and the pipeline blockage state s transmitted from the sensor information control unit 40 through the internet hub 50 and displays them on a monitor located in a building where the pipe p is installed a local management control unit 60 the water level value h and the pipe blockage state s transmitted from the sensor information control unit 40 through the internet hub 50 are the total number of pipes the number for each state the pipe status list the date and contents of the pipe inspection and the sensor error internet data center 70 which is a main server that receives and stores the communication error notification when it occurs and checks the error itself as a computer device that receives the water level value h and the pipe blockage state s stored in the internet data center 70 and displays them on a monitor the remote management control unit 80 located at a remote location outside the building where the pipe p is installed the sensor information control unit 40 measures the water level value h as the number of times of the water level duration frequency value lasting at a certain percentage for a certain time and includes it in the water level information the local management controller 60 displays a water level duration frequency value for each period in which the water level value h is maintained at a certain percentage for a certain time period the local management control unit 60 is a computer and monitoring device installed inside or near a building so that a building manager can grasp water level information including water level values and collection schedule information and high middle low positions for each pipe section"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a pipe blockage prediction system a central control system that can predict the possibility of blockage in each section of the pipe by measuring the water level in each section of the pipe by utilizing the fact that the water level in the vicinity of the pipeline where sediment is accumulated and the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "in addition the water level information measures the number of times that the time when the pipe line is measured as the medium or high level is detected for a certain period of time or more and the local management control unit or the remote management control unit displays the pipeline blockage state in color according to a predetermined criterion so that the manager can there is an excellent effect of intuitively grasping the state of pipe clogging due to the accumulation of sediment for each section of the pipe.1 is a conceptual diagram of a pipe clogging prediction system according to an embodiment of the present invention 2 is a conceptual diagram of water level measurement when there is no pipe clogging of the pipe clogging prediction system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "therefore the true technical protection scope of the present invention should be determined by the technical spirit of the appended claims.p pipe r conduit m sediment h water level value s pipeline blockage 10 water level sensor 20 sensor board 30 data collection device 40 sensor information control unit 50 internet hub 60 local management control unit 70 internet data center 80 remote management control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portabl