ies files it as a plant information actual value file in a plant information actual value file and detects whether a plant abnormality has occurred a water level plan prediction pattern on the day of water leakage monitoring is created based on the filed information actual value and a water leak occurrence water level pattern a water level upper limit value allowable pattern and a water level lower limit based on the water level plan prediction pattern a predicted water level pattern planning processing unit for creating a value acceptable pattern a predicted water level pattern memory for storing these patterns leakage monitoring calculation processing for comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water leakage occurrence water level pattern and comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water level upper limit allowable pattern or the water level lower limit allowable pattern and when the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence water level pattern it is determined that water leakage has occurred due to a break in the water pipeline and the actual water level exceeds the water level upper limit allowable pattern or the water level lower limit allowable pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here with regard to information on the equipment installed in the water pipeline that causes disturbance in water leakage monitoring information related to the water level plan prediction pattern of the equipment installed in the water pipeline is stored in the prediction water level pattern memory and the prediction the information in the water level pattern memory and the information in the plant information actual value file are compared and if there is a difference in the state of the equipment installed in the water pipeline the water level plan prediction pattern is corrected"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the sewage treatment plant 130 processes the sewage to remove the treated water producing stage d the treated water produced by the sewage treatment plant 130 is stored in the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 and the treated water is supplied to the first storage tank 110 to a supply water storage tank 110b of the storage tank 110 e supplying the supply water stored in the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage vessel 110 to the city water or the river maintenance water through the water supply pump 190 f if the water level is greater than the reference value the supply water storage tank 110b of the first storage tank 110 is switched to the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the process water reuse pipe 150 is switched to the sewage transfer pipe 140 g the wastewater flowing through the combined sewage line 200 is stored in the inflow sewage storage tank 110a and the supply water storage tank 110b as stormwater and wastewater and the sewage transfer pipeline 140 and the treatment water pipeline 150 transferring the storm water and the sewage water respectively h transferring the treated water storage tank 120b of the second storage tank 120 to the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and storing storm water and sewage water in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b and i discharging stormwater and sewage stored in the transfer sewage storage tank 120a and the treated water storage tank 120b to the sewage treatment plant and treating the sewage treatment plant 130 with stormwater and sewage lt rti the treated water recycling duct 150 may be embedded in parallel on the side of the sewage conveying pipe 140 so as to be utilized in a region having a small geographical radial gradient in order to secure the water supply end face of the combined sewage pipe 200 at the time of rainfall characterized in that the water supply and the flow control are adjustable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100690956-B1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "to this end the sludge removal packer 130 is provided with a rubber tube 131 that blocks the inside of the pipe line 110 while expanding and a sewage outlet 132 is provided at the center thereof so as to strongly discharge the sewage having a high water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "first if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20 it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "monitor screen which is attached to said cable s second end said cable s semi rigidness further provides limited means for inserting said camera lights and housing into said pipeline via access hole one and aiming generally in the direction of the flow route to access hole two and controlling the attitude or aim of the remote camera lens said remote camera also has on its anterior surface a means such as an eyelet or recessed peg eccentrically located whereon the attached lanyard thereto and with the combination of said semi rigid camera cable and said lanyard attached to said camera housing manipulating said cable and lanyard to position said camera lens anterior of or beneath said rubber test ball with said lens aiming at said test ball e attaching another said lanyard reel end to said test ball which has anterior or posterior ends by means such as a spring clip or pneumatic hose coupling or camera access cable dummy coupling or a loop formed on said lanyard end f connecting said test ball s posterior end to a pneumatic hose which allows the test ball to be inflated thereby and which hose has first and second ends and is connected on said first end to a supply of pneumatic air pulling on said lanyard s service end thereby inserting at least one inflatable test ball into said pipeline via access hole two said test ball which has anterior and posterior ends and said lanyard s reel end is connected to said test ball s anterior end and the test ball is inserted via access hole two in said pipeline wherein when said test ball is manipulated by virtue of the retrieval lanyard and pneumatic hose to a point in a pipeline which said test ball is inflated to produce a temporary passageway seal or blockage in said pipeline by virtue of said test ball s exterior surface coming in contact with said pipelines interior wall and by virtue of its ball shape g attaching a mechanism for measuring the amount of cable or lanyard that has passed into or out of a pipeline wherein said mechanism has a numerical display which can be directly read h inflating said test ball to produce a seal or blockage in the pipeline being tested h filling the vertical pipe being tested with test fluid or water and by viewing the monitor checking to see whether the test ball has effectively sealed off the pipe from the test fluid or water column above the test ball i repositioning the test ball or manipulating it to produce a satisfactory seal if required j viewing the column of water via the access hole two into which the water or test fluid was pumped into the pipe being tested for stability k determine that the pipeline segment thus tested is leak free if stability of the water level is positive or leaking if the water level recedes into the pipeline l repositioning the camera and the test ball to check further down the pipeline if the prior step indicated no leakage or further up the pipeline if the prior step indicated leakage m continuing to narrow the search for the leak by eliminating sections of non leaking pipe segments by the technique described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a shielding facility 110 not shown is formed in the upper part of the low permeability seabed sole so that incineration ash non combustible solid waste or dredged waste can be buried in the marine waste treatment plant 100 a marine purification treatment facility 120 for purifying the polluted water and discharging the polluted water to the marine environment a polluted water storage tank 130 for collecting and storing polluted water in the shielding facility 110 the water level is lowered by the water purifying treatment facility 120 by the water purifying treatment facility 120 while the water level of the shielding facility 110 is higher than a preset reference value onshore reservoir 140 which in case of difficulty the polluted water is transported to the land storage tank 140 and the contaminated water stored in the land storage tank 140 is transported to the contaminated water storage tank 130"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "the apparatus of claim 1 wherein the controller 180 an internal water level determination unit 181 for determining an internal water level of the shielding facility 110 an external water level determination unit 182 for determining an external water level of the sea surface of the shielding facility 110 a water level comparator 183 that compares the internal water level determined by the internal water level determination unit 181 with a predetermined reference value or compares the internal water level with the external water level determined by the external water level determination unit 182 a polluted water transport amount determiner 184 for determining an amount of polluted water to be transported through the first pipeline 150 when the internal water level is greater than the reference value according to the comparison result in the water level comparator 183 and a pressurizing and pressurizing pump driving unit 185 for calculating the driving speed and the driving time of the pressurization pressurizing pump 170 and driving the pressurization pressurizing pump 170 according to the determined amount of the contaminated water the hybrid pipeline transport system of a marine waste treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "here the control unit may include an internal water level determination unit for determining an internal water level of the shielding facility an external water level determining unit for determining a water level outside the sea surface of the shielding facility a water level comparator that compares the internal water level determined by the internal water level determination unit with a predetermined reference value or compares the internal water level with the external water level determined by the external water level determination unit a polluted water transport amount determining unit for determining an amount of polluted water to be transported through the first pipeline when the internal water level is greater than the reference value according to the comparison result in the water level comparator and a pressurizing and pressurizing pump driving unit for calculating the driving speed and the driving time of the pressurization pressurizing pump according to the determined amount of contaminated water and driving the pressurization pressurizing pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "in another aspect of the present invention there is provided a method of operating a hybrid pipeline transportation system for a marine waste treatment plant the method comprising the steps of a a marine purification treatment facility installed in a marine waste treatment plant b measuring the water level inside the shielding facility of the shore waste treatment plant and the external water level of the sea level c checking whether the internal water level is greater than a preset reference value d collecting the contaminated water in the shielded facility so that the internal water level of the shielded facility is lowered and storing the polluted water in the polluted water storage tank when the internal water level is higher than a preset reference value e determining the amount of polluted water transported by the control unit to be transported to the land storage tank f driving the pressure feed pump for transporting the contaminated water through the first pipeline and g storing the contaminated water transported by the onshore storage tank wherein the control unit is operable to transport the contaminated water to the land storage tank when the internal water level of the shielded facility is higher than a preset reference value and the first pipeline in step f transports the polluted water stored in the polluted water storage tank to the land storage tank thereby lowering the internal water level of the shielded facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "according to the present invention a pipeline is installed between the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant and the land storage tank and the polluted water of the shielding facility is transported to the land storage tank by the pipeline thereby reducing the water level in the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "according to the present invention by installing a pipeline for transporting waste between a marine waste treatment plant and a land waste treatment plant the waste is transported directly from the land to the marine waste treatment plant without transporting the waste it is possible to prevent contamination which may occur.brief description of the drawings figure 1 is a diagram illustrating a marine waste treatment plant for treating general managed waste"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "at this time as described later the contaminated water in the marine waste treatment plant 100 can be transported to the land by bypass and stored in the land storage tank 140 by using the press feed pressure pump and the polluted water stored in the land storage tank 140 and may be returned to the contaminated water storage tank 130 of the marine waste treatment plant 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "that is when the sea water purification facility 120 can not process all of the contaminated water even though the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 is higher than a predetermined reference value due to a large difference between heavy rain heavy rain or tide water and transports the polluted water to the land based storage tank 140 through the first pipeline 150"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_69", "text": "the first pipeline 150 may be installed with at least one small diameter since a large diameter pipeline must be used when a line is used and a high pressure is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_89", "text": "in particular in the case of a marine waste treatment plant if the difference between the inside and outside water levels is large it may cause structural instability of the reef to return the polluted water to the marine purification facility of the marine waste treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_108", "text": "the scope of the present invention is defined by the appended claims rather than the detailed description and all changes or modifications derived from the meaning and scope of the claims and their equivalents are to be construed as being included within the scope of the present invention do.100 maritime waste treatment plant 200 land waste treatment plant 110 shielding facilities 120 water purification facilities 130 contaminated water storage tank 140 land storage tank 150 first pipeline 160 second pipeline 170 pressurizing pressurizing pump 180 190 vortex generator 210 conduit switching equipment 220 waste pipe 230 polluted water pipe 181 internal level determination section 182 external level determination section 183 water level comparator 184 polluted water transport amount determining unit 185 pressure feeding pump drive unit 191 first water level meter internal water level meter 192 2nd water gauge external water level measurement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275597-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "in the method of installing and recovering the negative water cutoff device in the water supply main pipeline the method of installing and recovering the negative water cutoff device in the water supply main pipe line installing a main fitting and an auxiliary fitting in a main pipeline s21 performing perforation and small diameter perforation using the perforator in the main fitting and the auxiliary fitting s22 installing a camera module insertion system in a small diameter hole in the main pipeline s23 installing a water level blocking device in the perforation of the main pipe line s24 installing a connection pipe between the camera module insertion system and the water level blocking device s25 starting the entry of the cut off water blocking device into the main pipe while watching the inside of the pipe using the camera module and the monitor s26 opening a second sandwich valve under the camera module insertion system a first valve of the connection pipe and a second valve to form dynamic pressure on the left and right sides of the water cutoff device s27 observing the inside of the pipeline using a camera module and a monitor to completely block the main pipeline by inserting the negative water cutoff device into the main pipeline s28 crossing the second sandwich valve the first valve of the connecting pipe and the second valve of the lower camera module insertion system s29 blocking a predetermined construction section of the main pipeline by using the cut off device at both sides and then draining the construction section main pipeline s30 opening the second sandwich valve the first valve and the second valve in the lower part of the camera module insertion system to form a dynamic pressure on the left and right side breaker block s31 and recovering the negative water cutoff device from the main pipe line s32"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "9 the front water gate 40 is rotated by the water pressure generated by the elevated water level and is interlocked with the angle adjuster 53 of the good interlocking portion 50 the link section 60 is interlocked and the rotating plate 30 is rotated to reduce the outflow cross section of the grating 20 to block the inflow of rainwater into the fine powder chamber 2 so that a large amount of rainwater naturally flows out into the discharge stream soils inherent in stormwater are also naturally released into the discharge stream thereby blocking the introduction of the soil from the storm sewer thereby preventing the sediment from accumulating on the sewer sewer pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 sand rinse device 62 coarse aggregate rinse device 63 washing waste water evaporation device 64 be