  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-6052943-B1", "para_id": "para_88", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 disintegrator 62 disintegrated soil rinse device 63 washing wastewater evaporation device 65 blade 74 belt conveyor 75 disintegrated soil supply device 76 rinse water spray device 77 washing wastewater receiving tank 78 drive roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveying belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 washing wastewater discharge passage 84 washing wastewater storage tank 85 sand container 86 front end wall 87 rear end wall 88 left side wall 89 right side wall 90 bottom wall 92 roof 93 washing wastewater spray device 94 washing wastewater recirculation mechanism 100 ground 101 drainage groove 102 collecting drainage groove 103 convex 104 perforated plate 105 sand layer 107 left vertical frame 108 right vertical frame 10 horizontal frame 111 water supply pipe 112 drainage nozzle 113 intermediate pipe 114 cleaning waste water supply pipe 115 cleaning waste supply pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272217-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "in addition according to the present invention when the water level of the storage tank along the linearly located storage tank is more than a predetermined level by penetrating the overflowed rainwater has the effect of maximizing the penetration of the rainwater to increase the penetration efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a pipe blockage prediction system a central control system that can predict the possibility of blockage in each section of the pipe by measuring the water level in each section of the pipe by utilizing the fact that the water level in the vicinity of the pipeline where sediment is accumulated and the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101008852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the sewage pipe installed with the switchgear to discharge the clear rainwater to the pipeline and collect only the initial rainwater and the sewage into the rainwater discharge chamber a pair of fixing brackets fixed to both sides of an exposed cross section of the sewage pipe a first tube welded to the front lower surface of each fixing bracket a shielding plate shaped to correspond to the shape of the exposed cross sectional size of the sewage pipe a second pipe body welded to both sides of the upper surface of the shielding plate and and a hinge shaft inserted between the first pipe and the second pipe so that the screen plate is hinged to an upper portion of the exposed end of the sewage pipe so as to open and close the open exposed cross section of the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102290677-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition due to the inflow of rainwater interception and step by step exclusion are made so it is possible to prevent contamination of small tea houses and damage caused by backflow of rainwater from large tea houses"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in addition the present invention is to install a package type filter device made of stainless steel having a large number of lattice holes the structure is easy to replace the filling medium according to the rainwater contaminant and the initial excellent non point pollutant properties in series or it is another object of the present invention to provide a pipeline type initial excellent treatment apparatus which can be efficiently installed in parallel and can efficiently replace initial filler and reduce management costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "first if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20 it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "rainwater is discharged to the outside through the outlet 2 of the single closing block 20 located in the other end of the pipeline while the rainwater flows through the pipeline as in the supply process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "therefore the rainwater flows along the pipeline during the supply or discharge of rainwater thereby minimizing contamination due to the propagation of microorganisms in the rainwater by maintaining uniform time of stagnation in the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201943-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "disasters such as flooding can be prevented and water can be supplied to street trees in urban areas where rainwater is not well supplied because it is covered with an impermeable layer such as asphalt or concrete.as described above according to the present invention since a leak hole is installed in a pipeline in which rainwater flows down a part of the rainwater can be penetrated into the ground so that disasters caused by flooding of rivers where rainwater collects can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102004140-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "it is possible to prevent the inundation caused by abnormal rainfall in the city such that the excess water can be easily induced and discharged to the rainwater storage tank or the pumping station and the ability to cope with the abnormal rainfall where the heavy rain lasts for a long time is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "first the high initial initial rainfall that occurs at the time of sewage or rainfall inflowing into the city can be collected in the sewage subway pipeline through the sewage discharge section and the large amount of rainfall introduced into the large amount during rainfall is increased by the water pressure the opening of the sewage water discharge pipe is reduced by rotating the rotating plate by the linkage part and the link part linked with the open front water gate and the linkage part linked thereto to prevent the inflow of rainwater and soil to the sewage water supply pipe channel and discharging it to the discharge river it is possible to reduce the dredging cost by cutting off the earth and sand and it is possible to reduce the sewage treatment cost because it is possible to collect only the planned amount of sewage in the sewage subway pipeline as well as the breakage of the sewer pipeline and manhole due to the water pressure caused by the over can be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "9 the front water gate 40 is rotated by the water pressure generated by the elevated water level and is interlocked with the angle adjuster 53 of the good interlocking portion 50 the link section 60 is interlocked and the rotating plate 30 is rotated to reduce the outflow cross section of the grating 20 to block the inflow of rainwater into the fine powder chamber 2 so that a large amount of rainwater naturally flows out into the discharge stream soils inherent in stormwater are also naturally released into the discharge stream thereby blocking the introduction of the soil from the storm sewer thereby preventing the sediment from accumulating on the sewer sewer pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102104710-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if there are obstacles such as rainwater telecommunications and gas around the pipeline it may be necessary to remove and reinstall these obstacles for pipeline laying"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6052945-B1", "para_id": "para_93", "text": "r site s soil purification facility t chelating agent recovery device 1 crushing unit 2 classifying unit 3 sedimentation separating unit 4 filtering unit 5 chelating agent regenerating unit 6 chelating agent replenishing unit 7 rainwater supply unit 8 chelate agent removal unit 9 chelating agent recovery unit 11 input hopper 12 mixing device 13 mill breaker 14 trommel 15 cyclone 16 seal tank 17 sand clean 18 feed tank 19 ph adjustment tank 20 coagulation tank 21 floating material recovery equipment 22 thickener 23 intermediate tank 24 filter press 25 wash water tank 26 spare water tank 27 wash water tank 28 acid liquid tank 29 water tank 30 liquid fluidized bed apparatus 31 pump 32 pipe line 33 pump 34 37 pipeline 38 pump 39 40 pipeline 41 pump 42 4 pipe line 44 to 51 valve 55 rainwater storage tank 56 rainwater supply device 61 sand rinse device 62 coarse aggregate rinse device 63 washing waste water evaporation device 64 belt conveyor 65 sand supply device 66 rinse water spray device 67 cleaning waste water receiving tank 68 drive roller 68a shaft 69 driven roller 69a shaft 70 conveyor belt 71 support roller 72 guide plate 74 belt conveyor 75 coarse aggregate supply device 76 rinsing water spray device 77 cleaning waste water receiving tank 78 driving roller 78a shaft 79 driven roller 79a shaft 80 conveyor belt 81 support roller 82 guide plate 83 cleaning waste water discharge passage 84 cleaning waste water storage tank 85 sand container 86 fr