ir discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101921821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 to the sewage water collection line 2 and discharges a large amount of rainwater flowing into the continuous rainwater to the river smoothly a rectangular outer frame 10 which is formed in a box shape to be seated on an upper portion of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 to block malodors and opens to the front and rear to guide sewage an inner frame 20 detachably attached to the inside of the outer frame 10 by a drawer a wall like opening closing gate 30 connected to the upper side of the inner frame 20 by a hinge portion 31 so as to be opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced the sewage water supply system according to the present invention is characterized in that the sewage water supply pipe 2 is connected to the opening closing water gate 30 40 the flow rate regulator 40 includes a center shaft 41a at the lower end of the inner frame 20 and is rotated upward and downward to adjust the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while guiding the soil contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate center shaft 41a of the rotary plate 41 so that the rotary plate 41 and a link portion 42 for rotating the link member in a non the upper portion of the link portion 42 is engaged with the first link pin 42a at the upper end of the upper side of the interchange gate 30 and the lower end of the link portion 42 is inserted when the interchange gate 30 is opened by inserting the second link pin 42b an upper link 42c for transmitting the rotational force to the lower link 42e and a sliding hole 42d having an elongated shape for sliding the second link pin 42b of the upper link 42c on the upper side and a lower link 42e whose lower side is coupled to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 41a of the rotary plate 41 and is coupled together with the upper link 42c so that the opening and closing gate 30 is opened and the rotating plate 41 is rotated in synchronization with the rotating force generated when the rotating plate 41 is rotated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101222811-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "due to the mosquito formatting and bad smell is generated to form a liquid epoxy resin as a coating to prevent rust in the tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101834261-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide an excellent watertightness and a satisfactory workability in order to prevent leakage of sewage or rainwater through a drain pipe connection hole of a public pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101834261-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition the watertightness is excellent in order to prevent leakage of sewage or rainwater through a drain pipe connection hole of the public pipeline thereby providing an excellent effect of satisfactory construction"}]</data>
