  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-8703065-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in another embodiment the disclosure includes a production saltwater disposal facility comprising a separator configured to receive production saltwater from a pipeline or a vehicle and separate hydrocarbons from the production saltwater wherein the production saltwater received from the pipeline or vehicle is substantially the same composition as when the production saltwater was located in a subterranean formation a hydrocarbon storage tank configured to receive hydrocarbons from the separator a settling pit configured to receive the production saltwater from the separator and separate metals and or other solids from the saltwater an evaporator in fluid communication with the settling pit and comprising a nozzle configured to emit a stream of the saltwater along a path in air such that water in the saltwater evaporates and a collection pit positioned under the path and configured to collect the salt from the saltwater after the water has evaporated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 is a schematic view showing a flow rate control apparatus of a non dynamic flow rate control system according to the present invention a rectangular outer frame 6 which is seated on an upper part of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 and opens front and rear to open the lower part to block odors and to guide sewage and a flow control device 5 detachably mounted on the inner side of the outer frame 6 to control the amount of inflow of sewage and stormwater to flow out to the sewage water collection pipe 2 the flow control device 5 includes an inner frame 10 detachably attached to the outer frame by a drawer a plate shaped rotary plate member 20 having a center shaft 21 at the lower end of the inner frame 10 and rotating up and down to guide the sewage contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream while controlling the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater wow the water flow control device 5 includes a water flow rotary shaft 31 rotatably mounted on the inside of the flow control device 5 and is fixed to the water flow rotary shaft 31 so as to be in close contact with both inner side walls of the flow control device 5 30 of a wall like shape opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 21 of the rotary plate member 20 so that the rotary plate member 20 is rotated in the non and a link portion 40 the outer frame 6 is seated at the distal end of the sewage pipe and an inner frame 10 is detachably attached to the inner side of the outer frame 6 by a drawer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200430484-Y1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "it is introduced by itself while maintaining the same water quality and the same water temperature at the time of intake and at the same time prevents the contamination of the groundwater system and simultaneously withdraws and pumps the water automatically"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "specific embodiments relate to directing a fluid stream through an outlet at an outer surface of the pipeline to cause a vibration in the pipeline which simulates a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a third aspect provides a system for simulating a leak in a pipeline the system comprising a pipeline a fluid supply operable to generate a fluid stream an inlet in fluid communication with the fluid supply so as to receive the fluid stream therefrom a control valve having a valve input a valve output and a control port the valve input being in fluid communication with the inlet so as to receive the fluid stream therefrom the control valve being operable to selectively permit or prevent communication of the fluid stream from the valve input to the valve output based on a control signal received at the control port a controller communicatively coupled to the control port and operable to provide the control signal to the control port an outlet in fluid communication with the valve output the outlet being fixed to the pipeline such that when the control valve permits communication of the fluid stream from the valve input to the valve output the fluid stream is output onto an outer surface of the pipeline such that a vibration is caused in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the thermal change in the pipeline 4 generated by directing a fluid stream onto the pipeline 4 can be used to simulate the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline 4"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_65", "text": "in an embodiment therefore the system 2 can be used to selectively direct a fluid stream at the outer surface of the pipeline 4 to cause a vibration and or a thermal change in the pipeline 4 which mimics the vibration and or the thermal change produced by a leak in the pipeline 4"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "in this way an alarm signal can be generated if the method is malfunctioning such that an operator believes that a fluid stream is incident on the pipeline when in fact it is not for example due to a malfunction of some equipment such as the fluid supply"}, {"pat_id": "US-9005310-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in another embodiment the disclosure includes a production saltwater disposal facility comprising a separator configured to receive production saltwater from a pipeline or a vehicle and separate hydrocarbons from the production saltwater wherein the production saltwater received from the pipeline or vehicle is substantially the same composition as when the production saltwater was located in a subterranean formation a hydrocarbon storage tank configured to receive hydrocarbons from the separator a settling pit configured to receive the production saltwater from the separator and separate metals and or other solids from the saltwater an evaporator in fluid communication with the settling pit and comprising a nozzle configured to emit a stream of the saltwater along a path in air such that water in the saltwater evaporates and a collection pit positioned under the path and configured to collect the salt from the saltwater after the water has evaporated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200402435-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "however since the discharge point of the contaminated sewage cannot be accurately identified the tracer is analyzed and traced back by analyzing the contaminant component of the sewage discharged into the stream.therefore the main purpose of the present invention is to identify the cause of inflow of contaminated sewage or wastewater in the pipeline and to identify the location of the contaminated sewage or wastewater in the pipeline and to identify the cause of the inflow of contaminated sewage and to take prompt action"}, {"pat_id": "US-4823826-A", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "stinger 4 is in sealing relationship with elbow 20 to prevent leakage of water from pipeline 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "economic losses to construct sewage terminal treatment plant can be saved.the stream runoff procurement apparatus and method thereof according to the present invention always allow a certain amount of streams to flow through the river to survive the ecosystem of the stream and furthermore the contamination of the pipeline is prevented in advance so that the groundwater due to the corrosion and breakage of the sewer pipe is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "9 the front water gate 40 is rotated by the water pressure generated by the elevated water level and is interlocked with the angle adjuster 53 of the good interlocking portion 50 the link section 60 is interlocked and the rotating plate 30 is rotated to reduce the outflow cross section of the grating 20 to block the inflow of rainwater into the fine powder chamber 2 so that a large amount of rainwater naturally flows out into the discharge stream soils inherent in stormwater are also naturally released into the discharge stream thereby blocking the introduction of the soil from the storm sewer thereby preventing the sediment from accumulating on the sewer sewer pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173309-B1", "para_id": "para_238", "text": "the apparatus 580 further allows the water flows w1 and w2 to flow repeatedly in the circulation path formed by connecting the external annular flow path 585a to the suction side of the first pump 1p via the pipeline p"}, {"pat_id": "US-10156321-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "the method recognizes that impurities in the carbon dioxide stream change the phase behavior and fluid transport properties of the carbon dioxide effluent and that a variation of contaminant levels in the flow stream under an identical inlet pressure and temperature scenario may lead to the formation of two phase flow within the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101921821-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the entire amount of the sewage introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 is introduced into the sewage pipeline 2 at the end of the sewage pipeline 1 to be connected to the sewage pipeline 2 through the high 4 to the sewage water collection line 2 and discharges a large amount of rainwater flowing into the continuous rainwater to the river smoothly a rectangular outer frame 10 which is formed in a box shape to be seated on an upper portion of an excellent toilet 3 installed at a distal end of the sewage pipe 1 to block malodors and opens to the front and rear to guide sewage an inner frame 20 detachably attached to the inside of the outer frame 10 by a drawer a wall like opening closing gate 30 connected to the upper side of the inner frame 20 by a hinge portion 31 so as to be opened by water pressure when a large amount of storm is introduced the sewage water supply system according to the present invention is characterized in that the sewage water supply pipe 2 is connected to the opening closing water gate 30 40 the flow rate regulator 40 includes a center shaft 41a at the lower end of the inner frame 20 and is rotated upward and downward to adjust the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while guiding the soil contained in the stormwater to the discharge stream and the lower side is fastened to both ends of the rotary plate center shaft 41a of the rotary plate 41 so that the rotary plate 41 and a link portion 42 for rotating the link member in a non the upper portion of the link portion 42 is engaged with the first link pin 42a at the upper end of the upper side of the interchange gate 30 and the lower end of the link portion 42 is inserted when the interchange gate 30 is opened by inserting the second link pin 42b an upper link 42c for transmitting the rotational force to the lower link 42e and a sliding hole 42d having an elongated shape for sliding the second link pin 42b of the upper link 42c on the upper side and a lower link 42e whose lower side is coupled to both ends of the rotary plate central axis 41a of the rotary plate 41 and is coupled together with the upper link 42c so that the opening and closing gate 30 is opened and the rotating plate 41 is rotated in synchronization with the rotating force generated when the rotating plate 41 is rotated"}]</data>
</edge>
