  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the sewage inflow prevention apparatus according to any one of claims 1 to 3 wherein the sewage inflow prevention device comprises an inflow port formed in the upper end of the combined sewer pipe a main post having a columnar main post installed on the main frame a screen shaped grating installed at a rear side of the main frame to discharge sewage and stormwater to a sewerage pipe and to filter out foreign matter a rotating plate having a plate shaped central axis provided at an inner side of the main frame so as to be spaced apart from the grating and guided to the river while adjusting the inflow amount of sewage and stormwater while being rotated up and down and a plurality of vertical wall connecting portions connected to the inside of the vertical wall rotating shaft and rotated upward and downward and connected to a lower side of the vertical wall connecting portion a wall like openable and closable wall which is in close contact with a rubber pad seated in front of the main frame so as to block the water flowing backward when the water level of the discharge stream rises a link interlocking portion that is rotated by water pressure and operates the rotating plate in cooperation with the openable and closable flow wall in a non reciprocating manner when a large amount of storm is received by both ends of the flood wall rotary shaft and a lower link is connected to the central axis of the turntable so that the turntable is rotated only by interlocking of the link without any external power so as to control the flow rate of the inflow according to the opening and closing angle of the openable and closable flow wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a structure in which the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir frame 830 and white paper 88 are combined to block the inflow of polluted river water with a light specific gravity on top of the above mentioned green algae prevention eco friendly movable weir 8888 is formed a structure in which a shaped siphon action generating assembly partition 836 is sequentially fixed to the upper part of the eco friendly movable frame 830 for preventing the occurrence of green algae so as to preferentially discharge clean river water with a high specific gravity a structure in which the power generation water discharge pipe 3151 is constructed at an angle along the slope of the downstream part of the river starting from the lower part of the above mentioned eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth a structure in which an upward discharge pipe 3150 is formed in an l shape at a height that is 5 to 20 lower than the height of the lower part of the eco friendly movable dam 8888 for preventing green algae growth which is formed in the upstream part of the river at the end of the above mentioned power generation water discharge pipe 3151 a structure in which a terminal discharge pipe 3152 is formed in a t shape at the upper end of the above mentioned rising discharge pipe 3150 a structure in which an air exhaust unit 381 is formed at the upper end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a plurality of power generation water final pipes 262 each having a different thickness are connected around the end of the above mentioned end discharge pipe 3152 a structure in which a control unit 266 configured to control the discharge amount is connected to the upper part of the final power generation water pipe 262 a structure in which an upper storage tank 259 is connected to a lower discharge unit 256 configured in a different form with each storage capacity to store power generation water and discharge it to the lower part at the lower part of the above mentioned power generation water final pipeline 262 a structure in which a hydroelectric power generation unit 335 configured to generate electricity by hydraulic power is combined at the lower end of the above mentioned lower discharge unit 256 a nature friendly eco friendly method for naturally purifying polluted river water using an eco friendly movable dam for preventing green algae growth that is characterized by generating hydroelectric power by using an eco friendly movable dam that acts to prevent green algae growth"}, {"pat_id": "US-11098926-B2", "para_id": "para_564", "text": "here is also shown possible connection 369 to collect and transport runoff water that might not been treated properly to the pipeline 329 to prevent contamination of the northern section 204 and to be used in power plants 300 and subsequently to be used for replenishment of the depleting geothermal reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102100306-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the step of the server storing the sub zone information determined to be in need of maintenance in the database the step of receiving and saving the operation history information and and storing the simulation data in connection with the gis data collecting and analyzing measurement data by the server displaying by the server a simulation object rdii parameter and a flow graph using a toolbox the server constructing and calibrating a model for each small area the server further includes performing model verification and simulation evaluation the step of the server building a model for each of the small areas constructing a pipe network for model building and collecting attribute data estimating the input value of the pipeline model calculating a dwf dry weather flow model input value comprising the step of calculating the input value of the simulation object rdii model the step of the server to calibrate each sub area dwf dry weather flow model calibration step wwf wet weather flow model correction step for the selected rainfall event before the server collects and analyzes measurement data inquiring by the server information about an existing zone in a database to divide the small zone selecting by the server an object that is inadequate compared to the sub zone criterion as an object to be divided into sub zones when the division target area is selected the server establishes the boundary of the small area using the boundary of the back road the river and the railway or the boundary of the administrative area while conforming to the area standard determining by the server the compatibility with the sub region criteria by extracting the stored sub region information determining that the boundary condition is met when the server is determined to be suitable for a small area standard if the server determines that the boundary condition is met further comprising the step of storing the set and stored sub zone information as the new divided sub zone information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e ref