on the supplier side and injecting the washing medium into the conduit while applying pressure using the inlet pump s12 washing the inside of the pipe while passing the cleaning medium by increasing the pressure with the inlet pump inside the pipe s13 washing the inside of the water supply pipe with a washing medium and discharging washing discharged water discharged after washing through a discharge pipe formed in front of the water supply valve on the receiving side s14 a step of firstly and periodically transmitting the sensed water quality data to a controller by a water quality sensor installed at a rear end of the discharge pipe and sensing water quality data of discharged water flowing through the discharge pipe s15 determining whether or not the received first water quality data is equal to or less than a predetermined effluent water quality standard s16 in the case of the following the controller opens the solenoid valve installed in the discharge pipe to discharge the washing discharge water to the river s17 sensing the amount of discharged water discharged into the river by the flow sensor unit of the drained water discharge pipe installed at the rear end of the water quality sensor unit and transmitting the sensed discharged water quantity information to the controller s18 transmitting by the controller primary water quality data and discharged water flow rate information to a center server of a water quality management center s19 determining whether the received water quality data meets drinking water quality standards by a controller that periodically receives water quality data from the water quality sensor unit s20 if appropriate turning off the washing water inlet valve configured in the washing water inlet to stop the injection of the washing water and opening the water supply valve to supply tap water to the corresponding pipe s21 monitoring the secondary water quality data transmitted from the water quality sensor unit by the controller while discharging tap water supplied to the water supply pipe through the discharge pipe s22 and if the received water quality data meets the drinking water quality standards transmitting the water quality data to the manager smart terminal to block the discharge valve of the discharge pipe and open the water valve on the consumer side to supply tap water to the consumer s23"}, {"pat_id": "US-11280418-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in 1988 piper alpha platform fire accident killed 167 people and costed 3.4 billion because of removing the pump a s pressure safety valve in 1999 a pressure relief valve failed on a 16 inch gasoline pipeline operated by the olympic pipe line company in bellingham wash"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185543-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in other words it is necessary to develop a ubiquitous appeal management system that can monitor the quantity of water and water quality determined by various scattered water sources in real time and quickly observe analyze predict and predict urban river and ecological lake conditions.the present invention detects the quantity and quality of water inflow outflow pollutant inflow and pollutant source using inlet outflow using wide area water and monitors leakage and breakage by measuring the pressure of water pipeline to issue water quantity and water quality alarms it is to provide a ubiquitous based appeal management system that can remotely control the purification facility and analyze and predict the water balance for a long time and the water use index management method which is a dashin water usage guide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition due to excessive wear height and river water backflow the domestic sewer pipeline system is over planned in the upstream pipeline so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "in this way by continuously supplying river water to rivers a certain amount of running water always flows during the dry season so that the ecosystem of the river can survive and the urban environment is greatly improved and in terms of sewer pipes as the solids content and chemical oxygen demand are lowered corrosion and breakage of pipelines can be prevented in advance and through this groundwater contamination due to leakage of contaminated water air pollution due to odor and miniaturized sewage treatment plant can be miniaturized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "economic losses to construct sewage terminal treatment plant can be saved.the stream runoff procurement apparatus and method thereof according to the present invention always allow a certain amount of streams to flow through the river to survive the ecosystem of the stream and furthermore the contamination of the pipeline is prevented in advance so that the groundwater due to the corrosion and breakage of the sewer pipe is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "US-10859212-B2", "para_id": "para_149", "text": "thus these transfer functions are affected by physical changes in the pipeline 204 due to dents corrosion fluid density fluid flow rate fluid pressure within the pipeline 204 material surrounding the pipeline 204 and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315306-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "corrosion of the pipelines leads to a reduction in the service life of the pipeline and a decrease in water supply capacity resulting in economic losses by increasing the load of the pump and also causing consumer complaints and complaints due to deterioration of water quality due to corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101506117-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "first the high initial initial rainfall that occurs at the time of sewage or rainfall inflowing into the city can be collected in the sewage subway pipeline through the sewage discharge section and the large amount of rainfall introduced into the large amount during rainfall is increased by the water pressure the opening of the sewage water discharge pipe is reduced by rotating the rotating plate by the linkage part and the link part linked with the open front water gate and the linkage part linked thereto to prevent the inflow of rainwater and soil to the sewage water supply pipe channel and discharging it to the discharge river it is possible to reduce the dredging cost by cutting off the earth and sand and it is possible to reduce the sewage treatment cost because it is possible to collect only the planned amount of sewage in the sewage subway pipeline as well as the breakage of the sewer pipeline and manhole due to the water pressure caused by the over can be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-12013155-B2", "para_id": "para_585", "text": "here is also shown possible connection 369 to collect and transport runoff water that might not be treated properly to the pipeline 329 to prevent contamination of the northern section 204 and to be used in power plants 300 and subsequently to be used for replenishment of the depleting geothermal reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200285740-Y1", "para_id": "para_37", "text": "therefore in order to prevent obstruction by fine suspended matter and environmental microorganisms the lower sludge discharge facility 24 is installed at the lower part of the gravel contact oxidation facility 11 and the charcoal biofilm filtration tank 13 and is excessive by the diffuser 21 device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101658740-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore in order to solve this problem a method for repairing the excavated ground or repairing the damaged conduit large sewer pipes for sending a large amount of sewage discharged from densely populated areas to the sewage treatment plant for example sewage pipes around the han river constructed in the 1980s have a cross section of 2.8 x 2.8 m in width and a certain section of the sewer pipe it is very dangerous for a person to perform maintenance work simply by