  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101283731-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it is connected to the dredging suction hose 2 to dredge the accumulated sediment in the pipeline through the manhole 3 and the hydraulic hose 4 that the hydraulic pressure for the operation of the cylinder flows in and out of the rear in the dredging robot 10 is provided with a cable 6 is connected to the control unit 5 so as to transmit and receive the dredging operation to the server in real time a rectangular frame 100 which is provided with a driving device inside and is moved back and forth caterpillar shaped transfer wheels 200 which are connected to both sides of the frame 100 to transfer the dredging robot 10 back and forth a bucket part 300 connected to the front surface of the frame 100 and moved up down left right and back and dredging the deposit to discharge the dredging suction hose 2 a plurality of pipe support members 400 installed on both sides of the frame 100 and foldable so as to be in close contact with side surfaces of the pipe line 1 so as not to flow when moving back and forth and left and right a monitoring device 500 installed at an upper portion of the frame 100 to check a state and a working condition of the pipeline 1 bucket type pipeline dredge robot characterized in that consisting of pocket portion 700 for receiving the deposits of solids dredged in the bucket portion 300 in the rear of the frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100739858-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "that is the repair method according to the present invention basically relates to a non excavation pipeline repair method and is configured by the step of removing foreign substances by spraying pressurized water and the step of placing concrete by spraying thereby towing insertion and pneumatic pressure as described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181549-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "the method according to claim 4 or 5 each of the first raw water supply module the second raw water supply module and the third raw water supply module an oil pressure measuring unit installed in the supply pipeline to measure oil pressure of raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder a flow rate control valve installed in the supply pipeline to regulate a flow rate of raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder a bypass pipeline branching from the supply pipeline and bypassing the raw water supplied to the filtration membrane holder to the storage tank a bypass valve installed in the bypass pipeline to adjust a flow rate of raw water bypassed to the storage tank the pollution index predictor is configured to determine the hydraulic pressure of the raw water supplied to each of the filter membrane holders based on the hydraulic pressure measured by the hydraulic pressure measuring unit of each of the first raw water supply module the second raw water supply module and the third raw water supply module"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200193162-Y1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "by reducing the amount of water used to minimize the risk of rupture of the soft tube caused by the weight of the water and at the same time to increase the heat curing rate to provide a flexible tube reversal insertion device that can be easier and more efficient construction the purpose is to"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "attached to the lower end of the valve housing 41 the reducing portion 31 is integrally attached to the support groove 44 formed in the lower inner surface of the disk guide 42 facing the elastic member support plate 45 while being fitted the disc valve 46 is installed at the upper portion of the elastic member support plate 45 to open and close the water passage 41a of the valve housing 41 while selectively moving up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "64 a disk valve 66 for opening and closing the water passage 61a of the valve housing 61 is selectively installed while moving up and down and is elastic between the disk valve 66 and the elastic member support frame 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "analog to digital converter for converting to a digital signal a microcontroller for receiving the output value of the analog to digital converter in a pin to pin pin to pin method and corrected by an algorithm and output the output signal of the microcontroller in a serial method a sensor unit comprising a plurality of measuring devices including a hydraulic pressure measuring device including a communication unit which transmits to a field collecting device of a water supply pipe management system but transmits accurate data through a parity bit check for checking crc errors a plurality of field collecting devices collecting data provided from a plurality of measuring devices forming the sensor unit a data collection device collecting data through the plurality of field collection devices a water supply pipe network gis geographic information system device that organizes and manages geographic and facility data such as pipe codes installation blocks pipe diameters pipe types buried years pipe ages joint methods and coordinates of water pipes pipeline code date of report start of construction completion of construction whether to dismantle closure depth water pressure leakage surface leakage amount leakage area leakage classification cause of damage damage type construction subsidy measures an accident management device that stores and manages data related to the water supply pipe such as contents accident route photos and personnel opinions a weight extraction device that receives the factors necessary for weight calculation from the water supply network gis device and the accident management device and calculates the weight for each factor through the opinion of an expert integrate and organize the data received from the water supply network gis device and the incident management device by block and factor and unify the limit value and the comparison unit so that the strength of data can be compared and then determine the search order of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101257647-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "water supply pipe network integrity evaluation system using the hydraulic pressure measurement information according to the present invention for achieving these objects comprises a sensor unit comprising a plurality of measuring devices including the hydraulic pressure measurement device according to the present invention a plurality of field collecting devices collecting data provided from a plurality of measuring devices forming the sensor unit a data collection device collecting data through the plurality of field collection devices a water supply pipe network gis geographic information system device that organizes and manages geographic and facility data such as pipe codes installation blocks pipe diameters pipe types buried years pipe ages joint methods and coordinates of water pipes pipeline code date of report start of construction completion of construction whether to dismantle closure depth water pressure leakage surface leakage amount leakage area leakage classification cause of damage damage type construction subsidy measures an accident management device that stores and manages data related to water supply pipes such as contents accident pipeline photos and personnel opinions a weight extraction device that receives the factors necessary for weight calculation in the water supply network gis device and the accident management device and calculates a weight for each factor through opinion of an expert integrate and organize the data received from the water supply network gis device and the incident management device by block and factor and unify the limit value and the comparison unit so that the strength of data can be compared and then determine the search order of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101164867-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the variable tube 140 is sag due to its own weight and hydraulic pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100971995-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "one of the measures to reduce the flow and prevent leakage is to adjust the hydraulic pressure in the pipeline and the minimum flow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306445-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the pipeline expansion device 1 includes an expander 11 for reshaping the deformation of the pipeline a a hydraulic electric pump 12 for generating hydraulic pressure to supply the expander 11 it is composed of a hydraulic line 13 for supplying the hydraulic pressure to the expander 11 and the hydraulic pressure is recovered to the hydraulic electric pump 12 the pipeline image photographing apparatus 2 includes a cctv camera 21 for inspecting the state inside the pipeline a and monitoring the rehabilitation work with the expander 11 it is composed of a rotating device unit 22 having a circumferential rotation device 221 to enable the cctv camera 21 to rotate in the circumferential direction and a vertical rotation device 222 to enable angle adjustment up and down"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101206997-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "making a step installing fixed tube guide means each having a predetermined shape at an inlet of the manhole and an inlet of the conduit installing a movable traction force attenuator for reducing the traction force of the traction winch between the front fixing portion of the first flexible tube and the wire of the traction winch towing the first flexible tube mounted on the flexible tube feeder equipped with the freezing facility in the state where the curable resin is impregnated into the predetermined section of the pipeline to be rehabilitated through the manhole using a towing winch inverting injecting the resin impregnated second flexible tube inside the first flexible tube pulled into the conduit using hydraulic pressure or air pressure to cause the resin impregnated portions of the first and second flexible tubes to adhere to each other by inverting the second flexible tube a heat source is supplied to the first and second flexible tubes having a state in which the second flexible tube is in close contact with the inner wall of the pipeline to harden and integrate the resin impregnated in the first and second flexible tubes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101185420-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10 0816410 registered on march 18 2008 more specifically the manhole is made of a cylindrical one of the manhole the present invention relates to a water conduit inspection device which can prevent stress concentration from occurring in a portion and that lifting shafts are disposed at both side ends of the opening closing partition to prevent the lifting shafts from being deformed by hydraulic pressure"}]</data>
