e top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101137443-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sedimentation basin 100 installed at the bottom of the rain pipe 500 to remove solids and contaminants contained in the initial excellent water a sludge storage tank 120 located at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100 and collecting and storing the sludge of the sedimentation basin 100 and the filter paper 200 a rectifying wall 210 configured to stabilize the fluid flow of the treated water of the sedimentation basin 100 and flow to the filter paper 200 a filter paper 200 connected to the rectifying wall 210 and provided with a plurality of package type filtering devices 220 an upper cover 400 installed at an upper portion of the filter paper 200 and bypassing the existing rainwater pipe when the initial excellent water flow rate exceeds a designed capacity a maintenance door 410 installed in the upper cover 400 for maintaining and replacing the package type filtration device 220 in the filter paper 200 the treated water of the filter paper 200 is composed of a backflow prevention door 300 is installed to prevent the discharge and backflow into the existing storm pipe the sedimentation basin 100 forms a stepped aeration passage 110 in order to increase the removal efficiency of the non point pollutants contained in the initial rain at the inlet to the initial rainfall and the sedimentation basin 100 at the bottom of the sedimentation basin 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869052-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an adhesive tape 110 in close contact with an outer surface of a pipe material buried underground such as a water supply pipe a sewage pipe or an rain pipe sensing lines 120 formed on the outer surface of the adhesive tape at regular intervals so as to receive power from the outside in the electronic tag so as to detect leaks and damages and check the pipe positions a removable tape 130 formed on an outer surface of the sensing line a good adhesion treatment layer 140 formed on an outer surface of the detachable tape and for adhesion upon application of a material for protecting the tape consisting of the protective layer 150 formed on the outer surface of the adhesion layer in the sensing pipe that can easily detect the leakage and damage of the piping material using the detection tape 100 and the position of the pipe the sensing tape 100 is composed of a finishing layer 220 to finish the outer surface with a coating the sensing line of the sensing tape 100 is composed of four strands and a separate set of two strands of the four strands is connected to the electronic tag attached to the pipe connection for the exploration of the pipeline from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869052-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "the present invention to achieve the above object an adhesive tape 110 in close contact with an outer surface of a pipe material buried underground such as a water supply pipe a sewage pipe or an rain pipe sensing lines 120 formed on the outer surface of the adhesive tape at regular intervals so as to receive power from the outside in the electronic tag so as to detect leaks and damages and check the pipe positions a removable tape 130 formed on an outer surface of the sensing line a good adhesion treatment layer 140 formed on an outer surface of the detachable tape and for adhesion upon application of a material for protecting the tape consisting of the protective layer 150 formed on the outer surface of the adhesion layer in the sensing pipe that can easily detect the leakage and damage of the piping material using the detection tape 100 and the position of the pipe the sensing tape 100 is composed of a finishing layer 220 to finish the outer surface with a coating the sensing line of the sensing tape 100 is composed of four strands and a separate set of two strands of the four strands is connected to the electronic tag attached to the pipe connection for the exploration of the pipeline from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-9097390-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "in another aspect an embodiment of the invention provides a winery storm water protection system the system comprising an encapsulating capsule disposed under a crush pad of a winery the encapsulating capsule comprising an interior isolation chamber a valve assembly disposed within the isolation chamber of the encapsulating capsule the valve assembly comprising a valve body having a fluid passage including a upstream port and a downstream port and a valve member located within the valve body wherein the valve member is configured to move between an open position to allow fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and a closed position to block fluid flow between the upstream port and the downstream port and an electric actuator assembly operatively coupled to the valve member for opening or closing the valve member when actuated an upstream pipeline extending through a first opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the upstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the upstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery a downstream pipeline extending through a second opening in the circumscribing sidewall of the encapsulating capsule the downstream pipeline having a first end operatively coupled to the downstream port of the fluid passage of the valve body and a second end operatively coupled to and in open fluid communication with a holding tank a rain sensor a programmable logic controller operatively coupled to the electric actuator assembly and the rain sensor the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in response to receiving a rain sensed signal from the rain sensor to actuate the closing of the valve member from a default open position for closing fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly disposed in and under the crush pad of the winery and the holding tank while simultaneously opening fluid communication between the crush pad drain assembly and a storm drain system or waterway and the programmable logic controller being configured to provide a control signal to the electric actuator assembly in order to massage the valve member by opening and closing the valve member after a predefined period of time in which a rain sensed signal has not been received to keep the valve member free of binding or clear of debris build up"}, {"pat_id": "US-4997312-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when backup water pressure builds up the back flow preventing valve is closed or closes to prevent the water in the sanitary sewer line from backing up into the user s home"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when backup water pressure builds up the back flow preventing valve is closed or closes to prevent the water in the sanitary sewer line from backing up into the user s home"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a structure that is coupled to a conveyance belt for conveying contaminants to the outside on the rear side of the lifting bar the underwater pump connected to the conveyor belt constitutes a submerged pump at the lower end of the purifier box to remove the particulate contaminants remaining in the inside of the lifting jacket when lifting the particulate contaminants floating on the upper end of the booster box a pipeline coupled with the submersible pump an underwater pump for completely removing fine contaminants introduced into the purifier box by using a water injection nozzle formed at an end of a pipe connected to the pipeline and a discharge control valve coupled to a discharge control valve for controlling discharge of light organic matter molecules floating at the upper end of the purifier box at a downstream portion of the purifier box the process of cleansing polluted river water or contaminated rainwater using a river water or rain water purification system configured to purify polluted river water and contaminated rainwater by separate discharge is characterized in that the multifunctional water gate configured to store the river water to store river water or rainwater and to open the inflow adjusting gate constructed in the purifying box to inflow river water or rainwater into the inside of the purifying box and the air discharge pipe connected to the air pump continuously blows air into the purifying box to flood the contaminant molecules having a low specific gravity contained in the river water or rainwater flowing into the purifying box into the upper part of the purifying box and the large size lifting rake constructed in the damper is continuously rotated to remove large sized obstacles and small sized contaminants contained in the river water or rainwater and at the same time the lifting barrel coupled with the conveyor belt is continuously rotated thereby removing organic material contaminants which are light in weight on the upper part of the polluted river water or rainwater from the outside of the purifier box and at the same time continuously operating the submerged pump and the injection nozzle to completely remove the remaining particulate organic matter to remove through a point source and nonpoint source pollution river water and rainwater various waste and contaminants that are fully processed or stored in clean constant and non point sources of pollution generated in the processing system contained in the"}]</data>
