  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water level measuring device 400 periodically sends a measurement signal to acquire the water level information a pseudo accident process mode execution unit 725 for sending a closing signal to the water gate switch 650 for the sewage connection and controlling the water gate 600 for the sewage connection pipe to close when the information is received information on the occurrence of rainfall by the rainfall sensor is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "para_72", "text": "therefore non point pollution is reduced by using an accessory manhole and an rtu the accidental runoff water is supplied to the sewage pipe without being sent to the river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11098926-B2", "para_id": "para_564", "text": "here is also shown possible connection 369 to collect and transport runoff water that might not been treated properly to the pipeline 329 to prevent contamination of the northern section 204 and to be used in power plants 300 and subsequently to be used for replenishment of the depleting geothermal reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "US-8221029-B2", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "conduit 24 may be constructed of pvc but other materials can be used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101674110-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "it will be understood by those skilled in the art that various changes and modifications may be made without departing from the scope of the present invention.1 rainwater catcher 2 3 by drain pipe 4 infiltration ball 10 penetration ditch 10a infiltration ditch inflow section 11 perforated fan for flow equalization 12 shovel rake 12a contamination 13 flooding bumps 14 drainage filter fiber 15 observation 15a 15b plug 20 pretreatment tank 20a pretreatment tank inflow section 21 sand pack 22 stagnant water outlet 30 runoff water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10941535-B2", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "the above uses for the stormwater runoff and erosion control devices of the present disclosure are not intended to be limiting but are just examples of the multitude of ways in which storm water control carpets or blankets wattles also called dimensional tubes and compact drainage filters according to the present disclosure may be used in combination with retaining walls bioswales concrete barriers gross solids removal devices gsrds filtering vaults gabions drainage inlet filters and other best management practices to prevent erosion and minimize contamination of watersheds due to stormwater runoff"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399293-B1", "para_id": "para_59", "text": "economic losses to construct sewage terminal treatment plant can be saved.the stream runoff procurement apparatus and method thereof according to the present invention always allow a certain amount of streams to flow through the river to survive the ecosystem of the stream and furthermore the contamination of the pipeline is prevented in advance so that the groundwater due to the corrosion and breakage of the sewer pipe is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102373416-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "buffer storage facility control device and its control methodthe present invention relates to a buffer storage facility control device and more particularly it has a function to block direct inflow of accidental runoff water into a buffer storage facility and to reduce non point pollution during precipitation and link them with the sluice gate of the buffer storage facility according to the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "US-12013155-B2", "para_id": "para_585", "text": "here is also shown possible connection 369 to collect and transport runoff water that might not be treated properly to the pipeline 329 to prevent contamination of the northern section 204 and to be used in power plants 300 and subsequently to be used for replenishment of the depleting geothermal reservoirs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101450430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "1 to 3 rainfall runoff on roads and other road surfaces is introduced into an existing waterway through an induction waterway and a separate flow distribution structure a pretreatment tank and various abatement facilities are installed in the existing waterway it can be seen that the initial effluent is introduced into the abatement facility and the rainwater effluent from which the non point pollutant is removed through the abatement facility is reintroduced into the existing canal thereby removing the nonpoint contamination of the initial effluent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416507-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as described above the rainfall runoff treated by the action of the soil filter bed layer 50 and the plant 80 is collected into the hole drainage pipe 30 through the hole of the hole drainage pipe 30 and is transferred to the public water and the hole drainage pipe the treated rainfall runoff that did not penetrate 30 penetrates into the existing soil through the soil membrane 70 at the bottom of the soil media layer 50 thereby preventing contamination of public waters and groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300414-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "in addition it is equipped with an inlet line for introducing raw water and an external carbon source into the anoxic tank and by automatically adjusting the inflow of raw water and external carbon source the denitrification efficiency of the anaerobic tank can be improved operating costs can be reduced and the amount of external carbon source can be reduced this can be reduced to prevent further contamination by runoff"}]</data>
</edge>
