  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition due to excessive wear height and river water backflow the domestic sewer pipeline system is over planned in the upstream pipeline so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102444336-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "a solid separator 232 and a solid separator 232 a first processing unit 230 including an oil water separator 234 and a solids separator 232 formed under the enclosing hollow shape to separate outflow water and oil components and a sedimentation tank 238 for storing solids a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation storage tank 410 in which contaminants included in the effluent are precipitated is formed and fine pollutants and effluent are purified a second processing unit 240 provided with a microfiltration wall 440 to a cartridge porous filter 282 in which a third inlet hole 206 into which the effluent treated by the second processing unit 240 is introduced is formed and a plurality of refinery holes 510 are formed on the outer periphery to finally purify the effluent the inlet and outlet member 284 provided in the cartridge porous filter 282 and having a plurality of inlet and outlet holes 520 on the outer periphery the cartridge porous filter 282 and the inlet member 284 are fixed to a fixing part 288 and a third processing unit 250 including a filter support member 286 connected to the fixing unit 288 a storage tank 280 for storing effluent treated with non point pollutants by the third processing unit 250 and a drainage system in which a discharge line 260 is formed to discharge the effluent treated with non point pollutants and an effluent pipe 214 through which the effluent is waterproofed is formed on one side of the storage tank 280"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in addition due to excessive wear height and river water backflow the domestic sewer pipeline system is over planned in the upstream pipeline so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "rainfall conduit installed at least one or more monthly wear inherently so that rainwater flows from the predetermined watershed in rainy weather is separated into the initial rainfall and the continuous runoff a connection pipe connected to the rainwater conduit so that the initial rainwater flows in and a screen for filtering the suspended solids contained in the initial rainwater and filtering rainwater when rainwater exceeding an allowable capacity flows through the connection pipe"}]</data>
