  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200359694-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a second modular wetland infrastructure that physically filters influent through vegetation based modules a sedimentation tank installed at one side of the lower end of the modular wetland infrastructure to collect influent water that has passed through the modular wetland infrastructure and to precipitate foreign substances that are not filtered a contact oxidation tank installed at the bottom of the modular wetland infrastructure and having a modular microbial contact material installed to biologically purify water introduced from the settling tank combined with the modular wetland infrastructure and modular catalytic oxidation and filtration equipment including and the filtration tank connected to the contact oxidation tank and finally removes the fine sludge and suspended matter not filtered through the filter medium installed therein one river lake or runoff clarifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "an influent distribution step of reducing the energy of river water lake water or effluent flowing into the water purification apparatus through a flow distribution tank and evenly distributing it to the modular wetland infrastructure a primary purification step in which the influent distributed to the modular wetland infrastructure is decomposed adsorbed and settled by the microorganisms of the wetland plants and wetlands planted in adjacent vegetation based modules a secondary purification step in which the inflow water is physically filtered while passing through the vegetation based module arranged adjacent to the modular wetland infrastructure a drainage storage step in which the inflow water passing through the modular wetland infrastructure flows into the sedimentation tank through the drainage layer installed while forming a predetermined space a precipitation step of precipitating unfiltered foreign matter while undergoing primary and secondary purification treatments included in the influent stored in the precipitation tank a third purification step of biologically purifying the inflow water having passed through the precipitation step into the contact oxidation tank having the microbial contact material installed therein river water that combines modular wetland infrastructure and modular catalytic oxidation and filtration facilities including a 4th purification step that finally removes fine sludge and suspended solids that were not filtered through the contact oxidation tank through a filter tank equipped with filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the artificial wetland consisting of inflow culvert wetland space and outflow culvert the rainfall outflow and normal base flow from the inflow culvert into the inflow water is treated and then discharged to the outflow culvert a first connection between the inlet culvert and a wetland space such that an inflow consisting of a normal base flow including nitrogen and organic substances and a portion of the rainfall runoff of a design rainfall output wqv flows into the wetland space from the inlet culvert wetland intake channel deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100944122-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in order to achieve the above object the artificial wetland which can simultaneously process the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow of the present invention consists of an inflow culvert a wetland space and an outflow culvert the rainfall runoff and the normal base flow from the inflow culvert in the artificial wetland discharged and discharged to the effluent effluent after discharge into the effluent effluent the inflow water consisting of the normal base flow and the rainfall rainfall part of the design rainfall output wqv including nitrogen and organic matter from the inlet culvert a first wetland intake channel connected between the inlet culvert and a wetland space to be introduced into the wetland space deep in water to remove nitrogen and organic substances by oxidizing inflow water composed of normal inflow water and partial rainfall runoff of wqv which is introduced through the first wetland intake channel in the wetland space by phytoplankton"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "for example when rainfall continues for more than 1 hour and river flooding is expected a movable dam can be installed in the river and when the movable dam is covered all the holes or valves flowing into or out of the facility are automatically blocked thereby protecting the facility"}]</data>
</edge>
