  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100877621-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the problems of the prior art as described above the problem to be solved by the present invention but before the introduction into the screen tank of the wastewater treatment device to install a collecting basin to remove the contaminants and soils in advance the catchment is to provide an ozone oxidation type wastewater treatment device that is reinforced with a pretreatment process to be treated regardless of the amount of wastewater including rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100877621-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the cover of the sump is characterized in that formed of a transparent body that can identify the inside of the tank.according to the ozone oxidation type wastewater treatment device which strengthens the pretreatment process of the present invention the pretreatment can be treated irrespective of the amount of wastewater including rainwater in which a collecting basin which removes contaminants and soils in the pretreatment stage before entering the screen tank is treated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468245-Y1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the collecting basin 20 to block backflow and the collecting basin for dividing and filtering the soil sand and cigarette butts and rubbish mixed with rainwater or sewage so as to maintain a predetermined distance from the bottom and the side of the inside of the sump 20 in the rain gutter drain provided with 30 the sump 20 is of the upper and lower strait shape having a seating jaw 22b formed at the top edge of the entrance 22a to hang inside the manhole 10 via the support frame 42 of the manhole cover 40"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4334422-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "and the upper edge of the mud reservoir 5 inserted in the mud reservoir 4 is locked by the locking protrusion 16 of the anti lifting ring 15 to prevent the mud reservoir 5 from floating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100375130-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if blocked in this way the sewage or rainwater that flowed into the initial settling basin on the main wall of the body generated and discharged to an appropriate amount only holes the majority of the right sewage is one making it possible to prevent the closed end which is has excellent sewage treatment plant hameuroseo be leaked to solid stream through a solid to a discharge formed in an upper initial settling tank inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100957464-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "therefore the lower end of the odor prevention unit is also mounted to both sides left and right around the center line.odor prevention and dirt collection device for rain gutter collection basin of the present invention performs the function of a dirt collection device to prevent impurities from flowing into the flow pipe and odor to prevent the odor inside the rain gutter collection basin to leak outside not only does it perform the function of prevention but it also fulfills the first purpose of the rainwater collecting basin without clogging by collecting impurities through a large outflow hole formed in the upper part of the collecting network when an excessive amount of impurities and dirt are instantaneously introduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it receives the rainwater flowing through the paving layer once delivered to the screening means the water leakage pipe characterized in that it comprises a pit chamber 16 formed to be dug downward from the ground so that rainwater on the paving layer flows therein having basin soil low water increase"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "as mentioned above although this invention was demonstrated in detail through the specific example this invention is not limited to the said example a various deformation transformation is possible for a person with ordinary knowledge within the scope of the technical idea of this invention.the basin soil low water increasing device having a leaky pipe of the present invention made as described above by introducing the rainwater flowing into the ground due to the impermeable pavement layer into the ground to supply to the soil layer to allow the soil to receive abundant water as a whole it is advantageous for water resource management and even in cities with high land covering rate underground soil is not dried and rich in groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in vegetation reservoirs for preventing pollution and creating a healthy urban environment a reservoir for storing rainfall runoff on the surface of the ground a vegetation filtration reservoir located at a lower portion of the reservoir and having a height of 25 to 60 cm including humus soil and sand at least one es filtration layer located below the vegetation filtration reservoir a collecting part located below the es filtration layer and having a storage part including a first gravel layer and a second gravel layer and a permeate part disposed in a lower part of the storage part and including a third gravel layer and a sand layer a pouring pipe disposed in the infiltration portion and being buried in the pouring portion to collect rainwater flowing out from the pouring portion an outlet pipe connected to the pipe a drain pipe provided in the vegetation filtration reservoir and a water pipe for collecting the water collected in the pipe pipe upward a bypass pipe connected to the drain port for bypassing the rainwater flowing out of the storage compartment of the storage compartment a second accommodating portion having a first accommodating portion having an inflow port into which the rainwater effluent flows an outlet provided with a screen for removing foreign matter in the rainwater inflow water flowing from the first accommodating portion and a vertical partition wall arranged so as to be communicated with each other an es expanded shale filter medium is disposed at a boundary between the vegetation filtration reservoir and the original soil and a bottom surface of the bottom of the water outlet is at least 30 cm away from the bottom of the bottom of the water outlet the vegetation filtration reservoir includes fly ash within 5 of the volume of the vegetation filtration reservoir wherein an aerobic condition layer is formed on the upper part of the basin of the drain hole and an anaerobic anaerobic condition layer is formed on the lower part of the basin of the drain hole to prevent pollution and to provide a healthy urban environment"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the virtual pump well model is a model for reflecting the phenomenon that the water level of the river suddenly rises due to the operation of the pump in the water level prediction of the river and is a storage tank that stores rainwater that falls in the river basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however this type of catchment can cause an unpleasant odor generated from the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to leak out into the atmosphere due to a malfunction of the valve member provided between the catchment and the sewer pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5378872-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus conventionally as a drainage device that is attached to a water collecting tank in a side groove and prevents the release of odors mosquitoes etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5643908-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "15 the inside of the main body 41 and the bottom of the drainage drain 40 b a on the first outlet 53 side of the main body 41 is prevented from getting over to prevent dirty water from flowing into the first outlet 53"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416507-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition through the pollutant source management method that installs pollutant treatment device near pollutant source such as impervious area it manages the whole basin equally and removes from the existing rainwater pipe end"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "description of the related art generally on a pavement road a drainage system is provided to prevent rainwater from being stored on the road surface during rainfall"}]</data>
