  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in addition in the case of dam type power plants it is often unavoidable to avoid significant head fluctuations due to imbalances between rainfall and water usage and such power plants are sometimes called variable head power plants"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7117022-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "it may also be implemented in a mixed format with a partial hardware module that implements a part of hardware elements.brief description of the drawings it is a block diagram which shows the inland water flooding analysis apparatus which concerns on embodiment 1 of this invention.fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-5232307-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "in the past the general belief was that erosion and degradation of alluvial channels occur because of increases in peak discharge caused by the upstream development"}]</data>
