  <data key="d6">["place", "contaminate", "treat", "rise", "connect", "introduce", "base", "accord", "remain", "achieve", "cause", "minimize", "have", "instal", "retain", "flow", "add", "face", "can", "relate", "twist", "provide", "mention", "title", "proceed", "prevent", "scale", "arrange", "form", "file", "pass", "occur", "couple", "figure", "do", "settle", "bury", "issue", "purify", "support", "illustrate", "collect", "become", "fall", "reflect", "call", "locate", "direct", "remove", "show", "reduce", "reservoir", "cross", "may", "hit", "discharge", "store", "cool", "dig", "collide", "include", "dispose", "perform", "exhibit", "enter", "react", "constitute", "supply", "use", "distort", "avoid", "characterize", "shape", "select", "damage", "be", "describe", "generate", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039115-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "that is in the above mentioned construction method since the water pipe is connected in a long direction in one direction and the supporting force against the lateral pressure is extremely weak the water pipe easily buckles or twists due to the slight ground settlement of the water pipe buried ground there is a problem in that leakage of foreign matter and foreign matter may be generated through the gap"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224234-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "as shown in figures 1 to 6 the present invention provides a settling basin 82 and the settling chamber 50 to prevent soil from entering the interior of the storage tank 30 while a certain distance to the small river 60 selected and collected sewage and initial excellent on the sewage 80 installed a number of sewage the sewage is directed directly to the sewage end treatment plant through the drainage house the initial excellent is buried in the sewage site 72 of the main stream 70 it collects in the old storage tank 30 and discharges it for a long time below the maximum treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant after rainy weather and prevents contamination of small rivers and mainstream streams 70 and adds sewage end treatment facilities"}, {"pat_id": "US-5863422-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "negative indirect effects of acidification include fish habitat degradation increase in concentrations of soluble toxic metals such as aluminum and changes in predator prey relationships"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in addition in the case of dam type power plants it is often unavoidable to avoid significant head fluctuations due to imbalances between rainfall and water usage and such power plants are sometimes called variable head power plants"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "2 illustrating the vertical limits of walls used to form the porosity reservoir where extraction wells may be strategically placed to minimize the impact of dead storage volumes along the bottom of the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "6 840 710 titled underground alluvial water storage reservoir and method filed on may 15 2002 and issued on jan"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "however in the case of the initial stormwater treatment system according to the present invention the initial stormwater is introduced into the secondary granulator 60 through the gypsum basin 50 and purified at the sewage treatment plant thereby preventing the contamination of the river as much as possible do"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an overflow weir that faces the riverbank a basin formed behind the overflow weir to temporarily store the river water that has crossed the overflow weir and reduce its flow velocity and a river water reservoir having a three dimensional space retaining skeleton block provided inside the riverbed to dig down the ground of the river bed to store the river water flowing through the pond and the river water reservoir a concrete speed reducing block for reducing the flow rate of the river water by hitting the river water against the side wall a plurality of the deceleration blocks are provided in one or more rows the deceleration block is a cylindrical body having a rectangular cross section and is disposed with one side faced to the side facing the river water reservoir and one side face facing the river water reservoir and one side face thereof on opposite sides openings for the river water that has passed over the overflow weir to flow into the river water reservoir are provided in a staggered arrangement and the river water flows into the reduction basin beyond the overflow weir"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an overflow weir that faces the riverbank a basin formed behind the overflow weir to temporarily store the river water that has crossed the overflow weir and reduce its flow velocity and a river water reservoir having a three dimensional space retaining skeleton block provided inside the riverbed to dig down the ground of the river bed to store the river water flowing through the pond and the river water reservoir a concrete deceleration block provided between the pond and the river water to reduce the flow velocity of the river water by hitting the river water against the side wall and a plurality of the deceleration blocks are provided in one or more rows the deceleration block is a cylindrical body having a rectangular cross section and is arranged with one side faced to the side facing the river water reservoir and one side facing the river reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in order to further reduce the momentum of the water flowing into the river water reservoir 2 through the dewatering pond 7 a concrete speed reducing block 8 is installed between the river water reservoir 2 and the diversion reservoir 7"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "as a result the energy of the flowing water when colliding with the resin skeleton block 11 in the river water reservoir 2 is further reduced and the water storage space formed by the resin skeleton block 11 of the river water reservoir 2 is less likely to be damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100657177-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "that is in the above described construction method since the water supply pipe is long connected in one direction the bearing capacity for the transverse pressure is extremely weak and even if a slight ground subsidence of the water supply pipe is easily bent or twisted the breakage and gap of the water supply pipe may be generated"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the virtual pump well model is a model for reflecting the phenomenon that the water level of the river suddenly rises due to the operation of the pump in the water level prediction of the river and is a storage tank that stores rainwater that falls in the river basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the past rainfall data of the river basin and the operation history data of the pump are output to the water level prediction device 1 via the database interface 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200368757-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "that is in the above described construction method since the water supply pipe is connected long in one direction the bearing capacity for the transverse pressure is extremely weak and even a slight ground subsidence of the water supply pipe buried can easily cause the water pipe to be bent or distorted causing breakage and gaps"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "the second embodiment of the initial non point contamination excellent treatment system of the present invention is characterized in that it comprises an overflow collecting unit 100 which selectively supplies only the initial nonpoint contamination excellent due to the end of the conduit or the contaminated water a reservoir 200 for storing the initial non point contamination excellent provided to the water collection channel 130 of the water collection fixture 100 and performing a primary settlement of the contaminants a siphon channel 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the height of the highest part of the inverted u shape is higher than the height of the highest part of the inverted u shape a flow rate reducing manhole 300 for reducing the flow rate of the initial nonpoint contamination supplied from the siphon duct 295 and a second outlet pipe 320 for supplying the initial non a sedimentation paper 400 which is supplied through the first sedimentation unit and proceeds to second sedimentation and decomposition of contaminants and a drainage basin 500 located at the end of the sedimentation tank 400 and discharging the initial nonpoint contaminated soil from which contaminants have been removed to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802564-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "on the other hand the water treatment method using a chlorine based drug can achieve secondary color contamination such as formation of chromamine which is a carcinogenic substance by reacting with an organic substance in water when the treated water is discharged to the river it exhibits various problems such as destruction of the ecosystem due to fatal effects on various microorganisms in the agar basin due to the chlorine component remaining in the treated water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11225755-B2", "para_id": "para_101", "text": "blowdown 220 is removed from the basin 210 of the cooling tower to remove water as it becomes more concentrated in salt scaling minerals microbes and other chemicals and impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100751573-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "that is in the above described construction method since the water supply pipe is connected in one direction long and the bearing capacity for the transverse pressure is very weak even if the slight ground subsidence of the water supply pipe is easily bent or twisted some breakage and gap may occur"}]</data>
</edge>
