  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "in addition in the case of dam type power plants it is often unavoidable to avoid significant head fluctuations due to imbalances between rainfall and water usage and such power plants are sometimes called variable head power plants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in vegetation reservoirs for preventing pollution and creating a healthy urban environment a reservoir for storing rainfall runoff on the surface of the ground a vegetation filtration reservoir located at a lower portion of the reservoir and having a height of 25 to 60 cm including humus soil and sand at least one es filtration layer located below the vegetation filtration reservoir a collecting part located below the es filtration layer and having a storage part including a first gravel layer and a second gravel layer and a permeate part disposed in a lower part of the storage part and including a third gravel layer and a sand layer a pouring pipe disposed in the infiltration portion and being buried in the pouring portion to collect rainwater flowing out from the pouring portion an outlet pipe connected to the pipe a drain pipe provided in the vegetation filtration reservoir and a water pipe for collecting the water collected in the pipe pipe upward a bypass pipe connected to the drain port for bypassing the rainwater flowing out of the storage compartment of the storage compartment a second accommodating portion having a first accommodating portion having an inflow port into which the rainwater effluent flows an outlet provided with a screen for removing foreign matter in the rainwater inflow water flowing from the first accommodating portion and a vertical partition wall arranged so as to be communicated with each other an es expanded shale filter medium is disposed at a boundary between the vegetation filtration reservoir and the original soil and a bottom surface of the bottom of the water outlet is at least 30 cm away from the bottom of the bottom of the water outlet the vegetation filtration reservoir includes fly ash within 5 of the volume of the vegetation filtration reservoir wherein an aerobic condition layer is formed on the upper part of the basin of the drain hole and an anaerobic anaerobic condition layer is formed on the lower part of the basin of the drain hole to prevent pollution and to provide a healthy urban environment"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the past rainfall data of the river basin and the operation history data of the pump are output to the water level prediction device 1 via the database interface 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102261819-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the simulation and prediction unit uses turbidity and alkalinity as main factors during rainfall among the factors of the inflow flow rate of raw water hydrogen ion concentration turbidity alkalinity electrical conductivity and water temperature and hydrogen ion concentration and the mixed paper drug injection derivation unit 1310 that derives the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper with the water temperature as the main factor the raw water inflow of the flocculated paper and the settling basin the g value of the flocculated paper water temperature turbidity and the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper through the visualized interface image a flocculation paper settling cell sludge management unit 1320 that establishes a plan detects changes in the sludge interface through a sensor and corrects the sludge by checking the degree of agglomeration through light intensity detection and the number of loss head filtration duration and filtered water the filter paper management unit 1330 that establishes a plan for autonomous backwashing through turbidity information the advanced treatment management unit 1340 that performs accident and failure prediction through the status information of the ozone generating device and the maintenance of the water level of the purified water and optimum chlorine it is preferable to provide a purified water disinfection ability management unit 1350 for deriving the contact time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200368757-Y1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "that is in the above described construction method since the water supply pipe is connected long in one direction the bearing capacity for the transverse pressure is extremely weak and even a slight ground subsidence of the water supply pipe buried can easily cause the water pipe to be bent or distorted causing breakage and gaps"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416507-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in addition through the pollutant source management method that installs pollutant treatment device near pollutant source such as impervious area it manages the whole basin equally and removes from the existing rainwater pipe end"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "description of the related art generally on a pavement road a drainage system is provided to prevent rainwater from being stored on the road surface during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100751573-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "that is in the above described construction method since the water supply pipe is connected in one direction long and the bearing capacity for the transverse pressure is very weak even if the slight ground subsidence of the water supply pipe is easily bent or twisted some breakage and gap may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-910009261-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "the method of claim 12 wherein the rainfall prediction step includes receiving time series rainfall distribution data to calculate a center point where each set of rainfall overlaps checking whether the center point moves according to a predetermined rule and calculating the position of the center point before the predetermined time from the present by calculating the average value and the variance of the position of the center point in the past when moving according to the predetermined rule or when the center point moves without the predetermined rule the rainfall increase decrease rate acquisition step of acquiring the increase decrease rate of rainfall from the local mean of the region and the position where the latest rainfall distribution at the current calculation time does not fluctuate within a predetermined period and the latest rainfall distribution is limited by the calculated center point"}]</data>
</edge>
