  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "as a result contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102092239-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "generating a deep learning model using a first water level value and determining a pump operation value in a pressure field for a second water level value received in a subsequent cycle based on the abnormal time point based on the deep learning model it may include steps.according to the present invention when the communication state with the water level meter installed in the reservoir does not satisfy a predetermined level based on the deep learning model generated using the water level value previously received from the water level meter the pump operation value in the pressurization field is determined"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5479252-B2", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "and by arranging the discharge port 41 at the lower end of the drainage pipe 4 connected from the pumping pipe 3 via the separation tank 2 so as to be always submerged under the water surface in the sand basin the piping of the system during operation the equipment was watertight lifting pipe 3 separation tank 2 since the water inside the pipe conduit consisting of drainage tube 4 can be kept filled with the state can the principle of the siphon in pumping operation of the entire system it is sufficient if there is a head higher than the water level loss and the pressurized water pump 5 has an advantage that a pump with a low head and a small output is sufficient"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2678581-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "while checking the dryness of the surface layer and the soil moisture of vegetation adjust the water level effectively and effectively using the water level adjustment basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2678581-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "therefore the structure of the water level adjusting basin 9 includes a basin body 9a and a water level adjusting pipe portion 9b provided in the basin body"}, {"pat_id": "US-6869523-B2", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "optionally means can be provided to keep the barrier open whenever the water level in the basin rises above some reference level and there may be no adequate flow past the control to keep the barrier open"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4019893-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "a pipe shaped water level detection unit a pressure guiding pipe having one end connected to the water level detection unit a pressure air supply means for supplying a substantially constant air pressure to the water level detection unit via the pressure guiding tube and rotation of the pipe schema pressure switch that detects when the tip of the overflow section and the water level detection section which are one side of the opening is submerged under the water surface and detects the predetermined depth from the water surface of the settling basin when the air pressure in the pressure guiding tube reaches the predetermined pressure with the door to form the water level detection unit by a material having a low wear coefficient characterized in that bent downward such that the water surface substantially perpendicular to the tip portion of the water level detection part when entering the water surface water level detection device in the scum removing apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102168685-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "when external air is supplied due to a drop in the water level of the water filled in the sealed structure many pollutants in the atmosphere and foreign substances such as fallen leaves are blocked from entering the drainage through the ventilation port and on the contrary exhaust when the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in order to further reduce the momentum of the water flowing into the river water reservoir 2 through the dewatering pond 7 a concrete speed reducing block 8 is installed between the river water reservoir 2 and the diversion reservoir 7"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the virtual pump well model is a model for reflecting the phenomenon that the water level of the river suddenly rises due to the operation of the pump in the water level prediction of the river and is a storage tank that stores rainwater that falls in the river basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6690867-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "the past rainfall data of the river basin and the operation history data of the pump are output to the water level prediction device 1 via the database interface 100"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "at least one sensor device can expediently be provided in order to determine the degree of contamination of the retaining elements"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "a certain water level difference between the detected water levels in the basin chamber 5 and storage space 10 shows a reduced water flow between the basin chamber 5 and storage space 10 via the retaining element 8 whereby contamination of the retaining element 8 can be concluded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102261819-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the simulation and prediction unit uses turbidity and alkalinity as main factors during rainfall among the factors of the inflow flow rate of raw water hydrogen ion concentration turbidity alkalinity electrical conductivity and water temperature and hydrogen ion concentration and the mixed paper drug injection derivation unit 1310 that derives the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper with the water temperature as the main factor the raw water inflow of the flocculated paper and the settling basin the g value of the flocculated paper water temperature turbidity and the chemical injection amount of the mixed paper through the visualized interface image a flocculation paper settling cell sludge management unit 1320 that establishes a plan detects changes in the sludge interface through a sensor and corrects the sludge by checking the degree of agglomeration through light intensity detection and the number of loss head filtration duration and filtered water the filter paper management unit 1330 that establishes a plan for autonomous backwashing through turbidity information the advanced treatment management unit 1340 that performs accident and failure prediction through the status information of the ozone generating device and the maintenance of the water level of the purified water and optimum chlorine it is preferable to provide a purified water disinfection ability management unit 1350 for deriving the contact time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100888713-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the horizontal wear 22 is formed to correspond to the outlet of the settling basin 10 to flow in one direction of the settling basin 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100401380-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "therefore it is impossible that the shutoff of the vacuum valve is considerably delayed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a controller for controlling the water supply to be stored in the water storage tank while supplying water by opening the first on off valve and blocking the second on off valve at the same time"}]</data>
</edge>
