  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101039115-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "that is in the above mentioned construction method since the water pipe is connected in a long direction in one direction and the supporting force against the lateral pressure is extremely weak the water pipe easily buckles or twists due to the slight ground settlement of the water pipe buried ground there is a problem in that leakage of foreign matter and foreign matter may be generated through the gap"}, {"pat_id": "US-7491333-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "the flocculated process stream is then overflowed by gravity into a sedimentation basin the size of which is adequate to promote highly efficient separation of the liquid and solids phases in which suspended solids settle to the bottom of a significantly deeper excavated rectilinear lagoon with sloped sides"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100657177-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "that is in the above described construction method since the water supply pipe is long connected in one direction the bearing capacity for the transverse pressure is extremely weak and even if a slight ground subsidence of the water supply pipe is easily bent or twisted the breakage and gap of the water supply pipe may be generated"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "to limit contamination of the receiving flows and streams by untreated combined sewage the diverted flow may enter the receiving stream by direct overflow only when the soil percentage of the water to be discharged has been reduced to a level such that there is no further risk of appreciable contamination of the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-4076615-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "adjusting to the ph of the treated influent waste water stream to cause precipitation of the alum as aluminum hydroxide 3"}]</data>
</edge>
