  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101956785-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a sludge collecting unit for collecting the sludge settled on the bottom surface into a collecting hopper formed at one end of the bottom while being rotated by an endless track system and a secondary settler for discharging the collected water separated from the activated sludge through an outflow wear trough the induction water channel provided at the upper portion of the secondary clarifier so that the inflow water and the mlss flowing into the secondary clarifier are introduced in the same direction as the flow direction of the sludge of the sludge collector rectification means for supplying the lower portion of the induction water channel with the inflow water supplied from the induction waterway while lowering the drop energy of the mlss to the lower portion thereof a plurality of diffusion means formed in the lower portion of the rectifying means so as to evenly diffuse the mlss in which the dropping energy from the rectifying means is reduced into the secondary settler and the mlss diffused from the diffusion means passes through the diffusion means in front of the diffusion means the kinetic energy of the flow velocity of the mlss is reduced again by collision and the collision between the mlss and the mlss is induced again in the entire cross overlapping means overlapping at least two or more folds so as to have coherency the induction water channel is formed so as to be merged from both sides of the upper part where the collecting hoppers of the secondary settling basin are formed the rectifying means includes an inflow plate having a plurality of inflow holes through which the mlss flows together with inflow water on the upper surface thereof a solid plate and a superposed plate arranged in a lattice form to reduce the drop energy of the mlss in the lower portion of the inflow hole and a slope formed on the lower end of the flow path so that the mlss is not precipitated and guided to the diffusion means wherein the inflow holes are formed with different diameters the intermediate portion is formed with a larger diameter along the transport direction in which the mlss is introduced and the inflow hole is formed with a gradually smaller diameter toward both sides the superimposing means may include at least one superposed plate formed by vertically and horizontally piercing the mlss at a predetermined interval to form a plurality of through holes through which the mlss passes wherein the passage holes of the second settling basin are disposed at different positions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102617451-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a settling basin 10 consisting of a planar circular bottom plate installed in a sewage treatment plant or water purification plant and a side wall 11 outside the bottom plate and a side wall of the settling tank in 11 a planar annular channel 20 is formed which has a concave groove and an overflow wear surrounding the inside of the concave groove with a corrosion resistant steel material a cover portion 110 consisting of an outer frame 120 and a cover casing 130 in the shape of a trapezoid with an outer circumference width larger than the inner width so as to cover the waterway 20 and an outer support member 140 that supports the outer frame 120 on the inner surface of the outer wall 21 of the water channel 20 it is coupled to the sediment side end 151 of the overflow weir 150 of the waterway has a certain height is coupled to the outer frame 120 and consists of a connection hinge that can rotate so that the outer frame 120 can be opened toward the top"}]</data>
</edge>
