  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in vegetation reservoirs for preventing pollution and creating a healthy urban environment a reservoir for storing rainfall runoff on the surface of the ground a vegetation filtration reservoir located at a lower portion of the reservoir and having a height of 25 to 60 cm including humus soil and sand at least one es filtration layer located below the vegetation filtration reservoir a collecting part located below the es filtration layer and having a storage part including a first gravel layer and a second gravel layer and a permeate part disposed in a lower part of the storage part and including a third gravel layer and a sand layer a pouring pipe disposed in the infiltration portion and being buried in the pouring portion to collect rainwater flowing out from the pouring portion an outlet pipe connected to the pipe a drain pipe provided in the vegetation filtration reservoir and a water pipe for collecting the water collected in the pipe pipe upward a bypass pipe connected to the drain port for bypassing the rainwater flowing out of the storage compartment of the storage compartment a second accommodating portion having a first accommodating portion having an inflow port into which the rainwater effluent flows an outlet provided with a screen for removing foreign matter in the rainwater inflow water flowing from the first accommodating portion and a vertical partition wall arranged so as to be communicated with each other an es expanded shale filter medium is disposed at a boundary between the vegetation filtration reservoir and the original soil and a bottom surface of the bottom of the water outlet is at least 30 cm away from the bottom of the bottom of the water outlet the vegetation filtration reservoir includes fly ash within 5 of the volume of the vegetation filtration reservoir wherein an aerobic condition layer is formed on the upper part of the basin of the drain hole and an anaerobic anaerobic condition layer is formed on the lower part of the basin of the drain hole to prevent pollution and to provide a healthy urban environment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101694700-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however due to the nature of the water pipe which is mainly buried in the underground there is a problem that it is not easy to accurately grasp the breakage state and aging"}, {"pat_id": "US-5232307-A", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "sediment carried by the storm water is thereby transferred directly to the downstream channel without collecting in the basin 84"}, {"pat_id": "US-7640792-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "based on these measurements engineers can determine whether a proposed basin design is acceptable or otherwise determine alternative design parameters for a drainage basin"}]</data>
