  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 installed at the inlet of the primary sedimentation tank 1 into which the sewage flows and the suspended matter generated on the water surface of the incoming sewage is led to the suspended debris removal device installed at the downstream of the inflow portion to prevent clogging of the flowing sewage an apparatus for crushing and flooding suspended matters of a primary clarifier a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier 1 to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides an apparatus for preventing floatation and flooding of a primary clarifier using an acidifier the apparatus comprising an inlet to a first settling tank through which sewage is introduced an apparatus for crushing and preventing floatation of a primary clarifier using an acidifier to prevent clogging of sewage flowing into a sludge removal device installed at a rear end of a site comprising a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7117022-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "it may also be implemented in a mixed format with a partial hardware module that implements a part of hardware elements.brief description of the drawings it is a block diagram which shows the inland water flooding analysis apparatus which concerns on embodiment 1 of this invention.fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-4613253-A", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in this way the discharge system of this invention reduces i the high costs of pipe and pipe fabrication ii the weight due to long piping runs iii the danger of flooding due to pipe rupture and penetration seal degradation iv the necessity of an air removal system for start up to remove air from the inverted u of a gooseneck arrangement v expensive on site fabrication and vi problems associated with the height of the catchment basin"}]</data>
</edge>
