  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100416293-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "conventionally since the raw water which has been settled through the initial settler is sent to the flow adjusting tank to supply a predetermined amount to the subsequent reaction tank the processing time is long and the sedimentation tank and the flow adjusting tank are separately required but the present invention requires a separate settling tank and a flow adjusting tank it is not necessary and the processing time can be shortened to about 0.5 to 3 hours thereby increasing the processing efficiency.as described above the present invention divides the water tank of the water quality adjustment tank 10 into the blocking wall 40 but the blocking wall 40 is lifted up and down by the lifting part 30 and the water quality of the incoming raw water and by measuring the flow rate to control the blocking wall 40 the transfer valve 60 the storm discharge valve 70 it is possible to increase the treatment efficiency of the sewage treatment system in response to the water quality change of the incoming water no settling basin or flow adjustment tank is required and the treatment efficiency of the system can be improved"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "to limit contamination of the receiving flows and streams by untreated combined sewage the diverted flow may enter the receiving stream by direct overflow only when the soil percentage of the water to be discharged has been reduced to a level such that there is no further risk of appreciable contamination of the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-4225434-A", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "the frequency and the run time of the combined water diversion and therefore the contaminant yielded to the receiving stream are reduced and there is a considerable reduction in the discharge of suspended substances into the receiving stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-5232307-A", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "sediment carried by the storm water is thereby transferred directly to the downstream channel without collecting in the basin 84"}, {"pat_id": "US-7029201-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "for example where the utility line 44 is a six inch outer diameter pipe such as a water main a width 63 of the trench may be 18 inches or more"}]</data>
</edge>
