  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101993601-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a seawater amount measuring sensor 100 for measuring the amount of seawater flowing into the body straw an automatic rectifier 200 for controlling a potential difference and generating and outputting a direct current for protection corrosion a first anode 300 insulated from the hull and installed on the outer shell of the ship to output a current sent from the automatic rectifier 200 a second anode 400 installed inside the sea water supply line and inside the body cavity to output a current sent from the automatic rectifier 200 a reference electrode 500 for detecting a potential difference of the hull to form a potential difference for the scheme the seawater amount measuring sensor 100 the automatic rectifier 200 the first anode 300 the second anode 400 a control panel 600 connected to the reference electrode 500 and controlling the amount of current to be output a biosensor provided in the body and the seawater supply line for sensing the biological reaction in the seawater and delivering it to the control panel 600 when a biological reaction of the organism and the organism is sensed a propeller shaft and a hull of a ship are electrically connected to each other by a silver alloy slip ring and a silver brush to form a propeller shaft grounding device for protecting the propeller the propeller shaft and the engine bearing and a rudder axis grounding device for connecting the rudder strand between the roof of the wheelhouse and the rudder axis to electrically connect the rudder and the hull thereby protecting the rudder axis the automatic rectifier 200 adjusts the output current according to the amount of seawater measured from the seawater amount measuring sensor 100 the control panel 600 further includes a memory for storing a history of controlling the output current and an expected replacement date of the first anode 300 the second anode 400 and the reference electrode 500 including when excessive detection of an organism component and a biological reaction are detected according to a predetermined value according to information of the biosensor in real time the control panel 600 automatically or manually activates the proliferation inhibitor to perform ion or chemical treatment line side of the microbial sterilization apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2556400-Y2", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "as described above according to the present invention according to the use of hot water water from which dissolved gas dissolved oxygen has been removed by a membrane deaerator according to use of hot water is supplied from a receiving tank to a hot water tank via a makeup water tank"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4313255-B2", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "and a means 6 forcibly taking in the air provided below the equipment for example a ventilation fan and a chimney for raising the introduced air to flow while flowing into the equipment internal space as an air flow and contacting and absorbing inside the condensate atmospheric flow fluidization means 7 provided in the duct 4 having an effect for example a ventilation fan provided over the entire equipment internal space for condensing moisture as water in the vicinity of the dew point when the ambient temperature drops the first second and third forced cooling means 40 41 for cooling the atmospheric flow moisture installed in the condensing device 11 which will be described later and the condensing material body 21 in the condensing device which will also be described later"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "synthetic resin water tanks produced as synthetic resins can be expected to have excellent effects in preventing leakage and corrosion but they are not suitable for use as large tanks installed on the roof of large apartment houses due to their poor ability to handle loads such as large internal water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "US-5259166-A", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "more specifically the abutting standing seam elements are simply press fitted into a standing seam and preferably the orthogonal walls of the abutting seam elements are press fitted together at a position below the press fitted standing seam whereby a titanium waterproof standing seam is formed in the welding soldering or otherwise permanently affixing the seam elements to one another thus avoiding metal corrosion to assure potable water while forming waterproof seams capable of thermal expansion and contraction in a system having exceptional long life characteristics"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387133-Y1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "rainwater contains various suspended substances which causes the storage water to decay making it difficult to store for long periods of time resulting in a decrease in rainwater utilization.in order to achieve the above object by adding a rain filtration filter \u2462 in the process of storing the rainwater collected from the roof of the building or the roof of the rainy weather in the rainwater storage tank in order to achieve the above object by separating the dust or suspended matter and storing only the clean rainwater long term storage prevents decay due to organic substances in rainwater making it possible to use it as water for living and by using a corrosion resistant metal grid filter \u2466 it can be used semi permanently without long term maintenance costs caused by corrosion or aging"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102411899-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "however in the case of such a square water tank the inside of the water tank is complicated due to the angles 16 and 17 installed in the inside of the water tank complicatedly the drainage during cleaning is poor and many problems occur during maintenance and also the angle 16 since 17 is joined to the joint 13 of the panel 12 by welding the number of angles 16 and 17 increases in proportion to the number of welds and thus there is a problem that a lot of welding corrosion may occur"}]</data>
</edge>
