  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system where there is water leakage into the sewer line through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "US-9157227-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in sanitary sewer system where there is a water leakage into the sewer system through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof down spout connections are made to the system which normally should carry only the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machines drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4997312-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system leakage into the sewer line through manholes leakage into the sewer line through manholes where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "US-4892440-A", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "this risk is sometimes present in a sanitary sewer system where there is water leakage into the sewer line through manholes cracks in sewer line joints or where improper roof downspout connections are made to the system which normally should only carry the water and sewage draining from sinks toilets washing machine drain lines and basement floor drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "synthetic resin water tanks produced as synthetic resins can be expected to have excellent effects in preventing leakage and corrosion but they are not suitable for use as large tanks installed on the roof of large apartment houses due to their poor ability to handle loads such as large internal water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266017-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "is installed and the bent part 12 is formed in the interior pipe 11 the intermediate valve 21 is installed in the cross pipe 5 to reduce the water pressure to a predetermined pressure or less and is installed in the cross pipe 5 in the water supply pipe of the high rise building consisting of a first noise canceling unit 23 made of a pressure gauge 22 for measuring the water pressure by the adjustment of the intermediate valve 21 a fixture 27 having the same diameter as that of the indoor pipe 11 and having a main through hole 25 formed at a central portion and formed at equal intervals to the outside of the main through hole 25 it is attached to the main hole 25 formed in the fixture 27 to form a smooth angle of the bent portion 12 of the indoor pipe 11 by water pressure vortex water and softly formed stepped 30 on one side inner tube 28 water supply pipe noise reduction of the high rise building characterized in that provided with a second noise reduction unit 24 is installed in the front of the fixture 27 and the packing 29 to prevent leakage when connected to the meter 6 device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266017-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "to this end the downstream water supply pipe 4 connected to the elevated water tank installed on the roof of the high rise building the horizontal pipe 5 installed in parallel with the downward water supply pipe 4 and the horizontal pipe 5 connected to the meter 6 is provided and the interior pipe 11 having the bent portion 12 the intermediate valve 21 installed in the cross pipe 5 for reducing the water pressure to a predetermined pressure or less and the cross pipe 5 in the water supply piping device of the high rise building consisting of a first noise canceling unit 23 consisting of a pressure gauge 22 installed in the pressure gauge 22 to measure the pressure of the intermediate valve 21 the diameter of the indoor pipe 11 it is the same as the main hole 25 is formed in the central portion the outer space of the main hole 25 is formed at equal intervals of the fasteners 27 formed with a number of auxiliary through holes 26 the main formed in the fastener 27 it is attached to the through hole 25 to gently form the angle of the bent portion 12 of the indoor pipe 11 by the hydraulic pressure the second silencer made of a soft inner tube 28 having a step 30 formed on one side and a packing 29 installed at the front of the fixture 27 to prevent leakage when connected to the meter 6"}]</data>
</edge>
