  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101266939-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "manual valve operation method is unrealistic because the manager must operate the valve in the early stage of rainfall and it has the disadvantage of high cost and difficulty of maintenance such as failure when using devices such as flow meters and sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102731335-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "according to an embodiment of the present invention described above a river tributary odor blocking structure is used to block odors generated at the end of a river tributary such as sewage or rainwater pipes flowing into the river in normal times thereby providing a pleasant environment for users of bicycle paths walking paths or park roads along the river and to open the odor blocking during sudden rainfall to effectively drain rainwater or sewage into the main stream and to form a roof parallel to the ground from the upper side and to include an upper frame 100 provided with a first upper bar 110 arranged at the rear a second upper bar 120 arranged at the front end of the first upper bar 110 an upper cover material 130 covering the first and second upper bars 110 120 and a plurality of upper connecting bars 140 connecting the first and second upper bars 110 120 to each other in the front and rear directions and an upper frame 100 inclined forward at both left and right ends of the upper frame 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in order to provide a block for wind and photovoltaic power generation in a road or building it is installed in accordance with the width and length of the roof to be installed in the photovoltaic power generation plate 25 provided with a photovoltaic generator 58 induction pipe for rainwater induction around the outer side of the lower portion 24 formed in the upper and lower directions to the guide wall 28 and the guide groove 29 to the lower portion 24 is formed to be inclined in both directions from the side portion 22 in the power generation block 20 provided with 35 protruding from both side edges of the solar light collecting plate 25 on one side from the upper portion 22 to form a side wall 31 to the upper side in accordance with the inclination rotating shafts 45 are connected to each other and installed between the side walls 31 and the rotating shafts 45 are provided with a rotating drum 44 on the outer surface of the rotating drum 44 is inclined to rotate the rotary blade 43 at equal intervals to the outer side of the rotary blade 43 is provided with an outer wall body 33 for connecting between the side walls 31 the cross section of the outer wall body 33 is provided with an inlet 21 of the inverse trumpet shape and an inlet 21 of the other side to the upper side of the guide wall 28 the fixing bar 49 for supporting downward from the edge of the outer wall body 33 to the upper side of the guide wall 28 water storage block for solar power generation is configured to be inclined with a guide net 29 fixed to the induction pipe 35 for the rainwater induction groove 29"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a block for storing wind and solar power in rain or rain in a storage tank 38 while providing blocks for wind and solar power generation in a roof such as a road or a building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102812276-B1", "para_id": "para_124", "text": "although the preferred embodiments of the present invention have been described in detail above the scope of the present invention is not limited thereto and various modifications and improvements made by those skilled in the art using the basic concept of the present invention defined in the following claims also fall within the scope of the present invention.g1 landfill layer g2 cover layer 1 leachate recovery section 11 leachate plate 111 leachate channel 12 blocking member 13 leachate drain 2 leachate purification unit 21 leachate inlet line 22 purification unit 211 purification body 211a 1st body 211b 1st purification space 211c 2nd body 211d 2nd purification space 222 ceramic filter 223 1st activated carbon layer 224 2nd activated carbon layer 225 zeolite layer 226 silica sand layer 227 compartment filter 23 purification storage 231 storage space 24 natural stone 25 heating section 3 landfill gas recovery section 31 gas pipe 311 through hole 32 flow pipe 33 landfill gas purification unit 34 storage tank 35 landfill gas pump 36 control valve 4 high temperature sterilization unit 41 steam generator 42 storage unit connection line 43 steam line 44 steam pump 5 uv sterilization section 51 substrate section 52 uv ray generation unit 6 dust suppression unit 61 spray line 62 drum 63 spraying unit 64 supply pipe 65 spray pump 7 wheel washing unit 71 tunnel section 711 car wash area 711a entrance 711b exit 72 lower wash section 73 side wash section 74 rear wash section 741 hinge block 742 shaft 743 drive motor 744 spray pipe 744a vertical pipe 744b horizontal pipe 75 front wash section 76 wash water supply storage unit 77 sterilization wash unit 78 dry car wash unit 79 car wash water recovery unit 8 pedestrian safety section 8a pedestrian safety passage 81 outer structure 811 entrance 82 frame section 821 pedestrian passage 83 roof 84 blocking 85 1st rail section 86 2nd rail section 87 frame drive unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352820-B1", "para_id": "claim_11", "text": "means for atomizing the seawater by the rotation of the centrifugal force generator and spraying the seawater into the treatment chamber it has a hot air blowing means for applying warm air to the fog of the sea water in the roof of the processing chamber open the air vent to discharge the vaporized vapor in the processing chamber out of the processing chamber a device for treating seawater characterized in that it has a means for removing a salt attached to the net while installing a net to block the ventilation hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352820-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the vaporized water vapor rises because of its low specific gravity but since the vent hole is opened in the roof of the processing chamber only water can be discharged smoothly from the processing chamber and separated from natural salt crystals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352820-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "the vaporized water vapor rises due to its low specific gravity but since the vent hole for opening is open in the processing chamber roof only water can be smoothly discharged from the processing chamber and natural salt can be separated and separated"}, {"pat_id": "US-11465071-B2", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "more specifically the frame members 44 are attached to or integral with each other in a substantially open manner which results in most or preferably all of the sides of the frame 20 being open spaces that will not block or at least block as little as possible any movement and subsequent contact by the moisture laden air 14 against the condensation surfaces 28 30 the condensation panels 18 and the exiting of dried air 38 away from of the condensation panels 18 that comprise the apparatus 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101016329-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "nothing has been done.the present invention has been proposed in order to solve the conventional problems as described above the object of the construction is to replace the roof of the existing storage tank while being constructed in a simplified structure to block the inflow of dust and lower the construction cost as well as drainage of rain water the present invention provides a reservoir cover device and a reservoir including the same which can smoothly and easily handle odors or harmful gases and in particular the height of the lid can be adjusted according to the reservoir level thereby enabling the adjustment of the storage capacity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101016329-B1", "para_id": "para_33", "text": "therefore the reservoir cover device 1a of the first embodiment of the present invention will replace the roof that is previously installed on the reservoir and block the inflow of dust and the like and in particular will simplify the structure to lower the construction cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101552006-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however since the conventional rainwater storage tanks are manufactured in a conventional manner the rainwater storage tanks need to be manufactured separately in order to have a rainwater storage tank having a capacity suitable for the building there is not provided means for eliminating the initial storm contaminated with non point pollutants so that secondary pollution may occur due to the use of the stored water contaminated with the non point sealant material in the storm water storage tank the installation work takes a long time and the installation cost is also high.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide an air conditioner which can be easily assembled and installed according to installation condition and usage amount of a building to be installed the present invention provides a built up type rainwater storage tank which can be used as water potable water fire water and washing water can be used as drinking water in an emergency and can also function as a flood control in the city when it rains.the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage tank installed on a building to store rainwater in a rainfall and to use stored rainwater as various living water wherein the rainwater storage tank includes a water storage tank top for storing water a water pipe assembly having one end connected to a water inlet provided at an upper end of the water storage tank and the other end connected to a roof drain of a building a water supply pipe connected to the lower end of the water storage tank and connected to the water storage tank a water pump mounted on the transfer tube to pump the storage tank in the water storage tank an advanced water purifier connected to the water storage tank to purify and sterilize the stored water stored in the water storage tank and supply the water to the drinking water and a water spraying hose connected to the water storage tank to connect the water storage tank to the water storage tank so as to use the water storage tank as the garden water and the wash water.the assembled storm water storage tank according to the present invention can be assembled and used in a simple and quick manner so as to have the capacity of the water storage tank in accordance with the required excellent use amount and can be used as drinking water in case of emergency and also the effect of water saving and flood control of the water supply is very large and the installation cost can be remarkably reduced.1 is an installation view showing an installation state of an assembled rainwater storage tank according to the present invention fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972396-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "a lid formed of a rim shaped lower end portion an inclined rim shaped stop portion of upper and lower light beams extending from an upper portion of the lower portion and a roof completely covering the upper portion of the interrupted portion it is configured to include in the center of the ceiling inside the cover a support roller via a wire rope connecting the winch device and the protective cover is installed around the side of the floating means the concrete block and weight installed in the water pulleys passing through the connecting rope to connect is characterized in that it is installed in a plurality of equal intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100972396-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a lid formed of a rim shaped lower end portion an inclined rim shaped stop portion of upper and lower light beams extending from an upper portion of the lower portion and a roof completely covering the upper portion of the interrupted portion it is configured to include in the center of the ceiling inside the cover a support roller via a wire rope connecting the winch device and the protective cover is installed around the side of the floating means the concrete block and weight installed in the water pulleys passing through the connecting rope to connect is characterized in that it is installed in a plurality of equal intervals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102015918-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "in this case a filter or a strainer may be installed in the inlet 12a to block foreign substances from flowing from the inclined surface 11a of the roof 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101897063-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "4 is a circuit block diagram of the controller 15 the driving aerator 1 comprises a housing or a body 6 composed of a bottom plate 2 a wall body 3 an inclined roof 4 and a retractable door 5 a plurality of floating bodies 7 8 9 and 10 fixed on the front rear left and right sides of the bottom surface of the plate 2 a decelerating motor 11 provided on the rear end of the bottom plate 2 a propeller or a screw 12 provided on the rotary shaft of the decelerating motor 11 or the shaft portion of the gear a rudder 13 and its drive means 14 provided on the rear end of the screw 12 the first second third and fourth water quality measuring sensors 1 2 3 and 4 are installed at one side or the center of the bottom face of the floating bodies 7 17 18 19 and 20 a bottom plate 2 a flexible hose 21 connected to an outlet of an aeration means 22 protruding to a lower portion of the bottom plate 2 and a flexible hose 21 installed at an end of the hose 21 and a plurality of width mechanisms 24 connected to the branch mechanism 23 for aerating the air into the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "therefore rainwater or groundwater is collected and stored"}]</data>
