  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100912781-B1", "para_id": "para_73", "text": "in addition the inlet portion 10 and the dehydration portion 40 may wind the heating wire 75 on the outer surface of the body thereby preventing the freezing of the slurry type livestock manure introduced by the heating wire 75 in particular the viscosity of the slurry type livestock manure rises so that the efficiency of solid liquid separation can be improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200413569-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "because it is installed on the ground due to the weakness of the material that is weak in insulation and sound insulation of general concrete a separate insulation construction is required to wind the heating wire or install the insulation to prevent freezing of the motor pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "while the present invention has been particularly shown and described with reference to exemplary embodiments thereof it is to be understood that the invention is not limited to the disclosed exemplary embodiments but on the contrary is intended to cover various modifications and equivalent arrangements included within the spirit and scope of the appended claims.10 water circulation system 20 water circulation device 21 floating frame 22 wind blade 23 buoyant body 24 solar panel 25 housing 25a inner space 26 gear device 27 cold water jetting portion 27a cold water induction pipe 27b cold water nozzle 28 motor 29 hot water jetting part 29a hot water induction pipe 29b hydrothermal nozzle 30 impeller 31 expansion contraction tube 33 first sensor part 35 second sensor part 37 fixed wire 37a anchor 41 pump 43 freezing part 45 heating section 47 purge control section 49 battery 51 circulation line 52 block holder 52a 52b horizontal rod 53 cutting block 53a upper inclined surface 53b lower inclined surface 53c fitting end portion 55 55a inward gear 55b traveling groove 57 underwater motor 57b drive shaft 57c drive gear 59 59a height holding holder 59b receiving arm 59c roller bearing 59d support roller 61 sensor gateway 63 middleway 65 monitoring section 67 manual control section"}, {"pat_id": "US-11472717-B2", "para_id": "para_232", "text": "for example sensing or receiving weather conditions sensing relative humidity within an interior opening of the evaporation panel using timers providing automated wastewater loading based on timing or sensor driven analytics or the like can be used to automatically determine when the system should run should be loaded with wastewater and can actually control the actual running profile and or wastewater loading fluidics etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200266383-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "water meter double thermostat to prevent water meter from freezing even in cold winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100432778-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "water meter double thermostat to prevent water meter from freezing even in cold winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200170750-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "there were problems such as freezing.the present invention is designed to solve the above problems in particular before and after the water meter protection tube by forming a longitudinal horizontal line projection at regular intervals even if the water meter protection tube with a large internal space can withstand earth pressure or external pressure well appearance the upper edge of the water meter protector is equipped with a silicone rubber frame and when the lid is closed it closes to prevent wind and dust input and facilitates meter reading and freezes expensive medium and large water meters and water pipes during the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200170750-Y1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "it becomes smooth and the price is high in the winter season and it acts to prevent freezing of large water meters and water pipes"}, {"pat_id": "US-10562790-B2", "para_id": "para_203", "text": "for example sensing or receiving weather conditions sensing relative humidity within an interior opening of the evaporation panel using timers providing automated wastewater loading based on timing or sensor driven analytics or the like can be used to automatically determine when the system should run should be loaded with wastewater and can actually control the actual running profile and or wastewater loading fluidics etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_58", "text": "in addition although the external temperature of the winter season is measured by the external temperature sensor but may be lower than the temperature actually measured by obstacles or other factors such as wind the controller 30 of the present invention has an external temperature of 4 when the temperature of the water inside the water tank 1 becomes 4 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100871326-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a device for preventing freezing of waterworks and more particularly to prevent sedimentation water from freezing in winter in sedimentation basins of waterworks using geothermal heat and to freeze sedimentation water by wind blowing directly into the sedimentation basin"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387638-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "since the strap 10 is connected to the bottom the lid 5 is lifted off during the meter reading and even if it is placed elsewhere it is prevented from being lost or damaged even if it is blown in the wind or accidentally stepped on.as described above the present invention is simple in construction and the thickness of the water meter protective tube thermal insulation material is formed thicker than usual and the lid and the insertion hole is formed in the same shape as a tapered shape so that the lid can be easily inserted"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_142", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_157", "text": "the second threshold temperature tps2 and max time at second threshold temperature tpsmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_159", "text": "the second threshold temperature tss2 and max time at second threshold temperature tssmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_161", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle12 and max time at second threshold temperature tle1max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_163", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle22 and max time at second threshold temperature tle2max provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_165", "text": "the second threshold temperature tet2 and max time at second threshold temperature tetmax provides a factor of safety to prevent possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind dips in temperature or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_126", "text": "therefore any water lines exposed to outside temperatures including any water line runs inside the heated interior 206 that may be subject to freezing temperatures are protected and warmed by the circulating warming loops"}, {"pat_id": "US-7089955-B1", "para_id": "para_173", "text": "103 may be located at other points in the water line run including the area near water pump 16 if warmed by the warming system 50 is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100454430-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "when the lid 5 is covered on the upper surface of the water meter protector 1 the upper edge 2 of the lid 5 is formed in the taper recess 3 formed inside the water meter protector 1 of the border 2 the middle tape 7 tapered in the triple frame and inserted into the rubber o ring 27 is inserted and the outer frame 6 and the inner frame 8 are covered with the center so that the water meter protection tube 1 and the lid 5 is in close contact with outside snow and non cold wind can not flow into the water meter protection tank 1 thereby increasing the thermal insulation power to prevent the freezing of the water meter etc"}]</data>
</edge>
