water storage block for solar power generation is configured to be inclined with a guide net 29 fixed to the induction pipe 35 for the rainwater induction groove 29"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the invention is configured by.as described above the present invention provides a wind and solar power block while preventing damage to sound insulation and heavy snow in a long distance section in which a road or a bridge is connected particularly in a mountain or bridge section as well as ensuring safe driving"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "accordingly an object of the present invention is to provide a block for storing wind and solar power in rain or rain in a storage tank 38 while providing blocks for wind and solar power generation in a roof such as a road or a building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "referring to the operating state for the rotation block 55 described above as shown by the solid line shown in figure 8 the wind blowing from the south in the summer wind passing through the south solar power generation plate 25a wind moving while rotating the rotary blade 43 provided to rotate at the position a of the moving direction is discharged to the discharge portion a from the inlet 21 of the other side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "therefore when the structure of the embodiment of the present invention will be described in detail when explaining the operating state for the rotation block 55 described above as shown by the dotted line shown in figure 8 the wind blowing from the south in summer wind power moving while rotating the rotary blade 43 provided to rotate to position a in the direction in which the wind flows flowing while passing through the south side photovoltaic power generation plate 25a is provided to enlarge the length is the other side it is discharged from the inlet 21 of the outlet a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when the wind is blown the odor preventing curtain is opened and the odor is generated.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned disadvantages of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a non powered flow rate control device for preventing malodorous flow which comprises a flow rate control device which is detachably attached to a distal end portion of a sewer pipe and it is possible to collect all the high initial initial storms generated at the beginning of the sewage or rainfall that flow in the usual way into the sewage subtraction channel and the rain that flows in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall it is possible to prevent the overflowing of the stormwater by reducing the outflow section of the sewage and to naturally induce the slurry moving along with the storm into the river to prevent the accumulation of the slurry on the sewage drainage pipe which is in close contact with the inner side wall surfaces of the flow rate regulating device while being rotated up and down odor proof packing is installed on the wall to block off odors generated in the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352820-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "the vaporized water vapor rises because of its low specific gravity but since the vent hole is opened in the roof of the processing chamber only water can be discharged smoothly from the processing chamber and separated from natural salt crystals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352820-B1", "para_id": "para_114", "text": "the vaporized water vapor rises due to its low specific gravity but since the vent hole for opening is open in the processing chamber roof only water can be smoothly discharged from the processing chamber and natural salt can be separated and separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102377520-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "as a control method of the water quality improvement system according to claim 1 since the blade 107 is rotated by the wind power the air pump 105 is operated to pressurize air to the exhaust pipe 111 thereby generating bubbles in the aerator 125"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in a slope 62 formed over a wide area for the purpose of creating grassland and forest a road 63 formed with a slope 67 at the edge so as to penetrate the slope 62 a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 to prevent the slope 67 from sinking and a vegetation block 30 formed with a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to plant landscaping trees 46 in a protruding manner an assembly block 30 30 assembled in a layered structure and a slope 67 formed in an arid or hilly area where a renewable energy generation device 100 formed with solar and wind power generation devices 60 68 is built near a field 74 or a grassland or forest management area on the slope in a slope 62 in which a plurality of afforestation blocks 30 are stacked on a slope 67 equipped to be planted in the above mentioned vegetation zone 33 a water tank 71 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 of the afforestation blocks 30 30 assembled in the above mentioned stacked structure a vegetation zone 33 33 equipped with a vegetation wall 34 for planting landscaping trees 46 by protruding while a water supply hole 44 is perforated in the front wall 31 a moving gap 42 provided between a separate outer wall 32 in the rear wall 31 and afforestation blocks 30 30 are assembled in a stacked manner so that the moving gaps 42 are connected to each other an installation structure in a hilly area where a renewable energy power generation device for grassland and forest creation can be installed which is provided by assembling an assembly block 30 equipped with a vegetation wall 34 that is fixed to the outer section c of the vegetation block 30 connected to a water supply inlet 44 from a water tank 71 to support the lower section of the vegetation zone 33 33 while being assembled into the lower section of the above mentioned afforestation block 30 30 thereby preventing rainwater from collapsing due to subsidence on a slope 67"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in a slope 62 formed over a wide area for the purpose of creating grassland and forest a road 63 formed with a slope 67 at the edge so as to penetrate the slope 62 a water tank 71 provided between the front and rear walls 31 to prevent the slope 67 from sinking and a vegetation block 30 formed with a vegetation zone 33 provided with a water supply hole 44 perforated in the front wall 31 to plant landscaping trees 46 in a protruding manner an assembly block 30 30 assembled in a layered structure and a slope 67 formed in an arid or hilly area where a renewable energy generation device 100 formed with solar and wind power generation devices 60 68 is built near a field 74 or a grassland or forest management area on the slope"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_74", "text": "here the invention is that the installation of the second renewable energy power generation device 100 installed to prevent subsidence due to the harmful gas 49 or rainwater on the slope is preferably installed in a hilly area 64 where sunlight and wind power are well transmitted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102851468-B1", "para_id": "para_75", "text": "therefore the purpose of this invention is to provide power and equipment for collection in an economical and environmentally friendly manner by providing a