  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101385841-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "the wire 256 is fixed to the 210 and the drive motor 254 is installed in the middle portion of the rotation guide post 233 so as to wind the wire 256"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1350028-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "an electrically operated lift pump 52 conveys the brackish water via the raw water lift pipe 54 the rotary union 26 and the storage tank 27 to the pressure pump 20 in the nacelle 22"}, {"pat_id": "US-9024461-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "according to this conception the present invention provides a tidal energy seawater desalination system characterized in that it comprises a tidal energy power device a seawater evaporation tower and a steam condensation tower in which the seawater evaporation tower is configured with a vacuum pump which connects with a power output shaft of the tidal energy power device such that the tidal energy power device is capable of driving the vacuum pump to work the vacuum pump connecting the seawater evaporation tower via pipelines the output end of the vacuum pump connecting the steam condensation tower via pipelines and the steam condensation tower connecting a fresh water receiver via pipelines"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b ver