north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5189897-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the pipeline danger area monitoring system according to claim 1 wherein the gas leakage range calculation unit predicts and calculates gas diffusion in consideration of wind direction and wind speed data in the vicinity of the danger pipe section"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6254972-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "a method of listening to a water leak sound acoustic vibration transmitted from a water leak point with a sound stick or contacting a correlated water leak detector on a transparent plate covering the display surface 34b of the display unit 34a of the water meter 34 in the case of methods such as detecting water leakage sound transmitted from the location of water leakage both methods are affected by ambient noise and unnecessary vibrations wind effects and camera shake etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6254972-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "further by reducing the height of the water leakage determination device 1 it can be accommodated in the meter box 35 and in a state where the water leakage determination device and the water meter 34 are connected a state where wind or the like is blowing even so the stability is improved without being affected by it"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6254972-B2", "para_id": "para_36", "text": "therefore the stability in a state where the water leakage determination device 1 and the water meter 34 are connected is further increased without being affected by wind during the water leakage inspection"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6254972-B2", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "therefore even if the water leakage determination device 1 and the water meter 34 are connected they are contained in the meter box 35 so that they are not affected by the wind and the stability is further improved"}, {"pat_id": "US-12305815-B2", "para_id": "para_30", "text": "hence the one transport non return valves may be coupled to the transporting pipeline close to the first wind turbine and the further transport non return valves may be coupled close to the downstream located second wind turbine"}, {"pat_id": "US-12305815-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "hence if leakage in one system and one transporting pipeline respectively is detected the pressure control system of the respective system may close the flow of fluid into the main pipeline and the system comprising the leaking transporting pipeline may be decoupled from the main pipeline and the other gas producing systems respectively"}, {"pat_id": "US-12305815-B2", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "hence if a leakage in one of the main pipes is detected the leaking main pipe may be bypassed via the other main pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-12305815-B2", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "since a leakage in the leaking transporting pipeline section 1201 has been detected the multiway valve 801 of the left wind turbine 110 closes the second valve inlet b and directs the electrolyzed gas from the electrolyzer unit 111 and or from the storage tank 901 via the first valve inlet a into the transporting pipeline 131"}, {"pat_id": "US-12305815-B2", "para_id": "para_96", "text": "hence if leakage in one system 1501 1502 1503 1511 1512 1513 and one respective transporting pipeline 131 respectively is detected the pressure control system 140 of the respective system 1501 1502 1503 1511 1512 1513 may close the flow of fluid into the main pipeline 1504 1505 and the system 1501 1502 1503 1511 1512 1513 comprising the leaking transporting pipeline 131 may be decoupled from the main pipeline 1504 1505 and the other gas producing systems 1501 1502 1503 1511 1512 1513 respectively"}, {"pat_id": "US-12305815-B2", "para_id": "para_103", "text": "hence the leakage section by guiding the 1801 can be bypassed electrolyzed gas via the further main pipeline 1505"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312669-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the roof ventilation fan installed the rain water drainage equipment the present invention is a conventional roof ventilator for ventilation to open the pit opening that acts like a chimney open to the rooftop in the building it does not block the wind blown from the rooftops but through the rain water through to prevent this we get wet walls and cause water leakage mold etc"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4931039-B2", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "measurement procedure the procedure for measuring the degree of contamination of raw water by the water quality monitoring apparatus shown in fig"}]</data>
</edge>
