  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "according to the present invention only a crush stone is installed at the lower end of the reservoir structure so as to penetrate not only the reservoir of the storm but also the stormwater and by implementing the water circulation system penetrating into the ground through the reservoir with the upper reservoir and the lower reservoir it is possible to keep reservoirs and infiltration for water circulation and thus to prevent flooding even in temporary storms in areas where the impervious area is wide and the effect on the water circulation system is large.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "as shown in figure 3 the present invention is characterized in that the jaw 11 is formed to hang the strainer 21 to filter the dirt on the upper part of the rain gutter which is floating leaves floating on the road surface cigarette butts and dirt accumulate in rain gutters to prevent rainwater or sewage inflow or flow flooding the road or these dirt accumulate in sewers through rain gutters impeding the flow of sewage overflowing sewage pipes this is to prevent it"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_56", "text": "without proper maintenance backwater valves can become blocked or stuck giving building managers and homeowners a false sense of security that they will be protected during a flooding event"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101533943-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also when the water level rises the retractable watershed wall prevents the backwash of the river water to prevent flooding damage and the impoundment collection box having a filter net for filtering the contaminants contained in the sewage and storm seats is installed so that the contaminants do not flow into the wells and an odor chamber connected to the ceiling of the sewage pipe at an upper portion of the open the curtain can be installed to block the malodor generated in the sewer line and to move the sewer line along the moving rail to the left and right sides of the sewer line to conveniently remove and remove the contaminant lifting device connected with the wire have"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178211-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "the present invention is to block the upper surface of the drain cover due to foreign matters or in particular even when a large amount of water in a moment of heavy rain or heavy rains can be drained smoothly without clogging with foreign matter so that the water around the drain cover it not only prevents seizing but also provides excellent effects to prevent flooding and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102855051-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however it is difficult to identify trash inside the manhole by manpower and if the trash is not cleaned in a timely manner the trash can block the river connection pipe connecting the manhole to the river and as a result the mixed water of sewage and rainwater cannot be discharged into the river so the inside of the manhole becomes filled with the mixed water of sewage and rainwater and the mixed water of sewage and rainwater flows back upstream of the manhole causing urban flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101905810-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "2 2007 road structure for easy waste disposal summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above described problems in the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a rainwater garden at an adjacent location of a road to prevent flooding or subsidence the present invention provides a road structure having a multifunctional drainage line of a road surface that can enhance drainage efficiency and utilize collected watercolor as a multipurpose by forced drainage of water.in order to achieve the above mentioned object the present invention provides a road surface 12 comprising asphalt or concrete pavements a collecting fixture 10 installed on both sides of the road surface 12 to collect rainwater and a storm drain pipe 20 connected to the storm sewer 10 and discharging collected stormwater to the sewer a housing 32 formed with an opening 34 on the upper side and inserted into the road surface 12 a lifting block 30 mounted on the housing 32 such that the upper end of the lifting block 30 can be lifted up and down and the rack gear 31 is extended downward a spring 40 connected to a lower side of the elevating block 30 to press the elevating block 30 upward a pinion gear 50 meshing with the rack gear 31 a drive shaft 60 rotatably shaft connected to the pinion gear 50 and connected to the pinion gear 50 through a ratchet 61 and positively rotated only when the rack gear 31 is lowered a rotation limiting device 70 coupled to the drive shaft 60 to restrict the drive shaft 60 to rotate only in the normal rotation direction a housing 81 formed in a cylindrical shape and having a through hole 81a through which the drive shaft 60 is rotatably inserted is formed on one side of the center axis and a housing 81 having a central end 82a and an outer end 82b the center end 82a is connected to the driving shaft 60 extending to the inside of the housing 81 and the outside end 82b is fixed to the inner circumferential surface of the housing 81 and a rotation shaft 83 coupled to the outer side of the housing 81 so as to be coaxial with the drive shaft 60 so as to rotate together with the housing 81"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101788120-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "this patent has a dual exclusion capacity to prevent surplus outflows exceeding the existing sewer pipe s ability to flow out to the road surface and to prevent flooding and a dual the connection structures 140 a and 140 b of the exclusion structure are constructed to propose a methodology corresponding to immersion.registration no"}, {"pat_id": "US-5161911-A", "para_id": "para_94", "text": "sometimes flooding problems are worse in the one part of a city than in another portion thereof because of the differences in water drainage patterns"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100925049-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the roads installed by joining and installing s shaped protrusions on one side corresponding to and are maintained flat without step and v shaped and inverted v shaped joints are installed on the upper and lower sides of the s shaped coupling part to prevent road damage due to the vertical movement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259156-B1", "para_id": "para_71", "text": "the present invention relates to the fabrication of rainwater storage tanks having the ability to store rainwater and discharge or utilize rainwater rainwater to prevent flooding during heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment 811 the above flood control equipment 811 is the hull position movement construction machinery control equipment 811a the marine hydroelectric power generation control equipment 811b the power transmission control equipment 811c the harmful red tide prevention control equipment 811d the disaster prevention control equipment 811e the fishery spawning control equipment 811f and the dam water gate control control equipment 811g are each individually equipped and the floating dock device of the flood control equipment is connected to the inside of the flood control equipment body 1 to prevent flooding of the underground passage the floating dock device of the above flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding connected to the ocean tunnel traffic device 941 and the ocean hydroelectric power plant the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment has a length of 800 mm a diameter of 300 mm a portable lug connecting pin connection shaft for the inner and outer walls of each tank of the main tank and the outer block tank and a thickness of the steel plate of the portable lug is 150 mm and the pin connecting shaft is inserted into the portable lug to be connected and the processing hole of the connecting pin connecting shaft has a diameter of 30 mm and the portable lug pin has a length and a pin body diameter of 500 2 10 mm and is disassembled and combined with a nut at the threaded position processed into the end portion of the pin connecting shaft inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for preventing underground passage flooding the double structure block tank transported by the tugboat is a barge hull on the top of the holding tank assembled by a band jig mounted on a semi submersible work vessel with a length and width of 600 m and a height and steel plate thickness of 800 m and 40 m and 18 mm and the barge hull on the bottom of the holding tank has a pipe bridge at each of the four corners in the length and width of 15 m and a diameter and thickness of \u03c015 m and a length of 24 mm and a thickness of 1 km forming a double structure block tank inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment the size of the external block tank which is composed of the perimeter of the main tank and the inner block tank is individually combined to form a small sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 600 m a length of 800 m a height of 800 m a height of 600 m a medium sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 2 m a length of 3.2 m and a height of 2 m and a large sized floating dock for an offshore power plant with a width of 10 m a length of 10 m and a height of 10 m and the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and damage control equipment while operating according to the sea depth the portable lug pin is installed by fastening the bolt nut in the machined hole of the lug connecting shaft and at the same time the pin is bent to prevent the lug pin from coming off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helicopter station 619 and a thermal power plant 626 are equipped with satellite launch pads 643 and mooring towers 644 and space rocket launch pads to detect climate abnormalities and equipment for detecting the weather movement status of the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention flood control equipment to detect climate abnormalities in order to prioritize emergency rescue the flood control equipment in the flooded area is always equipped with several air compressors 80 connected to rescue tubes 130 and ropes 131 at the accident site and before the underground passage is flooded the flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment to prevent flooding by installing a water tank for rescue and flood control in the flooded area so that people can board the tubes 130 and be rescued by rescue workers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for underground passage flood prevention is configured to supply power to each pump using the marine hydroelectric power generator 213 facilities to prevent underground passage flooding in the above underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment the hydraulic power generator 213 is installed a device 218 for pushing a rotary shaft under an upper rotary shaft 217 is positioned and a stator coil 219 a stator frame 220 and a central stator 221 are positioned at the bottom of the device 218 for pushing the rotary shaft and an electric wire 71 is inserted into the gap of the central stator 221 and a fan 195 is positioned at the bottom of the central stator 221 and a braking device ring 223 a brake jack 224 and a low speed rotary shaft 225 are positioned at the bottom of the fan 195 and a low speed cooler 222 is positioned at the bottom of the low speed rotary shaft 225 and a rotating electromagnet rotor coil formed along the circumference of the rotary shaft 198 and an armature coil for a non rotating coil generator installed along the circumference of the rotor coil and a lower end of the rotary shaft 198 the conventional marine hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment which is provided with several waterwheels and turbines 267 for setting up positions turbine rotating shafts 227 casings 141 vane pumps guide vanes 142 and impellers 228 supplies power to each pump of the hydroelectric power generator 213 equipment to prevent underground passage flooding and is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flooding prevention and flood control equipment the vertical multi stage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the above underground passage flood prevention and water damage control equipment is as follows according to the control block diagram and the vertical multi stage pump operation method of the bf model the pump power 272 and the control power 273 are separated and distinguished and the emergency operation sequence circuit 274 of the control power 273 is connected to the dc power spray supply circuit 275 and the m c drive signal contact output circuit 279 and the output circuit terminal and then the m c switch contact of the pump power 272 and the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the contacts that enable each pump to be operated in emergency mode and at the same time the dc power supply circuit 275 of the control power 273 provides the input setting of the diac switch setting circuit 277 and the switch input circuit 58 to the micro control unit 276 and at the same time the led display circuit 278 and the drive signal contact output circuit 279 outputs a signal and the motor overload signal input circuit 280 is installed so that the circuit contacts of the unit 276 and the pump power supply 272 tip are connected to the inverter 47 circuit contacts and the inverter operation data input output circuit 281 is formed as a circuit for mutual input and output between the inverter 47 circuit and the micro control unit 276 and the discharge pressure transmitter 284 is connected to the pressure detection circuit 282 and then the circuit 282 is input set to the unit 276 and then the suction discharge pressure switch 285 is connected to the external status input circuit 283 and then the input circuit 283 is input set to the micro control unit 276"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1120", "text": "the present invention as a technical idea for achieving the above purpose is in the underground flood prevention and flood control equipment the above flood control equipment 811 is the hull position movement construction machinery control equipment 811a the marine hydroelectric power generation control equipment 811b the power