  <data key="d5">["force", "sedimentation", "completion", "collecting", "net", "prevention", "compressor", "power", "valve", "invention", "blade", "device", "gauge", "surface", "debris", "hammer", "time", "water", "clogging", "tank", "site", "plurality", "floatation", "socket", "matter", "order", "sludge", "settling", "portion", "air", "end", "inflow", "inside", "clarifier", "process", "property", "backflow", "burnout", "inlet", "filter", "problem", "drain", "vacuum", "check", "sewage", "acidifier", "netting", "flow", "apparatus", "downstream", "biodegradation", "damage", "flooding", "pipe", "suction", "removal", "pump", "drainage", "pressure"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["suck", "support", "solve", "provide", "prevent", "expand", "constitute", "supply", "connect", "use", "introduce", "catch", "crush", "lead", "suspend", "remove", "occur", "equip", "compress", "flow", "accomplish", "discharge", "be", "generate", "flood", "object", "instal", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "1 installed at the inlet of the primary sedimentation tank 1 into which the sewage flows and the suspended matter generated on the water surface of the incoming sewage is led to the suspended debris removal device installed at the downstream of the inflow portion to prevent clogging of the flowing sewage an apparatus for crushing and flooding suspended matters of a primary clarifier a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier 1 to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101700252-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides an apparatus for preventing floatation and flooding of a primary clarifier using an acidifier the apparatus comprising an inlet to a first settling tank through which sewage is introduced an apparatus for crushing and preventing floatation of a primary clarifier using an acidifier to prevent clogging of sewage flowing into a sludge removal device installed at a rear end of a site comprising a compressor installed outside the primary clarifier to supply compressed air the main settling tank 1 is provided with an air inflow portion 11 connected to the compressor to introduce air therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063307-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "not only burnout occurred but there was a problem of property damage due to flooding due to drainage.the present invention is to solve the above problems the air is compressed in the inside of the air pressure tank by the suction force of the drain pump during the drainage process was compressed in the air pressure tank when the water in the drain pipe back flow after the completion of drainage as the air expands it supports the check valve for preventing the backflow to prevent water hammer and at the same time to discharge the end of the drain pipe to constitute a water collecting tank drainage device equipped with a water hammer prevention air pressure tank to remove the foreign matter caught in the filter net of the drain pump biodegradation that is sucked together with water by suction power of the drainage pump when the drainage pump is installed by installing a vacuum netting connecting socket to which the vacuum gauge is connected to the suction end of the drainage pump and a plurality of foreign matter crushing blades are provided"}]</data>
</edge>
