  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100584084-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a barn bottom forming a through hole for discharging the manure of the livestock while providing a livestock breeding space a storage tank provided at a lower side of the barn bottom to maintain livestock wastewater by washing water and the manure at a predetermined level and to form a bottom with an inclined surface for smooth discharge of the wastewater a washing water control valve provided on an upstream side of the storage tank to control the washing water supplied to the storage tank from the outside and when the water level in the storage tank by the wash water supplied by the opening of the wash water check valve is a first class water level discharge of the wastewater in storage is started and discharged until it reaches the lowest water level and the supply of the wash water through the wash water check valve at the lowest water level is performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100656932-B1", "para_id": "para_44", "text": "third by connecting the sub pipe to the device for controlling the water level by desalination of water it is possible to prevent the micro leakage of the device to control the water level by desalting water by the check valve to maintain a constant water level at all times there is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300269-Y1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the pressure sensing pipe 42 is provided with a check valve 44 to prevent the inflow of raw water from the water supply pipe 40 to the water tank 50 and to transmit only the water pressure state of the water tank 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 6 it is installed at the lower side of the check valve and the third non power flow control device which operates in the shielding direction by the water pressure when the water level rises in the filtration tank and operates so as to be open while being homed by the weakening water pressure after the end of the rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "at this time the third non power flow control device 15 also operates in the shielding direction due to the water pressure applied as the water level rises in the filtration tank 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_1169", "text": "main switch button for off control 67 auxiliary switch button 68 input of display for vertical multistage pump or computer network input 69 current pressure value or set pressure value pressure setting value recognition nameplate 70 memory 71 power cable 73 disaster prevention material mixer 74 turbine water turbine 75 cloth cover 76 solenoid valve 77 ad balloon 78 airship 79 gas cylinder 80 air compressor 81 mobile service 82 portable terminal 83 low pressure cutoff valve 84 emergency valve 85 pressure reducing valve 86 first pressure check sensor 87 second pressure check sensor 88 electronic control unit 89 disaster prevention piping line or pumping pipe 89a vertical positive pipe 89b vertical downward pipe 90 ball valve handle 91 drencher head 92 valve body internal disc 93 emergency siren 94 spark or lightning as the initial ignition source 95 utility pole 96 transformer 97 reducer bushing socket 99 flashing warning light 100 paraffin nozzle plug 101 pressure gauge 102 bimetallic sensor 102a thermocouple configuration 102b thermal current generation 102c thermal electromotive force generation 102d measuring point 102e reference point 103 thermocouple thermometer switch for detection sensor 103a configuration of thermocouple thermometer 103b temperature measurement limit 103c temperature 1 103d ammeter temperature scale 103e metal a 103f metal b 103g potential difference generated 103h thermocouple and compensation wire 103i temperature measurement contact 103j thermocouple 103k compensation contact 103l compensation wire 103m reference contact 103n type of thermocouple 103o no protection tube 103p protection tube 103q high temperature object 103r protection tube there is 1