tom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "US-8418754-B2", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "since the lower valve 42 in the static chamber 32 is one way in the upwards direction the water 26 in the static chamber 32 travels through a left t connector 46a and over to the water line via another right t connector 46b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201275-Y1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "the present invention has been made to solve the conventional problems as described above to improve the structure of the water level control valve so that the predetermined raw water is discharged from the water level control valve and or check valve until the operation of the pump is completed in addition the purpose of preventing the overload of the pump cracking of the pipe and or breakage of the seam by stopping the operation of the pump by detecting the occurrence of the back flow pressure in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087622-B1", "para_id": "claim_15", "text": "in the discharging process the plc method control panel receives the signals of the timer the water level meter and the suspended solids meter that can prevent the leakage of sludge as a safety device when the discharge command signal is given to the treatment water extraction pump the treatment water extraction pump is driven water is sucked into the surging tank preventing the loss of suction pressure and accordingly the check valve configured at the suction port is opened and the lower treatment water is drawn in order to prevent the sludge from flowing into the interfacial layer of the lower sludge of the batch reactor the suspended solids meter is positioned to be 200 to 400 mm lower than the end of the inlet configured in the lower part of the buoyancy control buoyant fluid but configured to descend together with the buoyancy control buoyant fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101131116-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a closed cylinder portion 100 coupled to the lower side of the groundwater protection part a piezoelectric tube 210 installed at one side to prevent the groundwater from expanding due to internal pressure generated when the groundwater rises is coupled to one side of the piezoelectric pipe the other side is coupled to the plate check valve sand filter 220 for filtering the sand contained in the groundwater plate check valve 230 is coupled to one side of the sand filter the other side is coupled to the meter to prevent the groundwater filtered by the sand filter backflow a meter 240 coupled to one side of the plate check valve and the other side coupled to a pressure gauge a pressure gauge 250 coupled to one side of the meter and coupled to a three way valve on the other side a three way valve 260 coupled to the pressure gauge to form a flow path in the direction of the emergency water supply pipe 600 or the water supply pipe 700 an underground water level protection hole 200 including an underground water level protection column 270 formed along an inner circumference to prevent freezing waves it is configured to include and the controller 500 for supplying power to the underground water protection unit if the temperature is below the set temperature the controller 500 a temperature sensor 510 for detecting the ambient temperature a temperature setting unit 520 for setting a reference temperature for supplying power to the ground water protection protection vessel a memory unit 530 for storing the reference temperature set by the temperature setting unit a power supply unit 540 for supplying power to the ground water protection protection line a temperature comparison unit 550 for comparing the temperature sensed by the temperature sensor with the reference temperature stored in the memory unit a power supply signal transmitter 560 for transmitting a power supply signal to a power supply unit when the temperature compared by the temperature comparison unit is less than a reference temperature freezing prevention comprising a central control unit 570 for controlling the signal flow between the temperature sensor the temperature setting unit the memory unit the power supply unit the temperature comparison unit the power supply signal transmission unit and groundwater upper protection device capable of underwater discharge sterilization treatment"}, {"pat_id": "US-12168860-B2", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "the aquifer check valves 225 are preferably 1 inch to 2 inches set preferably at two foot four foot or ten foot intervals or the like along the production string 220 within the aquifer portion 245 and comprise small check valves which only allow water to flow one way or the like"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2926400-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it is attached to the front side to remove the sediment accumulated in the intake garden 7 regularly or irregularly and to reduce the water level in the closed intake well 20 indicated by the water level detector 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446279-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "another problem in the conventional water fountain device is that when the foreign substance is filtered water is supplied to the fountain and the foreign body is filtered by the water sprayed out of the fountain by the children are curiosity and fun to the body of water flow from the fountain there was also a problem that the skin contact with water caused by the microorganisms remaining in the filtered water causes skin diseases.the present invention devised in view of the above described problems the present invention is to filter the foreign substances contained in the water by pumping the water to reduce the pollution of the water the foreign substances are removed and filtered water by sterilizing the filtered water using ozone it is to provide a fractional filtration system to prevent skin diseases caused by.an object of the present invention is to provide a filtration system for a fountain the control means of the pump means according to the power supply and level detection and the control means capable of automatic and manual switching operation pump means connected to the control means for circulating water water level sensing means for sensing the water level of the water and transferring the detected signal to the control means a flexible pipe installed between the pump means and the conveying pipe to easily change the direction of the pump means a conveying pipe for conveying the pumped water from the pump means a check valve provided on the conveying pipe to prevent backflow of water introduced by the pump means filter means installed on a pipe of the transfer pipe to filter foreign substances an ozone sterilizer for sterilizing the water collected by the filter means a diverting pipe for diverting the water supply direction to clean the filter means it is achieved by a filtration system for a fountain characterized in that it comprises an electric valve installed on the transfer pipe and the direction change pipe to control the water supply direction to switch.this invention is designed to reduce the contamination of water by filtering the foreign substances contained in the water by pumping the water sterilizing the filtered water using ozone to prevent skin diseases caused by the filtered water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200494191-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a first coagulation tank 42 and a second coagulation tank 43 having stirrers 42 and 43 to react with the chemicals mixed in the mixing tank 41 to form a precipitate the pressurized floating tank 50 includes a sludge removal unit 51 provided with a floating sludge removal device 53 on the upper portion to remove the floating sludge floating on the water by air bubbles and a discharge unit from which the treated water from which the floating sludge is removed is discharged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100768328-B1", "para_id": "para_122", "text": "therefore even if rainwater present in the soil around the underground reservoir 10 further penetrates underground or evaporates due to a subsequent drought the water inside the underground reservoir 10 does not penetrate or evaporate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100768328-B1", "para_id": "para_141", "text": "when the body yield is reduced the water level when water flows into the external reservoir 119 from the outside is reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101890574-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "the decanter apparatus 1000 may further include a power supply unit 1010 for supplying power to the decanter apparatus 1000 and the power supply unit 1010 may include a decanter lifting apparatus 1500 a check valve 1110 the control valve 1160 the water level check device 1800 the decanter pump 1700 and the motor operated valve 1600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101172085-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "low quality high tds water may also be fed to solenoid or other control valve 162 along line 150 and connected to untreated water storage tank 168 along lines 164 and 166"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101212327-B1", "para_id": "para_95", "text": "while the present invention has been particularly shown and described with reference to exemplary embodiments thereof it is evident that many alternatives modifications and variations will be apparent to those skilled in the art.1 bulkhead 10 electrolysis device 20 chlorine injection pipe 30 check valve 40 on off valve 100 pressurization device 110 open tank 111 inlet pipe 112 inlet valve 120 water level sensor 130 pressure piping 140 pressure valve 150 sealed tank 160 pressure sensor 170 compressed air supply device a1 safety zone a2 explosion hazard zone b1 oil tank b2 ballast tank b3 pump room b4 fuel tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100805878-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "an elastic tubular body 11 which is installed in contact with the sewage pipe 1 adjacent to the river and forms a passage for discharging the fluid and installed on the outer periphery of the elastic pipe body and the river water level rises in order to block the reverse flow to press the elastic pipe to close the housing 10 to be coupled to the sewer pipe while wrapping the elastic pipe the elastic tubular body is installed on the pinch bar 21 which is installed inside the housing so as to be movable up and down from an outer circumference and the shaft bar 25 which is connected to the pinch bar while penetrating the inside and the outside of the housing while elevating along the level of the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100805878-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "however the existing flap valve has a problem in that when the amount of sewage flowing from the sewage pipe is small that is it is not easily opened at low flow rate causing head loss and enlarging the inundation area and also preventing the valve from closing due to foreign matter.therefore an object of the present invention is to solve such a problem a sewer buoy for effectively blocking the discharge and backflow of sewage by opening and closing the tube while lifting the ball along the water level is installed in the middle of the valve body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stormwater inflow tank 100 through which stormwater flows one end of the storm that is stored in the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 is connected to one side of the lower end of the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 and the other end is connected to the storm inflow reservoir 100 a sedimentation tank 200 connected through an initial storm inflow pipe 200a communicated with a central portion opposed to the first storm inflow pipe 200a to deposit foreign matter in the stormwater flowing through the initial storm inflow pipe 200a the filtration tank 200 is connected to the other side of the settling tank 200 through a filtration tank transfer pipe 300a and is connected to the lower portion of the one side of the settling tank 200 opposite to the other lower side of the settling tank 200 via the filtration tank transfer pipe 300a 310 for filtering the foreign substances in the rainwater conveyed from the water tank 200 and increasing the water level to a predetermined upward level a filtration tank 300 and is connected to the other central portion of the filtration tank 300 at the other side of the filtration tank 300 through a backwash water tank transfer pipe 400a and is connected to the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash water tank 400 through which the filtered water from the filtration tank 300 flows into the water tank 400a at a certain level is connected to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 through a discharge jaw delivery pipe 500a the filtrate discharged from the backwash water tank 400 is discharged to the outside via the piping 500a and the bypass pipe 100a is connected to the bypass pipe 100a in the case where the water level of the stormwater an excellent stormwater tank 500 through which stormwater flows the sedimentation tank 200 is disposed at a certain distance from the sedimentation tank 200 and is connected to the congestion water conveyance pipe 600a from the inside of the sedimentation tank 200 to selectively enter the sedimentation tank 200 a stagnant water storage tank 600 for discharging the stagnant water to the outside by extending the pipe 610 upwardly to be transferred to the vehicle through the vehicle transfer pipe 610 and the backwash water is selectively supplied from the backwash water tank 400 to the lower side of the filtration tank 300 so that the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 are backwashed by the backwash water and backwashing means for supplying air back into the filtration tank 300 to perform backwashing of the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 by backwash air the backwashing means may be configured to perform backwashing by the backwash water and then backwash with backwash air a sedimentation water drainage pump 710 disposed at the center of the bottom of the sedimentation tank 200 for selectively pumping sedimentation water in the sedimentation tank 200 to be transported to the congestion water storage tank 600 via the congestion water delivery pipe 600a wow a filtration trap water delivery pipe 210 provided on a drainage groove 210 that is downwardly recessed on one side of the bottom of the settling tank 200 and communicates with one side of the lower end of the filtration tank 300 which is conveyed from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side during the opening operation of the check valve 722 formed at the end of the filtration stagnant water transfer pipe 721 via the inlet 721 a filtration water drainage pump 720 for pumping water to be sent to the congestion water storage tank 600 the water level in the drainage groove 210 of the sedimentation tank 200 is detected so as to be sent to the stagnant water storage tank 600 and the sediment stagnant water and the filtered stagnant water are delivered to the stagnant water storage tank 600 a sedimentation tank water level sensor 730 for selectively activating the sedimentation water discharge pump 710 and the filtration water discharge pump 720 until detection the sedimentation tank water drain pump 710 is operated when the level of the sedimentation tank 200 is above the central portion of the sedimentation tank 200 during backwashing by the backwash water washing water level sensor 740 for transferring an excess amount of the backwash water into the stagnant water storage tank 600 a backwash water transfer pipe not shown connected to the backwash water supply pipe 753 provided in the lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 a backwash pump 750 for selectively supplying backwash water for backwash to the filtration tank 300 via the backwash water tank 400 through the backwash water tank 751 the filtration tank 300 is provided at a lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 and is disposed above the backwash water supply pipe 753 and selectively supplied with backwash air from the outside to supply air to the filtration tank 300 a backwashing air supply pipe 810 for upwardly floating the filtered suspended solids in the filter quartz layer 310 while moving upward from a lower portion of the filter quartz layer 310 the suspended solids suspended in the upper portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 are transferred from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 by the backwash air supplied through the backwash air supply pipe 810 one end of which is connected to one side of the upper part of the filter element layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 the other side is connected to the central part of one side of the settling tank 200 and the other end is selectively a backwash floating transfer pipe 820 having a check valve 821 for guiding a suspended material from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through an air transfer pipe 831 and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through the air transfer pipe 831"}]</data>
