  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10612227-B2", "para_id": "para_231", "text": "the storm water management system 100 can be sealed to prevent the accumulated storm water from entering infiltrating the underlying surface 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102240856-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method according to claim 1 the non point pollutant reduction facility a back washing water supply unit for washing the filter media by using the filtered water introduced into the back washing tank as back washing water and a backwashing means including a backwashing means for discharging the backwashing water after washing the filter media to the outside of the treatment structure further comprising the reverse wash water supply unit a first pump installed on the bottom of the backwashing tank and including a backwash water supply pipe connected to the discharge portion side of the first pump the backwash supply pipe extends to an upper side of the filtration tank while branching in a plurality so as not to interfere with the lifting operation unit of the filtering means and the first filter plate and the first filter plate on the backwash supply pipe extending to the upper side of the filtration tank"}]</data>
