  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-4383892-A", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in an apparatus for lifting evaporating and storing of water on a cyclic basic a vacuum chamber located at an elevation above a body of poluted water and having a double connection to the body of water and operating on fluxuations in pressure in the vacuum chamber to keep the concentration of polutants low with means in one connection assisting the flow of water into the vacuum chamber and means in the other connection assisting the return flow to the body of water the elevation of the vacuum chamber above the body of water being greater than water can be lifted by a vacuum as water without boiling it ejector means connected to the vacuum chamber above the boiling level to create the vacuum and direct the resulting vapor through a check valve to a condenser where the vapor is converted to distilled water means directing part of the distilled water through another check valve to where it is confined in the heating system and heated to a high temperature and pressure while confined between the last check valve and the ejector relief valve until it is released by it s own internal pressure with a blast that is directed into the ejector where it creates the vacuum in the vacuum chamber to start another cycle excess distilled water is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101396233-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the spring is absorbed by the spring acting on the stirring wing to prevent the stirring wing from being damaged and the lifting plate is caused to behave by the spring deformed by the absorbed force and the water is automatically supplied by the measured value there is a purpose to be able.in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a fueling apparatus for an axial flow resource in which an axial feeder for feeding axial feed to one side of a stirring vessel is provided and an extrusion molding device is installed on one side of a lower portion of the stirring vessel a water channel 33 is formed inside the stirring shaft 31 and a water channel 33 is formed in the inside of the stirring blade 32"}, {"pat_id": "US-7157011-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "blower 71 provides air or another active gas via feed pipeline 73 to waste water line 77 which running to conduit 44"}]</data>
