ace between the pair of installation tables 33 the heating unit 50 a rectangular shaped body 51 with an open upper surface a heater 52 installed on one side of the main body 51 and installed to have a predetermined length in a horizontal direction including in the body 51 a temperature sensor 53 for detecting the temperature of the thermal medium stored therein and an inlet and outlet pipe 54 for supplying heat medium oil to the inside of the body 51 or discharging the inside heat medium oil to the outside is provided the heating unit 50 it is installed horizontally along the middle part of the bottom surface of the inner housing 20 and is integrally fixed by welding the air exhaust unit 60 it is configured so that the air and moisture inside the inner housing 20 are discharged together the air supply unit 70 compressor 71 for generating compressed air a flow path 72 connected to the compressor 71 and a plurality of injection nozzles connected to the flow path 72 and supplying compressed air to the inside of the inner housing 20 including between the injection nozzle and the flow path 72 food characterized in that a check valve 73 is installed to allow compressed air to be discharged toward the inner housing 20 and to block moisture inside the inner housing 20 from being discharged through the flow path 72"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902009-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a combined maintenance management system for an offshore plant cooling sea water piping using seawater as cooling water the complex maintenance management system of the offshore plant cooling seawater pipeline includes a inhibits and kills the growth of seafood and other marine life in seawater through hypochlorous acid hocl b preventing corrosion of the piping by an external power supply cathode system with an insoluble anode on the inside of the pipe c a multi channel power supply device for supplying a method current a sea water box provided with a filter for introducing seawater a cooler a condenser a plurality of pipelines a seawater electrolyzer for adjusting the concentration of hypochlorous acid seawater boxes piping and seawater electrolysis devices the plurality of pipelines a first pipe connecting the sea water box and the seawater electrolytic device a second pipe connecting the outlet and the condenser a third pipe connecting the one end of the second pipe and the seawater electrolytic device a fourth pipe connected from one side of the third pipe to the sea water box a fifth pipe connected from one side of the fourth pipe to the condenser and a sixth pipe connecting the plurality of coolers a check valve is provided on one side of the plurality of pipes the check valve one side of the pipeline flowing out from the sea water box one side flowing into the sea water box from the sea water electrolytic apparatus one side of the piping divided into three quarters after flowing out from the sea water box one side of the piping through which the cooler s seawater flows a side of a pipeline through which seawater flows in and out of a cooler a side of a pipeline through which seawater flows into the condenser and a pipeline through which seawater flows out from the condenser and one side of the one side of the piping through which the seawater flows out from the condenser and one side of the piping leading to the sea water electrolysis device out of which the seawater flows out from the condenser the seawater electrolytic apparatus includes an analysis component for analyzing the degree of seawater seafood and bacteria capture a determination component for measuring and determining the concentration of hypochlorous acid produced by the power supply of the power supply a control arrangement for regulating the intensity of the received electric power a generating structure for generating hypochlorous acid an inlet through which seawater flows and an outlet through which seawater is discharged in order to determine the concentration of hypochlorous acid the ph and temperature of seawater are measured simultaneously d a seawater inflow step to inflow external seawater the seawater flowing in the seawater inflow step flows along the piping a pumping step of pumping the seawater flowing in the seawater inflow step so as to flow along the pipeline supplying a current to the pipeline through which the seawater flows in the seawater flow stage using a power supply device a step of collecting the flowing seawater when the seawater flowing through the seawater box flows through the pipeline after the seawater flow step a step performed after the seawater collection step the hypochlorous acid measurement step of measuring hypochlorous acid contained in the collected seawater based on the measurement result of the hypochlorous acid measurement step a current adjustment step of adjusting the current supplied in the seawater electrolytic apparatus so that the hypochlorous acid concentration of the seawater discharged from the seawater electrolytic apparatus does not exceed the environmental standard of 0.2 ppm a seawater discharge step of discharging the seawater into which the concentration of hypochlorous acid has been converted according to the current regulation through the current regulating step from the seawater electrolytic apparatus and the seawater is completely discharged to the outside of the hull or the like after the seawater flow step the pumping step the method potential supply step and the seawater discharge step of the seawater electrolytic device is performed wherein the cooling is performed in the course of the step of cooling the marine plant cooling water line"}]</data>
