  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101673421-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "rainwater gardens installed on roads an excellent line which is a division space formed by the order means and is linearly installed along the road at the lower part of the rainwater receiver a plurality of distribution blocks for supporting the space of the storm line and enabling storm drainage in the space sewer or grate network and a network connection pipe connecting the space and the network and having a check valve wherein the network connector is connected to the network through a sewer manhole of the network wherein the plurality of flow blocks are formed in a rectangular parallelepiped shape and have holes in the rectangular parallelepiped and a wall surface so that rainwater can flow freely in all directions the excellent line manhole is installed in the excellent line space where the network connection pipe is installed"}, {"pat_id": "US-4523875-A", "para_id": "para_57", "text": "1 and 2 a check valve 82 is installed in the manhole structure 70 to prevent backup problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977960-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a stormwater inflow tank 100 through which stormwater flows one end of the storm that is stored in the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 is connected to one side of the lower end of the stormwater inflow storm reservoir 100 and the other end is connected to the storm inflow reservoir 100 a sedimentation tank 200 connected through an initial storm inflow pipe 200a communicated with a central portion opposed to the first storm inflow pipe 200a to deposit foreign matter in the stormwater flowing through the initial storm inflow pipe 200a the filtration tank 200 is connected to the other side of the settling tank 200 through a filtration tank transfer pipe 300a and is connected to the lower portion of the one side of the settling tank 200 opposite to the other lower side of the settling tank 200 via the filtration tank transfer pipe 300a 310 for filtering the foreign substances in the rainwater conveyed from the water tank 200 and increasing the water level to a predetermined upward level a filtration tank 300 and is connected to the other central portion of the filtration tank 300 at the other side of the filtration tank 300 through a backwash water tank transfer pipe 400a and is connected to the backwash water tank transfer pipe a backwash water tank 400 through which the filtered water from the filtration tank 300 flows into the water tank 400a at a certain level is connected to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 opposite to the other central portion of the backwash water tank 400 through a discharge jaw delivery pipe 500a the filtrate discharged from the backwash water tank 400 is discharged to the outside via the piping 500a and the bypass pipe 100a is connected to the bypass pipe 100a in the case where the water level of the stormwater an excellent stormwater tank 500 through which stormwater flows the sedimentation tank 200 is disposed at a certain distance from the sedimentation tank 200 and is connected to the congestion water conveyance pipe 600a from the inside of the sedimentation tank 200 to selectively enter the sedimentation tank 200 a stagnant water storage tank 600 for discharging the stagnant water to the outside by extending the pipe 610 upwardly to be transferred to the vehicle through the vehicle transfer pipe 610 and the backwash water is selectively supplied from the backwash water tank 400 to the lower side of the filtration tank 300 so that the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 are backwashed by the backwash water and backwashing means for supplying air back into the filtration tank 300 to perform backwashing of the filtration tank 300 and the settling tank 200 by backwash air the backwashing means may be configured to perform backwashing by the backwash water and then backwash with backwash air a sedimentation water drainage pump 710 disposed at the center of the bottom of the sedimentation tank 200 for selectively pumping sedimentation water in the sedimentation tank 200 to be transported to the congestion water storage tank 600 via the congestion water delivery pipe 600a wow a filtration trap water delivery pipe 210 provided on a drainage groove 210 that is downwardly recessed on one side of the bottom of the settling tank 200 and communicates with one side of the lower end of the filtration tank 300 which is conveyed from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side during the opening operation of the check valve 722 formed at the end of the filtration stagnant water transfer pipe 721 via the inlet 721 a filtration water drainage pump 720 for pumping water to be sent to the congestion water storage tank 600 the water level in the drainage groove 210 of the sedimentation tank 200 is detected so as to be sent to the stagnant water storage tank 600 and the sediment stagnant water and the filtered stagnant water are delivered to the stagnant water storage tank 600 a sedimentation tank water level sensor 730 for selectively activating the sedimentation water discharge pump 710 and the filtration water discharge pump 720 until detection the sedimentation tank water drain pump 710 is operated when the level of the sedimentation tank 200 is above the central portion of the sedimentation tank 200 during backwashing by the backwash water washing water level sensor 740 for transferring an excess amount of the backwash water into the stagnant water storage tank 600 a backwash water transfer pipe not shown connected to the backwash water supply pipe 753 provided in the lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 a backwash pump 750 for selectively supplying backwash water for backwash to the filtration tank 300 via the backwash water tank 400 through the backwash water tank 751 the filtration tank 300 is provided at a lower portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 and is disposed above the backwash water supply pipe 753 and selectively supplied with backwash air from the outside to supply air to the filtration tank 300 a backwashing air supply pipe 810 for upwardly floating the filtered suspended solids in the filter quartz layer 310 while moving upward from a lower portion of the filter quartz layer 310 the suspended solids suspended in the upper portion of the filtration layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 are transferred from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 by the backwash air supplied through the backwash air supply pipe 810 one end of which is connected to one side of the upper part of the filter element layer 310 of the filtration tank 300 the other side is connected to the central part of one side of the settling tank 200 and the other end is selectively a backwash floating transfer pipe 820 having a check valve 821 for guiding a suspended material from the filtration tank 300 to the settling tank 200 side and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through an air transfer pipe 831 and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through the air transfer pipe 831"}]</data>
