tling tank 200 side and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through an air transfer pipe 831 and is connected to the backwash air supply pipe 810 through the air transfer pipe 831"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a permanent drainage material installed above the foundation construction reference plane and collecting groundwater that has infiltrated the foundation construction reference plane the foundation layer is provided above the foundation construction standard plane where the above permanent drainage material is provided and forms the foundation of the building a permanent drainage collection well provided at a predetermined location in the above mentioned foundation layer and providing a space for storing groundwater collected by the above mentioned permanent drainage material an architectural wall formed along the perimeter of the above mentioned foundation layer and extending in all directions to form the wall surface of the basement of the above mentioned building a facility pipe that is connected to a pump placed in the above mentioned permanent drainage sump and has the other end extended to the top of the building wall a storage block section including at least one storage block which is provided to be buried in the ground outside the above mentioned building wall and provides a space in which groundwater pumped from the permanent drainage collection well is temporarily stored before being returned to the ground layer a check valve provided at the other end of the above mentioned facility pipe to prevent pumped groundwater from flowing back toward the permanent drainage collection well a connecting pipe that is connected to the other end of the above mentioned equipment pipe and extends the other end into the storage block section to form a path for pumped groundwater to flow into the storage block section a reduction unit that is installed to be buried in the ground outside the above mentioned building wall and receives groundwater stored in the above mentioned storage block and returns it to the ground layer and a groundwater recovery system using a permanent drainage method for a building that is capable of being maintained and connected to a rainwater treatment facility including a discharge pipe that is connected at one end to the storage block section and at the other end to a rainwater treatment facility and forms a path for groundwater stored in the storage block section to be delivered to the rainwater treatment facility"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "1 to 3 a groundwater reduction system 100 using a building permanent drainage method with improved applicability according to one embodiment of the present invention may include a permanent drainage material d a foundation layer b a permanent drainage collection well p a building wall w a facility pipe 110 a check valve 120 a connecting pipe 130 a storage block section 140 a reduction section 150 a discharge pipe 160 and or a rainwater treatment facility f"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102907598-B1", "para_id": "para_91", "text": "according to the groundwater reduction system 100 by the permanent drainage method of a building linked to a rainwater treatment facility f with improved operational stability according to an embodiment of the present invention which includes a permanent drainage material d a foundation layer b a permanent drainage sump p a building wall w a facility pipe 110 a check valve 120 a connecting pipe 130 a storage block section 140 a reduction section 150 a discharge pipe 160 and or a rainwater treatment facility f the installation efficiency and economy can be improved through linkage with various rainwater treatment facilities f and there is an effect of preventing performance degradation of the system 100 and securing continuous operational stability through effective maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101619868-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the outdoor fire fighting box a control unit 8 for managing the operation of the firefighting box 100 as a whole an on off valve 2 for automatically injecting the fire fighting water upon opening a pressure gauge unit 6 connected to the transfer pipe 20 for spraying water for spraying water and for checking internal pressure changes is provided and the internal pressure state of the opening a pressure chamber 4 for transmitting the pressure to the pressure chamber 4 the control unit 8 controls the pressure change state of the pressure chamber 4 in real time so that the open close valve 2 operates by the control signal of the control unit 8 at the time of the pressure change in the pressure chamber 4 due to the operation a rotary motor 10 a pump 18 for allowing the fire water flowing through the connection pipe 12 to flow through the transfer pipe 20 at a high pressure by the rotation of the rotary motor 10 a fire hose 32 provided on the transfer pipe 20 for injecting a high pressure fire water for opening the opening closing valve 2 a rainwater receiver 28 for storing rainwater is installed on the ground and a check valve 30 for preventing foreign matter from entering the rainwater receiver 28 is provided at a lower portion of the rainwater receiver 28 a water storage tank 22 for storing the water for fire fighting and supplying the stored water for fire into the fire box 100 through the connection pipe 12 and a power generation unit 14 that supplies power to the fire fighting cabinet 100 by installing a self power generation facility among at least one of power generation using fossil fuel and solar power generation installed outside the control unit 8 checks the pressure in the pressure chamber 4 changed by the opening of the opening and closing valve 2 and operates the rotary motor 10 so that the fire fighting water is automatically injected into the fire hose 32 removable outdoor fire fighting cabinet"}]</data>
</edge>
