  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100561191-B1", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "in order to prevent leakage of the supplied hydraulic pressure the connection part of the housing connection part and the hydraulic pipe may further include a means for arbitrarily adjusting a check valve or opening and closing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100273822-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the water pipe 14 of the water intake well 12 the water meter 14 for displaying the feed amount of the raw water control valve 15 for adjusting the discharge of raw water a check valve 16 for discharging raw water in the pipe 19 in only one direction a pressure gauge 26 displaying hydraulic pressure in the pipe 19 an air valve 25 for discharging air remaining in the pipe 19 or when raw water is pumped from the pumping means 18 and a reverse circulation line 27 for backflowing the remaining raw water in the pipe 19 to the pumping means 18 to prevent freezing when raw water is not being pumped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "64 a disk valve 66 for opening and closing the water passage 61a of the valve housing 61 is selectively installed while moving up and down and is elastic between the disk valve 66 and the elastic member support frame 62"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101063950-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "on the other hand the present invention in the case of a general low cost submersible motor pump 3 is not provided with a check valve for preventing the backflow of water in the water supply pipe 12 is automatically prevented backflow and at the same time the stop of the pumping device 5 water remaining in the water supply pipe 20 the groundwater meter 21 the branching pipe 22 and the hydraulic pressure meter 23 which are components passes through the inside of the submersible motor pump 3 while passing through the water supply pipe 4 the total amount of water drained to 1 prevents freezing of the freezing wave thus eliminating the need for the electronic residual water automatic drainage device 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101680010-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "that is in the conventional case when the check valve structure includes a nonmetallic material such as rubber it can not withstand repetitive shocks and easily breaks to cause leakage and the check valve made of a metal material has an internal check function there is a problem that the fluid is not accurately and smoothly operated due to strong impact of pneumatic and hydraulic pressure and malfunction occurs or partial leakage occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100899657-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "on the other hand a check valve 170 may be provided at one side of the pressure cylinder 152 to block the back flow of the produced water that has passed through the discharge port 145 of the valve housing 142.the reverse osmosis wastewater treatment backpressure pump according to the present invention configured as described above is configured such that the piston is easily moved in the storage space of the valve housing by the operation of a pressurizing cylinder that receives pneumatic pressure or hydraulic pressure to overcome the water pressure applied to the filter portion thereby providing a pressure capable of easily reversing the production water"}]</data>
