  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-4306968-A", "para_id": "para_52", "text": "this lifting force has been found to be of such a nature and the sewage lifted so high that it tends to break down into a spray form comprised of multitudes of small bubbles and widely separated particles into which the applied air supplies oxygen by infusion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102895527-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "in addition the buffer support guide airtight tube is further provided with a water leakage prevention protection means and the water leakage prevention protection means comprises an inner elastic airtight tube fitted while wrapping around the buffer support guide airtight tube an outer elastic airtight tube fitted while wrapping around the inner elastic airtight tube connected to the buffer support guide airtight tube a water leakage filling space formed between the inner elastic airtight tube and the outer elastic airtight tube a buffer protection support tube fitted while wrapping around the outer elastic airtight tube operating support grooves formed on the inner surface of the outer elastic airtight tube arranged while wrapping around the inner elastic airtight tube an elevation guide support part connected and fixed to the operating support groove formed on the outer elastic airtight tube and supporting the inner elastic airtight tube a position detection sensor connected and fixed to the inner elastic airtight tube connected to the buffer support guide airtight tube one end of which is connected and fixed to the inner surface of the outer elastic airtight tube and the other end of which is connected and fixed to the inner surface of the outer elastic airtight tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654508-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "second the upper swash plate unit and the lower swash plate unit are provided and the lower swash plate unit is selectively rotatable such that the lower swash plate unit is inclined at a predetermined angle with respect to the upper end in the vertical state thereby selectively blocking the supply of the minute bubbles into the precipitation the sludge can be guided in an oblique direction to induce sedimentation thereby maximizing the sedimentation efficiency of the sludge.brief description of the drawings fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102508335-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a connection bracket screwed to and fixed to the connection bracket one end of which is screwed and fixed to the connection bracket and a rocking and vibration panel disposed in the water while maintaining a level with the bottom surface of the electrolysis tank and formed on the rocking and vibration panel circulation and electrolysis structure characterized in that the vibration and vibration panel is moved up and down while the vibration and vibration panel is moved up and down by the driving of the lifting cylinder"}, {"pat_id": "US-4383892-A", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in an apparatus for lifting evaporating and storing of water on a cyclic basic a vacuum chamber located at an elevation above a body of poluted water and having a double connection to the body of water and operating on fluxuations in pressure in the vacuum chamber to keep the concentration of polutants low with means in one connection assisting the flow of water into the vacuum chamber and means in the other connection assisting the return flow to the body of water the elevation of the vacuum chamber above the body of water being greater than water can be lifted by a vacuum as water without boiling it ejector means connected to the vacuum chamber above the boiling level to create the vacuum and direct the resulting vapor through a check valve to a condenser where the vapor is converted to distilled water means directing part of the distilled water through another check valve to where it is confined in the heating system and heated to a high temperature and pressure while confined between the last check valve and the ejector relief valve until it is released by it s own internal pressure with a blast that is directed into the ejector where it creates the vacuum in the vacuum chamber to start another cycle excess distilled water is stored"}, {"pat_id": "US-11518666-B2", "para_id": "para_423", "text": "the input unit 270 may include an elevation input unit 271 for inputting an elevation command of the lifting cover 210 and a water ejection input unit 272 for inputting an opening and closing command of the water ejection valve 94"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102541418-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "the maintenance guide groove part 42 is separated from the manhole 20 by erecting the backflow and fall prevention combination pad member 50 while the lifting position limiting bracket 40 is fixed to the manhole 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101396233-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "the spring is absorbed by the spring acting on the stirring wing to prevent the stirring wing from being damaged and the lifting plate is caused to behave by the spring deformed by the absorbed force and the water is automatically supplied by the measured value there is a purpose to be able.in order to accomplish the above object the present invention provides a fueling apparatus for an axial flow resource in which an axial feeder for feeding axial feed to one side of a stirring vessel is provided and an extrusion molding device is installed on one side of a lower portion of the stirring vessel a water channel 33 is formed inside the stirring shaft 31 and a water channel 33 is formed in the inside of the stirring blade 32"}, {"pat_id": "US-11389756-B2", "para_id": "para_421", "text": "the input unit 270 may include an elevation input unit 271 for inputting an elevation command of the lifting cover 210 and a water ejection input unit 272 for inputting an opening and closing command of the water ejection valve 94"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an upstream side main water supply pipe 101 connected to a water supply source and provided with a water supply pump 130 a downstream side main water supply pipe 102 connected to the upstream side main water supply pipe 101 through a main on off valve 110 a sprinkler bridge 200 branched from the downstream main supply pipe 102 and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and a sprinkler head 300 installed at a lower end of the sprinkler double pipe 200 first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the main opening closing valve 110 respectively further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flow meters 510 520 respectively installed at an inlet end and an outlet end of the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 a drain pipe 600 connected to the sprinkler bridge pipe 200 through the three way valve 610 and provided with a drain pipe meter 620 between the second sprinkler bridge pipe flow meter 520 and the sprinkler head 300 lt rti the main on off valve 110 includes a valve body 111 connected to the upstream main supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 a valve cap 112 covering the upper portion of the valve body 111 a valve seat 116 formed in the valve body 111 an opening closing plate 117 installed in the valve body 111 to open and close the valve seat 116 a lifting and lowering rod 118 coupled to an upper end of the nut 117 and a nut box 119 screwed to the lifting and lowering rod 118 and an opening and closing drive means 120 for rotating the nut box 119 including the valve cap 112 includes an elevation guide portion 113 for vertically supporting the elevating and lowering rod 118 a rotation support portion 114 for rotatably supporting the nut box 119 and a reinforcing connecting portion 115 connecting the portion 113 and the rotation supporting portion 114 the opening and closing drive means 120 includes a drive motor 123 mounted on a motor mount 122 fixed to a support plate 121 integrally formed with the rotary support 114 and a driven gear 126 coupled to an upper end of the nut box 119 and engaged with the driving gear 125 the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 and the first and second sprinkler pipe flowmeters 410 and 420 are controlled by controlling the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 according to the detection signals of the water discharge pipes 510 and 520 and the discharge pipe flow meter 620 and a control means 700 the control means 700 includes a fire detector 710 installed on the building an input unit 720 for inputting the normal mode and the test mode a main opening closing valve sensor 730 for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve 110 the sprinkler opening closing valve 210 and the 3 way valve 610 according to the fire detection signal of the fire detector 710 and the input signal of the input unit 720 the flow rate of the refrigerant is detected on the upstream side in accordance with the sensing signals of the first and second main supply pipe flow meters 410 and 420 the first and second sprinkler pipe flow meters 510 and 520 the drain pipe flow meter 620 it is possible to judge the abnormality of the main water supply pipe 101 and the downstream main water supply pipe 102 the sprinkler discharge pipe 200 and the water discharge pipe 600 to determine an abnormality position display command and an alarm command a control unit 740 for outputting a command to display the degree of opening of the main on off valve 110 a valve driver 750 for sending a driving signal to the main on off valve 110 the sprinkler on off valve 210 and the three way valve 610 according to a control command of the controller 740 a display unit 760 for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the controller 740 and an alarm unit 770 for outputting an alarm according to an alarm command of the control unit 740 in case the water supply through the upstream main water pipe 101 the downstream main water pipe 102 and the sprinkler pipe 200 is not normally performed because the main on off valve 110 is not opened normally a bypass means for bypassing the upstream main supply pipe 101 to the downstream main supply pipe 102 without passing through the main opening closing valve 110 and supplying water to the sprinkler head 300 through the sprinkler pipe 200 800 lt rti gt the bypass unit 800 includes an upstream bypass pipe 810 connected to the upstream main water pipe 101 a downstream bypass pipe 820 connected to the downstream main supply pipe 102 and a water pressure responsive on off valve 900 installed between the upstream side bypass pipe 810 and the downstream side bypass pipe 820 and opened and closed in accordance with the water pressure of the extinguishing water the hydraulic pressure on off valve 900 includes an upstream valve body 910 connected to the upstream bypass pipe 810 and having a cylindrical upstream side internal space 911 a downstream valve body 910 connected to the downstream bypass pipe 820 a downstream valve body 920 connected to the upstream side internal space 911 and having a cylindrical downstream side internal space 921 communicating with the upstream side internal space 911 a valve cone 940 which is installed in the longitudinal direction inside the upstream side internal space 911 and the downstream side internal space 921 to open and close the valve seat portion 930 and a valve spring 950 for elastically supporting the valve cone 940 toward the valve seat portion 930 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101753809-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "sensing switch.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided an air conditioning system comprising an upstream main water supply pipe connected to a water supply source and having a water supply pump a downstream main water supply pipe connected to the upstream main water supply pipe through a main on a sprinkler multistage pipe branched from the downstream main supply pipe and provided with a sprinkler opening closing valve first and second main water supply flowmeters respectively installed at the inflow end and the outflow end of the main opening closing valve and a sprinkler head installed at the lower end of the sprinkler multi branch pipe the sprinkler system according to claim 1 further comprising first and second sprinkler multi stage pipe flowmeters installed at the inlet and outlet ends of the sprinkler opening closing valve respectively and connected to the sprinkler multi wherein the main on off valve includes a valve body connected to the upstream main supply pipe and the downstream main supply pipe a valve cap covering the upper portion of the valve body a lifting screw rod coupled to an upper end of the opening closing plate a nut box screwed to the lifting lowering rod and an opening closing drive means for rotating the nut box wherein the valve cap supports the lifting lowering rod so as to be movable up and down a rotation support portion for rotatably supporting the nut box and a reinforcing connection portion for connecting the elevation guide portion and the rotation support portion wherein the opening and closing drive means is fixed to the support plate integrally formed with the rotation support portion a drive gear fixed to a motor shaft of the drive motor and a driven gear coupled to an upper end of the nut box and engaged with the drive gear a sprinkler opening closing valve a three way valve and an upstream side main water supply pipe and a downstream side main water supply pipe in accordance with detection signals of the first and second main water supply flowmeters first and second sprinkler multi and a control means for judging the presence or absence of abnormality of the multi branch pipe and the drain pipe and outputting an alarm wherein the control means is installed in the building and smoke detectors an input unit for inputting a normal mode and a test mode a main opening closing valve sensor for detecting opening closing degree of the main opening closing valve a sparkler opening closing valve and a 3 way valve according to a fire detection signal of the fire detector and an input signal of an input unit and outputs control commands to the first and second main water supply flow meters the first and second it is possible to determine the abnormality of the upstream main supply pipe downstream main supply pipe sprinkler discharge pipe and drain pipe according to the detection signal of the sprinkler flow meter drain pipe flow meter and main opening closing valve detector a controller for outputting a command for displaying the degree of opening of the main opening closing valve according to a detection signal of the detector a valve driving unit for sending a driving signal to the main opening closing valve the sprinkler opening closing valve and the three way valve according to a control command of the control unit a display unit for displaying an abnormal position according to an abnormal position display command of the control unit and an alarm unit for outputting an alarm in response to an alarm command of the control unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-6475395-B1", "para_id": "para_92", "text": "for example the level of liquid medium in the treatment tank may be lowered or if the diffusion elements are mounted in the tank in arrays on lifting means for lifting them from the liquid medium at least a portion of the diffusion elements may be raised to a higher submerged elevation in the medium using the lifting means"}, {"pat_id": "US-9873069-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "on account thereof pumps of a comparatively small constructive size with low drive power may be employed for the described object of lifting wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "therefore the ball top valve 35 of the embodiment shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "therefore in the filtration device of the second embodiment including the ball top valve 35 of the above embodiment when the level of rainwater filled in the upper portion of the horizontal blocking plate 31 is low or there is no rainwater the buoyant elevation part 353 descends the lifting valve plate 352 is lowered to block the lower portion of the vertical pipe 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102697803-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the above object is achieved by the present invention and according to one aspect of the present invention a water pipe freeze prevention device is provided comprising a water pipe a water faucet connected to the upper portion of the water pipe an opening closing handle for raising lowering an opening closing rod installed inside the water pipe and an antifreeze device mounted at the lower end of the water pipe for opening and closing the movement of tap water to the water pipe wherein the antifreeze device comprises a housing having a lower end communicated with the water pipe and an upper end communicated with the water pipe an outlet formed in the housing for discharging tap water contained in the water pipe to the outside and it is composed of an opening closing member mounted inside the housing to control tap water being conveyed to the faucet by the elevation of the opening closing rod so that when the tap water being conveyed to the faucet is blocked by the operation of the opening closing member tap water contained in the water pipe flows out to the outside through the outlet and the opening closing member is mounted at the lower end of the opening closing rod to prevent tap water from flowing out to the outside through the outlet when it is elevated the method comprises forming a step in the housing that is connected to the water pipe when the lower surface of the lifting valve is spaced from the step tap water is transferred to the water pipe when the lifting valve is in close contact with the step the tap water is blocked from being transferred to the water pipe a sunken cylindrical pinhole is formed on an outer surface located at the upper portion of the opening closing rod a connecting portion is formed at the lower portion of the opening closing handle into which an upper portion of the opening closing rod in which the cylindrical pinhole is formed is inserted a spring pin is mounted on the connecting portion so that the cylindrical surface of the spring pin is seated in the cylindrical pinhole so that the opening closing rod is moved up and down by the rotation of the opening closing handle the lifting valve is made of a rubber material and a valve body having a plurality of transfer holes through which tap water is transferred is formed the valve body is made of a metal material and is embedded in the valve body and is connected to the lower end of the opening closing rod by a screw thread and an upper ring and a lower ring in the shape of rings are formed on the outer surface of the valve body and a fin ring is additionally formed to protrude outwardly from the edge of the upper surface of the valve body so that the fin ring is in close contact with the inner surface of the housing and a fastening nut is additionally connected to the opening closing rod that is connected to the valve connecting portion by a screw so that the valve connecting portion and the opening closing rod are compressed and connected and the lower end of the water pipe is bent outwardly to form an expanded extension piece and a sealing ring is installed between the expansion piece and the housing and the sealing ring is in the shape of a ring and has a mounting protrusion formed on which the expansion piece is installed and a sealing projection that protrudes outwardly is formed on a portion that comes into contact with the housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102558746-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the control valve and the discharge fan receiving the signal from the detection sensor are driven to discharge the odor inside the sewer pipe to the outside thereby reducing the odor inside the sewer pipe the situation recognition operation guide means a connection fixing module unit that is screwed and fixed to the sewer pipe a pair of guide shafts having lower ends connected to and fixed to the upper surface of the connection fixing module unit a transfer module unit composed of a first panel transfer module a second panel transfer module and a third panel transfer module that are inserted through the guide shaft and guided along the guide shaft a first lift guide unit whose lower end is screwed and fixed to the upper surface of the connection fixing module unit and whose lower end is screwed and fixed to the lower surface of the first panel transfer module a second lift guide unit whose lower end is screwed and fixed to the upper surface of the first panel transfer module and whose lift shaft is screwed and fixed to the bottom surface of the second panel transfer module and whose lower end is screwed and fixed to the upper surface of the second lift guide unit a lifting guide portion comprising a third lifting guide unit having a strong shaft screwed to and fixed to the lower surface of the third panel transfer module the first rotation guide units screwed and fixed to the bottom surface of the first panel transfer module the first rotation module unit screwed to the rotation shaft the second rotation guide units to which the second panel transfer module is screwed and fixed to the bottom surface and the second rotation module unit to the rotation shaft and the third rotation guide unit composed of the third rotation guide units to which the third panel transfer module is screwed to the bottom surface and the third rotation module unit screwed to the rotation shaft a situation capturing unit composed of first situation capturing units screwed and fixed to the bottom surface of the first rotation module unit second situation recording units screwed and fixed to the bottom surface of the second rotation module unit and third situation recording units screwed and fixed to the bottom surface of the third rotation module unit a control unit that is screwed to and fixed to the connection fixing module unit is electrically connected to and controlled by the elevation guide unit and the rotation guide unit and receives photographing information of first situation capture units second situation capture units and third situation capture units transmitters and receivers screwed to and fixed to the third panel transfer module and transmitting photographing information of the first situation photographing units second situation photographing units and third situation photographing units transmitted from the control unit the method of constructing an eco friendly sewer odor reduction device characterized in that it is screwed and fixed to the third panel transfer module and consists of a status guide speaker that receives a signal from the control unit to guide a voice or generate an alarm"}, {"pat_id": "US-9587392-B2", "para_id": "para_98", "text": "the pump guide rail system is designed to easily allow the submersible pumps 22 to be removed from the pumping station 2 via a lifting chain or cable located at grade elevation and allow all pump service to be performed from outside of the pumping station 2"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102657628-B1", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "as the hole 65 is coupled to the fitting groove 75 the elevation of the lifting platform 60 due to water pressure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101889498-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide an elevating and reducing water producing apparatus provided with a disposable manufacturing container which can be conveniently used in replacement.the elevated water producing system according to the present invention comprises a main body to which the disposable container is detachably attached a support member vertically formed on the upper side of the main body and having a guide protruding in a vertical direction on the front side and a lifting member coupled to the guide so as to be movable up and down wherein a hollow portion formed in a rectangular shape and having a concave inner side is formed on an upper end front surface of the support member and a guide formed in the center of the space portion a sensor part having an orp sensor and a plurality of puncturing fins are provided at the tip of the elevating member and the puncturing pin penetrates through the sealing film of aluminum bonded to the upper side of the disposable container and the orp value measured by the sensor unit is displayed on a display unit formed on the main body and the sensor unit automatically raises the elevation member when the orp value reaches the set value thereby stopping the electrolysis as a technical feature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102638855-B1", "para_id": "para_120", "text": "monitoring unit 310"}, {"pat_id": "US-9855518-B2", "para_id": "para_42", "text": "a screen box sbx assembly in accordance with the present invention comprises an ultrafine screen a screen frame of flat plate and hollow tubing that incorporates air scouring at the lowest elevation of the screen the frame being sealed to prevent liquids and solids from bypassing the screen so all must pass through the screen a flexible discharge hose that may have swivel joints or may extend and compress in an accordion fashion to minimize forces on the screened decanter guiderails to define the vertical and horizontal movement of the invention a lifting device to raise and lower the invention in the liquid at controlled descent speed and multiple rise rates an effluent flow manifold with openings to allow liquid to flow to the screen from below the screen a deflector plate with drain ports an encoder to position the screen box in the tank to measure headloss and to insure the appropriate amount of screen is in contact with the wastewater a protective maintenance hood to backwash disinfect and thaw the screen controls sensors actuated valves modulating valve flow meter and in some cases a filtrate pump if required by the existing hydraulic gradient"}]</data>
</edge>
