  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100815578-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "3 pour secondary bottom concrete bc2 to the drainage channel 5 to the position and finally waterproof the inner surface of the drain trench 1 and then drain the drainage 5 apply mortar m while giving a gradient to the bottom and finally finish glazing 6 on the angle 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100758560-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the gradient precast trench structure block 100 located in the outer body of the block 100 when the block 100 is combined with another block 100 to form a trench structure the outside of the block 100 to prevent the inflow of dirt from the outside a stage 170 formed to secure the cover over the body a base portion 180 positioned at both lower ends of the outer body of the block 100 to increase the bondability with the cement placed on the floor where the block 100 is to be installed and fixed to install the block 100 a u shaped drainage portion 120 that performs a wastewater treatment so as not to leave residues and residual water at the bottom of the drainage path a drain pipe 160 for discharging wastewater flowing out of the drain 120 to a septic tank a drain pipe connection part 150 formed in an elliptic intaglio on one side of the bottom of the block 100 to discharge wastewater flowing out of the drain part 120 of the block 100 to the drain pipe 160 an embossed 191 formed on one side of the outer body of the block 100 to facilitate connection of the block 100 with another block 100 an intaglio 192 formed on an outer body of the block 100 on an opposite side of the embossment 191 and formed to facilitate connection between the block 100 and a counterpart block in combination with the embossment 191 it is coupled to the lower grooves on both sides of the connection portion of the block 100 100 through the attachment screw 210 and after the coupling of the block 100 and another block 100 in a trench structure to prevent shaking and bending a connection part 200 formed to easily install the trench structure wherein a connection part 200 supporting the block 100 when the trench structure is formed using the connection part 200 is formed on a bottom surface thereof the block 100 is modularized into 1m to 3m using the connection part 200 to connect two or more blocks 100 to form a trench structure and then embedded in cement installed at the installation location to shake the trench structure"}, {"pat_id": "US-11313755-B2", "para_id": "para_53", "text": "in some examples pipeline conditions determined and stored in block 802 above include but are not limited to pipeline internal diameter pipeline wall thickness pipeline material young s modulus pipeline length friction factor pipeline material type topography temperature gradient pressure gradient and unusual features if any"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "an inflow pipe 2 into which rainwater and sewage flow in a discharge pipe 4 for releasing some of the rainwater and sewage introduced into the inflow pipe and a collecting pipe 3 into which sewage including floating impurities is introduced from the inflow pipe and a overflow control device having a overflowware 1 arranged to block the collecting pipe and the inflow pipe from the discharge pipe a guide wall 7 interposed between the opening of the inflow pipe and the overflowware to raise a water surface in the vicinity to prevent a water gradient from the opening of the inflow pipe toward the overflowware the lower end of the guide wall is located below the upper end of the overflow wear the upper end is located above the upper end of the overflow wear the water surface control apparatus for drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "an inflow pipe 2 into which rainwater and sewage flow in a discharge pipe 4 for releasing some of the rainwater and sewage introduced into the inflow pipe and a collecting pipe 3 into which sewage including floating impurities is introduced from the inflow pipe and a overflow control device having a overflowware 1 arranged to block the collecting pipe and the inflow pipe from the discharge pipe a guide wall 7 interposed between the opening of the inflow pipe and the overflowware to raise a water surface in the vicinity to prevent a water gradient from the opening of the inflow pipe toward the overflowware the lower end of the guide wall is located below the upper end of the overflow wear the upper end is located above the upper end of the collection pipe the surface control apparatus for drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "therefore the dirt on the road surface is removed from the road by the initial rainfall so that the road surface is free of the dirt"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102423221-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "as an example the input space further includes a distribution block that is installed to protrude toward the top while crossing the center of the inlet to separate and partition the space and the bottom surfaces of both spaces partitioned by the distribution block are it is characterized in that a downward inclination gradient is formed toward each incision hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101026854-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as the bottom plate construction method for the prefabricated water tank placing and curing concrete in a formwork constructed to a size that can support the water tank to form a first base chipping the first base surface and forming a joint in the same shape as the water tank arranging and assembling the base frame to the first base surface in accordance with the joint seating an angle bent to be in close contact with the inner surface of the base frame and the first base surface coupling a fixing bolt having a support member embedded in the concrete of the second base to each fastening hole of the angle and the base frame is supported so as not to be pushed by hydraulic pressure and fastening the fixing support by fastening the fixing nut to the fixing bolt making a step fixing the angle fixed by the fastening support with a set bolt to a first base seating a drain portion of the same block as a drain box and a pipe for guiding drainage of water on an upper surface of the first foundation inside the base frame placing and curing concrete so as to be gradient in the direction of the drain portion in the base frame on which the drain portion is seated to form a second foundation separating a block of the drain portion in the second foundation and installing a plurality of polyethylene sheets so that the ends overlap the upper surface of the second foundation fixing the drain box and the polyethylene sheet by heat fusion in a state in which the drain box of the drain portion is seated on the second base from which the block is separated and a plurality of fastener mounting steps mounted on a second base to prevent the flow of the polyethylene sheet by contraction so as to fix the polyethylene sheet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102678778-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a body having a box shape with an installation space inside a mounting hole formed through the side and a cylindrical flange extending from the upper surface a manhole cover that is detachably coupled to the flange to open and close the installation space in communication with the inside of the flange and it includes a guide sleeve mounted on the mounting hole to guide the cable to the installation space an installation ring is formed on the upper and side surfaces of the body and a fixing groove is formed on the side of the body recessed to a certain depth along the circumferential direction of the side a drainage channel extends downward on the inner lower surface of the body and an inclined gradient is formed on the inner lower surface of the body toward the drainage channel a manhole installed at the lower part of the installation space and filtering foreign substances contained in the water flowing into the installation space and then intermittently discharging the purified water toward the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a cover seating end formed of a material and formed in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends of the trench body block in order to mount and fix the cover on the upper portion of the trench body block a drainage passage formed in a longitudinal direction in the inner center of the trench body block and integrally formed in a u shaped cross sectional shape from the cover seating end to drain rainwater or wastewater an embossed portion formed at one end of the trench body block and configured to fix a connection with the other end of the trench body block to be adjacently connected and a concave portion formed at the other end of the trench body block and configured to fix the connection in correspondence with the raised portions of the adjacent trench body block and the inner surface of the drainage passage formed in the u shaped cross sectional shape in order to suppress the generation of hydrogen sulfide gas by sulfate ions and microorganisms when decaying rainwater or sewage accumulated by the stagnant soil or residue inside the trench and to purify contaminants by the sustained release tio 2 photocatalyst alumina cement blast furnace a binder binder including slag powder nickel slag powder and silica sand a photocatalyst impregnated porous filler including zeolite powder pearlite powder feldspar powder and kaolinite powder in which the tio 2 photocatalyst is impregnated in the porous pores and water and a porous filter mortar layer cured by stacking a porous filter mortar including water is formed and the connection support fixing bracket includes a lower support portion for supporting lower ends of both ends of the adjacently connected trench body block both side support portions formed in a shape bent at a predetermined height at both ends of the lower support portion in the upper direction to surround both end side portions of the trench body block and a drainage level control member for adjusting the drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by integrally extending from both ends of the lower supporter in an outward direction of the both side supporters wherein the drainage level control member includes the lower supporter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an extension piece extending from a ball nut integrally formed with the extension piece and having a screw therein a ball screw coupled to the ball nut and rotated forward and backward to adjust a drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut a polymer using industrial by products having an easy drainage gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function comprising a support member supporting forward and reverse rotation while preventing the ball screw from sinking under the ball screw concrete precast drainage trench coupling system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0758560 registration date september 7 2007 in the gradient precast trench structure block 100 when a trench structure is formed by combining the block 100 with another block 100 by being located on the outer body of the block 100 the outside of the block 100 is step 170 formed to fix the cover on the upper body base portions 180 located at the lower ends of both sides of the outer body of the block 100 in order to increase the bonding property with the cement placed on the floor where the block 100 is to be installed and fixed to install and fix the block 100 a u shaped drain unit 120 that performs erroneous drainage treatment so as not to leave residue and residual water at the bottom of the drainage channel a drain pipe 160 for discharging the wastewater flowing from the drain 120 to a septic tank a drain pipe connection unit 150 for discharging wastewater flowing from the drain unit 120 of the block 100 to the drain pipe 160 by being formed in an oval shaped intaglio on one side of the bottom of the block 100 a relief 191 formed on one side of the outer body of the block 100 to facilitate connection between the block 100 and another block 100 an intaglio 192 that is located on the outer body of the block 100 on the opposite side of the embossed 191 and is combined with the embossed 191 to facilitate connection of the block 100 and the counter block it is coupled to the lower grooves on both sides of the connection portion of the block 100 100 through the attachment screw 210 and prevents shaking and bending after combining the block 100 and another block 100 in a trench structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "a cover seating end formed of a polymer concrete material and formed in a predetermined depth and length direction from both upper ends of the trench body block to seat and fix the cover on the upper portion of the trench body block a drainage passage formed in a longitudinal direction in the inner center of the trench body block and integrally formed in a u shaped cross sectional shape from the cover seating end to drain rainwater or wastewater an embossed portion formed at one end of the trench body block and configured to fix a connection with the other end of the trench body block to be adjacently connected and a concave portion formed at the other end of the trench body block and configured to fix the connection in correspondence with the raised portions of the adjacent trench body block and the inner surface of the drainage passage formed in the u shaped cross sectional shape in order to suppress the generation of hydrogen sulfide gas by sulfate ions and microorganisms when decaying rainwater or sewage accumulated by the stagnant soil or residue inside the trench and to purify contaminants by the sustained release tio 2 photocatalyst alumina cement blast furnace a binder binder including slag powder nickel slag powder and silica sand a photocatalyst impregnated porous filler including zeolite powder pearlite powder feldspar powder and kaolinite powder in which the tio 2 photocatalyst is impregnated in the porous pores and water and a porous filter mortar layer cured by stacking a porous filter mortar including water is formed and the connection support fixing bracket includes a lower support portion for supporting lower ends of both ends of the adjacently connected trench body block both side support portions formed in a shape bent at a predetermined height at both ends of the lower support portion in the upper direction to surround both end side portions of the trench body block and a drainage level control member for adjusting the drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by integrally extending from both ends of the lower supporter in an outward direction of the both side supporters wherein the drainage level control member includes the lower supporter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "an extension piece extending from a ball nut integrally formed with the extension piece and having a screw therein a ball screw coupled to the ball nut and rotated forward and backward to adjust a drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut polymer concrete precast drainage using industrial by products with enhanced drainage gradient and level adjustment including and a support member that supports forward and reverse rotation while preventing sinking of the ball screw under the ball screw"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "a cover seating end formed of a material and formed in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends of the trench body block in order to mount and fix the cover on the upper portion of the trench body block a drainage passage formed in a longitudinal direction in the inner center of the trench body block and integrally formed in a u shaped cross sectional shape from the cover seating end to drain rainwater or wastewater an embossed portion formed at one end of the trench body block and configured to fix a connection with the other end of the trench body block to be adjacently connected and a concave portion formed at the other end of the trench body block and configured to fix the connection in correspondence with the raised portions of the adjacent trench body block and the inner surface of the drainage passage formed in the u shaped cross sectional shape in order to suppress the generation of hydrogen sulfide gas by sulfate ions and microorganisms when decaying rainwater or sewage accumulated by the stagnant soil or residue inside the trench and to purify contaminants by the sustained release tio 2 photocatalyst alumina cement blast furnace a binder binder including slag powder nickel slag powder and silica sand a photocatalyst impregnated porous filler including zeolite powder pearlite powder feldspar powder and kaolinite powder in which the tio 2 photocatalyst is impregnated in the porous pores and water and a porous filter mortar layer cured by stacking a porous filter mortar including water is formed and the connection support fixing bracket includes a lower support portion for supporting lower ends of both ends of the adjacently connected trench body block both side support portions formed in a shape bent at a predetermined height at both ends of the lower support portion in the upper direction to surround both end side portions of the trench body block and a drainage level control member for adjusting the drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by integrally extending from both ends of the lower supporter in an outward direction of the both side supporters wherein the drainage level control member includes the lower supporter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "an extension piece extending from a ball nut integrally formed with the extension piece and having a screw therein a ball screw coupled to the ball nut and rotated forward and backward to adjust a drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut polymer concrete precast drainage using industrial by products with enhanced drainage gradient and level adjustment including and a support member that supports forward and reverse rotation while preventing sinking of the ball screw under the ball screw"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "3 the polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products in which the drainage gradient and level of the present invention are easily adjusted and the pollutant purification function is enhanced a plurality of trench body blocks 100 connected to each other having a cross section and a predetermined length in the connection portion where the plurality of trench body blocks 100 are adjacently connected connection support fixing brackets 200 for fixing and coupling while supporting the lower ends of both ends of the trench body blocks 100 connected adjacently however the trench body block 100 is formed of a polymer concrete material and a cover formed in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends 110 in order to mount and fix the cover on the top of the trench body block 100 a seating end 120 and a drainage passage 130 formed in a longitudinal direction in the inner center of the trench body block and integrally formed in a u shaped cross sectional shape from the cover seating end 120 to drain rainwater or sewage an embossed portion 140 formed at one end of the trench body block 100 and configured to secure a connection connection with the other end of the trench body block 100 to be adjacently connected and a concave portion 150 formed at the other end of the trench body block 100 and configured to fix the connection in correspondence with the raised portion 140 of the trench body block 100 connected to each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "the drainage level control member 230 includes an extension piece 231 extending from the lower support part 210 a ball nut 232 formed integrally with the extension piece 231 and having a screw therein a ball screw 233 coupled to the ball nut 232 and rotated forward and backward to adjust the drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut 232 it is configured to include a support member 234 supporting the forward and reverse rotation while preventing the sinking of the ball screw under the ball screw 233"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605553-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "therefore in order to solve the above problems a trap structure is formed inside a conventional sewage receiving device and a ventilation cap having a vent hole a spherical lightweight check ball a funnel shaped gradient ring a trapping pipe and a semi circular container a trap structure in which the parts are assembled in sequence is assembled and it is normally assembled and installed at the inlet of the sewage collecting device to prevent backflow of odors and pests through the sewage accumulated on the check ball and trap part which normally block the gradient ring as the sewage flows through the purpose of the drain is to be easily made by the rise of the check ball and the discharge of air through the vent"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to a multipurpose street culvert structure the purpose of which is to use a block of the same shape to guide water to a drainage facility regardless of a road gradient"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "description of the related art generally on a pavement road a drainage system is provided to prevent rainwater from being stored on the road surface during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned problems of the prior art and can use a block of the same shape to guide water to a drainage facility regardless of a road gradient"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "according to the first aspect of the present invention a street with a curb and a block having the same shape in which a drainage channel is formed is buried along the length of the road between the sidewalk and the sidewalk or between the road and the median strip"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "the city culvert structure according to the present invention is characterized in that drainage can be guided irrespective of a road gradient by using a block body having the same shape"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2886528-B1", "para_id": "para_83", "text": "as described above the street drain structure according to the present invention can guide drainage regardless of the road gradient by using blocks of the same shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "10 0758560 registration date september 7 2007 in the gradient precast trench structure block 100 when a trench structure is formed by combining the block 100 with another block 100 by being located on the outer body of the block 100 the outside of the block 100 is step 170 formed to fix the cover on the upper body base portions 180 located at the lower ends of both sides of the outer body of the block 100 in order to increase the bonding property with the cement placed on the floor where the block 100 is to be installed and fixed to install and fix the block 100 a u shaped drain unit 120 that performs erroneous drainage treatment so as not to leave residue and residual water at the bottom of the drainage channel a drain pipe 160 for discharging the wastewater flowing from the drain 120 to a septic tank a drain pipe connection unit 150 for discharging wastewater flowing from the drain unit 120 of the block 100 to the drain pipe 160 by being formed in an oval shaped intaglio on one side of the bottom of the block 100 a relief 191 formed on one side of the outer body of the block 100 to facilitate connection between the block 100 and another block 100 an intaglio 192 that is located on the outer body of the block 100 on the opposite side of the embossed 191 and is combined with the embossed 191 to facilitate connection of the block 100 and the counter block it is coupled to the lower grooves on both sides of the connection portion of the block 100 100 through the attachment screw 210 and prevents shaking and bending after combining the block 100 and another block 100 in a trench structure"}]</data>
</edge>
