  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101586456-B1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "3 the crushing unit 71 1 of the one impeller 71 has a downward slope so as to crush solids such as algae and form an upward flow of water based on the shape of the crushing unit 71 1 the crushing section 71 1 of the impeller 71 forms an upward inclined gradient so as to pulverize the solid matter such as algae and form a downward flow to form a downward flow based on the shape thereof"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100338306-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "conventionally in order to reduce the flow velocity of the pipeline the pipeline is laid with a gentle gradient and a drop hole or manhole is installed in the middle to adjust the step by step and in case of a cast in place concrete facility such as a box type culvert it is designed to have a small step inside the culvert to prevent crushing of the facility"}]</data>
