 "insulation", "transfer", "sensor", "capacity", "pm", "equation", "positioning", "simulation", "concrete", "circuit", "network", "value", "formula", "nozzle", "deterioration", "inside", "tm", "heat", "friction", "heating", "estimation", "correction", "ti", "bus", "control", "connection", "problem", "case", "drain", "mass", "residue", "unit", "waste", "shape", "input", "energy", "guidance", "body", "pressure"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["receive", "happen", "solve", "position", "take", "connect", "look", "introduce", "base", "accord", "substitute", "cause", "have", "ignore", "reinforce", "wash", "flow", "face", "can", "relate", "dot", "restore", "pump", "twist", "output", "provide", "set", "prevent", "attach", "enhance", "correspond", "leak", "describe", "form", "measure", "calculate", "represent", "pass", "occur", "couple", "decay", "follow", "correct", "determine", "facilitate", "bury", "accumulate", "purify", "discover", "pip", "result", "stabilize", "show", "find", "may", "discharge", "store", "detect", "change", "obtain", "include", "perform", "operate", "mean", "constitute", "supply", "use", "construct", "estimate", "know", "sense", "close", "rotate", "extend", "improve", "transmit", "be", "adjust", "collect", "generate", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_130", "text": "20 water leakage detection system 50 distribution reservoir 100a 100b 510 800 piping network 101a 101b sensor 110a 110b estimated water leakage area 120 piping 200 monitoring device 210 sensor device 220 communication unit 230 303 pressure sensor 240 access point 250 internet 301 control unit 302 317 communication if 305 318 internal bus 311 processor 312 memory 313 storage 314 external device if 315 input if 316 output if 401 data acquisition unit 402 dynamic water level calculator 403 difference calculator 404 visualization unit 405 abnormality determination unit 406 estimation unit 407 output unit 408 estimation data storage unit 409 judgment data storage unit 500 ground 501 502 503 504 650 810a 810b 810c 810d 810e location 520 water surface 525 hydrodynamic gradient 530 hydrostatic pressure 540 hydrodynamic pressure 550 booster pump 560 hydrostatic level 561 hydrostatic head 562 572 altitude 570 dynamic water level 571 dynamic water head 600a 600b dynamic water level distribution 620a 620b 750 760 normal vector 710 difference 900 910 simulation result 1000 1100 1210 visualization information 1200 1410 1420 1430 screen 1220 map 1310 1320 1330 contour map"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102669555-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition for example in the case of concrete forming a drainage channel there is a risk of water leakage occurring at the connection area and when rainwater or sewage flows in or leaks the concrete cracks due to deterioration or changes in the volume of moisture due to temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540454-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "it solves the uneven condition of the drainage pipes that are buried in the ground and solves the problems that may occur due to the subsidence of the ground in the soft ground and sometimes reinforces it to prevent the leakage of the connection part by twisting the drainage pipe due to the depression of the ground"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pipeline in which pressure gradient detectors are attached to the upstream and downstream sides and a device for detecting the occurrence of leakage in the pipeline is connected to these detectors the device comprising based on the output difference of the above detector the leakage detection index leak is calculated as leak nln 2_e 2m however n number of data 2_e error variance m leakage detection index calculation circuit calculated based on the order of the filter and the leakage detection index leak obtained as the output of this calculation circuit is used to determine whether or not a leak has occurred"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in this case as a first step it is necessary to promptly detect the occurrence of a leak and this is a prerequisite for discovering the leak location"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products in which drainage gradient and level adjustment is easy and pollutant purification function is enhanced and more particularly drainage gradient and level adjustment is possible when drainage trench construction drainage that is easy to prevent leakage from occurring at the connection part between adjacent drainage trenches and to purify pollutants that cause foul odors and decay accumulated rainwater or wastewater by stagnant soil or residue inside the trench the present invention relates to a polymer concrete precast drain trench coupling system using industrial by products with easy gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the present invention is to solve the above conventional problems it is easy to adjust the drainage gradient and level when constructing a drainage trench to prevent leakage from occurring at the connection part between adjacent drainage trenches and stagnant soil or residual inside the trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "it has a very excellent effect of preventing water leakage occurring at the connection part between the trenches and purifying pollutants that cause foul odors and decay rainwater or sewage accumulated by stagnant soil or residue inside the trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products with enhanced drainage gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function of the present invention constituted as described above facilitates drainage gradient and level adjustment during drainage trench construction this prevents water leakage at the connecting part between the connected drain trenches and has a very excellent effect of purifying pollutants that cause foul odors and decay rainwater or wastewater accumulated by the stagnant soil or residue inside the trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106330-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "according to claim 1 tilt detection sensor 40 is provided on the circumference of the main body 10 to detect the gradient change of the main body 10 leakage detection means 50 provided on the outer circumference of the body 10 to detect water leakage from the body 10 a sewage detection sensor 60 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to detect when sewage is supplied through the water supply pipe 14 a flow rate measurement means 70 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to measure the flow rate of sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 further comprising a washing means 80 for washing the flow rate measuring means 70 using the discharged water discharged to the drain pipe 15 the leak detection means 50 it is formed in a cylindrical shape extending in the front rear direction and having an opening 51a formed on one surface and the collecting case 51 provided so that the opening 51a is in close contact with the circumferential surface of the main body 10 it is provided inside the catchment case 51 and includes a leak detection sensor 52 for detecting the collected waste water inside the catchment case 51 the flow rate measurement means 70 a support bracket 71 provided inside the water supply pipe 14 an impeller 72 rotatably coupled to the support bracket 71 and rotated by sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 it is connected to the impeller 72 and includes a rotation sensor 73 for measuring the rotational speed of the impeller 72 the cleaning means 80 a water storage tank 81 connected to the drain pipe 15 through a connection pipe 81a to store a portion of the discharged water discharged through the drain pipe 15 an injection nozzle 82 provided to face the impeller 72 inside the water supply pipe 14 and connected to the water storage tank 81 through a supply pipe 82a it includes a water supply pump 83 provided in the middle of the supply pipe 82a the management server a receives the signals of the tilt detection sensor 40 the leak detection means 50 the sewage detection sensor 60 and the flow rate measurement means 70 the slope of the main body 10 is set it is changed to a reference value or more or the sewage detection means 50 detects the sewage or the sewage detection sensor 60 the sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 is sensed to the flow rate measuring means 70 when it is detected that the signal of the sewage measured by the dropping below a preset speed a warning signal or a message is transmitted to the portable terminal b if the rotation of the impeller 72 is not detected by the rotation detection sensor 73 in the state in which water passing through the drain pipe 15 is sensed by the sewage detection sensor 60 the water feed pump 83 is operated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106330-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "according to another feature of the present invention it is provided on the circumference of the main body 10 is provided with a tilt sensor 40 for detecting the gradient change of the main body 10 and is provided on the outer circumference of the main body 10 leakage detection means 50 for detecting leaks generated in the body 10 and a sewage detection sensor 60 provided in the water supply pipe 14 to detect when sewage is supplied through the water supply pipe 14 and the water supply pipe 14 is provided in the flow rate measuring means 70 for measuring the flow rate of sewage supplied through the water supply pipe 14 and the discharge water discharged to the drain pipe 15 to wash the flow rate measuring means 70 further comprising a washing means 80 the leak detecting means 50 is formed in a cylindrical shape extending in the front rear direction and an opening 51a is formed on one surface so that the opening 51a is attached to the circumferential surface of the main body 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "tm ti h ti to cp \u03c1 \u03b4 wherein ti is a temperature of fluid in the pipeline and the unit is k h is a convection heat transfer coefficient of steam and a thermal insulation layer 6 in the pipeline and the unit is w m2 k cp is a specific heat capacity of steam and the unit is j kg k \u03c1 is a steam density and the unit is kg m3 \u03b4 is a wall thickness of the pipeline namely a distance by which steam flows out from the inside of the pipeline via a leakage hole to the outer wall of the pipeline in unit time and the unit is m s \u03b4 mt\u03c1 a wherein m is a mass flow of steam namely a fluid mass of the fluid that passes through an effective cross section of a closed pipeline in unit time and the unit is kg s t is a unit time namely 1 s and a is the area of the leakage hole and the unit is m2 a corresponding relationship between a steam pressure and a temperature in the heating pipeline is obtained by an antoine empirical formula or by looking up a table of steam pressure and temperature enthalpy values as shown in a formula 7 below ln p 9.3876 3826.36t 45.47 7 wherein p is the steam pressure and the unit is mpa t is the steam temperature and the unit is k a value p calculated by substituting tm as the steam temperature into the formula 7 is the pipeline leakage transient pressure pm corresponding to the pipeline leakage transient steam temperature tm in step 3 the process of positioning a leakage location by the plc according to a pressure gradient method is specifically as follows firstly a pressure gradient p x leftbracketingbar u upstream of a leakage point and a pressure gradient p x leftbracketingbar d downstream of the leakage point are calculated p x leftbracketingbar u p 1 pmx 8 p x leftbracketingbar d pm p 2l s x 9 wherein l is a distance from a pressure sensor within a region of the leakage point to a temperature sensor downstream thereof and the unit is m s is a distance from a temperature sensor within the region of the leakage point to a pressure sensor downstream thereof and the unit is m x is a distance from the location of the leakage point to a pressure sensor upstream within the region of the leakage point and the unit is m x represents a gradient direction dot over p 1 is a pressure value detected by the pressure sensor upstream of the leakage point and the unit is mpa dot over p 2 is a pressure value detected by a pressure sensor downstream of the leakage point and the unit is mpa and pm is the pipeline leakage transient pressure and the unit is mpa it is known from a formula for conservation of momentum within a steam pipeline p x leftbracketingbar u f \u03c1 u22 d 10 p x leftbracketingbar d f \u03c1 u22 d wherein f is a friction coefficient u is a flow velocity of steam and the unit is m s \u03c1 is a steam density and the unit is kg m3 d is a pipeline diameter and the unit is m the aperture of a leakage hole is less than the pipeline diameter and a pipeline length and the variation of friction coefficients of two adjacent sides of the leakage hole within a short distance are ignored in the case of pipeline leakage no phenomena of obvious free outflow and flow reduction of steam occur because of the presence of the thermal insulation layer 6 and therefore pressure gradients upstream and downstream of the leakage point are approximately the same and after being stabilized the pressures restore an original pressure distribution along the pipeline it can be obtained from simultaneous equations 8 10 that x l s p 1 pm p 1 p 2 since the arrangement locations of the sensors are known the location of the leakage point can be positioned accurately according to a calculated value x and in step 3 in the process of positioning the location of the leakage point a correction coefficient \u03be is introduced and the value x is corrected by a method of using temperatures to correct pressures wherein the correction coefficient is represented by a formula below \u03be 2 tmt 1 t 2 a corrected new value x is x l s p 1 pm p 1 p 2 \u03be wherein tm is the pipeline leakage transient steam temperature and the unit is k dot over t 1 is a temperature value detected by the temperature sensor upstream of the leakage point and the unit is k and dot over t 2 is a temperature value detected by the temperature sensor downstream of the leakage point and the unit is k"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_55", "text": "2 performing energy analysis on fluid at the leakage location of the pipeline to obtain the leakage transient temperature taking a temperature variation as guidance for solving the pressure gradient positioning the leakage point of the heating pipeline improving positioning accuracy performing logical operation via the plc by the algorithm finding the leakage in time and outputting early warning signals"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_132", "text": "when an on off event happens to the heating supply pump unit at the starting end of the pipeline a great gradient variation of the pressure in the pipeline may be caused which can cause a false leakage early warning easily therefore the plc collects data from the pressure sensors and the temperature sensors to form a pressure dataset p1 p2 p3 p4"}]</data>
</edge>
