urces 933 barges or quarantine ships 934 seaweed 935 sawtooth plows 936 boreholes 937 pipe bridges 938 anodes electrode plates 939 cooling air bubbles 940 bits 941 marine tunnel traffic devices dock hull deck top sdu hull deck center sdm dock hull deck bottom s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100899798-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "a main inlet and a plurality of auxiliary inlets are formed so that the sewage flows in and the outlet is formed on the opposite side of the main inlet so that the sewage is discharged and a trap installed at the auxiliary inlet to prevent backflow of odor and the body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100696883-B1", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "in addition after coupling the upper and lower fixing frame 20 of the connector using the bolt 51 and the nut 52 the plastic stopper 53 to block the coupling hole 23 formed in the upper fixing frame 20b to rain water or it is preferable to prevent corrosion of the bolt 51 and the nut 52 by moisture or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "garbage strainer 20 consisting of a trash container 24 to accommodate a grating lid 30 positioned above the rubbish trap net 20 and seated on the seating part 11 and having a plurality of ribs formed in a mesh shape to be opened excellent receiving block for trash characterized in that comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101080118-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional technique described above has a problem in that leakage of the sewage is serious because it is difficult to cope with shrinkage expansion caused by torsion of the sewer pipe or seasonal factors.the present invention has been made to solve the various problems according to the prior art described above an object of the present invention is to facilitate the coupling between the above mentioned water outlet socket and sewage pipe while allowing the sewage pipe to be connected to the manhole using the water outlet socket the sewage pipe can be precisely combined and to provide a new structure of the manhole and the sewer pipe to prevent the external earth and sand inflow and leakage of internal sewage or rain water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101041716-B1", "para_id": "para_64", "text": "therefore the scope of the present invention should not be limited to the described embodiments but should be determined not only by the scope of the following claims but also by the equivalents of the claims.10 power generation unit 11 solar module 20 support 100 rainboard 110 first settling tank 120 second settling tank 130 valve box 140 contamination separation pipe 141 electric valve 142 valve drive motor 143 backflow prevention trap 144 gas backflow prevention albo 150 suspended solids filter 160 steel grating 200 rainfall sensor 210 rain gauge case 211 rain gauge bottom 212 lever 213 coupling member 220 bucket 221 bucket pillar 222 bucket pillar support 223 lever 224 weight 225 magnet 226 switch 227 lever pin 230 water inlet 240 filter medium 300 terminal box 310 control unit 320 charging unit 330 input unit 340 timer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_20", "text": "in addition the index plate may serve as a shock absorber against the shock that may occur when engaging the uneven portion of the wall block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200333114-Y1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "contrary to the operation both of the divided objects 10 and 10 are immersed to an appropriate depth to reduce the length.as described above the present invention is configured to adjust the length appropriately to the specification of the rain gutter to which the dredging container is applied so that it can be easily and widely applied to the rain gutters of various standards thereby greatly expanding the scope of the application"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100418252-B1", "para_id": "para_47", "text": "in addition by forming a cover 17 to block the entire upper portion of the frame 11 to prevent rain water from entering the area being processed during rain to prevent the breakage of aggregates generated in normal rain water purification the cover 17 may cover the top of the frame 11 of the floating reactor structure 1 using a sheet of water resistant and acid resistant material or support on the top of the frame 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101441852-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "together with and an inflow control gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at an upstream portion of the purifier box constructed upstream of the multifunctional watercourse constituting a double discharge regulating gate connected to the door frame and the hydraulic cylinder at a downstream portion of the purge box a structure in which a double air duct coupled to the regulating water gate is formed at the lower end of the double discharge adjusting water gate a dust collector is configured to lift up a large contaminant at an upstream portion of the purifier box the structure of the vibration damper includes a first screen installed at an inclined position with respect to inflow water and a damper main body for filtering contaminants such as inflow water through a first screen and a second screen the rolling chains being configured to be continuously rotated by a driving force of a first driving poly that is belt coupled with a driving motor along a plurality of sprocket wheels formed opposite to both sides of the main body of the vibration damper a first driven poly configured on the other side of a rotational axis associated with said first driven poly a large lifting rake pin coupled with the rolling chain so as to lift large contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain not shown so as to prevent the pins from being separated from one side and the other of the outer surface of the pin a transverse coupling plate formed between the rolling chain and one side of the large lifting rake coupled with the pin a plurality of large lifting rakes formed between the transverse coupling plates a third screen having a plurality of water discharging holes for filtering small sized contaminants between one side and the other side of the rolling chain wherein the upper end of the third screen is coupled to the plate member to form a curved surface up to the upper end of the upper sprocket wheel a first upper and lower guide rails which are combined with the large lifting rake and act to assist the rectilinear motion of the rolling chain while preventing the pin which is simultaneously engaged with the rolling chain from being sagged by the weight of the obstacle lower guide rails third and lower guide rails and fourth and lower guide rails are disposed between one side of the pin and the other side by the four upper and lower guide rails structure a hitting rake for hitting and removing the impurities contained in the large lifting rake wherein the driving rake is joined to one side and the other side of the driving rake case by a white bond a structure coupled to a second driven poly on one side of the white paper the second driven pulley which rotates the pulley in the reverse direction a first driven pulley axially coupled to the driving motor and a rotary belt coupled to the driving pulley wherein the pulley is rotated counterclockwise to remove contaminants trapped between the large lifting rakes a discharge conveyor installed at a rear side of the main body of the damper to receive the dirt falling and discharge it to the outside an air pump operative to float light contaminants having a specific gravity introduced into the inside of the purifier box the air discharge pipe coupled to the air pump is installed in the inside of the purifier box to float the organic matter material molecules of light specific gravity contained in the rainwater or river water flowing into the purifier box to the upper end of the purifier box a conveyor belt to which a binding plate and a lifting barrel for pouring and removing lightweight contaminants introduced into the inside of the purifier box are coupled a structure in which the coupling plate and the lifting bristle are combined with a white paper a structure in which a plurality of holes are formed in the lower end of the lifting bar a structure in which a nonwoven fabric is installed on the bottom of the lifting jacket and then the nonwoven fabric is fixed to the lifting jacket using an engaging member having a plurality of water discharging holes formed at an upper end of the non woven fabric the conveyor belt is coupled with a plurality of roller motors not shown to rotate the conveyor belt"}]</data>
