water supply"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101637212-B1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "on the other hand when the suction disk 40 is horizontally conveyed in the front rear left and right directions in the reaction tank 20 the corner round members 22 provided at the vertical corners 21 of the reaction tank 20 are slightly since the suction force of the suction disk 40 reaches the corner of the reaction vessel 20 because it has the curved surface 22a having a large diameter it helps to solve the suction blind spot.20 reactor 21 vertical corner 22 corner round member 22a curved surface 23 supersonic 23a sleep 24 sludge 24a surface 30 diffraction disk 31 end plate 32 ejection hole 33 branch pipe 34 downward cylindrical wall 36 first burring portion 37 47 kyonggi tube 39 air pipe 39a reinforcing rib 40 suction disk 41 elbow 42 inlet 44 upward cylindrical wall 46 side inlet 48 forming section 49 exhaust pipe 50 separating disk 52 54 notch 56 second burring portion 60 three dimensional transfer mechanism 62 moving frame 62a 62b vertical beam 62c upper cross beam 62d lower cross beam 64 forward backward feed mechanism 64a 64b connecting plate 66 left and right feed mechanism 66a connecting plate 68 shanghai song instrument 68a support plate 68b reinforcing plate g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 lm guide b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 lm block t1 t2 front and back padding t3 left and right padding t4 shanghai plywood r1 r2 reinforced plate e1 e2 side fixing plate u1 u2 u3 u4 bearing block l1 l2 l3 l4 feed screw m1 m2 m3 m4 servo motor d1 d2 d3 d4 rotary encoders c1 c2 c3 c4 coupling k1 k2 k3 k4 brackets n1 n2 n3 n4 nuts t4a cutting section 70 control section 71 72 73 74 motor driving part 75 heater 76 blower 80 temperature sensor p1 first pump p2 second pump s1 level sensor s2 depth sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970306-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "in addition another object of the present invention is to form a negative electrode or a positive electrode separately so that the negative electrode or the positive electrode can be replaced individually during replacement due to corrosion breakage respectively.in order to achieve the above object the present invention is a sensor for measuring the temperature or hydrogen ion concentration such as constant sewage is coupled to the holder the amount of residual chlorine in which a negative electrode and a positive electrode is formed on one side of the holder a device for measuring the amount of residual chlorine in the indicator by measuring the amount of residual chlorine contained in the measured water by galvanic cell electrolysis by combining the measuring sensor separately"}, {"pat_id": "US-4199407-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4204914-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100463940-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "in the sealant cover 8 described above the expansion and contraction plate portion 8a is formed so that the expansion and contraction portion 8a absorbs the axial deformation due to the change in temperature and external impact"}, {"pat_id": "US-10011509-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in laboratory studies that we have conducted we have found out that the unwanted organoleptic properties of smell and taste are mainly originated from the phenolic compounds found in nejayote at ph and temperature of nixtamalization"}, {"pat_id": "US-4235680-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102736709-B1", "para_id": "para_78", "text": "therefore when the temperature control storage pipe 201 and the cooling water storage pipe 211 of the present invention are installed while extending in the longitudinal direction they are first wrapped with a rubber socket and then secondly wrapped with a coupling band so that each temperature control storage pipe 201 and each cooling water storage pipe 211 are connected and extend along the longitudinal direction"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "the wireless power transmitter 72 and the wireless power receiver 73 may exchange information such as state condition or coupling information of the docking station 71 water tank 10 and or the inner assembly 100 power usage information battery charging information of the battery b battery output voltage current information control information or information from various sensors e.g"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200186594-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "it consists of upper and lower cases 1 2 having an o ring 3 in the coupling portion to achieve a predetermined size and shape and waterproof and the lower case 2 is suction of water to perform a buoyancy control function the ballast 16 is provided with discharge ports 9a and 9b and the piston 7a is moved up and down by forward and reverse rotation of the dc motor 5a above the ballast 16 to obtain diving and buoyancy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "however the coupling by bearing is possible in a fermentation device operated at room temperature and normal pressure but there is room for problems such as leakage and deformation due to thermal expansion in a drying device supplied with high temperature and high pressure dry air"}, {"pat_id": "US-4203806-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4118283-A", "para_id": "para_49", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101626616-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water leakage measuring apparatus for a water supply pipe including a plurality of water pipes connected by at least one joint pipe a peltier element formed into a plurality of pieces and fastened to at least a part of the outside of the plurality of water pipes a battery for storing electricity produced by the peltier device a plurality of pressure sensors inserted in the holes formed in the at least one coupling pipe and sensing a first pressure of each of the plurality of water pipes a data memory for storing preset standard pressure values a controller for comparing the standard pressure value with the first pressure to determine whether the plurality of water pipes are leaking and and a radio signal processing unit for sending a message informing whether or not the leakage occurs to the outside under the control of the control unit wherein the peltier element produces the electricity using a temperature change of at least a part of the plurality of water pipes the plurality of pressure sensors the data memory the control unit and the wireless signal processing unit are driven using electricity stored in the battery wherein determining that the leaked water is leaked when the second pressure which is at least part of the first pressure is lower than the standard pressure value determining a second water pipe corresponding to the second pressure among the plurality of water pipes wherein the radio signal processing unit controls the second pressure and the information for identifying the second water pipe to be sent to the outside together"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101626616-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a leakage measurement method for a water supply pipe including a plurality of water pipes connected by at least one coupling pipe a first step in which a peltier element formed of a plurality of pieces and coupled to at least a part of the outside of the plurality of water pipes produces electricity a second step of storing electricity produced by the peltier device through a battery a third step wherein the data memory stores a preset standard pressure value a fourth step of sensing a first pressure of each of the plurality of water pipes by a plurality of pressure sensors inserted into holes formed in the at least one joint pipe a fifth step of the control unit comparing the standard pressure value and the first pressure to determine whether the plurality of water pipes are leaked or not and and a sixth step in which the wireless signal processing unit sends out a message informing whether or not the leak is caused to the outside according to the control of the control unit in the first step the peltier element produces the electricity using a temperature change of at least a part of the plurality of water pipes the plurality of pressure sensors the data memory the control unit and the wireless signal processing unit are driven using electricity stored in the battery in the fifth step determining a leakage if the second pressure that is at least part of the first pressure is lower than the standard pressure value and and determining a second water pipe corresponding to the second pressure among the plurality of water pipes and the sixth step of sending out the second pressure and information for identifying the second water pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102722253-B1", "para_id": "para_70", "text": "the present invention described above is not limited to the above described drawings and detailed description and it goes without saying that various modifications and changes made by those skilled in the art within the scope and spirit of the present invention as described in the claims below are also included within the scope of the present invention.1 collapse prediction monitoring system 10 detection work 11 conduit 12 conduit trench 13 gas pipe 14 heat pipe 20 remote observation tower 21 camera 22 communications department 30 control server 40 worker terminal 41 sensor trigger 42 data reader 100 housing section 110 hollow 120 cover 121 wrench home 130 extension tube 140 hollow thread 150 screw 160 insertion groove 200 detector 210 reception hall 211 reception space 213 coupling screw thread 220 vibration sensor water pipe 230 power supply unit 250 1st sensor module 260 vibration sensor 261 probe pin 270 temperature sensor 280 gas sensor 300 surface protrusion 310 top cap 311 relief stud 312 cap screw thread 320 upper tube 321 external screw thread 322 slot 330 alarm 331 flasher 340 tilt sensor 350 2nd sensor module 351 mcu 352 communication chip 353 antenna 354 memory 355 gps 360 sensor for trigger"}, {"pat_id": "US-4343683-A", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the pumps 182 and 192 like pumps 132 and 134 are submersible and hence any heat generated thereby is utilized to raise the temperature of the water in the storage system"}]</data>
