m s dl machinery room floor surface top mfgu machinery room floor surface mfg machinery room floor surface bottom mfgl valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201275-Y1", "para_id": "para_38", "text": "therefore the lifting rod 8 may be attached to the bottom surface of the opening and closing opening 7b via the through hole 72 through the hole 7e"}, {"pat_id": "US-5467640-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "monitor screen which is attached to said cable s second end said cable s semi rigidness further provides limited means for inserting said camera lights and housing into said pipeline via access hole one and aiming generally in the direction of the flow route to access hole two and controlling the attitude or aim of the remote camera lens said remote camera also has on its anterior surface a means such as an eyelet or recessed peg eccentrically located whereon the attached lanyard thereto and with the combination of said semi rigid camera cable and said lanyard attached to said camera housing manipulating said cable and lanyard to position said camera lens anterior of or beneath said rubber test ball with said lens aiming at said test ball e attaching another said lanyard reel end to said test ball which has anterior or posterior ends by means such as a spring clip or pneumatic hose coupling or camera access cable dummy coupling or a loop formed on said lanyard end f connecting said test ball s posterior end to a pneumatic hose which allows the test ball to be inflated thereby and which hose has first and second ends and is connected on said first end to a supply of pneumatic air pulling on said lanyard s service end thereby inserting at least one inflatable test ball into said pipeline via access hole two said test ball which has anterior and posterior ends and said lanyard s reel end is connected to said test ball s anterior end and the test ball is inserted via access hole two in said pipeline wherein when said test ball is manipulated by virtue of the retrieval lanyard and pneumatic hose to a point in a pipeline which said test ball is inflated to produce a temporary passageway seal or blockage in said pipeline by virtue of said test ball s exterior surface coming in contact with said pipelines interior wall and by virtue of its ball shape g attaching a mechanism for measuring the amount of cable or lanyard that has passed into or out of a pipeline wherein said mechanism has a numerical display which can be directly read h inflating said test ball to produce a seal or blockage in the pipeline being tested h filling the vertical pipe being tested with test fluid or water and by viewing the monitor checking to see whether the test ball has effectively sealed off the pipe from the test fluid or water column above the test ball i repositioning the test ball or manipulating it to produce a satisfactory seal if required j viewing the column of water via the access hole two into which the water or test fluid was pumped into the pipe being tested for stability k determine that the pipeline segment thus tested is leak free if stability of the water level is positive or leaking if the water level recedes into the pipeline l repositioning the camera and the test ball to check further down the pipeline if the prior step indicated no leakage or further up the pipeline if the prior step indicated leakage m continuing to narrow the search for the leak by eliminating sections of non leaking pipe segments by the technique described above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937578-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the lower part of the unit part has a funnel shaped bottom connection part and a coupling part for coupling with a water pipe to prevent deformation or leakage even at high water pressure so that the flow meter and valve facilities from foreign substances such as sand or slime that are contained in the groundwater together it is to prevent the failure of the lamp in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "in the groundwater well consisting of water pipe 50 which is a pipe that moves to the ground the upper casing of the ground water well to connect the well casing 40 and the water pipe 50 and protect the ground water well from the contaminant of the ground in the form of elbow elbow tube 100 having a predetermined internal diameter the thread formed on a portion of the inner circumferential surface of both ends and the inner cylindrical hollow shape one side is open and a screw thread formed on a portion of the inner circumferential surface is screwed with the fastening bolt 30 and on the other side of the closing surface to form an elbow tube connecting hole 210 having the same outer diameter as the elbow tube 100 a part of the elbow tube 100 is inserted into one and a coupling part 200 including a water level measuring tube 220 which protrudes from the closed surface with a predetermined inner diameter and penetrates therein a main body 10 consisting of and a coupling part 200 of the main body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_66", "text": "5 does not form a conduit in the main body because the motor is installed outside and in addition to the water level measurement tube 220 a separate tube is not formed in order to prevent leakage of pressure from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100528613-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a drain pipe body 11 having coupling grooves 113 of different lengths formed in the circumferential direction with the coupling grooves 113 circumferentially formed on the gentle slope 114 the speed reducing plate 12 having a plurality of different lengths is coupled to the coupling groove 113 of the drain pipe body 11 to reduce the flow rate of the sewage and the steel ring 15 is bonded to the lower portion of the drain induction pipe 115"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102220579-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a water spray pipe for spraying washing water a bypass pipe installed by connecting the filtration chambers arranged at both ends of the arranged filtration chambers and a water level installed inside the filtration chamber while being installed in the bypass pipe to bypass rainwater it includes a bypass motor operated according to the water level sensed through the detection sensor a contaminant collection tank connected to the water tank to collect sludge and impurities filtered from the filtration chamber initial excellent treatment tank comprising a"}]</data>
