  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100758560-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the gradient precast trench structure block 100 located in the outer body of the block 100 when the block 100 is combined with another block 100 to form a trench structure the outside of the block 100 to prevent the inflow of dirt from the outside a stage 170 formed to secure the cover over the body a base portion 180 positioned at both lower ends of the outer body of the block 100 to increase the bondability with the cement placed on the floor where the block 100 is to be installed and fixed to install the block 100 a u shaped drainage portion 120 that performs a wastewater treatment so as not to leave residues and residual water at the bottom of the drainage path a drain pipe 160 for discharging wastewater flowing out of the drain 120 to a septic tank a drain pipe connection part 150 formed in an elliptic intaglio on one side of the bottom of the block 100 to discharge wastewater flowing out of the drain part 120 of the block 100 to the drain pipe 160 an embossed 191 formed on one side of the outer body of the block 100 to facilitate connection of the block 100 with another block 100 an intaglio 192 formed on an outer body of the block 100 on an opposite side of the embossment 191 and formed to facilitate connection between the block 100 and a counterpart block in combination with the embossment 191 it is coupled to the lower grooves on both sides of the connection portion of the block 100 100 through the attachment screw 210 and after the coupling of the block 100 and another block 100 in a trench structure to prevent shaking and bending a connection part 200 formed to easily install the trench structure wherein a connection part 200 supporting the block 100 when the trench structure is formed using the connection part 200 is formed on a bottom surface thereof the block 100 is modularized into 1m to 3m using the connection part 200 to connect two or more blocks 100 to form a trench structure and then embedded in cement installed at the installation location to shake the trench structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "the method of claim 1 the horizontal retaining rod is formed of a coupling groove of the one side opening type the coupling groove portion of the resin material characterized in that the vertical support rod for supporting the horizontal retaining rod is configured to be fitted to prevent the gradient deformation of the buried waterway pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "according to another aspect of the present invention the horizontal retaining bar is formed to form a coupling groove of one side opening type the coupling groove portion is fitted so that the vertical support bar for supporting the horizontal retaining rod is fitted to prevent the gradient deformation of the buried waterway pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101259860-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "the coupling groove 21 and the cover channel pipe 20 forming the drainage channel 22 and the support ribs 23 are coupled to each other and the side surface insertion holes of the squares facing each other on the outer circumferential surface of the buried channel 10 12 the horizontal holding rod 30 to prevent the gradient deformation of the buried water pipe 10 is configured to prevent rotation while the coupling groove portion 31 of the horizontal holding rod 30 in the vertical support rod 40 by fitting the vertical support bar 4 it is configured to be supported by 0"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101026854-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "as the bottom plate construction method for the prefabricated water tank placing and curing concrete in a formwork constructed to a size that can support the water tank to form a first base chipping the first base surface and forming a joint in the same shape as the water tank arranging and assembling the base frame to the first base surface in accordance with the joint seating an angle bent to be in close contact with the inner surface of the base frame and the first base surface coupling a fixing bolt having a support member embedded in the concrete of the second base to each fastening hole of the angle and the base frame is supported so as not to be pushed by hydraulic pressure and fastening the fixing support by fastening the fixing nut to the fixing bolt making a step fixing the angle fixed by the fastening support with a set bolt to a first base seating a drain portion of the same block as a drain box and a pipe for guiding drainage of water on an upper surface of the first foundation inside the base frame placing and curing concrete so as to be gradient in the direction of the drain portion in the base frame on which the drain portion is seated to form a second foundation separating a block of the drain portion in the second foundation and installing a plurality of polyethylene sheets so that the ends overlap the upper surface of the second foundation fixing the drain box and the polyethylene sheet by heat fusion in a state in which the drain box of the drain portion is seated on the second base from which the block is separated and a plurality of fastener mounting steps mounted on a second base to prevent the flow of the polyethylene sheet by contraction so as to fix the polyethylene sheet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1 the horizontal retaining rod is formed to form a coupling groove of one side opening type the coupling groove is installed so as to prevent the gradient deformation of the side channel canal pipe is characterized in that the front end of the vertical support rod to support the horizontal holding rod is fitted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "according to one aspect of the invention the horizontal retaining rod is formed in the coupling groove of the one side opening type the coupling groove is installed so as to prevent the gradient deformation of the side channel canal pipe end of the vertical support rod for supporting the horizontal retaining rod configure to fit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101306471-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "comprising in the side insertion hole 12 of the square facing each other on the outer circumferential surface of the side channel canal 10 is configured to combine the horizontal maintenance bar 30 to prevent the gradient deformation of the side channel canal 10 to prevent rotation on the other hand it is configured to be supported by the vertical support bar 40 by fitting the vertical support bar 40 to the coupling groove portion 31 of the horizontal support bar 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an extension piece extending from a ball nut integrally formed with the extension piece and having a screw therein a ball screw coupled to the ball nut and rotated forward and backward to adjust a drainage gradient and level of the trench body block by raising and lowering the ball nut a polymer using industrial by products having an easy drainage gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function comprising a support member supporting forward and reverse rotation while preventing the ball screw from sinking under the ball screw concrete precast drainage trench coupling system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products in which drainage gradient and level adjustment is easy and pollutant purification function is enhanced and more particularly drainage gradient and level adjustment is possible when drainage trench construction drainage that is easy to prevent leakage from occurring at the connection part between adjacent drainage trenches and to purify pollutants that cause foul odors and decay accumulated rainwater or wastewater by stagnant soil or residue inside the trench the present invention relates to a polymer concrete precast drain trench coupling system using industrial by products with easy gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the present invention is to solve the above conventional problems it is easy to adjust the drainage gradient and level when constructing a drainage trench to prevent leakage from occurring at the connection part between adjacent drainage trenches and stagnant soil or residual inside the trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "it has a very excellent effect of preventing water leakage occurring at the connection part between the trenches and purifying pollutants that cause foul odors and decay rainwater or sewage accumulated by stagnant soil or residue inside the trench"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "3 the polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products in which the drainage gradient and level of the present invention are easily adjusted and the pollutant purification function is enhanced a plurality of trench body blocks 100 connected to each other having a cross section and a predetermined length in the connection portion where the plurality of trench body blocks 100 are adjacently connected connection support fixing brackets 200 for fixing and coupling while supporting the lower ends of both ends of the trench body blocks 100 connected adjacently however the trench body block 100 is formed of a polymer concrete material and a cover formed in a predetermined depth and longitudinal direction from both upper ends 110 in order to mount and fix the cover on the top of the trench body block 100 a seating end 120 and a drainage passage 130 formed in a longitudinal direction in the inner center of the trench body block and integrally formed in a u shaped cross sectional shape from the cover seating end 120 to drain rainwater or sewage an embossed portion 140 formed at one end of the trench body block 100 and configured to secure a connection connection with the other end of the trench body block 100 to be adjacently connected and a concave portion 150 formed at the other end of the trench body block 100 and configured to fix the connection in correspondence with the raised portion 140 of the trench body block 100 connected to each other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215278-B1", "para_id": "para_50", "text": "the polymer concrete precast drainage trench coupling system using industrial by products with enhanced drainage gradient and level adjustment and enhanced pollutant purification function of the present invention constituted as described above facilitates drainage gradient and level adjustment during drainage trench construction this prevents water leakage at the connecting part between the connected drain trenches and has a very excellent effect of purifying pollutants that cause foul odors and decay rainwater or wastewater accumulated by the stagnant soil or residue inside the trench"}]</data>
</edge>
