  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101012226-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in addition the conventional partition wall has a problem that the shrinkage phenomenon occurs in the winter the lifting phenomenon occurs on the mating surface to cause leakage and the breakage of the partition wall due to expansion in summer.the present invention has been made in view of the above problems the object of the present invention not only can adjust the height of the main body according to the change of rainwater and sewage but also a plurality of the main body by fixing a single reinforcing beam and coupling force and by increasing the stiffness of the body to prevent distortion of the body due to water pressure and further provided with a support beam in the body to improve the durability and to adjust the length of the body in accordance with temperature changes to prevent damage to the body to provide sewage and storm divider assemblies for sewage pipes with"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100731773-B1", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "a storage block having a plurality of nut settling grooves formed at upper and lower portions of each column at least one side of the top plate having a stepped portion and a bottom portion of the bottom plate having a coupling portion integrally with the base surface it consists of a top block having a rectangular plate shape and the end is mounted on the top plate step of the storage block to form the same plane as the top plate of the storage block the storage block is repeatedly arranged in a straight line a plurality of the upper blocks are configured to be coupled between the storage blocks in a straight line to form a storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "a storage block having a plurality of nut settling grooves formed at upper and lower portions of each pillar at least one side of the top plate having a stepped portion and a bottom portion of the bottom plate having a coupling portion integrally with the base surface it consists of a top block having a rectangular plate shape and the end is mounted on the top plate step of the storage block to form the same plane as the top plate of the storage block the storage block is repeatedly arranged in a straight line a plurality of the upper blocks are configured to be coupled between the storage blocks in a straight line to form a storage space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248173-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "the pillar block 100 is a precast concrete block in which the main part 110 the support part 120 and the head head 130 are integrally formed and the main part 110 the support part 120 and there is no particular restriction on the shape and size of the main head 130"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582121-B1", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "therefore research on a new storm storage tank that is structurally stable easy to manage internally and unnecessary waste of materials has been continued in the art.the present invention is to solve the above problems to provide a new coupling structure of rainwater storage facility through the combination of the block and the slab through which rainwater storage tank to prevent waste of unnecessary materials and to secure sufficient internal space it aims to provide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582121-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "as a constituent means for achieving the above object the present invention is a column is formed in each corner of the top plate and the bottom plate so that each opening is formed on the side of the cube a plurality of nut placed grooves on the top and bottom of each column is formed at least one side of the top plate is formed with a step the bottom plate is a storage block is formed in the coupling portion to be integral with the base surface and an upper surface block having a rectangular plate shape and having an end mounted on the upper surface plate step portion of the storage block to form the same plane as the upper surface plate of the storage block wherein the storage blocks are repeatedly arranged in a straight line"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101883760-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the sewing machine according to the present invention is constructed such that one side and the other side of the sewing line are connected to one side of the sewing line and the other side of the sewing line and a wear plate operating spring 600 configured to elastically work such that the wear plate 200 returns to its original position as the wear plate 200 rotates in accordance with the inflow amount of the sewage in an automatic weir for use in a good toilette using an elastic action so that the wear plate 200 can return to its original position as the inflow amount is reduced in the frame 100 and is made of stainless steel material a shaft insertion groove on one side and the other side of the wear plate 200 so as to be engaged with the shaft 210 an anchor bolt coupling groove to be coupled to the upper side of the sewage pipe 10 and an anchor bolt 20 inserted and coupled to the anchor bolt coupling groove is connected to the upper side of the sewer line 10 the wear plate 200 the sewage and storm surge directly come into contact with the upper surface of the sewage and stormwater and the sewage and storm surge are rotated by the pressure applied to the upper surface of the warehouse plate 200 so that even if the pressure applied to the upper surface of the sewage and rainwater ware plate 200 is weak the upper surface is configured to be larger than the lower surface area a shaft coupling groove is formed on one side and the other side of the wear plate 200 so that the shaft 210 can be coupled to the wear plate 200 a fixing hinge 220 is formed on one surface and the other surface of the shaft coupling groove of the wear plate 200 for fixing the shaft 210 coupled to the wear plate 200 so as not to be detached from the wear plate 200 a shaft 210 and a spring coupling groove 211 are formed on one surface of the shaft 210 so as to be engaged with the wear plate drive spring 300 the drive spring adjusting nut 400 at least one bolt fixing groove 410 on the outer side so as to firmly fix the coupling state when the shaft 210 is engaged with the shaft 210 a fixing bolt 420 inserted into the bolt fixing groove 410 a spring insertion groove 430 is formed on one surface of the driving spring adjusting nut 400 so as to be engaged with the wear plate driving spring 300 and a shaft engaging groove 440 for engaging with the shaft 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "garbage strainer 20 consisting of a trash container 24 to accommodate a grating lid 30 positioned above the rubbish trap net 20 and seated on the seating part 11 and having a plurality of ribs formed in a mesh shape to be opened excellent receiving block for trash characterized in that comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101689857-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in an excellent water storage and utilization device for collecting and utilizing rainwater in a water tank t a support portion 100 for seating the water tank t at an upper portion from the ground a reservoir 200 seated in the inlet of the water tank t and extending at an inlet of the water tank t in a radially inclined manner to direct rain to the water tank t a superior guiding part 300 connected to the water collecting part 200 to guide the water to the water tank t and disposed in the water tank t so as to be stored in the storm water tank t except the initial storm and and a water supply pipe 400 mounted on a lower portion of the water tank t so as to discharge water stored in the water tank t and opened and closed by a valve 410 the water collecting part 200 an inlet 210 extending into the inlet of the water tank t a filter 220 mounted on the inlet 210 to block foreign substances entering the inlet 210 an opening closing part mounted on the inlet part 210 so as to open the inlet part 210 only when rainwater flows into the inlet part 210 and an expansion unit 240 connected to the inlet 210 and extending radially wherein at least one is radially connected the ball guide portion 300 may include a first pipe 201 having one end connected to the inlet portion 210 of the water collecting portion 200 and the other end extending inward of the water tank t and having one or more through holes 311 310 a second pipe 320 having one end connected to the first pipe 310 and the other end extended close to the bottom surface of the water tank t and the other end end sealed a drain pipe 330 having one end connected to the other end of the second pipe 320 and the other end extending to the outside through the water tank t and a valve 340 for controlling the discharge of the rainwater through the water pipe 330 the expansion unit 240 includes a first expansion plate 250 having one end connected to the inlet 210 and a second expansion plate 260 having one end radially connected to the first expansion plate 250 a locking protrusion 251 extending upward and a first coupling piece 252 extending downward and having a coupling hole 252a are formed at the other end of the first expansion plate 250 the second extension plate 260 is provided at one end thereof with a latching ring 261 extending upward so that the latching protrusion 251 can be coupled and coupled to the latching protrusion 251 and a second coupling 262"}]</data>
</edge>
