  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100925049-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the roads installed by joining and installing s shaped protrusions on one side corresponding to and are maintained flat without step and v shaped and inverted v shaped joints are installed on the upper and lower sides of the s shaped coupling part to prevent road damage due to the vertical movement"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "disassembly and assembly of the double structure block tank 598 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment is a lug connecting shaft coupling disassembly nut 604 is provided to be coupled to the bolt thread 603a of the bolt 603 for the portable lug connecting shaft coupling and a nut thread 603b is provided to fasten the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull first insert it into one large flange connection joint processing hole 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with a nut 604 and when connecting the block tank hull in a vertical form insert it into a plurality of lug processing holes 615 and fasten it to the bolt 603 with nuts 604 and fix it with a lug pin 608 so that the barge hull 591 on the upper part of the support tank of the floating dock device and the barge hull 592 on the lower part of the support tank form the floating dock device inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention and flood control equipment on the upper part of the barge hull 591 of the floating dock device of the above mentioned flood control equipment a helicopter station 619 and a thermal power plant 626 are equipped with satellite launch pads 643 and mooring towers 644 and space rocket launch pads to detect climate abnormalities and equipment for detecting the weather movement status of the floating dock device is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground passage flood prevention flood control equipment to detect climate abnormalities in order to prioritize emergency rescue the flood control equipment in the flooded area is always equipped with several air compressors 80 connected to rescue tubes 130 and ropes 131 at the accident site and before the underground passage is flooded the flood control equipment is configured inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment to prevent flooding by installing a water tank for rescue and flood control in the flooded area so that people can board the tubes 130 and be rescued by rescue workers"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in order to prevent underground flooding a vertical multi stage pump operation method is configured inside the main body 1 of the underground flooding prevention and water damage control equipment in the sump tank 34 connected to the above mentioned flood control equipment a control box 2 of a vertical multistage pump control panel and a pump isolation valve 5 and a pump backflow prevention check valve 6 are provided in the suction junction pipe 3 and the discharge junction pipe 4 to form a vertical multistage pump 8 and a fire hose 9 and a fire nozzle frame 11 and a hook 13 in a detection sensor 12 and a jig 22 in a pipe 14 are configured to control the flow rate to the disaster prevention waterway 17 while forming a vertical multistage pump operation method inside the main body 1 of the flood control equipment for flood prevention of underground passages the flood control equipment which consists of fire pumps and high performance submersible pumps a hook and a wire rope a machined hole and a shackle a bolt and nut a washer and a hinge a flange or a flange stopper a wire mesh a coupling a coupling female threaded body 30 a coupling male threaded body 31 a gasket or rubber packing a nozzle hose equipment holder a reducer and a pump wheel spray the discharged water through the fire hose and in the fire station 40 a water film or a curtain water film is formed and a double vinyl tent or bag controls the flow rate and an elbow or tie