  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101064335-B1", "para_id": "para_34", "text": "as shown in figure 3 the present invention is characterized in that the jaw 11 is formed to hang the strainer 21 to filter the dirt on the upper part of the rain gutter which is floating leaves floating on the road surface cigarette butts and dirt accumulate in rain gutters to prevent rainwater or sewage inflow or flow flooding the road or these dirt accumulate in sewers through rain gutters impeding the flow of sewage overflowing sewage pipes this is to prevent it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102765499-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the present invention relates to a road drainage device which is installed in a drainage channel formed by excavating the ground and receives and guides road rainwater and is characterized by comprising a guide water channel pipe body fitted into the drainage channel and having an open upper portion to receive the rainwater a grating member fitted and fixed to the upper portion of the guide water channel pipe body connected to the drainage channel water permeation guide holes formed on a side wall portion of the guide water channel pipe body connected to the drainage channel a shielding control panel arranged inside the guide water channel pipe body to open or close the water permeation guide holes an elevating and lowering guide means provided in the guide water channel pipe body to elevate and lower the shielding control panel and a strainer member fitted and fixed to the water permeation guide holes formed in the guide water channel pipe body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "adsorbent cloth 17 is installed inside the oil water separation tank 12 and the rainwater level side of the oil water separation tank 12 flows in through the outflow pipe 18 to bend in a spiral direction along the inclined surface while flowing into the inclined plate settling tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100574280-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "referring to the effect of the present invention as described above while the rainwater is introduced into the freshwater lake the ground waste b is mixed together in the rainwater to block the inflow into the freshwater lake the worker is horizontal vertical strainer 1 3 will be moved to the site and assembled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102742594-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in a drainage system constructed on a road 10 for rapid drainage of rainwater the above road 10 forms a slope that gradually slopes downward from the sidewalk boundary stone 20 forming the boundary with the sidewalks on both sides toward the center of the road a collection tank 30 is constructed in the center of the above road to allow rainwater to flow in along the slope a rainwater pipe 40 is buried at a certain depth in the lower part of the above mentioned collection tank 30 to drain the collected rainwater a rainwater guide pipe 50 is connected between the above mentioned rainwater pipe 40 and the water collection tank 30 to guide rainwater a cover net 60 is installed at regular intervals on the upper part of the above water collecting tank 30 to block the inflow of foreign substances a concrete part 80 is constructed between the above cover nets 60 a guardrail pillar 90 supporting a guardrail 91 is constructed on the above concrete portion 80 a road center construction type drainage system characterized in that a cover net fixing protrusion 31 is formed on both sides of the above water collecting tank 30 to allow the fixing of the cover net 60 the upper part of the above rainwater guide pipe 50 has a structure that protrudes a certain height h from the bottom surface of the water collecting tank 30 a conical shaped strainer 51 is formed on the upper part of the above rainwater guide pipe 50 and a sanitary coating layer 31 is formed on the inner surface of the above water collecting tank 30 to prevent the formation of water stains and the adhesion of foreign substances"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426715-Y1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "the second pre application is a cylindrical shape of the hollow inside the housing having a water collecting port on the upper surface a plurality of water collection tanks having an inlet on an upper surface and a drain hole on a lower surface thereof the plurality of water collection tanks being fixed to the inside of the housing as a pipe one end is connected in communication with the sump of the housing the other end is drawn out through the housing and connected in parallel with the inlet and the drain of each of the respective sump in parallel to the initial rainwater into the respective sump a bypass pipe for supplying the effluent and receiving the purified initial rainwater discharged from each water tank and discharging it to the outside while bypassing the initial rainwater water flowing through the water collecting port when the water tank is in full water it is installed on the upper side of the catchment inclined to discharge the initial rainwater discharged from the bridge drain pipe into the catchment and the strainer to filter the confinement purifying processing means for purifying the initial excellent effluent water introduced into the respective collecting tanks by filling the inner space of the respective collecting tanks so as to be exchanged with a predetermined height from the bottom it is composed of a plurality of one way valve is fixed to each inlet of the respective collection tank to open and close the inlet in one direction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "garbage strainer 20 consisting of a trash container 24 to accommodate a grating lid 30 positioned above the rubbish trap net 20 and seated on the seating part 11 and having a plurality of ribs formed in a mesh shape to be opened excellent receiving block for trash characterized in that comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "according to the present invention since the sewage accumulated in the sewer can naturally flow back to the ground through the inlet cover while suppressing odors and pests pressure can accumulate in the lowland sewerage to prevent the problem of loss of facility damage or backflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100662712-B1", "para_id": "para_35", "text": "the present invention accommodates the odor blocking holes emanating from the manhole and when rainwater is introduced the opening and closing plug of the odor blocking hole is opened and drained and closed when the drainage is completed thereby preventing the odor from being emitted to the outside of the manhole the foreign matter flowing into the manhole with rainwater is filtered out of the strainer so that it is easy to collect and handle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "to block the odor flowing back from the sewer and when the amount of rain water is relatively large the rotary drainage guide plate rotates downward to filter the filth by the strainer while smoothing the inflow of rain water odor countercurrent blocking function and dirt sewer rain gutter with manure function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "including a rod and one side is fixedly coupled to both ends of the hinge shaft and the other side is composed of second connecting rods respectively coupled to both side plates of the strainer the strainer is the main weight of the rotating drainage plate if the amount of rainwater flowing into the opening is relatively small by limiting the rotation of the rotary drainage guide plate by the self load of the strainer to close the drain hole to block the odor flowing back from the sewer rain water when the amount of is relatively large the rotation drainage guide plate rotates downward to facilitate the inflow of rain water while the manure the present invention provides a sewer rain gutter having a bad smell counter current blocking function and a dirt filtering function for filtering dirt by a net"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in many cases the rotary drainage guide plate rotates downwards to smooth the inflow of rainwater thereby filtering dirt by the strainer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wow connected to the connecting pipe 41 by bypassing the initial excellent drainage portion 20 and at least one connection valve 42 formed with one or more connection valves 42 at the connection pipe 41 it is connected to the connection pipe 41 of the purified water connection valve part 40 to receive rainwater the lower center is formed with a drain valve 51a the cylindrical shape having a support column 51b formed around the drain valve 51a while forming the water purification plant 51 a strainer 52 having a mesh shape is formed inside the water purification plant 51 and the primary water purification unit 50 including a cover 53 which closes the upper portion of the water purification plant 51"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046131-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "in addition it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulated in the initial excellent water tank rainwater tank and sedimentation tank thereby ensuring the long term security of the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity.1 is a block diagram showing an example of the initial excellent water quality treatment system according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046131-B1", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "this contaminant strainer 15 is formed in a cylindrical shape having a predetermined diameter as shown in figure 3 is configured so that one side of the upstream side is opened so that the initial rainwater with the pollutant can be introduced into the inside"}]</data>
