  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101210549-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the guide groove 111 is disposed to be spaced apart from each other the body portion 110 is installed across the river and integrally formed at both ends of the body portion 110 the floating material collected and collected floating material g g is a water barrier structure 100 having a collection box 120 having a space formed therein to be drawn out to the outside forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210549-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the network structure 200 serves to block the floating material g floating on the river while climbing the water along the water level of the river to prevent the ride over the water barrier structure 100 in the embodiment of the support frame 210 and composed of the strainer 220 and the buoyancy body 230 is installed in the main body 110 via the buoyancy body 230 to be elevated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_533", "text": "the above mentioned firefighter nozzle 10 is connected to multiple pipe nozzles 10 at a distance of 1 meter or 3 meters using a 