l valve body center line vbcl or pbcl fire water level bottom wld fire water level wl l discharge level wlu pump body pb pump body vertical line pbvl pump body horizontal center line pbcl equatorial line el north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102859794-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "1 a drain trap according to the prior art includes a drain trap sleeve 1 that is buried in an indoor floor and has an overflow pipe 1a that protrudes upward in the center of the floor a base panel 10 that is buried in an indoor floor and is positioned in the upper center of the drain trap sleeve 1 and has a joint formed in the center of a space that is recessed to collect water a sealing cap 20 that is installed to cover the upper part of the overflow pipe 1a of the drain trap sleeve 1 to block an unpleasant odor that rises through the overflow pipe 1a of the drain trap sleeve 1 while maintaining a water level at a certain level from the inner bottom of the drain trap sleeve 1 an upper strainer 30 that is formed to cover the upper part of the base panel 10 and filter out foreign substances and the upper part is installed in the joint of the base panel 10 and is composed of an inner filter 40 that filters out foreign substances such as hair from water passing through the upper filter 30 while guiding downward water to drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067184-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a housing 10 having a suction port 13 through which water is introduced together with the pollutant and a storage space 11 in which the pollutant is stored and a discharge port 14 through which water is discharged an aberration 20 installed inside the suction port 13 to forcibly introduce external pollutants and water into the storage space 11 a drive motor 30 for driving the aberration 20 a strainer 40 installed in the outlet 14 of the housing 10 and filtering contaminants introduced into the storage space 11 a stand 50 installed at a bottom to support the housing 10 and a height adjusting device 7 for adjusting the lifting height of the housing 10 according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067184-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a housing 10 having a suction port 13 through which water is introduced together with the pollutant and a storage space 11 in which the pollutant is stored and a discharge port 14 through which water is discharged an aberration 20 installed inside the suction port 13 to forcibly introduce external pollutants and water into the storage space 11 a drive motor 30 for driving the aberration 20 a strainer 40 installed in the outlet 14 of the housing 10 and filtering contaminants introduced into the storage space 11 a stand 50 installed at a bottom to support the housing 10 it is installed in the suction port 13 the pulverization apparatus for pulverizing the suspended matter 500 in agglomeration state by spraying water at high pressure and a height adjusting device 7 for adjusting the lifting height of the housing 10 according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067184-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "1 to 3 the agitator for storage tank a according to an embodiment of the present invention the suction port 13 is introduced into the water along with the contaminants and the storage space 11 is stored contaminants a housing 10 having a discharge port 14 through which water is discharged an aberration 20 installed inside the suction port 13 to forcibly introduce external pollutants and water into the storage space 11 a drive motor 30 for driving the aberration 20 a strainer 40 installed in the outlet 14 of the housing 10 and filtering contaminants introduced into the storage space 11 a stand 50 installed at a bottom to support the housing 10 and a height adjusting device 7 for adjusting the lifting height of the housing 10 according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102168685-B1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "when external air is supplied due to a drop in the water level of the water filled in the sealed structure many pollutants in the atmosphere and foreign substances such as fallen leaves are blocked from entering the drainage through the ventilation port and on the contrary exhaust when the water level rises"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2926400-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "it is attached to the front side to remove the sediment accumulated in the intake garden 7 regularly or irregularly and to reduce the water level in the closed intake well 20 indicated by the water level detector 22"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2926400-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in some cases the intake strainer 10 may be used as a red repellent color to keep fish and the like from approaching"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210560-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210560-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "referring to figures 1 to 5 the network structure 200 as a function to block the floating material g floating on the river while moving up and down along the water level of the dimension control structure 100 in the present embodiment is composed of a support frame 210 the strainer 220 and the buoyancy body 230 is installed so as to be elevated in the blown beam 110 through the buoyancy body 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937578-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the lower part of the unit part has a funnel shaped bottom connection part and a coupling part for coupling with a water pipe to prevent deformation or leakage even at high water pressure so that the flow meter and valve facilities from foreign substances such as sand or slime that are contained in the groundwater together it is to prevent the failure of the lamp in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and having a buoyancy member 132b for providing buoyancy the dimensional control structure 100 consisting of a retaining wall structure 130 is installed so as to be elevated on the guide plate 131 to prevent the overflow of the river forming a rectangular shape as a whole the support frame 210 is inclined toward the collection box 120 both ends are installed on the support frame 210 the filter net 220 to pass the water and block the float g and support a network structure 200 having a buoyancy body 230 fixed to the frame 210 to provide buoyancy so that the support frame 210 and the strainer 220 are elevated according to the change in the water level of the river with a guide groove 311 formed along the inner longitudinal direction the guide bar 310 is installed along the upper longitudinal direction of the support frame 210 and can be rotated in the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 the lead screw 320 and the guide bar 310 which is installed so as to be movable are inserted into the guide groove 311 of the guide bar 310 and are screwed to the lead screw 320 to reciprocate along the longitudinal direction of the lead screw 320"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101210554-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "referring to figures 1 to 5 the network structure 200 as a function to block the floating material g floating on the river while moving up and down along the water level of the dimension control structure 100 in the present embodiment is composed of a support frame 210 the strainer 220 and the buoyancy body 230 is installed so as to be elevated in the blown beam 110 through the buoyancy body 230"}]</data>
