north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985920-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a hydroponic cultivation hydrogen water supply device comprising a pretreatment unit a desalting unit and a hydrogen generating unit the preprocessing unit raw water storage tank for storing raw water a raw water pump for pumping water of the raw water storage tank a strainer having a thickness of 20 to 200 \u03bcm to remove the solid material contained in the raw water an activated carbon filter for removing organic substances and residual chlorine contained in the raw water a pretreatment water tank for storing the pretreatment water passing through the activated carbon filter and and a pretreatment water pump for pumping the pretreatment water stored in the pretreatment water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102106221-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "providing the effect of preventing freezing of water meters as the geothermal heat pipe that is higher than the average temperature flows through the geothermal tube.1 is a cross sectional view showing a water meter protection tube using geothermal heat according to the present invention figure 2 is a perspective view showing the strainer of the water meter protection cylinder using geothermal heat according to the present invention 3 is a perspective view showing a clip of a water meter protection tube using geothermal heat according to the present invention 4a to 4c are perspective views sequentially showing a clip of a water meter protection tube using geothermal heat according to the present invention figure 5 is a cross sectional view showing a state of mounting the clip of the water meter protection cylinder using geothermal heat according to the present invention figure 6a is a cross sectional view showing a water meter protection cylinder using geothermal according to an embodiment of the present invention figure 6b is a cross sectional view showing a water meter protection cylinder using geothermal heat in accordance with another embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904985-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "at this time the filtration device 350 includes a flocculation reaction tank 351 for injecting chemicals into the treated water to cause coagulation reaction to form flocs the filtration tank is composed of a lower support having a gravel sand and strainer as a downflow filtration system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904985-B1", "para_id": "para_68", "text": "at this time the filtration device 350 includes a flocculation reaction tank 351 for injecting chemicals into the treated water to cause coagulation reaction to form flocs the filtration tank is a downflow filtration system which constitutes a lower support provided with gravel sand and strainer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102370139-B1", "para_id": "para_41", "text": "according to one aspect of the present invention in the strainer for spatially separating both the reaction tank for removing contaminants in the incoming wastewater and the treatment water tank for storing the treated water from which the contaminants have been removed through the reaction tank the strainer block and the strainer block are formed the first nozzle socket and the fastening structure are formed to improve the fastening force with the strainer block including the nozzle disposed in the nozzle hole and the step with the fastening structure formed on each surface the first nozzle socket on one side and the first nozzle socket on the other side it provides a strainer comprising the first nozzle socket and the strainer block and a second nozzle socket that is fastened to the nozzle on the other side and has improved fastening force.as described above according to one aspect of the present invention the temperature of the cooling water can be lowered by heat exchanging the cooling water to cool the data center with the outside while minimizing power consumption and the temperature rise due to the heat exchange with the cooling water is actively used for water treatment"}]</data>
</edge>
