north pole np south pole sp longitude ld latitude lt road surface upper part glu road surface lower part gll road surface lower part gld sea level upper part slu sea level sll sea level lower part sld outside the machine room omr inside the machine room mr inside the machine room imr top of the spray nozzle a body of the spray nozzle b bottom of the spray nozzle c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102687112-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the water pouring device 30 is cylindrical water dispenser body 31 a drive motor m installed inside the water dispenser body 31 and exposed through the bottom surface with the motor shaft in a sealed state a swirl generating tube 32 flange joined to the lower surface of the water intake body 31 a plurality of water jets 33 installed to be curved in the radial direction at intervals around the swirl generating tank 32 a swirl generating plate 34 built into the swirl generating container 32 and fixed to the motor shaft of the driving motor m a screw type shaft 35 protrudes from the center of the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 a flooding guide passage 36 formed on the lower surface of the swirl generating plate 34 and having a curvature in the same direction as the flooding water outlet 33 a guide block 37 protruding from the lower surface of the swirl generation plate 34 to form the flood water guide passage 36 a lower plate 38 fixed to the lower surface of the swirl generating tube 32 and having a through hole h in the center a support cylinder 39 fixed to the lower end of the swirl generating cylinder 32 and having a plurality of outlet holes g formed thereon including in the fifth step after drying the sludge collected in the fourth step 10 parts by weight of lignin sulfonate 15 parts by weight of guar gum 5 parts by weight of borax and 5 parts by weight of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid are added to 100 parts by weight of the sludge"}]</data>
