  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102840248-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "figure 11 is a schematic diagram conceptually showing the concept of a water sand ground bed fluctuation transport system by a water sand coupled analysis function in a simulation that constitutes a 4 dimensional water cycle reproduction interpretation prediction visualization simulation system related to an embodiment and the state of formation of a reef shaped topographic relief by slope flow erosion sediment movement and deposition due to artificial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "US-7883622-B1", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "secondary bypass loop 163 may include a multi position valve 168 that may selectively route water flowing in secondary bypass loop 163 through a salt erosion feeder cell 172 in which may be placed a block or cake 174 of a salt or a mixture of salts"}, {"pat_id": "US-7883622-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "in another application multipurpose enclosure 700 may be used as an erosion salt feeder by inserting a rod cake or block 740 of a salt mixture into chamber 705 instead of electrode plates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102525988-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "according to the present invention the device for reducing the flow rate of the water pipe is a vortex that is repeatedly generated in the reduction block and the diversion block and the revetment block disposed on both sides of the main body of the device which are disposed in front of the inlet and outlet thereby reducing the pressure and it is based on the effect of reducing the flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101162228-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "there was.the present invention was created in view of the above mentioned problems in the prior art and the vegetation protrusions and vegetation holes are formed at both sides including the bottom surface of the waterway block so that the movement and vegetation of the animals are easy and the flow rate it reduces the erosion of the channel by reducing the erosion and the width of the channel can be freely changed because the lower part is a prefabricated type and the key is formed at the bottom of the installation to prevent conduction buckling and crushing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100607719-B1", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "at this time to increase the lifting efficiency the tornado block 3 of utility model registration no"}]</data>
