  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-8741100-B2", "para_id": "para_48", "text": "likewise the pump 40 may be provided with corrosion and or erosion resistant liners to extend the life of the pump 40 thus further reducing maintenance and replacement costs"}, {"pat_id": "US-5551472-A", "para_id": "para_67", "text": "this reduction in corrosion and or erosion occurs because at least a portion of the fluid introduced through the second conduit i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-9732911-B2", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "the above noted and other objects in one aspect may be achieved by an integrated pipeline protection system of the present disclosure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100900679-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "each pouring part of concrete material is finished by manhole body made of synthetic resin material invert and top plate frame and has high corrosion resistance to prevent weathering erosion and leakage of concrete by wastewater and various chemical gases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100900679-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "through this the wastewater flowing into the manhole body 10 and various chemical gases generated therefrom touch the upper frame 41 made of synthetic resin material having high corrosion resistance thereby preventing weathering and erosion of the pour portion 47 formed therein"}, {"pat_id": "US-7043373-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "the present invention may also be applicable to heat exchanger tube inspections and monitoring pipelines for erosion or corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100992912-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "as a method of treating organic wastewater a first step of mixing and reacting the introduced organic wastewater in the flow adjusting tank 10 stirring the organic wastewater that has passed through the flow rate adjusting tank 10 with the stirrer in an oxygen free tank 20 to cause a denitrification reaction a three step of purifying the organic wastewater passed through the oxygen free tank 20 to receive oxygen from the biological reaction tank 30 which is biologically treated and to remove organic matter in an aerobic state a step of returning a portion of the organic wastewater passing through the bioreactor 30 to the anoxic tank 20 and sending the rest to the culture separation tank 60 the culture separation tank 60 is a five step of filtering the suspended solids using the filtration membrane 61 immersing the erosion reactor 62 converts the water mixed solids to the corrosion precursor material to send to the distribution tank 70 the sixth step of distributing the corrosion precursor material converted in the culture separation tank 60 is distributed in the distribution tank 70 a part of which is returned to the flow adjusting tank 10 and the other part of the corrosion precursor material is returned to the bioreactor 30 and the bioreactor 30 is equipped with an mlss monitoring device 31 to stop aeration when the suspended solids exceed a predetermined concentration precipitate sludge and then draw a portion of the sludge in the bioreactor 30 organic wastewater treatment method comprising the"}, {"pat_id": "US-9689771-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "coating pipe and conduit elements such as elbows t sections and straight sections with ceramic coating or other protective coatings may prevent corrosion and external wear on the pipe but does little to prevent corrosion or erosion from within the pipe and will eventually wear down over time despite being more wear resistant than standard non coated pipe sections"}, {"pat_id": "US-9671068-B2", "para_id": "para_24", "text": "a combinational arrangement of the nanosensor the electronic circuitry and microchips on the flexible composite layer are capable to monitor and process a plurality of parameters associated with the pipeline to generate at least one of the plurality of real time data relating to the pipeline such as pipeline leakage predict stress strain fatigue measurement corrosion and erosion future leakage or failure and detect any attempt to theft or tempering in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "this causes a problem that the treatment efficiency is lowered and in the case of low concentrations the tank capacity of the liquid corrosion tank may be excessive and in the case of high concentrations there is a problem such as an increase in air volume"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "while denitrifying nox n nitrogen nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen of the circulating fluid circulated from the aerobic liquid corrosion tank using the organic wastewater introduced from the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank as a carbon source the aerobic liquid corrosion tank by removing residual organics in the circulating fluid from the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank installed in the liquid corrosion tank and the liquid corrosion tank which oxidizes nh 4 n ammonia nitrogen with nox n nitrogen nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen"}, {"pat_id": "US-11519560-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "material degradation can lead to pipeline failures and control of pipeline pressure and or remedial activities is an important factor in ensuring continued safety of pipeline operations"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the settled solids are supplied to the secondary settling tank 416 by the central cone cone it is possible to deposit active erosion material pellets minerals containing active minerals minerals or ceramics that emit negative ions and ultraviolet rays that emit far infrared rays and negative ions by the secondary transfer pump 417 the excess sludge is returned to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 and the secondary aeration tank 414 in which the secondary bioreactor 419 filled with the mineral or ceramics packing 420 is loaded and the excess sludge discharged is discharged temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater and the biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage together with the excess sludge to be discharged to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 sludge precipitated in the secondary settling tank 415 is supplied to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the secondary bioreactor 419 and the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 a corrosive microorganism which transforms water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors or corrosive substances by providing a polyphenol compound as a metabolite by supplying a wastewater and microbes in symbiotic relationships and sent to the secondary aeration tank 414 to induce the whole of the secondary biological wastewater treatment system to be subjected to the wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and the microorganisms which are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms and the secondary settling tank 415 the second biologically treated water which is the overflowing water is the second biological treatment step of the low concentration wastewater sent to the final biological treatment water tank 421 the secondary biologically treated water is subjected to sterilization treatment by a combination of at least one of oxidizing agent oxidizing agent ultraviolet ray irradiation electrolytic oxidation or electron beam irradiation and then subjected to sand filtration to remove suspended solids a final treatment step of the wastewater discharging the treated water when the dehydrated cake dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process is supplied to the mixer 500 a moisture adjuster and a soil conditioner are injected into the mixer mixer 501 while stirring to adjust the water content to 60 to 65 wt and fed to a fermentation tank 503 which is opened and straightened by the fermentation tank feed conveyor 502 and then flipped to the fermentation tank mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 30 to 50 days"}, {"pat_id": "US-11879568-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "many pipelines currently in operation are susceptible to leaks for example because they are or have become structurally deficient due to manufacturing defects corrosion erosion or other sources of damage to the structural integrity of the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "denitrifying removing the remaining organic matter from the circulating fluid from the anaerobic liquid corrosion tank and oxidizing ammonia nitrogen to n0x n nitric acid nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen in an aerobic liquid corrosion tank extracting the liquid corrosion solution treated in the anoxic liquid corrosion tank and the aerobic liquid corrosion tank into a mixing tank while the input and circulation of the organic wastewater is stopped for 1 hour per day injecting the liquid corrosion solution drawn out into the mixing tank into an agglomeration reaction tank and coagulating with a coagulant and a ph adjusting agent and separating the flocculated liquid erosion solution into sludge and desorption solution with a dehydrator when the organic sewage is introduced into the first storage tank 2 vol or less of the circulating fluid circulated between the anoxic liquid corrosion tank and the aerobic liquid corrosion tank is added to the first storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in this case if the treated water is reused as the washing water of the dehydrator the cod of the treated water accumulates and there is a problem of exceeding the target water quality standard.the present invention is to reduce the odor gas generation in the pre treatment process of the collected organic sewage maintain the mlss concentration of organic sewage to be injected into the liquid corrosion tank on an appropriate basis and set the volume and ratio of the anaerobic liquid corrosion tank and aerobic liquid corrosion tank in the case of alternating anoxic respirators the amount of circulation is calculated according to the inflow ammonia concentration and the input amount and the excess bod of the new high concentration organic sewage injected into the aerobic liquid corrosion tank is treated and the amount of bod and ammonia nitrogen flowing out of the aerobic liquid corrosion tank is minimized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100769997-B1", "para_id": "para_60", "text": "the amount of circulation is about 1.5 times the total amount of the anaerobic liquid corrosion bath solution and the aerobic liquid corrosion bath solution and the liquid erosion liquid that has completed liquid erosion is stopped while the input and circulation of the anoxic liquid corrosion bath solution and the aerobic liquid corrosion bath solution are stopped for 1 hour a day"}]</data>
</edge>
