  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "while denitrifying nox n nitrogen nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen of the circulating fluid circulated from the aerobic liquid corrosion tank using the organic wastewater introduced from the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank as a carbon source the aerobic liquid corrosion tank by removing residual organics in the circulating fluid from the oxygen free liquid corrosion tank elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank installed in the liquid corrosion tank and the liquid corrosion tank which oxidizes nh 4 n ammonia nitrogen with nox n nitrogen nitrogen or nitrite nitrogen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the settled solids are supplied to the secondary settling tank 416 by the central cone cone it is possible to deposit active erosion material pellets minerals containing active minerals minerals or ceramics that emit negative ions and ultraviolet rays that emit far infrared rays and negative ions by the secondary transfer pump 417 the excess sludge is returned to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 and the secondary aeration tank 414 in which the secondary bioreactor 419 filled with the mineral or ceramics packing 420 is loaded and the excess sludge discharged is discharged temperature aerobic digestion tank 200 in the treatment stage of the high concentration wastewater and the biological deodorization tower 601 in the deodorization treatment stage together with the excess sludge to be discharged to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 sludge precipitated in the secondary settling tank 415 is supplied to the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 air is supplied from the blower 422 to the lower portion of the secondary bioreactor 419 and the secondary microorganism culture tank 418 a corrosive microorganism which transforms water soluble organic substances into water insoluble corrosion precursors or corrosive substances by providing a polyphenol compound as a metabolite by supplying a wastewater and microbes in symbiotic relationships and sent to the secondary aeration tank 414 to induce the whole of the secondary biological wastewater treatment system to be subjected to the wastewater treatment by the corrosive microorganisms and the microorganisms which are in symbiotic relationship with these microorganisms and the secondary settling tank 415 the second biologically treated water which is the overflowing water is the second biological treatment step of the low concentration wastewater sent to the final biological treatment water tank 421 the secondary biologically treated water is subjected to sterilization treatment by a combination of at least one of oxidizing agent oxidizing agent ultraviolet ray irradiation electrolytic oxidation or electron beam irradiation and then subjected to sand filtration to remove suspended solids a final treatment step of the wastewater discharging the treated water when the dehydrated cake dehydrated in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process is supplied to the mixer 500 a moisture adjuster and a soil conditioner are injected into the mixer mixer 501 while stirring to adjust the water content to 60 to 65 wt and fed to a fermentation tank 503 which is opened and straightened by the fermentation tank feed conveyor 502 and then flipped to the fermentation tank mixer 504 for 1 to 3 times day for 30 to 50 days"}]</data>
