ve", "span", "deformation", "body", "height", "pretreatment"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["receive", "make", "position", "weld", "connect", "float", "accord", "increase", "have", "minimize", "accommodate", "reinforce", "fix", "flow", "can", "will", "provide", "mention", "expect", "bend", "prevent", "attach", "correspond", "describe", "form", "measure", "eliminate", "ensure", "switch", "filter", "pass", "couple", "say", "do", "assemble", "roof", "penetrate", "exceed", "become", "fall", "move", "induce", "insert", "intend", "seat", "remove", "cover", "reduce", "may", "discharge", "store", "grate", "obtain", "guide", "incline", "perform", "consist", "open", "block", "blow", "mean", "supply", "use", "transport", "close", "rotate", "extend", "control", "register", "characterize", "shape", "be", "hang", "span", "generate", "collect", "instal", "comprise"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100523904-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "of course such changes will fall within the scope of the claims.the effect of the present invention can be expected by the configuration and action as described above even if the underground pipeline connecting the indoor drainage pipe and roof excellent pipe around the building vulnerable to the influence of sedimentation to the sewer manhole storm manhole and storm pipe the pipeline naturally rotates according to the settlement direction and the length of the pipeline is also increased by the amount of settlement which prevents damage and excessive deformation of underground pipelines ensuring durability reducing maintenance costs extending the life span and reducing the maintenance work around buildings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when the wind is blown the odor preventing curtain is opened and the odor is generated.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned disadvantages of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a non powered flow rate control device for preventing malodorous flow which comprises a flow rate control device which is detachably attached to a distal end portion of a sewer pipe and it is possible to collect all the high initial initial storms generated at the beginning of the sewage or rainfall that flow in the usual way into the sewage subtraction channel and the rain that flows in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall it is possible to prevent the overflowing of the stormwater by reducing the outflow section of the sewage and to naturally induce the slurry moving along with the storm into the river to prevent the accumulation of the slurry on the sewage drainage pipe which is in close contact with the inner side wall surfaces of the flow rate regulating device while being rotated up and down odor proof packing is installed on the wall to block off odors generated in the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101744938-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "when the measured degree of contamination of the initial stormwater is equal to or less than the set reference pollution value 1000 formed on one side of the initial storm drain pipe 600 to provide a closure signal to the first storm drain pipe 600 in this case the opening closing means 500 is not closed even when the closing signal due to the lapse of the set opening time is received from the rainwater detection control device 700 and is closed when receiving the closing signal from the pollution judgment means 1000 wherein said non point contaminated initial good treatment system comprises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101560719-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the first filtered outflow in the pretreatment tank 100 is passed through the connection pipe 200 to the storage tank 600 the storm surges are temporarily stored in the storage tank 600 and then penetrated into the ground while storm surplus exceeding the storage capacity of the storage tank 600 flows through the storm drainage pipe 500 the present invention provides an infiltration storage structure using the assembled infiltration storage block unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101560719-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "the first filtered outflow in the pretreatment tank 100 is passed through the connection pipe 200 to the storage tank 600 the storm surges are temporarily stored in the storage tank 600 and then penetrated into the ground while storm surplus exceeding the storage capacity of the storage tank 600 flows through the storm drainage pipe 500"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "garbage strainer 20 consisting of a trash container 24 to accommodate a grating lid 30 positioned above the rubbish trap net 20 and seated on the seating part 11 and having a plurality of ribs formed in a mesh shape to be opened excellent receiving block for trash characterized in that comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101484891-B1", "para_id": "claim_14", "text": "in an initial high boiling point contamination treatment system 100 connected to the end of the conduit or the river water from which the polluted water is discharged to provide pollution excellence and selectively supply only the initial nonpoint pollution excellence a reservoir 200 for storing initial boiling impurity contamination provided to the water collection channel 130 of the overflow collecting unit 100 and performing a primary settling of contaminants a siphon pipe 295 discharging the initial nonpoint contamination excellent stored in the reservoir 200 when the water level of the reservoir 200 becomes equal to or higher than the height of the highest part in the reversed u shape"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "in order to prevent the foreign matter such as soil from flowing into the storm drain pipe 25 the storm drain pipe 25 may be inclined downward or the storm drain pipe 25 may be bent downward"}]</data>
</edge>
