  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102802400-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "however since the drainage hole formed on the upper surface of the rainwater pipe block of the conventional road curb stone is formed horizontally to the road surface and covered with a metal grid not only is it difficult to drain the water quickly but the width of the road that can be used by vehicles is narrowed and when the road curb stone is damaged due to a vehicle accident the entire block that comprises the road curb stone and drainage pipe must be replaced and at night especially during heavy rain the positions of the road curb stone and the road cannot be clearly identified which poses a risk of accident"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101740801-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "10 894022 discloses that the variable rainwater is formed so as to protrude upward so as to allow the initial rainwater to flow in and a gutter having an inlet pipe formed at one side thereof a solid separator for separating the effluent and the solids from the initial stormwater effluent through the inflow pipe an oil water separator formed in a hollow shape surrounding the solids separator to separate the effluent and oil components a first processing unit including a settling tank formed at a lower portion of the separator and storing the solid material a first inlet hole formed to allow the effluent treated in the first processing unit to flow in a filtration unit configured to deposit contaminants contained in the effluent and a microfiltration wall for purifying the fine pollutants and the effluent a second porous filter disposed in the cartridge porous filter and having a plurality of oil holes formed on the outer periphery thereof for final purification of the effluent a third processing unit including an outlet member having a plurality of outflow holes formed on an outer periphery thereof and a filter support member connected to the fixing unit and the fixing unit to which the cartridge porous filter and the outlet member are fixed and a drainage line is formed to discharge the effluent treated with the non point pollutant and a drainage pipe is formed at one side of the storage tank in which the effluent water is waterproofed quot non point pollutant treatment apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859669-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the rainfall information obtained from the rainfall sensor 900 the water level information obtained from the water level measuring apparatus 400 and the water quality information obtained from the water quality measuring apparatus 1000 an industrial complex comprising an rtu 700 for controlling the closing or opening of the well water gate 500 and the wastewater connection gate 600 via the water gate switch 550 or the water gate switch 650 for the water connection type initial stormwater and accident runoff classification system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102789466-B1", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "10 2014 0012031 title blockage prevention road drainage facility 2014.02.03 as announced in the official gazette includes a bypass drain installed at a location where a curbstone has been removed a manhole is installed at the edge of a road adjacent to the curbstone and the manhole has a bypass groove formed by removing a portion of an upper portion of a surface facing the curbstone to a set width and the bypass drain comprises a rectangular parallelepiped body having an empty interior an inlet formed in an upper portion of a surface facing the manhole of the body into which rainwater flows in an inlet formed at a lower portion of the inlet portion and fitted into the bypass groove of the manhole and formed by opening and protruding a portion of a surface located at a lower portion of the inlet portion on the surface facing the manhole so that rainwater flowing in through the inlet portion passes through an internal space of the body and is discharged to the lower portion of the manhole thereby flowing into a drainage pipe installed underground"}, {"pat