: "claim_1", "text": "garbage strainer 20 consisting of a trash container 24 to accommodate a grating lid 30 positioned above the rubbish trap net 20 and seated on the seating part 11 and having a plurality of ribs formed in a mesh shape to be opened excellent receiving block for trash characterized in that comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200303595-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention relates to a manhole drainage blockage preventing device to collect the rainwater or sewage and to prevent foreign substances from entering the clogged drainage pipe of the manhole discharged to the sewer pipe connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372189-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole for checking the amount of the deposited foreign matter on the ground at a predetermined interval in the sewage pipe or the drainage pipe or for discharging the precipitate to the ground in the manhole cover net mounted on the upper part of the manhole and connected to the rectangular frame and a plurality of supports in the transverse direction of the frame to prevent a large foreign object or person falling into the manhole a support frame made of a rectangular rod having an upper portion thereof open to be coupled to a lower side of the lateral support of the manhole cover net and having an inner coupling portion coupled to a lower side of the lateral support of the manhole cover net a flow plate extending from the bottom surface of the support frame to the side thereof to insert and block rainwater introduced from the top into the manhole by its elasticity sealed sewer cover plate characterized in that the cover sheet is attached to the upper and lower surfaces of the fluid plate to prevent corrosion of the fluid plate by applying an adhesive on one surface of the fluid plate to be attached to the upper and lower surfaces respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200372189-Y1", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "in order to achieve the above object according to a preferred embodiment of the present invention the manhole for confirming the amount of the foreign matter deposited on the ground at a predetermined interval in the sewage pipe or drainage pipe or to remove the precipitate to the ground in the manhole cover net which is mounted on the upper part of the manhole and is connected to a rectangular frame and a plurality of supports in the transverse direction of the frame in order to prevent bulky foreign objects or people from falling into the manhole the transverse direction of the manhole cover net the support frame is formed in the form of a rectangular rod the upper portion of which is open to be coupled to the lower portion of the support and the inner bottom surface thereof extends to the side thereof and includes a flow plate for introducing and blocking rainwater introduced from the upper portion into the manhole by its elasticity"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "method of monitoring drainage systems of rainwater reservoirs wherein a drainage pipe with which a throttling member is associated is associated with the rainwater reservoir and wherein the flow of sewage through the drainage pipe serving to divert sewage from the rainwater reservoir can be restricted to a predetermined nominal value characterised in that the flow through the drainage pipe is monitored to determine whether a predetermined excessively high value has been exceeded and or in that if the flow through the drainage pipe is restricted in a controlled manner to a predetermined nominal value monitoring is carried out to determine whether excessively rapidly succeeding changes in the direction of travel by the throttling member are effected by the controller and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether the water level in the rainwater reservoir or in a feed channel preceding the rainwater reservoir exceeds a predetermined depth while at the same time a predetermined low value for the flow through the drainage pipe is fallen below resulting in a blockage of the drainage pipe at this water level and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether permanent tightening of the throttling member is occurring and or monitoring is carried out to determine whether the actuator of the throttling member is overloaded and if so the throttling member is transferred into a safety position preventing the nominal value of the flow through the drainage pipe from being exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "monitoring arrangement for drainage systems of rainwater reservoirs for carrying out the method according to one of claims 1 to 3 characterised in that the monitoring arrangement 25 comprises first monitoring means which respond in a predetermined manner if a predetermined excessively high value of the flow through the drainage pipe is exceeded and or second monitoring means which respond in a predetermined manner to excessively rapidly succeeding changes of direction of travel by the throttling member caused by the controller if the flow through the drainage pipe 13 is restricted in controlled manner to a predetermined nominal value and or third monitoring means which detect if the water level in the rainwater reservoir or in a feed channel 11 preceding the rainwater reservoir exceeds a predetermined depth while at the same time a predetermined low value of the flow through the drainage pipe 13 is fallen below implying a blockage of the drainage point with this water level and or fourth monitoring means which respond to permanent tightening of the throttling member and or fifth monitoring means which respond to overloading of the actuator of the throttling member 14 and as a result of this response trigger a transfer of the throttling member into a safety position preventing the nominal value of the flow through the drainage pipe from being exceeded"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158955-B1", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "the solution of the present inventi