f the above mentioned disadvantages of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a non powered flow rate control device for preventing malodorous flow which comprises a flow rate control device which is detachably attached to a distal end portion of a sewer pipe and it is possible to collect all the high initial initial storms generated at the beginning of the sewage or rainfall that flow in the usual way into the sewage subtraction channel and the rain that flows in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall it is possible to prevent the overflowing of the stormwater by reducing the outflow section of the sewage and to naturally induce the slurry moving along with the storm into the river to prevent the accumulation of the slurry on the sewage drainage pipe which is in close contact with the inner side wall surfaces of the flow rate regulating device while being rotated up and down odor proof packing is installed on the wall to block off odors generated in the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "at this time since the amount of water is small so that you do not have to worry about inflow of the earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking the sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing the cross sectional area of the drainage pipe and preventing the burnout of the sewage terminal treatment plant while reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2598696-B1", "para_id": "para_279", "text": "for example in the event of a heavy rainfall where road water or water from the pavement may leak into the one or more open topped utility channels 20 the level of water can be eased by transferring the water from the one or more open topped utility channels 20 to the storm water drain 360 via the utility channel drainage pipe 380"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416507-Y1", "para_id": "para_45", "text": "as described above the rainfall runoff treated by the action of the soil filter bed layer 50 and the plant 80 is collected into the hole drainage pipe 30 through the hole of the hole drainage pipe 30 and is transferred to the public water and the hole drainage pipe the treated rainfall runoff that did not penetrate 30 penetrates into the existing soil through the soil membrane 70 at the bottom of the soil media layer 50 thereby preventing contamination of public waters and groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200234791-Y1", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in this case the amount is small so when you do not have to worry about the inflow of earth and sand the present invention can effectively prevent the earth and sand flowing into the tea house 3 during precipitation.the present invention prevents sediment inflow by blocking sewage flowing into the drainage pipe during rainfall thereby preventing cross sectional area reduction of the drainage pipe and burning of the pump in the sewage treatment plant and reducing the maintenance cost of the sedimentation lifting facility"}]</data>
