  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a first treatment part 230 formed in a shape and including a rainwater separator 234 for separating the effluent and the oil component and a sedimentation tank 238 formed under the solid separator 232 to store the solid matter a first inlet hole 202 is formed so that the effluent treated by the first treatment unit 230 flows in a filtration sedimentation reservoir for depositing contaminants included in the effluent is formed and fines for purifying fine contaminants and effluents"}, {"pat_id": "US-7661904-B2", "para_id": "para_31", "text": "thus the rainwater seeping into the soil 24 from the trench 23 can eventually recharge an acquifer and irrigate the soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "therefore when it is used for a long period of time it is deposited with soil or impurities due to the flow of rainwater in addition the blowing rain formed from the sudden occurrence of the heavy rain overflows the drainage capacity of the existing buried drain pipe resulting in an accident leading to the collapse as landslides in the valley or the soft area will be"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101902614-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "when the wind is blown the odor preventing curtain is opened and the odor is generated.summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above mentioned disadvantages of the prior art and it is an object of the present invention to provide a non powered flow rate control device for preventing malodorous flow which comprises a flow rate control device which is detachably attached to a distal end portion of a sewer pipe and it is possible to collect all the high initial initial storms generated at the beginning of the sewage or rainfall that flow in the usual way into the sewage subtraction channel and the rain that flows in a large amount due to the continuation of the rainfall it is possible to prevent the overflowing of the stormwater by reducing the outflow section of the sewage and to naturally induce the slurry moving along with the storm into the river to prevent the accumulation of the slurry on the sewage drainage pipe which is in close contact with the inner side wall surfaces of the flow rate regulating device while being rotated up and down odor proof packing is installed on the wall to block off odors generated in the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715378-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "10 1636033 registered on june 26 2016 environment friendly water and sewerage system for removing foreign material accordingly it is an object of the present invention to minimize the flow resistance of sewage water by eliminating the foreign matter in the sewage flowing through the sewer pipe to prevent foreign matter from being transported to the sewage treatment plant thereby reducing the burden on the sewage treatment plant it is also intended to provide a sewerage conduit structure having a foreign matter filter net structure that minimizes the generation of odor due to the corruption of foreign matter.according to an aspect of the present invention there is provided a sewage pipe system comprising a sewer pipe an excellent receiving portion provided at a predetermined distance from a drainage port provided between the boundary and the roadway between the roadway and the roadway and connected to the drainage pipe a foreign matter blocking unit installed on an upstream side of the excellent receiving unit to block floating foreign matter from flowing to the excellent receiving unit along with the rain flowing through the road surface and an excellent guiding boundary provided between the roadway and the drainage side to guide the roadside storm and foreign matter to the side of the foreign matter blocking part without flowing directly into the excellent receiving part and an upper end opened and having a flange portion at a top edge and a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the flange portion a lower flange portion that is inserted into the superior receiving body and opens at upper and lower ends thereof and is seated on the flange portion at an upper edge thereof a vertical portion bent upward from an edge of the lower flange portion a reinforcing cylinder having an upper flange portion that spans an upper end of a vertical portion of the superior receiving body a screwdriver coupled to the lower end opening of the reinforcing cylinder a grid like leveler cap covering the top opening of the reinforcing cylinder a cap engagement means for coupling the cap to the cap receiving stand and a connecting pipe connecting the excellent receiving body and the sewage pipe wherein the superior receiving body is inserted into a well receiving hole formed in the drainage port and the flange portion and the vertical portion are formed on the edge of the superior receiving hole and the mesh network is formed by bending inwardly at the lower end opening edge of the reinforcing barrel and the mesh network is formed in a state where the barrel mesh network is extended over the formed hanging jaws a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the mantle a nut welded and fixed to a lower surface of a central portion of the mantle and coaxial with the bolt penetrating hole a bolt penetrating hole formed at a central portion of the stainless steel cover a bolt head insertion groove formed in an upper end of the through hole a lower end portion of the bolt head insertion groove being in close contact with an upper surface of a central portion of the mantle and a coupling bolt penetrating through the bolt through hole the round bar and the bolt through hole to be coupled to the nut and having a head inserted into the bolt head insertion groove wherein the foreign a box shaped support frame whose lower end is closed and whose upper end is open and a foreign matter blocking lid formed in a lattice shape so as to be inserted into the support frame and the support frame of the foreign matter blocking portion is inserted and seated in the foreign matter blocking portion installation groove formed in the drainage port and a barrier block for blocking foreign matter the barrier block being provided at a position corresponding to the excellent receiving portion and provided with a plurality of through holes provided at a position without the excellent receiving portion wherein the boundary stones are formed so that the boundary stones installed in correspondence with the excellent receiving portions are formed higher than the other boundary stones so that the excellent flows flowing along with the foreign matters do not flow directly into the excellent receiving portions"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "garbage strainer 20 consisting of a trash container 24 to accommodate a grating lid 30 positioned above the rubbish trap net 20 and seated on the seating part 11 and having a plurality of ribs formed in a mesh shape to be opened excellent receiving block for trash characterized in that comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200348471-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a manhole for checking the amount of the deposited foreign matter on the ground at a predetermined interval in the sewage pipe or the drainage pipe or for discharging the precipitate to the ground in the manhole cover network mounted on the upper part of the manhole and connected to the rectangular frame and the support in the transverse longitudinal direction of the frame to prevent a large foreign object or person falling into the manhole a frame formed at the edge of the manhole cover net or a hook ring is installed in each of the four corners so as to be caught by the transverse support and the lower end of the hook ring is coupled and the lower cover is formed in a vertical direction with the hook ring"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102215279-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "however although the above described corrosion prevention drainage is not corroded by hydrogen sulfide in sewage or a concrete waterway pipe to prevent corrosion due to neutralization of concrete the acid rain that can be applied to the polymer concrete drainage pipe is alkalinized and neutralized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100529500-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "during the summer season large scale stormwater generated from sidewalks and roadways is drained through a vertical drainage pipe connected to the storm drain on the roadway in the drainage treatment method of the road characterized in that the rainwater is drained by a method of naturally falling during the drainage treatment through the vertical drainage pipe in the driveway 200 when a large amount of rain is generated due to heavy rain the rainwater collected through the rain receiver 210 is drained through the vertical drainage pipe 230 as it is the rainwater is penetrated through the drainage hole 112 of the permeable sidewalk block 110 of the sidewalk 100 and the rainwater that penetrates through the sand layer 120 is gradually inclined to block the barrier film collecting rainwater through 130 while collecting the rainwater generated in the sidewalk 100 in contact with the vertical drainage pipe 230 and through the drainage hole 142 of the rainwater inlet hole 140 seated on the seating portion 162 formed on both inner upper sides"}]</data>
